        StaticBook("\"An Undead Song\"", "Shadowninji", "The Undead are loose and Iblees may win. His assassins have come to rip off your skin. Evil eyes will see you if you try to run. The Undead will get you and laugh like it's fun. Walk away slow or they'll tear you apart, And laugh all day long as they rip out your heart. Evil eyes will see you if you try to stand still. The Undead will get you, Walk away slow or they'll tear you apart, And laugh all day long as they rip out your heart. Evil eyes will see you if you try to stand still. The Undead will get you, for Iblees they ki ll Hack 'em up, chop 'em up, cut 'em to bits Or else they will get you while laughing in fits.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Arrow\" by Birchwood Undead", "AnonymousMonster", "My legs are dangling off the edge, \n The bottom of the bottle is my only friend,\n I think I'll slit my wrists again and I'm gone, gone, gone, gone. \n My legs are dangling of the edge, \n A stomach full of potions didn't work again,\n Put an arrow in my head and I'm gone, gone, gone, gone. \nGone too far, yeah I'm gone again,\n It's gone on too long, tell you how it ends, \n I'm sitting on the edge with my two best friends, \n One's a bag of potions, one's a bottle of gin, \n I'm 200 feet up, yeah I'm up at the top \n I polished off this potion, now it's pushing me off. \n Cobblestone to me has never looked so soft, \n I bet my mother found my letter, now she's calling the guards, \n I gotta take this opportunity before I miss it, \n 'Cause now I hear their yelling and they're off in the distance, \n Believe me when I tell you that I've been persistent, \n \n'Cause I'm more scarred, more scarred than my wrist is, \n I've been trying too long, with too dull of a knife, \n But tonight I made sure that I sharpened it twice, \n \nI never bought nice clothes before in my life,\n But when you go to meet Aeriel you want to look nice. \n So if I survive then I'll see you tomorrow, yeah I'll see you tomorrow. \n My legs are dangling off the edge, \n The bottom of the bottle is my only friend, \nI think I'll slit my wrists again and I'm gone, gone, gone, gone.\n My legs are dangling off the edge,\n A stomach full of potions didn't work again, \n Put an arrow in my head and I'm gone, gone, gone, gone. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Beauty\", by John Masefield", "rittsy", "Have seen dawn and sunset on moors and windy hills \n Coming in solemn beauty like slow old tunes of Spain: \n  I have seen the lady April bring in the daffodils, \n Bringing the springing grass and soft warm April rain. \n I have heard the song of the blossoms and the old chant of the sea, \n And seen strange lands from under the arched white sails of ships; \n But the loveliest things of beauty God ever showed to me \n Are her voice, and her hair, and her eyes, and the dear red curve of her lips.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Casandra's Diary\"", "Orehime", "Entry 30: A select few Undead and myself were presented with new robes today from the Prophet himsel f, The dark forces inside my mind felt happy, well as happy as an evil spirit can be. I suppose \"I\" earned these clothes from my presence during the battle against the Orcs. The numerous bodies that fell at my feet must have pleased the Prophet and Overlord, although I trie d to will myself to stop attacking. Unfortunately, survival is an instinct that even an undead maint ains after being turned. I fear though that my \"comrades\" witnessed me holding back during the battl e. Could they see me, the real me, hiding inside the darkness? I must tread carefully for I fear the only way I can gain my humanity back is through the Prophet. Only he knows exactly what h appened to me that day in the alley. This evil force is beginning to stir, I must hide for now.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Death\", by William Butler Yeats", "rittsy", "Nor dread nor hope attend\n A dying animal;\n A man awaits his end\n Dreading and hoping all;\n Many times he died,\n Many times rose again.\n A great man in his pride\n Confronting murderous men\n Casts derision upon\n Supersession of breath;\n He knows death to the bone\n Man has created death.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Ember in Oren\"", "Triloq", "While traveling through Oren, two elves were alerted by a shout that the castle was in danger from foul sorcery.  The elves quickly went to the keep to help in any way they could. When they arrived, they encountered a creature called \"Ember\", which was unable to communicate in any known language.  The elves helped subdue the creature.  They wished to bring the creature back to Laurelin, where they knew the creature would recieve assistance. However, the humans threatened the elves, and forced them to leave.  As they were leaving, a shout was heard.  A princess was under attack by and assassin.  The elves defended her as best they could, but the assassin fled.  In the confusion, the humans let the creature escape When the elves tried to resubdue the creature, they were set ablaze. The creature managed to escape, though the assassin was eventually captured. But the treatment the elves recieved from the humans was disgraceful. Some of them even spoke of war between the humans and the elves.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Eros\", by Ralph Waldo Emerson", "rittsy", "The sense of the world is short, \n Long and various the report, \n To love and be beloved;\n Men and gods have not outlearned it,\n And how oft soe'er they've turned it,\n 'Tis not to be improved.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Flood\", by James Joyce", "rittsy", "Goldbrown upon the sated flood\n The rockvine clusters lift and sway;\n Vast wings above the lambent waters brood\n Of sullen day. \n \n \n A waste of waters ruthlessly\n Sways and uplifts its weedy mane\n Where brooding day stares down upon the sea\n In dull disdain. \n \n \n Uplift and sway, O golden vine,\n Your clustered fruits to love's full flood\n Lambent and vast and ruthless as is thine\n Incertitude!\n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Kin\", by Carl Sandburg", "rittsy", "Brother, I am fire\n Surging under the ocean floor.\n I shall never meet you, brother\n Not for years anyhow;\n Maybe thousands of years, brother.\n Then I will warm you,\n Hold you close, wrap you in circles,\n Use you and change you\n Maybe thousands of years, brother. \n \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Life\", by Sir Walter Raleigh", "rittsy", "What is our life? A play of passion,\n Our mirth the music of division,\n Our mother's wombs the tiring-houses be,\n Where we are dressed for this short comedy.\n Heaven the judicious sharp spectator is,\n That sits and marks still who doth act amiss.\n Our graves that hide us from the setting sun\n Are like drawn curtains when the play is done. \n Thus march we, playing, to our latest rest,\n Only we die in earnest, that's no jest. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Little Tiny Book\"", "Willizl33t", "This is a little tiny book...", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Love and Friendship\", by Emily Bronte", "rittsy", "Love is like the wild rose-briar,\n Friendship like the holly-tree----\n The holly is dark when the rose-briar blooms\n But which will bloom most constantly?\n \n \n The wild-rose briar is sweet in the spring,\n Its summer blossoms scent the air;\n Yet wait till winter comes again \n And who will call the wild-briar fair?\n \n \n Then scorn the silly rose-wreath now\n And deck thee with the holly's sheen,\n That when December blights thy brow\n He may still leave thy garland green. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Monsters and how to kill'em\"", "Botar", "(INTRODUCTION) Hello there! glad to see you picked up this book and with it the first step Into the task of defending yourself for the evil and deadly creatures that infest are lands , are lives and even are own homes also on that note any deaths as a result of this book are not my fault (CHAPTER 1: Zombies) Now a zombie in layman's terms is a corpse of a dead person who may have died a painful death, left things undone, or we unlucky enough to be friends with a necromancer but dont worry due to age they are rather slow and easy to hit but they also have massive amounts of strength and can hit hard and if not careful be snacking on  your face , but do not worry for with this guide you can slay them left and right. SWORDS: now they are good so slaying zombies for the fact they have great choping and sliceing power and easily chop off the head of a zombie killing it BOW & ARROW: now these are great killing tools for the fact you dont even have to get into the zombies range just snipe and laugh at the undead bugger as he has arrows sticking out of his face (CHAPTER 2 : skeleton) Now these bastards are aundead but due to there boney nature and do not really have any hand to hand combat ability they use the bow and arrow to shoot there target from afar. SWORDS: Now strangly enough these are the best tools for geting rid of the creature cause even if it has no flesh a sword cuting through ribs is still deadly. BOW & ARROWS: Now these are a good choice if you want to stay away from it but this could lead to a drawn out shoot out, beware. (CHAPTER 3: Spiders) These large, possibly altered arachnid's are fast and deadly but being nocturnal they are peaceful and relatively harmless during the day. SWORDS: these are the second best choice of tool to use due to the spider  's ability of fast movement and thus could get in hits on you before you kill it. BOW & ARROWS: now these are the optimal tools for dispatching the critter because of  range advantage you would claim over it and its eight legged stupidity. (CHAPTER 4: Creeper) Now these damnable things are a really big menace to all of us. they cause damage by blowing them self's up causing physical and property damage to everyhting in the area causing area's of land becoming no man's lands, filled with craters and ash. SWORDS: now for obvious reasons going into melee combat with this thing is a bad idea but if you can back up after striking it you can get enough shots on it to take it down. BOW & ARROWS: now these are the best tools to kill the creature cause ifit can not reach you it will not explode. (CHAPTER 5: Spiderjockey) Now these are rare but equally dangerous they are a example of enemy unions at work as a skeleton riding a spider granting the best of both and the weakness of neither due to the speed and deadly effective ness of it. SWORDS: now closeing the gap is the best idea here so swords are needed and will most likely what save's you bacon. BOW & ARROWS: now these are also useful for pelting the monster from affar and badly damage it before going in for the kill. (CONCLUSION) i hope you learned something from this book and that it should serve you well with its useful tips and help on how to kill the monsters of the everyday. thank you.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Nightpiece\" by James Joyce", "rittsy", "Gaunt in gloom,\n The pale stars their torches,\n Enshrouded, wave.\n Ghostfires from heaven's far verges faint illume,\n Arches on soaring arches,\n Night's sindark nave.\n  Seraphim,\n The lost hosts awaken\n To service till\n In moonless gloom each lapses muted, dim,\n Raised when she has and shaken\n Her thurible.\n And long and loud,\n To night's nave upsoaring,\n A starknell tolls\n As the bleak incense surges, cloud on cloud,\n Voidward from the adoring\n Waste of souls.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Poison Tree\", by William Blake", "rittsy", "I was angry with my friend;\n I told my wrath, my wrath did end.\n I was angry with my foe: \n I told it not, my wrath did grow. \n \n \n And I waterd it in fears,\n Night and morning with my tears: \n And I sunned it with smiles, \n And with soft deceitful wiles. \n \n \n  And it grew both day and night,\n Till it bore an apple bright.\n  And my foe beheld it shine,\n And he knew that it was mine. \n \n \n And into my garden stole.\n When the night had veiled the pole;\n In the morning glad I see,\n My foe outstretched beneath the tree.\n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Sign Language\"", "moon_stone", "Because It would scare you...", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Book of Child Rhymes\"", "NiNjAxR3M1Xx", "", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Dark Brotherhood\"", "NiNjAxR3M1Xx", "Introduction \n The world is very ignorant nowadays. And sheltered. If they only knew the truth of this world,they would cry and weep. The Brotherhood is one of these truths. It is my job to educate you on the lore and history of these evil rogues. Let us begin,first,with the History. \n History \n The beginnings of this guild are very humble,it seems. Abd very noble too. it started off as a few freinds banding together to fight off bandits,and evolved into the powerful influence to see today. I mean you. It is early morning in Laurelin at the moment. But let us continue.I may make many mistakes in spelling today. After this change, it started turning...nasty... The arrival of new recruits was enabled, but the arrival of \"The Stranger\" changed it all... Not much is known about him, but it is assumes that he is Iblees himself! It is worrying, but thankfully I have not seen him. Yet. Alas, that is all the history from the old lore I could find. Now onto the members. \nMembers Ranks \n The first and basic rank is the Recruit Danalus. They are the base of the guild, and they make up the majority of the newcomers. \n Next comes the Danalus. an advanced version of the Recruit variety, they are what comprise the guild at any given time. They are also decidedly more dangerous than Recruits, so look out! \n The final obtainable rank is the Koloth. This is the final rank- you cannot get higher. Except a few ranks...but they are invitation only. This is the next subject . \n The Invitation Ranks... \n These ranks are availible only from the Grand Master himself. They are very,very exclusive,and involve a significant level of risk too them. For example, the Silencer is a rank availible to the Koloths only, and is the personal assasin of either the Grand Master, High Councillor or lesser councel. They are given only the most dangerous and trusted contracts in recoginision of skill. If you see a Silencer, or s/he see's you, prepare for the Temple, because it is most likely that is where you will end up. If you survive,let me know. I will make sure that you get the proper treatment, for it has been known for them to carry cursed blades. \n The next invite rank is a lesser councel. They are seemingly for the purpose of helping with the main Council's meetings. At least 2 must be present in a meeting for it to be considered \"official\". They each have 1 Silencer between two at any given time. \n The highest rank for the invitations is the High Councillor. These are limited, and are considered important enough to have 1 Silencer each. Under special circumstances they may have a Listener instead. A Listener is a Koloth who doesn't get his hands dirty with blood. Rather, they hire other members to do it for them. A Listener is also a spy. They are chosen from the stealthiest members, and can blend into any situation. \n The Grand Master,or \"The Stranger\" \n Little is known about this man,or woman. They head the entire guild, and can have a Listener and two Silencers. These Silencers are a team. And are best known as \"The Black Hand\". A Black Hand member takes orders only from the Grand Master,and is allowed to break the Tenets. More on those in a minute. The current Grand Master is known only as \"The Stranger\". And has been head of the guild almost 300 years. A short time for the guild, which has been around since millenia. He cannot be challenged. He can only step down or have a \"perma-death\". It is unknown how the ceremony goes. For his initiation, that is. It is rumored that the Grand Master resides in Laurelin. This is nonsense. In all my time I have never even seen a Brotherhood member inside Laurelin. Or maybe I have... It is hard to tell. And now, we move onto the ways of recruiting. \n Recruitment(This is all speculation) \n The main way of recruitment is if you are approached by a member. This is usually the Grand Master. You are offered a position if you can be trusted. It is rare, but it has happened.  I personnaly witnesses it. It was...hard to stay concealed... but it ended ok.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The dwarves\"", "Darksalvo", "The Dwarves, are a strange people who live underground. They love two things: War and Food, like the orcs. They respect the elves, but they hate the humans for their arrogance anyway, some dwarves live in The Great Kingdom of Oren and some human in the underground holes of Kal' Uruguan.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Lamp burns brightly in the shade\"", "TheImpulseHQ", "Well done, you have been selected to join the Twin Lamps You will not be told what we do, until you are of High Rank You must not tell anyone, for we do not exist To even speculate on who That-Called-The-Vlagh is, is a death sentence Your First task is this, Spread Propaganda around Al'khazar about the ascended and how bad they are, do not be known, use a false name and no, Our real purpose is not to kill or weaken the Ascended it is much darker and sinister", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Ranger\"", "turret001", "Many years ago, far in the north, There was a village called, Arandor. || Arandor was home to my people called the Adunias Come in Join us", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Ruin\", by Walter De La Mare", "rittsy", "When the colours of the day\n Have from their burning ebbed away,\n About that ruin, cold and lone,\n The cricket shrills from stone to stone;\n And scattering o'er its darkened green,\n Bands of fairies may be seen,\n Clattering like grasshoppers, their feet\n Dancing a thistledown dance round it: \n While the great gold of the mild moon\n Tinges their tiny acorn shoon. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Sick Rose\", by William Blake", "rittsy", "O Rose thou art sick.\n The invisible worm.\n That flies in the night\n In the howling storm: \n \n \n Has found out thy bed\n Of crimson joy: \nAnd his dark secret love\n Does thy life destroy. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Spidus Climus Annoyus\"", "NiNjAxR3M1Xx", "\nHabits \n This species of creature documented in the fair land of Aegis is known as a nuisence. And the fact the get angry in the dark is all the more...Scary... However, they are relitivly easy to handle,and therefore are easily dealt with. The fact that some fall for them is...embarrassing,to say the least. The Minas found on the specimen however was pitiful,suggesting a very poor victim. This, accompanied by pork, suggests that this animal is aa natural predator. In summary, most of the time they are good for begginners in monster hunting. Except when they are accompanied by back-up , known only as \"The Spidus Jockeyus Dangerous\"! This variation of the creature should be avoided at all costs- You will find yourself at the Crypt instantly unless you are accompanied by a large squad of archers. This variation is host to an Iblees spawn, the Skeleton. It fires it's arrows at the victim before immobilising it with the spiders venom. Thank fully,they are so rare that I have only ever seen 2 in my life. I am lucky there isn't a 3rd... \n    This concludes this nature journel. I hope you have a great time hunting this beast, and that it doesn't kill you. Farewell for now! \n \n By Relok'oth Bob-Dylanus Sangreal. \n All rights reserved.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"the training grounds\"", "Zefmc", "Beyound these doors there was a great training ground. Many great warriors trained here to survive. Times were harsh and Iblees was strong we couldn't contain his minions for much longer. As Iblees grew in power injuries started appering in the grounds, it was ment to be safe.. As the warriors fell we had no choice we had to purge this area no trace could remain. We fought a long battle in the darkness of the tunnels they were the stronger. but we fought and we won at the cost of many. know only I remain a solitary gaurdian in the wake of evil....", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Wandering Wizard\"", "Darksalvo", "The Wandering Wizard is a strange person, who travel from kingdom at kingdom to help the people. Everytime is protected by a shield of powerful magic, and he know how use a lot of spells.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"The Worlds Need\", by Ella Wheeler Wilcox", "rittsy", "O many gods, so many creeds,\n So many paths that wind and wind,\n While just the art of being kind\n Is all the sad world needs.\n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"This is A NecrominconDigivolve\"", "Orehime", "How do I write in it now? Oh, there it is. You must keep your Digimon well fed in order to Digivolve to the next level. Patamon was awesome. The End.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Will\"", "Shuness", "Person of intrest: \"Will\" the Ranger. A man who is helping me on the Meagan case, was there when I lost sight of her in pursiut. Will not tell me his real name, for some odd reason. Seems to be a good man, although, they all act like that, don't they?", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Issue #4", "Possut", "A day after the attack against Alstion , me and my fellow staff member Darius,interview Oren Military Advisor Vardak Ciantar. We sit down and exchange some polite words , before the real interview. The Advisor is a good man it seems, with a very good manner, being an orc. \nWhen we get to business he early says that some guilds tried to defend Alstion, and attack the the undead . They were led and gathered around Vardak. But an Undead got to him very soon and he was not disposable for the upcoming battle. \n\" \"Was hurt by an undead, mangled my arm,\" he says. \"I sent my men towards Alstion, with orders to listen to anyone taking the lead. Do not know who did though. I had seven guards of Oren with me.\" We ask him if King Edmund had talk to him anything, if he had given any orders to defend Alstion. \n\"I was to await instructions from him. But I sent my men without word from him\", he says. \"I had to take the initiative!\" \n\"I do not know why no one else picked up the banner and gathered the soldiers. I thought if I did it, more would come to join us in future assaults. The guards stood tall and the morale was high.\" \nWhere was the King? \n\"I sent a scout who could not find him.\" We asked him why the King had not made any preparations for Alstions defences, with Snowy Fields defeated. The attack must have been expected. \n\"He was not truly prepared for it. All he had was rumors\", Vardak says. But why not expect the worst and prepare for it? \nVardak tilts his head in obvious thought and says: \"He was not prepared this time, to be honest.\" \nWhat is your comment on the guards not getting salaries but have to pay taxes? \n\"Guards do get paid. If they have not get a payment, they need to speak with me. I pay them 85 minas, I do not have enough to give them higher. Not until Chase, the financial advisor says so. Im waing for his word.\" \nBut the taxes the King collects would be more than enough to cover the Guard salaires, should it not?   \n\"The guards should not be taxed in my opinion. Neither should residential buildings.\" \nBut where does the tax money go? \n\"Stocking up on iron, paying the guard, and the rest is held for supplies for Oren.\" \nHow about the building of the keep in AlKhazar? \n\"That is being covered. The King paid for all the materials himself.\" \nAnything else you would like to comment, while I am here? \n\"To all readers who have heard the lies of me not paying the guard: I do pay the guard. I just have to wait for Chase to give me what I need. Its not a matter of not doing it, its a matter of not having the minas to do it. \" \nWith that, I thank Vardak. \n \n \nAfter the interview, I did some research. As a recruit you do not get paid. I do not know how many recruits there is. \n' Going to the bulletin boards I found a notice saying this: \"You question where the guards are? They are on the streets of Al'Khazar, begging for food. They are in the forests of Oren, hunting pigs. They are abusing citizens lookig for money, as their own King will not pay them. \nYou question where the guards are? They are not being trained, so having one nearby would only give you the advantage that a child with a wooden sword would. They are not learninbg how to fight, so they cannot help you to protect your tavern or shop. \nThe King neglects to pay the guards, so the guards neglegt to guard the people. THis is the King's fault, not the guards. Question him! \n~ L \n' ;;' \nGoing on, our reporter Kai, got a hold of Lord Tarus, Captain of the Oren Guard. Here is the interview. \n' \nWe met each other outside of Kramoroe. Apparently he had come to see me and ask for an interview. I was very happy to oblige. \nI asked him how he became captain. \n\"I became Captain a long time ago. I worked as a Templar and earned much respect.\" \nSo why are you seeking me out? \n\"I am dissatisfied with how King Edmund Sheffield is handling the guards. He is too peaceful and.. somewhat shadowy. He doesn't speak to or hear his people out. All he does is to build what he wants. There are problems that he seems to neglect. We are at war with a foe that'll end us all, and we can mostly see him in his \"Under construction\"- keep. He offers no solace to that in his negligence.\" \nWhat is the difference between the current and former king? \n\"King Perea was a good king. We held our lands, had a functioning army and no taxes. Now we do have taxes, but where does those minas go towards?\" \nYou are implying that those money don't go where they should. Do you have proof for this \" corruption\"? \n\"The guards are not tax free either. Why not take their pays in the taxes, eh? Maybe he's paying them all along by holing minas in his pocket? I 've heard many signs of corruption. Brett Perea was caught dealing with the Undead. The King's advisors had narry a job all their days in politics, but now their all heading branches. His (the kings) actions are generally suspicious.\" \nSo what do you plan to do? \n\"It's not what I plan, it's what the people of Oren plan. I can spout all my opinions all I want, but that doesn't mean things will change. People are the catalyst of newer things. Speaking out will fix things! If people want my help in change I'll be happy to be their voice.\" \nWhat would you say to the readers in Oren? \n\"Don't be afraid to step out of the line, and speak your opinions, citizens of Oren and Aegis!\" \nWith that we thank Lord Tarus. \n' \nWe are agreeing to the fullest with Lord Tarus. The Word is a powerful tool! Do not be afraid to use it! \nThat wraps todays issue. We will seek out the King for comments. \n' \n' \nPublished by: # THE AEGIS TIMES # \nTodays reporters: Kai and Glamdring \n' \nTerms & Agreement \nBy purchasing this newspaper you accept our Terms & Conditions which are freely to read at any property of The Aegis Times Newspaper Company.", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Issue nr.2", "Possut", "Today we will be talking to Lord Khronos of Alstion. With the recent Undead attack on Snowy Fields, is the proud town of the North  safe? \n \nWe will also be informing on how our subscription system will work. Be sure to get to the Closest Courier and get a subscription today! (Irba, 18th or The Deep Cold, 1309) \n' \nToday we will be talking to Lord Khronos of Alstion. With the recent attack on Snowy Fields, is th e proud town of the North really safe? \nWe will also be informing about our subsription system and how it will work, along with some other information. Be sure to get to the closest Courier and get a subscription today! \n' \n' The town of Alstion - danger or safety? \nDarius, reporter and chief Courier of the North, interviews Lord Khronos of Alstion. \n' \nAs I just sat down with Lord Khronos, lightning appears in the sky, indicating that Undead Hordes are close. \nAlstion is a town which lies to the North of Al'Khazar and have existed for two years now, which i s a short time for a town as well established as this. \nMy first question to the Lord is how he have achieved this sucess in suchs short time. He gives me a few, not too modest, words which should show us the professionalism of this town: \n\"Alstion is based of excellent leadership, effective marshalling of troops and resources, a good l ocation, a strong defence and also a good town design. \" \nWhat about the prices of houses, which are very low compared to other towns? \n\"Possibly yes, but mainly because it's a good place to live in\", the Lord says. \nAre the prices low because the Undead Horde are close? \n\"No, the prices were always this low and in the beginning of this town, there was no Undead. We ar e simply not interested in money in these parts of the land. Also, the poor people of Aegis needs a place to live at.\" \n' \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nAlstion Rangers \n' \nAlstion Ranger Commander Albrecht is looking for new ranger recruits and workers. Safeguard the No rth together with the strong Rangers of Alstion! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n' \nLord Khronos also warns us that the prices in Alstion will go up sooner or later, due to a high de \n\"Besides, the Undead do not bother us that much. Sure they are a great threat, but we have won the battles up until now, and if they try again, we can repell them again\", the Lord says with a smile. \n' \nAs most of you know, Snowy Fields was recently destroyed to the ground. Alstion prays that the tow n will not walk the same road as Snowy Fields. \nWhen you walk the city, you'll see guards and rangers passing by, to secure the future of Alstion. I ask Lord Khronos why Snowy Fields did fall to the Undead Horde? What did they lack? \n\"Snowy Fields was always risky, its defence was weaker than ours is now\", he says. \"However Alstio n needs as much support as it can get, everyone can help. We can always offer jobs such as gatherers and builders, along with Guarding, for those who are inte rested.\" \n' \n-------------Advertisement------------- Therving Agricultural - Your first stop for a bite of bread or the seeds for your farm, in the heart of Alstion! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n' \nTo end this interview, Lord Khronos gives us, The Aegis Times, and every reader out there, a few w ise words to think about: \n\"The key to success is not money, nor skills or items, but hard work and labour. That, above every thing else, will get you noticed.\" \nWe thank Lord Khronos for this interview, and wishes him luck and safety, on the walls of Alstion. \n' \n/General information regarding The Aegis Times and subscriptions\\ \nFrom this issue and onward, we will be offering subscriptions to our readers. Send a message to ou r office in Kramoroe toget a subscription. ((Please read our forum post for more exact information and how to get a subscription!)) \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nGuards of Kramoroe \n' \nLord Gabriel of Kramoroe is looking for guards to safeguard the town and the important highway. Go od pay, good housing, good company. Join TODAY! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n' \nThe Aegis Times has gotten quite a reputation, and we need more staff! Be sure to check the bullet in boards for vacant jobs, or contact Glamdring ((Possut)) for more information½! \n' \n' \nPublished by: # THE AEGIS TIMES # \nReporters in this issue: Glamdring and Darius \nWant to contact us?: Glamdring ((Possut)) - Office is in Kramoroe  \nI did a formatting mistake in the beginning, please ignore that.", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Issue nr.3", "Possut", "Joma,20th of The First Seed, 1310 \nToday we have an array of articles and news. Be sure to subscribe and also see the Terms & Conditi ons at the end ((Further information on Subscriptions is found on our forums)). \n' \n*Content* \nRoyal Wedding in Malinor \nGuildmaster Cataris being trialed \nThe Hooded, good or evil? \nThe Wandering Wizard, or The Wandering Gambler? \n' \n*Royal Wedding in Malinor* \nWhen walking in the forests of Laurelin, you can actually feel a new kind of joy in the air. I'll finish this fist Birds are singing happily and the trees are whispering even more than usual. Elves jumping around with big smiles on their faces. But why you might ask yourself? \nHigh-Prince Native is getting married! Of course every elf, tree and bird is happy with this lovely event! He is marrying the elven maiden Soriuss. \n\"Being 851 years old, it's about time I settled down\", the Prince says. \nThe ceremony will help gather friends of Malinor in one common place. The exact date and place is not decided yet, but we will update you as soon as we hear about it. \nMany congratulations to the couple, from The Aegis Times!  \n \n   \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nEast Oren Co. -Estates- \nDo you want to live in Al'Khazar but can not afford the 10.000 minas cost? Then contact Chase ((chase132)) or Lord_John ((SirPwnzalot700)) for cheap and affordable apartments for the everyday citizen! -------------Advertisement------------- \n \n' \n*Guildmaste Cataris is getting trialed* \nAs many of you know, a couple of days ago, there was a siege laid against the Undead keep, led by Guildmaster Cataris. As we wrote in our Special Isse #1, he led the attack succesfully. \nNow, Cataris is being trialed by the Mages Guild for leading the attack. The law of the Mages Guild is that they are to be defensive, not offensive. On these grounds, he is trialed. \nBut when listening on whispers amongst the citizens, most think he is actually following one of the most ancient laws of Magic: Above all, the Mages Guild shall uphold the balance of Aegis. The whispering citizens means that with Cataris attack, he was trying to uphold the balance. \nThe Aegis Times will seek the Mages Guild out, to comment this. \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nEast Oren Co. -Estates- \nDo you want to live in Al'Khazar but can not afford the 10.000 minas cost? Then contact Chase ((chase132)) or Lord_John ((SirPwnzalot700)) for cheap and affordable apartments for the everyday citizen! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n' \n* The Hooded, good or evil? * \nWe have gotten recent reports that group called The Hooded, has been raiding and killing innocent citizens. \nThe Aegis Times have gotten mixed reports and information about this group. Themselves says that they are a subtle part of the Guard of Oren, but with these news we start to wonder who they really are? \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nEast Oren Co. -Estates- \nDo you want to live in Al'Khazar but can not afford the 10.000 minas cost? Then contact Chase ((chase132)) or Lord_John ((SirPwnzalot700)) for cheap and affordable apartments for the everyday citizen! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n \n' \n* The Wandering Wizard or The Wandering Gambler? * \nYesterday, when I was out selling newspapers, someone approached me and claimed that the Wandering Wizard had just lost a bet, with 20.000 minas on the table. I was not able to reach The Wizard for a comment. The opponent was Master Gamler Tyler. Neither could I reach him for a comment. \nI think we all are laughing about this. The Wise One? You really do start to wonder. \n-------------Advertisement------------- \nEast Oren Co. -Estates- \nDo you want to live in Al'Khazar but can not afford the 10.000 minas cost? Then contact Chase ((chase132)) or Lord_John ((SirPwnzalot700)) for cheap and affordable apartments for the everyday citizen! \n-------------Advertisement------------- \n' That concludes todays issue. General news about The Times: We are setting up couriers in Alras, Laurelin and Serpent's Ridge. A new Office may also be found in Serpent's Ridge. We are still looking for a couple of new staff members. Find information about it on the bulletin boards. Also read about how to get a subscription at that same place! \n' \nPublish by: The Aegis Times Newspaper Company \nWritten reported by : Glamdring \n' \nTerms & Conditions \nBy purchasing this newspaper you accept our Terms & Conditions which are freely to read at any property of The Aegis Times Newspaper Company. Also found on the Bulletin Boards.", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Jobs", "InvincibleHawk", "", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Prices", "Possut", "Single Issue - 30 minas \nIssue + Appendix - 50 minas \nIssue + 2 appendix - 65 minas \nIssue + 3 appendix - 70 minas \nSingle Appendix - 30 minas \nSpecial editions - 40 minas \n*** \n*** \n--Subscriptions-- \nWeekly subscription - 350 minas \nMonthly Subscription - 1000 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # Special issue #1", "Possut", "The Aegis Time have been in contact with the Archmage Cataris, who had some excellent news to tell us. Here is the latest news about the War against the Undead! \nIn a discussion with Freya and Eze'kiel Tarus,Guildmaster Cataris was talking about the war against the Undead. The future of Aegis has been in danger many times, but according to Cataris this threat is to take very serious. In this discussion, Cataris suddenly remembered that he had found an ancient and secret passageway, leading to the Undead Keep. \nUpon arriving to the agreed meeting point in Alstion, Cataris is met by the overwhelmed army of Aegian citizens and soldiers, armed for battle. Together they snuck under the keep, through the tunnels and came screaming from the inside of the keep, charging the Undead! \nAll of a sudden, the Ascended jons the fight, battling alongside The Wandering Wizard! It was a great battle, and the Undead sure did pay for what they did to Snowy Fields. \nMyself though, was cut down in the battle. My friend saw everything that happened to me. I was running around inside their walls, when an army of Pigmen chased me.   I turned around and saw how a ring of fire had appeard around me. I ran through it  , ignoring the pain, which seemed to be endless. On the other side I met zombies and skeletons. I decided to cut them down, and I died in the process. \nI, Guildmaster Cataris, am proud to be the First ever person, to lead a succesful siege against the Undead Keep! \nThere people, is the first hand story. Excuse any faulty grammar or spellings, but this is a hasted issue, brought to you to get the Latest News, for the citizens of Aegis! \n**Written by: Glamdring \n**Published by: # THE AEGIS TIMES # \n**Source from: Guildmaster Cataris", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # The Economy", "InvincibleHawk", "", ""),
        StaticBook("# THE AEGIS TIMES # The State of the War", "InvincibleHawk", "", ""),
        StaticBook("#The Aegis Times#", "charliescott123", "Welcome to The Aegis Times feel free to explore these pages of all genres. The town of Kramoroe is coming back to life!!\n after a brakedown this town has managed to start istself back up again. The town has been repainted and is on itsway to completion. A new barracks!! new houses!!! new structures!!! Find all this in Kramoroe!!! but two single men have stood out during Kramoroe's time of need... ... Raffus and Gabriel!!! Congratulation's on your great success and also goodluck!", ""),
        StaticBook("#THE AEGIS TIMES# A guide to reading", "Possut", "This may be your first time reading a book or a newspaper. You may not be fully aware on how to read, but this guide will help you. \nFirst open the book ((Right click with a copy in hand)) . To switch pages ((/write -read #   - # being page number)) \nLastly, to copy a book, select an empty book and look through a bookshelf. I will not tolerate abuse of this, when it comes to recent editions of the Newspaper. Do NOT copy the latest editons of the Newspaper!", ""),
        StaticBook("#THE AEGIS TIMES# Edition nr.1", "Possut", "In this first edition of The Aegis Times, we give you first hand interviews from victims and travelers, talking about the lost Whisper Isles. \nI am walking the road to the town of Kramoroe. A passing traveler shakes his head and exclaims \"It used to be so beautiful.\" I stop and ask him what he meant. He tells me that there recently was an attack on the nearby \"Whisper Isles\". The traveler keeps going down the road, and I scratch my head. \nI went by the inn \"Ark's End\" and asked around. The current inn keeper and bartender Tra Zier answered my questions . \"Was a thriving town, many homes on the water, farms, rooftops and the likes\", he says. To make it further interesting he also tells me there was an Undead attack recently on the town inn. \nOn the question on who is to blame he says \"I don't know for sure. I took part in the defence of the inn, and those where definetly Undeads. I am sure they is to blame for taking down the Isles as well.\" He shakes his head and says: \"Just to see the whole thing...gone...I used to mine there.\" \nWhen Tra Zier takes me to the place of Whisper Isles, not too far from Ark's End, I see nothing left that would make it a town. No buildings, no people, no nothing. Except for a flagpost which probably used to be the town center. \nAs Tra Zier goes back to tend to the inn, I stop another traveler and asks him what he knew about The Whisper Isles. Vogron is the diplomat of the Ravenhold Guard, and he tells me this: \"I used to own an inn on the Whisper Isles. \"I was even planning on creating an alliance between the Whisper Isles guard and the guards of Ravenhold\", he says, looking down in the ground. \"This was the first town I went to... And now it is gone.\" He tells me the Overlord Tyrion used to love and live in that place. \"But now he is the one that has destroyed it. I used to know him when he was good\", he says with a grim look in his eyes. \n\"My plans now is to move and forget the Whisper Isles... some day. I now live in Ravenhold.\" With a fierce smile on his face, the last thing he tells me is that he hopes to be a diplomat for an Undead Slaying Clan some time. \nI soon meet with Erevan Dawnfire, an elf travelling down the road, just outside the remains of the Isles. I ask him what he knows about it and he scarily shouts: \"Is it gone? Has the Undead struck again?. I visited this place when I was a soul.\" \nNow, some time after the events, we do know it is a tragedy. Lets hope people will recover from those grim events and prosper, as they once did. \n \n \nSo with this I now end the first edition of #AT# and I hope you enjoyed it. Please come by our Headquarters in Kramoroe or contact Glamdring ((Possut)). \n#THE AEGIS TIMES# are hiring! If you are interested in a job in the next big business in Aegis , be sure to contact Glamdring!", ""),
        StaticBook("#THE AEGIS TIMES# General information", "Possut", "The Aegis Times is a nationwide newspaper that brings You the latest news We report everything from the latest Undead attacks to where you can make your best trading profits We also do interviews with all kinds of persons: the seemingly random traveller to high ranked officers and Kings \nOur main base of operations will be held in Kramoroe, right infront of the big fortress Offices will soon enough be held in or close to  most mayor cities You'll also find stations along the more important roads Last but not least travelling messengers will hand out the latest editons directly to you  We will do everything to deliver the latest news of Aegis to YOU!", ""),
        StaticBook("#THE AEGIS TIMES# On subscriptions and advertisement", "Possut", "", ""),
        StaticBook("''|\\/|\\/|\"", "Sode1", "';'';'';\\'\\; ';\\'\\;'|';', ';:\";\"|||/\\ ';';''';'/|'';'; \":\"\"*';'' \":\"\"|:\":\":>~:\"\":\": \"\":\"||\":\":/|\\\"\":\">\":\":\" \":\"\":>,,\"\":\":", ""),
        StaticBook("'A theory about killer pumpkins - A research by O.M. Winfield", "UndeadEd", "On my far away journeys, I encountered many strange species. Magical and some evil. A combination of both evil AND magical could result in the most foul and dark being ever unle ashed. I'm talking ofcourse about the so-called 'Killer pumpkins'. It is so easy. Evil or undead powers can summon evil spirits and house them in the most unexpected objects, like pumpkins. The pumpkin is a quite rare and wanted object, mainly used for decoration. This all makes it a logical trap to set by the Undead. Ofcourse, you don't have to believe me. But when the time comes and the Killer Pumpkins take over, You are warned! I wrote it myself and I've done a lot of research about it!", ""),
        StaticBook("'Before Aegis'", "GoldenGFX", ".. Don't you wonder? Wonder how.. when it happened to each of us? \n We all wake up, in that one spot, in that hallway of the temple? How did we get there? I met a man, long ago who knew. He understood. \n He told me his story, from before he was here.. in Aegis... \n Or was he? \n He told me, he was born to a couple, out in the woods. Their house, in the woods, no one around. He grew up, learning how to work from his father, and learning to speak and write from his mother. He became very skilled with his sword, he was a prodigy. He would slaughter pigs for their meat, and cows for their hides. \n He became a ruthless killer, but he only killed animals, as there was no others humans around. \n One day, he awoke from a long sleep, the sun in his eyes. He got up made breakfast, and began his day as usual. He got dressed, and went out to the barn where he would find his father every morning. \n His father was not to be found. He searched franticly, and eventually gave up. He went back inside his house and sat at his table hands on his face, not knowing what to do. He heard a knock at the door, and through the small window in the door, he saw his father. Answering the door with excitement, he opened, to see his dad's head on a stake. \n Stumbling backwards, falling to the ground, he moved backwards to the wall, looking at his fathers head on the stake. Coming up the walkway, he saw to men, one with a bow, already aimed with a arrow. The other, sword drawn. He began to get up in a hurry, and he saw the men approaching in a sprint, he dived for his sword, when he felt a sharp pain in his back. \n His vision blurred, and suddenly, everything was black. \n Blinking his eyes open he realised he was on a hard standstone floor. He slowly got up, not sure of where he was. He walked foward, into the world, hoping to someday return to his old home.", ""),
        StaticBook("'ow Ja shuld kill sumune", "mingsly", "chapter 1. Killing dem quick \nIf dere is sumune dat annoyed ja (In dis case a 'ummie) and ja sumwhere where killing no liked (like da 'ummie town) den ja must kill da tupid person quick and make sure they no scream . To do dat ja must first tell da piece of skah ta sum wit ja sumwhere quit den when ja dere, ja must pull ja sword out and cut 'is neck without da arse-hole hearing ja. If dis no work and da guards hear ja den ja shud climb ta da 'ighest place dat dere is and de n jump on da tupid guards wit ja sword, klomping dem une by une.  jump on dem wit ja sword until dey on da ground crying. When dis happens dell dem dat dey nee d ta give ja all dere stoff or ja will eat dem. If dis no work den  chop off dere head wit ja sword and wear it like a 'elmet. dis da end of dis chapter on ta chapter 2!  \nChapter 2 when da run. \nJa shud never run and if ja do i will kill ja. But if ja only a weak tupid 'ummie dat only knows ' ow ta 'ave babbys den ja shud run when an orc tells ja ta fight 'im. 'Nd if ja a yummy squel den it not very clever ta stay where ja are if dere an orcsie. Cause dat makes it too easy. Ja shud run quik den shuut da orc wit ja bow ta piss 'im off when he catches up spit on 'im ta make 'im super angry den jump inta a but of 'ot water fur 'im ta c ook ja. Da last ding ja shud know is whut is da best way ta kill twiggys. and dat's whuts in da next chapter so read it ja tupid skah eater! \nChapter 3 Huw ta klomp twiggys. \nFirst if dere's a twiggy ja know like, piss 'im off by burning 'is tree. Den when 'e goes da beardie ta tell on ja say \"It not me it was ja!\" den run away ta stop da tupid beardie getting ja. when ja 'ave run away 'ide outside da burned down tree. When da twiggy cums along eat 'im den piss o n 'is skull", ""),
        StaticBook("'The End'", "Tassyk", "The End is near We must be careful, the orcs have turned on the dwarves and humans be careful", ""),
        StaticBook("(( OOC: OOC book of How to Roleplay ))", "turret001", "(( OOC: Roleplaying )) OOC: Hello dear players of Lord Of The Craft. With this book, you will learn How To Roleplay", ""),
        StaticBook("((ideas for the town charter))", "omar1296", "The arrow whizzed through the air, pinning Ogrhen's cloak to the wall. A creature made of bone crept forward, bow in hand. The creature notched another arrow, aiming for DelGar'ad's forehead. DelGar'ad tugged on his cloak, his cloak tearing to shreds. DelGar'ad clutched the torn parts, not wanting his precious cloak to fall apart . The creature made of bone released the arrow, but DelGar'ad was already racing away. DelGar'ad continously glanced sideways nervously, checking if he was followed. He looked homeless, with his tattered robes, and his few possesions. Stumbling along, he came across a dwarf named Ogrhen. His home was fashionable, and luxurious. DelGar'ad asked for a home, and surprisingly enough, Ogrhen accepted", ""),
        StaticBook("((Ooc_log_for_Elotre))", "Houstonruss", "First steps: jdpower donates to 100\$ rank. Second: jdthen tree farms to make giant tree. Third: he then starts building a wall around the area Fourth: houstonruss enters the picture, helping jd build up the town Fifth: Houston builds first home/ jd uprights a shop. Sixth: A guild thenhelps jd make a ship and walkways around the town. Seventh: Guild members build homes Eight: Nobody around, Houston gets bored and mines like crazy. Ninth: Houston expands town walls for room Tenth: Houston builds palace. ((ooc log part 1))", ""),
        StaticBook("((Regioning my shop))", "racingbrother", "Hail King! I've been having a problem with my shop, It seems I can't break blocks on the bottom floor. I would very much appreciate if you could fix this. But please take your time, for i know you are a very buisy person. My shop is called the Carminian, it is located between the 1st and 2nd market districts \n \n ((MC info; Name, racingbrother (no caps) I will leave the opening to the bottom floor open you can easily recognize the shop because it was at one time a brothel)) \n Thank you King, I very much appreciate you taking time out for me. \n -Giovanni Carminian", ""),
        StaticBook("((SPOATSTUFF))", "professorshields", "I am wting this book because reeding it looks cool Here syblix Take this book Whoops Syblix", ""),
