        StaticBook("()", "Adagea", "", ""),
        StaticBook("(E2) Undead in Al'Khazar?", "xzpepijnzx", "In Al'Khazar, picking up new books, I noticed a figure in bright red robes, a kind associated with the undead plague to the north \n The guards seem hesitant to approach the figure, but many peasants bothered it haphazardly. It confirms my disgust for these commoners. How easy they seem to throw their lives away, their idiocy, their complete lack of... \n Anyway, hiding in a nearby house, I saw how the figure slowly moved into the fountain. He seemed barely present, responding to the peasants in curt and hissing answers, barely aware of their presence. \n It commited to leaving when the guards approached it on account of its robes, and vanished shortly afterwards. \n If it truly was a supporter of the undead liches threatening the north, I do not know. But, imposter or not, I feel like I will soon come across more of its kind.", ""),
        StaticBook("(E3) Search for the druids", "xzpepijnzx", "Recently I've met two particular young men. Brothers, in fact. Unlike many boys of their age, they spend their life in the persuit of knowledge instead of a life of 'quests' (known as bar brawls) and 'damsels' (the local wench) and whatever else those idiot knaves and ruffians come up with. \n I must say I am impressed. They've commited themselves as companions and, as interested as they seem in 'the creation' (which is all but proven to be nothing but a bedtime story) , they agreed to follow me in my interest in the order of druids. \n Who knows, perhaps having some fit men with capable sword-bearing arms can become useful if we run into trouble on the road.", ""),
        StaticBook("(E4) The Undead Menace", "xzpepijnzx", "On the way to Al'Khazar I've come across a foolish dwarf who tried to sell the fungus his grubby hands picked off the infested floors. Turns out, this dwarf was the constructor of a Wizard Tower in Alras, dedicated to a craft he's been studying. \n He invited me and a hot-headed young human to show off his multi-floored creation, where I was exposed to typical dwarf hospitality (retracting the drawbridge, oh how hilarious). \n While the wizard tower, with its empty library, was rather uninteresting, the three of us then went to investigate the site of a very recent undead attack on the Storm's Army Fortress, near Kramoroe. The place was totaled by lighting and crumbling in a malignant blaze. The undead seem capable of bending fire and lightning to their will. \n Of course, of the perpetrator their was no sign, only of the ruin he caused. In itself, the scene was more than fascinating. I am left to wonder what else these undead liches are capable of. \n Tolta, 31st of The Deep Cold, 1322 \n It has been a few days since the brutal Undead attack on Kramoroe. The town is in ruins, sandstone crumbling and stray fires still consuming the once so vibrant structures along the roads. \n From a distance, I always had a undercurrent of respect for the Liches, being a nuisance of nobility and an inspiring instance of power that corrupts. After this raid, though, I realize they are little more than thugs, just thugs slightly larger clubs than the rest of them. \n My home destroyed, I will have to seek shelter somewhere new. Gah, the injustice. The great intellectuals wearing knapsacks as the farmhands sit pretty in their cursed shacks. \n The librarian and good friend Cerlos has offered me a room in his library. It is an attic room, no doubt cold and damp, but it will provide the shelter my home no longer can. I had visited Malco's camp, but this turned out to be for traveling merchants rather than refugees. My calling definitely does not involve pebbling trinkets to commoners along the road.", ""),
        StaticBook("(E5) The move", "xzpepijnzx", "I have just about settled into my new house in Laurelin. It is peaceful here, shrouded by the forest and elven magics. The quiet fits me. I can still here the roaring fires of Kramoroe, my crumbling home and all within it... \n It seems that in its decay, the former town owners have run off with a significant portion of my possessions. How vile, they are, to abuse an attack to fill their pockets like this. It is insolence, and the greatest kind of betrayal. For the sake of all of Aegis, these pests must be wiped off the face of the planet. \n I am not sure what my next move is. But I know it will be bloody.", ""),
        StaticBook("* a small note*", "deanofantastico", "To Lady Luna Wildewyn, \n \n Please accept these roses. \n \n - Robin Drake", ""),
        StaticBook("* A Strange Note *", "iBurn", "We need to talk. Meet me at the Seek In.", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Green Glow Emits*", "Volutional", "You now have control of Aluinn, Golem Of Earth.  ((PM Volutional, OOCly))", ""),
        StaticBook("*a strange not*", "iBurn", "We need to talk. Meet me at the Seek Inn.", ""),
