        StaticBook("---Conell's journal---", "xChocoTacox", "Entry 1: I have decided to keep a journal of what happens, since everyone does. But, in my journal, I don't just tell the story in a couple of lines... This journal describes it from my point of view, and my thoughts on the event. Now on to the story... Date: 7/27/11 Tofay Bawapy and I were working at home, when Tend'el knocked on the door. We talked for awhile wondering where Ademas had gone. Then, I felt somethign no one else did...like...a thunder bolt had just shocked me. I felt as if something wasn't right, so of course...I knew something to Ademas... I felt like he needed me, I didn't know why, I just know he did. So I told Tend'el and Bawapy to follow me to Alk'hazer. Why did I choose there? I can't really explain it. I heard a voice, from..someone.   Halfway there we met up with Bell and a shaman who told us...grave news. She stated that Ademas had died from an unknown cause. This, was hard to hear. I almost ran away crying, but I realized... What would that solve? I cried a few tears and tried to hide it. Meanwhile the others talked and one thing I did hear was that Bell had been slain. But, luckily she had been brought back to life, a spark of hope ingnited within me. I asked about bringing Ademas back to life, she answered saying: its impossible... She said that even she, didn't know how she was resurrected from death. So, Bell went to stay at Tend'els Inn becuase of her injuries from her death. As they talked in front of the inn, Laetri heard talking from the house and came. Tend'el told her the news, and I sneaked into the fores for some time alone. I cried for awhile, then rememberd I had his journal... I started reading from start to finish...and cried the whole way through, I missed him, without him I felt like nothing. Bawapy was there, but he wasn't the same... They must have heard me crying becuase I overheard them talking about me. They asked me if I was ready, I replied yes and we began our journey to Alk'hazer. When we got Tend'el showed us to the temple, which I regret entering. We walked down to the crypt to see Ademas dead, with no eyes. We couldn't find the priest so we took his bofy near the wilds outside of town. At this moment, I just wanted to die with Ademas...My sadness was growing. Looking down at his lifeless bofy brought me to tears instantly. The shaman and Tend'el carried the bofy to the wilds, where we laid him to rest. We all said our own part, then closed the coffin and covered it up. I couldn't believe this, Ademas wasn't a friend to me...he was way more than that. I couldn't lose him, so after we laid him to rest, I prayed, for an entire day. We all stayed at the grave not leaving for a moment. I prayed to...anyone that would bring him back to me, to us. Suddenly I noticed the shaman wink and...what happened next...was a miracle. Ademas rose from his grave, with two normal looking green eyes. Bawapy tackled him instantly hugging him and crying tears of joy. Everyone showed happiness, except me for some reason. I kept quiet. I guess the shaman caleld the spirits to help resurect him... But whatever happened...I am glad. More than glad actually, I can't explain it. I cried so much...We all did. But in the end it was worth it. At this moment I am sitting here, next to where Ademas was laying in his coffin. Still thinking about how and what those words I said meant while I prayed. \"Dofle en raisenye, Ademas.\" Hmm... I have no idea. But, time will tellI suppose. For now its off to bed. Goof night...-next to this lies a drawing of a broken heart-  Entry 2: Date: 7/27/11 Now Tend'el is showing me the new guild hall, the location is hidden. Because of this, I am not going to even write the location in my journal. The guild hall is plain for now, just a meeting table with chairs. Once we find the purpose of our guild, I am sure it will prosper. We are now siting in the first meeting of our guild. At this very moment we are making a name and a purpose. There have been suggestions such as deafeating the Undead, but I say we start anew. Make a guild that no one would think of. Oh, where did Ademas go?! I'll write more later... Bawapy has found Ademas, I am not sure what has happened, But now Bawapy is calling a guild meeting... Bawapy says he saw Ademas's father, which Ademas thinks he didn't have. Apparently, his father was the \"demon\" controlling Ademas! He said that his father got the curse then passed it to Ademas. Then Bawapy said we helped Ademas's father get realeased from the curse... Lastly, Ademas's father jumped off the tower to be free... He gave Bawapy an iron sword and Ademas's journal. Entry 3: Date: 7/28/11 I awoke this morning to a demolished house and the farm was gone... There were no items in our chests, Laetri's entire room was gone also. There was one sign that said this: \"Griefed?\" then what look like a smiling face. I quickly panicked thinking: \"What do I do?!\" Then called for help. Thank Aegis that The_Wandering_wizard heard my cry for help, and came to aid. He used some sort of magic, everythign turned white, then everything was back. I of course thanked the wizard for his time, and he went on his way. Maybe one day I could ask him how to do things like that,,, I have done it! We are 1/3 of the way to protection we need for our home! Later tofay, I helped our neighbor dwarf named aDrago make a farm. Since he isn't an elf, I didn't expect him to be able to make it alone, of course. So, he gathered the supplies while I made the interior and planted. After that I decided to go home and rest for the night. I awoke to see Ademas and Bawapy at the home, where I told them about the 10000 minas. I questioned the wizard about buying protection for our house, also. He came by our house and protected it, for only 10000 minas!!! We thanked him, but to me, he seemed drunk, maybe thats why he sold it for so low... Anyway, I am currently remofeling my room, I shall write when I get more time. We are now sitting at the guild hall discussing the purpose. Again. It is Bawapy, Ademas, Tend'el and I. And now Abdul has joined us! Before we finished the meeting we were interupted by travelers. Tend'el was being harrased by one name ShadowGunx, so we all hid, then... We all jumped out and cornered him, he ran from us until we all found Bell. Bell helped us excort him to Laurelin where he was put into jail. Then something happened to Ademas, I found him in the streets of Laurelin, We took him to a druid's house, and Bell and Bawapy came to join from the jail. Wehn Bawapy got there Ademas awoke and then fell unconsious again. After this, there was a sudden flash of red light and Ademas....turned to dust. Bell and Bawapy freaked out but, I had a plan... I'll write more after the \"ritual\"... Entry 4: Date 7/30/11 Tofay, Whispering Isles was attacked by 8 Hoofed Man. They left a giant tower of lava that still stands in the city at the moment. After we defeated them Ademas, Bawapy and I met up with Bell at the isle. Bell had decided to build a dark elf town near Tend'el's inn in the dark forest. So, Prince Loganos hired Bawapy, Ademas and I for free, to help build the city. Currently I am writing this before I depart to help work on the town. Also, we finished making a fence that surrounds our house and a fountain. One thing that scares me though is that prince, I don't trust him, he isnt... a very kind person, to me it seems like that anyway. Well, hopefully this town will bring more people to my shop! Write more later!  entry 5: Date 7/31/11 Tofay, Ademas decided we would take a journey . He met Bawapy, Bell, Garret, and I and Alk'hazer and then he told us that Then he told us we we going North, so I went home to grab my belongings. I am leaving the house as I write this, write more later! We have arrived in the North and Ademas showed us where he used to live. He said he lived there with his brother Lossar and family. Ademas then showed us to a cave where he said: Leesbi co ark vo Medasa. We took Ademas back to the farm house where he lived as a child. We laid him on the bed and he started saying weird things... The one thing I do remember was that he said our house was burnt, But I didn't believe this...But Bawapy left to check on the house anwyay, Mean while, Bell and I watched over Ademas, but when he awoke.... He was surrounded by darkness, with hands that went for us. Bell took action and managed to defeat the darkness, it seemed... The darkness had recedded toward Ademas, and then he was sucked into a...void. Od course, I thought to myself, this damn curse won't give up... Bawapy came back and we all left for home... Entry 6: Date 8/2/11 Today I awoke to BAwapy and Bell speaking to a hooded figure. I walked into Ademas' room...", ""),
