        StaticBook("-title High Prince", "kittenaid", "", ""),
        StaticBook("-title Hwaldar, Wizard and Fevered Mind", "edronos", "The following scrawl and musings regard the wizard Hwaldar, who, upon his expulsion from the Mage's Guild and subsequent return, has created a great stir within the ranks of magi and Undead alike. Furthermore, these notes reflect on recent events before and up to Ahad, 15th of Suns Smile, 1305, a nd inqure into the actions and mental state of Hwaldar, the fallen Archmage.  \n Hwaldar and Whisperer are two names that cannot be said without the other being brought up , especially in a conversation regarding the Mage's Guild. Both men are responsible for, if not at least held in relation to, the recent strife within and surrounding the council and academy of magi. This first connection, their shared ire for the Guild, is clear, but there are others, and they all build to strange conclusions. Hwaldar once told me that he and Whisperer are close friends and, indeed, that may be true, but I believe there may be other explanations. In short, the two men may be the same, yet splintered mind. \n  Let me begin with some backstory.  I first met Hwaldar outside the iron and diamond portcullis to the Tower in the north. He, of course, was on the other side, telling me only mages were allowed inside. That didn't stop me, but that's an irrelevant matter for another time. Our conversation ended with me adding that one day,  Hwaldar may just welcome me inside, if only for company. Many weeks passed, and though I had achieved welcome into the Tower, it was not by Hwladar. In fact, the man had vanished and was expelled from the Guild. For a while, I thought that would be the last I heard of the Archmage. \n Some time after my first conversation with Hwaldar, I met with one who calls himself \"Whisperer\". He's a strange, albeit interesting character with supposed ties with the Undead, who he has qualms with, along with the mages (See \"On Whisperer and Other Strange Matters\" for more details). Several times while traveling with Whisperer, he remarked on mages, the Undead, and the whole of Aegis. \n Despite his world knowledge, many experiences seemed very much new to him. The concept of names and naming was beyond him, and he frequently used the terms \"disfigured\" or \"disfigurement\" to describe and indicate people or the environment. However, he specifically stopped outside of a Mage's Guildhouse in Laurelin. His hatred toward the mages wasn't some abstract story.  It was specific to the Mage's Guild. Since then, Whisperer tasked me with setting up a meet between he and Bell, a seemingly popular figure in Aegis, to discuess \"the truth\". \n  Not long after Whisperer's unrest, Hwaldar returned to me, with a simlar hatred for the Guild. Interestingly, he admitted that he and Whisperer are close friends, and even went as far to imply that he created Whisperer with his mind, if not several minds. Since then, Hwaldar has been brewing mischeif in attempts to raise himself up or splinter the Guild. Thusly, the connections find themselves. \n Both men have always contacted me seperately, as in there was only one, and never both. However, while the men never share obvious company, they share beliefs, dislikes, and circumstances. For example, both have some arcane and rueful connection to Bell, who gladly reciprocates her frustrations. Whisperer claimed she was a \"sister\", as she was once Ascended.  As far as Hwaldar goes, she has taken up a position as Archmage at the Guild, much to his anger. Both Whisperer and Hwaldar claim to have been tricked and stolen from by the mages. In Whisperer's case, he claims that the mages are responsible for many lost lives and the theft of the Tower after he himself rebuilt it.  As for Hwaldar, he was tricked out of his position as Archmage, again, by the mages. Also, word has slipped that Hwaldar may be a sleeper agent of the Undead,  thus connecting him with the ties Whisperer claimed to have, despite Whisperer having supposedly severing them. In fact, Whisperer may remain allied with the Undead, but that is irrelavent to the subject at hand. \n It is clear that both Whisperer and Hwaldar are tied closely together, but in what manner remains to be seen.  Is Whisperer a dissociative splinter of a once sane mind? Has Hwaldar suffered some personal cataclysm that helped spawn this alter? Maybe Whisperer is a clever ruse meant to serve some mysterious gains.  Maybe they are truly two different entities, despite ever-stacking evidence. If Hwaldar survives cleanly through the spate of wrath he faces from the Mage's Guild, time may just tell. However, if Hwaldar's mind has truly torn, and all irrational behavior can be explained in him, the situation poses one last question: How would the fevered mind of an old mage be dealth with?", ""),
        StaticBook("-title Message From Myst", "Volutional", "This is a message regarding your war you waged. You will lose.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title Notes", "Javelberg", "Claim the throne of oren :After many years of serving the king and being the lord of Whispering Isles The had begun to slowly fall with trust in the king fading Edmund that is So i decided to protest the laws that were in place in oren Regarding the successor the the throne So i took it upon myself to reclaim what was ine I tried to gather support from the orcs whom agreed to meet with me and his council. However the meeting never went ahead Due to the teutonic order assulting the kingdom. i had previously support from the orcs and the destruction of by them had lost a great deal of support for my cause", ""),
        StaticBook("-title notes2", "Javelberg", "the death of his father", ""),
        StaticBook("-title Ranger's Meeting 33rd of Grand Harvest 1324", "Jerry_Man", "Member's Present: \nGideon Marsh (Ctc9592)  \n Cralt Tumingleaf (CONORDUDE8) \n Elindor (Jerry_Man) \nUkar (droolguy) \nSlyph (Striker0079) \nBael (bobgraditelj) \nMember Count: 21 Rangers, 1 Ranger Party Leader, 3 Ranger Chiefs, 1 Ranger Lord \n \n1st Order of Business\nMore bases are required across Aegis. Major constructions are currently on hold ((till 1.9)).\nUkar is working on a 'sanctuary' near Aeriel to act as a fortress in the event of an undead siege. It is producing good returns on crops. Further work is expected. \nSide Note: A supplier of arrows may be required shoult Cralt's shop fail to provide a steady inlet. \n2nd Order of Business \nA siege on Cassandra's Castle will take place within the week ((Oct 8th 12pm EST)) RotF will be leading the flank with Gideon commanding us and the Shadow Rangers. \n \n3rd Order of Business\nInformation regarding patrol routes will be sent by carrier pigeon or raven, depending on region, within the week. Official requests for routes are to be made and first responses will have higher consideration. ((Keep checking the forum page until the webpage is running)) \n Final Note: All rangers must start practicing archery. A review of skills has shown a below expectation standard. This must be improved", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The art of Shamanism", "BKisKk", "I am to write and describe the ways of a shaman thorugh interviewing one. I pray I won't cause much of a ruckus seeing that I am a halfling. This task should be interesting as well and I feel it will be amusing to see the art of a Shaman first hand.  I am to go to Krugmar now I suppose and I hope this goes well... The last time I sought I shaman it ended with me gravely injured by being surrounded by cactus'  I return from Krugmar as of now greatly distressed. I had searched for an orc to guide my way but unfortunately she had a different plan. She had guided me to an orc who promptly grabbed me upon sight and dragged me into a chamber filled with creatures of Iblees. I had fought my way through towards the entrance barely able to escape and ran as fast as I could. The orc followed me and claimed it was merely a \"trial\" and that I should follow him back. Naturally I did not believe this and ignored him as I started towards Laurilen. Now it is merely a question of how I should go about this once more. I have decided not to take this such as this book upon my journey for its information is much too valuable to me and would be very difficult to replace but we shall see.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The END!", "pugsy", "", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The Escape", "D3LLI5", "The sound of trotters driving into the sun hardened earth thunered through the glacial valley. Echoed from mountain to mountain, it was amplified to a deafeneing volume. As his ears popped, and blood ran down the side of his head, the only thought was to escape, dread and regret would have to wait for later. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The Future of Oren: Operation Guardians", "colwin1", "In the best interest of the people, and the protection of Oren from the Undead, the people must take action themselves before it is too late. The guards do not receive payment, and they do not care about the people. They only care about power, and glory. The king is a fool, who cares only about himself, the crown, and his money. He does nothing to protect the people, or fix up the city. He will not even send his own troops to combat the advancing Undead. Also, something tells me that we will never willingly give up his power. So for the future of Oren, we, the people, will take control ourselves. We are the people, and we know what we need. However, the sudden cut off of a rule by a king will be confusing for some. So we should keep a king as a symbol of power. We will also need one to take charge in the most dire of situations. So for teh future of Oren, let our current king fall, and let the people rise! Long live the people, united and free! Long live the people, in peace and security! \nWe need to pay the guards, and get them on our side. They do not earn pay. So money will easily put them on our side. Also, we should gain an audience with the king, with \"news\" about the Undead's advancement. But during the assembly, the guards will cease everyone but the king prisoner. The king we should take ourselves. We will remove his crown, as well as his power. We will wall the bay, and the harbors. We will pay and train the guards. We will recruit more of them, as well, so that the city may be thouroughly watched. We will not keep money to ourselves. We shall not be corrupted by greed. Taxes will be lessened, seeing as our kingdom always has more money than we can use. The annihilation of the Undead will be our top priority next to improving kingdom defences. \nSince us, the Guardians, already have established relations with a few guards, we will not have trouble persuading them to join our cause. With no guards to make sure that the king does not fall hostage, we will take him prisoner. Lock him up, and present him to the public as the fool he is. Huh? We will take him prisoner, as I said, by prompting an audience with the king with intel of Undead army movement. If he does not want to anger the public further, he will accept our request for an audience. The rest of the plan from there, I have already explained. And in fact, everything I just said had already been summarized earlier in this text. \nBy the time this is over, Oren will be a people's government. Working for no one but the people. This may be changed at any time. \nWritten by Ardougnious.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The Guardian's. A Cause to Save Aegis", "colwin1", "Greetings. We are the Guardians, a clan devoted to saving and improving the world of Aegis at all costs. We are devoted to protecting you from the Undead, and sheltering the people from leaders that are less than what the people need. So if you are sick of unfair treatment, and fearing the Undead. Look no further. We are the solution to your problems. \nWe are one of the largest clans in the area, booming in size everyday. With many roles to be fulfilled, we have job oppurtunities for you. We have shelter for everyone. We have protection for everyone. And most of all, we have the finest warriors and workers you'll ever meet in Aegis. So stop wasting your time trying to make a difference, and actually make one now. All you need to do is join us, the Guardians. \nDon't have any armor? That's alright, we have a master blacksmith  on base. Also, our warriors go out to hunt monsters often. This is a great source of armor as well. So if armor is one of your main concerns, do not worry, we have plenty of it. \nIf you are worried about a weapon, those are even easier to obtain than armor. So you should never have to worry about that.  \nIf money is your concern, there are often monsters in designated areas where we can earn  money. If you cannot fight, and need money, we will offer you some regularly. \nSo make a difference and save Aegis, join the Guardians. We fight to protect the people. And we serve to fight the Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The Lost Orc", "Volutional", "Once Upon A Time... In Aegis, A Land Of Strange And Wonderful things.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title The Siege Of Dal Groguan", "D3LLI5", "The arrow whistled by, halved strands of hair difted slowly to the floor, Bob didnt flinch. The pigmen crushed against the walls of Dal Groguan, cracks splintered up the stonework and masonry tumbled to the cobbles below. The civilians screams were a million miles away. Homes burned to the ground in showers of smouldering ash. The blood of countless guards ran in torrents off the ramparts and onto the baying hordes below. Still, Bob remained still, a statue on the majestic defenses.   \n Contrary to his outer appearance, his fear was melting away at his resolve like a rock in lava. Bob knew that he couldnt stay here for any longer. Giving into his fear he vaulted over the ramparts, leaving the doomed castle to its fate and cleared the mob of decaying pigmen. The pigmen snorted as one and turned to the lone archer. \n  He ran for his life. The winds of the the North carried him on his feet as he fled from the accursed place. Images flashed through his mind, pictures of his parents being torn apart by the undead, pictures of his friends dieing before his very eyes at undead arrows.", ""),
        StaticBook("-title This was expected", "edronos", "", ""),
        StaticBook("-title Thordrin Floop's Daily Log", "Floopster", "", ""),
        StaticBook("-Title To the High Prince Native", "Javelberg", "To the High Prince from Scribe Duvain. It has come to my attention that lots of the travelers wanting to begin a life within our great city does not have the knowledge of reading or writing. So as a Scribe i see that it is my top priority to extend the knowledge and educate those in need. So therefore i propose that we build an academy or a school so we can teach wisdom and knowledge to those who does not posses that teaching. Yours truly Scribe Duvain. Blessings of Malin upon you most noble High Prince!", ""),
        StaticBook("-~- The Everlasting -~-", "Xanivic", "\n Silence soon broke into an uproar. The men's chants and shouts sounded throughout the destroyed city of Al'Khazar. The cries of women, the cries of children. The somber clouds casted over the blazing structures that nearly collapsed. Soon, the clouds griefed as their tears showered upon the city, crawling with Orcs. This day was never predicted. No one foresaw such an occurance. It was as if the brute, green-skined monsters of Aegis had never formed an alliance with the Humans.", ""),
        StaticBook(".", "tyler70", "", "")
    )

