        StaticBook("<Fighting an Undead Necromancer>", "tesawa", "If you find yourself up against a member of the undead, the key to victory is to NOT  retreat. The undead are adept at using their magic to keep themselves at a distance , out of range of your strikes. The way to avoid this is to stay mobile, avoid their  attacks, let them run out of mana, then close the distance to finish them off. Remember  men, the way to defeat the undead, is not only through strength of arm, but strength  of mind. Stay safe. -Tesawa", ""),
        StaticBook("<Genesis-Chapter One>", "PurpleDinoPanda", "In the begining God created the heaven and the earth. And the earth was without form, and void: and darkness was upon the face of the deep And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters. And God said, let there be light: and there was light. And God saw the light, that it was good: and God divided the light from the darkness.", ""),
