        StaticBook("<The Journey for Wisdom>", "Tomurohen", "Day 1: The orc are even more bloodthirsty then I though. They mind is more fierce then any other race. Their bond is incredible close and they would die for eachother. Day 2: The humans seem to have a gift for quarreling. Their knowledge about their history is great. They enjoy the fruits of labour and can cook the most delicious meals. Still: getting along is not their priority.", ""),
        StaticBook("<the writings of stia>", "stiason", "It was a norma day in the woods when I awoke. I had again sept under the shade of a tree on the edge of the even capa of    Laurein. the sun was shining through the eaves of the oak and there was a peasant breeze in the air that hummed wh the sound of birds. A was peacefu in the cy of Laurein for the moment.  I knew that I must start my day though I did so ove to ay under this great tree. As I stood up, I fet an urge to vis the druids grove today. I had no cue that  woud forever shape my ife. I traveed to the crossroad and reaized I coudn't remember where the grove was. I ooked for a whie and asked a kind ooking ef if he knew the ocation of the druid grove in which I seemed to be drawn to. this ef ooked at me wh kind eyes and said he woud happiy ead me to the grove. When we had made  to the grove, I had said farwe before asking him his name. I had no idea that this ef woud become a great freind to me. I went to enter the grove, but the gate was down. I headed up onto the wa to get to the main gate as fast as I coud so as not to oose this nice ef but I fe from the wa into the very pace I had just tried to enter. I met a nice druid decidant by the name of Thiste. He showed me the way out after I had gotten hopeessy ost in the druid grove. I had ended up in his quarters before he found me. Before eaving though, I showed him the damaged ceiing and gave him some wood to repair  it. He ed me out and I began to think over a that I had seen in the grove. I wondered around a bit and found mysef back under the tree I had woken next to. I ay down under it agian to think over a I had seen this day when the face of that kind ef pops back into my mind. I was thinking how kind he had been when I fet that urge to visit the grove again and see what kept drawing me to it. I went to the grove and met many other druids and decidants unti I met one named Dusk. I soon found out that she was the Arch Druid of the grove and amost before I knew what I was saying, I asked to take the decidant test. Dusk tod me that I must gather some diamond and then return to her. I was given one week to return with this rare gem and so I set out to find the rarest of things.  As I past through the gates of aurein, I recognized a famiiar face. I saw the very ef that had ed me to the druid grove and been so kind aong the way. \"Hai kind ef\" I said as I aproached. This time I woudn't et his name escape me. \"What might I ask is your name kind one?\" \"Finaire_Afakyn is my name and yours good ef?\" \"My name is Stia and I thank you again for guiding me to the grove,\" I said as I shook his hand. He tod me that he was working to be an author of many great books and even gave me one that he had just finished. As I ooked at the cover I saw \"Poem of the Ages\" written in god etters. As I read this poem, a strange feeing came over me. I fet at peace and a itte sad for what had passed that I never got to see. We parted ways and I went out searching for a pace to get this great gem. I ooked through the forests unti I had become weary and  a pace to bed for the night. I found an abandoned tree caed Dio's tower.  where I found many things of interest. I found a arge underground farm hoding a the wheat and sugar canes one coud ever need a in one pace. I set out in the morn to find again the diamond that was required of me and met agian the ef named Finiare. I had been in contact with a great beauty named Lirinya who gave me the diamond I  needed. he waked up to me as I was in deep conversation with Larinya when he tod me of a freind he was to meet and wondered if I wanted to come aong. We waked around Laurien for a whie as we taked of ove and oss. This is where I admitted a certain affection for the", ""),
        StaticBook("<Ther Rabger's>", "jowa2992", "help", ""),
        StaticBook("<title> Elvian Attack", "AlmostNermal", "<text> The undead came in wustful burst. They attack my family.. Friends anyone dear to me. <text> I shook in fear as they were torn to shreads, they turned to me and swung a thread. <text> They hung it around my small, small neck. Hung me high to make me suffer. <text> Every breath was as painful as the last, gasping for air. It hurt to breath it hurt to see. Then when I thought I was dead, mum spring up high and untangled me.. But at her expence she was killed, she died. They made me watch they made me suffer.  I had to watch each one die.. What's more torturous then death? Being forced to watch everyone else die, that's what. I visit their grave every year. My mums, dads, sisters and friends, all within a seperate private place, seperate from the rest of the clan. There lies, mum, Melanasia, dad, Alanoria, friend, Anna, and sister. It's painful to remeber. That summer festival.. But in my heart they will remain forever... I miss then greatly the clan and all... But I know, they did it for me. They live seperate in a different grave,  close to where I am now . Why couldn't it have been me that died. Why did we have to seperate from the clan? Why?", ""),
        StaticBook("<Undead Fort Location>", "tesawa", "The undead fort has been located, and the coordinates are marked on the map within this book. X: -4131.7 Y:79.4 Z: -3.1 F: 2. Use this information well, brothers.", ""),
        StaticBook("<Wills Operation log>", "coastercam0", "4 more dead. Bandits I think, Lykos doesn't know because they were informants. Don't know if I should tell him what I'm planning or not, I've come too far to mess it up. Sleeper agents, Spies, Politicians. Everythings ready...just need a little more time to set things up...and Lykos' permission of course. \n3 more dead. FEA. \nInforments in the north are telling me that the Undead are planning something big. Not sure what, but it might have to do with Al'Khazar, think I'll keep this to myself. In other news, had the whispering isles agent killed. Suddenly grew morals. Too bad. \n \nWell that went badly. Lykos didn't like what I was planning. I was sure he'd be open to it, especially because of his relations with Oren... I respect him enough that I won't go through with it but still, might be useful to keep the agents. \n Well I was right, Al'Khazar, 4 of us gone. Undead assholes. \nMade a renewed list of my contacts after a long time of no contact, surprisingly most are still onboard. Made a wall with how many in each city. \n2 dead. \n 1 more dead.  \nRecruited over 8 men in the past 4 days.  \nAl'Khazar under attack again. I'm in charge since Lykos is gone. Ordered the men to stand down, but the fools wouldn't listen. Hope that city burns down to the ground, after my men get out of course. All four made it out but I'm begining to question the loyalty of Recruit Niko, May have to have him removed while no ones looking. Can't risk him getting in Lykos' way. \nThe old king has resigned and it's our chance to salvage whats left of our relationship with the Kingdom of Oren, with a new monarch. \nWe've negotiated a memorial for those lost in the battle. But Lykos said it'd be alright if we shared it with the other factions. Not what I wanted at all. It should be dedicated to us Hunters only in my opinon, but I'll stand by him. \nLeaving this wall up when the king is here doesnt seem like the best idea. I'll take it down later I suppose....", ""),
