        StaticBook("A Ayleid Guide Guide To The Wilderness", "Minnan1", "My name is Aedan, The Last Ayleid. I was asked to write this book in order to preserve the knowledge of my race and share it to other people and, altough unlikely, to any other Ayleid left in the world. I shall share with you the knowledge of survival from my people so you may use it for the good of all of us.... \n \nChapter I: What supplies shall I take? \n \n \n The first and most important of all things you can pack is Food. You might run out of food in the middle of nowhere.... What shall you do! you'll starve!.... you'll have to eat creeper meat! \n Well my friend...I'll help you there.... \n \nI always recommend to pack Elven Bread, for it lasts the longer and is delicious. After you run out if it you might want to do the same as I do. I always keep with myself a bunch of seeds and a bucket of water, for you never know when you might need it. The bucket of water will help you for, besides growing your own food, many things. One of the most common problems is burning, you might find yourself burning without somewhere to turn the fire away, well, you shall use the bucket on yourself and survive!. \n \n You might also want to pack a bunch of tools, I recommend a Iron pickaxe, For when it breaks you shall already have enough stone to make another one and so on you'll have an unlimited source of it. You'll also need an Axe, Stone Axe, a Hoe, Iron Hoe, and a sword for survival.... \n \n Never, NEVER use the sword someone gives you, for there is no better sword than the one made by yourself, only you know how to make it perfect. I always make my own Iron swords, for I'm the only one able to use it as I wish. Having your own sword is important for speed and strenght... don't make it too heavy not too weak... \n \n Chapter II: Miscelaneous stuff: You might wan't to add a bunch of torches, coal, Iron, Wheat and paper for you'll always need to", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ayleid Guide To The Wilderness", "Minnan1", "My name is Aedan, I'm The Last Ayleid, and I shall guide you through how I managed to survive in the wilderness many times. \n \n I wish another Ayleid could read this book for I have many to share with them, but it seems I'm alone in this world so I'll focus it to share from my kind to all of you.... \n \n \n Chapter I : Getting over our emotions \n \n \n We Ayleids were the first race to roam this lands, for some reason, we are the longest living of all. While 10 human years equal 1 elven, 10 Elven equal 1 Ayleid and so on. I happen to be the last one, Born in the Ages before Recorded History 2700 years ago. Being the last one, and living longer than others has always been a problem to me, for I cannot have a family withouth living the pain of watching them die one by one. This idea always crosses my mind, although I've met a Wood Elf named Maiavel, a Fine and Interesting elf, I've been able to keep them off for a while. If you sometime feel overwhelmed by this emotions, seek help from a Druid or someone wise and try to find something that generates the opposing emotion to it or them.... \n \n Getting over emotions will be the first step to survive, for we tend to feel lonely after a while. \n \n Chapter II: Getting Supplies, What kind of stuff should I have? \n \n To survive we all know we MUST have food, although after a while this might run out and we will find ourselves in a terrible situation. This is why I recommend having Bread, Elven made if possible, for this fantastic bread will keep you out of starving for a while and you can then manage to find another source. I always keep a bucket of water with me and some seeds to be able to grow them into food. The bucket can also be helpful for when getting on fire by accident (hehehe) or might be used for many other things. \n The next step is getting tools that work, not too heave, not too weak. I recommend having a Iron Sword made my yourself for you will know how to use it and make it exactly for your qualities. Having a pickaxe is always important, try having a Iron one then make Stone pickaxes to keep a constant supply. Make shure to bring an Axe, Stone axe, and a Hoe, Iron hoe. Now we have some tools we can get to the miscelaneous stuff... \n \nBeds!... you can never have too much or none at all! This Supply will save your life in case of emergency, always bring one with you. Bring as much Wood, Stone and Wheat as you can, always pack books and bookshelves... don't forget at least a bunch of Coal, torches, sticks, armor, Chests and a Work Bench. \n \n \n Chapter III : Getting to the Wilderness.... \n \nWe ayleids need of a nice place to stay always. Try to find a forest with a water source near your \"house\" and somewhere to get Minerals from. \n \n In case you find yourself in the middle of the night without anything to make your home... Dig a 3 block deep hole in the ground and seal the surface with dirt so no one gets in. This works to make a quick house or you can later turn it into an underground house. \n \n Chapter IV: Building a House... \n \nWe Ayleids are smart to build complex structures, and feeling comfortable in them no matter how old, small or simple they are... Always have at least 1 Nature friend inside your house (aka a Plant) to keep yourself in home... \n \n DO NOT Make your house near a town or the road, Ransackers and Bandits will always go and steal your stuff... \n \n Make shure to have traps inside and outside your house but dont fall on them ( Believe me) And also have lotsa and lotsa new and interesting architecture options... \n \n Our ancestors, the first Ayleids built amazing structures with Complex tunnel systems in case of emergency and elavorated traps that still kill Ransackers even today in the Ruins.... \n \n Chapter V: Getting Friends and stablishing a town \n \n Always make shure to get friends that live around your House in order to have someone to help you... Always, ALWAYS help them and keep them alive for there is no better thing in this world that your friends.... \n \nIf you plan on building a town... Get as many materials ( I preffer Stone)) To make your Walls around the buildings You can never have too much defenses against the Undead... \n \nTry using Sticky Pistons and Fire arrow cannons to keep enemys away from your walls and your buildings... \n \n Using the Pistons between 2 walls separated by 3 blocks of redstone circuits will work to make a Staircase only controlable by you and so you will have no need of gates . \n \n Make shure to do anything in order to keep yourself and your friends safe.... \n \n \n If there's something we Ayleids are good at... is Building and Surviving.... \n \n I'm the living proof of that.... : \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid.... \n \n For my dear Wood Elf: Maiavel... For I have hope of someday know you more... \n In the midst of attempt to prottect my friends... \n I'm loosing them... pardon me...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Baron's Thoughts", "AceDaCase", "~Chapter One~ Before the core cubject of this book is to be discussed let us briefly talk about the author; so as to gain a better understanding of the concepts held herein. Baron Vanrourke, formerly known as Count VanRourke or Rourke Laedo, came to Alk'hazzar in its early days. He made fast friends and business partners with one Everard Hightower (who the reader may be aware is the currect High Chancellor of Oren.)", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battered Journal", "DefunctDivine", "Day 1 \n Da desert is harsh. Krugmar, harsh. We orcs, we strong, I think I can survive da snow too... It cold, an' orc not used t'cold, but I think if I make shelter, more orcs com t'the area, an' we settle a camp! This good idea. Shaman say krug agrees!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battle At Snowy Feilds", "EricTorchLighter", "The battle at Snowy Feilds in this book IS NOT the first, nor was it the last, Snowy Feilds was taken by undead and the oren guard and other brave warrios knew they needed to take it back. replace warrois warriors undo", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battle At snowy Fields", "EricTorchLighter", "This book is not speaking of the First or last battle at snowy fields. The undead had taken the town of Snowy Fields and the Brave warriors and oren guard knew they needed to take it back, it was one of the few towns left to fend the undead away from the rest of oren . When the warriors arrived the first thing they saw was Death, Houses burning Men running just to be shot in the back by a undead. The Brave men and ladies of oren and many near by lands knew this could be their last battle, yet the still charged forward. There was not necromancers however, any one who was their knows one necromancer can be worth 1000 undead . As some of the men charged others ran into a near by library to set up a medic base, The medic was in a old burning library that the troops used make-shift things from sand to stone to wood to patch the walls and roof. The Men that charged forward were met with many arrows from skeletons and many bites from zombies They were even met by balls of fire and lightning being shot at them by a necromancer as the other called upon more undead. The troops that had rushed forward quickly found out it was a bad idea, lucky for them the ones who set up the medic were coming to help, so as the troops who set up the medic rushed forward to hold off the undead, the others ran back to the medic and most made it, most but not all. The Brave people did what they could it was not enough and they knew it, lucky for them more and more people from the area around had heard of the battle and were coming to help them. Before they knew it they had pushed past the gate and were fighting in the city, the fighting was getting harder and more people were being killed just to be brought back as a undead who attacked the person they were helping defend just a short time before , The brave ones however did not give up,the kept pushing deeper and deeper into the city clearing houses, putting out fires, and some of the archers could even fire at the necromancers so as the troops charged up the towers the necromancers were in, and as the archers opened fire the undead did fall, they had slain many great people, they had burned many homes, but snowy Fields was safe, for the time anyway... much better ((sorry about much better first book and it did that by mistake)) Ah! Hello", ""),
        StaticBook("A Battle for Alkhazar", "HideInTheDark", "I arrived in Alkhazar having heard the news of an Undead attack. However I never expected it on such as scale! As I entered the town through the western farmland I immediately noticed the gargantuan lumbering figures that could only be giants. I had never encounted one before and the sheer scale of the beast sent a shiver down my spine. \n \n I immediately heard the shouts of the citizens as they fought to repel the Undead onslaught. Brandishing my sword overhead I charged into the fray only to hear the squeals of PigZombies as they fell beneath the blade and the bow. \n \n Lightning struck and all around were the shouts of blood-curling war cries and roars of fury from the undead hordes. Then from directly behind me came the unmistakable squeal of a  Ghast ..", ""),
        StaticBook("A Biography about my Life: Zoe Yohom Edition", "friar5", "How to begin... I was living in Sanhar with my father, when the Undead arrived, with their Damned Ghasts One, shooting at a brave knight, missed, and Destroyed our house, seperating me and my father Then, I lived in the Woods of Fair Laurien. Then, I recieved a message from my Father's Eagle, Isruphel. It said \"Zoe, I am horribly ill, and I am in a Inn, called the Dragon Breath Inn. Please come as soon as possible... while you can. If I... pass, your Uncle Mork Will Be there, waiting for you. Please be polite to my friend, Arunis Lezar, Im sure you two Will be great friends! I will see you soon. -Dad. \" It was two days after I got that note that I went to that nice old Inn. When I got there, I asked where he was, and Mork said he was \"Resting\" but the beds were empty. I, Then, looked in the back, and I saw his grave, A horrible sadness took me. Several weeks later, I was Almost back to normal. Then me, and Arunis, grew a liking for eachother. Just when his Inn wa was finished, he killed himself. *The Letters become hard to read, and blotchy from tears I am not going to say how he died, but, he did. End of Subject. That is when, I desided to Follow in my fathers footsteps, and join the White Ravens, to protect Aegis. *the letters become a little easier to read. there, I stayed, and still stay. I made a sub-devision, the Agents. Now, I command many agents, for I earned my rank for my hard work.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Black Tome", "Swgrclan", "*You see many strange drawing of large, ferocious reptiles with wings, and sketchs of a gloomy, dark, area with tall dark figures around it*   * As you turn the page, you see more details on the large, winged reptile. You see an arrow pointing at the reptile and the word \"Drake\".* *You turn the next page to find a more detailed sketch of the gloomy, dark place, with more detailed figures. They closely resemble Endermen in this drawing.* *You turn another page to find the another sketch of the gloomy, dark area, and it is entitled \"The End\".* *You turn another page to find drawings of a sword, made of gold. It has many runes on it, inscribed onto it's blade, and sketches around it make it appear to glow.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Blind Man's Inspirational Sayings", "The_Blind_Seer", "\"Hope\" \n  \"Hope\" is the thing with feathers- \n That perches in the soul- \n And sings the tune without words- \n And never stops-at all-  \n Dont Ever Loose Hope ~The Blind Man", ""),
        StaticBook("A Blind Mans attempt to Love!", "The_Blind_Seer", "Love is not a thing to understand. \n Love is not a thing to feel. \n Love is not a thing to give and recieve. \n Love is a thing only to become, \n And eternally be. \n \n  ~ The Blind Man", ""),
        StaticBook("A Blonde Bitch With A Big Dick", "bullyreece", "I was walking down the street, i saw a blonde big thighs and the perfect boobies... I got a boner as I imagined what her nipples would like, my penis began to let out its liquids... I walked over and said \"Baby, I have a big dick, you got big tits, i wanna fuck em\"... She smiled and took my hand and said \"lets go and fuck till It looks like a trainwreck down there\" \n I Layed her down on my bed and begun stroking her titties...Damn they felt good I Begun to masturbate, and I came all over her tits...They looked just how I imagined... But I thought...Hmm maybe downstairs is nice too so i slowly put my hand down... OH WAIT...! Shes got a dick The end! :)", ""),
