        StaticBook("A Book of Healing Spells Developed by Renzbro", "ComradeRenzbro", "I have developed many spells in form of healing minor to major wounds. It took much research in the ways of mortal healing and magic healing to develop or perhaps rediscover these spells and will increase your magic prowess incredibly. ;; One of the first spells I discovered was a cauterizing spell. This slightly burns the users hands but they will heal up after use. The incantation is \"Pomper napas ersonne\" ((you can just say *mutters incantations with all of these)) ;;The second I found out was a spell to heal most cuts unless they were caused by seriously dark magic. To heal this you say \"Cass non coup\" and your hands will glow a dull purple and place your hands on the cut. It will sterilize as well as seal the cut. To calm nerves one simply says \"Annul nervu\" which causes a swirling gray-blue ball to form which solidifies quickly and is to be swallowed by whoever needs their nerves calmed. Colds are dangerous to everyone and can cause serious effects if not treated. In the cold weather of the Keep it is difficult to heal them by natural means so magic can be very useful here. The incantation is \"Diparrais malad\" and your hands will glow a dull purple and you place your hands on the affected persons neck and then mutter \"Rezent spoir\" and the cold should disappear quickly if not immediately. I will write more books as I discover more healing spells. These will help you very often I hope. Your skills will develop right alongside mine and the spells will keep getting more and more difficult. Hope you can keep up.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book Of Nature Poems by Jonathan", "turbonerd714", "Poem One The Moon: Bright,glowing, Ever shining it won't rot. Like the sun it's always there, Even when you are not. The moon will guide your path, Even tell you north from south. It will tell you east from west, It will help you on a quest Poem Two Gray Wolf: Steel-grey eyes, Focused Grey Wolf hides in the shadows As does his namesake.", ""),
        StaticBook("A book Story Thingymagic", "ChromeWolf", "Once there was a thingymagic.\nO_o \n It was so ugly that everyone died \nThe End \n NOT!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Brief Guide to the Empire", "aheath4", "Laurelin - Capitol of the elves  The wardens protect the city, and act as the nations army", ""),
        StaticBook("A Brief History of the Anglonians", "thebowperson", "Long ago, two strangers met in the wilds. They protected each other's backs and soon became  very good friends. They soon decided to form a group of warriors, whose only goal was to be d efenders of Laurelin and to protect the innocent. These two mens' names were Cripson and   Blackbeard. Thus the Cripsons were formed. \n Everything was going smoothly. They had built a fort, recruited many veteran warriors, but Cripson had a different goal in mind which he did not tell anyone, not even Blackbeard. \nSuddenly one day, Cripson woke everyone up in the fort and declared that from that day  forward, the Cripsons were going to be evil. Though Cripson did not see this, but there was unrest among some of the Cripsons. They did not want to become evil.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Brief History of the Undead", "ComradeRenzbro", "The Undead worship a demon of sorts named Iblees. They tend to sacrifice in the name of this demon and will stop at nothing to please him. They kill for fun and are ruthless but never think that they are stupid. They are nearly as wise and intelligent as the Ascended themselves. Ways to spot the Undead out of the crowd and to help protect from them are as follows. If they are wearing dark or black robes trimmed with purple or red with their hoods up do not, and I repeat do not, trust them. Even if they insist they aren't, it's a risk one would be w ise not to take. Also not all Undead followers are actual Undead and aren't as strong but can be equally as dangerous. Ways to identify these are scarce but if they ever mention Iblees in a glorifying manner it's safe to suspect that they are worshippers and are just as bad as the Undead themselves. Knowledge on the Undead is a key factor in defeating them, the sharp of your wit is as good as the blunt of your axe, remember that.", ""),
        StaticBook("A burnt book", "ShadowoKing", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A cooking book.", "jens6851", "Porkchop. \n \n You have to take a raw peice of pork and put it into the furnace, remember to but some peper on it. \n \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("A COPY OF THE ORIGINAL TEMPLAR BOOK", "drumstick607", "My name is Sourimant Obadiah, I am the leader of an ancient society. The name is the \" Obadiah Clan \" or better known as \" The Templars \". I run this \" society \" with my four brothers, their names are, Cyrimic, Torthum, Aeromant, and Aerogan Obadiah. In this group I am what is called the Master Templar, and they are dubbed Nobles. We lead others in this group dubbed as Captains, Templar, and Rookies. They all follow different paths that the Nobles lead, the captains are the nobles first man. I started this group when Aeriel gave me her gift and blessing. I am writing this book in a time of great dispair and I fear if i do not write we will be los lost. They are nearing our last keep as a write and I have lost most of my gift from weakness in my stature. The undead have struck me well and I am lucky to be writing this day. Hidden within this book are spell only the choosen may read. If this were to fall into the wrong hands they may find a way to use these. If you found this that means you are of my blood, or you are an evil man that i spit on a man that has no pride and honor. As finder of this book you are also the protector, you must reunite my order, and succeed where I did not. They have just entered the gates and where I hide this book is my death room. Do not fail me, for that is my deaths wish, to live throughout you, my descendent, farewell.", ""),
        StaticBook("A dangerous pact", "Pepernoot", "A pact has been made between Ser Gideon and the Teutonic Knights, they plan to overthrow King Enor and destroy the kingdom of Oren, leaving only small lords to govern the scraps of the lands of Oren", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark,Rotten Book", "Hwaldar", "29th Of Amber Cold,1336 \n  \nCounting days before Tur'Gash would return, I had been given a book,by a strange man. It has stated no other, than the awful truth about...Dusk. She will be talked to soon enough. The Lord may find her life...Most interesting.", ""),
        StaticBook("A day As A Orc", "Hunter55444", "There are many things that a orc can do in a day. He can slay the mighty creeper in the dessert, ambush some silly elves in the forest. then when the day get longer he can return to his home in the sand and drink his ale. But there are many tales of orc that have strived to bring there brothers back into the light. To show that they can have a thriving business and interact with the other races. To expand the orc culture. that is the life of a orc the contant balancing act of strength and courage.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Day To Remember.", "Crippledbaboon", "A message boomed across the lands for all to hear..\" The undead are under assault! help all you can! Men mustered their swords and armour and gathered at Al'Khazar courtyard. \" Men! Tonight we fight back the slippery scum of Aegis! We destroy the undead! \"", ""),
        StaticBook("a dead mans tale", "bondb", "If you are reading this im probaly dead or in jail who knows. if i died nobody would care no family or anything nobody cares for me..anymore. I am lost, i could be in heaven or hell or maybe I am lost in a abysus a black hole in space im...divided by 0. A wise man once told me \"if you seek wisdom do not seek at all\" ive learned to take myself out of the equation..to not think about myself but about others. The truth is i miss my father he taught me evrything i know but he is...gone hes is gone to never be seen again just like me. for my name is Erik, a fighter, a lover, a lone wolf, I am the unknown i am Erik.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Deal", "TheImpulseHQ", "The Orc known as Gezmar, can take whatever he likes from the Vault of Sir Robert Banstir, on the gro unds that he pays back, in material or other possesions. Failure to do so, will mean death", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dedicant's Strength", "BlackBryer", "From the sky, \nThe moonlight shines, \nThe twinkle of the stars' \nBring tears to our eyes' \nDarkness' \nBlackness'", ""),
        StaticBook("A Description of Undead Magic", "AlphaCentaurus", "The undead are skillful in the works of summoning  because of being summoned from the dead planes as part of becoming an undead. They can use this magic to summon armies of those beneath them. Creatures once living that serve Iblees (such as a zombie or skeleton), once a citizen of Aegis, become a minion of the undead. The more powerful an undead is, the more minions they can summon. The most powerful can summon entire cities, such as Drauchriem. Also, due to their trips to the Nether, they have learned to better control fire and manipulate heat. This does not mean they're immune, but it does grant them some measure of resistence. Finally, the undead were given by Iblees the ability to corrupt the land around them, spreading lava conjured from the Nether and slowly turning the surrounding land into Netherrack and Soulsand.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Different Book", "AllenTheGreat", "You pick up a different book, but can't read it. You surely have a problem...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dragon's Demise", "Rhisereld", "It slipped and slid and slithered \nHeaving with all its might \nOver sea soaked, sharp edged stone \nSilently seething with spite \nBeneath its rigid iron scales \nThe demand for destruction lay \nFor houses to meet his fiery wrath \nFor blood to stain the day \n \nHunting the lands for his precious goblet \nSeeking day and night \nHe brutally slaughtered many beings \nAnd towns he set alight \nHow dare these two-legs disturb his slumber \nHow dare they raid his hoard \nHow dare they defy his claim for revenge \nHis ferociousness ignored \n \nPoised above the rugged sea cliff \nHe inspected the desolate lands \nNot unlike a bird of prey \nGuards the area it commands \nHis imposing, powerful, fearsome scrutiny \nSpied the men steel-clad \nWhose stone and iron swords were drawn \nCourage in a flimsy facade \nA menacing snap, a lick of flame \nThe group of warriors fled \nOnly three brave men remained \nIn each other's stead \nThe warriors approached in a steady gait \nBut the dragon's judgement was true: \nA possible threat lay only in one \nBut not the other two \n \nHis tail lashed out in a mighty blow \nAnd struck a warrior too brash \nHe turned to scorch a green-skinned orc \nReducing his shield to ash \nAs he released a fiery flare \nThe shieldless warrior drew back \nSheltering behind a remaining human \nWho had the nerve to attack \n \nHe took his chance and seized the man \nBetween his pearly teeth \nHe snapped his jaws and reared up high \nOnly to expose his beneath \nA cleave to belly by the last live orc \nCaused him to writhe in pain \nHe fell to the earth with a muffled thump \nNever to rise again.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dusty Book", "The_Blind_Seer", "*You begin reading something what seems to be an oath, but as you read the book recognizes you and moves letters, changing words to the point that it is unllegible. The only readable words are at the bottom of the page.* \n Battle Mage Diamond \n Battle Mage Golden Apple  \n Battle Mage Redstone \n Battle Mage Thunder \n Battle Mage Slime \n Battle Mage Cake \n Battle Mage Fire", ""),
        StaticBook("A dwarfs fantasy", "langstondog", "The dwarf and lady were all alone. The dwarf said want to see my beefjerky? The woman softly licked his wooden sword. The dwarf groaned. Want to jump on it? He agreed and they mad a huma n dwarf baby", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dwarven Kingdom", "Supertimmy4ever", "The Dwarven kingdome is great but, it can be better ;; first the King, why A king? why not A ministry? the king is a good man but i got problems he is ruling the kingdom on his own. a ministry is better with 4 ministers, like a republic. \n second why just cities not like states our kingdom is devided thats not helpfull. and the cities lie in others teretory that can start a war. but maybe we can start war to make our nation bigger? we got the best millitary. \n Third. i think the other races cant look down on us we got the best system and the largpop delete delete \n sorry, it's got the most largest population and we need to look down on them fourth the Orcs, kill them all i know its radical but they hate us to! the end justifies the means \n thats all thanks for reading, Longbeard Dragonslayer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dwarven Poem", "firespirit44", "I am the bone of my sword \n \n Steel is my body, and fire is my blood \n \n I have created over a thousand blades \n \n Unknown to death \n \n Nor known to life \n \n I have withstood pain to create many weapons \n \n Yet these hands will never hold anything \n \n So as I pray,  \n \n Unlimited Blade Works", ""),
        StaticBook("A Fair Warning", "JTheCreator", "Your time will come soon, King Enor.. Soon enough. We've been killing off your people slowly, one by one. We've relocated. You're coming soon. And we're going to gut you like the pig you are. We will feast. Signed, -Mogroka. *there is a smile printed in blood at the bottom* \n  \n PS: If you're not a guard, report this immediately, get this message to him...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Farmers Tale", "i7ivinedead", "Day 1: Damn crops.... I walk outside this morning and half of the wheat crop was burned to nothin' b ut ash. I swear, this farming gig might pay the rent, but its not worth it.... My wife told me that writing in this 'ere \"diary\" would help dose my anger, well honey, it aint help helpin'. Day 2: Well, I swept up most of the ashes, i hear it makes good fertilizer, we'll see 'bout that. Theres some funny lookin' clouds forming up to the west, im hopin' They'll bring rain. By Aiegis we need it. Me an' my wife woke up in the middle of the night, theres some mighty thunder in the distance, but i t ain't rainin'. Day 3: My lord! theres smoke in the distance, and a dark shadow is inching its way towards our homestead... Theres too many of them! I've baracaded My wife and I in the basement, and im fighting them off with my axe, I barely have time to write.... Day 4: We survived the night, barely. They're still some of them outside, we don' have much rations to last us a few days. The air smells of rotted flesh, and it feels...Evil, like somthing dark is above us. What is that? Oh god! More of them! I told my wife to run as fast as she can, to try to find shelter Im still here at the homestead, i got hit by one of ther' fireballs, and im badly burned. I hear one of them coming down the steps....OH MY GOD, ITS HIM I DI...... (( The story ends ))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Few Plants Of Aegis", "ITheNormalPerson", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A few queshtionsh...", "Ever", "I come ashkin' ya a few queshtions. I figured it be besht to ask ya shince you wear robesh and me mate wore robesh. I think ther may be shum type o' correlatshion 'ere. Firsht I come ashkin' about yer shop. I wush wonderin' if ya'd ever be shellin' ale? I'm a con...conis...consisho...I like ale, ya shee. I'm alwaysh interested in tryin' different alesh around Aegish. 'n Shecond, I wush wonderin' if yew knew me mate? He wore red robiesh, like you wear, but red, like I shaid earlier. Well we were sposhe to get shum ale or shumpfin together, but I haven't shee n him shince he wush at me inn. If ya seen him, tell 'em I shaid hi and wush wunderin' if he wanted to get 'n ale shumtime. On me, of courshe! \\ He wush 'n orc, I thinksh. Mishin' a bit o' his skin, that he wush. But I'm not one to hate on peoplesh looksh! Itsh wush inshide that mattersh, thash whut I always shay . Sho yea, if'n ya shee him, pleashe relay my meshage! 'n Think about the ale!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Fools Love", "deanofantastico", "It seems as though fate has something against me, as though it is playing with me in the palm of it's hand. Each time love sprouts it is killed off by fate, like the winter snowfall depriving a rose from sprouting from any more than a seed. \n When I begin to fall in love it always seems to end before I can tell the person my feelings. When I fell in love with the Princess Aliciana Sheffield I had wanted to tell her my feelings, but she was then murdered, her life ending before it's time had even started to blossom, leaving me in dire emotional turmoil. I had not thought I would love again, but foolishly I did. \n I fell for an elf, despite race and the fact that she would outlive me, I began to fall for her. Unlike Aliciana, this elf has not passed, she is alive and well. But she recently told me that she was proposed to and may be wed to another. I felt my heart grow cold, as though yet again the winter snow had begun to fall anew, snuffing out the warmth of any love and returning it back to mirrior the cold snows of my homeland. \n The elf who I will not name perhaps find comfort reading this that it is I who left the roses by your door. \n I Remember a guard named Janos asked me about love. I also rememebered what I told him, \"Love? Love is sadness. The good, happy times spoilt by the saddness you feel when the love leaves your heart and is replaced with saddness and regret.\" I hope he doesn't experience the same type of painful love as I seem to. \n -Robin Drake", ""),
        StaticBook("A Foreign World", "aaaa1188", "My name is not important, as I do not truthfully know it myself... Like the  other books I have written to store that which I have learned on my journey ,this book will be solely on the realm in which it was composed: Aegis. This book will keep a record of my adventure through this troubled land and keep record of that which may prove intriguing to those who observe it's pages in the future. \n Allow me to begin with what may seem to be purely opinion, due to the fact that, in truth, it is . This world is by far the strangest I have visited to date , mainly due to the fact that it so further evolved than any previous land i have  encountered. The people seem to have a noble, proud air about them that could not be found in Idaia or even in Cuo'Quen. It is amusing that I remember these lands so vividly, and yet cannot remember my true name, funny what a savage beating can do to one's head. But I digress, although this land may be strange, these very oddities play a major part in what makes the land so grand. \n It is at this point in the book I will begin to recount my experiences in this land day by day, experience by experience. \n Pre-Materialization-- After leaving Cuo'Quen behind, I began to drift towards this realm, gradually losing shape and form in the process, I became a spirit, a kind of... wandering soul, so to speak. I do not remember much about this state, as I had not truly formed into my being yet, but what I can recall is nothing more than a flurry of emotion", ""),
        StaticBook("A forgotten diary", "Phenge", "You've found what seems to be the diary of a bandit who worked the road between the Cloud Temple of Aegis and the Whisper Isles. \n Most of the pages appear to have been torn out, or stained beyond comprehension but a page near the end seems to mention a small cache of stolen goods that the bandit buried beneath a birch tree behind Al'Khazar. \n It seems the bandit marked the tree by tying a strip of red cloth high up around the tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Formal Invitation to the Royal Wedding of Alras", "CountJuno88", "By Decree of the Viceroy of Alras and the blessing of Arcadius the Elder, you are cordially invited to the joining of High King Syrio and Preceptor Shoi in the blessed union of matrimony. The wedding will take place in the Cathedral of Alras in the Nobility District in one month's time.  Your presence would be greatly appreciated as we celebrate this happy occasion. ((The Wedding will take place tomorrow, Saturday, 12/3/2011, at 5 pm Central U.S. Time.))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Formal Resignation", "KindaSpacey", "After much thought, I have decided to give up my position in the Diplomatic Corps. I feel that my time spent as a Diplomat has over all made me a better person, and I have absolutely no regrets. Sorry.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Gentleman's Proposals by Baron VanRourke", "AceDaCase", "", ""),
        StaticBook("a grand adventure", "blacksmith6", "help sorry about that this is my very first book. DAY 1 Colin1389 and i set out on a journey to th e north. we have a ton of supplies and we will be ready to kill orcs soon i have no clue what it will be like but i will write soon. DAY 2 we foun lots and lots of wood so we mined most of it. i now have two stacks of refined wood. all we did today was gather. DAY 3 Today we  collected more supplies we still have not lef. we have made a small shelter h DAY FOUR not much happened today except i saw a orc horde and i follwd them. one saw me and c hased me with a diamond sword i am back at the shelter DAY 5 alot of death going on. our jouney was a complete fail we died alot and we are trapped", ""),
        StaticBook("A Grand Journey", "Exaroz", "We set sail from Al'Khazar, we travelled to the south until we found an island. Hempshine's Island. We didn't stay very long and just passed by, as we passed the Glass Dome with the tree in it, we remember. \"This is the way to the Hooded's base!\", upon arrival we discovered that it was a ruin. A broken ruin from a broken people. We investigated it but didn't find much. We found Ratheldros' favorite book \"Memories\" by Sledder. We decided to stay the night in these ruins. It was a old home of hours... It felt... familiar. I stayed guard for the night, so no bandits nor monsters would ambush the boys in their slumber. Getting tired... need to sleep... \nMany hours later i see the sun waking up. It's beautiful. From here it looks like the first sunrise. I should probably wake the boys up. \nWe found a old tower. It was deserted a long long time ago. Night's falling. We'll probably sleep here tonight... \nAs night falls we see a grand city in the mountain. We're not able to go there since some magic forces us back. We sit at the campfire and discuss what it could be. My theory is an old dwarven city, carved out of stone. Perhaps it's the undeads doings, or maybe even the ascended we've heard about? No use thinking over this, we'll probably never know. Better get some sleep before we start moving towards Alstion and the snowy regions surrounding it... \nWolves. We've heard them howl the whole night. I dreamt that I tamed one, using a bone... I wonder... would that work? Maybe I should start hunting skeletons at nights? Night come again. But this time we embrace it and walk in it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Great Day in Krugmar. By: Rannulf", "loopmoploop", "Dis is da story of a great day in da lands of Krugmar. It all started at midday in Sanhar. A aumen named Loth came ta' Sanhar while a bunch a' orcs were dere'. Loth socialized with da orcs fer' a while till' 2 slave trada's came with an elf slave. Loth got very mad and demanded dat da slave be freed. Warlord Mogroka bought da slave and den freed er'. Me forget why. But den da craziest ting appened'. Da undead prophet and one of his minions came ta Sanhar! Afta a talk with dem, Warlord Mogroka killed da prophet with his blade and da otha orcs kille d da minion Afta all dat craziness. Loth left and 2 orcs got into an arguement. So der' was a great touriment in da arena. Mason'Gorkil was da champ at first befer' e' was beaten by an orc whos name i be fergetin'. Den we all went back ta Sanhar and had some ale and got drunk. It was one a da greatest days i've had in Krugmar! Da End!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Groundsmans Life", "lewismanu6", "When I came to Malrug I had a good Greeting I met Bravepaw He showed me around the bigest and most wondaful city i have ever seen I brought my first house after looking at some of the houses up for sale there was one that I liked the most. It was For sale at 7000 Minas I only had 81 minas at the time but he is letting me pay 500 every week .", ""),
        StaticBook("A grove.", "shiftnative", "To the west, a grove you'll see. Just below, perhaps a chest. Whats inside is the quest.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guard's Tale", "mylimo7", "help The \"Guards Tale\" all begins one fatefull night in the drawf kingdom. Future guard of Oren Throdo was only a kid that night, with his family. Then, there a group of horrible bandits, that were Orcs, broke into the home. The mother of Throdo quickly hid him in the house basment, where he hid for about an hour. Throdo then climbed out the basement window and fled into the wilderness. \n Chapter 2 After about 2 or 3 hours hiding behind trees in the wilderness, he comes back to his home. Comign back to his home, he find his brothers and sisters dead. His mom was tooken by the orc s. \n Chapter 3 :  Throdo spent another couple days in that house trying to survive on the last of the food. He then buries his family and leaves the house. never to return again he keeps walking forward. \n \n Chapter 4 : Throdo lives in the wild for almost 2 months before he stumbles upon Whisper ilse. He lives there for about 3 years. Then he travels West to the Dwarf capital.  There he finds a friend and travels with him for the next year. \n \n Chapter 5 : At the Age of 20, he and his friend were traveling to the Fortress of Oren. Then they reached there 1 year later. They went seperate ways and never saw eachother again. At age 21, Throdo had not enough money to buy himself a lot in oren so he did as always, foun d an abandoned house in the wilderness. After makign enough money he bought an apartment. He also became a royal guard of Oren. You knew then that he was never gonna see his mother again. Filled with sadness he countiues his life and guards Oren well. \n \n \n The End", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guard?", "impymut", "I'm looking for a guard. He took me to a place near Wrath's Store, and he ransomed me to a red haired elf for four hundred minas A nice elf though.", ""),
        StaticBook("A GUIDE FOR REDSTONE", "jens6851", "( theres alot of drawings and things about redstone in it ) here i got this book for you i hope you can read it its about that redstone thingy", ""),
        StaticBook("A guide to dragon tongue", "Sode1", "The Dragon born tongue is hard to learn. Often people confuse it with gibberish. this book will show you how to understand the basics of the language see A guide to dragon grammar", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guide To Sorcery", "silco97", "Forward \nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage. \n \n \nChapter 1 \n What is Arcane Magic? \nAll magic uses the smae power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often considered to be a more modern version of magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation. \n \nChapter 2 \nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic \nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect of your spell to be. Some scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done.  Many mages claim that their powers are akin to keys-necessary to unlcok the final effect of a spell-another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting that even the most learned of arcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that no one today questions their utility is anyone's guess. \n \nChapter 3 \nDiffrent Types Of Magic \nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.  Although they can often achieve a number of other magical feats that the other ,agical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then most often than not you will see a mage locking a door with a spell, shooting fire from his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any so any form of \"spiritual\" type attributes about it are gone.  A healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is a form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire or easing pain with a numbing spell.  Whatever the case is arcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Halfling's Guide to Herbology", "AcerBuddy", "To Start off, I'd like to dedicate this book to Faya. One day will I find her Mushrooms:    Mushrooms are a variety of fungus. A plant capable of decomposing trees, and capable of being made into a deliscious stew. Mushrooms have two varieties: Red and Brown. When combined, the mushrooms can assist you six fold Just make sure you have a bowl!  Flowers:    Flowers are the speech of love in Aegis. They come in colors of red and yellow, and when crushed or combined; they can make different colors of dyes! With flowers, bees tend to be attracted inside. Watch out!   Sugar Canes and Reed: These tall, elegant, plants can be used and be refined to make paper, sugar, and books. That also leads to cake and bookshelves! Reeds must be on grass, directly next to a level source of water. \n Weeds and Grass: A nusance of a living plant. You acquire seeds to farm wheat with. \n Saplings: Used to grow trees, when bonemeal is applied it makes for a faster development. Trees recquire space and sun! Imagine how long it took to grow the Druid Tree or any in Malinor! \n For now, that is all. Enjoy your small guide to plants and herbology!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hastily Written Letter", "Rhisereld", "Dear Alethion, \n \nI'm sorry you weren't here to wish me goodbye. You've been away for some months, I couldn't afford to wait. I have to leave, at least for a while . The reasons why may hurt you, or you might understand. Perhaps it's better not to put it in a letter. But I warn you: Natheus has turned bad. Don't approach him, don't speak to him. He will try to kill you. He has attacked me, done terrible things to me. I'm disappearing for a while, and i may be back in some months or more. Please don't follow me. I will be back when I can. \n I love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A heavy tome", "Cowsgomooand", "* This book is filled with indecipherable spidery runes penned in red ink *", ""),
        StaticBook("a hero beyond dreams, capable of the most stunning sword skills", "UndeadEd", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A High Elfs Views", "doctordemento", "There comes a time when all sentient beings are ask to describe themselves. This is one of those times it seems and it is through this book i am doing so . Ill start with describing my general personality. I am a serious person when not amoung those that i consider close to me. untill i know somebody i am very suspicious of them (few to many times ive been betrayed). Once i get to know sombody i am alot warmer torwards them. this is where i can be who i realy am. a fun loving slightly off elf who loves to give people nicknames and speak using odd phrases. Id like to say im driven but that would only be partialy true as i tend to jump from task to task often without finishing the first one. (irl adhd sucks sometimes) WHen it comes to leadership i enjoy myself very much . I love to help beings with my power almost to a fault (i have used many a mina(s) to bribe slave owners to free theyre slaves). I learned long ago that i am much better suited to not being the top leader but actualy the 2nd in command. this basicly meaning that i can lead or do a task very well with a little direction. id like to take a moment to say how i bacame a holmes . around my 361 birthday i was walking around being mischivious with my brother . as we walked towards arks end to drink after a string of pranks and jokes, we overheard voices coming from a cobblestone building next to the road. curious, we walked to the wall the voices came from. there were no windows so i broke a block and peered in. inside i saw two humans being interviewed, although this sight was only brief as my little viewport had been discovered and filled. i was asked if i wish to join and agreed to be interviewed. if i remember correctly one of my weaknesses was orcs. anyway after the interview was finished i was told i was in the holmes. at that single moment i had not the faintest idea how much my life would come to revolve around the holmes, nor how much the members would come to matter to me. today i look back and marvel at how ignorent i was. At that exact moment a new path to my goal of protecting laurelin and my loved ones had opened up even if i was not wise to this new truth. I believe that i can achieve my goal with and only with the help of the holmes as each member has become one of those i must protect. when Miggy(martin) showed me the vault it lifted a huge whieght off my shoulders. i saw in it how i could continue to protect my loved ones even in my death. It brings me the upmost joy to be closer to goal. times like when the vault reaches a new milestone or when i return with information helpful to the cause of good. I write this book to you bastion in hope that it may Allow me to better serve the holmes and the side of good. I feel i can be most effective from a ranking postition. however, i am not the wisest being and am humble enough to realise that if you assign me to a position it is because you believe it is where i can be of the most use no matter what the positon is. \n There it is. My view of myself. my book may be different than others but each being describes themselves differently because no being is the same. these have been my views. most of them anyway. - Midnus Deskota Anarion III, Anarion Family Head.", ""),
        StaticBook("A History of Freedom Ridge", "Estellan", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A History of the Dark Race", "Trevisdabomb", "Written by Malachi Dark Elves make good swordsmen and adventurers, one dark elf said He also said they make good hunters too Another thing he said was that Dark Elves don't make good farmers He said they were good swordsmen because they really don't do much else but training. He also said they are good hunters because they can sneak well and blend into the night with their dark skin. He also said they make good adventurers because of the other  two reasons. The main idea about Dark Elves that is different from normal elves is that they have dark skin. Their dark skin is usually twilight gray or obsidian, though rarely dark blue, with hair ranging from pale blue to black.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hobbits Guide To The Wilderness", "Crippledbaboon", "This guide should allow you to fully understand natures gift towards all living creatures. Before you head out on your crusade into the unknown you must learn a few things if you have not already. Simple tricks,  like how to brew a mushroom stew, or how to fight in different ways. Therefore, i shall name Chapter 1: Basics When provided with the common question  \" What is the best material one can find in Aegis? You must reply \" Wood, brother. For without wood there would be no stick. Without stick there would be no pickaxe, and without a pickaxe, nations would not have been formed. Great castles would not exist! Wood, is the fuel of war, and the fuel of life. You choose how you use it. When night begins falling and you have the common mans problem of having no tools to use, find the nearest tree. Then take 4 wood blocks from the tree. This will be enough for all that is neccessary to survive the night. With this wood you should be able to fashion an Axe. A Shovel and a Pickaxe. Enough to build you a shelter! Chapter 2 : Hold Your Ground! on your pedestal. Or, you can hold your ground! Earn yourself some Minas for whatever intrigues you. Once you have slain all your foes, set out into the world. Continue these steps until you reach your destination and you will be sure to survive!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hope", "AegisFTW", "Coming into the a whole new world, after gathering supplies, mastering swordsmenship in the overall 15 years, it's a bit uneasy for me to going into populated, huge, and marvelous cities that you would dream of, although it's uneast because it reminds me, if those, THOSE who murdered my parents, people, and every, single innocent child, could they be living here too? Not sure, but I have to get minas for a house, some gear, and I'm off.", ""),
        StaticBook("A ivy embroidered note.", "shiftnative", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A journal by Demor Novee", "Bgrape", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A Kings Savour", "bryce141", "Narrator: The Day Opens as young Dane enters Alras for the first time He stares in wonder at the shops of colours ((Does what Narrator says)) \n Narrator: He realizes this will be his new home!! For he loves this new found place! \n Narrator Suddenly, with out warning a great storm came upon The rain poured down as lightning shot out of the sky .  Scared Dane looks around and finds a sword lying on the ground, Quickly he picks it up \n Dane gasps as he looks lighing strike beside a tower \n Minion: heheeh ((while tieing up Syrio)) \n Syrio: HELP HELP He ((BEfore Minion grabs Syrios mouth and starts to hall him off \n Narrator: Dane sees the man struggling and runs for the man \nDane: STOP UNDEAD SCUM!! \nMinion: HAHAHAHAH try and stop me!! I dare ya \nDane runs at minion with sword and fights him with eventually killing him . Dane Picks up armour and gives to the man \nSyrio: Thank ye s.... \nNarrator: Syrio is cut off as lightning strikes the shop and tower \nDane bows: I must go sir ((He grabs ladders and climbs tower to Undead king \"\"Undead King: HAHAHA Mortal you dare come to my eyes? HAHAH \nDane: YOU SHALL DIE!!! \nDane jumps up and both climb down the ladder fighting while Syrio watchs .  Dane knocks the U.K. on to his back \nU.K. HAHAHAAH Nice try ((then dissipears)) \nNarrator: The storm clears and Dane sees the man he saved standing watching: Are yo uok? \nSyrio: Do you know who I am sir? \nDane: No sir? I am sorry.... \nSyrio: you risked your life for me sir..... and I am the KING OF ALRAS ((smiles as it ends)) \n \n \n THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("A l'ssussun d'l'orbb sol", "Nemiisae", "Ph'dos tahta ulu z'hin areion l'cahlindin har'olen?  \n Ph'dos ezsakil nindel l'orbben z'haan tarthe? \n Ph'dos petrified d'tluin belbaunin phor ulu Nemiisae? \n Rei harl pholod dosst la'uren lotha darthirii \n Lu'mir dosst rahi xuil suuril phor quarnus, \n Lu'falduna udossta 'chev orbb. ((the book is done))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Slayer15855", "Goodday Petyr, \n \n I doubt that you remember all that well, however last time we met we had some very nice times! Feasting and drinking! Ahh... So I came here on this rather drizzly day to continue our last adventures! Of feasting! \n \n But you were not home... I was most dissapointed... However (and I sincerly hope you do not mind) I stayed in your lovely burrow whilst the storm raged on outside. I thouroughly enjoyed reading through your impressive library! I love books. \n However I am not a unreasonable person. I left you a few items in a chest in your living room. To cover your unknowning hospitality. \n \n Oh! The weather has passed, I must be on. \n Yours most sincerly, \n Arcane Mage \n \n P.S: I left you one of your favorites!", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Crowley Falos", "XSilverWolfX", "Kai........ it hurts me to say this. The darkness is slowly taking me over. It won't be long til the full effects take place. I can feel it growing stronger while I'm writing you this very letter. The lightness in me will soon die out under pressure of keeping the darkness out. Nitholiak has placed a spell on both me and Lance. Lance turned instantly since he is not as strong as me mentally. I was able to hold it off, but I can feel my mind growing weak. I can't tell you this in person, for it will be too late. I talked with Blood about it. He was able to \"dodge\" Nitholiak's spell so to speak. The only way for the spell to be lifted from me is for Nitholiak to do it himself. Nitholiak was dieing, his ancestor gave him a chance to live. In return he would have to turn undead and let Gesthal Vonschlitin take control of his body whenever he pleases. Cataris is his partner in this, as you know he was turned undead as well. I can't give you all the details, you have to ask Blood. I hope that, the day I'm free of this curse, I can return working with you. Kai, from now on you can't trust me, Lance, Nitholiak, or Cataris. Kai, from now on you can't trust me, Nitholiak, Cataris, or Lance. I don't want to become a spy inside the Oren Military for the Undead once I fully turn to the darkness. I hope you understand. I'm turning in my Ranger Seal until further notice to you. The darkness will want to use it for wrong things. Kai, I hope I can pick up where I left off with the Oren Rangers once I am cleansed. Please, help Blood against Nitholiak and his ancestor Gestahl. I wish I could too, but he's already placed me under his spell. Please, don't tell the others about this. I want to come back to the Rangers without them knowing, you are the one I trust most out of all of them. * You see the last words written in sloppy handwriting and a drop of water near it* Goodbye Kai..........", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Danic Hello, Indelwehn! long time no see, eh? Indeed, I have recently moved tot", "jpiroden", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Dio Astóre", "Relinquo_Angelus", "I have frequented the path by this abode often, and have decided to inform ye that I find it a delightful residence. An apology for helping myself to the farm, although I have made sure to reseed promptly. \n I have refrained from indulging the urge to bake a cake with your exceptionally well hidden supplies. \n Regards, High Elf Dio.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Huwel-Apology", "huwbert98", "Dear Levi. Sorry for what I did. I can't belive I did it myself....and I deeply regret it. What was running through my head when we put you in that cell. I'm shcoked with myself and I feel bad. \n I'll buy you a drink and give you acess to my tent so you can store items in their. I'm sure Hysagi is sorry too. \n \n \n Sorry I ever suspected you it was partly family issues .I'm worried for them. And with this world being thrown into chaos ,I wouldn't be able to live without them \n \n Hope you can forgive me \n \n From Huwel.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Payon to Gefan", "Phenge", "It's a letter from Payon la Trobe to Gefan. \n It simply states that a pair of men from the Followers of Aerial visited the town and wished to meet with the leader. \n It then goes on to describe how he showed the pair the inn, and where your house was. \n Finally it describes the two men: One was a man named Olaf while the other was a halfling man. Payon couldn't remember his name, except that it started with an 'f'. \n\n\n\n  \n  \n \n On the other side of the letter Payon also writes to say that he had been attacked by a madman on the path to Laurelin and had had his face cut up and not to worry as he had been taken care of by monks and that there was no need to be frightened by his appearance as the wounds were still healing. \n \n Clearly he wrote this portion in more of a hurry than the main part. \n The letter is dated: Ahad, the 8th of the First Seed. 1331.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Rhisereld", "Rhisereld", "Raick is dead. I don't know what to think at the moment. Airion used to be my best friend, but now he's murdered my brother. I can't think clearly. I've lost my liveliness. I am exhausted all the time. I can't bring myself to anything more than eating and sleeping. I need to get away for a while, get my life back and return to the way I used to be. I'm sorry Alethion, I'll be back soon. I love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from the Arcane Mage", "Slayer15855", "practice*", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Vindex", "bloodnrose", "dear zebana i have not had a chance to talk to you in private and i need to get you this information. nitholiak has gone over to the undead along with cataris, lance, and crowley. i refused and i am now being hunted. i plan to kill nitholiak. If you can it would be very helpfull if you could help me take out lance and cataris. If you have any questions you know where to find me. \n -the man you once knew as blood", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from Xero.", "Demonxerov2", "Dear Reader, should you be reading this, you are locked in a cell im guessing. However, there are things that you can use to get out. But i guess i should explain who i am first, shouldnt i? My current name is \"Xero\". Not birth given, more of a cover name. I have been around in places where i shouldnt had been. ive also been locked in cells like yours before. Now, encase your wondering why im writing this. if you found this i obviously dont", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter of Recomendation for the Immidiate Promotion of Oren Guard Tamara", "begginfokillz", "This document is written by Guardian Recruit Dimitri Krechenko (Civilian). To the commander of Oren Guard Tamara, ;Guard Tamara had fought valiently and with distinction against the vile Undead in the region of al Kazer'a He came to the defence of the Anti Undead Militant group \"guardian\" in an effort to save the people of oren He helped lead a first strike against undead forces in Al Kahzer'a, and showed us (CLASSIFIED). He and a member of Guardian were on a diplomatic mission to gain support from another clan, known as \"SA\". They both were taken prisoner, and exposed to intense torture. He kept peace and gave hope to his fellow prisoner. The other prisoner escaped, and led a rescue operation to recover Guard Tamara. He was located, and proved vital to our efforts against the undead in al kazer'a He is a natural leader, and this letter expresses the hope that he be promoted with due haste for his aid to the people of oren & the clan \"Guardians\". He is a valuble member of the Oren Guard, and should be rewarded accordingly with a promotion. his actions were witnessed by Guardian Shaman Sertuk, And Guardian Recruit dimitri here", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter To Ashley", "martinvilla822", "When I was a young man, I had liberty, but I did not see it. I had time, but I did not know it. And I had love, but I did not feel it. Many decades would pass before I understood the meaning of all three. And now , in the twilight of my life misunderstanding has past into contentment. Love,liberty, and time: once so disposable, are the fuels the drive me forward. And love most especially, my love. For you, our children, our brothers and sisters. And for the vast and wonderful world that gave us life, and keeps us guessing. Endless affection my Ashley. Forever yours,  - Martin Loyola", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter to dear old villager.", "cometking123", "Haha! Black and Red Or White and Blue. Who will win this flat out fight. Green and Grey is always nigh. Just watch out or it'll be the end of nigh. *laughs quietly as he gives out the letter to the people downstairs, then leaves.", ""),
        StaticBook("a letter to Martin", "indy58", "Free Sugar for ye!", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter to the Followers of Aeriel", "Lagomorphia", "\"There is a book, held by a man called Milamber. It is called the Dragorum Tarasi. It is dangerous. \n The guard, Thaern, witnessed him 'reading' it. The book is not safe in Milamber's hands. \n The book is dangerous.\"\n \n There is no indication of who wrote this. The writing is faint, as if it were written by someone with a very light writing style.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter.", "Willizl33t", "Do you ever get mail?", ""),
        StaticBook("A list of traitors", "Al3xcog", "write   Vulgrax, and pox, have joined the undead ranks.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Man' Memory", "Yusoyung", "Why do people think I am a bandit or a undead I am just a plain man who wants peace. Sometimes I wonder what the world will come to if there were only bad people.", ""),
        StaticBook("A MANUAL OF ARMS AND ARMOURS By Garrick Forgeheart", "SapphireShard", "There are many types of Arms and Armours that have been, or still are used", ""),
        StaticBook("A Matyr", "MeGoRage", "The ones who went unamed, The faces that held no shame. They fought the unspeakable fight, Because they knew it was right. The dreams they had were impossible, the thoughts unthinkable. The strength unbroken, The force unstoppable Dying for what was right, But never getting any recognition. Most names have been lost with time, But still have been threaded with the same  twine. To the warriors of the future, and to all the other names to be lost. Honor, Dignity and Courage, Are your final marks. . Tennyson", ""),
        StaticBook("A Message", "ANPhiK", "I have a plan to attack Oren, specifically the throne room. I would require a few things from you to accomplish this plan. First, the attack would only work with a large enough fighting force to create a distraction secondly, a small contingent would be required to attack from the rear, in secret and enter the throne room. For this information, I require a few things  have your man find me again in Oren with your answer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A message", "Rattalyn", "Dear Torok, My heart aches as I write this message to you, However, this is what I must do. My body, mind, and soul is growing weaker and weaker. My nature requires solitude for revjuvanation. Therefore, I have ventured into the far, unclaimed forests of Malinor. Naught be need for worry, my decision lies of my freest will. My love rests with you, inside your heart always. I love you with all my heart, Torok Whitestorm. My return shall come when it is time. Speak this to only those which are trusted. Tell Voak and Alys I love them dearly, as well, and wish I could be there for the child's birth. Be careful. -Rattalyn", ""),
        StaticBook("A message fer tha' UAC", "skinner452", "30,000 minas will be due on Wednesday. If ye' don't pay, war may occur between us.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Message for Lucius Murmillo", "Cloudheart", "Dear Lucius, \n \nIt has been a long while friend. I know not if you know, but I have only just awoken, this 20th of Malin's Welcome, 1322. My memories of the last two years are gone, Lucius. I awoke in the castle. If you have been caring for me, I thank you kindly, dear friend. I am grateful, in any regard. However, I will not be able to see you before I leave. Your bannerman, Ser Twi Osit, has told me of the Undead's Advance. \n \nI never told this to you, as I intended to never worry you with such knowledge, but... I am cursed, Lucius. My whole family. By my ancestor. I still don't understand it's true nature, or in what exact manner it acts. I do know there will be someone who may break the curse though. Someone in my family, the El lineage. I believe it is myself, not in vanity, but in hopes of ending this for my children. If I ever have any. \n \nFor this reason, I must be off, I will seek the advice of the Druids first, then Slayer the Great Mage. I am soon to ask your bannerman, Ser Twi Osit, if he will accompany me. If not, I intend for him to deliver you this letter. I only ask that you don't forget me friend. I hope to return sooner than later. Keep a seat open for me! \n \nYour friend, \n \nTend'el the Elf", ""),
        StaticBook("A message from the Seer", "The_Blind_Seer", "I came wondering by and I found this home, Searching for where I could cook some pork I found your room. I enjoyed your book, I have also taken a copy of \"The End of Hope\" It was a nice read. Ill be selling it at my book store because it should be shared. All profits will be going to you of course . \n (/tell The_Blind_Seer when ever your on) \n \n Keep writing ~A Blind Man", ""),
        StaticBook("A Message from your Neighbor Hempshine", "Hempshine", "You just successfully read your mail!", ""),
        StaticBook("a message to the people of oren", "sconn", "Fellow citizens. I urge you to leave Oren at once. Oren isnt as it used to be. The number of guards is lowering, while our numbers are growing. I feel depresed when i sacrifice a pure soul. So i beg of you to run. please give this book to other civilians. I do not wish to take another pure soul.", ""),
        StaticBook("a minecraft love story", "Groobs03", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A Moment of Thought", "Baronvo", "As I sit by the riverside,\n Watching proud daffodils sway in the breeze.\n I am hit by a sudden thought,\n Which brings me to my knees.\n \n I gaze up at those longing stars,\n So bright and full of life.\n A reminder of times long past,\n When the world had much less strife.\n \n Past events fly by like soaring eagles,\n A prompt reminder of things done and taught.\n I am amazed at how all this could happen.\n In just a moment of thought.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A mysterious scroll", "leeloongsam", "In neat hand writting, Salvalia answers, and tells the tale of how she came to be.... help off ((how do i edit lines?", ""),
        StaticBook("A new beginning.", "Crippledbaboon", "To whom has recovered my books. This is the first book i create in my installment. i shall be creating a huge variety of topics throughout my books. This, being the Introduction to them all. Some books may contain stories. These stories would appeal most to those who have furnished their homes to the highest degree and have nothing to do but sit and read. Whilst my other books shall be on survival skills in the wild such as \" How to survive your first night! \" etc.", ""),
        StaticBook("A night under the birch tree", "Zapster101", "Under the birch tree i write this to thee, A crow flys by with a little glee The night rides on and the moon shines high, A clear tricle of water drops down in a fly. As i notice the water drop down the tree, I see the tree gleam with leaves. And when the rain is good and done, The a gleam of red shines on the tree, the sun is up and the night is done. -Elias.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "ANPhiK", "leave any messages for me here from you or your leader", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "DrZig", "Dear Archbishop, I am writing this note for later on when you have come out of the drunk state... But I went to the library (Forums) and could not find any book on the TOurnement\" I would like to speak tou you about it later Signed Vossler S.", ""),
        StaticBook("a note", "RHcrow", "Cataris! The Order of which i dreamed of.  An order of magic wielders who side with no kingdom, race, ideology just the good of the people. \n Bloodnrose has already accompanied me on my information gathering ventures. He almost put me to shame with his bluffings skills. haha. \nDoes Freya still follow you?  Or is she swayed by the Guild? A frost mage with a square head on her  shoulders could help us immensely. \n Lance and Blood have been researching ways to unlock undead ruins or access the nether. We may even have a lead on a one time chance to breach it. To finally bring the fight to those fucking bastards in their own home \n All is not lost.  This is only the begining. \n-Nitholiak \n \n ps:  Do you wish for me to make your trees giant?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Timgie", "You are so bueatiful, its true. When you walked into the room, the whole world froze and i knew i was in love with you. You are one of the few blessed with beauty and the whole room stares, they all think the same. You may not be the Queen of Oren anymore but you'll always be the Queen of my Heart. \n \n - Secret Admirer", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "GoldenGFX", "I, Leon, have left on a voyage, seeking out answers. I do not know if I will return. \n For my house in Sanhar, whoever finds this. May have it. Just let the Warlord know you have taken it *takes the book and reads it, with difficulty Oh! Danka!", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "octovian10", "Iblees doesn't forget, Gio. We shall be back.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for dawn", "Botar", "I found these inside alkhzar, in a florist shop near the center of it all. They where fine, untouched by the corruption. They will do well with you... And I hope they make you happy. With love, Botar", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Del", "serenityonyx", "Del, I want to thank you for all the help you've given me. It is very hard for me to allow anyone into my 'circle'... As you know, it's not safe. \n I don't know how to thank you properly... but I have gathered some things, for you. I hope that you use them well. \n Maylaunim \n P.S you aren't as mysterious as you make out. Just thought I should tell you that.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note for May", "KarmaDelta", "If im not hear that means im away getting supplies.  \n  \n I have decided to stay since you may need some help in the future. I will protect and and server you. No matter what you say. I will start a farm and try to find a better base for the future.  \n I will not take no as an answer to this.  \n Your friend Deltaro.  \n P.s Im planting stuff for future use.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for the undead invaders", "Botar", "well brovo if you got this, it means winterfell has fallen into your gruby, rotten hands. However you will find little in terms of items to use and only really find, traps and pain. and vardak if you are reading this... Im dissapointed in you, It seems I thought to highly of you. - a citizen of winterfell P.S you all smell like rotten week old arse", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("A Note from the Golden_Hood", "jeddeliso", "Dear Airion, I see that you have been much, \"harrassing\" people, I suggest you stop this, or you'll see me more often. fromGolden_Hood", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Arya", "Pinsir99", "I write this note to you Arya. During training I lost control and almost killed everyone if not for stia. I want to apologize for my actions. I also want to apologize for makeing ye unconforatablw when I gave you that gift. I hope ye will accept this apology. Thank ye, Athenril of Fire Pinsir", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note To Caden", "Norser", "Caden... You'v become like a son to me... Now that I'v lost you... I can't go on... Not aga--", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Lothiriel", "GoldenGFX", "I am about to go out and find you Lothiriel.. hopefully the best happens when we do meet. If I am to perish, then please. Listen to what I told you. Accept the fact that Bell is your mother. I am giving my life, in hope that you will listen. \n \n Thank you for doing what your mother once did for me. She turned me away.. and you did also. It must be in your bloodline. \n \n There are things, that I have left around this world. Ruins of the sort. They contain my journals, and poems. My treasures, and my apprentice robes. If you are to find the correct ruins, which I left hints of how to get to, I need them to be delivered to a certain person. You will learn who that is when you arrive. Please Lothiriel, search for them, I do not wish for the things there to go to waste.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to my wife", "StrifeOr", "If I die, Tell my wife Ka'el ((Gazelutza)) I love here", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Ogrhen", "omar1296", "I have completed yer first trial, I obtained a Golden Sword from the corpse of a Pigman. The sword is in yer mailbox, and me locked it so no 'un can steal th' sword . Once ye read dis, give me a notice, and I'll unlock th' chest. -DelGar'ad", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note To Self", "Norser", "Go to market, and buy some damned diamonds! I'm tired of stone...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note To Sillion", "Norser", "You're an ass, yes, but you'v taught me much. You'll be a great scholar one day.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note To Will", "Norser", "Will... You have a bright future ahead of you son, keep it up.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Orcs Choice", "roflcats", "i started out in sanhar. one day there was a raid on a rebel camp it was brutal and the camp was destroyed \n one day i found a shaman and with him and some other frends we went and made a guild on ravenhold. we where met by hospitality and kindness. i was supirised we recived a book it was called a orc destiny i talked about being a true orc about killing for land and other stupid things. raiding people and killing other races but if thats what a true orc is id rather be a outcast. i live here now with the elves its amazing i wish i was here from the start it seems as if its the only safe place in these hard times i wish i could talk to the orcs about this but they would just laugh i wish others would know this truth. fin", ""),
        StaticBook("A Picture Of Thomas_Larseand", "Mrmac23", "This is an old piece of paper with an artist's depiction of Thomas_Larseand, Desmond_Bratheal's father. \nHe is depicted as having blue eyes, a goatee and short black hair. He is wearing a brown, formal looking suit. There is someone else, most likely a woman, in the picture, but the paper here is worn to the point that her face has become little more than a blur.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Place We All Love", "NekoDanie", "", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem", "Javelberg", "When the winds blow an the sun shines,you become the beacon of beauty and valor you repell all that is dark and you could light up a whole city. Your smell,your eyes are like the diamonds of the world with neverending beauty. Yours Scribe Duvain", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem About Love", "jens6851", "From off a hill whose concave womb reowrded A plaintful story from a sist'ring vale, my spiri ts t'attend this double voice accorded, And down I laid to list the sad-tuned tale, Ere long espied \n a fickle maid fill pale, Tearing papers, breaking rings atwain, Storming her world with love oh wait... t they must begain again.     (( by shakespeare with extra things ))  thanks for all.. \n from Turin, Huwel and Jena The Aldaelon's,", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem by Sconn", "sconn", "Nature is beauty. Nature is as a guard on duty. Nature is againts aggressivety. But evil hunts it as a bounty. Nature is a deity. Nature has equality. Nature gave us geniality. It's powers are unknown until we know it's identity.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem For Dawn", "HeelioBagoon", "Roses are red\n ;", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem from a bygone era.", "Shuness", "\n I met a traveller from an antique land \n Who said: \"Two vast and trunkless legs of stone \n Stand in the desert. Near them on the sand, \n Half sunk, a shattered visage lies, whose frown \n And wrinkled lip and sneer of cold command \n Tell that its sculptor well those passions read \n Which yet survive, stamped on these lifeless things, \n The hand that mocked them and the heart that fed. \n And on the pedestal, these words appear: \n ' My name is Ozymandias, King of Kings: \n Look on my works, ye mighty, and despair!' \n Nothing beside remains. Round the decay \n of that colossal wreck, boundless and bare, \n The lone and level sands stretch far away.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem of Nature", "KarmaDelta", "Nature is not just green, \n Nature is the soul,  \n Nature is my soul, \n Nature can be protected, \n Nature SHOULD be protected", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem of nature", "sconn", "Nature is a thing to cherrish. I hope it will never perish. For your sunrise is a beautifel sight, and to me a delight. It's the little things that drive me in life. Like the sight of some beautifel wildlife. And the freshness after the rain, that brings me afoot again. Nature will always be here, it cannot be in contain. It will fall on evil like rain. And defeat it's wretched firers. It will chase evil like abandoners. And soothe Aegis and it's people. Nature is ample. Evil is cripple.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Nature", "jens6851", "The Nature is beautiful. The Nature is good. The Nature is something you are addicted too. The name of the nature is Malin. That's true.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Water", "Ruakik", "As I look out, into the bay, the flowing water catches my eye. \n I see the ripples, and the ebbs. \n And the crashing tides against the shore. \n How lucky the fish have it, to swim in that beautiful place. \n The water is truly amazing. \n The flow of the stream, the crash of the ocean. \n Untamed, and wild, the water is still in beauty. \n How amazing is this water? \n You decide. But if I were you... :; \n It would be pretty amazing. Petyr, I wrote a poem. Smells.... gnarled. help (( Ok", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem to Ashley", "martinvilla822", "The stars lean down to kiss you and I lie awake to miss you pour me a heavy dose of atmosphere 'Cause I'll doze off safe and soundly but I'll miss your arms around me I'd send a letter to you dear 'cause I wish you were here. I'll watch the night turn light blue but it's not the same without you because it take two to whisper quietly. The silence isn't so bad till I look at my hands and feel sad 'cause the spaces between my fingers are right where yours fit perfectly . I'll find repose in new ways thought I haven't slept in two days 'cause cold nostalgia chills me to the bone. But drenched in a thinking twilight I'll sit on the front porch all night waist-deep in thought because when I think of you I don't feel so alone. I don't feel so alone as many times as I blink I'll think of you tonight. When violet eyes get brighter and heavy wings grow lighter I'll taste the sky and feel alive again and I'll forget the world that I knew but  I swear I won't forget you. Oh, if my voice could reach back through the past I'd whisper in your ear, oh darling I wish you were here.      From: Martin", ""),
        StaticBook("A Primer on Shamanism", "Saviordude", "Shamans are the spiritwalkers, the seers, the prophets and the Doyen. Standing as the mediators between the living and the dead. Highly respected, they are the orcish equivalent of the human priests and the elven druids, althought there are instances of other races taking up the path of the shaman, such as the dwarf Lex. It requires a lifelong dedication and is not something to take up at a fancy, but it is a rewarding path to the few who follow it through. \n Shamanism at it's most basic level is interacting with spirits. Of those spirits, there are many kinds. The first is the Major spirit, which is also the small class. Being embodiements of virtues and strong feelings, it is recommended that only the most experienced shamans attempt to summon these. An example is Donuur, spirit of valor and vigilance. \n The next class of spirits is the Ancestors. Being the ghost of those who have passed away, they can offer much wisdom and aid to those who summon them. And example of an Ancestor is Thyst, first grand champion and Dominus. \n The last class of spirit is the most numerous, the lesser spirits. Each of these spirits can be tagged with an element, either fire, water, earth, air, or rarely life. Their is a spirit for everything, from tools to house, from trees to organs. These are the spirits that you would be most likely to call upon if you were attempting to help someone. \n Besides spirits, a good shaman also employs the use of many tools, the most important of which is the staff. A powerful artifact, the shamans staff is enchanted with a spirit spirit or ancestor, and is obtained in the first ritual a shaman goes through. The material used in making it varies, wood for lesser spirits, stone for ancestors, and iron or gold for major spirits. Usually, once a shaman obtains a staff of a better material, they shape their old one into a totem. It is important to note that diamond is never used because gems are used to contain souls, not spirits. \n Other tools used by the shaman are Totems, used to contact spirits,  A ritual weapon which is used to perform blood sacrifices and such, and the medicine bag, which holds herbs and stones used in rituals. \n      \n Although almost every shaman can be considered equal, there are some ranks in their order, the the first of which is the Apprentice. This is what every shaman starts as, until they complete a as set of tasks, upon which they become a novice. Upon summoning four different spirits as a novice, they are promoted to Journeymanm then Doyen. The final step is becoming the high shaman. There is always one high shaman, and each doyen can have two students.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Proposal to the King of Alkazar", "grand_kervall", "In the case of the Orcs involvement with the Undead, the Ascended's position on this shall be thus: if the Orcs strike against any party in the war between the Humans and the Orcs, the Ascended will intervene by first warning the Orcs to not attack, and then by fighting against the Orcs if they provoke the Ascended to do so. This order is propagated by Preceptor Shoi and prepared by her student Thaelen Zerant. May Aeriel's Will be Done!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Pure Civilization - The Inquisitry Manual", "UndeadEd", "At the time of writing, magic and magic users run freely through the once clean and pure lands of Aegis. Where magic came from, we still not know for sure,", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ranger Seal", "firespirit44", "*In elegant handwritting, you see a long document stating the vow and goal of the Oren Rangers This seal, this crest, this insignia represents the validity of Ranger Crowley, official Oren Ranger Signed by Field Marshall Jack, leader of the Oren Rangers. There", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ranger Seal", "XSilverWolfX", "*You see the Oakleaf shaped Crest of the Oren Rangers and see the elegant handwriting* This seal proves the validity of Lt. Oren Ranger Crowley Falos and his vow to Oren.  Wrote on Sabet, 14th of the First Seed, 1331.  Signed Field Marshall Hawk Whitestorm of the Oren Rangers.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ranger's Seal", "firespirit44", "With elegant quil writing, this document states the rules, the vows, and the location of the Ranger Base. Our motto is \"We Seek, We hear, We track\" At the end of the document says \"This seal and insignia recognizes the validity of Eze'kiel Tarus as Ranger of Oren\" Signed, Commander Jack, Leader of the Rangers.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Recruit's Diary", "siwasb", "s asdasdasdasd", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request For Audience", "RHcrow", "This message comes from a neutral messenger from a neutral party.   I am Nitholiak VonSchlichten.  A voidwalker by the name of Hwaldar wishes audience with King Edmund Sheffiel OI t", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request for Audience.", "RHcrow", "Hello. This missive comes from a neutral party and a neutral messenger.  The Voidwalker known as Hwaldar requests audience with King Edmund Sheffield.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ripped Paper", "The_Blind_Seer", "Once, at the wave of his wand. \n All the billows of musical sound followed his will. \n As the seas were ruled by Prophet of Old. \n \n Now that his hand is relaxed. \n And his rod has dropped to the ground. \n The glory of music endures in the depth of the human soul. \n The master of music..", ""),
        StaticBook("A Royal Writ to the Owner and Builder of this Community", "RubberStamp", "In the name of High Prince Native I; Sovereign of the Princedom of Malinor; Demesne of the Elves; its various outposts - Ravenhold, Elvindale, Alvadas, Serpent Ridge; and builder of its capital, Laurelin; you are hereby commanded to immediately remove this community in its entirety and restore the landscape to its former undomesticated state. Replant the trees and eliminate all traces of your activity. \n In accordance to the Laws of Aegis, this village has been constructed far too close to the walls of Laurelin. Permission from the Elf Prince Regnant was not sought out to build this within the Realm of Malinor. As such, this place must be expunged. You will remove, without exception, all evidence of this community within a reasonable amount of days or prompt action shall be taken against this village and it shall be done for you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Royal Writ to the Owner and Builder of this Community.", "RubberStamp", "In the name of High Prince Native I; Sovereign of the Princedom of Malinor; Demesne of the Elves; its various outposts - Ravenhold, Elvindale, Alvadas, Serpent Ridge; and builder of its capital Laurelin; you are hereby commanded to immediately remove this community in its entirety and restore the landscape to its former undomesticated state. Replant the trees and eliminate all signs of your activity. \n In accordance to the Laws of Aegis, the village as been constructed far too close to the walls of Laurelin. Permission from the Elf Prince Regnant was not sought to build within the Realm of Malinor. As such, this place must be expunged. You will remove, without exception, all evidence of this community within a reasonable amount of days or prompt action shall be taken against this place and it shall be done for you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Runt's Storwa", "MuckyD121", "Ma Storwa Begins, as a runt lat desires nutin more dan to become higher up in ranks as a warr", ""),
        StaticBook("A Scorched Book", "The_Blind_Seer", "*As you hold the book in your hand it begins to grow as hot as fire, you cant manage to read before you drop the book*", ""),
        StaticBook("A sealed envelope", "RHcrow", "(the author of this letter is never mentioned) \n Hello your highness.  We come from the shadows to bring something into the light. \n Do not trust the band known as the Shadow Rangers.  Their information does not benefit Oren \n We have evidence their information gathering is intent to cause chaos within the kingdom. \n We will need more time before we act against them. \n  Signed - The Order \n \n Use this courrier if you need a reply. alright", ""),
        StaticBook("A Seeress's Sorrow", "JCQuiinn", "Entry 1 \n I have decided to keep a diary of sorts, to help me think. To outline what has recently happened, Verash and Bowman are dead. I have signed up for the FOA, even though my faith cannot particularly be said to be strong. Perhaps I can learn some things here, more likely than not though, it is those damned voices again. This is the nicer of the two, the female one. She's always wispered in my ear and comforted me, unlike the other, who is male, strong, and harsh. Perhaps this is where I should be, that Fate has always been kind. \n There is a man here, Blaedr. He is the commander here, and seems to be one of the Ascended. I worry, that he may see who I really am, a poor, twisted, tainted soul. Perhaps this is where I shall truly repay for the twistedness of my soul. \n Entry 2 I forgot that I had this... It feels like years since I have paged through this. So much has changed. So much pain has been brought upon me. Mor is dead, and I feel my faith grow weak once again. I have sworn my soul, I have fought to the limits of my ability. I have served every way that I could. It has not been enough. I cannot save those that I care about, I am useless. An Undead killed Mor, who had been branded a traitor. His son is still alive, a young, adopted ork. I feel useless, weak. \n The dreams have been returning. Even in broad daylight the memory flashes across my eyes. I am afraid. A naked woman, tied to a tree. Rotting in the rain, her body bloody and bruised. Used in unmentionable ways. Two bloody, jagged holes where her breasts should be. And she has my eyes, my hair. My Death. Why has Aeriel cursed me so?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Shadows Tale", "KingCooper", "This is a tale told to me by my father, as he attempted to sing around a camp fire. Set in a foreign land it contains mythical beasts, strange happenings, and one tiny hero, who started a legend. But most of all it is a tale of courage, the courage of one small town boy who saved a nation. \n A bard I'm not \n My singing's snot \n But a tale I can tell \n A story long \n A shortened song \n The ending turns out well \n A young boy running \n Always coming \n Late behind the bell \n He grew up fast \n That name would last \n 'Though just a boy from Rivers Dell \nWithout a sword\n No golden gourd\n He left upon his way\n Down the road\n With no heavy load\n Just a hard earned days' pay  \nWith no team\n He crossed the stream\n Where great Quinoth lay\n He knelt to bring\n His small offering\n Right at the break of day\n The gardian of ethral gate\n Wakened from his sleeping state\n Passeth down through him\n A knowledge deeply hidden\n \n \n This gift unknown\n His path was shown\n Off to fair Arlon\n The vibrant trade\n Was then a shade\n Of the ages gone  \n Plagued by drought\n They all ran out\n Chased by fierce dragon\n Children slaved\n Would not be saved\n But he could not abandon\n With one last breath\n He faced his Death\n In the cavern of the beast\n Through him Quinoth spoke\n \"You'll leave these folk\n Your reign of terror's ceased\"\n Away it soared\n And from its hoard\n They prepared a mighty feast\n But amidst the joy\n There left a boy\n Their young hero from the east\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A sheet of paper", "Rhisereld", "I knelt before \nSome stranger's face \nI've never had the courage \nOr belief to trust this place \nBut I dropped my head \n'Cos it felt like lead \nAnd I'm sure I felt  \nYour fingers through my hair. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Shining Rock.", "Hothik", "Tis a glorious life to be a shiny rock \n Sitting, while the time goes tick tock. \n Often admired, never disgraced. \n That is, untill a pick meets your face.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Short History Of Oasis Village", "459pm", "Our founder and our leader is Gefan, he used to live outside lauren city and he owned a little shop called \"the golden apple\" you can still see    it outside of lauren today . about 1 year ago, Gefan, his wife Roza, Tolkien, SalmeerII all disided to move and creat a village with the wealth they had acumulated from there store. they found a small island off the coast of lauren's docks and disided to creat \"oasis village\" people moved in and the village prospered, and so lay the foundations of Oasis  i would write more but there is no more history of Oasis, we will continue to prosper here under Gefans leadership.", ""),
        StaticBook("A short letter", "Rhisereld", "Hello Rhisereld, \n \nI guess I am writing this to prepare for the future. I am you. This is a small letter to myselfjust as a precaution. I will be- [this last part is crossed out] You must be very confused at the moment , but you must read this and follow your- [scribble] my instructions carefully. Some things have happened recently that we would rather not remember.  Other things are too precious to forget. I might forget, or rather, you probably forgot. I am going to eat a golden apple to try to erase the last few weeks, but not too many of my memories. You must go to Whispering Isles and speak to the people there. If you don't understand why, that is exactly why you should go. Tell them what you- [scribble] I did, and exactly what you still know about yourself. Hopefully they will help you remember anything I don't want to forget, and have the wisdom to withhold the information I went through all this trouble to erase.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sight of Love", "WildeBoy98", "The first time i set eyes upon her, it was like i was being reborn. She was the most stunning creatur I have ever seen.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Simple Poem", "Jakbenimble", "Kamees, 33rd of Malins Welcome, 1312 Last night I dreamt of the final battle for Aegis. I knew that the scenes I saw could not e described with mere words. But alas! I am a simple man, words are all I have, so here is my attempt to recreate the dream. - Luc \n  \n  The bloody sun shall soon set, \n The smoke fills the evening air, \n After the two sides have met, \n The world shall be beyond repair . \n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  \n  -Verse 2-  \n Scorched craters speckle the field, \n Rivers of blood divide the land, \n To the Dragon, all shall yield, \n Held high is the blade, in his Black Hand. \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n -Final Verse- \n The sad cries for the lost,  \n The living filled with dread, \n The Corpses glazed with frost, \n Final victory for the undead. ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("A slimy tome", "Phenge", "This book has been exposed to the elements for far too long. \n It smells of salt and the pages have congealed into a thick mass of pulp that begins to ooze out from the bottom of the book as you take it out of the shelf. \n \n The faint silhouette of a tree or building can be seen on the front where a few flakes of gold leaf still cling.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Slip of Sheepskin Parchment", "drplat", "Dear Mister Sturdyfoot, \n We have met a few times, but you are a relatively new neighbor to me. Now that I've seen that the Elders chose you as Mayor, I a tad worried. I don't like havin' a leader that I don't know and trust! You must be a fairly good fellow if you were chosen, but I'd still like to chat. Sometime I would like to discuss yer plans for Dunwood's future. Sincerely, Petyr.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Stock of the Ruins of Montego by Zebana of the Oren Guard", "clayman730", "This is an account of my exploration of the Northwestern town of Montego which is now in a ruinous state. ~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("A Stock of the Ruins of Montego by Zebana of the Oren Guards", "clayman730", "This is an account of my exploration of the northwestern town of Montego which now sits in a state of ruin. \n The town itself is a dismal place, most of the buildings have been stripped of all valuable resources, and gaping holes can be found not only in walls, but in the very streets themselves. The remains of a large farm can be found within the walls yet it is long abandoned. The castle is the only thing that was in sound shape up on it's hilltop, yet it was over shadowed by another structure; a fortress being build across an impressive sized bridge. \n Disregarding the half completed fortress I looked down upon the ruin at towards the fountain. It was there I spotted a large hole in it through which water flowed into the earth below. Curious nature tempted me into the frigid waters, and a lack of sense drove me into diving down into the depths. It was there that I discovered Montego's dark secret. \n The town was in no way abandoned; instead it had been taken over by less than savory dwellers. I foraged through chests to try and figure out a clue as to whose mysterious vault I had stumbled into. After significant searching through the twisting maze of corridors I found a chest containing a number of curious texts. A dozen of the books were titled \"Oath of the Black Hand\" and their content had an interesting oath which was made for one to receit and another to answer. Another book was labeled \"The Black Tome\" and that was a prayer book to the dark god Iblees. Both of these books shed some light that whosoever owned the depths of Montego had in someway connections to the nefarious organization. \n Yet the most disturbing of the finds was a book entitled \"King Edmund Sheffield Must Step Down\" which spoke of a coup that needed to happen in Oren. It was disheartening to discover that the propaganda was written by a member of the organization known as \"The Guardians\" who claim to be a peace fighting group much like Holmes and Storm's Army. \n It was not until I poked around more that I stumbled across a nexus room accented with obsidian and plastered in signs stating \"YOU WERE WARNED GET OUT.\" It was then I realized I had stumbled across something much larger than I initially realized. Through one corridor branching off from the nexus, I discovered a small throne room with three thrones, with only the left hand one labled as \"Dead Priest\". From there many corridors branched in useless directions, in some places there were storage rooms, in others mere locked doors. \n In one such corridor I found an obstacle course consisting of jumping challenges and drowning room s . I circumnavigated the training rooms to find it's end where a sign was labled \"A: To Bring Peace to Aegis.\" Through the hallway I found myself in a lecture hall whose purpose I could not find, that could seat eighteen individuals and one speaker. \n From the nexus room I took a ladder down to a lower level and at last figured beyond a shadow of a doubt that this was not one man's labyrinth, but instead the base of The Black Hand, strong supporters of the Undead. The hallway I found myself in contained numerous chambers with the names of their occupants written beside them. Eleven names I counted before I began to copy them dow n. \n They were as such: : : Uug'Olg : Karl : Rasta : Lym : Ramirez : Lolindar : Vladimir : Tom : Luc : Juvens : and Belphagor. \n \n These eleven people could only be considered members, or at least directly associated with the Black Hand. Another assumption to be made is that the Guardians also have some connection to the dark organization and a formal investigation must be made into the Guild. \n \n Afterwards I decided to make a formal list of all that I had discovered within the labyrinth. \n \n Of all I found: \n \n One shop. \n Six Locked Rooms \n Four Supply Rooms \n One Jail Cell \n One Mushroom Cove \n One Tiny poorly cared for farm. \n One Training Room \n One Banishment Room \n One sacrifice room (by way of fire) \n Two Locked torture Chambers \n The Throne room \n The Lecture Hall \n An odd room filled with glass and spider webs \n Atleast Seven bows. \n At least two dozen swords \n And fourteen beds which with the lecture hall that seats eighteen suggests there are more than the eleven named. \n \n My last discovery was of an Unholy Chapel with fire on the left and water on the right. A script on the walls said \"Bathe yourself before Iblees.\" Some primal urge wished for me to comply, to allow the flames to burn me and for the waters to sooth me, and soon the scar on my cheek began to burn like the day I recieved it from the hooded man. A sound from the altar shook me from my trance and I realized that a man in black robes with blue trim was going about his business in the main room. I slipped off without him noticing with a smile knowing I had found the Black Hand's base in Aegis. I slipped from Montego without anyone being any the wiser.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Strange Book", "KarmaDelta", "I have done something that i most regret. I almost drove a species extinct. I say almost as in that there is one left. A female goddess of the species. The last words of the last god said to protect her and to keep her secret from anyone. She is a Dryad. A species of tree spirits that inhabit these forests. I had chopped down these trees to make room for a new city. I had doomed them all. \n But they had said that there can be more. They can be given the blood of the goddess, Rosethia is her name, and be made into a dryad. I do not know the the direct process but I do not worry about that. I kept a promise to the god and I shall keep it. I have hidden this book in a tree on the outskirts of the the forest. Where no one would look. \n I now finish this note and keep it with Rosethia. She can tell them the rest. \n Malin", ""),
        StaticBook("A Strange Ecounter", "SubjectTrek", "The story strts when I ws on my wy to Oren!  I ws pproched by  strnge mn nmed Brum, he ws  begging for food.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Study of Undead & Minions", "joshlmr", "Today I observed the effects of thrown snowballs at several Minions. The effect was underwhelming... The minions became irate and asked what I was doing. After some discussion, and explaining my goal. They politely invited me to stay for a while. Naturally, I did not trust a word they were saying! They likely planned to sacrafice me! I we entered the Undead fortress they promised me riches and food. I found this to be to much and lunged at them with my sword! Caught off guard the minion were briefly confused! I rushed back down the steps. The Monks however, saved my life for which I shall be eternally grateful.", ""),
        StaticBook("a swordman tale", "samler", "he stood in the arena, it was a hole with never ending fire on the sides, on the other side of the arena there stod a big orc, both of them had made the rule, no armor  and only wooden swords, it was raining as the second orc started to count down and as he shouted ''KLOMP!'' they started to fight they both charged into the center of the arena, the swordman landed the first hit and send the big orc backward, but the swordman was not done he rushed to attack the orc while it was stunned from the powerfull blow and the orc was dead. then he shouted ''I AM ATLAS THE BIGGEST SWORDMAN IN THE WORLD!'' he asked for some healing becouse the orc did hit him a singel time, then a new and bigger orc did walk down in the arena and wanted to fight this mighty foe and someone counted down still a orc so you did not understand the numbers that was said but then he shouted ''KOMP!'' and they both know it was time to show who its the best and they charged into the center of the ring the orc missed his attack becouse Atlas did move to the side just before the attack, then Atlas did side step so hes now behind the big orc and start  to slice it from behind the orc yells in furry and swing hes sword against Atlas and hit that make him send him flying just outside of the flames range, the orc was ready to rush into Atlas and send him into the flamesbut in last moment Atlas make a simple side step and the badly wounded orc run into the flames and he started to burn Atlas did make a mid air attack and slice the orc into two half orcs, the fight was over Atlas did win and he walked with hes price , then he walked out of the orc nation to the kings road and saw a highway tobbering, it was 2 humans robbing an elf  women, Atlas charged and attacked the humans before they even see Atlas was one of them send  flying backward while he sliced the other human into pieces the other human started to run  the elf women fainted becouse of the   blood, then Atlas took the elf women and walked all the way to", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tale Of Elves", "Insanist", "Prologue \n \n Life on the road is wonderous. Never settling in one place too long, you get to see more of the world that you live in. Sitting here in Dawn's Bakery in Laurelin I long for for adventure and to get back onto the road. But I have a tale to tell. A tale of mystery and of uncharted lands. A journey to the Northern lands of Aegis. The un-inhabited lands. Lands full of danger . What you are about to read is true. It is the story of my adventures into these lands and the tale of the evil that resides there.", ""),
        StaticBook("A tale of life", "HolyRane", "Newly spawned into the realm of Aegis Rane found a friend named tanath. He and tanath lived in a small, dark wood cabin close to the great city of Oren. They seemed to have set up quite a life by killing the monsters underneath them until one day where Tanath decided to start consorting with the undead, Rane was shocked and covered for his friend for quite some time . One day Tanath and Rane split ways, and Rane led on his own for a short while before he died a sudden, tragic death from the Hidden Dwarf. Then his soul fled to a nearby life source and grew Quanthelas . Quanthelas met some very nice people, Tamriel, drak, Nutakah, and Aero . They decided to open a shop along the main road to Oren. They then talked to the mighty Respiren to find a land agreement.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tale of Sorts. (Autobiography of Lance Ulhric)", "InvincibleHawk", "So where should I start? My life story? I believe I would rather not talk about my past. So I will talk about my recent travels, the past isn't the important part. I awoke in this new land, as I traveled with my companion Bloodnrose, we met a man named Ferin. He led us to a small destroyed city, and asked if we would join the cause to restore it. We did, and now we live and work there, trying to restore it. One night in town, we were threatened by the Undead, and charged in to attack. Thanks to our General, Sir Tim, we experienced no casualties. The group call themselves the Sword of the West, and together we hope to restore the town. A few days later I decided to explore this new world. Soon I came across a small town. I was greeted by a few guards, who warned me about the Undead, and the lightning. Apparently lightning means that the undead are very nearby.. Hearing it is one thing... Seeing the lightning means they are very close and.. you need to run.. While on watch duty, Bloodnrose and myself saw many bolts of lightning strike the ground nearby.. Only later did I learn that the Undead are closing in on the Capitol of Oren.. We should be careful. I decided to visit Oren one day, when I met a man on the road who was experiencing a Bandit attack. His name was Finn_Fennix.. I decided to give him backup to save his small hut from being robbed. We drove the Bandits away, saving the nearby homes from theft, Finn was greatful. Later in town I noticed Finn being questioned by Oren Officials. I decided to find out the reason. It turns out that they were out asking the population for ideas to help the government. I suggested more roads, and hopefully a road to the SotW Town will be built someday. They believed this info had helped them sort out their troubles, and I hope it did. Anything to help the government as I always say! Heh. Joma, 20th of Malins Welcome, 1308: As I have feared.. the Undead want to take the capitol.. During a conversation with a few other people in the town, we have agreed that more roads would allow us to get our troops where they need to be.. Hopefully in time. Of course sir, I will do that with most haste. I told this to a fellow I met in town, his name is Zebana of Holmes. He wanted me to tell Tim who he was, and I will do so for him. It seems that the guard are taking security more seriously, maybe this will keep the undead out. I have learned that the current leader of the Oren Guard is not focusing on his job.. This is not great news.. A few of us decided it would be a good idea to speak in the pub.. Less people to eavesdrop on us. After a long conversation, we bid each other farewell, and were on our seperate ways.. I wonder if I will ever see them again or.. if anything we discussed will even matter. There appears to be a large group gathering to fight off the undead.. This could be a large battle. I will defend this Kingdom with all my might! If I fall.. this book will let the world remember me. Dear man or woman who finds this book.. Let it live on as my legacy! The battle did not go as planned.. we were easily defeated.. Another push was denied by their minions.. We need support! We are now deep in their lines! We can win if we stick together! We have been pushed back yet again! During the battle one of our men fell.. I was able to claim his things.. Thank you kind sir.. You're death will not be in vain! I promise to use your items to the fullest! Today we have fought valiantly to defeat the Undead at the fallen city! I am most relieved to find this book unscathed after the long and painful battle.. I am most certain that, although we suffered many losses, the battle was a success! After the battle, I thanked Botar for saving this lost book, and escorted him home. When we returned I was shocked to learn that he himself, had killed the Undead Archlord. We can home with the news of their defeat, and I believe that I have finally found the place I want to settle down.. Right here.. In the Capitol of Oren. So I guess you are wondering about my past now right? Well.. I guess I can tell you some. I grew up in a simple village, learned how to use an axe, farm, and a variety of things. One day, the place was attacked by Orc Bandits, and I was one of the few survivors... I sword revenge that day.. I lived the next few years in bitter anger towards all Orcs. We tried to rebuild, and we were able too in a few weeks. I decided to protect my town as a guard, and I did fight a few battles.. However, in the end, it was not the life for me. So I traveled to Aegis, and so far, it has been what I want. The people I meet here, how they share my same ideas or fears, motivate me to continue. Even during the battle of Snowey Fields, I am proud to have been there.. for Oren! I will always be there for Oren.. even during something that could be our last battle.. Even if I go down with the ship, I am proud to do it.. for my Kingdom! I will just have to wait and see... just how my future plays out... King.. Peasant.. Guard.. I am glad to have something to live for.. Oren. Haha, and who knows, maybe one day we will defeat the Undead, and I can finally find that peaceful place to settle down... Until then reader, this is the end. This Tale of Sorts has come to a close! \n ~The End.~", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tale of Sorts: The VonSchlichten Inn (By: Lance Ulhric)", "InvincibleHawk", "So how should I begin? This tale is much different than the last. I have finally settled down and live easily in the VonSchlichten Inn.. It is a peaceful place. If I am correct reader, it has been about 6 months since the end of my last tale of sorts. Not much has changed in Oren, it is still a city on the verge of collaspe.. and under threat of the Undead. During my stay at the Inn, I have met many different types of people. Some living, some dead.. but that will be explained later in the story. Anyways, during a pretty busy night, some guards overheard that somebody had broken into the Inn. They offered, \"assistance\", for a price. Weighing in at over 50 Minas a week! They surely wanted to rob Mr. VonSchlichten! When he refused their offer, they began to threathen the safety of his Inn. Bloodnrose jumped up to defend the Inn, and the two left without a word. Later that week, we were greeted by a few.. shushpicioush individualsh.. Ahh.. The effectsh of thish drink.. They do not help.. I will continue later..", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tale of The Bird.", "Hothik", "A bird flies. \n High above the ground . \n Yet lands, to eat, to live. \n When flying, loving the sky. \n And grounded, calm and precise. \n Oh what a wonder, the birds are. \n How I wish I could fly. \n With the soaring birds. \n Majestic rulers of the Sky. \n Knowledge filled. \n Knowing what the ground looks like, in way we do not. \n Oh, I wish I could fly with the birds.", ""),
        StaticBook("A tattered old note...", "Hwaldar", "If one seeks to find... \nA treasure worth his while... \nHe must seek out the Elven Home... \nThe Library hides the start! \n \n OOC NOTE:Do not take books with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A tip...", "CrabGuy", "You might want to check above you more often, as I've been following you for quite some time. If you need information on a certain someone, find me. I am usually found on the road to Oren. \n-Dion", ""),
        StaticBook("A torn up book", "Hwaldar", "...I hid it at AlKhazar's fake Father. \nHis cold hands will keep it safe \nHis cold heart will make us safe...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Transcription of The Ancient History Of Aegis Volume I", "greggbot", "The history in this book was first told by the wandering wizard. \nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the emptiness of the Void. None know why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in fact, herecy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.   \n Truly none can describe the majesty of the creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of the        Seven Skies. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God. \nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theatre for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and good our actions can be. \nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.    \nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and the man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the man a partner, from the exact same clay and exact same breath, she was the first woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying it's pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Treatise on Absolute Monarchies. Part I: Of Man", "Baronvo", "Written by Everard Hightower, Joma, 6th of Malins Welcome, 1304 \n \n \n NATURE (the art whereby God hath made and governs the world) is by the art of man, as in many other things, so in this also imitated, that it can make an artificial animal. For seeing life is but a motion of limbs, the beginning whereof is in some principal part within, why may we not say that all automata (engines that move themselves by springs and wheels as doth a watch) have an artificial life? For what is the heart, but a spring; and the nerves, but so many strings; and the joints, but so many wheels, giving motion to the whole body, such as was intended by the Artificer? Art goes yet further, imitating that rational and most excellent work of Nature, man. For by art is created that great LEVIATHAN called a COMMONWEALTH, or STATE (in Latin, CIVITAS), which is but an artificial man, though of greater stature and strength than the natural, for whose protection and defence it was intended; and in which the sovereignty is an artificial soul, as giving life and motion to the whole body; the magistrates and other officers of judicature and execution, artificial joints; reward and punishment (by which fastened to the seat of the sovereignty, every joint and member is moved to perform his duty) are the nerves, that do the same in the body natural; the wealth and riches of all the particular members are the strength; salus populi (the people's safety) its business; counsellors, by whom all things needful for it to know are suggested unto it, are the memory; equity and laws, an artificial reason and will; concord, health; sedition, sickness; and civil war, death. Lastly, the pacts and covenants, by which the parts of this body politic were at first made, set together, and united, resemble that fiat, or the Let us make man, pronounced by God in the Creation. \n To describe the nature of this artificial man, I will consider: First, the matter thereof, and the artificer; both which is man. Secondly, how, and by what covenants it is made; what are the rights and just power or authority of a sovereign; and what it is that preserveth and dissolveth it. Thirdly, what is a Christian Commonwealth. Lastly, what is the Kingdom of Darkness.", ""),
