        StaticBook("Account: Ellser ((tigergamer)) Balance 3500 [Stone Account] Has paid 200m", "Shadowninji", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aceeri's Biography", "Aceeri", "Age: 21 \n Height: 5 Feet, 9 Inches \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Aceeri's Poems", "Aceeri", "Table of Contents: 1.) Faraway Lands burn", ""),
        StaticBook("Actions of Alethion", "Alectriciti", "With every poor action there is a consequence. Some do it by pure mistake or foolishness. I can blame it on this curse all I want... For it was the curse that sent me into this vexation. But was my foolishness a part of her seduction? Or was it the curse? Just as hard as it was to break free from what I did before, this was worse. It was my own lust built from the curse. It was me who gave in. I was not as strong as I had hoped. With such a poor action, there is a consequence. An end to this marriage is the end of my life. But we made that promise 'til death do we part. Rhisereld, please don't give up on my weak heart. How can I say your mine when I take another? Am I worthy of your majestic love? So it was not the curse that sent me into despair. 'Twas my fault and my fault alone. Rhisereld, I give you all of my apologies. They won't matter... \n\n For I fear there is no Aegisly way you can forgive this. Though you are the strongest I know. You and I have pulled through so much. I cannot see you in such a hurting state. As you and I are one... it hurts me just as much. For what A FOOL I am to have done such a thing ! I don't know how, but I want to fix this. Please help me!", ""),
        StaticBook("Active Initiates", "Ranovak", "Kyle \n Elessar \n Sypher \n Donovan \n Cael-Que Im trying to find out who out of the initiates are still wardens. ((Im gonna do some research to see who's active and who isnt))", ""),
        StaticBook("Adagea's Journal", "Adagea", "It's been quite a few days now since I started in this direction. I'm surprised I've made it this far, actually. It's been raining almost non-stop since I left my home, I can't be sure that isn't a bad omen. I've set up camp on a remote island just off shore, hopefully I can use it as a mid-point as I continue to search for the end of the world. My parents said it's nothing but a fool's errand, but I won't be deterred. I'm going to find the edge of lands. The source has to be there, the source of everything, just like in the old books I read. Power flows through the sea and land into those who have the ability to control such things. Maybe I don't want the power, but I want to witness it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adagea's Journal (2)", "Adagea", "It's taken more than a few days to get back to the outpost... I was badly injured and nearly killed more than once! Fortunately during the worst of a rainstorm I found shelter in a small mansion where I met a man I presume to be... Kispling? Kipsling? I can't remember what the sign said now, but I suppose that doesn't matter too much. He said he plans to come see the outpost, maybe telling him where it was could have been a bad idea. No time to go back on it now though, so I'll just have to keep an eye out. Also, I ventured much farther South the other day, but I didn't find anything of note. I'll have to continue my quest soon, maybe build another outpost there.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adagea's Journal (3)", "Adagea", "This is a test within a book. This is an additional test. It's been a while now, since I made it to the island. It's made a fine outpost thus far, but the wheat is slow to grow and it wasn't easy getting materials to build the furnace. The rain... it's abrupt and always comes and goes in the blink of an eye, like something is messing with my head. Some divine power trying to drive me mad with the pounding lullaby of the storms. I can't make any progress while it's raining... I can't move forward or back. But I'm losing focus now, this is one more stepping stone on the path to the edge of the world, and I can't give up my courage, will, or sanity yet. Still, these outposts will be useful if... in the end I don't find anything more at the edge of the world than the edge of the world. After all, I don't quite intend to jump off of it, if it is like I imagine it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ademas' Journal", "Ep152", "Entry 1: \n \n  I decided to start a journal after I saw Bawapy doing it. I think it will help me kepe my mind off of things. clear", ""),
        StaticBook("Ademas's Birthday!", "xChocoTacox", "Happy Birthday! *<(:)-+=: Hope you have a great  birthday! From: Conell, Tend'el and Bawapy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adian Brod's Journal", "tyking919", "Day 1: I traveled deep in the woods because i hate it", ""),
        StaticBook("adoption", "saromon50", "meh don't know about dis i hearby adopt Gro'tok Hu'shuck Korbec", ""),
        StaticBook("Adoption", "UltimateSpy", "King, i was wondering if you knew of anyone who was adopting, you see when i was 10 my father went to a war, he never cam back, my mother was so heart broken, she starved herself , she died 2 weeks later Our house caughtm on fire (on purpose by the Undead) and i lost everything. all i have left is 3 porchchop(raw), no job, no money, and no home. I have been living like this for 6 years i am 17 now, and for the last year i was living under a tree in the middle of nowhere , So please answer this question. Can you or someone else you know adopt me, i can't live like a rat any longer. Best Regards, Scar_DiamondSword (This is not real last name)", ""),
        StaticBook("Adoption King, I would like to ask you if you know of anyone adopting, you see my father wast", "UltimateSpy", "Darn! it didnt all go through!!!!!! How do you scrap a book, i messed up, how do you start over How do i scrap a book, i messed up i want to start over", ""),
        StaticBook("Adrian Forbrought's Journal", "Arcadious360", "Day 1: Since Al'Kazard's laws are becoming strict, and it's taxes are soaring. So I've had no choice but to move out of my apartment in East Al'Kazard and out onto my own residence. So I've decided to create Fort Everend. A free place to live for weary travellers craving fre e land and property without taxation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Advanced Healer Magic", "SimplePancake", "Being a healer is one of the most satisfying things that a light bringer can do. But ye can not successfully become a healer without knowing the ways to act, and the spells to know. \n One of the most useful things about being a healer, obviously, is being able to heal. First, to become one, ye must have pure blood in you. Being able to heal is a pure thing, so ye must have no living soul in your ancestors that has done  an act of evil. Once ye have become a healer, ye have many powers at your disposal. Ye can heal weak to moderate injures at will, ye can repair broken bones. But, ye must swear never to use your powers for evil, but only for good. If ye wish to become a healer, ye will need to know how to make a variety of potions. \n Elixir of Life (Mushroom Stew, 5 Hearts) \n Gather one of each of the mushrooms, One Red, One Brown, and crush them in equal amounts. Once crushed, put them in a cauldron, and stir until steam comes out. One that has happened, ye may pour it into a bowl, and add a pint of hot water, and it is ready.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventure of Thomas_Bowman and Elrith_Pelreemer", "f6776", "Date Irba, 32nd of The Second Seed, 1337\n we have stumbled upon what appears to be an abandoned town, we are going to start serching it tomorrow morn. \n we are moving on, after finding no valubles or people here. we found an entrance to a dungeon but alas we don't have the sufficiant tools to dig we have encamped in a man made cave create by Elriths mighty strength.. we have begun cooking some food, Elrith named me the cook Just discoverd a new friend by feeding him a bone, i think ill call him Dog we have discoverd a house, and someone is in it, we are being cautious as he might be undead", ""),
        StaticBook("adventures at night", "superdman2011", "During the Night, outside of the villages of Aegis, is a perilous world that has almost no end. The world is filled with Giant Spiders, Zombies and other monsters, that want nothing but to kill you . Also if you are not carful, you willing get attacked by poepl who are  willing kill you for food.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventures from other Worlds", "PilotAce1812", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventures in the Verge", "trotski24", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventures of a Ranger", "DiFrenzo", "I'm not quite sure how to start this, as it is a personal journal and I'm only keeping tabs on stuff that has happened since I left the great city of Oren. I met a man in Oren who directed me West with him, to a small population of humanfolk. He introduced me to them, and I've been traveling with them since. We've been through a few towns, but have settled on our own land, Greenshire. We've began setting up our town and things have been g -oing rather smoothly. Today is Tolta, the tenth of the Deep Cold, 1308. My name is Sparos Gilraen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventures Of Nymolg", "BawbTehOldDude", "Nymolg Barrityl is a Dark Elf fighter, skilled in the ways of the sword Nymolg is also trained in the skill of merchantry. He once sold books to happy customers. \n Nymolg was not known very well in the lands, but was friends with most people he met. Hail Sorry Sorry", ""),
        StaticBook("Advertisement!", "RHcrow", "The VonSchlichten Inn now features music and live entertainment!  Just outside of Alkhazar towar s Kramaroe!  Food and Rooms now with magical protection.", ""),
        StaticBook("Advin's Journal", "kidchaos10", "The world has become quite horrible.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan", "Minnan1", "I can't explain to myself the situation I'm involved on... For here is my predicament I was born Ayleid in the province of Hawkhaven during the Alessian order to exterminate all of my kind", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Field Research Volume I", "Minnan1", "It has been a long time since I came to Aegis, I didn't find anything about my people the first days. When we arrived at Oren I had a small fight with Romanen involving my race, Bircalin calmed the fight and I stayed at the place we were living at to go to the library and see what I could find. What I discovered there was kept as a secret from my brothers for I did not want them to have wrong thoughts of my people nor me. \n \n \n Later on I got sick of a terrible disease of unknown origin that made me suffer a lot. While I was sick I had visions of the Aurorans and the Undead. The Aurorans were the ones who sent the Undead to Aegis and before the First Era had contact with the Ayleids who tried to have them on their side. The Aurorans had been planning on taking over the Mortal World after finishing the deal with the Ayleids. My people discovered this treason and created the Dragon Fires to keep them away from our lands forever. But they did not expect humans to riot against them, for they were their slaves. During the riot, their leader, Alessia Septim found an artifact to keep the dragon fires working and prevent the Aurorans from coming. She stole this artifact believing that Ayleids used the Dragon Fires to bring them to this world. \n \n The Dragon Fires weakened over the years until the point of disappearing and releasing the Aurorans into Aegis and the rest of the world. Aurorans called their armies of Undead to roam over the lands and spread their taint over the Ayleids to turn them into Evil and use their power to destroy what was left from the Dragon Fires: The Varla Stone, and release them from their prison. \n \n The Varla Stone's location is unknown for me or my friends I shall seek for it in order to activate it with the enchantments that I'll learn from an Ayleid coming to Laurelin in 6 days. \n \nUntil then I shall keep this as a secret to protect my friends from the evil to be released over this lands. \n \n The less they know, the safer they will be... \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid.... until now....", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Field Research Volume II", "Minnan1", "I've been feeling lonely lately, I shall keep this books safe in my house in Laurelin. \n \nWe recieved news of the Undead planning an attack near the city of Oren. Bircalin really wants me to go there to help him fight. \n \n The date is close to be and I cannot miss it for this could be my only chance to meet another Ayleid in a long time if not forever. I've got some flowers just in case is a female... One never knows... \n \n The fight was the same day as the date, I couldn't leave my friend to die against the Undead so I had to choose between my friend's life and the Ayleid. For some reason I chose my friend Bircalin over the Ayleid and went to fight with him at Oren. \n \n Short after I arrived to the Battlefield, Lightning began strike the land and kill people. I helped some of them with food and weapons while trying to deffend myself and my friends from the terrible dead. I was struck by lightning after helping the elven prince from dying in a lava pit. I did not die from the Lightning but I did feel how my soul was taken from me and taking my willpower with it. \n \nI returned home as quick as I could and looked for the Ayleid at the meeting spot... It was gone... \n \n I felt a little bit sick each day from then forward, I haven't been able to sleep since I got sick at Oren. I've tried all kind of things to get my strenght back, seems like I won't succeed. \n \n I found myself meeting with Verigan and Romanen the other day at the Museum. They noticed a strange thing in my face, we ran to the nearest pond and tried to wear it off with water from it. It didn't wear off so we decided to look for the Druids at Raven Hold. The Druid didn't help us, we found a guard that took us back here in search of Respiren, but he wasn't here. I began to feel better and went for a drink with Verigan. After that I came to my house and wrote this book. \n \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid once again.... \n \n \n \n *As you turn the page you see a bunch of scrap writing, almost unreadable* \n \n \n I... I don't understand... I felt better after returning here, but the thing in my face is still there and doesnt wear off.... I feel a pain so loud I can barely stand or do anything involved with moving. \n \n I...I need to seek help... I cannot stay like this... my friends... they're in grave danger.... \n \n * You see bloodstains in what remains of the page * \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayl (Bloodstain)  Agaiayae Cei Das Marghathar  ( Bloodstain ) \n I (bloodstain) shadows of my (bloodstain)....", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume I", "Minnan1", "I've Finally arrived at Aegis. I was sent to somekind of Temple along with other travelers I hope I find what I seek in this lands . I've begun to write a journal in order to state all my adventures somewhere and in case I complete my quest, other Ayleids shall read it... \n - Aedan, Last Ayleid. \n First Entry: \n I've found a group of travelers that don't seem to feel unfomfortable with n Elf among them . They seem to rather enjoy my company. One of them, a man named Bircalin has a certain feeling towards me. He shurely thinks I do not know but if I've learned something about my kind is that we are cappable of more than others think . I better not tell him and leave this entry for now... \n Second Entry: We found a church in the way to Oren, Human Capital, and begun to talk about our story and what brought us here . Some of the stories are rather sad to me Haelphon: A Human that lost his father at a young age. Recieved his father's welth but used it for evil deeds and became selfish. Soon he left to travel in search to purify his eagerness. Struck by lightning many times as a signal from the gods of his forgiveness. Now he seeks for his family... \n Something about his story seems rather unlikely to me , I suspect of his fathers dead. I rather not say anything for now.... \n I'm going to continue this entry in the next Journal, I'm short on paper for now and we need to g o to Oren as soon as we can \n - Aedan, Last Ayleid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume II", "Minnan1", "First Entry: I've contracted some kind of disease, pain goes through my body, I faint constantly, I can barely speak, I don't know what's wrong with me, we are heading North searching for elves to help me... \n \n We arrived at some place, they put me in a bed and Bircalin came to tell me he would go get some food for me... I yet dont understand humans, they seem to be more kind than it seems. \n \n I got cured after a while, we returned south heading for Laurelin, Haelphon suggests I stay in a place inhabitated by elves so I may find more of my kind among them. \n \n \n Second Entry: I've got a nice house from an elf named Midnus he seems like a good person and already knows of my origin, he promised to keep it as a secret. \n \n After a while we got a meeting with the High Prince to talk about me, he gave us some copies of a book with possible proofs of Ayleids founding Laurelin. Bircalin left to Ravenhold looking for a better place to live. \n \n I shall continue what follows in my Field Research for I almost run out of paper. \n \n \n Third Entry: I've contracted a disease once again... but this one seems different from the previous one, I went to meet Romanen and Verigan at the Museum to have a talk. When I arrived they stared at my face saying I had something on it, we ran to the nearest pond to wear it off with water, wich we couldnt do. We went to Raven Hold in search of a Druid to help me althoguh he didn't help for an unknown reason. \n \n A Guard helped us come back to Laurelin to see if Respiren could help me, he wasn't here. \n \n I began to feel better after a while so I decided to go get a drink with Verigan at the tavern. \n \n I knew what I had, I just didn't want to tell my friends for their own safety. I had been Tainted during the fight at Oren against the Undead. The Aurorans had found me, The Last Ayleid... and they want me in their side... I do not know how to get rid of it for is not a common taint... I shall keep it in secret and try to wear it off somehow in order to keep my friends safe from it.... \n \n \nFinal Entry: I cannot wear it off! I've tried everything in the book, even tried mixing different potions and still.... I cannot get rid of it... \n \n Sunlight is beginning to bother me, I cannot stand it so I've closed all light access to my house... The Weeks of staying in bed have kept me from cleaning my house and now I have a mess.... \n \n \n I feel how the taint is getting over me, I've run out of hope... I had so many things to do, so many things to share.... \n \n Seems like I'll die before getting old... hehe... seems rather Ironic... the words of the Last Ayleid... I'll die... before finding others of my kind... if they still live.... I cannot write anymore, my handwriting is getting bad and I can barely think.... Is time for me to say goodbye... \n \n Bircalin,Haelphon,Romanen,Verigan.... My Brothers.... I wish this had ended otherway.... I can die in peace, knowing you will always keep me in your memories...knowing that my kind wasn't extinct until now.... \n Bircalin, You have plenty of knowledge from me as to fill a whole Library with it....thank you for being so kind with me.... \n \n Haelphon... thankyou for always helping me get over my emotions... \n \nRomanen... I forgive you and I hope you forgive me.... I wish we could've talked more... \n \n Verigan... fellow elf... I barely knew you.... you've been a nice friend to me, a loyal friend to all.... take care... \n \n I wish this had ended other way.... \n \n Farewell my Brothers!.....Farewell.... \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid..... \n \n Ny Hath Agaiayae cei das Marghathar dos garlas vas motheneth You shall not fear the shadows of your ancestors.... \n Hathes margoth nas volegheth vohkul as Auror.... You shall trust the shadow you leave behind......", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume III", "Minnan1", "First Entry: \n \n I fell in love with a Beautiful Wood Elf named Maiavel, She helped me while I was sick of Taint. I proposed to her no so long ago under my friends recommendations. We decided not to marry for reasons I cannot tell. \n \nSecond Entry: \n \n My friends have changed a lot since we met 2 years ago... \n \n Bircalin has existencial problems being accepted as a Halfling. \n He wishes to know nothing from me or Maiavel. \n \nHaelphon is lost, he doesn't find a place to belong to... \n \n Romanen is dead, he became undead due to his foolishness. We tried to help him but he seeks power for unknown reasons... \n \n I have found peace and decided to make a new beginning in laurelin. \n \n Third Entry: \n \nAfter a long time, I managed to reunite my friends to fight the undead. That ended in a fight with Bircalin and I left the campaign to return home. \n \n \nFourth Entry: \n \nBircalin is back to himself, Helphon left without saying a word, Romanen became undead to get Power and become feared. His Ignorance prevents us from helping him. \n \n Maiavel got a home in some place wich name I forget everytime. \n \n Fifth Entry: \n \n Maiavel met an old friend named Garn, they now live together in Old Laurelin. Good Old Bircalin is back and Romanen insists that we all become Undead with him. \n \n Sixth Entry: \n \n We infiltrated the Undead as a mission for Prince Native. Bircalin and the others Hided while I and Romanen infiltrated the fortress. When we got inside, they turned on a fire trap, Romanen burned and I survived to get the information and left with my friends. \n \nWhen I got home, Maiavel said she could see my Spine, Skull and Most of my chest's insides for my flesh had burned... \n \n Seventh Entry: \n \nAfter a while of resting and Maiavel taking care of me, I got fully healed and I'm back to normal. I decided to create a secret organization for the good of the kingdoms... The Mythic Dawn.... We will focus on Stealth and Information recovery missions... \n \n That's all what happened lately, resumed for I get tired of Writting... \n \n- Aedan. I'm tired of waiting for others to do the right things... Its now my turn to do something for the good of Aegis...", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume IV", "Minnan1", "First Entry: \n \n No so long ago, war struck a small village no so far from Kramoroe. A undead Lord was killing travelers and all those who walked by. So, I took my sword, jumped to the roof he was at and killed him... I thought it had been easy, but I was wrong. \n \nRight after that, Lightning struck me and pigmen attacked me. I remembered only waking up in Midnus' house bleeding from everywhere and being able to see my skull with my left eye that had been turned by electricity. \n \n They seeked all help they could, I had little bits of flesh and I was dying slowly. Even High Prince Native was there... I went to Al'Khazar with the bit of energy left. There I seeked help of a Healer friend, Freya. She's a beautiful human, Sapphire blue eyes... Pitch Dark hair... \n \n She almost runs out of vital energy to heal me, after I was healed, I offered her a Golden Apple. .. \n \n She restored her energy and I thanked her. \n \n Second Entry: \n \n My friend Indelwehn seems to feel something towards me... What shall I do? \n \nThird EntryL \nThird Entry: \n \n I met a Blind Dark Elf... She seems different from others... Clean minded, Kind... I shall do my best to help her. \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume V", "Minnan1", "First Entry: \n \n I met a beautiful Wood Elf named Indelwehn no so long ago. Since I first saw her I have this feeling... It tickles in my heart... I feel butterflies in my stomach... \n \n She mentioned she felt the same towards me, so we went with Hempshine to ask him about it. \n \n \nSecond Entry: \n \n That cheeky bastard... When we got in a private place to discuss our feelings with him... He lighted on some of his \"Hemp\" nad left us locked in the room saying he wouldn't let us go until there was 3 of us in there. \n \nWe got out thanks to Dawn and Hempshine got punished. We talked to Dawn about the same thing and she answered it was \"Love\"... It seems I fell in love with Indelwehn, does she feel the same? \n \n Third Entry: \n \n Indelwehn and I are deeply in love with each other. She is the greatest elf I ever met. \n \n No so long ago she told me she was an Ayleid too... I got really excited for she was the only Ayleid besides me in Aegis and we fell in love with each other... \n \n \n Fourth Entry: \n \n I decided to propose to her, she said yes in Al'Khazar's Park after we got out of a room where Hempshine locked me to keep me as a pet. Indelwehn refused to leave me alone in the room. \n \n \n Native agreed to create The Mythic Dawn, Indelwehn is the second in command, we now need to find a place to build the HQ. \n \n We plan to build our own house after the wedding... Everyone says it was obvious we were going to marry for some reason and also expect us to have babies... I yet don't understand why.... \n \n \n Fifth Entry: \n \n Indelwehn is everything one could seek in an elf... \n \n She's Kind, Strong, Loyal, Beautiful, Silly, Nice... I love her...", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal Volume VI", "Minnan1", "Aaah... Marriage is a lovely thing . \n \n \n Indelwehn and I have a great love towards each other. \n \n Indelwehn and I now have a daughter, her name is Arya. She looks just like Indelwehn but with my hair. \n \n I've turned deaf after some whispering voices invaded my head in Oren. Indelwehn is suffering a lot because of me, Bircalins is doing his best to help... I admire him. Arya seems to be the only one without problems and I'm happy for it. \n \n We adopted a little elf named Sparrow, we will take care of him for a while.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Journal: Final Chapter", "Minnan1", "I've lived a long life in this world. I've met many people, I've had many friends. I've died many times and I have been brought back to life each time. I've met the love of my life, I've had wonderful children, and I've lost them all. \n \n I've wrote all my life since I decided I had started one I liked. I've seen how the people I met died, one by one. \n \n My life has been unique, most people wished to be in my place and recieve the same blessing I did. I consider myself a lucky being, but also...at a great cost. \n \n This is the last chapter of my Journal. The last day in presence of my only love...and possibly...my last day in this world of wonders. \n \n I've found the location of the capital of the Wild Elves. I've received the title of their ruler: Dragonlord. \n \n \nI now put aside both, my life and title, in order to understand life and help others in need. \n \n Here I write the words of the last Wild Elf...My last words... \n \nAgaiayae cei das Marghathar vae cyrod's voyae nye diil. Cei ayae naethos vae skal nye diil'vae Cyrodiil... \n \n \"You shall not fear the shadows of your ancestors. You shall trust the shadow you leave behind...\" \n \n -Aedan, Last Dragonlord of the Wild Elves of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Mind", "Minnan1", "I've Finally found peace with myself thanks to Maiavel... \n I shall now only wait for her answer to be happy once and for all....", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Testament", "Minnan1", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan's Thoughts", "Minnan1", "I've Finally found the way to sleep thanks to Maiavel. She's such a nice and beautiful Elf. \n \n I have this strange feeling... My Hearth tickles, I feel butterflies in my stomach.... I've never felt like that before... I wonder what is that feeling?..... \n \n \n I've found out the name of this feeling... Is Love.... or so Verigan says when I ask him. \n He says that I might be in love with Maiavel. I got really surprised when he said that... I wonder if she likes me.... \n \n \n I've finally given Maiavel the bow I made and the Roses just as Verigan said... \n ;: \n I decided to give her what used to be the most important thing in my life...Until now.... I gave her.... My Soul... \n \n I shall now wait for her answer... Verigan, Romanen, Haelphon, and Bircalin said that she was the right one.... I yet don't understand the meaning of \"Right One\" .... I yet don't understand humans completely... \n \n But anyways... I must wait for her answer... \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedan...", "Indelwehn", "Words cannot describe how sorry I am. But going to the undead fort was a mistake. It gave her the strength to overcome me, and lock me away in my own mind. I have managed just enough time to write you this letter. I hope you can forgive me. Whatever she does, remember : She is not me. I do not want to hurt you. I love you so much, keep Arya safe. Kepp her away from Lilly and Ar'Kelos. I will come back to you my love, ~ Indelwehn", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedans Journal Volume II", "Minnan1", "Aedan's Journal Volume II ........ this is no Journal I just messed up the titles What I write here... are my emotions.... My friend Bircalin told me to for I cannot get over the emotions that overwhelm my soul to the point of no release .... \n No so long ago....Bircalin told me about him dating a woman That matched perfectly with what he looked for... I felt happy for him I even had fun with it... but then I felt something awful in me, like something was eating my soul... Sadness \n \n My face turned pale and I went out to catch fresh air I began to have one of those darn reflexion moments that disturb me so much ... I remembered my race how I was the only one... How I had been so close to meet another one but I missed the date... then I thought.... \"What if it was a woman... a female Ayleid...\" This thought began to cross my mind as a leech taking all happiness from me .... I felt devastated ... I had lost my only chance to preserve my kind then the Ayleids would be extinct for real I would have to roam the lands alone.. watching how my friends and close ones died one by one as Ayleids have the longest Lifetime of all creatures it cannot be matched by magic It cannot be changed.... I wouldn't be able to have a family for I would live longer than them ... I wouldn't be able to love someone... for I cannot have a family not even elves live as long as I ......... I would be destinated to roam the lands of Aegis.... alone... for the eternity ... I cannot kill myself.... for I get revived by the monks ... No matter what I do I cannot Die.... I will die of old I'll have to live milleniums.... of pain and sorrow... ... oh I know sorrow well I was born when sorrow sang the songs of grim I cannot keep writing.... \n \n ( you find small tears as you read the final page....) \n \n \n - Aedan, The Last Ayleid...", ""),
        StaticBook("Aedin_Ealdvor's Description", "Tyber1231", "Name: Aedin Ealdvor    \nRace: Human \nAge: Unknown As for now \nProfession: Trader \nHome: His friend lends him a room, location unknown. \n \nDescription: , wears a green outfit with brown shoes and accents. He seems to be a nice person, knowing how to trade. He came to Al'Khazar to trade, Iron as far as I know . He is considering staying in here for longer, permanently perhaps. \nPrecisely, he wears a green shirt and brown pants. He's also got ginger hair.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegan Acadmy", "patato12", "The Aegan Acadmey is where you can learn new thing's such as .. The Art Of Cooking Smelting and Hunting We Are currently looking fo Students if you wish to become a Student or Teacher. Contact Ebs ((VonEbs or look on the forums)) yes Janitor", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegdaeron", "moloha", "His true name long forgotten \n His kin nothing but dust \n Aegdaeron the twisted and crazy \n His former self nothing but a ghast. \n \n His strenght was not too great \n In combat he was weak \n But his voice was made of gold \n He could even make the earth weep. \n And then he met a maiden \n More fair than the sea \n And he loved her very dearly \n For his doom he could not foresee \n The maiden heard his singing \n A song of love and longing \n She then knew, she too loved him \n Together, they belonged. \n For long they were together \n They laughed and danced and sang \n But at last the day came \n And the bells of his doom rang. \n A great battle came to pass \n His maiden first to go \n By an orc she was overpowered \n And his heart seemed to know. \n A madness took him over \n A rage so great and strong \n That Aegdaeron started singing \n For annihilation, a cursed song. \n And everyone that heard it \n Fell down to the earth \n His song had so much power \n That he called forth Death. \n When the foul deed was over \n He set her body ablaze \n For if more of her blood was spilled \n The very earth he would raze \n In the smoke of her body \n A second song begun \n Of lust for power, of need for blood \n And when it finished too, his sanity was gone. \n For Iblees rose from that smoke \n And split his soul in two \n A side was a relentless killer \n Strong, but insane too \n The other side was himself \n With his song as his only friend \n Aegdaeron roams Aegis \n Untill the time will end. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis", "availer", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Advertisement", "RossssM", "Is your shop not making any sales? : Are you looking for a materials collector?", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Freedom Fighters", "professorshields", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis History", "skinner452", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Rebels", "moop123", "We fight for the people of Aegis. Not for there rulers . We have good intensions. When ever a man is thrown in the Orc arena for no reason, we'll be there. When peoples serious problems are pushed to the side by the king, We'll be there. And when people cant pay there tax and have a fair reason, we'll be there. You have been given the chance to join us. (( I'm going to gather 2 members who will act as l leaders then i will post on the forums to get more members )). The location of our hideout (not base) will be given to all who apply. Good day future soldir. I hope to see you on the battle field. (( if you want to join /msg moop123 I want to join rebels )) the Clan's real name has yet to be decided for now it is the Aegis rebels .", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Shop", "tuarzen007", "Bread - 1770 \n Iron Block - 0 \n Iron Ingot - 49 \n Mushroom Soup - 0 \n White Wool - 0", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Survival Guide: Volume 1: Surviving the Urban Jungle", "racingbrother", "Surviving in Aegis is a hard task, not all are able to make it in the four main towns. These people resort to living in the wilds. If you do not want to be pushed out into the wilds, read this book. It will teach you how to make money, and ultimately survive in a big city. \n Chapter I, Making it Rain: To make money is the most important thing to do in Aegis. This is the center of everything that happens in Aegis. Minas can get you anything you want in Aegis, from poorly brewed ale to diamond blocks. To get money you must first get a job, or sell valued goods. I personally would recomend selling valued goods to normal citizens in your own home town. First you must choose what you want to sell. You can sell precious ores for a very high price. But selling ores is a very difficult task. This is a difficult task because to get precious ores you must first buy a mining permit. Or you could try to sell coal, which is not valued what so ever. So I wouldn't try to sell ores. If you want to sell goods, I would go with selling food. Food is needed in big towns for not starving to death. So to get food you must get kill animals who carry food, or farm the food. Farming is nearly impossible in the city due to not being able to create a farm without out buying land in the city. So killing animals to get food would be the best solution. What you'll need to do is go far enough out until you can chop down trees. Once you can cut down trees, create a crafting bench. After you have made a crafting bench, you'll need to make sticks. After this create a wooden pick. Once you've done this get three pieces of cobblestone, create a stone pick. Once you've done this, get about a stack of cobblestone. Make a sword after this task is done. Kill as many animals that will drop food as possible, these animals include pigs, cows, chickens, zombies, and spiders. Now after getting food, go to the most populous area in your main kingdom. Announce that you are selling food at a low price. When some people start to buy your goods, you'll be getting money.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis the begining", "tfortacos", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Zoology: Common Species", "Ohaythar121", "Hail friends, I am Sillion, the author of this book. From my many years of living in the wilds, I grew a strong bond with the species that roamed its grassy knools, and dark crevices. But, up until recent times, I've never fully studied these creatures to any extent. However, thanks to recent developments, I've taken the time to examine many specimens of almost all species. \n In this book, we shall take a look at the peaceful members of our ecosystem. These beasts feed us, cloth us, and sometimes even fight with us. But, it's not often we take the time to figure out what they are really doing whilst we aren't gettign something from them. Luckily, I've taken the time to see their habits in nature first hand. \n Chapter 1: The Pig \n Ah the pig. We feed on it's succulent meat, find mushrooms with it's help, and raise them like the intelligent pets they are. But, we don't often give them the credit they deserve. For one, their meat is often known as tasty, but it's not quite that simple. Raw, a piece of pork will not only fill your belly, it's old body was so resistant to diseases that it's almsot impossible for one to catch anything from it. However, when the meat is cooked, the real magic hapens. When a piece of pork is baked, the protein and nutrients release from the crevices of it's fatty deliciousness. THis means, a more satisfying meal, and it helps a adventurer build the muscle and strength needed to survive in our beautiful land. \nPigs are also well known for their quickness to become attached to people. THis is because of two major factors. One, the pig is a little scavenger, well adapted to the lands of Aegis, and will discover the easiest path to survival very, very quickly. And two, pigs are highly intelligent creatures, known for their very advanced breeding patterns that roam amongst the land, and their extremely adept sense for mushrooms. Therefore, they have a knack for most races of Aegis, when treated correctly. \n So, in conclusion, be kind to the gentle, wise pig, for they are worthy of our respect, and admiration. Perhaps even, our love. \n Chapter 2: The Sheep \n The gentle sheep. A curious creature, known for it's penchant for sugar cane, and it's obviously fluffy coat, the sheep is a important part of our ecosystem, and daily life. Anyone who has worked as a tailor knows the supple, comfortable, poofy material known as wool far too well. Easily harvestable using a pair of shears, the wool produced from sheep makes up a vast majority of our clothing. \nThe sheep also has another odd quality, it's completely inedible meat. As an ex-huner gatherer, this quality is a mix of infuriating, and biologicaly fascinating. Upon further study, the real reason of the sheep's odd meat acidity, and poison, is it's Upon further study, the real reason of the sheep's odd meat acidity, and poison, is it's diet, and lifestyle. The sheep are known for eating large amounts of sugar cane, not a volatile mix itself. But, when coupled with the amount of toadstools sheep consume, it makes a strong poison to most sentient races in Aegis. Perhaps the future will hold a soylvent to cure the posion is sheep meat, but for now, we must gaze upon with distaste, and dissapointment. \n Chapter 3: The Chicken \n The little chicken. A creature known for it's annoying habitual clucking, it's succulent meat, and it's feathers, which are invaluable to archers world wide. Now, to begin observing the chicken's life, you must first observe the chicken itself. Well known for its small stature, the chicken is an abundant food source. Due to the fact that it's meat is easily obtainalbe from it's corpse, many a hunter has been saved by this little fellow. Their feathers are another interesting trait of the little chicken. While it chickens are small, their feathers are notoriously tough, making them a very viable component of arrow making. But, chickens also have one more thing about them that stuns zoologists everywhere. When observed from a upclose, the chicken appears to just be a normal animal, going about it's buisness of procreating, eating, and sleeping. But, when observed from a distance. the chicken begins to display signs of intelligence. Not only will chickens gather together, in seemingly meeting-esque groups, they also appear to watch places of sentient inhabitance with odd curiosity. What does the mean for us? Perhaps the chickens are much more intelligent then we know or perhaps we're simply paranoid of the little guys. Only the future holds the answer to this mystery. \n Chapter 4: The Cow", ""),
        StaticBook("Aelcor's Journal", "sk8r1056", "Me and my friends bought a new house today! Its very nice. Hopefully we'll have enough money to buy two more stories! Me and Artemis are going monster hunting , Maybe we'll find some things on the way that will help us with money problems. We found various items on our monster hunt , Maybe enough to get a basement or a 2nd storie. Well , Im off to sell our things that we found , Its turned ou to be a pretty good day today Well , I sold the valuables and came to a whoppings total of....... 100 mina. Yeah , its not alot but , Money is money. The High_prince is coming today to sell us a 2nd story! HE should be here any second/minute n ow.... ((Now*)) (( Well , He could be a roleplay butler )) Artemis and I were talking about our new butler arrival , And where he should be most of the time. High_Prince-Native came to our house today to give us another story , It looks fantastic!!! 8/30 Me and Lysaenai stumbled upon what seems to be a tomb on the Whiserping isles we are about to enter the tomb as I write. There was nothing in the temple , SAdly. Lysaenai says there is another part of the tomb , Hopefully there its of some signifigance. The warden course is getting harder and harder each minute!", ""),
