        StaticBook("After Action Report: Undead Attack on Al kaze'r", "begginfokillz", "This report is written by Recruit Dimitri Krechenko, Acting Commander of Emergency Operations against undead in Al Kahzer at time of this writeing. Begin After Action Report: me (dimitri), Shaman Sertok, Recruit Jordan, Recruit Eriic, and Brigideir (NAME CLASSIFIED) were in the fort when suddenly, Recruit Eriic reported some grave news: the Filthy undead had taken Al Kazze'r! we beleived the guards were collaberating. we began planning a first strike into al kaze'r, and we planned on allying ourselves with S.A Dimitri and a friend named Tamra, who was a Oren Guard. went to the SA Fortress. They tricked dimitri and tamara and tried to forcibly conscript us dimitri fled and the clan mounted a rescue operation for tamara we were ambushed and we fled FINAL REPORT: Clan SA is a menace, filled with brigadands and theives. they must never become ally with us", ""),
        StaticBook("Afterthoughts", "VonEbs", "A short note. If you are reading this Felore, then I am so sorry. I went and died on you. but you need to be strong. I ask you to do two things for me. One, I want you to find hapiness. You can't stop looking, no matter what. Secondly, my nephew os coming to Aegis, and I want you to help him get on his feet. He was like a son to me back in my home country, so I will be grateful if you aren't too hard on him. \n A Poem Some people say, that people come into our lives for a reason\n ,bringing lessons we must learn. And we will grow, with them, if we help them in return. Well I don't know if I believe that is true. But what I do know is that so much of me is what I learned from you. So I can say, firmly, that because I knew you, that I have been changed for good. I ask forgiveness, for the wrongs I have commited. and I give thanks, for the good you have done for me. And I know, we will never see eachother again in this lifetime, so ask before we part. Will you remember me, the good and the bad, as a friend, the best of the kind? And you should know, that for better and for worse, that I have always *tears blot out the rest of the poem*", ""),
