        StaticBook("Akeron", "Royced", "I have a hidden castle, deep in the frozen wilderness. In the castle are diamonds and jewels. the castle itself is directly above orc camp, for many, many miles. You have found good fortune when you found my journal. Use the reward wisely. Akeron", ""),
        StaticBook("Akeron's detective book.", "Royced", "I was hired by the king of Dwarven Might to help work the Minecart tracks throughout Aegis. I am currently assoicating with a member, who informs me that i cannot work untill Lord Algoda returns and helps us on the project. I will keep an eye out and wait for him to come back.. .", ""),
        StaticBook("Akiviri's Journal", "Uberr", "Date 1, today was uneventfull i got about a stack of logs and found sugar cain. I also found about 5 pigs, its good i was geting hungry and apples were running low. My father always said \"An apple a day keeps the doctor away, but nothing tasts like ham!\" I miss my father. \n Today I killed two creepers! I found on them 50 minas! OH and a skeleton wich droped lether ar mor  The weat seems to be growing nicely aswell, OH father the lybrary almost seems posible! \n Date 6, I whent on a short sand run a couple days ago and got lost for a couple days, just then did i realise how far that silly litle druids quest brought me .Im at leat 5,000 blocks away from ANY civilization. mabie i should head back? \n Date 7, I just had an idea! mabie i should make the lybrary under the sea? OH! then mabie ill travle around make copys of all the books and put them in my lybrary! Oh father you will love it! \n Date 8, I got about 240 blocks of sand today! the projects comming nicely! \n Date 9, I dont know what happend there must have been a hex or something! I was sent to this weird graveyard, fortunatly i still had all y stuff. the problem is finding my way back, I think I can do it... Till then im just gonna stay in other peoples houses, I hope no one see's me!", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta", "Angelus_Obscurus", "*Everything within this book has never been told to anyone else before* \n Everything i have told everyone has been a lie.. This Akorta character i try to be is all just a lie! I cannot continue, but i must.. I have to.. I will! Even though it's eating at me day after day, chewing away at my ver being! The pain within my skull, within me is unbearable which is why i write this, to finally tell the truth. \n \n The blood coursing through my veins doesn't feel my own, it feels wrong.. But for now i must sleep. \n The days go by, inside i feel myself being ripped apart by all these lies by all these.. all this hatred at myelf.. I CAN'T TAKE IT ANYMORE! WHY DO I HAVE TO PUT UP WITH THIS TORTURE?! \n Today i just stood watching the water, watching the trees swaying in the wind.. Everything was just pure, so perfect.. But then i saw a Human and i was reminded of what life is really like, damn i hate the races of Aegis, they make me sick. \n It has now been a few weeks since the last time i bothered wasting my time with this book, I have thought i was going to be killed many times since then, but sadly i don't get the satisfaction of my life leaving my body, oh well there will always be other times. \n \n Today a child came up to me and asked if could have a look at my mask, the very thought of this disgusting child touching my made me sick, this pathetic thing will eventually be killed if he follows the path of most people around Aegis. \n Alethion.. Alethion... Daughter? Alethion told me he has a Daughter that wasn't his But yet.. she looks so much like him, this place confuses me.. She is so innocent and small, it almost brings warmth to my heart, the way she calls me \"Uncle Akorta\" I.. Do not want someone like this to go through the pain of love, or hate. But.. Then i remember that she is only a Human, but.. .... \n \n Zhotia.. Aletions Daughter, why do i feel emotion towards this child, i do not feel emotion damn it! But then again, Alethion has been like a brother to me, i have thought about telling him all of this, but i cannot, and i will not. \n \n Alethion and I have gone back to what we doing best, Adventuring. This has brought great memories back to me, but i got to stay focused, because it isn't me \n Akorta.. Akorta..... Akorta........ I am Akorta, but why.. Why am I Akorta? Why did i have to be born this way, why can't i remember my childhood! all i can remember is hatred, and the lust for death of all the races.. Who am I? \n \n \n You reading this, who am I?", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta", "isagirl909", "Akorta \n \n I've been worried about you lately. You seem...distracted . Please, if there's anything going on, you can tell me. I know how to keep secrets. I just hope that you would trust me enough to let me know. I care about you, Akorta. \n \n Signed, \n \n Annora.", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta", "Alectriciti", "Is mean. write Don't leave him alone with Annora.", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta and Annora", "Alectriciti", "I cannot express how much I admire your friendship. You both now gone... Though we've had rough times in the past, you two have been the best friends Rhisereld and I could have asked for. Besides Brett. I love you both so much, and I will miss you. I will cherish every memory we've shared in the past. Rest in peace, you two. ~Alethion Celebtaurë~", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta Pt. 2", "Angelus_Obscurus", "Zho.. Zho... Zhotia... I tried to tell you that anger was an ally, an ally that could make you stronger as a person, which in my mind is the truth. But i had to have the help of an orc that you know as \"Uncle Vardak\" to remind me that i am not the only person in this world with a mind. \n \n Zhotia.. I am worried for you, this is an emotion i have never felt before.. Why now.. Why after all these years do i feel this emotion to someone i barely know,t Nothing makes sense anymore, i should not feel this, i should only feel anger.. Anger towards all of Aegis, but why? Why do i hold this anger deep down inside.. \n \n I know why, It's because the first time in years it feels that i actually have a family, a family that cares about me, Alethion, Rhisereld, and you, Zhotia. I think i am truly happy with my life, now there is more to life then just survivng each day for now i know i survive because of yous... \n I used to only ever care about being able to watch the sunrise and set, it was the only thing that showed me warmth, it is the life giver to us all, i used to watch it rise and set with pain and anger in my heart, hating this world, but not anymore . Now whenever i look at the Sun coming and going i will think of yous, my family.", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta the Squid", "Alectriciti", "Once upon a time there was a squid named Akorta. He was very ugly and nobody liked him. He was also an asshooelee ... *you see a drawing of a poorly drawn squid with a frowny face on it* Nobody likes this squid so we should get our fishing rods and harpoons Death to thish oceanish sea beast thingy! The end, kind of I guess", ""),
        StaticBook("Akorta!", "Angelus_Obscurus", "I am still the ale champion! *You see a poorly drawn picture of Akorta drinking ale with Sal passed out in the corner \n \n Date: Everyday \n \n -Akorta.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar", "Pepernoot", "Al'Khazar is the capital of the human kingdom of Oren. It has grown a lot over the years, and is continually expanding despite the neverending attacks by the undead. On top of the mountain that overshadows the old part of the city lies the Keep, where the king and his entourage live. There are also docks, and countless of shops. The city is the beating heart of the economy and military of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar Attack Plan", "Acornlad", "This is the Orc Battle Plan on the Human City of Al'Khazar \nThis plan is only for the Orc Nation, If the Elves are to join the attack, they will assist our plan with archers and warriors. \nThe Orc Army consists of between 20-30 Warriors. Each of the Warriors is trained, well-armed, and disciplined. The Human Army consists of about 50 warriors; however these warriors are poorly trained, poorly equipped, and unorganized. Even though the Human Army is weaker pound-for-pound they still can win due to their numbers. But numbers do not win wars. Careful planning and a disciplined army is what wins. \nThe Plan \nThe Attack will be launched at dawn. At around midnight of that day; half of the Orc Army will move to the North Gate of Al'Khazar, this force must be discrete and have to take the path around Al'Khazar. The other half of the fighting force will leave to Al'Khazar at 3/4ths through the night. This force will consist of about 10 Orcs, these Orcs will move to the main gate of Al'Khazar. These 10 Orcs will split up again into a group of 7 and a group of 3. Both the group of 7 and the group of 3 will be armed with bows and arrows, along with their swords. \nThe group of 3 Orcs will move to the top of the small mountain near the main gate. The group of 7 will move across the ground to the front of the gate. The group of 7 will serve as a distraction to the humans while the group of 3 move down onto the wall and neutralize the guards. The group of 3 orcs will then open main gates into the city, elimanting the main gate as a choke point. \nThe group of 7 orcs will move along and destroy all men at the first gate. The group of 3 Orcs will move across the roofs and go to the second choke point, the old Al'Khazar gate. From there the group of 3 orcs will nuetralize the men on top of the gate. The group of 7 will begin to push through the second choke point.  \nWhile all of this is occuring, the group of 10 Orcs at the North Gate have been moving towards the main gate, and they will approximately reach the other group of Orcs at the second choke point, where they will flank the humans, eliminating the main human force from the fight. \nThis will have eliminated 2 of the 3 main choke points in Al'khazar. The next choke point will be the path towards the the Keep. In theory the humans should the advantage due to them being elevated above the Orcs, but this can be avoided. The group of 10 orcs that came from the main gate will move onto the wall and climb to the top of the keep, while this is occuring, the other group of ten will move across the path towards the keep. This group on the ground will serve as a main distraction. The group on top of the keep will then come down behind the humans firing at the Orcs on the pathway. This will eliminate the the other main part of the human army. \nWith most of the Human army eliminated the Orcs will then enter the keep and take it in the name of Krug. Even though Al'Khazar will be taken, some humans will still be in Al'Khazar. To eliminate the rest of the humans, the Orc army will split into a group of 12 and a group of 8. The group of 8 will stay in the Keep and defend it. The group of 12 will be split further into groups of 3. These groups of 3 will move throughout Al'Khazar and kill any remaining humans. \nOnce this has been done, the battle will be over and the orcs will have successfully taken over Al'Khazar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar Construction Report", "monkeychez", "Our agents have robbed the orcs blind, we're able to complete the new Keep using these funds. We'll have no problem completing the Keep on time at this rate. Signed, Diplomat Dolir", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar Rulebook", "Lord_Kashi", "This book will go as follows \n [Offence] - [First Time Punishment] - [Second Time Punishment] \n 1. Sword out in the city - Strong Warning - 50 Mina fine \n 2. Standing on the walls or roofs - Jailed for one day - Arrested and fined 100 Minas \n 3. Entering through the docks - 100 Mina fine - 250 Mina fine \n 4. Trespassing - Jailed for one day - 250 Mina Fine (This fine increases depending on the location) \n 5. Treason or <attempted> murder - Execution \n 6. Iblees/Undead Propaganda - Jailed for one day - 250 Mina fine then removed from the city. \n 7. Wearing dark robes and/or a hood - Get them to remove the hood, if they're Undead, jail them and request a senior officer, if not, tell them not to wear one again. \n 8. Posession of an unauthorised farm - 250 Mina fine - 500 Mina fine \n 9. Theft - Jailed for one day and pay back twice the amount stolen to the victim (increase this number as offenses increase) \n NOTES: \n Trespassing means inside houses that do not belong to the culprit, inside restricted areas such as the gatehouse, and the keep, or private rooms inside buildings such as inns. \n If the culprit attempts to resist arrest by attacking the guard, the punishment is to be made more severe \n Just because you are not on duty, does NOT mean you can let crimes slide, you must always be on the lookout for those up to no good. \n Remember, be firm in your judgement, but be fair. \n If a villain is unable to pay the fine, they can ask for a friend to pay it for them. If no friends pay the fine, one of two things happen. If the fine is under 500 Mina, the villain spends one extra day in jail, if it is over 500 mina, the villain is executed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar Rulebook.", "RossssM", "The book will go as follows. (Crime): (1st Time Punishment) (Repeat Punishment) \n Sword Out In The City: 1st Time: Strong Warning- Repeat: 50 Mina Fine \n Standing On The Roofs Or The Walls: 1st Time: Strong Warning-Repeat: 100 Mina Fine. \nEntering Through The Dock's: 1st Time: 100 Mina Fine-Repeat: 250 Mina Fine \nEntering the gatehouse: 1st Time: Strong Warning-Repeat: 100 Mina Fine. \nTreason: Execution. \nIblees or Undead Propaganda: 1st Time: Arrested And Jailed For Susupicous Acts   - Repeat: Arrested, Fined 100 Minas, Then Escorted Out Of The City \nMorally Improper Conduct: Use Common Sence For Your Decision. Generally Just Strong Warning. \nWearing Dark Undead 'Like' Robes: Always Arrest And Escort Out The City. \nMany Of These Rules Do Not Apply To Ourselves 'The Oren Guard'. Be Strong But Lenient.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al'Khazar Stocks.", "tuarzen007", "Diamond - 0 \n Iron Block - 0 \n Mushroom Soup - 22 \n White Wool - 201 \n Bread - 1870 \n Gold Ingot - 68 \n Iron Ingot - 127 \n Moss Stone - 61 \n White Wool - 39", ""),
        StaticBook("Alan Remmer's Log", "dabrander", "Today I heard about the undead invasion out in the Winterfel area. I decided to start writing a journal, as I don't know if i'll survive this invasion of monste rs. I hope this book will survive the war so I can leave some small mark on Aegis. Entry 2: I traveled the King's Road today towards Winterfel. When I arrived, the gates were wide open. After some exploration, I discovered that everyone was either dead or gone. There were only bones and ash. None of the said \"intelligent\" undead were present . Winterfel sustained some damage from undead fires, but the majority of the outpost remained untouched. What frightens me is the close proximity of Winterfel to Alkazar. The walls of Winterfel were high and mighty. And these undead brought them down. Every night countless mindless undead appear out of nowhere. With any sort of general, the walls of Alkazar will surley fall. Entry 3: Too much ales, can't barely write. Ughh.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alanors Last Words", "Cookie9000", "As you may wonder why my sudden death, this is something you must read. I was with my friend, Aster, in my insane state, walking along with him... I was thinking... What do I live for? Why should I continue to live.. My actual family died when I was 5... By undead. And for SEVEN years... I lived... Alone... In the wilderness.... Until some druid found me... And let me in his home for awhile, everything was normal.. Joined the Nical, met a man named Will and then happily left the Nical, when I found Will with a friend, he asked me if he wanted to \" join\" him... I asked what that meant, he said he made a new family.. Called the Adelban family, its a blood brother sort of thing, I joined it, and felt accepted... We attacked people who threaten us, and everything was all family and fun... Until we caught some kid... By the name of Alek, Alek Halblood, we caught him, brung him into the Slums of Alras... I promised not to tell his father we caught his son... But his father found me... And tortured me... Until I confessed, and the moment Will found out, I was banished... Forever. You may of not noticed, but for the last days I was on the edge of mentally breaking down... Losing the only thing to give me love... It hurt me... And I couldn't take that hurt in me any longer, I gazed at a poison... A poison to kill a man.. For good, as I stare at it, I realize my way out of the pain, my way. Out of life... And as I drink it, I know the clock is ticking for my life, so I quickly have dug a grave for me in my very own tent... Someone will see it... And know of my death... And I left this here... to let you know... Why I'm not here any longer... ~Alanor, or Dreadmoore, as few know him as.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alanors Ponder", "Cookie9000", "While I drank one of my test poisons, just enough of a shot not to kill me... I thought. What would happen if Alanor passed on... My alchemy... For nothing... All my years.. Years of life.. All for nothing... Then I thought \"What if... What if I made... Another version of me... Like a copy... \" Then it began I have been getting items to help me build... Another me... It doesn't have to look human... As long as it works... Ender pearled eyes.... Redstone wiring... Bronze body, or better yet, Iron! It shall work out.. As I write this, I tested another poison.. And some man named \"Thork\", I think he is in the \"Black Hand\" ... And Nical hunt me down... And the military in Galahar want to hang me as a prize... I must finish this soon People grow suspicious in this camp about me, I can feel it... I will make this being like me unstoppable... Making it last twice as long as me... And nothing standing, in its way... - The Alchemist Wait!", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht Funeral", "HarrisonBitzis", "Erm.. I find it quite hard to write this, Tom. Albrecht is deceased, and his funeral will take place ((Tomorrow, 7:00 Pacific.) You will attend as a guest of honor, due to your close relation with Albrecht. Thanks for reading this.... ~Will Forestin", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht Therving", "firespirit44", "Name : Albrecht Therving (Garukumush) \n Race: Northerner \n Age/Gender: 31, Male \n Skillsh: Fighter,... hic! diplomat... hic!", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht's Funeral", "HarrisonBitzis", "Erm.. I find it quite hard to write this... But a good friend, Albrecht Therving, has deceased recently. Due to your close relation with Albrecht, We would like you to attend as a guest of honor. The funeral will take place ((Tomorrow, 7:00 Pm Pacific Time.)) I'd quite appreciate it if you came and honored him, Braxis. ~Will Forestin (( By the way. (( (( If you get this a day after it was written, It'll just be TODAY at 7:00 PM pacific. Okay?))", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht's Funeral: Gio's Speech", "racingbrother", "Hi everyone, I'm new to Aegis. If you don't know my name is Gio. I don't know a lot of people here, but I did know Albrecht. He didn't perticularly like me, but he was a friend. A very good friend. I'll always remember the first time we met. He was serving me in his tavern and I was drunk. He thought it was funny, than kicked me out of the tavern. I don't remember much about that night but I remember that I met Albrecht. Albrecht, from the stories I have heard from various people, was a true gift from from Aeriel. He was the founder of Alstion, leader and founder of the rangers and was one of the founders of Talun. These were all amazing feets that he was able to accomplish. These are feets thatI hope I can one day accomplish. He was a real role-model. He was serious and stern but was more succesful than most people in Aegis. He was a teacher to you and me, and a fantastic brother , father, and most importantly, a friend to us all. Hopefully Throdo can lead the house of Therving well, and his son Rupert will carry on his name with respect and dignity. Rest in peace Albrecht, you will be missed. And I know you can here us all Albrecht. So I think I can speak for all of us, Thank you for all you have contributed to Aegis and us. Thank you for you're time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht's Last Will", "Garukumus", "Well, I am getting old, and as my frieds have reminded me, I need to be prepared incase something happens to me/ So I leave all me possessions to my one son, Rupert Therving. When I die he will inherit the family name, which will become Ruprecht Therving. I also want 500 minas given to the King when I die, and all ownership of the Inn to transfer to the King, unless he sells it, if he tries to it willl go to Rupert. Thats all I want when I die, no fancy graves or nothin'. ~Albrecht  Will, this is my will. help  *falls to the ground", ""),
        StaticBook("Albrecht_ Therving", "Wahsrof", "1) So how is the resturant? How much is made per weel? a) It is quite a bit, per week, We have rentals rooms, they bring alot in, its usually 800-3000 per Protection, danguras job. -forget that last line lol 2)  What all does the store sell? a) We sell common foods, such as bread, pork, chicken, steak, and stew, also ale at 3 minas. 3) How much do the rooms cost? a) We have two size rooms, a smaller room for 50 minas for 1 week, a large room for 150 minas, and a Luxery suite for 150??? theres some errors there. Oh, Luxery are 150, large are 100 and its per week.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alcarin's journal", "OlYeller", "If lord john talks to me it's about the knights templar trading companies old stall Contact Dacripla99 for huge ass sto", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_3(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Alchemica Compendium - An Alchemist guide to all potions", "Sir_Wyvernos", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemist", "Royced", "Hello there, reader. By the time you are reading this book, i have probably lost it. I am writeing this novel to keep me sane, for i am now trapped inside of a tiny hole, hiding for my very life. Do not feel sorry, for it is my fault. I have stolden the Arch of Kal Alras, a very, very valueable item which belongs to the dwarven culture. I plan to sell it for alot of money, though. I will write more if i do get out alive. (The next day) Hello, reader. I'm out of my hole, but i've been trapped for several hours. dirt is covered acrost my body, and i look hidious. Atleast i will be decently camouflaged. (One week since the first page) I have sold the archways, but unfortunatly, they found my money. i am now a poor man, with no money at all. Lets see how i get along! I have found a large open cave in the middle of nowhere, i plan to inhabit this cave untill i can find a safe shelter. A little backround check for thouse who do not know whom i be: I am the Alchemist! I am known for being an infamous killer, and i have started two wars, entirely myself. I feel as though i have the power of a king, when i am no more than a man with a silver tounge. The war between the Human and Dwarven cultures, that was my fault entirely, and i'm glad to say so. It took no more than a little blame for each side against eachother for it to start. (The next day) I am going to go pray to Iblees, i will write more when i have returned.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemist's Compendium", "ElynxYon", "There are two parts to every potion; There is the base reagent, meant to boil into the vial to change the properties of the water, and then there is the secondary ingredient that finalizes the result. After countless and tedious months of experimentation, failure, and labor, I have found all of the reagents that are compatible with the brewing stand, and their properties. Here, now I write, to give to you the results of my work. \n \n The Base Reagents \n Fermented Spider Eye - Creates a WEAK potion base.  This potion property is meant to lessen the positive effects of the secondary reagent and induces the negative affects. \nGlowstone Dust - Creates a THICK potion base.  This increases the affects of the secondary reagent and decreases the durationn of the potion. \n Netherwart - This creats an AWKWARD potion base.  This gives the seconday reagent no affect. \n Redstone Dust - Creates a MUNDANE potion.  This type of potion decreastes the affects while it increases the durationn. \n Gunpowder - Creates a SPLASH potion base.  This means this potion can be thrown and, from 3 to 5 square feet, affects the area it affects. \n \n Secondary Reagents \n Seconday reagents imbue an Awkward Potion with a particular effect and do not affect potion duration or intensity.  When brewed with a water bottle, any of these reagents will produce a MUNDANE potion. \n \n Blaze Powder - The effect is strength. \n Ghast Tear - The effect is regeneration. \n Glistering Melon - The effect is Instant Health \n Magma Cream - The effect is Fire resistance. \n Spider Eye - The effect is poisoning. \n Sugar - the effect is speed. \n \n Tertiary Reagents \n Tertiary reagents are reagents that create negative tertiary potions when followed by a fermented spider eye.  These are not recommended to be handled by alchemists of beginning level, and so, will not be found in this book, but in the Alchemist's Compendium Vol. II, which is for the more advanced of brewers. \n \n Alchemical Components \n Once you are sure you have all of the necessary ingredients needed to make a specific potion, you must then also make sure you have the proper equipment. These pieces include : A brewing stand, a glass bottle, and water. \n Some also cater to holding their water in a cauldron, but that is optional. As long as you have a water source, you do not need one. \n Up to three water bottles can be placed in the stand, and the ingredient is set atop the stand to brew out and distill into the water. This is key for making your potion. ..", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemist's Compendium II", "ElynxYon", "Though there are positive affects to a potion, this means there are also negative affects as well. In alchemy and brewing, there are reagents that create negative tertiary potions when followed by a fermented spider's eye, and these are called Tertiary Reagents. \n \n Spider eye > Fermented Spider Eye =Harm \n Glistering Melon > Fermented Spider Eye =Harm \n Sugar > Fermented Spider Eye =Slowness \n Magma Cream > Fermented Spider Eye =Slowness \n Blaze Powder > Fermented Spider Eye =Weakness \n Ghast Tear > Fermented Spider Eye =Weakness \n \n However, these affects are not to be taken lightly, and can harm you and others. Be careful with what you use these potions on. \n \n POTION CREATION \n (Primary) \n \n All primary potions are created by brewing a single reagent with a water bottle. Mundane Potion and Potion of WEakness can be combined with Gunpowder to create their throwable splash potion counterparts. \n \n Awkard potion = Netherwart + Water Bottle (precursor to: Potion of healing, fire, resistance, poison, regeneration, strength, and swiftness.) \n \n Mundane Potion (extended) = Redstone + Water Bottle (precursor to: weakness) \n \n Mundane Potion = Ghast Tear, Glistering Melon, Blaze Powser, Magma Cream, Sugar, or Spider Eye + Water Bottle (precursor to: Weakness) \n \n Thick Potion = Glowstone Dust + Water Bottle (precursor to: Weakness) \n \n Potion of Weakness = Fermented Spider Eye + Water Bottle (precursor to: Weakness).", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "Royced", "Alchemy is an ancient tradition, the primary objective of which was the creation of the mythical \"ph ilosopher's stone,\" which was said to be capable of turning base metals into gold or silver, and als o act as an elixir of life that would confer youth and immortality upon its user. Alchemy can be vie The best known goals of the alchemists were the transmutation of common metals into Gold or Silver ( less well known is plant alchemy or \"Spagyric\"), and the creation of a \"panacea,\" a remedy that supp osedly would cure all diseases and prolong life indefinitely; and the discovery of a universal solve In the eyes of a variety of esoteric and Hermetic practitioners, the heart of alchemy is spiritual. Transmutation of lead into gold is presented as an analogy for personal transmutation, purification, and perfection.[4] This approach is often termed 'spiritual', 'esoteric', or 'internal' alchemy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "lol00011", "Mushrooms, Ale, and Flowers are a good source to use for Alchemy... \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy and Dies- Notes", "Lexperiments", "Dyes are fundamentals for potions! Similar to essences. Great example to showcase fundamentals of potionmaking. Need alchemy set. Includes a burner, range from red to blue fire. Color of flame is nesssecary to extract colos. I wonder if those weird nether-fire-things could be used for this. Or just a regular fire. Dunno. Some essences- i mean dyes- can be put together to make a NEW dye! Bone meal's one of the most versatile ingredients. It's just too fucking hard to get. Lightened dyes are useful. Much more useful. I just copied this from a book in a private library. This is incredibly asinine.  There is a secret within Malin's Sister... By the way, when I said dies in the title, I did not mean dyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Guide, Advanced", "SimplePancake", "Elixir Of Life \n Start of by crushing two mushrooms, one brown, one red, with the flat sided blade of your knife. Once this is done, add them into your cauldron. . Once the two mushroom crushings have been added, mix in some heated water, and mix it clockwise 3 times, and anti-clockwise 2. (Heals 5 Hearts) \n \n Dough of Death\n First, kneed the dough, so that it has no air bubbles. Then, make it into a shape of a few roles. Once done, put it into a furnace for 40 seconds. Once the 40 seconds is done, pull it out of the furnace, and Enjoy!", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy research", "JustinMC98", "Dyes mixed with redstone dust, red mushrooms, and water sometimes causes eyes to change color and sometimes it causes skin to change colors it seems temporary but I am still unsure", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Vol. I- Components and Reagents", "silco97", "\nForward \n \n \nChapter 1 \nComponents of Alchemy \n \nEvery proper alchemst needs their proper set of tools in order to master the trade one must first acquire the following materials: \n \nBrewing Stand \nThis is one of the most important component to become a successful alchemist. The brewing stand although is quite a pricy thing to make.  In order to craft such a rare piece of equipment you must retrieve a magical blaze rod found only in the nether. Now this of course may lead to the question, is it worth it?  Well my dear reader it is indeed worth it.  This blaze rod can be found from the fire spirits that reside in the ruins there. You must then attach 3 bits of cobble along the bottom of it in order to harbor the bottles. When placing bottles in it, it can hold up to three, you must then place the ingredients in it and wait as the materials mix with the water.  Once the ingredients are done mixing you may remove the bottles.    \n  \n Cauldron \nThis is a necessity for those who want to make their potions in bulk. A simple cauldron can be used for a number of things other than cooking. You must place a bucket of water in it, it can then be used as a trip of tree refills of water for just your bottles and such.  The crafting process it not near as costly as the brewing stand one must simply smelt a bit of iron in the shape of a hours shoe. \n \n Bottles Glass \nThese are what make an alchemist.  They must fill up these bottles with water. preferable with the cauldron, and place them in the brewing stand to begin making and mixing your compounds. When you might find handy is that when you are brewing only on ingredient is needed to fill all three bottles if all three are in the slots of the brewing stand \n \n \nChapter 2 \nBase Reagents \n \nThese are often the most common although the most importent for making your base potions.  Although most of them have no immediate effect when brewed, when mixing them with other potions it can create the more powerful potions that every alchemist strives for. \n \nFermented Spider Eye \nThis is quite a simple thing to make.  One must simple obtain a fresh spider, suger, and a brown mushroom.  Mix these together with a mortar and pestle [[crafting table]] and you will have your fermented spider eye.  It should appear brown in color and a bit dry or mushy.  The basic effects if this ingredient most commonly used for potions are lesson positive effects and induces negative effects. \n \nGlowstone Dust \nA common material often found in no longer used glowstone. It has a powdery texture and gives offthe faintest light.  The effects found in glowstone dust that are used in potions are increase potion effects, and decrease potion duration. \n \nNether Wort \nAn unfortunately rare material to come by despite its use in alchemy. Nearly every potion needs this in the porcess of making it at some point or another.  It comes from the ground for the nether wort mushroom that grows best in soulsand. It has a glossy red pungent appearrance and oder. \n \nRedstone Dust \nA most common material that has a number of uses.  Its shiny red appearence and its strange ability to conduct energy gives it an array of possible uses such as decrease effects, and increase potion duration.  This can be found while mining best when you are in a cave, although redstone foten signals lava. \n \nGun Powder \nThis rare material comes from the deepest depths of earth in dungoens guarded by undead.  Its black powdery texture and seemingly explosive behavior allows it to be used in the most useful \"splash potions\", which will be told more about later \n \nChapter 3 \nEffecting Reagents \nThese reagents tale use of nether wort the most.  Althougn nether wort when brewed creates a rather useless clear blue potion it can be used and mixed with these reagents to make more useful potions. \n \nBlaze Powder \nThis rather rare material can only be found from the extracted oils of a blaze rod which are used to craft brewing stands.  They can only be found in the bowls of the flame spirits in the nether.  Simply grind the rod and you will have a healthy supply of powder.  It appears in a red orange color with an almost creme like texture. Its most common effects unsed in potions are strength. \n \nGhast Tear \nThe small clear and valuable ghast tear.  with crystal like sheen and seem to weigh nothing at all it can only be found in the tear ducts of a dead ghast.  They seem to cry for long periods of time, although killing a ghast is another story.  It's sought after power when brewed is regeneration. \n \nGlistering Melon \nAn expenzive melon created when you near a bit of gold to it.  It gives it a shiny almost \nmetallic sheen and also has the effect of instent health regeneration. \n \nMagma cream \nIn the same correlation with the blaze powder.  Simpley mix together blaze powder and a ball of slime from the strange organisms that live in caves.  The cream is of the same consistecny of slime although it takes on a red orange color of the powder. Although one must be careful, it is said to burn to the touch. Its effects in a potion are resistance to fire. \n \nSpider Eye \nFoud in the eye socket of your common spider.  Often purple in color and and in a number of sizes depending in which you retrieved it from. You want to take the eye ball its self as well as the long cords that are attached to it for both are importent.  The effects used in potions are poisoning. \n \nSuger \nA common household reagent although you will find a number of other uses for it besides cooking cakes and tarts.  When mixed properly it can give you a boost of speed that one might need for swift travel. \n \n  \nConclusion \n Now that you have read this book of alchemy reagents I would suggest to you reader that you continue reading other volumes of \"Alchemy\"to continue your studies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Vol. II- Primary Potions", "silco97", "\nForward \nWhen reading this volume of \"Alchemy\" you will find you will begin learning how to actually brew the potions talked about in the last volume.  Many diffrent reagents will be used during this volume and I would ask you not to read on unless you feel you are ready to learn. \n \n \nPrimary Potions \nThe most basic of any of the other potions that can be made.  Most of them have no effect what so ever, although they often act as building blocks for more powerful potions. \n \nAwkward Potion \nBrewing- Place glass bottles on the brewing stand and then brew nether wort with it. The potion produced should look no diffrent than that of the water in the bottles, although it is going to be used the most in later volumes. \nEffects- None \nPotions Used In- Instent Health, Potion of Fire Resistance, Potion of Poison, Potion of Regeneration, Potion of Strength, Potion of Swiftness \n \nMundane Potion (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone into bottles of water, the potion produced is used for very littles though. \nEffects- None \nPotions Used In- Potion of Weakness (Extended) \n \nMundane Potion \nBrewing- Brew a non fermented spider eye or glistering melon or blaze powder over water bottles \nEffects- None \nPotions Used In- Potion of Weakness \n  \nThick Potion \nBrewing- Brew glowstone over glass water bottles \nEffects- None \nPotions Used In- Potion of Weakness \n \nPotion of Weakness \nBrewing- The only potion of primary origin with any form of effect, brew fermented spider eye over glass water bottles \nEffects- The user becomes weal, and often cannot fight correctly [[when user inflicts melee damage the damage they do it halved]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Vol. III- Secondary Potions", "silco97", "\nForward \nSecondary potions are brewed when you take a primary potion and one or tow other reagents to create a more powerful potion.  All secondary potions can also be brewed with gunpowder to create potions that can be thrown to make effects of a potion appear on the target. They are divided into two sections, positive and negative effects. Often negative potions are used in the splash potions to give their target a nasty surprise. \n \n \nPositive Potions \nThese potions give the user a positive effect \n \nPotion of Healing \nBrewing- Brew a glistering melon over an awkward potion \nEffects- Upon drinking you will receive 3 hearts of health \n \nPotion of Fire Resistance \nBrewing- Brew magma cream over an awkward potion \nEffect- Upon drinking you will get resistance to fire and lava for 3 minutes \n \nPotion of Regeneration \nBrewing- Brew a ghast tear over an awkward potion \nEffects- Restores a full heart every 45 seconds \n \nPotion of Strength \nBrewing- Brew blaze powder over an awkward potion \nEffects- Adds a heart and a hlaf of damage to every attack with or without a weaping for 3 minutes \n \nPotions of Swiftness \nBrewing- Brew a sugar over an awkward potion \nEffects- Increase your sprinting speed and jumping length for 3 minutes \n \n \nNegative \nThese give the user a negative effect upon drinking although they can be useful weith a splash potion \n \nPotion of Poison \nBrewing- Brew a fresh spider eye over an awkward potion \nEffects- Poison the user until they only have half a heart left \n \nPotion of Weakness \nBrewing- Brew a fermented spider eye over a thick or mundane potion \nEffects- All damage inflicted by the user is halved for 1 minute and 30 seconds \n \nPotion of Weakness (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone dust or fermented spider eye over a mundane potion (extended) or a potion of weakness", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Vol. IV- Tertiary Potions", "silco97", "\nForward \nBy far the most advanced of the potions.  These tertiary potions can only be created if you mix reagents with secondary potions or other tertiary potions.  Although these potions can often get pricy to make in the end reap the most rewards.  Redstone and glowstone are used quite a bit in these potions so having a large amount on hand is useful \n \n \nPositive \nThese give the user a positive effect upon drinking \n \nPotion of Fire Resistance (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone over a potion of fire resistance \nEffects- Become immune to fire and lava for 8 minutes upon drinking  \n \nPotion of Health II \nBrewing- Brew a glistering melon over a potion of health \nEffects- Upon drinking you will have 6 hearts of health restored immediately \n \nPotion of Regeneration (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone dust over a potion of regeneration \nEffects- Restore health over a period of time of 2 minutes  \n \nPotion of Regeneration II \nBrewing- Brew glowstone dust over a potion of regeneration \nEffects- Upon drinking you will receive a heart of health ever 22 seconds \n \nPotion of Strength (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone dust over a potion of strength \nEffects- Adds a heart of health of damage to every attack you do with or without a weapon for 8 minutes \n \nPotion of Strength II \nBrewing- Brew glowstone dust over a potion of strength \nEffects- Adds 3 hearts of damage to every attack you do with or without a weapon for 1 minute and 30 seconds \n \nPotion of Swiftness (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone dust over a potion of swiftness \nEffects- Upon drinking your sprinting speed and jumping distance will increase for 8 minutes \n \nPotion of Swiftness II \nBrewing- Brew glowstone dust over a potion of swiftness \nEffects- Upon drinking your sprinting speed and jumping length will increase quite a bit for 1 minute and 30 seconds \n \n \nNegative \nThese have a negative effect on the user although quite useful when combined with gunpowder to make a splash potion \n \nPotion of Harming \nBrewing- Brew fermented spider eye over a potion of health \nEffects- Upon drinking the user will instantly be inflicted with 3 hearts of damage \n \nPotion of Harming II \nBrewing- Brew a fermented spider eye over a potion of health II or poison II, or brew glowstone dust over a potion of harming \nEffects- Upon drinking the user will be inflicted immediately with 6 hearts of damage \n \nPotion of Poison (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew redstone dust over a potion of poison \nEffects- Poison the user for 2 minutes decreasing their health from the poison at a minimum of half a heart of health  \n \nPotion of Poison II \nBrewing- Brew glowstone dust over a potion of poison \nEffects- Upon drinking the user will be inflicted with a heart of damage every 22 seconds \n \nPotion of Slowness \nBrewing- Brew a fermented spider eye over a potion of swiftness or fire resistance \nEffects- The users movement will be slowed to a crouching position for 1 minute and 30 seconds \n \nPotion of Slowness (Extended) \nBrewing- Brew glowstone dust over a potion of slowness \nEffects- Slow the user's movment to a crouching position for 4 minutes \n \nPotion of Weakness \nBrewing- Brew glowstone over a potion of weakness (extended) or brew a fermented spider eye over a potion of strength or regenteration \nEffects- All melee damage dealt by the user is halved for 1 minute and 30 seconds \n \nSplash Potion \nSplash potions are not tertiary potions although brewing them is much the same. Simple place any potion from the tertiary potion rank or secondary rank on the brewing stand and brew a gunpowder over it.  This will make the potion throughable as well as make the effects of it go to its target. \n \nConclusion \nThis being the last book of the \"Alchemy\" volumes you should now have clear but understanding of what alchemy truley is and the ways one can master it.", ""),
