        StaticBook("Alenom's Spell Book", "dood01", "Sending: /tell <player name>", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion and Rhisereld's Marriage", "Alectriciti", "Everyone of Aegis, \n Human, Elf, Dwarf, and Orc, \n You've all shared a part in our lives, \n So we want to share a part of ours with you. \n \n \n Alethion and Rhisereld are uniting as one in marriage! \n invite you to witness our vows to eachother, and celebrate this glorious and long-awaited day! \n \n \n OOC: Venue is Al'khazar Church \n Saturday, October 1st, 8 PM EST (GMT -5) \n We'd love for you to show up! Spread the word! \n ~Alethion and Rhisereld", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion and Rhisereld's Wedding!", "Alectriciti", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion Celebtaurë", "Alectriciti", "Alethion is a sexy beast. Enough said.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion OOC", "Alectriciti", "Hey whoever is reading this book! I'm talking OOC right now. This means I can talk about stuff like the internet, air-conditioning, automobiles, women, and other things that LotC severely lacks. :P Seriously. This server rocks. Whoever found this book is brilliant, and i present to you this random book of OOC nonsense. Well, first of all I just would like to thank everyone who played a part of Alethion's life. This goes especially to Rhisereld. Freaking incredible roleplayer- it nearly killed Alethion. Yeah, awesome job my friend! Despite the terrible madness and ruined life you gave Alethion, hope we can still be friends. Akorta, (AKA Angelus_Obscurus... AKA Luke) Best friend evar. We're always on skype. 14 hour long skype calls? That'd be Luke and I. This guy rocks! His character snuck up on Alethion wherever he went. Raick (aka Conster_monster) He's a really awesome and loyal friend to me, and Alethion. He's an incredible Oren Guard, in fact, maybe the best. He is very respectful, even when not quite sober. *thinks of who else*...... There are tons of more people trust me! Hah. I'd like to say this before I go on. This server, and everything that has happened on it has really been exciting. I'm writing this book as a checkpoint in Alethion's story. I don't know what to do with him at this point. But he's not dying. He's growing. I wont say anymore than that. I hope everyone who's been a part of his story stay in it. This goes to: (no particular order \n Rhisereld, Angelus_Obscurus, Conster_monster, Cowsgomooand, Hempshine, Juggernogg, sgtteddybear59. (I lied about the no particular order thing... :P ) This is only the beginning. I have a feeling it's about to get darker for Alethion... the hopeless romantic (nearly emo) elf. \n  \n Again! Kudos to you, whoever found this book. You decrypted that very... small riddle... Hah. Well, TTFN! :D \n (P.S. Pass this on to people mentioned in the book.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion's Bio", "Alectriciti", "Born in the Holy Princedom of Malinor, Alethion was raised by normal parents. He grew up with his brother, Reignor. One tragic day, on the outskirts of Malinor, their mother and father were both killed by an unknown group. A year later, by his rageful temper, Reignor hunted down the ones who he suspected of murdering his parents and violently murdered them. After he dug himself such a giant hole, he accused his little brother Alethion of the murders and Alethion was banished from the Princedom of Malinor.  Falsely accused, torn apart, and all alone, Alethion was to find his way through life. He learned from what happened to his parents and his brother and moved on. 5 Years later, he was allowed back to the Princedom. At that point, his brother went missing. Seeking a better life, Alethion strives to remove the core of the evil in Aegis: The Undead. For he is certain the undead is the reason his family fell apart... Now he has a companion, Akorta. A friendly wooden masked human. He has quite the story as well... But that's for another time. I have to go Soz!", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion's Secrets", "Alectriciti", "I'm recording this since my wedding day. I'm unbelievably happy that we're together now! I'm starting this book as a new chapter to my life. I will store all my feelings, my desires, and secrets here. Annora tried to read this, but thankfully nothing too important was written in it. Thank you Rhisereld for returning this book to me. You're so sweet. SECRET: Though it seems impossible at this time, my deepest desire is for Rhisereld to become an elf. We would share a long lasting life. For our lives to span out the same length would be like connecting two hearts as one. SECRET: Rhisereld is sexy. I just cannot help but write it down. Like, TOO sexy. I'm getting all excited thinking about her. SECRET: This is a secret place.  Muwhahaha. This is a secret book too, by the way. SECRET: Magic has grown most interesting to me. Ever since Rhisereld's taint by the undead, I've been studying it and how it works. I have only been able to harness one spell... and that did not go well. But it's still magic, and I was able to use it! SECRET: I found a tree that grows IRON. It was very far to the west, beyond the bridge that once lead to Haven. I brought Henry along with me, and we cut the whole thing down. We are now filthy rich. SECRET: I have betrayed Rhisereld. This curse will send me mad! I fear she may no longer wish to be with me. I hope it isn't so... I cannot live without her. I need to stay strong for the sake of our marriage. It's all Cataris' fault, and the fault of my lustful flesh for Persephone! I hope she forgive me in the end... SECRET: Rhisereld has left me. It's over. I tried to resist it, but failed, miserably. I wish I could undo what has been done to this family. My daughter, my son... this will scar them if things stay the way they are. I've crossed the line, and things got out of control. I have to fix this. I have to fix this. I have to fix this. I have to fix this. I      have      to       fix       this. I swear for the rest of my life, to continue to do the right thing. That statement goes to my death. SECRET: I am the luckiest elf in all of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethion's Vows", "Alectriciti", "Here we are, united at last. \n We've journeyed a long way from the past. \n Through the good times and the bad, \n staying true to eachother with all we had. \n \n \n My soul was in a prison, \n I was scared and full of fear. \n But after you were Rhisen, \n You took my heart and kept it near. \n \n \n I'm seeking her always, the beat of her heart. \n 'til death intervenes, we'll never depart. \n No more ignorance, no more strife. \n I'll hold you tight for the rest of my life. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Alethions little story", "Alectriciti", "Rhisereld? *holds blade down. But...", ""),
