        StaticBook("Alras Job", "Spartan216", "Im hoing to find a job in Alras hopefully i can be a guard such as an archer or knight If im lucky i can get to be the king's ranger i asked the viceroy if i can apply and he said yes hopefully ill be accepted into the army ....wish me luck", ""),
        StaticBook("Alras's Head of Diplomacy - Application", "Roze", "Greetings Gentlemen of the Alras Council, I Brayden Roze, Human Citizen of Alras, seek to join your council. So henceforth I will be submitting the following application. Within this application, I am applying for the position as the head of Alras's diplomacy section. I take it as a honour that you will allow me to apply for this position. I find myself capable to join this position, as I have already been able to setup a business alliance between the War Nation of Krugmar and our Kingdom of Alras. Furthermore I believe I am able to setup further alliances with other nations, business or strategic. Given my welcoming and persuasive personality I believe that I will fullfil this role with great professionalism. My history fits this role well, as I have traveled most of my life. Only until recent years have I looked to provide loyalty to a single kingdom. However saying that, I know many people within high places which will benefit our kingdom in allowing contact to the other legal bodies. If I was to be accepted my next move, excluding the Krugma/Alras Coalition, would be to seek a business alliance with the Kingdom of Kal'Urgaun. As for the fact that the Orcs will be allowing us to sell whichever we choose within a high populated area, we can seek ores, gems and smithery from those that live underground. I've heard from Warlord Morgroka that they seek a lot of iron and are happy to accept many other metals. Which we will be able to set the price for. So a conversation between the Grand Merchant and myself would be ideal. In summary, I give thanks to King Syrio and Viceroy Gordok, for allowing me the honor of applying for this role. I appreciate your time and look foward to your response. -Signed Brayden Roze.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alrin's Jornal", "macman1717", "Day 1- I had finnaly escaped and found a small path that seemed to be made by humans \n Day 2- The path i had found led to a small human town that was populated by people who seemed normal enough \n Day 5-I finnaly got away long enough to write in my jornal. These people have kept me under heavy watch, i dont think they trust me... \n Day 13- They threw me in jail just for saying one little remark to there so called \"hero\". I had used my lockpicking skills from the bandits to escape and run away from that awful town. \n Day 15- I have found a path that seems more trustworthy than the other one and seems to have more sandstone in it that a normal path would have. \n day 17- The path ended up leading the brutes called Orcs, i've decided to not go to them because of the stories that i heard from the thievs. \n Day 23- I've stumbled upon what appears to be a town with one of those \"Big Trees\". There's a castle there with what appears to be a ranger or druid leading it. I dicided that i'll aproach them tommorow to ask for a home and a job.  \n Day 24- I met with the one they call Houston. He gave me a home along with the job of loremast and alchemist. \n Day 54- I love my new life and I know i made the right choice by running from those bandits which feels like so long ago. I think that this will be my last entry and that i hope to live a long a happy life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aluinn", "Volutional", "T'is was the Year 84 , Ancient Druids have gathered, back when lands were low, and mountains high. The Druids however, were not of the Circle, these were Dark Elf Cave Druids. They crowded around a large container, constructed of logs and a pool of water. As the ritual they had been conjuring was almost over, the room had begun to shake, and crumble. However, the ritual had been entirely successful, and Aluinn emerged from the log prism. He, was trapped upon the rubble, unable to escape. Free from emotion though, he could wait, without being harmed mentally. So he slept, and slept. *You see a small note attached* Dear Reader, make sure this book finds it's way to the Druids, they must know about thi--", ""),
        StaticBook("Alvadas, the dark elf town of Malinor.", "shiftnative", "Alvadas has been protected by a powerful spell cast by the Malinor Elders. The Town has a dark elf Prince who was appointed by the Malinor council. The Caretaker, and Owner is Prince Loganos. This town is a private outpost, and you must speak to Loganos to live within his walls. Hail Take this, Loganos", ""),
