        StaticBook("Ancalime 1st Generation List", "theKYLAN", "Caney Ancalime. First Ancalime to bear the name. Status: Desceased, Cause: Slain in battle. Lea Ancalime, Wife of Caney, Born 1 son 2 daughters. Status: Desceased, Cause: Fire", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancestor Orcs", "TheImpulseHQ", "One part of Orc Worship is the Ancestor's, ancestor's are great orcs who died and their death caused such a distrubance in the afterlife that they were able to come back to life in a spiritual way \n The Ancestor's find it very difficult to interact with the physical world and therefore use mental \"magic\" to attack or get things done and this magic can sometimes get them distrusted by other races \n Ancestor's are not like the Undead, they cannot do anything physical to the world nor do they wish to, many are kind and only stay in the world to pass on their wisdom and knowledge \n In the event that an ancestor does try and attack and kill, it will usually be destroyed by shamans, who will send it back to the great beyond and destroy its ties with this world", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Civilizations", "DoctorTinman", "Everyone knows that Aegis has a strong history behind it, \n Such as many long-lost societies and civilizations. \n But, few know the greatest secret of all about them... \n They still EXIST. They've honed their minds and bodies. They are demigods. \n Some have the power to take away life, and are feared across Aegis. \n Others, however, GIVE life. These two groups balance the world. And you'll never see them. \n In fact, only the Wandering Wizard is known to have seen them in person. \n He is not one of these omnipotent beings, but is a very powerful link to the Aemon. \n No, the two remaining races of power are the Undead and the Ascended. The Undead are beings that commune with the dead, and live without life's necessities. And the Ascended are mystical beings, not alive themselves, but able to grant life to others. \n These two legions have been at war since the dawn of time. And if you ever should see one, do not run. It is impossible to defeat them or escape them. Just say hello. Or die.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elven Folklore Vol. I", "Cloudheart", "The Story of the Drow - (and Moonlamp Mountain) \n \nIn a land far far away, from the homes of the fair folk called Elves, there lives a race of people called the Drow. The Drow were Elves too, but they had strayed from the lovely forests to dark magics. The Drow preferred the shadows that matched the blackness of their magic, and they lived in the marshes, swamps, and spider-infested forests of Aegis. Few know of this land anymore, and even fewer still know its name. It is now only known as 'The Darklands'. \n \nThe Drow, however, disliked one thing about their home: they had no light to see by. The lightstones of the true Elves were lost to them. Thus, the Drow every so often would take the moon to use as a lamp, putting it away in a dark mountain, hidden in their muggy swamps. This is why they say if you ever lose track of the moon one night the Drow have stolen it. \n \nThey would only give the moon back on one condition: If someone cut down a tree from the Elven homeland and gave it to them. If you didn't do this? Oh Aegis forbid! The Drow would sneak into Malinor - in the blackness of night - to find the naughtiest, unruliest elf and...SNATCH HIM UP! The elf would then work for their army, to live in their horrible, spidery forests, forevermore. \n \nSo be good, all little Elven children, or one night the Drow might take a liking to you and you might never again see the beautiful trees of Laurelin. \n \n The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elven Magic", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "~~~Tier1~~~  \n \n Nature's Touch \n Malin's Wall \n People of the Tree \n \n ~~~Tier 2~~~ \n \n Nature's Grasp \n Malin's Box \n Power of the Forest \n \n ~~~Tier 3~~~ \n \n Nature's Vigour \n Malin's Trap \n Power of Malinor \n \n ~~~Tier 4~~~ \n \n Healing Touch of Malin \n Power of the Trees \n The Power of Aegis \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elven Magic Part 2 (Definitions)", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Nature's Touch: Cure the target of minor wounds \n Malin's Wall: A wall of branches and leaves is summoned by your magic \n People of the Tree: You have used magic to give life to the plant before you \n \n Nature's Grasp: Cure cuts and bruises \n Malin's Box: You summon entangling leaves to trap your opponent \n Power of the Forest: Use your magic to give life to the area around you \n \n Nature's Vigour: Heals opened wounds, and sprains \n Malin's Trap: Entangling branches and cobwebs trap your opponent \n Power of Malinor: A large area has been given life \n \n \n The Healing Touch of Malin: Heals broken bones, and repairs dead or missing skin \n Power of the Trees: Branches and cobwebs trap your opponent, and a large wall of cactus appears. \n The Power of Aegis: You channel your magical power to give life to a forest around you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient History", "Bal0rCIM1", ". A scant few Aenguls chose to stay and live amongst the other races of Aegis as mortals once Iblees h ad been banished. They had many descendants, but the knowledge of the Aenguls was lost to them over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient History o' Aegis", "Zombiebillybob", "Kur's Journal", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Inscripted Texts", "Xanivic", "\n Introduction \n - I came across a few strayed parchments that were resting upon the ground near Malinor. I attempted to read the texts, but I couldn't actually understand what the inscriptions meant. Arriving back at my home, as the erie clouds cried, the parchment had gotten wet and had torn. However, I was able to record some of these inscriptions within this book. \n Anonymous Inscripted Texts \n (_ |=, ,^, () ;|. || ./. )( (These are some sort of hieroglyphics that I have yet uncover.) (The next segment is a series of foreign language. One of these phrases has been shown in a book that goes by the name of The End Of Hope.)      Anonymous Language : \n Dick holes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Magic", "Benboboy", "Some say that there was a time when wizards ruled the world because of their powerful magic abilities. It is said that the most powerful of wizards could summon mountains to block their enemies, or even call upon Iblees to slay them. They were feared and loved by many, not even God would stand in their way. These days have long gone because of a time they call the great cataclysm. The wizards learned more powerful magic every day and soon began to challange each other. They would bring wars to the land destroying everything in their path. The world fell into chaos. It was not long before the world was completely destroyed. nothing left but ash. there may still be some of the magic scrolls left in the world, and are yet to be discovered. Maybe it is best to not find the scrolls, to avoid history repeating itself.     \n-Father Eynon", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Tongue of the Elves", "Jerry_Man", "My Friends, we know little of the Ancient Elves, and much remains riddles and ambiguous. To even hope to complete our knowledge of their language is laughable, preposterous. Progress, however little, I present to you in this tome. \n \nELVEN WORDS \nthis incomplete list is sorted in common alphabetical order. \name: forest\nayla: good\n bortu: dwarf\nento: next\nevareh: protect\nkae: me\nkarinah: sunrise (also day)\nker: dark, sunset (also night)\nleyu: graceful\nilir: friend\nlye: we\nmali: elf/elven\nnae: you\nnor: land\nomenta: meet\ntenna: until\nuruk: orc\nvalah: human\nVelulaei: moon -Named after the moon goddess. \n \n*This book is clearly incomplete*", ""),
        StaticBook("Anger", "Cookie9000", "I dont believe it... They kicked me out, kicked me out of the Nical guard! How could they? I was their best guard, the rest of them are lazy, intolerent slobs I was the only one who was good, yet they kick me out, as if I was a bag of dirt! I feel like killing the petty Commander Caleb as I write this, I WILL get my revenge... Perhaps by joining the Black cross... Indeed, I shall, I saw their hate for the pathetic Nical... Their hate even rivals mine... It even suprises me how much they hate them, but it isnt as much as my hate, my eyes feel like little fireballs and my heart feels like an Inferno, I infact think about joining them but I will give this petty Nical one more chance, if they \"Exile\" me one more time... I will join the Cross and watch the Nical's fear as I rip their commanders heart out....  - Alanor Hedgewell", ""),
        StaticBook("Angry Message", "Rokhazula", "fuck tae orcs!", ""),
        StaticBook("Angry message!", "Rokhazula", "Hell to tae orcs, filthy green skins!", ""),
        StaticBook("Anima Templi", "VeggieDelightful", "M'lord Enor. I address this letter to you in hopes of your approval of a new group, the Anima Templi. Meaning the \"Soul of the Temple\".  This is a group of religious crusaders, protecting I, the Church, and following the will of God. It will be lead by Grand Master Terrowin, but under my supervision and control. We will also offer aid to the defence of Oren, and all neighboring territories.  If you decide to approve this, we thank you deeply, but also ask for a grant of land. I thank you greatly.  Sincerely signed, Hogarth, High Priest of Oren. Done. ((hello))", ""),
