        StaticBook("Another random poem", "Alectriciti", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Anthology of the Races: A Foreward", "Sarge878", "Dearest Reader, \n \n My hope when you read this book is that you get a comprehensive Idea of  the four races that inhabit Aegis, along with the way their forms of government work, their laws, their way of life, their relationship with each other, and the things they bring to Aegis. I can only pray that my words speak to you, and that the information I have gathered will prove useful. \n My name is Nero Sable. I am a Cartographer, aspiring Author, and Information Broker. My way of life consists of always being on the road, experiencing new things, and meeting new people. In the following volumes of text, I will relay to you the information I have gathered in my trials, my experiences, and my adventures.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anthology of the Races: Volume I", "Sarge878", "Anthology of the Races: Volume I \n Written by: Nero Sable \n \n The Elves; a mystical race filled with a vast expanse of magic and lore. Nature lovers at heart, this race of tall, pointy-eared men and women live their lives in the forests, among the trees in Aegis. However, the Elves are an almost secretive people. Their luxuries are hidden deep within the trees. A wonderful and large amount of culture live within the gates of Laurelin, a beautiful city in the middle of the Princedom of Malinor, created by the High Prince Native. \n \n While the appearance of the Elves are no mystery to the other races, the inner workings are. Lead by a Council, the government within Laurelin rules with a fair and just fist. Laurelin boasts a massive amount of homes and apartments, whether they be on the ground or suspended in the air, built on platforms and within the great trees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anu's Notes", "aheath4", "- People of Interest: Delthor, Algor, 'Leftclick' & Delthane . - Delthor is paying algor and his men.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anu's scout report", "aheath4", "Undead being pushed back. But for every one that dies, more join Occasional assualting from both sides Allied forces outnumber the undead . Abmushes are common frosty fury doing most of fighting at the moment.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anu-El's Journal", "aheath4", "-Delthor has employed Bandits to attack people on the streets, and to raid the SA base. -Algor and his men are payed by Delthor (so i believe) - Th group have ties to the undead. -Delthor has gained rank back in the SA. They cannot be trusted", ""),
        StaticBook("Anyone out there who gets this book.Help.", "digdog7789", "Help me im royer i need help i have been captured.Please help me. Anyone please.Help Im going to die.I love all you.Bye life.Snowy fields.Mom dad,Freinds.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apollan", "firespirit44", "Name: Arhdruid Dragon Apollan\n Race: Elf \n Age/Gender: ?/Male\n Skills: Make trees grow \n Knows as the Dragon Druid for his fierce thirst of knowledge, and his protective nature. Good friend to the late John. Was voted as first official arhdruid. Created the druid code.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apollan's Search for the Ruins East of Laurelin", "Elite117", "My quest started when I happened upon a book in the Druid Grotto in Laurelin. I visited there often. I came upon a book writen by our loved High Prince, Native. It described, very vaguely I might add, strange structures east of the Capital. As you can imagine, I decided to investigate. I started my quest at the Laurelin Docks headed east. For the first part, I found mostly abondoned dwellings, two deserted commuities and one arena . The land east of Laurelin is mostly desert except for one strange place I found. It was a small grove of trees in the middle of the desert. In the grove was a small hut, built in the way of the elfs But sadly, it was locked with magic and I could not enter. Further on I found another seemingly abandoned city. It was different then the other commuities I had seen. It was larger then the others, and raised off the desert floor by stilts. It was undamaged but there were not signs to tell me whp lived there or even what it was call . Sadly, this is were my tale ends. For at that moment, the great God of Agis used the four winds of the world and blew all people of Aegis to the Cloud Temple. To this day no one know the reason for it. Maybe God did not want me to find the ruins. What ever the case, I will not be venturing out again for some time. There's knowledge to gain and things to do. New adventures to be had. Maybe you who read this will continue my search. And maybe, one day, we will finally find the Elven Ruins East of Laurelin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apollan's Search of the Ruins East of Laurelin", "Elite117", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Apollan's Task Results", "BKisKk", "help", ""),
        StaticBook("Apollans Great Challenge Results", "BKisKk", "Well I asked what I assumed to be a human named Will Forestin in the grand city of Al' Khazar. He proclaimed to not know much of the Druid Order but said that \"I know theyr'e some nature loving elves that control certain elements and stuff.\" I then asked him what he thought of us. He replied that from past experience and common knowledge he assumed us to be fairly pure. I then thanked him for his time and promptly left. - Dedicant Remus", ""),
        StaticBook("Apoloy", "Tyrellius", "", ""),
        StaticBook("APPLE!", "sirbubbley", "appleS", ""),
        StaticBook("application", "Themastermoo", "Name: Moo Age: 107 Position at AFF: Footman", ""),
        StaticBook("Application", "drumstick607", "I would like to join the guard Titus Obadiah", ""),
        StaticBook("Application Example", "jammer562", "My Skills: I am a great miner and I am very good at gathering. Why I want to work here: I would like to a of service to Chris Ford and the customers What I expect: I expect to be treated fairly and have respecful co-workers and customers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apprentice Journal", "Jon021", "Kamees, 5th of The Grand Harvest, 1339 \nI was told I was supposed to write a Journal yesterday, and this is that journal. Yesterday's lesson was moslty an introduction to what we'll be doing today and this week.. Today, we'll be taking a test on Aegis's History. I spent all night in the Guild 's library studying. I hope the questions won't involve any modern history, most of which isn't detailed in the library. \nI turned the enderpearls my master ordered me to gather today. He promptly took me to the library to read all the books. After many hours of reading, I completed that task. He then asked me what balance was as a final test. I gave him my answer, and he judged it good enough. He says I am worthy of being a mage, but I haven't been in the guild long enough to become one officially. I only need to finish this week's lessons, and I can become a mage. \nKamees, 26 of The Amber Cold, 1339 \nAhad, 1st of The Deep Cold, 1339 yesterday's test wasn't as hard as I thought. I only missed two questions, and they were on Oren. I don't know Oren's history too well, and the library had nothing on it . Today we went on a field trip up to Alk'hazar. We stopped in an inn and Ogland told us about it's history. A knight named Soljir came there and fought off a number of bandits, saving it. When we came to Alk'hazar, Ogland noticed the blight. He hadn't realized that the Undead cursed it. We went around the city to the Tomb of Krees. He apparently served as Overlord under Iblees. Iblees is said to have been in his temple . Only after the Arcane mage eradicated it of monsters was it safe. \nJoma, 13th of Malin's Welcome, 1339 \nToday's lesson was about alchemy. We brewed harmful potions, and Ambros had us drink them. I wonder about some of his teaching methods. He did have some netherwort, something I need to brew actual  potions . He ran out during the lesson, after some crazed zombie attacked. It appeared out of nowhere, and no amount of force behind my blade would harm it. I need more power to deal with such powerful beasts. Unfortunately, Ambros is being vague about when we'll learn magic. The power of potions won't work as well, due to the scarceness of netherwort, neccessary in everything. \nTolta, 17th of Sun's Smile, 1340 \nToday's lesson was about balance. Ogland had us discuss for a while. I maintained that the Undead were the cause, but no one else seemed to be able to identify that. Ogland had to leave, and we continued our debate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Approaching Death", "Areontrade", "Tolta, 17th of Malins Welcome, 1338 - I have been thinking of how the staff will help me approach the spirit of death. I guess I will see when I approach him. Kematian, the name stuck in my head during the times I spoke with Athaki, This curious being. Irba, 18th of Malins Welcome, 1338 - Today the be the day I approach Kematian while meditating. I hope I have chose the time to meet death well. When I enter the world of spirits Athaki, nods at me, as if he knows what I am doing. I approach the lizard-like creature with wings, and am startled. \"Hello Shaman,' He says 'I know why you have come.\" He knows what I have been wondering all this time? \"Blah me den!\" I blurt, This question has been bouncing in my head for a long time. \"Why rush?' he said in the same monotoned voice. 'We have until you choose you are done.\" \"Okee\" I said. \"Den blah me, why do me see lat?\" \"You see the the way you do, Because I am a sign.\" Said the spirit. \"I am in the form of a 'dragon' Called many other things.\" \"I appear to you like this as a warning.\" \"I will come to all corners of aegis, many will not escape my grasp.\" Said the death spirit. \"Da undead?\" I asked. \"You will see in time young one, you will see...\" Said the spirit.... As I fade back into the normal world I hear a human come into my shop. He was looking for supplies, obviously a survivor from Al'Kahzar, It made me think. Will this happen to krugmar?", ""),
        StaticBook("Arana Hating on the Wardens", "Amethain", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Arbelas's Diary", "Arteh", "I have reasons to believe that Iblees is taking his toll over my soul and body.. I have the urge to kill and the urge to... to eat hu.. Humans I think that they become a part of me forever after i eat them. Day 2 - Today i built a Netherportal in my basement.. I can now speak to Iblees freely. I also plan on building a shire on iblees on the roof.. Hopefully that will give the right message to all thease ignorant people they will feel my wrath. Today i ate my first man.. he was Delicious so fuffiling but i believe my fantasies are taking over me I.. iam cold.. and afraid. I hear some guards yelling my name outside. I wonder what its for i ..........", ""),
        StaticBook("Arbrek", "zac20169", "Unlike many of Aegis's denizens, Arbrek led a realitivly peaceful life for most of his life, and even then, it was not by the hands of Orcs... Arbrek was born into the great and powerful Starbreaker Clan, descended from the great Warrior-Smith, and Dragon, Gotrek Starbreaker. By the time Arbrek was born, part of the Starbreakers had split, and formed the Silverhand Clan led b y Arbrek's uncle, Haggar Silverfinger, while the Starbreaker's where led by Arbrek's father, Skalf Starbreaker, in the citadel of Karak Rikkaz. One day, soon after Arbrek was born, Haggar wished for a son. Arbrek", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Journal I", "Slayer15855", "Arcane Journal \n Journey to the node \n \n \n \n Written by the Arcane Mage \n It is time for me to leave now... I am not sure whether I should, I still debate the decision in my head but I can feel it is right. It is right, I must do this. I can see the dark times ahead for the people of Aegis, where all they hold dear, all they have built, with their sweat and blood, will come crumbling down around them. The nations fractured at present time if they approach the end divided then what I set out to do now will be for naught. There is no future in division. But united, I see the people of Aegis stand a change, albeit a very slim one. I hope they com The nations lie . I can see the dark times ahead for the people of Aegis, where all they hold dear, all they all they have built, with their sweat and blood, will come crumbling down around them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Power: Curses.  by Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "In all the types of magic spells in Aegis, none are more feared than curses. Curses are the spells cast to specifically inflict injury, mental or physical, or to kill. The curses are not known by many magic wielders not because of their ethical issues but also they are very difficult for mages who are not consumed by darkness to cast. \n To be truly a master of curses, one must NEED to inflict the harm on its victim. Not just to want. This is why many magic wielders of the darkness have such ease.  They see a need to inflict harm.  While mages not of the darkness find this difficult. \n At best a curse is used only in defense for ones life.  If attempted at other times the mage will find himself with an underpowered spell. \n Be weary and wise if you are to ever cast a curse on another living thing. alas \n Remember, You must channel absolute hatred and anger towards your target. Practice bringing forth the anger.  Then soon your curses will be most effective. Evan", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Power: Immobilize Spells. By Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "One of the most useful types of defense spells are immobilization spells. Such spells rather stun or disarm opponents rather than killing them. While some may scoff that these spells are not powerful, many stunning spells can inflict seriou harm. \n Some druidic magics can trap foes in thorned vines causing immense pain. While simple stuns just feel like a horse kicked you in the chest. \n The wise wizard would use these spells to his advantage in situations where curses are not the best option Close quarters situations these spells work great.  Also immobilization spells are great when trying to flee combat. It helps to aim these spells at the extremities of the victim.  The legs are a favorite target. \n All in all. Immobilization spells are in some way even more powerful than curses.  Allowing room to escape or simply subdue a foe. -Nitholiak VonSchlichten", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Power: Protective Charms. By Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "Magic comes in many forms and types.  Many seems to overlook the usefullness of protective charm s in their everyday lives. From charms that deflect dark energy to simple locking charms, they effect most citizens of Aegis. \n Protective charms can be split into two categories: Spell and Runic. \n Runic charms are used for to protect doors, chests and other property from theft or destructi n. Only those experienced enough in rune enchanting can master this ability. But for those who do possess it, it makes for a very profitable source of magical revenue. \n Protective Spells are different from the runic charms. Protective spells can protect vast areas from disturbance.  Most cities in Aegis have powerful protective spells cast over them. This means nobody can destroy parts of the cities.  The only exception is dark magic. Protective spells can also be cast on a much smaller scale. Forming shields against arrows. Or just supplementing your own armor. \n Both types of Protective Charms require much study and practice. Do not get discouraged if you fail repeatedly.  Practice must be done for months.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arch Druid position: Jameson's Diary", "123trevmo321", "So latly ive been thinking alot about who is fit to be the next Arch. In my honest opinion i think i am suitable. Im not just shooting my own cannon or anything. I mean i am alwways around trying...doing my best to make sure everything is is order. Everyone is doing ok..helping. It seems Darrian and I are the only 2 left to be Arch. He is also a very knowledgable druid. If he were to get the position, i would respect that in every way. But if i were to be Arch, i swear i would do my very best to lead and teach and ..ya knwo just do my best. To whoever is reading this, i hope you understand. ~Jameson", ""),
        StaticBook("Arch Druid position: Jamesons Diary", "123trevmo321", "In my honest opinion I feel i am fir to be the next Arch Druid. Not just fireing my own cannon either. I am constantly trying to keep things in order around the Grove. But my opinion does not matter. For it lies to the decision of Valas and Makia. I hope one of them has seen the progress ive made in my time with the Druids. Darrian is most likey going to be taking the position... If he is chosen i will not go against that choice. I will respect it. But if I am chosen, I can assure i wont let anyone down. These are just my thoughs on the situation. And to whoever reads this i wish they would understand. ~Jameson", ""),
        StaticBook("Arch Mage Bell's Response to the reports of Cataris' trial", "TehLulu", "Cataris was put on trial for breaking our laws and my direct orders. He did NOT uphold the \"balance\" by attacking the undead. He put all of the Mage's Guild at risk by doing so. Everyone who participated in the attack, which he claimed to me personally he did not \"lead,\" (thoug h I have read differently in the Aegis Times newspaper) was nearly killed by the Prophet, including the Wizard. He has gained us an enemy. The undead want revenge on the Guild now. They will come after me first, as one of the Arch Mages. I will likely be tortured more, as they have been doing recently, whenever I dare to venture up nort h to guard it. I may even be killed. Magic has not yet returned to us; the Veil which exists between this world and the one which magic seeps through from is not yet weak enough. The Veil is the reason why undead magic is so strong and Ascended magic seemingly less potent. I will write more on the subject, but to put it bluntly, the undead are closest to Iblees. He is imp risoned on the other side of the Veil, where the powers of magic wait. He has given his servants, the undead, a more direct connection to the other side of the Veil than A scended or the rest of the world. That is why the Mage's Guild does not yet have magic yet...but we can feel it coming. \n Cataris, in attacking the undead base, broke our rules and my direct orders as Arch Mage. He betrayed my trust in doing so, but he was given simply a warning and sent on his way. But other evidence has appeared which shows our problems inside the Guild are not yet done. We will be working quietly to fix these. And we will be attempting not to make the undead irritated at us by attacking them for a very good r eason... Should the guild fall before magic returns, we will not be as well equipped. Magic will not be as us eful to all of us as a whole, and our tomes upon tomes of knowledge will be destroyed, or used again st us. That is why we put Cataris on trial for his actions. I sincerely hope you understand and do not give in to all the propaganda circulating at the moment. The Guild stands for the long-term defense of Aegis. If we fall even before magic returns, we will b e of no use. But we will continue defending and working on collecting knowledge to better prepare Ae gis for the return of magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Archers", "RossssM", "Sergeant_Archer_Felix ( RossssM ) \n Oren_Archer_Tom (tomsim9611) \n Oren_Archer_Boiendl (DanielDJD)", ""),
        StaticBook("Archers Journal", "Corpean", "Today Ahad, 22nd of The Second Seed, 1330 I Nicolas Treyarc, AKA Archer am going scouting on the Orcs. I belive I have been spotted, finding another position to scout form. Splipped by the armed guards at the entence, on the wall now. Leaving the Orc Capitol, very savage there. ((File ban report on h8pvmnt A pigmen attacked me in the crurch, their always near the church.... Undead near the local village, having Raymond come as backup. Hopefully all things go well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Architects and Buildings in Ageis", "Sykora87", "In this Book I will go over the Architecture of the races, towns, And some good Architects. \n Elves \n Laurelin", ""),
        StaticBook("Architectural Assistants Book", "DefunctDivine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Archive & Recordings", "Xanivic", "*Edit - Archives & Recordings.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Archives & Records * Vol. 2", "Xanivic", "\n - Kamees, 17th - 18th of The Deep Cold, 1324. \n o Yet another grim scene in Oren. The portal to the Nether, the domain of the Undead, remains in the main square. For 3 days, relentless waves of Undead - Giants, Ghasts Pigmen, Zombies, Skeletons. \n o This is unbelievable... King Perea emerged from the wretched portal... \n o The people of Aegis, including myself, are standing in the crowd, listening to Parea's s peech. \n o After being away for some time, I discovered that the portal has been destroyed. \n I asked a local man here, threw a few question towards him, but he wasn't aware of how the portal had been destroyed. He assumed the Undead withdrawed it. \n I do not know of the date, but it is 1326. \n o I traveled.. far into the north and ecountered MANY unprotected cities/towns. \n o In my Thieving Logs & Locations I have noted the coordinates and such. \n o I have found a copious amount of valuables, and I am going to return to commit even more theft within these locations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcitecture for Dummies", "TheNander", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Aren Whitestorm's Journal", "Tyber1231", "Itnan, 23rd of The Deep cold, 1331 What is the point of life? Why do I exist? My life is pointless, I did nothing good, I'm just a blindfolded man in the darkness. I am not useful, wise, or lovely in any way. My heart is rock, and I feel pain trying to open it. No hope for me. Irba, 25th of the Deep Cold. Why, Just why? Why do I have to be lonely? Why do I have to bear that pain? I cannot find the answer.  Where is the answer?", ""),
        StaticBook("Aren_is_Awesome", "james2k", "Aren is awesome. THE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("Argos", "ggt3416", "On my first encounter with Argos, he didn't make too shabby of an impression. He was on a quest to profess his love to Arya. As I stood under that window with my ear to the wall, I was thinking, \"Seems like a gentleman, but he'll have to be unique if he wants to snag himself a lady.\" After    having spent much more time with Argos than I probably should have, I discovered that he he posseses good and bad qualities, and is quite a character. \n Argos is ultimately, a good-hearted, honorable dwarf who has his silly moments. Just don't be female around him when he is intoxicated.  Don't be around him at all when he's had a few drinks, actually. Ale makes him a bit insane. Despite his sometimes flawed judgement, Argos does admittedly make a worthy companion. He would stay loyal and caring to the very end. Argos intends, most of the time, to help others. As for his sense of humor... well, it's better than tree bark.  All joking aside, I am glad I met Argos. I can't imagine a better dwarfy friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aricans auto-biography", "ariczzz1892", "Test haha", ""),
        StaticBook("Aricans Kal'Rog Store", "awesomerer", "arrow: selling: 60 buying; 20 bundle: 32 \n gold block: selling: 750 buying N/A \n iron helmet: selling 150 buying: N/A \n iron hoe: selling 50 buying: N/A  \n diamond: selling: N/A buying: 195 \n iron ingot: selling: N/A buying: 22 \n iron ore: selling: N/A buying: 20", ""),
        StaticBook("Aricans Note Book", "ariczzz1892", "Sillion sold me the journal of King Simppa", ""),
        StaticBook("Aricans sale and payment history", "ariczzz1892", "HoAV1: donated 1 to reformed church \none TsotNI1 Mayctor 100M \n1 creeper to druid respiren 100M \n2 SotN & 1 HoA1 to Serastus (Bastlzzz) 250M \nall we have to Heracles (DoctorTinman) 325M \n2 TSotN to Respiren 200M \n1 herb. guide to Heracles 75M", ""),
        StaticBook("Ark's End Tales", "Arkensald", "Day 1 - Queen Dawn stopped by, with an entourage. Stayed overnight, to keep away from the monsters. In thanks, she offered to give me some portraits. We travelled to Alkhazar, and she gave me three amazing portraits to hang in the refurbished resthouse. That makes it a Prince, a King and a Queen to visit me. Not to mention the Wizard himself. Day 2 - Holmes' entourage stopped by. I have a couple of new assistants, too though they're both still getting the hang of it. An old friend, and a new. I'm still unsure of what happened during the months I was gone. I don't remember", ""),
        StaticBook("Arminas's Jorunal", "MrCyberMonkey", ". I saw the first orc since my pa g", ""),
        StaticBook("Armor of steel", "ninjamana", "Once there was a fiery dragon that flew around devestating land. Wildhammer The Great was sent to kill the fiery beast but first he would have to get prepared. He went to far away lands to get armor from the dwarfs but when he got there he found out the dwarfs kingdom of Kal'Urgan was a fiery mess like the others. so Wildhammer new what he had to do, he would have to mine himself. After days of mining he finally had enough iron to make some armor. It was \"The Armor Of Steel\" . He ventured off to find the dragon after a week he arived there to find the beast. When the dragon used his fiery breath it would not cut through the mighty steel. So Wildhammer killed the beast on that day and saved aegis.  The end", ""),
        StaticBook("Armory log", "Harrfuzz", "may i have your name to log you in our records \n Mo_bananas: ! leather set and stone sword Eternis Luckmor, inittiate set \n Icarus 1 iron set\n Crazy jake iron set\n aaaa1188 1 iron set \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Armory logs", "Harrfuzz", "crazyjake  1 full Ironset \n durzio, kenji and casus 1 iron set \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Armour", "theo13", "Leather Head: 20 m, Chest: 35 m, Pants: 30 m, Feet: 15 m, Fullset: 90 m \nChain Head: 15 m, Chest: 30 m, Pants: 25 m, Feet: 10 m, Fullset: 75 m \nIron Head: 125 m, Chest: 220 m, Pants: 190 m, Feet: 100 m, Fullset: 590 m \nDiamond Head: 1150 m, Chest: 1960 m, Pants: 1690 m, Feet: 980 m, Fullset: 5500 m", ""),
        StaticBook("Armour And Weapons", "machinegunliam", "Leather Cap-13 Leather Tunic-25 Leather Pants-23  Leather Boots-12 Chain Helmet-15 Chain Chestplate-35 Chain Legs-30 Chain Boots-13 Stone Sword 3 Bow-7", ""),
        StaticBook("Arnh Junns", "AutarchCosmos", "Name: Arnh Junns ((a98x))\n Age: 22\n He can FARM at an advanced level.\n He can't MINE.\n He can't FIGHT.\n He can read and write.\n Note: Very friendly and open. \nNote: Trustworthy.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Arnh's Exploration Journal", "a98x", "My goal is simple: to set up colonies of a single production focus.  This will enable \"mass production\" and wholesale. 34 of Malin's Welcome, 1328: I have so far one partner, Lord_Lykos_Daekon. We explored north some ways, but found nothing but random forts of stone. The snow was nice, however.  Soon I plan to head west out of Dunwood, which seems to be fairly empty.  I hope to set up one experimental colony first, and gather buyers of supplies. 3rd of The Grand Harvest, 1329: What better way to start the new year than with some exploring?  I have done some preemptive exploration on my own.  The west seems to be a better direction to go.  I am close! 5th of Suns Smile, 1329: It seems south past Laurelin is a good direction. I will have to inform my partner, and ask his advice.  I believe I would prefer west, because it is close to home and Al'Khazar. Further investigation shows that any direction out of Dunwood is good. 21st of The Deep Cold, 1329: I am almost at the crossroads heading north of Dunwood.  That is where the colony will be.  I have not been able to contact Lykos.  I can manage without him.  Once the settlement is built, I will hire. After the first shipment I will distribute payments to them. EDIT: My drawings were accurate, and I have made it to the spot I found before.  It is far enough from everything and quite serene. 22nd of The Deep Cold, 1329:  The building of the colony is underway.  I have chosen to keep this spot.  A sign is placed for travellers to see.  For Mobeus! EDIT: The first house is now complete.  I will make a few more before hiring. UNKNOWN: I have lost track of the date, but the colony is complete.  There are 3 houses, a farm, storage room, and meeting hall.  I will now connect to the road to Lunavara, which it is near.  Then I will advertise it, in hopes of workers. I managed to contact Lykos, who said he would visit.  I have a good feeling. EDIT: The colony is now connected. Now I can begin hiring and producing wood.  The next task is to contact King Enor to try and get Oren rule and protection.  Mobeus shall flourish someday! 13th of The First Seed, 1331: Mobeus is doing well.  I am hiring and many have applied. I still need protection.  I have gotten threats from an unknown entity about killing anyone in Mobeus.  I wish to neutralize this threat, but not with force. My time away from my family's farm seems to be corrupting me.  I must prevent this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aronel Teilief, The dark elf who could.", "shiinchan", "I am Aronel Teilief, this is my book... i fight for good and destroy the wretched, but i have one problem, i have an addiction to archery. i like to shoot arrows at things.... or people once i shoot i cannot stop so if you come across me and i shoot an arrow at you do not take it as a threat, more as an obsession gone wrong  title Aronel, the dark elf who shoots", ""),
        StaticBook("Arrest and stupid people....", "Jr4life24", "Da shovel", ""),
        StaticBook("Arrith's App.", "Sirnecron77", "Name: Arrith Race: Orc Age: 28 Possition: Hunter", ""),
        StaticBook("Arron's suicide note", "battlezeke98965", "i have been thinking for a long time now... i have come to a desicion... by the time you are reading this ill be long dead... i know this is a harsh decision... but i haven't found love... my best friend is dead... so what's the point!? if you try to find my body you'll have no luck... i will kill my self by fire and crmation... i can't even spell right... so good bye cruel world... good bye forever...", ""),
        StaticBook("ArrowWood Drink List", "TheRedNinja", "Beers: \n Oren's Finest....15m \n Dwarven Stout...20m \n Kruggy Lite Ale...20m \n Stella Laurel...25m \n Elvish pale ale...25m \n Mixed Drinks: \n Kungaloosh...20m \n Grateful Pigzombie...20m \n White Russian...20m \n Bloody Iblees....20m \n Pink Diamond...20m \n Sandy beach...20m \n Queens Revenge...20m \n Hairy Elf...20m \n Sour Arial...20m \n Royal Flush...20m \n Golden Appletini...20m \n Shots 3 for 25m: \n Royal Crown Whiskey \n Arrowwoods pine whiskey \n Rose Garden \n Happy Creeper Rum \n Captain lorgo Dark rum \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Arrowwood Drinks Menu", "TheRedNinja", "Beers: \n Oren Light Ale \n Dwarven Stout \n Kruggy Lite Ale Oren's Finest \n Stella Laurel", ""),
        StaticBook("Art of Swords", "durzio", "The Blade. An innovation that was probably made entirely by accident,yet is the symbol of Close Range Warfare. In order to master The Sword, you must have discipline, strength, stamina, and a clear mind. it is recommended to meditate at least twice a day", ""),
        StaticBook("Art Of The Sword", "silco97", "Note That this is all written in OOC \nThe Sword is a usefull tool as it has many more uses then killing your average human.  They can destroy certain material much faster then any other tool could such as webs, wool, and soulsand. This book will explain how to effectively use a sword to its max potential. \nChapter 1 The Durability- Each sowrd made of certain material has a diffrent amount of hits it can take before breaking. \nWood- 60 hits \nStone- 132 hits \nIron- 251 hits \nGold- 33 hits \nDiamond- 1562 hits \nChapter 2 The Damage- Each sword also has a certain amount of damage it inflicts on its target usually increasing depening on the rarety of the material. \nWood- 2 and a half \nStone- 3 and a half \nIron- 4 and half \nGold- 2 and half \nDiamond- 5 and a half \nThe formula to find out how much damage the sword will inflict in its life time is DurabilityxDamage Per Hit \nChapter 3 Combat-The Sword is a short range weapon, there for it is good agents long range weapons due to the fact if you stay close to the enemy it will be harder for them to hit you. The best way to deal with a stronger enemy is circle them and when you are behind them strike then continue circiling until they attempt to run. Some people prefer a bow over a sword when infact the bow has many downfalls, one it needs ammo, two it does far less damage then a sword. In my best stratagy the best way to deal with an enemy is run then turn around and strike once then continue until they give up or die.", ""),
        StaticBook("Artemis", "nickdabeast135", "kjdf", ""),
        StaticBook("Artemus", "nickdabeast135", "Originally, Artemus wanted to live a simple life, a life of farming and mining, he wanted to end up in a nice house with a family. But one day, that all changed. Artemus was robbed by orcs... attacked by undead, even betrayed by dw dwarfs! He decided he would try and put an end to it by enlisting in the KalUrgaun legion and help bring order to the land. He proved himself loyal, and was eventually promoted to an ironbreaker. He fought many battles, and was looked upon as a hero.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arthane's Northern Journal V2", "aaaa1188", "Day 0: Here I sit once more in my meditation chamber, under my hut in HQ preparing myself for another journey towards the undead . I have a few contacts I must meet with before setting out, as they may have the information that keeps me alive in this venture. \nSide Note to self: Oren Strategist Romanen is not right in the head, and insists on attempting to convince others that I am to blame for the execution of many rebels. Besides stating that I was in fact, not behind these events, I have only one thig to say: It is rather unfortunate he was not among those executed...", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_4(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Arthane's northern Log", "aaaa1188", "Day 1: I left Al'Khazar today, and followed the road through the woods and into snowyfields , where I investigated the Obsidian spire that now stands in place o the keep. The town itself is completely destroyed, with only fragments of small buildings left. The obsidian spire itself is an imtimidating sight, but I was happy to learn that the Humans had gained control of the area,  and were questioning... something, something very hostile. The thing was adamant in it's resolve to stay silent, but I couldn't help but notice it's screams of agony as i left the town... For now I will set up camp near the town, but still within the concealment of the woods. \nDay 2: I've made my way across a frozen lake, stopping to examine a mass funeral ground... There were too many graves there, just too many. i only hope this curiousity of mine wil not put me among them. To anyone reading this, A small disclaimer: I do this for personal matters, any group i am affiliated with had nothing to do with this, it is my own will to venture out here. \nDay 3: I've made my way back to the Large wall of Obsidian i had to run from a week ago, Day ??: Hit in the leg by a skeleton, not that bad, bleeding has stopped. DaY: ??: I ThinK i found a way back, no tricks, just following the road. Day ??: Finally, I found my way back to SnowyFields, no sign of the humans, or their screaming prisoner. \nI'm finally back in Laurelin, but sustained heavy damage on my way here. I can still walk, however slowly, so i pln to return to the Wardens and perhaps find a way to patch myself up. I'm resting on the bridge now, two more skeletons have injured me further, i can still limp, however, so i plan to keep moving. Just... a bit... injured... I was... trying to learn more", ""),
        StaticBook("Arthane's Northern Log V2", "aaaa1188", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Arthur Dragonsbane background Information (liamhillikier14)", "coconuta", "Name: Arthur Dragonsbane \n Job: Unemployed \n Home: Looking to rent a place in Oasis, currently has no home", ""),
