        StaticBook("Attack on Celistine", "Acornlad", "In the late hours of tomorrow (October 9th) an attack will be launched upon the land of Celistine.    \nCelistine is a land tainted with evil and poisoned with the name of Iblees , It is a place where the undead are worshipped and praised. We have no choice but to destroy the city. There is no point in negotiating, for it will all be in vain. \nIf  wish to join this attack come to the town square of Al'Khazar at 2:00pm GMT We will discuss our plans and an prepare for war and we will launch the attack at 2:30 pm GMT \nThe Ascended will lead this attack along with their comrades. \nSpread the Word", ""),
        StaticBook("Attack on Celistine", "Garretty", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Attack on Shad'Rin's base", "firespirit44", "Itnan, 23rd of the First Seed, 1326 \n Tharl'Mar and his bruddah claims to be robbed by the people called the Shad'Rin. The leader is Miles. We assembled a strikeforce of about 20 people led by King Enor himself. We shouted at them, they did not respond. When we tried entering, they activated the trap. The Shrouded then attacked us from their fort besides us. The Shrouded and The Shad'Rin have declared themselves as hostile bandits, smashing any lies about neutrality. They wouded King Enor. They are formal enemies of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Attack Plan- Al'Khazar", "Acornlad", "This is an attack plan on the Human City of Al'Khazar. This plan includes the Orc Army and the Teutonic Order. The Teutonic Order consists of about 10-15 men and the Orc Army consists of about 10-15 men also. \nIn attacking Al'Khazar it is best to take a path where the fighting force will not be noticed, that is why the 2 fighting forces will be moving across 2 oceans to reach Al'Khazar, rather than taking King's Road, where the fighting force will be noticed and the Human Army will be notified. \nThe fighting forces will launch from the Sanhar docks where we will travel to the shores of New Terriko, this is a place where land will have to be crossed. We must move across this land quickly. When we reach the other shore, we launch on our boats again and travel to another section of land that divides the oceans. We will move across this land quickly. then launch from the other side of that land. From there we will travel to New Terra, a town just out side of Al'Khazar. If we are confronted by anyone in this town we must kill them quickly. \nFrom this point we will travel to Al'Khazar which is directly to the left of where we land. The walls of New Terra are easy to get onto and they are also connected to the walls of Al'Khazar. We can travel across these walls and reach Al'Khazar. There are 2 point of entry. 1 takes us to the Al'Khazar church and another takes us near the North Gate and onto the roofs. \nFrom this point the fighting forces will split into 2 groups. The Teutonic Order will take the path to the roofs and the north gate, the Orcs will travel to the church. The Teutonic Order will kill all those who are at the north gate and then begin moving across the roofs to the main Al'Khazar gate. The Orcs who will be at the churh will move from there to the main gate and kill all guards and people that are there. the Teutonic Order should reach the Orcs a bit after the attack on the main gate. By that time the humans throughout the rest of the city will probably be moving towards the main gate. The Teutonic Order will ambush these people from the roofs. After this, the Teutonic Order will move down from the roofs and take the path leading to the front of the Keep. The Orcs will take the path moving to the back of the Keep. The Teutonic Order will reach the keep first, where they will meet heavy resistance. The Teutonic Order will serve as a distraction, where the Orcs will come from behind the Keep and flank the humans attacking the Teutonic Order. \nAt this point most of the Human Army will be dead. Both parties will then move into the Keep, killing everyone inside and then claiming the Throne. Once the Keep is claimed, both forces will break into groups of 3 and then move throughout the city, killing the rest of the people that remain. \nThe Human City of Al'Khazar will now be Ours. \nEpilogue-Addressing the Fighting Forces \nThe Teutonic Order consists of Warriors and Archers. They are trained very well and have all weapons and materials needed to fight. The Orc fighting is very much alike, but is better suited for fighting with swords and axes. The Orcs are trained to the highest of standards, also all Orc warriors are well equipped and prepared for battle.", ""),
        StaticBook("attempt of murder", "Sir_Vilku", "Valikor's life was attempted to be taken by two men, who claimed to be part of serpents ridge. they were, yohman and mork. yohman is a dark elf, he wore dark suit and mask that day. mork, looked like most of the orcs. savage. he was clearly lacking intelligence as well. first, i had a peaceful discussion with them. i applied to help them with their buildings, until suddenly, mork slapped me. to this i reponded with modest offencive sarcasm. which then caused yohman, for no reason i know, to go rage at me with a sword. after he nearly killed me, i started to run away, which then, mork responded by shooting arrows at me, which i dodged to behind a building. after that, the chase was on. i then run into the forest, and sneaked away with my refined skills as elf.", ""),
        StaticBook("Attempted Murder at Grove", "Blackdragonhole", "Attacked: Darrian Name of Attacker: Justin Justin wanted a book untainted Never gave it to Darrian Darrian said that it is illegal to have that kind of object to Justin Justin finally gave him the book but Darrian never gave it back Justin wanted it back but Darrian kept it Justin said he will kill Darrian if he didnt return it Darrian ran when Justin pulled out his sword Justin had armor on and slowed him down having Darrian a chance to escape Story: End", ""),
        StaticBook("Attention Arrim", "ljcrzynfree19", "Arrim! ye' are chosen by th' Masters and Lords tu go on a quest. The quest, if completed will grant ye' a place of importance in th' kingdom. Ye'll also gain in riches and power. But ye' must prove yerself! If ye' accept, ye'll need tu follow a trail of lapis tu find a scroll which will instruct th' nature of this adventure! Only ye' are tu 'ave knowledge of this, or ye' shall forfit yer prize!   AYE OR NAY.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Attention, all Elves of Malinor.", "shiftnative", "Greetings, High Elves, Wood Elves and Dark Elves! - I write this to all of you today stating Building small townships for your subraces, is absolutely expected. Band together, defend your settlements. And make a living. With enough support An enchantment could be cast over your town, protecting it. I have hopes for them.. it seems they're some darkelves with ambition, different ambition", ""),
