        StaticBook("Bael's Journal", "DefunctDivine", "Entry 1, Da shadow Dwarf\n Never seen something like dis. Dwarf was cursed into a differen form. He become black skinned, and red eyed. He calls himself Highlander. Didn't know unde had powers to curse like that... 'Parrently, he was imprisoned, an orc he met while in prison had me vouche for him. He seemed suspicous of Uug. Keep note... End of entry. \n\n\n\n\n\n Entry 2, lex's journals  \n I headed over to lex's house, saw some strange graffitti on his walls... And his diary which contained information on the recent going ons, and a shadowy organization in laureli called the dark brotherhood. Lex is trustworthy, reminder: Ask him about this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bael's Will", "DefunctDivine", "I'm so sorry lex... I wish you the best of luck on your journies from here on out. You've been a great friend, and an even greater ally. Give Morgan my staff. \n -The Text from here on out is illegible, except \"Keep the rest, lex\"", ""),
        StaticBook("bakery notes", "daniel7121", "day 1 i am adding a wheat farm on my roof", ""),
        StaticBook("Balance, -by Sythra Duskwind", "Aerinyes", "Balance is a very important part of our everyday lives. Without it, one would stray from the path they set before themselves. In nature you have night and day, the moon and the sun. And of course the elements themselves; Fire and Water, Air and Earth. But there is other forms of balance that are also important. Life and death, love and hate, as well as darkness and light. Everyone understands that all death would be a terrible thing. But they don't understand the consquences of life being out of balance. Imagine if the entire world was covered in growth, it would choke out the very essence of the world. And then there would be no life. Only death and nothingness. Now take love and hate. One would think a world without hate and envy would be ideal. This couldn't be further from the truth. Without envy, one would not try to better themselves. They would stangnant and atrophy, leading again to nothingness or chaos. Of course hate in the extreme is also dangerous for obvious reasons. Darkness and light must also be kept in balance. The old saying is you cannot have light without darkness is very true. With too much light, one would judge others too harshly. Think of the overzealous knight who encounters a village that has a suspected undead presence. The knight might injure or even prosecute an innocent for thinking them tainted. Again having too much darkness in ones heart will also cause destruction. With so much wickedness, one would simply seek to cause harm, resulting in chaos and discord. To keep the balance is to look ahead to the future and improve oneself through enlightenment. To stay motivated, to keep on their path of success and higher learning so one may understand not only themselves, but the world around them. To change it and themselves for the better.", ""),
        StaticBook("Baldwins Writin's", "drangob", "'Ello, I am Baldwin Frostbeard. This is my book. I write on this paper to tell ye things that i want ta tell ye. So, les' get this book started.. We, tha Frostbeards, are from a place tha's called Jornheim. Its qu ite a distance away from 'ere. It was destroyed, tha's cause ... Uh.. My mind is failin' me.. Ah yes. There was fightin' I think it were the goldsterns, Yes. They rebelled There was war Jornheim was torn apart", ""),
        StaticBook("Balin's Journal", "luchian", "Kamees. 5th of The Grand Harvest \n \n I have finally finished my torture devices, And they are all operational. Personally my favorite is the one where you can both melt somone or drown somone. Now i am just working on finishing my study room, And also gathering books and knowledge. \n \n Itnan, 9th of The Grand Harvest, 1315 \n I have now Gotten more exemplares for my study room. I even got some books from the old prophet Rott. Also i got a few books on Necromancy and other stuff. \n \n  Kamees, 12th of The Grand Harvest \n There has been words that we will attack the Orc Capitol in a few days. Finally we can eradicate the foul greenskins! They will all die and join our armies as zombies.. Wont be that big of a diffrence if you ask   me. They fit the role perfect! Big, Dumb and green! They even got the foul smell! \n So many greenskins was killed that day, haha! So much blood was spilled even ascended blood! Me and William, The one i had the cermony with enforced a tower with obsidian and lava. So many of the fools was killed that day, The only bad thing about it was that the ascended spells was focused at it. They are weak against flesh, But they can really destroy buildings. And the water somhow reflected some of our spells like summoning and lightning. So William often hit the water and.. Hurt me and other undead. But we can all fail in spells! I did so to in the beggining, but its annoying to be have to deal with friendly fire. \n \n Tolta, 17th Suns Smile, 1315 I am thinking of writing a book on the ascended spells, And also how to easely kill them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ban Togther Against the Undead", "tyking919", "If all of Aegis bans togther under one Banner, We could do what no Sage has ever done. He have all fought togther but never under on banner. If we all unite under Aegis not just seperate races or guild or anything. We would be able to do something nobody has ever dreamed of doing. We would be able to finally put an end to the undead. I say no more fighting against our own people but only against the Undead. If you truely want a better tommorow, then We must Unite Under Aegis and fight for her. We have had way to many days for us being cowards and letting others fight for us. No its high time we made something of ourselves. We will bbe famous for what we did. If we focus on the Undead then we will not have to be afraid of them burning you, or them shooting you with lightning. If we Unite and finally take out the Undead then we can truely be free. Those who have died to the Undead will be revenged. We have a responsibility, no we have a right to do this. Unite and Fight for we are the only ones left to do it. If you agree, make copies and pass them on and send me a letter Adian Brod ((Tyking919)).", ""),
        StaticBook("Banana", "Alectriciti", "What is a banana? And how can I possibly get one? Questions like these keep me going. Now I will write a song about bananas. \n \n Oh banana, what are you? \n Are you pink, green, or blue? \n Are you something I can eat, \n Or something I put on my feat. \n Banana ship, banana tree, banana ocean and or sea! Bananas with hats, bananas in boxes. Bananas on mountains or sitting with foxes. \n Banana of death, banana of love. A banana shaped monkey, owl, or dove. \n Suddenly I grow hungry. This concludes my book of bananas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bandit", "impymut", "He tried to kidnap me. He had a partner named Sparrow. He didn't tell me his own name. Same one that hit me on the road, wanted revenge I assume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bandit Camp", "Darkdragon274", "Mission Category: Reaper, General Combat \n Group Size: 2-3 \n Location: Small castle just south-west of Galahar, and just north of the Knights of the North . It is no the top of a small hill. \n Objective: Eliminate the bandit threat and claim the work under the Spectres ((Place a sign on the road in front of the keep)) \n Notes: The keep has very good walls, and a trap within the gates. Use an Enderpearl to gain access. It is also to be noted that there are rarely more than three people inside at once , but you should do some scouting first. \n *The Final page is adorned with a red-inked Spectre Syombol*", ""),
