        StaticBook("Base ideas -Maximus", "froyo17", "So for this new base i was thinking that we have 9-10 differnt floors . I think the bottom 2-3 floors would be the prison, armoury and irterrigation chambers Then floors 4 and 5 would be farming and then 6 and mabey 7 would be a meeting hall/ gathering place floors 8 and 9 would be housing and storage for other members and then floor 10 would be the rooms for the 2 leaders... and mabey me the enterence would be on floor 6-7 (meeting hall) and thats all for now", ""),
        StaticBook("Base Needs", "Meman46", "Add regions to the bottom two guard houses. \nPrivate Mine. \nMake all regions no mob spawning \nStorage room. \nremove parents from lust", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Alchemy Mixtures", "silco97", "Chapter 1 \nOne might find that alchemy is far too difficult and complex.  This books will do its best to make alchemy as simple as possible for any and all begginers. \nChapter 2 \nA Restore Health Potion \nMix one mushroom of the druid tree and a white mushroom found in the wilds.  Mix these well in a bowl with a pestal and stir quickly until liquidation drink by the bowl full until scars or sickness passes. \nCure Posion \nThis is a simple alchemy potion to cure most poisons weather it be a spider bite or food posioning this should cure it. Mix red flower and lapiz in a small flask and drink.  The effect should not take place for about 30 minutes although it will be cured in the end. \nElven Potion \nThis is the best alchemy potion for all of you gardeners.  Simply take a human bone and cruch it in a bowl with a pestle.  Then apply to the ground and plants will spring up like a child to candy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking: An Elven Cook Book", "themuffinmasta", "Mushroom Stew: -Ingredients: Brown Mushroom and Red Mushroom. Make a bowl and put one mushroom on top of the other and put them on top of the bowl. Enjoy! \n Cake: -Ingredients: 3 Buckets of milk, 3 Wheat, 1 egg, 2 Sugar. Put the 3 milk on the top. under that put the egg between the 2 sugar. Put the 3 wheat across the bottom and you have yo ur cake!", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Gate Keeping Stratgies", "silco97", "To guard a gate is one of the most importent duties a soldier can have.  To protect the people of their city or town can be challenging though. In this book it will teach you some strategies for the gate. \nThe Bottle Neck-This one is probebly the most commen as it goes well with dealing with a large grouph of intruders.  What you must do is get the enemy to come through the gate then while thay are few in numbers in the front you can pick the enenmy off more easly. \nWhat to do when you see and Undead-The Guard duties most importent role is to keep out undead. The undead are dangerous and if let inside will install chaos to the town or city. So what you as a gate keeper must do is put yourself behind the gate.  This way the Undead can not hurt you. Also put yourself under something so they can not strike you with lightning.  Most importently do not engage the Undead wait for backup. \nWhat to do with a bandit-If the Intruder is a bandit of some sort ((Ask him if he has a villen application accepted)) If so do not hesitate to turn them away.  If they do not wait for backup to arrest the bandit. \nHow to handel an army force-If the city or town is being raided or invaded by an army you must heep all gates closed and wait for the rest of the guard to arrive.  At this point I suggest that you end men up to fire arrows down on the enemy to were them thins before advancing the enemy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Knownage of Monsters", "calvinnok", "Zombie \n-The power of Undead awaken the dead! These hungry creatures is the easiest to deal with \nThey often appear in a group \nSpiders \n-Seems like the spell of a wizard failed, mountated spiders are always around Aegis \nSkeletons \nRise of the Undead awaked the dead, they use arrows to attack far-distance enemis \nZombie Pigmen \nThese evil creatures were came from the Nether, Undead brought them to the Aegis, they are hard to deal with \nSlimes \nMythical creatures, not much information of them is given \nCreeper \nExtincted creatures, some rumors that a farmer spotted them in a forest", ""),
        StaticBook("Basics of the Undead", "XSilverWolfX", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Basics on the Undead", "XSilverWolfX", "The Undead are a cold and ruthless race. True some of them are nice mabey some of those kinds of undead are reading this. what is the one the undead worship again I know it starts with and I iblees? shoot lol! um ahh! ugh . replace And burning it", ""),
        StaticBook("Bastion's Diary", "Lastchance2099", "July 7th 2011. Working on the huge outside farm someone built... It's amazing! Now we won't have any food shortages! after I've finished that, I'll probably head over to \"The Fort\" and see if I can fix it up any. July 6th 2011. \n The farm is now complete, and we've actually built our own shop to raise money to purchase more land. Also, I cleared out the Fort and completely redid the floor with sandstone, to make a better base. Besides that, I turned the small pond beside our HQ into an actual fountain. it looks pretty good, and Our base is really coming together. Even More! At our shop, a man named Shadow requested cake, so I added a 'Cake of Truth' to my Bread of Justice. I was kinda kidding, but I guess Chief liked it cuz thats what its named :) I also removed the small original farm, and I think we'll make a Library, since books are getting pretty big. Did I mention that I had to give a triple interview the other day? If that doesn't show you how many new people we're getting... Besides all that, I have big news! Today I was promoted to Colonel!!!! :D I've been working hard, but I think Chief deserves half the credit, because I know that without an enjoyable leader I wouldn't have been so willing to put in effort. We get along pretty well, and his decisions so far, have been wise and surprising in a good way. Well I'm literally starving to death so until next time... July 8th 2011 I'm getting stressed I suppose. I was locked out of the farm and library... I did finish excavating the fort, and I even built the base for a few rooms. However, after that out of need I went in search of a nice tavern. However there didn't seem to be one open, and so sadly after roaming around for an hour and recieving only one bit of ale, I returned home more heavyhearted. and only a tad tipsy... What's more, the Vanguard has built an incredibly large castle in Kromoroe. I fear that if Holmes does not begin doing the same, we will end up sitting beneath their thrones... Did I mention my need of ale? \nJuly 9th 2011 It was just sitting on our HQ's front step... all it says is \n \"Kal'Bryst Coordinates\" and then the coordinates From what I\"ve gathered it is an incredibly long journey, but I am too interested to not try. I'll write more later, but for now I'm on my way! Well, It seems I have stumbled upon Kal'Bryst... However by luck as the coordinates were not very accurate. of course, now I wish to go to the coordinates it gave me, so I'm off! \n Day Four of my journey I am roughly half way to my destination, yet it has taken me four days. It has been a smooth journey so far, I've discovered a few riches that makes this quest worth it even if I arrive at nothing. I even stumbled into the Wizards town, what's it called winter...winter something As for right now, I'm standing near a cavern filled with surface lava. So powerful, and destructive... This is the first time I have set eyes upon lava, and I find it quite impressive... anyway, I'm burning daylight. I shall continue. I made it. As i suspected there was nothing... nothing on the surface. the coordinates led deep underground, however I am not such a skilled miner to reach it. instead I have left a beacon... I wrote the coordinates, and a message. If anyone else journeys to these coordinates, they will hopefully search for me as well. However I must make haste, night is falling and my food supply is low. I have returned. The journey was not as easy as before, starving I fought countless monsters. Many times I nearly fell off perilous mountains, or drowned in the furious sea. But all is well. I returned before I starved. Ready to serve the people again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bateman's Autobiography", "ZenithV", "My name is Patrick Bateman. I am twenty-seven years old. I live in Serpent Ridge on the West.  I bought  my home on Itnan 23rd of the Second Season, 1315. \nI believe in taking care of myself, in a balanced diet, in a rigorous exercise routine. If my face is a little puffy, I'll put on an ice pack while doing my stomach crunches. I can do a thousand now. \nThere is an idea of a Patrick Bateman, some kind of abstraction, but there is no real me , only an entity, something illusory, and though I can hide my cold gaze and you can  shake my hand and feel flesh gripping your and maybe you can even sense  our lifestyles are probably comparable: I simply am not there. \nSabet, 28th of The Second Season, 1315. I finally own my own home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battered Poetry Book", "DefunctDivine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle on Celestine", "firespirit44", "Queen Cassandra pleaded Hochmeister Gaius Marius of the Black Cross to help defend her land from A gaggle of man called the \"Free Company\". The attack force had at least 3 Ascended, at least 30 men from the IA, Oren Guards, ROTF, and a bunch of militia men. Hochmeister Gaius rounded all the Sarient, numbering not more than 10 men, and proceeded to the defense of Celestine. They camped at both sides of the road, waiting in patience for the attackers. However, they were found out, and they lied to the enemy and claimed to be helping them. Gaius and the Free Company gathered at Celestine's gates. But after the initial shower of arrows They retreated. Gaius took the chace and seperated his men from the rest. When the group was about to regroup to attack the gates, Gaius gave the order to kill. The attacked were took completely by surprised and were smashed. Defenders took the chacne and rushed out of the gates and kill the men in the front. No casualties were sustained. About 20 attackers perished. The battle was a complete victory. Everyone was treated to cake and ale afterwards in Celestine's Inn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle plains against the undead", "pugsy", "Dwarf Kingdom: As of now they have no battle plans against the undead hordes so my intel info rms me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle Plans", "SirPwnzalot700", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle Plans (Classified)", "colwin1", "This book is only to be seen by the most trustworthy and highest ranked members of Guardian. If they, as a group, choose to let another party see the contents of these plans, then so be it. If one is to die with these plans, it is crucial that they are recovered, no one else must lay eyes on them. Anyone who shares the content without an official vote shall be punished. As anyone could be a spy for the Undead.  \nStep One-Preperation: It is important to keep in mind that the Undead are very powerful indeed . So do not take anything of much value with you. Some food, and stone swords would be best. This is because stone swords are inexpensive, yet more efficient than wood. Leather armor is also a good idea, if you have any. Protection is always valuable. Some ladders should be brought (See step 3, the attack) as well. And for others, an axe, and a pickaxe. This will also be explained later. \nStep Two-The Road to Battle: We should start by travelling up the road to Oren, visting other cities along the way. This is so we can gather other adventurers to aid us in our battle. Our last stop will be in Oren. We should have an Oren guard aid us, so that we may legally open the gate to the snowy fields if no one else will. Along with the benefit of gate access, the presence of a professional guard will raise morale and convince far more people to aid us in our journey. Then, after we have entered the snowy fields, we should go to our base in the fields to make sure that everyone is clear on what they are to do. \nStep Three-Commencing the Battle: Once everyong knows what to do, a small party (3-5) should take ladders to lay on the enemy walls, while the rest of us travel by tunnel into the keep. Depending on how heavily guarded the tunnel is, we may need to dig and mine our own. This is why we need shovels and pickaxes. We need axes in case we need to gather wood to repair our base. We should bring wood with us anyways if that is the case. The Undead should be distracted enough by our small ladder party that we can easily slip in from behind, and devastate their ranks. Once the enemy notices that we are within their keep, we must get reinforcements to support the warriors that originally stormed the front. They will at this point, be too confused to react logically to our attack, and thus retreat, or die trying to figure out what's going on. This is referring to the Undead, keep in mind. \nStep Four-The Upkeep: Once the keep is ours, we should send two messengers (for saftey) to Oren to tell others of the news, and bring more people to support the keep, and make sure it is not retaken by the enemy. Anyone that comes to help should bring their own armor and weapons, as well as food, etc., for everyone else. Obviously there are going to be injured men who need medical attention. For that purpose, we need beds for them to sleep in, and food for them to eat. Once this whole ordeal is done, if it goes according to plan, the Undead keep will be ours, and the Snowy Fields will once more be safe from the terror of the Undead. :These plans are to be seen by officers of Guardian, and can be changed at any time. However, nothing MUST be changed unless a very fatal flaw is detected. \nWritten by Ardougnious ((colwin1)) \nLookover 1: We will not bring random people off the streets, instead, we will gather forces from S.A", ""),
        StaticBook("Battles of the North - By Crowley Falos", "XSilverWolfX", "Over the past few years the undead and humans have been fighting in the North. In the past few months both Snowy Fields and Alstion were destroyed by the undead. More recently however is that we have destroyed the undead's keep in the area. Leaving them on the defending side for a good time, allowing us more time to repair our cities and regroup. However once the undead are back they will be worse than ever some predict. Keep your houses locked and chest secure for that day may soon be here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bawapy's Journal", "Bawapy", "7/19/11 It is six days before Ademas's birthday. Conell and I are building a mansion as a surprise for when he gets home.  7/20/11  We did not work much today. I've nearly completed my room and Conell is working on Ademas's room.  7/21/11   I was not around today. I'm not sure what happened! Conell says we have been stolen from!  7/22/11   We have decided to store our belongings at Tend'el's Inn. We also found Ademas! He told us a story, as did Tend'el. Then we met an Orc. Ghilbre_Akai. Also, Ademas has given me a cactus from a desert far north! I love it!!! Ademas said he would start a journal... I may need to read his at some point. Sure would  answer questions.... We have decided to start making money to save up to 30,000 minas. We need it. We also found Leafwind! He is demolishing a house! A man named chinaboi415 visited the house. He left at morning after entering unallowed. He also calls himself Templar. 7/23/11 Templar was caught destroying part of our home, the princess took care of him. 7/24/11 Conell finished Ademas's room and I finished mine. We prepared for the party that we are having as soon as the day changes. 7/25/11 Ademas's party was a blast! Tend'el, Garret, Conell, Ademas, and I all had fun. Well until the war at Kal'Bryst started. All of us except Garret went and were slain. Conell was injured, but Leafwind healed him with a magic Ale. also, Ademas transformed again. .... or whatever it is. Tend'el and him had a mighty battle that began and ended by a strange storm. We eventually fended off the \"demon\" and Tend'el set up a ritual or something. Later that day, Laetri obtained a room in our home. Its nice to have someone else here. We also found yet another entrance to the mine below us, it seems to grow everyday. We are heading there now to get rid of some undead that are quite annoying. We have gotten luckier! Ademas has found and sold some gold and now he is off to sell a diamond that Conell got from a spider! 7/26/11 Nothing happened today. 7/27/11 I have gotten terrible news. Ademas has died. As I write these words I am preparing to go to where he fell and create a grave, leaving my most favored items... We are now standing at Ademas's body...  I've held in all sadness and will continue to do so for longer... We will make a grave for him soon. Conell, Tend'el, Seanwenz, Nel'Thok and I. Laetri is resting at the gates. Dear Ademas, I leave you with my journal. I have also left you with my first cactus and our first workbench. May you rest in peace...... WONDEFUL!!! ADEMAS IS ALIVE!!!! and Tend'el has turned darker and Conell suddenly got new clothes. We have also got a base for our \"organization\". Well that was today 7/28/11 We got our protection! For 20,000 less than we thought! We now own Wilder Farm. Before that though, Ademas's \"demon\" talked to me on that tower. He told me that he is actually Ademas's father that was cursed upon death. He also jumped and died saying he was realesed after giving me Ademas's Journal and his blade. He also mentioned someone named Kai'el.... I don't know of anyone named that... hm.... 7/28/11 I helped Bell chase down a scumbag today. We jailed him, but then he was set free and Bell had left. Then he did something to me... I think he pulled out and ate my soul and then spat it back to me, it was all black now. He also said one day the Void would claim me, I now curse this main, Wyvern. I have been turned into a Dark Elf. 7/30/11 Started today off with an undead attack, they are getting more frequent. This one happened on Elvindale and Kal'Urguan. They survived, but many died. After that Whispering Isle was attacked by eight hooded men, they left a terrible lava pillar after they were defeated. While there Conell, Ademas, and I met up with Bell, she mentioned starting a Dark Elf town in Darkwood Forest. I might live there, its not too far away. Ademas and I, and a few others, followed Bell to a camp, but the person we were looking for was not there. On our way back to Luarelin at Fort Krug, we were attacked by a crazy Shaman and defeted him. Then we went to Tend'el's Inn, now Loganos was with us, the future prince of the Dark Elf city. I don't like this guy, he is rude. He stayed in Tend'el's room and didn't even pay. *sigh* Tend'el should be the prince, not him, it is Tend'el's forest after all. We started construction on the town, unfortunantly Ademas got all of us drunk first, it was embarassing, Conell is still drunk....", ""),
        StaticBook("Bayde and Umbra Sullkyn", "AnonymousMonster", "Bayde Sullkyn \n Male \n Born To: \n Keziah Sullkyn \n and \n Ior Sullkyn \n On: \n Irba \n Year 1335 \n On the 14th Day \n Of The Second Seed \n Umbra Sullkyn\n Female\n Born To: \n Keziah Sullkyn\n and\n Ior Sullkyn\n On: \n Irba\n Year 1335\n On the 14th Day\n Of The Second Seed", ""),
        StaticBook("Bayron's food gathered", "Charlie22", "Sugarcane 417     Watermelon 1623  Wheat 1271", ""),
        StaticBook("bbbb", "CentralGuard", "bbbb \n bbbb bbbb", ""),
        StaticBook("BE WARNED", "pcgeek61995", "This house be haunted!!!! you Have been warned!!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Beauty", "mercury199", "Beauty can be found for some one the mountain side, in the clouds on high, in lakes below,   in the shout of a commander, or the wisper of a preist. Or even more in the grace of life or the glory of blood. There is beauty in the setting sun and the spoken word. In all things beauty may be found. But none compare to the beauty that mine eye does focus on. On raven locks and violet eyes, mine own do catch like fish by the anglers hook. And when these gem do gaze upon myself they sing a song that brings forth raptue from the earth itself. And a face to match that puts to shame the stars themself, and the moon above. A woman who commands the attention of all who glance upon her. She does set my heart a flutter when even a wisp of her essence I do come across.   For in her I see beauty greater than most desire feverishly to see in their dreams. Tis this woman I do love. \n Dedicated to the most beautiful one I know Skyler.", ""),
        StaticBook("Become a \"Regular\" Today! Only at the VonSchlichten Inn and Bar!", "InvincibleHawk", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Bedtime Storys", "jordy0208", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Beginnings of a Breakthrough", "Jerry_Man", "The excavation is coming along well. If we can get some more mining power to get through the harder rock we'll really be on to something. \nI snuck into the orc shaman tower near Sanjezel and found a library. There are books about orcs who have met with spirits and spoken to them. All kinds of spirits for all kinds of purposes. If one of these shamans still lives and is willing to help, they might be able to communicate with an ancient inhabitant of the semi-permanent camp. Their names are ((Carnivore91)) and ((c_h_r_i_s121)). Also ((_Player_2_)) seems to have contacted similar spirits to who we might find.", ""),
        StaticBook("Being a Druid Guide", "ElynxYon", "A guide's job is to send the dedicant out on tasks to get them in touch with nature. Also, answer any questions they have along the way. \nList of Tasks Tatks allow the dedicant to become both resourceful and wiser, as well as attuned with nature To ensure that a dedicant is true to the cause of becoming a druid, a guide needs to send them on a trial that makes them gather something in nature. then from there, they may be sent out on their regular tasks, such as making a staff  as well as planting a smal forest and even brewing.", ""),
        StaticBook("being a gatekeeper", "JackWack", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Beings of the Old Times :Daemons", "boodilly", "Daemons. These beings have been the subjects of legends and lore for ages. Servants of God, these beings are incarnations of fire. Their main duty is as instruments of change. They appear in the form of fire or lava to a special person. Some choose to try to reform evil with a stirring proficy, While others gift pure mortals with holy tasks. They rarely take the form of a mortal, and are smiths and warriors when theydo. They used to walk more freely, before Ibees corrupted their fire and made it painful. Before this tragity, Daemons walked the earth gifting mortals with fire for cokking and smelt ing. *There is a blank page after this*", ""),
        StaticBook("Belin's Will", "skinner452", "I have lived in Aegis for many years now, and if you are reading this I have probably been killed or died by a fall or a tragic accident. If you killed me, then ye best find me in the temple and give me back my stuff or you will be cursed by the Gods of Aegis. \n-Belin", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Final Journal", "TehLulu", "I have not been as diligent with keeping writings as I once was. This is disappointing on my part, but...circumstances prevented it. What is there to say now, really? I have given up. I have been...captured, tortured by the undead many times now. I have removed the spells which cause the Monks to retrieve my body with ease, even within such a tainted place as the Undead Keep. Why they...he...wants me to join him, so badly, I do not know. Nor do I care to know. \n But, before I go into that, I should clarify what I have been doing. The Arcane Mage graciously offered me a position as an Arch Mage a few years ago. I was happy then. I was expecting to be able to find a way to save Aegis, to protect it... I failed, obviously. But I am sure now, more than ever, that the disturbance in the Balance has been caused not by a fail ure on the part of any of the Four Races, but on the failure of those this \"test\" was administered t o. I believe more than ever that this all was a test for the children of the Aenguls. A test which they failed. The Undead were never meant to have the massive effect on the world that they have. The Veil is falling apart. With it, Iblees is gaining more power. Yet, ironically, the further weakening of the Veil is the only thing which could grant us the use of magic! How the world laughs at us. The Veil must be sealed. This has gone on long enough. Magic is not worth the insanity that the unde ad bring, the chaos and destruction and pain. \n But I have not the power to do so. I have been fighting the undead in my own way. Defending the places they attack... And turning their own followers against them. Latsi, I truly hope you are happy. I...truly hope you do not allow them to get to you, either physic ally or mentally. Do not fall, my would-be apprentice. I realize you will likely never read this. If worst comes to worst, I will have to either end my own life...or have someone end it for me. I will not allow myself to be turned. And this book will likely rot on the shelves of the Library...which is fine by me. There is no need for the world to read words from a traitor like myself, who...has many times nearly given in to the temptation, just to make the pain stop. Latsi at least must stay a bastion of truth. An example of what you can become... Though it would have been better if he had not joined the Ascended, though if he stayed with me he s urely would be being tortured also. Regardless, it would be selfish of me to try and attempt to change his mind. He is free. Let him do as he pleases. And I...am free for the time being, as well. Hence I write this missive quickly lest they find me again. \n Unfortunately a side effect of the....things that have been happening to me is the return of numerou s memories. Some from long ago, long forgotten...these hurt the  I care not to get into them, but I...I ca nnot believe I forgot them in the first place. All of them hurt, really. I recall meeting the first Prophet. I recall the offer he gave me, the things...that happened then. How I almost fell to my temptations. The current Prophet simply loves brining those memories up, the ruddy... I believe he was upset when he lost me the first time. The fact that I rose back to fight against him again made it  worse. That, and the fact that I turned Latsi against them angered them as well. I failed at changing Kevin, though at first I thought I suceeded. I failed at convincing Algor otherwise. In truth, my failures outweight my successes. And the betrayals that I have faced have made me bitter, angry, paranoid. They belittle the trust I place in people and the friendships that I keep. I fear death....but I fear rising from it more. If I can survive this trial...I will write again. More frequently than I have been. If I do not...I apologize in advance. If I somehow falter and become tainted, please. Please kill me. Do not let me hurt my compatriots, my friends, the people that I hold dear. Killing me would be the greatest favor one could grant me. I need to finish this now. I do not want to lure them back to the Mage's Tower in their hunt for me. I...there isn't much to say. The Ascended and the Undead were put on this earth as a test, a test which was failed. The Veil needs to be strengthened, not weakened, even if it costs us magic. That...is all there is to say. \n Stay strong in the face of these circumstances. \n Signed, \n The Arch Mage, Lady *a longer name is written here, then scratched out beyond recognition* Bell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Journal", "Riznam", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Secret Book", "Riznam", "I have made a pact with the Undead Overlord_Freyj. The overlord promised my a new life, reborn in the dark arts . I can not belive everyone has such trust in me as i spy on their cities. I have no desire to be mortal anymore. I soon talked king Charles into joining my cause. He belives with his protection i can complete my missions to the fullest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Belyn And The Alras Captain", "Minst46", "The Captain is working with Belyn, Apparently some sort of love or family. Zoe mentioned, Belyn wants only to help Alras. Apparently cannot. Belyn may be mind-controlling the Captain, then again may just be Love. Belyn wishes to join the guard. Will not turn them in. If i give this to you, Captain, Understand i will do nothing. Do with this book as you wish, But i will not Do to you as many have done to families and lovers. This is the only copy, there will be no more. I understand what you feel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Beowulf", "ABoyNamedSue", "Prelude Of The Founder of The Danish House \n LO, praise the prowess of people-kings of spear-armed Danes, in days long sped, we have heard , and what honor the athelings won! oFt Scyld the Scefing from squadroned foes, from many a tribe , the mead-bench tore, awing the earls. Since erst he lay friendless, a foundling, fate repaid him: for he waxed under welkin, in wealth he throve, till before him the folk, both far and near, who house by the whale-path, heard his mandate, gave him gifts: a good king he! To him an heir was afterward born, a son in his halls, whom heaven sent to favor the folk, feeling their woe that erst they had lacked an earl for leader so long a while; the Lord endowed him, the Wielder of Wonder, with world's renown. Famed was this Beowulf far flew the boast of him, son of Scyld in the Scandian lands. So becomes it a youth to quit him well with his father's freinds, by fee and gift, that to aid him, aged, in after days, come warriors willing, should war draw nigh, liegemen loyal: b y lauded deeds shall an earl have honor in every clan. \n Forth he fared at the fated moment, sturdy Scyld to the shelter of God. Then they bore him over to ocean's billow, loving clansmen, as late he charged them, while wielded words the winsome Scyld, the leader beloved who long had ruled... In the roadstead rocked a ring-dight vessel, ice-flecked, outbound, atheling's barge: there laid they down their darling lord on the breast of the boat, the breaker-of-rings, by the mast the mighty one. Many a treasure fetched from far was freighted with him. No ship have I known so nobly dight with with weapons of war and weeds of battle, with breastplate and blade: on his bosom lay a heaped hoard that hence should go far o'er the flood with him floating away. No less these loaded the lordly gifts, thanes; huge treasure, than those ahd done who in former time forth had sent him sole on the seas, a suckling child. High o'er his head they hoist the standard, a gold-wove banner; let billows take him, gave him to ocean. Grave were their spirits, mournful their mood. No man is able to say in sooth, no son of the halls, no hero 'neath heaven, --who harbored that freight \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Beregrim's Family Lore", "lichtkang", "Long ago, from the Kal'Urguan caves, the ancestor of the Beregrim family set out to settle in the woodlands. His name was Beregran and the family name origantes from his. He became a wealthy carpenter, but fell out of business after a great fire that devastated half his town. He wasn't hit, but from now of on the inhabitants preferred stone furniture! He retired and died soon after, but his son, Eric Beregrim, used his father's fortune to invest in trading articles. His first trips weren't that succesfull, but through the import of weapons he quickly succeeded! The dwarven Kingdom of Kal'Urguan went to battle with the Orcish fiends and the demand for weaponry raised faster than the number of recruits that were eager to join battle! \n Trade continued to be the main source of income for all the descendants of Beregran, but every now and again one of the line set out because of a craving to mining and smithing. Something given down generation on generation because of their Cave-dwarf ancestry. The last known descendant at the writing of this book, (Kamees, 33rd of the First seed, 1314) is Thorg Beregrim, a Blacksmith and architect who established himself in the town of Terriko, protectorate of Krugmar, the Orc nation. It is he who wrote this book, and his descendants who will keep record of the family tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Berserk's Log One", "Desires", "Figured to start one of these since \"Kitty\" is asleep, she can no longer see what is going on, nor hear the words that people speak.. It terrifies me about how empty it now feels in here. I always wanted it to be like this until I got to know her, how delicate and innocent she is even though she very well knew what I did, she still loved me. I can't grasp the pain she feels right now, even though I am fully aware of what is happening. Though my ever longed love for her is the same as she loves the damnable gypsy, I can't help it.. To feel sorry. When she finally slipped away, I could still feel the urge to freeze my attacks against the vulnerable cursed dark-elf. Why?... I just wanted to help you..", ""),
        StaticBook("Besarn I", "Kamberli", "Besarn is a city far out in the wilds. It's a little city, but really lovley and the city is still growing. Besarn is open for all races, if they are accepting the laws and want to be a part of the commuity. \n        To reach the city, you have to travel to many dangerous places, you even have to pass a desert. but if you are there the resident of Besarn help you to get energy again. So, why do you wait? Go and find Besarn and be a part of it!", ""),
        StaticBook("Best Brother Bone", "sparten4ever92", "I love Bone! He is the best brother ever! He is always so nice to me! I wish I could tell him how much I'm sorry for hurting him with my axe. I was so sad when I hurt him I hope he will forgive He is So smart too! He make cool tingys out of redstone! He even built a lighty thingy! *whimpers that he has some in his room Bone is da best brother ever He isn't ever mad! I love my brother! He is the best This book is for him!", ""),
        StaticBook("Best Mummy!", "mdhegs", "Once there was a elf named Bone! A mean sea monster ate Bone's daddy. But, Mummy alice saved Bone. Mummy alice is the best mummy ever! I love Mummy alice! Dis book was writen by Bone! hi aah erase erase", ""),
        StaticBook("Better than the Necromimicon", "Royced", "I will admit the first three. The first trial of the undead: Kill somebody in a unique fashion: You can use traps or simply sacrifice them to iblees.  The second: Turn an lightsided man into an evil one. To do this: You can simply trick them with one of your friends, or you can do it the hard way. The third: Make a sacrifice to iblees: The simplest way to do you is to kill somebody while shouting \" You're death is for iblees! \" The fourth trial involves four hard tactics: Acrobatics, Knowledge, and Strength. You must complete a hard jumpquest, solve four problems, and kill the inquisitor in battle. The questions aren't very hard, and there is a stone you can stand on. If you stand on the stone, the fire cannot hurt you if you misdo the question. (( :R ))  This book.", ""),
