        StaticBook("Bio on nilk the elf", "Nbar97", "text", ""),
        StaticBook("Biodoc's Contract", "braner321", "As a resident of Dunwood village, I will respect and aid my neighbors as best as i can. I accept my free home, materials, and support from the fellow villagers, and in turn I will aid Dunwood Village as best I can by working my chosen career as Craftsman. This includes farming. Working in a different career that belongs to someone else without consent of that person or an Elder is warrant for eviction if deemed necessary by the Elders of Dunwood. I am aware if the chosen career is not taken by anyone or is not viewed as a career of Dunwood, I am allowed to do that career, however, it will not be recognized by the Elders of Dunwood as aiding the community. If I do not aid the community to satisfaction, I understand my home could be given to someone who does. I also understand are baths are important and will take one at least every week. \n I also agree not to build in Dunwood Village without an Elder of Dunwood's permission, and when allowed, will stick to the Halfling archecture present. I acknowledge the mountain Elduren will remain preserved and not scarred by any Halfling architecture. Same goes for the lake. \n I am entitled to my personal storage and belongings, but also understand hoarding goods that can or should be used by or forthe community is frowned upon and could lead to eviction. Personal items may include, but is not limited too: weapons, trinkets, tools , armor, pictures, objects of sentimental value, and pets. I understand all Halflings that are residents of Dunwood Village are required to drink one pint one pint of ale a week. I am aware anything in the community storage of Dunwood Village is not available as a personal item and should not be taken home for personal storage unless otherwise approved by the Elders of Dunwood. \n Theft, murder, trespassing, or blackmailing another villager of Dunwood Village will result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. Bringing trouble from outside Dunwood Village too Dunwood Village could also result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. That includes, but is not limited to bandits, war, Undead, or Orc Raiders. I am not secretly an Undead follower, Iblees worshipper, or a spider and will evict myself without causing harm to the village of Dunwood Village if I am. \n I understand that interpretation of this contract is entirely up to the Elders of Dunwood. The Elders reserve the right to evict, restrict, or banish you from Dunwood Village if it is seen nessesary. I am well within my rights to question any of the Elders in matters that this contract does not cover. \n xBiodoc_Goodbody", ""),
        StaticBook("Biodoc's Notes: The Mysterious Sword", "braner321", "Odd.....Only word that I can think of that can describe me sword. It be no regular sword either. It be a special one....dropped from one of those funny lookin' Pig fellers . Petyr looked at it. When he touched it, it cut him a bit. He said it reminded him of something he was about to say, but didn't. When I asked him, he said not to worry about his bussiness. Back to the sword, It feels odd. I believe it to hold some kind of Magic. It was held by one of those pig fellers. I'vee heard they come from where the Undead reside. The sword's magic may have brought the Pigmen here. Maybe that's why they all hold one! Odd it is indeed. This curiousity of this sword and it's possible magic has sparked another curiousity... Me as a Halfling using magic. Could it be possible that I could use Magic? Maybe...just, maybe. I will keep this sword in a hidden chest until I feel the need for it. The need to study the sword. Today, I went and bought some gold. I'm wondering if I keep it near the sword long enough that some of the sword's magic will rub off", ""),
        StaticBook("Biodoc's Will", "braner321", "I, Biodoc Goodbody, bequest all of my possesions to my one and only heir, Whidoc_Goodbody. Seeing as my house belongs to the town, I will leave it with them to decide on what to do with it. I would prefer it if my son could have it, but alas, that choice is for the town to decide. As for my funeral, I would like to be buried somewhere by the Sacred Mountain. But that is for the town to decide. If some people could say something at my funeral, that would be very nice and with that, my soul would finally be at rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("biography", "Ptoipa", "Since  I was a young boy, I have always dreamt of moving to Central Aegis lookin fo fame, glory and wealth. On my 21st birthday I moved into Laurelin to achieve my goal. I've met a lot of people since then, but non stood out as much as my good friend Luke_Starglow. One of the very first persons I met in here. He helped me troughout my quest and I hope he'll continue to do so until it is complete. Since a very young age I have been doing all sorts of jobs, and practicing with a sword and a bow in my free time, so I'm very skilled. In this book I'll report my life, which I hope will be full of stories to tell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Biography", "sleien", "I was born 557 years ago. My parents were happy to have a child, because they needed help with working to survive. They both were miners, but their mine was really old and it seemed to be exhausted. When I was old enough, they gave me a pickaxe and I had to follow them into the mine. Ich teste mal was", ""),
        StaticBook("Biography of Mark_de_Altair", "Markdeevee", "It began long ago Altair was born alone in the woods were his mother shortly after died. Nature kept him alive, it wrapped her arms around him and protected him. He was found wandering around in the woods fendin g for himself at the age of 14, by one of the kings patrols. He was brought to the castle barracks,", ""),
        StaticBook("Biography of Rayle, and Kayle Seek.", "StandUnited", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Bircalin's Poem", "Crippledbaboon", "A way to begin, where do I find one. Perhaps with a kiss, an elf's heart I've won. No question of love, my feelings are true. This poem I write, for no other than you. Dark times came our way, but these times I had slain. For no being, mortal or not, can stop me, fmo tying the knot. Winters pass, summers fall, but my love endures through the pain of all. These words may be weak, the meanings seem rough, but these words won't matter. I can't love you enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bircalins book.", "Crippledbaboon", "I am mute. I cannot speak. I live in peace with the Ascended. Please do not harm me. As i mean no harm to you. Once you have finished reading this. Please return it to me. This book is my only means of communication. I once lived in Laurelin, with the elves, thinking they were the kindest of all people. However, one night my old companion, an elf. Left to meet a female elf for reasons unknown. I did not trust him. I followed, i listeneed to what they said, small talk altogether, but, i began to walk away. Thinking it was nothing, when my name was mentioned. They called me heartless. Said i cared not for others but only myself. They mocked me. So i left, i ran as far as i could, escaping them, grief-stricken. Abandoned by the only hope i had of a normal life once more. I found myself within deep wilderness. I remembered the Ascended city, Haven. I ran there, as fast as my feet could carry me. I made it eventually, I met Master Sage Riizu there, he told my how i could stay, for how long i do not know. And that is where i am. I have no destiny but to exist in this world. No means to live, nowhere to live a normal life again. Once i am asked to leave i do not know where i will go. Nowhere will accept me. Not even my own kin want me in their homes. Im desperately alone... I need to find someone, somwhere that will accept me. I must travel to the dwarven realm. It is the only other place i have not tried. I can only hope they do not kill me on sight. Human to Dwarf relations are not the strongest they could be recently. Once again, i may die here.. May the gods bless me. Bircalin, The Mute.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bircalins Diary. Entry 1", "Crippledbaboon", "I have arrived at Al'Khazar in search of any leads to the whereabouts of Dunwood, my homeland. So far, i have come across no help, the locals are ignorant here. I must find my own way. Aedan speaks of a \" Varla Stone \" that can stop the undead rising. Supposedly. I will look into this as much as i can... I do I do want to join But they wont listen.. the hustle of the street covers the faint cry of my voice \n Entry 2", ""),
        StaticBook("Bircalins Undead Infiltration Plan", "Crippledbaboon", "Step one - Gather sufficient men to re-claim Snowyfields. Step two - Give ALL fighters full leather armour at the least. And two mushroom soups. ( And of course, an iron sword ) Step three - Enter siege tower and jump from very top. Once you have reached the walls make sure all men have eaten ONLY one mushroom soup. Step four - Begin attack on Snowyfields undead minions. Step five - Find the ale, have a celebration to remember...", ""),
        StaticBook("black legion", "danielbreen", "Guide book for Black legion leaders Lance and Drake we are a mercanaires guild that does various type of jobs ranging for private army to assasinations all new initiates are to read the rules and laws of this guild if any of these rules and laws are broken you will be vanished Banished* and you will be hunted down and slain all terms and condidtions of our guild can be found on our fourm page at www.lordofthecraft.net/fourm then look us up under economy and war then hit guilds andr then search our topic called blacklegion merc guild", ""),
