        StaticBook("BlackLegion Members", "danielbreen", "Leaders Lance (Danielbreen) Drake (Faldio134) Members\n Drifter (CorprlSkyler) Adephon (Killerbreakfest) Slyth (ZIEatBabaysZ) Lord Rasta (Glynax) lief (mellowmatthew) Bacil Hedgemage (xXWOLVERINEXx)", ""),
        StaticBook("BlackStone", "Zombieslaughter", "the BlackStone guild is an all encompassing guild. \n they control farms, storehouses, and shops, though their main focus is their mercenaries. \n BlackStone will contract out soldiers to anyone, for practically any purpose, ranging from guards, to soldiers, to watchmen, to even, it is rumored, assassinations. the Guild is run by a quintet of high ranking officers; the Guild Master, who oversees the guilds welfare and overall upkeep, the Arms master, who trains and recruits new members, the Tactician, who helps decide on contracts and command troops when the guild is in need or in heavy use, the Librarian, who keeps the records of the guild, ranging from contracts to battle reports. the last counciller is the Treasurer, in charge of the Echelon ranks, or non combatants of the guild. \n the Echelons have many ranks, split in two, some commanded by the librarian, some by the Treasurer. the Treasurer controls the Merchantmen; the lower class Echelons. Merchantmen are typically farmers or miners, vital for the guilds survival, but not very independant. next is the Mercantile, typically shopkeepers or landowners, who can recommend contracts and meet the normal people. next is the Aristocrats, those rich individuals who help finance the guild, and allow diplomatic relations with Nations. \n the Librarion controls the Keepers; men and women in charge of maintaining the guild's forts and archives. the next rank is the Seekers; records keepers, sent out with mercenaries to record important events and ensure contracts are carried out to the letter. \n the known military ranks are as follows; Phalanx, recruits . Sigma, Men at arms. Lancers, the elite archers. and Praetorians, the elite soldiers of the guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("BlackStone military", "Zombieslaughter", "anyone joining the guild as a soldier will start out as a Phalanxe, a novice. phalanxe are allowed their weapons of choice and leather armor. \n when proven, they may advance to the Sigma rank. sigma are allowed any weapon of their choice, and are given chainmail armor and iron armor. \n Lancers are not necessarily the next rank up, lancers are the guild guard, and must be proficient with bow and arrows, as well as sword. these are our elite archers. \n Praetorians are the final rank, before the actual council, and are given diamond armor, when available and the best weapons available. \n the Arms master is the best fighter in the guild and is responsible for training and testing members. he is one of the 5 council members in charge of the guild. \n the tactician is selected for his ingineuity, and does not need to be particularly good at hand to hand combat. he is in charge of deploying guild forces and managing certain contracts.", ""),
        StaticBook("BlackThorn's Book", "BenjaminKayEight", "TEsT one day there was a frog that went ribbit nom nom nom said the frog I'm feeling fruity! real strawberrys folded with double cream for a soft dreamy centre", ""),
        StaticBook("Blade's Journal", "BladeCreep", "The First pages are ripped out of the book... You continue reading. Sabet, 21st of The Amber Cold, 1317 I located the Ender Shard in Sanhar yesterday. It is located in 'the Heart' which appears to be in the center of Sanhar. It will open when the Moon darkens the Earth during the day, which will happen in about a week. Then I will return to Sanhar to claim the shard. After that I'll go after the second shard near the Cloud temple. (end of message) Several pages are missing again... You continue reading. Irba, 18th of Snows Maiden, 1317.  My calculations were wrong. The heart will open in about a month! I guess I'll have to wait. Let's just hope that stupid Mogroka doesn't spoil my  plan again. Soon, the first Ender Shard will be mine! Kmees, 12th of The Grand Harvest, 1318 still waiting for the day to come... It's getting closer. In the meanwhile, I have located the Ender Shard of Laurelin. I'll get it right after the one in Sanhar, using  my soul stone. Kamees, 26th of the Second Seed, 1320  Years have passed, I have been in a deep sleep. I have found the Heart of Sanhar, which seems to be located in the slums. Though it did not open, due to the need of a sacrafice. and when I tried to sacrafice a pig, it did not open either.  I did some research, and it seems I need an orc body to sacrafice. this is turning out to be a harder task then I thaught. Sabet, 7th of The First Seed, 1321 I've gotten 2 of the Ender Shards... I'm feeling powerfull. now there are only the two in Sanhar and Laurelin to go. As the book said, a mark has started burning itself into my chest and right shoulder. But they just seem to be halfly done. The Immunity to the sun would be granted by the Shard of Sanhar though, which now disables me from walking in the sunlight without suffering... I almost had it twice! Once Scott Rumoss almost gave a part of his soul for the Heart to open , and the other night I got followed by a large group of Orcs. I have to get it soon! It's my only chance at Summoning 'them' I've succeeded in summoning some, but they are corrupt.", ""),
