        StaticBook("book of the dead", "redbaron", "The ancient magic of the undead is a mysterious thing.  There magic is based on fire and necromancy magic. Many people do not understand the undead.  They are more then destructive beings. There minds are corrupted.  Some of them may be power hungry though.  Iblees curse is very strong, and any man would find it hard to resist. Iblees first talks about power.  Many men in aegis love power and would do much for it.  Through all the attacks that i have been through the undead first cast high amounts of lightning and fire balls.   Then when the mortals of aegis get close.  They summon hells minions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of the Keep", "Da_Emperors", "The Book of the Keep is the book of ranks, its first volume will state its leadersd The Head Founder is Jay (Da_Emperors) and founders include Arrim (Blake) as well as the Dark elf Theo. All three of these men are a part of the Council the last of the council members include Sniper. To join you must contact the counsil after joining the IC, a meeting must take palce for any major even like that What? What? . ff", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Thieves", "ikeyman232", "A warm and moist day filled the streches of the plains. Farmers harvested their wheat, butchers chopped, and lumberjacks cut. Everyone was up and about. Small villages like dots dotted this plain, each with a diffrent culture and government. The first, was a normal Human settlement. This was run by a council, instead of one head. The second, a smaller Human settlement. This was a small farming village with  a manor and workers. These were two completelly diffrent places. The first settlement was a happy-go-lucky, feel good place. The second, however, was a place of dispair. Workers were almost forced to work, by their head, Tatsin. Tatsin ran a corrupt government and used bribery andillegal tactics to keep in power. In the first town, a man was forced out, due to thievery. He quickly walked to the second, and applied for a job. He would work as treasurerer. A grave mistake by Tatsin. Slowly and slowly, the \"treasurer\" took more and more money. The power of Tatsin lowered, and lowered. Until officially, Tatsin was thrown out, and supprisingly, the thief became the head. The thief changed ways things were done, supprisingly, for the good. The people were no longer forced to work, and they did as they pleased. The 2nd settlemtn grew larger and larger, ntil it passed the 1st. The Thief king would be remembered in history as a born leader, and not as a petty thief.", ""),
