        StaticBook("Braxis Silverblade", "isagirl909", "Former Knight Lieutenant for Oren. Braxis completed the Beginner's Course on his first day and bought a home in the Isles. His Squire is the son of Vikram Mournstone. He shows resiliance, courage and honor. I expect a quick promotion for him, should he remain in the Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Braxis's Fathers Journel", "Jroy96", "Dear Son... if you are reading this then i have died... In my passing i want you to take care of your mother and finish your training . \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Just rember i died in battle protecting Our homelands from the Acursed ones and i hope one day you will become a Warrior better then myself \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n - Althos Silverblade", ""),
        StaticBook("Brett history", "Javelberg", "He was the son of pampo perea The previous king of oren,he was a prince of oren Until the was about 20 when is father passed away Then edmund sheffield became the king or oren Under the senechal laws of oren He became very close to edmund He was constable for many years Until he then promoted me to this position in the whispering isles After lord tyrion turend to the undead", ""),
        StaticBook("Brevias's Journal", "Brevias", "Today I have had a vision.  I saw a wolf, devouring pigs at an alarming rate.  After every pig it ate, it became plumper, rounder, and turned a little bit pink. Eventually dat Wolf turned into a pig... and another wolf came along, and devoured him.   \n \n Today be da first day I wear my blindfold. I be doin' dis to train my third eye.  It be difficult at first, I've stumbled a few times, soon I will adjust though, and no longer need my eyes to see. It be amazin' seein' through the elements, dis seems to be givin' me a new perspective. \n  I've had my blindfold on for almost a week now. I be seein' tings much clearer now and my mind is less clouded. Many people ask if I am blind, but I am not and I find that amusing.  Being mistaken for a blind person does have its advantages sometimes.       \n  \n My vision without eyes is perfected.  I know see through the earth, land, and sky. I don't know if I'll ever take dis blindfold off, seein' I don't need to. \n \n \n \n  I've been spendin' all my time in da new orc village of Kell'og. I've done alot for dat town so far.  Besides building my own home, I've worked hard in da mines, and build many other homes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Briamoth's Book of Herbalism", "Briamoth", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Briamoth's Journal", "Briamoth", "Testing the book writing function. \n I have gained quite a large amount of Minas over the past two days.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brian's Dunwood Contract", "bhorner", "As a resident of Dunwood Village, I will respect and aid my neighbors as best I can. I accept my free home, materials, and support from the fellow villagers, and in turn will aid Dunwood Village as best I can by working my choosen career as Outdoorsman . This includes restocking supplies when needed. Working in a different career that belongs to someone without consent of that person or an Elder is a warrant for eviction if deemed necessary by the Elders of Dunwood. I am aware if the choosen career is not taken by anyone or is not veiwed as a career of Dunwood, I am allowed to do that career, however it will not be recognized by the Elders of Dunwood as aiding the community. If I do not the community to satisfactory, I understand my home could be given to someone else that does. I also understand baths are important and will take one atleast every week. \n I also agree not to build in the Dunwood Village without an Elder of Dunwood's permission, and when allowed, will stick to the halfling architecture present. I acknowledge the mountain of Elduren will remain preserved and not scarred by any halflings architecture. Same goes for the lake. \n I am entitled to my personnal storage and belongings, but also understand hoarding goods that can be or should be used by or for the community is frowned upon and could lead to eviction. Personnal items may include, but is not limited too: weapons, trinkets, tools, armour, pictures, objects of sentimental value, and pets. I understand that all halflings that are residents of Dunwood Village are required to drink one pint of ale a week. I am aware anything in the community storage  of Dunwood Village is not available as a personnal item and should not be taken home for personnal storage unless otherwise approved by the Elders of Dunwood. Theft, murder, trespassing, or blackmailing another villager of Dunwood Village will result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. Bringing trouble from outside Dunwood Village inside Dunwood Village could result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. This includes but is not limited to, bandits, war, Undead, Orc Raiders. I am not secretly an Undead follower. Ibees worshipper, or a spider and will evict myself without Writing the last paragraph now, I am an Outdoorsmen without causing harm to the villagers of Dunwood Village if I am. \n I understand that interpretation of this cntract is entirely up to the Elders of Dunwood The Elders reserve the right to evict, restrict, or banish me from Dunwood if it seems nessesary. I am well within my right to question any of the Elders in matters this contract does not cover. \n Brian", ""),
        StaticBook("Brodien's Journal", "spartan13357", "Itnan, 23rd of The Second Seed, 1331: Today, I finished mining out my mine, and it still continues to rain for the past 3 days, (I wonder if it will ever stop.) I haven't heard or seen any other dwarfs or anybody for that matter, and I am begining to worry. I have decided to wait on the road and see if anybody passes by, I hope it's fruitful. Let's hope Azura wishes me luck. I've changed my mind, I will travel up (down?) the road to find shop's so i may buy iron. Ahad, 29th of The Second Seed, 1331: I've finnally returned home and it has stopped raining. (Thank Azura.) So, i've decided to stay home for the next couple of months and then go back to Kal'Al---something, I don't recall what it was called, but i've been raiding their homes for supplies, I do hope no one finds out, and I believe the cooridinates along The King's Road is Z: 1678 and the Y and X are unknown to me. It has just started raining again and I fear I might go mad soon, if it keeps it up. Itnan, 9th of Suns Smile, 1331: I'm going back into my mine to look for more iron. I just hope I can find iron this time, Azura knows I need it. I've found a good iron mine, but alas, the ground is too hard to break. Irba, 32nd if The Second Seed, 1334: I'm going back to raid that town, once again , if I so much as get ooked at i'll have to leave, may Azura guide me!", ""),
        StaticBook("Broken Golem Heart", "Lagomorphia", "A broken golem heart, crafted by the Ascended and corrupted with undead magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Broski's & Duggy's Shop [Kal Urguan]", "BrutalBroski", "List of what we sell, And the prices: \n \n Coal - 5 \n Iron - 25 \n Gold - 60 \n Diamond - 195 \n Redstone Dust - 2 \n Lapis Lazuli - 7   \n Obsidian - 200 \n  \n Mossy Cobblestone - 45  \n Bread - 5 \n Cooked Porkchop - 9 \n Raw Porkchop - 7 \n Ale - 10 * Return Cup *     \n Cake - 200 \n  \n Cobble, Dirt, Sand, Gravel - 1 \n Clean Stone - 2 \n Wood - 2  \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Brotherhood of the Candle", "swordcoast25", "In a world filled with greed, hate, selfishness, and death, it is far too rare to find those souls willing to help others at their own expense. Individuals willing to work hard, and suffer just so others can be comfortable and happy. This is what the Brotherhood of the Candle represents. A small group of those that wish to make Aegis a better place solely through the love and generosity they possess. To rid the world of the evils that haunt us everyday. They have no need for a sword, instead they wield kindness.", ""),
