        StaticBook("Chrisdena", "leeloongsam", "Name: Chrisdena Silverfeather \n Race: Human \n Age/Gender: ?/Female \n A proud, stubborn, once a lu mberjack. She joined the FOA and became great friends with the Ascended Zephyr. They are now married . She has becomed a Ascended without a trial, questioning her legimitancy as a decended of Aeriel. She thinks she can handles most situations by herself, and wont hesitate to speak up. Here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chronicals of a Dead Man", "darkdladety", "People say dead men tell no tales. Well, I guess that's why I am writing this. To prove to myself that I am still alive. In my final act of life, I write down this story. \n It all happened in an instant. They poured out of the woods, silent as night itself. We spotted them before they got to close. This is what we had prepared for. I got the weapons and tools, and she got food and supplies. We were ready to defend our house with our lives. Thats when everything went to hell. \n One must have gotten past us and into the house. The roof we stood on fell in. With most of the house gone, they poored in. I put arrows into all of them. Creepers disintegrating before they hit the ground, skeletons being blasted apart by my spray of arrows. But there were to many and they slowly advanced on us. She was completely unconscious, so I dragged her into our escape tunnel in the back of the house. \n I whipped around and put an arrow through the tnt above the passage entrance. I pulled her down the tunnel as far as i could. She had a large wound in the center of her forehead. I took bandages and a pork chop out of her bag. I fixed her up as best I could, but she wouldn't last long. I gathered all my strength and put her on my shoulders. After what seemed like hours of walking, we arrived at the mouth of the tunnel. \n The sun had just come up, and in the distance I could see smoke rising from the ruins of our house. I knew we could never go back, but I didn't know where we could go. \n I did the only thing I could do, I walked. After a day of walking, we came upon a house. I walked over to the door and collapsed. I layed there, with no will to move. Someone opened the door, but I couldn't see who it was, because I blacked out. \n I woke up, and it was light out, and an I was on a bed. I looked over and saw her, laying on the bed, pale white. I looked around but no one was in the house. I ran to her side and tried to get her to wake up. Then it hit me. I collapsed to the floor sobbing, then I blacked out agian. I woke up once again, this time at night. I tried to get up but I found that I was restrained. \n Looking around I saw a man in the corner. \"Hay, what happened.\" I yelled. \"Well,\" he said, \"You showed up with your friend over there in quite bad shape. I fixed you up, but I am afraid I couldn't save her.\" I struggled with the restraints. \"Oh yes, you smashed your head when you got out of bed so I had to restrain you. Sorry\" He untied the rope and I got up. I had a raging pain in my head but I forced myself to focus. I asked the man if I could go out for a few minutes and he said yes. \n I grabbed my bow and quiver. I walked through the forest, and I was myself again. Cows, pigs, sheep, even chickens fell when two arrows pierced their skulls. While I was hunting, everything melted away, the pain, the fear, everything. I was at peace once again. I reach for another arrow but found my quiver empty and that night was coming so I returned to the house. \n I handed the old man some pork and he cooked it for me. That night we eat mushroom soup and pork in silence. In the moring I got up early and made my way to the door. The old man grabbed my shoulder and said, \" Kid, you're going back to the place where this happened to you, I can see it in your eyes.\" I turned to him, looked him stait in the eyes and said \"I have to end this, I am doing it for her, goodbye, forever.\" And with that I grabbed my fallen compainon and headed out the door. I made my way all the way back to our ruined house. \n While it was still day a dug a grave for her, layed her in it and covered her. Placing a single rose to make the grave. With the rest of the day I built a small wall where I would make my final stand. \"There.\" I said to myself, it's done. I armed my bow and waited. \n Then they came, just like before. This time I cut them down as they emerged from the woods. I was holding them off until I began to run out of arrows. I grab my sword and ran into the center of them, cuting down any monster I saw. They slowly pushed me back to the ruined house. Once again they flooded the house, but this time there was no exit. \n Most of them were dead. I was almost dead. I thought I killed them all when I saw it out of the corner of my eye. It stood there staring at me with its always saddening face. I ran over to it and slashed it with my sword and it fell. I turned and walked away when I realized it didn't disintegrate. I turned just in time to see it go off. \n Thats it. I fell to the ground, my legs no longer working. I saw a book in the ruble near me. It was a book that she was writing for me. In it I wrote this book. \n With that my story ends. I... I... can see the light now. I am coming home Lilly, I am come back to you, Charles is coming home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chronicles of a Hermit: Part 1", "Froggerbob", "Day 77: I came out of the tunnels today. Day 78: It's time to plant my reeds", ""),
        StaticBook("Chronicles of Houston", "Houstonruss", "As I began My journey, It was plain tough until some generous soul lent me money ,I then was able to purchase a mine permit and gater plenty of ore . I am now in a small new town with my possesions trying to farm spruce!", ""),
        StaticBook("Chronicles of Iblees", "serenityonyx", "The chronicles of Iblees are the official records of encounters and meetings between the Inner Circle of the Druids, and the Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Church's Mind of importants", "omnomska", "Dear Reader, This book is for the eye of my pupils, for thou is importants of many, many ask the secret to my living combat and mind, and thought it may be easy, thou shall think again, for it takes many, many days to get into your piece of mind, if wish to learn, continue on \n For so many time and effort i spent in training, i gain little for so long learning to get a peaceful mind, takes long to study you life and actions for so many gratitude for thou has hatred in your body greetings i said to myself, thinking thou shall make a new life in the land of Aegis , with great wisdom in soul and mind, show others you are in control of your actions and show superior to ones self . For thou does not want to hold back to my wants and needs, but resist to it, ye will see a differences, and gain life itself. \n Many crave for combat, i do myself, but craving for a blood spill shouldn't be in a state of mind . It is for that you should wait, wait for someone to talk to you for there time of need , if thou knows a being is introuble, then go forth with pride and conquer thy enemy. If thou gets confront with thy enemy. stay calm and talk to thee, make a wall in your mind between you and your enemy, if thou craves blood, do the same, vanish anger in yourself and think ahead , results will end to your liking \n Now go forth and Live, theres a world out there in the world of Aegis, until we meet again \n -Church", ""),
        StaticBook("Cirdan's Journal", "MrHobo", "Today, I met a queer man on a path. I stared at him, a little entranced somehow. He stared me back, and asked, \"What?\". I was a little taken aback by his afrontness in conversation. The tribe was never like this... I asked him about father's harbor. He said to ask the druids. Who are they though? And where is this \"Respiren?\" I must find out... I want to at least know about my father before I pass on into the afterlife. I think I should now go and talk to that strange man  from earlier... Ask him for his name, and see where the druids are. Then, I will venture there, and find out about my father. *scibbles in journal The stranges man's name was Ashur.  \nWoke up outside the Druid... Garden thing, to say it delicately?  I cannot think, I mean to say, of how to put it. Apparently, from what I have  collected, the Druids and the Wardens are less than friends. Apparently, one has angered the other so much that the Wardens are banned from the Druids... Grove! Ah, that is the word! \n I have seen my first glance of Respiren. I 'twas excited. He truly seems as a druid would be, judging from the clippings of books I have seen. But, before we could speak, another Dark Elf (oh, the excitement I felt in seeing another of my kind!) asked to join the druids, completely ruining my chance to speak with him. I shall wait until they are finished, then, I shall speak to him, with the hopes that he can tell about my father, Fealnor. I cannot wait untill the moment! But what if he was a terrible person? Oh, the woe I would feel! Perhaps I shouldn't ask this Respiren? No. I shall. I must know, or else I will be driven mad. I hope they are not much longer. I shall stay, as previously mentioned, but my conflicting emotions may cloud my thought. I must stay true to my task. I must remember his name... \n The meeting is dragging on. I just want to see Respiren... But, I was accepted by the Lunavara Worker's Guild, so, I will have to go there soon... But then I will have no time! This MUST be done soon! I am going mad, I know not a soul here. The only person I know is that nice man on..  What was it? King's highway? I think it was. I haven't seen him since then. Oh, I am so alone in this world! The rain is ceaseless and merciless. I am going insane, as I sit here, and expect different results from just sitting here. I have to take action. But how...? What shall I do...? \n I left the druids. As I was leaving, I saw an arrest unfolding. It seemd the Law-breaker was winning It appears as if the guards are winning... Oh so sad in this place... \n I am off to Lunavara, in hope of fortune! A day has passed, and I could not get to Lunavara. I am outside the Druid Grove, waiting for a seemingly high-ranking Druid and a lower ranking druid to quit conversing, so, I may speak with the higher ranking about Respiren, and possibly, my father. Apparently, the lower-ranking druid also became a Battlemage, so, now, he has to choose. From what I gather, he has chosen a battlemage's life. How sad, though. I would rather be a druid than this \"Battlemage.\" \n I think a man may have just been robbed... Or, he violated a dress code...? I am not sure \n I have finished the trials for the Wolverines... I am in! I have reclaimed father's house. It seems some of the valuables here were taken in the abscense of an owner. I see a fine line of iron dust in some places, and a miniscule diamond in another. I will have to restock what was taken. Off to the mines, then! \n I am within a place called the Verge. I have settled in a town called Oasis. I am talking to a dwarf currently. Apparently, this town is in need of a lorekeeper, which I may fit the position of!", ""),
