        StaticBook("City Plan", "Jaknifed", "Going to wait until they figure out what to do with 1.8 They might have to do a world reset so we will plan accordingly Test out some concept builds in the area if you can Plan for it to be a port town initially and then extend it to have defenses erase all", ""),
        StaticBook("City Plans", "Jaknifed", "Hey, We will have to wait until Availer figures out what to do about 1.8. Might be a world reset and would hate for our work to be undone. Test out any concept builds you might like in the surrounding area. It's going to be a semi-port town built along a beach so we need docks and such. We will then extend out for defensible structures and housing and such. plan to use glass, wooden planks and cobblestone. Use whatever you like though to build. Thanks Mate. -Zyn", ""),
        StaticBook("Citzenship of Krugmar", "Sultan_Mogroka", "This was give by Walord Mogroka'Gorkil To Loth as she is a friend of da orcs and one of Krugmar if she wishs signed Sultan Mogroka'Gorkil", ""),
        StaticBook("Clasification of Books by Number in The House", "Pauldell1", "The books in this house are filed with a number system, showing their classification. The first numb er represents the type of book, the second represents topic, and the third and beyond represents the information type, seperated by a slash. The first number is assigned to the following categories: (1=report) (2=fiction) (3=history) (4=nonf iction/instructional) (5=newspaper) (6=mail) The second number is asigned to the following categorie s: (1=Ascended) (2=Human) (3=Undead) (4=Elf) (5=Dwarf) (6=Orc) (7=Aengul) (8=World) (9=Iblees) (0=other) The third number and beyond represent the following: (1=base) (2=Mailinor) (3=Krugmar) (4=Oren) (5=K al'Urguan) (6=Alras) (7=Haven) (8=Undead Kingdom) (9=info) (10=Wilds) (11=lore) (12=magic) (13=sub-r aces) (14=other)", ""),
