        StaticBook("Counting 1 to 10", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Oem = 1 \n Niut = 2 \n Hael = 3 \n Vailu = 4 \n Kulin = 5 \n Banih = 6 \n Laier = 7 \n Esun = 8 \n Moiel = 9 \n Telu = 10", ""),
        StaticBook("Coupon for the Falos Inn", "XSilverWolfX", "This costumer has been allowed cheaper ale for 1 mina - Signed Crowley Falos", ""),
        StaticBook("Courier's Handbook", "Themastermoo", "This is the couriers handbook. There are certain things you need to know, if you are to function as a courier in the AFF. First off, you need to have specific equipment ready to  at all times in your personal chest, so if you called off on duty you can grab it and  go. As of right now, the equipment you need is this: 1 journal, 1 weapon, 1 shovel, 1 pickaxe, 1 stack of building materials, 1 Crafting Table , 1 flint and tinder, 4 items of food.", ""),
        StaticBook("Covenant of the Dead", "Dalek348", "\n1. You shall not commit murder against any other Undead. To do so would be to invoke banish ment from our ranks and action to be dealt ruthlessly. \n2. You shall not steal from any other Undead. To do so would invoke harsh punishment and po ssible banishment. \n3. You shall never reveal any inside information to an outside party whose allegiance is ag ainst the Undead. Banishment and punishment will be dealt out on you. \n4. Do not scar the realm of the Fallen One, the Nether. To harvest large amounts of materia ls from his realm is scarring our land that we live in. \n5. Always respect those in a higher rank than yourself. Address them appropriately with res pect. You may disrespect those in a rank lower than you, but only in a roleplay manner, and nothing personal. \n6. Adorn the robes appropriate to your rank, to wear the colour of another rank would cause disruption and confusion. \n7. You may only cause large scale destruction and war on a city or town with the approval o f the Overlord or Prophet ((or a GM)), you may cause minor destruction without their consent, but yo u should not destroy a lot. Any minor destruction you cause, i.e destroying of a house, you must lea \n8. You must speak and be spoken to whenever you make a sacrifice to Iblees. When you spill their blood, you must always speak to them as you watch the light leave their eyes. \n9. It is not necessary to distribute and offer your valuable minerals to the bank, but it i s encouraged and will help our cause greatly. \n10. You are expected to know every server rule, have a decent understanding of them, and ob ey them at all times. We don't want to get a reputation for rule breaking. You are expected to uphol d your characters story and act in his or her persona consistently.", ""),
        StaticBook("Covenant of the Undead", "Dalek348", "((Castellano, do you have improved chat?))", ""),
        StaticBook("cow", "boodilly", "cow\"\" cow cow\"cow w  Cowcowcccccc' Cow\n Cow cow Cow \n \n cow", ""),
        StaticBook("Cracker Jack Tavern", "firespirit44", "The Cracker Jack Tavern was founded by a man named Jack and a elf named Ebs. It was a simple partnership, but many people flock to the tavern to watch Jack mix his personalized cocktails for each customer. Not to mention being able to watch food being cooked over a pit and stoves while they sip their drinks. The Tavern has also installed a industrialized Brewery that produces the finest draft ale from its machinery . Gone are the days of dangerous home made ale that might poison someone. Come visit us at Al Khazar, on your left from the Brick building/shop!", ""),
        StaticBook("Crafting tables by Ralm", "Ralmslb", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Craglode's Journal", "brent42817", "I've decided to create a journal about my life in Aegis So far I have bought a home and set up a shop. If your reading this go to my shop! ENTRY 1: Kal'Uruguan was raided by wrath last night He sent a plauge to wipe out the dwarves An elf wanted to join Wrath but the dwarves killed him. All of the dwarves were hiding in the guard HQ while some were locked out. They didn't allow them in because they feared they were infected. ENTRY 2: I have joined the Order of the Sun and Moon They teach that all things good and bad should be equal .", ""),
        StaticBook("Cralt's Journal", "CONORDUDE8", "Terror has fallen upon Al'Khazar now. Death surrounds me, \n The snow falls slowly, and as the lightning is cast upon Galahar, I hide in a small houser My nerves  are tingling, I am aging, My anti-Age curse will dissapear soon. Arcadius has fall en \n With the wandering wizard dead, What is there left. We must defend the last few cities. When the anti-Age dissapears, And Arcadius' Help is gone, I will turn feeble. I will become a Monk of the Daemon Erebus, Or a Druid. \n Entry 2: The Ideas, and the Truth. \nIt is time, I finally know what I'm going to do as my fighting skills fail. I will send the message of Erebus Free, A monk of erebus, The high Priest. the Har'Shareil. \nA Delayed Reaction \nThe other Ascended seem to Be maintaining the Magic of Arcadius. I Will follow the Order of Codrik, Until other problems Arise. Of course, I  plan on picking up new Recruits and such soon. \nEntry 4: The defenders of Shad'Rin YES! It is wonderful, The Apprentice of Arcadius, Shoi, Is maintaining the Magic. I can not Believe It. It is either me or [Kwakamungus] Who is going to be head of the Squad, \"Shadralia\" Which apparently, Is a make believe nation. \nI will try to show my leadership skills, and why I'm Worthy to be in Charge to Codrik. But either way, I will Become second in command, Or top job, So it does not matter. \nThe Build up. \nI have been servicing Codrik to my best Manner. Uncovering our history, Doing jobs,  And finding more Shadow touched. Now, Is my time, I will see all new recruits i Pick up for the Shad'Rin. and Mark them in her", ""),
        StaticBook("Cralt's Request", "CONORDUDE8", "Cralt's request I need a Garb for a wedding, It needs to be fancy, But pratical, Something to fight in. (it's up north) \n It Needs to be a light gray, with a hint of green. And a robe ((if you can, two skins with and without robes.)) I need the Shad'rin Emblem on the front ((Look at Codriks shirt)) And to jog your memory, I haveBlonde hair, and blue eyes, Light build", ""),
        StaticBook("Crazy", "connorr1", "It seems to be as if i was resurected from the grave. My speech isn't doing well.", ""),
        StaticBook("CreatePhoenix - Guild Profile", "calvinnok", "Guild Name: CreatePhoenix \nCreator: Noku (calvinnok) \nGuild Type: Supply Team \nSupplies: Weapons, Food, etc. \nInformation: A little guild that provide supplies to the fronts. As its location is next to a farm, food can be easily produce. Also have free supplies of books, is giving away weapon in front of Headquaters, but free weapon is no longer avalible.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creations", "Jolot", "1. The \"piston\" : a device that when a current is applied will push a block, enemy, or person away from it. \n 2. the sticky \"piston\": a variation of the piston discovered by a slimeball falling on the piston after completion. any block pushed stays attached to the piston. useful for hidden passages.\n 3. The A.A.F.D. (Automatic Arrow Firing Device) : a variation on something i saw called a \"dispenser\". by recalibrating the mechanisms. i found it would fire arrows at the push of a button. not easily mobile but could make for static defenses. \n 4. the \"repeater\". finding that redstone can only be extended so far before the spark can't travel anymore, a little tinkering with redstone torches helped develop a device that allows for the spark to be strenghten and \"Repeated\". by changing the length of the two torches can cause a delay in the repeat. very useful for complex redstone circuits.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creature's that creep and crawl", "Juggernogg", "Chapter 1: \n In this book i will be teaching you how to identify and fight the creature's that roam the night and how to genrelly survive the night. First on our agenda is the creature's that many people call zombies but they also go by the title \"The dead that walk\" or the \"Undead\" these creature's are foul beast's that were once a man who long ago died, and was re-animated to do the work of a \"Mage\" or \"Necromancer\".", ""),
        StaticBook("Creatures of Aegi's", "gombie", "The Creatures of Aegi's", ""),
        StaticBook("Creep", "Juliangonzalez", "Unsteady feet stammered through the forest. Heavy panting ensued as his lungs desparately  begged for air. He was so far lost there was no hope of finding help. \n What was that creature that woke him in the night? Strange and thin seemingly covered in  grass. It didn't matter now. What mattered was getting as far away from here as possible. He stopped to catch his breath.  His heartbeat had reached his ears and the loud pattern blocked out his hearing. Panic rose as he realized he couldn't tell if the monster was near.  He began to run harder than before out of endless paranoia. Was he ever going to get out of this madness? Just as he found a clearing he tripped over himself and fell into a pool of cold sticky mud. Frustration and fear rose as he twisted about in the mud pool. \n He Laughed outloud at himself for acting so childish. Sighing, he stood up carefully and looked around the now calm forest. He wondered how far he had ran and when the forest had become so beautiful. The monster certainly had to be quite far behind. Just as he seemed to reach a sense of calmness a *crack* of a branch tore through the silence. \n  Turning, the boy saw his fate inching closer. A deafening hiss filled the air and the boy was never seen from again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creep.", "Juliangonzalez", "Testing this book. help", ""),
        StaticBook("Creeper Hunting", "Ken_Brandon", "The reason I made this book is that so pelople will stop complaning about getting attacked by creepers and start killing them. \n Creeper hunting is also the fastest way to get minas. You get between 20 to 30 per kill. You also can get 0 to 1 coal ores, 0 to 1 coal, 0 to 1 porkchops, 0 to 2 iron ingots, and 0 to 2 iron ore. \n Now the part you've been waiting for. I'm gonna tell you how I hunt them. This doesn't mean that your way is wrong, (unless you get killed) it just means that I'm gonna tell you how i did it. \n First, find a creeper. Then, run up to it and hit it with a sword. Run back, and wait for it to stop hissing. Repeat until it's dead. \n Now that you know how to quickly kill creepers, profit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creeper Hunting Guide", "Ken_Brandon", "The reason I worte this book is so that pelople can lose their reason to complain about creepers. First, let's describe them. They have no arms, 4 clawed feet and are colured green. The only sound they make is a hissing noise that they only make before they explode. Their explosion is equal to a explosion from a single block of TNT. \n Now you know how they look, it's time to learn how to fight them. First, find a creeper. It can be in daylight or night because creepers don't burn in the day. Then, if you are using a bow shoot it until it's dead. But, if your using a axe or sword, it's a little harder than that. For swords and axes, you run up to the creeper and hit it once and only once because usually it explodes before you can hit again. Then you run backwards until it stops hissing. Run up to the creeper and hit it again. Repeat until it's dead. The best thing about creepers is their loot. they can drop up to 2 iron ingots, 2 iron ore, 1 porkchop, 1 coal, 1 coal ore, and you can collect between 20 and 30 minas. \n If any of this information is incorrect or bad, please conntact me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepers; The Camoflauged Bomb", "Lord_Kashi", "The 'Creepers' as the people of Oren call them, are large green monsters with no arms, but very powerful legs. They will batter you to aid the other monsters, but will not kill you themself. However, if they feel they are losing the battle, Creepers will detonate themselves, killing both them and you. This explosion will destroy a substantial area of land around them, though stone and obsidian seems to be fairly resistant to the explosion, the latter more so. Somtimes Creepers will just sneak up on you out of the wild grass and explode, if they have no backup. The explosion will be made even more violent if the Creeper is charged up, so Undead Mages will often strike them with lightning in order to charge them up. I believe gunpowder to be the source of this explosion, as Creepers can drop a large quantity of it when the are killed without exploding. Creepers have a small delay between starting up the explosion process and actually exploding, so if you hear a 'ssssssssss' the run as fast as you can...", ""),
        StaticBook("Creppy Man", "henrya15", "This explain my story, I was knocked on the head and forget every thing about myself . if found please return to warden caden my master here me no slave just not smart here", ""),
        StaticBook("Criminals", "FishFr0g", "Dont let criminals in   Criminals: Algor , Cripson", ""),
        StaticBook("Crimson Vale", "coconuta", "Location: Crimson vale is located where the ruins of snowyfields used to be. \n \n Defences: Crimson's defences are few, but strong, it has large towers around the walls and a moat filled with lava to protect it from the sides \n \n State: It is in a ruined state as of this date, irba 18th of the second seed, 1326 \n \n Purpose: Crimson was built to fix up the land, and re build oren towns in the north \n \n History: The town  was infiltrated alot, used by undead to harrass people, now in its looted state, the undead have gone, but its lord juvens has also gone \n \n This ends my report on crimson vale -Rio", ""),
        StaticBook("Critters and Creatures", "Hwaldar", "This book is merely a catalog of different Creatures,which exsist in Aegis \nSkeletons: Undead skeletons are normally raised by Magic They normally use Bows to attack passing by travelers Use caution when traveling in darkness \nZombies:Undead People,which are normally raised by Magic. They normally do not use weapons against travelers. Travel with caution at night or in dark places.Carry a Torch. \nCreepers:Most likely a rare spawn of Orcs,which lives in Sulphur caverns. They are to be avoided at all costs,since they can explode. Creepers,unlike Undead,do not use weapons,nor burn in sunlight. \nSpiders:Overgrown,Magic-Imbued vermin. They are quite fast,and are able to climb walls which is why the best way to kill them is with a Bow. \nPigs:The Main Source of meat. They are not aggresive at any point but if struck by a lightning,they may transform... \nChickens:A perfect source of Feathers and Eggs. They cannot become aggresive at any point. \nCows:Cows provide two useful materials:Milk and Leather Be aware,as Milk is rather alcoholic. \nSquids:Squids are water animals,so you won't find them in forests or mountains They are a perfect source for Ink \n --------------- \nFor more catalogs,contact Hwaldar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crminals", "FishFr0g", "Criminals dont let them in. Criminals: Algor (( williewonka01 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Crowe's Journal #1", "Juggernogg", "Today i ran into ArcanMage_Slayer he said he may be taking student's in to learn about magick i will have to keep him in mind if i wish to travel down the road of a mage. I also roamed around seeking for a shop or a house to buy with kaine, we plan on starting up  a bakery franchise, slowley growing one shop at a time it will be a good income that is if kaine dosent eat all the food \n I joined Holmes it is only a temporey movement until i can get back on my feet again one day i will open a massive franchise and forget all my troubles it will be a good day any way it is off to laurelin for some buisness i will continue this after that.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crowley Falos Journal 1340", "XSilverWolfX", "Kamees, 19th of The Deep Cold, 1340. I.... I don't know what to say. I have lived in Winterfell for over 20 years. My estate has always been home to me, and in more recent years, my family. Now...... I sit here... in the rain.. watching the Winterfell I once knew, being turned into ruins..... by the undead. For the first time in over 20 years.... I don't know where to go.... where to take my family! If I stay here.... my family will surely be destroyed. No... I will take the coinDoin sword and my family with me to the rest of the VonSchlitchen House. Atleast.... I know my wife and..... barely one year old son will be safe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crowley Falos's Journal Part 2 \"A new day\"", "XSilverWolfX", "I woke up to a  beautiful morning. The birds were chirping and the sun was rising. Today was the day I would travel farther North than ever before. Farther than Crimson Vale, farther than Casteline.", ""),
