        StaticBook("defending a castle", "danielbreen", "ok its easy to defened a castle but how to make a defendable castle is hard first a good castle must have strong outter walls with turents ment to hold one man per station these turrents must also be big enough for your archer to shoot out of but no so big that it makes your men easy tagets the walls should be made about 5 m thick and 6 m tall making it hard to go over or throu through so after you have made that you need to make it defendable first make a lege on the outter bit of the wall 1 m tall then add another 50cm on top of that along the entire wall now add another 50cm every 2m after that is complete add 50cm blocks directy next to the turrents so that u can steap up onto it for a better view or to shoot arrows since the wall is rasied up it is hard to see the defenders from out side when they arent rasied up allowing people to run along the wall with minimal risk of being killed or injured after that you should make a few stair case allowing the movment of your soldiers on and off of the wall then add a few buring oil traps make a stong gate room and then your good to defend the walls on that note of a gate room you want to make it as hard as possible to ener the gate room because if that falls your all dead so good luck with your defending", ""),
        StaticBook("Defensive Building", "Ansh98", "Interesting in defending your land from pesky monsters and caniving thieves? Great!  The Defensive Building Division is perfect for you! The Defensive Building Division takes pride in keeping buildings safe from intruders. \n This Division is reccommended for VIPs and creative minds who think of intelligent traps. Members will mainly build traps and tools to defend threats away from buildings. Dean challenges would mostly consist of traps. \n What do you say?  Do you have the upper hand in traps? Then join the Defensive Building Division and build on!", ""),
