        StaticBook("Descent into Darkness I", "ilikepiefoo", "This is the story of Malin Keshar the man turned Undead. \n Parthyn is a town near the northern borders of Krugmar. Every summer when the mountain passes clear of snow, the orcs raid Parthyn seeking to prove themselves in battle. The townspeople repel the raids but often at the cost of many lives. \n When Malin was 10 a traveling mage sensed magical ability in Malin. His parents arranged for Malin to study in the magical community on the Isle of Alduin. Malin Keshar studied there for eight years but was expelled before finishing his apprenticeship. After being expelled Malin returned to Parthyn. \n Malin returned home in the middle of one of the fierciest raids in the history of Parthyn. During the battle Malin watched his father die to an orcish arrow. The orcs rallied upon the death of the villager's leader but were suddenly repelled by an onslaught of undead creatures. The townsfolk were amazed to see skeletons and zombies pour from the forest to cut down the orcs. Then, as suddenly as they arrived, the undead returned. \n A short while later a robed man emerged from the woods. He said his name was Darken Volk and he was a necromancer in command of the undead who had turned the battle . He said although necromancy is forbidden in the kingdom it was the only way for those on the border to stand against the orc menace. \n Drogan the captain of the guard, said they were thankful for Volk's assistance but they could not take up with a practicer of the dark arts. He would let Volk leave this one time but told him to never return to Parthyn on pain of death. \n Drogan sends most of his soldiers on a mission to attack the retreating orcs before they have a chance to regroup and attack. However an orcish raiding party makes it past the scouts and begins an assault on Parthyn. Malin is charged with the defense of the city. Pressed against the wall he uses necromancy to summon undead to the town's defense. Although he is victorious in battle Drogan banishes Malin for practicing Necromancy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Star", "Ranovak", "The sandstone ruin that looms over today's Serpent's Ridge once served higher purposes than a tower. It was known as the Desert Star, a research center, homing ancient Elven technology and innovations . \n In its earlier years, it served the purpose of a \"Safe Haven\" for Elven scientist and druids. The land, once a lush rainforest, became a mere desert, corrupted by the experiments in the tower. The elves adapted to the new environment, as they were banished from the forest. They were known as the Desert Elves, or Sandkin, as they evolved into something less Elven. The secrets they brought upon the lands created dry, forsaken soil. So forsaken, so unforgiving, taht the land eventually turned on its creators. The exact fate of the Sandkin is unknown, but it is believed an enormous sandstorm swallowed them. \n After many years of silence, the Desert Star became once again active. An explorer found the Desert Star, finding many of its parts to be sealed off, while some remained. It was located it the harshest parts of the desert, Ground Zero of its creation. The explorer decided to make the Desert Star into something important, something useful. He made it a Haven for explorers, safe from the toxic environment, and he enchanted it with glowing powers, so the travelers would be guided toward it. \n After the days of the Desert had past, and the Desert Star became all but forgotten, the desert began to dissolve under the influence of the Druids of Laurelin. Now it is but a forgotten relic in the middle of a lush forest, a cemetary of old, forbidden technologies, which were sealed by ancient, unbreakable magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desmond Bratheal's Guyd to Monsters", "Mrmac23", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Desmond's Calendar", "Mrmac23", "The First Seed \nThe Second Seed \nThe Grand Harvest \nSuns Smile \nThe Amber Cold \n (birthday on 22nd) \nSnow's Maiden \nMalin's Welcome", ""),
        StaticBook("Desmond's Map", "Mrmac23", "On this piece o old paper are reminders o several locations. \nThe Scarlet Queen:   X-1326  Z 190  \nAlkhazar Square: X-1277   Z 103 \nHawk's Hotel: X-1106 Z 114  \n   Alkhazar Docks: X-1352 Z 103 \nFishing Spot: X-1016 Z 153 \nAncient Pirate Ship: X-1732 Z 100 \nThat House I Want: X-1294 Z 197 \nLykos' Hut: X-1024 Z 1021", ""),
        StaticBook("Devotion", "Elite117", "Devotion is hard. But it's damn well worth it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Devtraven", "StrifeOr", "The Negativia is a secret network of mages dedicating their lifetime studies on eternal life. The master of the network, Enphermes Dioxidize, is the only human to switch bodies for eternal life, often using his own students as his vessels until they rot awat. They are a dangerous organization, hell-bent on gaining eternal life and eventually taking over the world as we know it . Their religeon is mostly Satanic, often doing rituals to transfer their masters soul to another vessel . The ones used in the ritual are condemned to suffer eternally for their masters transgressions.   Some of the members are slaves from villages that they ransacked, and are usually the sacrifices. ----RITUAL------------ ----------- Rituals usually take place on a waxing gibbous moon. The needed ingredients for the soul release potion are 64 units of rotting flesh, 64 units of redstone, and a diamond. They forcefeed the slave,which releases their soul . Occasionally, the members may rape or torture the soon-to-be victim. [edit The Negativia is a secret netowrk of mages dedicating their lifetime studies on eternal", ""),
        StaticBook("Diabola Adorus", "Willizl33t", "Diabola Adorus, more commonly  reffered to as \"The Brethren\" is not a clan, it is no guild, it is infact the true religion of Aegis. \n \n For you see, Aegis is a lie, it is not a place of purity like it once was. It has been corrupt, this is no secret, however, it is not Iblees that has corrupt it, no, it is infact the living, the Elves, Orcs, Humans and Dwarves alike. For they have grown greedy and war hungry. However there is still a chance for redemption! Join us, join Diabola Adorus, and help us cleanse the world. \n \n We must not be rash, do not go around attacking random people, instead, help them to see the truth, enlighten them infact, let them see they are following the wrong God and by doing so it is THEY who corrupt the world! At the moment there are few of us, but together we can grow, and by doing so cleanse the world of this \"God\". Let him be forgotten! \n \n If you will open your eyes for a few minutes, you too will see the truth. If you join us, when the time comes, you will be rewarded, and those who did not join us will fall! Think about it, don't fall for the lie that is current, cleanse the world, don't corrupt it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diamond Slots, How to Play", "Lomaticc", "1. Place your bet.  25 Minimum, 1000 Maximum \n(/money pay PlayerName Ammount) \n2. Wait for red torch to light up \n3. Hit the slots button to activate Diamond Slots game. \n4. three items will pop out corresponding to the PAYOUTS \n2x Cobblestone = You Lose \n3x Cobblestone = You Lose  \n3x ? = 10 Minas \n2x Iron = 25 Minas \n2x Gold = 50 Minas \n2x Diamond = 100 Minas \n3x Sandstone = Payback \n3x Iron = 2x Bet \n3x Gold = 5x Bet \n3x Diamond = 10x Bet \nEvery Cake = 10 Minas \n \nOnly at The Oceans Casino! Located Between Kal'Urguan and Kramaroe on the King's Road!", ""),
