        StaticBook("Disuise Characters", "indy58", "Mercenary Milgius: \n Age:25 \n Job:Mercenary \n Backstory: \n He was once in a job at a blacksmith as an apprentice.He had an accident and was angry at his Teacher for not telling him how to use his hammer properly. His hand was broken, but ironic as it is,he now has the best sword hand in the Whisper Isles, his home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Doc's Life Manual", "doctordemento", "First thing you have to know is if you dont know the awnser the awnser is 42. If your lucky the person willget the referance and write you of as a funny person. Of corse this is my first rule of Business relations. Second rule: Be generous to peoploe when you first meet them (or to people who are low on cash) The reason you want to do this is that YOU NEED A GOOD REPUTATION! A good reputation is IMPARATIVE in business relations, it may let you haggle that little extra bit or even save your ass in bad situations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Document #1", "Plizga123", "The tests are complete. A possible target could be the stone golem. He seems to be a nuisance. contamination has begun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Documentation of Ascended Skirmishes with the Undead", "Brokencrowe", "Waves of fire covered the sand as the Undead fortress came into view. Ascended clashed valiantly with the Undead forces. Lightning rained down from the heavens above; the sky void of storm clouds. The skirmish ended as the light drained from the sky and sun fell beneath the horizon. The Ascended pulled back to a hill overlooking the fortress. They were slightly shocked by the increasing strength of their Undead adversaries. Uncertain of what to do next they spoke to the amassing group, their expressions grim. A sudden sense of sorrow swept across the crowd; eyes were downcast, and weary. The battle had been taxing for all, but the skirmish had been worthwhile. It gave the Ascended valuable information: a good gauge of strength of the Undead. Moments later, as everyone was packing up and getting ready to leave this field of death, stray lightning bolts blasted the sand all around their feet. Causing waves of fire to once more spread across the land; ash fell like snow. The corpses were all consumed by fire. Undead, Ascended, Orc, Human, Elf, Dwarf, alike, the fires weren't biased. \"The Prophet! The Prophet is here!\" One of the onlookers shouted, and pointed to the top of the fortress, as the lightning faded. The sun rose above the field, as the sweltering flames dimmed to embers. Atop the fortress with a golden staff held high above his head, a masked man could be seen standing, gazing out across the battlefield. The healers were all busy tending to the wounded, and an eerie silence filled the air. As the last flames died down, the Ascended healer stood up, and brushed off her robes. \"They've grown stronger,\" she remarked, her face almost expressionless. -Joma, 19th the second Seed, 1320. .", ""),
        StaticBook("Dolir ((monkeychez)) [account Balance 5000] has paid 650", "Shadowninji", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Dolir's Big Book Of Cake", "monkeychez", "When the world was created, many things were brought into the world such as cows, pigs, chickens... And the many races of Aegis. People combined these things to create many other things. Be it wheat into bread, stone into tools, or eggs, wheat, and sugar into cake. Cake was an invention that was brought into the world by God himself. It has been disputed that Iblees accidentally brought it here with his wrath, or that Aeriel brought it as a gift for the people of Aegis. But whichever way you believe this sweet desert came from, it is a wonderful survival food. The Undead use it in wars, and for downtime, while the very lazy Ascended always have it. In my opinion, i believe Iblees brought it to this world for the Undead and Iblees' followers to enjoy. But hey, thats just me.... Undead Suprise \"Chocolate\" Cake Recipe: 2 Eggs                 2 buckets of ale            3 pieces of  wheat Pour the ale into a bowl, crack the eggs into the bowl, and add the wheat while stirring. Bake at 360 degrees in a furnace. Enjoy your cake of doom! Aeriel's Enlightenment Cake Recipe: 2 Buckets of milk, 2 eggs and 3 wheat. Cook in furnace at 20 degrees for 3 days. Enjoy! Thank you for reading my book! THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Dolir's Life in Al'Khazar", "monkeychez", "Day 0: It has recently come to me that perhaps i should record my times here in Al'Khazar, possibly the busiest city in Aegis now that i'm here so often now. I have rented a room from Dawn, not too bad of a price, and pretty roomy. I wonder what tomorrow will bring? Day 1: This is very odd! In Al'Khazar, it is snowing! The bay is covered in a thick sheet of ice, and the bakery has a blanket of snow covering it. Time to take out my old mittens and coat. This actually isn't too bad. I like the bustle, and the new weather as well! Day 2: I found some old string, and rigged together a nice fishing pole. I think i'll get some fish to eat and trade from the frozen bay today.... Day 3: I had a wonderful day of fishing yesterday! Today i'm doing some rennovations to my room at Dawn's bakery, giving me a bit more space where i need it. So far it looks pretty good! Day 4: Met up with Nailena today. Shes a wonderful girl... Has a strange addiction to enderpearls, though. Anywho, i guess we'll do some fishing, and go from there. Oh, and theres some severe talk about an apparent attack from the Orcs on Al'Khazar.... Hmm.... Anyway, Nailena is taking a nap for now, we'll see what tomorrow brings us. Day 5: Its been quite a while since i've last wrote. Nailena died, and i swear her ghost came to see me. I was in the ruins of the church from the battle. Al'Khazar has seen beter days, indeed... Day 6: I stuck upon luck! 2 Stacks and 13 extra blocks of diamond! I also found... 3 stacks of gold blocks! This will help me dearly in my dreams to open a shop that offers enchantments as well as a variety of potions. Day 7: Business has been slow today. I sold 10 gold blocks to the Druid store across from Dawn's Bakery for a fair price of 7,200 minas. I have plenty of rarities left over to continue my selling.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dolir's Trial Journal", "monkeychez", "In my day, i have gone through many things. Please exscuse the old Dwarf like context, but it is true. I was once Ascended, but now i follow Iblees. I was hoping to be pure, and help those in need, but the Ascended misguided me more than a lost wolf pup. So here i am, preparing for the final piece of my trial... Showing my worth to Iblees, and The Undead. The fourth trail has been told of by many, and i believe i have filtered the truths, and lies from the bunches of voices. The trial begins with a small agility course, easy enough for a Dwarf as long as you have the will, and strength to make it cliff to cliff. If you can succeed from there, you move onto a series of questions... I suggest you prepare for anything, but you must know the lore of the Undead, and of the Fallen One to succeed. If you fail, you will recieve another chance when the Undead deem you worthy... (( 2 Days )) And if you succeed in the question section, then you make it to the final leg of the race... The maze... I have only heard stories of it. Apparently, it is a maze like any other, with a twist that can either aid you, or lead you to failure. There are signs in this maze, and you must listen to the right ones to make it to the end... To pass this, as well, you must know of Undead and Iblees related lore... I am in the works of retaking the fourth trial, due to a foolish answer. And if i do pass, i will go to the Undead ceremony to be judged, and see if i am worthy to Join the ranks of the Undead, to aid in the Fallen One's revenge...", ""),
        StaticBook("Dolir, the Ascended.", "StandUnited", "Dolir, one of the many peaceful Ascended that inhabit the world of Aegis. Doli lives a great life, full of peace, tranquility, and peace. His only strive in life, is to spread peace, and destroy those Undead fools. Dolir lived in a family of miners, they were skilled in the art, and were very famous. They were all killed in a mining accident, and only Dolir survived. Thus, his nickname, Dolir the Deathless. Dolir made is living on, mining of course! Just like his ancestors. He gathered enough cobble to build the walls of Kal'Urguan! With his amazing task, he got the job of Foreman of uilding, and an overseer. Dolir was appointed Overseer of Building by the new King, Charles Grimlie Dolir was honoured, he wanted to do more, he extended Kal'Urguan, and built towers. So that the city would be alerted of Undead attacks. Dolir was very tired, he could barely work, he then decided to wander Aegis. He examined its beauty, especially Laurelin, where he bought his first house. He then traveled to the beautiful Ascended city of Haven. Where he helped on creating their \"white road\" After many hours of gruesome work, an Ascended Sage, by the name of Sue, offered him somethih He asked Dolir if he wished to be an Ascended, Dolir had no second thoughts. He agreed immediately. Now, Dolir lives a life of Peace, he helps filling Haven's library, building. And spreading the peace, that Aegis rightfully deserves. The End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dom's notes on the battle against the bandits", "Domainoft", "The battle against the bandits will take place on the first day of Winters Chill the Dwarves will lead the assult at the main gates, along with the Aeguls above. The humans lead by the very Princess that was attacked will storm the west wall. the wizard has sanctioned our force to demolish the keep and leave no survivors. our forces will gather at the druids grove to the south before the attack to prepare .......................... To Everyone the man known as Sparrow is not to be harmed,", ""),
        StaticBook("DoMA: Ancient History", "iBurn", "Although the Life Mother is just a spirit that inhabits the World, this wasn't always the cas e. It is told that she once had a psychical form, a women. Most likely the wife of Malin, as he, and his elves \"were the first to create a tongue and be gin to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\" Along side with her help no doubt. Who better to decide what the World's nature shall be name d, then Mother Aegis herself. When she died, instead of her spirit returning to God, both her body a nd spirit was returned to the World.", ""),
