        StaticBook("Dose who work wit undead.", "deavs", "Dose who work wit dah undead. Dese skah nub worship Ibilees, dey just 'elp 'im for dah quick Mina. ASH: GORAIM: Dis Goraim be 'un of dah triksy sort, but 'e can be reasoned with... If lat 'ave dah minas of course. 'e is a dwarf who likes to wear a black robe wit red trim. Works fo' Wrath. Is a squad leada' TWO: KANE: Crazy twig with red eyes an' blonde 'air. Works fo' wrath. 'ad a bounty on 'is 'ead in Galahar. Nub be reasoned with. THREE: LUCAS BLACK: Dis 'uman affiliation wit dah undead is complicated. I ash thought dat 'e was a minion, den I thought 'e was in dah Black 'and. But den I realized dat 'e isn't part o' dah undead at all. Maybe 'e does dis fo' minas, but I nub tink so, 'e is nub common criminal. Dis guy gets around. 'e 'as been mentioned or been in, almost every undead-followa group I've seen. If lat could capture 'im. Lat whould know almost everytin dat lat could know about undead. 'e is a 'uman with White 'air, a red eye, an' is mage. ?", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragga", "c_h_r_i_s121", "She not tell me much about herself today, but she look botiful,  she had dark red skin, like me, and long black hair . She was wearin a brown dress wid a gold clip a lot like mine. I pray to her again today, she say she from San'har but i dont belive 'er  . I think she from where i from, far west but i duno i keep prayin'. Aye. she be from Drograk, where my clan from ,but why she keep comin' to me!? i tink she 'bout to tell me er story! She wasnt born in Drograk, she was born in San'har, but she had red skin he' parents leave er' in wilderness but she strong so she keep goin' until she find a town. She pass threw a town and heard a rumer bout a redskin clan in Drograck she say it was a long journey but she determined to get some where she would be accepted . Durin' her journey she face lots of monsters but she had no weapon so she use her fists, and her head she make dem follow dem into a cave where she set up lots o' traps den she would finesh dem off wid a single punch to da temple, she did nock da heads off of skelatons She journey for 43 days an' 43 nights on da 43rd night she finaly reach Drograck and was greeted by other red orcs eventually, when she got da power in da clan she produced an army and tore every place apart until she find her parents , eventualy, after destroying many camps and towns she find dem but dat was when she found out, herparents were 'eumens. she threw her golden pin in da ground an ran off. an she was never seen again until she come to me when i pray i will need ta figure owt what dis golden pin means...", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragnork", "_Player_2_", "My name be Dragnork, a dark green orc with black eyes and a beard. They called me \"Natures Gift\" when i was found by orcs, i was only 5 but they told me \"get in the arena, prove yourself, show them you are orc!\" so they put me up against a man with a rusty sword, he was about 10 times my hight had a scar on one eye and the other glowed red he swung his sword at me but he would miss every time, i finally saw my chance and i pushed him into a cactus, he started to scream in pain as the crowd was cheering, after the fight everyone told me that, i was a true orc. I lived amongst my orc brothers till about the age of 17. \n I left the orcish lands, in order to travel and find meaning in my life i believed to find \"peace\" it was to become one with nature, so i tried to learn every bit about it, so i can understand why things happen, i saw all kinds of animals and trees. Visted nations and explored new islands, came across land consumed by darkness, I never had a house ,nature was my home, i would sleep out on the grass and eat apples and meat. I felt like nature accepted me, like i was becoming one with nature, it would shelter me and feed me, clean me and raise me. \n I returned to the Orc land when i was about 100 years old, most of the people there didnt know who i was and called me \"soft skin\" or \"fresh meat\" when i knew more about the land then any of them but i was paitient and calm. \n My Death was a cruel death, i was captured by 5 humans who said i will be excuted for my fathers crimes, they surrounded me with sharp edged, stainless swords, i never knew what my father did, or if he was still alive but i had to protect myself, so i pulled at my fathers sword, the only thing he left behind, when he left. I used my fathers sword killed 5 of them humans but i was badly wounded, and ended up bleeding to death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragon Encantation", "Thaddeus12", "en li bone and stick beef the esence of powder AND LAST A DRAYGON BONE", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragons", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "A Dragon is a Legendary creature, with serpintine or reptilian traits. Although seeming rather beast-like, Dragons are intelligent, capable of speech and comprehending other languages. Their language can be used to cast spells by Dragonborn, half-dragon humanoids. Dragons are considered to be near extinction, but that has always been the case, until more showed up later on. \n It is rumored that a human once befriended a dragon, and it allowed him to ride on it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragonspeak", "DecoLamb", "\nAi: a \nVar: Hail/Hello/Hi \nKahim: You \nKahir: They/Them \nVai: Me \nLairo: Dragon \nNa: No \nYae: Yes \nHailo: The word used to describe the bond between dragonborn and dragon. \nYairn: Light \nKairn: Dark \nJux: Good \nFaren: Bad \nQueel: Evil \nJael: Good (reffering to alignment) \nTaaok: Found \nJair: Lost \nUrak: Pain \nEn: Of \nWaryn: Protect \nGar: Him \nHar: Her\nHar: Her \nBair: Attack \nIngtah: Dead \nNair(a): Sir/Madam, a term used to show respect, for example when addressing a superior you would call them Nair (if male) or Naira (if female) \nLair: Home \nGarn: Human \nOrak: Orc \nAcro: Elf \nDranuk: Dwarf \nXaryx: Egg \nNar: Fire \nDagnir: Bane \nJael Kae n: Ascended \nQueel Kae n: Undead \nDaes: Shadow \nVarei: Go \nKarei: Stop \nHyn: It \nGarahain: Danger/Dangerous \nKazny: The term used for the child who inherits their parents egg. \nFen: Are \nDariek: Perhaps \nFarak: Should \nKhad: Too \nHan: Is \nVaranai: Crowded \nNaram: Luck/Lucky \nMakta: See \nLayas: Leave \nKaibgan: Friend\nKaibgan: Friend \nKaway: Foe \nAno: What \nAresal: Weapon \nSio: Who \nIto: This/Is \nGrammar\n:Grammar: undo undo \n \n \nIt is worded the same as English and can be intertwined with it, like Orcish and Elven. \nShowing different meanings: \nr: Shows possession I.e. to say your it would be Kahim r. Mine would be Vai r. \n n: Makes plural \n z: Shows sarcasm", ""),
        StaticBook("Drans Notes", "drangob", "annoying, gave a creeper some gunpowder and it blew up on me. Made the road Found Dalfares cave home.. looks riversidey", ""),
        StaticBook("Draort Founders", "Dalejin", "Founded in 358 of the 2nd Age by Sacon and Sakiram Kal'Tahar. The Twin Brothers of the War of Brothers. It was during the war that their villages of the Silver Valley were destroyed that they realized the need for a central gate into the valley, thus was the creation of Draort.", ""),
        StaticBook("Draort, Volume I", "Dalejin", "Itnam, 16th of Snows Maiden, 1323 \nMonths passed since Dalejin journeyed out into the wilderness, and the chronology came to be recorded within this tome. It was on this day that he began to take note of the building, laying of the foundation of this glorious city. His efforts have yielded much to his dedicated manner. Having estableshed the basis of the High Dragon's Keep and the ramp that led up to the ramparts of the citadel. He now feels as if there is hope for this city to prosper and grow. He has been joined in the taming of these harsh lands by Malbak, an orc, who he met when attending a recent wedding in Al'Khazar. King Perea after the 12 day siege on Alkahzar gave his blessings to the High Dragon Lord to commence the rebuilding of Draort on Ahad, 22nd of The Deep Cold, 1324", ""),
        StaticBook("Draygo <3", "ViolettaUnicorn", "I wuv him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dreaming my Life Away - Cataris conDoin", "Archmage_Cataris", "When I want you in my arms \n When I want you and all your charms \n Whenever I want you, all I have to do is \n Dream \n \n When I feel blue in the night \n And I need you to hold me tight \n Whenever I want you, all I have to do is \n Dream \n \n I can make you mine, taste your lips of wine \n Anytime night or day \n Only trouble is, gee whiz \n I'm dreamin' my life away \n I need you so that I could die \n I love you so and that is why \n Whenever I want you, all I have to do is \n Dream \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Drehk's Dairy", "TotalMan", "Day 1 I just go in the Guardians fort I was recruited. I'm meeting new people already, there haven't happend anything yet. I have finally finished seeing the whole fort. I'm now thinking about geeting my stuff from my little hut. hi I finally got all my stuff to the fort! Day 2 I was looking over the walls of the fort there is not really happening anything maybe I will try go to Al'Khazar for buying gear . \nday 3 I didn't go I wanted to be sure that I wouldn't miss an attack, I also heard that the dwarven king were about to get married! I'm not sure where the Dwarven city lies but I could find out . \nDay 4 \nI did go to the wedding with Blundermore but we were late... really late. When we got there it had ended! But not only that the undead was attacking! Me and Blundermore had heard some thunder on the way to the wedding but didn't think the Dwar ven city was about to get attacked! \nDay 5\nI was on my way to the fort after I had brought some stuff in Al'Khazar, on the way", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_8(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Dreticus's Journal", "backup_fruit", "We found some books in a home we raided earlier, going to keep a journal of events from now on. We stumbled upon an empty fortress, strangley with all doors open . We finally set up a house and are waiting through the night. Weve got an old friend moving in, Ban'Mor. Im quite excited. Today, a new floor was added to the house. It's real nice. I have been feeling really tranquil about my solidarity from society, so thats a plus. Ahh, fresh new day with a sunrise and the snowy landscape. I woke up to some bread and the sunrise. Life is good. I've added four more rooms on the sides of the house. With a new friend moving in, we have just enough rooms for everyone. I'm hoping to expand even more. Today, we found loads of clay. It's cookring as a write this. erase' delete", ""),
        StaticBook("Dretus' Journal", "Pravino", "Me bought a new zult. It be made out of diamond. It very strong and me need to train wiv it. Me go huntin every night. Me now a master swordsman. Me still gonna train. Me want to be faster and stronger den all me brudahs. Me also is now 9ft. Me is very bubhosh. Me dunno why me so big doe. It doesn't make any sense to me. Me writin is improvin. Me really needs a wolf. If me had a wolfie me could be respected. Me has to hunt now.", ""),
        StaticBook("drinktest", "TheRedNinja", "Drinklist 1 2 \n 1 \n 22", ""),
        StaticBook("Drown My Sorrows", "Slayer15855", "Drown My Sorrows \n \n \n \n \n Transcribed by the Arcane Mage \n He studied the parchment; a crudely drawn map had been brought to him with various obvious landmarks and a red X in the North Eastern portion of the map next to what looks like the old ruined watchtower. He asked for Sir John Hales to gather some of the Nords, Sir Arthur and Jimmy Lockheart, the Adventurer. Samuel Bealcrest stepped into the hall with his Nords closely behind, Sir Arthur and Jimmy lagging behind; wiping off the snow from their shoulders they all took seats around the long table, muttering to each other. The Nords were quickly silenced when Samuel", ""),
        StaticBook("Drown My Sorrows - Cataris conDoin", "Archmage_Cataris", "When I woke up \n The rain was pouring down \n There were people standing all around \n Something warm falling into my eyes \n But some how I found my baby that night \n I lifted her head \n she looked at me and said \n Hold me darling just alittle while \n I held her close \n I kissed her our last kiss \n I found the love I knew I had missed \n but now she's gone \n even though I hold her tight \n I lost my love, my life that night \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Dante's Recommendation to Ambros By: Sala", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Dante is a close friend of mine, for various reasons. He has done everything I've asked, accepting my requests with kindness and determination. He is a druid, so he knows a bit of magic already, and seems that he could be fitting to the Mage's Guild. Below are things he has done, that I am witness to: \n I was attacked by a group of bandits, soon after talking to you, Ambros. They cut my eyes, because i refused to give them any money, or my things. I blindly walked around Laurelin, recieving help from a few Elves nearby, and was taken to the Druid Grove, where I met Dante for the second time. He needed 2 enderpearls, for I knew not what at the moment, but he supported me as we walked to the mage's guildhouse in Laurelin to retrieve enderpearls i had in my chest. We went back to the Druid Grove after getting them, and he performed some miracle on them, I could not see, so I know not what, but I could feel mass amounts of heat during this time. He took my old eyes out, and replaced them with Enderpearls, thus, I have been given the gift of sight once more. This next act i will speak of, is a simple act of kindness he has done for me. \n \n As I was now a Mage, and because I see you with a staff everytime I see you, i decided that I would create a staff in the future, although I know not how. So I went to the Druid Grove, and Dante was there. I asked him to bless the shaft of what I would use in my staff, and he did so without question. I got to watch him in this process, unlike last time, and he blessed the item I gave him. I took it, and thanked him for everything he had done for me, and was off. \n \n \n \n Dante shows interest in become a member of the Mage Guild, as he has told me. He does not plan to leave the Druids, I don't believe, but he will double-task, both groups at once. I hope this book will at least give you a bit of interest in getting to know this person, or checking up on/observing him. \n -Salamandra", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid of the Quill Olwe Laelithrin's Writings", "WhiteReaper", "This a personal collection of the poems and stories of the Bardic Druid Olwe. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Respiren's Ledger", "Respiren", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Tome", "Respiren", "Every plant contains life's essence, through communion with nature we gain nourishment. It is a wise druid that sees the promise of life in a seed, and life's sweet waters will pour forth from his staff", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid tree book", "animeguy377", "In a grove to the west a chest, a quest perhaps?", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid's Silverspoon", "Respiren", "Mushroom Broth - Take equal measures of brown and red mushroom. heat after mixing in a pultice, best served with old bread , no spoon required.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Axiom", "CrunchySushi", "The seeds of our destiny, are nurtured by the roots of our past.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Encantations :", "shiftnative", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Encantations Vol XVII", "shiftnative", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Encouragement", "Respiren", "The tree lies within the seed, \n and the seed within the tree. \n Be bold! \n By the Gods of Aegis, \n when your body perishes \n you shall be renewed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Journal", "ElynxYon", "Druidic Journal TASK 1: \n Make a staff from a sapling grown yourself. \n Task is complete. \n \n TASK 2: \n Find 32 bones. \n Task is complete. \n \n TASK 3: \n Find a blaze rod for making a brewing stand. \n Task is complete.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Meditation", "mattr41018", "Day 1: I have been sent to meditate on my path to be a druid. I am perched ontop of the talltest tree, Hoping to see some birds... after 2 hours, No contact with anyone... I am begining to doubt myself as if this was a smart decision... I see where i went wrong, I thought this would be easy... it won't be.. I accept that. Maybe i shouldn't rush into it... After about 3 hours... I have lost track of time... no contact. I am begining to forget my own voice. The tree i am meditating on seems to be... talking to me? It keeps saying the same thing \"in, out, in, out, in, out\" I think i am breating WITH the tree... Me and the tree have become good friends... His name is george.. He's nice... He says the birds poop on him too much... And that the skeletons kill to many adventurers on him. he let me build a small hut on his head to protect me from the rain and undead. He also let me use a torch I like george, he has lot's of siblings... They are nice too... I .. hear them.. am i crazy? or maybe... im joining with them! I feel as if now I know why Respiren is seen as crazy.... \n \n Day 2: I slept wierd last night... It was almost as if I was hibernating... Like a bear does. The rain and lightning are still going from last night... The rain and Lightning Stopped going on for hours. \n Day 3: I can't wait to be a druid... I think i might be a seeker druid. I hear deltaro might give up his position... maybe I can have it... Oh well, It is getting harder for me to write... Less talking is happening with me and george , now it is more like telapathic communication... strange... Maybe I will become a druidic tranmutician... If i think hard enough.. I can mae leaves sprout form my arm... the day ended with a bear attacking george... \n Day 4 : I thnik tha my writin is being affected by my telepethid link with georje.. I can't seem to write more than this... ((had a weeding to go to, sorry)) \n Day 5: today was not the same as the others... i experienced... a flash... not the bad kind, but i got an enchanced capacity for knowladge... as if this si my destiny my writing skills are slowly coming back, and instead of hearing just george... I hear all the trees.... huh.. I think... being a druid is the right path for me... I feel the urge to help as the undead attack around me... but i musn't leave my meditation. I was knocked out for sevral hours from a strike of lightning that hit me in my hut... George was caught on fire and burned down... i kept his only seed close to me... \n Day 6: I miss george, we were good friends... I want to find the undead responsible... Butt i can't... I need to sleep... I won't be writing more... \n Day 7: *the text is too scratchy to read but you can make out these words* I... Trees.... Must..... Help.... Need... Magic Power... Too weak.... Tired... Writing slopy. ... crazy... need... think.... done...", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Proverb", "CrunchySushi", "To take in the food native from an area, is to become one with those forces by which its life came into being.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "Lexperiments", "Is this what the druid college is like...? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I'm a druid for some reason... It's as if they're brainwashed. They think I'm an elf, too! I'm a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She's also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe...? I'm just jotting down notes... And my thoughts... And why is htis happening!? So, what do write now. I don't even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I've been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact... It's a magical artifact from Winterfall that the undead want. Now it's in the hands of one, named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It's from the Kar'Lani tribe, and is hidden in the \"fake father of Al'Khazaar\". It's cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books written by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact. \n \n I've been living in Al'Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al'Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went to Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while. But then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of course. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me enough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us or something. He kept on saying we were elves and druids, which neither of us were. Bell's human and I'm a dwarf. And I don't think either of us would want to study druidism after this.... Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it. Er, not it. us. He tried to break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house . We found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I'll go back to Al'Khazaar... but I'll write about the next adventure . \n \n I went to go to Al'Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell's help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell dissapeared. I still don't know where she is. We continued on the path, along with an orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and died. \n \n A while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fun at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits . The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil bandit. It's obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al'Khazaar didn't even notice. He, along with the rest of human royalty, is just STUPID. There's no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn't even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point...no. Untrue. Just untrue. Anyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. veryone thought he was a pale orc, even though he's admitted to be undead many times . The fools... the idiots, the fools... I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead came. He even used the same teqnique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponets. The fools.. no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on... \n \n I would write more about my life, but I realize I just don't know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can't let people know of my feelings or all of my thoughts. That's pretty much all of my life so far that I care to share.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology - What is a Druid?", "Respiren", "Druid are the drui, the dryw, the druwid.\n Nature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower. \n For those that know the oak, the troew is both the tree and the truth. Mysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning master of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender of unspoiled Nature. \n The Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements. All druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the wilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druids", "ShadowGunX", "The Druids have remarkable healing abilities that rival that of the Mages. They can grow anything in an instant. Whether it be a flower, some wheat, or even a tree. They describe it as an art to be attuned to such a level with nature that one might bend it to ones own will.  The Dusk Druid will not give her opinion on mages since she is supposed to be as neutral as possible. \n The Druid Dusk, seems to be very violent. Upon entering the grove, some druids told me that I was lucky she wasn't there. That she would cut out my heart if she was. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Druids of Mother Aegis: The Lore", "iBurn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Drunk", "Hunter55444", "many thinks happen when you are drunk ya", ""),
        StaticBook("Drunken Duck Inn Records", "Lomaticc", "Room001 - WhiteFox1456 (Finlay) \n100m/day - 8/9/11 \n 200m Deposit alright (/shop buy mushroom soup 1)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dryads", "krislove45", "Most people do not know what a dryad is. Some just think it's another name for a druid. It most definitely is not a druid. For those who want a simple explanation, here it is: Dryads are like Druids, but they are more powerful. Of course, there's much more to that. Dryads are really only similiar to Druids by their love of nature. A dryad's life is connected to a special tree or bush. They usually catch a male's eye because of their beauty, but beware. Evil dryads, like those who live in a special forest I've been to recently, use their beauty as a weapon. Their strategy is to flirt with the male, then start walking away, convincing the male to follow them. It usually ends in the males falling into a trap, then killed by a creature of the night. Of course, it'll usually work again. However, not all dryads use their beauty for traps. Some use it to tame partially male creatures that could help them, should a war ever occur. Dryads are not found in Aegis, and are hardly found anywhere other than the forest I mentioned earlier. Dryads are not just very beautiful, but they are also quite good with their weapons and stealth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dues", "Ansh98", "With great power comes great responsibility. Being in the Oasis Crafters is a privilege.  However, you must pay a due. This due is 80 minas a week ((IRL)). Depending on your category, you will pay your Due Collecter your dues. Each category has one Due Collector. The Due Collector of each category receives a small portion of the dues as a salary. DO NOT beg and annoy Deans or founders for you to become a Due Collector. Due Collecters are chosen by preference of the two founders. This concludes this pamphlet.  Build on!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dues paid", "Jr4life24", "This person has paid there taxes this week. From Zod ( Melons have been placed in the wearhouse)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dues paid seal", "hayden34666", "This citizen has paid their weekly due. signed Oren Lt. Hayden (leave this book in the chest)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dulce et Decorum est", "Dalek348", "\nBent double, like old beggars under sacks \nKnock-kneed, coughing like hags, we cursed through the sludge \nTill on the haunting flares we turned our backs \nAnd towards our distant rest began to trudge \nDwarves marched asleep. Many had lost their boots \nBut limped on, blood-shod. All went lame; all blind; \nDrunk with fatigue; deaf even to the hoots \nOf tired, outstripped watchtowers that dropped behind. \nFire, fire! - An ecstacy of fumblimg \nFitting the clumsy helmets just in time; \nBut someone still was yelling out and stumbling, \nAnd flound'ring like a man in fire or lime \n Dim, through the misty fog and thick red embers As under a ruby sea, I saw him drowning. \nIn all my dreams, before my helpless sight, \nHe plunges at me, guttering, choking, drowning \nIf in some smothering dreams you too could pace \nBehind the wagon that we flung him in \nAnd watch the white eyes writhing in his face, \n His hanging face, like a devil's sick of sin; \nIf you could hear, at every jolt, the blood \nCome gargling from his froth-corrupted lungs, \nOf vile, incurable sores on innocent tongues, \nMy friend, you would not tell with such high zest \nTo children ardent for some desperate glory, \nThe old Lie; Dulce et Decorum est \n Pro patria mori. \n  \nA battered old journal scavenged from an ancient war-torn battlefield. \nThis extract from a journal expresses this soldier's thoughts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Duncan amell I,D format", "Lord_Zack", "Name duncan_amell \n: sex:male \n: criminal-history nothing \n: Age 19 \n: amout of time as a citizen one day", ""),
        StaticBook("duncan' book", "Lord_Zack", "well how do i start this book? well let start from the keep. when me and grad got to ravenkee p a guy name zoe up the gate for us. grad ask him if i can be a raven. he said yes. i wanted to be an agent. so zoe to me to the agent base(it is under the keep. if raven keep falls so dos the world", ""),
        StaticBook("Duncan_Amell", "Lord_Zack", "My name is Duncan amell", ""),
        StaticBook("Durack, Victor of Krugmar", "Jerry_Man", "*This book is a restoration of a tattered manuscript that was found during an axcavation of a brigand camp in Krugmar. Details remain in-tact but the broken english has been reworded.* \n \nWe're the most feared bandits in all of Aegis! We don't often do terrible things, that is to say, we don't murder women and children or needlessly burn down villages. There's normally a very reliable excuse. At least most of the time. \nOur boss Durack is a big man. He's suppossed to be part orc but he certainly doesn't have green skin or pointed teeth. He's taller than the rest of us though, he's even a head taller than the Krugmar Warlord: Rex (a name was written but I could not be sure of spelling so have left it out lest I offend orc history).\nThe purpose for writing this is because we all returned to camp from Krugmar today after one of those Arena fights. Durack wanted me to record the day's events. He said that if I made his victory into a world renowned tale people could always remember Krugmar as a broken and humiliated nation. He can't read or write but he weaves words like a twiggy. We normally stay out of Krugmar, but we made a special trip to Sanhar today when Durack promised we'd see some blood and broken bones. \n \nDurack fights with his fists. They're mangled from too many punch-ups and there's fragments of metal and rock imbued in his knuckles. When he steps into the arena his blood red eyes deman all attention.\nHe quickly eliminated every opponent. There were creatures from all over Aegis fighting for that prize money and Durack knocked them all asunder with just his fists. The Arena was a bloodied mess of piled bodies of those too proud to admit defeat, and Durack stood alone in the centre of the ring. He must have been consumed with bloodlust because he still wasn't satisfied. He bellowed at the Rex to come down and face his challenge. No potential Warlord could resist a physical challenge from a human, so all of them entered the ring one by one. All of them fell to the ground.\nThe only Warlord left to face Durack was Rex (I apologise for not providing a name) whose boystrous laughter had now ceased. They fought viciously for hours amidst the deafening roar of the crowd. The Rex, glimpsing his pride at stake, ripped an  battleaxe from the Arena walls and violently swung it at Durack's head. Durack ducked and landed one knock-out punch to the Rex's jaw. The Warlord was felled like a tree, crashing to the ground with an almighty thud.\nDurack stood alone in the arena with every spectator and traveller in Krugmar staring intently upon the rightful ruler of the sand nation. He walked towards the exit, stopping in the gate. He turned to face the audience and gave this speech.\n\"Today you have seen the weakness of Krugmar. You have misplaced your pride and are now left castrated and disgraced at the hand of a pink skin. Krug would be ashamed to see what has become of his people. You have no purpose. Your only desire is to fight to defend your hollow honour. Well, bestow your honour upon one of the rabble in this bloody mess. You are broken Krugmar, and you need to be fixed. Otherwise one day you will be utterly removed from the face of Aegis.\" \n \nWhen I asked Durack about the things he said he described a brightness flooding his eyes and a loosening on his tongue. He said something about experiencing a spiritual moment, as though something wanted to talk through him. \nAnd then we left Krugmar and returned to camp. The celebrations are wild and we are overjoyed to be following the mightiest one in Aegis. \n \n*I doubt there will be any records of this to be found in Krugmar. From what we can tell of the site the brutes suddenly dissappeared or were disbanded and nothing further became of mighty Durack.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dural'Duthnur Construction Instructions", "ZazarusDious", "Keep on getttin' smoothstones for slabs. ((We gonna need alot)) \n Low Priority: Mirror and copy First Platoon barracks to each wing. \n Clear  whats above the gate atleast 20 units high. For tower and future statue. \n Clear whats behind the gate. Market District will be here so next time we together we will beh brain storming on layouts. \n Make more books and book cases. \n Expand de farm to  'ave reeds. \nClean up dog poop. ((dis job is fer Flandre)) \n Start Makin Iron blocks fer hammer for statue(( 45 blocks!)) \n Secure de area and mark caverns dat can beh exploited fer Iron. ((Raghnok I beh countin on ye fer dis)) \n ~Signed by Drazdun Silvermein.~ *Stamped with blue wax and white feather.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dural'Duthur Imported", "ZazarusDious", "1000 Minas has been comissioned te Raghnok. \n For slime 'n' Lapiz.", ""),
        StaticBook("Duralsavot - Suport", "ZazarusDious", "General Wango of de UAC - Geo- Supplies. List in stacks: 4 Dirt 6 R.Stone Slabs 2 Cobble Stone", ""),
        StaticBook("Duralsavot- Gone.", "ZazarusDious", "As I went back te Duralsavot frem de embassy, on de third day o' travel I was pushed back. De winds of magic beh foul. And per'aps those with it be gone now. Te much it beh te much... I 'ave decided to take Akathrash, Winter's Death. Per'aps it was meant te beh. I shed 'ave perished with de rest o' mi clan long ago... Dis final document shall beh de last o de recordin's of Duralsavot. Khezdi, ye be de soul survivor of de Silvermein's now. Live with honor, valor, and wisdom. May de creator guide ye in heart and spirit. Yer ancestors strenght of heart and body.  Theza Ameth will beh wid ye. She knows maneh thin's dat will aide ye. : De blood of Derinthor Silvermein flows to ye. Axes High lass. May ye do yer ancestors proud. :Drazdun Silvermein 11th Generation", ""),
        StaticBook("Duralsavot-Honorstand", "ZazarusDious", "By Drazdun Silvermein \n Duralsavot-Honorstand. Built upon a small floatin' isle I have found in me travels. I fer dinnae its own location te myself. It is a home away frem home, and to those who find it, take care of 'er. \n Blood, sweat and tears went te her construction. Let 'er take care of ye like she did te me. \n I dinnae whenever I will come back to 'er again, but me time 'er endin'. Per'aps one day, I will see what has happened to 'er. Fer de beter or de worse. \n Ged bye, Duralsavot. \n May de Creator bless ye te be a safe-'aven fer all. \n Drazdun Silvermein~", ""),
        StaticBook("Durgrim's Guide", "ljcrzynfree19", "Durgrims th' best.", ""),
        StaticBook("Durin's day", "ForestMaid", "\n The world was young, the mountains green, No stain yet on the Moon was seen, No words were laid on stream or stone, When Durin woke and walked alone. He named the nameless hills and dells; He drank from yet untasted wells; He stooped and looked in Mirrormere, And saw a crown of stars appear, As gems upon a silver thread, Above the shadow of his head. \n The world was fair, the mountains tall, In Elder Days befor the fall Of mighty kings in Nargothrond And Gondolin, who now beyond The western seas have passed away; The world was fair in Durin's Day . \n A king he was on carven throne In many-pillard halls of stone With golden roof and silver floor, And runes of power upon the door. The light of sun and star and moon In shining lamps of crystal hewn Undimmed by cloud or shade of night There shone forever fair and bright. \n There hammer on the anvil smote, There chisel clove, and graver wrote; There forged was blade, and bound was hilt; The delver mined, the mason built. There beryl, pearl, and opal pale, And metal wrought like fishes' mail, Bucklerand corslet, axe and sword, And shining spears were laid in hoard. Unwearied then were Durin's foke; Beneath the mountains music woke : The harpers harped, the minstrels sang, And at the gates the trumpets rang. \n The world is grey, the mountains old, The forge's fire is ashen-cold; No harp is wrung, no hammer falls; The darkness dwells in Durin's halls; \n The shadow lies upon his tomb In Moria, in Khazad-dum. But still the sunken stars appear In dark and windless Mirrormere; There lies his crown in water deep, Till Durin wakes again from sleep.", ""),
        StaticBook("Durin's Log", "bighead201", "Irba 18th of Malins Welcome. After travelling for many weeks and moving from place to  place, My friends persuaded me to write a log. Being a protector of a camp is pretty boring. I hardly have anything to do. \nKamees, 26th of the Second Seed During the last time I wrote and now I have done not so well. I may have many wheat for ale but not the items I need as described in The Art of the Ale by drplat. However I have found some new ingredients that change the taste of said ale. I hope of mass producing this ale for a profit. I will not reveal the steps or ingredients. I have heard a great many things of this camp but none about me. Everyone is so impressed by the seer. Half of them dont relize what I do for the camp. Hunter/protecter is hard work. No one has ever thank me except for the other leaders. One thing no one sees is my art of many things, archery literature axe skills, mostlyliterature. living with the Elves has given me a great understanding of writing. All for now. \nTolta, 24th of the First Seed. We have succesfully moved to the orc capital. DAMN IT! No matter how much it sucks I must not forget to check on my brewing still.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dusk", "Chrome_", "Winter has started and I feel the need to begin reccording my travels. So far I've been all over the Kings Road met many a fine maiden and now I'm in Al'Khazar living off food I get from my travels up North. In fact just before the cold season started I was up north gathering seeds. Sadly seed was my only loot. Now I have alot of it. Hundreds.  In my travels I have come across no maiden more peculiar than that of Julia. When I met her or saw her rather for the first time she was with Princess Idelwheln. I met her again in Al'Khazar in Mr. Therving's tavern. She had no memory of the event. She was engaged to a blue sinned Orc, who will remain unnamed for the sae of privacy.  When I was escaping from the Guard, I ran into the sewer and found Sewer City. However, I'm still cuffed and it's taing lots of time to writhe properly. Sewer City is much nicer than it sounds, it contains shops and housing, all on clean streets. I have sworn to not give the location, and I won't. All I can say is that it's in the sewer. I have reccently learned Throdo has fallen in love with Julia. I don't now what to mae of this. I'm currently traveling the King's Road to Krugmar. Got lost around the Oren Mine, I found a broen tower when it started to rain. I'm going to go as some travellers for direction. The travelers had slashed me across the face, the only reason I'm writing this is because a nice man \"cured\" my vision. I have learned Throdo and his many affairs... Apparently, Throdo has fallen in love with every maiden in Oren and has been rejected. In other news, I have met a niceee Elf while waling around Al'Khazar.  In the case of anyone I love reading this, she will remain nameless. I have also killed a man named Saren. I won't go into detail on that right now . All I can say is that he wanted a book from me. I'm drunk right now, I think I might be a drunkard... I think I'll just drink away whenever life sucks... I'm put... Sorry about the cut off entry, something came up. I'm fighting Throdo soon. I'm drukn tried and blindde. I dnot' thikntihs is comprghehensibely. I thikn THROdo has dnoe something wiuth Jukia... Nowt shure whate. I may as well ptu my will in here... I want Julia to have all my belongings except this book,  and for Throdo to have all my minas . I have a feeling it's the only way he'll get females. A lot has happened since my last journal entry. Most recent would be me getting accepted to the guard, Julia commiting suicide and me meeting a fine young maiden named Riona . Sadly, we haven't spoken face-to-face since a while after we met, the reason being she got a job north. She works for a man named Zyn. I'll have to visit sometime.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dusty Tome", "Cloudheart", "*You are barely able to make out the scratches of info that litter the pages* \n \n To the one who...----...I shall teach. My words, words of the....----...move mountains. My words, the greatest being the ones taught to me by...----..., are the powers between life and death. I must exercise...----...with caution. Without control what I do will surely be uncurable. \n \n - Eindry'el \n \n Entry ...----... \n \n I HAVE BEEN ROBBED! THEY HAVE STOLEN ALL FROM ME! MY VERY CHILDREN! I will teach them for their insolence...for taking WHAT CANNOT BE REPLACED! Upon you all, upon even the seeds I have sown a CURSE! \n \n You will rue the blood you spilt! You desire power? You thrash, as a fool, in defiance of wisdom? YOU WHO, POSING IN THE PLACE OF THE LEARNED, DISRESPECT LIFE ITSELF?! A curse on us all! \n \n   Any Elf from my lineage, from Eindry'el first to Eindry'el last, shall suffer this curse. Upon witnessing the death of a family member, your sin-filled hearts will blacken the very skin you wear. You will be consumed by fear, and agony shall know you! You will have the powers you seek! In your blood, without your knowledge, it will flow freely! But even with your great power, you will not save yourself! The nights will visit you with...----...and your peace will leave. \n \nFear not, though, my faithful children. This curse can be broken, but only by one true of virtue and hands clean of blood. He will be afflicted, without having done wrong, even before his curse. One he cares for will leave him. \n \nOnly then will he save any of you. He will seek the words and power of old and in them be rewarded. But the power will do nothing. Only by giving up what he has earned. What is dear to him. Only by speaking in actions the weighty lesson I want you all to learn, will you be saved. \n \n - Eindry'el the Agonized", ""),
