        StaticBook("Dwarf on the Moon", "dudog", "How did I get here?", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Speechcraft", "jdetterline", "\n The owner of this book has purchased it from Uggg. \n The owner shall from here on out have the ability of Dwarven Speechcraft. \n Dwarven Speechcraft shall in all manner allow you to have Dwarvish accents.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarfen Guard Handbook", "CentralGuard", "Hello there, today i will be teachin everythin to know bein a dwarfen guard at the Kal'Uruan  gates. \n \n Chapter 1: What we do. \n The guards of the gate are here for one job, to guard the gate from any intruder. There are two wings, the north wing (Located closest to the exit door)., and the south wing (Located farthest from the door). the south wing controls people comming into the city. if you are in the south wing you MUST ask why the travalers are here, if they gust say \"let me in\" that does not work. the north wing handles people coming out of the city. When letting people out you do not have to ask why they are leaveing, you can gust let them out. NOTE: if you are in the north wing and have to let somone out and and the south wing is asking why someone is here, dont let them out untill the people coming in are in. Now, if you are working by youreself, you can let people in/out from watever wing  you want. Now if you need to leave for any reson, and you cant find another guard to take a shift, keep the gates closed. \n \n Chapter 2: What to do with an intruder. \n Dealing with intruders is farly simple, but you do have to follow some rules. First off you have to ask if they are a guard, we dont want a civil war here. Secondly if they are not a gaurd, you have to say something like \"Im sorry, but you have to die now\" (ooc: to keep the rp). And thats how to deal with intruders. \n \n Chapter 3: The homes. \n Each guard that works at these gates gets a free 9x9x3 home to call theres, this home is fully  custimisable, you can change the walls, floor, and cealing, without intrudeing on anothers home. The arias on each corner are like \"stalls\" these are not free, if you want you will have to buy it, but you can set up some shops and stuff in them, or we can make public arias for them insted. Each home is connected to a hall, to get out of the hosing aria, and a Cortyard, that is shared by seven other dwarfs (ooc 8 including you).", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven City Greeting", "Sidhion", "Hail, I'm Raban and would like to be let into the city as I live here. Please return this book after reading, thanks", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Guard Handbook", "Mystronghold", "You must read this book before becoming a guard!!!    \n Part 1: Do not let ANY citizens into the guard area. Only let in members of thee High Council, free dwarves army, and thee guards of course . A sign is posted outside where they can't go. If someone goes past that point and says they are a guard, always check the guard index and make sure they are there. If they are not on the list, tell them. If they do not agree, you may have to use force on them. \nPart 2: How to guard. When a citizen approaches, always ask them what they are doing here. A response such as \"just let me in\" or \"open the gates\" are not acceptable, so don't let them in. A good answer would be \"i have a home here\" or \"I have a job here\", Just use common sence when letting people in to the city. Always keep tha' gate open when you are going off duty. You may let citizens out when they want to leave, but if there is someone who wants in, make sure you ask what they are doing here, then the person may leave. \nPart 3: Pay All guards will be payed IRL hour. The Head Guard Stronghold will tell you how many hours did you go on guard duty. Rookies get paid 30minas per IRL hour. Regular Guards get paid 50minas per IRL hour. Officers get paid 70minas per IRL hour.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Guard Handbook", "skinner452", "You must read this book before becoming a guard! \nPart 1: Do not let ANY citizens into the guard area. A sign is posted outside where they can't go. If someone goes past that point and says they are a guard, always check the guard index and make sure they are there. If they are not on the list, tell them. If they do not agree, you may have to use force on them. \nPart 2: How to guard. When a citizen approaches, always ask them what they are doing here. A response such as \"just let me in\" or \"open the gates\" are not acceptable, so don't let them in. A good answer would be \"I have a home here\" or \"I have a job here\". Just use common sence when letting people in to the city. Always keep tha' gate open when you are going off duty. You may let citizens out when they want to leave, but if there is someone who wants in, make sure you ask what they are doing here, then the person may leave. \nPart 3: Pay. All guards will be payed 50 minas per IRL hour. You must work an entire hour to be payed. Tell King Belin if you have worked for an hour, and you will get payed as soon as possible.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Guard Index", "Mystronghold", "ALLOW ALL HIGH COUNCIL MEMBERS INTO GUARD HQ \n \n King Algrim, Archbishop Thordon, Highmerchant Skaeyne, Lord Baron Xavier, Grand Master Of The Smith Gotrek, Grand Master Architect Lukas, Lord Marshall Thorik Braveaxe , Head guard Stronghold \n Guard Officer Flynn, Guard Officer Broski, Guard Officer Goldbeard, Guard Bob, Guard Orik, Guard Gragon, Rookie Guard Bravo, Rookie Guard Zack,", ""),
