        StaticBook("Edwin and The Wench", "HarrisonBitzis", "NARRATOR: This is the tale of Edwin, The Traveling Mercenary from the north This is a story of Tragic happenings, Insane Fights, and Devilishly Handsome Woodsmen Now.... Our story begins in the streets of Al'Khazar...... help He Heard the words loud and clear It was a woman. She was trapped under a heavy log of a burning Building Edwin Couldnt resist, and Ran to help the woman. Edwin ran in, Greeted by a Elderly lady. ELDERLY WOMAN: Help! My daughter is in there! Please! EDWIN: Dont worry, Ma'am. She will be fine. NARRATOR: He went to pick up the log trapping the woman. He put in great effort, But couldnt lift the Log. He Cried for help, only to be greeted by gagging and coughing. There was too much Ash. Then, A man in a cloak walked in. PREACHER: This happened for a reason....... You all must listen. I...... am a man who controls things..... Events.... I made this happen NARRATOR: The preacher then faded into the Background EDWIN: I need help! Help, Gaurds! IRIS: No.... Its fine..... NARRATOR: Despite the ash and Smoke, She spoke Beautifully. EDWIN: I promised I'd get you out of here, and I will. OREN GAURD NO.1: Sir, You need help! Steven, Go get that log! Warren, Get the Girl! OREN GAURD NO. 2 and 3: Yessir! NARRATOR: And with that, The wench was saved. Afterwards, she went to thank Edwin IRIS: um.... Hello.......... Are you the man that saved me? EDWIN: I didnt save you. The gaurds did. IRIS: You called them...... Thank you. IRIS: *kisses Edwin on the cheek* EDWIN: It... It was fine. NARRATOR: For the next year or so, Iris worked as a lowly wench. She still Saw Edwin, But very rarel y but one day.... a strange hooded man appeared in the bar Iris worked at. Edwin was sitting at the Table, Staring into Iris' Eyes. He spoke, With A cold voice, fiercer then any undead..... WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Hey. You. at the bar. \"Points ad Edwin\" You look like you can take a fight EDWIN: What if I can........ WILL THE HUNTSMAN: I need your help. My villiage of hunters has been burned. ... I need help with it EDWIN: Whats in it for me? WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Come outside and Ill tell you. NARRATOR: They walk outside the small bar, and He explains WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Okay. You obviously love the Woman in there. So..... I will provide what I can to make her yours. NARRATOR: Edwin was taken back, Because he did love her. He was surpried this small, Scraggy man.. Could tell. EDWIN: Okay....... Ill do it. WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Great, Gather your things and meet me at the gates. NARRATOR: After gathering his things, Edwin departed with The Huntsman They werent to far along the road when they were greeted by a heavily armored man... KNIGHT: Halt! Halt! NARRATOR: Edwin stopped immediately, But Will kept walking. EDWIN: Will! Get back here! The knight asked you to stop! WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Ha! Knight? You are so funny! This man is a petty criminal, one I dont have time for ROUGE KNIGHT: Hmph. is it that easy to see through? Oh well.... \"draws a sword and points it at Will\" Give me that bow. NOW. \"Will looks over shoulder.\" WILL THE HUNTSMAN: Oh, This bow? \"Pulls bow off of shoulder.......\" \"Draws, and fires in 1 quick moment\" NARRATOR: Edwin was taken aback by the show of Violence. EDWIN: Will! You killed him! WILL THE HUNTSMAN: No, I didnt. Look closely. \"Edwin looks, To find 2 arrows lodged in each Shoulder.\" EDWIN: Oh... Its still not nice!!!! \"Will's eyes grow grey as he grows aggrivated.\" WILL THE HUNTSMAN: This man... Burnt my town....... I have every right to shoot. EDWIN: You still shouldnt. \"Will walks away from Edwin, and continues on his journ alone\" EDWIN: Wait! Wait, Will! WILL THE HUNTSMAN: I dont have time for you............ ( End of act 1 ) *sighs How much is the stage...", ""),
