        StaticBook("Elm's Royal Guard App.", "SimplePancake", "MC Name: SimplePancake RP Name: Elm Why I want to join? I wish to join the Royal Guard, so that I will be able to protect the most important of Oren's people. I will protect the King and Queen with my life, and make sure no harm befalls them while I am fighting. I will swear my loyalties to Oren, but beware. I am an Elf, and am, and always will be, a person of Malinor. If any nation is at war, I will protect the Human Royals, and make sure they live, no matter the consequence. But, If my two nations, the Humans and the Elves, are at war, I shall not side with one, but try to stop the fighting before it becomes too agressive to stand. My skills in Weapons? I am currently learning how to use the sword, and so far, I have mastered all but one sword. I can fight most men with contempt ease, and will fight whenver I see there is a threat to me, or one of my nations. I currently have the strength to use a Iron Sword ((37 swords)), but am quickly learning how to use the finest swords available, Diamond. I hope you find that I would be a worthy guard, and you will accept me into your most great presence.\n Humble Regards,\n Elm.", ""),
        StaticBook("elolir drui bilok'al", "Jerry_Man", "*The foreign characters are that of Ancient Elven* \n \nyallira'leh taliamean. lye yallirane ito amene. ame druian'haleir evar 'ehya talar'leh ito taliamean evaran. \nailer'al ame evaral karin'ante. ker'oem meracahe larane narnyem'leh.\ntalar'leh meracahe ailer'al'leh lin narnante evar. 'ehya oem ailer'al ame'leh narnante'ne. Swifthide lae'leh drui elolir narnante'ne'ehya eloer. lae acal makarin ame par'bilok ehya caelan sirame parsalume.\nailer'al narnyem. 'ehya Swifthide renarnir'an parnaelu. ile hiylu'leh sirame par'lomi. ito drui Swifthide renarnir'an'ehya par'bilok. drui ame evar laureh ker'entoyem.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elrith Pelreemr's 2nd Report- Irba, 4th of The Amber Cold, 1328.", "CloakandDagger", "I wandered into Alk'hazar looking for a man that until recently only knew through stories. There he was, next to the City's Fountain...Kane. I had learned of his name through an associate of mine, a Druid Dedicant named Lirfanel. Lirfanel was questioning me about the whereabouts of his \"friend\" Kane-Little did I realise he wasnt the only one looking for him. Lirfanel refused to tell me anything other than his name but you could tell that he was hiding something dark. & \"Kane...it appears our paths cross again...\" I stated. \"he responded with a somewhat sarcastic response, \"So it seems, story man.\" (((At this point Kane doesnt know im part of the wardens))) Kane recognised one of the senior wardens that i was with and bolted, leaving me to give chase. We ran across the rooftops of Alk'hazar until i lost sight of him. After searching the district for him, I gave up and went back to Laurelin. -Chapter 2- After a rest for the night (((i got off the computer))) I was making my way to the Warden Base when Kane ran right past me with a couple of Wardens in pursuit. I joined in on the chase and was able to see a warden capture him. We led him to the Laurelin Jail and from thier threw him in a cell. The senior wardens told me to guard the front gate(((door))) while they questioned him. The only thing i was able to make out was, \"Leave Lir(Lirfanel) out of this , he was only trying to help me. I am Broken inside, He was trying to cure my darkness.\" -End of Report.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elrith Pelreemr's Last Will and Testament.", "CloakandDagger", "I leave my armour to the one who killed me . I leave this book to the one who killed me. I leave my food to the one who killed me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elrith Pelreemr, Espionage Diary-1", "CloakandDagger", "*This Information has been gathered by Elrith Pelreemr(CloakandDagger) for the use of Warden Officers and Elven Nobility. It may not be copied or reproduced unless agreed upon by a Warden Officer or Elven Nobility. This morning while I was walking towards Alk'hazar I came across 15 humans all huddled around. At first I was startled but i realized this was a excellent chance to gather information. I walked pass them making sure that my hoof concealed my ears and that they did not get a clear glimpse at my face. I then backtracked along the trees until i was able to hear them (they were whispering now). From their conversation i was able to make out a few of thier names, Airion, Dondo Rondo, Rhaegar, Unfortunaetly i was unable to find out the others. From their conversation I could tell they were mad, i shall do my best to retell what they said. These quotes may be out of order but i have done my best to recount them- \"The elves can be reasoned with, the orcs on the other hand...\" \"why would we want to reason with those that attacked us!\" \"what about the dwarves? surely their allegiance can be bought.\" \"yes but for what minas...land?\" Of thier conversation that is all i was able to get. *The text ends here*   i have a book of information for him .", ""),
        StaticBook("Elrith's Report-2", "CloakandDagger", "cancel help The Kane Chronicles Part 1-(As Told By Elrith Pelreemr)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elvador's story", "sx421", "Elvador started off in this world as a wandering soul with his brothers. As he walked out of the temple he saw the choice to become good or evil. He thought about this choice until his brother wandered off. Quickly Elvador followed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Hovel", "shiftnative", "To the east, is a grove. A small place with no one home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Language", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Ito Narne = He Walks There \n Ito Ame Narne = He Walks to the Forest \n Ame'Ito Narne = He Walks Within the Forest \n Ameto'Eyha Narne = ...And I/He Walks in the Forest \n Ame'Eyha Ito Narne = The Forest Walks There \n Ito Kae'leh = To His Spirit", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Magic", "TehLulu", "Joma, 34th of The Second Seed, 1305 \n Written by Arch Mage Bell \n Prologue: \n The magic of the Elves is derived from nature, taken from the trees and the plants surrounding them. Holding a strong connection to the lifeforces surrounding them, including those of plant, beast, and man, Elves are able to manipulate or augment these forces to their advantage. Yet they always must keep in mind the delicate connections they hold to nature, and never allow the lifeforces they hold sway over to become corrupted or tainted. These writings are dedicated to the Druids of Malinor and to the Elven Council of Malinor, especially High Prince Native, Princess Ariana, and Prince Toren. \n \n  \n  \n  Each race has its own unique magic. Within each race's magic exists four levels of spells. Four races, Four levels of magic, Four elements. Within each level or tier of magic there exists 3 spells of differing effects and power. Each spell requires its own special actions and concentration to activate. And each tier of magic requires its own materials with which to activate it. \n Tier One \n The spells of the first tier involve the healing of others, the manipulation of nature, and the augmentation of the world around you. The first spell is Nature's Touch. With this spell you may heal another person for a small amount of damage [one heart]. There will be a 3 second time between casting periods for you to regain your energy, and this spell will take one-tenth of your mana. The second spell if Malin's Wall. Summon a wall of branches and leaves through your connection with nature, using two-tenths of your mana. There will be a 5 second delay in casting periods while you regain your strength. The third spell is People of The Tree. Use the essence of your magic to give life to the plant before you, using one-tenth of your mana, with a 20 second delay while you regain your strength. \n Tier Two. \n The first spell of the second tier is Nature's Grasp. Use your magic to heal the wounds of someone near you for a small amount [2 hearts]. This spell will take two-tenths of your mana and has a 6 second delay between castings so you may regain your strength. The second spell is Malin's Box, with which you may summon entangling branches with which to trap your opponent. This spell will take two-tenths of your mana and has a 5 second delay so you may regain your strength. The third spell is Power of the Forest, with which you may give life to the ground around you. This spell will take two-tenths of your mana and has a 20 second period of rest. \n Tier Three. \n The first spell of the third tier is Nature's Vigour. Heal one of your associates for a more substantial amount [3 hearts]. This spell will take two-tenths of your mana and has an 8 second period to rest. The second spell is Malin's Trap. Summon entangling branches and spiderweb to help trap your opponent. This spell will take two-tenths of your mana and you must rest for 5 seconds between castings. The third spell is The Power of Malinor. Use the essence of Malinor to give life to a large area around you. This spell takes two-and-a-half-tenths of your mana. There will be a 25 second rest period between each castings. \n Tier Four. \n The first spell of the fourth tier is The Healing Touch of Malin. Heal one of your associates for a substantial amount [5 hearts]. This spell will take four-tenths of your mana and you must rest for 10 seconds between castings. The second spell is Power of The Trees, with which you may cause branches with deadly thorns to split through the earth and trap your opponent. This spell will take four-tenths of your mana and you must rest for 25 seconds between castings. The last spell is The Power of Aegis. Channel power through all of Aegis to give life to a forest around you. This spell will take four-tenths of your mana and require you to rest for 30 seconds between castings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven names for Voak and Alys", "Jerry_Man", "Haler'yalli or Yalli'haler (with or without apostrophe) Means \"to promise life\" \n \n Karinah'leyu or Leyu'Karin (apostrophe not needed) for a girl. Means \"beautiful sunrise\" \n \nYallr'Laureh of Laureh'yallin (' thing again) for a boy. Means \"Chosen life\"\n \n Sulito Ker'ento or Sulito with another word. Means \"Light to the future\" or just \"light to\" \n \nThese I have found without diggin too deeply. Other combinations of these words will also work. If you don't like any I can keep looking. It is hard as many elvish words sound harsh to our ears, where once they were pleasant. Also we tend towards shorter names these days, whereas traditional Elven names were long.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Postal Service Instructions", "ariczzz1892", "\nLetter Layout: \nfirst page: adressee (mc and rp name) and location /post box, sender address/post box \nPayment \nbuy as many books as the delivery will cost from the shop (we will see if you really bought them), then sell the books you dont need back to the shop. \nPrices \nTo-Post-Box delivery 10 Minas \nTo-Person/Home-Delivery (Laurelin) 50 Minas \nTo-Person/Home-Delivery (Aegis) 250 Minas", ""),
