        StaticBook("Eric's Diary", "URCRAZYERIC", "Oh dear  I ran into Lirinya again today in Laurelin  She was giving out cookies  She gave me 4 cookies  All I had was a shovel, a bed, and some Soul Sand  She then jumped off of the notice board and onto a tree  I followed her I had no clue what to say  I just stood there stuttering retardedly And so I moved to the other side of the tree, where she wouldn't see me And so I began to write this book ;;  And here I am, still standing on this tree in the middle of twilight, writing ;;     Oh shit  I can't leave;  She will undoubtedly see me But I will have to risk it", ""),
        StaticBook("Erirc's Plan", "muchoman798", "So i have been the one to bring up the topic of how poor the city of Al'Khazar's defenses are, as such, I am writing a plan of invading the city, as I know every in and out of every defensive structure in Oren. First, I would like to use some of Dimitri's idea to buy recruitment houses all over Aegis in order to amass more men. This would be the first step in winning a war. Second, I believe we should use General Adian's idea to pay off the guards so they will help us, as they have not been paid by the King in any manner. We will promise them pay AFTER the assault, so we know that they will help us and have helped us instead of just running off. Third I would like to use part of Ardy's plan to have men go in the gate house and open it and make sure that any guards we have not paid off are killed stealthily. Fourth we use my large knowledge of the main weaknesses of the city of Al'Khazar in order to s a large assault party into the city. This will be done by using the recruits we gather from Dimitri's idea and from alliances we make with bandits and fellow factions. I apologize that we must ally with the likes of bandits, but it is to protect us against the Undead. Read on to find out how we will invade the city of Al'Khazar using the weaknesses. Weak points of Al'Khazar: The bay, the sewers, the open Northern Gates, the easy to pass by Southern Gates, the farming section of the city, the mountain next to the keep. The plan for exploiting these weaknesses is as such: we s groups of five men each into each point of weakness in the outer city, these are both gates, the sewers, the harbor and the farms. After this team is able to destroy what is left of the guard, we have each group run to the two entrances to the keep. At this point, we will have already used Ardy's idea to infiltrate the guard and have inside men open up the keep gates. This will allow our men to flood the final hold out of the rest of the guard and the King. At this point, the city of Al'Khazar and Kingdom of Oren will be held by us. A human leader will be chosen (I personally nominate Puppy at this time.) That is all.   I encourage us to read the entirety of everyones plans.", ""),
        StaticBook("Erunak's diary", "harryscott123", "my last diary was destroyed in my sleep . joined a clan far from kramaroe 2 homes now feel good joined a keep owned by my brother have 3 homes feel bad ....... raffus kicked out of kramaroe and old mayers taken over . no news of wrath but my goal still stands. i am lord hunter and a donater for gaarag now i can pay my dept back to him.i like writing better then talking thats for sure. i am hunter lord of the castle and have made a hunters lodge .............. (the slaves stash is ready). gaarag is an a****** i will betray him....the slave is stage 1. the slave was freed and all is normal.......   THe capital of the orcs was attacked many died but the  day was saved and we returned to norodrun i have 4 hunters at the moment and the BH was destoyed. i have started the lodges expansion and norodrun has a town a manor and a cathidral in destrucion . I dont know wat to do gaarag died i dont know how but he did im alone. kramaroe is gone turned to ruin by the undead a battle happened at a near bye relic the undead won...... 3 blocks from the light at norodrun lodge is the secret escape tunnel and a weapons stash . not many people left me and a couple dark times.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Erunak's tale......", "harryscott123", "after 4 months of harsh desert i found gaarag. I have obtained a home in the town of Kramoroe. I had a run in with a dark warlock Wrath, he was eventualy driven away but i nealy died. i will soon depart for phonex hold wish me luck. 4 days later... we reached the fort but it was destroyed we collected evidence and some 3 dwarves arrived we gave them the details and headed back,covered in a tower for a night then came straight home. we met the lord of the town and now were going apple gathring. the apple gathering was succesful and im going again today . went to the town wrath chased me out of to get sand gaarag turned up and now we are removing the buildings. a archer of wraths chased us away there hiding somthing near that castle i can feel it , oh and i found a stash under the sand in the town i plan on eventualy confronting wrath but his influence spreads further then i expected the archer......why? i was hard a work and the ruin town is now sand the town is reduced to sand and i returned home. gaarag is gone currupted by evil i saw a battle squad leave alk hazar and i lost myself in the woods this happened after i chased gaarag through the town and now i am home again ,new allies new enemies!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Essential Supplies for the Assassin", "Jexdane", "There are a variety of supplies that any assassin is reccomended to have in their possession when on a mission. Here are a few. \n - A Sword. Preferably diamond or iron. Stone won't get the job done. \n - Armor. Really depends on your style. A ranged assassin will want full leather. Swordsman iron. Very few people have diamond armor, so it's usage can be suspicious. \n - Webs. They slow down enemies, and prevent them from escaping. At least 10 at a time. \n - Food. Any type works. 15 of it should suffice for a while. Hunt animals regularly. \n - Dirt. Great for getting over high walls, etc. Waste blocks can be used for many things. \n -A crafting table. This and any weaponry making materials can be useful when away for a while. \n Finally, a disguise. Hoods are suspicious, but when push comes to shove, you don't want people knowing your face. \n I hope this helps, and that when on the road you'll always be prepared.", ""),
        StaticBook("Etheral's Journal", "ThatDutchIdiot", "Day 1: After brutally being robbed yesterday and nearly getting killed, I decided to buy a empty book to capture my whole life in here. I am glad that I finally learned how to write and read! I headed out East from Al'Khazar, after a strange man told me a nearby town called Lunavara would provide me with a job! My curiousity nearly got me in trouble again. For now I am on my to Lunavara! Day 2: The travel was further than I expected. I stumbled apon a small settlement on my way. A small dwarf rushed up to me and accused me from stealing from his land! I explained where I was going. I took shelter below a bridge. I'm scared, dirty and cold.. How far away is this Lunavara?! Day 3: After a lot of walking, I spotted a big wall! Is this Lunavara? Day 4: Hmm... The gate is closed and there's some paper hammered on the wall \"No entering!\" I need to find someone who can tell me what's going on.. I am looking for a way in, hoping to find someone inside.. Was this town attacked recently perhaps? Day 5: I managed to find a way inside, but I can't find anyone inside. The place is infested with spiders.. Should I search around for some stuff? I took the opportunity to take some wheat from the farmlands. In a open house I baked something that looks like bread.. I stay here for the night. Day 6: Early in the morning I head out, away from this ghost town.. Still clueless what happened here, but I do not care at the moment. I need a place to work and live! Next thing I find seems to be a small building at first sight. A dwarven hold... Maybe the- *dusty page* These tunnels are endless! Where is the exit? Where am I going!? *torn out page* Day 9: Finally! I see sunlight! I think I am going to travel back, to that place where the dwarf accused me from stealing. Maybe he can offer me some work? I just keep walking through the night. I am tired after this whole week of travelling so I want to settle down somewhere as soon as I can Day 10: I found someone around Lunavara. They closed the city down because of the heavy attacks. Newcomers need to sent an letter to get into the city.. I'm not sure what I should do at the moment...", ""),
        StaticBook("Etheral's Journal II", "ThatDutchIdiot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Evark", "shiinchan", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Evening Devotions", "Maiavel", "\nBlessed be this house from site to stay, from beam to wall, from end to end, from found to summit \n-Envision bands of light encompassing and protecting your home.- \n-Go to our bedroom and extinguish the lamp or candle with the following words:- \n I am smooring the fire as Brigid would smoor: May she bless the fire, the family, the home ; Brigid the fair to guard us till fair day wakes us. \n-Settle into bed and repeat the following prayer before sleep:- \n I am laying down tonight at peace with my kindred, at peace with my forebears, at peace with my gods. The sacred Three. To save, to shield, to surround. The hearth, the family, the home. This night and every night. With the ebb, with the flow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Events", "Telanir", "-CONFIDENTIAL- Property of: Telanir \n Entry 1: Lab 8 was built. Nero knows of it's location. It has chests and farms. Enough for surviv al Entry 2: Finished building house in village. Entry 3: Constructed notice board in village. \n Entry 4: Finished my house in the village. \n Entry 5: Me and Nero have talked about protecting the village. We will ask the village members to pitch in to the cost. \n Entry 6: Constructed a library in the village. We also named the village \"Talamh\" \n Entry 7: I put my research into bookshelves in the library. \n Entry 8: A person named Talam entered our village. He seemed to have a tremendous loss of memory. \n Entry 9: The king at Al'Khazar turned undead, betrayed us all. He rained lightning upon his own keep. Queen Dawn took his place, a horrible replacement, and the citizens started a riot \n We discussed this in Talamh and decided on going on cautiously in the city. \n Nero revealed that his mother was the queen of elves. Personally I am in disbelief, but he said she was executed for committing adultery against the king. Nero plans on using this connection to get the elves to help us unite against the undead. Nero asked for several people to accompany him on his long journey. They will take a sword. I'm very suspicious of Nero and Daniels recent behavior. They seem to be purpously leaving me out of the leadership in Talamh, even though I'd say I am one of the key contributers and helped set the foundation for the city. Nero also seems to be asking for donations which he appears to want to use for the towns needs not his own. I doubt this but I will see what happens in the near future before coming to any conclusions. I actually don't think I will be attending this journed to the elven homeland. I have too many doubts. Unless that may give me a chance to find out what's going on... Possibly it could be a planned ambush but I doubt this after all Nero has done. Nero is telling everyone not to take too many belongings with them. A warning? I'm probably hugely overthinking the situation. I'l have some rest and continue later. \n Entry 10: It's the next day, and it seems things are still haywire. I can hear lightning coming from Al'Khazar I hope it doesn't come this way... \n According to Nero, lightning from the undead can be heard all throughout Aegis. He says that the undead are far from Alk'hazar. We will be safe for a while. \n Entry 11: Thondi found a chest full of wool and iron in the elven house we were in the other day. He gave the wool to me. Such a kind man. \n Entry 13: I overheard the last part of a conversation between Nero and Father Ailean and it ended with Ailean saying \"Now you know who I really am\". It sounded extremely suspicious. I'l be watching out for Nero and Ailean now. \n Entry 14: I've returned from the Nether intact! I'm so glad. It was a nightmare, exact same as when I went last time. Just as horrid and frightnening. There were undead everywhere and I constantly suffered from the sheer amount of dark magic. I was almost caught at some points. I left the Nether in tatters, I was a total wreck. I almost went mad down there, the ghasts almost killed me, the pigmen were endless! I'm so lucky I survived... \n Entry 15: I made a house, and Nero wants it torn down. I'm begginning to like this man less and less by the days. I hope things turn out well. \n Entry 16: I transformed the house into a medical center. Nero is pleased. \n Entry 17: Something odd happened, it appears Father Ailean was a hitman, and recently he was killed... I must investigate further, this is quite saddening news. \n Entry 18: Nero's chests were robbed. And he accused me. What an imbecile. Oh well, I'l deal with it later. \n Entry 19: It appears there was a librarian, he came to our town of Talamh and visited our library. His name was Cerlos Ithelias(pepernoot), I'l make a note of contacting him later on. \n Entry 20: I have found a dirt trail in Lab 8. Someone broke in through into Lab 8 through digging. It appears Lab 8 was near a large deserted mining shaft and was found by digging into the mining shafts side. This is a huge security issue. I should find some time to fix it. However, the issue may not be present anymore because Nero locked his chests. I am left to wonder, how did this man get into Lab 8 at the right time? How did he know that if Nero moved his items they would be unprotected? It could also be a coincidence but the chance of this happening is minimal. The person left behind a trail of dirt blocks, It led to the mining shaft which is how I found out. \n Entry 22: Daniel returned from a vacation and has siezed sudden and abrupt control . He decided that he wanted more control and stopped all of our actions regarding the expansion of the city of Talamh. He believes building a wall would be a wrong course of action, and provided a good point. I really don't like this, because me and Nero have been the largest contributers to Talamh and I think it is unfair and wrong to have a leader that does jack shit take control. It appears that Nero wants himself, Shamus(who does nothing), and Daniel to lead the city. He pretends to change his thoughts and make a council of 5 men. The council of Talamh are Nero, Shamus, Daniel, Telinir, and Jolot. I'm personally not sure why Nero wants Daniel and Shamus to be leaders so bad. [OOC: Probably because they are friends in real life. Jeez >.>] Nero wants control really bad, but keeps putting Daniel at command. He uses the term \"Founder\" to stray me aside as not being a proper leader. Apparently, the founders are always the leaders. I heartily disagree with that statement. The people that put in the most effort and contribute the most should be leaders but... I have no say right now, Unfortunately. I'm beginning to feel out of place in this town. I am more of a researcher I guess. And they are relentlessly leaving me out of this. I am incredibly dissapointed. I thought they were better. I'l see how events turn out, I might start working on Lab 9 further. It will be a hiding place to look after the town. Shamus arrived to the conversation and stated that he wanted at least three leaders. Obviously he wants himself, Daniel and Nero to lead. I'm beginning to doubt these peoples leadership qualities. They all center around each other because of their friendship. I will remain the same. I would rather go back to being a lab rat than this. The wizard arrived lately from the Order of Scientific Research and Technology so I might go there.", ""),
        StaticBook("events and places", "bondb", "-667   -346 Terriko < seems to be made up of mostly humans,a small town with friendly people \n\n\n\n\n: -764  103  Ghalahar, a human town seemed to be ran by the city of oren, \n\n\n\n\n : : -916 62 Shad'Rin, a small fort made up of humans they are not very nice -948  245  Alras, a bi-racial town made up of mostly shops and nice people hail \n \n -1133 80 help swords of lorem a merc compnay giving protection \n -1223  74 Oren A large human city witha military, king, and many shops \n 6 99 LAurelin the elf capitol, very nice people and large amount of activity \n 648  357 Warden HQ", ""),
        StaticBook("Events and Places- A Collection", "aaaa1188", "Editor's Intoduction- What you are about to read is a series of locations and observations (as you may have previously deduced from the cover and title) that were recorded by the Warden Initiate Erik in an effort to keep a clear, concise, and accurate record of, well, events and places. It shall be said now that all authorial credit must be bestowed upon said Warden Initiate Erik, and I, Arthane_Lazul, am merely stepping in as an editor to his efforts. My goal is to accurately convey the work which Erik has recorded in his original work to you, the reader, so that you too may benefit from his work. Now that credit has been given where credit is due, let us begin, \n New Terriko \n - \n -667, -346 \n New Terriko seems to be a fairly small town who's majority of inhabitance are members of the Human race. These Humans are rather friendly, do not seem hostile, and are rather willing to comply with any requests you may have of them, unless, of course, you cross the boundries of reasonable requests. \n Gahlahar \n - \n -7, 103 \n Ghalahar is a small Human settlement that seems to be either under the rule of, or recieving aid from the Kingdom of Oren. \n Shad'Rin : \n -916, 62 \n A small fortress created and inhabited by a rather unfriendly group of Humans, Humans who do not seem all that pleased with the presence of outsiders. \n Al'Khazar \n - \n -1223,  74 \n Al'Khazar, the grand capitol of the Human kingdom of Oren, stands between a vast range of mountains and a large ocean. This lively center of activity has many shops, inns, bars, and bakeries that one can visit to partake in Human culture. It should also be noted that this city has its own dedicated, if not slightly over-zealous, guard, and any crime will not be tolerated. Apart from the guard the Nation of Oren also has many branches of military service, most of which are based from the Al'Khazar region. Recently, this city has been the subject of many undead attacks and infiltrations, causing a deep sense of worry to spread among the people. Oren is ruled under a singular figure, in other words, a monarchy. The current king is Enor Sheffield, but nobody knows how long he will reign for. Kings of Oren are infamous for their ability to \"dissapear\" after a short time as ruler. \n Swords of Lorem Mercenaries Company  \n ----------- \n ----------- \n -1133, 80 \n A Merc company offering protection. For a price, of course. \n Laurelin \n - 6, 99 \n Ah, yes. Laurelin. Laurelin is the spectacular capitol of the Elven Nation of Malinor. The beautiful trees that grow from this blessed soil stand tall amongst all that surrounds them. These magnificent wonders of nature often bring tears to the eyes of those who gaze upon them. Malinor itself is governed by a council of Noble Princes and Princesses, a system that has proven itself most effective throughout the years. The city of Laurelin is a peaceful and tranquil place, but also a lively and active locati on. Many elves can be found amongst the trees and buildings of Laurelin, and most will be friendly and welcoming, traits many elves posses. There are many markets and shops in Laurelin and its outlying areas, and is a generally comfortable place to reside. The Princedom of Malinor is also protected by the pious and noble Wardens, a large group of highly skilled, greatly disciplined elves that have sworn their lives to the protection of Malinor and its people. \n \n \n Conclusion- \n From all who were involved in the inscription of this knowledge, we hope you find this to be a useful resource in any future endeavors. Now go forth and explore the vast world of Aegis! Experience all that this great land has to offer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ever", "Ever", "If I die, these belongins are of Ever. Please return 'em to 'im.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ever was here", "Ever", "I borrowed this book~", ""),
        StaticBook("Ever's profile (ever)", "coconuta", "Name : ever \n Job: owns a inn \n Job he wants : to own a inn in the largest cities in all aegis \n Other: he would also need staff to run the taverns", ""),
        StaticBook("Everen", "ttwesten", "this is the seal to give to Everen he has been very loyal to me and my family i give this seal for him to be remebered in the lands. ~ from the king.", ""),
        StaticBook("evil", "sconn", "Evil, I am calling! Evil, do you hear? Evil, I am imploring. Evil, I beg you ear! Citizens of al'khazar i have found a way to rid yourself of your mistakes The world in which we live in is a horrible place. greed, sloth, lust, mercy those are the mistakes the creator gave us. there is  a way to save yourself from these mistake and world. Take your own life and be free of your crippled body. This death is better that dying in the hands of the undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Example", "TwilightStorm", "This is an example book It is completely pointless May you lock mine as well? Haha", ""),
        StaticBook("Example Letter", "Themastermoo", "To: Randomguy \n Lives at: Kramoroe \n From: Moo \n Lives at: AFF Main Keep \n Extra instructions go here, directions to unusual city? \n \n This is the meat of the letter, this is where you say whatever to whoever. We won't read your message, out of courtesy of course. We will only read the front with instructions. We would like the front to be in orderly fashinon. To get new paragraphs just type:  \n \n  to get a new paragraph, just type a colon. The two dots above each other.", ""),
        StaticBook("Execution report.", "Juvens", "Today, 3 persons were executed. 2 Unknown ones, and an orc named Jack. Jacks crimes were: Kidnapping Torturing and Worshipping Iblees.     Afterwards another guy was catched, who helped in a prison break. His name was Tom Hawkinson.    Joma, 27th of Suns Smile, 1313", ""),
        StaticBook("Execution Warrant", "Baronvo", "Let it be known that Pud ((pudclud)) and Ben ((hmqb)) are hearby sentenced to death. A bounty of 5000 minas is put on Pud. ((screenshot to prove the kill)). \n \n Signed, \n High Priest Everard Hightower Someone take this book", ""),
        StaticBook("Expedition Notes", "Blackwidow920", "Tis not working The portal tis not working yet, Our leader is going to find the pieces to fix the blasted thing The portal is now working, we went through to what looks like an abandoned dungeon T'is very dark, but many brave men and women are traveling through the cobweb infested halls There is a sort of broken bridge and structure... We are now entering. This land has been takin by the spiders, some have died I ventured up a stairwell. only to find a single book shelf, I shall look into what this is.. We have found a broken bridge, We are now venturing downwards through the hole in the bridge. The hole led to what looks like a library infested with spiders, we shall have to inspect... Men are going insane in these lands, Bodyguard_Gralka went crazy today... I dropped my book as a spider attacked me, I retrieved it along with many other objects people have dropped. I seem to be trapped in this accursed library, people are grabbing ropes to help I made it back up, Somehow tis raining in these accursed lands... I found a grand library, I shall inspect it! All the books I inspected were damaged... I shall have to let this be... I found stairs, they are damaged and it has holes in it, I must be careful... WE FOUND THE EXIT! We popped out of the cave in some sort of forest... I discovered we were in a different realm now, I shall inspect... I found a sort of... broken cathedral... a druid shack I presume. Giant mushrooms?! Where are we... The cavern we just came out of must have been a spire of some sort... The spire has beautiful architecture, I wish it were not crumbling. A storm has started. A man has been strucken down by Zeus himself! I must get back inside the chasm, this storm is getting too much The storm has cleared up a bit. The giant mushrooms seem to have doorways, I am to go inspect them. It seems like someone or something has been living in these mushrooms! There must be a civilization here. On one of thee mushrooms is a sign that says- Petyr's Lodging I see Apollo starting to drive his chariot. The storm is still pouring down on us... I am taking shelter in a mushroom for now. I have rested in a bed in the mushroom. A man attacked me last night, stole some of my food. I saw a tree grown into a little house, I walked inside... It looks like a bakery. Where are we I have no idea. I was walking around the forest today... There is a gigantic cavern system... T'is to dark- To venture downwards... I found more ruins! I shall go inspect... SPAWNERS DOWN HERE! A kind sir Jallentime is helping me kill off these blasted spiders. I broke one of those blasted spawners... two more to go. I was mistaken with Jallentine's name, 'tis Delaselva, the Seer We have slane all the spiders... This is my last expedition around this dimension... I found nothing on my last expedition... I am venturing back through the portal towards Aegas", ""),
        StaticBook("Expedition one", "Royced", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiences with the Undead: A personal account", "AlphaCentaurus", "The term \"Undead\" carries with it an miasma of fear and superstition. Few actually have met one, but many throw around the accusation of consortation with Iblees without real evidence or thought. Most accused are mere troublemakers or pretenders, hoping to inflate their own ego by taking on the guise of one more powerful than they. But even most of the pretenders have not actually met who they imitate. All they have heard is the second- and third-hand accounts, most twisted and distorted by time and distance. \n I have met them.. \n It all started in this city, Celestine. I came here when it had almost no workers, looking for a job. I was exceedingly poor, and knew little of the world. It was an act of desperation. And yet, it payed off. I got my feet under myself, and began to flesh out my abilities. But as I worked, I noticed that many of the inhabitants - not the workers, but mere  residents were extremely strange. They spoke of awful things, and wore dark robes. I knew enough of the world to suspect what this meant. But I also knew enough to keep my mouth shut. I worked my way into the nominal trust of Queen Cassandra. At least, I was trusted enough to be told of who she was. \n My suspicions were confirmed about both her and some of her colleagues. I continued working. I realized that while the undead posed a threat, they also were an opportunity. \n Power. What it means to me is control. I've had little enough of that throughout my life that I've learned its value. So I stayed. I worked and would make occasional trips to Al'khazar. While Celestine is a lovely place, it's not exactly a center of social interaction. It was on one of these trips that my life changed. \n As I arrived, I saw that wave after wave of dark creatures assaulted the walls. Through the crowds of milling people, I saw that in the center of the square there were two robed shapes. They called for those loyal to Iblees to join them. I was never a religious man. Aerial did not involve herself in my life, and I did not involve myself in her's. \n I joined them. We traveled to an evil hold and after a brief test of our loyalty we were forced to defend ourselves from the nearby elves. Killing my own people... it would have once held only terror and disgust for me. But then... it held a bitter, glorious feeling of triumph. Every drop of blood my sword spilled filled me with the feeling of joy. We won. Their bodies littered the floors, burned and disfigured. \n Unfortunately, our celebration did not last long. Another attack came, this one much larger. We were outnumbered 6 to 1. Despite the undead helping us, with their lightning burning the skies, we lost. I barely escaped with my life. \n I joined up with other minions who made it out of the fortress. We stockpiled weapons and awaited orders. Unfortunately, none came. I will not bear you, reader, with an account of our actions. Suffice to say that we made ourselves a nuisance and occasionally did something that was meaningful. The minions fell apart without leadership. And so I returned to Celestine. \n I no longer serve the dark lord directly, but my life has been changed. I whisper into people's ears. I spread unease. I can't do much. But I do what I can. And I forever bear the knowledge of what I have done, and what others have. \n I hope that this can shed some speck of enlightenment on what others might feel should they involve themselves with the undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Experimeantal Enchanted Notebook 2", "Eric_Armadillo", "This is the first test for a newly developed communication spell. 1.) First test . I hope this works fine.", ""),
        StaticBook("Experimental Enchanted Notebook", "Eric_Armadillo", "now there are letters in your book", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiments", "halt99", "We have made little progress in developing what Brooke calls \"a potion\".", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiments on the Strange Pearls", "Pepernoot", "First experiment: Water test \n Results: \n -The pearl dropped in the water and sank.\n-No change in color, or consistency.\n \n \nSecond experiment: Crush Test The pearl was crushed by a piston moving down. \n Results: \n-The pearl appeared to move through the piston, without any problem. We were unable to crush it. \n -There was no change in color or consistency. \n \nThird test: Fire test\n We dropped the pearl in a small woodfire. \n \n\n.\n Results: \n -The pearls dissapeared\n-It might have blinked, or just burned. \n-The pearl did catch fire. \n \n\n \n \n \n-Cerlos Ithelias, with the assistance of Riona.", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiments to be done", "Pepernoot", "-More research on the strange pearls \n -Research on mind altering substances (Cactus green, smoking saplings etc.) \n -Brewing Ale \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiments with Mind Altering Substances", "Pepernoot", "The first experiment is with \"Cactus Green\", or relaxers, as some might call it. \n I convinced a friend to try it. \n Results: \n He could not answer my questions correctly... I don't know if it is because of his condition, or if it's normal for him. \n He seems slower than normal. \nSide effects: \n  A little bit of dissyness after use, it wears off within hours.  \n \n I recently encountered a man in Al'Khazar who apperently is addicted to \"Sugar\". \n The man snorts the sugar, and it brings him into a state of extacy, and it makes him very active.\n Side effects: \n A strong addiction. \nMore effects on the brain are not yet know, but I don't think it will end well for the addict.", ""),
        StaticBook("exploration", "nuttyy3", "", "")
    )

