        StaticBook("Farmer of the Knights", "Everman111", "Day One \n They have placed me in the lower quarters near the caves.  find them an odd race . They showed me most of everything in this castle if you can call it that.  find my  curiousity pulling me to the locked doors of the chambers.  know not where they go. \n  \n Day Two \n  have worked in the fields for the first time today. The farm is a very large one indeed.   The wheat we grow here lacks the sun and grow by torch light making it rather  dry and tastes of nothing.   \n Day Twenty \n I spoiled over and entered the Council Room while they were gone. It is a very plain place . I suppose the men of this race do not take account of beauty. These men remind me of my father. Plain and hardworking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farmer's Manual", "Meet2012", "In order to have a successful harvert, there are many things that must be done in preparation.  First, a good location must be selected.  The farm doesn't have to be big, but it should be flat and have a source of light.  Torches and glowstone work just as well as sunlight.  Second of all, the crops should have a constant water source.  Not all plants need water, but those that do need it for survival.  A simple way to supply water to your crops is to place water around the farm (assuming that the farthest crop isn't more than 3 blocks away from the path, mind you) under the walkway.  The water should be level with the farm, and have half-steps covering it.  Third,  seeds should only be planted when the farm is free of animals.  The seeds are easily trampled, leaving a less-than-favorable harvest. Finally, seeds should only be planted when the soil is moist.  Often times, seeds will die because the soil is not moist enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farming", "Ansh98", "Interested in providing for the guild? Great!  You will love farming. Farmer create farms for buildings assigned and also harvest food for the hungry guild members. If the hoe is your best friend, the surely, join the Farming Division! \n Farming is reccommended for members who have a farm, a hoe, and (( a high farming level)). Dean challenging consists of the creation of the most ideal and effective farm. Join the farming division if you'd like to be a great support and build on!", ""),
        StaticBook("Farming Stock", "TheWoWMasta", "From ((28/9/11)) \n Mushrooms: 3 \n Melon Seeds: 59 \n Saplings: 100+ \n Sugar Cane: 72", ""),
        StaticBook("Faroth's Story", "TommyRedblue", "I came to orc land just to explore. I wandered into the town of Sandhar. I joined the legion but I don't know if that mattered. They didn't have any room for me. Because of that, I stored my stuff in a hole south of Sanhar. It was ok, but I was worried it would get stolen \n There was a human and dwarf war. It lasted 2 battles. It started with big booms from the north. I didn't get to see the first battle. I'm not even sure who won. The orcs(and I) went to help the the humans. We charged to dwarf territory. They fired arrows from the high wall. We did not win that battle. It was resolved in 2 battles, though. \n Later, the orcs(and I) attacked the Bloods. It was for territory. We trashed the place. They later surrendered due to a lack of manpower. We took Riverside! \n I later got a home. Good price. 500 minas. Not very big, but it's in Sanhar and not in a hole south of it. I like it here. The orcs are friendly and always ready to help.  \n I met a human named Slade. Not very many humans in orc land, so I talked to him. We talked about the human and dwarf war. I showed him Sanhar and told him the houses were cheap. He said he needed a home. I told him to wait for Bein. We went out to adventure together. We decided to go to Oren. ALong the way, we thought we should try a dungeon that we passed. We went back to Sanhar and prepared. We fought hard in the dungeon, but failed. We decided to try again. We found that arrows seemed to work well there. We went to Laurelin to buy some bows and arrows. We had trouble getting in the gate. We snuck in. We got caught later on. We thought we'd be in trouble, but Prince Flefal said he'd sell us supplies. He showed us around some of Laurelin. He also took us to Ravenhold and showed us a part of it. We headed back to Laurelin. I had a blackout around then(Logged out). \nI've been looking for Slade since that day. I've asked around and even put it on a message board. Haven't found him. \n I found Slade. We've explored. We have a long-term goal to get 1 million minas. Not going to be easy. We've also come to the conclusion that the dungeon wasn't made to escape from.", ""),
        StaticBook("fart", "Paulie2499", "hello", ""),
        StaticBook("fasf", "redbaron", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Faustus's Diary", "obsidian494", "1301, Suns Smile, Itnan. Today is my fourteenth birthday and for once I am not filled with ha tred, for I received this diary. 1301, Suns Smile, Irba. It has been two passing since last I wrote in this diary.. My mother asked me what I find interesting, and so I told her that I always found magic interesting. I ofcourse did not tell her that I would rather be studying the darker sides of it, which are more fascinating, but she still was furious and said that no magic will ever be practiced , s tudied or learnt in this household. I am furious at her I know that deep within me I have pot ential, perhaps for necromancy, the art of raising the dead. 1301, Suns Smile, Kamees. I am hateing all this sunlight and warmth, I'd much prefer Snows Ma iden. I only just realised that I have not been recording the number of the days I will try to find the date next time. 1301, 6th, Suns Smile, Joma. I do not care what my mother says I will studie magic. I have no idea how I will study it without her knowing, but I will find a way.  1301, 7th, Suns Smile, Sabet. A new child moved in across the street today. So far he has already become a nuicance and has tried to talk to me. If he keeps it up he may have an accident.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fe found him trying to eavesdrop before. I do not think he is trustworthy.", "Spinzir", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Fealnor's last will-", "MrHobo", "I bequeth all my worldy possesions to my only blood relative and son, Elrond Tiwele. Let it be known that I express my sorrow as best as possible in this book. I am sorry for all the evil I have caused in this world. \nAnd, Respiren, if you ever read this, don't forget me. My name has almost been lost in time, and only you, and my son if he shall ever show his face to you, and few others will ever remember me. I hope you can forgive my sins I have commited before death.", ""),
