        StaticBook("Field Operations Manual", "callum2357", "(( Sorry what? i was afk)) NO! What ( it was supposed to be a field manual but i did it wrong))", ""),
        StaticBook("Fifteen Birds in Five Fir Trees", "MrZombez", "\nFifteen birds on five fir trees \nTheir feathers were fanned in a fiery breeze, \nBut, funny little birds, they had no wings! \nO what shall we do with the funny little things? \nRoast 'em alive, or stew them in a pot; \nFry them, boil them and eat them hot? \n \n Written By Len of Dunwood", ""),
        StaticBook("Fight Back!", "muchoman798", "\n For obvious reasons, I am not disclosing my name on this pamphlet. \nThere is a peace treaty with the Undead! \nBut it is not good. It gives our kingdom a false sense of safety. Is this good? No. It makes us more vulnerable. We think they won't attack unless we attack. Well, they will attack. They are conniving monsters. Do not let them fool us. They will kill us. \nIn addition, there is a condition to this \"peace\" treaty. The Undead are allowed to freely walk the streets of Oren and Al'Khazar without the guards telling them to stop or imprisoning them. Even stopping and imprisoning are not enough against the Undead, and we are not allowed to do that. They should be killed on sight. We should not let them in the cities. \nAnd this is all under the King's direction. He could have stopped it, but he did not. \nFight back, the King is leaving us vulnerable. We can be destroyed. Keep Oren alive. \nJoin the revolt. ~ L", ""),
        StaticBook("Fighting Tactics", "pandalex12", "This book will tell you how to fight with tactics and so on .", ""),
        StaticBook("File: Everard Hightower", "DanielJamieson97", "Everard Hightower Evarard Hightower was the High Priest of Oren at one point. He served both the King as well as the Cloud Temple.", ""),
        StaticBook("Final Words", "Archmage_Cataris", "*The letter has blood smeared throughout and the bottom right hand corner ripped* I can hear Sarugon bellowing at the doors with his massive hammer, I fear they will break into the Crypt soon. I have my household guards take my sweet Jyana away with the twins, I can just picture it now, Elgon and Cataris practicing in the yards, Fighting off in mighty battles. But i will not be there for them. Me and Hugor have held them off for as long as we could but i fear those ancient doors will soon burst asunder. I did not mean for this to befall the House of conDoin, I can only regret each icy breath i take before i plunge into darkness. I can hear the hinges creaking more loudly with each blow to the door. Goodbye Jyana, My sweet wife and my  *The corner is ripped here*", ""),
        StaticBook("Final Words", "Groobs03", "I'm so sorry that I did this, but i couldn't take the sights of war anymore. I am in a better place now , peace rests in my soul. \n -Wolverine_General_Groobs_Blackbeard", ""),
        StaticBook("Find out what are Oren's allies, and the diplomatical ussues.", "Eltyer", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Find this and it's yours.", "Ratemenatorz59", "....... ............. ....... Uhm bye.", ""),
        StaticBook("Find us!", "Shuness", "Haha! We five pumpkins have hidden ourselves around New Terra! Come find all of us, and we might give you something for it! Pumpkin 1: I might be hidden in plain sight, but you'll have to go in another building to get my letter! Pumpkin 2: I like trees, but also like mines. Pumpkin 3: I'm the farthest from the start. You can find me where there is water, but you still hear fire. Pumpkin 4: Underground, I lie, near a place of plantlife! You may have to go inside a spooky house, though. Pumpkin 5: I scrape the skies, trying to reach for the heavens! General Rules: All contestants must stay in the groups given by Shun. When you find the pumpkins, unscrable the letters, and then come fine me for your reward. Only one pumpkin is in the Residential Area. Ther rest are in the Market/Forest area. NO running through other owned houses, we don't want to bother anyone. You are free to use /tell to talk to your teammate. Any other questions, talk to Shun. And remember, have fun!", ""),
        StaticBook("Finding Delthor", "aheath4", "An ex member of the S.A, a new mercenary group, has aparantly paid bandits to raid his old employers keep . The dwarfs name is Delthor. We must locate him, and shadow his movements. Once we have gathered enough information. We can 'Talk' to him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finding New Oasis", "YifengZhong", "Kamees, 12 of Malins Welcome 1339 \n We leave the house in the Verge to find this settlement known as \"New Oasis\". I travel with Delfyr and his apprentice.  It will be a dangerous journey but they are both skilled in swordsmanship so it should be relatively safe. Anyway, we must set off now, I'll record more later. \n We have arrived at some town west of the portal, it's population as of now is Zero. Blazes and slimes marred our path for most of the night, and I am thankful for the moment of rest. Despite her annoying and irritating personality, Arelia is quite skilled with a bow and has served her purpose as a useful ally in our travels.  I hope she continues being so. Timayame is as arrogant as always, but of course is power is quite formiddable and commands respec t.  Oh, excuse me, Delfyr.  *The name \"Timyame\" has been scratched out.* For now, I see that he is attempting to, as is his way, breach the barrier between master and appr entice, and woo Arelia with his charm and bed with her in this world forsaken by any deity, God or otherwise. Now day has risen, and I see that I have wasted my night recording this knowledge. Joma, 13th of Malins Welcome, 1339 We've arrived in some elven town.  It seems abandoned, another indication of the massive damage inflicted by the curse of Iblees. But it isn't too destroyed, and I find the town hall that I am leisurely occupying to be quite comfortable under the circumstances. As yesterday, our travels were quite fruitless until we happ'd upon this town, according to Arelia New Oasis is supposedly near a large Elven settlement.  So hopefully we will be there soon. \n Sabet, 14th of Malins Welcome, 1339 \n Success!  We have arrived in New Oasis, well, Timayame and I.  That idiot apprentice of his dwells elsewhere and he has backtracked to find her. I sit in a bed, ready to refresh myself and explore this new town.  Although, truthfully, I am unsure if I could find my way back here if I tried. At any rate, I find myself fulfilled having journeyed and found what we searched for. I shall close this chapter as a successful adventure, and the three days of roughing it I can only hope were worth it. \n Itnan, 16th of Malins Welcome, 1339 \n I sit in the home of a man named...actually I don't know his name. But he knows *name scratched out here* Delfyr and I am forced to wait while he takes him and Arelia about his home asking druidic suggestions for decor. ((Did you just say Scandanavia.)) ((omfg)) Mt the last phrase \n At any rate I have decided to leave this ridiculous home and make my way home. The men here are angering me with their attitudes and idiocy , and I fear that I may lose my temper and slaughter them all in their sleep.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finding The Kin", "ReaperT", "The Kin, are an elusive group, known only to a few. They are few and do not tell their secrets easily What I write now, was all I was allowed to learn when I found their secret group. \nThey told me that if I wanted to find them again, I would have to follow the dirt corners out of the home of the great trees. Although this was cryptic, I suppose that it is their way of finding the worthy. After finding them, the person has passed his first test. \nThere are supposedly two more tests, but those are decided on during training. For those who wish to become kin and learn the secrets of magic... search for them. You will find them where the corners point and then you will have passed the first test.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finlay Information Sheet", "guyplayingpc", "Name: Finlay Race: Northerner Age: 25 Gender: Male", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire", "Undeelad", "Fire...the greatest element of destruction, causing explosions,dangers,and gasses of death everywher In Aegis I now have logs and netherrack on fire, and lava down the ladder. To show my love for fire, it is great to see my entrance.\\", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Wall", "Todd877", "((This requires a flint and steel.)) Fire Wall is your basic fire spell. It can be used as attack or defense depending on your situation. Be warned, do not use in wooden buildings you don't want to destroy. When you have prepared the spell, say Brisingr (or any other spell) and fire will be summoned to you. Also be aware that once summoned, the fire will acte like regular fire. You can get burned.", ""),
        StaticBook("First  Undead Experience", "gombie", "okay friend", ""),
        StaticBook("First Kill", "BannanaToYou", "Yes the first kill, my torture. It was oh so loverly. I burned him and slit his eyelids open, cuttin g at his stomach, it was so juicy     when his guts spewed all over the floor onto my feet \"Haha, its already came out. Kill him\"", ""),
        StaticBook("First Prophecy", "501warhead", "Tolta, 10th of The Second Seed, 1338 \nI write this because even now it haunts my dreams. \nI was reading through the scroll of foresight, one of three I own... \nAnd a particular phrase jumped out at me. This was no accident, I am sure. \nIt reads... \nFate, The Harshest Mistress of them All, \nDoom, the Man of Few, But Unforgettable Words, \nBoth of These guide a young man to his Fall, \nTo allow a tale that unravels us like Birds. \n- What would this possibly meen? Hm.. \nClues point to this period roughly in time, it will occur soon. \nBut what Fall could it meen? Who is the young man? \n I do not belive it is an accident that fate and doom are both personized \nBut who? \n*These words are strange, as if someone spilled water on the page, but they form letters* \nB \nI \nT \nO", ""),
        StaticBook("Flare's Diary", "LordCtmon", "Entry 1 \n \n I joined the Shad'Rin a few weeks back. They have taken me in as if I were family. I have been trying to gain their trust ever since I joined. I have gain the trust of almost all their members, but I have a feeling some don't like me. I have built the wall around outpost in this new world that has yet to be completely  discovered \n Enrty 2 We were attacked by a horde of ghasts today! We had to fix the walls that were blown to bits by the ghast fireballs.I was severly burned by one fireball that hit the ground near me. I plan on exploring the verge more tomarrow! \n \n Entry 3 \n It has been writing for awail while the rain ran down my windows. I have been writing for awail.It has been raining for most of the day,and Arthus and I have been stuck in our houses.Once the rain stops we plan to visit our neighboring towns and peopl e.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fleeing the Fight", "Kahzo", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Flyer", "Ren1010", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Flyer - The Rusty hook tavern", "Pur3pros", "cancel", ""),
        StaticBook("FOA attack plan", "MrJakKiD", "Three stages of attack- Preperation,Agrovation,Finalization - So.. We must prepare lots of Arrows, Building Materials, Armour,Weaponry, Lots of our Brothers must aid us and one or two Undead may be a usefull asset as they would be good to keep the Ascended fools off our backs. -So the preperation of the Attack is mostly done but we need two attack lines and a final place where we may fend off any stragglers if we get overwhelmed", ""),
        StaticBook("FOA Beginnings", "ComradeRenzbro", "The FOA, or Followers of Aeriel, is mostly made up of all the members of UAC and collborated with the Wardens. The FOA are now the official \"army\" so to speak of the Ascended while the Wardens, now known as the Paladins, are the, well, Paladins of the Ascended. The FOA follow the same rules of the UAC so no differences in anything like that. There isn't much of a history to them yet but great things are expected of them very soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("FoA records", "erik0821", "FoA_Commander_Maur , And Captian Sam FoA_Diplomat_Davan", ""),
        StaticBook("FOA_1", "j1j2j3j4j3", "((Somehow, I screwed up the first book, I'll try to reqrite.)) ((Tommarrow, skills come out! I am excited, as I believe 1.4 is the best thing since sliced bread)) \n Today, Mor'Guant (Mor') has left the FOA for who-knows-what. I would ask, but I repect his privacy       to much. He was a great lad, I hope nothing happens to him.", ""),
        StaticBook("FOA_2", "j1j2j3j4j3", "((Today, skills are coming out. We expect 1min-~30min till arrival. So excited!)) \n Today, Cmdr. Blaedr decided I should be promoted to private due to my dedication! I feel that I earned it, but I could not do it without the help of Maur, Erik, and Mor' before he left. Much thanks to all!", ""),
        StaticBook("FOA_3", "j1j2j3j4j3", "((Skills have come out, bout 29 in sword. Not bad for one day of training.)) \n Today, the Druids have decided to make a park in Aeriel's Keep. It is a nice tree, and I thank them for it. But it actually turns out that Sage Arcadius wanted a park, and they made a tree. \n Also today, a rather strange man came to our gate. He asked Garn and I to retrieve his diamond sword, which fell down a well. We doubted the story, but offically turned him down due to that not being our job.", ""),
