        StaticBook("Forbidden", "bryce141", "Scene Opens with 2 Orcs walking through woods. \n Orc 1: Me No Like Thisss \n Orc 2: Me tew \n They walk past Tree with 2 elves in it and elves jump down and surround them \n Taka: What now litlle orcs? \n Orcs draws swords \n ORc 2: Me family ill hear bout tis \n Taka: Lets hope they do \"Smiles\" \n 2 elves atack with swords and Taka sends arrow through them both \nScene Cahnges to in the Orcs castle, with warlord on his throne \nWarlord: Attacked ye say, on tuh patrol? \nAssistant: Tats right, twoo dead, its dem treehuggers \nWarlord: hmmmm den pwepare a raiding party, and bewing me lad \nAssistant: yess 'ir \nScene changes to warlord, assistant and son sneaking on to elven farm .  THe horn blows in the distance and Taka runs with other 2 elves with swords to fingt. ((fight)) THe Warlord and assistant charge while son scared slowly sneaks a way \nScene changes to elven garden where Shila sets reading .  W.S comes around corner and finds her reading .  Shila looks up to find him and goes to scream . W.S. Grabs her and covers her mouth. \nW.S.: Ye scream and ye die \nShila Nods \nW.S. Lets go, pushing her to the ground \nW.S. Sits on bench and Shila joins him.  W.S. looks at feet sad \nShila: Is somthing wrong? \nW.S.: Im thee warlords son, And yet me a 'orword Im scared to fight \nShila looks at him \"Everyone has their own special talent\" \nW.S. Smiles \"hmm\" \nTaka: Shila? Both on bench jump up \nShila: \"Go\" As she pushs him \nW.S.: Wait, me vant to see ye gain. \nShila Thinks \"Come to the castle tomorrow and climb thee vines to me chambers\" \nW.S. Smiles and runs off \n New Day \nNarator: W.S. Comes the next night looking for his new elven love \nShila comes out onto her balcony while W.S. comes forht from the shadows and begins to clim ((climb)) for her \nShila runs to him and helps pull him over hugging him \nW.S.: I missed 'ou \nShila: And me as well They stare into eachothers eyes \nNarator: W.S. did this for many moons each time sneaking to the elven land for his new true love . However, The Warlord was getting suspious of his sons silences at night so he sent forth his assistant to follow them \nAssistant comes forth and seems them and scene ends \nScene opens back in throne room \nWarlord: HE WHAT! Me own lad 'ith thee treehuggers........... (looks at assistant) bring me thee girl And bring me lad 'ere  Assistant leaves and in comes W.S. \nWarlord: Ahhhhh goooood.... Lad I been noticen ye ben a little kind lately, not Orcish \nW.S.: ((shrugs)) I........ I'm just not a fighter! ((braces for hit)) \n When it doesn tcome  he looks up, ((Warlord stares at him)) \nWarlord: We will make a fighter of ye yet......... We have captured e TreeHugger and we eh 'avin um killed 'or motivation to our people, and lad 'oull kill um. \nW.S.: Yes father ((bows)) \nAssistant walks in with Shila tied up \nWarlord: So ye be the one that be distracting me lad ((Shila struggles)) HHAHAHAHAHA Throw 'er in thy cells.  ((looks at Shila)) Rest up, for tomorrow ye got a 'ig day \nNext Day \nScene opens to a orcish city where Shila is taken through the city to the stocks W.S. Is looking the other way as she is put on the stocks, Warlord hands W.S. a axe \nWarlord: 'ere lad \nW.S. turns around and stares down at Shila as Shila stares back up at him. \nW.S. turns to his father: YOU MONSTER!! Trys to swing axe at him however Assistant catchs his hand \nAssistant: W.S. Do you duty kill the enemy, strike at Taka's daughter and deal him a blow \nW.s stares down at Shila and drops axe \nWarlords eyes widen: YOU, YOU ARE NO LAD OF MINE((picks up axe)) If you 'will not, the I 'ill kill the both of ye \nAssistant removes Shila and places W.S. on the stock.  Warlord raises axe \nTaka and 2 other elves run in to camp, Taka sending a arrow through The warlord \nAssistant runs off to hide, as W.S. undoes chains bounding Shila . Taka walks to the 2 lovers looking at both in turn finishing with W.S.:you truly love her? \nW.S. Aye me lord ((bows)) \nTaka nods and walks offwith other elves trailing \nThe lovers stare into eachothers eyes before leaning in to kiss. \n \n \nTHE NED ((hahah END))", ""),
        StaticBook("Forbidden Love!", "xHyPeR_AuSSiE", "A few years ago, an Undead and an Elf, fell in love. It was unfortunate for the Undead, she was tortured and jailed for years for telling Iblees of this elf, she did not care, all she wanted was the elf. When the elf finally met up again with the Undead he cried, and said.. \"I thought i'd lost you\" That is when the Undead said, \"I could never leave you, I could not live without you\" The elf did not like the Undead or their Nature but could not care less around her They are still together today hiding in secret hoping one day she will be freed and become not Undea d They still spend any moment they can, it is a scary thing for the Elf, because if he is caught by Iblees, he will die end", ""),
        StaticBook("Foreign City Greeting", "Sidhion", "Hail, I'm Raban the Mute and would like to enter your town. To either spend the day or night and trade a bit. Please return this book after reading, thanks", ""),
        StaticBook("Forever Spoken", "JoeqMafia", "Trees wear oval blades and make the great blue shirt above have splashes of grass against it. The wooden hand holding the shining crystal ball giving off rays of fortane. climbing trees is like a skyscraper climbing to the heavens. Written by Josiah Q. Ojerio \"Scilence\" Those moments before you spoke were bliss. You've disturbed them; You've chapped the libs Of scilence The atmosphere has become tense, The euphonic atmoshpere of scilence. Written by Helen Williams \"The Battle\" Violent clamourings locked within, A thousand squirming worms, Burrowing through loops and coils, Sealing the light, the warmth, the sun. Paired voices, incessantly, Orchestrating my downfall. Gnawing away with the assurance of validity. The proud stammering defense, Weakens, stretches an arm like a drowning man, That is finally pulled under. The glimer of hope, Smothered snuffed out, Crumpled, exhausted, Defeated again. Written by Louise Yvonne Clare \"Scissors\" You gave me scissors to cut the bond between us, a tool to do the deed you did not wish to be attributed to you. Written by Saundra Akers", ""),
        StaticBook("Forging your first Artifice - a Artificing Guide by Garrik Forgeheart.", "SapphireShard", "Creating your first Rune Weapon is not something to be take lightly - it is a undertaking that will take you several days - if not months, to create. Here is a brief guide to creating for own Rune Weapon, although the process will vary from project to project. Firstly. You will need a item to Rune-Spell upon. This should be a weapon that can be easily maintained - since a broken weapon will lose it's runes in a effort to stay together . It should also be a weapon that you are profficient with - otherwise, what is the point? For my example, i shall create a Rune-Axe, which was made with the intention of cleaving opponents armour and defenses. It is important that you give your weapon a unique name - it will make apply runes easier, as the weapon will answer to its name, meaning that only the person holding its true name can wield it. This axe shall be called Wall-Breaker. Secondly, create a area in which you can easily sit in quiet and comfort - since runing can b e a hard and arduous process - and you dont want butt-cramps to be part of your weapons runes, right? Harharhar! Then, lay the weapon out in front of you, and place your hand on it. Then, think of the action of the rune you wish to apply to the weapon. for instance, i thought of cleaving opponents into itty-bitty pieces for mine! the rune for Cleaving is Ar-wyrn-dur. however, for your own runes - you will have to discover the names for them yourself! As i said, this isnt meant to be easy! Over time, the applications of runes will build up a lattice of runes over the weapon surface . The thicker and more consistent this lattice is, the stronger the weapon will be. Take CARE over this! This is the important part of the Rune-Spelling! If you continue to build up these runes, eventually the weapon will be ready to use! If you've followed this guide- hopefully you will now have your very own Rune-Weapon! Use it well! Use it often! Use it wisely! For this weapon will last as long as you care for it! Do not underestimate it's power! Of course, every rune-weapon has it's drawbacks - all of them will have their own consciousness - and can freely choose whether to do what you want to use it for. Forcing a weapon against it's Will will have negative results- usually bad ones!", ""),
        StaticBook("Form of Government of the Reformed Church", "whoppering", "In this book are all the rules, jobs, do's and don'ts written with respect to th employment. \n In the 'Reformed Church of Aegis and nearby districts' we have the following order: \n \n \n\n: God; the Aegis God, our truth.\n: Upper Pastor: This person is responsible for the whole church, and leads it through Gods word. He is the head of the whole council (After this: Synod). He can write books. \n: Pastors: Pastors are responsible for one of a few churches. The have a vote in the Synod. They can write books after they are approved by the Upper pastor. \n : Missionary: These people are starting a church. To do evangelism, education in a country where people are not very religous active. They have to be at the Synod, however they dont have a vote. \n : Members: These people vote for a pastor and for their church and are a member of one of the churches, and help and donate them \n \n \n We have rules for every employment in our church. Because of these rules, the organization can function properly. \n Local missionary post: \n A local reformed mission post is sponsered by the whole reformed church. All pastors need to help build them, and members can donate minas for the missionaries. Missionaries need to bring the word of God, and the doctrine of the Reformed Church. If the synod decides to shut down the mission post (what happened in Krugmar twice), the missionary needs to stop immediately with his evangelism. \n Local Church: \n Members of a local church need to respect the doctrine of the church. They'll have to be respectful against the pastor that leads their church. If all members want a new pastor they can remove him. However the members first need to consult with God and the upper pastor. The Upper pastor is responsible for the Big reformed church near the Aegis temple too. There is his home. It is forbidden to drink ale in a church. Swearing will not be accepted \n Reformed church organization: \n The synod has a meeting every month. There they discuss about God, and things that are happening in our world. Like war or wicked developments. The synod manages the minas , the church buildings, and the pastor homes. And they appoint missionaries. The pastors can vote for an upper Pastor. In the synod they approve written books too, and they can remove Pastors who dont preach the word of God and our church.", ""),
        StaticBook("Formations and Tactics", "huddwudd5", "Arrowhead Formation \n aye", ""),
        StaticBook("fort destruction stratagy", "Kingkiwionia", "first, we need 4 battlegroups, group each should have at least 5 people in each. then we send 3 of the 4 to attack the gate.  while the 4th group desroys the fort from behind. Option A: they see the destuction team and send a group to attack. focus attack on that group Option B: they flee to their secondary fort.  send everyone into the main frot and rain arrows upon Option C: they kill the attack group. send the destruction group back to the base, and re group Option D: if they surrender. take conrol over the fort finish", ""),
        StaticBook("Fort Kios's House Architecture", "Aceeri", "Flooring: The floor of a house in Fort kios is mainly just wooden planks. \n Walls: The walls of the house in Fort Kios have regular wood in a line around  the bottom of the walls. On the corners of the walls are regular wood going up all the way to the roof. In between all of the wood, is wooden planks. On the front view of the house, 2 blocks off from the door is a window. On the backside of the house is just plain wooden planks. On the side walls of the house there are wooden planks going in 2 blocks on each side and then in the middle is a 4x4 window \n Stairs: The stairs of a house in Fort Kios are on the side of the back wall only 1 block wide. \n \n Roof: The roof has wooden stairs on the edges and wooden halfsteps on the corners. In the middle is wooden planks. In the very middle of the roof (4x4 Area) You put wooden planks. And surrounding the wooden planks are wooden halfsteps. \n \n That is how you make a hosue in Fort Kios.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fort Norodrum Advertisment", "HICHERV07", "Head up north to Fort Norodrun to get a high paying, enjoyable and safe job!  the job includes: \nFree House! \nChoice of Job ( Woodcutting, Mining etc) \n Friendly Workmates \n to find Norodrun, exit the north gate and head on the western road and past the ice river, across it, you find the brilliant Fort Norodrun", ""),
        StaticBook("Fort Report", "Tyber1231", "By Aren Whitestorm, on 6th day of Joma, 1336 \nI have got some information from suspect Henry O'Brien, worker who works there. He was working on the walls, but he says he seen hooded and robed people, Dressed in blue, red and purple robes, entering the fort with 'normal' people. He also claims that they were holding the meetings in the mansion. Also, he wasn't aware of prison cells, indicating workers were not told fully of this place. \nLast clue I managed to get was name of the owner, Goblin. As far as I know, he owns or owned an inn beside King's Road.", ""),
