        StaticBook("Frenchie's Fantastic General Store!", "AFLpro", "Frenchie has been told he is the cheapest salesmen in all of Aegis! First of all, he sells coal for only 5 minas! That is around 20-30 minas below market price! He is also amongst the finest chefs in Aegis, selling PERFECTLY cooked cakes for only 70 minas, imagine quenching your sugar lust for only 70 minas! ; Frenchie also is a master blacksmith, offering high quality tools, armour and repairs at extremely low prices, just look at the signs, that chain armour is cheap, isn't it! ((OOC: Frenchie's Fantastic General Store is located in Terriko Suburbs (x-700, y-300) ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Frenchie's journey", "AFLpro", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Freya's Diary.", "SapphireShard", "Day one, Itnan, 23rd of Snows Maiden. Today i was shown around the Mages Tower, which was a great honour. I learn many things, such as the Guild Masters of each Capital. Cataris, our Guide, told us he is the Guild Master of Al'khazar. Ogland is the Snow Fields Guild Master. To Become a Apprentice i must gain the Guild-Master's approval. Apprentices are trained at the local Guild Halls. If they are worth, they advance to... *pause* *a small annotation next to this line says \"Worthy, my pen spilled.\" So, as i was saying, once you are Worthy, you will advance to a mage... But not a full mage, not by a mile. I hope this book is enchanted, i have five pages already... I hope this book is enchanted, i've written a fair bit already. Oops, i'm still getting the hang of this. Anyway, you need the Arcane mage's approval to advance further. You can also find a \"token\" to get a good chance to become a apprentice. I should enquire further... Me, Elena, and Grimbeard, have agreed to find the token, for better or for worse. We were told that the Mage's are looking for a special virtue to join. I wonder what it could be...? *many small annotations adorn this page* We are told that there is another token near... excuse me, Shits End. a fort near the undead keep in the frozen north. The Undead. It's always the bloody undead, isnt it? I've finished my journal for today! Perhaps i should show it to Cataris... Yes. Cataris Hints that there is a journal by \"Nitholiak\" that could help us. Kamees, 26th of Snow's Maiden. Today we reached Shit's end in the north. Lightnnig endlessly pierces the horizon... fortunately, Cataris helped us. We read a book by Cataris's Brother. It writes about him being \"Mr. Lonely\" We left that place, and headed north, to the Gravestone of Cataris's Daughter. When we arrived, we were struck with horror. Cataris's Daughters tomb has been defilied by undead. I swear i see a tear in Cataris's eye. We camp for the night here. In the morning, Cataris is gone. We move south, passing the Undead's Keep. Guraim blocks our way, and we promptly give him something we wont forget. We arrive back at winterfell, worse for wear, but alive. Itnan, 9th of The Second SEed, 1307 Today i spent minding the Al'khazar gate, making checks on the gate for signs of magical or more physical sabotage. I also caught two necromancers, with the help of the city guard. One, named \"Sconn\" who ranted all the way to jail about Iblees, poor bugger. he sure enjoyed his time in prison, although he escaped shortly thereafter... Joma, 13th of the Second Seed. Today me and Grimbeard started arranging a expedition to the North. We hoped to find the tomb which had eluded us for many previous expeditions. Although, Cataris hinted that the Tomb may or may not be found [?]. Sabet, 28th of Sun's Smile, 1305. This week i am helping Gabriel Hightower develop Kramaroe. I have invented a ingenious (his words not mine, hehe) system for growing crops. i shall look forward to installing it. Joma, 31st of Sun's Smile, 1305. Today me and Gabriel set out, to establish a base in the Far North.", ""),
        StaticBook("From Alethion to his Wife", "Alectriciti", "Dear Rhisereld. Dear Rhisereld, It's been a whole day without speaking to you and it kind of sucks. It's a lot like the frustration I get WHEN Akorta talks. Let me get to the point. What's this whole thing with seven? I know it means a lot to you, but I don't think it's really good for you. It's become an obsession. Items in the chests have been stacked in groups of seven, I've seen some of your writings... I just don't want you becoming obsessed with it or anything. I'll be off on a little journey for awhile so I may not see you. I love you very much. Please be careful how much of these things you take in. By the way. I like your new clothes. Especially your jacket. I'm working on something myself I think you'll like. Not my military clothing... Just my casual wear. Anyway... *draws a smile* =] Love you! \n ~Alethion", ""),
