        StaticBook("Good Luck With Your Exams! - PyroFuzion", "PyroFuzion", "Study Hard!", ""),
        StaticBook("goodbye", "bondb", "(( ooc))  I Erik (bondb) am leaving the wardens. I am leaving because of my fellow wardens well basicly hate me so i think its best to just leave I will miss some of you and others not at all well gooooodbye wardens. bondb out peaceeeee <3 Quazar", ""),
        StaticBook("Goodbye For Now", "Jtheo2016", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Goodbye.", "moon_stone", "Goodbye, Salinor. I will miss you, but I dont think I  can handle this world alone. Please be happy. I dont wish to be in a place that doesnt need me. I really was never good at goodbyes... hah hah... Thank you for being my only friend. Please have a good life. I'll be watching over you... Again, thank you, and goodbye... Just... be happy... okay? -Sora", ""),
        StaticBook("Goregaths Diary", "Uboob", "Day One: Today i have been informed that my farther is passing away and that he has gone  to live the rest of his few days in peace. Day Two: Its my birthday tomorrow and i am excited, shame my farther cannot be there. I have been introduced to Veneton and Rogorin, friends of my farther. They seem nice. Day 3: Today is my birthday, horrible weather.     Day Four, I am in search of a cure for my bloodline curse. No luck today. Day Five: i have found a man called NightShade he seems to be helping me. But i dont know if i can trust him Day Six: I took the cure me and NightShade made today. It does not seem to have worked. But it has made me age two years. Day Seven: FIRST KILL, it was for a good reason, an Undead entered New Terriko. I was to start training today but it never happened Day Eight: Today we berried my father. It was sad and he had alot of friends there. The Mayor of New Terriko has gone in search of a cure. Hope he has more luck than i did. Day Nine: Nothing interesting happened today. We are going to be putting my father in his grave soon RIP Karak. Day Ten: The Mayor returned with his friend the enchanter Jordan. Jordan is sick with some curse put on him from the Undead but he said that he wants to help me befor he turns. Day Eleven: Its time, we are about to attempt to cure me once more... Success i have been cured!!!.. But poor Jordan.. The spells he did took alot away from him, he went mad and jumped from the highest point in New Terriko.. RIP Jordan... Day Twelve: Entering New Terriko was strange there was writing on a wooden wall... Written in BLOOD... Day Thirteen: Jordan has still not been seen and i fear he may be lost for ever... Strange... There is some writing on the walls of my fathers old house but it is not his hand writing... i need to look into this. Day Fourteen: I have done it! I have joined the Wolverines and can fight along side them. I want to get into the fighting spirt like my father. and become Officer of the Archers. Day Fithteen: I have done alot at the market place today. Finally finished the new tunnel and will be working more into that soon. My father would be pleased with me if he saw me now. I went to my fathers grave today. The Wolverines have marked his gave telling the world HE WAS A WOLVERINE.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorelath", "_Player_2_", "I am a tall orc with many scars from countless battles, I am known as \"wind\" because i am like a harmless breeze but if i will i can cut foe into 2 with one strong blow \n Ever since i was young i was feared for my advance swordmen skills taught to me be a Warboss who made me kill countless Zombie Pigmen and always put me in arena fights because he would always say \"You are the only fighter that can entertain me\" I was told not to kill my opponent, so i would try not to swing at full pace, but i still ended up scaring my foes. They started to through multiple enemies at me so i would have to fight between 5 to 10 people at once, they would get 1 or 2 hits on me but i was a man of my name, just like the wind it was impossible to kill me or even touch me \n i was sent into war multiple times to take a whole nation on my own . i did it with ease, i would only get a scar or two at max aftertaking down many nations i started to get old, and tired and ended up on my death bed at the age of 400, i asked my wife \"why cant i die like a warrior, in combat, why do i have to die like wimp on a death bed?\" my wife replied \"When the warboss gave you the name of \"Wind\" he ment it, you cant be hit, you cant be killed, you move swift and kill quick\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Gortan's Biography", "TheHarveey", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Gortan's Log Book", "TheHarveey", "18/10/2011 Whilst standing Guard at the new Oren Guard Outpost, I was approached by a nervous man, claiming to have been attacked. As with any other person, my initial reaction was to leave the Guard Outpost, an d deal with the problem immediately. However, a slight concern for my personal saftey arose when I noticed the man was gearing himself up with armour, as though he was ready to fight. Being weary, I told the man that I was currently busy with work, and would tend to the matter when I had time. I know that this was a lie on my behalf, but I belive that the Gods shall forgive me of my lies, as it was for the greater good of my personal life. The man in question did not state his name, but I w ill remember his face. May Ariel forgive my treachery, and see through a blind eye at what I may have done. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorthok", "c_h_r_i_s121", "Today Dragga helped me hear da voices of another spirit .He is also a red orc and has the same bands on his arms as me he must also be from the same tribe as Dragga and i . He lived in the tribe all of his life and he met Dragga when she joined, he says that he was in the army that helped search for her parents i think that there was something more between them. . Finally i find that they where married! Gorthok and Dragga where married. They faced many difficult times togeder before dey when searchin for Draggas parents Gorthok say das one time dey whent huntin togeder and dey come accross an undead camp, der was dozens of them he said, he describe de smell as 2000 rotten fish, hur hur. Dragga used ere fist and Gorthok.. Gorthok used magic! he was a shamen! it where a mighty battle, many undead died da day bye afder dey slew all de undeads dey looked at eachoders injuries Dragga looked over at Gorthok to see da he was missin an arm . Dragga helped to get Gorthok back to de tribe and called de High Shamen to see if he could do anthing wid his arm . Da shamen whisperd a spell and the hole on his shoulder healed over but as Gorthok was a shamen he recognized da spell, and he say \"What did ye do to me?!\" Because the spell tha shamen used was dark magic the side effects slowley turned Gorthok into a zombie . The effects are where very gradual he told me, but every night he could feel a bit of himself turn evil...", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorund's Journey; Drumportal, Part I", "Groundhawg", "It was a grey day, the day I left for the open plains. I had assumed that I would be settling down in the big city. I assumed wrong. Almost the moment I arrived, I was being shipped off. The expedition comissioner told me that my skills would be essential to the founding of the settlement. I was to go with six dwarves, to a remote location, and establish a dwarven fortress. The fortress was to be called Drumportal. It would be a name to honor all dwarvenkind.  \n \n It wasn't three hours out of the city, before the arguing commenced. Arguing of when mealtimes were. I grew irritated quickly, and eventually stopped the cart entirely atop a large grassy hill. I grabbed a paper and quill, and scrawled out a schedule that fit everybody's eating habits as close as possible, and still left time for actual travel! it was no easy task, but getting it done proved more useful than expected. In fact, none of the dwarves with me were literate. They thought me some sort of scholarly genius, and I was named expedition leader for it! \n \n When we reached the point marked by the map, we realized why it was ideal. We saw a large, cliff face, going up very steeply for miles. I ordered the carpenter to cut and haul some logs to a pile at the base of the cliff, and he rushed off eagerly, while the rest of us climbed the mountain eagerly. When we reached an acceptable height. Midheld, the miner and I began digging into the rock cliff face. We made an entrance that was wide enough for only three dwarves, stood side by side, and we raised the cieling to fit two dwarves, standing on each other's heads. We dug in and rooms took form. midheld was a more experienced miner, and flew through the stone much quicker than I did. But nobody minded, I was after all, the \"mastermind\". We carved out some workshops, a storage area, a dining hall, and some basic housing. Then came the great haul. Everybody dedicated all their time to bringing all our goods inside. Workshops for our mason, carpenter, jeweler and mechanic were built from the stone which we dug. And we built a fairly strong drawbridge in the main gateway. \n \n Within two weeks we were settled. We had also recieved immigrants from a nearby settlement. Our population reached 83 within two years of settling there. But our traders were noticing strange behavior from the elves. The elves became agitated, and jumpy. Our broker was Kilthan Krespool at the time, and he thought it best to ask why the elves were so on edge. A question to which their only response was, \"Trees... All trees dead.. Murder..\" well it seemed harsh to us. But we left them be. I had assumed that they were just uncomfortable in the deforested plain. But, once again, I assumed wrong. \n \n \n Then the raid landed on our doorstep... \n To be continued...", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorund's Journey; Drumportal, Part II", "Groundhawg", "The first warning signs were the fact that the trees on the border of our territory seemed to be moving. We soon realized that it was actually hundreds of wooden armoured elves, wading like a sea of wood towards us. They flew from the forest with lightning speed, across the plains they swept, towards our main gate. Luckily one of our guardsmen had sounded the alarm, and the gate was puled shut. Creating a wall that they couldn't pass. \n \n The sky then darkened, the sun blocked from us by a swarm of deadly arrows, thousands strong. Our marksdwarves pulled the metal slabs over the cliff face's windows, that we used to fire down on the enemy, and only one dwarf was wounded. \n \n Panic rushed through my body as I realized that Orren, our woodcutter, was still outside! He was frantically banging on the gate for us to let him in, when the elves approached. Orren's wife however, knew he was outside. She rushed to pull the lever to let him in, she thought she could have the gate open long enough to let him in, and close it in time to keep the elves out. Well.. Orren was standing at the base of the gate when she closed it on top of him. Crushing him into the mechanisms, and jamming the brodge open. She had doomed us all and I knew it. I rushed to the military quartder to grab the one crossbow that wasn't in use. Melbul Ottenshikes. A legendary steel crossbow forged by our forgemaster. I had forbidden it's use, for it was too beautiful a weapon to sully against elves. But I grabbed it anyways. Along with a quiver of bolts, and rushed off to my family, hiding in my bedroom, behind my office. I encountered one elf along the path, wrestling with a peasant. I jammed my knife in his skull, and it stuck there. I was too worried for my family to bother pulling it free, and I rushed down the crowded halls. I got to my office and barred the double doors shut. Then pushed my desk in front of them, to keep the elves out. I then retreated to my bedroom to find my wife, Laania, and my son Kenbu, sat in the corner. Kenny had tears down his cheeks and Lania looked panicked. \n \n **The pages here are tear stained, but still legible.** \n \n I barred the bedroom door and pushed the bed in front. I then sat and put my free arm around Laania. She couldn't hold her emotions any longer, and broke down to a pitiful sobbing . Quite suddenly, from the halls came screams. The elves had broken into the dining hall, where everybody hid. I reckon the dwarves probably killed a few before they were beaten down by wooden blades. Then came a thud. Loud, it shood me to the bone. Then another, then the sound of footsteps, they were in the office. I stood and raised my crossbow at the door. Then a thud, the door slid open three inches, and the bed slid with a squeel. Kenny screamed and an elf hand came through the door. The crossbow fired and the arm was soon pinned to the wall through the wrist. Then the door was flung wide and I fired again. Putting a bolt in another elf's head. As he fell I grabbed Lania by the arm and soon we were all flying down the halls, I was leading with Lania carrying Ken behind me. Three elves spotted us and gave chase. I spun around and fired a bolt, killing one of the three, but the other two were close behind. \n \n As we entered the deeper cavers, where the ground was rough and freshly dug, disaster struck. Laania tripped on a loose rock, and fell. the elves reached her and showed no mercy. By the time I reached them, my wive and only son's heads were caved in. They lay in a pool of blood. Soon my screams of rage drowned out all other sound. I smashed both elves over the head with the crossbow, the crossbow broke off in his skull. The other one I bludgeoned to death with the what remained. My screams of rage caused a shake in a weak spot of the tunnel, and it caved in behind me. Luckily there was a mining pick in the tunnel next to me, and I evenually managed to dig my way out. To find everybody dead, lying around the tunnels of what was once my home. The elves had left by the time I made it out. So I set off, back to the dwarven city. It would be a long and treacherous hike. \n \n That concludes \"Gorund's Journey; Drumportal\" \n For continuation, find a copy of \"Gorund's Journey; Trip home, Part I\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorund's Personal Journal", "Groundhawg", "Well, I've gone and done it... What I said I'd never do. What I thought I'd never do.. Not after Laania..  \n But it's happened. A woman named Annora, she has the most beautiful and fine hair, and those eyes... Brown as the elven wood of Laurelin, and fourty times as beautiful.. At first I hoped it was a passing crush, but it's lasted longer than a crush would, and those EYES! \n \n I could write fifty ballads about her beauty alone, without going into detail about who she is. I've spoken with her often of late, and every word she says just further's my ever deepening love for her.. \n \n I met another woman today, she was friendly enough. It was strange though, I didn't notice how attracive she was until another man pointed it out to me, and that still seemed like an empty beauty.. Then after we all returned home, Annora came into thr room, and I was immediately washed over with the radiating warmth of her presence.. Feelings like this must be what I know only as love.. \n \n Disaster struck today, I went out for a drink with Lynx and Annora..... Beautiful Annora... We were all havin a great time, when this regally dressed-in-royal-blue fucker comes in! He wander's around us like we're peasants.. Well, I didn't want to be weak or even LOOK weak in front of Annora... So I tossed a quiet insult at him, but he heard it! So I responded to his questioning with \"What's one as regally dressed as you, care what a single dwarf thinks of ye,\" Soon we were nearing fisticuffs when he does the unthinkable. He tosses me a single Mina, and says \"You need it.\" Well, I fuckin lost it! I went berserk! In the end though, I ended up making more a fool of myself than he ever made of me. I don't know why it happened, but my theory is that my blind lust to impress Annora drove me to it. I hope I can quell this problem soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gotrek was like any other Dwarf, mined and smited by learning from their fathers.", "DwarfGuy45187", "The Story of Lefor", ""),
        StaticBook("Gragor's Journal", "JonnyC2011", "Day 1 \nToday me went to North Orc Camp with Bein to see damage. It be terrible up dere. Camp be destroyed with fire everywhere. Me thinks there be no survivors but me still be hopeful. We see Alstion half destroyed and it be in fire too. But Winterfell be in good shape again, it be strange mon. Maybe Humans plan to be holdin da line dere again....... \nDay 2 \nI been tasked with buildin da Dock for Sanhar. Dis will be intrestin! After thought me know how to be constructin, me not wait to see finished! \n Day 3 \n Me be hungry, sortin out da land be good work but need food soon. Okay, me really need food now, stomach hurtin now.... Spinerippa be givin me food, not hungry now! Tasty! Back to work soon. These Undead be on ma mind a lot, seein them around our lands. But, Craotor be tellin me there be a war between Human and dem pesky Dwarfs. This could be an oppertunity to be crushin dem Dwarfs and get me revenge!! \nDay 4  \nMe be startin up work on da Dock again when me find Dran. I not be seein him. Me meet Pikto of da Elves today too. Me go buy some Sandstone. Me went to Holmes' Bakery and buy Pork, was good. It be night now, no Sandstone to be findin, me head back to Sanhar and see what me can do. \nDay 5 \nDa Docks main platform be almost complete! It be lookin alright me think. Still be very 'appy to be avin da Dock!", ""),
        StaticBook("Grand Master", "Busenki", "This is the office of negotiation between the Shuuhei company and the Anima Templi. Please act formal and be polite. Thank you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grand Merchant Duties", "Rasun37", "Payment: 500 Minas a week \n Duties: \n Starts Trading Contracts with other cities \n The merchant also has to manage resources within the city. They also conduct trading missions within the city.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grand Merchant Trades", "zuluman111", "First trip out of Kal'Alras a success. Visited Kal'Rog, Kal'Urgruan, and Laurelin. sold chocolate and smooth stone to the elves Also sold much smooth stone to the goblin inn. total profit was 1,200 Minas. Paid to Overseer seeing as Lord Baron has taken ill", ""),
        StaticBook("great news!", "friar7", "i aprehended your thief....ah, who am i kidding, this never happened", ""),
        StaticBook("Green Ravens", "Kamberli", "The Green Ravens are an old elit unit of Besarn. They are founded in the year 1293 whit the objective to protect the Lord of Besarn. They are a small unit but they only recruit the best soldiers. To get recruit you have to do 1 of 3 tasks. \n 1. You have to go to an dungeon of your own and you have to finish it 2. You have to overlife a undead attack and kill minimum 2 of them. 3. You have to fight the leader of the Green Ravens, and if he thinks you'r good enough you pass.    Any race or gender can join the Green Ravens but you have to respect the law and the other members.  \n Rules:  \n 1. You have to serve the Lord of Besarn and the Leader of the Green Ravens. \n 2. You have to respect the laws whit no exceptions. \n 3. You never serve an other army! \n 4. You have to life in one of the barracks of the Green Ravens. \n 5. You have to fight for the Lord and for Besarn, you never surrender. Even if it means your death . If you disregard one of these rules, you get punished by the judgment of the Leader of the Green Ravens! \n \n", ""),
