        StaticBook("Greetings", "tigergamer", "This letter is a notice to Janos, the king and Rhycey. It is about a profession i wish to obtain... well you see over the years i have lived in oren there has been Battles for life and death and i do not wish to see these happen again so i am writing this as a letter to become a Royal_Architect for Alk'hazar I am quite the skilled builder for where i used to live in Malinor and am trying to achieve t his newly found goal!. that is why i ask that you take your time to inspect my architecture and tell me your opinion ((the pic will be on the fourms )) (( mistake", ""),
        StaticBook("Greetings owner of this house! i took shelter here for the night", "jens6851", "Greetings owner of this house i took shelter here for the night... i have gived you some food and materials i hope you can use em i have to say that i took your lether armor i was close to die and i cant survive without one thanks for this amazing hideout", ""),
        StaticBook("Greetings!", "skippy369", "Hello I am Skippy Irongut! I like Mining and I live in Kal'Urguan! I also like lumberjacking and farming! So.... GREETINGS FELLOW!!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Grey's Diner and Body Guards", "greyP", "Come down to Grey's Diner and Body Guard service where we have every food possible, not to mention our Guards that you can rent for a day and night for only 100 minas We have rooms for rent so a tired traveler can rest for just 45 minas, You can find us down the road from Oren to the Right side of the road, or from the temple to the lef t , Come get an Ale and a warm Soup! disable stop", ""),
        StaticBook("grief", "transphat", "yesterday after we both logged off the stairs to the castle was griefed, and sseveral items stolen We know after we both logged off there was only one person left . I must leave now.  may or may not be able to log on for several days. I hope this whole thing gets sorted out and some one kicked from the UAC. sorry i must leave at this time - Thimble", ""),
        StaticBook("Grievances Against King Edmund", "muchoman798", "Signatures are at the document's end \nWe, a group of many people, feel that the King of Oren is not satisfying his duties. We would like to list our grievances against him in this text. We would hope that he one day looks at them and understands why we have spelled them out and looks f or a way to fix them. \n-The King permitted a 'peace' treaty to be drawn with the Undead for a period of time. He could ha ve prevented the treaty from existing, but allowed it to continue until an Undead broke it. \n-The King allowed the Undead to freely walk the roads of Oren unscathed by the Guards. \n-The King has allowed the township of Snowy Fields to fall without his presence in battle. \n-The King has not had anyone try to rebuild or reclaim the township of Snowy Fields from the hands of Iblees. \n- The King has spent the Kingdom's minas to build another tower on his Personal Keep, where citize ns are not allowed, when the city of Al'Khazar has many gaps in its walls and when the Guards of Ore n are unpaid and untrained. \n-The King has let there be holes in the defenses of Al'Khazar. They are as follows: \n--An unmanned and usually open Northern gate. This is in the direction of the Undead and leaves Al'Khazar very vulnerable. \n--An unwalled harbor area. This allows any invaders to easily circumvent the need to even breach the walls, since there are none present. \n--An unwalled farming area of Al'Khazar. This allows invaders to do the same as listed in the last opening. \n--A Southern gate that is often untended by guards. \n--Sewers that are not patrolled by guards. \nThe Grievances resume here. \n \n \n-The King has left the Guards of Oren unpaid. \n-The King has left the Guards of Oren untrained. \n-The King does not present an Army of Oren. Should the Undead invade a city other than Al'Khazar, the Government has no ability to save the city, which happened in Snowy Fields where the guards decided to fight for Snowy Fields AGAINST orders. \n-The King does not have any plans made known for a counter attack against the Undead. \n-The King has presented taxes against the shops of Al'Khazar, with a random amount for each shop, and no consideration for the shops profits. \n-The King has not considered asking the people of Oren what they think a fair tax would be. \nThis is our list of Grievances against the King of Oren, in full and unabridged.  We present them to you hoping you will do your best to fix the problems listed in the text previous. We believe that you have had ample time to address most of the issues in the Kingdom with the amount of time you have held the throne. They should now be addressed immediately. \n \nSignatures\n \nErirc Loftson, Sergeant of the Guardians   Adian Brod, General of the Guardians  \nOdkell Huscarl", ""),
        StaticBook("GrimBeards Journal", "dirtryhary", "pretty good", ""),
