        StaticBook("Guide To Being Awesome", "connorr1", "1st Step: Get some good looking clothes to wear. \n 2nd Step: Be friendly and find some friends to hangout with. \n 3rd Step: Find your true love. \n 4th and Final Step: Now your awesome!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Blackjack", "Benben582", "How to play: Blackjack is a simple game where the objective is to reach 21 without going over. If you go over it is called a bust, that is a loss. Your opponet is the dealer. At the start you roll TWICE out of 11. ((/roll 11)) And then the dealer rolls twice out of 11. Then it is your option to say \"Hit me\" or \"Stay\". \"Hit me\" Means you roll again out of 11. Adding to your total score. If you ever go over 21 you lose as stated before. If you say \"Stay\" you cannot roll anymore and then the turn goes to us. Now we have the option to hit or stay. Whoever has the highest number without going over in the end wins. \n1. Roll out of 11 TWICE. ((/roll 11)) \n2. Dealer rolls out of 11 TWICE. ((/roll 11)) \n3. Choose to \"Hit\" or \"Stay\" If you go over 21 you lose. \n4. If you do not go over 21, and choose to stay keep reading. \n5. Dealers turn to \"Hit\" or \"Stay\" \n6. Whoever gets the highest number without going over wins. \n7. ??? \n8. Profit. \n~Only Can be used at the Oceans Casino. We do have the Right to fine if we see illegal Copies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to building a house", "collgrin", "Hello, you have picked this book up cuase ya bored of musta picked the wrong book.But no matter your readin it so lets begin  \nFirst, you must check to have enough materials for a house here is a list that works to da house i be given instruction for 1.64 wood planks 2.64+32 cobblestone now that u have basic list of a small house lets begin Second step, dig a 6x6 plot for your base to outline length and width of house .Once thats done put wood planks in empty space now to place walls go AROUND da 6x6 wit cobble go up bout 4 layers of cobble and place roofing as if it was a floor and dats how to build da most basic house i can imagine with good materials", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide To Farming", "The_Dark_Rage", "in this book I will tell you how to be a good farmer. First up we have Wheat farms.  These are easy.  First you will need a hoe of your skill. Also you will need at least 1 seed, and a water source ( bucket of water) Wheat farming is basically strip farming.  Straight rows of wheat and water. make sure every wheat may get water", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide To The Undead", "Benboboy", "The undead are facinating creatures, they seem to have no real goal other than total destruction. They have an amazing resistance to fire and lava which means the Nether realm is a good secure place for them. Although they may seem brutal, I have found that you can escape them with words and not combat. I have escaped 3 undead this way myself, just tell them you mean them no harm and you hope they mean none to you. I have found them to admire  bravery towards them as long as you do not intend to harm them. The undead are very magical creatures and are able to cast fireballs, summon lightning and call upon the dead to aid them in battle. The undead use the lightning spell a lot and this makes their location easy to find, if you see a random flash with no rain, it is the undead. The undead are normaly dressed in black robes with hoods, so many get blamed of being undead by the colour of their robes. The undead are very powerful but very weak too. They would not stand a chance against a sword, they mainly focus on long range magic attacks. Because of their weakness, they do not normaly wear armor because the just cant hold up the weight of it, after all, they have been dead for a while. The undead are servants of Iblees and they all worship him greatly. Do not ever make fun of Iblees in front of an undead unless you would like to see your own ribcage pulled out.  \n I have been to the undead capital in the nether and the air seems to be tainted with sulpher. this makes attacking the nether very hard as only the undead can survive there, This taint can appear anywhere in the world too if the undead take control of somewhere and create a nether portal. It appeard that the closer you get to the source of the taint the , the stronger it becomes. Getting close the it is almost impossable for non undead. on my recent journeys to the undead, I have discovered that they have a portal from the city in the mortal realm, to the large city in the nether. this is how I got into their capital in the nether. The door was open thankfully and the undead were busy fighting of orcs. While I was inside the city, I saw a strange chapel building, I can only assume that thats where they worship their master Iblees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Tur'Evelon", "rittsy", "- Introduction -\n \n Tur'Evelon is a city where members of all races can live together peacefully. It is governed by The Council, which is a collection of four members of each race. Four members within The Council , a member from each race, form The Grand Council. A Prince and a Princess lead The Grand Council. \n \n - Location - \n \n Tur'Evelon is located far to the south of the elven city of Laurelin. To get to it from the Laurelin docks, head to the elven mine, but head down the diagonal road right before the mine and follow it until you reach Tur'Evelon. \n \n - The Law -\n \n -Absolutely no fighting, racism, or feud between races.  Punishment determined by severity of crime by The Council. \n -No murder. Punishable by a week in jail.\n -No assassination. Punishable by ten days in jail if unsuccessful, or death if successful.\n -No theft. Punishment determined by severity of crime by The Council.  \n-Respect members of The Council, and don't aggravate them. Punishments range from a warning to a jail time of four days. \n \n - Activities -\n \n ~ The Arena ~ \nThe Arena is located in the Orc district, and holds tournaments every so often. (( every other IRL day at 8:00pm EST )) \n \n ~ Competitions ~\n \n Occasionally (( Saturdays 6:00pm EST )), Competitions are held with various prizes to win. Prizes are announced at start of competition.\n \n ~ The Marketplace ~   \n Besides a place to buy or sell your favorite items, the Market is a great place to converse with other citizens and catch up on the latest news. \n \n - Homes - \n \n As Tur'Evelon is still a new city, homes are available everywhere, in all racial districts. Prices range from 600m to 3000m for homes. Home layouts and appearances are based on the race they were designed for. Elves have wooden houses, humans have wool houses, dwarves have stone caves, and orcs have sandstone houses. \n \n - To Sum It All Up - \n If you want to live in a diverse community where quarrelling is at its minimum, there is strong leadership, and fun activities for all citizens to enjoy, then Tur'Evelon is the city for you! In order to join our wonderful community, all you have to do is buy a house here, and you are immediately able to participate in the wonderful things offered at Tur'Evelon!", ""),
        StaticBook("Guidebook of Alstion's Allies.", "SapphireShard", "Quick Reference list for the Gate Duty Guard. \n \n Allies; Alstion Civilians, Grimbeard and his Trooops. The Architect Jino, The Followers of Aeriel. Gabriel and the Hightower Family, Alek Treefellers , Nitholiak VonSchlichten, Oren Guards, Vardak, Ivrae, King Edmund, Saint Daniel,Druids of Malinor, Laurelin Rangers/Wardens.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guidelines of the Creed.", "Psiop412", "The Three Tenets \n \n 1. Stay your Blade from the Flesh of an Innocent \n \n 2. Hide in Plain Sight \n \n 3. Never Compromise the Brotherhood \n \n Nothing is True; Everything is permitted", ""),
        StaticBook("Guidlines For Ranking Up", "patato12", "In the W.A. there are six Ranks And recruitment phase . As a recruit you must be in the Guild five day's. After that you move on to cheif getting to cheif is quite easy it recurie's you to be active and helpful toward's the guild to get to cheif donate wood or small amount's of mina's this greatly improve's the chance's of us noticeing you . : To get to Sergant Your best bet is to be Active and participate in War's. It Also Help's if you donate Full stacks of Wood and small amount's of Iron. And Donate A medium amount of the mina's you have and this will help get you noticed. \n Crusador To get to crusador you have proven that your very active And Donated a Good Amount of Mina's. Also It help's If you donate a diamond or two and and quite a bit of Iron. \n To get to Vetran This is a few Select the best of the best These few have given their lives to the guild They have  Given countless iron And mina's and a few diamond's Vetran is the Goal of all Warrior's Vetran's Must Always Have Iron on hand. \n The ONE This Person is a diplomatic person overseing all and logging the work's they are a Vetran And Have donated more to the guild then the Average Vetran. Thee_ One is Able to step in to vote If A council member is Unable to vote A part of being the one is righting current mission's and Keping track of recors's Record's* And makeing sure recruit's are Active and Busy", ""),
        StaticBook("Guild Invitation", "Ashyer", "You've been selected to join the guild of Dawnlight, We are fighting back at the undead! We are near the whispering isles. This invitation must be brought along to our hideout.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guilt", "Rhisereld", "I've hardly been outside my room in days \nI don't feel that I deserve the sunshine's rays \nThe darkness helped until the whiskey wore away \nAnd then I realised that conscious never fades \n When you're young you have this image of your life \nThat you'll be scrupulous and  maybe even be a wife \nYou make boundaries you'd never dream to cross \nAnd if you happen to you wake completely lost \n \nI remember someone old once said to me : \nThat lies will lock you up with truth the only key \nBut I was comfortable and warm inside my shell \nI couldn't see this place would soon become my hell \nSo is it better to tell and hurt ? \nor lie to save their face? \nI guess the answer is don't do it in the first place \n \nI step outside my mind's eye for a minute \n \n \nLooking over me like a doctor looking for disease \nOr something that could ease the pain \nBut nothing cures the hurt, I \nI bring it on by myself \nJust remembering how we were", ""),
