        StaticBook("Henry's Journal", "henrya15", "i am trying to decide if i will try and unite the halflings   and protest the eating  our k ind by orcs its been a tradition by orcs for a while and i just dont know if its possible i dont even know if the orc king can make a law saying no orcs can eat halflings maybe i can get a law passed saying orcs can only eat halflings on orc lands this will be no easy task and i dont even know if other halflings will want to help me if they did maybe the orcs would just capture us all and it would be a gaint feast for them     \"day 2\" i didnt manage to get any support i went to the dwarfs the humans and even the elves but no one seemed to be where i went they were either away or  busy im hoping to hear from someone soon i have heard of a town called dunwood its a town made up of all halflings! isnt it great news i am excited to go and find it it is somewhere in oren and i intend to find it Were doing it! were finally going to do a peaceful march on krugmar i am trying to get as much support as possible more good new i have just been promoted to Medic in the Fo A . The bad new is i think my involvment with the FoA may be ruining my relationship with the knights legacy. The commander baruk who i respect very much seems like he is annoyed with me being in so many guilds and having so many jobs but i am a man who does lots of things he has to expect me to do some other things then just help the knights legacy. being in many groups helps me in very political ways. ive found dunwood its north west on alrlas I have just finished my last source of food I am hungry and almost insane. Dunwood seems almost impossible to find ive been  looking for dunwood but is one hard place to find. today the whispering order is shipping out to winterfell and i still dont know why apperntly i am not to go up north anymore? very confusing sition right now. but if the order need help i will get everyone i can to help us . i hope the orders leader alethion and his wife (who i both respect very much) will not get harmed. . I am now learning the proper way to be a medic from FoA Lt. duvan Still no luck with Dunwood but more monsters after me halfling flesh there was a gaint party in arlas was really fun apperently this group of humans and dwarfs are going to the nether im appart of em I just went into the portal world its very diffrent there are many ruins across the land of the verge I plan to stay at the FoA camp", ""),
        StaticBook("Henry's Journal #2", "henrya15", "DAY #1: I am very worried. Persephone and Alethion      have gone missing. Im afraid they are in love which i really really hope they are not. Im very depressed about these turn of events that i have started drinking a lot more. Alethion has already married Persephone out in the wilderness i bet! Why would Alethion do such a thing to me? I thought me and Alethion were friends. DAY #2: Akorta has made me promise to back him up IF and when Alethion and Persephone return. The only way i would back him up is if he does not kill Persephone. Even though Alethion and her ran off i still very much so love Persephone. I do hope that eventully i will get the chance to marry her, But i feel as if she dosent like me even though she said me and her would be together when we kill Cataris. Then again she ran off with Alethion so i dont know what she thinks now. I still have little hope that me and her can be together.", ""),
        StaticBook("Henry, you can do better than this.", "Alectriciti", "Tell her how you feel, an that you want to protect her from harm. Tell her you will. But don't just tell her. Act upon it. Tell her how her eyes reflect the beauty of nature. Her blue eye reflects the sky. Her green eye reflects the green grass of Dunwood. Tell her the two are precious, not for the way they look... But for the fact that she is a unique halfling. Tell her, act upon it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heracles' Travels: Volume Four", "DoctorTinman", "This edition of my chronicles shall prove very difficult for me to write. Today, all of Aegis has come together at the top of Alkhazar's hill. The Wizard and all of the land's dignitaries are in attendance. My fellow Ascended and I are dressed in our black uniforms. \n Today is a day of mourning, commemorating the death of Oren's great king, Perea. After a few words, the funeral procession is lead down the hill and through the town's baren streets. The assembly of people arrives at the grand church of Al'Khazar. People pile into the pews, and many unable to find seats stand to the back or side. \n The silence is broken as High Priest Everard begins the ceremony. After his share of blessings, Everard was replaced by the king's widow, Dawn. She sputtered out her words through grief-stricken tears. Her face aged and eyes dark. Following Dawn, Master Sage Riizu offered condolences on behalf of the Ascended for failure to our duties to protect Aegis' people from Undead. Riizu showed less emotion than the mortals, but it was clear that he too felt the pain of the people around the building. \n After Riizu finished, High Prince Native of the elves and the Wizard offered their respects to the family of the dead, and spoke to the congregation. \n The events after are hazy in my memory as I am now writing after the fact... However, King Belin addressed the gathering next. Soon after a celebration began due to the NEW king of Oren. Edmund Sheffield addressed the people as Oren's new king, followed by his new seneschal, Saint Daniel. \n We have all been reminded today of the pain caused by Undead, and the holes that one death can leave in the lives of many others. We've also seen how all endings must lead to new beginnings. Dawn has returned to being a humble owner of her bakery, meeting spot of many people who visit Al'Khazar. The new king is regaining control of the Oren Guard and establishing a new army. The old king's carnival has been taken down and is being made into new buildings. \n It is almost as if Oren is facing a period of renaissance now, as they all attempt to move forward. More books are being written, better houses are being built, and more people have joined the great fight against the Undead. For once, everything may finally begin to seem right soon. Random witch hunts have been occuring in Oren lately in wake of the king's passing, but this should lessen as the grief passes. May Aeriel's blessings be upon the new king and his nation of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heracles' Travels: Volume One", "DoctorTinman", "Upon my my recent voyage to the town of Alstion in the Northern Territories, I have fallen into a dark cave located just outside of the city's gates. \n There are strange writings all over the walls and there are various monsters everywhere. This place is most certainly dark. I sense the powers of evil flowing through the corridors here. After some stumbling around the cave reading the numbers on the walls, I happened upon two adventurers. Their names are Frowman and Devor. They say they are searching for something... a book, of sorts. They refer to it as the Necronomicon. \n They same quite interested to learn what this book could contain. I myself am intrigued as to why they seek it. However, I fear that anything found in this place could be tainted with dark magic. I fear for the lives of these brave adventurers for seeking something that may be evil. After all, Iblees' children have been known to fool the mortals into traps before. I shall continue to follow the brave duo in order to investigate their activities, as well as possibly protect their souls from the corruption of the Dark One. I hear horrific echoes all around, but I know that these words are not spoken with a voice, but with a feeling. \n Some of the signs here are gibberish, referencing serving dark powers. Some of the writings seem to be more helpful, though. One of these wall writings continually lists the numbers \"4 8 15 16 23 43\". Could this mean something? Coordinates? Dates? I have a feeling that this place will reveal all of its secrets in due time. I have found a small furnished room, such as a living room or parlor, at the end of some tunnels. There is a hall that branches off with two bedrooms. One is marked \"Rokt'Crag\" and the other is marked \"Sediyou\". Perhaps these are dark persons? I shall find out. Master Sage Riizu also appeared in the cave as we travelled on. The others believed he merely crept out from the shadows, but I could sense that he was drawn magically to my psychic senses that gave me bad feelings about this place. \n Riizu has explored the caves with us as we have showed him the oddities we found in the rooms and tunnels. I know now that he can sense the presence of the Undead followers in this place. He also seems apprehensive of the others. Could there be something about them that I am not yet strong enough to sense? I wish I could see with the Master's eyes. Leaving the dark place and splitting from the others, I headed into the town of Alstion. Immediately inside the gates, I met three men who were talking about something that really caught my attention. They were talking about a book, just as the men in the cave had. These men were seeking some other book, though. I followed them to a place in the wintery forest. They searched a small hiding place in the ground, stating the book they sought after was no longer there as they had hoped. I introduced myself as a member of the Ascended and they told me I would be interested in their situation. \n One man named Lex explained to me that he had found a dark book that lead him to the Grand Library of Laurelin. Here, he found another, leading to the crypts of Winterfell. In Winterfell he found a book writing in a dark manor, stating that there existed an artifact. This artifact, he went on to say, was an evil and powerful object once owned by an ancient race I have never before heard of. He stated the race's name was \"Kal\" something. I do not recall the full name, as the entire conversation happened quickly and I am attempting to write this book after the event. \n He also told us, though, that the book mentioned a fourth book, and also that the ancient treasure had been moved from Winterfell to a new home. He claims the cold heart and cold hands of \"Al'Khazar's fake father\" now keep it safe, buried somewhere. The men carried on to investigate near the home of the the one man, Brevias, in the Whisper Isles. These two and their Orc friend left me behind as I stayed to investigate the hiding spot they had led me to earlier. I found nothing of interest but my time was cut short by the setting sun. I fear now it would be too late to voyage south to the Whisper Isles to meet up with these explorers, but I must try to catch up with them first thing in the morning. For now, my main concern lies in finding food and weapons, as I am not prepared for such a long trek. \n I have killed and cooked a few pigs that were surrounding the walls of the town, and will now be resting to prepare myself for the trip ahead of me. I am currently carrying many books that I plan to place in my private library later. They are too heavy for much extra equipment, but I find preserving these novels to be essential, as I strive to be the most knowledgeable of all the citizens of Aegis. \n After being unable to leave the next morning, due to a snowstorm, I've decided to wait here. I am continuing to write as I wait for the storm to pass. I think I will explore the lands north of here when I am able to leave. I have not been there before, and feel there is much I have yet to see. to as Alstion this entire time was not Alstion at all, but rather \"Snowy Fields\". The real Alstion is shortly east of Snowy Fields. I shall be exploring this town for a while now. I found nothing significant in the real Alstion, so I continued my travels to Winterfell. I also found nothing unusual in Winterfell, and I cannot seem to find the crypt mentioned to me earlier by the human Lex. Perhaps it does not exist at all? I shall keep searching. \n After some searching, I've found an obstructed entrance to an underground tunnel. Surely this is what the Humans were refering to earlier. I can not get in now, though, so I shall be suspending this current investigation. I will return in the future if I come across any new information on the subject.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heracles' Travels: Volume Three", "DoctorTinman", "I have met today with Head Elven Diplomat Lafthi in Laurelin. He has lead me to a secret door beneath the tram tracks that leads below ground. I followed the passageway into Laurelin's underbelly into bland room centered on a circular table in the middle surrounded by benches. There were already 5 other figures gathered around the table as we arrived. \n I took my seat on the bench furthest away from the door, observing the others. Sage Okonkwo used his magic to teleport in shortly after we had entered, making us a group of 8. We all went around the circle saying introductions to begin the ceremonies. Okonkwo hs seated himself to my left, and working around the table counterclockwise from myself are the human Lord John, clad in a suit of diamond. Next to him is the famous Oren Captain by the name of GrimBeard. Then comes the elves Lafthi and Prince Toren, both dressed in traditional Elven garb. Next comes the dwarf Hiebe, in an armor of chainmail tunic and leather pants. Finally, the hooded orc Brevias of the Whisper Isles. \n After the formalities, the discussions began listing a few suspicious persons in the world of Aegis. A man named Eldar has been named as a bandit, banned from Oren for his numerous crimes. Also mentioned was a man named Atles, who is known to be warden of the Oren guards, but will from now on be watched more closely. He has been rumored to consort with Eldar in his dirty acts. \n The next topic of discussion has moved onto the Dwarven politcal state, which seems to be in a grave state after the last 2 kings have both ended their terms quite prematurely. The new king has far less influence over the people than the last two, and the situation is dire, as the dwarves are less unified than ever. News from the dwarves tells that an archbishop, Berin, is attempting to take control of the dwarven people as a sort of leader. He is reinstalling a government and a military to help keep jobs and safety in the dwarven nation. \n The next matter brought up by Lafthi concerns the Undead. The tales say that they are looking for new recruits and shall be accepting new initiates very soon. This is horrible news, as it means the evil plague of Aegis will spread. And recent battles in the northeastern territories show that the people of Aegis already struggle to fight back the current evil. This could be a very bad thing. \n Shortly after, the meeting concluded and Lafthi granted a key to each member. We departed from the magical entryway and went our seperate ways until the next meeting. \n After leaving the meeting, I set off for Oren's capital of Al'Khazar. On the path just ahead of the gates I encountered 4 men talking about thieving and banditry. One of these men was Eldar, previously named as the council as suspicious. I observed them from a secluded spot for some time. They discussed a pact between them, a sort of bandits' code. Two of the other men were named Elrond and Gustaf_Tarus. I have considered bringing this to the attention of the council, but I shall decide over time. \n Once within the gates of the city there was a large commotion. Everyone seemed in an uproar regarding a man named Ben Powell. For whatever reason, the guards ejected him from the town. Richard, a fellow memberof the Ascended, was off to the side of th crowd. I spotted him and asked if he knew what had caused the ruckus. He said he was just as clueless as I was. Perhaps I shall also keep my ears open for tales on this \"Ben Powell\" character. I'll ask around later. \n I've managed to catch up with Grimbeard, the one from the council. Being a captain of the Oren Guard, I figured he'd be the man to ask about this Ben fellow. Grimbeard informed me that Ben Powell is a rebel and traitor to Oren. I must be wary in the future, should I happen to run across this man. \n After a short period away from Al'Khazar, I've just returned to find parts of the town now lie in ruin. It seems that I somehow missed a raid by the Undead in my leave. There are many injured walking the streets, and there is a panic amongst the people. They have managed to hold the city for now, but it is in a dire state. Lord John of the Council lead a small party into the town's sewers to slay the remaining spawns of the Necromancers, whilst others tended to the wounded and the repairs of the city. I popped into the Queen's bakery, as it is a common gathering point, to seek information. The queen herself was in a healthy state. She handed out rations to those less fortunate as they recounted the horrors of the battle. The city has been won for now, but is in more danger now than ever before. \n Stories abound in Oren. The largest piece of news passing around is the death of the king. He was slain in the fray, and the queen is left widowed, and the people are afraid. The evils of the Undead are a plague on their minds. Mental wounds are always the hardest to heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heracles' Travels: Volume Two", "DoctorTinman", "I begin this adventure at the Laurelin docks. I had just exited from the Druids' Grotto when I saw a group of people storming down the path. These men seemed to be quite invigorated and in a hurry to get somewhere. My non-confrontational ways caused me to duck behind cover until they passed by. Curious as to what was going on, I followed the rag-tag band of elves, dwarves, and orcs. After a short jog, I caught up to the men in discussion at the Laurelin Gauntlet. There was a great commotion amongst some of the Laurelinians around the square. A tall green orc extended a finger, pointing to some of the onlookers, \"You! How would you like to join the Grand Army of Aegis?!\" From my position behind the crowd, I could barely count their numbers, but they were quite a large group, comprised of 3 of Aegis' main races. A small questioning session began as the bystanders asked the Orcish captain about this Army's intents and purposes. \n The orc explained, \"I am Munifex_Sornof, and we are Aegis' Grand Army in the war against the evils of the Undead. We accept warriors of all races!\" This went on for a few minutes until the group announced a voyage to the far north in order to seek an audience with the Humans. A clamor arose as the swords and armor of these people went marching onward. \n I tagged along as this motley crew paraded down King's Road at a brisk pace. In less than a day's travel, the kingdom came into view, nestled between the mountains. We gathered around the gates as the leaders of the pack pulled off to the side. They spoke in low whispers in far away from the group, so nobody knew what had been discussed, but on of the dwarves seemed to leave promtly after they concluded. We summoned a guard to open the gates for us, and once inside of Oren we were confronted with the sights of people everywhere. Al'Khazar is always so crowded! \n We crowded into a local shop as the same sort of events from Laurelin took place. There was much talk as I sat in the corner to begin writing. Soon, a few humans joined the ranks of the order, but our band was denied access to speak witht he Royal Court, as they were away at the time. \n Next, someone mentioned that the races were not fully unified until they had spoken with the Ascended. After a short debate, the horde decided to leave promptly en route for Haven. They took the White Road while I took a shortcut. I managed to meet them at the gate and summoned Master Riizu. In lieu of recent thievery, we are not allowed to grant entry to Haven to anyone who is not a descendant of the Aenguls. The weary travellers pleaded that Sage Riizu allow them refuge inside the city. However, he knew it was a decision that had to be made by the entire council of sages. \n He could see that the small army was upset at this verdict, and assured them that their deeds would be sanctioned by the Ascended. He made it clear that we would lend our support to their cause as much as we were able. One of the humans asked if it would be possible to establish a sort of rally point outside of the city's walls. Master Riizu seemed to like this idea, as it would allow for a nearby defense force, as well as informants, and it didn't require letting the others into the city. \n \"I believe I can arrange that,\" said Riizu. He chose a spot of land just a little way off the path to the main gate. \"Let me show you the power of Aeriel,\" he told the mortals, \"Now please stand back.\" He offered a few silent prayers to the sky and then began to mark out spots in the ground. Suddenly, as if by some miracle, a tower bursted forth from the ground. In just a few moments, the entire 3-story structure was erected before all of our eyes. Riizu gave the deed to this tower to the leaders of the warband. \n The leaders then decided to named the group the UAC or United Aegis Coalition. This tower now stands as proof to the magic of the Aenguls, a testament to the power of the Aenguls, and the new headquarters of the UAC. Perhaps the UAC will prove to be a powerful ally against the evils of the Undead? We shall all find out eventually. For now, their camp is still small, but might gain popularity and grow larger very soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herald of Destruction", "Ned_Lud", "The Herald of Destruction calls his praise,\n      The seven skies will shake,\n     And the pillars of Aegis will crumble,\n      Under the one born of shadow with blood in his eyes.\n \n In Krugmar, me heard lightning strike near da Towers of Aemon and Daemon. Da earth began \n to tremble as if it were torn. Me went to da source of dis sound, ready to klomp.  What me found was pile of rubble and a lone elf standing der.  Elindor of da Mage's Guild blah me dat a ruin had risen from da earth and den sunk back belo", ""),
