        StaticBook("Heritic volume I", "picklesickel", "The heritic,The evil,The maniac... That is what they call us. I belive i am in the right of way mortals think above of us. I am above them the udead are stronger,smarter,and more cunning. The humans are pitiful excusses for a race we are all mighty. we the followers of Iblees are the true way. Iblees a dark all powerful god of the nether has gathered a force large enought to take over agies and keep it for himself and his undead minions. He intends on useing this power he has shown it more then once The fall of al'kazar the scorching of snowy feilds the undead are showing that there power is strong. I would like to say before i continue that i strongly belive in Iblees and that he has shown way . I belive that these ideas i show are done under the knowing factor that you may get hurt. I will start with explaining a shirne of Iblees Nether rack is the most common material to build a shrine to Iblees out of. add a dead animal/mortal and or valuables as an offering to the dark god Iblees. Shrines a cerimonial and are used as a thanks to the god himself. a better way of going into something like this is to make a portal. You are going for a nether gate", ""),
        StaticBook("Hero's Rest Graveyards Ad", "IlumTarus", "Eze'kiel Tarus has various sorts of graves, crypts, catacombs, and coffins available for purchase to safely let the dead rest. Contact Eze'kiel Tarus, [IlumTarus], for information and purchasing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heroic Deeds: Viadar in the North", "Canadianwarrior", "Aye gather round while I tell you a tale of my travels in the North. I had spent most of my youth wandering the Wilds and so I am more at home there than anywhere else. I had since started to explore further and further into the snowy wastes. It was on one of these journeys that I came across a great structure that housed a great burning heart in the ground. Exploring this land further I came across two cloacked figures. They stunk of death. One noticed my movements and began to close ground. Out numbered I took cover in a nearby building as the skies lit up with magic. One of my pursuers followed me into the building that a sought cover in. Leaping from behind the door I slit his throat and he collapsed, lifeless. The other was not as dumb as his companion. Suddenly the undead began to rise from the ground. Zombies began to lash ou, my armour began to wear on the constant assult. Bleeding out I started to loose consciousness...", ""),
