        StaticBook("High Price Native", "professorshields", "Date Irba 18th of Snow Maiden, 1312 While out in the jumping course a Elf come and spoke to us. There was no indication of where he come from. I was as if he had appeared from No where His name was High Prince Native He took us on a journey to the great city of Laurien. It was a remarkable City! never before have i seen such an amazing city! The hospitality of  High Prince Native was one to worship!", ""),
        StaticBook("High Prince", "kittenaid", "High Prince Native, You may already know that I am fond of you. Every moment I spend with you I enjoy. I appreciate the time you spent planning the clues. You did not have to. I understand you are a very busy man and I must be last thing on your mind. I don not believe I have met a man just like you. You are a breath of fresh air to the people and are loved by many.", ""),
        StaticBook("High Starhold", "Darkdragon274", "This tower is owned by Relgard and the Spectres, given to him by Braxis , lord of Galahar. This is not a \"Seers Spire\" as a sign may say. \n If you think you have claim to this, talk to relgard. ((Darkdragon274))", ""),
        StaticBook("High Treasurer", "clayman730", "Tom Fust and I, Zibaen Vivyaen need to speak with you regarding our job. Khronos has told us we must report to you, and we have been having some difficulties doing so. We need to have a meeting regarding the taxes and what you okay and what you don't. We do not want to begin taxing without your complete and total approval. Please respond with promptness, we would like to help our Kingdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("HighTower Tavern Record Book", "mylimo7", "\n Room 1 : Tamar: 75 Minas Rent: Every Friday Hail", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Aegis", "zevandir", "", ""),
        StaticBook("History of House Drake", "deanofantastico", "The House Drake was formed in 1013 by Ulric Drake when he was appointed Margrave of Eridell, a flourishing trading town situated on rolling plains not far from a dense forest. It was here in Eridell, where the Housed Drake grew into a powerful noble house. \n \n Margrave Ulric married a fair women named Wyia in 1015 and had several children, though all but Kair Drake, their first born son, perished in a dragon raid in 1032. \n \n Over the next 140 years, Eridell started to decline in prosperity. Constant attacks by bandits and tribes on both the town and the traders, gave the area a bad name. The decrease in trade casued tension in the town with many either leaving or others who started to rebell. \n \n In light of these events; in year 1173, the current Margrave, Standar Drake, sent his son and daughter away with his most trusted friend under instruction to keep them safe and take them far from Eridell.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Kramoroe", "Sykora87", "Kramoroe Began when a group of travling merchants ccame throu an area and set up a small camp", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Talamh", "Telanir", "Property of: Talamh, Written by: Telinir \n It started out as an idea from Daniel, Nero and Shamus. \n They started building a village and encountered Telinir who tagged along. \n Together they built a small settlement hardly worth noticing. But, people started noticing the settlement and they were recruited. \n After a while the village started to form into a larger place, now a town. The town was named, Talamh. \n Gradually people settled in to Talamh and a notice board was made, then a town hall and library. After a while as Talamh was finally starting to settle, in Al'Khazar the king turned undead. After a series of horrible turn of events the people of Talamh decided to stay neutral to all sides. After a while Nero, Telinir and Father Ailean headed to the nether during a huge battle between Al'Khazar and the undead. Only Telinir made it into the nether successfully, which he soon dearly regretted. The king returned back from the nether, it appeared he was held captive. Things started to seem better. Unfortunately, over the course of many days, the town was assaulted by Queen Cassandra and many other undead. The people recovered quickly from this assault. However, thieves started finding their way to Talamh after a road was built connecting it to Al'Khazar. Later on, once Talamh grew to larger extents, Nero, Telinir, Shamus, Jolot, and Daniel all gathered and decided on a rulership for Talamh. It was decided on three leaders, Nero, Shamus and, Daniel.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Aegean Academy", "Jerry_Man", "The Aegean Academy was built in Aeriel in 1321.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of The Blue Isles", "G79", "One day, Before the times of recorded history, the town of Blue Isles was the birth place of the Black Beard Dwarves. These were no ordinary Dwarves. They had more mining, and fighting abilities. They also had the finest army of all. But then came the rise of the Undead... Then during the rise of the Undead, thier Headquarters was discovered, ransacked, and decimated. But it was not the end. The Black Beards survived had half of the army left over. Then they went to the Undead Fortress and tore it open. It was a fine battle but in the end the Black Beards won and they thought the evil was defeated. Then after the week long journey back to Blue Isles, the dwarves feasted and thought it was a job well done. However they forgot that there was still an undead fortress in the south. It was a mistake they were sure to never forget. The Undead attacked and burned the town to the ground... The Black Beards were almost defeated. But during the fight a man put a baby dwarf into the ocean and sent it off into uncharted territory. This dwarf was the dwarf known as Groffon. He ended up in Kal' Urguan and was adopted by an Orphanage. There he grew up and was taught the ways of his former kin. But he never was told about how they died and also was never told the location of Blue Isles. He went off into the North to look for it but had no luck. East and West were the same. But after a long weeks trek into the south he found it. It was next to the old Isle of Wisps but he saw everything. There was nothing left of the town but flat land and ash but he still could make out where the buildings once stood. He was furious with the Undead and vowed to defeat them once the town was rebuilt.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Cal'ek Warband", "Slayer15855", "History of the Cal'ek Warband \n \n \n Transcribed by the Arcane Mage \n \n \n Joma, 27th of Suns Smile, 1313 \n This is a Marvelous day. Today is the day upon which we have finished the mainstay of the walls and the towers. Today, is when we finally have carved out, through tears, sweat, and blood, a place to call our own with in Aegis. From Valiant Lords to Simple Peasants, Warriors to Workers, the Exiled to the Exemplary, Humans to Halfings, we have united. We are the Cal'ek, we are Righteous, and we are One. \n \n \n \n Ahad, 29th of Suns Smile, 1313 Among the next few pages of this book, you shall find our history. We do not have the dates of the following events, only the order they happened in. \n \n The Warbands Origins: \n The Warband grew out of my personal pursuit for glory, and after seeing the state of Aegis, justice. I grew up in some swamps, deep in the south. Abandoned, or perhaps taken from, I never knew my birth parents. I was raised in the swamps by a band of Orcs who found me, and took me in as their own. They raised me as their own, replacing many of my naturally human traits with their own, removing greed, selfishness, fear, and cowardness, and replaced them with honor, courage, equality amongst races, and ferocity in battle. I set off when I was a young man, driven by my goal to bring honor to myself and the family that raised me. It was this which brought me deep into the heartland of Aegis, and this which drove me to seek out and rid the world of its fiends, thieves, and later, the undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Cal'ek Warband (Transcribed by the Arcane Mage)", "Slayer15855", "History of the Cal'ek Warband \n \n \n Transcribed by the Arcane Mage \n Joma, 27th of Suns Smile, 1313", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Cal'ek Warband I", "Slayer15855", "History of the Cal'ek Warband \n \n \n \n \n -Transcribed by the Arcane Mage- \n Joma, 27th of Suns Smile, 1313 \n \n This is a Marvelous day. Today is the day upon which we have finished the mainstay of the walls and the towers. Today, is when we finally have carved out, through tears, sweat, and blood, a place to call our own with in Aegis. From Valiant Lords to Simple Peasants, Warriors to Workers, the Exiled to the Exemplary, Humans to Halfings, we have united. We are the Cal'ek, we are Righteous, and we are One. \n \n \n Ahad, 29th of Suns Smile, 1313 \n \n Among the next few pages of this book, you shall find our history. We do not have the dates of the following events, only the order they happened in. \n \n The Warbands Origins: \n The Warband grew out of my personal pursuit for glory, and after seeing the state of Aegis, justice. I grew up in some swamps, deep in the south. Abandoned, or perhaps taken from, I never knew my birth parents. I was raised in the swamps by a band of Orcs who found me, and took me in as their own. They raised me as their own, replacing many of my naturally human traits with their own, removing greed, selfishness, fear, and cowardness, and replaced them with honor, courage, equality amongst races, and ferocity in battle. I set off when I was a young man, driven by my goal to bring honor to myself and the family that raised me. It was this which brought me deep into the heartland of Aegis, and this which drove me to seek out and rid the world of its fiends, thieves, and later, the undead. \n \n \n The Beginning of the Warband: \n I first started out by setting off to Al'Khazar, determined to find capable fighters to begin the Warband with. I found several, most of which have long since departed. Only three stick out in my mind now. \n Relyt, a young elf with high hopes for the Warband and its goal of bringing justice to Aegis, currently the closest thing I have to a second in command, though there shall never be one. \n Ares Stark, a man with the Oren Guard, tired of the way the Guard Operated, where he is now I do not know. \n And lastly, Ogland, another member of the Oren Guard, also disappointed with the way the Guard was being operated. Last I heard, he is a scribe in Al'Khazar now, but is no longer with us. \n With these three men, and several others, I set out to shape Aegis. We slayed several bandits and hundreds if not thousands of fiends in our short while before our exile. We had a small cave near Al'Khazar. I hear its still there, and the ruins of the old base still intact. \n Then, there was the human king. Pampo Perea. He seemed to be leading Oren into madness, recklessly spending the kingdom's coffers on his throne room and a cathedral to the god of Aegis, speaking of demolishing peoples homes to make room for construction. The Cal'ek were certain he would bring nothing but Darkness to Oren. \n So we planned a coup... \n", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Cal'ek Warband II", "Slayer15855", "History of the Cal'ek Warband \n After the Beginning \n \n \n \n -Transcribed by the Arcane Mage- \n We had vast portions of Oren on our side before it was all said and done. A priest named Seth who operated a fort along the kings road, aiding travellers. My dear friend and tavern owner, James Arkensald, who owned an Inn along the kings road and also aided travellers in need. The current king, Edmund, though I find it likely it was he who ratted out the Coup, as it benefitted him most. The King's diplomat who I ended up having to threaten to kill his dear friend Banok if he did not help us. This was only due to such circumstances, as the King's advisor held in his power to convince the elves to help us, or to simply stand aside. We had vast portions of Oren on our side before it was all said and done. A priest named Seth who operated a fort along the kings road, aiding travellers. My dear friend and tavern owner, James Arkensald, who owned an Inn along the kings road and also aided travellers in need. The current king, Edmund, though I find it likely it was he who ratted out the Coup, as it benefitted him most. The King's diplomat who I ended up having to threaten to kill his dear friend Banok if he did not help us. This was only due to such circumstances, as the King's advisor held in his power to convince the elves to help us, or to simply stand aside. \n \n The elf council and high prince at that time were very supportive of the Warband and its goals, and I knew if the advisor spoke in favor of our cause, they would support the coup, giving us overwhelming power, and with it, the ability for a blood less victory. I also had over half of the Oren guard at that time as well as the Guard captain in support of the coup. The rest of the guard I did not ask, as they were driven by the kings greed and nothing else. I had several other people in favor of the coup, willing to fight for us. Ranging from black smiths, to shop owners, to various business owners and hunters, to even dwarven guards and elfish soldiers. \n \n The coup was ready. Our forces were amassed, the plan ready, the Cal'ek Base moved to a long house in the east, all there was to do was to explain the plan to our masses and then to promptly take over Al'Khazar from the inside and to march upon the king, and to take the throne. But, I was called away. I was informed by another traveling member of my native Orc Band that our Chieftan had fallen gravely Ill, and so I made the march back to see him, and to aid our clan in any way I could. He died several days after I arrived, his illness contracted from zombie bites in a recent battle. After mourning, I set off back to Al'Khazar, ready to take the throne and to use the Guard to rid the land of Aegis of the fiends. \n The Trials of the Warband: \n \n But we had been ratted out. I returned to find all of the Coups members either in disarray, hiding, or for several, dead. We also did not have the support of the elves, and as such, the Coup fell apart. We were labeled as enemies of Oren by King Pampo, our log house burnt to the ground, and our supplies stolen. All the surviving members of the Cal'ek Warband went into hiding. And so we stayed for several months. \n \n With only Relyt, Ares, and Ogland by my side, rebuilding in secret was difficult. We did not have the man power we needed, and while most of Oren's citizens welcomed us with open arms as they supported our cause at the time, we still had to be vigilant. The King had his portion of the guard on high alert, ready to imprison or kill any of they found. \n Rebuilding: \n \n After months in the wild, debating reforming under a new name and banner to hide our past, and trying to rebuild at three new locations, I travelled forth with a new recruit, Urack the Dwarf, and we set out to find a new location, hopefully the permanent home of our base, and as such, The Cal'ek, as we decided we would not back down, but rather, stand tall and proud of what we had done. We traveled far and wide, searching all over for a place to call our own before finally we found it. But finally, we did. \n \n It was a vast, untouched plateau, with access to the top from only two locations at the time. We quickly set to work, chopping down tree's, digging out roots, filling in the many pockets of land and caves that menaced the surface, and removing a thick layer of soil from the top so that we had a flat surface to begin construction. \n \n With in a week, all of the tree's had been cleared and the ground leveled. Within a month, the first bits of stone began being laid for the walls and towers. And with in several years(Time system hadn't been implemented when we began, but judging from how time currently goes, I'd say about 8 years prior, and its year 13 now, so, 21 years?), the fortress's defenses had been vastly completed. Well enough to hold off any threat the Cal'ek faced, at least. \n We have labeled all those who cause pain and anguish our enemies. The Fiends, Bandits, The Undead, Corrupt leaders, cultists. Any who actively bring death, destruction, and fear to Aegis, we shall wage an endless war upon, until they are no more. A Cal'ek may be mortal, but the Warband is Immortal. One may fall, but another even more powerful shall take his place. \n \n And that's how we got to where we are now. Our crops are flourishing, our walls stand strong, our soldiers powerful, our supplies complete and our bellies full. Through everything except the nether and back we've been, and through it all, we stand powerful. We are the Cal'ek, we are Righteous, and we are One. \n \n \n Written by the Arcane Mage: \n And so their past ends, but it is not the end as some may suspect. Although the Warband has seen its trials it still exists today. \n We may never know the outcome of their effort. But perhaps there is still some to see...", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Carved Mountain", "Lokito", "", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Obadiah Clan", "sprintindwarf", "The Obadiahs have been a well loved family that has been around for many generations. They were a nomad family for the longest time. Until one generaion settled down. They settled down in an open area up North. People quickly came and a villiage was formed . That man that settled down was Ernest Obadiah. He had many sons, one in example Ezekiel. he was the youngest, but grew to be big and strong. Life was going great for the Obadiahs. Until one day, the undead attack without warning. The Obadiahs, being the leaders of the Village, and great warriors lead men into battle. Ezekiel was shoved into the celler, and was told to be quiet. The battle seemed to last forever. Ezekiel found a tunnel in the celler, so he took it. He walked until it reached an end. He dug the tunnel on. He dug until he reached Kal'Urgaun, he was week and tired. with his savings he got poor dwarf housing and stayed there for some time. He is now currently active in the Knights of Aeriel and other things. The result of the battle with the undead, and the rest of the Obadiahs is unknown . When news is uncovered this book will be expanded.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Pathfinders", "zevandir", "This History of the Pathfinders begins on the 5th of July. \nToday, three new Pathfinders, Kalen, ValiantBrasser and Lavanthus were trained. They were given the standard training, learning how to pitch a tent etc. They were then tested in the wilds outside of Laurelin, making an excellent camp and surviving we ll. \nEarlier that day, another squad had assualted a village of bandits, killing a few. Zevandir's squad then went to this village again, and discovered the village had both bandit and non-bandit members, the non-bandits had also suffered due to the raid. Zevandir's Squad put things right and are now firm allies with the village. The squad then went on to the Orc Capital, where we were called HUMANS! What an insult! The squad stormed into the city, but then had a nice chat with the orc, educating him on the difference between the races. He didn't seem to get it. Oh well. \nThe rest of the day went mostly uneventfully, until the afternoon. \nAt this point, the squad decided to fix the Elven Hidey Hole, creating a hidden prison, store room and Elven Sanctuary. \nHowever, some rude rangers decided to investigate, one extremely rude ranger would not leave, so the squad trapped and tortured him a little. He refused to hand over his armour, but we let him go anyway. It grows late, but yet I still wait for my exalted leader, Lord Blackthorn.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the RotF", "CONORDUDE8", "", ""),
        StaticBook("History of the Temple Akavari", "Royced", "Upon a snow-covered land, many miles behind The Temple of Aegis, lies the e of Akavari The e itself was home of Akaviri Knoland, a generous man whom was rich beyond all standard His primary mission in life was to protect those whom could never protect themselves in me of need, so he took it upon himself to do it for     others. He asembled a large crew of faithfull men and called them \" Akavari \" meaning \" People of the True \" . The men whom, under his control, eventually lead to a downfall, due to a small lack of trust between the members. There lack of faith and trust with another, led to there lack of interest in the good for Society . They became so ignorant of trouble around them that they no longer cared for the people, rather they were only to care for themselves. A small band of the Akavari Warrior's, including the lowest rank's, up to Mr. Knoland himself, removed corrupon inside of the cort, and never openly saw them again. By then, only eight whole-heartedly members were left in the giant e of Akavari, and over  time, the group disbanded. A new peasantly figure, Akeron Dav'iance, found the e on his hunt for food, and admired the detail and work put into the e. The e itself, was infact falling apart in all directions, and covered in heaps of snow, and single handedly rebuilt the e himself. He found an old book discribing the names of people whom belonged fo the cort, and what the  temple stood for. He liked the concept, but was not an good fighter. He aranged the Temple to be used as a protection area. Rather the Knights of Akavari coming to Civilians, the the Knights would come for protection of Royalty. Thus, the temple of Akavari became the Headquarters of Protection for those figures whom are in power, and kingdom are under Seige. This, is how the temple came about.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of The Undead", "itechify", "Twin brothers were born in the Great city of Al'Khazar with the names \"Phillip\" and \"Rodrick\"", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Turin", "Grayslayer", "Here is my story. ;; When I was but a baby elf my people where forced to ran from our homes. Beacuse a war had broken out and my home was burnt to the ground. All I remember was running and then suddenly blackness. when I awoke I couldn't work out where I was all I could see was dense forest. And then I heard a noise I turned to see a wolf mother. At first I was scared then she came to me and poked me with here muzzle. she then picked me up by the scruff of my clothes and and carried me to here den where she put me down and let me sleep. edit History of Turin test ;;", ""),
        StaticBook("Hitch Hiker's guide to the realm", "moop123", "Long ago in the realm of Aegis a small Human man sat outside is house in the mid seemingly fo r no reason. It turned out he was blocking a group of people attempting to demolish his house. To make way for a brand new market street. He had to stand infront of his house to protect it. If they wanted to demolish it they had to go through him 1st. nice . He thought to himself. As he dose every day. It was then that a strange dwraven looking man came up to him and said \"You need to some with me to the inn sir we need to talk\" James (The man trying to protect his house) replyed \"Im trying to protect me house sir if i leave this spot it will be destroyed. So i plan on staying here for as long as they can keep this up\" while sitting down and making himself comfortable on the cold hard paving. The strange man grabs who is seemingly the head of this opperation and places him in his spot \"now you must take this man's spot for a second okay ? No sneakly demolishing his house\" And the opperation head lay down on the paving like James had for some good week. A the pub just outside his house this strange man (Called Horse) said to James... \"You do realize that Aegis is soon to be destroyed right ? because no one els in this bar seems to be very alarmed\" The bar tender comes over to ask if everything is okay and thats when horse tells him the new s. The entire pub bursts out laughing at the words came out of Horses mouth. \"Destroyed ! Destroyed by what me freind\" one of the customers replyed thinking it was a joke ... Ignoring them Horse carryed on with his disscussion with James. Thats when James saw outside that his house WAS being demoished as he spoke ! He ran outside quickly to see why it had been done. All his possetions lost, all his money lost, his home lost... He was now no more than a poor man, a hitch hiker to the realm we know as Aegis. Thats when a crackling sound came from the sky ! No one knew what it was. But then in an amplaphyed voice someone said \"Erm... Its hard to tell you this but Aegis is being bemolished to make way for you constructon of a realm bridge its like the cortals of your world but alot bigger\" thats when the world fell under darkness... A large blue light bigger than the moo gathered above aegis. And then it crashed down to Aegis in an instance totally destroying tthe world All were killed eccept for James... He lived on with those who destroyed Aegis...", ""),
