        StaticBook("How to be a cat", "RobbehRawr", "1st: meow. 2nd: your done.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to be an succesfull hunter using bow and arrows.", "ClayDoc", "The first thing you need to do is to make sure your bow and arrows are not broken in any way. Next thing is to make sure you got nice and sharp arrows for the hunt. Now you're ready for the hunt! When you spot your prey make sure to identify it. If it's a zombie pigman make sure to get close to it and look again. On the day atleast becouse the sun usally trick your eyes. On the night it's good to go from a distance. Spiders are fast so stand away from them as long as possible. The rest are not a problem if you follow these rules: Rule number 1:Keep your bow steady on the first attack to get maximum hit chance. Rule number 2:Refrain from panicking so that you don't fire all your arrows at once. Rule number 3: Wait until the prey is close before you start to walk backwards to get maximum precision. Rule number 3 should not be used against skelleton bowmans becouse they have a long distance attack too and you will be killed if you don't get back. That was all from this book remember this is the basics the rest you need to learn yourself.", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Become A Good Guard", "conorb", "Step One: \"Respect\" One Of The Most Inportant Rules Respect Every One Higher Or Lower Ranks Step Two: \"Fighting\" Practice Any Time Ye' Can In The Trainging Area Step Three: \"Donations\" Ye' Are All In This Together, Share Your Items With Other Guards, Step Four: Rules Allways Inforce The Law, help How To Become A Good Guard By Smith", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Become A True Success", "Ace__Spades", "There are many ways to become a successful, wealthy person. There are many products, businesses, and trades. Though there are these many ways, there could be a key ingredient missing in you. That key ingredient is one that without it you will just meander through life hoping for your big br eak. I can promise you from experience that the big break you are praying to God for will not come. The key ingredient you must have is: Your Attitude! \n Your attitude determines your latitude in this world, whether it be financial or some other aspect of life. You must have the right attitude if you want to be successful and wealthy. In this book, I will tell you what I have found to be the best ways to become successful and how to use your attitude to propel you to that success. \n The first way you can become successful is by being a great salesman. When I say salesman, I dont mean the guy on the side of King's Road yelling about his sugar cane and gravel for sale. He has the wrong mindset, the wrong attitude. He is looking for his big break that won't come. A great salesman has the attitude that he has something the people around him need. A great salesman goes out of his way to gather goods that he knows people are in need of at the moment. When the Undead arose and began wreaking havoc on the innocent people of Aegis, the greatest salesman was'nt marketing his fishing rod, he was selling his swords, armor, and bows. His attitude was to supply the people with what they need. And you my friend can do the same thing every day. \n The second way, the last of which I will put in this book, you can become successful is by having an attitude of zealousy. You must have an attitude that you will never give up, no matter the cost. I once knew a man who was a great warrior. He would go out night after night in search of all types of monsters and beasts. That was his livelihood, a monster hunter. It was good money and he loved the thrill of battle. I asked him one day, \"Friend, what about death? Do you not fear it?\" What he said to me changed my attitude about life. He said to me, \"Brother, death is nothing, but for those who live lives of fear and defeat, they die daily.\" What a warrior mentality! So, the next time you think of running from that PigZombie for your life, remember my friend's words. Never giveup! Do not settle for defeat, but use that moment to bring out your best! \n I wrote this book not for myself, but for you! I want to add value to you and give you the knowledge that I hold so that you may use it to your prosperity. Never forget these two attitudes: The attitude of a servant salesman and the attitude of a relentless warrior! May God be with you forever! \n Written By: Ace ((Ace__Spades))", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Breed wolves.", "doggydigger", "First get to wolves. Then make them stand.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Complete your Initiate Training", "TheGiver17", "This guide book will tell you how you are to begin and complete your training as an initiate. The first thing you should do is decide if you want to become    an Eternal Guard or a Glade Guard. Eternal Guards are deadly swordsmen. Eternal Guards will solidly stand against any who threaten Laurelin. Eternal Guards are frequently utilised as bodyguards for Highborn and Noble Elves. They are the only ones standing between the enemy and the destruction of the forests of Malinor.\n Glade Guards are renowned for their magnificent longbows. They are skilled bowmen whose understanding of the woods allows them to move seemingly unhindered through thick brush and", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Earn Your Stars In The Wild.", "Crippledbaboon", "Chapter 1: Know your shrooms. When in deep wilderness, days away from civilisation, you must become one with your surroundings to survive. The wilderness is a cruel and un-forgiving place, few come out unscathed.  Food is your first objective, and lots of it. If you are reading this at night, when the undead are on the prowl for weary travellers, then you are actually in a good position. Take time out from smiting those undead hooligans to sit and prepare equipment for the next day. Check your food supply, weapons and armour. A great thing to carry with you into the wilderness is your trusty flint and steel. This can be used to outstanding effect if used correctly. Find a swine of good proportions and simply set it alight! Let the pig burn to death peacefully then collect the pork. However, there is a twist to this pork, it's cooked for you! The fire cooks the pork for you instead of you finding cobble and coal for a furnace that you will leave behind anyway. This can be done multiple times until the flint is broken. Now, forget what your instincts tell you, because sometimes, darkness is our greatest ally. Check dimly lit areas for mushrooms of both kinds. However don't venture into a cave for that sole purpose, it may lead to disaster! Check under trees or at the beginning of a cave instead. If, like in most cases you find mushrooms under a tree, gather them. Then using the wood from the tree, fashion yourself a workbench , and with spare planks, create an appropriate amount of bowls for your mushrooms! Then simply use the workbench again to create a most delicious broth! Good luck in the wild, and remember, Don't die! When we reach the grand archive , you may sit and erad with me", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Fight Like a Man: Vol. 1, Proper usage of a sword", "Destroyer_Bravo", "How to wield a sword: ALWAYS keep one on you. It does not matter what your combat duty is, keep one there. Two, have fast reaction time. Too slow and you will be dead. Three, Almost always have armor. Armor can prevent unneccesary wounds and slow your death. But, it wont do anything about fire! Four, if ye are primarily a swordsman, KEEP TO THE FRONT LINES Unless!, you are injured. Nobody wants you dead except the adversary in a battle! This is how to be a good swordsman, disoey, and you might find yerself dead. Happy slaying!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Fight Like a Man: Vol. 2, Shootin' and Lootin'", "Destroyer_Bravo", "Necessary economics to wielding a bow and arrow correctly: One, like I said in the first book, keep a backup weapon on you . Two, ALWAYS conserve arrows. You will end up short of arrows and bad at swordfighting if you are a person who trained archery their whole life . Three, Target before Firing. If you just fire randomly, you will also end short of arrows. Four, keep AWAY from front lines. Unless you have diamond armor or something, refrain from this area unless you are short of arrows. This is basically all you need to know to shoot properly.      Happy hunting!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Fight Like a Man: Vol. 3, Noob Actions, and why you should not do them", "Destroyer_Bravo", "Noob actions: Running into battle with nothing. DO NOT RUN INTO BATTLE WITH NO KIT . This will get you killed. If you really want to die be my guest. Two DO NOT GO INTO BATTLE IN DISGUISE. It will get you killed also. And worse by your friends. And do not sob about it. Three DO NOT GO INTO PLACES YOU ARE NOT ALLOWED OR ELSE YOU WILL GET   JAILED. Do not piss off Guards either. This has been the guide on how to not die. Good Luck! (Your gonna need it...)", ""),
        StaticBook("How to fight the spawn of the night", "Juggernogg", "Zombies: Circle them hitting them once then jumping back as to avoid their atack's which are extreamly powerfull \n Skeleton's: Get as close as possible to them and swing, circle around them for maximum effect \n Slime's: DO NOT FIGhT THESE without a bow and arrow's as they are extreamly dangerouse \n Creeper's: Swing, and jump back you know they are going to explode when the tell tale hissing sound \n Spider: Time your attack between their jump's, or use a bow", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Free-Run", "Plizga123", "Al'khazar Addition ((Edition)) Author: Frederick_Plizga \n Hello, My name is Frederick. I am an experienced Rooftop runner. This is my guide on how to free run succesfully. \n Step 1. Know your area. As you know, in a chase, you DO NOT want to end up in a dead end. Or in this case, a ledge, with no roof nearby. You need to plan ahead on where you are going to go, if you want to lose your pursuer. \n Step 2: Get on the rooftops An easy step, but you need to know HOW to get on a rooftop. The best way to go is to Make a jump from the Keep to the roofs nearby. The guards attempt to patch the entrances to the roof tops. There are two paths to follow from the King's Keep. One way, to the Church district, and one way, to the main square. \n Step 3: The Church District Path If you take the first path I mentioned, There are now two ways to go from here. You can run around just around that area, or jump from the trees to the other side.", ""),
        StaticBook("how to groom a beard", "blake11120", "1. a good gomb;; sorry comb \n 2:use slime jell comb carved from the finest wood of lurlen o, do you know anyone that does \n 3: take fishbones and give it a good brushing \n 4: pick bugs out in the morning \n 4: cut with sharp sword", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Heal: A Druids Guide", "Saviordude", "It is no secret that druids are among the worlds best healers. Many a life threatining injury has been cured by our hands. However, some younder druids may not know how to go about healing wounds. This book has been written with them in mind, although older druids may find this useful as a refresher. \n To begin healing, expose the wound where you can see it. Then, using your hands or preferably a staff start to channel nature's energy though it, and into the body. You must also picture how you want it to be healed in your mind. This is where an understanding of the body's structure is important, for if you don't know how everything works with one another, then you risk the chance of seriously injuring the patient. \n After picturing it in your minds eye, continue applying your energy until it is healed. It is critical to stop healing at this point, or a tumor might develop. After any healling, some food should be given to the patient, as it is tiring on the body. \n Rememeber, perserving nature isn't the druids only task, they must also preserve life. I wish you luck in your in your healing endeavours, and may the trees look over you.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to hunt monsters safely", "monkeychez", "Hunting monsters is an easy, but dangerous, but easy way of making minas. Creepers drop 20-30 minas, and coal, iron  ingots, and iron and coal ore. Skeletons drop roughly 15 to 25 minas, and drop food and arrows. lastly, zombies drop 10 to 20 minas, and drop coal, iron, food, and armor.  The best stategy to killing a creeper is to attack once with a sword, then move back about 4 or 5 blocks, and repeat until creeper is dead. To kill a skeleton, always be on your feet. Attack with a sword, but keep circling while attacking the skeleton. Repeat until dead. Zombies are the easiest to kill, but very dangerous. Either shoot with a bow, or keep swinging a sword at the zombie from 1 to 2 blocks away. I hope this guide helped you. You will have many treasures and pockets full of minas, as long as you stick to this guide!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to join the Alras Fight Klub", "Gropier", "The Alras Fight Klub (AFK) uses a free external website to track standing. Therefore the process of joining has a few steps. \n1. Visit the website http://www.myleague.com/lothcafk and click the Free Sigh Up button. \n2. You will receive the following message: This is a private league. You must receive an invitation before you can join. To request an invitation please contact the league admins. Click the Contact the league admins link. \n3. Complete the form using your MC Name as the User Name and select \"Invitation Request\" in the drop-down box. \n4. In the Lord of the Craft game, contact Gordok (Gropier) and tell him you have requested an invitation. At this point, you will be asked to pay the one-time membership fee of 1,000 minas. \n5. Once the minas are paid, you will be sent an invitation code, which you should return to the above site and use to register for the league. \n6. You will then be given access to the gym and assigned a locker (private locker). \n7. On the AFK League website, click on the home tab and then select Rules. Read all the rules and good luck. \n.\n.\nThanks,\n.\nGordok Yon Hammer", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Kill Ser Delcius", "TheImpulseHQ", "*The Entire book has been ripped, with only a few words left like heart, soul sword of valour, a pure knight and the words impossible have been branded on the front*", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Kill Stupid Monsters", "TheGiver17", "Introduction\n Hi my name is Leafwind and I'm going to tell you how to kill those stupid monsters so that YOU can take their MONEY and use it to buy some shit. All you need to do is follow these simple instructions and you will soon find yourself a swords skill level admired by everyone in Aegis. Except your girlfriend. She probably   won't like it.\n Chapter 1: The Zombie\n The Zombie, a stupid and brainless creature, is the easiest mob to kill.    All you have to do is hit it with your wooden, stone, metal, or extremely precious diamond sword and smear its dirty blood all over it! \n Chapter 2: The Spider\n The Spider is a stupid little noob that can climb walls and jump on you from a million  feet away, but all you really have to do is run circles around it so it can't jump at you. Also you should never stop hitting it because if you do, then it will be able to lunge at you.\n \n Chapter 3: The Skeleton\n The skeleton is another really stupidly annoying mob that fires arrows at you. The method that I use to kill it is to run circles around it swinging like a madman. This is effective but can be tricky if there are multiple skeletons. Then it is best to sidestep the skeleton(s) avoiding their arrows.   \n \n Chapter 4: The Creeper\n The Creeper is easily THE MOST ANNOYING MONSTER IN MINECRAFT and it is rightfully named \"The Exploding P***s\" The method for killing a creeper is to run up to it swing your sword and run away. Doing this multiple times will eventual annoy it so much that it will just die. For advanced monster hunters you may be able to swing at the creeper twice before running. This is achieved by hitting it right as you are running backwards out of its range. There is also a super-charged version of the creeper that appears when they are hit by lightning. If you see one... run the HELL away from it! \n \n Chapter 5: The Slime\n Yeah sure slimes can be cute, but not when they are massive mutha f***in tree climbing slimes! If you EVER see a giant slime in a tree run away or at least tell your friend that giant slimes drop diamonds 'cause then you'll actually get something out of it. ... his stuff! :D \n \n Conclusion\n So I hope you enjoyed this educational and entertaining book, because I sure did!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to knock on Durzio's Door", "hellyeahz", "1. Approach the door 2. Choose to either emote knock or don't 3. Begin rapidly opening and closing t The door.  If allowed to enter, admire Durzio's OP basement size, and enter his valuables room Finally use Durzio's easy to access valuables room to steal all his belongings.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to make a Mine-Sword", "Lexperiments", "A Mine-Sword is a simple contraption, invented by Lex the Dwarf. To create one, you'll need 10 sticks, sticky ball paste, and 5 or more of a material of your choice. First, you glue the sticks together with the sticky paste in a 2-stick long and 5-stick thick staff. You then craft a large pickaxe head out of three stone, which is plenty, then attach it onto one side of the staff just like a normal pick. You then craft a sword out of at least 2 pieces of stone, then attach it to the other side. Possibly, you might want to make a sheath to not kill yourself while mining. To do this, craft 2 leather into a sheath, and line the base of the sword with sticky paste. Then attach sheath. The sticky paste WILL stay no matter what. \n \n Adem's house is the lair. Use the water.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Make Friends", "MamaLuigi412", "", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Make Money", "Telandriel", "", ""),
        StaticBook("How to make: Potions", "tthorn3", "This is a small guide for starting potion making. Don't expect any secrets to be divulged in this volume. \nChapter One : Equipment \nA potion maker should have a few things in order to brew safely. The first is a pair of thick gloves. Preferably made of leather. This is to avoid acids ruining your hands; you need your hands in top condition in order to apply correct amounts, and get them out of the way of explosions. The second thing you will need is a brewing stand. These are specilized devices designed to conduct burnt regents in to your bottles are madw with the physical parts of a blaze man. This stand is a MUST have for any aspiring alchemist. There are very few potions that can be made without it. The potions that can are only able to fix menial things. Warts, hair color, etcetera. The last thing you will need is a water source. Many swear by a cauldron, but in my experiance it tends to taint the water with unwanted iron. \nChapter 2 Regents \nThe hardest part of potion brewing is collecting the potion materials. The basis for all potions, nether wart, is held by a select few. they do not part with it easily. Another item used in potion making is glowstone dust. Considering it is only found in the nether it is even harder to come by. The glowstone dust is used to increase the power of potions. Redstone,  is only found in the bowls of Aegis. It can extend how long potions effects last. Often, instead of doubling it, it can triple the duration of the potion. I am not going to tell you the secret regents to make specific potions. otherwise you may put me out of buisness before I even start!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Overthrow the King", "Sandonthefloor", "You Don't!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Play: Casino Blackjack", "Lomaticc", "1. Place your bet (50-500 minas) \n(/money pay PlayerName ammount) \n2. The Object of Casino Blackjack is to roll closest to 21 without going over. \n3. Start out by rolling twice (/roll 11; two times) \nthis is your starting number, the dealer will now roll twice. \n4. The two numbers are compared and the player chooses to hit or stay. \nChoosing to hit - player rolls again (out of 11) and the number is added to their base number \n Choosing to stay - player does not roll again. \n5. After a player chooses to stay, the dealer rolls until a bust, push, or win occurs. \nBust - rolling a total that is over 21, results in a loss \nPush - rolling a total where the dealer and player are tied and the player stays, results in a replay \nWin - whoever is closest to 21 without going over is deemed the winner.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Play: Casino Diamond Slots", "Lomaticc", "\n1. Place a bet (minimum and maximum bet varies) \n(/money pay Hostname ##) \n2. The red light will turn on when you are allowed to push the slots buttons \n3. Push the slots button \n4. 3 items will pop out corresponding to the PAYOUTS \n2x Cobblestone - YOU LOSE \n3x Cobblestone - YOU LOSE \n3x Random Items - 10 MINAS \nEvery Cake - 10 MINAS \n2x Iron - 25 MINAS \n2x Gold - 50 MINAS \n2x Diamond - 100 MINAS \n3x Slimeballs - PAYBACK \n3x Iron - 2x BET \n \n 3x Gold - 5x BET \n3x Diamond - JACKPOT! 10x BET!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to play: Casino Dice.", "Benben582", "\n1. Place a bet between 50-500. \n((/money pay Hostname ##)) \n2. Roll out of the amount you bet. ((IE. You bet 200 you type /roll 200)) \n3. You win 1.5x Your Roll! ((You roll a 175 out of 200 you win 262.5 minas))", ""),
