        StaticBook("How to Ride a Pig (OOC GUIDE)", "whiteberry14", "To ride a pig you need first get a saddle... ((Saddles can be crafted...)) You need to tell your pig where to go... But in pig language.... OINK OINK! (( Use /mob go (north/south/east/west) to tell your pig where to go...)) Also you can make the pig stop by telling stop in Pig Language... OINK! (( Say /mob go stop to make your pig stop)) As a last lesson it is prefered to put the saddle to the pig with some distance... (( If you do it far you may no loose your saddle and you can reuse it)) So thats it for this How To ride a Pig guide! Now go and tame some pigs!", ""),
        StaticBook("how to send mail", "jacksonsp1170", "start by geting a book and puting from: your name to: sending to name than 1,2, or 3 day shiping than put in chest to send a package do the letter but put in the package box. put letter next to package NEXT TO 1 day 20 minas   2 day 10 minas   4 day 5 minas do /money pay jacksonsp1170 (amount)", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Sentence Prisoners", "Starsweeper", "First ye should learn how to deal with arresting people Get them to stop, in whatever way possible then continue to tell them they're under arrest and that they have to follow you If they resist simply state that if they resist anymore they will be banished and killed onsight     ((If they countinue to resist/ignore you then start taking screenshots and try and get them banned for ruining RP)) After you get them jailed and locked up then you should give them their sentence I will write down the most common crimes along with their sentence but if you run into an odd one then just use yer best judgement The most Common crime your going to run into is being an Undead There are a few undead that have already been discovered thhat hide amoung us, their names are Lodrick_the_Feared ((jiig21)) James_Servant_of_Ilbees ((123trezmoo123 this isnt the most accurate but its something like this)) Guriam ((pugsy)) These are the Undead we have discovered, penatly for being an undead is 2 weeks in jail ((IG)) and then followed by death, which is to be down in the Execution Chamber The Second Crime that's common  is Impersonating a Guard, it isnt very serious but still its a crime The Second Crime that's common  is Impersonating a Guard, it isnt very serious but still its a crime This is defined by opening the gate for people, questioning people,  and going in the guard house If they question people or open the gates for people then its 2-3 days in jail, if they are found in the guard house then its 4 days in jail with a 200 minas fine the next crime is being a bandit, its defined by ONLY reports from other people so they're not to common but if you DO enounter one then the penalty is 6 days in jail And the last crime Im going to cover is threatening other people or other guards The penalty for threatening other people is 5 nights in jail if they continue to do this while injai l then they must be put to death If they threaten a guard from the beggining then its 1 week in jail, If they countine to threaten its Death Thats it, and remember DON'T abuse your power ((Also NEVER metagame or hold a prisoner for more than a hour, this will result in getting in troub le from the GMs if anything I've previously said goes against these two MAJOR rules then disregard them, make sure to Roleplay the arrest of people that are started in this book )) ))   \n Good Luck, \n \n Guard_Campington", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Spice up your Love life with a Wizard", "anorexichippo", "", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Spice Up Your Sex Life!", "Epic_Potatoe", "", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Survive an Undead Invasion", "dudog", "The Undead are living dead. They are very strong and well equipped. If you encounter an Undead by yourself I suggest you run. If you have other people around or are very well equipped you could probably take one down. Undead use fire as a weapon so I would stand close to a fountain or water source. It is best to fight Undead in groups as it is to fight other mobs. Sneaking up on mobs and Undead is also a very effective way to survive. Always carry extra swords, arrows and food. If a whole horde of Undead or coming and you're by yourself it's best to hide somewhere and sneak Use these tips to survive when the Undead come to your city.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Survive in Aegis - By Noku", "calvinnok", "Tip 1, Beg for money ;;Be s sucker, don't care about your pride, you can't even survive without a single Mina ;;Tip 2, Find some wood ;;As most of the trees are protected, you have to find a wooden building that is hardly damage , and get some wood from it, same when you need stone ;;Tip 3, Get a sword, and slash some zombies ;;Kill monsters to get Minas, it is common sense ;;Extra!!! ;;Important, don't try to kill ZombiePigmen before you get an iron sword ;;Tip 4, Upgrade your gears ;;Buy iron with your Minas, then upgrade your tools, stone tools aren't strong enough ;;Extra!!! ;;The easiest way to get diamond tools is to pick up the others' leftover, although is is rude ;;Final tip, Get a home ;;As mensioned in the tittle, a home is the best way to keep you safe at night ;;More extras: ;;1. Never pass by Kramoroe, tons of undead and bandits ;;2. Never get into woods, even in the morning ;;3. Donate to get more functions (although I didn't donate as well) ;;The End", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Survive the North", "Swgrclan", "Written by Thral'Mar DeathHammer. In this manuel, you will find all nesscessary means of surviving the North. Step I: Get good gear. To survive in the North, you need equipment, such as leather clothing, a sturdy pick, and a sharp sword. These are the basic items you need for any trip to the North. You also need an abundance of food. Without food, you will starve and die. If you run out of food, you can hunt for pigs or Cows for their meat.   You can also harvest Cows for leather if your warm armor break and becomes useless. Step II: Making a Camp Making a camp or outpost is vital when it becomes dark, because terrible creatures of the night will try to find you, and murder you. In the North, you should dig out a hole in the ground and wait until day. A simple camp in the middle of some forest will not protect you from the evil creatures that lurk the dark forests. Step III:  Gathering Materials. If you are a wandering merchant, the North is a good place to find many valuables resources. Such as: Wool, Coal, Iron, Clay, and wood. Iron sells at a high price. Coal is not so valued, but it is very common, and if sold in large amounts, you can make a good amount of Minas. Wool is favored by many people, so if you get an abundance of that, you can sell it and also make a nice sum of money. Wood is everywhere, and people would rather buy it in bundles, so if one was to amass 288 Logs of wood, you can get alot of money. Step IV: Battle. If you are marching into the North by Military means, or just revenge of the things that inhabit the North, such as the Undead, then You must bring A great amount of food, armor, and weapons. I diamond blade is recommended for battle with Undead, and a set of Iron armor can defend against their dark spells. If you are marching to Undead territory, you must bring a Bow, A diamond sword, a set of Diamond armor, and ann abundance of food. Allies are needed if you are invading Undead Territory. If you have no allies, a large pack of dogs is good for the job. Epilouge: That is all the things you need to survive in the Cold, unforgiving North. Good luck!", ""),
