        StaticBook("Hunters of The Guardians", "NorAlvarin", "Hail, fellow Guardian. I am Rinn, Master Hunter, Leader of our Guilds Hunters. And you, maybe you are a new recruit, interested in becoming a Guardian Hunter? Or maybe you are just interested in learning about our choise of specialization? Anyway, I shall tell you about our ''section'' and our role in the Guild. Our guild are split up in several ''subranks''. Each different subrank includes different jobs or tasks. One of these subranks, is the Hunter. The Hunter is the Ranger of the guild. Usually wielding a bow and leather- or iron armour, the Hunters' are the Support Infantry of the Guardians. But the Hunters' main task is not battle,  it is supplying the Guardians with materials like feathers and leather, as well as food like porkchop or stake, things usually only found in the wild. These materials are important for our guild, even though it may not sound that decisive. Feathers for example, are a must if the Guardians are to have a constant supply of arrows. And then we have leather. Leather is important as a cheap and light armour, perfect for any fast moving fighters, or assassins and infiltrators. Also, a high-ranked Hunter is usually trained in surveilling an enemy force, and is a high-quality scout. And no faction has ever won a war without knowing the strengths and weaknessess of the enemy. \n Now, we are at the end of the book, and I hope you have gained what answers or information you may were looking for. But if not, you can allways contact me, or any other Hunter, and we will do the best we can to give you the answers. May the light of Good and the Guardians protect you on your travels. \n -Rinn", ""),
