        StaticBook("Iblees", "ComradeRenzbro", "Iblees is the main focus of the Undead. Pleasing him means everything to them. Not much is known about Iblees to those who don't worship him. I know very little about him but the things I do know are mostly on a need to know basis. What has been discovered very recently, within the past week or 2, is that Iblees is either multiple beasts, or can multiply himself. In the battle that inevitably destroyed the Undead Keep of the north Iblees was summoned a showed his true form. It was a terrifying expirence for all those who witnessed but Iblees was eventually overwhelmed and taken down. It was a great victory for the people of Aegis and the moral booster everyone needed after the shattering fall of Alstion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Iblees", "Benboboy", "And when Iblees turned to his minion he said \"I own this land do I not\" to which the minion awnsered \"Ye.. yes my lord...\" Iblees smiled with glee as his power had begun to grow. \"The mortals of this world shall soon bow to me. But not without help.\" Iblees's gaze turned to a large manor at the edge of a town.\"We need allies in our efforts\". Iblees turned into a normal looking man and walked up to the manor. The sign outside said Eynon manor. Iblees knocked on the door twice. \"Hello?\" spoke a voice through the door. \"I am here to give you great power and wealth. What is your name?\" Iblees asked. \"My name is Albert Eynon. How could you give me those things?\" Albert questioned. \"I am Iblees, lord of the undead, and I have a task for you.\" Iblees boomed. \"Wha...what! Iblees? What do you want?\" asked Albert with a wary expression on his face. \"I will give you as much minas and power as you desire if you worship me and do a single task for me. \"What is the task?\". \"You must k...(page is torn from book) \"Im glad you understand Albert, this is for the future of Aegis\". \"Ye...yes. I understand\" whispered Albert. Iblees saw a young boy peering round the corner in the hallway. \"Is that your boy?\" asked Iblees. \"Yes, he is destined to be a priest, but Im not sure he will now that we worship you my lord\". Iblees just smiled, then turned back to Albert \"Farewell Eynon family, if you decline the contract I shall bring the curse unto you.\" Iblees smiled as he said this. \"We will not fail you\" exclaimed Albert. (the rest of the book has is been torn out)", ""),
        StaticBook("Iblees Worshipping", "vegan166", "The undead are awesome", ""),
