        StaticBook("In enemy territory", "Jackbjossi", "Hello. I'm Jack Mercy and I am a guard of Al'Khazar. I am writing this book while just outside of an undead villa near the road from Al'khazar to Kal urgan. I have been here before, with my friend: Carl. Its Savet, 35th of suns smile, 1321 When I encountered the Undead for the first time I was helping Carl to seek rumors for his up coming news paper called the Aegis Herald. We met a man on the road, he told us to get in side to get away from the hot sun. The floor opened We fell down in a room covered with netherrack. I ran to the door in fear of the netherrack igniting. Carl didn't make it for the door and the netherrack was ignited. One of them just stared at me as I used my soulstone. I ran to Sgt. Hayden and told him about this. He said they already knew about the Undead owned villa. I suggested attacking but they told me not to.", ""),
        StaticBook("In ignem autem non cadit.", "Lastchance2099", "Aegis. \n \n Here, I sit. In Aegis. Wrapped in its arms, I currently shiver. Yes, Here I sit; In Aegis. Yet my skin and my mind rest against a tree. A cold night as usual, I have only met Luna once on my journey. My journey to learn of Aegis. \n Aegis. \n Next to me is a tattered sign, barely erect on the path. Faded with time, it whispers a small message. \"in ignem autem non cadit\". \n This script means nothing to me. I run my tongue across my teeth; decipher this magical code. \n I do not. My journey shall continue, As, with Aegis. \n Aegis. \n Resting against this ancient bark I breathe lively. I hear far, my hand is nimble with the pen; I will sleep well. While the sign was faded this place is not. Above this tree, and above this sign, is constructed a behemoth against the ground. Glass from our greatening minds, creates a glove, stuck upon Aegis to form a magnificent dome. In such a glove I feel safe. Whether this dome serves as a web, or a candle against the darkness I do not know. This is a common truth in Aegis. \n Aegis. \n As God rose his hand to conjur good, so too was a shadow cast. \n Within every man, dwarf, elf, orc, lurks this shadow. Against the torches, so too does this ancient tree, faded sign, and magnificent dome print their shadow. \n Aegis was born in twilight, and Aegis shall die for twilight. \n Aegis. \n I have experienced much. Above me an apple quivers in the branches of this ancient tree. Luna shines and dazzles its unpleasantly green skin. \n My pen falters for this apple. \n I weep for this apple. \n My stomach yearns for such an apple; my mind prays I can reach it... Tart;sweet;Rotten;Ripe. I have seen the apple Aegis offers a  thousand times. \n Yet. \n I will never be able to taste this apple. No one in Aegis can taste their own apple. \n Aegis. \n Here I sit; In Aegis. Against a tree. Next to a faded sign. Under a dome. Above a shadow. Beneath my apple. \n Yes, Here I sit; In Aegis. \n \n In the morning as I woke; \n The apple and the shadow met; \n Twisting writhing as they spoke; \n 'In ignem autem non cadit' \n \n -Bastion- \n", ""),
        StaticBook("In Laurelin: Journal of Rhisereld", "Rhisereld", "At first I was just focused on leaving as quietly as possible. As I'm sure you remember, that went to dust pretty quickly. I was forced to face you, and our conversation left me just as torn as you were. I was so confused, almost split in two. I'm half me and half you, Alethion. I had to get out. I couldn't bear to face you every day, even at the polite distance we kept from each other. I couldn't bear knowing that you'd given your love to another. I couldn't bear the begging for forgiveness that I can't give. \n The way you held your hand out for mine. \nThe promises you made, ones I couldn't trust. \nI had to get away from that. \nIronically, it was these very same things that kept me tied to the Isles and you. I was hurting you, and I could see that. I watched you slowly grow more and more dejected, each time I moved away you were overcome by grief inside. You hid it well, but not well enough. You have no idea how much I wanted to comfort you. I just wanted to hold you tight. That's who I am. Empathy is a part of me. \nBut I knew what you had done was wrong. What happened... there's nothing stopping it from happening again. This wasn't the first time it had happened. It was going to happen again and again. So I had to force myself to abandon my empathy and leave you there, if only to end this cycle of sin and repent. Akorta said that you were playing with my empathy, to convince me to come back. I can't believe, I won't believe that you would do anything like that. Your tears are real.   So now I have found refuge in Laurelin. Uprooting yourself from your home is not the greatest feeling. I am alone here, danger lurks in every hooded stranger. Avoiding the people that you love is heartbreaking. Indescribably difficult. And the worst thing? \nI feel so free.", ""),
        StaticBook("In Lieu of Flandre Scarlet", "ZazarusDious", "I 'ave 'eard ye 'ave shut down de inn, meh good king Though frem me and others whom enjoyed each company in such a corner of Kal\"urguan I request, no I beseach ye te reconsider Flandre Scarlet,  although young, 'as been a wonderful host te our community  . I kin see certain problem's occuring since de said inn is by yer estate. De noise will cause problems te ye. However, since its construction I 'ave yet seen it being utilized. Also in fair observation, me own plot doubles 'as a 'ome ''ear as well as handlin certain  affairs.   In addtion Chris Fords' Pub and Restaurant exists within' de vicinity as well. Although ye do 'ave de final say on such matters mere den a handful o' us would like to see her conduct business in de lines o' hospitality. May yer decision 'ave wisdom and finesse. ~Drazdun Silvermein~ *A stamp of Duralsavot is embedded in wax with a white feather casted within it*", ""),
        StaticBook("In Memoriam of Gruol, My Fickle Friend", "Ohaythar121", "\n A winter gust \n a desert breeze \n equal in power, inbalanced in life \n one grows and lives \n one smolders and dies \n both were in Gruol \n now both are in the breeze again edit", ""),
        StaticBook("In Memroiam of Gruol, My Fickle Friend", "Ohaythar121", "\n A winter gust \n A desert breeze equal in power, unbalanced in life w", ""),
        StaticBook("In Pursuit Of A Criminal", "Qwertyasdman", "Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1312 Today I am at the VonSchlichen Tavern, looking for a room to store my belongings. The reason is because my home at Kal'urguan is not exactly safe as the crag (a hole in the ground) i s expanding and this will soon take out the town, and my belongings. So I am looking for a new home untill the city will be rebuilt. That is my day...   Thank ye Itnan, 23rd of Snows Maiden, 1312 Today, I am sitting at my home in Kal'urguan, which I know will not be here for long.. The crag is expanding everyday, soon my house will be gone. I am looking over the wreckage it has caused, It's horrible .. You may think the undead caused it, but no, Mother Nature is angry. We have ruined her. She used te be pretty, but now she is not. The buildings we have made have scared her face, now there is no running from her rage. Tolta, 24th of Snows Maiden, 1312 Today I found the criminal I have so long searched for, but he ran from me, a coward he is. There is one upside for this though, i have learned his name, Ritos. But I must now search for him again, to see if he will be kind enough to hand my items back. But I think he won't be so kind, so, in preperation, I am bringing along a full set of Iron armor, two full stacks of arrows, a bow and some mushroom soup for the cold nights. Wish me luck! I forgot to mension, I am also bringing my book!", ""),
        StaticBook("In Search of the Isle", "Lail_Ravengem", "1. Tonight is the night before our journey.  Zephyr Galewind and I, Lail Ravengem, are settin g out for some odd place an Elf told us about. It seems odd, but I'm in dire need for an adventure. the lands outside of malinor have changed. . . \n 2. We've traveled a day and a night.  We've found a strange undead-like structure.  It's very disconcerting. \n 734 \n 65 \n -219 \n 3.  Another day, another odd location.  This was a large mountain with a melon farm underneath.  A quite massive one at that! \n986 \n71 \n -96 \n Also, a house just south of the Crag \n4.  We may have found it, but we're not too sure.  After slaying pigmen, we found a large druidic tree.  It's rather empty, but fantastic nonetheless.  We're continuing south, as we both have our doubts as to if this is the Wisp Isle. \n1032 \n69 \n130 \n There's a large walled in area SouthWest of the Tree \n5 An old Warden's base, very far south.  Very nice, but a tad dapper in shape. \n1302 \n71 \n263 \n6.  Hmm.  A place Zephyr tells me is called Elotre.  it seems to be inhabited, and they've materials like vines and stone bricks. \n1842 \n97 \n276 \n7.  The wealth of the inhabitants of this place is astounding.  Such a beautiful city.  Though, all was not well. Zephyr fell off of a steep ledge.  I thought he'd died. But God had another plan, it seems.  The monks saved him.  I sent a messenger and told him what happened.  After a few days, he'd walked all the way back .  Our adventure continues. \n8.  The most gorgeous city I've ever seen.  Words do it no justice.  It's just east of the rich city \n1860 \n76 \n-86 \n9.  Another strange place. . . \n2186 \n82 \n-525 \n10.  My god. . . I'm losing faith that the Isle exists.  A large stone circle in the water was just that ;  A large stone circle. \n2316 \n66 \n-738", ""),
        StaticBook("in terviwe with dominius bein", "craotor", "Q:so how did you start your career as soldier? A:i signed up for a job as a guard,to warlord tyhus then i got sent so war against the dwarves soon after dat i returned to sanjezal and stood guard for 3 years those were quiet days A:you started of quite humble did you ever imagine yourself as a dominuis? I always Imagined being Dominuis,never thought that i would reach it though .But i always had thee chance,being part of the Noble Clan of Lur . Who were strong suporters of tyhus and they were killed of by the Or'ta's clan for suportinng tythus Q:i know you have been in many wars,fighting in so many wars changed your view of the world? A: Aye,so much blood has been shed and i felll we orcs need ta get past our primaal instincts and start collaborating and working together Q: you were the founder of a big organisation the ferox legio was it hard to let go leadershi p A: it was hard to let go of the Leadership,well sort of.The Ferox was already dead at the tim and i realised that i coudnt lead it whiled leading a town .But hopefully the New Orc Army will be a better replacement and will survive this is my last question A: when you founded shar did you ever expect it to be so big and influencial? Nay,i never expected it to be dis big or Great, i owe a lot to all the consuld and especialy Tirok who designed many parts of it and is now being considered for lower Dominius A:well thank you for youre time bein Anytime", ""),
