        StaticBook("Job Payment", "jtringl", "\nWhen the guild takes on a job, we expect payment. Payment usually comes in three forms. Items, land, or minas. Minas is the easiest to deal with, but we still accept the other forms. \nWhen taking items as payment, the items will go strait to the accountant for the division. The accountant will divide them up evenly amongst the workers, and take out the guild cut. Accountants know the value of each item, so trust them to do it right! \nWhen we recieve land as payment, it can be a bit trickier. Immediately the founders should be notified. They will decide whether or not the guild needs the land. If they decide the guild does not need the land, they will either sell it and divide the money up between workers, or give the land to a specific worker. If we give the land away, workers will be payed with guild funds. If the founders decide we do need the land, however, we will build a guild hall there and pay the workers with guild funds. \nMinas is the easiest to deal with. The minas is paid to the accountant, who then divides it up. The percentages go as follows: \n10% Guild Fund \n5% Division Dean \n5% Accountant \n5% Division Fund \n75% Workers", ""),
        StaticBook("Jobs for houses", "Eltyer", "Good day, if yer looking for a job. I have good news for ye. We be rebuildin Sanjezal, we orcs need lots of Sandstone. Becuz we need housas for da people! So yer job is to gather 8 poundz (8 stacks) of Sandstone fer us. Then ye earnt yer small house. When ye gather more ye get more extras like biggar housez. Give da sandstone to: Mogroka Krink Yaghy Gezmar Dey will spread it over da architects. When ye gathered your Sandstone and ye gave it. Ye will get a place on da 'board'. Dere ye can see who gathered whad. If yer not on da board ask for: Krink Gezmar And say whad ye donated to us, we got documentz of yer. ((we check everything)) ((OOC NOTE)) Don't landscar, make everything look natural. If you don't do that, it will get you in trouble.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jobs to do", "Sykora87", "\n Farm- Farming is a key part to geting food for our troops :) \n Mineing and collecting wood and other stuff to build great forts and castles", ""),
        StaticBook("John's Guide to Fighting Monsters", "Gjon3", "Zombie: Wait till the sun is coming up", ""),
        StaticBook("John's Journal", "123devmo321", "Day 1- I start my undead hunt today, I plan to head north to annihilate all those rotting bastards. \n Nightfall, I made it to Alstion, there is nobody here, completely abandoned... I'm staying in my friend Banok's house tonight, I'm sure he won't mind. \n \n Day 2- I head off for Winterfell today. \n Again, this city is abandoned, people must be scared that the undead are so near. Taking refuge in this old ranch I found. Hopefully in the morning someone is in the city so I can ask them if they have seen anything... Middle of the night I traveled to a nearby watchtower and watched the sun rise... \n \n Day 3- I can see nobody, no houses from this watchtower, not sure where to go... There are no more roads, My journey thru the wilds begins.... My journey left me facing an ocean, I quickly made a boat and sailed across. Night approaches, made a quick shelter to sleep during the night \n \n Day 4- I found a building, If my journal ends here, assume the worst...", ""),
        StaticBook("John's Journal", "319am", "I John Roontz swear I shall serve the priest and the Anima Templi in the holy Kingdom of Oren . I shall wield the shadows, and wear the shadows, and love the shadows from which I strike.", ""),
        StaticBook("John's notes", "123devmo321", "All I remember is a blur, I was in some sort of feral state, trying to protect my tree from these blurred figures, I couldn't make out any of their faces. One of them came at the tree and I snapped, I attacked him, I'll admit it. Next thing I knew I was on the ground, staring at one of the blurs hacking at the tree. In a flash the same blur was on me, and I felt a sharp pain in my chest. All went black, and the chaos of the last moments of my apparent life faded, and I found peace. I lie down in a field, full of wheat, ready to harvest, with occasional overgrown mushrooms dotting the field. All of my worries were gone now, and I looked about, confused, not knowing what was happening, but oddly enough, I didn't care. This state of bliss lasted only a few moments, perhaps not even a minute, til I was in a section of the trunk of the tree which in my view jusst a few seconds ago was nearly hacked to peices. After a few minutes of sheer pain, unable to move, I completely materialized, and came to life before James, and a strange face. I couldn't make out what they were saying, but the two kept care of me til I was on my feet. Now, I write this, confused as ever about what trasnpired in the... thirty years I have been gone. The Grove is different, Mahten has died, And only a few faces seem familiar, and those look very aged, and I can barely recognize them. \n Writings of the Former Arch Druid John, Druid of the Oasis Hello there.", ""),
