        StaticBook("join the white ravens!", "colin1389", "the white raven are the protecters of the road. protect people from monsters and bandit. we have large strong hold where you'll get free housing and a lock chest. we do a lot build a our strong hold so there a place for you if you like to build. there are ranks we raven which is where you would start then there white raven,captins,councilmen an d high councilmen there are three high councilen they are our leaders alvaska shadows and gregory. the rules of our guild our as fallows: no killing of fellow white ravens all raven are to be treated with respect. no stealing from the guild or it members you MUST obey higher authority. destruction of the white ravens central WILL NOT BETOLERATED and will be seen as griefing. any violation of these laws will be punised! to join the white ravens pleace pm (ogedi) or (coiln1389) they will help you if you have any questions just pm any of the name list. thank you and we hope you join. :)", ""),
        StaticBook("Joint Agreement between The Guardians and The Oren Guard, Version 01 ALPHA", "begginfokillz", "preamble: we, the guild The Guardians, wish to ally with and Join forces with the Oren Guard, and wish to make the following agreement, to benefit both parties. this agreement shall benefit The Guardians by granting them these privledges: CLAUSE 1: The Guardians, as a independent guild, shall have PARTIAL ATHORITY in dealing with ALL MATTERS involving the Undead, in the lands under the jurisdiction of the Oren Guard, not including ANY CITY guarded by THE OREN GUARD. This PARTIAL ATHORITY shall grant the following Freedoms to THE GUARDIANS: Clause 1: ALL UNDEAD found in the teretories NOT INCLUDING ANY CITY, under the jurisdiction of the OREN GUARD, may be investigated and dealt with by THE GUARDIANS with the following Exceptions, whcih may be moddified by the High Constable of the Oren Guard, with 3 days notice: THE GUARDIANS may NEVER make an arrect, THE GUARDIANS may ONLY investigate and deal with UNDEAD, and may deal with them WITHIN LIMITS OF THE LAWS OF OREN\n ALL GUARDIANS shall be allowed to join an investigation by the OREN GUARD, in the role of ALLIED OBSERVER, and may aid in investigations\n ALL GUARDIANS, Within certain limits set by the High Constable of the OREN GUARD, shall have ANTONYMOUS AND LIMITED AUTHORITY in ALL MATTERS dealing with investigating and fighting the UNDEAD, Their ASSETS, amnd THEIR FOLLOWERs, which shell allow a member of THE GUARDIANS to deal with these matters as they see fit (in thesae matters, an officer in THE GUARDIANS shall write a full report on what occured, and shall hand deleiver it to a member of The OREN GUARD.) The GUARDIANS shall be treated as an independent allied force with limited athority in dealing with THE UNDEAD and their assets, and shall have their athority respected by all members of The OREN GUARD. \n ALL GUARDIANS shall HAVE SAFE PASSAGE IN AND OUT OF OREN DURING EMERGENCY SITUATIONS AND DURING LOCKDOWNS OF THE CAPITAL CITY OF OREN. IN RETURN for these benefits, The OREN GUARD shall receive the following: ALL INFORMATION AND EVIDENCE GAINED BY THE GUARDIANS SHALL BE TURNED OVER TO THE OREN GUARD. \n ANY AND ALL INFORMATION GAINED BY THE GUARDIANS SHALL BE GIVEN TO THE OREN GUARD (And Vice Versa) 50% of all net profits, weapons, and food the guardians make shall be tithed to THE OREN GUARD, free of charge. Also, if the capital of OREN falls, we, THE GUARDIANS, Shall attempt to retake and rebuild the city with due haste. lastly, ALL OREN GUARD MEMBERS shall have UNLIMMITED and UNFETTERED acsess to THE GUARDIAN FORT, for use during any operations THE OREN GUARD does in the area surrounding the GUARDIAN FORT\n this concludes the peace agreement", ""),
        StaticBook("Joke book", "Miner_300", "After the Great Britain Beer Festival, in London, all the brewery presidents decided to go ou", ""),
        StaticBook("Joke Book (Beer festival)", "Miner_300", "After the Great Britain Beer Festival, in London, all the brewery presidents decided to go out for a beer The guy from Corona sits down and says, ''Hey Senor, I would like the world's best beer, a corona.'' The bartender dusts off a bottle from the shelf and gives it to him. The guy from Budweiser says, ''I'd like the best beer in the world, give me a Budweiser.'' The bartender gives him one. The guy from Coors says, ''I'd like a beer made of Rocky Mountain spring water, give me a Coors.'' And He gets it. The guy from Guinness sits down and says, ''Give me a Coke.'' The bartender is a little taken aback, but gives him what he ordered. The other brewery presidents look over at him and ask '' Why aren't you drinking a Guinness?'' and the president replies, ''Well, I figured if you guys aren't drinking beer, neither would I.'' \n Made by Zeke", ""),
        StaticBook("Joke Journal", "Jon021", "one day in my travels around laurelin, I was walking through the woods. I see this beautiful woman walking throught the woods as well. I yell to her \"hey, how are you doing? what brings a lady like you to the woods ?\" I hear no response, so I assume, with my man-brain, she's playing hard to get. So I chase her until I finally catch up. then She turns around, and I see a creeper's face. SSSSS yep. that's my life for ya. \nhave any of you ever been to the Orc nation? I went there with one of my guard-friends once. as soon as we enter sanhar he says to me \"hey you might want to take your a rmor off.\"\" I think to myself \"why should I?? Are they going to kill me because I'm wearing armor?? \" Then after we finished our business in sanhar, an orc stops me in the road and he says \"I'm g oing to kill you!!\" I say \"why kill me?? what'd I do??\" He says, \"You're wearing armor! I hate armored men!\" I hardly escape from that guy, and later ((lol)) I ask my buddy about how he knew about that guy who hates armor. aye", ""),
        StaticBook("Jokes", "Vicentee", "Ok, so I was standing in Al'Khazar, before an Undead attack.  Everyone is being crazy, and there is like three Ascended.  Since ascended are so useless, everyone was disorganized, goin crazy, and nothing happens. And everyone said the ascended were useful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Joma, 20th of Malins Welcome, 1322", "459pm", "IC DISMEMBERD? Yesterday we spoke with IC leaders and found that they are under major  civil suit from kalan (name not disclosed for privacy) saying that he was greived serveral times and forced to leave his home \"we have appsolutly no idea why they did this\" says High Prince Native but we think they needed to expand and the house was too close to there fort. ORK FARMERS GO HUNGRY friday ork farmers were raided by undead and were pillaged for food, we dont know why exactly because undead do not require food, it may be just to starve out there oponents but we suspect it is because they are feeding there slaves to the north TABLES! HOW TO USE THEM, AND HOW NOT. the next new thing? tables!!! everyone is talking about tables, you make them by placeing a pressure plate on a fence or stick it makes a great single person table, but not for a bar because the 2 pressuse plates linked do not touch each other so it leaves a large gap between FISH ARE PLEANTIFULL, PORK IS NOT for some reason unknown by experts pigs and doing terribly this year while fish are having great meals allmost everyday so it may be time to bust out the 'ol fishing pole and head down the the pond to find some of the best fish of the decade. SKELLETONS DROP DIAMONDS!!! skelletons now drop diamonds a 1 in 1456 chance a allthough not profitable to kill skelletons for diamonds you might just get one if you try.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jon's Diary", "LukeSkyFoker", "I'm all alone in the sewer. My friend is missing. All that is left is his wedding ring.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jordan's Enchanting Book", "JoeqMafia", "Elgahnt fas bor shactlin----- Dragon spell \n Mentula fas verpa------ Penis Enlarger \n Amoveo pestis de vita animus-------- Curse Removal \n Spiritus medium novus initiu------ give life", ""),
        StaticBook("Jornal", "iohnoh", "3rd night. I finaly found some people. Im joining their guild. I had to start over again because some strange bug. Iohnoh out \n Damn me I lost them :( Im alone again. \n 4th night. Getthing really lonely and hungry. I have walked for days and havent found anyt hing . I need to find some group and join them or im going to die alone. . . I currently have 115.0 Minas and i need more to buy land and stay alive. \n I ended up in strange city where i found elves. I traded this book for 2 meat because im really hungry and weak. I shall end my diary here. Good luck. \n Iohnoh out... \n Well i got my book back because the elve was libraryan and i get payd for writing and im finaly getting closer to my dream of owning land in our main city. \n its day 5 and im ready to head out into wilderness. I hope i wont die again. Currently im in Psychologist_Banok_Gary's home and just got payd. 1 step closer to my land \n I have to admit that those elves are very helpful and some houses have damn nice view \n Iohnoh out. 7th night., \n I finaly started my career as writer. I like it because  it pays itself out. \n 2nd day in mines. Im on the quest of iron and diamonds. Hopefully i will get alot so i will get good payment for this nervwracking job. i dont know if its day or night i just mine and mine and mine. Im lost. \n Day something. I have lost track of my time. Well the good news is i got out from there. Bad news is i only got 20 iron and 64+ cloal. Public mines are too clean and big. I think i have to start going into caves again. I dont want to but i need to. Job is job and aslong it gives me cash i have to do it. my hopes of getting back into central is hight. I found stragne piece of map from caves. But i cant read it. Its in acient language and i dont know it. Well Im going to end it here. I have to find other ways getting iron and diamonds. \n Iohnoh out. \n Day something 2. I made myself hole hight enought i can make mine downstairs. I got some coal and flint from it. Now i have 16 arroes and 1 bow. Also got alot meat too. I wont suffer in hunger anymore. thank you pigs and spiders for this delicious meat. Tomorrow im going for hunt of more wood and maybe raid some houses in wilderness. \n Iohnoh out. \n Note to myself. Do not jump off the walls if you see something interesting you may not get back up or you need to walk alot to get back. \n Day something 3 . * whole page is painted red by blood * \n They got me. Creepers found out where i live. I must run or I ... \n I hear banging on my door. Must hurry. AAH they are in. I must find other way out from here. They are getting too close. \n Well i got away from them for now. And i started working as slave. Well if i want to get my business up i need some money. Best way earning it is with slavejobs, Cutting trees, getting feather, getting dirt... exc... \n I have skiped some days from writing. Nothink interesting has happened. Ah yea i sold 1 stacks of trees for 120Minas and im happy about it. i made my bunker underground and those spider noises are annoying. Sun rises and then they are dead. I must go and fine more dark trees and collect them for payment. \n ** I made mistake. Find not fine. ** \n Iohnoh out. \n My tream is to go AlKhazar", ""),
        StaticBook("Joshua Highblade", "Groobs03", "After countless hours, I have made it back to Torn Hope. Unforunetley it is barren. I left coal in exchange for the small bit of wheat I could farm. These are grim times when not a single Wolverine was left to guard the city. I blame myself for this. Joshua Highblade, Former Commanderr", ""),
        StaticBook("Josiah", "Groobs03", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Josiah's Journal", "JoeqMafia", "Joma, 6th of The Amber Cold 1306 Returning from the Cloud Temple. Austin met a newcomer. His name is Rocko, and he's a Orc. This suprised me since Austin \"used\" to hate Orcs. Considering the fact that his Father was killed by one. On another note, Earlier today Austin and I were in Oren purchasing gear when I heard a loud chanting in the nearby tavern. I peeked my head through the door to see a group of drunkies around a man who appeared to be chugging down ale. When he finished I saw that it was the Wandering Wizard himself! I decided to join in without Austin's approval and got wasted. I was more drunk than I was on my 14th birthday. But as everyone poured out of the tavern. A man confronted the Wizard. The man wore a purple cloak of some kind. He threatened to kill the Wizard but the Wizard poofed away. The man was angered. He commanded his men that were amongst the crowd to kill the civillians. We scattered around not knowing who sided with the purple cloaked man. I was almost killed when a dwarf went to strike me with his battle axe. I used my diamond sword to deflect it but he managed to pull the sword out of my hands. I fell to the floor and he came up over me with my sword over my head. He began to launch it into my face when Austin came behind him and shoved the short Dwarf to the ground. We ran away from the Massacre alive in one peice.   Itnan, 30th of Snows Maiden 1307 New Terriko is suffering from a major Black Magic storm. The majority of my blacksmith lies in ruins. The Ark towers have been reduced to a pile of debris. Citizens of New Terriko remember the desperate days of the original Terriko. Everyone is working together to rebuild our small cozy town. We are all asking one question. Why us? Why does this happen to us again. Sabet, 7th of Malins Welcome,1307 I technically nominated Austin as the new Mayor due to Karnin's dissapearence. He is very determined to rebuild. But Orgri for some reason says the land is dangerous and says we should rebuild erything in the suburbs. Austin is rebuilding the town as we speak as I lay in bed with Lag. Still studying this disease I am not sure what the possible cause of it could be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Josiah's Journal The Second Start", "JoeqMafia", "i hav resently picked up riting agen. i havent gotten usd to it yet. i wanted to rite about wats been hapening to me resently. to start off. im josiah. i lost my memory. we dont no how but it hapened. after several months i have begun to remembar stuf. psiop gave me my old jurnal wich helpd out very litle becus most of the pages were riped. more resently i hav ran for mayor. i am winning. but if peple new i couldnt right they would nevr have voted for me.    Day Two I Have Lernd too Capitalizd My Werds", ""),
        StaticBook("Josiah's Mysterious Notebook", "JoeqMafia", "It has been 1 week since the battle at Aegis. Ever since then I have been having these feelings. I have decided to write down my feelings to try to flush it out. Psiop says I used to write alot before my memory was wiped. I guess it was soothing. I keep on getting these visions of a party. And I am there but only as a baby. This vision is beutiful. But it slowly molds into the event at the Cloud Temple. The dancers turn into soldiers burning alive in the fire, the women begin to scream, the food turns into blood and guts that stains the grass, and the grass is a bloody rock. That burns your feet to a crisp. The baby version of me transforms into a man, a shady man. He is wearing a hood. He is killing those around him. He is powerful and strong,. He wields the strongest of swords. But he kills all in his way. He slashes women in the face, and impales the soldiers. He walks up to me and I am afraid. Then I see. This hooded man is me. I pull down my hood and so does the man in front of me. We are the same person. His face is ugly and covered with blood. He has power and he get's what he wants, I can tell it pulses off of his body , like an magical force is around him. Then the vision ends. \n 1 1/2 weeks after the battle \n I am cold and tired all the time. I try to go out and talk to my friends but I cannot. I feel like I am a failure. I have nver won and never will. I feel powerless and depressed. The visions are coming on an hourly basis. Every time I am frighten. Knowing that they will come again. I almost want to stop them by doing the one thing I can do. Suicide. It will be quick. Just one slice with the sword. But I cannot. I want to be strong. I want to be powerful. I thirst for a kill, and I am hungry for death. \n 2 weeks \n I feel better, and satisfied. I captured a pig. He oinked and squealed and tried to escape me. I felt powerful. I felt significant. But instead of killing it I tied it up to the wall and took the utensils from my diner and stuck it into its stomach. It tried to free it self, but it could not. I laughed at it. I felt great and I need more. The torturing is what I always needed. The times I was tortured by those men. The lashed at me. I didn't know why. Now I do. \n 3 weeks \n People are noticing the absences of pigs and me. The people need me but when I try to help others it pains me. I feel like a tumor in my head is stopping me from doing what I do best. \n *the rest of the pages are torn out and covered with blood.", ""),
        StaticBook("Josiah's Notebook", "JoeqMafia", "Sugar+water= Speed Potion ;; Spider Eye+water= Poison \n Blaze dust+water= Strength Potion", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Kr4den", "ENTRY ONE-It's been far too long and I've still only a home with the Orcs. I haven't seen my Legio brothers in days, and I fear I'm going to have to do this on my own. \nENTRY TWO-I've still not found a home. It is night and I found some sort of guildhouse or castle. Their base of operations is \"The Cathedral of the Damned.: I think I shall make my home not too far from here. There's a valley nearby with no homes in sight, but I still fear bandits , having no way to protect my belongings. \nENTRY THREE- Thank the Gods!  Traveling a little further I found not only a man's home,  but a large chasm in the ground.  I shall explore and document my results. I am lucky to have not fallen in as I happened by it. \nENTRY FOUR-  Nearing the Chasm's edge, I feared falling to my death. I did not enter, and used the power of my soulstone to go back to the human kingdom. I'll have to slay some beasts and try to  purchase a home somewhere . . . Perhaps even continue living with the Legio. . . given they take me back. \nENTRY FIVE-I am scared.  I've taken it upon myself to find out what these hooded men are.  I've been seeing them everywhere, and they're all short with me or don't speak at all. First that damned crazy preacher screaming about undead, then this? I fear something's wrong.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "iohnoh", "This is my 2nd night in here. Im getting hungry. Need food FAST! Tomorrow im going for hunt of food. I hope to find some farms and homes to raid. \n Iohnoh out", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Wolfie_Seekar", "It is late now, I have gotten A job n winterfell, As a farmer. I like the humans here. They are nice. Thy want me to build a Piggi farm. Me no know how, that is somethng I will have ta study. Open up", ""),
        StaticBook("journal", "kaicz", "DAY 1: Today I start my adventures I have created this journal to share my adventures with those around me . I plan on making a house where I can hunt to raise minas to purchase a home later in life. once i have found a nice plot of land i will start to build. Day 2: I have set of on my adventure earlier today and hope to find a plot of land later toda y. I plan on spending the night in the Whisper Isles. during the night I was encountered  a group pf thiefs. they wanted all my minas buy I ran away as fast as i could back to the tmple. Day:3 I'm now resting in the dwarven town of Kal'Uragaun and plan to set out at dawn. Day:4 I have found where I will build my home. I have started construction and plan on finishing it towarow. Day:5 I have been killing zombie pig men for minas and have about a quarter of what i need. Day:6 I thought i had enough money so I returened back to Laurelin only to learn i need much more. I have stared my journey back to my home although I forget where it was built. I have begin retracing my steps and im starting to remeber where it was. Day: I'm very close to my house and i'm starting to see familiar landscapes. Alas  I found my humble home and have allready started to hunt monseters and grow sugar cane. Day: 8 I have returned back to Laurelin and plan on staying for a while. I asked a villager today if they new any ways to earn good minas. They replied with \" I can give you s job\". after talking to them a while about it and asking them questions I came to a conclusion thatt it was a illegal job so I turned it down. i wanted to visit the whisper isles but I was attacked by monsters . A man was kind enough to give me some soup and bread to  restore me back to health. i have heard of a town know as Alstion town where I am adventuring to I have arrived in Astion town and have met the town owner and houses are muh cheaper here thL n Laureline. Day:8 The undead live very close to Astion town and we have been on high alert. Also I now have enough money for a home. Day:9 we are stil under alert but I am wating for a house to open up for sale. I have come back from a small journey to find Astion town in ruins! I have heard it was caused by the undead and they plan on rebuilding. i still plan on living here but my thought about its safety have lowered.  Day:11 its been a while and astion town has been almost rebuilt.  Day: 12 Once again i have comback from a voyage in to the forest but returned only to find Astion town completely wipped out! Day 13: I have reunited with old friends Dayereth and Beorn. they are alowing me to sta with them but Day: 14 Today we have started our adventure Dayereth and I have began and will be joined by Beorn soon. We have just arived at the towers Aemon and Daemon . Dayereth has said that there is a maze here and we atmted to coplete it but backed out. Day:15 We have come to the town of Kal'Uraguan which i remebered from earlier  journey's.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "trotski24", "Joined UAC I have contructed a nice secret mine.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "sconn", "It was a crowded day in the Al'khazar marketplace. I was looking at the new building, when a man walked up to me. He said: Do you know of a book called Sconn's philosophy. i froze. I knew what the man was looking for. And i knew that he knows about my dark past. I acted like i dont know what he was looking for. But he wouldnt give up. Then he told me that he will pay 200 minas if i give him the original copy. I was desperat for money. I had to accept I told him i will be right back with the book. I ran home. I immedietly threw over the bed and took the book from the secret bookshelf. When i came back i saw the man talking to the king. He asked him if he could meet someone called the whisperer. I started to suspect him. When they stopped talking he took me to his shop. I gave him my book and he gave my his money. I was a little afraid that he will give it to the guards. But the Sconn that did those things is gone. Now only the new Sconn remains. The old Sconn died when he set himself on fire. But that experience is in another book. A book that i have hidden and is more important to me than life itself. For it describes the moment when i lost my insanity. later that day i met an archmage I have seen him alot in Al'khazar. I asked how to join the mages guild. He told me that i have to keep a journal. And so i started wrritting. Later this day i saw some people gambling in the city I joined them in there game. I was loosing a lot of money. I keept loosing but i couldnt stop. It is a good thing a zombie pigmen stopped me gambling. He badly injured a lot of people and we were took to the monastery to heal. one of us lost diamond armour and plenty of golden hoes. when we came back there was a long fight onwho took the stuff. Eventuly he got all of his stuff back. I must have lost at least 100 minas in the gambling. Today i noticed a lack of guards in the city. The only people guarding is the new captain and his wife. I also noticed that there is a inn just under my house. I am scared that someone might hear my footsteps, or me closing the door. my house has plenty of valuables so I must keep it a secret. I listen to their conversations every day. They are just normal people. THESE NEXT COUPLE OF PAGES DESCRIBE MY SEARCH FOR CATARIS'S JOURNAL. I was walkin on th bridge betwenn Kal'alras and Winterfell. That is when i noticed a body on the frozen lake. I jumped from the bridge and ran to the body. I searched the body for clues of death. All i could find was arrows sicking from the ground. The dead man had a book. The name of it was rumors. It described forgoten knowledge, and an Archmages journal. The book said that the treasures lie on the bottom of the lake near Winterfell. I immediatly started search the bottom of the lake for signs of this treasure I found nothing. Then i decided to look in the other lakes. I could only find water and ice. My search brought me to a small mansion. I stayed there for the night. When i awoke i went back to my search. In the middle of the day i found a great tower in the middle of nowhere. I wanted to check if there is anyone there. But the tower was locked with iron blocks. At that point I was completely lost. I had soulstoned out of that place. But my search is not over. Today I decided to go scout the undead base. I traveledmany days and nights. Luckely there was no one there and the gates were open. I sneaked in the main tower. I observed what they could see. I tried to mark a position where the attackers could hide. The tower seemed to have a good view of ewerything. Then I spotted a huge mine. The undead seemed to have rooms there. When i wandered in the mines I spotted a halway with rooms that had teryfiying names. One was called the drowner, the other the chrusher, there was the burner and many more. The names told me exactly what they were made for. But I had to test them. The drowner is a room with pistons that unleash water that completely fills the room. The burner is just a big furnace that lights the floors on fire. The chrusher was a room with pistons on the side, which crush you into the naxt wall. There was a room which floors can dissaper, and it throws into the dephts. At that moment i heard lightning. I knew that the undead were here. I looked at the rooms again and said to miself that I cannot be caught. I decided to sneak up on the undead and kill them. I ran outside but the undead were nowhere to be seen. it was a bright day but lightning striked outside the fortress. I ran as fast as I could knowing that I am a sitting duck if they see me. I ignored all of the monstrosities that were chasing me. When I finaly came to snowyfields I rested and continued my journey to Al'khazar. When i arrived in Al'khazar i heard news of a party i Haven. I immedietly emptied my bag and headed to the kings road. On the kings road I meet to other humans. They were also heading to the party. When we arrived we wnt to the inn. There a man showed us to the lower part of the inn where the party was hosted. We drank a lot. The ascended had to empty out all of Haven of its ale. When most of us begin to sober there were the questions. If we anwsered correctly we would get diamonds. I caught 2 diamonds when the questions were anwsered. After that came the dangerous part. If we would anwser wrong there would be arrows firerd from dispensers. Everyone was drunk so there were alot of arrows sticking from the wall. Soner or later we anwsered all of the questions. Then came the games part. everybody was locked out of the main hall, while the ascended preparred mazes for us. On the end of each maze were 4 diamonds. There were water mazes, piston mazes and just plain mazes. I got 4 more diamonds. after that the party moved to the southern gate. I didnt stay too long. I then soulstoned out to Al'khazar. There i sold my diamonds. With the money I got I rented a room in building. I moved all of my belongings from my inn. I setlled in and began to re-decorate. When I finished I was contacted with old friends from the time when i was evil. I will not reveal there names even in this journal. They still tought that I was evil. I didnt explain to them that I have turned to the right side. I just left them. I hope I will not have contact with those evil people. I tried to reveal their names to the guards but I could not. Tonight I awoke refreshed and rested. I feel a great power growing within me. Then i heard lightning. My great morning was immedietly destroyed. More thunder stroke. I stumble out off my bed. I get dressed. I grabed my armour and weapons. When I was prepared I ran outside to see what has happened. The thunder stopped. A few hours later i hear news that the king is dead. It was a reliefe when i saw the king in person and realised that they lied. After that I head out to Winterfell. I always wanted to see the great prison tower in person. Sadly the doors were locked. I tried to go around but there was no way. after some time I see a cave. I explored it and mined some minerals. I continued throw the cave. Suddenly i found miself exiting from an unknown entrance. It was getting dark fast. I had no items and no weapons. I ran to tha nearest house. I entered and stayed there for the night. soon I left the home. I was lost for a little while but soon i found my way back to civilization. Today I have discovered my houses history. I have searched In the libraries for years now. And I think that I have finnaliy found my history. The only thing I know is that my mother worked in a brothel. And my father ran away when I was born. My fathers name was Alashar Hawkwind. He had no wife and no money. My family was always poor. It was not a noble house but a house obsessed with magic. They used to have a house in Al'khazar. My father used up all of his money in the search for magic. I read books he had wrriten about his experiments. All of them were a faliure. He spent his last days wandering around brothels spending all of the money he had left. I wonder how many other brothers my father made me when he was on his trip throw the brothels of Aegis. I have mistaken myself. I am not from the family Hawkwind. A new district has been built today. The houses are still under counstruction, but not for long. They are only 1500 minas. The houses are fairly big. I will buy one when lord thunder finishes them. I will be glad to rid misellf of my current tiny apartment. I finnaly bought the house. Originaly it had 2 stories but i added another one. One floor is the size of my appartment. I still need to tell the owner that i will be leaving my appartment. Later that day i had a visit. It was a friend from when i was still evil. I couldnt afford anyone seaing him. I told him to crouch and whisper to me. An annoying orc almost found out about him. It was a good thing I had an iron door locked. I told my friend that i will meet him in the sewers. I will try to explain that i turned to the right side. I tried many times to tell the guards about him. But i just couldnt do it. I have decide that i will lock the entrance to my house with cobble. That way no orc will bother me. I bought another house that is right next to my house. I connected both of them. Now I have more room than i need.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "knight4239", "8/10/11 Got a job as a Guard at the Mountain Dwarf City Captains Log SHITS GOING DOWN PENIS", ""),
        StaticBook("journal", "KnightPuppy", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "cradleofphilth", "The name is Thrim, Thrim Stonejaw. Where do I start? Well I've been travelling for a long time now, probably over two years.  I'm not going to go into much detail about that, apart from this small part.. The only elf I've met with hospitality such as his. I was badly injured from a small war outside a village, my battleaxe was damaged and my shield was missing. The elf came out of nowhere, holding only a sword. Close inspection led me to believe the sword was made of gold. The elf defeated several orcs advancing towards me, with a single blow. He offered me food, shelter and friendship. After several months of recovering, and helping him with what I could I decided to leave. I cannot remember his name, I feel so bad about that. So after many more months of travelling, I came across a few helpful people. They directed me to a town called 'Greenshire' and well...I'm still here today.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "mattr41018", "Off on a trip to oren . I am with my 2 good friends Goleth and Lance , Lance doesnt talk much, but he is good in a fight. Goleth isnt the best fighter, but loves talking. I believe myself to be a mixture of both . We entered Kal Ugrauan, the dwarven city, and the large statues seamed to be following me . Entered inner Kal Ugrauan, It is amazing. The palace, is amazing, Huge lava moat, Giant castle, all under ground. It is insane. The world of Aegis is most Amazing The view from the top of the palace is beutiful, and full of stone. 8/21 with friends gone, i am all that remains here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Zefmc", "we found a valley far from civilisation Well Froar found it I followed and then came Tom Friar has had to be gone for a while Left advice for setting up a town so We built A town square a town hall a barracks houses a lot \n Not bad for my first try at writing still need to learn grammer", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Lanthorn", "I've met an orc called Ur'garosh today, while wandering around like usually. He asked me if he could show me his village, i was looking for a place to call home so i followed When i asked him howmuch a house costs, he said it was about 800Minas. Unfortunately i didnt have that much Minas at the time. But he said i could pay off half of the payment by doing stuff for the village, he said he was working on a church that worshipped an old god he praised, I had some stuff in my old hidden chest on 'The' Island. So i told him i'd get it. When i returned with the Wood and Cobble i had collected over the years he simply responded with something along the lines of ''Woah, that should be more than enough!' He also said that if i'd help him build the Church somewhat 75% of my debt would be payed. I am currently helping him build the main room for the Church. Day 2: We did the Walls and the Ceiling of the Main room today, it's looking good! Day 3 - 6: We started building on a tunnel in a lake today, took a few days and half way trough the Orc was getting very tired. I understood why he had to sleep, he's an old orc. I have finished the tunnel, just getting the water out is another thing. The Fifth day while i was walking around in town a guard stopped me and asked me why i had a bounty on my head. I explained to him it was when i was in the guard myself and was suspected for theft and murder. Turned out it wasnt me after all. The bounty of 27Minas sticked around for some reason though. Day 4: There's something strange in the air today. They say a portal opened to the north of here. I should check it out. Day 6: I heard a noise outside this night, a scream. When i looked outside all i saw was some dark figure leaning over a person. It looked like they were fighting. Just one thing that really bothered me. One of them was missing his arms. I must've been imagining things. I am currently looking for that Portal. Day 7: I looked at the Goblin's Inn today. It's abandoned. The night's are really dangerous so i'm staying here for the night. Too bad this place fell apart. It was a nice Inn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "MrJakKiD", "I met a nice fellow today.. he offered me a home", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "halt99", "Journal Entry 1 - I have finally made it to Al'Khazar. I am staying at Van Rourke's Inn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Austinpowers999", "Tolta, 31st of The First Seed, 1318 \n Today I continued training my swordsmanship and made a quick travel to Alkhazar to grab some goods . I am very happy with my new home it is quite nice also as a favour for Lothiriel I am Protectecting an elf named Sadi from a Dark Elf named Thork who is possesed or something Being an orc is hard considering that everywhere I go someone always acuses us of things we never di d ... Itnan, 9th of the Suns Smile \n Today there was dueling happening at the new arena. Both of my dogs were killed in and when I faced Mogroka; he cheated afriad to lose honour to a grunt like me I will probably leave krugmar becuase of his arrogance.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "redbaron", "\n Ahad, 8th of The Deep cold, 1320 \n Im here in dawns bakery, drinking a mug of ale looking at these travelers.  Some old, some young.  All very loud, its all the same people here when i came, like the oren guard huron, will, and sadi, I come here and sell my goods that i hunt, spending my time here is nice besides the noise . \n Ahad, 22nd of snows maiden, 1320 \n The snow falls melting on my skin.  The birds are gone and im sitting beside my fire. I look out my window and I see the men and women walking on the docks. I'm thinking to myself how nice it must be for all of them. To not have to plow a field so i may raise a living.  The golden harvest has treated me well though so i shall not complain. \n Joma, 27th of The Grand Harvest, 1321 \n Back in Dawns Bakery, the smell of the place is what drives me here, the fresh bread, the cakes, everything. She goes down stairs and when she opens the door to where she cooks, the smells are grand. The rain still poors outside, so back in the bakery to let me think.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "leka213", "( I did) Sept 30. Today, I bought me and Zoe and diamond sword, it was pretty expensive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "GoldPlaya11", "Hi I am Aragonis Today I saw my house and its totally ruined and my old house has been stealed from me by ther by the mayor. And because of that I am very angry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "lotteje13", "Test Subject: Miss von Rosea Race: High Elf Gender: Female Age: 100+ at what we believe Test's: We will try to recreate one of the lost powers of the elves this is not sure if we are able to... (some blood covers the words that where writen) Day 1: we gave her some potions and we used some spell of miss Rosea we are not sure what this will do yet but the life in her eyes do have left... day 2: her body is giving some odd sign's not sure of what is happening to her... (lots of pages where torn out of the book! and some pages where covered with blood) Day 148: The signs are getting worse and she is showing a diffrent character... some have seen red eyes on her we have the feeling that she created a alter ego... (pages where filled with blood and torn pages...) Day ...: last one.... curse.... alive.... last time!... wings?... demon... angel?....last wor (pages is full of blood and faded words the last word's seems like nothing...)", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Jarhead90", "Day1 Its been 4 years since my village was destroied. On my quest to find the Undead Ive found many settlements. But none was how I wanted to live. I built this house for myself. And ONLY myself. Bringing someone allong is too dangerous. Day2 Ive met a great warrior today he has decided to train me. Ive killed 13 zombies. So far I think I shall live here until I get found upon by Orcs. ;; ;; ;; Day3 After my run in with the undead I am starting to write books it seems quite enough. I could use a break. \n Day 4 I have found a man named Jason. Him and I decided to start a village together. Hopefully he's not a theif if i see him steal I will kill him. \n Day 5 Jason has returned. But with no luck seling wood. Tomarrow I will travel and sell items Hopfully I make a profit. \n Day 8 Yesterday I met a gaurdn in Aralas I helped him kill a few fiends. Then I met to elfs who was building a shop they needed wool so i traded with them. Elfs seem to be really quite and nice creatures. He gave me some redstone which I used to make a map finaally I have a map! Thank god I hope Jason returns soon though. I miss company. \n Day 10 Yesterday I went to Alalas and bought diamond. I have made the most powerful weapon ever! I am so happy. Hopfully It dont break fast.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Quinton16", "Today we saw strange lightning from across the lake. We went to investigate only having just missed the attack on Lady Dawn's house. I went to investiagte more to find a destroyed town . worried I returned home. There was more lightning and we hid in the bunker until it passed. Several days later I visited Talem's house. There was writing all over the walls they refered to a \"us\". This worries me, there are strange things afoot and I want to get to the bottom of it . I'm journeying out to the sea... An abandoned port city? This is odd. I seem to have stumbled across some sort of mercenary compound. A sign reads \"More will come if you don't disband\", odd. It is land of a kindom called \"Tinra\" the independent kingdom. At the entrence to the town a sign reads \"The Energy from the ground is slowly being taken, Decaying please remove all of your items within the next week. If YOU DON'T LEAVE WITH YOUR ITEMS THEY WILL BE DESTROYED!\". The undead have taken the city? The place is built primarly of sandstone, perhaps an orc city? The streets have a red glow on them. Is this the energy being drained? I've arived at a place called Pirate Cove. I've decided it's best to head back. I've ended up back at Lady Dawn and Hempshine's home. A thief went through town and stole valueables from all of us. Chanol fell into some tunnel system. Telinir knew everything about them. Suspicious much? I followed the tunnels more, it seems they end up in Lab 08, all the more suspicious.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Busenki", "Hello! I am Terrowin, a ranger, a hunter and an adventurer. I work for a company that helps new players to get started in the world of Aegis. Today, I sneaked into the warden's fort, into the forbbiden area with my firend and co-worker Amras. He was once a Warden, but was kicked out. We \"visited\" them and we almost got caught trespassing. It is Ahad, The 29 of Malins Welcome. Today I did some patroling for the rangers on the King's road. There was no trouble on the road, which is a blessing, since these are dark times. Elves, dwarves humand and orcs fight amongst eachother and some even serve Iblees!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "monkmonktoodle", "It has been 5 whole days. No food only some water. The spiders have made it impossible for me to leave the church. I do not know if I will survi........", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "123devmo321", "help 4", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Fenodyree", "Tolta, 25th of Malins - 1341: \n Walked the length of the kings road, nothing else happened. \n \n Tolta, 26th of Malins - 1341: \n", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_13(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Journal", "Royced", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Sykora87", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "ReaperT", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #1", "DrZig", "Today Balin started to construct the barracks!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #1", "TheWoWMasta", "Kamees, 19th of The First Seed. \n Waiting at the Temple of Aegis for my apprentice, Samuel. \n Met a man looking for work. Will continue search for resources. \n \n  Joma, 20th of The First Seed. \n Met up with Samuel today, waiting for Janna to meet with us at the warden HQ. \n \n \n \n \n Joma, 27th of The First Seed. \n We are at the Warden's Base. Janna has joined us and we are looking for a place to build. We have exited the Warden's Base and are now heading South-West. \n \n Itnan, 30th of The First Seed. Janna and myself are in the woods. Janna has resorted to mining. I am woodcutting. We have lost my apprentice, strangely. We don't know where he is. I am leaving my Journal in the chest for awhile. \n \n Irba, 11th of The Second Seed. \n I have stumbled upon a sewer city underneath Al'Khazar! One of the entrances is in the Market District sewer system. I will continue exploring until I find something.. \n  Irba, 25th of The Second Seed. \n Gathered many redwood logs today, such a heavy load on my pack. I think there are about 200 or so logs in my cart! Still looking for a place to sell all my goods, however. \n  \n Irba, 32nd of The Second Seed. \n Done nothing all day. Useless guard duty. Meeting up with Jena in Laurelin. We have stumbled upon some strange markings on the top of a mountain. We will now look for a place to build! \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal - Lord Nairog Stark", "NairOG", "\nThe scout reports about the storm are rather disturbing. He told me that it is forming north of Winterfell but is in constant move. At first I tought cold got to him but when I saw his eyes it was clear that what he saw was there, lurking in our world. After scout, Axelgor, rested he took haste and went to Cloud Temple of Aegis. God clear his mind! I must admit, I was scared, I did not know what will we go against. How to prepare for the unknown? How to prepare!? \nToday I invited Saint Daniel for a meal and told him everything. We had a long talk and decided that I should continue constructing outposts on the  border. Saint Daniel will talk with the military. \nThis may be me just paranoid but the blizzards have become more frequent. \nAxelgor is still not back from the Temple, I hope he is alright. \nI am going to go look for Axelgor. He has been gone for a week. I will go to Al'Khazar and follow the King's road to Temple.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal - Nycthel", "nevermint", "I can hear spiders outside my house I was milking a cow.. What I don't understand is that I'm drunk all of a sudden. I am soooo drunk right now.. I can barely write... bbuauughhh  .... I keep dropping my pen. jasodjasdioasdn  alcoholsdfmfodfhpoisoningwieods.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1", "jkkid", "Creeper's drops iron gun powder minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1", "cgw123", "This book is in a bookshelf", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1 (Lethodus)", "IcyHot", "Kamees, 19th oTDC, 1331: I have finally arrived in Alkhazar", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 2", "aheath4", "The Caravan members: Wrath greed Envy eldar Dijin", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 216", "runawayguy", "Today was a hard day. I just have returned from the citadel with some books given to me; I hope Shoi enjoys the selection. After furnishing the house I've been working on for the past 47 days, I think it is finally complete. It truly looks amazing.. I hope Shoi loves the house.. Just as I love her. I have tried everything to falter her heart away from Ralith.. But with no avail. The days I spent with her.. Standing up to the Earth Demon... The poem I wrote... And finally her Dream House. Everyone should have a chance to allow their dreams to come true. I'm glad Shoi could experience that feeling and that's all I will ask for: Her happiness. I've decided to take a journey. I don't know when I will return..Or even if I will return. But it probably won't be soon. I don't know what I will be searching for. But this journal will be placed along side the other 215 journals I have written. I am Zephyr, and this might be the last journal I compile.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 230", "runawayguy", "This is my 230th journal. It sure has been a while since I wrote one of these, and there is so much to be said. I think I will make this more of a journal to recap all that has happened.. With insight into the future... Ever since my parents were killed and I was raised by a group of bandits, my life has been a been nothing but trouble. With my encounters... Almost become undead.. I feel as if Aeriel has been watching over me from the first day I was born.. I know she is the one that has kept me alive all these years, until she handed me to Sage Arcadius.. The one that pulled me back from the darkness and showed me the light... That day changed my life. I became a new warrior of Aegis. Aeriel must have been so proud.. From the day I was born, to when I recieved my Ascended scroll, to the day the Sages were taken back by Aeriel.. My life has been a very long and twisting path, never knowing where I'll end up next. I've also noticed that I am rarely happy.. All this changed a few weeks ago when I met Chrisdena, or should I say Chrissy. I fell in love with her instantly, almost as if it was meant to be.. No, not almost. It WAS meant to be. We were on the followers of Aeriel encampments.. Where we finally were alone, watching the sunrise together. That was the moment I proposed, and she accepted. We've bought a house in Alras provided by Syrio...And we'll be living happily in that home. My mood has completely changed. I'm enjoying life more than ever alongside Chrisdena.. Which brings me to the insight into the future.. Before I fall asleep everyday, I pray to Aeriel, to thank her for all she's done for me. In my dream..I was confronted by a white figure made of only light. I don't know if it was truly Aeriel, but she spoke of a great war ahead. She told me that one day.. After the war that will decide the fate of Aegis.. I...I will have to sacrifice my life, for the life of Chrisdena...and...and our child. She told me not to worry, because I will be ready to step off this world and join her and the other Sages. She told me that it wouldn't be soon, and that I'll be able to live a full life with the one I love. I am prepared to make this sacrifice, whenever it may be, because I know Chrisdena will realize that I'm doing this for her, and our future child. She will make an excellent mother one day. I am Zeph, and this journal will be placed alongside the other 228 unseen journals. Bless you Aeriel..Bless you.", ""),
        StaticBook("journal exploration", "jesk200", "day 3 nailena died, but came back now resting it s called help day 4 going on a new trip", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal For (RL) Hours", "connorr1", "Sunday 11:00: Bored Dawn and Hemp arent here and im talking to Ivrae and Ninja. 12:00 Still bored watching Ivrae and Ninja build onto  the new theater.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Blacksmith", "Thebadjazz", "Irba, 4th of the Second Seed, 1310 \n \nIt has been but two years since I was born into this world at the Cloud Temple of Aegis, and already I've accumulated a large sum of Minas. \nI credit most of my success to my father, who died long ago at the hands of the Undead. He has tought me to be strong and to rely on myself, for I am alone in the vast  stretches of Aegis, save for my brother, Zelkk, my only surviving family member. \nBut farewell for now, Journal, I'm off to the Wilds to find a place to  settle down. \n \nSabet, 21st of The Second Seed, 1310 \n \nJournal, the sun is setting, and I fear for my life. I've quickly taken shelter on an abandoned scaffold in The Wild. I can hear the undead emerging from  their underground shelters beneath me... \nI have not yet found a suitable place to set up a settlement in The Wild. If I do not find a suitable location soon, I will need to return to Al'Khazar to restock on supplies. \n Ahad, 22nd of The Second Seed, 1310 \n \nJournal, I've found an old crypt just beneath the surface of Aegis. It's infested with the twisted shapes of giant spiders... I'll have to get my hands dirty if I want to explore further... \n \nJournal! I've found a chest within the recesses of the crypt and much valuable moss! They will fetch a good price when I make a trip back to the city. What fortune! Hopefully things hold up for me! \n \nItnan, 23rd of The Second Seed, 1310 \n \nI've found a suitable place to construct a nice home. Away from the city and general population. There's no need to worry about thieves or burglars here, and I'm far away from the grasp of the King Edmund, not that he's oppressive, but it is nice to be completely free.  Anyway, journal, this location is perfectly suited for a small settlent.  It's very close to the shore, there's plenty of flat land and trees, and there's a mountain range not far North of here to mine from. \nAt any rate, it's getting dark so I'll take shelter in a nearby cave... \n \nThe cave was not as secure as I had originally hoped. There seems to have been a small nest of zombies. I managed to slay the beasts, but I am weak. One of the zombies dropped a map... I'll examine it tomorrow, Journal, I am tired. \n \nTolta 24th of The Second Seed, 1310 \n \nUpon further inspection of the map from the zombies last night, I found that the geographical detail of the map was extremely specific, but there are no labels and I cannot for the life of me figure out what portion of the countryside that this map describes. Oh well... Perhaps I'll figure it out later, Journal... \n \nSome work must be done on the location I originally found. While most of the land was indeed flat, some portions were not as flat as I had initially thought. I'll have to flatten it out. It may be a while until I am done, Journal, so farewell until then. \n \nJoma, 34th of The Second Seed, 1310 \n \nJournal, it has been a while since I've written, and I'd like to jot down a few updates. I've cleared most of the trees and wild grass, and I've also flattened most of the land, but I've formed a good portion of the hills into a short acropolis, which will one day hold the noble's houses.  Also I've noticed a tall plateau, which may prove to be an excellent spot for the keep, if it proves defendable. \n \nAhad, 1st of The Grand Harvest, 1310 \n \nAh, it is the beginning of The Grand Harvest. There will be no harvest for me... Not since I was a young boy, merely the tender age of 7. \nThis month is always one of sadness for me, ever since my family was killed... I miss them dearly, and I slaughter the undead in their name, but I cannot forget my remaining family, Zelkk. I will watch over him and defend him with all my strength.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Coward, Volume ??", "TehLulu", "As I ran down the King's Road towards Kal'Urguan, Mayctor always at my heels, that devilish cackle of his ringing through the air, I began to wonder to myself... Where, or when, exactly, had I gone wrong? I realized it was a moot question at that point...I had bigger problems to worry about. Namely, the High Guardian, who I feared was drawing ever closer. But now that I think upon it, I realize it is quite obvious. I relied too much on others, and the assistance they gave. I should have worked for myself, done all of my research myself. I should not have involved innocents, like Prince Toren, or Atles...whom I can only hope is safe, after disobeying orders to assist me... But I am ahead of myself. I suppose I should start at the beginning. \n I believe I had mentioned Mayctor in my last journal entry, though I have lost count of the volumes and being away from Laurelin, am unable to check the numbers. But I will assume I have mentioned him, my suspicions about him, and the whirlwind of evil which seems to have engulfed the Elves of Laurelin. I will assume that I had also mentioned the Dark Brotherhood and some of their possible members. Now, I will mention the new threat that has emerged...the Undead. I firmly believe, now more than ever, that Mayctor had something to do with them... That the Brotherhood at least works alongside them, if not for them. I had just finished a meeting with the  Pathfinders, along with other allies of mine, including Dalejin. Dalejin had left back to Oren with the news I had given him, of Mayctor's involvement in the scheme to kidnap the Queen. I believe he reached the capital in time, right as there were shrieks of horror from the North which we in Laurelin did not hear word of until a messenger came a bit later. As soon as we had heard it though, we left. I and a number of the Pathfinders, including Atles, headed North. Unfortunately, in my condition...I did not reach Winterfell, or Alstion. I am ashamed of this fact. I nearly collapsed on the road, bidding Atles to go on ahead Yet, he returned a short time later. He had made it to Alstion, but had been ordered back to Laurelin by High Prince Native. I left with him. He told me what he saw, of the Undead and the chaos, as we left. When we reached the gates of Laurelin, Mayctor was standing there on top of them... Looking down on me.... I lost control, screaming at him. He had to have had something to do with it! He hated the humans...He sought our end. But he only laughed. I refused to enter the gates of Laurelin at that point. I would not be inside the city with that...devil. I headed to Kal'urguan after that, to make sure the dwarves were prepared. A merchant by the name of Algor told me Hiebe was preparing the army for war, and that he was making axes for Hiebe, but had run out of wood. I went to get him some, knowing it was the least I could do. As I headed back, I ran across a group of strange men, one of whom bumped me off the road. All of them wore white robes...I had no time to question their intentions though. I can only assume they were some foolhardy, arrogant Templars. Or some other guild which thought it could defeat this evil easily. I returned to Laurelin after delivering the wood to Algor. Mayctor was no where in sight...I attempted to locate him, but failed. Then Princess Araina announced she was going to the Capital to help the wounded. I could not let her go alone, and I knew I had many spare supplies I could deliver. So we set off with them. The whole of Oren was chaotic. I found Dalejin right upon entering and we gave him what supplies we had, for the soldiers. As many arrows as I had and iron for armor. An uproar started suddenly, the guards yelling about an escaped prisoner. One of the Undead, apparently. I ran off to search the city, but coming up empty handed, returned just as the guards were escorting the Queen up to the Keep....when I saw him. Mayctor, hiding in the crowd. I yelled at him and he immediately ran for the gates. I gave chase, but he leapt off the road and I lost sight of him. I desperately wished to follow, to capture and question him....but I dare not leave the Princess alone. I found her and we went to the Keep together. She mentioned some kind of Traveler who was going to escort her back to Laurelin. We found that Traveler in the Throne Room, causing a ruckus. He was apparently trying to convince the Queen to come to Kal'Urguan, to hide. She refused, and the guards grew angry, attempting to arrest him. He fled quickly, and then the escaped Undead was discovered. Dalejin, I, and the Princess moved the Queen to the Barracks, as she requested. I left them there to speak, while I went to look around the city, mostly for Mayctor. I knew he was still hiding there somewhere. But then the Princess sent word that she sensed something happening in Laurelin. I immediately found her again and escorted her back to Laurelin... But not without running into the Traveler again. He refused to go to Laurelin with us, and the Princess refused to go anywhere without speaking to him first. By this time we were accompanied by 2 Pathfinders. So I took us to the Whisper Isles. I still had access to the Guard Barracks there. The Princess and the Traveler spoke privately inside for some time, then without a word, we left for Laurelin. When we arrived...well, I had no time to rest. Mayctor was skulking about, odd as usual...then a man pulled me aside. I recognized him. Relok. One of the possible members of the Brotherhood... He wished to know what I knew, how much of it, what I knew about Mayctor. He claimed to be a spy, who was sent to spy on Mayctor. I did not believe any of it. I refused to speak to him, and he threatened me. I do not remember the exact wording, but he ordered me to tell him \"Or feel the wrath of the Dark Brotherhood.\" The Princess pulled me aside then, right as Relok claimed there was no such thing as the Dark Brotherhood. I could not comprehend what he was up to. Was it a plot to discredit me? To fool me? To drive me mad? I found out quickly what they wanted from me though. The Princess wished to speak to me in private about my....condition. She is quite observant, unfortunately. But I did not know what was the subject of our discussion until we reached a quiet place. But before that....Mayctor followed us. He crept along, hissing and making odd noises, half bent over all the while. We finally got somewhere quiet and had our conversation in whispers... And the Princess told me I should leave Laurelin. That it was dangerous. That she had overheard word that the Brotherhood wanted me captured. That was when Mayctor came across us. And the Princess bade me, no....commanded me, to flee. And flee I did. I ran as fast as I could from Mayctor as he yelled for me to halt. Claiming I was under arrest, and cackling. As I neared the gate, one of the Princes joined him in his attempts... I could not believe he had tricked them, too. So I screamed at the Pathfinders, who guarded the gate, to open it. While the Prince yelled in retaliation to keep it closed. Someone, I do not know who, but someone whom I owe my life to finally opened it. And I ran out of the city. But I am injured, and slow. The young Prince caught up to me easily, as did Mayctor. I thought all lost. The Princess had commanded me not to let Mayctor catch me, no matter what. But I could not attack the innocent Prince. That was when Atles, my savior, arrived, demanding an explaination. Mayctor claimed I was under arrest for conspiracy, and Atles asked for proof... I could not stay any longer. I yelled an apology to Atles, then ran. Now we return to the beginning of the journal... I ran down the road from Laurelin, Mayctor cackling behind me. As I entered the King's Road, I thought I saw someone familiar, up in the trees... But no. Even if it was him, I could not expect him to assist. I reached the Isles, then hung a left, running as fast as I could. I believe it was at that point Mayctor's cackles seemed to fade... But I could not be sure. My blood was pounding in my ears. I ran past the marketplace I had met Agnor at, down the trail... Until I finally reached Kal'Urguan and began banging on the gates, demanding to be let in. And directly behind them stood the Traveler, whom the Princess had bade me to meet when I arrived, saying he would help me, and I should tell him all I know. I was allowed in and we quickly retired to a private room. I told him of Mayctor, of the Brotherhood, of my wounds, of the Princess... When finally the story was done, King Charles came upon us. He graciously offered me his protection... \n \n \n \n \n \n ...ah, I drifted off. I'm afraid there are more people here, including...the Princess? And one of those men in the white robes....", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Soldier", "TehLulu", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Soldier, Volume Three", "TehLulu", "I feel my skills are increasing, ever so slowly. They are nowhere near the level they once were. But I do feel stronger now. I, along with the Lord of Whisper Isles, have begun something of a quest. We and our two comrades, a dwarf and an Elven ambassador, are searching for a tome. Having found the first tome here in the Whisper Isles, we now seek to find the second. It is said to lie in the High City of Laurelin, home of the elves, an concerns \"The Lost Ones.\" However, after searching the library at Laurelin, we found nothing. The Elf's High Prince himself even assisted us, but to no avail. Yet I have seen many things, which soothes my soul somewhat, the great structures of the capital of Oren, and the beauty of Laurelin. But while these sites bring me pleasure, as does the knowledge I found in Laurelin, I am still yet uneasy. I feel as if I have...forgotten something. A feeling of foreboding, and confusing. If what I have read is true, then there is not much else in this land beyond what I have seen already. The home of the orcs, and the dwarves, I have yet to see, yes... But if what I have read is true...then it is not possible for me to have come from where I recall as my home. Now I lie awake and ponder, is it the history and knowledge of this world that is wrong? Is there perhaps something beyond it that these people are unaware of? Or...is it I, and my mind, which have failed? I will seek further answers to my questions. I cannot accept that the powers I once yielded, and the people I knew... And these...injuries I sustained, are mere figments of my imagination.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Soldier, Volume Two", "TehLulu", "I've met a great deal of people here in the Whispering Isles. The other guards seem friendly enough, but I ran into trouble upon becoming a guard. It seems I no longer have the skills I once had, or at least the ones I seem to recall having, once upon a dream. As a matter of fact, my skills are so far dwindled, I have difficulty with even the weakest o f monsters. As well, my ability to draw a bow is weakened. I can barely draw the string taut. But that is not the least concerning of my weaknesses. Aside from the consistent night horrors which plague me when I sleep, it also seems as if I can no longer practice my \"craft\" as it were. The loss of my powers and my skills are a surprise to me. I can remember vividly the last few hours I spent before I....wound up, here. But I am beginning to become confused, disoriented. Instead of attempting to discern why this has occured, I have decided to focus on the task at hand. I will blend in with these peoples, and hopefully, in my work, I will find the answers to my questions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Something, Volume 4", "TehLulu", "To know anything at all is to know nothing at all. After all, the very act of being a sentient being is to know that there is an obscene wealth of things you do not know. I've walked headfirst into this wall, this problem, many times now, and it blocks my advance in this world at nearly every turn. I've kept quiet about the memories that I seem to have in my mind, about the things I have done, and the wars I have fought, and the things I have lost. And most importantly, about the vivid details I have of the time right before my arrival here in the Land of Aegis, and the man I met directly before it all went black.. Of all my memories, of fighting, killing, surviving, living, loving, those are the most  vivid. But whether what I remember was even real...*the text here is blotted out by some sort of dried up, red stain, which seeps through onto the next page* \n I've still no idea where the book of the Lost Ones lies. It doesn't matter. More important things have come up. I've run into a strange man in the Isles. He is, by all accounts, and even my own, a Wizard. I learned this first hand when dear Rinscher, my dwarf friend, irritated the man, and he shot us both with lightning. While I can understand wanting to smoke his pipe in peace (Though I would have enjoyed a smoke as well), it did seem a bit of an overreaction on his part. No matter. I saved an elf later that same day, a woman named Aerovine. I had been passing through Kramoroe when I heard a few fellows yelling things along the lines of \"Kill! Go out, loot!\" in their home. I hid in the alley and watched as one of them, armed, left the small hut. I followed him quietly along the road to Oren, never getting too close. We passed armed men he paid no mind to, then came about the Elf woman. Hardly armed, she immediately ran as he attacked. I ordered for him to stop, to surrender. Alas, he did not. I was forced to slay the man. I escorted the woman, with her thanks, back to the Isles and the road to Laurelin. It seemed all roads pointed to Laurelin lately. An expansive library, an educated people... Although, there were a few of her residents whom I have had trouble with...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Something, Volume 5", "TehLulu", "My physical health has deteriorated as of late. I do not wish to go into details, but regardless whether or not my memories are fact or fiction, it seems the injuries I sustained are all too real. But what is worse than the physical pain is that which keep me moving when it grows almost too much to bear. I wish to find out the truth, or at least a hint to it. I ran into the Wizard again. But what caused our meeting is what I sit in Diplomat Lafthi's home, waiting to explain. You see, I decided I ought to move to Laurelin. It has been...calling me, it seems, for far too long. When I arrived, I ran into the elf woman I had rescued before, Aerovine. She was gracious enough to show me around the town to any properties for sale. I found a home I liked quite a lot, which suited my purposes well. Plenty of room for the piles of books I would like to accumulate, but sadly, outside of my meager price range. Aerovine however, has a kindness which knows no bounds. Or perhaps she is simply Virtuous enough to not know the sin of Greed. She offered to give me the money I needed to buy the home, and after some insistence on her part, I accepted, and promised to pay it back (And pay it back I shall) Afterwards, I went back to the Isles to turn in my Guard Uniform. I did not tell the others of my ailments though, and only mentioned them to Lord Tyrion. I will continue to defend people on the roads, make no mistake. A few events occured, but afterwards I headed to Laurelin and purchased my new home from High Prince Native. It seems I was not the only one eyeing it. An elf named Elvador and his brothers Had also hoped to buy it. I'm afraid I got there first, though. They were not upset though, which made me glad. Aerovine assisted them in looking for an apartment, when Elvador mentioned something to me as I was about to leave. On his way back from the Isles, he had heard of a plot by a group of Orcs and Elves. This plot was the kidnap the Queen of Oren and overthrow the Orc Leader. I could scarcely believe my ears when I heard it, but I knew I had to act. I sent Elvador and Aerovine to tell their High Prince, while I set out for Oren. It was as I passed through the Isles, looking for a guard to tell my tale to, that I happened upon the Wizard again. And oh, how it vexxed me!!! He weaved and bobbed, moving quicker than light, perhaps even teleporting. He commented on the rain and mumbled to himself....and oh, how I wished I could speak to him, to ask him if anything I remembered could possibly be true. But I felt my wounds clawing at me, and I knew I would not last long before I had to rest. I had to reach Oren before then. That duty came before my own wishes. So I apologized to him, stated I wished I could speak...and left. I know not if I'll run into the man again. But I had to deliver my message...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Former Something, Volume 6", "TehLulu", "As I reached Kramoroe, I ran into Sergeant Urg of the Isles' Guards. I quickly told him what I knew and bid he be on his way quickly, as would I. We parted, he for the Isles to warn Lord Tyrion, as the Isles sit dangerously close to Orc lands, and I to Oren. But I ran into one more acquiantance on the way. A man named Dalejin. We had scarcely talked, only exchanging a few words on a pleasant basis before, but still I liked and trusted the man. I felt he could be trusted. So I told him what I had to say This proved to be a good idea indeed. It seems Dalejin is a close friend of the Queen. So off we went to Oren, to find her and her guard and warn them ourselves... But...we could not find any of them. Not a soul of use in the town was there. I felt my wounds again, and knew I had to leave for Laurelin before something happened. I left Dalejin to deliver my message, and headed back. The Wizard was gone from the Isles, as I expected, so I didn't even stop. I arrived in Laurelin again, after a time, and collapsed in my house. Well, I assume I collapsed. I blacked out, you see. I woke up there many hours later. When I was lucid again I went out to the library to begin some work. But I ran into Lafthi on my way, which was good luck as she has not heard of the plot against the Queen and the Orcs yet. So I went into her office as she took care of some business, and here I wait. I can only hope she returns soon, as I feel that journey has taken more of my strength than I originally thought. I will continue this journal once I have informed her of the situation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Freedom Fighter", "professorshields", "Date: Joma 13th of Snow Maiden 1311 Journal #1 THe biter cold of the north is starting to get to the men, many of them falling ill, no matter, we m ust press on. Upon arriving in the once festive town of Tanl we see the faces of the people. They are starting to lose faith, starting to wonder if they will survive. A local tells me that it had been worse before we arrived. She told me that people had lost all hope, and that we had helped to restore a morsel of hope. We are patrolling the boarder but there is no sign of this Undead force> I'm starting to wonder why we came. Date: Joma 14th of Snow Maiden 1311 Journal #2 Late at night the undead attacked. They seemed to know when our defenses were att the weakest . I have never seen such a ferocius attack in all my years. Wave after wave of enemy forces crach upon our walls like watter on rock. Victory seemed eminent until a great catapult emerged from the woods. The prjectiles launched were beyond description. Dismembered bodies were launched at us as we tried to stop the waves of enemies There were too many. They smashed through the gate with a great crash, but our finest warriors were ready to intercept . our men cut down row afer row of theres until there forces were foced to fall back . That victory was not without it's costs, Many of our finest men sustained wounds but the towns folk were safe. we did our job", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Highborn", "Ranovak", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Holmes", "Fabz2115", "Today has been a crazy day. I have finally started a Journal just to ensure that everyone will see how crazy Aegis has become. A lot of crazy things have happened over the past week. Such as these weird people coming back as the undead. It is really weird. They seem to be extremely powerful aswell. I am lucky as I have not had an encounter with one yet. And please God may I not find one. Also this new thing called a Dungeon has appeared at the Temple. It seems to be overrun with monsters and I am afraid that I have lost a comrade to the Dungeons Spores. Rob Mills has gone crazy! I had to put him down when he attacked me, I felt really bad. But it looks like he is ok. Thank God for those healers. I wouldn't live with myself If I had known I killed a past friend. He is still very crazy, so we must warn people about him...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Oren Rebellion rebel", "PwnCaiks101", "Joma,13th of the amber cold,1324 \n Must make this quick,the undead have taken the keep and Iblee has killed the  queen and made the king eat her flesh!How horrid. They bombed the city.Very few remain! Wardens are telling rebeling citizens to head to the prison.I followed the order and so did most of everyone.As i was running a lighting struck close and knocked me out! \n \n 3 Hours later i awoken to find the Wardens and Milita in the prison all dead! The place was covered with undead and Iblee follwers only few remained or  fleeing...i was lucky to get out of that part of city . The main gate was packed with citizens and gasped as i told them the news. Jesus. More rain and lighting. \n \n Hour later.The milita has ran off into the keep to keep fighting(None returned) some had ran off.I still be here writeing my story! I only see a few remaining here. Half the city was bombed or set on fire. I dont know when or where to run.. Iblees himself.He summons lighting from the sky and kills 1/3 of the milita guarding the gate!! I ran out so fast!!I can still hear Iblees voice in my head! \"You are all weak.Flee the city now or face the wrath!\" Of course i ran out before he said that.So does that mean i am a wimp? No.Undead with iblees vs 3 milita huntsmen. Sounds just about write.. \n \n \n Dear the could temple destory the forces of the evil in the Oren kingdom! \n \n \n Jesus.Now that the Undead have left the streets are filled... \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher I; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I'm leaving Laurelin. I've spent my life amidst these majestical trees in uninterrupted solitude, but I sense a yearning that I don't understand. There's trouble in Aegis and in all my years I remain barely aware of it. Tomorrow I shall embark on a journey of discovery. I'm not sure why I'll be keeping a journal, perhaps I'll meet an untimely end and my head will end up on a pike outside Krugmar. This way someone might know who I was.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher II; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I journeyed towards Oren and come upon a small city outside Alras. It was here in Kramoroethat I spent days absorbed in the dusty old pages of a towering library. I never saw a warden, but I'm sure that there would be one, for the place was well kept and the books, vast in numbers though they were, were organised. \nI felt a presence. For the first time since leaving Malinor I forgot about my desire to learn my own history and sensed the forthcoming of something bigger. We were too sheltered in Laurelin to realise how far Iblees had spread. We were too foolish. I read journals that made me shiver and old parchments that illustrated the same heinous shadow which brought back my undercooked porkchop sandwich. \nThe fate of Aegis hangs in the balance of a war that only days ago I wasn't even fully aware of. I've no idea the role I have to play, but I know I must do something.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher III; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I met an ascended in the gates of Alkhazar. She was well learned and spoke with a gentle tongue, yet went to great measure to answer my queries. Of course I was delighted to siphon a bounty of knowledge and wisdom, but I am just an Elf, and a wanderer at that. I had no idea of her importance until I entered the Followers of Aeriel library and read of her holy bloodline. This meeting has got me thinking more about God. His servant's presence is here in Aegis, both Good and Evil, as is their power.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher IV; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I sit in Oren's castle library surrounded by magnificent rows of books. There's floor after floor of ancient tomes, kingdom records and glimpses of history. I could spend a year here, but I know that I must not. For whatever purpose the Creator God sent me on this mission I must be moving forward. There is more to be discovered! \nI'm beginning to wonder if I have been called to be a messenger. Surely far be it from me for such an important mission, for who would be MY audience? The elves wouldn't heed my word, and men seem disinterested in the sayings of an elf, now that they have the ascended walking among them. The orcs seem ready to fight, for what cause they couldn't care less, and I haven't met the acquaintance of many dwarves, but as I understand it they aren't on the friendliest of terms with us 'tall ears'. Still, there is a bigger picture in all this, I just cannot fathom it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher IX; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "My insides churn at this Evil that pits brother against brother, harbors such hatred of love and shatters friendhsips. A father having to drive a sword into his own son. How can this be in the name of God? If this is an end on the path that is our lives, what God could be in such a thing? \nI saw a strong and compassionate elf turn on his lifelong friend and his lover at the hand of the corruption of a tormented soul from Nether. But the turned one did show a weakness. Not as far as compassion, but he was not the bloodthirsty animal I expected. The Tainted have purpose and drive, each seeming to follow their own will but still under Iblees' command. It revealed to me many things, but above all that I am not ready to face the horrors that make their way across Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher V; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "This entry may consist entirely of my thoughts, but I've been wondering... The Ascended do the work of Aeriel, who is an Aengul and an immortal creature that serves God. So in balance the Undead do the work of Iblees, who is a Daemon and likewise immortal subject of God. With the assumption that Aegis is a trial period for us mortals to pick a side before our lives end, then we would be taken out of our mortal bodies to be made another form. Does this mean that the Undead, who are in a sense immortal, have chosen their side and moved on? \n Given the choice of being Undead for an eternity or absolutely anything else, I don't think any amount of tempting power could have me settle for wandering around Aegis slowly disintegrating. But what if I'm seeing it wrong? Perhaos they have received an enlightenment that they desire to share with us mortals. An enlightenment that stinks of rotting flesh and hungers to tear muscles from bone and be drenched in warm blood. \nI think I should seek a druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher VI; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "The modern druids were of little assistance. They seem now to be a reflection of their ancient power. They desire to protect this world but harbor little soncern that it may all burn in a Nether fire. They also don't beleive that God formed Aegis but that it was the work of wizards and druids. I came with questions of spirituality and our theologies were far too disconnected to formulate any answers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher VII; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "The Imperial Coalition will be another indepent force fighting valiantly on our frontlines. I spoke with their commander, a strong man who seems weary of battle but honourable enough to lead the charge again. I realise from our conversation that there are few who are attempting to understand this battle in a deeper sense, and fewer still who have considered God's perspective. They are but men and they will more hastily pick sides than come to diplomatic reasoning with something they deem a threat. The preservation of Aegis needs them, just as it needs the Druids, just as it needs the rain. It troubles me that so many good people are lost against a struggle that we don't comprehend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher VIII; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "While praying today something dawned on me. It is so simple to question God in all this, but what if the knowledge that we lack is in our understanding of suffering? I haven't seen the devastation of the North through my own eyes, so I should probably hold my tongue; however, what if suffering is just another mortal emotion, like content or anguish. It is nothing more than our response which we bare for just a time and then continue along towards our purpose. I fear that there is no question that I would not want to discover the answer to more than 'what is suffering?' But I know that I will find an answer, and it will shatter my heart.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher X; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "Today I am beginning my journey through the North. In search of what, I know not. I expect that when I find my answer it will be staring me in the face. I have stopped for the night in Al'Khazar. I thought it wise to get off these roads while the sun was hid, but inside Oren's walls is more dangerous than the open road. Lightning crashes down within the city igniting thatch rooves, and even people, ablaze. All the while they fight between themselves. The old King Sheffield's followers may start a revolt against Ponpao's son, all the while the Undead army  encamps the nation's walls. A seperate Aegis is a doomed one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XI; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I journeyed to Crimson Vale only to find an abandoned town. As I made my way back to the road I was stopped by an Ascended with maroon stripes. This came as a confusion as the Ascended fort lies outside of Crimson Vale and I had heard tale that the town was under Iblees' control. The man was willing to speak with me and was willing to speak with me and answered many of my queries about the war. But as he illustrated the impending doom of Aegis his voice grew deeper and I noticed a horrible stink of rotting burnt flesh. Realising that he could no longer remain hidden, the man removed his robes and I saw that he carried no Aengul blood but the stain of the Nether. He introduced himself as Wargoth and I saw that he was once a man, now only a fowl and corrupted worshipper of Iblees. \nWargoth lead me to some kind of dungeon under Crimson Vale with a few rooms intentionally constructed in the art of killing a man. After much heated conversation about God, power and liberated knowledge that resulted in a philosophical stalemate, he commanded me to pick a room. I knew that his promised 'path to enlightenment' harbored dire consequences for my ability to share this knowledge, so tempted though I was to learn the secrets of the Nether and Iblees' true form, I lowered my head to accept my death. There are many ways to discover the universe and all its knowledge, but none of those paths can be forced into an immediate instance. Except death.  \nI will not bow down to him. May knowledge remain liberated forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XII; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "The undead attacked. Right upon the gates of Laurelin. The voice of Iblees boomed through the trees about imminent destruction and bowing before his power. Not denying, the display of might was tremendous, but still found its match against our united strength. I won't stop trying to understand the Undead, but I won't let Iblees take control of Aegis either. \nAll noble paths need a path of less nobility to reap recognition; the truly noble path is unseen by others. The presence of such evil makes it easy to pick the righteous side, but our paths should not be so easily chosen for us. Has God taken away the choice so that all might come to him or suffer? If so, Iblees was formed by God, because there is a little bit of Iblees even in Him. I must go, the thunder has returned.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XIII; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "The ascended are gone. The sages left and the remaining followers of Ariel are scattered among the races they once left to discover Haven. It serves as the desperate wake-up call that the war involuntarily concerns everyone. That is isn't happening in some distant land being taken care of by the holy kin. Now we're all required.\nFinally we're going to see the prophecies fulfilled and the descendants of Horen, Malin, Krug and Urguan will come together again to defeat Iblees. Ariel guided us this far, but another will rise as a shining light to lead Aegis to victory. That light could be someone as unexpected as myself; but it would never be me.\nThere is great suffering still to come. This war's violent crescendo has only just begun. We, including myself, still have much to learn of pain. Dark days ahead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XIV; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "A pungent aroma of ale and an untunefully recited dwarven drinking song shroud the busily cleaning barmaid as she removes blood from the counter after yet another drunken brawl. I do enjoy Dawn's Bakery in Al'Khazar.\nA female follower of Aeriel came in yesterday and a brute of a man, who I had seen only days earlier terrorizing a woman for the fun of it, placed a blade against her throat. A long and hideous fight followed in which I got my fair share of blows in defending her. After the assailant was zapped with a ball of light and dissappeared I went with the Priestess to listen to Aeriel's guidance.\nThe remaining ascended, and consequently the Followers of Aeriel Guild, seem futile without their Sages. I likened her efforts in recruiting me to Wargoth and his militant enlisting through fear mongering. Both sides have identical goals: essentially to indoctrinate all of Aegis to follow their ways. I seeked spiritual guidance and all I received was the same diluted ramblings about an Aengul come to save us.\nThe war is not between Iblees and Aeriel, but the evil that men hide away in their hearts and holy sanctity. \nThis is the crescendo of our trial time. God is watching.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XV; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "I rented a room in Al'Khazar to buy some time to meet her again. It is Snows Maiden 1327. Much has happenned in the last 3 years, but nothing has changed. The war continues, the frailty of humans prevails. \nI have begun research at an institute in the studies of 'souls'. Such a broad and non-descript field to be thrown into, but I expect that my findings will change the way we view our lives, this war, the balance of Aegis. I've also been spending much time absorbed in the culture and company of our allies the orcs. They differ greatly from the rest of us, but their ways are so simplistic. It is complex to discern why so few people understand them. Perhaps it is no more than the fear of receiving a \"klopming\" that cripples their curiosity. \nBut onto why I have returned to journalling. There is a  woman here in Al'Khazar whose name neither I, nor any I have spoken with, have knowledge of. She was once hauntingly beautiful, and parts of her still are, but the Nether's taint has disfigured her. I see the loneliness and torment in her eyes and it brings my heart to tears. She is not hateful. She does not despise love. She doesn't declare the impending doom of Aegis. This woman is nothing I though the undead represented. But still she yearns for and worships only Iblees. His pull on her damaged heart is strong.\nI distracted some guards long enough for her to slip away earlier today. I may have put someone's life at risk by letter her free, as she has attempted assassinations on high figures in Oren before. I  did it as a demonstration that I am worthy of trust. My desire is to learn of who she is and get to know her, though she cannot speak. I do it under the guise of my research, but I know that is not what motivates me.\nAs the endless rain pelts upon this apartment roof and thunder booms about the city walls, all I can think on is where she is now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XVI: Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "My mind has been so troubled, which I presume is why I have returned to this journal. Normally at this point I would observe how much of Aegis has changed, but little change has my eyes beheld, yet great change in myself.\n \nThere is no real place to begin in recording the places I have been, the things that I have seen, what events have transpired in the years gone by. So my writings may be collected with similar chaos to that with which my mind can process. First and foremost, which may explain the degredation of my intellectual processing, is that I've become alarmingly aware that Aegis is soon to crumble. I find myself drifting between a rambling doomsayer and a melancholic hermit. Yet still I hold on to the actions that stand as evidence for my sanity. I've joined the mages guild, I'm developing a college for advanced education called Aegis Institute of Technology, and I constantly find myself embarking on historical explorations, many of which occur in 'The Verge'. Albeit these titles appear as nothing more than busywork to preoccupy my mind from its wanderings, they may be what defines me in my last moments before the foundations of this world collapse to the end. How pitiful.\n \n The war with the undead was becoming seemingly irrelevant. As the powers and numbers of the ascended would drop, so too would the frequency and severity of the undead's attacks. And again, the balance has been restored, but this in this circumstance it will be in preperation for our coming destruction. I cannot explain my meeting with a six thousand year old being, and the appearance of Iblees in the flesh, and the bestowing of immense power during the baptism of an undead, in enough detail to validate how I know that the end is coming. But the Ascended Sages have returned to Aegis, and thus we simply bide our time till the final battle that rips the world apart. I am in too deep to warrant picking sides now. I can do no more than wait and pray that God is in all of this, and in His divine wisdom will bestow on us what is best. Please be in this God. \n \nAlso, I have not seen 'her' in such a long time. Once I would have been troubled out of my wit and been praying like mad that nothing terrible would have happenned to her; but she is the something terrible that happens to others. Yet still, I pray that her soul is not lost. Perhaps she is the only guidance I have left to my life. \n \nWhere are you Maeghan? *tears soak the page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Philosopher XVII; Elindor's Travels", "Jerry_Man", "The approaching end is all I can think on. Aegis' inevtiable fall to the void. God will cleanse us all. \n \nThe Wizard Availer was killed while the Cloud Temple was being attacked. He was shouting something about protecting the relics he held. I saw a glimpse of them, strange coloured eggs. He seemed adamant that all would be lost were they to be captured by the Undead. Of course they were taken, Iblees can't resist anything he hears he shouldn't have.\n \nIn my dreams, when I'm not haunted be 'her' face, I see serpents with wings and talons, like the ones I saw as a child in an old story book. The images are so vivid, and the darkness surrounding its presence is crippling. Perhaps those eggs contain the strange creatures in my sleep. \n \nThere is little that can be done now but wait and pray. Whatever becomes of those eggs, and the outcome of the horrors of today, they are nothing more than a demonstration of how close we are to the void.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Of a Soldier in the clan wars", "craotor", "Year 1200 Hot season me be Krta of da vilage of Urlat new line", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of a Something, Volume 7", "TehLulu", "I grow increasingly frustrated As Prince Toren commented, \"Spider webs within Spider webs\" I have stumbled head first into these webs, and now I am stuck I've determined no more about my past, but that matters not now This plot I mentioned reaches further than I imagined, clawing its way into nearly every  race in Aegis. I have confirmed that this plot is being perpetrated by the Dark Brotherhood. They wish to see the empire of the humans fall, and likely the Orcs as well. It seems they plot to attack within the next month. Elvador also made mention of a portal they wished to create. Inside lie some sort of monsters that the Brotherhood wishes to kill. It seems the elves are the ones most manipulated by this evil. The leader of one of their army branches, the Sentinels, is a worshipper of Iblees. High Guardian Mayctor... He is evil, yet his intentions appear good...he wishes to protect the Elves. So he assures me that Laurelin will remain safe, and that the Elves will not be attacked. What he has done to gain this assurance, I do not know. But I believe he may be a threat to the High Prince, if the Prince decides to act against him. I have found a new ally in the Pathfinder's current leader, Atles. He also believes a great evil is coming...but I will believe that when I see it. For the evil he predicts is far greater than that of what the Brotherhood could manage.  Had I the strength for it, I would go to the North, where he claims to have found a small, dark village. Yet this same village his associates say is part of Oren. But as I have mentioned, my condition worsens by the day. As I spoke to Mayctor in Ravenhold, I was prepared to fight him should he strike me. Yet in truth, I do not believe I could have held my sword up. Prince Toren, who I had met at Ravenhold along with two other princes and the PRincess, agreed with me that Mayctor seemed quite mad. I sent him with a book of my notes to deliver to Native, in the event I was attacked. All turned out fine however, and he has become a quiet ally of mine, as the other Princes are far too blinded to see Mayctor's true face. Mayctor claimed he had information I sought, but refused to tell me. He also told me that only one other knew of what he did, and that he would never talk... In addition, Atles told me that some of the Pathfinders that had deserted had become bandits. I will have to see if they have anything to do with this matter. But for now, I've but one lead... a name Lafthi and Prince Loren both told me. An elf by the name of Rolok, who supposedly lives in Laurelin. I must find and speak with him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Ahkrael", "Ahkrael", "I write the beginning of my life, as I feel as if there is a hope someone will learn from my experiences . \n When I was a young boy, I lived far up north, in a small log cabin with me father , mother, and two younger sisters. I don't remember many dull times in my childhood", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Of Ajax", "jessdawg98", "Day 1: I am aloud to leave the temple now i have decided i will go to laurelin. Day 2: I am exploring laurelin, looking for a job but I have not come across one yet. Day 3: I just asked a Noble by the name of leafwind if he knew of a job where he answered \"Join the Wardens\" i agreed and he led me to their base and I then made an oath. Day 4: I have been travelling around the warden camp and have found some interesting things. Day 5: I have now raised enough money to buy a permit to mine in the sister mine time to start.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Amras'Tullum~By Amras'Tullum", "Ranovak", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of an Elf", "ggt3416", "JOURNAL ENTRY #2 \nYears have come and gone since that day I lost both my brother and my home, yet the memory never ceases to haunt my thoughts. The look on my brother's face as he collapsed, his blank eyes staring out of that cold, lifeless body once capable of love and laughter. These images stubbornly imprint  in my mind. His memory still never fails to reduce me to tears, even if my brother was an arrogant fool. I've far from forgotten his mockery of my every pursuit. \"Your cooking could put the undead in their graves, again! (I can't disagree with this one.) You swing your sword your sword as if you are afraid it will get hurt! Ha, you'll never be anything but weak, delicate little elf girl. Just give up now.\" \nIf only my brother still remained... he would see how accurate he really was. I AM weak... Even after all these years of training, I managed to be defeated by a single bandit wielding a stone sword, while I myself was fully suited in iron. Now look at me, rendered helpless by this blasted wound he gave me. I have not been able to wield a sword in months, as their weight sends the most agonizing pain down my being. Delicate and weak indeed. \nIt is no wonder everything was stolen from me on that day, how could I ever have hoped to protect anything? \n \n JOURNAL ENTRY #1\n These Wardens are not my favorite bunch. After sharing a (stinky!) barracks with these rowdy elves, I've developed a dislike for most of 'em. Any Warden who is not an Initiate fancies  like royalty, with their condescending orders and snobby scoffs. \nJust today, the Wardens captured an suspect Undead associate by the name of Sparrow, along with Initiate Caden. I'm not too sure what Caden is accused of, but Seth suggested that Sparrow had successfully pitted the Wardens against one another. He also fears other Wardens will be brought in for questioning. I can't help but be amused. Is that awful of me?", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Blackbeard", "krille120", "Joma, 27th of The Amber Cold, 1306. Collecting wood for the boat, pigmen are really starting to get dangerous along with the undead getting stronger. Tho' we live in peace out here, they come  and harm us.   \n Sabet, 28th of the amber cold, 1306 The new farm has recently been made by James Smith, Our great farmer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Braxis_Silverblade A Gallant Knight", "Domainoft", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Dio Astóre, Vol. II", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Ahad, 15th of The Deep Cold, 1324\n\n Most of the stone is now gone. The warmth of the wood reminds me of Laurelin. I plan to visit there again soon. \nThe forest may have its share of monsters, but I learnt today that it has blessings among them too . Not far from my dwelling is a Dark Elf couple, both of whom have shown me kindness.\n The lady Aviala I met upon arriving to the woods, with nothing but clothes on my back and a will. She provided me with food and shelter from the darkness. After night had passed I wondered a little while away from their home, to discover the place in which I now live.\n Today her husband - Moloha - traversing the forest happend across the path that I recently laid. This lead him here, and alas it was my turn to play host, and return the favour. We engaged in light banter and before long I found myself back at their home, reading some of the texts that Moloha him self wrote. A poem in his collection I am particulary interested in, and I shall ask him for a copy in the morn' . \nThat night a friend sent word to Moloha, requesting his aid for a battle, which I immediately offered to accompany them to. I followed Aviala to the shore, close to the Laurelin Mine, but when we sto pped to account for our company, Moloha was not among us.\n  \"I will search for him!\" I announced to her before returning a way whence we came. Through the forest I looked, back to the homestead, the surrounding area, back to the shore again (Aviala now missing too) all the while shouting not only Moloha's name but now Aviala's as well. Inquiring in regards to their whereabouts I spoke with several Elves that were passing by. The next thing I knew I was searching the desert in the vain hope of finding them.\n As is becoming of the desert; my labours bore no fruit. What did I expect? To simply happen across them when they were summoned to aid a location or person only known to them?\n Worried after them, and hoping for their safe return I eventually came to learn that they both suffered a defeat against their opponents. If only I had been there, if I had assisted them ...\n No point in brooding over it. Life does not leave the people of Aegis lightly, and they are alive. \n It is almost time to begin, I sense it; wanderlust will move these feet a great distance. \n Soon..", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Dio Astóre, Vol. III", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Joma, 6th of Malins Welcome, 1324\n My home is gone and the High Prince Native is responsible\n Was I simply negligent, living so close to the borders of Orcish land? Where the green reaches; there lies Malinor. The sands expanse; the no-mans'-land; so I thought at the time. As dusk set I  made to return to my dwelling, driven out by a pair of Orcs as I was installing a battlement to better fortify against the Undead that roam about at night.\nCaught completely unawares the threats upon my life seemed almost too surreal, the severity of their shouts and warnings not dawning upon me up until I hear \"5....4.......3......2.....1...\"; counting down how much time I had left before my flesh would learn just how sharp and diamond blade could be.\n I am sprinting for dear life, with several wounds to carry too, with the violent curses of my pursuer close behind me. The garments are drinking in my blood, and the once prestine white of my robes is now dyed with the most ancient of crimsons.\n I reach my hand down into a damp pocket . \"Wha's tha'?!\" I hear yelled. \n \"What if it doesn't have enough power?\", I wonder to myself, barely managing to formulate this thought into a coherent monologue. I start to feel light-headed, and the rifts in my body are pulsating in pain. The object in my grasp begins to emit its own rhythmic energy, as if in unison with that organ which even now was struggling to keep life and memory from escaping me.\n  \n \"One more...\", I utter to myself, my knees in the moist, cool soil.  My mind drifts to Laurelin; the caressing breeze of the wind and the soft sounds of the leaves as they play in their endless folds, the dancing... \n I longed to be back there. More than anything I wished to be under the canopies of the trees, to bask in their ageless wisdom and strength. \n I feel a familiar sensation as the object in my hand starts to warp; the smell of the Orc in my nostrils as the world around me begins to change faster than my darkening mind can comprehend. \n Fortitude fails me as I succumb to the pull of the Earth; muscles slackening, body rolling slowly to the side. \n Some time passes before I realise something peculiar. The presence of the death-dealer absent, I pondered to myself: \"Did I die?\", still lying; head against the firm surface. I drifted in and out of consciousness, not much caring what the answer was to the question I posed the sky, which was also not to be seen. \"Where am I?\", I ask myself, my senses sharping at a slow but steady rate. Cautiously I begin to sit up, in as gentle a manner as possible, before scanning my environment. \n I crawl backwards to a log wall for comfort. Deeply I sigh, closing my watery eyes with and equally deep sense of relief. \"Home\", I say to myself. \n I was back in Laurelin. \n The valour of the Elves grace me with renewed strength; a Power to Will. \"My body may still ache, but I am determined to return there\", so I resolve myself. \"They are probably ravaging my work even now!\"; noticing my fist clenched, relax and regain my composure. \"Very well. My belongings may be pilfered, but even if not they are not what I will go back for. No. The truth is what I want. Krug may have been cursed with blood-lust, but he also had honour. If they dismantle the walls, the Undead will surely enter and attack them. Those diamond swords do not make them invincible.\" \n I began to concern myself for the Orcs safety, despite having nearly been slain by the duo. Dusk was falling, and with the rising of the moon brought with it urgency. \"Now is the time. I must go, lest my questions fall on the ears of a corpse!\" \n And so I made my way along the walls of Laurelin's frontal gate, as I had so often done before when returning to the Wilderness from the city. After finding the usual vantage point some 70 meters to the South I leaped from the edge of the wall, over the moat, falling a distance to land that was far from as comfortable as I would have liked it to be. \"When will they ever build an Eastern Gate here? Perhaps they fear that a gate would be a liability if ever Krugmar went to war with Malinor. I pray that day may never come.\" \n I proceeded to head East - under the cover of darkness - some 130 meters before arriving at my destination. I take an underground route to enter, in the hope of buying more time to investigate the condition of the property and my possessions. \n \"Everything seems to be intact. The chests have yet to be plundered\", I whisper to the dully lit redwood. \n \"Twiggie!?\" I hear off not far from me. \"I smell Twiggie!\"  \"Pointy eurs?\", another voice inquires. \"Take down dis wall, dis gonna be firewood!\"  \"Unklomperz!\" \n \"What a rough brood\", I voice only to my ears as a though occurs to me: \"Ha! Imagine what Nether they might bring to the Undead!\", the irony of which struck me a moment thereafter. \n \"AHH! BEIN ATTACKED!\", I hear, suddenly alarmed. I rush to the balcony that overlooks the garden. Zombies are below and the Orc is attempting to fend them off. His companion is a litte way off. I unsheath my iron sword and spring to the defendants aid, completely ignoring the ladder leading down. The impact does not stagger me. As I strike the beast from his flank it lets out a low, deep moan, before turning on me The Orc drives his diamond blade into the creature, but fails to be pay him any notice despite the grievous wounds it's already sustained. It's arm lands a medium blow, made all the worse by what I had already pushed my body through to even get here. I exclaim before laying the foul creature to rest with a final blow, when I hear another zombie nearby and the Orcs companion yelling to me: \"Wha?! You die!\", accounting only a wounded friend and my bloody blade. He steps forward, ready to return my spirit to the halls of my Ancestors. \"Wait!\", the other says, \"Twas zombie, not elf.\" \n I say to them both: \"I came here, because I know no place else.\"  \"Ya got 5 seconds ta leave\" \"Wait\"  \"5\"  \"4\" \"Ya die if no leave\" \"3\" \"2\"  \"He is a elder.\"  \"1\"  \"0\"  \"Ya dead\"  \"We cannot kill and unarmed elder!\" I said to them in between that exchange: \"I made this my home, and now you say the High Prince has ordered you do destroy it.\"  \"We can't kill 'n' unarmed elder! That is just unworthy.\" \"Uhm, okay den\", he says, although I do not feel assured of my safety because of it. \"We all have a common enemy.\"  The Orc throws a rough, stone blade ay my feet, brandishing his own diamond blade as he does so. \"Now I can kill him\" \"I will not fight you\", throwing away the blade. \n \"Lissun elfie, we gonna destroy dis no matter what. Leave before we kill ya ukee?\"  \"If lat hash problem tell Mistuh Prince\", one says to me, the other still keen on killing me, judging by the wild glint in his eyes. \"Slay me if you must, but allow me this small favour: what is it that brings you here? I must know! The truth is something  will have, if it costs me life too\", and so my request was posed. \"We destroy 'cause Worgoth said so. Don't need no more reason. Ya shuld leave.\" \n \"If only I knew the motivations behind this..\", I half say to myself. \"I don't care 'bout that.\" The Orc I aided begins to speak again: \"Lissun, you make big pretty tree on OUR land, we klomp it.\" \"And you have every right to it, but are these not the borders of Malinor?\" \"Nub\", both of them say together. \"The High Prince give us shiny to destroy dis\", one says. \"He say we can destroy too\", says the other. \n Very well. Go about your business. I will talk to the High Prince myself when I can. I shall take my things before I go.\" \n \"Now ya got 5 seconds before we klomp\", and he begins counting down again.  \"Wait, let him take heesh stoff\", the other demands. \"Ya shood run, twiggie!\" \"Toopid twiggie \n \"Do not intimidate me, I will do as you say.\" I hand them my armour; \"Take this. You will have more use for it.\" The countdown ends. \"Run twiggie! Me wants to kill!\", and I do just that, having finished collecting my things. \n He chases me through the woods, his speed formidable, and despite my superior knowledge of the terrain he manages to close distance between us. \n As we approach a denser part of the woods I feel I will be able to lose him. I underestimated the gap between us, and he managed to grab hold of the pack in which I kept my things. Struggling to break free I lose my possessions before being able to shake his hold on me, and made my way back to Laurelin. \n Now it is time to find the High Prince and discover the true meaning of all this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Dio Astóre: Vol. I", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Irba, 25th of the Amber Cold, 1324\n Today started as any other day does; one wakes up, nourishes the body and then proceeds with attending to the domestic chores and such the like.\n The abode progresses well, although the stone is not to my liking - the price one pays for living in the security of the earth - although in time the forest will provide; I do not intend to stay here forever.\n I believe there is another whom resides here, but I cannot be sure. The excavation and tunnels suggest this is so. Who is it that I share this place with unknowingly? Indeed, this must be what it is like to live in a haunted house. A presence that you cannot engage, but that you know was there before you, and will some time be there after you.\n No matter; few evil spirits are in the history of Malinors land, but the growing taint of the Undead unsettles me at times. Skeletons and Zombies are to be seen frequently, and I have already implemented measures to better defend against them.\n They are not too much trouble and can be dealt with quite promptly; pigmen not so easily dismissed. Much Minas is to be found on their corpses, all of which is being saved for a trip to the Laurelin Mine; I need better tools, despite being ill suited to the tasks of stone.\n I miss strolling through the forests in peace. Some supplies are already here to be found in the caves, but nothing of the quality which I seek. Upon mining today I heard the conversation of a large group, speaking in the manner that is unmistakably that of the Orcs. As easy as it was to recognise those voices, one among them was different in tone.\n More refined. A voice that knew authority. Of all the people that I may have expected to see in these parts - so near the borders of the forests - High Prince Native was certainly not among the top of my suspicions.\n Under his supervision the Orcs proceeded to demolish a building that came within their territory, very close to a large tree home safe-guarded by the Wardens; the owners name I cannot recall for this account. I offered them what supplies I could, and made myself a guard against the Undead that were to the South and West.\n No match were they for us though! The Orcs are great warriors indeed. The females among them had no hesitation in engaging them, even unarmed! Much respect have I for their courage; it is a strong peoples' who have Women and Children that can hold their own in battle; a comfort for my mind this be.\n After they finished going about their business I farewelled the last of their kin, but not before providing her with a stone sword (the best that I could offer at the time). She seemed confident to find her way along the roads: '..as good as any Twiggy' she says to me.\n Her children were being minded by her Ancestors. I am sure she wouldn't let even Iblees get between her and them...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Dio Astóre; Vol. III", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Sabet, 21st of The Grand Harvest, 1326 \n I have returned from my journey, and this entry will simply be an account of the places I visited and their locations. \n Kal'Urguan: X -410 Z 360 \n Elvendale X-500 Z 1060 \n Kal'Menor X -600 Z 1600 \n Town of Woodburo X -1410 Z 1560 \n Lunavara X -1830 Z 1740 \n Butcherblock Fortress X -2040 Z 1780 \n G'Khar X -2490 Z 1880", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Dom", "Domainoft", "I am sad, my original journal was lost to an known thief. Today I work on the future pumkin/watermelon farm, The Wisps and I are very excited!!! .... After many weeks of testing and working with the watermelons I think I have found the best way to place them so they grow quickly and effectively. .... Today I set out in search of many books across the land for my library. ..... The search for books has been amazing and I have gotten to know a good deal of people in the process. Nearly 2 chests full of books now and they are all from the elvish lands, soon I'll head to Oren and search there for more. ....On my way back to the Isle of the Wisps with a load of new books I came across, what looks to be a mineshaft with several warning signs on it, I would usually ignore this except that the upper most sign said there may be an important book inside, I must find out for myself. ..... I have found what I was searching for and what it was I could not imagine. I dare not tell anyone details until I can prove my suspisions.... This will be the most dangerous task I have ever undertook, but one that may very well benifit all of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of FreeBird", "Trippydays", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Freema A. Grenedad", "freema5", "[Itnan, 16th of The First Seed, 1331] Well it has been a long journey by foot, but I think I have made it to AlKhazar. Maybe I should stop at a few shops and run some errands for them to get some money. Soon I should have my own blade, my own home..... maybe even my friends I have lost long ago. ~Freema A. Grenedad \n [Ahad, 22nd of The First Seed, 1331] Well today was a reasonable day, made myself some  as clearing out a cave for a miner. It was quite easy, those cave spiders didnt have a chance. ~Freema A. Grenedad \n [Joma, 27th of The First Seed, 1331] Just met a nice couple of people. One is Salvia and t he other is Akorta. Nice friendly people. Hope to have a good future with them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Galo", "Galoi", "It is a poor Elf who knows nothing of his kind, I guess that makes me a poor elf. I seem more akin to the Dwarves that of my own kind. I lay that blame upon my upbringing, as a bandit. I never was told of my heritage, My mother had fallen from grace a long time ago. My father....Well, lets just say thats yet to be found. help help I seem to hear those words most common of all. Yet, I cannot bring myself to give them fruition for I was never taught to. Maybe I'm just a lost cause, although it is never apparant to me that is the case.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Garrett 2", "SimppaFIN", "We had an raid tae \"undead base\" under whispers isle. The guy blocked us out. He was wearing Black robes, similar that undead does. He claimed that he used that tae protect his skin from th' sun. Lady Bell also said so.. \n Pastor Judas said that when he first did go there, there was Undead there. Ah gave him the copies of mah books, those books that Ah copied. Ah also told him about mah \"intel\" from there. About the controlled pumpkins on top of the tower. :. Today dwarves attacked tae Al'Khazar, and Ah was there too. Ah was there, on the rooftops, defending mah brothers from humans. After the war, The Wandering Wizard started to lead humans towards Kal'Urguan! Bloody Hell! Mah city! After that, King Perea jailed me for being an dwarven spy.. A spy!! Bloody marvelous.. Hopefully they wont notice mah house here. Good that it has wrong name on sign..", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Gavin", "drusbek", "alright I will work on it. erase * knocks on Gabriel's door hello?", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Hooded Traveler", "SimppaFIN", "Today Ah have discovered an secret base in Whispers Isle, and told about it to Pastor Judas and other guy, whos name Ah can nae remember . The base is connected tae Ag'Na'Rok ur something like that, base. There was book about The Dark Brotherhood, and their Leader, \"The Stranger\" Who might be the Iblees himself! Brotherhood is connected to Laurelin somehow, Maybe they Maychor has something tae do with it Because Princess Ariana mentioned him and the brotherhood Also Bell knows mah secret...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Iona_Mackay", "ForestMaid", ":Finaly after many days of traveling i have made it to my brothers village. I have just finished building my house it took a lot of stone. :After i woke from my sleep i was surprised to see that some of my crop had been harvested.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Jack Mercy", "Jackbjossi", "They are coming, I'm being followed. They are not going to leave me alone until I do what they want. I must do what they want. I must follow their orders. I must not crumble. I must not collapse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of James Moffatt", "Zdrok", "ENTRY 1 \n After gathering ample food and tools, I departed from my home. My parents did not approve of my journey, but they did not stop me. I do not know where I will go, but I need to earn my own living. My life cannot be simply handed to me by \"loving\" parents. \n  \n ENTRY 2 \n I have come upon the Cloud Temple of Aegis.  From here I will head to a nearby human city.  Hopefully I can find work soon, as I am down to a few meager slices of bread. \n ENTRY 3\n\n I have wandered through these streets all day and found nothing. This city is cluttered and convoluted; I have lost my way countless times. I do not even know the name of the city I currently reside in. No job offerings have come up despite my constant searching for any work. \n \n ENTRY 4 \n In desperation, I left a notice on a board that I would take any job availible. A millitant by the name of Thaern has offered me a job as a farmer on his estate. It will pay 300 minas per week and he will provide shelter and food. I took the job and am waiting on him so we can walk to the place. \n \n ENTRY 5 \n I am writing this while warm and dry inside a house that I earned myself. No inheritance, no allowance, just pay and rent. My employer has provided a two-story house of high quality in exchange for the simple labor of harvesting his wheat and reeds. I cannot believe my good fortune in finding this job.  \n  \n ENTRY 6 \n Working on the farm is so peaceful. The estate is well built and far from the clutter of the city. I am able to make good pay, and the wheat that I produce fills the air with a pristine scent. Everything I need is provided here: food, shelter, and work. I may not be so quick to take off after all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Of Janux", "freakout286", "Entry #1 - I shall be keeping log of my travels from this point on. I will write frequently. \n Entry #2 - I have decided to mine for myself for once. I shall give in any gold to the lords. \nEntry #3 - I found 2 green things today. There were about 15 minas inside of them, killed t hem .", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Joshua Drake", "Jarhead90", "Ahhh finally I have a permenent home. And a job. I am a solider now. And glad I am. My commanding officer says Im one of The best I have a good feeling about this. Hard to belive just a while ago I was alone no home or job but now Im not. I have a home and brothers in arms! Hoorah! I am very proud to be serving and will never stop serveing!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of King Belin", "skinner452", "I have lived a long life and I have learned many things along the way. My first role in the dwarven government was as a Baron of a land called Kal'Himmelen. It was a great start in my career buy I knew I could have taken the next step in becoming a great leader. When King Charles stepped down from command, I quickly jumped on the opportunity of becoming the next king. To my surprise, he chose me out of a few candidates who wanted the position aswell. A few days later, my coronation began because Charles was very eager to get off the throne. Many people showed up and I quickly gained respect from the entire nation. Many people showed up and supported me as I took the throne. That was a great day for me and I was ready to take on challenges of my future. \nMany would say that I was successful as I was on the throne. I made many changes, starting with reconstructing of Outer Kal'Urguan. I hired an entire high council, and I was able to maintain relationships with the other nations, with very few wars. Although many would say that now is a bad time to resign, I am getting old and I want to live the rest of my life freely. All of the stresses of being king have made my hair turn gray and my own beard is about to fall right off. I will be living the rest of my life peacefully in a home nearby. I hope for the nation of Kal'Urguan to survive forever with King Algrim and all of the kings to follow him. I hope to see all the dwarves again on my travels. Farewell!\n- King Belin", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of King Simppa", "SimppaFIN", "The Dwarven King, me, at least former one. Ah was just original dwarf who likes tae drink ale . Still ah was born to rule, or so they thought. When Ah finally became an King with kingdom, it was a surprise. Those citizens of mah, they meant lot of work tae me. Ah did nae like that. Never time fur mahself! Nae time with just me and mah  ale! It was very tiresome. Ah was hiding. Hiding from mah own kind. From mah brothers! When Ah was hiding, there was one dwarf, only one that took care of mah duties. Overseer Charles Grimlie. Good dwarf, if Ah might say. Time passed and Ah rarely did mah duties. Mah right hand man, Overseer took care of 'em. Until finally, Charles decided that he would be better King that Ah was! Ah gladly agreed with him. Council and other dwarves agreed, and so there was coronation. Ah gave mah crown away happily, there would be new, better era fur dwarves! Now Ah am nae King, and Ah travel around Aegis. Ah am still hiding, behind hood of mah. Hiding mah face from others. It is good solution. Ah can be no-one, with no past.. Only with the future... \n Former King Simppa \n Now.. Mah sickness.. Ah can nae take it.. Darkness is comin'.. Farewell.. Mah fellow brothers... We well meet agin'... Someday...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Lord Nairog Stark", "NairOG", "Entry One \nThe scout reports about the storm forming further north are disturbing. He described it as darkness.....blackness correctly. At first I tought cold got to him but when I saw his eyes I saw fear, fear of the unknown. After taking a rest he told me that he has a need to visit Cloud Temple of Aegis. \n \n \nEntry Two I asked Saint Daniel to join me for a meal and I told him what I found out the day before. We had a long talk and decided that I should continue building Outpost towers around the north bo rder.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Lym, the Hermit Mage", "Lymdil", "This is the Journal of Lym, the Hermit Mage. Kamees, 12th of The First Seed, 1331 \n My life.. it starts to be twisted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Micyn", "gaiusmarius8", "As intructed by my OrdenMarschall, I write this to give observation of the Ankabut This camp is quaint, but the men are worn from trying to defend, thus we believed it best to infiltrate and gain evidences for other more learned men to take into consideration it seemed these Ankabutkind are responding to the mass exodus, the many marching have awakened these spiders within the land and flustered, have sprung forth in anger they seem to consider us invaders and want only to throw us from these lands which they hold dear ...what is troublesome to me is how violently in throes they attempt... so numerous and capable of replenishing their numbers has led me to even attempt to seek entry and to investigate. Fighting alongside my brethren Cole and Kyle... we discovered vessels, fleshy eggs that squirm with the birth of their ranks and they come forth so violen.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Naelron Laethil", "XWolfSpearX", "I am Naelron Laethil and I'm going to explain a bit about myself. When I was young, my parents had died defending Laurelin. This had inspired me. I had wanted to protect people so they wouldn't lose their loved ones like I had. I decided to become a hunter and hone my skills so that I could later join the elven military This didn't exactly work out though, as one day, while I was hunting, I injured my leg. With the condition my leg was in, I couldn't hunt. This led me to reading, studying, and researching things in many different libraries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Neutral Grey", "KuroiHonoo", "This journal is a record of the events of a person named Neutral Grey. An odd name for the man who wishes to know all. A seeker of knowledge and wisdom. \n I will not begin at the begining, that is for another book I will write. I will, instead, begin at my journey to Haven. \n Earlier that week, I was at a structure devoted to knowledge, Cerlos' Library. It was there that I came across a journal, a book describing Haven. As I read, there was a line that caught my attention. It described a vast library, with all types of knowledge! Without a second thought. I left the town of Nalemtoff to seek this knowledge. \n I found the large road leading to Haven. I had gone to Haven one before, but unintentionally. \n The journey was long, but mostly uneventful. I stopped to collect meat from spiders once, but shortly continued. \n Upon my arrival, I was astonished. Not at the beauty of the city. But, instead, the ABSENCE of it! As I stand here writing this book, I can observe only a desert where Haven once stood. \n The only evidence of Haven, was a sudden stop in the road, and a few signs. On the signs read: The Ascended are gone. . .The Undead will follow. \n  Realizing this event, I wished to log it. Sadly I had no books. Suddenly, the Elven girl who also observed the same events, wished to know my story. She handed me a book, of which I began to quickly fill. \n I will now return to the town of Nalemtoff. There is much to do if we wish to complete it. Farewell reader. I fear danger in the future. -Neutral Grey     \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Neutral Grey II", "KuroiHonoo", "In this book I will desribe the creation of Nalemtoff. Nalemtoff is a small town not too far from Al Khazar. The goal of the town is to train people to work in the economy, but from what I see, it may have an unintentional more noble goal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Niko Althered", "RustyJusty123", "When I was a young boy I never got to see my family and I dont know if they are still alive . My family and I were taking by the Undead and brought into the Nether. I was separated from my family and that day on I never saw them again. There I was put to work, I was a smithy and had to craft weapons and armor for the Undead soldiers. Every day as I worked I would look up from my work place and see the Portal. I knew if I could get through there I would be free. One day I was able to sneak from my work place and up to the higher part of the Nether. I slipped past the soldiers and made it through the Portal. I quickly ran in one direction and kept running and didn't stop. I finnaly stopped at an Inn where they treated me well and I had a home. As time went by I started to forget wondering what happened to my family, but I knew I would never see them again.. I stayed strong and when I was able to head out on my own, I made my way to Alkazar. Through the years of being free I was able to work and earn a little money aswell. I couldnt find a home there so I made my way further North. I came across a church with a few men inside wearing light armor and a symbol on their backs in the shape of a \"t\". they welcomed me in and gave me something to eat and a place to stay.   The next morning it looked like they were going somewhere, they had their armor on and swords sheathed. I asked if I could help them in anyway but one man said \"Its to dangerous for you lad. You are young and need to stay here.\" Most of them left the church and went off. One man stayed and said to me \"Those men that just left might not live.  The Undead are numberous in the North. But im going to train you so that one day you too can finnaly help us.\" That day on I was trained: Strength and Speed. I became stronger and faster each day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of People", "The_Blind_Seer", "Princess Aliciana is the Pincess of Al Khazar \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Secrets", "Epic_Potatoe", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Seed Donations", "Nalayna", "This journal is to keep track of Seed Donations. I'll try to remember who  donated seeds in the previous weeks..... UAC (via several people, and once via Seventh who was the most creative giver so far), Overseer Maximillion (largest so far) Donation by Agathor . Seeds recieved from Viceroy Gropier via Bito. Seeds... Acquired... by Urasept. Another donation of seeds, brought by the Lanavarian Trade Advisor Destro. He brought twenty stacks and thirty seeds. He also brought the suggestion of a trade agreement with Ellesar for wheat since we've had so many problems lately. I've forwarded the suggestion to the Viceroy and King via letter. Eruza has donated seeds via Bito. More seeds donated from Seventh, who is now the largest donator.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Shamus", "hughlorin", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Sir Bito", "DarkSoundwave", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Sparrow", "Blood_Wolf213", "Day 1 Dear journal.  I have decided to make one to keep record of some of my journy's to reflect back when i want to. Somthing of a legends for my life to keep track of previous records. Anyway, Today i joined a group called Aegis Freedom Fighter's. They seem to be a peaceful group. But they will stand at arms against the undead armies moving in from the north which im glad to be apart of. There was a jumping course here that i passed my fourth try through. Impressive for me to catch on so early in my recruitment, I will be heading off now. I've got work to do now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Sparrow Part 3", "Blood_Wolf213", "Dear Journal, \n Day 3. I've decided to go by day's that i write in my jounal. Earlier today i was injuryed by the undead. I managed to get back to the keep to rest. Though two of the creature's made there way here. I dispatched them easily, only problem was the arrow's i've got in my arm. I removed it with ease. Now im heading off to journy these lands before heading back here. Im going to head off soon and keep my books with me. Wait, I heard something. But im the only one here at the moment, aren't I?", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of the Green Ravens leader", "Kamberli", "Ahad, 1st of The Amber Cold, 1309 \n Today I start my journey to the Northern Portals. I want to reach the Undead City to scout their plans. I stocked myself in Laurelin whit armor and food. It will be hard and dangerous. I hope I survive!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of the verge", "Pinsir99", "11/30/11 I have settled into my new house and am now gathering resources. Max has been very kind. I have also seen Availer's tomb.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of wolf part1", "Steelwolf19", "well we finally found a place to build. I traveled with a drawf trooper to this mountain we found a cave and have started to dig in it. I wonder why a harden trooper would want a petty monk Well it tis the first night. Still much to do we started to shape bed rooms and storeage I maybe a monk but I perfer the open lands of the forest over some fancy temple I wonder when and where shall I find that wolf that saved me at my birth. Till I find more ink", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of Zatina", "LukeZzO", "The island is expanding as we continue to gather more of a population - hopefully in a good way. However, everything can change. I hear thunder, and it seems like the undead are near all the time. Which is alarming, must I add. However, it does not bother me aslong as they do not hurt me. The current population though, is five. It consists of a dwarf and four humans, and there's still more to come. Hopefully. James is the farmer of the islands, Abe is the guardian, and I mantain the islands I guess. I bid you a farewell for now.", ""),
