        StaticBook("Kal'Urguans's idea's:", "CaliMkali", "Get rid of housin and replace it with fresh farms. Move all dwarf housin underground and build more rooms and appartements. sir anyone 'ave ideas Maximus said lakes and pools. any more ideas you denied me strong hold", ""),
        StaticBook("Kalak, Spirit of Water", "Ned_Lud", "I am Kalak, spirit of water. I laugh often to those who listen and those who look will find my golden eyes watching vigilantly from the darkest corners of the mind. My tanned and brutish form bears the scars and tattoos of many years at sea and my mind holds the thoughts and whispers of the lowest scoundrels.\n     I was once a cunning, orcish smuggler and cutthroat, working the alleys, ports and waterways of every major trade city in Aegis. The first man I ever killed, I opened his belly with a sword and the blood and guts flowed forth like a river, spilling off the slippery dock and into the sea. I filled him with stones and fed him to the fish, never looking back.\n     For years I murdered and looted along the rivers and coasts, honing my blades and notoriety. I became known to lesser men as \"Two Hands Black\" for the constant stain of squid ink, coagulated blood and filth on my calloused hands. Those who would become my enemy did not live for very long and there were never any friends in my line of work. Business contacts began to fear for their lives and it was only a matter of time before I woke up at the bottom of a river with a back full of arrows and a belly full of stones.\n     Ned Lud'Gorkil has called upon my spirit and I have answered, my words transcribed within this book through his own entranced hand. There is a dark strength in the warrior, patient as the still waters of the pond and dangerous as the raging storm that approaches from across the sea. I will guide him down this path of shadows and hold his head above the waters as his enemies drown alone in darkness.\n     My spirit may be called upon by the drowning of man or beast or by the offering of a dead man's possessions, thrown into the waters. Taking the ink of the squid onto one's body or weapon will give my blessing in stealth and combat. Rain is the time for meditation and prayer. I take pleasure in these things.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kalderon Info Sheet", "DeathofChrono", "AFF_1st Lieutenant_Kalderon 20 Male Monster hunter", ""),
        StaticBook("Kalderon's Little Black Book", "DeathofChrono", "\n      8 No\n 1 Maybe", ""),
        StaticBook("Kalen's Tomb of Travel", "501warhead", "x: -2417 \nZ: -644 \nKalen's Castle \nOn mountain", ""),
        StaticBook("Kallen's Biography", "ErcMan", "There was a dwarf named Kallen who searched for his freind Arthus who was", ""),
        StaticBook("Kalum's Diary", "Calum510", "Well, hello. I'm Kalum. I've had quite a... different life, let's say. Right now, I'm living in an abandoned fort, in the wilderness, up north somewhere. Let's start at the beginning. I was born in the snowy mountains, 21 years ago. My mother died at birth, my father when I was a child. I lived by myself, for a while. I barely survived. I was picked up by bandits, who forced me to do terrible deeds. Well, years later, on my 21st birthday, I escaped. Undead attacks were getting bad. But the things those bastards were doing were worse. I came to the kingdom of Aeris. After visiting the Cloud Temple, I went up king's road. I passed a small city, where I met some detectives, who go by the name of 'Holmes' Nice guys, they were. Up the road, however, slavers were waiting for unexpecting travellers! I was held at ransom, with a king's guard, and we were both ordered to pay 300 minas! I paid 200, but the guard refused to pay. We were forced to fight to death. I won the battle, but I'm not proud of it. A kings guard! I was set free, and I reported the slavers to Holmes. Good move, I say, and I continued on to the city of Oren. I met a man called DarkBringer, and we both came guards at the city of Oren. He also had a brother. I'll miss out the stuff of being a guard. Opening gates is very boring, however. However, my friends brother, Cedric Darkbringer, had found an abandoned fort, which had quite a lot of goodies, let's say. We ventured on further, and found a small fort, abandoned. We took refuge in it. Well, that's my story, up to this point. Kalum. Day 1 Well, today, a woman took refuge in the castle, for the night. I redirected her to the location she was meant to be headed, and she managed to get Kutul to join her cause, to take down the King of Oren. Betrayel, torure, all that stuff. Anyway, Kutul has joined the cause, and we've got a heeluva job to do... take down the king. Hey, if we do, we get to become Nobles, or Counts, or whatever, so it's a win-win situation! Kalum Day 3 Bingo! Lot's of iron :) Kutul has went into the woods, and hasn't resturned for a day. Getting worried... Day 5 (I think) Kutul still hasn't returned... oh dear :S Ok, I'll be down there in a jiffy UPDATE! I'm venturing to the city of Oren to see if he's there! Hello Sorry for the last line, talking to some guard who didn't recognize me, and wanted to kill me Just chilling in the city centre, hopefully my friend will come3 It's great being a (Former) guard, you can waltz into places a citezen can not. You just change your title! And bam! You'er a guard agian! :) Found Kutul he was waiting at the northern gate! it was a touching re-union... No it wasn't. Haha. One sec, gonna regenerate haelth Day ??? Well, we're back at the fort, after god knows how many days... Also, Kutul is out yes, it could! Sorry, talking to Kutul, wrote it down by accident Anyway... Just us 3, rollin' sorry, did it AGIAN! ANYWAY! We elected Kutul as our official leader! Hoozah! I'm terrible at talking/writing thing. I keep talking when I'm meant to write (Awkward) and write when I'm meant to talk (Annoying!) Anyway, only I should be reading this, and if you ain't called Kalum, then PISS OFF! Well, I have no idea what day it is, comlpetely lost track, so I'll just write down stuff when I feel like it. Ok, so here's what has been on my mind lately... Why are those that dress like the undead, or even are undead, quite a lot nicer than mortals like us? That has been on my mind lately. A man called Jack, an immortal, offered to lock our three chests for only 75 minas! Bargian I say. Oh well, uh... bye for now, I guess. Well, Kutul has went Oren and hasn't returned... Again. Me and Cedric are going to explre a fort he found. End of today's writings! :) Well, we've got a functional gate now! Got to break thorugh it if no one is there to let you in, however Bloody soulstone! I keep accidently teleporting to the city of Oren when I don't want to! And it's a long journey back. The x Co-ordinates are in the 2000's! That's deep into the northern fields, for people who don't know... not that there ARE OTHER PEOPLE. Baha, putting away a map while looking up from it at the same time looks cool! :) Holy shit, I'm easily amused... Just changed one of our farms to a reed farm, and reluctantly called it a sugarcane farm ... A rollback actually affected me! Lost some work Id been doing to the towers, and the walls. Also lost a lot of logs... :( Fnished work on towers, added glass, made one of our forms a sugarcane farm, cut down a load of trees and am working on the inside of the walls. Also locked Kutulu out of the fort and asked him 'Name, Buisness?' - thought that was pretty funny. :) I have FINISH the walls, and made the staircase to the castle significantly nicer. I'm going replace the dirt foundation with cobblestone in the morning. We're building an underground farm under the castle or somehing, due to it being build on a huge hole someone is staying for the night, a man called Redbain, very nice person. Accidently teleported to Oren, spending the night here. travelling back to the fort, hopefully I don't lose the diary on the way. Or journal. Or what ever the fuck you want to call it... Saw a pigman in the guild hall of Kutul's cause. lol What's the deal with oren and Alkhazar?? Can't they decide on one name!/ ? Music's playing, night up upon me. I should get home and stop writing in this book!! Accidently soulstoned to Oren... again. Awaiting a noble to come and do buisness. I've been warned to carry a weapon. Oh, and guess what? I'm on gate duty, again! :) Writing in here to pass the time should probably do something constuctive. Going to do something constuctive. Can't think of anything constuctive to do. Maybe I should use one of the watchtowers, to see if I can see the noble in the distance. I can't see the noble in the distance. All I see is trees. Standing on top of the gate. Will wait here for the noble. Waiting Waiting Bored I'm gonna put my diary away, I'm just filling these pages with crap. Still waiting, been a day now... Cedric's with the Noble, by the way. 20 pages of this stuff... Kutul is just standing next to the fountain Those zombies are starting to piss me off... Where is the NOBLE!?? Well, I just made contack with Cedric ((/tell Chumpchump)) and apparently, the guy we gave shelter to is a noble! Wow. Well, he's trying to make him come back here, so standing on top of the gate is pretty pointless, so I'm going to do some building to the dirt foundation.. af after a snooze... ZzzzZzzZZ... Just read through the diary, Wow, am I unorganizaed. lol They're actually coming! I'd been working on the fort and they contacted me! I'll tell you th Well, RedBain and Cedric are going off together, for a while. No buisness was done. We said our farewells, and they want off into the sunset. Exccept the sun was setting in the west, and they were heading east. I looked at the sunset for a while, nonetheless. It was sad to see him go. We said our farewells, and I hope for his safe return... Cedric returns! He found the 'New' undead base, and off to sell the co-ordinates, written in the book I gave him, to someone in Alkhazer/Oren! Cedric is back, and has been offered 1000+ minas for the book! Also, the 'basement' is nearing completion! Will have dungeons, guest rooms and a mine! Going to go 'Plunder' a few places with Kutul, dug up the path, as I need to do the basement roof. Hopefully he won't fall through a hole. Don't know what's going on, an undead follower and Kutul are doing something... I don't know. And I guess I won't ever know. He was writing something in a book, and the undead one was clogging up all the water flows in our mine. What the hell is going on! Hopefully it doesn't have anything to do with Cedric knowing the wherabouts of their new base. Kutul has a mingin permit, the farm that Cedric has built is awesome and I've finish the base ment! Still haven't got to the bottom of the 'undead Dealings' 'The guest will be here soon' Well, I heard Iblees. And I'm scared. Not sure about this 'Visitor' (The guy from before) I'll tell you how it gies down. I mean goes! :) - Killing, Slavery, Banditery, Stealing, Supporting Iblees, Torchering.... Well, I'm clogging up holes with an undead follower, Kutul's mining or something and Cedric's gathering food. So much for evil. Anyway, me and Cedric are keeping the co-ords a secret. Travelled to Oren, trying to get rid of the map. No luck (Yet!) Things are going fine.. no wait, better, since Gaarag came here. :)", ""),
