        StaticBook("Laurelin History", "fabian9696", "A powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of Laurelin's tree's. I met him at the cobblestone spires west of the Aegis temple. We set of on foot towards a mountain gorge i had come across that would as a natural barrier towards to our foe's Once we arrived, the druis wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch on his hip so often. He showed me teh seeds in said pouch, and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a shine very similar to glow stone. Whilst my brigade of builders built the city defence walls , The tree's to grow exponentially", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin Patrol", "Darkdragon274", "Mission Category: Reaper, Scouting \n Group Size: 1-2 \n Location: Laurelin and it's surrounding area \n Objective: Learn what you can about the activities of the Elven Vanguard \n Notes: Keep special interest in the activities of The Princess and her nephew Polcari. \n *The final page is adorned with a red-inked Spectre Symbol*", ""),
        StaticBook("Lava Element", "c_h_r_i_s121", "I thaught a good place to start my search for harnessing the power of lava would be in the temple So i swam through the seas to get there. I new it wouldnt be easy as lava created Aegis, but i had Dragga. I knew she could help me as she has the element of fire in her soul. I hadnt even left Krugmar yet and i was confronted bye a group of savage spiders. But they where no trouble for me, and i carried on my trip. I finally got there. I was tired, and cold after the long swim, but i sat in the middle of pool of lava ontop of a cold block of obsidion. I closed my eyes with my staff in hand and began to pray. I couldnt concentrait. I dont know why, normally when i meditate im compleatly relaxed. Some thing is wrong. I prayed harder, this time to Dragga to see if she could help me concentrait. She came to me, but she was not in Krugmar, she was in Haven. This must be where i should pra y ....I just heard some bad news.. It appears that Haven is no more, it has been destroyed, i am not sure why yet.. I will have to pray to Dragga again. Maybe be can give me some more information. \n This time she was in the cloud temple. I will travel there. It must be one of the fountains she wishes for me to pray at! Yes! Im here, the fountain of death. I thaught to my self, I must concentrait, I can do this. And with that i closed my eyes and sat down on the warm sandstone and began to pray to Dragga. This time i could concentrait with ease. Dragga took me to a weird place, it was very, very hot. I could smell the scent of burning bones. As we walked on for 5 minuets all i could see was red fog, i cant explain it. Kind of on a cold day when the clouds come from the sky. But it had been soaked in the blood of 2000 orcs. After another 15 minuets of walking through the hot gravil, i saw a silhouette through the deep red fog. \n I could see it was very tall, but thin, it had very long and pointy fingers. It had to be it, who else could it be but the Lava element himself. As we moved closer the temperature grew bye atleaset 15 degrese.  He had black slicked back hair, he was wearing a loin cloth wich was understandable in this heat. He was facing away from us as we walked towards him, you could see his spine bobbling out of his back, as he was so skinney. as we grew closer, he became awear of our presance and turned around. He asked ''What do you two want?'' His voice was astounding, it was so deep i could feel the vibrations through my tusks. I replied ''I seek the knowledge you have to offer, i want to harness you power, the power of lava.'' \n ''How can one mortal possess the power of lava? Do you know what its like to controll the power to create or destroy anything. '' \n ''Im willing to try.' ' \n ''The lava element nods his head and turns.'' He opend a chest that was behind him and pulled out a bucket of water, he breathes in harshley as the bucket must of been hurting him he quickly poured some water onto the ground and threw the bucket into the fog. He closed his eyes and started murmering to himself, and lava appeard from his hands he guided it towards the water and landed it ontop of the water .  A loud sizzeling sound echoed and water vapour filled the air. the mist cleared and stone was on the floor. He asked Dragga to mine it while i prayed for the power of lava, and getting ready for it. Dragga mined it and crafted it into a stone staff Dragga handed the staff over to the lava element. \n He knealed in a pool of lava holding the staff above his head, he said a and dipped it into the lava saying a prayer. He through the staff at me drenched in lava and I opend my eyes. I rubbed my eyes and I saw i was back in the cloud temple, I could feel a burning pain in my hand I looked down and i was holding the stone staff he had thrown at me, but i didnt drop it. I held it. The pain was his test, and i think i passed. \n I could feel the power in my new staff, it pulses in my hands   .  \n I must tell the others.", ""),
        StaticBook("Law Of Succesion", "Tythus", "The law of becoming a rex states clearly that the orc in question must be of high birth and defeat the current rex in unarmed combat if multiple people where to challenge the rex the power would be dived among them .................................", ""),
        StaticBook("Law, vs Religion", "Groundhawg", "Recently in Kal'Urguan there was a small rebellion. It was caused by the breaking of a law by a man named Chris. \n The law he broke was small, he sold goods that he produced from his home. Kal'Urguan law states that one can not make profit off their home, only designated shops. The guard of the city noticed his infraction, and came to his door. A small argument led to Chris ru nning away from the guard. The officer who was on the job called the guard together, before persuing. While the guard assembled, Chris ran to the chapel. He told the priests that the guard were out to kill him. The priests took him into their shelter, and went out to confront the guard. \n \n Now, here's where the story get's interesting. \n \n Eventually conversation broke down, and the priests retreated to the inner grounds, where the chapel lay. The guards managed to close the gates to the inner grounds in time to trap one (1), priest between the two gates. Now, the priest was TECHNICALLY a criminal by this point, they all were, because they were aiding a criminal escape the law. \n But should they have been classed as criminal? They were doing what their religion stated as correct! They were protecting the life of another. His life was being threatened! And law typically states not to interfere with religon. \n Eventually, after more failed negotiations, the priest was broken free, and returned to his brethren  \n \n but this LEGALLY only furthered the criminalization of the priests. Eventually, passed threats had the guard sitting outside the guardhouse and the priests in the chapel. With occasional negotiators passing accross to each other's side of the combatless battlefield of words. There was alot of shouting, and alot of ideas cropped up on both sides. Until eventually agreement was met, we would throw Chris out the gates, and banish him, never to return to Kal'Urguan. \n \n This still raises the question, how far can religion go, before law can or must intervene? Were the Priests right to protect Chris? Were the guard right to capture the priest? \n As it stands, the reached resolution worked, the priests excused of all crime. Though tension is very high between guard and priest. And argument often breaks out. \n \n \n \n  Thank you for reading. This has been a book by Gorund Nilcagith, Bard and Guardsman of Kal 'Urguan", ""),
