        StaticBook("Legend of the Mooshroom", "Jerry_Man", "I've always been a little wary of mushrooms. They grow like a parasite and give my tongue a tingly feeling when eaten, so I recommend them not to be trusted. They also seem to have a strange effect on animals that suffer fungal overexposure. \nStrange, other-worldly beasts were sighted moping around freakishly large mushrooms by a Dark Elven group of explorers. In a report back to the Druids they had named the beasts 'Ilythalim Armenyk', however the Sage Druid felt that a more relatable name would be required, whether the beasts truly exist or not. He named them 'Mooshrooms' and declared the mushy bovne a protected species in the event that someone might actually discover one. \n \nThese events were transcribed to me by a hooded Dark Elf who appeared on my doorstep, never mentioned a name and dissappeared into the evening fog.", ""),
