        StaticBook("Leoni's Blade", "moop123", "What  hold in my hands is not just a simple Diamond sword. It has a history. It went through generation after generation to get to me. And this is its story. On a cold dark night In Laurelin a man by the name of Gregory Johonas was mineing and found 2 diamonds. He was very exited and his heart lept ! He was going to be rich once he sold these. but then... They shon. A strange green lite was beaming into Gregor's eyes and as he looked deeper into the Diamonds he saw a figure. What looked like a baby. A baby with a strange symbol on its four head. Later on that day he found a broken stone sword. With the handle lying on the left of him and the blade on the right. He wondered if he could make a diamond sword the same way stone ones were made. He went right back into the mine and took those diamonds. Attatched them to the broken handle and had the strongest wepon since dwarven war axes . It was 100+ years later and his son hade just turned 150", ""),
        StaticBook("Leoni's Tale", "moop123", "In the land of Hakashiri lived an Elven tribe know as the Siki . Leoni Grew up there learned to walk and talk. Untill the age of about 10 . Two weeks before his 10 birthday his tribe was attacked ! By a band of Orcs . They burned down the village and killed all but Leoni and his younger sister... They fled the town together and escaped by boat . They sailed for year untill Leoni was about 15 me ?", ""),
        StaticBook("Leoni's Tales", "moop123", "In the far away land of Hatiki . There lived an Elven tribe by the name of Hanakea . I (Leoni Johonas) grew up there learned to read and write . To walk and talk . Untill 2 weeks before my tenth birthday ... Are town was invaded by a band of evil Orcs . Me and my little sister were the only ones left alive . All the huts burned to an ash . Me and my sister managed to flee . We sailed away from our land . Hoping to find a new one . We sailed and sailed for years on end untill i reached the age of 15 . We found the land of Freedonia where we settled . 2 years later it happened again . My younger sister was assasinated . By what seemed to be the same band of Orcs . I ran and ran, I had no choice . Then i stumbled upon the land of Aegis ! When i exited the cloud temple i could only imagain what opportunity i would find in tihs wonderfull land . I joined a group of people called the Wolvarines (i was now 18). They provided me with a home . And there i could use my profesion . Baattle ! Today i am doing very well for my self . Who knows what my next advenutre will bring me ? Only time will tell . THE END long*", ""),
        StaticBook("Lesson 1 The Tomb Of Krie", "redbaron", "\n I will start by asking if anyone has seen it.  Then if anyone knows about it i will ask them them what they know about it.  Although i do expect that many many people will say no.  I will then discuss the story of Krie and i will write it down here for further memory. \n Krie was a undead inquisitor.  He struck fear in the hearts of many citizens of aegis.  Although many beleived he was more then just an inquisitor but iblees right hand man himself.  Although none of this is proved and never will likely be proved.  As some of you may or may not know the tomb of krie is in the area.  Not far from here infact.  The tomb is covered by an ancient evil \"protection.\"  Apparently there is a certain room where this evil is most strong. Thought enough talk about this.  I will show you part of this tomb \n Then i will take them to the tomb and show them only the first entrance. After answering some questions if they have any i will finish the topic by saying you would do well to remember this lesson.  Also a very important think to remember is water!  That concludes this lesson.  Be safe my young mages.  Then i will leave them to ponder what they've learned", ""),
        StaticBook("Lesson on Balance; Ogland", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Ahad, 15th of Suns Smile, 1340 \n*\n \"Can anyone tell me what the main thing the Guild wishes to uphold is?\", asks Archmage Ogland \n*\n Apprentice Jon responds: \"Balance?\" The other apprentice Elindor speaks an Elvish term: \"Meracahe\". \"It's an Elven word for balance of all things, both light and dark, this world and beyond\", Elindor proceeds to explain. \n**\n Ogland speaks again: \"Balance, more tricky than it seems.\" He then asks the student by my side - Algrim - to tell him anything he may of the balance. Algrim re collection fails him, and Ogland answers: \"Now then, the balance is upholding in yourself, not choosing sides is a good example\". \"Although it is not the only thing, but the easiest to explain. I have seen it many times in the Guild\" he adds shortly after. \n*\n \"Does anyone here know of Cataris?\", Ogland poses to the class. Everyone ventures what they have heard, or know of. Soon it is learnt that Cataris was the Guildmaster for the Human branch of the Mages, before making the mistake of leading a frontal assault against the Undead. \n*\n As a result the Undead retaliated by damaging the Mages' Tower and was the cause of the death of one Archmage Bell. The effects deeds have on the future is briefly discussed, and the term 'ripple effect' is used to summarise. \n*\n Elindor proceeds to tell the class a story, after being granted permission from Ogland: of his encounter with an Undead by the name of Vardak, whom Elindor prevented from dueling one called Safen. Vardak nonchalantly left the scene, having told Elindor he would fight those who confronted him. Intervening before the fight could take place prevented the fight from occuring altogether. \n*\n The moral was that if the Undead were not directly challenged, so too would their offensive be lessended. \n*\n A debate ensues over the Undeads role in keeping balance, and whether their existance permits balance to exist. \n*\n Points such as the threat of the Undead have united Aegis are made, and counter-arguments using the pain, suffering, and fear the Undead cause as leverage. \n*\n After the class is dismissed the discussion continues among the apprentices. It seems to be ag reed that the Undead are too close to realising their goal. \n*\n*\n Scribe: Dio Astore", ""),
        StaticBook("Let our Kings rule high.", "Ruakik", "Let our King's rule high. \n Perched on the mountain top \n In the trees, \n In the valleys. \n Let our king's rule High! \n Strength and devotion to them. \n Let our king's, \n Waiting, \n Let our King's Rule High!", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "SerahLove", "", ""),
        StaticBook("letter", "similan", "Hello Orison my name is Similan. I can see you are incharge of the farm. While you where away I helped your farm by picking up some wheat and replant it. If you think I need to give it back to you please feel free to say. PS I live down the hill.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter : To whom it may concern", "Agith", "If you are reading this letter, it means that most likely I Agith amberlance am no more. I ask that, if I once knew you, that you do not mourn over my death . I do however, have a favor to ask of you. I have a son, his name is Malin. Please, if you are able raise the boy proper, his life has not been one of ease and comfort. I can only give you two locations where he may be, that is the scholar district in Kal'Urguan, or in Al'khazar. He is much like myself in the sense that he loves to read and write. Please, take up the boy and raise him well, teach him to defend himself. Though never introduce him to such violence. I do not wish the life I have, to be placed onto his shoulders. Only, when Malin comes of age to be 50. Are you to reveal my existance and my past relations with the chosen few ascended. He is not to know that he is of their bloodline until he can handle it. He has very light blue eyes, and last I saw, was rather tiny. I sent him several lovely garbs on his 2nd birthday. I can only hope that he has grown into them and adorns those garbs. I bid you farewell, in the hope I may speak with you one day. Today, is not that day. Thank-you. Sincerely, Agith Amberlance. : I would like to say that, he is not an amberlance. ... I have only recently come to learn of my fathers last name. Though, I wish for him to take up the name of the one who takes him in. Once again, thank-you...May Aerial be with you all the days of your life. (( Kay.", ""),
        StaticBook("letter for danyn", "ariczzz1892", "hello my friend, i just returned from farming and will be heading to the gauntlet now. only wanted to put the probably first letter in your box. \nsee you soon, Arican", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter for Discordian", "Pepernoot", "Hail Discordian,\n I saw your house isn't locked. I am able to make some basic locks for you. \n I live in the library to the south. Contact me there if you want some locks. \n -Cerlos \n P.S.  I made this mailbox for you, I saw you didn't have one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Auckes ~", "Xanivic", "Hello, friend! As you can see, I've installed a few mailboxes around town, which should increase communication between us. I sent you this letter in order to inform you of my departing. It may be temporary or perhaps may be postponed to a later date. The purpose of this is due to me forming a crew - a fleet clan/faction. I'm going to inhabit an abandoned city with decent infrastructure and amazing architecture. It goes by the name of Adradrome. It's far north. I've already informed Aquilus of the citie's wonderful architecture, and a splendid port that will be used for my sailors and thieves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Bito", "DarkSoundwave", "Hail Shoi, I'm writing to you today to inform you of a dream that Wyvernos thinks is a sign of impending doom. Last night when I was asleep I dreamt I was surronded by undead... All kinds of horrible monsters. My sword was glowing white and I was wearing white robes... I cannot describe the robes further. Eventually they overwhelmed me and I was leaning against a tree hearing a woman's voice telling me not to give up that all of Ageis needed me. The voice was beautiful beyond words. It had a havenly like call to it. I awoke shortly after the tip of my blade glowing white as if I had called forth something in my sleep.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Dio: Absence", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Joma, 34th of The Deep Cold, 1341 \n*\n If the event of myself failing to attend a class should take place - something I shall do my utmost to avoid - I, by means of this letter, request a recording to be made of the lesson so that I may not lose on the knowledge it will provide. \n*\n A memory spell would be most apt if it can be afforded. A scribed summary will suffice as well if need be. \n*\n (( OOC: Some screenshots of the chat dialogue or an in-game book.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Felune", "Ep152", "Bawapy, Conell. I am Felune. I must tell you something. I know how to save Ademas. His soul was ripped to pieces. Those pieces exist. They are four pieces of his life scattered around the world. First you must start with his birth and his childhood. I believe you are smart emough to know where to go for that.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Thistel", "Thistel", "To Appolan [.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Recomendation for the immidiate promotion of Oren Guard Tamara", "begginfokillz", "this report is written by Dimitri Krechenko of the Anti-Undead Clan Guardians Oren Guard Recruit Tamara, whilst off duty, fought valiently & with distincition while aiding the clan \"Guardian\" He using, his expertise in the fighting of the undead Menace, fought in the frontlines of a battle he, Using his finess in Diplomacy, Tried to make an allience with the clan SA however, in said diplomatic action, Tamara & myself (Guardian Recruit Dimitri) were taken prisoner of SA and they tried to forcibly conscript us into their evil ranks however, Tamra stood resolute, and made an effort to keep the peace He, with effort, stood firm with his alliegence to the Oren Guard, and when things turned sour, fought with distinction and was an example of truth, justice, and ord these actions were wittnessed by the mighty Guardians Sertok and Dimitri. it is with great honosty & pride that I, Dimitri Krechenko, do hereby recomend, as a fellow warrior against the undead, that Oren Guard Tamra, for great honor in battle, vallient efforts,m and professionalism, do be herby be promoted in the Oren Guard signed this day, Dimitri Krechenko & Sertok", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter signed by Dio", "Relinquo_Angelus", "I and Strife have gone hunting to the East. We will return before long.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Atriana from Exaroz & Ratheldros", "Exaroz", "Janos. A liar if you ask me. This man lies about everything. He takes credit for my and Ratheldros' deeds. He threatens to fire us from the guards. He treats us like rats and acts like he's done more for the guard than us. We've been in three wars. He's been in less. About capturing criminals, we've done Al'Khazar a bigger favor than him. First it was the one  that tried to murder someone. We caught him after chasing him through return to the city for many hours. Then we drowned him on Atriana's orders. Let's not forget the undead he wanted to keep  in prison. That man was sick, he ripped out his eyeball for crying out loud. He ate a part of his own arm, and then ofcourse under Janos' watch he gets lose and we have to chase him halfway to Alstion and then kill him. After that he YELLS at us for killing him. The undead was running to the undead tower for Gods sake! A couple of days later me, Ratheldros and Skril take care of this lawbreaker that actually disrespected Horen's grave! He also ran on the rooftops, ARMED. We chased him, I warned him two times and then shot him since he didn't stop. After that Ratheldros return to the city. Moments later I find Janos yelling at him because he said that Ratheldros had let in a man in a dark hood even though he himself had done it. So we started escorting them through return to the city, nothing happened. But Janos gets pissed and starts yelling at us, that's when it snapped for Ratheldros, he couldn't take it anymore. He proceeded to yelling back at Janos, telling him what a corrupt guard he is; lying, taking honor for others deeds, acting like he's the Lord of the Oren Guard itself. That's when Janos told us he'd have us fired, and started asking people higher ranked than him to fire us. No one did thatSo he decided to find Atriana and Felix. But he didn't, and now he keeps harrassing us and saying that we're going to be killed  by Felix and fired from the guard. My conclusion is that Janos can not be trusted with the position as a guard. He abuses his position bossing over all the recruits and yelling at them when he makes mistakes. He acts like he is the King of Oren or something, it's disgusting. If you by any chance take his side, and listen to all his lies and actually fire us, we wish you good luck defending Al'Khazar with that man on your side. Kudos to you if you manage to pull that off... \n  \nDue to recent events he apologized to us. We were on the brink on accepting the apology When Captain Felix walked in. He had misunderstood what we talked about and thought we had called Janos a Heartless bastard and a dog who follows orders. Now Janos didn't decline this. We were REALLY close to get fired, but we didn't. (No thanks to Janos). He turned out to be a two-faced jerk. So with this report. Me and Ratheldros turn in our resignation. We're tired of being treated like shit by Janos, Alliances and Felix. We deserve better. We've done so much for this Guard Force, and we're underrated, we're non-paid recruits who can't do anything when anyone treat us like crap. So thank you Atriana for being the only one in the Oren Guard who haven't treated us this way. You have been a great leader for us. \nFarewell, and good luck. \n ~Exaroz & Ratheldros", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Auckes", "Green_Mind", "Excellent work with the mailbox-system, I am most pleased with this development. I am sad to hear of your departure, yet the knowledge of your plans takes care of that. I am highly interested in this abandoned city, you simply must show me it sometime. Know that there will always be room for you in Shallowfield. Should you permanently leave us, your house will be made into a library. I'm sure you'd agree. \n - Von Hollow", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Auckes", "PwnCaiks101", "I love the library.I visit this place when i am bored and i really enjoyed your stories .I brought my son here too,to admire the library also.I hope you havt noticed  but someone raided your farms in town and buildings,Maybe that should be fixed sometime around! I would like coordinates to this city you found also! Sounds amazeing! \n  \n  \n \n ...ah yes now i remeber what i wanted to say .Any way i could help? \n \n \n Orodreth Anacline and his son.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Bell", "Ep152", "Bell, I am back. My soul was restored to its rightful place, and I am once again in the living world. While trapped in the sword, I had to witniss all the things my physical body did. The horrors he committed against you. And I want to say, I am deeply sorry to have gotten you involved. I hope you can forgive me and maybe come to Wilder Farm for one more visit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Callum", "luchian", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Charon ~", "Xanivic", "OOC: Might I inform you that what you did is powergaming. I didn't give you coordinates to this location, yet you find it. It's not the easiest location to find. Also, you went through my chests, and took things that didn't belong to Libertas. Items which I obtained on my own, without commiting any theft. Before I report this, if needed, I'd like to settle this without an authority. And for the books that you obtained - I did NOT leave ANY of my books in a tower in Adradrome. There is no way you could've obtained those books without powergaming/metagaming. This is urgent, and needs to be taken care of NOW. ( I'm sure you'll get this letter via spawning it or something of that nature. )", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Ebs", "Pepernoot", "\n \n \n \n \n \n \nHail Ebs\nI found some strange text a while ago, and I hope you can decipher it, or know someone who can. My guess is that it's old Elven, but I don't know for sure. The text was \"Op'em kan. Len ioe Letho\".\n \nAnyway, how are your breweries doing? I hope I can order some ale soon, as my barrels in my cellar are as good as empty.\n \nBest regards,\nCerlos Ithelias.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Enor", "Sir_Wyvernos", "Dear King Enor, you suck. Love Everard. XOXOXOXOXO Alright its good", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Fae", "moop123", "Dear Fae, Remember me ? I helped you on your 1st day in Aegis. I have found love for you. I heard your home town was destroyed by undead and i feared the worst. For weeks i have been searching for oyu. But please if your reading this. Contact me as soon as possible. yours truely Leoni Johonas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Goregath (From Josiah)", "JoeqMafia", "Hello! I like your mailbox! I just noticed it now. I like the idea of having a mailbox. Think of the possibilities. We should have a meeting about every house haveing a mailbox. We can use it for taxes and invitations! \n From Josiah, Town Mayor", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to High_Commander_Storm", "whiteberry14", "Im sorry about leaving...  I had something in my power that I needed to deliver to someone far in north... Now that I had finished my job... Im back to oren... I have a house in Alstion Town and I was wonder ing if I can rejoin S.A now Im back... Im very very sorry but the King left me this task to me and I couldn't deny it... Please forgive me... Your friend... Edward_Talbot...", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Indelwehn", "Minnan1", "Dear Indelwehn: \n If this letter arrives intact, make the honors of naming Twilin \"Laurelin Postman\" \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to James the Oren Guard", "angmar1", "title Letter to James the guard Can't come right now but if you don't know im always watching you and you can't see good luck finding me with best regards Stranger....", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Kiffe", "459pm", "okay. urm....this is a reply. i have allreddy set up a newspaper office to get weekly news for 150 minas a  month!!! 4 issues for 150 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Kiffe", "Mercius", "Dear Kiffe \n\n After finding your letter I have since created my own mailbox, feel free to post me letters in the future. This is a genius idea and I salute you for presenting it to me. \nYours sincerely, Tyraelius.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Lucius", "lcflaherty97", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Ragunthos ~Auckes", "Xanivic", "~~~~~ Aye! I see you have a liking for the mailbox innovation. I believe I'm going to hold off on the faction forming, and focus more on a new profession. Thieving will still be a part of me, yet I'm going to get more involved with something more social friendly, hahaha. So, do not worry of my departure, it won't be anytime soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Respiren", "huwbert98", "Hail Respiren \n I was wondering  if you wanted to come to Turin's and My New home. You would be the first guest round and i would like to show you around and have a meal. If you do accept this invitation send me a messager bird (/t huwbert98) and we can arrange a day. \nFarewell for now Huwel", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Rhisereld", "sgtteddybear59", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Salmeer", "Kiffe_Y", "Hail, Salmeer! Just testing the Mailbox. Its a nice idea to hve mailboxes in the houses, isnt it? it would be even better if we had someone to deliver the letters. This way, we would talk to people from distance, with a little cost. Imagine you talking to someone in Laurelin, or any other city, without leaving Oasis...? Anyway, reply to this letter when you recieve it! -Kiffe", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter To Sean", "Thatpyrodude", "There is a woman named Ivrae \n She must die \n She is crazy and destroyed alstion \n Signed, Banok Gray \n \n Enjoy the knifes they are worth 10,000 Minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Shoi", "DarkSoundwave", "Dear Shoi, I'm writing to you to inform you that your welcome to move into Alras.  I've spoken to King Syrio and it would be a huge honor for you to live here. I personally hope you will move in so I can learn more from you. I cannot seem to get the tree out of my head nor will the dreams stop... I've had many a sleepless night from them... They seem to be getting worse. This last one I saw the tree fully grown and on fire. I saw you with a small child crying as undead swarmed around the tree cheering. I fear this is an omen of something to come. I'm hoping eventually I can speak with ye about the dreams and meet the man Gaven that ya spoke of in our last talks. Thank you for the time - Sir Bito Minesmasher.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Tamara", "darkjames", "\"Dear Tamara, I know who you are, in these last minutes of life, I recognize that....you're my Father, I know so much we been trough, and I will never forget you...Hail....Dad... \n-Vikram", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to the Arcane Mage", "Archmage_Cataris", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to the Archbishop", "Gropier", "Dear Archbishop - It is with great sadness that I write this letter. I must respectively resign my position as a priest here at the temple. Earlier this month, I recieved notice that my father has passed beyond the veil.   He had been ill for quite some time.  My family is at a great loss of such a noble dwarf.  As one of four sons, I have been entrusted with one quarter of his lands and fortune. I have received a large parcel of land and the title of Lord of Dagumba.  Consequently, my attention is needed elsewhere and I can no longer remain in Kal'Urguan. Please accept my resignation and remove me from the temple roster.  -- Sincerely, Gordok Yon Hammer, Lord of Dagumba", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Tyraelius", "Kiffe_Y", "Hey Tyraelius, just wrote this letter to ask why dont you have a Mailbox. so, WHY DONT YOU HAVE A MAILBOX?? its an nice way to communicate. make one. now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Valon", "DarkSoundwave", "Dear Valon, When yer able to please seek me out signed Sir Bito", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to W.Jones from Elsa Smyth", "tomsim9611", "Dear Mr Jones, I am sorry that you have gone through all this trouble to contact me . The reason i never let Tom near our child was not because i did not want him to help me raise Richard. But it was because i was already married. When Richard was concieved i was very drunk. My husband still thinks to this day that Richard is his own. And i would like to keep it that way. Tom seemed like a nice man and in another life perhaps things with him would've worked out but i am married and i won't ruin my family for Tom. Good Day to you Sincerly Mrs Elsa Smyth", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter: To Whidoc", "braner321", "((Whoever I give this too, just pretend you sent it off. Theres 100 minas in it for you if you RP it.)) Dear Whidoc, \n I have sent this letter to you as a request that you come to the land of Aegis. I have settled down in a nice town of other halflings that I know you will come to like. There is plenty of room in my house for us both to live. I know that your interest in Magic is great and I would like to tell you that this land is full of Magic. Here, you may be able to study it further and maybe even become as mighty as The Wandering Wizard, Availer. He is the mightiest in all of the land. You make me so proud my son. I will always love you. I hope to see you soon. \n Your Loving Father, \n Biodoc Goodbody  .", ""),
        StaticBook("Letters and reading: A Guide to Literacy", "Ohaythar121", "Hail! I'm Sillion Luthais. Many across this beautiful land of Aegis lack the skill of literacy So, using this guide, you can teach anyone to read, write, and enjoy the literary world \n First, one needs to learn the basic letters, and their sounds So, help them read, and memorize the following letters, and sounds A- aaaa B- Buuh C- Cuuh D- Duuh E- Eeh F- Fuu G- Guuh H- Huh I- Ie J- Juuh k- Kuuh L- Luuh M- Muuh N- Nuuh O- Oooh P- Puuh Q- Quh So on, and so forth \n make sure to use repition, if they can't memroize the letter and sounds, there's no use! THis means teaching to end a sentence in a period, and teaching them tqhat a sentence is! \n Alright friends, that's it, using these tips, and the guide, you can teach anyone to read write, and become a good member of society, good luck, and be safe in your travels \n ,Sillion Luthais", ""),
        StaticBook("Levaticus Information Sheet", "guyplayingpc", "Race: Dwarf, Age: 23 Gender: Male Role in the AFF: General/Commander", ""),
        StaticBook("Lex's Journal", "Lexperiments", "To whoever is reading this: Hello. I am Lex of Kal'urguan, and this is the journal of my accomplishments and what I have done. I will mark down everything important to me here; and if you find this book, all of the secrets are now yours. \n On the first day that Kal'urguan opened to all, I was the first to come in the new doors. I was the first to experience the wonders of the lava lakes and the castle blocking out the molten fire. It was an amazing experience, truly. \n \n A while later, a demon appeared in Kal'urguan- the fabled Herobrine. Me and some of my brothers dealed with it quickly. Personally, I wanted to study it, but the others used it as a petting zoo. The wizard himself came ot look at it, and before long, both were gone. Sad, really. \n \n While it was still there, me and two fellow dwarves went to other civillizations to spread the news. We all went to the human land, then split paths. The other two went to the elves, where one was captured and barely got away, while I went to the orcs and found that their leader was missing. Around this time, the Kal'urguan farm was finished.  \n \n The king was missing for a long time, and finally he decided to give up the throne. Our overseer, Charles, became the new king. As I'm writing this, he remains our leader and is doing well. I watched the ceremony. It was truly great. Sadly, I never became part of the council... \n \n A while later, me and a friend saved up funds to buy a house. I am writing this book currently from our property, which is behind the Kal'urguan castle and next to the giant, iron anvil that can fix anything. In this house, I found an amazing secret; While trying to mine through the walls, I destroyed some stone and came upon a huge cavern, that expanded all the way around our city! It was completely abandoned and unknown, but there was one odd redstone contraption that did nothing in there. I eventually showed Charles. \n \n Since then, I've been relatively poor. I'm now writing about the present, for- wait! I completely forgot to talk about another topic. Forget I never wrote this paragraph, whoever is reading this! \n \n Before the ceremony, I also established a trade route with the elves, by myself. I still don't understand how I didn't get the archbiship position... I also built a makeshift road between our two kingdoms.  \n \n Now, it is the present. I'm pretty poor, making a living however I could. Er, can. Why must there be no way to erase pens? Anyways, I'm writing this book now in my spare time. I'll add more if...anything happens. I sure hope it does. Oh, also, a new floating dwarf city has been created. How did they manage to make it fly!? \n \n THE UNDEAD ARE HERE, THE UNDEAD ARE HERE! One day after I created this book, the undead attacked Winterfall. WE ARE ALL GOING TO DIE. The sky rained with fire and lightning, and Winterfall was destroyed. Another human town was, too. The next night, nothing bad happened... That's a good sign. No one knows what will happen. All efforts have gone to defence. This might be the end of Aegis... I believe only one person can help us. The Aengul Wizard, Avalier... \n \n This will probably be the last time for a while I write in this journal. Kal'urguan is under complete lockdown. I must escape through the mines. There will be a way... I hope so, anyways. Goodbye, the greatest city in Aegis \n \n Maybe that wasn't my last entry... I came back to Kal'urguan about 5-7 days after I left. Many things happened in this time. For one, I went to Al'Khazaar to escape my imprisonment. And when I arrived, guess what - The undead attacked. I was one of the two dwarves who survived the battle. It was amazing. After the battle, many came to know what happened. The Wandering Wizard himself explained that we need to find the Ascended to defeat the Undea. Damn pens. I meant Undead. \n \n I stayed there for a while, but then two elves had a private meeting with the Human Queen. Of course, I had to eavesdrop from a safe distance. I found out that Laurelin somehow had turned evil. One of the elves was taking a journey to Kal'urguan. Me and another spy went to follow her. The other one knew her and was caught. I, on the other hand, at least it seems, wasn't caught until the end. The other spy had actually approached her first. They started talking,a nd I listened in plain sight. They knew I was listening. They explained what that \"evil\" was- an evil orginization called the \"Dark Brotherhood\" or somethign like that that had inflitrated the Laurelin council. Then they threatened to make Charles kill me if I didn't leave. So I left, and came to my room where I am writing this in now. I'm going on another journey. Where to this time? Laurelin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lhug Gul", "Sode1", "Rana, May Malin be with you, You have found the book of the Dragon whisperers In this book you will find powerfull spells and attacks to kill or disable your enemies . First let me start with \"The Roar\" The roar can only be used by whisperers or dragons themselves The roar is used to knock all opponents out around you, and can be used only once a day, for it tires the user. Another attack used commonly by undead or ascended is the Fireball Everyone can use this spell, though the whisperers can use it without a staff simply yell \"Lhach Paur\" A small warning: never use the fireball when inside the fireball at close distances is extremely dangerous and will instantly kill your enemy . Now the next attack is rather powerfull, and can only be used by whisperers , It is \"Song of the Rider\" It is a long and loud song,a tradition amongst whisperers The song is mostly elvish though there are some dragon words in it, Before using this spell make sure you have no wood or wool nearby \"Lach Nar Kimbatu, Lach nar Paur, Paur Talan Panas\" and then the spirit of Montagh whil take your voice and you will continue to sing without having to be conscious *The page seems to have incomprehensible patterns beyond this point*", ""),
        StaticBook("Liber Anima de Saviticus", "Saviordude", "*Opening the book, you see page upon page of delicately etched gyphs and runes, all shaped into circles within circles. Flippin through the pages, you get the sense that the book is alive. Looking at the name, it dawns on you: This book contains Saviticus's soul. You wonder what to do with it....*", ""),
        StaticBook("Liber Mortuorum", "redbaron", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Libertas Housing Laws", "tomsim9611", "Law 1: Plots must be purchased legally from any of the founding fathers. Law 2: Plots can have any type of building on that the owner wishs. errrm Law 3: Any illegal structures shall be removed and the owner punished accordingly. e.g. Iblees shrines, out of era builds. Law 4: No entering houses or plots without the owners prior permission. Law 5: Do not damage other people property, if you break this law there will be extreme consiquences! All violations shall be dealt with by the founding Fathers. Charon, Tom Hawkinson and Friar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Library watch list", "Jallentime", "Dom the High Elf from Whisper isles: A beautiful girl I might add.", ""),
        StaticBook("License", "tnfccrew", "I, Dalien Glaft, Give permission to Juliana to Kill the animals in our farm. *rushes to his office *steps back, startled My!", ""),
        StaticBook("Lief-Montagu's 2nd Journal", "Rivendog", "Hang on \n Day 6 \n I met caleb at oren. He said he must hurry. He kept mentioning his group and who was captured.. I'm confused. I heard him mention \"good thing we aren't at war.\" Rest break is over... \n Day 7 \n we went to cilistine? We are right now in his cursed friend's house. He had a large collection of books. will return later. This guy has a study full of everything. Going to try to grab some of the books. the books are fake. \n Day 8 \n I left the house. Now heading to cilistan again. To gather information. I don't understand is my friend evil? or good? I made it to cilistan. Found a sign saying to myla'sland.. I found 2 cells.... I wonder. I found the trone and only 2 people \n Day 9 \n Cassie's Land is actual a very pleasent place. It's just that it's so far north I thought.. nvm.. I'm still not sure what Caleb was spying on in oren. Cassie's land is a very strong fortress. Nothing can get past these walls. Maybe around though. Tomorrow I'll Hopefully found the nether base. I have no blocks", ""),
        StaticBook("Lief-Montagu's 3rd journal", "Rivendog", "Day 10 \n I found a explorer willing to take me there. We are heading there now he isn't saying much. There is the distance is a gaint floating nether rock base with some lave flowing down from t he sides We are currenctly trying to find a way in. Maybe if we had enough (lag) and do the block stacking (glitch). We can make it. true It is time to leave this place...Sadly. uhhh", ""),
        StaticBook("Lief-Montagu's Journal", "Rivendog", "brb help delete", ""),
        StaticBook("Lieutenat barons journal", "redbaron", "This is my journal, i will write down everything in my travels on here. i hope to pass this onto other people so that my story and mistakes are recgonized and pray that no one will make the same mistakes i will make. Humans, we are a race of strong pride and are an arrogant race. I've have killed 14 bandits now, i can remember each one. ending a life with my hands. I have just found a nice little town, Wondering if this new place could be a new buisness place, maybe there looking for a guard to be set up? they have found me, people burning, they have surrounded the city. theres no time i must leave this place and never return ive brought them to these innocent people.  The undead have arrived", ""),
        StaticBook("Life As A guard", "Onslaughted", "Life as a guard is very fun. even here as the cpt of the Guards in Whisper Isles if you wabr. if you want to join ask the lord_tyrion or me and we will talk about it and to be a guard you always have to be active. Are you active?", ""),
        StaticBook("Life as a Warrior", "MuckyD121", "title Becoming A Warrior", ""),
        StaticBook("Life As An Apprentice.", "sgtsomebody", "Hmm... LIfe has been very rough as an apprentice I have made multiple staffs for my master, The_Forgotten_One. But I have a feeling this will all lead up to me becoming an undead. Oh boy how much i wish to become an undead soon. I will have to kill an ascended. Bhorner is my target in mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life in an undead prison", "Bgrape", "I have been trapped here trying to save someone from the prison.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life inside the FoA Headquarters", "Garretty", "As I first entered the headquarters, I was warmly welcomed by a guard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life is a gift.", "Tomurohen", "When we were born, we have been gifted with something that has intrigued people since the beginning of time: life. You may think, silk, feathers or a small butterfly is fragile, but nothing can break so fast as the life of a being. So if you read this, stranger, in good or in bad times, be aware of that what never left your side, that what will always be with you, no matter what do you, no matter what choices you make, untill the moment you pass away, your life is your best friend. Don't throw him away, don't make misuse of your life, because in the end, when life takes revange in the Open Fields, you will regret it with every fiber in your body. Take care of it, give it everything it needs and you will be repayed greatly. Written by Thokul The Wise. ((ok throwing a book, hoping someone will take care of it lol help", ""),
        StaticBook("Life is like a river starting high in the clouds but then becomes worthless when it reaches t", "coopermar", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Journal of Thorknor", "MrJakKiD", "My Master Is Dead.. Im Lonely Now.. BloodBlade is Gone.. I Must Go To Aegis and Find out Who I Am. I am In Aegis.. Its Beautiful. Im in The 'Cloud Temple' So its called.. I met another Elf His Name was Eridhian.. We are becoming good friends I was involved in a Battle today.. Eridhion is.... Dead *Page Is Torn off* I was Injured by an Undead untill A Human found me and Probably saved my life I was Saved By A Guard called Niko Wow.. Niko is an amasing Chap were becoming the best of friends!! After a Few Torn Pages the book states.. Niko and I have become Great Friends *After a few more Ripped pages the journal reeds Ha.. Today was a Blast Me and Niko On Guard Duty.. Hes The Best Friend Ive Ever had.. * More torn Pages* (( No youll see inabit ;) )) I met an Orc Today He was a master spy for the S.A ( The Faction Im in) We didnt see eye to eye but i feel we can be friends Today I Met An Amasing Elven Girl called Sadi her eyes.. Amasing They are a definition of Beauty", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of a Guard", "PakastainiPaul", "As a recruit you have to regular duties which are Gate duty and patroling the cities.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of Kuseran Elensar", "Mezua", "Week 3: I found this empty book and decided to start a journal in it. It has been many moons since I moved to Aegis. I do quite enjoy it. I have met many people and made many friends. My first friends was the High Lord, Dalejin. He found me wandering the streets of Laurelin and helped me find my way around the city. He built me a house and helped me meet new people. Without him, I would have been lost for ages! Ha! In these three weeks I have explored many lands and even became High Council of Lord Dalejin's city, Draort. To the south it lies, far south of Laurelin. It is a grand place! I feel kind of bad though, for leading Mi'lord on like that. I do like him a lot...See at times I like to dye my hair with blood and change my eyes with the magic of my people. When I do this, I become evil. I terrorize and torture people. I do not wish Mi'lord Dalejin to find out though, him knowing...it would tear him apart! The worst part is that his friend, Ariasalamus, he is evil too. We once pillaged the wild together. I am afraid of Mi'lord finding out about us and our evil ways. I hope he does not. It would kill him, and me. Well, until then, Farewell Journal!      \n Year 1335: Many moons have passed. I have done much since then. I rarley travel to Draort, Mi 'lord never seems to be there anymore. I have taken a liking to Al'Khazar latley. I have met many people here...an Orc raped me. Murgraw is his name. I tried to kill him, but an Undead overheard me. He figured out my reasons and went to \"speak\" to Mugraw. On that night, I was Arrested under suspicion of wearing a robe. I had found some robes with a symbol on them, and they looked warm. I managed to resist arrest, however, and walked away unharmed. After a few months, I discovered other people with views like mine. They accepted me as one of their own, with no questions. They are my family now. The Black Hand. I am just a Scion at the moment, but once I get a higher ranking, I will be viewed with more honor. \n In this year, I met back up with that Undead. His name is Vulgrak. We ran around in the Verge together, finding people to taunt. We found this one girl, Eoin, and her lover boy. I took her eyes. They are the most lovely shade of green. Her boy ran off. We tainted the girl. Now her eyes sit on my shelf. I admire them, and I wish to find that playtoy... \n Year 1336: I wrote a letter to the Eoin girl. Asked her to meet me, to see how the taint working for her. She seemed normal, and quiet. I offered her my life and her eyes. She refused them. I offered her a home. She now lives with me in Malinor, because her \"friends\" think of her as a freak. She is not a freak, with her zombie eyes. She is beautiful and she is mine. \n More months have passed.... Eoin almost died. Lucas used his black magic to save her, now she is but a pet to him. I met another like Lucas, a mage, Rilath. He is a dark elf like me. A cannibal too. Me and Lynx, who is a vampire now, kidnapped a girl to feed to Rilath. That was a fun night. People heard us, tried to fight us. Undead had to help us, we stoof on the roof of the houses to fend off the people. I feel closer to the undead, in a way... \n Year 1337: Thral has fallen more into darkness. What a shame, really. He is letting his Demon take over. I was idiotic, and followed an undead to his house. He brutally burned me... The monks found my charred remains and brought me back to life. Vulgrak was there...He is now one of those Ascended...Yet I felt calm around him. I almost left to join them, but I got my head on straight now. I think of Draort often, Might visit tommorrow... Year 1339: I have made a home in the verge, underneath Eoin's boy's house. He knows Alchemy, and is teaching me the arts of it. I once kidnapped him, yet he still likes me. Odd...Oh! Yesterday I kidnapped a girl. I kept her for five or six months. Her stupid husband finally decided to come pay her ransom. I was surrounded by 12 others too. He didn't even Pay, his Mage did. She walked away with the mage, while the husband kept yelling at me. Pathetic. Valer still writes me, from time to time... \nYear 1340: I have kidnapped a man who overheard me speaking to Thral of being a minion. His name is Robin, and he is obdient. I call him Drakey.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of Sebring.", "digdog7789", "First day of journal.Me and Nic'Kolias and a few others are building are home/base", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of the Alchemist", "Royced", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of Vigleiven Auldwind", "Vigleiven", "Greetings, my name is Vigleiven. I am a Baron of the mighty Norsemen  in Aegis. Our location is very far, we are located north of Oren, far far away. We are slowly gaining power, we will be big and strong soon, and known. But that will take time. How I got ere' ye ask? Well... I was a Disciple of Valor back in the day. We were noble knights, fought .  I went far away from Aegis, and I don't know what be happened to the Disciples. They're gone, I haven't seen them in Alras.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Saving Grace by Tend'el", "Cloudheart", "I have just started to pen this. I believe it's the 21st of Malin's Welcome, 1322? So much just went awry. Should I start from a few days ago? \n \nI saw a man, on my way to Oren. I had just woken from a sickness or sleep, I know not which. Just before Alras I saw a man who appeared to be Cataris. Naturally I flung myself before him. He laughed in my face, and he and his cohort tore me asunder, could I trust no one? Not even my memory? Needless to say, I was wrong, it wasn't Cataris. My things were stolen, and my life saved by the Cloud Temple's Monks. \n \nA day or so later, I foolishly arose and went after my attackers. I was bare, not a possessions but what bread I just bought with my few minas. They even stole my life journal and note to Murmillo. I raged toward them, my enemies gone. I was angry, but decided to continue onward. \n \nI had begun my quest in an attempt to find Slayer. I had forgotten so much, and the Druid were , of course, no help. With no possessions, I blindly stumbled, as lost as a sheep without shephard. I came upon the rangers outpost and traveled across an icy lake. \n \nAt this point, my worst fear began to come true. I was alone, and starving. In a matter of minutes I would die. I ripped logs down, in an attempt to fashion a sword. To no avail, though, there was no animal in sight. I staggered, upon deaths door, to the abandoned city just outside the tower. I could no longer run. I was forced, in the dangers of night, to walk to the tower. \n \nIt was there in the throes of starvation, I was petrified to find the hidden entrance missing. My mind raced. I was going to die. I... I'm still confused at how I managed. With the last seconds I had I fashioned a pickaxe out of a log I stole from a tree behind the tower. And with this pickaxe and my last remaining push I tore a hole into the magically strengthened tower , at this point my vision blurred. I could almost not stand. There was nothing in the foyer, and I couldn't reach the branches to check for apples. I fell down the stairs. I screamed, \"HELP!\". I screamed, \"HELP!\". On my third, final shout, a miracle occured. I found the cakes in the lounge. \n \nI am still quite amazed at how it all turned out. It was such a miracle for me. I truly believed I would die, and my last words would be the scream of \"Help!\". \n \nAt any rate, I started coming to, and calming down. I was amazed to find the enchantments on the storage rooms mysteriously gone. Perhaps the tower responded to my need? As of writing this particular line, it is Tolta, 17th of The Second Seed, 1323. I have prepared myself against any attackers, should the tower truly be disenchanted. I have also done a bit of exploration as I've grown comfortably relaxed in the tower. It appears a quite troubling addition has been made to the tower. A map room. This is not just any map room, I fear it gives us military advantage over all the kingdoms of Aegis. The room is a scaled replica of Aegis, providing warp portals to any town desired. I trust Slayer's judgement, for the most part, but this power may be too tempting! I worry he, or some other military leader, will find out about its powers and move on the tower, to deploy troops where they please! \n \nApart from this discovery, I have been pleasantly provided for. No sight of Slayer. I will write when I next see him. \n \nI have discovered more secrets than I believe it is right for me to know. I am so confused Bell. My amnesia isn't helping any. There are secret passages all throughout the tower. I knew this. I never knew how to open one though! From what little I can see, I can't even tell if I can come back. What if I am trapped down there longer than in the wilderness? \n \nNo. I have made my resolution. I will gather some food, and venture down. If the tower is revealing its secrets to me I cannot hesitate. I must learn these secrets. I need the power to heal, to stop this wave of death and undeath! \n \nInto the depths of this secret, I plunge! Oh what an amicable little secret. If I could laugh in a book I would! I thank the tower for one of its secrets. I take back my words in jest. I am quite trapped here. \n \nWhile down here I have had two rather vivid dreams. In the first, I walked and I believe found the solution to a problem that occured. In the second, I saw these great black things, from the depths of a nightmare. They were tall, slender built, and stared with hateful eyes. The dreams were so real I could swear them to be astral walks, as if. I think I've found a solution, at any rate. I dreamt again. I don't think they are dreams. The tower must be showing me the danger of exploring secrets without being prompted. This is a rather dangerous secret. Perhaps I should use it as the trial? Or would that be too reckless? \n \nToday is Tolta, 10th of Snows Maiden, 1323. I have decided I will attempt to use the map room. This will be my second attempt to activate its abilities. My test was a failure. It seems I am still kept from the rooms purpose. If it is not for the expedience of travel, then what is the room's purpose? \n \nI have tired of waiting. I fear Slayer may never return. I have decided to leave the tower for now. I will return when I believe Slayer or the magic has, whichever comes first. There is a rather large town hidden on the hill just outside of the tower. How have I not noticed this? A rather large monument of a sword stands at the town's entrance gates. I see from a construction sign that the town is not yet open to the public. It is called New Alstion, a project likely under the command of King Edmund . \n \nPerhaps I shall check in on the Wilder Farm and return to Murmillo's Keep? I have found the hideout of Goblin, the famed Orc-creature. A rather luxurious keep has been built here. It seems they have cut a chasm straight though a mountain. I also see a keep with an engorged trench right next to, or part of, Goblin's hideout. These outposts are far too close to the Tower. Do they push for it? It is Fort Alstion, Est. 931. There has been even more expansion to the North! What foolish bravery of Edmund's! Another town, Crimson Vale. All of Oren has entered a deep chill. I dislike it. I must hurry to the grove to find the Arch Druid. I will take a shortcut from the Dwarve's home nation to Moonlamp Mountain. I hear a fearful thunder. One I have heard many times before. I am not so surprised to see the Dwarven town changed. I can see Wilder Farms. I shall cease writing in this book and return to my journal when I re-enter Aeriel's Crown. No one is in the mansion. plans have changed. Dwarves under attack. Undead Menace. I must help \n \nI was tortured and burned. Made captive by the Necromancers. They threw my body aside, into a corpse pile. Luckily I was nigh death, but not dead. I awoke a long while after, to be healed by the Crypt Monks. They have seen me more than my own family! I would laugh, but I ache. Their leader asked me one question though. He expected a correct answer, and should I be correct, if I did not die from burning, I would live. The question? \"Is this statement a lie?\" I hear them! At my inn!", ""),
        StaticBook("Life with Elves", "iohnoh", "Currently i have been in Elves city for 2 or 3 days. I like here alot althought it has alot dark places so there are alot monsters but im not afraid of them. It is final time to fight with my fears and start hunting like i used to hunt when i was younger. I still remember the day my mom and dad died in that cave system we lived in. Those stupid mindless creepers just had to blow up near lava vain and kill my family. If i get powerful someday i will kill the creeperqueen who killed my loved ones. Every day when i go out and see a creeper i see my family in the cave and then comes the explosion. :'( \n I promised myself not to go back into caves but someday i need to get materials and its the best place to find them. Hopefully i will get some army of friends with me to protect me. PS: That fucking spider below our house is annoying shit out of me... \n Anyways I shall conuctie my story about Elves. \n I really like them. Ofcourse some elves are angry and dont talk with anyboddy whos not from their town. But there are alot nice elves who have helped me. Actually there are only 1 so far. He gived me food and shelter for 1 iron ore and promise to write my journal", ""),
        StaticBook("Life, The Universe, and Everything", "Qwertyasdman", "Ye' may beh wonderin', 'bout life, ye' may beh wonderin', bout death, and ye' may beh wonderin', bout what yer' future beh holdin'. The answer teh these question's, beh 42 ,42. Simpleh, 42 I aint got much knowledge 'bout math, boot I got a mate who does. He be like a.. a.. scientist ting. 42 The Meaning Of Life, The Universe And Everything. !", ""),
        StaticBook("Limericks of Dunwood - by Petyr", "drplat", "These are a collection of limericks that I've written about Dunwood, meself, me friends, and some other fellas I know! I hope ya enjoy. They can be a bit dirty, and they're always comical, yes! No.1 - A Dunwood halflin' friend o' mine,/When asked how much he did dine,/ Replied, \"Both me breakfasts,/Elevenses, lunch, /Tea, dinner, supper, and wine! \n No.2 - Ol' Seth did go to the bar,/And met a fine lass from Sanhar,/ And now when I visit/His small halflin' home,/ There be too many half-orcs dar! \n No.3 - An elf lass whose clothing was strewed,/ By winds that left her quite nude,/ Saw ol' Kip come along,/And unless I am wrong,/ Ya expected this line to be lewd! \n No.4 - When the Wanderin' Wizard fer sure/ Entered me bar sayin, \"Sir,/ I require all the ales/That ya have fer sale,/ The rest o' this rhyme is censored. \n No. 5 - Harvestin' crops ain't no fun,/ Nor is plantin' seeds none, yet/ I love me hot bread/ And ale in me head,/ So I'll work all day in the sun. \n No.6 - Yer the prettiest lass that I've met/ No prettier lass could I get,/ Wow, I must be drinkin',/ If this is what I'm thinkin',/ Fer this beautiful lass is me pet! \n These rhymes pack laughs astronomical/ In a space that is quite economical!/ But the good ones I've seen/ So seldom are clean,/ And the clean ones so seldom are comical!", ""),
        StaticBook("line", "ThatMine", "Sadri Corfi's: Guide to Swordsmanship", ""),
        StaticBook("Linking a dedicant to nature", "urpenguin", "tell them to close there eyes and clear there mind. begin chanting softley and whisper to them that they begin to hear the leaves rustle Begin chanting slightley louder tell them they begin to feal the grass curl around there feet chant loudley now tell them that they see the forest almost as it is alive stop chanting and tell them that the link has been forged you are now attune with nature tell them to pick a title and your done", ""),
        StaticBook("Liquids Research", "Telanir", "Property of: Telinir \n Telinir's Research on liquids. Research on Water: Water can be walked in and through and can carry people and objects. It appears as a fountain which spews out infinite water. This could very well be an effect of MF exposure. The fountain can be scooped up with a bucket, the remaining water will quickly vanish from MF radiation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lirinyas Reply", "kittenaid", "That sounds delightful. Name your time and place. You know where you can usually find me. Yours, Lirinya~ Why hello there~ unf/weire -erase e~", "")
