        StaticBook("Lover Letter to Scarlet", "Happy_Go_Unlucky", "Scarlet, whenever I see you, my heart throbes like it did the first time we met. We used to run through the treetops, hand in hand. Exploring the riches of nature. You were as beautiful as the honeysuckle that we wrapped ourselves in. As beautiful as the moonlight through the leafs, reflecting off the pristine waters of the forests. As tender as our first kiss. And as soft as the silk you covered yourself in. I wish you would return soon so I can relive these moments. My heart aches more every day. Scarlet, I lov-- *the writing ends abruptly, the ink jar has spilt across the page  and two specs of blood dot the page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Lucky Numbers, How to Play", "Lomaticc", "1. Place a bet. All bets are 25 Minas \n(/money pay PlayerName ammount) \n2. Pick a number 1-4 \n3. A prize will pop out of the number dispenser you picked \n4. Keep your prize! \n \nPrizes Include: Diamond, Iron, Gold, Lapis Lazuli, Brick, Redstone Items, and much more! \n \nOnly at Oceans Casino! Located on the King's Road between Kal'Urguan and Kramaroe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Luke is a fag", "Trevisdabomb", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Luke's Daily Expirences", "andyboy124", "Day 1: I oke from my home to the warmth of my fireplace. I then went upstairs(my room is downstairs) to my office(im a healer in a town owned by a  friend of mine   who was kind enough to build the building for me. I then greeted a few other residents and made my way out of the town. I went into Alkhazar and s many people gathered around the kings cross. Curious i went up to the crowd and asked what was going on. I got an answer from a guard who seemed to be the cause of the crowd. He said to me \"We are going to raid an undead fortress up North\". I said to him \"Surely you will need more men than this\". Then he said \"Yes i know we have more coming from other towns\". After that more people arrived and they were off. After that i went to Dn's Bakery,a great place for food. I greeted her and then asked for some pork. She gave me my pork,i paid,then i left and s my friend  Banok. I went up to him and asked how he was. He said he needed to hire people for his shop. I offered to and he said he would let me know then walked off. Realizing it was getting dark already i walked back to my home and had a nice pork dinner. Day 2: I oke to find a man wanting apples in my shop. I asked how many he wanted and he replied \"10 please\". I gladly gave him his apples,he paid me and was off. I greeted my friend and went outside the town. I was barely outside the gates when i heard the HHHSSSSS. I leaped ay before the i was killed. Creepers are always around the gates so i should have seen that coming. So carrying on with my day i met a man who wanted to sell me iron. I told him i wasnt interested. Oh but he was percistant,he told me he would cut the price in half.I still said no but yet he  wouldnt give up . So i told him to leave me alone or else i would alert the guards of his harrasment. That sent him  away. I then went fishing,but was unsuccesfull. I decided to go to another friends town. When i got there i found nobody,so i left and went home.On the way back i saw the biggest pig! It was huge! I got out my sword and killed it. Cruel yes,but i needed food and had little money. I felt bad about it,but was a little better when i shared some of the pork with my friends. After that i went to bed and slept better than i had in weeks.   Day 3: I slept pretty late and when i finally got up no one was around.So i grabbed and apple and left. I spent the rest of my day exploring Aegis. Nothing much happened though,so i got a little bored. However, on the way back i saw a drunk man passed out on the street. I rushed to him to . I quickly got the strong stench of booze in my nostrils,but i still stayed to aid him. He awoke and told me to go burn in a pit of fire. Suprised by his words i just shook my head. I told him he was on the side of a road and that he should get up before he is robbed. He looked at me said a odd variety of words,got up and jumped off a cliff. I ran to the edge thinking the poor man must have benn killed,but i saw him swimming in the water. Knowing that i could  him no more i continued home. When i got back i was still alone in the  town. So i ate an apple and went to bed. Day 4: I woke up early and didnt feel like doing much that day. So i thought about magic and how nice it would be to have it. I would use my magic to  the good people of Aegis and defend it from evil. I knew that to use magic i would need hoes. I thought it would be nice to collect every hoe. I used my wood,iron,stone,gold,and diamonds to make one of each.I stored them in a chest. I then made a wooden one for myself,but soon discovered i dont know any magic. I went into town and heard of a mage guild.I asked around about it. I was told to speak to the high priest. I found him and asked about the guild. He said that i must speak to a man named Slayer. I thanked him for his time and left. I looked everywhere for slayer but i couldnt find him. I looked at the mage tower and the guild house in Lorelien. He was no where to be found. I was tired from my day so i went home. I had an apple and went to sleep. Day 5: I woke up to a man calling my name in my shop. I went upstairs and asked what he wanted and how he knew me. It turned out he was an old friend. He said he dropped by to say hello and get some food. I gave him his apples and he was off. I went out to the Cloud Temple later in the day. I sat there and admired the land. A little while later a man approached me and asked for some money. He looked very hungry and tired so i gave him 200 minas and asked him to come with me. We went to my house and i gave him some apples. He ate them very quick. After that i asked him if he wanted to stay the night. He glady said yes and thanked me. In the morning i awoke around the same time as he did. I gave him more apples,he thanked me and left. I never got his name,but i knew he was a dwarf. It was still very early so it wasnt quite Day 6 yet)) I went back to bed and slept well. Day 6: I awoke again to te warmth of my fireplace. I did nothing that day besides swim in the vast ocean. I saw many squid and wondered about them. I swam down and tried to touch one but they quickly swam away. I swam back up and sun dried. I fell asleep and when i awoke i saw zombies all around! I ran back to my home and hopped in bed. I dreamted of learning magic and ing the people of Ageis. ******Extra******* I apoligize for the mistakes throughout the book.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lull, Spirit of Air", "Ned_Lud", "I am Lull, spirit of air. My singing drifts freely in the wind and my whispers stir in the silence, rustling like leaves in the treetops. My lithe figure has been caged and withered and my soul all but broken, but my song remains the same.\n      I was capture as a young elven girl and forced into the vile service of a band of hedge knights, mostly human. These dreadful men kept me in a wooden cage, hanging me from the highest treetop. During the night, they would drag me out, used, abused and beaten. During the day, I would simply rock, cradled in my prison, singing exhausted melodies to the birds. These creatures of the air became my comfort and my solace.\n      Years passed as my sanity dwindled. My body was too weak to resist and my mind too weak to care. I sang a final song to the birds, asking them to release me. They pecked and clawed until at last I wriggled free. The fall was deep but there was simply no other way. My song carried me as I plunged downward towards the ground, towards freedom.\n      Ned Lud'Gorkil has called upon my spirit and I have answered, my words transcribed in this book through his own enchanted hand. There is a fortitude in the warrior, silent as the breeze yet strong as a raging stormwind. I will carry him down this windswept road, holding him high as his enemies fall like leaves to the wind.\n      I may be called upon by birdsong or by throwing leaves into the wind. Feathers worn on the body and clothing or applied to weapons will give my blessing in times of persecution or combat. Windy days are the time for meditation and prayer. I take pleasure in these things.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lullaby to Zhotia", "Rhisereld", "Grow tall, sugar cane \nEat that soil \nDrink the rain \nBut know \nThey'll chase you if you play their little games \nSo run, run fast sugar cane \nAnd he said, \"Always be afraid.\" \nYou should always be afraid", ""),
