        StaticBook("Making the town bigger", "nikias_1996", "I really like the ideas that you propose in fact we are looking to build a mine at the moment . as for the tree farm I like  the idea but first we need to find a place to put it. About the whole tuk town thing at the moment the relations between our two tows aren't verry good. There was lots of discussion and he behaved like a child, that is not the kind of person I like to work with, but we will see what happens in the future. Keep up the good work                                               Signed Eledyr Edit: apperantly the reltions between our two towns are getting better so it is verry likely that we will become allies", ""),
        StaticBook("Malachi Information Sheet", "guyplayingpc", "Name: Malachi Race: Dark Elf Age: 137 Gender: Male Occupation:   Druid q To the barracks Scholar! I thought ye be gone I had recuited two more My sheets aren't allways the best, and you may fix them as you wish", ""),
        StaticBook("Malachi's Adventures (Journal)", "Trevisdabomb", "Written by Malachi (of course). Today  my first travels, since beginning this book, I shall be heading to the Isle of Wisps . At which, there is a fascinating library.    On my travel to the Isle of Wisps, I met an Acolyte named Garn. He was an ascended in his white robes that had blue trim. There seemed to be a glow about him. I talked to him about the recent attacks of the undead and the leaving of the Sages. He told me to not be afraid. As I bade my farewell to him. I met a dark elf, suprisingly for they are rare, and we spoke about the history of the Dark Elves. He was very helpful and nice. His name was Lumas.  At this very moment, I prepare to attack the undead at the Monastery. Sage_Okonkwa is rallying the troops to attack There are so many people here and there is so much talking. I pray that we may defeat Iblees once in for all If this is my last writing then so be it.", ""),
