        StaticBook("Medical Records", "Lastchance2099", "Patient: Bastion Murdok \n Age: 36 \n Other information:  Patient is mildly traumatized, but should require in time. Physically, he is covered in minor lacerations, bruises, and burns. While it will be painful, he should recover in a few months.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicen And Natural Ailments", "silco97", "This book will teach the commen docter how to treat illnesses with simple remedies. First be warned you wouldnt want to make your patient even more sick.  \nThe Basic Remedies \nCommen Cold: This is simple to cure simply give your patient a mixture of red flower and bone, then sleep and stay warm. \nMental Illness: This goes for if your crazy or simply deppresed this will cure it all.  Simply mix in a bowl a red muchroom tree leaves from a Birch feed by the spoonful and you will feel normal in no time. \nSpider Bite: Feeling a bit woozy after a spider bite then eat some food first then rub pig meat and string over the bite and it should close up. \nUndead Curse: This requires a bit more preperation to cure this.  If an Undead curses the patient with what ever nasty Undead do. Here is what you must do. Mix in a bowl water that has been purified by an acended or one possesing magic. then lay the cursed on down and draw a redstone circle around them.  Now shout out \"He who has possesed this soul let his mind be clensed from the dirty hands that have contaminated him\" Then pour out the water and stab him once with a golden sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicinal Solutions", "cometking123", "Potions are quite complicated, but local plants can heal injuries and diseases just as effective as potions, without the harmful side effects that may occur. Of course, potions may cure some diseases that herbs can't but herbs can be found easily in the forest, unlike ingredients that usually come from the Nether. Nether and other rare avenues. In the end, potions and poultices can be helpful in ways that compliment each other . \n Chapter One: Herbs \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n Herbs are quite easy to find in forests, but only specific kinds of ingredients can be found in specific enviroments, such as deserts, swamps, and urban towns. One example is wormwood, found often in Al'Khazar's forests and in general in forests around Aegis. It is an potent healing herb on its own boiled with water, and with a few hours can cure minor cuts, scrapes, and bruises on its own. \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n Medical Conditions \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n Fever: Fevers are simple. Just put a cold towel on their forehead to reduce heat . Mix one part of Wormwood with one part of redstone, and orally give to person. Give plenty of rest. \n \n Headache: Glowstone mixed with any palateable substance can work for this. Give rest (One day) and discharge. \n \n Zombie Bites: First we must disinfect the bite. Mix glowstone with water and wash out wound. Be careful with the patient. If he suffers convulsions, or shock, then try calm him down. If unsuccessful, a small dose (1/100) of spider eye can wake his up to his senses. While washing out the wound, be careful for pus (Yellowish Substance) and blood. They may cause infections among other patients in the area. After washing, stich up the wound with string. If not holding, keep it together with a piece of leather. If that does not work, use a combination of the two, along with some rags (clean) to make sure that it does not get infected. \n \n For an Arrow. \n \n Note: Treatment for Arrows may differ in prochedure depending on the location of said arrows. I shall be ranking difficulty with *, **, and **** , with * being easiest to treat, and **** meaning the hardest of operation. \n \n * Arrow to the limbs (Legs, Knees, Arms) \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n An arrow to the limb can be either a nuisance or a grave injury depending on where it hits. An arrow to the muscle usually means diabled, while a arrow to the bone is minor. A general note for arrow wounds is to never, NEVER remove the arrow in one piece. Not only will the arrowhead inflict more damage on the way out, but it could cause more dama ge to organs and muscles in the afflicted area. To treat an arrow, break the arrow so that it is easier to work with. Note that arrows usually are fragile, so please break with caution. After you break the arrow, make an incision around the afflicted area. This is to remove the arrowhead so that it can not inflict more damage while inside the flesh , and also to peruse the damage dealt by the arrow so that you can respond to it. Scout out for the arrowhead, taking care of areas like the muscles. One mistake can cost them an arm. Once you find the arrowhead, inspect it for a moment. \n \n Is it barbed or not? \n \n devestate flesh with its multitude of barbed points. If this is the case, remove with care, and be on the lookout for any barbs that still stick o ut If the arrow is of the regular variety, take it out gingerly, but otherwise easier compared to the barbed variety. \n \n Is the arrow poisoned or not? \n \n Poisoned arrows can be dangerous, and sometimes fatal if shot anywhere in the body. For the limbs, it could mean amputation for the soldier, reducing his efficientcy in combat. Poison can range in venomosity, ranging from benign poisons to the deadliest of toxics. An great source of poison comes from the spider, and its more toxic cousin the Cave Spider Poison from the eye can be strewn on the arrow, and is distinguishable by the arrowhead's red dish hue. Spider venom is considered normal on the toxicity scale, and can be  usually cured by a mixture of glowstone, rose petals, and redstone in a ratio of 1/2, 1 petal, and 1/2 redstone. \n \n NOTE: Poisons, especially in the hands of a skilled herbalist, CAN be more deadly than regula poisons, due to the complexity of the poison the herbalist have made, and/or different varietys of herbs/plants being mixed together. It is HIGHLY recommended that you obtain a sample of said poison at all costs, whether it be in a bottle, arrowhead, or even on the tip of your toungue. This can make a doctor's job infinitely more easier in both saving lives, and prevention of poison through an antidote, which can only be made from said poison itself. \n \n At this point, make sure that ALL wounds are treated before tackling an arrow wound. After making a cut in the area of the arrow, carefully probe for the arrow head using tweezers. Wipe blood and give secondary treatment as nessecary. Upon finding the arrow, carefully extract it with the tweezers you have now. If you do not have tweezers, gingerly take it with your hand, after washing it of course. If the arrow is barbed, use a small knife to \"cut\" the barbs from the flesh. Once the arrowhead is removed, carefully extract the barbs, making sure not to rend or damage the flesh/muscles. Once finished, stich up (providing you know how to stich a wound) the wound and discharge. If in critical discharge, put the man in a bed and let him rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medievil", "char615", "poop my book1 !", ""),
        StaticBook("Meditation of Todd Tanner", "Todd877", "I had my condition taken care of a few days ago. A side effect of it was that I lost most of my arcane magic. I can now only do one spell ((at the moment)), summoning fire. Even then it is only a small ember, unless there i already fire around me. But enough of that, I will tell you how my meditation went. \n I went to meditate in the forest like you asked. I opened my mind to the forest and listened to it. I heard it, but I felt no affinity with it. I then climbed a tall tree and opened my mind to the wind. I heard it, but again, I felt no connection with it. By then it was dusk. I sat next to a stream nearby and listened to it. A third time I felt no connection to that element. \n I was determined to continue through the night, and becuase of the cold, I built and lit a  campfire. As I continued to meditate, I hear a voice coming from the fire. Turning my attention away from the river, I focused on the fire and opened my mind to it. I didn't exactly hear this, but I felt ... \n The fire happily eating the wood...  \n The embers leaving their mother and seeking a place to eat themselves ... I felt through it the way fire brought destruction, greedy and constantly seeking to devour everything.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medril's Diary", "ZeSybbyl", "[Itnan, 30th of the Amber Cold 1327] I have been accepted into the Sword of Lorem, I hope it It will reap the rewards that I think it will. \n [Tolta 31st of the Amber Cold] My masters have been talking alot about an order known as the Red Fist, they have disgraced our group, and I am going to investigate their whereabouts. I have learnt that their base of operations is in Al'Khazar Bay \n[Kamees, 33rd of the Amber Cold] I have searched the Beachfront as well as I can, but therf ((there)) was no sign of the Red Fist. I got as far as I could until the way was blocked by those blasted Pigmen. I have decided to leave the rats at the Red Fist alone, as I will need to have all my conceni tration on upholding the law and values of the Sword of Lorem \n [Joma, 34th of The Amber Cold] Today I ran into the strangest house, I was investigating a series of ominous signs which have since been removed, I came across a normal house, butit had a compartment underground, where I fell into in my curiousity, I was suddenly attacked by all manner of monsters, spiders, zombies. skeletons, and the worst, Pigmen , the spiders covered the roof, and zombies infested the floor, lower still, there were skeletons shooting at me from below, and the Pigmen were with them, preventing me from jumping down and slaying the skeletal archers. Eventually I managed to slay the zombies, and climb to the roof, were i was assaulted by Spiders, I fought and slew them, but I was nea r death, I climbed out and returned to the guild hall to rest. \n [Ahad, 1st of the Deep Cold] I just put a sign up for the Sword of Lorem at the Public not ice board in Al'Khazar for the Sword of Lorem, I am really enjoying my time here and I cant wait for my first contract \n \n My diary is starting to get clogged up now, so I will only add things of great importance. \n \n [Tolta, 3rd of the Deep Cold] Today I returned to the strange house to find the doors o open and the house unoccupied, I stepped inside to see if I could find anybody, and saw a lad der going down into the underground. I went down it and found I was close to the are I had be been in before, I was exploring and I found a map washed into an underwater stream, I am yet to dicover the location it has recorded. \n I will enclose the map with my diary in my bedside chest in our guild hall, and will bring it to our librarian as soon as I can", ""),
        StaticBook("Meeting a vampire", "meanking", "Hi, This is the story about how I, Chaecus, Met a vampire, a living vampire... So here it goes I was walking in oren, going north, i then went east, past this town... then i saw this man, in heavy armour, he was calling this \"man\" names, i soon knew this \"man\" was a vampire. I went into this vampire's home, or cave or anything you want to call it. He knocked me out, i awoke in a dark cave... He was sucking my blood, draining my life. I was stuck in that things prison for days, I think it was about a month before i got out. And when he did, it was a month later, i was hanging on a thin thread, i soon made it to Oren. I was so happy i made it out, but i dare not tell anyone about what happend that month...", ""),
        StaticBook("Meeting a Warlock", "Jerry_Man", "They're considered by those who lack understanding to be evil. Unfortunately in many cases this proves to be true.\n \nThis Warlock was quite old, considering we expect them to be consumed by their lack of control while still young. It seemed as though he hadn't discovered that much of his potential by shrugging off some of his magic as simply tricks and useless entertainment; which in essence was how he went about discovering this dark potential. It seems obvious now that the only way to live long and safe as a warlock is to ignore the power within. But it will always be there, beckoning to be unlocked. \n \nSimilarly to Arcane, more abilities and potential can be discovered in desperate circumstances. Wielders of Natural Magic seem to encourage its' use out of desperation, the concern placed on control only administered later.\n \nCertainly, we were both foolish to be engaging each other in the unhindered demonstration of magic. But our curiosities each towards the other's manipulation of magic drove out of him a potential that would have better been forever ignored: The Shadow. \n \nThere are few I know of who have any control of shadow, and fewer still who are around to talk about it. All seem to be dragged away to their death, or to serve the shadow. In balance, the light posesses the same pull on mind and soul, yet it is often viewed as a noble pursuit, while the descent into shadow is announced as 'evil'.\n \nWhether of evil origin or not, his mind and soul were altered somewhat from summoning the shadow, even so much as a darkened blemish remains across his forearm. An emblem of the power that is held at his fingertips, the potential that he has ignored until now, the dark pull towards his own end that has only now been awakened. \n \nThere is some truth to the myths we hear of Warlocks. All of them will eventually descend into madness, consumed by the power that surges through their blood.", ""),
        StaticBook("Meeting I: Fresh Wardens", "Ranovak", "To talk about: \n -State of the Wardens \n -Behaving as an army (going on missions and to war) \n -Warden rules \n -Training abilities -Being strict \n -Being active \n -Having events \n -Acting as a team \n -Finishing what we started \n -SWT \n \n SWT--Mission System--Battelion System--Role System--Training", ""),
        StaticBook("Mel'kath", "cgsphinx", "", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_16(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("members", "gwarrior1212", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Members of The Trisian", "PtahWithin", "Aceeri - Leader \nAlpaca (alpaka_man) - Co-Leader \nMolokai (Molokoa) - General \nSaint Daniel (TheDangerDan) - Commander \nPtah (PtahWithin) - Corporal \nKendrick (nitnisuadeschenes) - Corporal \nSedayu - Corporal \nSlayer_Aso (BoltofFusion) - Private", ""),
        StaticBook("Members_Of_The_Ravenhold_Guards", "djurreman", "*djurreman - Walthraban_Captain_Of_The_Ravenhold_Guards * *shandydeath999 - Elessar_Colonel_Of_The_Ravenhold_Guards* *dannyboyy97 - Alistair_The_Raven_Warrior* * King_of_Gondor12 - Thorodan_Kolanthel_The_Raven_Warrior* *Squirt0 - Spitter_The_Raven_Warrior* *shadowl00t - Eliolos_The_Raven_Warrior* *xDyingdutchman - Evrin_The_Raven_Warrior* *Uhmiforgot - Wesley_The_Raven_Warrior* *Iced_Pineapple - Draketh_The_Raven_Archer* *Forgottendebt - Eramil_The_Raven_Scout* *Xerxes_XIII - Syn_Valkerye_The_Diplomat_Of_The_Ravenhold_Guards * *KingOchros - Rhoswen_Historian_Of_The_Ravenhold_Gurads* *ijsselzichta - Kamiera_Shadar_The_Raven_Recruit*", ""),
        StaticBook("Memborable People", "alex612", "Maeghan_The_Vile       Shoi And Codrick     Thrall'Mar     Gladail      Dax", ""),
        StaticBook("Memiors of an Hempshine", "Hempshine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Memoir of Eziano Mortale", "Markdeevee", "I am Eziano Mortale, this is my story \n \n I was raised on a large estate, northwest of Al'Khazar. The middle child in a family of ten boys, i had little responsibility. I roamed the woods, hunted, living a wild life, mostly in seclusion. I had little to do with my father, Lorenzo Mortale, who ran our family business. My eldest brother Marco headed up the farm ,growing just about anything, while my father handled the business and marketing. We where one of the tycoons, so my mother told me, competing with some very large businesses , so naturally we had enemies. I was thirteen when they came... I had been out in the woods, hunting, spending the weekend alone, as i often did, when coming home i could smell the smoke, and hear the flames.", ""),
        StaticBook("Memorable Locations", "alex612", "Orcish Arena     Shadow Falls          Laurlin         Every Ruin          Orcish Cage", ""),
        StaticBook("Memoradum of Silvermein", "ZazarusDious", "Nothin' so far fer today.", ""),
        StaticBook("Memories", "Sledder", "Time passes, the day is anew, my sorrows and fears renew, yet this muse is new. Darkness conveys weakness, vulnerability, a sense of bittersweet vengeance. Tears of angels stained with the venomous concept of repentance, for the heart once wished for such sins to occur I concur that my demiseis self-inflicted, along with my past. Stroll down memory lane let us visit a cursed cemetery with tombstones as far as the eyes could see. This isthe permanent rest place, of my heart's aspirations, dreams and hopes. Darkness invites misery,agony; companions of the night, that prey on the weak Consuming the souls, and hearts of many, but sparing the life of conscience ; an act of true cruelty, for over thinking is an inevitable future. Does it bother you that you're allowing lifeto slip right by? Does it enlighten you that you're victimized by your regrets each night?", ""),
        StaticBook("Memories", "Ratemenatorz59", "I walked along the road, the breeze picks up my hair. The summer air, so hot, so refreshing. I stumble upon a city, Al'khazar. I stand in amazement, the view is all I could think of. I soon meet my two friends, Hempshine and Dawn. I come to greet them. I look into the waters, seeing myself in a blur. Yes? I hold a book, a stone sword and some saplings", ""),
        StaticBook("Memories behind the fog", "AnchyBelanchy", "I was laying on the floor. I opened my eyes. I was surrounded by darkness. Everything around me was black. I tried to get up, but my body was too heavy. Suddenly I heard a sound! Words, sentences... But I couldn't understand them. They were blury, confusing, melting into each other... Then light came! The white shine blinded me as three silhouettes approached. I got paralised by the fear. My hands were shaking, I wanted to escape, but it seemed like an invisible barrier stopped me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Memories of Nobody", "duramon", "You are my one.My Only you provide a spark of the divine that lights up my life. You are what I exist for and why I am in this world.You are as beautiful as a rose and as Graceful as a daffodil that dances playfully in the wind.You are the envy of many and the enemy of none. I love you with all my heart and if you were to dissapear my heart would dissapear with you. For no matter if you want it or not My heart is forever yours and my soul is bound to your beauty.", ""),
        StaticBook("Men To Kill", "Jtheo2016", "1: Valve_Guard_Maith 2: Devor (A.K.A. daver_dave) 3: Alchemist (AKA Royced)", ""),
        StaticBook("Menel Nen Arda", "Alectriciti", "I'm ashamed of that instance, the man that looked like me. \n I should have fought or resisted somehow, but no, it could not be. \n \n \n What could have possessed him or gave him the nerve? \n I screamed as he cut my ears to a curve. \n He crushed my ribs and smashed my head. \n It's a wonder that I'm not dead. \n \n  Menel Nen Arda, gives me a feeling. \n It's soothing, relaxing, perhaps even healing. \n Is it the magic that empowers my life? \n Or merely the thought of my friends and my wife? \n \n \n So many memories filled with power. \n I'm closing this book. Time to take a shower. \n A shower to cleanse the blood off my ears... \n \n \n \n ...to cloak the pain I exposed with my tears.", ""),
        StaticBook("Menu", "sean0520", "Menu ____ Breads _____ Fresh Wheat Bread -10 Fresh White Bread -10 Fresh Rye Bread -12 Day Old Bread (assorted) -8 Soups _____ Steaming rustic beef stew, only the freshest spices in Aegis -20 Mushroom soup, home style -18 Light mushroom soup, exotic truffles from Laurelin -50 Classic chicken soup, because mom knows best -18 Lean beef stew, as gormet as it gets, cream based, Slimeball used for thickening -60 Spicey chicken soup, best flavor you'll ever taste, even if your mouth hurts -30 Local sheep stew, all ingredients from here in Oren -24 Sanhar style beef soup, an orcish delicacy and a must try -32 Mushroom sheep, very tasty, slimeball thickened, 20 karat edible gold flowers -65 Classic zombie, hard to get, but its worth it, included with Laurelin truffles -45 Beef ____ Lean thigh cut, lightly seared -30 Quickly seared, very fresh Oren beef -28 Lightly seasoned, still moving on your plate, beef heart -60 Sanhar beef, well done, Oren seasonings -35 The reaches of Aegis steak, as exotic as it gets, 24 karat gold toppings -100 Fish ____ Delicate cod, raw, fresh lavander -28 Laurelin Salmon, pan seared, Laurelin truffles included -40 Arkeye swordfish, our own special toppings (slime is a hint) -40 Lordly Feasts _____________ Only for the richest people, and the richest palets. These are for Lords! Lordly Soup feast, Comes with exotic aged bread, one of a kind soup -300 Lordly Beef, Comes with a rye bread, several cow parts -300 Lordly Fish, Laurelin fish, white bread, Oren seasoning -300 Feast of the Gods, Comes with fish, beef, soup, and choice of bread -900 title Menu", ""),
        StaticBook("Menu", "MinistryofGamess", "Entree - Soup \n Main Course - Cooked Porkchop, Bread and Ale \n Desert - Cake", ""),
        StaticBook("Mer'kog-The orc.", "JackWack", "this book is my life being an orc Chapter One: Getting a job. My first job was a gatekeeper to the fist orc gate. Then there was a sudden change, soon our leader built a wall surounding our capital. With that wall we didn't need a gatekeeper any more and i had to move on. Chapter Two: Life alone. After that the change in my life i was a living alone. All i had to do was fight and eat two things that i love to do now, it was a good thing.", ""),
