        StaticBook("Military Report", "Eltyer", "Scouting mission, Coordinates x=-2800 z=1100. Dwarven village, features a cactusfarm. A secret door, with an underground part. We don't know if the village is protected.", ""),
        StaticBook("Minas: A beginners Guide", "williewonka01", "Hail, If ye are reading this book then yer new to the great land of Aegis. Aegis is a wounderful place full of great mystery. The currecy in Aegis in know as Minas. There are many wat to earn Minas: Trade, Hunting, Mining, and work. But we ye are new the only one that is easy to get money is Hunting. \n Hunting is not always easy to do but can be very rewarding. The first thing that ye need to do is make or get a sword. Just find a tree and cut it down and make sticks. Get cobble stone and make a stone sword. Now kill a few cows and get leather. Ye dont need full Armor just some to get protection. Now that ye are ready it is time to start hunting. Once ye Have all of yer gear it is important to know the monsters ye are hunting The first we will speak of are Spiders. Spiders are very common and do not die during the day. they can only earn ye up to 10 minas but if yer very lucky ye will get a diamond. Next are Skeletons they have a bow and some arrows. They can be dangerous but shoud not be a big threat. They will mostly give arrows bows and bones and about 10 minas. Then there are Zombies. Zombies are very difficult but ye earn about 15 minas. They also mostly give out coal when ye kill em. Now the most important moster is the crepper. They are very sensitive to blowing up so to kill them you must be very careful. But if ye kill one ye can get up too 30 minas. And they drop iron a lot so ye can upgrade ur sword, or armor. So creppers are a beginners best friend. Now Slimes are very risky to kill and they only give up to 5 minas. So i would stick to creppers, skelitons, and spiders. Now stop reading and get out there and make some minas. And Good Luck.", ""),
        StaticBook("mine locations", "bodinian", "New Taliko; X: -700; Z: -340", ""),
        StaticBook("Miners Log", "legoman144", "Today I have returned to the mine with fresh picks. I still have not yet managed to crack the tough iron ore in these caves but i am close. Also i have noticed a strange red material in the floor. It seems to have electrical propreties i must figure out a way to pull it out of the floor undamaged ,on other news i found a rusty old iron helmet and several unused arrows in some rubble. I will repair the helmet and test my bow with these arrows tomorrow. This job is dangerous by myself i should hire some workers next time im in town. title Silent Woods Mine eraseall", ""),
        StaticBook("Mini Nen Arda", "Alectriciti", "Rhisereld, head to our bedroom. I must show you many secrets of Whispering Isles. Make sure no one follows you. Not Annora, not Akorta. This is for you, and you alone. And I like being cryptic, so have fun. I love you very much. <3 Alethion", ""),
        StaticBook("Mining Contract", "TehLulu", "The undersigned do agree, in exchange for 2,000 minas each, to use said minas to purchase a Ravenhold Mine Permit, and of the things they mine in that mine, they will pay Bell (Tehlulu) 10% of materials mined or found. The undersigned: Respiren and Wild_Shaman_Zafus", ""),
        StaticBook("Mining For Dummies", "silco97", "By: Ambros \nMining is in my opinion the best way to make a quick prophet.  Although mining does not come with out its risks.  First mining is not for the faint of heart, it is a dangerous task and if not done properly will cause your death. \nChapter 1 What You Need: Mining requires many tools for the job.  This chapter will explain each one and why. \nPick-This is rather obvious, although the bast pick to carry with you is the diamond pick, but carry some extra iron ones just in case. \nTorches-I suggest carry atleast 32 torches with you at all times. \nShovel-To dig away the dirt in your way. \nArmor-The minimum for this would be leather but you could go with iron just in case. \nSword-Anytype of sword but I prefer Iron or diamond over anything else. \nLadder-Just in case your in a tight spot and need away out. \nFood-In case you get hurt. \nWater Always bring water with you if you going deep, you wouldnt want to catch on fire.", ""),
