        StaticBook("monkey43251", "Battleme33", "monkey43251", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Hunting And You", "devin52992", "(( thats meta'ing man I nvr said my name)) There are many ways to earn a profit in Aegis, but monster hunting is by far the most profitable. How do you hunt monsters like a professional you might be wondering ? Well thats what you got this book for! I will endow the secrets of hunting monsters to you! Now we'll get to the good stuff the secrets of monster hunting! Secret #1 Keeping a good distance, now you may be wondering why this is a secret . Well it's a secret because you suck at it! now it is easily doable to slay any monster in Aegis naked with no weapon without even getting hit once. Part of how is by keeping your distance!                                Rule #2 Openings! Now this only really effects slaying skeleton archers but if you keep your distance, sidestep and watch the arrows you can easily see an opening for close to 3 seconds inbetween each arrow shot. You can get close hit him and back up all while sidestepping and slay the beast without getting hit!                      Secret #3 avoidance! We talked about this one a little in secret #2, but monsters turn rather slowly it is easy to sidestep and slay any of them without getting hit , so Keep your distance! Watch for openings! and avoid those blows!        now this is the best secret to most. Monster hunting is about profit and this secret will raise the profit for 1 slime from 8 minas to 168! almost guaranteed .                              Secret #4 The Unarmed Slime Slayer! Now when you kill a slime with a sword it almost never splits into tiny slimes, but if you slay a slime with your hands, or bow depending on slime (arrows are valuable). you can turn that big slime from 1 to 4 to 16 to a total of 21! Guaranteed!                                        Well those are all the secrets I can share this time . But look for my next book \"Strategys To Slay  All Monsters In Aegis\" in stores soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("MONSTER HUNTING It takes courage, strength, and a sword", "Blandorthegreat", "MONSTER HUNTING It takes courage, Strength, and dedication. Anyone can start though! As long as you can hold a sword properly. You must answer to avery call for help! Monster hunting doesn't just go in the lines of Creepers and Zombies, Theives are another threat! Noone likes a thief nomatter how little the theft! RULES: NO STEALING! You get enough from monsters. REPLANT ALL TRESS! And don't leave floating branches! TIPS: Creepers are the best for loot! Strafe forwards and back so they don't explode on you! Zombies are like spiders! just keep attacking them and advance slowley! sure as long as you replant hello", ""),
        StaticBook("Monsters and how to kill them By Botar Blackrock", "Botar", "<text> Hello! this is the first book in a series that will hopefully educate people and eraticat <text> e monsters! lets start shall we? in these next 7 books we will touch apon the various <text> monsters and creatures that roam these lands and hopefully teach ya how to kill them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monsters and their weaknesses", "xzpepijnzx", "By Rivell Gordian \n ____________________ \n For people like myself, fighting hostile creatures in 1 on 1 combat isn't a very desirable concept. In this tome, I've outlined how to exploit their weak spots in order to kill them without requiring much combat prowess. \n \n Skeletons: These creatures require headroom to fire their arrows. Trapping them in a space with low ceiling (2 meter height will do) will cause all their arrows to richochet off the stone above them, rendering them harmless. \n Drops: 5-10 Minas, Leather armor, Bow, Arrows(1-5), Bones(1-5), Gold Ore, \n \n Spiders: While able to scale obstacles with a vertical slope, the bodies of these creatures often do not allow it to crawl through spaces humanoids can. Making a small (1 meter broad) space in the wall to hide in, you can strike at the spider while it uselessly claws at you, unable to reach you. Eventually, digging a 1x1 metre hole in the ground will allow you to strike the beast's belly while it won't be able to reach you. \n \n Drops: Minas (5-10), Pork, Cobweb (1-2), Diamond \n Zombies: While dangerous up close, even unathlethic humanoids find they can outrun the zombie as well as outreach it. Fighting it in the water slows the zombie down enough to strike at it without it arms ever coming within range. This way, the undead can be taken out and its spoils collected safely \n Drops: Minas (10-15), Coal, Chainmail Armor \n Zombie pigmen: Very fast and very dangerous. Unlike zombies, they might strike at you while in the water, so the above method will have less effect. The best way to get a pigmen is to trap it in a sufficiently deep (2 or 3 metre) hole and strike at it from above. The pigmen will not attempt to free itself and only rarely will fling its blade upwards to harm you \n Drops: Minas (50), Cobblestone (1-4), Smoothstone (1-4), Chainmail Armor", ""),
        StaticBook("Monur", "empirerebel", "You are blessed, god, te ruler of the universe, who has blessed us with his rules. The magnificent lord we thank you for these set of rules we follow. Bless the almighty lord for you are great. Oh lord who has great wisdom, may you give us understanding and your wisdom. I will serve you with justice, kindness almighty lord of ours. We thank you for everything! May it be your will lord our lord and the lord of our forefathers that you help us reach peac . Help us live in peace and prosper. Help us reach our desired destination for life gladness and peace. Please bless us and grant us with kindness, grace and mercy. Blessed are you lord who hears our prayers. Recite this \"Blessed are you god\" \"Ruler of the universe who has blessed us with this life\" Heal us lord, then we will be healed, save us then we will be saved. For we praise you almighty lord of the universe. We are faithful for you through bad times and through good times. Here is a tale of a great man who rose from a place called Hardal. A man called hamass. He was born in Hardal, in a time where you couldn't be a Hasar. His mother put him in a little boat and lay it down in the river and it took him down stream. And thus the daughter of th king picked him up. She brought him to the castle and asked the king what to do with him. He decided to keep him not knowing he is a Hasar. He needed an heir to the throne. As time passed the king grew more and more attached to the child. Years passed and he now became a teenager. He saw a man beating a Hasar and he almost instantly ran over to kill him. He then heard gods words, and from that moment he knew he was a Hasar. He stayed true to his people and helped his people any time he had the chance. What is the moral or the lesson of the story? Be proud of who you are do not let anything stop you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Moo's Test Book", "Themastermoo", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Moo's Travelling journal", "Themastermoo", "I start my journey today, scouting the land, searching for signs of the undead attacks. \n I came across something troubling today, more rumours of The Wandering Wizard's connection to the undead. Apparently he's orchestrating more attacks against the S.A. because he want's them to move. I must look into this some more... \n I met an interesting dwarf today, by the name of Juvens. He's a lord of Oren. What's a dwarf doing being a lord of Oren? Hmmm... The most intriguing part is the fact that he is rebuilding snowy fields into a fortress calle d Crimson Vale. Claims it is to defend against \"Any enemy that threatens the people.\" I can't blame him, there needs to be a good fort up there. There's also a new gate just north of Crimson Vale, to mark the northern border of Oren. I must rest for the night now, will continue my journeys in the morn. \n Todays travels were informative. There is a sadness over me today, I was searching for alstion, and I could find no traces of it aside from a couple broken down rotting houses. But in its place was a beacon of hope amidst the rubble, a strange man named Reiugi had built a hall right in the midst of the destruction, it was of good craftsmanship, and beautiful  stonework. It had a courtyard in the middle with a single tree. He offered me his bed for the night, and gave me torches for my journeys. He claimed he was cursed to the shadow, and the guards of Alkhazar wouldn't let him in, so he built a refuge in the wilderness for  those seeking shelter. A good man I must say. I am taking refuge in a signal fire tower as I write this. I have but one more thing to scout before I return to the AFF fortress. \n As I neared the mountain that was my old home, I knew something had changed. As I went to where the undead had put the new entrance, I saw a waterfull spilling over the g ate , and that's the main problem, there's a gate. I couldn't get into the gate, I wasn't small e nough to fit or strong enough to break it. But one thing I learned from my youth as a bandit... There's always a back door. I quickly found an aboveground entrance into the tunnel system I created. The stupid undead thought a layer of dirt could keep me out. Unfortunately, they had blocked up the entrance from the tunnel to the main mining area. The fortress is pretty impenetrable. Theres a pit  right in front of where they blocked up the tunnel. My journeys took a slight turn for the worse when I fell down it. Luckily I activated my soul-stone before I went unconscious. And the kind monks tended my wounds. I am now journeying to one more undead fortress before I head home. \n As I searched for the undead fortress I came upon an FOA forward  battalion and was let inside. They did not trust me at first, but once I explained my purpose as an ally they warmed up to me and fed me. I had a run in with one named Glow, he was a sergeant. I had assaulted and killed a friend of his in my youth as a bandit. It almost came to blows until his superiors intervened. Things calmed down a bit after he left, and I had a nice chat with a captain, and learned a f ew things from him, his name is  Garn, and a helpful sort he is. I learned the undead fortress in the north has been destroyed, by a large alliance of a hundred men, dwarves, and elves. The official report is that King Edmund led it, but rumour is that The Wandering Wizard Avail er was there, and led the charge against the undead. Either people cannot get their story straight, or The Wizard is a two-faced liar. Garn's theory is the Wizard does the things he does for the greater good. He also believes Alstion and Snowy Fields were corrupt places. I don't know much about that, but I do know that I don't trust two faced folk... I am off to explore the ruins of the undead fortress now... I cannot find the ruins... I've been wandering around in the wilderness for days, My supplies are running out and I wan't to go home. I'm using my soulstone to go to Kal-Urguan now.", ""),
