        StaticBook("My Apologies", "loion", "So, here i am, writing an apology to you. Syrio. But i guess it's for the people who was offended too but it seems more right to say it's to you. First of all, before i became a Guardian, i was a bandit. One of my specialities was Assassination which may, or may not explain why i asked that. But i hope you will understand. Kal'Alras is an bigger part of me, then you could understand. I hope to get unbanished. If not, farewell friends. See you on the road", ""),
        StaticBook("My Apology", "Tyrellius", "I am sorry, dear Iblees. I was foolish to think that the Ascended were right, and thus i hope you forgive me. I wish to aid you on your conquest to return to Aegis. In the very near future, I will send you many Sacrifices to show the debt I have caused. I even have a large sum of Minas I wish to pay you, as compensation for my foolish acts. I hope you will accept me as a minion, so i may proove my worth to you.", ""),
        StaticBook("My arrival in Kramoroe", "xzpepijnzx", "Kramoroe is mayored by Malco, a young dark elf. I thought I read somewhere that the founders of this town were all human . Apparently, this is incorrect. \n He showed me to the town fort, which is built on top of an old ruin of unknown origin. The guard was quick to bult it into a meeting hall. However, my interest is piqued. I wonder who built it and why . \n I also had the displeasure to meet the town idiot, a giant elf who calls himself a 'purifier'. I do not know this term, but I assume it is simply the ramblings of a fool. Nevertheless, I shall read into the term. write \n Second Entry: \n I have found an old book in the bowels of the Kramoroe fortress. Written by Gu'Tav the warchief of some sort, it spoke of a lost town far to the east. \n Following the directions, I have found the location of this town, and I must say that the clamations of evil are very much exaggerated. around the town, which is deserted but mostly persevered, are several scribbles of lunacy , as well as signs left by travelers who have come across this town. It seems that the tomb which is spoken off has already been looted, and the graverobber spoke of a large treasure. Finally, the twin towers were anything but evil, though they link up to a small cavern that seems like a mining shaft of some sort. All in all, I would not recommend the journey.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Bathroom Story", "KindaSpacey", "I had to poop. I looked for a free stall in the bathroom. My poop was liquidy", ""),
        StaticBook("My belongings", "darkjames", "My belongings now proceed to Merrigan , Son of Darrus , Son of Arewen , and brother of Milkur  My room, and my chest things go to him, the room can be shared by the ones Merrigan select. Owership is passed to him, he's a wise friend, and he can handle things like I couldnt. Obey him, for that he is the new leader, and he is the jointer between  Family and Mournstone. He is a strong mage, and he is a wanderer, I leave my legacy of swordsmanship and axe mastery up to him, all my coin is up to him, and all my belongings...go to him, He is also now in charge of Aval, my son, who will problably like him, since both have many things in common, now, while I leave with Captain Magaly off to the new lands over south, I say, Goodbye, Friends, Family...And hope to see you soon.   Signed,  Vikram Valrik V Mournstone \"Vik.\".  \n \n Signed, \n Vikram Valrik V Mournstone, \"Vik\".", ""),
        StaticBook("My Black Days...", "DeadDew", "It's time I loved you, you made me, hate me. \n You gave me, hate, see? \n It saved me and these tears are deadly \n You feel that? \n \n I rip back, everytime you tried to steal that. \n You feel bad? You feel sad? \n I'm sorry, nether no skah that! \n It was my heart, it was my life, it was my start, it was your kni -fe \n This strife it dies, this life and these lies. \n and these lungs have sung this song for too long, and it's true i hurt too, \n remember I loved you! I've, Lost it all, I fell today, It's all the same, Im sorry oh, Im sorry no \n I've, Been abused, I feel so used, Because of you. \n I wish I could've quit you. \n I wish I never missed you, \n And told you that i loved you, everytime I kissed you. \n The future that we both drew, and all the things we've been through \n Obsessed with the thought of you, the pain just grew and grew! \n How could you do this to me? \n Look at what i made for you, \n It never was enough and the world is what i gave to you. \n I used to be love struck; Now i'm just Skah'd up! \n Pull up my sleeves and see the pattern of my cuts! \n Seems like all we had is over now you left to rest \n And your tears are dried up now, \n You just lay without a sound. \n Seems like all we had is over now, you left to rest. \n And my fears are over now, I can leave with my head down. Goodbye, old friend", ""),
