        StaticBook("My Life So Far...", "monkeychez", "Fuck my life. I failed the fourth trail. THE END Anyhow, i am not done. A bunch of shit has gone down, and i almost oiled my jocks in fear. (( I made a combination of Fruit Loops, and Frosted Flakes... It was delicious. I think i  will make some tomorrow... I will call it \"magical unicorn mix\" Yeah.... Thats good )) THE END Anyhow... I am not done i guess... I have another shot at the fourth trial. Balin believes that i will succeed, but Tyrion likes to call me a failure, which has put me into a slight deprssion. (( A good night's sleep helped me get my shit together, but i was rudely awakened by the damn snotty kids that live near me.... Ughhh... If i dont pass this, i'm going to flip shit )) THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("My Life Story", "urpenguin", "I am Valas a humble druid of malinor protector of nature. This is my story.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Life.", "hayden34666", "This is the story of my life. Who am I? I am Hayden Rusakov. My life has not made a lot of sence, I have no family.. no parents.. no sence of belonging. \n My life began far in the North, up on the cold icy highlands.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Little Zho", "Alectriciti", "It has been over 7 years since I last saw Rhisereld, and I was finallly coming home. People approached me in the city telling me I was a father. I couldn't believe it at first... but I was overwhelmed with joy. I rushed home hastily to find her sitting in front of the warm fireplace eating mushrooms. She asked who I was... I hestitated, and let out \"I'm your daddie.\" I'll never forget her shouting \"daddie!\" as she ran to hug me. She reminds me so much of Rhise! I can't help but love her. My wonderful Zhotia. I will love you forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Lone Travels", "vehikill", "In my time of venturing I have seen many glories and wonders, from the generosity  of the people to the hoard of the forests.  I set off in my travels to a land fabled to me as a great kingdom. Along a clean stone road, I past numerous people of different kinds, from Dwarfs to Orcs, most generous... Some not so... By these paths were villages and towns of great proportion all finely organized! But, by some were ruins of forgotten places, from where I infer happiness was. These ruins tell me that not all is right, and whatever it is, is hidden. By nightfall, I was starving if not for a village inn keeper offering me a free stay and bread. I thank the innkeeper occasionally nowadays with tips. Over my travels I would've struggled if not for his generousity. I past Whisper Isles. A large town with a fine lord. Many houses lay there but I cannot find work, and the placement is inconvenient. I hear there is a overpopulation as so, but I hear they are developing more lodgings. Soon after I came to, I think... Kamaroe village? The place of the nice InnKeeper. A smaller town but very nice and more so organized. With their shops and housing. It would have been a nice place to live in but I must move onward. By next nightfall I reach Oren. As they say... It is a grand kingdom. I find the houses all occupied and the streets bare of people. But I find work! Work as a Guard for the Kingdom of Oren. I accept, because I feel Oren is to beautiful and great to be defiled. But I hear rumors... Of  bad tales of people trying to overthrow the reign of the king. I applied as a Guard to Oren and was accepted quickly at what I assume is a shortage. The General was a kind man, who supplied me with armor, I used it carefully, I have since lost it But he has supplied me with one more pair, and I shall be careful, I have even repaired it for battle daily. My work is fine and simple the pay is great, but the dangers are greater. I work all the time if I can to remove foul monsters from the roads of Oren and to. As I cannot find abodement, I travel back. Looking at my steps and where it has gotten me. I then stumble upon Salvador and Rinschers shop, at a very convenient location. It placed at a nice spot for my work and they repair and supply me with things I may need. As well as buy spoils of battles for a nice sum. Days after my employment, I set off to venture to the other lands fabled to me. I travelled to Kal Uruguan, I think it's spelled that.... A vast Dwarven kingdom. I must see it, as I have yet no abode, all I fear is it crippling my work of protecting Oren. As I travel to Kal Uruguan I find Kal Aras, a massive castle perched atop a mountain. I am astounded that is not their Capital! I am led to it, to seek its innards of Kal Aras. But I find the gates locked! A Dwarf then comes to the gate and opens it up for me, and he brings food! I am grateful as I was in desperate times and help in my travels to their kingdom. I quickly set off for Kal Uruguan. Led by words of the kind Dwarf. I reach a small settlement with wood structures outside Kal Uruguan and am astounded. at their work, and it has since raised my thoughts for these Dwarves. I travel the path, to Kal Uruguan and enter their grand hall. I am even more amazed by their work To see their structure have been dug out and carved into a kingdom. As I walk the halls I notice the fine pillars ornately carved and brushed clear of debris. The flat smooth stone with the merchants stalls lining the hall. As I reach the center of the Capital I see a small castle in the center surrounded by a moat of thick lava, no doubt for their king. I search around their land and it is clean without a speck of dust. I notice their houses are built into the capital itself. The size of the chamber gives a air of greatness and power to these Dwarf people. I walk around their capital only to notice that I cannot find or purchase a abode. This saddens me, a little, due to the fact I have seen a great wonder. Time is short, live lay eyes on the great wonders.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Lord, I have skills and information that i believe would be very beneficial to you. I", "bloodnrose", "would like to request that you accept the aid of myself and my colleage as your personall guards . we have acquired much intel which implies that many people \"of Oren\" worship Iblees. We ask for no pay, or honor, we just", ""),
        StaticBook("My Love for You", "123devmo321", "When you told me not to love you so fast, I did not give up. When you told me that I'm not good enough, I did not give up. When you told me to go away, I did not give up. How could I possibly let you go, when i love you, more and more every day. Your my one and only love, the only one for me. I can't see the point of life, when I'm not staring into your gorgeous eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Loving Thoughts About Claire Kitty ((Please Read All))", "fiendin", "I write this book to talk of my one true love, Claire Kitty. She is beautiful and my  favourite thing to do is fish... for her. She has a strange addiction to raw fish and I love to make her happy by fishing all day. Then I would give it to her for free just to make her happy. I do it because even though my parents have died it makes me feel lifted from the fact they're dead. When I give her the fish it makes me smile and she smiles back and we both exchange loving looks. I have reason to suspect that she likes me because everytime I head over to Dawn's Bakery she's excited to see me. I am scared for her because I thought she was hurt or killed when Al'kazaar was attack by the dreaded Undead. I am saying that I thought she was hurt to make myself feel better but I have no clue. I ran to Dawn's Bakery to see if she was there but I could only see Dawn so I got scared. I better go check to see if she's there... \n I went to Dawn's Bakery today and foudn Claire, she's perfectly fine. She took some more of my fish and she gobbled it down in two pieces. She was very tired though she hid in the corner and fell asleep for a bit.  When I walked in she rubbed her head for some reason I wonder if someone hurt her. If they did I will make it my vow to kill who ever hurt her.   \n You are my love, \n Whom makes me liftless like a dove, \n Whom always makes me smile, \n Even when in denial, \n You are the love of my life, \n And I will always say this with strife, \n I give my heart to you, \n So that you may love it too, \n I hope you love me as well, \n and then I will never go to hell, \n For your love will keep me good, \n And that is certainly understood. \n By: Ior Sullkyn   I wrote this poem for my love and I wrote it with all my heart and soul. Please Claire I beg of you to accept my love and cheerish it as I cheerish you.", ""),
        StaticBook("My name", "drumstick607", "My name is Titus Obadiah head of the Templar Order", ""),
        StaticBook("My name be Dragnork, a dark green orc with black eyes, they use to call me \"natures gift\"", "_Player_2_", "Dragnork \"Natures Gift\" eraseall", ""),
        StaticBook("My name is Alethion", "Alectriciti", "A lot has happened in the last few days. I don't have a lot of time before nightfall. There's the possibility of death, and I'm eating a golden apple. I might forget everything. Alethion. My name is Alethion. I am married to Rhisereld. My best friend is Akorta, and growing to be real good friends with Annora. I am the leader of the Whispering Order. I saved Rhisereld from the Undead, I fought the undead. I serve Lord Brett of Whispering Isles. *scribbled notes of the past* Akorta, the moment you led me out of those caves... I thought you were the meanest person in the world. But you still wanted to be friends, and i've always respected that. You're my best friend. Annora, you're fearless. You are a great friend. I'm glad you've helped me with my ale addiction, and many other problems. Thank you. Rhisereld, my love. You made me who I am. I love everything about you. I don't want to forget anything about our past. It only strengthens how I feel. My name is Alethion Celebtaurë... *blood is on the page here* Rhisereld... I cannot express how I feel about you, towards you... I want to tell you so much but I might die unless I eat this apple. And that'd suck. I love you so much. Please help me remember. *scribbles madness here and a big heart*", ""),
