        StaticBook("Mythic Dawn's Achievements", "Minnan1", "During our time in the field we achieved many things, some great , some not so great. This book is the registry of all of them. \n \n-Aedan, The Last Ayleid. \n \n \nAbandoned Eastern Tower: \n \n We have found this crippled ruins outside of Laurelin, and recovered many of what was lost. \n \nThe Bandits of The Road: \n \n This group of criminals was brought to justice thanks to our stealthy and highly experienced leader. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Myths About the Undead", "RHcrow", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Myths About the Undead  by Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "With the rise of the Undead the citizens of Aegis are more in danger of misinformation than the Undead them selves.  Being armed with the best knowledge guarentees better chances of survival. \n Myth: The Undead are mindless drones. \nAnswer: False.  The Undead are sentient and can even communicate in our tongue. \nMyth: The Undead are just a local threat. \nAnswer: False.  The undead are a threat to everyone.  They have portals that allow them to appear in many regions of Aegis. \nMyth: The Undead are all a mob. There is no real leadership. \nAnswer: False.  Undead heiarchy is just as complex as mortals.  The more powerful Undead reside as leaders.  The bottom ranks consist of the brainless cadavers you see roaming the night. \nMyth:The Undead can control powerful Dark Magic. \nAnswer: True.  Not all Undead possess the  Dark Arts. The ones who do have varying skill. some can command vast power.  Some can only do minor jinxes. \nI hope you find this book helpful.  -Nitholiak VonSchlichten", ""),
