        StaticBook("Nancy Dwarf", "KingToten", "Hello. You Are About To Embark On A Journey Of The Great Nancy Dwarf. While Reading You May Have Sudden Sensations Of. Anger. Excitement. And Dissappointment. Enjoy Nancy Dwarf Was A Young Female Dwarf. She Didnt Like To Mine But Solve Mysterys With Her Freinds. Mork. Erik. And Ken. They Were About The Same Age As Nancy Lets Begin The Story With Nancy At Her House. It Was A Stormy Day And Nancy Was Looking Forward To Her New Book Nancy: \"This storm isnt about to let up anytime soon. I might aswell start on my new book. Just When Nancy Was About To Start Reading Her Book There Was A Knock At The Door. Nancy: \"Whos knocking?\" She Said To Herself . Nancy Went To Check The Door When She Heard The Back Door Slam Nancy: \"What Was That?\" As Nancy Went Into The Kitchen To Check The Back Door She Heard Russeling In The Bushes In Her Backyard. She Had Noticed There Was Muddy Footprints Near The Backdoor. *crys on his bed about his emotions Want to read a demo for my book? Good Want to read a demo of my new book dawn?", ""),
        StaticBook("Nashtoff's Bookstore", "divinemine", "Nashtoff's Bookstore is located near the King's Cross Cardinal Points, and right next to The Open Quiver and The Olde Knavery. The Library holds some interesting books, at a resonable price. The books' prices are determined by the amount of pages in the books. \n The Pricing Formula of Nashtoff's Library : [Pages] * 2.5 + 10 Minas. Books with short contents will be a lot cheaper than books with many contents. For example, a book named 'The Legend of Pork' has 3 pages, so the price of the book is 17.5 Minas. On the other hand, a book named 'The Wizard of Aegis' has 64 pages, so the price of the book is 170 Minas. There's a lot of books being published through Nashtoff's Bookstore lately, so be sure to check the store often for more books! \n [Book Written by Scia]", ""),
        StaticBook("Natheus' Book Of Sins", "sgtteddybear59", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Natheus' Journal", "sgtteddybear59", "\nEntry 1 - I have decided to write in a journal so that I may be able to look back on my adventures. It's kind of corny I know but it's nice to have something to look back on. Something that will show me how far I have come. Well, we will see what happens. \nEntry 2 - I ran into this wonderful woman named Rhisereld. She is very kind and pretty cute to boot. We talked for a bit then she showed me her house. Which was a small house, very small to be exact. But I decided to help her and build a massive house that she can live in. I am still working on it, but I already got got one room done. \nEntry 3 - I have worked even more on the house, everything is coming out perfectly. I added a pool and a few other things. She loves it and I do too. We layed down together on the bed and when she closed her eyes, I thought to myself... That this woman has begun to grow on me. I have began to have feelings for her, but I doubt she feels the same. I will continue on the house. \nEntry 3 - I finished the house, everything came out perfect and just the way I wanted it to. She was overjoyed with what I have done. Hopefully I can get to know her even more. \nEntry 4 - I haven't seen Rhisereld in awhile. She may be busy, no matter, I will collect some food for us and maybe even get some more supplies while I am at it. \nEntry 5 - In secrecy, I have grown an interest to Iblees. I began to read up on this \"Fallen one\". I am really interested to what I have learned so far. Is this perhaps the path to Eternal salvation? I have no idea, but I think it is. I will not tell Rhisereld about this, she may respond negitavely if I do. \n Entry 6 - I began to build a shrine hidden behind the house. I am pretty pleased how it came out. I am adding a sacrificial table soon to hopefully give gifts to the great iblees himself. Hopefully he will accept them. I am eager to continue. \nEntry 7 - I have taken a lamb and tied it to the table. I took my knife and ran it along it's stomach. The damn thing would not stop screetching! I continued with the insision untill it's stomach was cut open. I reached in and pulled out the heart, soon haning it by a chain for iblees. It almost felt good when I finished... Like, it was the right thing to do. \n Entry 8 - I need more than a lamb to offer to iblees. I set out to the main road tommarrow to search for anyone worthy of being a sacrafice to Iblees. \n Entry 9 - I found a young man walking along the kings road. I decided to get a bit crafty and trick the man, rather than fight him. I told him my good friend got stuck in a mineshaft and that I needed someone to help me free him. The idiot fell for it, and I soon took a club to the back of his head. He fell unconcious and I dragged him to the shrine. He will make a great sacrifice... \n Entry 10 - The man screamed and begged for mercy when I began cutting into his flesh. He bled really good, and I imagine Iblees would have enjoyed devouring his soul. I let his heart hang from a chain, I also flipped his skin, inside-out. It almost felt pleasurable as I sunk my blade into his chest. \n Entry 11 - I have been feeling different lately... My mind is not my own. I get these sick thoughts of killing someone or even raping an innocent girl. I feel sick to my stomach. Why would I even go so low as to think of these horrid ideas? I hope it goes away soon, I don't like it. \nEntry 12 - I didin't sleep at all last night. Everytime I closed my eyes, I would have this odd dream... Everything was distorted and made no sense. Only a few parts I were able to see... And what I saw was not pleasent. I had dreams of bodies hanging from the walls of my house, bound with a thick barbed chain. The corpses skin were removed and there eyes plucked from there skulls. It was a horrid dream and what made it even worse... Is when I saw Rhisereld, spead out on the floor, bare and dead, with the hints of someone raping the corpse. Was it me? I hope not... If it is, I need to watch how I act when Rhiserelds around. \nEntry 13 - My head is aching... Another night with no sleep. I can hear whispers in my head. They speak of things I do not understand. I try to shake it off and keep my cool, but the voices just get louder... \n Entry 14 - It feels like there is a demon clawing at the walls of my sanity as I struggle to keep my head in order. I can hear the screams of woman and children each time I try and go to sleep. They sound so real, like there is someone yelling in my ear right next to me. I cannot take it... Whatever is doing this to me isn't going to stop until the last ounce of humanity is stripped from my mind. \n entry 15 - I claw at my ears until they bleed, I weep in the sewers of Oren as an endless war rages within my mind. I try and fight back but I am easily defeated. I have began to have a phobia of large crowds. I cannot be with too many people or else I will lash out and try and stab someone. It's not safe for me to be around anyone. I am afraid I will do much harm... I need to talk to Rhisereld. \n Entry 16 - I approached Rhisereld and told her to move on from me... It was hard but it was what I needed to do. My mind was collapsing beneath itself from the constant bombardment of voices, screaming, and searing agony my mind possesed. I told her I was a danger to her, she would not listen to me. I tried to convince her, to move on and get away from me. But a damned guard was easedropping in my conversation with her. He soon arrested me, tossing me into a cell... Fools, they think they can keep me in a cage? Pathetic... I picked the lock and easily made my escape.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native bests's Vardak", "shiftnative", "Ahad, 22nd of Malins Welcome, 1331. After Vardaks brutal assault on the elven encampment, He returns and is spotted by the High Prince of Malinor. The Prince then challenges the orc to fight. \"I will show you death.\" After blows returned by both fighters. The High Prince then stands above the orcs injured body. Vardaks soulstone glows and returns him to the monks of the aegis temple. Aye?", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's  Journal, Tolta, 10th of The Amber Cold, 1327.", "shiftnative", "I left Lirinya three notes, leading her her to various parts of the city where I left gifts of my affection. A wonderful day was had today, I was sly and well. Tried to tell her someone was seen entering her house, to push her in the direction of the quest I made her and... well.. she seemed to have already completed it! She held the book in her hand! I gulped and asked her how many books she had gotten. In which she replied \"3\". All of the books! She had aquired All of them! I straightened up and looked at her and she smiled back at me. At this point i'm dancin g all over inside. I'm practically dragged away by a group of question bearing settlers only having looked back at her a few times as I was carried off was not enough. She stood outside her small home smiling still, she seemed to understand my.. duties as the High Prince and the wishes of many. As I was out dealing with these said settlers, a dove came to me with notes from lirinya. She thanked me for my words and I was sure to send her back responses as the group chattered. She is very patient with me, I know the looks ive given her around were more affectionate than I would any other. I know sit in my bedroom, with my back against my bookshelf. This book will lay in my shelf, aside my bed, and my pillows.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Autograph", "shiftnative", "Native of Malinor~ *chuckles.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Book", "shiftnative", "If you hold this book, you've completed the gauntlet. Bring this to Native.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Journal", "shiftnative", "Aye Under ground aye Aye", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Marriage Purposal", "shiftnative", "Princess Lirinya, will you be my wife under the sun, moon & stars. Growing alongside the trees, devoting our attention to one another and provoking the betterment of our own ideals. Lirinya, you are jewel in our forest and I wish to stand along side you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Note", "shiftnative", "Aye, Lady Lirinya. My time has been spent in the wilds alongside the Wardens, traveling into the horizon seeking more gateways to the undeads firey realm. My heart nearly burst when I read of your worry for me and the planting of the flower I left you.  Being in your home is so very quaint and cozy. It's very much like a sanctuary. \\ May Malin guide our paths so that the both of us may meet in harmony and solice.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Note.", "shiftnative", "Perhaps we can get a bite to eat somewhere? -Native", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Quest", "shiftnative", "Sabet, 7th of The Deep Cold, 1336. The Wandering Wizard sent an owl to balcony in the heart of Old Laurelin purposing a Quest. He then told me of a library, in the wilds. That there, a book may lay within its shelves that is a keystone in recovery of one of Aeriels Weapons. The Axe. I relenquished my title of High Prince shortly after recieving his owl. I travel lightly now, deep into the horizon under Malins Moon. Be well my friends, I will return. Greetings, Alys Please, distribute these two elves, if you would I have spoken to many (( wow i messed up everybook )) (( i CANNOT figure out the /bw -remove command ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's tattered book.", "shiftnative", "The Elven Embassy in Kal'Alras is nearly finished! My hands still ache from all of the labor. The Cripson Isle just south of laurelin has been protected once more aswell. I've also met an interesting elf named Aeowinn. He's built a Beautiful camp north of Raven Hold. He even constructed an entire road to the said camp! It's a lovely place. Day 2: A war was waged on Al'Khazar and the elves of Malinor answered the call, upon arriving I climbed up the keeps hill and gazed across the city, the buildings were engulfed in flame and boughts of lightning struck everything in sight. A flurry of footsteps & swinging swords were prevelent.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Wedding Ritual", "shiftnative", "When the desired amount  of guests have arrived, The male stands at the alter as the female is accompanied by anyone of her choosing. Once taken to the ceremony. She is to walk  to her partner, and stand beside him at the alter. I then adress the two, by name to the gathering. Then speak on behalf of their love and it's growth. Adressing their matromony in relationship to Aegis and their ties to settlements. The Male and Female to be wed are then asked seperately, to speak on behalf of their love. Once they're finished, I begin to seal the ritual with a few words and the couple are asked to embrace.     .", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Word", "shiftnative", "You have my blessings, friends.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Word on \"To whom it may concern by Princess Indelwehn.", "shiftnative", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's word on \"To Whom it may concern\" by Princess Indelwehn.", "shiftnative", "I approve of her decision with the robed traveler.", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Word.", "shiftnative", "Back up, orc !", ""),
        StaticBook("Native's Words", "shiftnative", "May your love carry on into the distance, beyond the mountains and forests of ancient landscapes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natives Journal vol. 02", "shiftnative", "I sit outside from the druid grove aside a small elf named Sadi. It seems the druid grove is quite full! It has just been Druid Mahten, and Jenathia's wedding. It wa s held south east of serpent ridge at the same area where Indelwehn and Aedan were wed. Just doing some writing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natuer where could I start. It's every where you go. Inside or outside it will be there", "zapper239", "Good. Good Natuer is a sign of life and peace Natuer can not be made it must grow. ((lol", ""),
        StaticBook("Natural Law Vol. 2", "a98x", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Natural Law Vol.1", "a98x", "There are some laws one must adhere to in nature: 1. For every tree cut, three must be planted (Druidic saying) 2. Do not leave a floating tree, for it is a sign of disrespect. 3. Do not scar the land on the surface, where all passerby will see. 4. Do not leave a farm without a full harvest of each grown wheat. 5. Do not cut only the stem of a large mushroom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature", "Roxses20", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature", "sconn", "Nature is a thing to cherrish. I hope it will never perish. For your sunrise is a beautiful sight. And to me a delight. Nothing i am just thinking out loud.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature", "MeGoRage", "When i sat and thought about the past, a drop of water hits me. I look up and the tree that hangs sadly drops tears ,see . The tree has a scratch over its side, witch it cant try to hide. I think, is this what humanity are doing, taking down every single piece of love Because without narute, we wouldnt breath, walk, or live", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Poem", "Skelly247", "Nature is mighty \n Nature is strong \n Nature is usually always right \n Nature is rarely ever wrong \n Nature is beauty \n Nature is moody \n Nature is smart \n Nature always has the greater part \n Nature is blue \n Nature is green \n Nature is every color possibly seen \n Nature is true \n Nature is beaming \n Nature is dreaming \n Nature is in every place \n Nature is always with grace \n Nature is true \n Nature is you \n Nature is me \n Nature will forever be free Love.", ""),
        StaticBook("nature poem", "spychicken956", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Shield", "Todd877", "((Need leaves for this.)) Nature Shield is a spell that raises nature to form a barrier in front of you. This spell doesn't last very long outside of wooded areas. You usually need some leaves as a locus (fancy word for focus point) for this. When you are ready to cast the spell, say ******* (say *cast Nature Shield). Note that this will not hold off a determined attacker with a sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's beauty", "sconn", "Nature is a thing to cherrish. I hope you will never perish.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's Flow, By Dedicant Saviticus", "Saviordude", "No one controls nature's flow, \n Where she comes or where she goes. \nShe will go upon her path, \n Nature is the only thing that ever lasts, \n Her intentions are always true, \n Helping me and helping you. \n \nHer warm embrace surrounds us all \nThough certain people hear her call \n To go out and mend and fix \nThe things that make nature sick. \n \nSo let ye know that this is true \n That nature is there to help you \n Fairly take and fairly give \n And stay true to the life you live.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's Flow, by Druid Dedicant Saviticus Treebeard", "Saviordude", "No one controls nature's flow \n How she comes or where she goes, \n She will go upon her path \n Nature is the only thing that ever lasts. \n Her intentions always true \n Helping me and helping you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's Heart", "darthalex99", "When you think about nature you think about trees and plants. You must also think of how there will always be a beating heart in all of nature that is keeping all living things alive. Without this there would be no life and the world we know would be nothing. This heart beats inside of every person and living thing throughout Aegis. Never forget this heart of nature. It will always be there no matter what happens to you or to anyone else", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature, the Muse", "CrunchySushi", "\nNature is my muse, \nHow you dance with your animals, \nYour birds and sheep \nThey sing and jump about \nAs the forest gathers in \nGentle yet unwavering \nProsperous with provisions \nBearing trees and all \nYou are the muse of many \nEver loving, Yet ever scornful \nYou are the muse that drives me  \nLeading me to your ways \nTeach me oh Nature, as you have taught those before me \nGive us all inspiration \nAs we give you our unwavering thanks \nNature is my muse, and it is beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Lesson", "silco97", "I watch the waves crash in, breaking on the shore.  All their anger dispensed on the oceans floor \nI look at the blue sky, sun shining so bright.  Spreading heat and happiness with its blinding light \nLong blades of grass swaying in the gental breeze.  Danceing in rhythm with so much ease \nLook up at the trees hearing the sining of the birds.  Happily chirping at ease without words Laying here holding my hands to my chest.  Watching and hearing nature at it's best \nI ponder how nature could get it so right.  When we have let nature's lessons get so out of sight \nWe hold our anger, let out happiness slip away.  Making out survival a struggle each and every day \nWe have forgotten the little things the mean so much.  Like the laughter, the freedom, and someone's loving touch \nif only I could make people stop, watch and listen to natures tale.  We could all sit back happily and out world would not be so frail. \nIn each pthers existence in harmony we could all survive.  I'm sure like the sun, wind, tree, and birds out lives we could revive. \nIf only we let nature take its course in each and every one of us each day and night. As I let and ponder how nature got so right", ""),
        StaticBook("Navy Units", "Groobs03", "Corporal Fealnor ((MrHobo)) Navy Spec. Jowa ((jowa2992)) , BlackBear ((BlackPython007)) , benah ((benah)) ,Oghren ((Craftsmaster))", ""),
        StaticBook("Nayr", "FishFr0g", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nayr's Journal", "rricher", "I started off in Aegis unlearned and a little confused, but made my way to the town of Al'Kazar. Wandering through the city square one day there was a group of people asking me if I would like to join there house as a gaurd. Happly I accepted and up to date I have been helping them gather recources for there estate and upcoming town. One day while walking through the city I saw a group of people who call themselves the hooded , they had asembled in the center square.  I missed most of the conversation but noticed that gaurd captain Vardek was feeling ill. I was asking him about it when his eyes started glowing puple and he fled us. worryingly we chased him down into the sewer were we found out he was possesed by a demon. after a long chase we found out that he had it under control. hi hello hello hello. hello", ""),
        StaticBook("Nazushdoren", "ZazarusDious", "Agith Amberlance found a blade covered in green canvas and undoubtedly of necromantic infulence. I 'ave dubbed de blade Nagushdoren. Blood Diamond as fer its effects are rather horrifyin'. From what ever de blade cuts and makes bleed, dat blood will be syphoned inte a layer of diamond. Sharp and deadleh. It glows purple when it does this unholy act. Agith says it hold some kind of jelousy, and will not let its current wileder use anythin' else. A mind o' its on it 'as. It will even return back te de currentwielder even when casted out to de deepest of chasms. It returns to punish de wielder fer doin' so as well. Te make thin's worse de wilder will die if not passed on to anoder victim. Though to stop it frem what Agith tells me: The bearer must diw with de blade and wrapped in dat same green canvas, deep under an elder tree... How in de blazes can we 'elp Agith in a small period o' time?", ""),
        StaticBook("ne lo key shan  flas", "Thaddeus12", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancy", "Castellano", "Necromancy - Black Magic; The art of communicating with the Dead; Witchcraft;  There are many forms of Necromancy, but in this day, there is only secret Necromancy. \nA group that people call the \"Undead\" have been known to use Necromancy to their full extent.  The Necromancers in their organization have been using Necromancy against the people of Aegis.  The powers that the dead give them threw Necromancy, gives them the ability to summon the dead, use the weather, as in lightening, and use magic that comes from Hell, or also known as \"Nether\". \nThe people of Aegis have started to follow the \"Undead\" and Necromancers and have been studying their ways, giving them the ability to use this form of Black Magic. The Ascended (Good guys) have been known to be against this magic.  Ascended does not potral the open roads like the Necromancers and Undead do.  Rumors around say that they stay at a heavenly place near the Cloud Temple. \nThe attacks of the Necromancers have been deadly, and usually have won the battle and took the victory back to the Nether and celebrated with the spirits.  The only known places that have been attacked are Snowy Fields, Winterfell, Alstion Town, and Kal'Bryst. Now if you haven't noticed already, it has been going from north to south.  In that case the conditions that have been gathered threw predictions that the next attacks could be at the following cities:  Al'Khazar, Stone Leaf, Whispering Isle, and Kal'Aras. They are just slight predictions, the Undead probably won't even attack them.  It's just prediction. \nThe Undead are growing in numbers, the last known report of them traveling in a pack was the number count of five.  But the last report was long ago.  The numbers could have been doubled, no one knows. \nSo from what you have been reading, The Necromancers are deadly, and you should avoid them at all times.  If not, you could lose your life, or loved ones around you. \n \n I, the Author, is leaving the book un-signed, so that if an Undead member finds this I won't be slain.  A second book could be created if any more records or information is released. *Books is un-signed and has blank pages in the back of the book* \n \n \n", ""),
