        StaticBook("Necropolis", "nachotp", "I was scared, I didn't know what to do, They were everywhere, I couldn't leave this hideout otherwise they would see me, and they attack with no mercy, I shoud never came here. \n Let me tell you my whole story, It all begun with a tale, a tale about a big city, a city like n  o others, a city almost unreachable, this city ws in another dimensio n, a dimension totally different from ours, a dimension with no sun, no water and no trees but in despite of that with life, All the water was lava, all the light came from fire, lava, and glowstone, there are natives too, the zombie pig-man they are neutral but if you dare to attack one of the m, they will all strike against you but there are beasts too, huge beasts, beasts that flies, they are aggresive amd they will attack you with explosive fireballs, peopla have been able to deflect them but yet they are a huge threat, if you achieve to attack one of them, they will scream so loud that everyone hears it,  everyone in the Necropolis, in the entire dimension, and also they come out of the portal , everyone hears their crying, these are the guardians of the Necropolis, leaving only the citizens alive and the strangers dead. The citizens are made from rotten flesh, people say that they, time ago where humans, elves, orcs and dwarves but once the entered the city they became the undead. \n So I went towards the north to reach these portals, when I arrived I heard screams coming out of them, screams of pain, I was not sure to cross but my adventure sense was thinking something else, So I went in and it felt like everything was spinning, then I saw it, The Necropolis was in front of my eyes, when I approached it was already too late, they saw me, I fortunately found a palce to hide, so I ran there, I was scared, I didn't know what to do, they where everywhere, I couldn't leave the hideout otherwise they would see me, and they attack with no mercy, I should never came here. I thought it was the end of everything, but then when I was about to surrender I saw a shimmering light coming out of nowhere, then I cleared my eyes and I saw him, he was one of the 6 Sages, the light was his aura, he said \" It is not time for you to die\" and then I appeared in my house next to the fireplace with a bit of headache, next to me I found a note that said that I should never came there, the dimension called \"Nether\" was a soul extractor, and that there is a war coming, a war that we could win, a war against the Undead. But every nation should come together to fight with the ascended agaisnt the undead, a nation will betray us all, but we should be ready to fight! ready to protect our cities! ready to protect our family, and when we achieve winning we will ahve an eternal peace. \n \n [Nashtoff Library Productions]", ""),
        StaticBook("Nel'Thok's Journal", "Carnivore91", "I be startin dis today. Recently my mind be strugglin to be rememberin what I did and said. T oday I returned from my great journey to be gettin away. I met wit Dominus Bein near da new fort for our guild. It be a grand new structure dat us oOr Orcs be proud of. I den made my way back to da Elf city and be learnin new, not good things. \n Dere be a man dere dat be seein da Undead have been talkin to da High Prince. He be sayin possibly all da high powered people of all races maybe corrupted. I be not trustin dis mon, but I be keepin a lookout! \nDere was a man dat was on ajourny for many books dat be hiden around da world. He be saying sometin about da undead. Not sure why but he be seemin like a smart mon. Have to find him aga in someday. \nI be seein da High Prince tonight, but unable to talk to him bout da Undead issue. But I be able to listen to da conversation he had wit anotter, about how some his guild be go ing evil. He be good though and be protectin da Elves once again. It been a long day today, so I be restin soon, continue this anodder time. \nNot much be happenin today. Barely seen any of da Orcs. Need to be makin my way back to da homeland and be chattin bout recruitment here in da city of da Elves. Also be findin out more information bout dem undead. Deh be all over me tink! \nToday I be visitin da evil place underneath dose towers. I met my end down dere. But luckily da spirits be bringin me back again! \nToday be busy mons. I be defeaten an undead at da cost of my life. Den a bandit fooled me into buyin da rare undead book, but it be fake. Den some wierd meetin between Elder SHaman Brevious and Val guy. Maybe evil doins... \n The last few weeks I have been lazy in this, but I got aid and my language is much better. I'm happy for this! Possibly help shorten the barrier between Orcs and th other races. \nBought a mining permit today in the new Elf mine, and picked up a big hall of iron. Made myself a new set of armor and repaired my sword. Hope to increase my smithing skills. Thats enough for today, will continue this another! \nToday was a very chaotic day. First, Craotor informed me that Bell had invofrmed him that there was a rogue Orc forming a group of Dwarven bandits to asault Laureling. I immediate made the trip and informed High Prince Native. He quickly set up guards to protec him. Then an Undead worshipper showed up at the gates but was killed. So much evil in the world. Oh Petri was the Bandit Orc. After a long day I was walking when I heard Tre'bok shouting he was looking for a Shaman apprentice! This will apease those voices. Hope to hear from him soon. Enough today write again soon. \n It has been a long time since I have last written. First I have started my training as Sha man. Passed my first lesson and wait for more. Have traveled great distances recently. Hearing new stories. One good one is of Shaman Lex telling me a story of a hunt he went on recently involving books located in tombs. He was stuck on the last clue, \"The fake father of Al'kazar\" \"In his hands\" \"In his heart\" At first he thought it was Horen, but he was the real maker. I do not know enough of the history of Oren to know historic names, but soon hope to learn more and perhaps find this artifact, before it's in evil hands. Many weeks since I last wrote. I have learned many things. First I met an Elf that I went to talk to the King of the Dwarves. He was not there though, so he told us the news he had. Hwaldar was healed by a priest! Which in turn brings me to my next discovery. I have located the Artifacts location that Shaman Lex was searching for. The sword is locked away though, and I believe Hwaldar is the only one to open it. But I have hopes to possibly retrieve it. A few stories here and there but they are not important. Enough for now, continuing again soon. \nAdventure since I last wrote. I was in Oren when the undead attacked. Many fell, specifically the King. We fought them off, but I seen a man by Ademas and Bell injured so I tried to help. Bell was ok, but Ademas was worse. I tried everything I knew, but he died. I was then was told by a note in his pocket to delivier his diamond eye to Bwaldar. I cannot remember the exact name, but anyway Bell and I made the journy. We found him delievered the news then decided to see the body. It was a long journy back and forth, but we found it. We went to bury it near Oren. I place a sabling by him in hopes he would grow new again. I then felt a wierd presence. I could feel Ademas' spirit return. He then rose from the grave! As he once was. \nThe next adventure was with an Orc by the name or Vadrak. He was gathering Human, Orc, and Elven troops to stop Powell from rebelling against Oren. It involved the new king of Oren, High Prince Native, and the former Queen of Oren. Was a grand sight to see them all in one area. I will continue this when I fidn out more. A very long time since I last opened this. \n To finish the Rebel incident it was quelled by Vardak and many others. He is a brave on and glad to know him as an ally. \n I made my way to Oren to meet up with my good friend Bell. Apperently Ademas died and risen again, but to be forever changed. I did not press Bell for more info, for she seemed angry of the ordeal, but learned of something new. She has apperently joined a guild and has sent a request that I bring her this journal for a chance to join this guild! A grand honor if I have to say. It may be a time before I write again because of this, but it may be worth it. \n I finally opened this book again. I can't believe how long it's beens ince I've writen in this. Much has happened since My last words. . At my last writing I was just joining the Mages Guild. Wow so much to cover! Well to begin witha  death. Bell was killed in action against the Undead. I miss her so. She was a good friend and her passing was untimely, but her passing wasn't a complete. waste, her replacement is Lothierel. And she a damn spitting image of Bell! Can't help but smiling writing about her because of how much She reminds me of Bell. But need to move on. Dominus Bein was killed and returned as a spirit. Dominus Thyst died challenging the Re. Rex. Tythus was slained and power is now to Warlord Mogroka Sanhar was torn down, rebuilt, attacked and semi destroyed by Undead, and now rebuilt again. The Mages Guild is on hold until magic releases itself. But I am now Elder Shaman since Tre'bok has died. Teaching students in the Guild house. My first apprentice Draygo is nearly done with training. Lets see what else... The Orcs have been rising in power recently. And the Undead seem to be gone for the moment. \n Ah yes, the ancestors.... Bein's spirit and a few others have been around recently. Demanding sacrifices and blood to the Heart of Krug. Was fine and good until the Festival of Krug happened. Was a glorious day until... The Undead attacked and corrupted the heart! It corrupted the ancestors immediatly. And the two that touched it, Bog and another. I did not know it at the time, but it came appearent when an ancestor lead me there. He tried to kill me but I survived, only to be told that I should bring the Shamans another day so he could kill them all, and if not he would corrupt all those I love. The Heart.... became Corruption itslef! The very thing that Drove Iblees to his dark fall! The Shaman's and I shall go. We must destroy the heart before it ruins the world! Will write again after this happens.", ""),
        StaticBook("Neo-Druidism", "drplat", "This tome was originally created by Petyr Brandybuck. \n With some modern druidic practices wandering astray, it has been necessary for me to scribe another text - that of Neo-Druidism. Throughout my travels and my meditative studies, I have had revelations unknown to others. It is important to understand that there is a special type of balance that druids themselves    remember to study - action and non-action. Let me clarify. Action is motion, the motion of restoring balance, and of being the hand of Nature. Non-action is meditation and silence; invisible motion. You see, this is the only Way to truly understand Nature, the Universe, the \"It\". For, through non-action you may feel \"It\", and through action you may be \"It\". Call this \"It\" what you want; most druids will call it Nature. What is important is to understand what Nature truly is, and how it relates to you. To reveal this is the goal of this tome.  \n Section 1 - The Unity of Nature *** The first fault in thinking is to make distinctions - those between you and Nature, between life and death, between good and evil. Everything is Nature, despite what any given piece believes. A druid does not use nature: a druid is merely a piece who realizes the profound truth. Through non-action, one may truly understand this concept and feel it course through them. However, while meditating in non-action, one also separates themself from the flow; the Way, the path that Nature chooses for its pieces. To rejoin with Nature, one must practice action. \n *** Section 2 - The Way of Nature *** Nature does what it will, and while we realize this while meditating, sometimes we forget in action. We are merely moving along the river of life, the tides of balance. While we believe that we are restoring the balance, it is balance restoring itself in an everlasting self-conflict. Thus, through action, we are the hands of Nature, of balance, of the Way. One must not think of \"using\" Nature while playing their part, but of \"being\" Nature. This is a common mistake as well among young druids and non-druids. They think to restore the world by planting lots of trees... but that is not balance, nor is it even the way to achieve balance. Action alone is not the Way, for one forgets the purpose of action. Only with the mix of action and non-action can one achieve the goal: to have your cake and eat it, too. \n \n Section 3 - The Druid *** So as we can now see, the Druid is simply the most important hand, the piece Nature uses to govern itself. To truly try to understand is a task that lies within meditation and non-action. However, there is a limit to the mental reach of the pieces, for as no one truly knows all of themselves, Nature does not know all of itself. This is a fairly important observation: that even though Nature is unified, the unification is marked by threadlines of dubiousness and doubt. The Neo-Druid should not fret, however. There are uneven surfaces in every river. No tree has identical leaves. Just so, nothing, no \"It\", can be the symmetrical perfection one would like to see. Randomness and uniqueness are inherent in Nature, as defining as the unity itself. Paradoxical though it may seem, through balance of action and non-action, it shall be revealed to you, and only then will you understand the phrase.... \n \"All is One\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero Sable's Report", "Sarge878", "Unfortunately I do not have very much to report. It is fairly quiet in Oren. I just met with the new King, and he told me to find Elves who may be interested in future job opportunities in Oren. Over the next few days, I will carry out this task, along with keeping my pointy ears and my sharp eyes open in order to do my job in better serving Malinor and Oren. I hope that my next report will be a lot more interesting. \n \n ~Nero Sable", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero Sable's Report I", "Sarge878", "Nero Sable's Report I \n \n My first diplomatic errand to Al'Khazar, the jewel of the great Kingdom of Oren was a huge success. High Prince Native gave me the task of asking an official of Oren permission to build a Wood Elf camp North of the kingdom. After a few days of searching, I finally contacted the King himself. I asked him for permission, and he said that it would be perfectly fine for us to build an encampment. I also met with the Chief Ambassador of Oren, and he welcomed me with great hospitality. He sends his warm regards to High Prince Native. He also tells me that he might require my assistance soon. Very soon I shall depart for Al'Khazar once again, to see if they require my aid. \n \n The Elven Diplomat to Oren, \n \n~Nero Sable", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero Sable's Report II", "Sarge878", "After a few days of trying to get in contact with someone from Oren, I finally managed to get ahold of King Sheffield. We chatted for a bit, and I told him of the High Prince's request for a Store of Malinor. King Sheffield seemed on board with this idea, however he informed me that there were no current building openings as far as he knew. I will keep my eyes open and watch for an opening, and inform you of any new updates. \n \n -Nero Sable", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero Sable's Report III", "Sarge878", "Itnan, 16th of The Amber Cold, 1321 \n \n Today marks a grim day in Oren's history. At first when I arrived to Oren, I went to the keep and witnessed a large dispute between the current King Sheffield's followers, and Perea's old followers . I left shortly to see if I could get the attention of the High Prince or any other Princes. Upon returning, it seemed as though King Sheffield arrived to break up the conflict. With Perea's followers defeated (and Perea himself), all seemed well again.\n \n Then, it happened. The Princess went up to her room to check on something. We then heard her scream. I went around the corner to witness some man gripping the Princess's throat. The man proceeded to cut her throat. She bled out in her room, and died there. \n \n In the coming weeks, I will spend most of my time in Oren, helping the King during this dire time. \n \n ~Nero Sable", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero Sable's Selling List:", "Sarge878", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nero's Story", "alien1workshop1", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nether?", "DefunctDivine", "A portal to the nether? In an elven prince's house? I'm sure the public would love that... Ohoho... I reccomend a vote.\n ~M.V.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nevarren History: The Rise of Brandmark", "Raptor14", "In the seed year 614, in a land not far from Oren, was a great mountain. This mountain stood alone and stood strong, unlike the other mountains. Its peak was covered in snow while its base was abundant with nature. For hundreds of years it was undisturbed by people or creatures, but that year a group of humans approached the mountains mighty face. This group settled at the bottom of the mountain and built a small community. These people were had some different features to other humans. Their eyes were not the same colours as normal humans. They ranged from Crimsons and Reds to Purples and Greys. Soon more and more of these people flocked towards the mountain, until the community grew to a humble village. Brandmark was born. \n\n For hundreds of years Brandmark lived peacefully and quietly, not attracting any attention. But in the seed year 826 something incredible happened. The leader of teh village Ne'amar, looked into teh distance and saw what he thought was a large bird. But, as it got closer, he realised it was not a bird but a great winged reptile. The creature flew over and around the village, seeming to eye each and everyone carefully. Finally it flew up to the Great Mountain and rested on a large ledge on its face. \n For 10 Years the  Dragon did not disturb the villagers. It would only sit upon the ledge and watch as the people went through their lives. The people of Brandmark dubbed the mountain Dragon's Peak. In the year 836 the Great Dragon flew down off the peak and landed in the town square. The Dragon raised his long neck and arched his wings and spoke in a great and powerful voice, \"I am Andoral the Great Dragon of the Silver Fire. I have watched you people for years. I have admired your peacefulness and determination. I have the power to make you a Great Nation that kings from all around will look up to. \" And that is exactly what he did. Andoral forged the Stone walls and the iron doors, the weapons and the throne of Brandmark . Over the next 100 years Kings came and went, nations rose and fell, but Andoral remained at Brandmark. \n In the seed year 930 the people of Brandmark began to change. They became arrogant and power hungry, thinking they could take on every challenger because they had Andoral on their side. They even began to worship Andoral as a God. Andoral, being a humble Dragon, did not want to be worhshipped by anyone. So he decided that it was time to leave. But before he did, he had one more task to complete. He left a Descendant in the form of a human, and named him Fen'Harel. Fen'Harel had crimson eyes and was the first in this Dragonborn line. Over the next 30 years, Fen'Harel grew strong and wise, and Brandmark became arrogant and aggressive. (to find out about Fen'Harel read \"Fen'Harel: a true hero\") \n One day King Ainara of Brandmark challenged the Orc Nation. He believed that they could crush anyone even without Andoral. The two great nations fought for weeks upon the Silent Hills, until finally Brandmark was nearly defeated. They were pushed back all the way to the city and teh orcs sieged it for 50 days and 50 nights. On the 47th day Fen'Harel heard a voice inside his head. It was the Great Dragon Andoral. \"There is a tunnel through the Dragon's Peak, lead you people to safety.\" Fen'Harel gathered his wife and newborn son, and told as many people as he could of his plan. As the remaining people of Brandmark left their beloved City, Fen'Harel looked back, only to witness the Orcs penetration of the mighty walls. They killed  everyone left inside and burnt the city to the ground. \n Now the people of Brandmark are scattered all across Aegis, in hiding, waiting for the right time to rise up once more. They now call themselves Nevarrens and wait for the day when a hero will come and wait for the day when a hero will rise and save them once more.", ""),
        StaticBook("New", "MeGoRage", "", ""),
        StaticBook("new", "fabian9696", "", ""),
        StaticBook("New Guard System KOTF", "chas5511", "The new guard system is meant to maximize the guards progress in protecting our home, as well as increase there pay (Minas, Rank) as well as keep those horrible bandits away. The system will implement using a \"one week\" guard post. This will allow each member to know ahead of time where and when the will be on duty. Also an extra pay will be provided to those who agree to be a guard. For example. Guard1 will go to tower3 and stay in that area for a weeks time (5 minecraft days) for a total of 4 weeks untill the cycle is restarted. This will protect our home, and satisfy our my at the same time. Guards should be provided with Iron weponry and armor to minimze harm in case of attack. IN CASE OF UNDEAD ATTACK: If there is ever an attack. The guard will get some Flint and Steel and light a fire on the top of there tower. Alerting anyone near by.", ""),
        StaticBook("New HOme", "Ghost_Storm", "New Home", ""),
        StaticBook("New Mansion Owner Guide", "JayRocknWeezy", "Welcome to New Mansion Owner Guide! Purchasing and moving into a new home is a very exciting time in you life and we are pleased to share it with you. We have prepared this book as a companion to our publication New Homeowner, A Guide To Your New Home. We would like to thank the thousands of Real Estate agents nationwide who are participating in our program by distributing free copies of New Homeowner to home buyers like you. Take a few moments to check out the helpful info on the book. All of the topics featured here have been prepared just for you, the new home owner. We hope you enjoy your new home and don't forget to thank your real estate agent.", ""),
        StaticBook("new member", "Thatpyrodude", "Dacripla99", ""),
        StaticBook("New Navy branch", "Groobs03", "My Sargeant Jowa has made a new branch for the navy called the Navy Rangers, i allowed him to do so . if you have any objections of course tell me and i will have it revoked. Basically its navy with bows and axes.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Terriko", "ShAadow0", "New Twerriko is a blooming just past whisper isle. Mining there has been fruitfull", ""),
        StaticBook("New Wrath's Clutch Report [King's Road.]", "MechaWolf", "I was patrolling around Malinor as I had recently been promoted to a Guard. Along the way I wanted to check out the old Wrath's Clutch ruins as a memorial from the last attack , as I went down King's road as per usual the people walking past were plenty but most of which look frightened and such, I thus went down the path further to look around to see what's going on. What I saw had me confused for a moment, a large fort had erected itself over the past few months [days] that I had not travelled past these paths. Many humans were shouting up into the fort so I get closer to have a look to investigate. To my dismay lightning struck down from the skies and the clouds turned dark around the fort. It would seem that the Undead has graced the land with it's presences once again as their minions struck at the humans as they peered out of their horrifying temporary portal [Spawning]. The fort had people that I couldn't quite make out in it but they were yelling at everyone who got close to the gates. [I couldn't tell their race from the skin they had on them, they were too far.] The humans seemed angry and tried to invade the fort, only to be burned by some sort of magical fire and lava trap at their gate. Which they promised to bring back different and more reinforcements \"next time\". I had to take my leave as the guards of the fort were coming down to try and keep bystanders away. -Elessar Celebrindal [16/10/2011 7:15AM GMT +8]", ""),
        StaticBook("New Wrath's Clutch's Report.", "MechaWolf", "I arrived here in the middle of the day, it would seem that the walls are now properly built and there are more people in the insides now. Most of them look out of the towers and yell at people who attempt to get close to the \"fort\". It would seem that this IS indeed the fort of the undead, as lightning flashes and thunder crackle through the air, people scramble about as mobs of the undead were spawned. Evidence of the mobs and people talking about the lightning is captured but not the lightning itself directly as it went past too quickly and unexpectedly. Most of the people who attempted to enter the fort were Humans and some Orcs it seems. The leaders of the invading party spoke of returning with larger and different armies of sorts. Traps visable from outside are the one like the fire trap and lava trap at their gate. Nothing can be seen as of now. -Elessar. 16/10/11 7:15AM GMT +8", ""),
        StaticBook("New_Horizons", "x_I_AM_DEADLY_x", "New_Horizons Hey", ""),
        StaticBook("News from he Dwarven Capital (9/25)", "KindaSpacey", "My attempts to contact Algrim have been unsuccesful, hence I've been unable to form a trade agreement with the dwarves. If I an unable to track him down in the next couple of days, I will speak with another High Councilman. I am hoping to get a hold of some darkwood, as it is always in high demand here. Some iron would do nicely as well, are Wardens should always be equiped with the best equipment minas can buy. Moving on, I've heard from one semireliable that the current Lord Marshall, Campington, has been fired. He had developed a reputation for being a bit of a scoundrel, after taking part in several illicit acts. Most notably he abused position to rob a fellow dwarf. His replacement will be bringing back the Dwarven Legion, replacing the current Free Dwarves Army.                    ~Zaros", ""),
        StaticBook("News from Kal'Urguan", "KindaSpacey", "Outer Kal'Urguan being redone", ""),
        StaticBook("News from the Dwarven Capital", "KindaSpacey", "~Outer Kal'Urguan is currently being redesigned and rebuilt. \n~Orc spies attempted to get into the city, but were stoppe by the guards \n~Many dwarves feel that with the absence of the King, very little has been accomplished \nLafthi's Request: \n1. Ask the King Belin or a member of the High Council if they are willing to build a rail to Ravenhold \n2. Figure out whether a coup could take place in Kal'Urguan \n3. Ask for Belin's opinion of Kal'Alras \nA coup seems highly unlikely, but if one were to occur it would be most likely led by Guard Brokk and/or another nation \n~Belin considers Kal'Alras and it's citizens allies \n~Beling would be willing to build a rail to Ravenhold, as long as the construction was supervised by an elf \n~Outer Kal'Urguan struck by lightning, causing a building to be burn down ~Orlock named the new Archbishop of Kal'Urguan after Barin's resignation", ""),
        StaticBook("News from the Dwarven Capital (9/15)", "KindaSpacey", "Kal'Urguan is a quiet place, not so different from Malinor. As I have mentioned in our past conversations, Hogarth was fired from his position as Archbishop. I have had an oppurtunity to speak with Hogarth since then, at his new home in the City of Aerial. He has no ill feelings towards Algrim and the rest of the High Council (excluding the Lord Marshall) , but is unsure as to why he was fired. I'm sure Algrim has his reasons though, I'll be sure to speak with him about this. In other news, the nation of Kal'Urguan has been hiring dwarves as state workers. Jobs that they are offering include farming, woodcutting, and fishing. This was a wise move by Algrim, as not every dwarf is interested in joining the guard. That is all the news that I've been able to gather, I hope that you found this report helpful and informative.                              Your friend and colleague, Zaros.", ""),
        StaticBook("News from the Dwarven Capital (9/18)", "KindaSpacey", "Very little has changed since my last report. I have tried to make contact with the new Archbishop, but to no avail. The Outer City is a ghost town, as is the Inner City. However, there are several notable that I thought would worth mentioning in this report.", ""),
        StaticBook("News from the Dwarven Capital (9/22)", "KindaSpacey", "The Kal'Urguan that Belin worked so hard to create is now virtually gone. King Algrim has completely redone the city from top to bottom. These changes are evident from the moment you enter the city. First of all, the area that was once the Outer City has now been converted to farmland. This are is now frequented by farmers, lumberjacks, and fisherman alike, all hoping to sell their wares. Beyond this part of the city, you will come across a newly built housing district. Houses here go for around 7000-75k minas, providing homes for moderately wealthy dwarves. Past this, in Kal'Urguan Inner City, two new districts have sprung up. A scholarly district and another holding with a tavern and several houses for sale. This will encourage more dwarves to live underground, as they once did under the rule of King Simppa.                                             Moving on, I recently received news of Belin's passing. He will be greatly missed by his dwarven brethren. He will be remembered as a great ruler, somebody who embodied dwarven kindness and generousity.", ""),
        StaticBook("News from the Dwarven Capital (9/5)", "KindaSpacey", "Since his coronation of Algrim, Kal'Urguan has undergone a fair few changes.", ""),
        StaticBook("News of Great Importance", "mercury199", "High Prince Native, I have some very grave news. I have reports from many citizens and wardens. That the druids have turned sides and cast their lot with the UNDEAD ! The arch druid has been disapearing lately with no excuse, and she is very defensive when  approached about it. Also when walking along the kings road the number of undead is striking ( I can smell them ) There was a woman amongst several of the, m, she did speak with the same tounge tone pitch and voice of the arch druid, and did have an identical body build. She is a traitorI think, and we shall loose laurelin to the undead if w e do not act quickly !  May I add it is not all the druid attacking the innocent but I have seen some do the such with mine ow n eys Attack those In and out of Laurelin I fear the worst.", ""),
        StaticBook("News of my whereabouts.", "MuffinSpankz", "I will be going on an expedition with my cousins of the Blacklocks. Reserve my belonging in these chests until further notice, I will not part without them. ((Also going on holidays for 7 days, so i wont be on)) ((and making a new character for the moment)),", ""),
        StaticBook("newspaper revised edition", "browler4153", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nical Empire Report - Relgard", "Darkdragon274", "9/FirstSeed/1331 \n I stand at the gates of The Empire, awaiting entrance. The tower on the western side appears to have the gate's control lever. There are trees on the southern side. You can climb over the walls via them. \n 13/FirstSeed/1331 \n Recruited into the Empire, soon to do training. Things are good.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nical Town Charter", "pallino", "This charter will instate the Nical, as an official full fledged town of Aegis. By supporting, and signing this charter you are helping us get one step closer to becoming a town.  \n Sign here- \n ((To sign your name do /write (yourname)\n )) Thanks for supporting us! ((Also all signed names will be used on a fourm post)) cucmucy\n bryce141 ,oHawkZo", ""),
        StaticBook("Nice try", "HogLoot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nick's Diary", "Bambrick", "Dear Diary - Today i met a new friend his name is Tayldor_Grims, he is a joly dwarf with lots of ambition and is always thinking about others.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nico Pay Slip", "sam2far9", "Golden Harvest Pay-Slip \n Nico \n 17th October \n Signed Lylth Sylvaris", ""),
        StaticBook("Nightmare's Diary", "bullyreece", "Day 1 I was walking down the road, a nearby fan came running up to me and asked for my autograph I can't Believe how famous I have gotten I am only a monk its quite a surprise really! Then I had come across a mysterious object in the middle of a forest...I picked it up A pain struck through me..It began burning me...the pain was unbearable..I screamed...but no one cam e to help Day 2 I awoke from my slumber with burnt skin and weak....I had to move quickly before i could be found I needed answers on what the device I had found really was...I found none \n Day 3 I awoke at a nearby streetside in Laurelin...I was tired...But Work had to be done \n As I carried on through Laurelin...i was being insulted from all angles I was scared...hypnotised with depression I ran over to a nearby lake to remove the sadness that was burrowed in my life I began to feel...Happy a small smile appeared on my face... But as i looked into the reflection i saw a shimmering image of who I really am A monster... \n With depression I ran into a cave miles from any cities... I lived my life in there...And hid away for years.. \n Day 1254 \n I have been in the cave for many years...I believe I have lost count I am afraid that I must leave this cave and venture on through Oren So i headed to the icey depths of snowy fields where I found an offering for the undead... I believe it will make them proud \n Day 2000 \n I have just been recruited into the black Hand, it seems they offer me hope and salvation", ""),
        StaticBook("Nightshade's Diary", "redmatthieu2", "day 1 - today i found a place i want to live and it has hobbets like me. I hope in the future i will get to live there. untel tomorrow Dairy day 2 - found some new friends they are great day 3 -those friends are nothing but assholes and robbed me day 4 - found some better friends and one of them is a king, I was kind enough to rebuild his farm's Wind Mill and if i do say so my self its looking day 5 - The Wilnd Mill is finished and looks GREAT! Hopefully i get a good pay from the king. Day 6 - got payed for the hard work i did, 5,000 minas! also met this wonderful woman named Valon. She is the greatest thing that has ever happened to me. Hope to be her futur boyfriend. Day 7 - Valon is a bar tender and imet Valons uncle today, nice fellow he is. Hope to be good friends with him. Also Valon gave me 3,000 minas to help pay for our futur home. I hope to spend the rest of my life with this beautiful woman.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nightshade's friends/foes", "redmatthieu2", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Nikolai's place", "Eltyer", "This is a great place to have a room, i strongly approve this. He helps people in the darkest times, just like his personal. This is the least i can do for him. Gezmar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nirum", "Carnivore91", "Today is the first day of praying to the spirits. I shall meditate to Nirum and learn as much as i can. I just prayed to Nirum. I did not learn very much today. I shall focus better tomorrow. I learned two things that will aid me though. First Nirum is a female spirit. Second she requires two sacrifices, The extinguishing of a fire that I must create and the death of a black squid, which pollute the waters. Soon I hope to meditate to her again and possibly meet more spirits. \nPrayed again offering my offerings. She was pleased and revealed she was and Elf before she was a spirit of the water. She has not chosen to let me see her features yet. Soon though... very soon.... \nThe last few weeks Nirum has told me she appreciates my praise, but requires more time. I will soon See her. \nTonight wad the night. She has agreed to show me her. She is beautiful. She was as tall as me with clear blue skin. Her eyes were two bright yellow lights, whish wavy, green hair. She told me in life she lived on the sea. She was born on it, lived on it, and died on it. She di not give me mnay details of her life, which I do not wish her to. Her past life is her secret and she has no need to reveal more. \nShe explained to me the duties of water. Water is both harmony and destruction. Water grows crops, but also washes them away. Water cools the land, but also drowns it. Water fills life, holds life, heals wounds, but it also ends the lives of anything. Nirums is a peaceful but dangerous spirit. I'm glad she chose me. \nThis finished the book of Nirum. I have learned all that I need. I hope to meet other spiri ts soon.", ""),
