        StaticBook("Nonsense", "sprintindwarf", "Ladies and Gentlemen Peons and Peasants Cross Eyed Mosquitos and Bowlegged Ants. Grab a chair and sit on the floor, and ill tell you a story ive naever heard before. One great day in the middle of night, two dead boys got up to fight. back to back they faced each other, drew their swords and shot each other. a deaf gaurd heard the noise, he came and killed the two dead boys. If you dont believe this lie is true, ask the blind man, he saw it too!", ""),
        StaticBook("Norgox Grimebeard, Business card.", "Xorgon1", "\nName: Norgox Grimebeard \nProfession: Redstone Engineer, architect and hunter \nContact name: Xorgon1 \nCall be if you need any of these jobs done!", ""),
        StaticBook("Norgox Grimebeard, Identification Documents", "Xorgon1", "\nFirst Name: Norgox \nSurname: Grimebeard \nAge: 38 \nDOB: 22nd July 1295 \nRace: Dwarf \nProfession: Redstone Engineer, Architect, Hunter", ""),
        StaticBook("Norhem's Journal", "Enfourvie", "I woke at a place calling itself the Temple of the Clouds. \nIt seems the events at Marienburg got a bit out of hand, I do not remember much and what I do remember is hazy. I must find a way to return to my men and to the band of the cockatrice. \nI have a problem. Two actually, It seems my powers as a Grey Mage have been stripped from me. The second problem is I do not know the date, or where I am . \nQuestioning the monks at the temple has gleaned little information. These people have never heard of Marienburg, or even the empire of man! What kind of backwater is this place? \nThe monks here have decided I am healthy once more and capable of venturing forth into this land I know nothing of. Strange names and architecture continue to baffle me. What is this talk of high elves, wood elves and dark elves all living in one nation? I have heard of High elves and Wood elves in uneasy alliances, but Dark elves? I am begining to think this is a dream brought on by black chaos magic. \nIt is not a dream. I left the temple this morning, travelling along a road known as the Kings road, when a giant spider like the ones the Night Goblins ride attacked me and the wounds it dealt me are very real. I am hiding in a cave from the nightmares that prowl this area. \nIt has taken me a few days to reach the City of Men as it is known in these parts after a helpful Dwarf showed me the way. However, as I arrived at night there was no one about, and all the inns I tried were closed. Odd. \nI was forced to leave the city walls. I was driven out by a band of thieves looking for coin, and as I have lost both my sword and my magic, I fled where they would not follow. I am now lost in a forest. It has been days. I have made it to a port town that I do not know the name of. Having looted enough coin from the bodies on the undead to buy myself a replacement sword, I am journeying into the land of the dwarves in the hope that a longer lived can help me. \nI had no luck with the dwarves. I was not allowed entrance, I headed back out into the wilderness. \nI have met a man named Dondo, who has invited me to stay in his village until I know what my next course of action is. \nI lost Dondo. We were making our way through a forest when I was assaulted by spiders. In the attack we were seperated. I am now alone and without a guide in the wilderness, taking shelter in a tree. Great. I have come across a road, on it was a recruitment poster that interested me. It was for a group known as the Shad'rin. I will have to investigate. \nI have made it to the Shad'rin keep. I am attempting to join. \nI was accepted into the Shad'rin, and on my first outing, who do I meet? Ulfvarr Stigandr! My old friend from the campain at Marienburg, I have advised him to join, and we plan to go on a hunt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Norodrun Notes", "Wasp2100", "Baron Brothers Cedric (Chumpchump) and Kutul Darkbringer are in command of Norodrun :Cedric: Seems an extremely capable ruler, and a great guy. A lot of water in the catacombs, secret tunnels underneath Norodrun that connect most buildings.", ""),
        StaticBook("North Report at Unk", "erlend0501", "As I, Jordan, went north to scout on the Undead Keep, I noticed activity ther. The undead were build ing two more structures at their base. If they manage to complete this, it will be even harder to br eak into their base. The undead are advancing. It's just a question of time before they will attack the major cities. If they fall, we are doomed. We have to sabotage the structures, in a way the unde ad won't notice us. This probably impossible, but it's the only chance we got. Open war doesn't hlp out much, because we don't have enough men. Once we get more men, and I'm talking of whole nations, then we shall strike, and take the \"Un\" from The undead. ~Jordan Stilwell", ""),
        StaticBook("Northern Report", "muchoman798", "Recently, we have had ventures to the North. Our latest had a group of about 13 people and resulted in the recruitment of 3. All but 4 of these 13 died, and I was one of the few to survive. In my opinion, the deaths were due to a lack of strategy and planning and overzealous battlecries by a few of the group. After the main group died (us 4 held back, knowing they would be slain) we attempted to make bases. There was a grave guardian there who would not let us, but Ser'tok and myself were able to create one forward operating base. From there, we planned to dig tunnels under the great undead keep, this in order to invade them safely, of course. I began digging a tunnel when Recruit Pulley found a large tunnel to under the ice made by the Undead, so I stopped making the tunnel. It is my opinion that we will need to make the tunnels and several hiding holes in order to make any headway in this battle. Since I had to stop this tunnel, I dug around so I would not be near the Undead tunnel, and found a chest at the end of my tunnel. It was in a room made by the Undead, and had much gear. I looted all that was worthwhile, and I put it into a chest in the fort to be analyzed by Ser'tok fo r the taint. That is all I have to say on the most recent raid to the North. end", ""),
        StaticBook("Northern Wind", "impymut", "Blow, northern wind \n Send me my darling \n Blow, northern wind \n Blow, blow, blow! \n \n - \n Radiant in her chamber is the fair lady I know \n She is so stunning to behold \n That this lady overpowers me \n A fair and noble pleasure \n - \n Never have I encountered \n A woman of flesh and blood \n Who could be more lovely \n In all this splendid world. \n - \n Blow, northern wind \n Send me my darling \n Blow, northern wind \n Blow, blow, blow! \n - \n Her luminous cheek is alight \n Like a lantern in the night \n Her face gleams so bright \n So fair she is, and fine \n A lovely neck she has, to embrace \n Her arms and shoulders are all men could wish for \n And fair fingers to enfold \n Would to god she were mine. \n - \n Blow, northern wind \n Send me my darling \n Blow, northern wind \n Blow, blow, blow! \n - \n I petition Love again and again \n Saying how Sighing has followed me \n And logic threatens to overpower and destroy me \n As if he could! \n - \n And sorrow would keep me in dire bondage \n To this fair creature \n Shamelessly and against all the rules \n Until my life's end. \n - \n Blow, northern wind \n Send me my darling \n Blow, northern wind \n Blow, blow, blow! ((Okay, my book saved.)) Thank you. Book is ruined...", ""),
        StaticBook("Nosors Book of Riddles", "trotski24", "For some I go to fast for others to slow.To most people,I'm and obsession relying on me is a well practiced lesson.   What am I. \nAnswer Time", ""),
