        StaticBook("nothing", "jessbot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Notice Regarding Tools/Armor", "SuperZac", "To all UAC Members: If you are using a STONE, IRON or WOOD tool and it is about to break, PLEASE save it and return it to the smithy shop. We can use less resources and get more tools this way. Also, all armor except leather and chainmail should be saved as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("notice to Oren Guard Tamara from the Guardians", "begginfokillz", "tamara, this note is written by dimitri, your friend and ally listen, you must flee oren. it is not safe for the moment..there is a man...he is after my life, and yours i hold you dear to me, so he is also out to kill you i have tried to protect you, but i can do no more you must make haste, and meet me as soon as possible... if i do not see you again, know this.... you are one of my greatest friends and know that i am no traitor, and.... i love you like the brother i never had stay safe sincerly, dimitri *a box is attached to this letter, in it is a medal and a newspaper clipping saying \"hero disgraced\" sorry))", ""),
        StaticBook("Notona", "c_h_r_i_s121", "I have not seen my masta for days now, but i must keep up my training. I will attempt to summon my final spirit solo. I started to pray, it was alot harder without Nel'thoks energy to guide me. But i found her with the guidence of my other three spirits she is of water, my final spirit. I must keep praying, find her story. She is more shy than the others. I took a break from praying to grab my staff. Perhaps dis will help. I start to pray with my staff in hand, and she begins to come out. I couldnt belive my sences, she was another red orc. She will have to be from the clan also. She was Draggas daughter! Dragga and Gorthok had a daughter but i dont sence she was an only child, there must of been a brother some where. Dear Krug, I just learned dat i am her brother. We where seperated at birth as a male i was sent into da woods as a baby, but she stayed there with them. . Most babys find dere way back to the clan but not me, i got lost but this is not about my life. She say she had a good life with her parents But it all come to an end when she drowned .It had been a gud day she said, she was just walkin back to the camp after a days huntin she was very tired after killin' multiple skelatons and zombies, so she couldnt defend herself when she was taken bye a group of 'euman religous peoples. Dey belived that she was a spawn of Iblees because of her red skin so they tied her to a rock and throw her in da ocean.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nroca's War Plans", "denboy444", "Nroca is an elf who wishes to assimilate into the orcs, he shows loyalty and many other characteristics of someone who wishes to join the orcs, I Jarkarll to test his loyalty gave him the task of spying on Al'khazar and their guard duties. He has done as i told him to and he has returned with these plans for a possible attack. One near the outer wall is a mountain, that mountain is large enough to jump over the wall it is also easy to scale, so one plan is that some orcs or allies climb the mountain and jump onto the rooftops of Al'Khazar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Numba three report notes", "vegan166", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Numing Potions Ingredients", "ttwesten", "potion for numing: ingredients: water bucket, slime ball, flower,  mellon seeds , bone meal redstone . how to use: put them all in the water bucket carfully and then stur with a stick or anything . then pour some in a water sac (inc sac) and then pour it on the wound. don't drink it unless that is were the wound is ......... numing ingredients part 2 : ingredients: bone meal, suger .... how to use: put the bone meal in first then the suger a few secons later. then after pour some water down. in there mouth this goes. ............................", ""),
        StaticBook("Nursery Poem", "gaiusmarius8", "Giggling young child, no matter what you are the one who has smiled Untidy and wild, nonetheless your energy is riled Run more than your mommy, longer than a mile", ""),
        StaticBook("Nuw list of Minions: klomp dese skah as soon as ju peep dem.", "deavs", "Ash tings ash, A minion is a skah that submits itself to Ibilees. Dey nub as powaful as Black 'and, but dey can still be dangerous. Some of dese skahs may nub be minion dey may be in Black 'and or just work fo' undead, but all of dese people are still skah, so lat should klomp dem on peep. ASH IOU: Dis is dah first minion dat I encounta'd 'e is a 'uman wit Black robes wit some green trim. And 'e 'as graying 'air. 'e is pretty bad wit a sword, so 'e should be easy to klomp. TWO MORRIGAN: Dis dark twiggy skah tried to getz me arrested by callin me a minion! She is a skahin liar. An' likes to be with Kane an Squire Adorellan. She also 'eld a bounty in Galahar fo' a while.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nyan cat", "MeGoRage", "Nyan nyan nyan nyan nynyan nynynyannynynynynynynynynynynyan nyan nyan yan nyannya nayayayayan", ""),
        StaticBook("Nyx Looking for a shop", "clayman730", "((MCname Senectra)) I will write you are looking for a shop in Al'Khazar You are interested in the plot next to Dawn's down at the docks? Erm, miswrote. Ignor that.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nyx looking for Shop", "clayman730", "Looking for a shop in Al'Khazar. Interested in the plot next to Dawn's where the Golden Harvest stand used to be. Zebana says to segment the large plot into small stalls. She has 4k I told her that if she gives a percentage of the funds to Enor until it is paid off it should be fine. Contact her at ((senactra))", ""),
        StaticBook("O.M. Winfield 'Lacadorus'", "UndeadEd", "This is the tragedy of the seafaring hero Lacadorus A hero beyond measures... Once upon a time the hero Lacadorus travelled across the seas searching for his one true love, he once saw in his dreams. Her name was Belinda, an elf so beautiful even the sun and the moon where jealous of her beauty. One day a terrible storm destroyed Lacadorus' ship and his crew and hanging on to a piece of wood, he cursed in his anger The Almighty God who, upon hearing his curse, sent an Aengul to Lacadorus. Good afternoon, my Liege!", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Anthem", "459pm", "Oh Oasis Oasis, you great salty sea, you beautifull gardens and trees Oasis Oasis i bid my life to thee, for you and my neghbors, we love your earnest soil, and your minerals galore but the thing that makes you perfict, is the people, Oasis people. They are as kind as you seas, forgiving as your skys, and as just as your leaves oh Oasis how we love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily", "459pm", "ENCHANTING TABLES!!! (the next update for minecraft will inclued Enchanting tabbles ) you will be able to make yourself sronger, fasting, smarter, and wiser! APPALOGY FROM SALMEER: i'm sorry i couldnt write paper yesterday, (internet wasnt working) THE DAILY DROP: spiders drop porkchop?!?!?! apparently! for some reason unknow by experts, spiders now drop porkchop! we think the acdended have something to do with it SNOW IN OREN: Yesterday, hundreds of humans in Oren looked up to see, thats right snow!! this is the first time snow has fallen in Oren and many resedents are exited! \"this is the first time i've throughn a snowball!!!\" says one small child. OASIS GUARD HOUSE BUILT: the Oasis guard house was build yesterday, at an impressive hight of 10 blocks of stone high, it has many resedents gauking at its hugeness OASIS DAILY, NEW POLICY: you can now buy ads in oasis weekly for 30 minas a day just drop it off in our local shipping office, (under Salmeer's house) and make a sign saying you want to purchase an ad", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/21/11", "459pm", "KING OF OREN MARRYING: the king of oren was wed to sara love today in al'kazar \"we are so happy!\" says the king PRICES FOR IRON ARE LOWERING IN LAUREN: the price of iron in lauren has decreesed from 32 minas avrage per. iron to 24 minas per iron! THE DAILY DROP: Skelletons accualy drop ale! thats right 1 in 16 chance a skeleton you kill will drop a bucket of fresh ale! WALL 1/4 COMPLEAT: the current wall around oasis is about one fourth of the way complete.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/25/11", "459pm", "ORKS ATTACK NORTH LAUREN: Sunday, about 15 orks attacked north lauren, near sister city and plundered towns and homes they killed about 19 elfs and 3 humans. \"We must figh back!\" says elf high prince native THE DAILY DROP, SPIDERS AND STEAK?: the rumor is untrue, ther is no chance spiders drop cookde nor u cooked steak ROYAL WEDDING IN LAUREN: the kings wedding to SerahLove will be somtime this week in lauren docks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/26/11", "459pm", "WEDDING THIS WEEKEND: somime this weekedn Laidy SerahLove will be marrying the king of Oren in lauren docks there will be free food and entertainment THE DAILY DROP: Skeletons and bones...well duh... GEFAN BUILDED AMAZING HOME: Gefan and his wife are building a huge home with all the aminitys, secret passgeways, fireplace, and tools at a touch of a buttion!", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/27/11 HUGE CAVERN FOUND UNDER CLOUD TEMBLE LIBRARY:", "459pm", "Yesterday a cavern 17 by 16 meters was directly underneith Cloud Temble library/archives GMs are stuned at this breach of locked blocks WEDDING APPROCHES, BRIDE IS NERVIOUS: as the royal wedding nears soon-to-be queen and king are getting pre-wedding jidders \"i'm so bussy! i have time for nothing!!!\" says future queen SerahLove THE DAILY DROP: squids drop inc sacks, you all probobly knew that. you can create black wool with it!", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/29/11", "459pm", "MASIVE UNDEAD ATTCK ON ELVENDALE: may resedances of oasis heard metalic thunder yesterday as 3 stone oboliscs desended out of the sky over elvendale \"if elvendale falls, life it self will fall\" says one proficy the oren guard and wardens held them back for today, but it looks like the undead will be attacking all week long. and High prince native sugjests staying indoors MELON NOT AS NURISHING: in this part of the year, melons you eat only cure 1 food, difrent from last month when it cured 3", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/30/11", "459pm", "OREN GUARDS RUNNING LOW ON IRON: we spoke to the head of the oren guard today, he let slip that the oren guard will be buying iron at VERY high prices since most of the guard's armor are falling appart! BLACKPAW TRADING CO. COMPLEATLY BROKE today, our experts tryed to sell iron to blackpaw trading co. and apparently, they are broke! so unfortunatly, you'll have to walk to a nearby city to sell your wares. PIGS BECOMEING MORE RARE: the drought over the last few days have left pig farmers speachless \"they're just ain't no pigs!\" says master farmer for the White Ravens BANKS MAKING LOANS TO TRUSTWORTH CUSTOMERS: now, you can walk right over to the Oasis bank and get yourself a loan at relitivly low intrest. (the exact intrest is unknown  at this point)", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Daily 10/31/11", "459pm", "DWARFEN KINGDOM DECLARES WARE ON UNDEAD: friday, the king of the dwarves spoke to us and made the statement \"we had a scout come back from elvenhold, compleatly burned exept for his face and 1 arm, he crawled into the city about 3 o'clock and yelled \"Undead...in....elven dale\" we asked what was rong, but before he could speak, he died, this man was my brother\" AEGIS GETS REDDY FOR WAR OF THE CENTURY: experts say that because of the dwarven king declared war on the undead, the undead are planing to strike, derectly at the heart of aegis, the Oren cap. all nations are redding for war including orks, elves have send wardens, and humans have sent guard THE ROYAL WEDDING, HAPPENING SOON: we do not have the exact date yet, but we are relitivly sure that the royal wedding will happen within the next week or so.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oasis Dayily", "459pm", "ORKS ILEGALY TOLLING ON KING'S ROAD: Today, the illegal Ork toll road was distroyed\\ by order of the king. The orks would sit above on a bridge, jump down, and mug unsuspecting travelers if they didnt pay a toll of a rediculissly high 300 minas to pass FISH ON FIRE: Fish are now 60% more likely to bite because of the cold weather. \"they are extreamly hungry from the hard winter and need food!\" says one elf expert THE DAILY DROP, ZOMBIEES DROPING BURNT FLESH: as you probobly know, allmost all zombiees drop burnt flsh apon death, but what you didnt know is that it is eatable thats right! you can eat burnt flesh! it makes you sick, and it will slowly kill you but it will keep you alive!", ""),
        StaticBook("Oath of Malinor", "Ranovak", "", ""),
        StaticBook("OATH OF THE BLACK HAND", "sgtteddybear59", "By the blood of this mortal vessel, Do you promise to serve the hand until death and beyond? \n- \n Are you willing to kill withour hesitation, Mercy nor Regret for this order? \n- \nDo you understand your place? Will you listen to your leaders withour a second thought? \n- \n Do you devote your body and soul to aid our great god Iblees? \n- \n Then I welcome you to the Black hand! I welcome you... To your new family. May Iblees guide your soul.", ""),
        StaticBook("Obin's Journal", "halt99", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Obin's Journal #2", "halt99", "Sabet, 7th of the First Seed, 1333. I have returned from my hunting trip with my dog Darreth. I am proud to write that I killed over 200 spiders on this trip. My house in the Verge remains intact with all 5 floors untouched. I fear that the monsters in the Verge will one day overrun the town.         lol", ""),
        StaticBook("Object Words", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Talibortu = Dwarf Halfling \n Talivalah = Human Halfling \n Tal'Uruk = Goblin \n Ailer = Wizard \n Avern = Wanderer/Confused Person \n Bortu = Dwarf \n Drui = Druid \n Draoi = Warlock/Sorcerer \n Llir = Friend \n Valah = Human \n Uruk = Orc \n Mali = Elf \n Athrinarn'Acaele = Dragon \n Taliame = Tree", ""),
        StaticBook("OBJECTIVES", "Kended", "1.Kal'Urgan: Find out Current leaders, How big their force is, and Commander needs to speak w ith the king. Well Commander, we best be off fer' now, expect us back soon", ""),
        StaticBook("ObliskLord_Jack", "Gamerhqweb", "By writing and reading this book I \"Jack Walls\" accept to be faithful. text I shall do the following things: text -Always serve the king text -Never be rude to any person text -To fight in all wars concerning the king text -Never risk any soldier lives without point -Never to attack an ork,human,elf,dwarf and ascended test \n \n erase eraseall erase-all", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations  of the Wisethorn", "sconn", "It was just a harmless sappling a few days ago. It seems as if i found it just in time to save it from the darkness it lived in for decades. It used to be weak. Its leaves lost all trace of their once blood red colour. And its wood was as weak as wet bread. But things have changed. Its leaves started to gain more colour and its wood was now as hard as stone. I planted it in my house in a secret location. And it continues to gain strenght. The strangest thing in happening with it. Little thorns started to grow all over it. That is when i decided to name it Wisethorn. It gets bigger every day. The space seems to contain it. No wonder that it didn't grow in that cave. I have to dig the ceeling for it to grow. But there is no more space. It will have to wait untill i can buy some sort of sanctuary. The Wisethorn is starting to make me mad. It tells me things i will never understand. I am starting to wonder if it is a curse or bleesing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations from the Front", "aaaa1188", "In this observation of events, I will attempt to travel as close to the undead fortess as I possibly can without being detected. I bring very little, my only on-hand items being this book, enough bread to last me during my journey, and my soulstone. I have no weapons, no armor, those would only be unnessesary weight, my only option should I be discovered is to run and activate my soulstone. Hopefully I'll be able to get something back to Laurelin in one piece. I'm not familiar with the enviroment there, so I have no idea what to expect, but I will go, perhaps something I see will be of use to others. I am safe in Laurelin at the moment, when I finish writing this, I will begin my journey. Hopefully there will be another chapter in this note... \n At the moment I am stuck in Al'Khazar, trying to find any information on where to search . It isn't all bad though, these humans make some fine ale, and I could use the comfort of some good drink at the moment. After gathering information from a few citizens, I am no closer than where I began . It would appear, however, that my next step is to visit Snowyfields. The more I learn, the less I wish to go. \n Back in Al'Khazar, overheard a strange conversation between two (assuming) undead. One of them (Lodrick) seems to be inviting another (Frowman) into the undead. Frowman has just mentioned that he intends to decieve those opposing the undead into conflict with one another. The now say they will be the voice, and protectors of chaos and madness. They have agents among us... They may be allowing me to record this right now in hopes that it will spread fear. Either way, this is troubling.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations from the Front V2", "aaaa1188", "After my encounter with the two agents of the undead in Al'Khazar, I realize that I cannot trust anyone. From here, I go alone. \n From the sudden change in climate, I would guess that I have entered  the North, however, I still have not found any sizable settlement. That dwarf seems to have been correct when he told me the North was a treachorous place. \n Came across some Kotr soldiers today, luckily I was able to remain hidden they seemed to be looting travelers, judging by the conversation I heard. \n Today I am back in Al'Khazar . I came here simply to restock, but when I entered town, there as a bit of commotion surrounding a strange hooded man who's name I did not catch. So, i decided to follow the strange man to see what I could find out. He walked to a darker part of the city, where another man seemed to be waiting for him, I attempted to inch closer, and managed to hear some of their conversation from around the corner of a nearby building, soon though, they saw me and I was forced to craft a ridiculous story about why I had been following them. Luckily, they soon moved off, and I was able to follow them from a distance. I moved from building to building, until they moved into a small burrow in the side of a hill. I moved to the entrance and attempted to hear their conversation. I could only make out a small bit, but it was most disturbing. This is (to the best of my memory) what I heard: \"All you need do is present them with something useful, in exchange for the magic you seek.\" (different voice) \"I HAVE! I have offered everything I have, my loyalty and my invasion plan for Oren were all rejected! They still will not respond!\" (Once more the first voice) \"Then I cannot.... A SPY!\" It was at this point I had to run from the pair, and I managed to make it to the guardhouse before they could catch up. I fear whoever the \"them\" mentioned by the one man may be notified of my affairs now...", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations from the Front V3", "aaaa1188", "cancel", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations Of - The Endermen", "KuroiHonoo", "This is a book on the observations of the being known as the Endermen. The observations were made by Neutral Grey. \n The physical appearance of an Enderman is comparable to a human. Endermen are reconizable by their tall, slender appearance. Their eyes are a pink-ish, purple color, and 'sparkles' are noticed floating around them. \n These 'sparkles' resemble those of portals to the Nether, leading people to beleive that these creatures my be connected to that. \n Upon death, Endermen are known to sometimes drop 'Ender Pearls\". While the usefulness of these pearls is still unknown, some theorize that it may be part of their soul. \n The Endermen are a relatively peaceful race, which leads people to the theory that they may be a cursed race. However, if attacked, they will instantly charge after their offender. \n As mentioned, the Endermen are a tall race (about 3 meters). This means that they cannot fit into any room with a ceiling less then 3 meters tall. This is good to know when being chased by them. \n To conclude, the Endermen are a race of tall, slender, black beings. They have been somewhat easy to observe, due to their initially passive nature. If you wish to see one in person, get looking. They are a rare race. THE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations Of a Young Warlock", "Sode1", "Entry I Inan, 9th of Snows Maiden 1340. Mania is getting worse, The taint from his magic spreading across his body like an infection. He wants to die, but not until the child is saved. He showed Voak and Elindor the future. It was not bright, although i was sent out because me and kishin squabbled. I knew something was up, Mania told me everything. ~~~~~~~~~ Sabet, 21st of The First Seed, 1341 I met A Beautiful lady the other day, she took me into a tub of war, water. She Brang me close to her and whispered in my ear that she loved me. I replied \"I do to\", she then kissed me, it was the most softest thing i had ever touched. I hope to see her again tommorow. ~~~~~~ Ahad, 1st of The Second Seed, 1341 Me and Leyun are getting closer, We often Touch Lips. It feels wonderfull to have a sence of purpose. Like i can just return home after a long day and see her there. Its amazing. This is all Great, but while i rejoice. Mania is getting worse, The taint has spread across his body, almost fully covering it Ahad, 8th of Suns Smile 1341. Im not sure if i can continue loving her. I love her so much but i must leave her, She cannot be in danger because pf me Mania, Havent seen him in a while, Though last time i saw him he looked terrible. the taint, almost covering his full body. He wont last long im afraid. Tolta, 31st of Suns Smile, 1341~~~~~~~~~~ Alexander, my Dwarf friend. Another that i promised that i would not let die. He died, by my hands *a wet spot, possibly a tear*. He was tainted just like mania, except an undead curse. In his final hours, he was in a dark library being consumed. Me and Elindor had no choice, he had to be killed. Joma, 34th of Suns Smile, 1341~~~~~~ Im slowly gaining a bit more control over my abilities. I can now carry out a number of attacks. Concussive, Blast, Discharge. thats just the terms. I still cant get over Alexander's death. im going to see if my teacher is at the mage's guild. His name is Ogland, an arch mage. Im not sure what type of magician he is, but i heard rumors he uses shadow. so much trouble revolving around shadow. Im not sure if i will like this guy. Tolta, 31st of The Deep Cold, 1341~~~~~~ I sit once more in the mages guild's empty classroom. I really wish a teacher was here, seems i always come at the wrong times. Irba, 32nd of The Deep Cold, 1341~~~~~~~ Alot has happened at treetop inn, i feel so close to the people here. But there is just something that brings bad luck to it. Murderes take refuge here, Rogue orcs attack. I used to come here to look at the stars, now i come here to protect people. Kamees, 33rd of The Deep Cold, 1341~~~~~~~~ I woke up this morning with a few books on magic, Im really thinking too much. Im going to see if anyone is at the mages guild today, Hopefully i will find Ogland .Sabet, 35th of The Deep Cold, 1341~~~~~~~~~ Yes ! I found someone who can help me, his name i am unsure of. He has a long grey beard and wields a staff. He showed me a library deep in the guild's roots. Im here now, Is this some sort of Test ?", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations of New Terriko", "aaaa1188", "Allow me to begin by saying that New terriko is under observation due to its close proximity to the new Wrath's Clutch", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations of Raghnok", "pcgeek61995", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations of Strange Pearl", "gabester27", "i Henry Warner found this pearl when i killed a weird black creature. It was three blocks high and it was all black like obsindian . It also has this weird purple essence coming from it. It also walks on weird quid like legs. the actually pearl was a weird blue blackish color. Then we tryied to heat it but nothing happend. then we threw it down from a high point and it cracked. Then it reformed its self. It must be some kinda force  of the undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations of the Phantasmal by Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "Please explain this ghost if anyone could", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations on undead magic", "Demolicious", "Observations on undead magic\n by Licios \n Undead are mostly known as bane of all life, the pure evil of Iblees and with many other names. But rarely is interest focused on more than quickest way to behead and burn them. \n How many have actually given thought to their powers over magic? Few, I would say. Still, their might is something never before seen upon this world. That alone would be worth closer study, though many would disagree with me. \n My own encounters with the servants of Iblees have shown me strength of their magic, and I was lucky to leave those encounters alive, in one piece. Even close to as close to death I was during those enconuters , I cannot help but admire their effortless command over raw forces of universe. \n With surprising ease, even weaker among Iblees's servants are able to conjure fire and lightning upon those mortals foolish enouch to cross their path.  One can only be fascinated by the raw power they wield. \n And this does'nt even yet give a thought to the power  mightiest of Iblees's necromancers wield. I have seen the flying city of undead with my own eyes.  I cannot but watch in ave and respect the amount of power it must have taken to summon part of Nether itself and lock it hovering high above the ground. \n Yet we have not given a thought to their powers of summonin g. To bring force of life, that, according to our knowledge, is gift from creator himself, so easily back to rotting carcass it once inhabited. One can only wonder, how are mere servants of Iblees, who was a servant of Creator, summon Creator's gift so easily to the masses of shambling servants they make use for. \n This is indeed fascinating subject, but we have not yet covered the one mystery. The source of necromancers' power. \n For would every necromancer draw his power directly from Iblees himself, surely would even Iblees be weakened, even as powerful as  he is, being able to grant such powers to his followers. \n If this power does not come directly from Iblees, then where is it's source? I believe Im able to answer that question. During my encounter with a necromancer, I saw him wielding staff with a golden head. The staff seemed slowly to fade away from this reality, as he harnessed more of his magical powers. I believe, that necromancers use the elemental power locked within  gold as a source of power for their spells, channeling Iblees's will trough the staff. \n Magical powers of undead are a fascinating sight, for they are something few have ever seen, and far less have lived to tell abot it. Many are drawn by the lure of power that Iblees promises. Humans are swayed even easier than most, due to our short lifespwan. Once Im gone, my work will be in vain, for no one will carry on my research or my studies. \n No wonder many seek the way to immortality, trough undeath. \n Author's note: Contact author for any information regarding undead or their legendary Necronomicon. You shall not go unrewarded.", ""),
        StaticBook("Obsidian notes", "pugsy", "This rock is so enticing I can not seem to leave it and I cannot even find it in me to cause damage to it such as lightning it on fire or breaking it this rock... I have noticed it used in rather arca ne writing depicting a portal of sorts with rather horrid monsters coming out and ravaging the lands", ""),
        StaticBook("Oceans Casino", "Rubber_Duckies", "Come down to Oceans Casino south of Kramaroe! We have Slots, Wheel of Luck, BlackJack, Dicing, and Lucky Numbers! So come today! Also make sure to check out our new casino in AlKhazzar", ""),
        StaticBook("Oceans Casino and Tavern.", "Benben582", "Would you like to become rich in a matter of seconds? \nCome on down to Oceans Casino and Tavern! We have an array of games, ranging from Blackjack to Slots! Come with your pockets nearly empty, and leave with more money than you can spend! \nYou could win up to 10,000 Minas! \nWe are just South of Kramoroe, right off of Kings Road. A red carpet and Glowstone lamps signify that you are close. Cheap Ale, Music, and lots of Gambling!", ""),
        StaticBook("Oceans Casino Dice, How to Play", "Lomaticc", "1. Place a bet . Minimum 50 Minas, Maximum 500 \n(/monay pay PlayerName ammount) \n2. You roll a dice out of the ammount you bet \nEXAMPLE: You bet 200. (/roll 200) \n \n3. You win 1.5x the number you roll on your dice", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd but Beautiful", "Nethrel", "Siting in the Resturaunt, Waiting here for you. Looking for that pretty face, This really can't be true. You enter through the doorway, Looking all around. But the more you look the more i'm lost, my heart falls to the ground. *Continues writing the song Your never early, your always Late You even missed our 2nd date. Sometimes your lovely yet very dull, to me. Your Odd but beautiful", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to an Orkian Ore", "PaxKivimae", "Thou still unravish'd bride of quiteness. Thou foster-chils of Silence and slow time. Sylvan historian, who canst thus express . A flowery tale more sweetly than our rhyme: What leaf-fringed legend haunts about thy shape. Of dieties or mortals, or of both. In Tempe or the dales of Arcady? What men or gods are these? What maidens loth? What mad pursuit? What struggle to escape? What pipes and timbrels? What wild ecstasy? ---------------------------------------------------- Heard melodies are sweet, but thos unheard. Are sweeter; therefore, ye soft pipes, play on;. Not to the sensual ear, but, more endear'd. Pipe to the spirit ditties of no tone; Fair youth, beneath the trees, thou canst not leave. Thy song, nor ever can those trees bare; Bold Lover, never, never canst thou kiss, Though winning near the goal- yet, go not grieve; She cannot fade, though hast not thy bliss, for ever wilt thoulove , and she be fair! Ah, happy, happy boughs! that cannot shed. Your leaves, nor ever bid the Spring adieu; And happy melodist, unwearied, For ever piping songs forever new; More happy love! mor happy, happy love! For ever warm and still to be enjoy'd, for ever panting, and for ever young; All breathing human passion far above, that leaves a heart high-sorroeful and cloy'd. A burning forehead, and a parching tongue. ------------------------------------ -------------- Who are these coming to the sacrifice? To what green altar, O mysterious priest. Lead'st thou that heifer lowing at the skies, And all her silken flanks with garlands drest? With little town by river or seashore, Or mountain-built with peaceful citadel. Is emptied of its folk, this pious morn? And, little town, thy streets for evermore. Will silent be: And not a soul, to tell. Why thou are desolate, can e'er return. --------------------------------------------- O attic shape! Fair attitude! with brede Of marble men and maidens overwrought, with forest branches and the trodden weed; Thou, silent form! dost tease us out of thought. As doth etenity; Cold Pastoral! When old age shall this generation watse, Thou salt remain, in midst of other woe. Than ours, a friend to man to whom thou say'st, Beauty is truth, truth beauty,-that is all. Ye know on earth, and all ye need to know. +                             + --Pagar Narfang. -End of Poem-", ""),
        StaticBook("Of Cloud and Flame", "Slayer15855", "Of Cloud and Flame \n \n \n \n \n By the Arcane Mage \n The shore line fortress stood resolute in the new day, dwarfing the perilous rocks that littered the beachfront. Positioned atop the rocks, which were raised towards the clear sky along the beaches edge. The red rays of the rising sun shone brilliance on the strong and mighty walls, which rose up in defiance ready for the coming storm. \n The majestic fortress stood amid the wondrous scene of sweeping planes, undulating hills and the calm tranquillity of the rhythmic ocean, each blending seamlessly into the other. Amid it all stood the fortress in perfect harmony with the tranquil surrounds, a beacon of peace, a magnet to hope and salvation. The fortress, a labyrinth of walls tiered from perimeter to its core, where stood the keep, rising majestically. From the keep rose a tower which looked benevolently over the dwellers below, as though with arms outstretched and open. The fortress was constructed from mighty blocks of the purest masonry, a chalice of light and", ""),
        StaticBook("Of Forest and Flame", "Dalek348", "*this book is dusty and worn, pages are torn and many words are illegible but you read what you can eagerly with interest* .....with sterility......Fallen.....more ways.....fight...war.....blood-lust........veil of ruby.....smoke........choke.......life.......drown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of Life and Death", "Dalek348", "*the book you hold in your hands is clasped in ancient worn leather, black as the void. The book exudes a strange ominous presence, you feel nervous handling it, but you continue to read reluctantly* .....meddling.....weak.......blinded......land.......mighty cities........collapse.... themselves.....quarrel........each other......ardent men.......throne......death..... themselves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of Magic", "Slayer15855", "Of magic v.1 \n \n There are two sides of magic. \n Neither evil; Neither good... \n It is only the choices and actions of the weilder which will shape the fate of all man. \n We can only say... \n \n Choose wisely.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of Stone and Greed", "Dalek348", "*the book is dusty and worn, pages are torn and some words are illegible, you read what you can* .....have.....believed.....courage and honour........immovable.......might......curse Iblees.......insatiable greed......nation.......fall.......pillar....hope....collapse.", ""),
        StaticBook("of the wicked arts.", "Eric_Armadillo", "Preamble \nMagic is everywhere and keeps our world going round. But as every other thing magic has its shady side: Black magic, the dark arts. This book doesn't only teach the darkest arts, no, it also allows for a profound insight into its mode of functioning and mediates an impression on its hazardousness. \n \nCentories ago, when magic was still strong in our world, this kind of magic was not yet considered evil, though most of the spells and rituals which would be deemed black magic nowadays were already forbidden. Not due to the harm they caused to their victims, although those were partially atrocious. No, forbidden and banned simply due to their impact on the casters very soul. No living creatore can use a dark curse without scaring his own soul. Each and every curse, every dark ritual, will slowly but steadily erode the users humanity, leaving only lust for power, reluctance, dread and delusion. It is by far no coincidence for dark mages to become more and more inhuman and cold-hearted: its the very consequence of a lively cursing habit. \nHowever, the casters body also suffers from the dark arts: the body gets weakened and the casters life drastically shortened. \n \n The classification of curses: \nEnough of this preamble, let's get to the actoal topic. The dark arts can be subdivided into three subctegories both by their power and natore. With power there are jinxes, rather weak, playful spells, barely considerable dark magic, hexes, stronger and far more dangerous spells, able to cause quite some harm, and curses, strong, dark spells, which represent dark magic itself. In this book I will look only into curses. With natore, the three subcategories are chronic, halfchronic and direct curses. \n \n Chronic curses are barely used in magical combat but rather using a ritual to influence the victim from a distance. Hair, fingernails or an item of importance to the culprit may be used to make the curse get to its destination. Such curses often operate lifelong and belong in the most flagrant class of magic, especially due to them being virtoally incurable and more often than not tremendously cruel. The werewolfs curse, of which the associated ritual luckily was lost centories ago, belongs in this categorie. \n \n Direct curses are pure combat curses. They hurt, disable, dismember, tortore or kill. These are the curses that damage the casters soul the most. Some of the most infamous curses in history are direct curses. They take effect briefly but powerfuly. \n \n Halfchronic curses are cast like direct curses but have much more long-lasting effects. Only very few curses are meant to be halfchronic curses. More often than not a direct curse becomes a halfchronic curse by being used improper, lacking power, resolve or need, leaving the victims body or soul scared, be it a wound refusing to heal or a loss of memory. \n The only halfchronic curse I dare to mention here is the Carnivora-curse, eating away the victim's body slowly and painfully. \n \n The creation of curses: \n An interested reader might now be asking himself where all these cureses came from. Curses are manmade. Someone bearing a far reaching understanding of the mode of functioning of spells may succed in creating a new spell. One can imagine this as putting a knot into the magical field, containing informaton on both the natore, effects and summoning of that spell. Yet this is a highly complex process even for advanced mages. Last but not least magic, and black magic even more so, is not a tool: magic uses mages just as much as mages use magic. This is the reason why casting dark magic taints the casters very soul.\n \n Almost all of the curses know nowadays were created at the heyday of magic and therefor are hundreds of years old. I might mention here that curses tend to get stronger the more often they are used. And to my deepest depression some of these curses were used far more often than anyone would believe. \n \n I may not mention any details on the creation of new curses here. \n \n The darkest curses: \n \n Let's move on to the actoal curses now. I will go into detail on the darkest and most potent curses of which the usage is a misdeed so apparent that anyone should be aware that this whole chapter is also meant as a warning. Anyone using one of these curses harms his soul to such an extent that he will never be the same again. I can only repeat myself by mentioning that the dark arts are both highly dangerous and tricky to control. \n It may be pre-suggested that any mage being sufficiently powerful will be able to cast these spells without a wand or proper incantation. Nonetheless it must be said that improper use of a curse or lacking the resolve or need to use it, may cause the curse to backfire on its caster. \n \n Carnivora: \n The Carnivora-curse, summoned by the incantation \"carnico\" and the movement of a sting, sends a muddy brown, misty spell. On hit it tints the victims skin black around the impact spot. If this wound isn't treated instantly the curse will begin to spread unstoppable. It will slowly erode the body of the person concerned till his or her painful death. If the curse hits extremities, a quick amputation has proven to seal the curse in the affected body part. There is no counter curse, but a potion made from the poison of a spider may cure it in the first few minutes. \n \n Netherflame: \n One of the most popular curse with Iblees followers. It summons a redish-orange flame reducing everything in its way to ashes. Performed ragged, this curse may act just like the Carivora-curse. It can be blocked for which reason it is one of the weakest spells on this list. It may be summoned without an incantation, but with the wand movement of a whip. \n \n The Lacerari-curse \n The Lacerari-curse is known as one of the most hideous of spells for it magicaly cuts the victims inner organs up. Upon uttering its incantation \"Inio\" it summons a cloud of pale red needles in the air that then pierce the victim from all angles. This curse has claimed many lives due to its wounds refusing to close up. It is blockable. \n \n The Torno-curse: \n This curse is one of the two most feared curses, due to its ability to cause unbearable pain. It doesn't use any wand movement, but the incantation \"torno\". However, as this is one of the most powerful curses ever to be made, its quite a gamble to use it, for it can easily backfire. Most mages will not be able to use this curse, even if they trained for years. One has to really feel an incredible amount of hatered to use it. \n \n Eneco-curse \n Believed to be the darkest of the dark curses the death curse is also the hardest to perform. It takes far more than just to utter its incantation \"eneco\", as both a high degree of willpower and an inhuman killing intent are needed to use this spells power to the fullest. It is so hard to use, that even I have never seen it with my own eyes, which I am utterly happy about. \n \n Of the jet-black curses: \n Etherion: \n Only few have ever heard of this curse and I myself have the doubtful honour of being its very creator. A curse so atrocious it dwarfs all the other spells on this list. It was created especially for dealing with the undead. Etherion, creating a bluish-black, burning flash when summoned, burns the victims soul itself beyond repair. A soul broken like this is forever divided from the material world, crippled to a degree far worse than anything imaginable by even the darkest warlock. It cannot be healed, it cannot be blocked and it is nearly impossible to dodge. Even other spells like the death-curse will be canceled due to Etherion burning their very existance. It is unbelivably hard to summon and even harder to control. Hence i beg the god of Aegis to forgive me this sacrilege. \n \n Phylactery : \n Of this plain-black magic I may only mention that no mortal being should ever misuse its power for a deed this wicked. For deterrance I might add that the associated ritual includes the use of many disgusting and utterly cruel ingredients like the blood of an infants heart being member of the casters family. \n \n The ritual of Undeath: \n This ritual is used by Imblee to torn his followers into undead. even I have no further knowledge concerning this foul piece of magic. \n \n I can onl hope that this book won't fall into the wrong hands, \n signed, \n Ragnar Severin Halldrum.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of War and Hate", "Dalek348", "*a book clasped in ugly green leather lies loosely in a bookcase . it possesses a strange, repulsive stench, yet it still draws it to you. You begin to read the book in increasing anticipation* .......hated......forever cursed......ugly.....heartless.....pillage.......murder.... .....chaos.....terror.......not in the name of........destroy........own kin....... one to stand against............punished.", ""),
        StaticBook("Offcial Passport of Krugmar.", "Sultan_Mogroka", "Wandrer Offical Orc of the nation of Krugmar Signed Warlord Mogroka Gorkil", ""),
        StaticBook("Offensive Songs for Halflings (Part 1)", "Jallentime", "There once was a maiden who lived by the sea\nI loved her I did, but she didn't love me I'd go to her door with roses and daisies\n But all I got back was a bag full of feces.", ""),
        StaticBook("Official Base Member List", "sgtsomebody", "Ryno2, sgtsomebody, Phelo2k8, MichealB2K8 , Gamingshadow , Pito44, TheHarveey, Digdog7789, Wolf, Sorensic_Steel . Omnomska . DarbySorich", ""),
        StaticBook("Official Waiver", "Gropier", "By order of Viceroy Gordok Yon Hammer of Alras, this official waiver grants Evark permission to wear his hood inside the city. This waiver is granted due to a medical condition Evark has. Evark is to carry this waiver on his person at all times within the city of Alras and if questioned by guards about his hood, he should present this document to avoid penalty. Should he not have this document on his person, he will be subject to the penalty as normal. \n     Signed Viceroy Gordok Yon Hammer ||   * Official Seal affixed *", ""),
        StaticBook("Official WR_citizenship_I.D. format", "friar7", "note: this is just the layout of how your I.D. must look, so get one book to write it in *-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-* Note: this means next section: ;;; *-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-* WR_Official I.D. ;;; Name: <first and last name here> ;;; Sex: <your sex here> ;;; Criminal-history: <put it in here, be honest, if we find out you lied......bad stuff will happen to you> ;;; Age: <be honest :P> ;;; Amount of time as a citizen: <allways update this area!> ;;; this concludes the layout for your I.D., note: get yourself a book and get writing!", ""),
        StaticBook("Og'Gash", "MojoKronic", "Within all of you lies a wild expanse of spirits, ghosts and gods. We have names, though none utturable in the tongue of men. If you wish to see this wilderness, cut open your belly and you will see our palaces. I am called Gash by the Orc in which I reside, the Shaman Shaggo. But this is not my name, just a name.  I am a spirit of fire, in service to the god Og'Gash. Og'Gash is the lord of this wild, one who walks the line between ghost and god. I mediate between his dark realm hidden deep inside the mind in the shadows of the soul, and the entire populace of this wilderness. Now I am the messenger of Shaggo to all the kingdom. I am called Gash by him, and I reside in the chorus of his veins. Find my counterpart, all who read my words transcribed now by Shaggo who has given me his hand to write with for a time. Find my counterpart within you and you will hear the voices within you and realize you are at their mercy. You will feel the wild hot dance of the dark king that dwells deep within you, and you will bow down. Or you will begin the long journey to the center of nightmare and emerge the true lord of the wild within. And Shaggo will be Og'Gash once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ogland The Mage", "redbaron", "My father had died when i was young. in the fight for iblees.  There is not a day i do not remember him. Before iblees was struck down and cast away.  there was a great battle. and in that battle.  Killed by a lightning by iblees himself.My father had died when i was young. in the fight for iblees.  There is not a day i do not remember him. Before iblees was struck down and cast away.  there was a great battle. and in that battle.  Killed by a lightning by iblees himself. he died a honourable death if there ever was one.  My mother I had never known. she could be dead right now. she could be looking for me.  I may never know.  Ombie, my only sibling and my best friend.  He lives in sanhar running a school for orcs to teach them to read and write. We have not spoken in awhile and i am sure that he is doing well in sanhar. My trials My trials were not as were expected when you think of the mages guild you think of spells and staffs right? this was not the case at all. mind games, they ask you a question, i answer with a honest heart. then they make you doubt your answer. i believe there is a reason for think. arcane mage is a wise man.  The first trial consisted of a group of clones, or duplicates. they are looked the same, walked the same, sounded the same.  he asked me if what i see before me could be real? am i dreaming? i told it it was a illusion such things are nigh impossible.  i still believe my answer to this day. The second part of the trials was the most painful thing ive ever had to go through. Although not as you would expect.  i walked into a small room, and was confronted with a man of a smaller build. he looked strangely familiar. What arcane mage said made me stand in shock. The man before me killed my father in the wars. it was not iblees.  not even a undead. it was a general. who had turned corrupt. arcane mage asked me if i would kill him. i refused. i do not kill for vengeance.  The final trial still confuses me to this day. i do not understand what it was ment to be for.  there were 4 hall ways. each with a label.  Water, Fire, Earth, Air. i went with water. im not sure what that ment though.  I have been accepted. i will work in the ancient ways. and i will continue to train in the mages tower. Today the Undead tried to attack my home town of snowy fields.  I defended it with my lifeand i went after the undead as the fell from a group of war mercenarys that called themselfsthe lost ones.  The undead are strong are a distance but get close and they will fall with ease.I followed them to a old building sitting on a mountain.  i saw the dark figures sitting ontop the roofs casting there dark magic at the merc group below. i met up with the leader and we made a battle plan. i was to sneakaround while they drew the front of the attention.  along my way around i stopped at small cliff so they could not see me.  when i stopped i waited for a second because the lightning had ceased. then i heard foot steps running and a undead jump right over me. i went up behind him and stuck my sword through his should. he then turned around and i stabbed him again through the breast.  my fourth undead kill.  i have killed many know... perhaps more then anyone one in aegis.  i must continue though the undead will never stop and give me mercy i will continue to hunt them down if they continue there ways.  This is the end of this entry. i will add more at a later time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oglands journal", "redbaron", "ive found a strange man today he tells of a ancient town in the north call Ha'Nar with apparent ascended and undead living in peace.... I have found a woman who has told me the town is real, i must visit it soon. The girl has agreed to show me the town, i am very curious indeed of how this town will town out. its the first night of our journy, we made little wood huts and are staying here until dawn, i wish tomorrow will bring my insight on this town.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oh hi there", "Alectriciti", "If you're reading this book, you have found the property of Alethion and Rhisereld Celebtaurë please take good care of it. <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Oh what is a banana?", "Alectriciti", "Oh banana tree, oh banana tree, \n How beautiful your bananas are. \n You are tasty and yellow. So says my fellow. \n \n But surely he's mad, much like my dad. \n \n Are bananas real? Do they not peal? \n How do they feel? Do they come with a seal? \n So many questions, so few replies. \n I'll geta banana. Even if it means I must die(s)!", ""),
        StaticBook("Okonkwo's seal", "OmtraSpectral", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Book", "William_Talbot", "[You cant Understand most of the Words in this damaged journal although you can understand 4 words] -----The End is Coming-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Old messages", "BenjaminKayEight", "1.Our leader blackThorn is back!!!. 2. Leafwind will be handeling all new initiates. 3. initiates are not allowed in the HQ 4. Check the message board everytime you log in 5. telling any non warden or an initiate where the warden HQ is or any of the passwords you will be kicked from the pathfinder ranks with no warning. 6. for normal misdeeds one warning will be given before being kicked. \n a dark tower was spotted south of ravenhold general duties include patroling the elven roads \n books and bookcases are needed on the 5th floor", ""),
        StaticBook("old terriko", "ShAadow0", "Old Terriko was a nice blooming city. many began to live there, until the wizard sent his dar k magic", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Torn Map", "Lagomorphia", "A map of the north. A large cliched 'X' is written at a point near Crimson Vale.  [-1753, 71, -100]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Olwe Laelithrin's Journal", "WhiteReaper", "This is the personal account of Olwe's travels through Aegis. \n Day 5\n After waking in the Cloud Temple I finally made my way to Laurelin, the City of the Elves. I was amazed at it beauty and grandeur. The people were friendly and I met High Prince Native. He offered to show me around his city and I met a druid Respiren. They took me around and made me feel at home. The High Prince himself build my house! \n Day 7\n I have moved in finally and now this place feels like home. I have furnished my home and it is  comfortable, if a bit small. I should probably make use of the lower floor. I have crafted my self some tools and have managed to scrape out a good Mina supply  by killing the many monsters near Laurelin. I have gained knowledge of the Undead and the Acended. The Acended are the protectors of life and the Undead are bane of all creatures. I know I must pick a side... \n Day 8 I have heard rumors of an Undead attack on Laurelin. I know High Prince Native will know what to do. \n Day 10\n I am debating what to do with my life. I feel I should join a group here in Laurelin. So far I have heard of the Druids, The Wardens (formerly the Pathfinders) and The Dragon-Riders. I will think on this issue greatly before making my decision. \n Day 11\n I have sent in my application to the Wardens. If I am rejected I shall speak with the druids about joining thier order. I have recinded my application and instead I will attempt to join the Golden Harvest. I hear the pay is good and the work is easy. I will also speak with the druids as well. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Olwe Laelithrin's Journal Vol. 1", "WhiteReaper", "This journal is my personal account of my journey through Aegis. I suppose you should like to know a bit about me. I am a humble elf who, at the time of this writing, lives in the city of Laurelin. This city is grand and beautiful. I the few days I have been here I have had myself a home made by High Prince Native (a fact I will not soon forget) and been inducted in to the Order of the Druids under the name: Druid of the Quill Olwe. I am to be their bard, their storyteller, the keeper of the lore. I hope that I am up to the challenge. I am begining to feel as if a tree, my roots growing into the dark fertile soil of Malinor, much like the Druid Tree the city is built around. When ever I leave its walls I know I will always return. So far I have seen the Market in the desert, though I forget its name, I have seen the kingdom of Oren and its jewel, Al'Khazar. I have seen the mighty city of the Dwarves and the palace Kal'Urguan, hewn and carved out of stone with skill only the dwarves could possess. I have yet to see the Orc nation of Krugmar, but it is next on my list of travels . \n Today I met a most curious orc, one that wished to learn about all the religions of Aegis. We taught him of the Druids and our ways. He seemed to understand and went off to think of what we told him. \n *********************\n I have shown Brother Respiren my hidden library and he approves. But he must speak with Archdruid Swiftquill about it. I will also speak with Native about getting it protected. \n ************************ \n I grow anxious. I hear of undead attacks to the north. I hope that Oren is able to hold the tide I have also heard of a newspaper that is being published in Al'Khazar. It is a publication containing news and stories of recent happenings. The druids shall have to archive these documents. \n *********************: \n Today the Diplomat asked me if I had a Necronomicon. It seemed a bit suspisious. \n ********************\n I suddenly feel the need to find a Necronomicon. I will not use it but instead study it and thus learn the secrets of the undead. \n***********************\n I will being my search in the cloud temple library The library proved fruitless. It was new and the shelves were bare. I shall head to Oren. Perhaps my luck will be better there. What an occurance! During my travels I came across the Wandering Wizard! I shall head to winterfell. The Undead seem most active there. My search in winterfell proved useless and I fear I shall not be welcomed back because they believe I tried to attack one of them. I fear the cold has addled their minds. \n**********************\n I spoke with Respiren. Apparently there is a secret organization looking for a Necronomicon.It also spans all the races and kingdoms. This is troubling. \n*************************\n My search for the Necronomicon continues. I do not have any idea where to start. I will ask around. Perhaps I shall go even farther north. Today the undead attacked Al'khazar. I fear the city was lost. \n************************: \n I have returned to the land of Ageis after a long absence. I have traveled far and wide and seen many things. I was worried my home would be sold and my possesions taken but my fears were unfounded. \n***********************\n Itnan. 30th of Snows Maiden, 1304 \n Prince Toren approached me about the book of the dead. He told me that brother Respiren asked him to seek me out. I will tell him of this when I see him next. \n***********************\n Kamees, 33rd if Snows Maiden, 1304 \n The eastern mine has been magically refilled. I have gathered a small supply of iron that should last me a while. \n*********************\n Irba, 32nd of Malins Welcome, 1305\n in breaking out of jail and keeping him healthy when he fell. I became....friends with his servant and I was allowed enterance to the city and was instantly put to work by the undead. I hope this will allow me to gain their power if I continue to serve them. I believe Iblees is testing me. \n******************: \n", ""),
        StaticBook("OM1", "Eltyer", "OM2 Find out how big the military differentces between the Rangers and Oren guards are. And how many soldiers Oren has in total.", ""),
        StaticBook("Omni's Book", "OmniPriest", "the church thanks you and may Aeriel bless you mighty warrior. He is indesposed at the moment I will let him know you wish to speak to him when he is available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Omni's Book 2", "OmniPriest", "", ""),
        StaticBook("On a quest for revenge      By Ademas Ragthieu", "Ep152", "As I trek through the barren wastelands of the north I am alone with my thoughts. I think back to that night. And I remember how angry it made me, how merciless those undead monsters were. Now, I am on a quest to avenge the death of Bell. And restore peace to my life. \n \n Botar has told me that the main Undead fort in the north has been taken  and destroyed. Now they are weaker in the north. This would prove very helpful for my plants. \n \n As I write this I am preparing to head to the north again and I watch Botar train Conell. I want him to fight with me, but I just hope is is trained well. I don't want anything to happen to him. \n \n I now sit on a ridge, watching some undead fiends mingle. I hope I can get something out of this. \n \n I am now in a fort in snowy fields. With a group of soldiers. I killed an undead today and it felt good... Real good. We are pushing back the undead and things are going well so far. \n \n I also watched the wizard fall... He told me to take his food and staff and fight well. Though I don't know how to use the staff, the food has done me well, saved my life once and allowed me to kill that one undead fiend. \n \n Everyone is gone. I have now killed two, but I can't find any of the soldiers. I found one hopping around on a gate that wouldn't speak to me. Now I'm just alone in this wasteland... Wondering whether or not I should go home. I just fear I will be abandoning good men out there. \n \n Weeks have passed, I have seen Lothiriel a few more times. She is the playful elf that showed up after Bell passed... She reminds me of her. Now, it's just like the good ol' days, Bawapy, Conell, Laetri and I will be going to the north on a small mission. I just hope they are all able fighters. \n \n Here I lie in my bed... The life draining from me. I haven't accomplished what my mission... But I have lived my life. Conell, become a great mage and live your life to the fullest. Bawapy, settle down with Laetri and keep away from all the conflict. And Tend'el, you haven't been around lately... but I must say, thank you. And Gabriel, my son, never forget who you are and what your family stands for!!", ""),
        StaticBook("On a quest for revenge :: By Ademas Ragthieu", "Ep152", "", ""),
        StaticBook("On Elves", "Juliangonzalez", "Elves are the longest lived of all the races; the oldest recorded elf was Naunrai, Lady of Laugh ter, who lived to be one thousand and two elven years old (this is approximately four thousand and e ight hundred Human Seeds or Orcish Seasons). Although they are the longest lived, they are also the  prolific of the races, only reliably fertile for the first five centuries of their lives and wi th elfesses only capable of conceiving ten to fifteen years after their last birth. This makes pregn ant elfesses a very rare sight. And it is very unusual for more than two children to be seen   seen together in the Holy Princedom of Malinor, as elves mature just as quickly as the shorter l ived races, reaching the fullness of puberty in about two decades. \n Elves are graceful protectors. In combat they prefer the use of bows to harry their enemies a t a distance and their magic revolves around protection. Elven architecture features nature, rather than competing with it. The tree houses of Laurelin a re some of the most stunning examples of this elven fusion. \n Elves tend toward fair skin and hair, just as Malin, their forefather. However, their time among nature has molded them toward a wide variety of appearances. Elves are also the most likely among all of the races to dye their hair in natural colours, with green and aqua the most common   and conservative colors. Those of the High Elf bloodline can usually be pointed out for their very long ears, platinum ha ir, and the golden tint to their fair skin. Wood Elves have brown skin, ranging from cinnamon to coc oa colored, and are the most likely of all the races to dye their hair green, though it is usually a shade of dirty-blonde, and very rarely a Wood Elf is born a brunette. Dark Elves have dark skin, especially for elves, usually twilight grey or obsidian, though rarely dark blue, with hair ranging from pale blue to black. Elven eyes are usually purple, blue, or green, and very rarely brown among Wood Elves.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Healing", "Ned_Lud", "", ""),
        StaticBook("On Monster Spawners, by Saviticus Treebeard", "Saviordude", "A curious thing, the monster spawner (commonly refered to as a spawner)  is a device found most often underground that spews out creatures of varying evilness. Their origins remain a mystery. \n One theory suggests that they were placed by the God as a way to test us, and make sure that we are strong enough to fight off evil. Another theory states that they were placed by Iblees in a bid to kill his enemies. While both theories have their flaws, they both make good points and should be taken into consideration. \n The spawners only seem to work under low-light conditions, and placing a few torches around it will stop it from working. The only other way would to destroy it with blunt force, which few people do since it provides monsters to train on. \nIn closing, whatever their origin may be monster spawners remain a dangerous, if useful, artifact that one should avoid. It is said, however, that they are commonly found around treasure...", ""),
        StaticBook("On Orcs", "Juliangonzalez", "No race is more adapted to the harsh deserts and its predators than the muscular Orcs. Masters o f combat and wrestling these 7ft high Goliaths can destroy most prey with their bare hands. To an Orc the most important thing is the hunt and the protection of his tribe and clan. For that reason, t they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred and respect for the Dwarves of they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred and respect for the Dwarves of Kal'Urguan because of their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because because of their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because because of their ferocity and strength. However, they heavily disdain other races simply because they're not big enough. Where other races establish cities and build monuments to their predecessors, Orcs establish tribes and build strong clans around the mythic figures of their ancestors. Orcs tend toward nomadic life, but what villages they do choose to establish are usually built from the ruins of other cities, swallowed and spat forth again by the drifting dunes of the desert. \n Although Orcs can naturally live longer than humans, this rarely becomes a point of debate. The oldest Orc to ever live was Karugk of Clan Pyrathon, who died in glourious battle on the turning of his two hundredth year (Eight Hundred Orcish Seasons). Orcs are just as prolific as Dwarves and Humans, but their children have the shortest period of puberty, somestimes reaching full adulthood in only fifteen years. Orcs are also the race in Aegis most likely to cull their own, whether purposefully leaving the incapable behind in the desert, or removing the weak through ritual trials. However, the strength of the clan is paramount in an Orc's eyes, and they will defend their young and wise to their very last breath - even if it is only to give enough time for the wise to show the young how to best attack after their elder clansmen have fallen. \n Orcs are usually brownskinned with green tints, varying from sandy to dark green and rarely black, and their hair is usually very dark, with brown and black the most common. Most Orcs follow the practice of coloring their hair with the blood of their enemies. Because their hair is so dark, this coloring rarely shows until many dousings, and it is considered a sign of a great warrior for your hair to glow red with the blood of your enemies. Orcs of the Shaman bloodline tend more toward green skin and black hair, usually distinguished from other Orcs by \n Size and musculature set them apart from all other races on Aegis, sometimes considered giants at two and a half meters tall. Orcs of the goblin bloodline, are most notably smaller most notably smaller than other Orcs, usually only reaching a meter and a half. Goblins are the most likely of all Orcs to have black skin and fairer hair. Orc eyes are usually brown or black, with a rare few blessed with blood-red.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Potions", "Ned_Lud", "Da wilderness hold many strange and ancient wisdoms. It knows in da ways of healing and harming. In da ways of life and death. Me momo knew of dese ways, but her was flat before she ever taught dem to me. Many of her old ingredients was lost and forgotten. But in dese dark times, me has begun to see some of dese ingredients in da wilderness dat me remembers as a cub. It am as if da wilderness am offering dem in time of need. It am for dis reason, dat I, Ned Lud'Gorkil, set out to recover dese ancient ways of healing and harming. Of life and death. Me will hunt and gather dese secrets from da wilderness so dat dey may be returned to da uruk once again. May dey help us in our struggle and bring us victory. \n \n*The following pages are spattered in blood and scribbled crudely with various notes and illustrations.* \nBrewing stand and cauldron be da basis for making potion. Many glass bottles too, fill with water. If latz have big hands like me, plan on break many of dem. \n \n Spider and cave spider drop spider eyes which is poisonous to eat. Me ate handful of dem and found out hard way.  \n \n    \n \n   \n   \n Fermented spider eye brew to make Potion of Weakness. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("On Standing Branches", "Razgriz_Legend", "For one who walks on treetops forgotten The silent air speaks whispered promises That else your heart for another gotten My own provides for you the solaces Yet with your promises my heart survives Until the time it can care for its own But if that promise completes and deprives Then I shall topple from my heartbind throne But even as these thoughts scour my mind My heart warns that such fears cannot be true So tis these thoughts that I will choose to find Forbid my mind to leave itself askew And still my regard in a flower lives And as it does, your splendor still forgives", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Battlements", "huwbert98", "I stand on the battlements,waiting for the beginning knowing that it could end any minute.... I string my bow feeling the cold drops of fear running down my forehead.... Lightning strikes and fires burn as fearful faces watch concerened.... I see my brethren struck down by steel and fire I stand admiring their courage and and skill Knowing mine is equal and that no matter what happens I shall carry on.... Here I lie on the battlements finally at rest, Here I lie on the battlements never to fight again....", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Governing of This Devout Kingdom...", "GavLan", "Section 1: Respect \n The governing of a Kingdom runs deeply off of respect for the Prince. All subjects should have respect for the Prince, including family. Make it clear, you are the lord and master, nothing else. Some may say it is better to rule with love rather then fear, I am different. Like many other philosophers before my time, I beleive human nature is nothing but greed. Humans are very egoisitc characters. Use me as an example. As I started as a peasant begging on the street, I was saved by his majesty's grace, King Syrio. I was raised from that peasant into a noble advisor. As my political power rose and my place in the social class, so did my ego. With a king ruling in fear, people with egos bigger then their breeches will be forced to submit to the sovereignty of his majesty and his land. Along with respect comes the proper addressing. Since my time as a peasant I reffered to his majesty, King Syrio, the way I should in fear of his wrath. \n Section 2: Foreign Affairs and Warfare \n It is held in my highest hopes that our Kingdom will rise to the top, even if it takes warfare and conquest. Foreign affairs should be handled by the King himself to prove his absolutism over the kingdom. We should not rely on others for the backing of our military, but rather our own. Alliances can be broken, and debts must be payed. An addition to the fact we should use our own military, mercanaries cannot be trusted. They fight not for the King himself, but for pay. They do not fight from their soul, but from their greed. \n Majesty, I will have more parts to include ammendments. This is the basic structure of a successful kingdom. I pray for a great campaign with your majesty.", ""),
        StaticBook("On the killing of lifeforms.", "fatwampa", "Now the taking of a life is a serious buisness, not one to be taken lightly. If you seek to eliminate an opponent you must realize a few things. One: Do not overestimate your opponent. Many say to never underestimate your foe and this is true but giving them more respect than they deserve can be just as dangerous. You should always air on the side of caution but still, he's probably not god so don't treat him as one. he has weaknesses too. Two: Don't consider a powerful weapon the only thing that matters. Quite the contrary, it is you that must kill him not your diamond sword. Sure it helps to have top of the line gear but a weapon isn't going to do it all. \n Many say a good suit of armor helps... Now this is true. Even a leather jerkin is better than your bare skin. Will it win a war for you? Absolutely not.", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Nether", "hughlorin", "", ""),
        StaticBook("On Whisperer and Other Strange Matters", "edronos", "To the Blind Mage, the Arcane One. \n \n The voidwalker known as Whisperer has recently come to mold the affairs of Aegis to his wi ll, and I would like to discuss the matter or, at the very least, bring it to your attention. \n I have spoken with Everard, who took some interest in the matter, but I believe he, like m yself, feels that this Whisperer may either be a lunatic or of little consequence.  I send word to you, however, as the voidwalker has taken a painstaking, and possibly wrathfu l interest in the Mage's Guild. \n I met the voidwalker alongside a fellow of mine by the name of Latsi. It was he who first  took interest in Whisperer.  They didn't know eachother, of course, but it was Whisperer's malevolent robes that caught h is eye.  We took chase, eventually re-discovering the voidwalker  atop a hill overlooking Al'Khazar's North gate.  Latsi inquired into the man's robes, suspecting that he was a follower of the Undead. \n Surprisingly, the man admitted to it, openly, but with a certain rage and dismay.  He added that the Undead took him in, only to betray him, and soon he would make them pay fo r their mistake.  He tore away his robes, the symbol of his allegience, revealing his dead white eyes  and red body paint, of which he would not tell the purpose of.  He bid that we follow to the city square. \nThere, he began shouting about the Undead and revealing their supposed secrets.  The people of the city wouldn't have any of it. To be blunt, very few cared to listen.  He was met by one called Wywern, I believe, who wore a similar, but green body paint.  Together they left the city for Laurelin, where Latsi, a bandit named Boney, and I followed. \nOn the road to the Elven capital, Whisperer revealed some things, which further twisted my  ideas of him.  He spoke of one called \"Death-Caller\", the supposed son of Iblees,  and how he has usurped the fallen god, as this son's strength is far greater.  Apparently, this Death-Caller has a certain vision for the world and wishes to change it. Moreover, Whisperer claims to have come from \"the void\", where Iblees himself hails from.  However, that was not all. \n The voidwalker desperately wished to speak with his \"brothers and sisters\", the Ascended,  who he knew were meeting in Laurelin. We found one Eos and Bell, who he had particular inter est in.  Above all, he needed to speak with her.  About what, I am not sure, but it concerned \"the truth\".  As with the city square, none would have him, and he was brushed off like so much dust.  He demanded that I or Latsi win an audience between he and Bell,  but Latsi refused in the face of his treatment of the Ascended. \n Some time passed without word or sight of Whisperer, but one day when I was tending my for tress, which neighbors closely to the Mage Tower, Whisperer happened upon me.  He asked if there was any word on the situation with Bell. I hadn't refused him, you see, fo r I enjoy intriguing company,  but I also had nothing to report.  However, at the time, I had gotten word that Bell had become a, if not \"the\",  new Archmage of the Guild. I later learned that Bell is a new Guild Master,  but his reaction proved interesting;  Whisperer burst with rage and stormed off toward the T ower. \n Now, of this outburst, I am curious, and I was especially so at the time, considering that  I knew one Hwaldar  to be the, if not \"a\", Archmage of the Mage's Guild.  I wonder if the two are connected. Before he hammered away, the Whisperer said one last thin g.  He claimed to have rebuilt the Tower, only to be cast out afterwards. . Is he a mad liar? Some fool wanting to purchase fame with strange tales?  Regardless, he has something against your magi and the Guild. Possibly, you knew him once? Maybe he was one of yours. I do not know. \n If we can speak one day about these matters, Arcane Mage,  please contact me ((edronos)).  I will be wating eagerly, for I feel there is a fine story brewing here, and many answers to  be had. No matter the end of this story, I trust it will be noteworthy. \n \n -Ashdoune", ""),
        StaticBook("Once_More_Unto_The_Breach", "I_am_Twiggy", "It was a warm summers evening, Loatas wandered through the cornfield as the sunset He was hunting deer so he was walking as quietly as he could, stalking the poor, doomed beast . He strung his bow, drew an arrow and slowly walked forward to the animal, it was a stag, 17 hand high and with eyes that seemed to be blood red off", ""),
        StaticBook("One Block", "The_Blind_Seer", "I am going to die. Heart beating furiously as I huddled into the corner of a makeshift hole I had managed to dig into the side of a hill, that  was the only thing going through my mind. I clutched my only form of a weapon to my chest. A wooden pick axe I had managed to craft early in the day, cracked, worn and nearly broken from digging this little place of satey from the horrid world outside. \n \n There was no lithe. I had not managed to find coal before nithe fell, so I was not able to make torches. I didn't have any wood left over aside from my pickaxe, which I was not going to burn. Not when I could hear them, rithe outside. They moaned and groaned, huffed and squawked, hissed and and screeched into the nithe with the clattering of bones. Monsters ruled the land during the nithe... and they knew I was here. \n \n Animated skeletons walked in this nithe, blindingly brithe in the moonlithe, faces cast in deep hollow shadows. They jumped and clattered ominously, shooting at me with suprising accuracy. Early in the nithe, I had a small hole opened so I could see out to keep track of the hours... an arrow had shot through it, just narrowly missing my temple. The skeleton peered in, hollowed eyes boring into me, and I filled in the hole with just one block.", ""),
        StaticBook("One Last Farewell", "SpazmaticSniper", "It seems my Time in this world may be limited, For recently I found out my brother Jay is Undead, I didnt know i had a brother till he told me. I fear for my friends now he threatens to kill them all to get to me, I cant let that happen. I only can think of two ways out of this, The first is to run far away and trick Jay. The other is kill myself in hopes that when I am gone Jay will leave them alone. I will reflect on this futher - Torok It seems the second one wont work, I threatened to do it to get him to leave it seemed to work at first, but he threatened Voak would die with me. He then threatened Alys I cant let it happen again, I fear for both Voak and Alys, and all my new family at the INN I must find a way to end this. - Torok I met my other brother. Jay told me to seek out Hawk of the Rangers, I finally found him and we had a small chat before heading our different ways He confimred that Jay him and I are brothers. Our mother Whitethorne took him away while abandoning me, I am hurt by this, but perhaps it allowed me to grow up safer then Jay or Hawk. It is weird how fate like to play these games I must find a way to end this between Jay and me I fear for my new found brother as well, He is a good man, but Jay wants all of us togther for some reason I will return when i find out more stuff - Torok Seems my luck has turned around, I havent seen Jay in quite sometime, perhaps his overlords k illed him, Haha if I was so lucky, But I do feel that I am a bit lucky, their is a new girl h ere at the inn, Rattalyn, a very pretty elf, We seem to be hittin it off a bit, I wonder were this will go, If my luck holds who knows. - Torok Well. It has been sometime since my last entry. Rattalyn and I are courting, Voak and Alys are marrying. And My brother has joined the ranks of the Ascended, perhaps Aeriel blesses me, and not all is lost. I do not know when Ill write agian. Farewell - Torok", ""),
        StaticBook("One Ring to Rule Them All", "drplat", "By the time you are reading this, I am most likely dead or gone from this world. Though no one has known 'til now, I have struggled with a terrible burden for years. In my possession came a magical, mysterious object. At first I enjoyed it for the powers it gave me, but I started to go insane. I threw it away, but it kept coming back. I eventually found a location to keep it, which is probably aparent now. It must be destroyed, yet at the time of the writing, I have not discovered how. It is an evil object in all regards. I can only imagine how it was created. I hope that the answer is obvious by the time you are reading this. Good luck.", ""),
