        StaticBook("Oren Guard Training Book", "hayden34666", "If you are reading this you have been recuited in the Oren Guard . To be in the Oren Guard there are many things you have to know. This book will explain them to you. If you prove yourself in your duties as a guard you will become a full Guard of Oren. Lets begin... \n This section will cover Gate duty: Gate duty is one of the most important duties in your job. It keeps the scum of the world out of Oren. When on gate duty you stand next to the gate lever. You ask people who want to get for their name and business, if they do not complie you do NOT let them in. If you see them in the city after you did not let them in you have to arrest them. yes that is an offense. Unless it is their house people arn't allowed on the roofs. They are to be told to get down. If they refuse it is either an arrest or a fine. \n This Section is on Arresting: When arresting some one you got to put cuffs on them. First ask if their going to come quietly. If they say no (you have to use /roll 20 and  do *attemps to cuff) Depending on who gets the highest number is successfull. if you do not do this it might be considered power gaming)", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Guards...Oh Darn. By: Kayle Seek", "StandUnited", "When I was first born by the god's of Aegis, they told me I would be a Human. I had no problem with this, for if it is what Aegis wants, I go with it. I was told to go to AlKhazar, the capital of Oren. Ah AlKhazar, its beauty is unmatched. The Market district smells like a variety of foods. The Houses are as elegant as any can be. The keep is austounding, The Architecture is overall, just, simply beautiful. But, not when the guards keep annoying you for your buisness when walking to the gate. I mean, do any of us look that intimidating that you must ask that every time we come. And I quote \"...whats your buisness here\" I mean, what the hell do you thin? Most humans live here for god's sake, and own shops here! Soon, i got fairly annoyed, and told one of them to rot. Usually, Im a nice person, and I got jailed for my, and I quote \"language\" Langauge....Language...Langauge??? I tell you to rot and I'm arrested for language! Thats how stupid they are! Ugh, it makes me irritated. But I met someone really sweet who was won of the gatekeepers. We talked for a while, and when he propsed to me that night, I slapped him. Dah, Oren Guard idiots..", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Must Die", "Jallentime", "\nThe moon was beautiful that night. The cold and dampness seemed to hang in the air around u The moon was beautiful that night. The cold and dampness seemed to hang in the air around us;", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren prices for Cobblestone and Wood", "1997man", "Cobblestone: Vonschlichten Potions and Magical Oddities for 0.78 Cobblestone: Hempshine's Common Goods: 0.78 Logs: Pumpkin Bruddahs: 3.00 Logs: Hempshine's Common Goods: 2.34", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Punishment Book", "RossssM", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Rebellion", "blackhawk77g", "Members \n Ezekiel_Obadiah ((sprintindwarf)) \n Diplomat_Darius ((blackhawk77g)) \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Report", "Xight", "I arrvied in Al'khazar through the power of my soulstone. Many people were bustling about as usual, but what surprised me, were the orcs who were there. I would have thought that after the orc raid, AL'khazar would not have been Orc-Friendly. But that does not seem to be the case. Venturing out of Al'khazar, I made my way for Alras. Alras has made much progress, with many new buildings standing grand and tall. King Syrio has been investing in many building materials, such as cobblestone, but mostly wool.  Leaving the great walls of Alras behind me, I started to head back to the castle. But I was confronted, along King's Road before the old ruins of Karamore. The Orcs have grown more hostile, over the psat few weeks. With many taking to King's Road, with the intention of robbery. But this time, they have taken it one step too far. Being so daring as to attack the buildings set up along King's Road. An Orc noticed me, and that was my queue to escape. They chased me, but I managed to escape their grasp.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Report [2]", "Nelyan_Narvarein", "On my return to Oren today, There was no Guards at all and gate left wide open. So I took it apon my self to work the gate and keep security... I am representative from another city, and I have to keep their guard today... this concerns me of the truth of Oren's security and safety. I heard rumors today that there is a underground city or bandit hide out hidden in the sewers of Oren. I will have to investigate myself to confirm this. I have the underground city in the Oren Sewers, it is under the Market District. There are wooden structers everywhere even a boat under here. This underground city is definately a safe haven for bandits..There are no guards patroling down here, and barely anyone around. If you run into trouble here..You're going to be out of luck.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Reports", "Nelyan_Narvarein", "Oren is growing in size rapidly, guards are being recruited fast but have little training. There was an undead battle a few days ago, but it seems that not the only problem. according to Orens News there is also small orc groups attacking citizens just outside of the gates. A copy of the Newspaper will be included with this report. the stores here are also growing and seem to be boomin which could make Oren a bigger Target for increased crime, and bandits in the area. General Gifford Claim the Oren Guard is strong and well armed, and does not need any Wardens to help them here. Gifford seemed to be reluctant to have any help at all to keep Oren safe. which could end up being a problem in a state of emergancy. After speaking to Lt. Cataris of the guard confirmed that the new guards are under trained. and cant be reliable to the security of Oren. Today, I was returning to my home for lunch, When I heard a strange noise coming from the sewer  entrance, When climbed down the ladder I realized that it was a Zombie! Inside the walls! Monsters are getting into the sewers some how.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Rumors", "Corpean", "Yesterday 21st of The Second Seed, 1330 I overheard a mailman saying Orcs claiming he was on their land down by kings road, making him pay taxes of 80 minas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Scout Report", "Killzar", "there was 5 strikes of lighning in Kamoroe. It ended up being an annoying undead. I attempted to see his name but i could not. I did not see many people on the roads, i only passed about 10. I have noticed a lot of zombies during the day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Scouting Report", "Killzar", "the roads are quiet .... hic! I was drunk for a little until i saw lightning. There was a lot of unnatural lightning in thats ok", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren shall burn", "Volutional", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren supply list", "TheRedNinja", "Needed supplies: Cobblestone", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Victory", "TheEdward", "It was dusk when Edward arrived at the battle, for it had just began, he rushed in, with a group of others to win the battle he looks around soon, no one was left it was him and a stranger in a creator He asked the stranger his name, it was Nical they killed the many soldiers charging at them soon after a few days they were tired, but were not giving up they charged one last time and got into the fortress, as soon as that everyones moral went up and charged with them nical managed to kill five minions while edward killed four undead mages and a messanger by the time the others entered, the battle was won by nical and edward Yeah you can Hey Nical=Nicl Nick*", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren will be taken by rebels, I swear it", "Volutional", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren. The Epic.", "cometking123", "In the land of Aegis where all is good, was a man named Iblees. Not a man, but a monster of the highest kind, its boundaries for torture knows no end, The end was upon us...upon me, when Aerial came. So beautiful she was, her hair flowing like the waves upon the shore. Her eyes a deep, rich blue, and her face like a teardrop that God himself made. Aerial was...is the most beautiful being I ever saw. And I won't forget the things that she did for us. She has blessed us with the Ascended, holy beings that did everything they could to protect us. She blessed us with farming, so that we could not starve in the caves we once called home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orethy's Dream Journal", "moop123", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Organization", "Nanomatrix", "I have organized all of the chest's other then, the black smithery and the Mis. chest i will do those soon , can you tell the men to keep things more organized i dont want to have to spend another day organising chests", ""),
        StaticBook("Orgri's Diary", "Thelordofu", "Dear Diary \n Today I've met this Dwarf \"Frenchie\", he led me to his home town, New Terriko. The town is a pretty normal town from what I can tell, and the poeple are very friendly , but it seems that I've got no place in this town, I've got little money, and no job . I need to figure out a way to get money. I hear monsters have alot on them. \n \n Day 2 \n Dear Diary, \n Today I've met 2 inhabitants of New Terriko, The builder and the Blacksmith. Both seem very close, and very friendly. The Blacksmith offered me a job collecting ink sacs from squids. Not the best job but it's still work. \n \n Day 3 \n Dear Diary, Today I've got a house! My good friend Austin started building new housing, and let me have one! I've helped him build this \"Sub-Urb\" and it's really good to be usefull.", ""),
        StaticBook("Origin of the Shad'Rin", "Shadowninji", "When the land was formed so were both Light and Dark...along with them, the Shadows . The Shadows are the spaces That seperate Light and Dark. Along with this \"Netural Shadow Boundry\" seperating Light and Dark, Gardians to Protect it as well . Thwy are the Shad'Rin. In the modern tongue of man they are called the Shadow Rangers . They work for the balance of life and no other athuority. Only when the balance is tiped do they seek to side with tonse or the other. The Shad'Rin are found in every race.  Those who have the calling of thae Shadow are sought o ut to protect the balance of life and death.  If you have recieved this Book chances are you have the calling of the Shadow Seek them out ((Fourms/Guilds))  and they will help you fufill your destiny!", ""),
        StaticBook("Ork Blah in tuupid' pinkskin langauge. By Rannulf", "loopmoploop", "Dis buuk be fer de tuupid pinkskinz whuu nub know da Ork blah . Lat- You Skah- Word tuu bad fur pinkskinz ta read Klomp- Fight Flat-Kill Ash- One Dub- Two Gaak- Three Twiggy- Ekf Me make mistake. So me fix. Twiggy-Elf Auman, umie' or uman'- Human Stout, or Dwarfie- Dwarf Dat all me can translate. so figure da rest out lat self gib back grrr i hate this))", ""),
        StaticBook("Orkish Magic", "TehLulu", "Ahad, 8th of the Snows Maiden, 1305 \n Written by Arch Mage Bell \n Prologue: The magic of the Orcs is derived from their beliefs, their connections with their ancestors and the spirits around them, both of the dead, of the elements, and of the living. Far more intelligent than they are often given credit for, the Magic-users of the Orcs are the Shaman. Maintaining their special connections to the world around them, the Shaman have a varied skill set, often relying on a specific element to which they maintain an affinity. Brave, strong, and widely respected, Shaman do not use their skills merely for offense, but are capable of a number of other spells as well. This book is dedicated to Dominus Bein'lur and the many Shamans of the Orkish lands, especially Shaman Tre'bok and Shaman Nel'thok, who have been of great assistance to me in my times of need. \n  Every race has 4 levels or tiers of magic, each tier containing 3 spells.  Four races, four levels of magic, four elements. For each race the magic is unique. Each spekk requires its own special actions and concentration to activate, and each tier of magic requires its own materials with which to activate it. Before one may move onto the next tier, they must master the first. \n Tier One. \n The first spell of this tier is the Blood Dance of Sanhar. Imbue one of your comrades with a more powerful atack for 5 seconds. This spell will take one-tenth of your mana and 1 gunpowder and requires a resting period of 10 seconds between castings. The second spell is the Dance of Frenzy, with which you may strengthen one of your brother's resistance to damage [0.5 damage reduce] for 5 seconds. This spell requires 1 Lapis Lazuli and will take one-tenth of your mana. You must rest for 10 seconds between each casting of this spell. The third spell is Poison of the Cacti, wherein you may poison an opponent [0.5 damage] for 3 seconds. Throw your poison cacti at your enemy, taking two-tenths of your mana, with a resting period of 10 seconds. \n Tier Two \n The first spell of the second tier is Blood Dance of the Nomad, wherein you may imbue your brother with a more powerful attack [0.5 heart damage buff] for 10 seconds. This spell with use 2 Gunpowder and one-tenth of your mana, and requires a resting period of 10 seconds between castings. The second spell is Advanced Dance of the Frenzy.  Increase your brother's resistance to damage [0.5 reduce damage] for 10 seconds. This spell will use 2 Lapis Lazuli and take one-tenth of your mana. You must rest for 10 seconds between each casting of this spell. The third spell is Fire of the Shaman. Create fire in the flesh of your enemy, burning them for 3 seconds [1 heart DPS]. This spell will use 1 Flint and four-tenths of your mana. You must rest for 10 seconds between each casting. \n Tier Three \n The first spell of the Third Tier is Blood Dance of Sanjezal. Imbue your brother with the power of Sanjezal, increasing their attack power [0.5 hearts] for 15 seconds. This spell will use 2 gunpowder and one-tenth of your mana, and you must rest for 15 seconds between each casting. The second spell is Dance of Protection. Strengthen your brother's defenses [0.5 heart reduced damage] for 15 seconds. This spell will use 2 Lapis Lazuli and one-tenth of your mana. You must rest for 15 seconds between each casting. The third spell is Wolves of Krugmar. Let out a bellow and summon two large direwolves from Krugmar to attack your enemies for 10 seconds. This spell will cost 4 leather and three-tenths of your mana, and you must rest for 20 seconds betweem castings. \n Tier Four \n The first spell of the Fourth Tier is the Empowering Dance of Krugmar. Imbue your brother with a more powerful attack [1.0 heart damage buff] for 15 seconds. This spell will use 5 gunpowder and one-tenth of your mana, and you must rest for 20 seconds between castings. The second spell is Dance of Protection. Increase your brothers defense [1.0 heart reduce damage] for 15 seconds. This spell will use 5 Lapis Lazuli and one-tenth of your mana. You must rest for 20 seconds between castings. The final spell is The Final Ritual of Krug. Using your blood connection to the Father of all Orks, empower your friend with increased strength and defense. [1.0 heart damage buff and 1.0 heart reduced damage] This spell lasts 30 seconds and you will need 5 Lapis Lazuli and 5 Gunpowder to cast it. It will take one-half of your mana and has a 20 second rest period.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orlanden: The Ranger", "Payne2225", "Prologue - Before we start to hear of tale of a human ranger named Orlanden, perhaps we", ""),
        StaticBook("Orlanden: The Ranger - Part I", "Payne2225", "Prologue - Before we start the tale of this skilled Ranger, perhaps we should get to know him  a little, first. His name, Orlanden Payne. He is quite the 'country boy', if you will. He is  , no doubt, a human; a man. He stands at 6'1\" and weighs approximately 207lbs. \nI think that should do well enough to start us off on this magnificent tale of one man's journey though life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orlin's Contract", "chad_stumph", "Stromgaul Contract As a resident of Dunwood Village, I will respect and aid my neighbors as best I can. I accept ((As you write, it is limited to the number of characters in normal chat)) I accept my free home, materials, and support from my fellow villagers, and in turn I will aid Dunwood Village as best I can by working my chosen career. as an outdoorsman and spiritual guide. This includes gathering wood and pork. Working in a different career that belongs to someone else without consent of that person or an Elder is warrant for eviction. I am aware if the chosen career is not ts taken by anyone or considered a career of Dunwood, I am allowed to eprform that career. however, it will not be recognized by the Elders as aiding the community. If I do not aid the community, I understand that my home can be given to someone else who does. I also udnerstand baths are important and must be taken once a week. I also agree not to build a home in Dunwood without an Elder's permission. and when allowed, will stick to Halfling architecture. I achknowledge the mountain Elduren will remain preserved and not scarred by any architecture. Same for the lake. I am entitled to my personal storage and belongings but understand hoarding goods from the community is frowned upon and can lead to eviction. Personal items may be kept. All Halflings must drink at least one pin tof ale a week. Anything in the community storage should not be taken home and placed in personal stoprage unless approved by Elders. Theft, murder, etc. against another villager is prohibited. and willr esult in banishment. Brinign trouble into the village can also result in banishment I am not an Undead or follower of Iblees, nor am I a spider. Interpretation of this contract is up to the Elders. They may evict me at their whim. signed Orlin Stromgaul", ""),
        StaticBook("Orodreths Exploration Notes", "PwnCaiks101", "A strange tree change,i found these pines that belong in the Artic in the Savannah.. \n Aye i do say! The Dwarfs make the best ale and mine like crazy! \n This peculiar but amazeing private home has left me with many secrets,some enough worthy of murder. \n I finaly reach the road i must've needed and headed to Dawns bakery", ""),
        StaticBook("Orodreths Journal", "PwnCaiks101", "Much lighting.Dont understand.Are the Undead seigeing a kingm? It sounds like its close I hope i nt have a run in They could rip me apartment Lucky i am takeing shelter in this market.  Well it seems a populated citizen of some faction.I will take a look around. Its a interesting place. x-403  y-67  z240 Remeber those codinates. Really!?   I found a fleeing Warden he said he didt know the name of this land but he said Malin was under seige by the undead!  Itnan,9th of the Amber Cold,1324 Comeong up on Legion Ft IronGut. Nevermind! Run! I ran across a villager and he said the name of this land was Kal'Urgan.Great.I got stuck in in the Dwarfen lands   Tolta,10th of the Amber Cold,1324 Its quite now.I think the undead have won  lost  the seige of Malin Ello! I wonder.This is the great Dwarven capital Kal'Urguan? I never thought i'll see the day!  Going in f the night! So much rain ! Might as well restock my firewood suppile maybe find a decent price on arrows. 150 minas!?! Kal'Urguan has a wonderful and beautiful park! I must be in the outer  lower section of Ka'Urguan because the long fields of wheat. Undead! I think i found the upper city.Its roads ar filled with Dwarfs.I feel out of place as a Elf!   11th of The Amber Cold,1324  I can smell the ale in the air! I walked past a group of beaten up Dwarfs.I thought they were bandits.. I might as well leave the city and find some riches.I cant buy a very well house with 509.45  What a  swim to get across to find a closed off castle.Guess what its still raining! The better scent of ale hangs in the air when i approached Kalurguan.Too bad i need to keep going on past the city to the fests.    Destyed village.I wonder what happened to it,i am going to investigate! I looked at the building and they have sand and logs in the stone walls. Dirty well and ...just destyed and raided village basicly.I wonder if the bandits  undead are still here.Hmm i better get out of here! I wonder if this is the mays man of the raided village.Hes huge with destyed walls! I wonder why the building is intact from this side.  \n Von Hollow Man. \n I found a few book!.. One of them called \" The end of hope by Sanivic\" I mean Xanivic! Whoops Ok.Another called \"Instructions to the Isle of the wisp by Domainoft\" Another book-\"Anonymous Inscripted Texts by Xanivic\" A extra volume of the \"The End Of Hope\". Maybe Xanivic wont mind if i took a copy' \n \n \n Gasp! A private liberty!I nt think its a private liberty anyme.. Xanivic again!The book says he found a  city that goes by the name of Alras.Attacked by the Undead.. \n \n \"Wrothgars Slave logs by AllenTheGreat:\" Appears most of them were burned.A slave called TobiTwo escaped..i wish to meet him!\" \n AHHHHHHHHHH! I fell off the wall into a MASSIVE cp field! So far i cant even see the end! Great make that 3 fields! \n \n \n Cerlos Libery x:1217  y:71  z:524 \n Strange castle- x:-1352  y:65   z:453 Itnan,30th of Snows Maiden,1324 \n Its been a long time since i wrote but its been very dangerous I must write quickly ,the undead are blocking our passage to the wilderness and i cant reach my home! I finaly got past them late at night while it was empty and escaped. I retreived this journel to countine writing but f now i must stop as the undead are checking us at the gate. \n \n *Rest of the page is bloody* \n Irbra,32th of Snows Maiden,1324 I survied! Gasp! Very bloody indeed and i got it all over my book! Krug of Aegis.. I barely escaped the undead with my life I am in Oren now...i hope the Undead weret following me ,i am sure the Oren guards would give me up because they nt want to die! \n As in Oren i try to sell my books and journels f a quick buck. \n \n I arived at the Warden camp in my disguse hopeing,only hopeing to find some of their secrets  repts of battle/coversations. : \n The Warden Liberian let me into the restricted zone,i am now publishing my books. Maybe they wont notice my disguse.. Its wking.. my plan is wking and the Warden seems very interested. \n \n Now to see if i can find any infmation Lets see...the journal section Lets see...Lone travels,Adventures in the Mountains...Anes Journal and Obeservations! \n \n \n The Histy Section-Dark Brotherhood,Sty of Laurelin,Desert Star,Siritus Accuentes, Maycts Hand,Refmed Church Yearbook,Ancient Histy, \n \n \n Ah! A Article and News section what i needed,First warden meeting wont be useful right now.. \n \n War and Conflict,most interesting is \"The Lost ones\" Volume one\" A one paged book on Geography of Oren?! \n \n \n \n This day-Joma,6th of Malins Welcome,1324 \n  Mission Complete \n I  wonder if i completed it because my disguse.A dress! \n I got myself another job,bring unique books to the Warden Scribe f 100 minas! He isnt too sure about Orodreth bring them .. \n \n I think i charmed him too good.. \n I think i should keep the disguse on a lil longer to get cash! Oh my! \n \n Ghasts! \n The crowd is not very smart and leaveing it to the Oren guards...po people. \n My plan to get into warden camp failed,they didt belive me when i said i couldt get in the   door!Not very beliveing they are! Hahah.Writeing a threat in their farms.. \n \n \n \n \n As i wait for the Warts,my new nickname for Wardens,find my thread i hunt pigmen! \n \n \n Kamees,19th of Malins Welcome,1324. \n I came across a group of orcs  not very nice. Captureing these humans but i hang around some reason. \n \n \n Itnan,9th of The first seed,1328 \n \n I have finaly \"made\" my dream house well...uh dream house is a little bit lieing but i do agree it is nice of a house with a lil't of fixing it will be greater then what i think it was . Did i mention i got this wonderful future wife Moonrider and i hired a man to help around the house , he a Human with great grammar and skills worthly of a Dwarf I hope Moonrider does not mind him. Did i forget something?Oh to mention his name . Nathan is his name. \n \n \n \n I brought Nathan to the small mansion or manor,i handed Moon the coordinates to get here ,by a few days everything should be in order! \n \n \n : \n \n I have twins? Amazeing how large this family grows and fast.Elves may live on forever as this family grows. \n \n \n I brought myself to build a small summer camping area,its pretty nice and  beautiful . \n I have a small farm near it, not that is needed! We got a Dwarfen village near us so incase something bad happens! Not too far from home either,like on the same island..i wonder if the catacombs  reach under our tent Its a wonderful small tent and hunting area...y \n \n I'll bring my family here over the summer and days off. \n \n \n \n \n I have come to the Great land of Warriors and Shamans to  find a suitable job and maybe some peace. And to sell my information on the Wardens hahaha.. Seriously.All due love but we must make some cash...... \n \n Did i mention i was a private investigator as well as a hunter?Yes yes.. ...I was payed to find some \"information\" on the Wardens.I was so sucessful! \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Joma,20th of the Amber Cold,1329 \n \n Dear lord! I just got the biggest discovery in Aegis!?! I was searching the Oren sewers as my friends Jade_Starstruck and Lyewlen stood guard outside the sewer entrance , it took me long time to walk through the muddy waters and  then i had to face a challenge . A challenge to walk betweeen lava . Long and sweaty but i completed it to find one thing \n Respirens treasure. \n Inside it contained three items. The first melon slice in all of Aegis \n A Elf master bow  and a compass. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Other Elven Words", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Tal'Ame = Part of the Forest \n Nor'Sae = Farming \n Tos'Sae = Pillaging \n Narn'Vallei = Swim \n Narn'Acaele = Fly \n Par'Karinah = Before Sunrise/Dawn \n Par'Ker = After Sunset/Dusk \n Ito Kae'Leh = To His Spirit", ""),
        StaticBook("Ouity's Last WIll", "Ouity", "if you are reading this, I have likely been killed in combat If I have, then these are my last wishes, my last chance to convey who I was, and what I want. First off, I would like my personal effects to be donated to Aeriel's Keep. All my armor, weapons, and other materials are to be put in storage. I would like to be buried in the Keep, perhaps under the Tree of Aeriel's Wisdom, I think I would like it there. It would be nice to have a bit of ceremony, lots of pomp and circumstance, many crying beautiful women... I also ask that nobody be sad. I've picked too many fights in my time, there's no way I can possibly win them all. Besides all this, I only ask that my contribution to the Keep and the cause of it not go unforgotten, I was but 17 when I first arrived at these gates, and since then I have dedicated my entire existance to this place. I have always held the Enlightened in such high regard... Perhaps because they represented what I have always aspired to be, but could not be. You see my goal in life is- was- to bring myself to my potential, to reach up and brush the celing. My goal has always been to get to a point in my existance where I can look back and say with certainty that nobody else has come as far as I, that I have led a good life... If I have a wife, perhaps kids at the time this is written, then I AM sorry, but you probably know how I am, I cannot just give up the fight. With that being said, even though I don't know you at this point in time, I probably love you very much. That should be about it, feel free to quote this at the funeral, if there even is one. i only write this because at this point, the greatest battle of all time draws nearer and nearer... The air thickens, the Sages have returned, the Wandering Wizard has fallen, great battles have been waged, and three very powerful objects have been stolen... I pray we all make it out alive, though I know it will not be so... -Ouity", ""),
        StaticBook("Outside Farm Perms List", "HideInTheDark", "HideInTheDark [Galroth] \n  Juliusbob   [ Astraeus]   \n RichieBoyUK [Thogen]  Aleksis [Aandie]", ""),
        StaticBook("Overgrown Sactum", "Alectriciti", "There's a torch on the ground. \n Put it back where it was found. \n The mossy underground, \n will keep us safe and sound.", ""),
        StaticBook("Owner's Manual", "sk8r1056", "This house is currently owned by sk8r1056 (Aelcor) ActOfGod (Artemis) Monkay98 (Lysaenai)", ""),
        StaticBook("Ownership of this Fortress", "Zezimus", "I Valen Blackaxe, Grand Councilor of Kal'Urguan, officially declare that this fortress has been purchased by Justin Longfellow from the Tazarak Alliance of Kal'Urguan and Oren. All ownership will be transferred over to him and anybody who has made claim to this fortress in the past will no longer have any authority over it. If you wish to challenge this decision you may contact a Kal'Urguan official and we will discuss the reasons as to why this fortress has always been under our ownership until now. If you take claim to this fortress again, we not hesitate to respond militarily so this is your final warning. \n - Signed by Valen Blackaxe, Grand Councilor of Kal'Urguan and Councilor of Tazarak", ""),
        StaticBook("Pampo Perea", "firespirit44", "Name: Lord Pampo Perea \n Race: Human \n Age/Gender: 45, Male. Skills: Immense strength? \n Married to Dawn Perea, he was once the King of Oren. But due to some strange incidents, he died and the whole nation mourned his loss. His seneschal was Edmund, who became King Edmund. The strange thing is, he was revived. During the death of Kind Edmund, and Dawn and Gaius's fight for the throne, Pampo Perea emerged from a nether portal, claiming that he has survived in the nether on cooked pigmen and mushrooms. He was temporarily crowned, until Prince Enor returned and rightfully claimed the throne. Lord Pampo Perea is now Lord of Winterfell and is rebuilding it with Lady Dawn Perea. He appointed William Talbot as caretake. Like this, Store the books here for the time being And grab a pick", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Lefor", "trotski24", "Lefor was born into a normal dwarven family. His Father worked in the mines, His mother at home. Lefor Was raised in the mines as he helped his father there from a young age. When he came of age Lefor told his father he wanted to be more than a miner ,he wanted to server his king by joining the army. Lefor's father was stubborn but eventually let Lefor join a training camp, sending him off with the family armor and axe. Lefor had a hard time at the camp, he was smaller than many of the others but he strived to be the best, and so he did after much hard work he finished training and was made sergeant of the new battalion. \n Before the beginning of the Great War between the Orcs and Dwarves tensions where high and there where many skirmishes between both races. The Orcs where bloodthirsty and hungry for land and the Dwarves had expanded very close to the orcish border. Neither the Warlords of the Orcs or the High council of the Dwarves could maintain peace and so the war began. In the early stages of the war dwarven losses where high and they slowly retreated. It was at the small village of Kas-Grit that Lefor and his men were stationed to protect the villages whilst they gathered their items in preparation to seek refuge in the Capital. On the final day before they where to head to the capital a great horde of orcs attacked, the villages fled in panic and Lefor and his men fought their best to contain the great horde but the orcs where to many and lefor gave orders to retreat and protect the villagers. Lefor however did not leave he told his men that he was going to hold back the orcs as long as he was able. The orcs attacked again and again but Lefor kept them at bay and so he slew many orcs fighting them in the narrow alley ways of the village. However Lefor finally tired and was cut down by the orcs and his head put apon a spike. \n That day Lefor saved many dwarves and because of his bravery the king and council made him a paragon. To be worshipped along with the stones of the earth. Lefor's family were made nobles and his bloodline still survives in many dwarves. Lefor is seen as the incartation of bravery, sacrafice and warrior-hood . \n Even today many warriors pray to Lefor before battle . So is the story of Paragon Lefor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Parchment", "Sultan_Mogroka", "If you ever find this Parchment, return it to Warlord Mogroka for a REWARD!", ""),
        StaticBook("Party Invite", "ErcMan", "Come to Justins birthday please at 3:00 today (( inreal life))", ""),
        StaticBook("Passport to Kal'Urguan", "Chafferccino", "This bears Kasil the rights to Kal'Urguan for Military and Non-Military actions. This can be overruled  by a Highlord or above. \n \n Signed Kirrekith of the Remembrancers  \n 'Knowledge is Power, Guard it Well'", ""),
        StaticBook("Password Book", "Hwaldar", "To enter the Guildhouse \nOne needs the password \nThat password be \nA word which marks \nThe Name of the Father's \nTomb...", ""),
        StaticBook("passwords", "Charlie22", "hq - whq  \n gate a - wga \n gate b - wgatehouseb", ""),
        StaticBook("Past Titles", "Archmage_Cataris", "Oren Lt. \n Mage \n Mages Guild, Guildmaster for Al' Khazar \n \n All i can say is, How many people get the chance of ever becoming a Lt. for Oren? and how many people ever get the chance of becoming a Mage least of all a Guildmaster for the Mages Guild! But somehow along the way, Ive lost it all. \n I now sit here, without a job or home, out in the wilds. Cataris The Fallen. \n \n Only the good die young.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pathfinder Code of Arms", "501warhead", "The Ranking System \n Highborne \n    \nThe Highborne are the leading rank of the pathfinders \nBeing Teir five, they are in command over all \n Noble \n \nNobles are the second in command, with as much power as the highborne \nWhile equal in power, they are still subject to be commanded by Highborne \n \n Waywatcher \n  \nWaywatchers are a step above all the rest, the elite pathfinder  \nAs such they are more privledged \n Eternal Guard \n \nEternal guards are the swordsmen of the pathfinders. \nThey are most often found on the front line paving the way \n Glave Guard \n \nGlave Guards are the Archers of the pathfinders \nLaying down Covering fire for the front lines, they are invaluable \nEternal and Glave Guards are equal in rank \n Initiate \n \nInitates are those yet to prove themselves to the pathfinders. \nThey have undergone training and vow, but not yet proven. \n Rules \n \n1. Obey Authority. If a person is higher rank, you are to adhere to them. \n2. Rules are posted around pathfinder bases, these must be followed. \n Punishment \n \nPunishment will be given at the discresion of officers based on severity and reoccurance. \nThis can range from doing something forbidden to treason, and can be quite harsh. \nThe Pathfinders \n  \nThe Pathfinders themselves are a military faction of the Holy Princedom of Malindor \nThey are devoted to the saftey of its capitol, leaders, and colonies. \nHousing \n \nHousing is based on rank, while Tier 3 4 and 5 get the best housing Within the base tree \nTeir 2 and 1, the main forces, get housing on the outskirts of the tree. \nThis has been the pathfinder code of arms, stay stong! \nThis was writen to inform new pathfinders about our ways and the outside world... \nShould they read this... \nForever in wisdom shall you florish, \n Mage Noble Kalen", ""),
        StaticBook("Pathfinder Member Register", "zevandir", "Leader of the Pathfinders: ElvenLord Blackthorn \nCaptains: Zevandir \nMaster Trackers: \nSwordMaster: Tailion \n Trackers: Lavanthus \nSwordsman: \nPathfinders: Atles, Arathana [DWMosley], NisoCaniso, Kalen [501Warhead], ValiantBrasser,", ""),
