        StaticBook("Poem of the Ages", "mercury199", "All that is gold does not glitter Not all those who wander are lost the old that is strong does not wither Deep roots are not reached by the frost From the ashes a fire shall be woken A light from the shadows shall spring Renewed shall be the blade that was broken the crownless again shall be king All that is gold does not glitter All that is old does not wither All that is long does not last Not all that is over is past Not all that have fallen are vanquished A king may yet be without a crown A blade that was broken be brandished And towers that were strong may fall down", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem to Alethion", "Rhisereld", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem to Rhisereld", "Alectriciti", "Creepers are green, \n You're being mean. \n You want me dead, \n I suffer instead. \n \n \n You're headed down a dangerous trail. \n  Your eyes will turn red, \n Your skin will be pale. \n \n \n \n Aegis will shake, \n for goodness sake! \n Look back on the past \n When you made me that cake... \n \n \n You brought me a gift, \n A housewarming meal. \n ((It was not a lie :P )) \n The cake was so real! \n \n \n Your gift was delightful. \n The weakness of male. \n Look back when we were drunk \n and merry with ale. \n \n \n You milked a cow \n or a sheep, somehow. \n We were so drunk, \n I can't remember it now! \n \n \n We sat in a house, \n No one resided. \n You laid in bed. \n I sat right beside it. \n \n \n I sat on that chest \n that had spikes all around. \n Still I stay to make sure \n you're safe and sound. \n \n \n I bring you life! \n Which will never perish! \n Everlasting kindness and laughter to cherish. \n \n \n \n    \n \n \n Anger was there. You took it and fed it. \n Rhisereld come back to me! \n ((OOC: Please, I'll regret it!))  \n Re-enter this world, come here, take a seat.  \n \n \n You will be fresh, renewed and complete. \n \n \n This book cannot change you. \n Not a word that I say. \n Rhisereld, I love you. \n Every single day. \n  ~Alethion", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems of Aceeri", "Slayer15855", "Poems of Aceeri \n \n \n \n \n Transcribed by the Arcane Mage \n Table of Contents: \n 1. The Land is ours \n 2. Falling into the depths \n 3. The Creation \n 4. Hidden Fear \n 5. Endless Wars \n 6. The beauty of Land \n 7. The Crooked King \n 8. The Rise of a New Dawn \n 9. Trisia \n 10. Farewell \n 11. Raining and Snowing \n 12. Armies \n \n \n \n \n \n The Land is ours \n \n Come now my soldiers, \n There is land just ahead. \n Fertile soil, and our enemies no where to be seen. \n \n Come now my soldiers, \n we can settle here. \n There is land to build on and land to farm on. \n Come now my soldiers... \n \n \n Falling into the depths \n \n I see the world in my eyes, \n falling into the skies, \n beholding those in the mines, \n finding those in the trees, \n I see the world in my eyes, \n demons, creepers, skeletons, \n all trying to destroy, \n I see the world in my eyes, \n fearing those who seek the gods, \n overcoming those who disobey the laws, \n I see the world in my eyes, \n feeling the water so cold and deep, \n staring into the lava so hot and dangerous, \n I see the world in my eyes, \n destruction and deceit, \n falling into chaos, \n the never ending depth... \n \n \n \n \n \n The Creation \n \n Nothing to be seen, \n but the endless void \n gods churning to make a new world, \n Nothing to be seen, \n but monster's souls waiting to be released into the world, \n seeking destruction at every point, \n Nothing to be seen, \n but an stranded man's land, \n trying to survive in the deserted wasteland, \n Nothing to be seen, \n but an explosion of great magnitude, \n caused by the creepers of the night, \n Nothing to be seen...", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems of Love", "MeGoRage", "My eyes beheld a sky one night, it seemes so long ago. A perfect painted portrait, Be-Speckeld with blue and gold.  As i sit and ponder more, It strikes me that you were there. And it was truly your simple beauty , That gave the stars their perfect glare.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems Of the Cinders", "CONORDUDE8", "", ""),
