        StaticBook("Potion Reagents", "ttwesten", "base reagents: Fermented spider eye- potion of weakness, Glowstone dust- thick potion, Nether wart- awkward potion , Redstone dust- Mundane potion(incressed time), Gunpowder- make the potion be able to be thrown. ===== Secondary Rwagents: Blaze powder- Strength, Ghast Tear- Regeneration, Glistering Melon- instant health, Magma cream- Fire resistance, Spider eye- Poisoning , Suger- Speed ===== Tertiary reagents: folloq these recipies with a Fermented spider eye . spider eye or Glistering melon- harm, Suger or Magma cream- slowness Blaza powder or Ghast tear- weakness ============== ~Evark. this is the end of book one", ""),
        StaticBook("Potion Recipes", "greeneggsnham555", "Corruption Destroying Potion = 3 Bones - Tree Sap (10 Saplings) - Ale - Sugar - Pumpkin - Cactus Dye (Green Dye) - Mushroom Soup    .......... Energy Milk = Milk - 3 Brown Beans - 5 Sugar - Grinder (Stick) - Brown Wool : Heat Milk. Ground up the beans. Put beans on wool. Run milk/water through wool/beans, and collect  in a mug. ......... No Nicks! Sword Polisher! = Red Flower - Yellow Flower - Stick : First, use the stick to grind up the flowers. Take the ground up yellow flower and drip the juices onto the tip of the blade. Wait until the juice coats most of the blade than take the ground up flower and rub on a piece of leather. Than, clean the blade as you would usually, but with the soaked leather.", ""),
        StaticBook("Potions and Alchemy: Dyes", "RHcrow", "arts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Potions and Alchemy: Elixirs. By Nitholiak VonSchlichten", "RHcrow", "After Dyes, the next most complex type of potion is an elixir.  However, the learning curve with alchemy slopes up in this step. \n Elixirs are the first type of beneficial potion that will grant yourself immediate increases to areas you feel weak in. Elixirs of Strength improve your overall physical strength.  Elixirs of Agility allow you to become more flexible and move quickly. Elixirs of Wisdom open up the mind new new ideas.  These effects sound almost too good to be true. Skilled alchemists have brewed elixirs that can make a weak man lift boulders, a fool study the stars and a turtle sprint.  But there are drawbacks to these blessings.\n To start, all effects are temporary.  The elixirs will wear off after a certain time. Next, the elixirs depend on their alchemist's skill. A novice alchemist's elixir may work for 5 minutes.  While a potions master can make the same elixir last for days. Third, to become comfortable enough with alchemy to attempt elixirs is a long journey. Brewing dyes is an easily learned skill.  But as said before, elixirs require even greater skill. To be a master of dyes, to know every detail and nuance of the art will put you into a junior novice experience level with elixirs. \n Brew your potions well my friends.", ""),
