        StaticBook("Ralm biography", "Ralmslb", "There once was a guy named Ralm wich born at Aegis Temple.\n After that he got shelter from a poor family of pleasents from Al'Khazar city. \n Grown up as a normal kid but at age of 12 he had to move out to the wilds, sce his parents couldn't afford to live at Al'Khazar. \n Some years later his parents died  when some thiefs tried to take thier belonggs. And  the middle of that danger his mother told him to run away and hide until she would go to get him. Ralm waited and waited and waited. 2 days have pass and he was hungry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ramirez' Journal", "loion", "Alright! Started a journal Should probably go guard now . There never comes anyone. Still waiting for Kerdirr. I wonder where he went? Kerdirr is here again! By the way Kerdirr is my friend in the guardians. Newly trained by me. Finally someone to let in. Gulroid. Idle chatting with Kerdirr. I hope i get an promotion soon. I have trained alot of guards and im the second one joining.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rane's Adventures", "HolyRane", "Rane started his adventure with Shortyy_oD. He moved into his small log cabin he created. Then Rane and Tanath we're chased by people after saying they supported the undead. Tanath then turned to slay them all and slave for the undead army. After many mysterious knocks on the door by strangers asking questions, tanath and Rane decided to slay the intruders .   Then Rane attempted to make contact with the undead. It did not end well. Lots of fire and lighting, ended in Ranes death. After multiple disagreements, Tanaath and Rane decided to split up. Rane changed his name to Quanthelas and lived with greyP and his crew After having some fun in the bar, we decided to raid the undead The raid failed very badly. We accepted the undead as a lost cause and are in the progress of creating a shop We saw a fight today, babb1e tried to stop it and it ended up not happening . Back to work on the shop", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Apprentice Seal", "Awackypenguin", "*You see the silver seal of an Oren Ranger Apprentice stamped onto the book* I, Oren Ranger Lieutenant Hawk Whitestorm, declare this man, Raymond, as my apprentice and is officially a Oren Ranger Apprentice", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Apprentice's Seal", "XSilverWolfX", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Crowley", "XSilverWolfX", "Today was a stormy day. I travelled from KOTF HQ to the Snow Fields. I will go forward to investigate the undead fort when dawn breaks. My superiors are worried about what they're plans are, that's where I come in . \n Kyle and I's type scouting mission wen't semi well today. . We were told to find three spots for future watch towers. I found spots for 2 of them, but th e other place I had in mind was blocked off. \n Today was a crazy, but amazing turn of events. Chris my Captain in KOTF I just learned was taken student by Cataris to become a mage in the Archmage guild! What's just as exciting is that Chris said he will take me as his student once he becomes a full fledged mage! Today my comrad and I found out that the Snowy Fields had discovered ruins of the Ascended. We are returning to the town soon, he is becoming a mage and a few weeks. Hopefully soon me after. I took part in defends the Snowy Fields from invasion of the undead. The siege lasted only 2 or 3 days but it was painful. We lost many brave soldiers to the undead. \n A few days after the defense of the Snow Fields all of us held of any more undead advance. We made a siege camp and a wall near the entrance to their fortress. For a week we were able to hold them off. Our camp had a hospital, command post, and tower. After seven or eight days the undead charged though. First they weakened our numbers with they're minions. Then the actual Undead charged and we lost the camp. \n It's been a week or so since we lost the siege camp to the undead. my commander chris who is going to become a mage is leaving the KOTF. I knew ever since I joined him I would leave it eventualy. Soon Chris will begin his Journey to become a Mage in the Mage's Guild. Soon I will be leaving the KOTF. So much is going on. Once Chris begins his training I don't know where I'll go. I'm buying a house in Anvilion, but I still need to contact the Saint Daniel so he can make i t. I hope Chris does well in his studies. I hope to one day follow in his tracks and become a member of the Mage's Guild as he will. I am trying to find a few books on Magic. They are hard to come by if you aren't in the Mage's Guild. I know Chris said he would take me as an apprentiece when he becomes a Mage, but I want to start studying and learning now. I have a friend named Tom who also wishes to become a Mage in the Mage's Guild. I hope one day if he and I make it in we will become even better friends. I owe everything to Chris. He's the one who gave me this great offer. He's an amazing mintour and friend. \n It is as though god has shined light on me. An inn keeper named RHcrow sold me his old estate for 3500 minas. The estate is one of the nicest houses i've ever seen and for a good price. I have to fix her up I got a discount of 500 minas since it was run down. His new estate he made is amazing too. I still owe him 2100 minas which I will pay him over time. Good news is it has a study with a mini library and several books he wrote! Time to start reading. \n As it turns out Chris needs to talk to RHcrow. I suspect Crow is in the Mage's Guild. He has talked about \" I study Arcane Magic\". Also since Chris needs to speak to him about permission it's just more obvious.  \n It has been a week or two since I last wrote in my journal. Not much has happened. Chris and I found ruins though. Chris had been wanting to see Crow the man who sold me my house and made himself a new one. I had my thoughts that he could be in the Mage's Guild. He talked with Cataris an Arch Mage and Crow. I left them be with their talking. \n The past week I have been studying about alchemy and the history of magic. I learned that a boy named gabrial saved the cloud temple from iblees. I hope to learn more about this gabrial. And mor about the powerful wizard Availer, and the undead lord Iblees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Guidelines", "Winner123456789", "VOWS \n \n Ye will defend the vaults walls at all costs. Ye will listen to the vault commander and me and only me and the commander. Ye will vow to kill the enemy on the sight. \n \n NEED TO KNOW AND HAVE The wall's gates are maned by the valve guard. rangers are no guard so we don't go in the gate house. Rangers are no guard also by how they are an Elite Task force for the commander A bow and a Axe is our weaoon If I nor the comander are here take orders from the next high rank. There is an inner wall and outer wall. Need to know all parts of them weak points and strong points. above all and most imporatant rule: Stay ALIVE be smart and use yer AXE!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Index", "Winner123456789", "1. Winner123456789 delete d", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Lord Duties", "Ctc9592", "1: Be in Charge when the Head Ranger is Off 2: Recruit Members Ingame Don't Ambush Bandits unless there is 2-3 Rangers 4: Guide New Rangers to the Base", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Manual", "501warhead", "The Ranger Rules: \n 1. Obey ranks higher than you \n 2. Traitors will be executed(Stealing/Going AWOL/Killing without reason) \n 3. Do not ask for ranks. Asking this will get you demoted. \n Ranger Code of Honor \n I, the ranger, delare to defend my assosiates to the death \n And to always do what is right and to keep my superiors in check", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger Seal", "firespirit44", "In a elegant handwritting, this document shows the vow of the rangers, the seal, and the crest of th e Oren Rangers On the last line, it reads 'Proof of approval of Oren Ranger Hawk Whitestorm, signed by Field Marsha l Jack", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranger's Seal", "firespirit44", "You see a elegant handwritting detailing the vows and the policies of the rangers. But at the bottom of the parchment says \"This seal, this signature, and this document is proof of the validity of Ranger Crowley Falos.\" Signed, Commander Jack. Irba, 18th of the First Seed, 1328", ""),
        StaticBook("Rank and Equipment", "Spartanx007", "Captians get Diamond or iron armor/weapons Lieutenants are same as Captain Sergents and Corporals get iron weapons/armor Private and Enlited men get Leather and stone weapons", ""),
        StaticBook("Rank and Structure of the Laurelin Vanguard.", "Aerinyes", "Grand Highborn - The Grand Highborn is Commander of the Elven military and its supporting forces (Vanguards, Wardens, and various other sects) \n \n Magistrate/Magistrix - Commands the Laurelin Vanguard. The Magistrate/Magistrix answers only to the Grand Highborn and the High Prince. \n \n Sylvan Warder - Assists and aids the Magistrate/Magistrix. Depending on the size of the Vanguard there could be 1 to 2 of these or more if it grows larger. The Sylvan Guardians take command when the Magistrate/Magistrix is absent, missing, or incapacitated.Sylvan Warder - Assists and aids the Magistrate/Magistrix. Depending on the size of the Vanguard there could be 1 to 2 of these or more if it grows larger. The Sylvan Guardians take command when the Magistrate/Magistrix is absent, missing, or incapacitated. \n \n Sentinel - These are the regular officers of the Vanguard. They manage the every day affairs of the Vanguard such as wages, personnel, materials, and equipment. These officers can manage and command small squads during time of crisis or war. \n \n Watchman - The trainers, the standard of discipline, and the focus of the Vanguard. These brave guardsmen are veterans that imbue their knowledge into the newer members. They enforce the standards of the Vanguard and correctively retrain those members that stray. (Think Non-Commissioned Officer) \n \n Guardian - Full fledged members and battle hardened elves of the Vanguard. These warriors possess great skill and courage and are ready to inflict the wrath of Malin's Children upon all that threaten Laurelin. \n \n Scout - New recruits to the Vanguard. The bravest members of elven society, these new members of the Vanguard have taken up arms for the defense of their families, their culture, and their sacred homeland. Malin bless these courageous individuals.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rank Suggestions for KLs", "erlend0501", "1. Recruit 2. Private 3. Corporal 4. Seargent 5. Lieutenant  6. Captain 7. Major 8. Commander 9. Chief 10. General  \n [Rec] Newly joined member, limited access to some rooms/buildings. Cannot participate in voting ceremonies, but allowed to witness. \n [Pvt] Promoted recruit, more experienced, trusted fully. More access to base than [Rec]s May participate in minor voting ceremonies. \n [Crp] Promoted Pvt. Can take charge of fort if no other higher ranking member is around. . Full access to almost every room/building in fort. Can participate in major  voting ceremonies. \n [Sgt] Promoted Crp. Access to all rooms/buildings, but there are exceptions. Permission to take charge of a troop outside of the fort if there are no other High rankers . \n  [Lt] Promoted Seargent. More permissions. \n [Capt] Fully trusted, full access to all buildings and rooms.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranks", "Spartanx007", "Cpt.34Swords/Axes Lt.30-35 Sgt 25-30 Cpl 12-25 pvt 8-12 Enlisted man 0-8 Archer ranks Master Marksmen 35 Archery Marksmen 30-35 Archer 12-30 Recruit 8-12 Enlisted man 0-8", ""),
        StaticBook("ranks", "Kingkiwionia", "recuit,private, privateG1, Corpral, sergent,SergentG1, major, SergentMajor, Lt.Colonal, Colonal, Brigader, brigaderG1, BrigaderG2, FeildMarshal, Commander, Master Chief, General.  Description of Rank \"Recruit\" A newly joined member, has little rights but to do what their superior officers tell them to.  \"private\" Next to bottom, the private is little more that a recruit with better skills. \"privateG1\" The private grade one is a higher rank than a private, but still has to listen to their commanders. \"Corpral\" A corpral is a rank who is allowed more rights to battle than social affairs, when in battle, a corpral can command those under them. \"sergent\" Basicly a squad leader, a typical sergent commands a squad of about 3 or 4 privates and corprals \"sergentG1\" Usually comands 2 or 3 squads lead bylesser sergents. \"major\" usualy  commands groups or camps to keep things in order, they are experienced soilders. \"sergentmajor\" basicly a major but with the ability tho engage an enemy without permission. \"Lt.Colonol\" Commands small fortifications if needed, usually required to know some stratagy of defence and have done some sort of deed in battle. \"colonol\" usually a Lt.colonol who has proven themselfs. \"Brigader Grades 1-3\" High ranking officers usuallyare sent in groups to bring renforcements to battle or bring order to some revolts, basicly the S.W.A.T compared to police. \"Feild Marshal\" usually given to war hardy veterals who have proven themselfs time and time again, they are the ones who bring order to bases in chaos, or just tell people what to do. \"commander\" An over all leader of the battle group assined to, he will plan the battle, lead the battle, win the battle. \"MasterChief\" An over all leader with no specific rights, theese soilders have superior command to anyone but generals. if you have a commander, and a master cheif comes to your base, you listen to what he says. A Master CHief also will have suerior battle skills and tactical genious. \"general\" An over all leader that has command over anyone in their guild/group.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ransom note.", "Vardak", "We have ye Dawn ye skahs. If ye want 'er back, we want 75,000 mina and some gold. \nUse a pidgeon to contact us ((Vardak and Alphacentaurus))", ""),
        StaticBook("Rants and Momentos", "Pizzafreak5", "Rain. I write this book in the rain. Rain is peaceful and soothing, as long as you're not standin in it If you ARE standing in it, it is a pest Such as when you stand in the rain and try to write a book the water soaks the pages, smears the ink, and makes the writer uncomfortable . And once you find shelter from the rain, it leaves. in terms of rain, I've never understood how it can snow AND rain at the same time ,I think, surely, the rain must freeze if it can snow at the same time. rain is a mysterious thing. It waters my crops though, so it's live and let live. ======================================= Always buy low and sell high. It seems like common sense, and indeed it works. So when I sell, I make it seem worth more than it is with clever wording, saying how much I can get for it elsewhere, and saying I'll GIVE it to you for this much less . For those who say I'm a con man, I'm not. I don't hide anything, my iron is iron. All I do is make a product look attractive and sell it for as much as possible. I often here of people selling Iron for 35 Minas. I will buy this iron, and sell it for 40, or 45 .That is the art of haggling. And speaking of haggling, if they price it to low  and you at your lowest, just repeat your price, and try and word it right. \n \n Farming and gardening is one of My great pleasures It is so satisfying to watch a plant grow larger and larger by the day, and then to harvest it and reap the rewards, Either in fresh bread or cake or in Minas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rare items & Minerals", "theo13", "Diamond: 270 m \nGold: 70 m \nIron: 30 m \nCoal: 5 m \nRedstone: 4 m", ""),
        StaticBook("Rasun's New Journal", "Rasun37", "Since my old journal was lost, I begin this new one. Day 1 \n I am writing this in my brand new home in Kal'Teran. Why am I in Kal'Teran? Lets begin from the start of the story... \n It all began in a normal day in Kal'Alras. I was walking around town building, and helping other people. When I see Syrio walk up with many elves behind him. He says he needs to talk to me and Janik in the meeting hall. In the meeting hall he brings up a shocking topic: To replace me as Overseer! Of course he explains that I do nothing around here and am making the Nation Plummet downward. Angry I try to defend myself but was not  successfull. With the help of the entire elven council he was able to overthrow me. Soon a lot of citizens were unhappy and followed me around spying on Syrio and his followers. Then another day, Algoda returned. At first he kept me as overseer then went with Syrio and made him overseer again. I had told algoda and a few others that I would not stay under Syrio's rule and would flee the nation. So with a few friends, I packed my things and fled to Kal'Teran, my new home. \n Day 2 The Wandering Wizard came today and said Kal'Teran is not to be kept! I cannot believe this and now I have to move back to Kal'Urguan again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Raturm", "Carnivore91", "Do to Tre'bok going on an adventure and, who knows, died I had to summon my last. spirit on my own. I knew it was going to be tough, the Air spirit. It had tooken control of my body once and threatened to end my life to my own teacher, so i knew this was going to be tough. I went out to the old shrine and prayed to my other three spirits first. Nirum of Water, Yeltur of Fire, and Airent of Eart. When i felt them there I started. I strained hard but I made contact with the spirit. I fought hard and the others helped me well. I do not know how long it took to summon him, a few hours I think. Was nearly blown down the shrine before it was said and done. When the wind stopped he showed himself. His name is Raturm. Spirit of Air. My final spirit! He revealed himself immediately. He was.... Human! Strange that my four spirits were of the four races. Nirum was Elven, Yeltur Orc, Airent Dwarf, and Now Raturm Human. He was tall and lean. Had short Black hair, like most humans. He was an explorer when he was alive. He found many locations for a new house or townor even cities to be built! But one adventure went bad. He was on a snowy mountain when three bandits followed him to the top and tried to kill him. He fought well and killed two of them, but the third pushed him off the top. He knew he was done for, but with his last will he thought of wind pushing the Dwarf. bandit off with him, so he prayed hard for it to be so and it came true. Right before he hit the ground he smiled as he watched the Bandit fall from the top.", ""),
