        StaticBook("Report", "Archmage_Cataris", "Undead have been sighted in large numbers at the Winterfell Graveyard, too many for me and no one was around in Winterfell to help. \n \n - Haelen Blacklocks \n Written by Dolgan Blacklocks ((Haelen can't read or write))", ""),
        StaticBook("Report", "ikeyman232", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Report #2", "Archmage_Cataris", "Luna has informed me of a man threatening to have her killed if she dares step foot near Winterfell, i am going to organise when i can, i will escort her here safely when she needs it \n \n Apart from that, not much to report.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report - Tolta, 24th of the Deep Cold, 1335", "Cerilean", "On this date, i was patrolling the city when i came across a man trying to knock another man out in front of the town storage area. He was wearing full iron armor and had an accomplice dressed the same. \n \n I Clashed swords for a few minutes with the accomplice, who is reffered to as Vardak by his friend, before he knocks me out with his sword. An unidentified amount of time later, most likely very quick, rain started and stirred me. I awoke and engaged in combat yet again. I parried his attack, then tried to stab him but failed. He succeeded in slicing my knee and dislocating it with the force, but i swung my sword from one knee and managed to get his leg as well. A few seconds later, his unnamed friend helped him up and they  managed to escape. Guildmaster Mathis, who had been engaging in battle as well, tried to give chase but lost them. I popped my knee back in place, hastily bandaged it, then went back to the original scene of the crime. \n \n The man who was knocked unconscious was missing, but a scene of utter chaos was just be yond. There were mangled body parts everywhere. According to Mathis, Braxis had lost his eyes, he was unsure about Oscar. Apparently the two men had tried to eat them. At this time, i have no more information. \n \n Signed, Oren Sgt. Ceril", ""),
        StaticBook("Report of Latsi", "Pauldell1", "Undead city between orc city and whisper isles Hidden in a ruin, with a hidden lever And a portal Posibly protected against distruction by undead magic More reconisance will be done, contained in future reports Latsi is working on a plan to enter this area Believes (conjecture?) that laurelin may be the next thing to be attacked Found floating city, but there was no way in East of Oren Lies the city in the sky Wisperer seems to have an obsesion with Bell He thinks they are children of the Death-Crawler and that they come from a land called \"The Void\" He believes her to be his sister The death caller is Iblees son, yet, he is more powerful than Iblees himself And wishes to destroy Iblees and take over the world", ""),
        StaticBook("Report of the Verge", "Cody_man14", "+the fort is very popular and has lots of inhabitants .  + The fort has had several modifications made including; new entrances, holes and such, houses and other buildings have been removed to make way for lots of new buildings and shops. + The inhabitants request a system of protection for those living there + there are some very wealthy people now living there  +The fort has expanded some END REPORT", ""),
        StaticBook("Report on Alstion Town's Undead Activity 'Aug 17 - By Dralen Dralith", "visualjaw", "DO NOT REMOVE THIS BOOK FROM THE GOLDEN SUN'S LIBRARY WITHOUT SPECIFIC PERMISSION. As I enter the town, there is no sign of the guard. For that matter, there is no sign of anyone, in Alstion. This means that the material destruction will outweigh the populatory destruction, should the undead launch an attack on the town. Another alarming factor, is the location of Alstion relative to Unk. It was chilling to get so close to the fort alone. Having inspected Alstion's defences, I would say that if they were manned, they would be able to resist a plain assault from Unk until reinforcements arrived. I then proceeded to a small hideout that I and Orpheus visit often, and noted any undead acti vity. I stayed for 2 Aegis days, and managed to get an idea of undead behaviour. ;; \n 1. They are much, much more active at night. \n 2. When threatened, they prefer to summon mobs to dispose of enemies, rather than use lightning. \n 3. There is a strong concentration of them at Unk. \n 4. They have many traps around Unk, which are very effective. \n 5. Undead are impossible to defeat at range. \n In conclusion, if the undead were to attack a deserted Alstion, the town would be doomed. However, if the town had a sufficient amount of defenders at it, I belive it would survive. - Report by Dralen Dralith.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report on Bandits on King's Road", "bitewhite", "Intelligence gathered from Squire Williams: bandits have been seen actively at a place called Wrath's Clutch, an organization called the Black Hand is known to conduct banditry, a known m member of the black hand is Guarim.  \n Intelligence gathered from Nalfein: Wrath's Clutch is the headquarters for the Black Hand, they have recently been weak due to undead targeting, Lucas Black is a key Black Hand member who would destroy the Black Hand if killed, Hev is also a member.", ""),
        StaticBook("report on taking over the purifier's house", "JackJbear", "The following report is about the reasons why I accidentally took over the purifier's house I was figuring out how to get myself a place for settling down when I first came to base Then I asked the apostle whether I can live here and build or not After that, the apostle gained me permission in the base from the guild and I was allowed to build here However, I haven't got enough materials for building at that time Then I came into a nice house will elegant structures, but there was nothing in it I thought that I was a disposed house and I went ahead to have my home built here I have wandered around here for five days, but still I couldnt see anyone entering the house Therefore, I went into it and started to build my settlement, farm, etc. If I knew that I was a house owned by someone, I would not ever make changes to it Instead,I will build myself another one at the base where there is space ; ;I admitted that I had done wrong in taking over the purifiers house, but I really did not know it was belonged to him, and I would definitely not take if I know I dont know how I can express my apologize to him, and I promised that I will not do this at future times I promise to build up structures in the base and make it more comprehensive to show my apolog y I am also willing to help the purifier rebuild his house. At last, I express my apology to the purifier again, and promise that I will never do this ag ain. i am ready to hand in the report yes i am ready", ""),
        StaticBook("Report on Willowgate's attack", "lordnaylor", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Report-Eziano Mortale", "Markdeevee", "Scouting Report \n  First place i covered was the sewer city in Al'Khazar. I figured that they may have 'claimed' it like they claimed our HQ a little while back, but that search turned up empty, though there is only one way in there now... something to consider I then headed North East of the Harvest HQ. I found out in the waters a huge boat, which turned out to be a pirate vessel... Now the black hand are slavers, so that may be a part of their organisation, but i am unsure . I moved further NE and found a Settlement, this is a prime spot for possible Black Hand set tlement. In there i found a stronghold, with a sign in front of it saying 'THIS LAND WILL BE IBLEES'. I also found another sign inside labling a room 'Political Prisoners  This stronghold certainly looks like a place that they will move too. But at the moment it looks deserted . I will monitor it, and continue my search. Brawn Boldshoulder knows its location. \n That concludeds my current report : Eziano Mortale : Guard of the Harvest", ""),
        StaticBook("Report:Siege of Wrath's Clutch", "durzio", "Date: Joma. 13th of The Deep Cold, 1324 i stand,looking over Fort FairLeaf with a ever renewed feeling of pride.. on the day of the 12th,Kamees,the Wardens of Malinor had finally lain siege on Wrath's Clutch aftewe after weeks of preperations,stockpiling,and building we went in about our numbers of fifty and one,if my count was spot on. when we came out..we numbered but twenty.. many were lost,upon coming to the Clutch's Courtyard. Wrath stood upon the masonry and dropped wicked bolts of lightning on our heads eventually we broke through the wall, where many more met their untimely demises Zombies. by the hundreds, we hacked and we slashed,but many were merely crushed by the innumerable amount of dead flesh charging towards us. when we had slain all of the monstrosities,we were met with more lightning, this time,none died,as we knew from the thunder to take cover we climbed the castle,slaying those who opposed us we were a righteous force indeed! Wrath,Naturally,Fled from us,on his ship the coward. more than half of the wardens returned to the warden headquarters. Prince Mylas left a memorial inside the main room of the Clutch,in honor of those we lost during the Siege. despite having a victory,many were disheartened with a sense of defeat due to Wrath's escape,and FairLeaf was nearly empty i tended to my duties,farming,collecting materials,reorganizing the supply room,etc but later on that day,when i hear thunder,i immeadieatly knew what was happening i called an owl,speaking to nature with elven tongue,and sent a message to the warden headquarters,hailing them,and hoping for a haste return to FairLeaf for Wrath had returned. maybe he wanted to take advantage of the wardens return to headquarters, maybe he just wanted revenge,ill never know. wrath practically danced about the ruins of his destroyed castle,and i watched as he brutally murdered 4 Orcs,as they simply looked around the Ruins. lightning charred there Green skin to a sickening,and smoldering,brown. i could hear his maniacal laugh,all the way in the tower,and i wanted to retch this was a being that reviled,in the murder of the innocent. it was then that the Wardens returned,with the speed only elves could muster. i quickly informed Warden Noble Theyador of the situation,and off we went,our number about ten and seven. the coward dropped lightning as usual,but we were well used to it,and only one,Warden Waywatcher Arma,was injured. eventually,Wrath realized the lightning would no longer work, he raised his staff and spoke in some kind of gutteral chanting that vaguely hurt my ears our fallen bretheren and many nameless others pulled their way out of the Earth some of them armed with bows,and virtually no flesh left, others,rabid and knashing their teeth Zombies as if imatating we Elves, Wrath jumped to the trees to watch as we fought our own bretheren,now his slaves. i remember hacking away at them,i still have night terrors about it tremors of impact shook my arm,cold blood splashed my face but i kept on,for every impact,every drop,kept me and my fellow wardens alive and freed our enslaved Bretheren from his servitude. we chased him,as he lept from tree to tree, the forests seem to not end, but that was a good thing to us elves, perhaps wrath did not know we are at home in the trees? we overtook him,and began to strike at his heels in the end,it was Warden Initiate Wildthorn who got the killing blow,and slain the monster we dragged his body to the earth,and buried him,only after we buried our own i spat on his grave. we took his necromancer-staff,as a trophy of our great victory we hope to put it on display in the warden headquarters keep afterwards moods were greatly lifted,after avenging our fallen brothers ale flowed like water,and bread was passed around we ate,drank,and were merry now today as i look over FairLeaf,when before i saw only the escaped enemy now i see that the Wardens victory,in whatever we set out to do,will always come eventually (finished Sabet, 14th of The Deep Cold, 1324)", ""),
        StaticBook("Request from Kramoroe", "Jallentime", "I am going to make this message as short and to the point as possible so as not to take to much time away from your duties, so you will have to forgive me if my writing is not quite so eloquent here. Kramoroe has been having an increased amount of Undead activity outside of the city and in the very streets themselves; the Founders as well as I believe that a major Undead attack is almost completely certain for several reasons: There is a shrine to the dark god Iblees located only a few steps away from the town, in the place on the old S.A. base. In fact there is a recently built bridge from the shrine leading to the old Guardian base which they may possibly be using as a foothold for further attacks. Speaking of further attacks the Undead are a somewhat constant menace in the city already, with frequent smaller attacks consisting of only a few Undead running through the streets chucking magic at anyone unlucky enough to be in their way. Last but not least my contacts in Alras have informed me of an Undead Adept near their city who they eavesdropped on, my contacts were unable to obtain more than, \"Kramoroe will burn.\" You must understand that since the evaporation of the Vanguard Kramoroe is almost completely defenseless from any kind of organized attack This I why I have sent this message to plea to Oren for some form of aid in this very uncertain time where so much could go wrong. I will eagerly we awaiting a reply. -Delaselva the Librarian of Kramoroe Can one of you open the bloody door now? sorry about that last line I tend to write down what i'm thinking. The irony is palpable.", ""),
        StaticBook("Request Letter", "KindaSpacey", "As Laurelin's diplomat to Oren, I humbly ask you to serve as an informant. Since I am unable to hear and see everthing that goes on within Oren's walls, I will need you to be my eyes and ears. :Hi", ""),
        StaticBook("Rerowin's Diary", "SnazzyEnglishman", "Day one in my robed disguise, arrested for wearing a hood. A man named Tarl accuses me of being Undead, and makes up the rule of no hoods. I'm inprisoned for the first time. Excellent. Redskye is on top of Horen's Grave shouting about a democracy. Ah, Greybeard has created a force to attack the Orcs. Surely this will end well for the Human Ashkae is in prison. Redskye says he's with the Undead. The man spews lies. Surely he and Tarl are up to something. Perhaps Thaern is in this too? He seems to have gotten aggresive as of late, and spends a lot of time with Tarl and Redskye. Hayden seems to have distanced himself from the rest of the Guard. The man i refered to as Greybeard earlier is actually named Grimbeard. Tamara and Ashkae seem to be the same. I know that Tarl and Tamara have had feuds before. I actually know that Tarl had hired an Elf named Kane to kill Tamara, though it failed. A supposed Knight named Sarim and Tarl just attacked a man dressed as a chicken!", ""),
        StaticBook("Research on Magical Fragrance", "Telanir", "s  Property of: Telanir \n Research #1: \"magic fragrance\" an invisible substance that is everywhere. During the day, it is active. During the night, is it inactive. When the \"fragrance\" is active, experiments and day-to-day things will not work as intended. For instance, zombie pigmen are dissintigrated by the \"fragrance\". \n Torches appear to intake fragrance and thus do not burn out. Still need to figure out why they don't burn out during night. Zombie pigmen have not developed a resistance to magical fragrance. In this you could make a conclusion that in the nether, magical fragrance is minimal or nonexistant. Otherwise they would have developed a resistance. It's power and force on reality is tremendous. Meaning if you don't have a good enough resistance your existance may be split apart. Like the zombie pigmen. \n Torches intake magical fragrance and convert it to energy therefore allowing the torch to burn indefinately. However, there is some excess energy left over. The waste energy could be used to fuel other things. Furnaces to replace coal is one. Torches generate a lot of heat, so you would need a cooling system. Magical fragrance's effect on snow is that it doesn't melt and stays cold. It could be used as an effective method for cooling.", ""),
        StaticBook("Research on Redstone - LAB 08", "Telanir", "Property of: LAB 08 - Writer: Telinir", ""),
