        StaticBook("Richard Tarus' Journal", "Lanader", "I have spent weeks in Aeriel's Keep.. I'm starting to like this Thaelan man. But is getting rather corrupted- is it the sages? Well, who knows really. I also have tried to help their community, but they tend to kick me out- Especially Willy. I'm not supposed to be in there anyways. Week #2 There is a portal to this new place called 'The Verge. Eze'kiel is starting a house here, but I believe there are some dangerous people here. Eze'kiel said he has been robbed atleast twice. My god! Our house has been taken. This is terrible news. We are building a new one right now. It's unfortunate, I really liked that house. But the new one is by the Oren Rangers. We have concealed the base with trees, and no one has found us yet. Other then that, I doubt anyone -will- find it. Week #3 I'm starting to hate the Verge. Not sure why, just don't like the feel of it.  Week #4 My room was just finished. Looks pretty nice, but there's nothing inside of it. Anyways, I believe I shall be heading back to Aegis soon. There is nothing to do inside of the Verge, honestly. Hopefully something exciting will happen. Sometimes I just want to get away from Aegis, and explore. But I feel something is waiting for me. Not sure what it is.. But maybe it has to do with the Ascended.", ""),
        StaticBook("Richard's Journal", "1337Sammiches", "-----------------Book I-------------------------- Day 1 \nI have travelled to a nice, solitary land with my Elven counterpart Elessar. We have set up a small, cozy hideaway to gather supplies to sell in Al'Khazar. It is cold here, especially with the bitter freezing that the winter season has brought. Despite the weather, however, Elessar still hunts and brings back game for me to skin and make jackets and hats from. Whilst Elessar is hunting, I go into the mines to fend off hordes of goblins and mysterious Nether creatures some call pigmen. It is a nice, undisturbed life. \nDay 2 \nIt is becoming colder each day. I have lost a finger to frostbite. I hope Elessar keeps all of his , as an archer can't shoot without a middle finger. I just wish this Godforsaken winter would end... \n Until then, I suppose we can spare more coal for our heater. \nDay 3 \nElessar has gone missing. I am without food, without company, and without a friend. I hope he returns, seeing as he would die in only a few days without shelter and fire... \nDay 4 \nI fell whilst walking down the stairs to the mine. I broke my arm, and I broke the handle of my sword. I got ambushed by goblins after my fall, and without weapons to defend myself, they made off with my pickaxe. Now I can not mine coal, and my heater is only on 4 nuggets left. I hope Elessar is okay... \nDay 5 \nI heard screams coming from Al'Khazar. I decided to abandon this cramped hellhole of a hideout to investigate. I left a note for Elessar, should he return, along with the last of the coal and some fur that I fashioned a coat out of. \nDay 6 \nThe cries I heard from Al'Khazar were the result of an undead attack. I gazed upon the ruins of the gate and crept into the city. There I found a celebration of victory within Al'Khazar; the undead portal was destroyed and a monument was put up to celebrate. Despite all of this, the best part about the visit was that I found Elessar. He didn't tell me why he was there, and I didn't care. I was just happy to see him alive. \n(There is a mass of torn pages that can't be read) \nDay 15 \nElessar and I decided to stop by the Rusty Hook tavern for some cheap liquor and a place to lodge for the night. \n(The rest of the page is soaked in ale)", ""),
        StaticBook("Richard's Travels", "1337Sammiches", "Prologue: The story of Richard is entirely true, while some parts may be fabricated this is just to enhance the story The people however, are entirely factual. CHAPTER ONE: THE BEGINNING OF RICHARD I, Richard, come from a small village far away from the land of Aegis. The village was running out of water and was on the verge of desolation. I, the hero of the town, was tasked to find a steady water source. I began my journey right outside of the towns small, wooden walls that never succeeded to keep people out. Outside of the town, I found a strange creature with long legs and arms, and it resembled a tree. I didn't pay much attention to it at first, but its purple eyes began to burn into my mind... I was so frightened that I threw my sword, made of simple stone, and it hit it square in the face. The beast only got angry after that, and it chased me. It chased me into a corner, and I was trapped HEY! I said as I waited for it to draw nearer... It only looked at me, as I saw its jaw unhinge... it was about to swallow me. It lunged at me at first I tried to dodge it, but it just grew nearer... as it crept up, I heard the voices of many souls... it said \"I am Enderman, and your soul is mine\". Knowing that my life would eventually end, I did something stupid I took the sword from his face with a movement so swift, and I cleaved him as many times as I could. My desperate cleavings only broke the sword. It was then I realized that I only had one option... I reared my leg back, looked at him, and uttered a catchphrase that was perfect for the situation Then I swung my leg right into the beast's groin. The beast, quite surprised by this act, got on both of his knees, and grabbed his groin region. The mighty Enderman had fallen. It was now that I realized that my skill was paralleled to no other- I stopped using my broken sword and began using my hands to fight. Richard's log , part 1 I'm just gonna set this right here...", ""),
        StaticBook("Richard's Travels- Volume I", "1337Sammiches", "These are the recorded travels of Richard. Not much is known about his past, but his actions speak much louder than his words. Entry One- So here I am- Al'Khazar. The big, booming city of Oren. You know, I kind of expected a city like this when I heard the tales. The guards are nice, and the citizens let you mind your own business, I guess... I don't know, it seems kind of boring here. Perhaps I shall travel elsewhere Entry Two- I've gathered up my equipment for the travels. I have my sword, my leather jacket, my pickaxe, and my axe. I have all I need to fare the wilderness of Aegis. Here's to adventure! Entry Three- I pass through the gate of Al'Khazar into a snowy, harsh wilderness where the undead are rumored to lurk. As I gaze into the horizon, I see a majestic city slowly fading away. I'm alone. The town's glorious blue-and-white colors have been replaced by a wasteland of white and gray. Perhaps I will return to Al'Khazar... perhaps... Entry Four- I'm on the verge of death by starvation... I haven't eaten in days... I pray that someone will find me before I die...", ""),
        StaticBook("riddles", "stiason", "what has roots that no one sees, is taller than tree, up, up it goes yet never grows? alive without breath, as cold as death; never thirsty yet ever drinking, all in mail yet never clink ing, what am I? gd", ""),
