        StaticBook("RULES", "tyler70", "no killing innocents, but always kill bandits or lawbreakers (but rp it of course) ;; respect people and be nice, unless they are bandits, you are representing us in a bad way and will be kicked from our guild if you do so to much", ""),
        StaticBook("Rules", "Spartanx007", "1 Dont Steal or kill anyone unlessy they're Bandits and you must have proof or will be kicked from guild 2 Share Resources amoung your Battle Brothers does not mean donate means to not take more than you need of anything 3 Respect all people and Races unless they be  a bandit 4 Read signs and obey them.Use message bord to report your location  and how long you will be gone  and read the orders and do as they say", ""),
        StaticBook("Rules of Aegis", "ReaperT", "Here are some simple things to remember here... First of all, RolePlay or RP whenever possible Secondly, never kill someone with out Roleplaying first and not without a good RP reason \n If you happen to do that you could get banned. Thats bad. \n Also, never metagame. This is when you use information you gain out of character without bothering to find out that same info in character. This can also get you banned. \nNow the wilds are an interesting place. Most rules dont apply there. Unfortunately, you still have to RP to kill someone else. If you don't you can get banned. Once again, this is bad.", ""),
        StaticBook("rules, vol. 2", "VANCe42", "1. Don't take Luchian's stuff \n2. The mushrooms are Vance's", ""),
        StaticBook("Rumor", "Timgie", "Rumors have it that there is a chest at the bottom of a frozen lake near Winterfell that has several books containing that of magic, One of those books being Cataris' very own journal when he was only an apprentice up until magehood is when he threw the journal away. The other's being that of a long lost journal found in a cavern but it is now torn with only a few pages remaining and the last book being Cataris' twin brother's suicide letter to Cataris upon his death of which these books contain little is known but some hear if you ever retrieve them from the frozen lake and given back to Cataris you will be rewarded greatly.", ""),
