        StaticBook("runawayguy Wool Order", "machinegunliam", "All white wool. 20 stacks. Mc Name- runawayguy . \n8-29-11= Delivered 2 outta 20 Stacks. Current Price fer client is 576 minas. \n 8-30-11= 232 white...", ""),
        StaticBook("Rusty's Dunwood Contract", "Lomaticc", "As a resident of Dunwood Village, I will respect and aid my neighbors as best I can. I accept my free home, materials, and support from the fellow villagers, and in turn I will aid Dunwood Village as best I can by working my chosen career as Fisherman/Hunter((whichever)). This includes Fishin' and slaughterin' hogs for trout and pork. Working in a different career that belongs to someone else without consent of that person or an Elder is a warrant for eviction if deemed necessary by the Elders of Dunwood. I am aware if the chosen career is not taken by anyone or is not viewed as a career of Dunwood, I am allowed to do that career , however it will not be recognized by the Elders of Dunwood as aiding the community . If I do not aid the community to satisfactory, I understand my home could be given to someone who does. I also understand baths are important and will take one at least every week. \n \nI also agree not to build in Dunwood Village without an Elder of Dunwood's permission, and when allowed, will stick to the Halfling architecture present. I acknowledge the mountain Elduren will remain preeserved and not scarred by any Halfling architecture. Same goes for the Lake. \n \n I am entitled to my personal storage and belongings, but also understand hoarding goods that can or should be used by or for the community is frowned upon and could lead to eviction. Personal items may include, but is not limited to: weapons, trinkets, tools, armor, pictures, objects of sentimental value, and pets. I understand all halflings that are residents of Dunwood Village are required to drink one pint of ale a week. I am aware anything in the community storage of Dunwood Village is not available as a personal item and should not be taken home for personal storage unless otherwise approved by the Elders of Dunwood \n \n Theft, murder, trespassing, or blackmailing another villager of Dunwood Village will result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. Bringing trouble from outside Dunwood Village to Dundwood Village could also result in Banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. That includes but is not limited to bandits , war, Undead, or Orc Raiders. I am not secretly an Undead follower, Iblees worshipper, or a spider and will evict myself without causing harm to the villagers of Dunwood Vilalge if I am. \n \n I understand that interpretation of this contract is entirely up to the Elders of Dunwood. The Elders reserve the right to evict, restrict, or banish me from Dunwood Village if it is seen necessary. I am well within my rights to question any of the Elders in matters that this contract does not cover. \n \n x_Rusty", ""),
        StaticBook("Rusty's Log", "SpottedSnail", "help today we are close to makeing our house, it is big very big house.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruycken Fyst", "gao252", "I was walking in the forest last night, it was a calm night at that. Just like any other normal night. As I was walking down the path, I was ambushed by zombie pigmen. It had me cornered, I swore I was going to die. But then out of no were I shreiked Ruyken Fyst. Rapidly all the stone in my bag vaporized and my arm turned to stone for a split second. Just enough to block the blow. I managed to escape unharmed, but I still wonder. What was that, a sign, the start of my internal magic? I hope some day I will find out and possibly be able to control it. Someday.... -WR_Acolyte_Eirin-", ""),
        StaticBook("Ryan Burniston's Diary", "Burniston", "Day 1\n Well here it is, I am going to start a diary explaining my adventures in this land. I've been meaning to do this for a while but have not been able to find the time till now you wouldn't happen to have food would you? I've met up with an old friend that helped me heal Frowman a year or so back", ""),
        StaticBook("Rylus' Journal #3", "alex612", "Entry 1,Day 1.I Feel Strange,Empty. Entry 2,Day 5.Life Is Good.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rylus's Journal", "alex612", "Entry #1,Day #1.Spending My Day At The Laurlin Gates,As Usual.Nothing Unusual So Far Today Entry #2,Day #2.Same As Yesterday. Entry 3,Day 2.A Strange Dark Elf Asked Me Questions About The Undead Entry 4,Day 3.Watching the Moon Rise From Atop Witheroak.Magnificent. Entry 5,Day 4.It Rained Through The Noght.Didnt Know If The Lightning Was Undead Or natural. Entry 6,Day 5.Still Raining. .      Entry 7,Day 6.Watched a Female Elf And A Male Human Duel.He Won. Entry 8,Day 7.Took Gladail To Shadow Falls. Entry 9,Day 8.'The Shadows Fall Where Light Shines Too Much'.Qoute Of  A  Long Lost Freind. Entry 10,Day 9.Spent The Day Pretending To be A Oren Gaurd,Operating The Al Khazar Gate. Entry 11,Day 10.Spent The Day in Jail,Couldnt Find A Single Open Bar.I Need A Drink. Entry 12,Day 11.I Golem Got Stuck In The Al Khazar Fountain. Entry 13,Day 12.The Golem Is Out Of The Fountain.I Have A Bad Feeling About This Entry 14,Day 12.The Golem Is Alive Now.And Oren Doasnt Like Him. Entry 15,Day 17.I Must Free The Golem.....He Shouldnt Be A Slave", ""),
        StaticBook("Rylus's Journal #2.", "alex612", "I Saw A Woman Today,And I Knew She Was The One In My Dream. I Remember Seeing Her A Long Time Ago.She Was A....Rabbit.... her Name Was Jade,Jade StarStruck. Entry 2.Day 1. I Followed Her,But I Was Interuppted By A Orc. This orc Tried To Kill Me by Slitting My Throut,But He(She?)Didnt Cut Deep Enough And I Was Just knocked Out. Entry 3,Day 1. I Saw That Woman Again,She Was With A Man in A Fish Costume Playing Games.She Has A Childlike Quality About Her.Is She The Right One?", ""),
        StaticBook("Rytto_Jaw's Diary", "visualjaw", "Today I met Bowrim. A Kinght of the Flame. He showed me to their fortress near Al'Khazar, and I was recruited. ;;No sooner than I had arrived, there was word of an undead attack at snowyfields. I was rushed off my feet, and found myself following a platoon of Knights led by the Captain. ;;We saw lightning and fire in the distance. we were getting close. ;; When we arrived, I was told to scout out part of the town. I did so diligently. read -2 \n I soon found myself alone in a market district. There was a crack of lightning close by, and I looked towards that direction. That's when I saw him. Pulling down vengeance from the sky in the form of lighting, for he was undead. I dared not engage him in combat, yet I hurried back to the main group and reported the sight ing. The Undead retreated soon after. I was promoted to a Private for my efforts. 'The Night after the undead attack' [[]]", ""),
        StaticBook("S.A Recruit Book", "gombie", "As an Recruit of the S.A you can choose between Being An Archer or an Infantry Commander im writing an recruit book hold one", ""),
        StaticBook("Saadiya's Diary", "Saadiya", "Kamees, 26th of The First Seed, 1341  I have taken to writing a diary.  Right now me and Kishin are listening in on Rune and Voak's argument. It's a bit invasive,  but it is for the good of their new child. Kishin is so cute, I just wish he had more emotions, and you know, wouldn't freak out if I held  his hand. Mania is in a state of decay and death is imminant. ( Rune seems to be having the same issue, but Mania fights shadows, Rune fights his other personality.   Joma, 27th of The First Seed, 1341   Rune and Voak argued all night and day.     Sabet, 28th of The First Seed, 1341   Rune and Voak finally finished their argument, but I don't know who won. All I know is they left Voak's room.    Ahad, 29th of The First Seed, 1341   Kishin, Rune and I are off to find Alys, Voak's love. Kishin is using his sniffing powers to find Alys. We found Alys after a while.   Itnan, 30th of The First Seed, 1341   We went to see Alys, and Voak showed up, they wanted to talk in private, so Kishin, Rune and I went into the inn. Kishin also said that he got over his fear of being touched, this is AWESOME! ^.^   Tolta, 31st of The First Seed, 1341   Voak and Alys are having a long talk.   Irba, 32nd of The First Seed, 1341   I am off to go hunt some animals for some minas, need to pay for food some how. I am leaving my Diary at home, for safety reasons. ((Going to bed.))   Itnan, 9th of Suns Smile, 1341   I am back at home. I can continue writing in my diary. Kishin got his own guard room at the Tree Top Inn, he sais I'm always welcome in. *fan squeel*   Irba, 11th of Suns Smile, 1341   Kishin insists I get my own place, he even got a friend to come help me move stuff. I am going to have to build it from scratch too... I'm sure Kishin and his friend Mindus will be a big help though.   Irba, 18th ofSuns Smile, 1341   The building of the new house is coming along GREAT! Mindus is a real help.  \n \n Sabet, 21st of Suns Smile, 1341 \n \n I almost lost my diary! I was ready to kick over my entire new tree house! I found it though. Mindus treated me to cake after we finished the chest room. I have 7 bookshelves now, that should be enough for a bookshelf to hold my diary. I can't wait until we build my room. We just need wood and leaves. Mindus may be a bit charming, but Kishin is a lot cuter. And the way he is, with no emotions,  I don't know why, but it makes me just want to hug him until I die. Am I weird? Something messed up all my pages so it's not in paragraphs anymore. I'm just going to leave it for now though. It's easier to just keep writing with paragraphs now than to re-write it all... I over heard people at the Tree Top Inn talking about shadow taint taking over... I assume that they are talking about Mania... I don't think I can face him, it's just so sad, and I don't want to see him the way he is now... \n \n Kamees, 5th of Snows Maiden, 1341 \n \n I helped Rigrud get over to my new house. The frame of my room is laid out now. Kishin smelt his way over here. Someone decided to build nearby, I left a sign saying that they should come say Hi, and asking who they are. \n \n Ahad, 8th of Snows Maiden, 1341 \n \n My room is near completion, Mindus thankfully dropped off some more leaves. They were needed. The underside is completely covered now too. It's just a matter of making this place look good, then add more... \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Sacred Heroes - The Brotherhood", "JoakimVonAnka", "\"... I died in The Nether... They called it Aegis...\"  - Asyrian, Sacred Leader of the Sacred Heroes. Asyrian didn't look back. He continued the travel with no fear in his eyes. His cold hand and feets wouldn't stop him. He had decided to leave the safe life as a piece in the large puzzle that the leaders of was putting together.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sacrifice pits.", "sconn", "There are many ways to make a sacrifice to Iblees. Some are as simple as stabbing. Others involve machinery. In this book i will teach you how to make your own sacrifice pits. Sacrifice pits ussually involve just you trapping a person in a room. And the machinery does the res A good sacrifice pit is something i call the crusher. To make this sacrifice pit you will pistons. This is one of the simples ti implement to your home. You need to trap a person in a small space. The space must be just enough for the person to fot in. It has to be the exact height as the person. On the floor of the space must be a piston facing upwards. It is up to you to activate the piston. this pit will chrush the person into the upper wall. This is also one of my favourite torture mechanics. I already have the pit implemented in my home. And it seems to do its job well. The next pit is a bit more difficult to create. Especialy in tight spaces. It is called the spiker. It must be created like the chrusher. But the piston on the floor is removed. Place the piston so that when it is extended it holds the person above a cactus. You simply deactivate the piston and the person falls on the cactus. I also have this implemented in my home. It is not as usefull as the chrusher for it cannto torture people. But it is a great way to have the person suffer. remember that the room has to be realy small so the victim wont be ablr to jump on the floor from the cactus. This next on requirers netherrack. Make the sam room as the other pits. Simply place netherrack on the floor and attache redstone to it. When you trigger the switch the netherrack ignites. Also good for a slow death but not as good as the chrusher. The next one is pretty simple. Make the same small space. on the floor place a trapdoor. Make a small hole under the trap door and fill it with water. on the bottom of the pit that iss filled with water place a cobweb. The victim will slowly drown. This is also used in the Oren guard for executions. If you have enough money you could create the ultimate torture chamber. I will describe one that i have created. I have made a large room but it is only the height of a person. in its middle i placed a glowstone. around that glowstone i placed pistons that trap the victim. Right above the glowstone on the roof is another piston that can crush a victim. I placed arrow dispensers on each side of the room. That is just a small torture room that i have created. There are many different ways to create something like that. Farewell.May Iblees be with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sadi..", "MrJakKiD", "<3", ""),
        StaticBook("Sadness", "Cookie9000", "I had to watch it, watch my home village get burnt down by bandits, I had to watch them slaugter friends and enemies alike, watch them burn the pigs and animals until they crisped, they scarred me. Mentally, watching the sight of them killing them all saddens me, as I write now I am crying. Only if I could go back in time... That isnt even the worst part. When the bandits ran off, for a few years it was good, my family didnt get killed, only one or two of my friends died..... Until the undead came. They put me in a cage and made me watch my father get decapitated, and my mother burnt until she was COMEPLETE crisps and ashes... Just remembering this is making me bawl as I write this... These memories curse me for life and the worst part of the undead was they didnt do a thing to me. They forced me to watch family and friends slowly die by torture machines. If anyone finds these years after my death I hope you know what my life was like. -Alanor Hedgewell", ""),
        StaticBook("Sadri Corfi's Guid to Survival", "ThatMine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sadri Corfi's Guide to Survival", "ThatMine", "Chapter 1: Introduction \n Now in opening this book, you probably think to yourself..\"This book will give me the tools to", ""),
        StaticBook("Sadri Crofi's Guide to Survival", "ThatMine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sage Okonkwos time in prison", "OmtraSpectral", "I was captured by the undead in my attempt to save bell from being tortured. they tortured me and droped me in a pit thinking I would die. By some power my life was spared and they threw a rope down for me to get out. They then put me in the arrow toture chamber. much to my surprise the machine did not work and they gave up on tortuing me", ""),
        StaticBook("Saint Sertok the Twice-Born, Patron Saint of Virtue", "begginfokillz", "This scripture is a holy tome recounting the deeds of St. Sertok. Compiled by Father Dimitri of the Guardians. St. Sertok was born for the first time as a humble greenskin child in the land of Aegis. he lived a innocent childhood, and was later educated by a order of priests. He lived well, not careing he was a subhuman greenskin. In Fact, he was quite civilized, and was not as feral or criminal as his brethren he brought honor to the priests under whom he studdied and was destined for greatness soon after leaving his studdies, he joined the Guardians, a virtueous order formed to fight the undead scourge, by any means nessacary in his first battle, the undead threatened Oren. rising above the rest, he brought honor to the Gaurdians, and helped nuetralize the threat against oren soon after, he found, by divine will of god, his inner powers, and became a shaman and beacon of hope for the people. He was destined for greatness, and, after suffering the 9 holy wounds at the hands of the undead, he was born again as Saint Sertok the Twice Born, Patron saint of virtue using his powers for good, he became, through the will of god, a master shaman so that he may smite the undead wherever they hide St. Sertok is a living saint, a powerful avatar of the will of god. he is a shining example of what all humans wish to become and he hath trancended mere mortality, though he may still fall in battle St. Sertok is wise and humble, and is worthy of a thousand songs to his name he hath been thrice blessed and twice born, and has a prayer dedicated to him \"Blessed be St. Sertok, he who smites undead. Please save us from evil. Amen\" St. Sertok was christened a saint of the clan Guardians, by Priest Dimitri. may his name be praised a thousand times, in a thousand lands may his blade never dull, and may he deliver us from evil. amen", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Book", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "I built this home, because I had none. The White Ravens took me in, and I tried my best to help in their cause, but now it is too late.... I write this so that somebody may remember me one day, as i was before, and not... a monster. \n To Grum the Orc, my greatest friend: You are special, the kindest Orc one could dream of. I'm glad I had the peasure of getting to meet you, and I will miss you buddy... \n To Sythra: I hope that you may find love one day, and happiness with that. There isn't another Elf like you; positive, wise, and beautiful above all else. I'm dissappointed in myself. I'm sorry I did not save you that day.... I wish i could have spent more time with you , Who knows what could have been... \n To the White Ravens; I'm proud to say a was a member, let alone an assassin. Thank you for allowing me . into your family. If i ever get over this... I'll rejoin you with great pride, knowing i can serve once more, alongside the mightiest warriors in Aegis. \n To The Sariants; It was an honor to fight alongside you in the seige of the Nical Empire. I hope we can meet again.....if I overcome this.... \n To Anonymous Reading This Book; If you know any of the people listed above, give this book to them, for this is the only copy . Now I must leave you....i can feel it taking effect.. *scribbles cover the next page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Book Edition No. 4-1", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Ame Ito Narne \n Ame'eyha Ito Narne \nIto Vull", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Curse", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "I've finally woken up from this terrible dream..... But i can feel the curse isn't quite lifted? Sometimes I'll lose myself to it....and then return an hour later, I don't understand \n #2 - I've gained most control over it! But it only comes out now when I'm hungry.... Isn't that strange? If i can just keep enough food in my body, i should be okay. \n #3 - I woke up on the floor of the living room, and upon going downstairs, I found a completely new chamber!? What is it planning.... I can't keep running out of food like this...", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Final Words", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "My Fellow Ravens, and Friends...... I've been sick for a quite a long time now, trying to hid e it, but there's no use. I am forcing myself to leave the White Ravens, as much as it kills me to say... I'm afraid that if I stay, i will endanger or harm many of you.... I have done research... I will not be able to control myself when curse takes full effect. Furthermore, If any of you see me again, ever, I leave you a warning. Run.", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's SpellBook", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "ame ito narne \n ame'eyha ito narne \nito vull", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Spellbook (Lord A Edition)", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Ame Ito Narne \nAme'eyha ito narne \n Ito Vull", ""),
