        StaticBook("Salamandra's Spellbook Edition No. 1", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Vines: Vines sprout from the ground, holding the targets feet in place \n Sala's Vanish: Leaves swirl around him as he disappears from view", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's SpellBook Edition No.3", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Ame Ito Narne \n Ame'eyha Ito Narne \n Ito Vull", ""),
        StaticBook("Salamandra's Staff", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "His Staff is blessed by Raven_Druid_Dante, a close friend, and parts of the shaft were made by Arch-Mage Ambros. When Salamandra falls in battle with his staff, it is transported back to his chest in the Mage's Guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Salmeer's Jornal.", "459pm", "12/16/11 I honeslty wish the undead would attack more, Galahar becomes so boaring if they do not. Throdo has began work on the new wall, it will cover Galahar compleatly, and most of the sorounding villages. I deeply want to help him, but i have not obtained the keys to the city yet. but i think Tarus is giving them out somtime tomorrow.     Throdo's still working on the tower. I hope it will be finished by the next undead attack.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sam's discovery.", "Curion", "I could only see blur .... everything was ... black..... I saw a man, with black hood. He looked a lot like a Nazghul. I woke up in .... Mordor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Samuel_Ironheart's Journal", "legoman144", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar", "Pepernoot", "Sanhar is a city of Krugmar, It is located in the desert, and the most commonly used material is the abundand sandstone. It has been attacked by the undead on multiple occasions in the last decade.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar Guard Journal", "Volutional", "I, Rogash, will write who is being monitored in Sanhar. I will write it in dis' book. Some  be banned.", ""),
        StaticBook("sanhar times", "zemchy", "ok ahhggg! shoot AHHHGGGG! ahhggg! im messing up i cant stop writing!", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar Times I", "MojoKronic", "Sanhar Times. I. \n \n In the holy name of Krug the All-Father, Krugmar his children, the sacred names of his saints, the glorious song of the Ancestors and the secret names  of all the blessed ghosts, spirits and gods as well as the mighty Rex Tythus I, Shaggo Dhanksmoek, Krug's humble shaman, bless this book and all editions to follow for the glory of  the people. \n \n Krug bless the hunt. \n \n Our world is one of trial and tragedy, a truth the Oren Capital of Al'Khazar learned recently . King Pampo was killed during an invasion of Deadites, the walking dead. His funeral will  be held on the 1st of August at which point King Edmund Sheffield will coronate the new king . \n A darker shadow has befallen the children of Krug. Our beloved Dominus Bein'lur,  blessed of Krug and Orc of esteem and honor, has been captured through foul means  by his enemy of old: Or'ta. Or'ta has declared his intention to reclaim his throne from  the current Rex, Tythus. If the children of Krug knew pity, the air would be filled with  lament and wails of woe, but we are the Orc and the desert sky instead quakes before  the terrible howls of wrath and bloodlust that rise in unison from every soul of Krug's  faithful. Will the Rex rise to lead the people against Or'ta? What will become of Sanhar  without the leadership of Dominus Bein'lur? What will his new founded clan do with its  head so suddenly ripped away before they had scarcely opened their newborn eyes? May Krug bless our hunt with blood and glory, and may our enemies know us as Hell itself. \n \n In other news our nation still lacks a specialized economy. Young Goblins, take up the call! Our nation is growing exponentially and our military power is unamatched, let us now  conquer the world with coin and industry. Krug calls us to be strong, this is not limited  to strength of arms alone, but wealth also. \n The ancestors have blessed us with an influx of gifted young shamans. Now we are  blessed with Ma Tinra, called by some 'a shamans paradise'. Possessing over 1000  book cases, expansive farm and a Yggdrasil of its own, land is sure to be sold quickly. \n \n In this special first edition of Sanhar Times we would like to offer an exclusive interview  given to us by Dominus Bein'lur only days before his capture. \n \n \n \n \n Sanhar Times: How did you begin your career as a soldier? \n Dominus Bein'lur: I signed up for a job as a guard, to warlord Tythus. Then I got sent  to war against the dwarves. Soon after that I returned to Sanjezal and stood guard  for three years. Those were quiet days... \n ST: Your beginnings were quite humble. Did you ever imagine yourself Dominus? \n DB: I always imagined myself as Dominus, but I never thought I would reach it.  But I always had the chance, being a part of the noble clan of Lur, who were strong  supporters of Tythus.  They were killed off by Or'ta's clan for supporting Tythus. \n ST: You have been in so many wars. Have they changed your view of the world? \n DB: Aye, so much blood has been shed and I feel we orcs need to rise beyond our  primal instincts and start collaborating and working together. \n ST: You were the founder of the Ferox Legio. Was it hard to let go of leadership? \n DB: Was it hard to let go of leadership? Well, sort of. Ferox Legio was already dead  at the time and I realized that I couldn't lead it while leading a town. Hopefully the  New Orc Army will be a better replacement and will survive. \n ST: This is my last question. When you founded Sanhar did you ever expect it to become  so big and influencial? \n DB: Nay, I could never have done it without the consul and especially Tirok who  designed many parts of it and is even now being considered for Dominus of lower Sanhar. \n ST: Thank you for your time Dominus Bein'lur. \n DB: Anytime. \n This has been a special first edition of Sanhar Times. Future periodicals will not be  as extensive in text but we promise that our quality and topicallity will remain worthy  of the Krugmar. If you wish to subscribe seek out Craotor. If you have an ad you'd  like to run, an article you'd like to see, a question to ask or anything else please  contact either me, Shaggo Dhanksmoek, or Croator in person or through the Krugmar  Forums. \n \n May you walk in strength and honor. May Krug bless your hunt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar: Born Of Blood", "T1MadSmurf", "The Riverside attack came quickly and as a suprise, they jumped through the glass in the gasd", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_21(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Sanhar: Born of Blood", "TheMiner15", "The Riverside attack came quickly and as a suprise, they jumped throught the glass in the gatehouse and ran outside. They stabbed Jackel through the chest before he could even get his sword out. Bein pulled out his sword and managed to cut down one before the others slashed him down. ,, The Riversiders : held", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar_Guard", "Zhoboz", "", ""),
        StaticBook("sanhara", "JORDANB885", "orcs are cool", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanharhome 2", "Sultan_Mogroka", "Sold to Aeolwyn, he owns the shop until the warlord deems otherewise helo help", ""),
        StaticBook("sanharshopp1", "Sultan_Mogroka", "Sold to Aeowyn, he owns it until the warlord deems otherewise Signed Warlord Mogroka", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanity an ... ((the ink has spread all over))", "Aandie", "*You see that the ink has spread all over the first pages of the book. The name, what you believe to be the author's name, has been partly ruined by the spread ink. You figure out that the first three letters are 'Ale..'. The ink has spread all over, till the middle of the second page where the story seems to begin. \n \n I feel insane every single time I'm asked ta compromise.  Because I'm afraid and stuck in me ways and that is the way it stays. So 'ow long did I expect love ta outweight ignorance.. By that look on your face I may ave forced th scale ta tip. *You notice that the next couple sentences have been written down, by a shaking unstable hand. 'I'm not insane.. I'm not insane. I'm not insane.. I'm not.. insane..' \n \n \n *The unstable handwriting chances into more stable handwriting. \n \n Rage pulses through me 'eart, from the things I 'ave done ta  you. It's hard ta face but the fact remains, that this is nothin new.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanity an.. ((Rest of it, is unreadable. Caused by spread ink.))", "Aandie", "*The first page is ruined by the spread ink also. What you believe to be, the authors name only has three first letters remaining, 'Ale..'. You notice that the first page had two really differing handwritings on it. One stable, one le. The ink has spread all over, till the middle of second page, where the story seems to begin.    I feel insane every single time I'm asked ta compromise. Because I'm afraid and stuck in me ways and that is th way it stays! So 'ow long did I expect love ta outweight ignorance?  By that look on yer face I may 'ave forced th scale ta tip.   *The following couple sentences have been written by an le,  shaking hand. They say 'I'm not insane.. I'm not insane.. I'm not insane. I'm not .. not insane.'    Rage pulses through me 'eart. From th things I 'ave done ta you. It is 'ard ta face, but th fact remains. That this is nothing new.   I left ye bound and tied with suicidal memories. Selfish beneath th skin, but deep inside..  *Unstable handwriting again, saying 'I'm not insane.'     Now that I 'ave lost ye, it kills me ta say. I tried ta 'old on, ye slowly slipped away. I'm losing th fite. I treated ye so wrong, now let me make it right. *Shaking, le handwriting again 'I'm not insane.. I'm not insane.. hahaha.. I'm not insane.. I'm not .. not .. NOT INSANE.'     \n \n \n \n *The ink spreads in this part of the book too. Where it ends, the handwriting seems really  unstable, hard to read. \n \n 'Tis is me letter ta those who don't care, the ones I think they 'ave been reasonable and fair.. I want ye ta kno what lives in me mind, because it's hate that you'll always find.. It's to everyone around me, who lives careless and free.. \n \n I want ye ta kno what lives in me mind, because it is sadness ye will never find. It is th reason I go to sleep and dream of ye, it is the reason I wish ta kill ye. \n \n I want ye ta kno what lives in me mind.. It is darkness ye can only find.. It is where I sit and wallow, and begin ta feel oh so hallow. \n \n Now there is good bye, ta all that I kno, because ye will never see, what I 'ave done ta ye..'. *Theres a tiny space in between and after that space, there is a signature, which you can't make sense of as it is too blurry. ((Do not meta my name, please))", ""),
        StaticBook("SanJezal Housing Book", "DefunctDivine", "Possible Architects\n Peter [Peter9930] \n Lex [Lexperiments] Note: Dwarven Shaman, most likely not fulltime architect", ""),
        StaticBook("Sapphireshard Redpoints", "monkeychez", "Sapphireshard (20)", ""),
        StaticBook("Saren's Journal", "HICHERV07", "Kamees 5th of The Second Seed, 1315;; Evern is a bastard, the prick beat the shit out of me and i was kicked out     for no reason!, i will be back though, just you wait Irba 32nd of The Second Seed 1315\n i cant belive it, i was kicked out of the damn city, exiled if you will. now ive got to make a living outside....... but i didnt do any wrong! thre is NO justice in the city Joma 34th of The Second Seed 1315, it is a funny thing kindness, on my jourey i came to an inn called The Rusty Hook seemed quaint and simple at first, but boy, was i wrong, Tiberius ( Ti ) is one of the most kind people i have ever met in this land, i have a bed, and a job it can only go uphill from here!, ...... at least i can hope..... ;; met a man named Methodius today, seems like a nice person, he was raised by monks after he attemeped suicide?, i dont know , there is no time like the presant   \n: im headin to the city later on today, seeing if i can make up past greveances mainly with Evern, i only hope this isnt a mistake ;;; im at the gate, no one is maning it, and the gate is closed? carelessness? ;;; some clown let me in, dont even know he was a guard some guy pulled me over asking if i was looking for a job, i followed him \n;the man took me to a fort by the name of Norodrum, it is currently looking for a scribe how could i pass up an offer like this?, i must pack my bags away from the inn but i must remember to tell Tiberius my sincerist thank you, he saved my life....... Tolta, 10th of The Grand Harvest, currently walking back to Norodrum with guess who? it is Evern!, ha! i guess that tif is the past now, this walk has also given me the time to t hink, i may of had a shady past, at best. But now i can look to the future :;; i heard about a mysterious book today, it is called the Necromicon.... it is affiliated with the undead, hm it could become a powerfull tool in the hands of a person like me......... i will be sure to keep an eye out for it \n: Currently in some old in, me and Evern are camping the night, it sure is cold up here so much diffrent from the Kendallian desert. \n\n scored the Scribe job at Norodrun, though archives arnt compleate yet i will get a job at the labor for the next few days.... Sabet 14th of The Grand Harvest. 1315, i have been working my ass off these past few days it is however paying off, i have got over 200 middas now ( and counting! )", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus Pay Slip", "WOOSH10001", "Golden Harvest Pay-slip\nRecruit Saviticus\n10/12/2011\nSigned Overseer Max", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus's Book of Reagents", "Saviordude", "This is a list of all the reagents used in Shamanism I know of. \n \n Cactus Dye- Used to summon minor spirits of the four main elements. \n Ink Sack- Used to summon fire spirits. \n Bonemeal- Used to summon water spirits. \n Cocoa Beans- Used to summon life spirits. \n Glowstone- Used in major rituals. \n Lapis Lazuli- Used to summon water or earth elementals. \n Red Dye- Used as a ritual booster. \n Yellow dye- Used as a ritual booster.", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus's Book of Spirits", "Saviordude", "This is a list of all the spirits I have summoned. \n \n Baldash- Male Earth Spirit \n Ayra- Female Water Spirit \n Gur'gar- Male Fire Spirit \n Yahre- Male Air Spirit", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus's Journal", "Saviordude", "Day 1: I've moved into the temple, but the library isn't finished so I must wait to do my work. Also the Undead attacked Krumgar while I was there and I barley got away with my life. I am worried for the safety of Kal'Urguan. \n Day 2: The library was finished and I have been working on filling it up. The Arch-Bishop said he was pleased with my progress. I went to the Elven lands to seek becoming a druid, but they said there was no one to teach me and they would get back to me. I doubt that they will. \n Day 3: I talked to the Wayward Druid himself today, and he took me with him as he went about his druidic tasks. It was an honor, but he had left early. I intend to seek him out as soon as possible to ask him to take me in as a druid. There was an emergency in Kal'Urguan today, as the crag swowed up the outer city. It was completely destroyed, and they are working on rebuilding it. \n Day 4: Great newsh! Oashish Druid John brought me into the order, and I have begun my teachingsh. He sheemsh to be a mosht capable druid, and I am eager to learn from... hic! him. Unfortunately, Priesht Kane died today deshpite Johnsh besht effortsh, and Arch-Bishop Hoggarth wash removed from office. I no longer have any reashon to... hic! shtay in Kal'Ulguan and I dishagree with King Agrim, sho I have moved to Laurien and... hic! purchashed a nice home there with help from Hoggarth. I am eager to invite him to come live with me. Alsho, Krumgar wash attacked again by the undead, and I was caught in the middle of it. We won, but their w was destroyed and many lifes were... hic! losht. I pray to the crafter that they don'y attack my new home.... hic! I 'ave decided to start this journal as a record of me life. I looked around me, and saw  that I looked around me the other day, at this world which was changin' so fast. Towns are born and empires crumble, all while the undead plot against us. I 'ave decided to start this journal, so that one day people may read it and learn about what went on in me lifetime.", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus's Shaman Journal", "Saviordude", "I 'ave started this 'ere journal as a record of me journey as a Shaman under the teachings of Lex'lur. Let it be a testament of me struggles to learn the spiritual arts. \n \n Entry 1\n I started me training today, and met with Lex'lur in Krumgar. He taught me the uses of different reagents, and together we summoned a water and earth spirit.  We still 'ave to summon a fire and air spirit, I suppose we'll do that next time. \n \n Entry 2\n We continued me training today with the summoning of an air and fire spirit. The fire spirit ws a bid 'ard to control, but I eventually got it to give me it's name. Afterwards, we went out and planted a sapling, and used the meal of the bone on it. Chopping it down, Lex'lur crafted it into a staff fer me, with a spirit of water in it. Her name is Aelia, and she is quite easygoing. I think we're goin' to get along nicely.", ""),
        StaticBook("Saviticus's Staff Spirit", "Saviordude", "My staff's spirit revealed herself to me upon meditation, her name is Aelia and she is a water spirit. From talking with her, I have learned that she is easygoing and playful. She likes to make jokes and lots of them. She is cheerful and talkative too. From what I can tell she has goals of her own, which include seeing the world and helping others heal. She also wants to help a shaman teach their students. She enjoys melon, and asked me if I had any on me. When I told her no she frowned, and told me to go get some. She also enjoys the sound of the rain, and asked me to take her somewhere where she could hear it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sayings and poems", "Roxses20", "\"love is sometimes magic,but magic is sometimes a illusion\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Sayings Of Ambros", "silco97", "\"Mastery is achived when telling time becomes telling time what to do\" \n\"Magic? Anyone can pick up a brush and paint, call themslves an artist even.  But only through years of dedication and study can you create a true masterpiece.  A sorcerer is like a child with paint, barly understanding what they are doing.  You must master the art\" \n\"Don't make me angry. You see, when Mr. Tibbles gets scared. And when Mr. Tibbles gets scared.... people die!\" \n\"Your deeds can not be undone, like a path of melting ice, you can only go forward\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Sayings of Archdruid Cicero Vol. 2", "Respiren", "True glory takes root, and even spreads; all false pretences, like flowers, fall to the ground; nor can any counterfeit last long.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sayings of Archdruid Cicero Vol.3", "Respiren", "If you have a garden and a library, you have everything you need. \n\n Cultivation to the mind is as necessary as food to the body. \n Druid Petyr (drplat)", ""),
        StaticBook("Sayings of Wanderer_Druid_Mithrandir", "CrunchySushi", "\nA cluttered collection of my sayings. Keep them in mind with you as you travel. \n*Those who reap the benefits, will sow the fields of success. \n*Knowledge is comparable to a tree; The roots stand firm, but the branches may sway in the wind.   (Be firm in your knowledge but also listen to the knowledge of others)    \n*Plants are animals also, albeit very slow ones. \n*When you leave your home for a stroll, realize you are coming into your true home. \n*Nature does not make haste, yet everything it does, is accomplished. \n*The force of nature cannot be reckoned with or measured. \n*The mind is a terrible thing to waste. \n*Let nature be our church of worship. \n*Listen to the birds sing, for their songs are beautiful. \n*Animals may be mute, but their eyes speak many things. \n*You and I are but animals living in this world. \n*Children are very bold things. They come into this world naked and are not afraid to ask questions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scara, Spirit of Fire", "Ned_Lud", "Me am Scara, spirit of fire. Me flesh bear da scar and burn of da enemy and me bone am soaked wit der blood. Many men has me flatted wit da axe and da fist, women and children too, it make no difference. Lat will hear der scream and cry in da flame when me am near.\n      Across da land of Aegis, lat will hear many of da lesser race tell tale of how der family were slaughtered by da orc. Father slain in glorious death on da battlefield. Mother stolen, ravaged and left for dead. House and village burned as da family was smoked out like pushdug rat and murdered in da street, flesh eaten, skull mounted on post. Many will tell dis tale of how dey crawled off and survived, wearing it like badge of honor, wielding it like zult. Not one of dem filthy orphan have da stone to speak da name of dem orc nor da strongest one dat led dese raid, da one dat spared dem for later, da name of Scara and him headhunters.\n Da runt of each litter me always spared and sent off into da wilderness. Der dey would grow to be stronger warrior and when dey returned for dem vengeance, Scara would be ready for dem. Seemed like bubhosh idea at da time, yet many moon passed and me were still fighting no ting but coward, come crawling up to Scara in da night wit wooden zult screaming, \"You killed my father.\" Me had enough. From den on, me flat everyting in sight.\n      Man, woman, child, baby, old lady, dog baby, kill dem all. Leave no survivor to tell der story and shame demself on da battlefield year later. Cut dem down and move on, for no enemy dat cross path wit da orc and live to speak of it will ever find him strength again. Death is da only honor dey will ever know and it be a mercy to give dem even dat.\n      Ned Lud'Gorkil has called upon me spirit and me have answered, me words written in dis b ook through him own haunted hand. Der is a fire dat burn in da warrior, hot as da Krugmar sand and spreading like da flame in a wheat field during da Grand Harvest season. Me will lead him across dis burning wasteland and keep him from da flame as him enemy burn screaming in da fire.\n      Me can be called upon by da burning of man or beast or by da offering of a dead man's head, thrown into da fire. Taking da burn or brand on one's body will give me blessing in strength and combat. In da presence of fire be da place for meditation and prayer. Me take pleasure in dese tings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scarlet Queen Prices/Info", "DanteKreed", "Food Warm Cookies ... 1.25 minas each Roast Chicken ... 8 minas (bought in person) Fresh Melon Slices ... 5 minas (bought in person) T-Bone and Ribeye Steaks ... 10 minas each (bought in person) Salted Cod ... 8 minas Hearty Mushroom Stew ... 10 minas Loaf of Bread ... 10 minas Crisp Apples ... 5 minas Delicious Cake ... 180 minas Char-Grilled Pork ... 10 minas Home-brewed Ale ... 10 minas (bought in person)                             Rooms          300 - 400 minas per month (1 week in RL)", ""),
        StaticBook("Sconn Mormont's biography", "sconn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sconn Mormont's Last Will", "sconn", "*this is only to be read in the case of my death* I leave all of my belongings to my brother Bergoth Mormont. I wish that my money would be given to the Oren guard. And the Oren Rangers I also wish that my body would be burned so i could never rise from my grave. My ashes are to be scatered in the northern wastes so i can return to my true home. (signed) Sconn Mormont", ""),
        StaticBook("Sconn's philosophy", "sconn", "The creator has created mortals with mistakes. Mistakes like pride glory honour mercy I have trid to overcome those mistakes. I tortured myself just so I can stop feeling lust Why did he give us mistakes i do not know. But i know a way to get rid of those mistakes. Some people have achieved it. Many tried and failed. The only way to get rid of humanity is to die. The undead overcame those mistakes. They are now pure beings of power. I fight for the undead just for that reason. I fight for immortality. The undead do not wish us harm. They only want to rid your soul of its crippled body. The creator gave us mistakes so we couldnt overpower him. The one who created us is now afraid. But Iblees gave us gifts. Iblees gave us deception, betrayal, hatred, wrath. Those are a few usefull traits that we were given. The crator wants us weak, but Iblees wants us strong. Remember death is just the beggining.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sconn's poem", "sconn", "Nature is a beauty. It is a guard that is always on duty. It makes way for life. And gives home to the wildlife. Nature is a gift. A gift we should embrace. But now it left. Leaving us nothing buy space.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scooba Diving (OOC)", "Shutter_Bugg", "I went Scooba Diving, and I thought it would be a beaut, if I warmed my self up quickly by doing a wee in my wet suit. I did a wee and it went great, but I would've preffered, if I hadn't accidentally done a terd.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge, a fictional-tale of an Undead.", "IlumTarus", "About e Auor. Eze'kiel Tarus is a blacksmi and architect by trade, recently made Templar. He lives wi his Grandfaer and has fought some undead before. He does not have e best undersnding of ere ways, is should not be considered an accurate guide to e workings of e undead, but for enjoyment. \n  DISCLAIMER! I am not an Undead, or affiliate myself to em. This is merely a work for enjoyment of someing sinister, keep in mind, is is a Mature-book for Mature people. \n  \n \n THE SCOURGE. \n \n \"NO! PLEASE! DON'T!\" These final words echoed in e forest as a wicked crack was heard, for Kel'ieon- is was almost his sound of merriment. For is poor farmer, is was simply e last sounds of his life fading to noing. Kel'ieon dropped e corpse on e ground, next to a pile of two oers... his family,   a woman, two children... ey'd susin him wi eir flesh tonight. Kel'ieon grudgingly sent his hand to a dismembered limb, devouring flesh off dripping red  muscle. Grudgingly, his mou sank and chewed into it. Anger wiin each gnaw. \"The world made me is way, so is world will pay.\" Kel'ieon tensed his arm to e sound of snapped branches, turning quickly to it. He dismissed e oughts after a while, a sneaking predator... much like he was. \n \n It had to have been six years ago, wi Kel'ieon in Alkhazar. He was a cutpurse, a ief, a common-crook wi an uncommon end. Kel'ieon found himself sprinting rough e city, over e rooftops, away from his latest  target, he found himself vaulting over roofs and shingles sloppily. \"JUST LEAVE ME BE!\" He shouted to his pursuer, whom was cloaked, head to toe, yet nimble as an arrow. Kel'ieon darted over one last roof and felt himself spinning, wi no ground benea. He flew for a few moments until e sounds of crunching bones were heard. Moments after, e soft patter of footsteps fell from e sky, next to him. A hand cast over Kel'ieons face and pulled him up, his hand was like a bear- locked. \"You are a foolish child- to not know who you're dealing wi.\" The man's hood flew up and down momentarily, e words seemed to echo out, as ough ese words came from e deps of hell itself. \"Don't... kill me,\" ese words choked out, muffled by blood filling his mou like hot iron. \"Kill you..? There is an idea... no boy. Your life is mine now, you will suffer more.\" \n \n Kel'ieon tried to recall his old name... he could not. Much of whom he was seemed to be overlapped by screams of e dead and damned. He heard e same crack is time, turning to face it once more. two arrows flew out, one following anoer like two-bees wi stingers of steel. Kel'ieon reacted and lifted his staff, deflecting one to e side and letting e oer go  through his hand, letting the blood drip down his arm. After that, he waited and stared to the direction, a sudden roar emerged, \"You murderous, bloodlusting fiend!\" As a man Iron-clad rushed at him. Kel'ieon jerked his staff forward and fire washed over the man like a bath from hell. He jumped back just in time to his suprise as a sword swung through this. He then slid back as another strike came, spinning to the side once more after. He sent out his hand to the Warrior's head, the arrow still pierced through. It went directly through his eye, the sword dropped to the side as Kel'ieon leaned him back. He then slid his hand off the arrow, still lodged in the nearly-dead man's eye. He lifted his staff and and looked down, but hesitated. In that moment he found himself in weakness by his own memories. He pictured himself at his feet and bit his lip hard, letting it too bleed. He then lept back and ran through the brush with the vigour of nature itself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scout intel- mission humans", "snooshix", "Storm Army We attack the oren kingdom at 2:00pm central time. We will sneak 2 men in to open the gates before the army comes. this will happen on Wednesday july 27 eraseall Get to lord_John - snooshix", ""),
        StaticBook("Scout Report : Undead Northern Raid", "deanofantastico", "bw/I decided to do some more scouting and to see how the dwarven bastion was progressing from the last time I was in the area. I was also considering expanding the cave beside Watchtower 2 to allow them to create a road between their bastion and the main road. As I viewed the walls from atop the cliff i noticed their gate was broken, this was rather odd and then it got stranger. Large chunks of the wall started to be broken what seemed in an instant. This continued along the whole wall for around 20 seconds. I decided to get a closer look at what was happening. To my horror i saw 5 men cloaked hooded and with a bright trim, which are common traits of an undead. I shouted at them hoping they would flee but they paid no heed. So i decided to retreat to Winterfell as i was tired and not in fighting condition. After i rested i headed back towards the dwarven bastion. I then saw a chunk of the second watchtower vanish and a cloaked man in its place. \n In fear of an impending assault on Winterfell i retreated and put my armor on and carried only vital equipment. As i then Left Winterfell i saw our fishing lodge surrounded by the 5 or 6 hooded men. I made haste down the road and yelled Halt. Even before they said anything lightning fell from the sky followed by screams of \"Die Mortal!\" I was outnumbered and outmatched. I managed to slay one as he just drew his golden hoe, but the others kept their distance and eventually bested me. After I the monks tended to my wounds i headed straight back deciding to use the New Kings bridge we constructed. But to my dismay it was damaged. The southern entrance was a mess and for most of the rest of the bridge there was chunks missing. I tried to fix it up the best i could but i had no materials to do so after coming straight from the Cloud Temple.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scout Report of Wrath's Clutch", "VonEbs", "Wrath's Clutch was originally a Caravan Trading Post untill the Undead took it over. The area around the base has been devasted by constant battles on the scourge of the Undead. Undead and their followers have heavily fortified the castle. It's location is west from the King's Road near FrostyFury's shop. Note: Heavily defended sometimes. The walls are currently two tiered, providing no way in. Some tunnels do run under the base, but there is no evidence of a entry point into the clutch The trees around provide good places to shoot into the castle, but there is no cover around the base to speak of. Two attacks with 10+ Wardens and Allies have failed to disloge the undead and  they remain firmly entrenched in the clutch. \n -VonEbs", ""),
        StaticBook("Scout Work", "Psiop412", "Sgt. Farabeards and I recently scouted the Undead base, it seemed empty at first. untill I saw a undead walk into the base, i seen the gate was open so i followed seeing if i could find anything useful inside that could help . The Undead base seems to have a guard on the Wall at all times. Groobs and Fealnor moved up but was attacked by the guard. luckily they survived and retreated, im staying near and scouting the area. Im seeing 3 guards now it looks like 2 of them are working something. im gonna check it out when i see its safe. Whatever the two undead were working on its been covered up. The only way i see us able to submit an Attack on the undead base is underground. Otherwise we would have to wait till the base is inactive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scouting", "jdpowercool", "Scouting is a dangerous business. You never know when it will fail, and when you could die at that split second. However, when it does work! It always helps. It saves lives, and ocasionally can get you some respect in your town.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scouting", "G79", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Scouting Report", "Amethain", "I am near the raven stronghold and hace come upon a small outpost of the guild the \"walkers\" I will record the names of members of this guild and their rank in the guild  \nNightwalker Duncan  \nNightwalker Osham \nNightwalker Bofaim \nNightwalker Brandon \nDuskwalker Crowly \nDarkwalker Vain  \nDarkwalker Polcari  <note> I am uncertain, but I Believe this is the same Polcari that was once a Warden \n  \n {All messages on night walker guild board} \nDuncan Wanted for Betrayal of this Guild -Vain \n. \nRelgard and his men should not be attacking us soon, Vain and I dealt with him-Polcari [Daywalkers] A division of the walkers \nonly one member so far--  Daywalker Artemis <Note> Nothing more of interest found in Walkers encampment \n. \n. \nNear the front gate of the Walkers encampment there is a tall tower made of Birch Wood. I am going to  Investigate \nTower found to be owned by Relgard.  <note> Relgard was a part of the Malinor Rebelion which was  led by Caden. \nTower is called Skybreak tower and Relaxation room .  The tower is located on the property of the Skybreak Inn Owned by Relgard \nThere is an Odd cave entrance titled Spectre Cavern I am entering the cave now, hoping to find something of interest. \nA note found inside the cave reads \"Attn: Hostilites with the Walkers have ended.\"  The Spectres must be \"Relgard's Men\"  as before mentioned in the Walker Section. there is a Barracks in the cave. I am looking inside for information There is a sign pointing to Head Spectre Relgard's Quarters.  Relgard is the Spectre's Leader .  I found nothing of interest in Relgard's room. There are three rooms other than Relgard's; Driz, Duncan, and Sulla. <Note> Isn't Sulla one of our Warden Initiates?  Also I assume this is the Same Duncan as with the Walkers. {Nothing more of interest in Spectre Barracks or Base} \nI will once again infiltrate the Raven Fortress looking for information I found a Log of missions by Relgard, He and other Ravens broke into the base and broke an unknown person from our holding cells. I Copied the book for Refrence. \nHere ends the report, Signed Amethain Marethel, VGG  Date Ahad, 8th of The First Seed, 1336", ""),
