        StaticBook("Ser Adgar the Great's Note on Ser Delcius", "TheImpulseHQ", "Ser Delcius was my squire once, a strong and noble lad who only dreamed of helping the innocents, strange isnt it, that he turned away from this path. I believe that it was many different things that changed him and he is not all at fault for them as he was bullied by the other squires, until the fateful day when he faced Onhar the main bully in a duel to the death, and cut him down easily, we should have acted from seeing his anger and evil, but we thought that we could use it, how wrong were. Delcius was knighted soon after, and was a loyal, and good knight but he wasn't like the others, he rised through the ranks with ambition and greed which none of us saw except for the old Knight Commander, but before he could act, Delcius bribed the King into using Emergency act 2, the Knight Commander was executed and Delcius replaced him Times, became very dark. Delcius eventually purged all Knights who didn't agree with him, and soon we were a small order, weak and ruled by a Tyrannical Knight Commander. Eventually, we rose up, Ser Hortar led the resistance, and Delcius recruited Dark Knights and necromancers onto his side. Hortar charged into Delcius keep, andh  *there is blood spattered on this page, and nothing else", ""),
