        StaticBook("Shaman Skills", "Lexperiments", "I am training to be a shaman. These are the things I have learned. \n\n Different essences can summon different spirits when burned on a candle. Burnt cactus summons a non-fire elemental spirit similar to the area you are in. \n\n Once you learn a spirit's name, you can summon it anywhere. \n\n \n If you grow a tree with bonemeal at a spiritual place at midnight, you may be able to enchant a staff with a spirit. Mine is a Life spirit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shaman tome", "Ultion", "In the beginning there was Krug and the great Desert he was born upon. The desert was mighty, it had slain all lesser beast's of the world. But Krug tamed the desert, through wit and awn, securing food and water. But all was not well. Krug's son's would die to the desert without help, and Krug could not care for them all. So krug gifted his second son and said \" This is your boon and burden, you must guide your  brother's to safety, and so must your second son guide his brother, and so on in blood \" and so the shaman's were founded, to guide and watchover their less gifted kin", ""),
        StaticBook("Shaman, part 1", "Lexperiments", "I recently became an apprenticed shaman to an orc named Thyst. This is what I have learned so far. \n I have learned of two spirits, Donuur and Arya. Donuur likes no-weapon or armor fighting and is the spirit of loyalty and valour. Arya is the spirit of healing. Donuur likes cactus juice and sand, Arya likes milk and candles. \n On a torch or candle, you can burn different type of essences to summon different spirits. A cactus dye can summon lesser non-fire spirits. \n To plant, use bonemeal on, then cut down a tree at midnight can enchant a staff.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism", "eggerstimothyr", "Shamanism is powered by the main elements, earth, water, air, fire. Each element has around a billion spirits that have different personalities. However, the different elements ALSO have there own personalities. All shamans gain there power through spirits, and/or elements. \n A typical shaman is to find a partner spirits, conquer is by defeating it, or understanding it and befriending it. Befriending it is the most common, for the spirits are very smart. Not to mention, if the spirit dislikes you... It might not listen to you. \n Shamanism is a way to conntect to the elements, and life around you. Most shamans dont support technology. But who knows, maybe some do. Anyway, in order to connect to the spirits is a difficult process, and it takes a while if you don't have a teacher. Shamanism is also used for the healing of others, shamans usually don't use there power to fight, but only to help others. If it is needed, then they wont hold back. \n Connecting with your inner shaman... \n The traditional way is to meet the spirit first by lighting a piece of dye over a torch. The dye does not however burn. You shouldn't hold it over to long. This process may take a few tries, when doing this, you have to think of the element you are trying to connect to. Concentrate hard, and don't think of anything else. Also don't let people discourage you from being a shaman because of your race. \n After this process is done, you should befriend the spirit, or conquer it. Conquer it by beating it. I recommend befriending it. And remember, if you don't like that spirit, summon another one. It can't be that hard. \n If you have a teacher, ask him to help you make a staff to bind the spirit to. There is a certain way to do this. \n If you don't, I would recommend getting a teacher.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism", "Lexperiments", "I am on my first task right now. I have been apprenticed to Thyst, a shaman in an orc town. I came to learn shamanism, and I am. My first task is to collect gladiator blood and a mushroom. I have just collected the blood in a leather sack. Thyst has told me I could find mushrooms just south of the arena I have learned of two spirits so faar- Donuur and Arya. Donuur is the spirit of strength and valor. He respects non-weapon fights of loyalty. He appears in a battle where both sides have a reason to fight, and likes offerings of sands of the desert and juice of cactuses. \n \n Arya is the spirit of kindness and generousness. And healing. I believe she can heal many ailments. She likes offerings of fresh milk and candles. \n \n I have finished my first task. I met another student of Thyst's, Shaggo. Oh, Thyst is starting a ritual. He told us to look at the lone building floating outside his house. He told us to burn an incense on a candle. He says it will cause a spirit of water to come. Note : Cactus dye burned on a candle = water spirit. We went out to the hous at sea and burned the incense on a candle. Shaggo looks like he went insane. He was laughing insanely and eyes rolld back into his head. Water spirit posessed Shaggo. He says that water spirits are the water of time. He says the orcs are like a river, powerful in numbers. The spirit's name was Bongblud. It just dissapeared. \n \n It turns out, the incense I used earlier lures lesser non-fire nature spirits. We are summoning the earlier spirit now by using its name. Many different types of spirits. Ex. fire, water, earth, air, metal, thunder. Different insences burned = different spirits. MANY types of incenses. \n \n We were reqired to find a sapling and grow it ourselves. We are to cut if with a stone axe to summon a spirit. I grew my tree at midnight with bonemeal. I cut down the tree and gave my thngs to Thyst. He told us to wait otuside for a while. Shaggo angered Donuur by using the ritual tool as a weapon and actually DIED. The skies then spewed out with leaves and fire. Shaggo came back, and Thyst gave us our staves. Shaggo's element was fire. Mine was life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism and Druidism", "Lexperiments", "Shamanism and Druidism are closely related. From many sources, including shamans and druids, I've put together some facts and found out about the relations between them. \n \n The first Druid was an orc shaman. There was a major war going on between two nations, ravaging through nature and destroying everything. The god of Aegis came down to a shaman and spoke to them. He said to be one with nature, and to form a different \"branch\" of shamanism, the Druids.. \n \n The shaman gathered some followers then spread out, helping protect the land. Eventually, the more nature-like Elves became the druids, while Orcs stuck to shamanism. \n \n Obviously, the druids and shamans have many similarities. They both work to protect the world from harm to nature and the elements. They both origionated from the same thing. They both are heavily influenced with natural beings. Shamans and druids, without realizing it most of the time, do help each other in keeping the balance of the world. They are both nessecary for Aegis to be the way it is today. Thank you for reading this short book, and I hope you learned from it. \n \n | Written by Shaman Lex on Tolta, 31st of Suns Smile, 1318 |", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism and Druidism. Volume 1.", "Hothik", "Hello! If you have picked up this book, you are probably wondering what Shamanism and Druidism have to do w ith each other. The answer is; Quite alot. Shamanism uses spirits and elementals to stem their power. Like druids, their goal is to keep and protect nature. Druids however, use the force of nature itself as the source of their power. Druids do not communicate with elemental or nature spirits, untill they have picked a title. Then, they can freely communicate with that animal or elemental, though they might not be aware. There are four basic elementals for shamans to communicate with; Fire, Earth, Water and Air. Each of these elements has many lesser spirits that represent them, and one extremely powerful entity to direct the element as a whole. Shamans directly communicate with these spirits, and by calling them by their true names, harness their power temporarily. Druids, however, use Nature as a medium to communicate with these elements. This is why the effect of the two magics are, overall, much different. In order to master both Shamanism, and Druidism together, one must communicate with the spirits of Nature and the elemental spirits in a way that is simply natural, and can be done without thinking, as breathing. When advancing to an official druid, one picks, or is assigned an animal or element. Some Druids pick elements that are not of the basic four, such as lunar, solar, or Storm, While Storm is not considered a basic element, it is still one of the most powerful, and should not be underestimated. Nature itself is a spirit, though it is broken up into many other spirits, representing it. Most animals are spirits of nature that have chosen a particular embodiment. Strangely enough, animals are represented as are the elements. A collection of weaker spirits, and a much more poewrful enitity that controls them all. As Druids pick an animal, their subliminal connection to that animal's spirit increases, and so does their connection to any elemtal in particular that animal might also be representing. Shamans, at the end of their training, can select two elements to further study in, such as earth and storm. A true master of Shamanism is said to be able to master all elements, but this is impossible, as such a task would take tens of thousands of years. To master Druidism, one would have to master Nature itself, and for the same reason one cannot master shamanism perfectly, one cannot master Nature. Incredibly powerful druids, and incredibly powerful shamans can summon lightning from the sky. Though, this feat is rare. The next volume will be written soon. Deltaro? Ello Respiren! I have finished my first volume on druidism and shamanism.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism Pt.1", "Areontrade", "Tolta, 24th of The Deep Cold, 1338 - TO BE WORKED ON", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamera's_Resignation", "Bigalow40", "I, Shamera, resign from the Alras Guard. If you wish to contact me, you may send me a bird, or you will find me at the Narwari Trade camp. \n \n  May Aria Guide your path, \n Shamera", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamus' Journal", "hughlorin", "Journal 1 \n \n From a small home blossoms a town. Beginning with just Daniel, Nero, and myself, we planned to stay in a small settlement to sustain ourselves and save up until we could afford a house in Al' Kazarh. That plan,  however, has changes. In the city Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento met a perculiar  by the name of Telinir. Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento made acquaintances with him, and invited him to live with us. He is an interesting  man. Mysterious and somewhat suspicious, yet kind and fair. He invents, and studies many things. He has createed a device, called an ITCD, that allows you to talk to someone even when they are long distances away. He has other inventions as well, however he says those are classified. He seems to be a man of great brilliance. \n Not too long after, Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento met another two wanderes. He seems to be quite the social  butterfly. The name of the men are Max and Boure. Max seems a little slow at times, and often wanders aimlessly. I don't know Boure very well, so I can't say much for him. He seems to be absent from the  city when I am around. \n One more man, a hunter by the name of Olek. He ofthen roams into the forest in search of meats and other foods. He is rather quiet, but when he does speak it's worth hearing. I like him. He seems like a good hearted, hard working, and honest man. A great contribution to our growing city. \n So far, that is all there is to be said about our town, Talamh. I hope to see it flourish. \n Journal 2 \n \n It has been an eventful few days. Two more wanderers, by the names of Chanol and Ventris, have joined Talamh. Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento brought them in from Al' Kazarh. They seem to be happy individuals, excited and full of life. I haven't gotten to know them well as of yet, however my gut feeling tells me they will be a great addition to our town. I look forward to working with them. \n On another note, Telinir told me his hazard suit was destroyed by a Pigman in his lab. This is rather unfortunate, as when he died the blueprints for it were destroyed. The loss of his suit sets him back far in his research, as now he has to redesign the whole suit. I feel badly for him, the loss must be aggravating. I hope he can figure out how to reinvent it. \n Telinir also figured out why torches burn indefinitely. The magic fragrence acts as a fuel for them, and keeps them burning long after the coal  is used. He discovered a way to harness this power and use it to create a new device, called the MOT. The MOT uses magic frangrance, a torch, and snow as a coolant in order to find any object the user desires. It's a rather ingenious invention. He also mentioned a substance called redstone. I've heard of it before, but only in myths. Telinir says it can be used to harness magical fragrence for specific purposes. From what I know, it can be used to open and close doors, power minecart tracks, and power lights and switches. I know not how it works  exactly, though. Further more, it seems to be an extremely rare substance. Telinir wishes to find it, he says it will jump his research very far ahead of where he is at now. \n That's all I have to report for today. I hope to have more news as of tomorrow. \n \n Journal 3 \n \n Two more have settled in our city. One man by the name of Hiram, and another by the name of Father Ailean. I know neither of them, as Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento brought them in and settled them rather quickly. They do seem like good men, though. Both again, were wanderers. They seem to take a liking to us. \n The library/town hall building is finally finished. We've begun to fill the shelves with books, a few on the history of the town and it's citizens, some about lore and myths of Aeigis, and even some that Telinir donated about his findings on magical fragrence and inventions. It's a grand library. I cannot wait to see it filled with writings of fantasy and history. I hope that one day, this journal will be put in the library as a testament to the beginnings of Talamh. \n \n Journal 4 \n \n A terrible fate has befallen on the great city of Al' Kazarh. Screams of terror rose up from the unfortunate citizens. The Undead lead a vicious attack against the capital of Oren. Streets glistened with the crimson red of innocence. Mothers and and their children hid, praying the Undead wouldn't find them. Two great kings fell, although not both were so honourable. Fighting until his last breath, the king strove to protect his nation and his honour. The other king, however, turned out to be an Undead, turning on his loyal citizens. As quickly as they came the Undead left. The citizens of Talamh, frightened, gathered in the library. Amongst them was Telinir, Daniel, Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento, Jolot, Thondi, and myself huddled in the dark, careful not to raise our voices above a which he gladly accepted. We stayed and talked for awhile.sper. The great city of Al' Kazarh had been ravaged and destroyed by the Undead; what was to happen to us? We are nothing but a small town. Arguing and bickering filled the air. Soon enough, Daniel spoke up. He gave one of the greatest speeches I have ever heard. \n \"Men, please listen. Alone, we are powerless against the Undead. But together, as one, we will fight. Not just as Humans, but along side the Dwarves, Elves, and Orcs. Only then can we overcome the Undead. All races are equal under Mother Nature; Elves, Orcs, Humans, and Dwarves alike. We must ban together and unite as one. Only then can we triumph over evil.\" \n The Light of Aeigis truly spoke through Daniel. Daniel's plea of unity and togetherness raised a new spirit, a new goal. For if we are together, we are unstoppable. Nothing shall get in our way. Not Ibelis himself. \n Later, an aliance was formed, dubbed \"The Whisper Order\". This order is a collection of brave volunteers who are willing to fight the Undead, even at the cost of their lives. Daniel, Jolot, Nero, and myself  traveled to their headquarters and signed up as soon as we could. Anything to protect Aeigis. It seems many other people have signed up as well. It's good to see such patriotism among the people after such an attack. It seems as though the strike of the Undead has not split us apart, but instead created a unity amongst all citizens of Aeigis. Although what happened today in Al' Kazarh was a horrible tragedy, I fully believe that we will come back even stronger than before. The Undead better look out. \n The events of these last few hours make me think; what if this were to happen to Talamh? All the people I've come to know and share bonds with and all the hard work and effort we've put into the city would be worth nothing. Just the thought of losing them brings sadness over me. Hopefully, Talamh will never suffer that fate. I can only pray so. \n \n Journal 5 \n \n Al' Kazarh was again attacked by the Undead. I had the opportunity to witness the attacks first hand. The main street was a mess of zombies, skeletons, and pigmen along with the massive crowd of knights fighting them. I pulled out my sword and joined the fight, swinging at monsters left and right. But a lucky arrow hit my hand, causing me to loose my sword. I quickly ran to find another but I could not find a spare. I fought with my fists, I wanted to do anything to protect this city from the Undead. Towering over everything was a giant. I had only heard of them in myths and legends until now. The beast was huge, towering at least 4 stories tall. Knights surrounded the wretched thing, swinging at it with all their might. It was one of the most awe inspiring sights I had ever seen. \n Mobs stopped coming, the bloodshed had ceased. In the middle of the town square stood a blackened portal. No mortal tools could destroy it, and the people were in a panic. There, I ran into Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento, Telinir, and Jolot. We found a quiet space outside and discussed a plan Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento devised. Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento suggested that we sneek into the North and attack the Undead which he gladly accepted. We stayed and talked for awhile.le they were distracted. It was risky, but we decided to do it. \n We traveled back to Talamh, where we gathered supplies to make the journey, however I fell ill and couldn't make the journey. I saw them off and waited for them to return. Seeing a figure walking through the forest back to our town, I lept out of bed and went to meet it. It was Telinir, and he was the only one. The other two had gotten lost and injured. He had made it to the Nether, and BACK. He appeared exausted and frightened. He did not speak much. I left him alone for awhich he gladly accepted. We stayed and talked for awhile.le before he came and talked to me. \n We heard thunder in the distance. It seemed to be coming from the direction of the queens house. Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a governmento, Jolot, Talam, Chanol, and myself decided to go and make sure she was safe. When we came up on the island, we ran into Dawn Perea and Hempshine. We asked them if everything was alright, and if they needed help. Dawn said she was alright. However, right after that lightning struck. The whole island shook. Fearing for our lives, we stayed the night with the Queen. Hempshine was not doing okay. He seemed psychotic, and was running around throwing objects around and screaming. The Queen had been taking care of him. The poor man... We made sure the Queen was safe and well, and we went back to Talamh in the morning. \n \n Journal 6 \n \n A meeting in the library was called between Jolot, Telinir, Daniel, Nero, and myself to discuss the creation of a government for Talamh. I'm going to spare the details, as it was a long and uneventful meeting, but eventually we decided on making Nero, Daniel, and myself the Lords. The three part government should work very well. It has a good balance. \n Today a man by the name of Reanon wandered through the city in search of string. It was late at night, and only me and Daniel were out. I told the man I had some, and went and got it for him. Daniel had to go to sleep, as he had had an exausting day. The night was dark and dangerous, so I offered the man to stay in my house for the night, which he gladly accepted. We stayed and talked for awhile. He was a young adventurer set on seeing the world. I remember when I had dreams of seeing the world- I still do. I'm still young at only 18 years old, I still have time. Anyways, Reanon's excitement made me smile. I knew he was going to enjoy his adventures. I hope he comes back and tells me of them some day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shank", "MythMaster26", "*high fives shank t", ""),
        StaticBook("Shattered memories", "Ratemenatorz59", "I stand in Al'khazar, the cake party begins. A strange hooded man I see. Lightning strikes down on me, my hands fill in blood. I see myself falling.. As if I am a ragdoll. My memory wiped, I forget all things. I cry in agony as blood flows out of my body. There I lay, half dead. Waiting for someone to help me....", ""),
        StaticBook("she has the ok by jacksonsp1170 or Sgt.jackslayer to stay", "jacksonsp1170", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheffield needs to step off the Throne!", "erlend0501", "King Edmund Sheffield is a lazy king. He only cares about himself, and his nearest. Lately he has been giving taxes to shops and merchants. He also removed the salary for the guards, which means That the guards does not do their jobs, and don't take it seriously, leaving Al'Khazar defenceless! But what does that matter when he allows the undead walk in the streets freely? This madness must end! For the sake of Oren, and for the whole of Aegis! Fear not, my friends, A coup is the way to Salvation! We must bring Edmund to his knees, and take the throne by power! A new king will lead us to glory! That is yet to be decided. Maybe you are the new King of Oren? ~Jordan Stilwell of the Guardians.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheriff Tengen, Sheriff of Corvus_Animas", "friar7", "this is an official badge, Guard captains signature: Cpt. Mork Yohom", ""),
        StaticBook("Shhh", "Desires", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Shoi", "runawayguy", "This poem is written for the one I love, Shoi. This poem contains a part of myself. My mind..My heart..My soul. This Poem was written because I've had the subject pondering my mind and this is the only way I think I could share my feelings. I have not been able to put my thoughts into words, until now. I am Zephyr, The King of the Gauntlet Shoi, as the sun sets revealing the marvelous moonlight, to burst out of hiding from behind the shining orb, I think about your smile. Your smile...Is infectious. I can not help but smile every time I see you walking in Laurelin. The time we spend together feels eternal, and I wish that that feeling would never end. Watching you leave, is such sweet sorrow. As I know I will see you the next day. Everyone has something special that stands out to others, Just as the orcs have their green skin, or the elves have pointy ears, You Shoi, have your beauty and intellect. I would give up anything to spend another day with you, to hold you in my arms, and to love you to the end of time. I hope and I beg that you aren't still unhappy with me after our last conversation. I was just trying to proect you... I overreacted and I apologize. I will still protect you, no matter what the consequence. I love you Shoi. And I felt you should know what has been on my mind. -Zephyr", ""),
        StaticBook("Shop instructions", "ariczzz1892", "\n/shop info <id> \nreturns information about that specific shop \n \n/shop browse <buy|sell> \nShows a list of items currently in the shop \n/buy [item name] <amount> \nPurchases a specified item from a shop \n/sell <item name> <amount> \nWith an item name defined, a specific item is sold to the shop", ""),
        StaticBook("Shop Instructions!", "RHcrow", "Goron, You can automatically sell items at each store. Food in the Tavern and Other stuff in the magic shop\n to sell an item its /shop sell <item name> # \n I am buying Ink Sacs, Bones and Bonemeal, Lapis Lazuili, Glowstone dust hello? hello?> oi mate oi mate", ""),
        StaticBook("Shop manual", "ariczzz1892", "\nBUYING: \ntype /buy item name amount \nSELLING \ntype /sell item name amount \nLIST OF ITEMS BOUGHT/SOLD \ntype /shop browse buy:sell", ""),
        StaticBook("Shopping List", "RHcrow", "Nethrrack -3 \n Soulsand -50 \n Glowstone Dust -25", ""),
        StaticBook("Shopping List", "Baronvo", "Always keep on stock: \n \n 5 pork - cooked or raw \n 10 bread \n 5 fish - cooked or raw - ( if possible )) \n 20 mushroom soup", ""),
        StaticBook("Shops", "Fluffymeister", "TukTuks little shop. Location: Close to the White Ravens keep, go out of the keep and turn left. Pass the Wisp's Late Night Tavern, and it's on your left.  Excellent quality products at a decent price. Price example (at time of writing) Iron Sword: 75Minas Bread: 5 Minas. Professional owner.    \nJoma, 13t of Snows Maiden, 1327", ""),
        StaticBook("Shrooms", "123devmo321", "Shrooms are magical and oh so grand. Shrooms alter your brain so you can't recognize your own hand. Shrooms are so wonderful and taste so good. They taste like butter, or at least should. I wish I had a tasty orange. So my hands would be sticky so I can touch a door hinge. God damn, I really need to poop. If I hold it in any longer, I'll do a loop. These shroom messed me up so bad. I loved every moment of shrooming that I had.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shuberry's Biological Guide to Fungi.", "shoeberrypie", "Mushrooms\n In order to make a proper Elven meal, enjoyed by many races,\n one must aquire stew.  Mushroom stew. Mushrooms are a rare substance to find in the wilds of Aegis,\n  but when one gathers both toadstools (though poisonous, the brown mushroom rids\n  the stew of any poison, thus making it edible. Greetings *does a quick nod of the head \n (pen mistakes are hard to remove) \n The first thing one must do upon gathering a sample of each mushroom\n is to make a patch for each type of mushroom in a darkly lit area,\n which means that undead can spawn. Make the cieling no higher\n than 2 meters (2 blocks) above the ground, preventing skeletons\n from ever hitting you with their projectiles. It would be \n adviseable for you to make patches as small as comfortably\n possible, if you are new to Biology.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shuberry's Records", "shoeberrypie", "Name: Shuberry, Race: High Elf, Age: 93, Position: Apothecary, Herbalist", ""),
        StaticBook("Shun's Diary (Vol. 3)", "Shuness", "Day Three? \n Time goes by slow now.. no one knows what is happening with undead. It has been quiet though.. perhaps this all blew over. \n Day Four \n The undead are in force now, screams were heard from the north. They have taken a dwarven town, and burned it to the ground. Kayle is now following under the Acended, who I do not trust.. I tried to show him the errors of his ways, but he would not listen. War has broken out between the dwarves and Humans. I do not know who to support in this.. my race, or my friends.. \n Day Five \n Nothing is happening.. aside from a small fight in Al Kahazard. Kal'urguan. Right before gates, a path. right. at end, is a manor. Help for group there.. Say that Darfin sent me, and I wish to fight alongside the vault. \n Day 7 \n Those who are undead find shelter. The Bell has arrived. Answer the Toll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siege of Antioc", "Fluffy5", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Siege of Antioch", "Fluffy5", "We arrived at Orontes River outside Antioch. The three major leader leading the crusades were discussing about what to do next Raymond wanted to make a direct assault, While Godfrey and Bohemund preferred to set siege to the city. Afer the first day, We encircled the city, The city's Byzanite fortifications were strong enouh to resist a direct attack, Although Yaghi-Siyan may not had enough men to adequately defend the city, A messenger told us that he was relieved and emboldened when we didn't attack immediately. Bohemund encamped on the northeast cornor of the city at the gate of St. Paul, Raymund set his camp further to the west at the Gate of Dog. And Godfrey placed his troops at the Gate of the Duke, Also further to the west Where a bridge of boats was built across the Orontes to the village of Talenki. To the souh was the tower of the Two Sister and at the northwest cornor of the Gate of St. Gergo Which was not blocked by our fellow Crusaders, And were used throughout the siege to supply Yaghi-Siyan with food. On the southern and eastern side of the city was \"Hilly\" area known as Mt. Silpius, Where the Citadel and the Iron Gate were located. \n  \n The First Siege \n In mid-November Bohemund's nephew Tancred had arrived with reinforcements, And a Genoese fleet had sailed into the port at St. Symeon, Bringing extra food and supplies. At the end of the month Bohemund and Robert of Flanders took about 20.000 men and went foraging f or to the south, But while they were gone, Yaghi-Siyan made a sortie out of the Gate of St. Ge orge on december 29 and attacked Raymond's encampment across the river at Talenki Raymond was able to turn him back but he was not able to capture the city itself. Meanwhile Bohemund and Robert were attacked by an army under Duqaq of Damascus Which had marched from the north to come to Antioch's aid. Although the crusaders were victorious here as well, They were forced to retreat to Antioch with little food. The mond ended inauspiciously for both sides: There was an Earthquake on December 30 And the following weeks saw such unseasonably bad rain and cold weather that Duqaq had to return home without further engaging the crusaders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried On: Obsidian", "Religious_Pie", "It is an interesting material, the fact that a rock can be stronger than diamond. Stronger than diamond, it is known to be possibly only mined by diamond! But, it has a hidden power, bursting from it's seems, lies a deep enrichment of Netherick Energy, so much that is the only known way to travel to the nether. But, it is because of this material, that death and corruption has reached this fare lands. We have harboured the power to create such an ore, by stirring tow of teh elements into a being of one, how 2 flowing materials, form teh hardest known to Mortals I warn all who read this, I have been to the nether, but it is not a friendly sight and can wreak havoc on a man's soul, so if you are plannig on using this material use it for it's material qualities, not it's divine powers, this block can tear worlds asunde and should never be trifled with, thus, if possible leave it be, it is not for our hands . . .", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried's Memoir's Part 1", "Religious_Pie", "The Undead, they attack without warning, they attack as if we have no enemy. they take this land as if it is rightfully theirs, but...what makes it ours? who's to say that undead have greater causes for this land? call me a heretic if you wish, but I do not worship false gods, I have stared into OverLord Tyrions eye's, no man remains, only a soul wrapped in flesh slowly decaying his last remains, he is like them all, men with week minds... many a man has tried to succumb the agonising pain that is the process of becoming a follower of Iblee's I shall keep writing these, for these lands are becoming worse everday. Corrution is spreading like wildfire, and men are being converted as easily as children, we live in dire times, a new land of peace awaits us, but we shall not leave this land without a fight...", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried's Memoir's Part 2", "Religious_Pie", "I write this, as thunder rumbles and lightning strike the bare ground. near the Warden's fort, in proximity to the crumbling city of Kramoroe, cobble walls, with obsidian lining, lies forth, under the rich black sky, for no stars hang tonight , only those who are loyal, and who are corrupt, I continue here, around 40 mortals and 4 ascended, including Freya, fight with us, there is talk of a Nether Portal Below and I plan on gaining samples, the battle is heating up, beasts from the depths of man's worst dreams clamber onto the rooves of encampments and storage rooms while firing vollies of unholy arrows and swinging rotten fists and corrupt gold swords around as if they were toys. There is a dark essence here, under the darkrock flooring, miles of hidden bunkers slumber, waiting to be awakened, for this is where the corruption is at it' strongest . Ascended shine up the tunnel's like beacons of pure hope, that we are not fighting this war alone, the maddness is breaching on insanity, a man wanders the fort selling bread as if it were a calm day at Kal'rog market! This is the first time I've been in a war, the stench of bodies fills my nose and mouth with bile, I hear people shouting they've found the Portal, it does not seem fit, it wouldn't be so high up, I expected it to be as far as tipping on the edge of the 'Void' As I make my way down however, it does seem fit, blood stains lies on the walls from previous sacrifices, nd inscripted ruins of a forgotten language lies vacant on the ground, I have found all manner of hell-stones, such as 'Netherack' and 'Glowstone' and even a small clutch fo Soul Sand. A piston contraption whirres and the doors to the crypt swig open, breakig apart as they do nd there it lies...a portal that could shake the world, a manifestation of pure hell cries can be heard through it, as pieces of stone and weaponry is sucked in and warped to a dimension that sucks the life out of a mortal man. Runic messages lie on it like a mad man has been inscribing them with accurate care for years, but these were not made , they were spawned. I shall continue the series, and hope to travel to the floating city, or stay alert for the next battle in Aegis, for it shall not be long before the Undead strike again. Signed: Siegfried Hathorn, Undead Reseacher OSRT", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried's Memoir's Part 3", "Religious_Pie", "The poor king Sheffield has passed, just days after I am writing this. I travelled into the nether, I saw what no man should see, I have joined a make shift guard for oren, to get a front-line view on what is happening to our kingdom for it is a dire timne indeed. I have clad myself in iron armour, to keep a low-profile, no one see's my face and no one checks who I am. My dearest friend Jonathan has also joined this guard as a recruiter. Tension is growing in Al'khazar, conspiracies are spreading like diseases, a pandemic of lies, truth and rebellion. I keep hearing new stories of who our ruler is, and I have not bothered to find who the real monarch is, but it is most likely fare dawn, she was the top candidate of course. 1 day on however, arguments have broken out in the square of Al'khazar about who the actual king could be. . . or queen. It seems uneccesary to be having all this commotion, I can understand it's important, but shouldn't there be a succesion?The whole court cannot have died!? I am in the Guard tower, in the main gate, in Al'khazar. There is conspiracy over whether the Oren_Guard are fit to protect the citizens and whether they should be in charge of all the rebellions while undead run rampant through teh gutters while the undead torturer stands on the tomb of Heron as if it were a street path. The men and women around look astonished, as pure blaspheme stand on stone defieing the Great man that was Horen, I hear lightning striking around the city! Thunder rumbling like a beast of legend, for Hell has coem to al'khazar, inone man But by the looks of it...hell shall arrive by the dozens... I shall be there when the battle comes, I shall be there when Al'khazar is under siege. I shall be there, when the four races unite as one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried's Memoir's Part 4: Battle For Al'khazar", "Religious_Pie", "The shining jewel of Oren, a town striving in these lands. 'Twas a cold night, the winds from the north escaped and swept across Al'khazar like a wave of the coldest water. It was this night, that Iblee's forces struck the centre, and obliterated teh city. Men fell, buildings fell, and so did the moral of Hundreds of Mortals. Giants spawned out of the immaterial realm, and cursed the city with Netheric energy. Unholy beasts of unimaginable horror struck the city with flaming pieces of flesh and bone. The ghasts dominated the sky, smoke on acrid bile either rose or fell to the ground.# Pigmen, zombie's and skeletons littered the ground, as if waiting to suckle their mom. Light began to dawn, and hope slwoly grew throught the crowd, until the sun turned to the moon, and night fell again, 24 hours, of solid darkness. as more and more undead and more and more cultists drove inthrough teh gates. we all los hope in teh ascended, their supposed portal, that was forged to protect us, lay in ruins, but at one point, it grew again, but as obsidian and purple matter. A shining light shone from it's core, and netheric energy irradiated rfom within it. A booming voice spoke from within it, but we all knew what the voice was...Iblee's The master of the Undead, the force of pure Death, a sound as strong as plague. Ascended, now flocking to the city, tried to close the portal, but did not. I stood in the shadows, behind heron's tomb, as ranks of warriors poured in. The portal was broken many times, but each time, it regenerated into a stronger form. Then, another voice boomed, this tme of Overlord Tyrion, his golden robes, shining in the moonlight, inscripted with runes and etches of long-lost languages. his face was concealed by his hood, and three other mysterious men joined his side, one infront, one to his right, and one to the left. Silence fell, and the four chanted word after word of incantations. Those who saw watched in fear, ascended knew this was not going to end soon. The lightning struck like splinter cannon's on the blood covered floor. an achrid goo blotched the ground, black as night, but reflecting light like the moon itslef. The portal expanded, and ignited, glowstone, netherrack and obsidian spewed forth. and from there, lava corrupted the ground. those who stood above it fell into it's maw. Men's flesh fell from their bones, as their eyes tunred to puss. But not puss that our body creates, puss, thatemitted a purple flare. Pieces of roof tiles fell from above, so I clambered to get und-\\_ I awoke in the morning, inside Dawn's bakery, pieces of glass hung from their hinges. I must have been hit by some debris, however, the lands were not scarred physically, but through thought, no one was assured, new thoughts of outbreak ran through the streets as if they were school girls hissing a new song. This shall be the last of this series, for in the next fights, I shall be called to arms, my scrolls and tomes taken from me, for it shall be a time of only war.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siegfried's Scrap Journal", "Religious_Pie", "I am writing this whiel watching lightning strike the bare landscape, near the warden's fort the crumbling lands of what is left of kramoroe lies around me, in broken dreams. again, I write this while fightning with a horde, I hear talk of giants being summoned in the walls, death embedded into titans of colossal power, we cannot win, but we shall hold them back! The battle seems to be breaching the verges of insanity, there's a man sellign his wares as if it was a calm day at Kal'rog market. There is also talk of a portal, I shall try to gain samples. I am in the fort, Undead, ascended and mortals, fightning for their gods. Did anybody see the nether portal? a phrase shouted by many at the ned of teh battle, Is survived, buth portal sucked a part out of me, it was a dark sensation, a feeling as though, there was no good..only power. I hope to get this information around, the undead are growing citizens, beware. ((lol, I write a book all the way through that battle, still killed 2 blokes C:)) NEW CHAPTER:", ""),
        StaticBook("Sig test", "ljcrzynfree19", "Lukas confirms this iron donation \n burn this immediatly after reciept", ""),
        StaticBook("Sigmar's Slave Diary", "bookworm954", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Signs", "Archmage_Cataris", "\"Szor Axai reborn\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Silk's Diary", "Apanaczka", "Firt Entry Kingdom of Oren Haven't had any oppertunity to trade very much. Haven't done much. I think I'll venture to the wild oon, with my friend Grim. Hope I'll urvive long enough to get on a dventure with loot....    \n Orc tournament. \n \n Orc tournament. I need ome training. Didn't go o well. Korgath defeated me. Ill get him!  \n Traveling to Laurelin. I am going to try to join a merchant guild to begin my tru life. Trading i my life. I will get to the point when I will be leading the trading. In whole   . Aegis. \n Wandered to The Land of The Dwarves. A bunch of pathetic dwarves tried to kill me! Got away as you see anyway, reader. I might go back. But not for a time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillion Luthais's Journal", "Ohaythar121", "My name is Sillion Luthais. This, is my story. I was born, 19 years ago, as all are. My family found me, and took me to their camp, far off into wilds. I was raised amongst the trees, and life was as abundant as air. The trees stood tall, leaves shining a dark green, hosting countless forms of insects and rodents. The animals all wandered about soaking up the beauty of the landscape, and the untainted air swirled about them, showering them in the beauties of nature itself. My family was the Luthais clan, a group of humans and dwarves, a few elves lived amongst us as well, teaching a few the ways of the druid. The most unique part of our clan, was we had our own dialect, a escewed form of English, only spoken by us. My accent is still thick, but it makes for a very useful code language, as maybe 26 in the whole world speak it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillion Luthais: Druid Dedicant", "Ohaythar121", "Writer, Dedicant, and brewer, Sillion Luthais. Take this", ""),
        StaticBook("Silvan's Book of Knowledge", "Deathlord555", "I must become Elemental to fight back the Undead once and for all. I am to learn all forms of magic and today I start at life magicks and it's power.", ""),
        StaticBook("Silverside Battle-Games", "TheMineyMan99", "Test test alright, so what this is is a battle, hosted by none other than me and my uncle, Aalto. \n The prize would be collaborative. For each person who pays 400 minas for entry in the games, adds 250 minas to the grand prize. \n The winner is decided by a ladder plot. Contestants must defeat, player after player, climbing up the ladder. Eventually the battles would get more intense, throwing in different factors into the arena. \n Such as, fighting staff, who are out to kick your ass. Traps, obstacles, pitfalls, each round growing more and more intense.", ""),
        StaticBook("Silverside War-Games", "TheMineyMan99", "Aalto /Aisos: Founders of the SWG's. \n James/Bryce: Advertisers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Simon's Journal", "HeelioBagoon", "((Background info\n Eldarwood is a non exsistant place used to explain where simon came from)) Today I arived in Oren from Eldarwood. The boat was extremely rickity and I began to feal sick. Hoping to cure the sea sickness I stumbled into a bakery. I walked up to the counter and found myself infront of a verry hairy man that goes by the name of Hempshine. I ordered a coffee figuring that would settle my stomach. After a feiw days in oren I  noticed people... wel not people hooded figures. I also noticed people with great ora, ora of great holiness. After askin' around I found out theese people are called Ascended and Undead. A feiw more days have passed and i noticed theese people have abilities. The undead use them for great evile. And the ascended the opposite. I wondered why none of the other races seemed to have magic. After a while I found another halfling like me. He eventualy showed me to Dunwood. let me out! leave ((last to words where not writen on purpose)) ((im halfling we are rude to tall people)) ((once again not on purpose )) It hass been a while since i have writen in my journal. Been bussy building a house. I live in between Dunwood and greenshire. I found a golden staffin the mud while diggin'. I have tried to summon the magic from the staff as I saw the ascended do but I can not.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sionor Neverwinter", "CheeseBallz01", "i have done so Elf 80 collector/builder ok i have done so i have completed this task shall i return the book?", ""),
        StaticBook("Sir Salvador of Konigs Journal", "dercsalvo", "1st Entry, Ahad, 15th of The Amber Cold, 1324 near  dusk\n It has been many days since we first began work on the Order's new premises . Kolland and Ernair come and go, often leaving me to myself.  I have completed my own home, just east of the Citadel and have begun my work with my small farms. They inform me that I shall be the Citadel Keeper . I do not know what this yet entails, but I believe I will spend many of my days hard at work studying and keeping records. \n  We are worried for Aegis, what with the death of the King and Queen in Oren . Since all three of us are humans, we are greatly disturbed by this news . We hope that our Order of Knights will be a worthy adversary against this great evil . Eranir continues work on the Citadel. I must do my part and tend to my gardens. \n Itnan, 16th of The Amber Cold, 1324 mid-day \n My home is overrun with undead. This scourge must perish. Sir Kolland appeared at just the right moment to fend off these beasts . We live to fight another day. \n Joma, 20th of The Amber Cold, 1324 mid-day \n It was decided today that our order shall be officially known as The Order of the Knights Fortis. Our Citadel shall hence forth be known as Triberitus. This is a momentus day for our order. We have something to hold on to. \n Ahad, 22nd of The Amber Cold, 1324 Dawn \n Turmoil has struck. While I am fine with my role as keeper, Kolland and Eranir seem distraught over who should lead our Order. I listen carefully to their conversation as I continue to work on the expanded Sugar Cane fields. \n Sabet, 21st of The Second Seed, 1325 \n Utter turmoil has arisen amongst us. I have been away and unable to write. The Order has failed. While we squabbled over titles, Eranir broke from the group . He hates Kolland and I. Kolland had joined the Order of Teutonic Knights when we first broke apart. I know not of his whereabouts now, nor Eranir's. I am alone. A man named Sporadic, some call him, has contacted me. He has a job for me within his group of historians. I believe I can continue my studies there . I meet with him soon. We will see. It may be many days before I write again. I am sorry father. Perhaps your training was not enough. I now venture.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sir Wyvernos' Recruit List", "Sir_Wyvernos", "Rank: Name: \n Grunt Verilius_Aurilane(Saber952) \n Soldier Aislin(SnowmanE88) \n Soldier Verigan(Spartan216) \n Grunt Callum(iflarg) \n Grunt Katie_Wolfmane(KatzieCutzie) . Aislin has shown the skill and knowledge to become a great warrior for Alras.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sir_Ior_Sullkyn's Journal", "fiendin", "Kamees, 19th of The Amber Cold, 1334 \n I ve just proposed to the most beautiful dark elf named, Keziah. The best part is tt she said, \"Yes!\" and we're going to get married. I ve yet to talk to the priests about arranging a wedding but surely they will be willing to fit us in for a wedding. I mean it's rude for them not to. I am so excited I can barely wait much longer. The diamond ring I gave her is genuine and so is the Ender Pearl necklace. Both of them I made myself. Wt she doesn't know is tt I cut my own arm and put a small drop of my blood into the necklace to symbolize tt I'm always with her. I will now be going out to talk to others and show off tt I'm married! \n Itnan, 16th of The Second Seed, 1335 \n I am smed... I ve d to resort to using my own wife for blood. She was okay with it but it still didn't seem right. I mean I bit my own wife just so I could obtain blood... wt s become of me. I know, I know, she was okay with it but tt still doesn't make it right... No one should  have to go through that. On the bright side she doesn't hate me and she loves me for who I am and not what I am.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siritus Accuentes Dal Aegisia Reanimatus", "aaaa1188", "Aen cenimatus priore dal reanimatus struden dea suerfat dal Aegisia, soelimonten ien chreatrus mortalis leiven ien wueorde. Ien wueorde suervian dal peaqcat aen haermoquen, uantiel ein miendus dal curroptanes bein pouvre. Todanus dal raqienes dal Aegisia seaken dominatus dal ien otranos, aen ein atempta ien gadre maer pouvre, necromancia aruesen. Recirente, huevre, dal chreatures dal necromancias revolizen aen doeminaten Aegisia aes uin indiquien.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siritus Accuentes Dal Aegisia Reanimatus", "ogedi", "*the pages are torn and faded but you can tell they once held elaborate designs* Aen cenimatus dal reanimatus struden dea suerfat dal Aegisia, soeunten chreatren liaven inhiabet dal laendren. Ien wouerden theiven dal Pequet aen Harmoquen, priore puedre curroptine dal miendus dea chreatrenas dal Aegisia. Necromancia begien dominatrus al otanes raquines dal ein laindren aen reanimatus beorn aet. Recimntem, ien reanimatus revioluzen. Reanimatus infialimen Aegisia, aen otranos cheaturenas assimalutes. Hueveren, sieven muertales gaithren abilitanos aen banishina reanimatus al netherium. Altuert reanimatus nue luenren strueden, unei meas ien ceirtan; Ien reanimatus shiall retrendas evientuallen, aen ien huel dal Aegisia shiall inflimaen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siritus Acuntenes Dal Aegis Reanimatus", "aaaa1188", "*the pages are torn and faded, but you can tell that they once held beautiful decorative designs* \nAen cenimatus priore dal reanimatus woeld struden dea suerfat dal Aegisia, aquila solenatmen craetahres simplicaten ecsiten. Peacquent adem haermequon pevatet dal comlepten dal Aegisia, todana wehs prefriten utiln peowdren domiantus sius meindus. Alat ein pointanus, todana dal raquienus dal Aegisia seikan maes peowdren dal sel ortoras, aen manei revolveden al necromianca taeh acievan sel dominatarunus. Sues necromianca quin obtiniane ien miende dal indetpedentia, houetro, aen soen dal complepten dal Aegisia dal inflaminen. Manea yeatimes paseina priore ien necrogriampi dal llouesien al Aegisia, aen dal Reanimatus dal baenistish al ien Netherium. Nadaiem unastehy remainiatus huenein remiembre ien kiey, perios solium unastehy dal sierten: Ien Reanimatus shiallem ruetrena einvuitenla.", ""),
        StaticBook("Six days", "Lastchance2099", "I am in hell. I lay against a burning floor. I cannot stand for long, as my feet are seared. I am a prisoner here. It feels as if I've been here for eternity, but It is probably far less I was given this tattered paper to write orders for my friends, But instead I attempted to make out a deal. I will not make it out of this fortress alive. Screams of ancient prisoners will confrim that Wrath dragged me out of my cell today. I was beaten, and dragged into a glass hallway. Laughing Wrath stood behind the glass and repeatedly pulled a lever releasing water into the room. I could not breathe. I could hardly move. \n I awakened back in the glass hallway. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. Again. I don't remember much else, except for Wraths laughing. He smile when I passed out and he was smiling when I woke up. \n (writing is scrambled, and shaky.) I WaS sEVerly bEAtEn tOdaY. NOX burnt aN eDGe of ThIS boOK to hUmILIatE mE. \n A prisoner filled the cell next to mine. It is an elf, Nailena. \n I have met her in my travels before. She looks unharmed which is promising. But she is confused. She doesn't understand the situation...", ""),
        StaticBook("Skeleton, Preliminary Notes", "Distuth", "There is a marking on a skeletons middle left rib. It has appeared on all skeletons observed thusfar", ""),
        StaticBook("Skeletons And Spiders: Fighting The Predators Of Aegis", "Lagomorphia", "When possible, you should travel by day. However, if you are somehow forced to travel at night or if you are actively seeking monsters, this guide should help you survive your encounters. \n \n \n #1: Weapons And Armor \n Always make sure you are armed and armored before attempting to take on monsters. Even simple leather can mean the difference between a terrible death and survival. However, if your armor is damaged enough, you should remove it and keep it to repair. It will not protect you in its ruined state, and it is far cheaper to fix it than to buy or make a new set. Place your armor on a crafting table with two pieces of the material it is made of (either leather, gold, iron or diamond, chainmail cannot be repaired) and you should be able to fix it. Chestplates require three pieces of material due to their larger size and greater protection. \n When choosing armor, the chestplate is the most important part. It can take the most damage and provides the greatest protection. It is usually wise to have the best chestplate you can afford. \n Take your armor off when you are safely inside a city. Falling damage will damage your armor, which is a waste of your armor's limited damage capacity.. \n You should carry both a bow and a sword if possible, and the sword should be iron or diamond. While a wooden or stone sword are better than fists, you should still avoid combat if you do not have sufficiently powerful weapons. \n \n \n \n \n #2: Injuries \n You will be injured when fighting monsters. Even if you fight with a bow, it is unlikely you will emerge from repeated combat unscathed. You should always carry food with you to heal after combat, and if your health is even slightly low you should avoid combat altogether. If your health drops low, abandon the fight and run. Find a building with a door and barricade yourself inside. Do not open the door again until daylight, even if you heal back to full health. \n Sleep instead of eating when you can. Sleep is free, food is not. \n  #3: Zombies \n The zombie is the most basic enemy you will fight. They move slowly but their attacks are powerful. Fight zombies from a distance. Attack them with a bow, aiming each shot carefully. Fall back slowly. The arrows should push the zombie back, but you may still need to give ground to stop the zombie from closing to melee range. If a zombie closes to melee range, draw your sword and slay it quickly. If you are on low health, disengage from combat and flee from the zombie. It is slow and should not catch up, which should give you time to heal. \n #4: Skeletons \n Skeletal archers are dangerous foes. They should not be attacked directly. One way to deal with them is to fight them with a bow from a range and try to dodge their arrows, but the most effective way is to draw your sword and circle them. Once you are close enough, you will be able to circle the skeleton faster than it can turn, so you can stay at its back, circling and striking until it falls. If on low health and fleeing a skeleton, take the most erratic path you can, which will make it hard for the skeleton to hit you. \n \n #5: Spiders \n Spiders are arguably more dangerous than even zombies and skeletons. They can be fought in a similar way to zombies, but you must fire faster to keep them at bay, and if they close in, you will not be able to outrun them. Slay them with your sword if possible, but find shelter if you can. \n \n \n \n \n \n #6: Zombie Pigmen \n When fighting a zombie pigman, DO NOT engage it at melee range. Fall back at high speed, and fire arrows as fast as you can. You can pick them up if you kill the pigman, if it kills you, you will lose all of your arrows. If a pigman closes in, run. Do not engage it at close range unless you are heavily armored and at high health. Run and wait for day. It is better to fail at killing the pigman than to be slain by it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skeletons, Preliminary Notes", "Distuth", "Day 1: I noticed something odd on one of the skeletons, after I take", ""),
        StaticBook("Skeletons: Preliminary Notes:", "Distuth", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Skeletons; Fleshless Archers", "Lord_Kashi", "This creature is one of the more dangerous of the beasts, as they can attack from distance, so you may well be unaware when theya attack. They are effectively Skeletal Archers, all without flesh, all bow-wielding. They, like the Zombies were taken by the undead from their graves, but apparently lost all of their skin to them as well. Both the Archers and their bows disintegrate upon death, leaving only arrows, money, and sometimes armour where they once were. I first encountered these when leaving the city of Oren at night. They ambushed me near what is now a bread stall, and very nearly killed me. I was lucky a number of Dwarven warriors came to assist me in fighting the demons. Since then, I always carry a bow on me just in case of another ambush, despite my being useless with it... \n It has been a few months and I have been told we just call these abominations skeletons  \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Skelton Hunting Guide", "Ken_Brandon", "", ""),
        StaticBook("SkillBook : Fishing", "siikshotzz", "Fishing Is An Important skill For Survival as its a great Source of food . To craft a Fishing Rod you make a diagonal Line of sticks , then Two string Below The Top stick , if you understand.  To fish You simple find some wtaer 3 blocks deep and 5x5 or more wide,  and then you right click where in the water where you wont to fish. Then Wait until the Bait Bobbles Down the Right-click again and hopefully you will get a fish !  If not Keep Trying until you Get one . A Raw Fish heals 1 heart and a Grilled/Cooked heals 2/2.5", ""),
        StaticBook("SkillBook : Level 3 Bash", "siikshotzz", "SkillBook : Swordsmanship", ""),
        StaticBook("Skippy's Awesome Book.", "skippy369", "Why do people leave FLOATING TREES!?!?!?!?!?!??!?!?!", ""),
        StaticBook("Skippy's Journal", "skippy369", "test delete IGNORE THIS BOOK", ""),
        StaticBook("Skippy's Redstone Journal", "skippy369", "Entry One: Irba, 4th of The Grand Harvest, 1334, Today I learned a brilliant way to use the power of Pistons to stop dangerous lava falls . What you do is put a piston down on the ground infront of the lava source. Then you place a lever, redstone torch, or whatever can activate it. Activate it and the Piston stops the flow. Entre Two: Today, I headed to Aeriel's City to see if I could be taught about Aeriel. The White Road was a bad path, but it was the only. When I arrived there, no one was there, so I left. I kept going down the road to go to my home in the Wilderness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skippy's Travels.", "skippy369", "Ahh, what a nice day. I woke up, and I started eating my bread. I got my armor on and headed out of my home in Kal'Urguan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skirmishes at Al'Khazar and Laurelin", "everblue2er101", "Trouble was first noticed when lightning rained from the sky, striking rooftops in Al'Khazar and setting them ablaze. There were few people in the city at the time, and they rushed to put out the fires. A strange, cold voice rang out, stating that the lord of darkness would take Oren and Al'Khazar. \n This identified the attacker as Iblees, and proved itself to be different than many Undead attacks. No Undead minions appeared, only lightning over several days. The fires were easily suppressed, leaving those putting out the flames  to stand around, waiting to see what would happen next. \n At some point during the battle, HighPriest Hogarth arrived. He went into the Al'Khazar Cathedral and said a prayer. In a cowardly and despicable act, lightning was struck down upon him in the church. Thanks to the quick thinking of a few of those present, he was pulled from the flames alive. Badly wounded, Valdyn, Axl and myself took him to safety and healed his wounds. The attack ended at this point, leaving us in confusion. We decided to go to Laurelin and ask if the Elves knew about any recent attacks and hopefully tell Native at the same time. We were lead to the Elven capital by Elindor, and it was for the most part a safe journey . We were just outside of Laurelin when we were again attacked. \n There was more lightning, which was alarming in an area full of trees. But these fires were small and extinguished easily. Of more concern were what attacked us. Reanimated skeletons and corpses struck again and again. I was well armoured and well equipped, using my bow when my health grew faint, standing back and recovering. When the attack finally stopped, we regrouped. No one was lost, although several were close to death. We quickly entered the ELven capital. \n Prince Toren was passing by, and we told him thgat we had been attacked twice recently. He was concerned and agreed to pass the message on to High Prince Native. Following this, our group disbanded, although we have remained in contact. During other attacks we have banded together, doing our part to stop the Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Slave Logs", "AllenTheGreat", "Slave Tobi - Released \n Slave Tobi - Escaped \n Slave Jobi - Escaped Slave Dobi - Burned \n Slave Trollbi - Burned \n Slave Nobi - Burned", ""),
        StaticBook("Slavery", "sx421", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Slayer's Journals v.1", "Slayer15855", "This is the first entry of my search, what will become indubitably a long and trecherous journey. This is the search for a arcane, ancient power, with its roots within the very depths of Ageis. This is my search for that power, so that I may better myself and the greater world. The magic is said to consume the soul... But for the chance to create life... I would do anything. \n There is little that we know about this power, it is too ancient. Only a few have ever tapped into its infinite depths. Here I refer to Availer, the wandering wizard, the most powerful being in Ageis. Who has waded deeper into the mystic magic that any other. He has retained his self... For now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Slayers Journals 1", "Slayer15855", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sleep", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Welcome is sleep, more welcome the sleep of stone \n Whilst crime and shame continue in the land; \n My happy fortune, not to see or hear; \n Waken me not - in mercy, whisper low. \n*\n*\n But I, in the chilling twilight stand and wait\n At the portcullis, at thy castle gate\n Longing to see the charmed door of dreams\n Turn on its noiseless hinges, delicate sleep! \n*\n*\n Of all the thoughts of God that are\nBorne inward unto souls afar,\nAlong the Psalmist's music deep,\nNow tell me if that any is,\nFor gift or grace, surpassing this-\n\"He giveth His beloved sleep\" \n*\n*\n Sleep hath its own world,\nDeath and existence: Sleep hath its own world,\nAnd a wide realm of wild reality,\nAnd dreams in their development have breath,\nAnd tears, and tortures, and the touch of joy. \n*\n*\n Care-charmer Sleep, son of the sable Night,\n Brother to Death, in silent darkness born;\n Relieve my languish, and restore the light. \n *\n*\n Sister Simplicitie!\n Sing, sing a song to me, -\nSing me to sleep!\nSome legend low and long,\nSlow as the summer song\nOf the dull Deep \n*\n*\n \n*\n*\n**********\n Scribed by Dio Astore", ""),
        StaticBook("Slightly Creepy Old Book", "Lagomorphia", "A tattered book of unknown origin. The cover is dirty and broken, crinkled as if once soaked and drenched in what looks like dried blood.  \n The book has no writing, but the pages glow faintly with a pale yellow light. It feels as if the pages are reaching out to you, trying to communicate. \n [[To communicate with the book, you need magical ability. If you have such ability and wish to attempt communication, hold the book in your hand and /tell lagomorphia. If Lagomorphia is offline the book does not respond to your attempt, but may at another time.]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Slimes", "Yay5089", "Slimes are dangerous gooey creatures.Once a slime has taken enough damage,It will Split into smaller slimes. Slimes are very powerful and it is recommended to get rid of one with a bow . If slimes manage to get you inside them.They will slowly eat you're soul while tearing up you're corpse until both have dissolved", ""),
        StaticBook("Slimes turn into leaves", "cowsgopoo", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Sly", "iohnoh", "Sir im taking a little vacation... I wont be online for some time. I try to get back next month. I just have shitloads of work to do and no time to play anymore... I wont quit Golden Harvest and minecraft. I will play if i have time . Thanks for the fun times. I try to get online if i get my work done faster.", ""),
