        StaticBook("Spyin' in th' Whispering Isles", "Aandie", "\n We enter the Isles from the front, from Dawn's bakery. We noticed that th' flag poles 'ave been replaced. They used to be iron before and they're now made out of cobblestone. Signs ordering to evacuate and other signs saying that they should stand up and fight, protect their 'omes. \n \n After we've gone around th' 'omes in th' Whispering Isles.. we noticed that they 'ave built towers that are made out of stone. There is no entrance on their sides so we assume that there are underground tunnels leading to these towers. We tried to get on one of them to get into the tunnels without success.. We did notice that each tower 'ad a single chest and a trapdoor on top of tower. \n \n We entered the Whispering Order barracks and noticed down the stairs a door that 'ad a sign above it sayin \"Whispering tunnels\". We assume tis is the doorway to th' tunnels underground. That may lead to th' towers. There is no chance of gettin on top of these towers from th' roofs since none of them is close enough. \n \n In me 'ome, Alek's 'ome, I 'ave a book that 'as all the Whispering order high ups listed. They 'avent made a list of their recruits, so their number is not yet known. \n \n There 'ave been rumours of the rangers 'eading to the Whisper Isles.. They're not 'ere yet.. ((20/10/11)) Day after the orcs attacking Whisper Isles. \n \n Things to do: Copy the love letters  to/from Rhisereld's bookshelves again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Spyin' on th' whispering order", "Aandie", "((20/10/11)), Day after th' orc invading Whispering Isles, they 'ave started buildin up archer towers made out of stone. These towers 'ave no entrances on their sides, so they must have ladders going up from underground tunnels. \n \n We also noticed their ranks.. Captains are the only ones who may modify the barracks.. Sergeants are the only ones who may open the gates.. Signs sayin' the words of spreading the word of world ending and found some recruiting fliers \n \n We found a door that leads to th' Whispering tunnels.. They may be the ones leading to th towers.  \n \n We found their training rooms and obstacle rooms.. They're massive. \n \n ((MC Names found in the chests: Spinzir, tomf1982, henrya15 conster_monster, Chief baruk(??), Arkelos, Almostnermal)) We 'ave a book of the higher ups in me 'ouse. I don't know 'ow old is it .. \n \n Each tower made out of cobblestone, has a single chest on top of it and a trapdoor. We haven't found a way to jump on to one .. yet.. \n \n Be careful what lies inside of th' towers in th' isles.. We didn't make it to get on top of them, no chance. \n \n On our way out from th' Whispering Isles, we noticed that the flag poles were changed from iron into cobblestone. aye", ""),
