        StaticBook("spys", "Lord_Zack", "this guy name polcari is a wardens spye", ""),
        StaticBook("Squidfood Joe", "Lazryus", "This is a historical recount of the last actions and resulting downfall of Lumas \"Squidfood Joe\", an Elf convicted and executed for the battery and assault of Sir Bito, a Knight of the Alrasian Council. \n During his recent occupation as one of the Alrasian Guard, Lumas was repeatedly seen ignoring the chain of command and shirking duty. Oftentimes he was found wandering about and claiming to be patrolling and doing his rounds, even when he was asked inside his own domicile. Lumas was reasonably fired as such, and responded rather positively to it. \n A few days later he ran and chased after Sir Bito, demanding compensation for his lost job. Sir Bito refused to compensate the ex-guard under the reasoning that his firing was of his own fault. In response, Lumas demanded a duel to the death. One of which Sir Bito accepted eagerly. \n With several witnesses, the duel took place at the entrance into Alras, near the main gate. Cookies and concessions were passed about as the witnesses looked on at the ensuing duel. The terms of engagement were laid and agreed upon, one's loss occuring at their withdrawal or death. Lumas believed himself to be a mage and attempted to draw upon an obtuse power of the Elves he believed his race had, only to result in flinging himself at Sir Bito in a drunken rage, screaming \"Die! Die!\" at every breath he drew. \n Sir Bito took the apparently delusional criminal head-on, with a calm mind and a steady hand. The Elf wailed his iron sword with a frenzy, Sir Bito easily deflecting the blows. As for the ones he didn't, it merely left scratches upon his armor. Attacking in kind, Sir Bito swung and stabbed at Lumas with zeal, expertly honed strikes tearing apart the enraged Elf's armor and knocking off his helmet in the process. The duel lasted only for a few minutes before Sir Bito had won the match, killing the Elf with fatal external wounds. \n The crowd quickly cheered and went on their merry way, content in seeing his execution having carried out. As for the body, the Guard picked up the freshly bled corpse and tossed it into the sewer, where Lumas earned his new name: \"Squidfood Joe\". \n \n Needless to say, Jerry the Squid got the most out of everything that had transpired. He feasted like a king that day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Staff Creation -Mages-", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "You will be asked to accomplish 3 different tasks, and the materials you choose will greatly effect what kind of staff you accquire. \n Here are the outcomes you can achieve: \n ~Diamond Staff~ \n Diamond/EnderPearl/Ghast Tear + Blaze Rod  \n ~Golden Staff~ \n Diamond/EnderPearl/Ghast Tear + Stick \n Gold + Blaze Rod \n ~Iron Staff~ \n Gold + Stick \n Iron + Blaze Rod \n ~Stone Staff~ \n Iron + Stick \n Stone + Blaze Rod \n ~Wooden Staff~ \n Stone + Stick \n Wood + Blaze Rod", ""),
        StaticBook("Stage Acts and Schedules By: Crowley Falos", "XSilverWolfX", "Regular Entertainers get payed more than first timers here at the inn. Regular Entertainers Are required to be at as many inn events as possible. By doing this they are getting payed more.   \n (( potsy29 )) Jack Regular Comedian \n (( Vicentee )) Dazen Antolochus Regular Comedian (( cocokyle )) Kyle Poetry Writer First Timer", ""),
        StaticBook("Stage One: General: Markings:", "Distuth", "It all started with the skeletons. Due to their fleshless nature, they were the easiest to observe the markings on. The markings are spread over their body, and were it not for the fact that they are identical on every skeleton (save for places where wear and tear had damaged the markings) they could easily be mistaken for nothing more then scratched bones. Similar markings were found on the zombies and pigzombies, once they were sufficiently restrained to remove the flesh obscuring their bones. However, the bones on the two types of zombies were on average thicker, and coated with different markings. This led me to believe that the bones of skeletons were in fact, shaved down zombie bones, with their previous markings destroyed in order to make space for the new ones. This implies someone is doing this shaving, and that the monsters serve a purpose. As of what this purpose is, I am as of yet able to come to a supportable conclusion on the matter. But if these bones are in fact shaved down, the monsters are not some formless evil. Further investigation is warranted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stage One: Zombie: Markings:", "Distuth", "The markings on the zombie are the most basic of the bunch. Aside from the basic rune for animation sprawled across the ribcage, the zombie possesses galvanizing runes on its legs. The arms possess stiffening runes, while the hands themselves have runes I am unfamiliar with. However, due to the nature of the zombies flesh, and the lack of galvanizing runes on the arms, I suspect these runes are somehow designed to inflict damage on whatever they touch. This may explain the reasoning behind the zombies outreaching arms. But how do the runes on the bones reach past the flesh? If the runes are designed to damage what they touch, why is the zombies flesh intact on the hands? I will have to look further into the matter, see if I can perhaps reproduce the runes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stallmerchant's Guide", "Royced", "A simple way to pay people is to /money pay [ACCOUNT] [AMOUNT] This is needed in transaction. Iron goes for about 50MINAS Gold goes for probably 100 minas! Diamonds can go up to 500 minas per peice! Coal is around 30 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Starags advantures 1 English", "Tigrex75", "Today we have the 33rd of Kamees 1328. I live in the house of my friend Gandrion. Today I got my own room. Our friend the Elv Seronat cant live in Kal Urguan so I havent seen  him for long time. I hope this night will be peaceful. Ok I will write next time more. \nToday we have the 31st of Malins 1328. I and my friend Gandrion tried to find a cow,  because he heard that milk should be beer. So we search and search for a cow. When I was  checking out a hole he went away and I havnt found him yet. I used my soulstone to come to  Kal Urguan. I hope I will found him shortly. Now I have found Gandrion. A stupid villian has put him into a cave by an evil trick. He has ask him to help him and than he put him into the cave. But than the villian  let him out and than the villian attacked my friend. So he took his sword and fight  against him. My friend win and has dropped a diamond and the evils soulstone, too.  What an epic story! Todays the Kamees, 33rd of the Second Seed 1329, today I and my friend Gandrion make us  drunken. It was very funny... \n My friend Gandrion has set me 3 times on fire this night. I havnt found that very funny. Then we have killed some monsters.  Now I have 1053,07 Minas. I hope I can be me a home soon.", ""),
