        StaticBook("Store Prices", "Hempshine", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Stories for a Tired Traveller", "1337Sammiches", "These stories are all fictional, with a few pinches of truth, such as places, towns, and small events. Enjoy! \nTHE CASES OF THE AL'KHAZAR CHURCH \nMany strange things happen at Al'Kazar, like sudden storms and deaths in the sewers. This, however, was different. I was sitting in my apartment above a local shop in Al'Khazar. The shopkeep had handed me the keys for the door and storage cabinets when all of a sudden, there was a loud clap of thunder. This was no ordinary thunder; this was right above us. I jumped at the sound of it, and he told me it was nothing. I went to bed later that night, when all of a sudden, a strange light spread across the town... at night.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stories of the Undead Vol. I", "krislove45", "Introduction: We all know who the Undead are. They are evil people who kill Elves, Humans, etc. just for Iblees. In this book in your hands, I'll be talking to different people, asking about their convict and confronts with the Undead. Some people have died fighting the Undead, but others have survived a war. Up North is where they attack, so going that way is forbidden to any elf. Yes, that's right. I am an elf writing this. I'm an elf and I'm getting 'Behind the Scenes!' Who should I ask first? Well, I will see who I can ask. First, I will be asking Prince. Toren. The Prince's First Encounter- Many died via the hellish lightning strikes of the Undead. His first encounter was the Battle of Whisper Isles. I arrived during the heat of the attack. The Undead had staked their spot on the tops of the highest homes and the highest tower, as they so liek to do. They rained their lightning upon those who had come to fight them. Elves, Dwarves, Orcs and Humans all had to come to defend WHisper Isles. At their beck, they summoned hordes of fell creatures of the night to attack the warriors. The monsters were held back, while many tried to climb the roof tops in attempt to slay the Undead. Many were struck by hot lightning of the Undead and many were slain because of it. The battle was messy as suck affairs often are.", ""),
        StaticBook("Storm's Book", "Ghost_Storm", "I am Storm,Admiral, and Leader of the S.A. My life is different from when I was a child. Back then I was a young boy in my village. I had a brother,a father, and a mother. I was trained by my father in the ways of the Sword. I was also taught how to use a bow . One day while I was training with my sword skills,A army of orcs attacked my village. Most of the village was destroyed and the children had to flee the village. For a few months I had to fend for myself. Then I gathered my things and headed to the Capital of Oren,Al'Kazar. I joined the Oren guards as a new recruit. I enjoyed being in the guards. I hoped that we were going to get payed but I found out they didn't pay any of the guards . There were things that also bothered me. Like that how the guards treated others. After many months I was fet up with all of these things. I traveled and tried to help others,Then I came of the fact of making an army. I started my army to recruit my first General Named Natheus. He was very loyal. Also he led the troops to do good. We had many problems with the undead and others. To this day Many of my friends lost their way and became followers of Ibees. I helped some of them come to their senses and stray from that path. I hope that we will help others. And defeat Ibees. Also get my old friends.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Storm's Journal", "NightlyShadow", "Dear Journal, I have finally started my adventures, my quest to become like my father was, I have ventured and met Siladir, a high elf who has invited me into his town. I have chosen to stay with him, and the others. Things here, are intresting. At last, I can start building myself up, to become stronger and be worthy to use Silzar, the bow my father left me before he died on his quest. The people in this town I have become quick friends with. For now, I live with Siladir until I can afford my own house. The room is small, but perfect for essential things. Now, I must rest. Who knows what tomorrow has in store for me? My quest, my life, has finally begun. END ENTRY #1 Entry #2: \n I woke to a new day alone. The others were gone, probably on thier own adventures. Seeing an opprotunity to work alone, I left with wooden tools to strenghten my awakening abilities. The first day of training, I chopped wood. I took a break for the night, and talked to Nailena, who must have returned from wherever she was. She was with someone, although I can not recall if I knew them or not.", ""),
        StaticBook("Storm's Journal 2", "NightlyShadow", "Entry #6: After a fight against the undead, I was killed by lightning. The pain was quick, but excruciating. I found myself awake again before I could be in Death's grip by mages. I owe them my life. In Oren, I met a human who had the same dreams of adventure and quests as me, named Eranir. I also met Loma, another dark elf, who owned a casino. He offered me and Eranir a free round at the slots, which I won 20 mina from, fortunately. I offered to bring Eranir back to Tur'Elvenor, which he accepted happily. We agreed to meet back at King's Road. While I was waiting for him, I saw many lightning strikes pounding the ground: a sign of the undead! I quickly found my way over there, easily defeating every one of them along with another ten others. However, the Iblees saw me as a threat and overwhelmed me with the lightning that overwhelmed me and killed me instantly. When I woke, Malin bless those mages, I headed back to Tur'Evelon. On my way there, I met the great man himself, High Prince Native, along with Achilles, who I think was also of royal elven blood. I make a note and vow here that I will give any spare rescources I bear to them. It was a high honor to meet them. I reached Tur'Evelon in the high morn'. I headed to the market and bought this book, along with other essentials. I will never forget the cold abyss I felt as Death crawled towards me. Nor will I forget the faces of the mages who brought me back. I was down in despair when I lost my bow, Silzar. However, out of sheer luck or destiny, Prince Native gave me a bow for my travels, and it happened to have the marking only Silzar had! I could control my astonishment and happiness in front of the prince, but once I was out of ear shot, I celebrated. For now on, I am keeping it at home, unless I am absolutely sure I will live through a journey. The same goes for a journal. I hope I can make my father proud.", ""),
