        StaticBook("Subject Aedan - The Effect of The Taint", "KarmaDelta", "Most severe case \n \n He had a mark under his left eye", ""),
        StaticBook("Subject TC report, day 30", "georgebg", "we are progressing rapidly , subject's mind is begining to show signs of breaking , after being subjected to intense physical and mental pain , the subject's mind is begginging to fracture . we expect in the next few days it will begin to fragment , currently the most likly parts to cut themleves out of the brain are , Memory, logic, anger . we anticipate it will be possible to capture these fragments, and replicated them, then perfected . provided that the physical and mental torture continues , subject tc's mind will cut out its anger, and logic in order to prevent destruction . soon other parts will too be cut out, to prevent destruction , memory we belive will be next , we plan to take these fragments, and use them to torture the subjects mind further .  \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Subjects: Zombies", "Green_Mind", "Subject one: The rot and decay of an average zombie is strangely enough, a cause of one of their major weaknesses: fire. This was experienced first-hand by my first zombie test-subject. Though it moaned loudly as it caught fire, I do not believe it to feel actual pain. In their lesser state, I think their minor-functional brains register what would have caused them harm in life, and force their body to act acordingly. Therefore, it is but a state of mind, which is interesting, as the subject is quite intelectually degraded. I attempted to disect it's body, but found it's remains severely charred. This was but a minor set-back. I will fetch my second subject at once. \n \n \n Subject two: I dissected the second subject rather quickly after having ended it's \"life\". This was to prevent it's body to enter rigor mortis, though, I quickly discovered that it had allready done so. Wheter their bodies go trough such process while they are \"alive\" or if they have an extremely quick rigor mortis which starts the very second they die, I made some discoveries. None of their vital organs are functioning, at any level. In fact, the only thing inside their body that has any function at all is their brain. While not as great in potential as the living, it's body seems to have optimised it's own excistence. What was that? It needs to eat but once a month, though it certainly indulges itself more than that. It can substain severe injury, and still walk. In fact, the only effective way of killing them would be to sever the head's connection with their body (by breaking their spine) , or setting them on fire. A lot of people claim to have killed one without breaking their spine, or setting them on fire. But that is purely boasting. Surely, the zombie suffered damage to the spine in one of the many physical blows dealt to it by it's slayer. All in all, if it's possible to copy this undead state by medical procedures, without degrading the mind, the possibillities for humanity would be endless! I must do a closer examination on the next subject's brain. \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Sugar addiction.", "Crippledbaboon", "I met an elf, namely Airion. He has this \"condition\" if you will, where he feels the urge to snort s sugar. It has this odd, strange effect wherein it will give him a \"buzz\". I hope to pursue this said \" addiction\" and find a cure. If I can't do so, at least find a substitute.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sugar cane", "Rhisereld", "Our baby ballerina is \nHiding somewhere in the corner \nWhere the shadow wraps around her \nAnd our torches cannot find her \nShe will stay there 'till the morning \nCrawl behind us as we are yawning \nAnd she will leave our games \nTo never be the same \n \nSo grow tall, sugar cane! \nEat that soil \nDrink the rain \nBut know: \nThey'll chase you if you play their little games \nSo run, run fast sugar cane \n \nYou see my piston booth is handy \nThere's a one way only mirror \nSo I can dance here with my hair down \nBut I don't see if you get bitter \nAnd there's a button right beside me \nIf I happen to want a wall to hide me \nIf only the ballerina had one too. \n \nSo grow tall, sugar cane \nEat that soil \nDrink the rain \nBut know \nThey'll chase you if you play their little games \nSo run, run fast sugar cane \nAnd he said, \"Always be afraid.\" \nYes, you should always be afraid \nOh you better run, run fast sugar cane", ""),
        StaticBook("Sugar Cane and You, How To Farm Sugar", "dyldo", "So, you've got sugar cane, and don't know what to do? \n Plant it next to water! Let it grow! \n Once grown to a 3 foot cane, punch it down! \n Now, what to do with your sugary bounty? \n By smashing it up on a workbench, you can make granulated sugar of the sort that's suitable for cakes. \n \n However, you can also make books out of it. \n Carefully line it up in a flat line on your workbench, then compress. \n You should have some pages afterwards. \n Now, line up these pages in a vertical line, and... Shuffle! \n If you do it right, you should have a hardback book. \n \n \n Yeah. We're not sure either how paper can make the cover that easily.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sugar Man", "shiinchan", "5 Units", ""),
        StaticBook("Suggestions/Ideas/Observations 1", "emberhard", "I think this will be somwhat long so pull up a chair.... \n I think we need to see about getting some more public spaces in, one important thing would be an official tree farm. I think we should also see if we can get a commision for a mine, and maybe throw in that park you had in mind earlire. On that note, love the public farm! \n one thing we may wish to think about is makeing our doings more public, such as updateing the anouncement board more often, or creating a town councle or somthing. \n Tuk's new town is starting to grow, and he is putting much effort into it, I do not belive it has any one liveing there yet though. One thing we may wish to start thinking about is more relations with him, or possibly even combining the two towns, or makeing them sister cities, however before beging discusions with Tuk about this I would highly suggest talking with seventh first. One issue with that idea though is I doubt tuk would want to give an inch, and nor would we. \n How is the advertising going? ((We might want to make a page on the wiki!)) \n Well that is all I can think of at the moment, but this note is extreamly subject to change, and notice I labled it \"#1\", I often get many ideas. \n Signed Emberhard", ""),
        StaticBook("Suggestions/Ideas/Observations 2", "emberhard", "I don't think This one will be as long as the other, but who knows! I might get inspired mid way through! \n First off this man very much wishes to become a gaurd, I told him it would be fine with me but we will have to run it by Mork and you, there is also the issue of I think he wants to be paid. \n (( also we had a run-in with a greifer, so I dont know if you got my earlire message so the Contents of that one will also be in here)) First off thank you for the land grant but where exactly is it? Would you rather me just choos a spot that seems out of the way? \n How goes the mine, and advertiseing? \n Also I cut down as much of the floating trees as I could around the city, but it left our forests looking somewhat barren, but I did not replant as it also opened up a great deal of land for expans ion! But if you would rather replant the land than develop it I have the saplings \n t \n How goes the talks with tuk, any news worth hearing?", ""),
        StaticBook("Suicide Letter", "Archmage_Cataris", "Lonely, I'm Mr. Lonely, I have nobody for my own. I'm so lonely, I'm Mr. Lonely, wish i had someone to talk to. \n I'm a soldier, a lonely soldier, Away from home through no wish of my own. \n That's why im lonely, I'm Mr. Lonely, I wish that i could go back home. \n Letters, never a letter, I get no letters in the mail. \n I've been forgotten, yeah, forgotten, oh how i wonder is it i failed. \n I'm a soldier, a lonely soldier, Away from home through no wish of my own. \n That's why i'm lonely, I'm Mr. Lonely, I wish that i could go back home... \n - Elgon, Twin to Cataris and last of the Vulgarian", ""),
        StaticBook("Sukavi's Journal", "SuperStewie95", "Day 1: I be gettin ready to go huntin. It might be a challenge with all of my enimies out there. Day 2: Still no sign of Dominus Grum. He has been gone for a while now. Maybe I should go and look for him. Day 3: I have been searching for 2 weeks now, I'm thinking about giving up the search. Day 4: I have decided to give up the search. If Grum is still alive, he will have to find his own way back Day 5: I began heading back home when I was ambushed by a group of bandits. I managed to kill three, but there were to many. I have been inprisoned in their camp. Day 8: This is the first time I have been able to write in here. They began executing other prisoners, I'm lucky that they didn't kill me. Day 10: It's been almost a week since they inprisoned me. Most of the bandits went out to try and find more people to imprison. I am going to try and kill the guard and make a run for it. Day 11: I was unable to escape, these guards are tougher than they look. I think somone is coming I hope they aren't coming to kill... (The page is slightly torn.) Day 12: They came to execute me, but were unable too. Right when they were about to kill me Grum came out of nowhere and kill the bandits. I am writing from our makeshift camp in the woods. Day 13: Grum Tells me that he has been spying on the bandits for weeks. He also tells me that they killed his family right in front of him and that he was waiting for the right moment to attack. If you ask me, it was. Day 14: Grum and I decided to start heading for home. Hope we don't run into any more bandits.", ""),
        StaticBook("Summoner's Book(C)", "Hwaldar", "About the Book \n \nThis book was made,as a Manual,for easier understandment of how to properly use the Summoning Cauldron. For more information,contact Hwaldar. \n  \n Summoning Instructions \n First of all,you must choose the category of Summonables. Immediately after that,you must choose a Summonable. A Summonable,is a creature or effect,which can be made with the Summoner's Cauldron. Once a Summonable is chosen,proceed by adding the ingredients into the Cauldron. There are no preset sequences,so add them as you please. However,you must NEVER attempt to add additional ingredients,without knowing the effect. \n \nWarning \n \nAlways be careful with adding the ingredients! It is advised to add them at the same time,as some reactions are effective immediately. Last,but not least,NEVER MIX GOLDEN APPLES WITH HELL STONE! \n \n \nCopyrighted by Hwaldar Richards.", ""),
        StaticBook("Summoner's Reciepts", "Hwaldar", "Diseases \n \nCold:Throw in Lapis Dust and Flesh \nShaking:Throw in Rotten Flesh \nVomiting:Throw in Rotten Flesh and Redstone \nPoison:Throw in a Red Mushroom \nAntidote:Throw in a Brown Mushroom \n \n Injuries \n \nBreaks:Throw in Bone Meal \nConcussion:Throw in Bone Meal and Redstone \nStab:Throw in a blood-soaked dagger. \nCuts:Throw in a kitchen knife \nDecapitations:Throw in a blood-soaked axe \n \nCreatures \n \nBugs:Throw in some honey or sugar \nRats:Throw in some rotten mouse teeth \nGhosts:Throw in some Glowstone dust \nDemons:Throw in some Hell Stone \nAg'Na'Rok:Throw in Hell Stone,Glowstone and Lapis dust,Rotten Flesh and a Golden Apple \n \nCurses \n \nTripping:Throw in a stick \nDrowning:Throw in a water lilly \nFalling:Throw in some stones \nDizzyness:Throw in rose essense \nFlesh Rot:Throw in Redstone and Rotten Flesh \nWywern's Curse:Throw in Stone,a Pearl,and a Feather", ""),
