        StaticBook("Sword Styles", "silco97", "As you should know the art of the sword is one of the oldest form of fighting in the world. starting as perhaps as a club then evolving into an iron blade.  What ever you want to think the art of sword play is old and complex.  This book will explain the diffrent styles of the sword and its orgins. \nTsnathaid :;This is one of the oldest styles of fighting and probebly the most basic of styles. It comes from the word needle created by the monks of the Elfs. They were said to be the first to create an iron sword. This style is requires your basic sword and a quick hand.  When holding the sword use both hands for this style.  As it uses much moving and turning.  When you engage the enemy hit them then back away until they are close then circle around them striking them again then reapting the backing away motion. \nUscese :This style was laso created by the evles.  by a martial arts master from the far east. This stlye is a onehanded style and requires slow smooth thinking. You should dodge the enemy gracfully and quick.  The sword should be help loosly letting the swords own weight do most of the fighting.  You sould not flail your sword and hope you hit your enemy in this stlye but only hit them when you know you can and not waist your strength. \nCasur :This style was created by a dwarven scholar who made a living as a phcision. This style requires great streangth and power. Using you sword as a club more then as a sword and holding it in two hands swing in wide archs. This style is best used agenst a large amount of enemies and monsters.  These wide archs for one that is weak would leave you open but with great strength you should be able to recover quickly before the enemy has a chance to attack.  The basics of this style are keep a strong deffence and only attack when you can break the enemies deffences. \nThe Human Style : This style has no name due to the fact that it is constenly evolving and changing.  Hold a sword with two hands and heep in a stance with legs at shoulders length apart When doind this style you must do quick clean cuts moving back into your basic stance afterward.", ""),
        StaticBook("Swordsmithing I", "firespirit44", "The first step to making a sword is to have the correct ratio of two materials \n Iron and Carbon \n The two materials fuse together and create what we call Steel. It is the Swordsmith's job to find the perfect ratio, as does a muscisian needs to find the perfect pitch to create a beautiful work of art. Steel enables the blade to have a far sharper edge and to withstand much greater stree without breaking or staying bent. \n Place the two materials in a mould and smelt it over a heat as strong as a lava bucket. The first step is done. Now to Forging.", ""),
        StaticBook("Swordsmithing II", "firespirit44", "Forging. \n Where a Swordsmith invests his blood, sweat and tears the most during this process. The swordsmith had to shape and mix metals of different known qualities, some softer for the core or sides, some harder for edge and point. This was done by pressing harder steel around softer iron so that the blade could flex under sudden impact but resist deformation. Hammers chimes and the anvil cries, the Swordsmith needs to masterfully mould the metal to his liking over a short span of a few ticks, before the metal glows and fades into a dull grey colour. Reheating of the blade is often needed before the Swordsmith can achieve the \n Length \n Thickness \n Width \n of the sword. \n \n Now the forging is done. Tempering is now due.", ""),
        StaticBook("Swordsmithing III", "firespirit44", "Tempering is the process of Quenching and Heating. The purpose of Tempering is to loosen the bonds  that hold the metal together, like stretching a dough and allowing it to relax before it is baked. \n The way to do Tempering is by dunking the hot metal rod into water and then heating it by letting it sit in lava. Repeat the process til Sword may bend easily without snapping or breaking. Be careful, and always use tongs. \n The main body of the sword is now completed \n \n Now we make a hilt and guard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Swordsmithing IV", "firespirit44", "Before making the hilt and guard, the blade needs to be sharpened to cut and stab. \n \n Use a whetstone (stone and pressure plate) and carefully hold the blade against the giant grinding stones while pedalling furiously. \n Thick on the edge, but sharp enough to cut. \n To fashion a hilt and guard, carve the design while cold, and heat it together with the pommel of the sword to firmly attach the two. \n Lastly, the blade would be polished and inscribed with decorations or place precious stones in the sockets created during forging. \n You see the end of the page there is a seal of a hammer, surrounded by a pool of lava, and above the hammer is a shining Golden Anvil.", ""),
        StaticBook("SWT", "Ranovak", "SWT (Standardized Warden Test) \n When an initiate has served in the wardens for a certain amount of time, he/she may approach an officer to be tested in hopes of becoming a guard. \n \n The SWT consists of the following: \n Endurance Test: Survive in the crucible for half a day, without armor or weapons. \n Yes. You have until noon. Start initiate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Syblix's Diary", "Syblix", "Intan 16th of Snows Maiden, 1314 Here I am Sitting in my room, awaiting for daylight. We formed a fort in hope of defeating the Undead, which are almost undefeatable. I will head out to hunt some animals in the morning, which will hopefully bring us some food.. Sun has risen, I am off to my quest! I'm sitting on the beach, I haven't found a living soul in the cold forest.. I'll plant some more trees that will be harvested later on, so we can continue the construction of o ur fort, which will someday become a city, if not destroyed by the undead! Its nighttime diary, I'm leaving you in my chest, so someone can find you someday, and if we achieve victory, so that man can read all about triumphs! I bid you a farewell! Joma, 27th of Snows Maiden, 1314 - We are marching towards northeast to find another fort , which will contribute our battle against the undead! We're in an abandoned building, and trying to make walls on a mountain nearby.. Hopefully we'll atract people to live here.. Its a nice location..", ""),
        StaticBook("Syngard Cunaide's Diary", "Philush", "Day 1: Finally... I've found my son. He's alive. Living in some city.... I can't remember the name, But now I live with him in the attic, along with 'is friend, Willard or something..... and I found Magdrum, didn't talk to him, but that don't matter. Godfrei... still alive...  Thank goodness.....", ""),
        StaticBook("T.Hawkinson Diary", "tomsim9611", "day one. Me, Harralak and Charon have left Oren. We've moved to a small clearing in the elven forrests where we hope to make a small town. Day 5: The town is starting to take shape now, our houses are set up and Harralak wants to expand, make some shops and an inn so travellers will come. I just want to mine the rich untouched ground beneath us. Day7: I'm starting to miss felix now, he was my best friend and i never said goodbye. Day 12: we've just had a huge thunder storm it sounded as if lightening was getting quite close to our village but it eventually passed. it gave me horrid flash backs to my war torn past. The battle of Al'Khazar where the King fell. Snowy Fields, when me and two other Guards scouted ahead to look for undead when lightening struck down on my collegue in front of me, i could only watch as he was destroyed Yes i've seen a lot of battles in my time here, thats why i left i couldnt bare to watch the north fall. Day... i forget: Ive become a wealthy man in my time away from oren. It's been 2 nearly 3 years since i left and i earned almost 10,000m! The town is constantly expanding and making allies life couldn't be better. 29.Snows Maiden.1313 I hear whispers from the north... Alstion has fallen, Grimbeard is dead as is Captain Vardak... The Northern towns are gone, there is nothing to stop the undead Al'Khazar will soon fall, as will the King and as will Oren. And then soon all of Aegis shall choke in the iron grip of the Undead 1321. I have returned to my home in libertas after a night of drunken adventures in Oren. I met a wonderful girl, her name was.. Elsa, that was it Elsa. Things went well and i ended up spending the night at her house. I wonder if i shall ever meet her again... The Deep Cold, 1321: I recieved a letter today from Elsa. She is pregnant. With my child. She says she respects me but does not want me to be a part of the childs life. What can i do now? Nothing i guess, she's made up her mind, i'll never meet my son. ; 1324. Word has spread to Libertas of King Edmunds betrayal and turn to the undead. With Prince Enor away, the kingdom is without a leader and there is civil unrest with several people trying to take the throne. I will return and help as best i can as i fear an Undead attack while the kingdom is so weak. I got to Alkhazar without trouble, but when i got here i was in shock. A huge hell gate stood before me at the main gate. I hurried to the keep where there was a meeting taking place, I was now even more shocked to see stood before us all King Perea, the man that had been killed by the undead nearly 16 years ago. He began to tell the crowd of how he came to be  there today. During the battle in 1308 he had not been killed but merely fell through a  hell gate. Since then he had been surviving on rotten flesh and mushrooms. He had then found a diamond pick and proceeded to make him self a portal back home, the portal in the square. Some members of the crowd didn't believe this thinking he was another undead imposter. they were now very wary of people from the nether after Edmunds betrayal. ; There has just been an attack on the city! I have been wounded slightly and am bleeding from my head, but i should be fine. The guards are gathered around the portal, where the beasts came from incase of more. ; More have come i have led men to the rooves to fire upon the ghasts and giants that litter the streets. I must return to my duties now farew.... *the diary ends here ,its pages splattered with drops of blood and dirt. The page also appears to be charred and you notice that it has a distictive smell, a smell of death*", ""),
