        StaticBook("Tale Of The Crow And The Bear", "silco97", "Once there was a bear he would always go into town dressed in the best and most recent fashin. He would were puffy coats and a wigg and he would get many complements at how well he was dressed. One day the bear cam to town wereing his finest clothes when a crow approuched him and told him \nYou know they are wereing bags on their feet and pans on their heads today\" Said the crow. \"You would look like a fool going into town like that\" Horribly embaressed the bear ran home and put a pot on his head and bags on his feet and trotted into town feeling rather proud of hiself. The people laughed and pointed at the bear for the way he dressed as no one was dressed like him. So the bear ran home and lived the rest of his days alone with a pan on his head and bags on his feet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tale of the Silver Fox", "xzpepijnzx", "It is said that by the light of the very first moon of every Malin's Welcome, a silver fox makes its run through the heart of the Darkwood Forest. It is also said that the hunter who captures this fox and spills his blood will have eternal life. \n There once was a poor huntsman who lived with his ailing son. They lived a happy, humble life, until one day, in early Malin's Welcome, when the young son's health took a turn for the worse. \n The village healer told the father that his son did not have long to live.  So in desperation, the huntsman set out for the forest with his trusty hunting dog. As the silver light of the first moon filled the forest, the huntsman caught sight of a streak of silver, faster than the arc of a gleaming sword, shoot through the underbrush. \n It was the fox, and the hunter and dog followed after it. And just as the fox dove for its burrow under the old ash tree, the dog caught onto the tip of its tail and bashed it against a tree. \n The hunter seized it by its throat and held it aloft. \n \"I have caught you, Beast, and now you shall grant my son eternal life,\" he declared, and the fox blinked its wide black eyes back at him. \n \"So he shall,\" the fox spoke in a calm, wise tone, \"but eternal life comes at a price. For each day he lives by my blood, so much another's be spilled by his hand.\" \n The hunter heard this, and brought the fox home. As the boy slept, for he was a very deep sleeper, the father placed his hunting knife in his hand. He gripped the boy's hand in his own around the blade, and opened the fox's throat, spilling three silver drops of blood onto the floor. \n The boy was out of bed the very next day, as if he'd never ailed. \n His father supplied victims by night as the boy slept. This way, the boy never knew the terrible sacrifice that prolonged his life. \n The father supplied most of the necessary victims by dragging away passed out drunkards from the local drinking spots . The tavern was quickly emptied of its unruly regulars.  They were only ruffians, he figured, and no one would miss the rabble. \n The boy grew to be handsome and kind, and soon won the heart of a lass with eyes as fine as the mind she possessed. They became wed before the boy reached his twenty-first birthday. \n And one night, the boy's father brought home another victim. The boy's new bride slept lightly, and was awakened by the sounds. \n Horrified, the wife leapt out of bed, accusing the father of murder and declaring she'd turn him int o the authorities to be hanged. The huntsman, desperate, tried to explain the situation to her. \n The wife would not hear him. She insisted her husband never approve of such sacrifice on his part. She was determined to tell him at once. \n So the huntsman, not knowing what else to do, silenced her, and then hurried away in a fright just as day broke. \n When the boy awoke to find his bride dead beside him, he was heartbroken. He wept, and cursed the skies as he held her broken body. \n And then he spotted her hand, closed around his father's blade still buried in her heart. And with closed eyes, he wrapped his fist around the cold hand of his wife, held the knife aloft, and cut his own throat, spilling three silver drops onto the floor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tale of the Soulstone Curse", "Gunground", "The land is littered with magical entities, presences, essenses, and beings.  On any given sun risiw", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales from the Wilds", "Saber952", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales Of A Quest Giver.", "Charles_Grimlie", "I am the Quest Giver... I am often called \"Quest\" or \"The Quester\"! I hand out many interesting quests to those who wish to partake! My most popular Quest is the one about slaying the mightiest tree in the forest near by with my trusty [Mighty Fish Of Tree Slaying] The reward is usually 2 [Iron Ingots], and 100 Minas... I often sit outside my tower, originally a abandoned Dwarvern relic from the orc wars. To note, I usually keep one of my chests open, thus you found this book! Take good care of it, as it might become a mighty artifact itself, hopefully it'll be called [The Ancient Tome Of Quester]. Usually folk think me odd, mad even... But cant a humble dwarf help new folk learn their footing, and become mighty knights of the realm? Seems not.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of a Scribe", "Ranovak", "Thank you then.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of a Traveler", "BobNorton", "There was an orc named Auot. This orc, unlike others, was not as war-like, but still liked a fight. He won many areana matches, but not knowing the areana code, picked up a corpses loot. This got him in trouble, but he gave it all back, and never did it again. Auot was recently mugged, well, sort of. A nice elf lady (not to mention she was pretty) tacked the would be bandit, Bog, and saved him. Auot then installed a metal door so he couldn't be robbed again. Author Note: Auot's services are available, he works as a Merc. He will guard you, attack others, or escort you, or someone else. He might also collect resources, although he is not a fan of it. Auot charges a low fee, and will generaly help the new people for free. For details, visit Auot at his home, in the Slums, or find him on the road. But be careful, if you act hostile, he might just attack. Julia_Archer is the elf that saved me, gotta remember that.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales Of A Traveler", "459pm", "Once apon a time, there was an elf of about 30 years of age who lived in a small home in the woods south of lauren with his uncle, Darus This boy's name was Lou he was a skilled archer and relitivly good at mining, but the one thing he exeled at was \" Earth Magic \" earth magic is using magic to manipulate plants to do your bidding, you can make them grow, shrink, or even attack so when Lou was 45 years of age his Uncle let him leave and go to the city of Lauren. there he learned from great mast Krom how to make plants do, shall we say, interesting things. he learned how to make them attack, defend, and make wonderfull fruit and poisonis fruit. He left Lauren and master. Krom when he was 97 and disided it was time to perchase a home, outside of a city he perchased a hom about 18 miles from ravenhold under a little mountain called St. Jar's Peak so he called his home St. Jar's manor about 3 years of meditating in his home and teaching magic to a few boys who lived next door. he was attacked by orks. they rushed down the mountain in the middle of the night and our hero barly escaped alive. CHAPTER 2", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of a Traveling Merchant", "Pizzafreak5", "Day 1-I Left For Kal'Rog early last night. I saw a human enter the metro and I followed him. He is a holmes seargent named Chase. I gave him some drinks and let him wander around Bryst. He left via the metro soon after, and I departed soon after. \n Day2-I came across a large ungerground house. Much larger than Our rooms at Kal'Bryst. Perhaps I should invest in a retreat outside of Bryst? As a secret Hide Away? I took shelter is this underground Manor during the night. It was nice and warm, but it had no furniture. \n Day3-I Left the underground Manor and tried to get my bearings. I met three travelers who were on their way to found a villiage. We talked for most of the night, but they did not know of the Blind Scribe. I told them they were near Kal'Bryst, although I gave no specifics. Day4-I left the travelers, promising them a drink should they find themselves in bryst. I found a tower I recognized, and made my way to a town near Bryst . I dont know its name. I took shelter in a empty house from the night. I really should have thought to bring a Bedroll with me Durning the night I was rather bored. I checked my equipment. I was pleasently suprised to find that my boots looked new still, with no scratches of any sort. My axe was in the same condition as when I had left. I was down to only two loaves of bread. I might need to resupply. My wares where still in good shape, although I could not vouch for the worth of them. \n Day5-I Left the small villiage Today. I still do not know its name. I Past Krugmar and swam to The Whispering Ilses. My bread got soggy, but I dried and ate it. I arrived at kal'rog by Nightfall \n Day6- After making no profit in Kal'Rog, I left and found a elven ship. It was built of birch, rather small, but beautiful all the same. I stayed the Night. \n Day7- I spent the day farming sugar canes. I like to care for plants, and I enjoy chewing on the sweet stalks while traveling. I found a miniture castle type building called the Hermit's Sanctuary. I stayed the night. I belive it was built be an orc \n Day8- I stumbled upon Lorilen (Or however you spell it) today. I've always Admired the elven city, even though I could never find my way around. I ate my last loaf of bread, and took refuge in a tavern. I talked to an elf, and we discussed orcs. Elves don't seem to like them much. \n \n Day9- I left Lorilen today. I stopped and admired the Temple of Ageis. Just out side of whisper isles, I encountered a group of mercenaries, called the Cripsons, attempting to kill a Holmes, named Kaine. I was told to leave or I would 'Get hurt'. I snuck around the back of the holmes head quarters. Apparently Kaine entered some sort of bunker, and the Cripsons could not get in. \n Day10- I Met a friend of mine, Belin, along the road, and we traveled to the trading post outside Oren. Along the way, we passed through a desert city, which I had not seen before. We returned to Whispering Isles once we saw that there were no traders at the post \n Day11- There seems to be no one to trade with. I'm heading back to Bryst \n \n Day12- I am halfway to Bryst. I stayed in the Small house again. Perhaps I shall visit the villiage the three travelers founded", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of a traveller", "KPDGaskell", "This book is the tale of Richard Willard, a traveller in this fair land. help", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of a weary traveler.", "Imitatio2", "Day 1, I've awoken in a strange crypt, unknowing of the land ahead. The only thing with me was this wierd thing that looked like cheese. As I was very hungry, I tried to eat said thing. Needless to say, the results were somewhat terrifying. I was whisked away to a large city of which was active with citizens. As I walked around, I began to come to my senses. I began talking to townsfolk. I asked for directions, asked where I was, and I also asked what the wierd cheese-thing was. It is known as a, \"Soulstone.\" I began to ponder at why I awoke with such an object. I sat down near a shop at started", ""),
        StaticBook("tales of a young miner", "awesomerer", "", ""),
        StaticBook("tales of an underground man", "Sode1", "page 1 I know have a job with a strange man named banok he sent me to go get some meat, after my first payment i am quite happy also today i met a prince in the morning he gave me some bread i was very hungry but very gratefull . I do not know what has just happened, i was killing a few pigs and then i woke up and it is night time very strange, well i shall continue hunting", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Braxis Silverblade", "Jroy96", "This is one of me First major battles and one of me hardest the battle for snowy feilds This was back of me Oren Guards days i lived with me best friend Urun the Dwarf a snowy feilds guard one day after he bought the inn the undead seemed to get closer every day one day a major battle went on there were many of us trying to defened the town me and Urun stuck to gether and fought and killed some followers me and Urun spotted the Head Prophet s owe charged him The Undead light urun on fire and i lost sight of him i was furious and charged the undead he threw fire and a horde of undead at me i almsoted died just to get to him when i did get to him we fought i drew me Iron sword and so did he we fought and fought parry after parry he landed two well planted hits on me arms with the last bit of me energy i threw a massive strike at the undead killin thier prophet after he died the rest were easly killed after me and a few others killed the rest of em off we checkd the town it was in ruins... many houses were destroyed including uruns and my house when i saw that i looked for Urun at once I searched and searched and i found him he was dead,,, lying on the ground in his Tavern The monks could not have saved him We buried him in his home town of Snowyfeilds after that battle my home was lost so i wanderd and wanderd  after a while i found a new job i couldnt be a guard anymore (a later story) i became a Squire Of Sir Grimbeard of Oren and i still am today but im about to be Knighted When i do i will write a new tale \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n:", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Psiop the Assassin", "Psiop412", "July 6, 2011 2:35 a.m. \n Another Assassination complete\n Target Name: Brum\n Reason: Stealing from people and killing those who do not agree to his thievery", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Psiop The Assassin.", "Psiop412", "It was cold, dark, and most of all Silent.\n I was watching over my target a wealth slave trader who's been illegally stealing innocent people and killing them. You could smell him a mile away, wasnt pleasant not even for an Assassin. Ive been watching him for about 2 days knowing his position, his behaviour and his style.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Talrend", "Doom_Lich", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of the Magical Gem (Part 1)", "Gunground", "The world is filled with magican beings, entities, presences, and essences. One cannot travel farther than 20 paces without encountering some form of un-explained force . The ground around you, the fountains of aegis, and the mysterious stones infused to every soul. This tale is the story of an estranged and lonely goblin, who embarked on a quest the likes of which has never been seen. His name was Jekyll, a lone traveler seeking refuge after his town was pillaged and set aflame. He had been travelling the deserts for weeks, scrounging what little food and water he could to surv ive. The Desert Cacti provided basic sustenance, but the sharp needles caused his gums to bleed over time , a gruesome and agonizing pain. After much travel, the desert rapidly shifted into a thick and lush forest, where at the corner of h is eye, he spotted a cobble road, the signs of civilization, at least he had made it! Exhausted by lack of nutrition and water, Jekyll collapsed on the road, as his eye slowly grew heavy . The world began to darken as his eyelids shut, and he drifted out of conciousness... The first part of my novel is complete!", ""),
        StaticBook("Talks with Orc Warlord", "benny508", "Me , Talun and Tamara proceeded to speak with the orc warlord after you had to leave for some improt ant matters. When we arrived we told the warlord about the tolling booth and he said that he had never heard of it. The warlord then informed us that alot of orcs act on their own accord and claim to be working for somebody high up. Half way through Tamara had to leave due to personal matters to Felix came to replace him. Felix told the warlord about the current situation and Talun told him that relations with the orcs and humans had not been the best lately. The warlord then told us that there would be no war and again stated that orcs will kill loot and st eal because that is what they do and that they are acting on their own accord not his. Felix then spoke to them about taxing the orcs taxing people on the kings road and the warlord said that he did order that and we did not really get any further after that. So at the end of the talks we found out that there would not be a war but it seems that the orcs wil l continue to tax people on the kings road.", ""),
        StaticBook("Talmah", "Daniel_J", "Talmah is a small town outside of Al' Khazar. Shamus, Nero, and my self Daniel started this town Over the past few month our small town has grown in size very fast at this monent we have 8 m help", ""),
