        StaticBook("test2", "Slayer15855", "The evil will of the clouds could not long be held at bay. They soon recovered and surged forwards anew, now reaching their long awaited destination. Bolstered afresh, driven ever onwards by the malevolent hands. The dark clouds now surrounded the fortress walls, a thick rolling fog, a void on the surrounds, sucking the very being from land and soul. The pressure on the fortress redoubled, the clouds trying to squeeze the life from the mighty flames, to no avail. The force of the flames pushed back on the clouds, with such vigour as to dispel them from the wall, but the clouds kept mounting, redoubling the pressure, again and again, drawing closer to the mighty flames. The fortress could hold out on longer and buckled under the vast force of the pressing clouds.", ""),
