        StaticBook("The Art of Combat", "firespirit44", "The Human body consists of 2 arms, 2 legs, a head, and a body All are made out of nothing but weak cells, but if bounded together, forms a impressive peice of weaponary. This book will teach you how to count on your body instead of swords and armour. The Sambo is a technique wherein you act defenceless and without strategy, letting the oponent's guard down. The defenceless you will attempt to get closer, and once within striking distance, jump punch the opponent, knocking them out with one move . Next is the Technique Ataka. This technique was invented by some halflings who needed to punch orcs that wants to eat them. The technique involves dazzing the opponent with repeated attacks randomly, swivelling in and out of your opponent's body to make him too confused to retaliate. This technique should be used cautiously, as if once caught, will result in the opponent overpowering you . The last form is Angrabe. It involves a guerilla tactic whereas you run as fast as you can, leap, and elbow or kick the attacker in the face. Doing this will create a knockback, and you may retreat and do the same tactic. Be wary, if the attacker strikes you midair, you will be at a overwhelming d isadvantage. \n Signed, Jack Ah, Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Deception", "susitsu", "Th art of dcption is simpl rally, it is so asy to do with all th simpl mindd fools around On of th asist ways is b th prson thy would lik you to b If you ar somon th lik thn you will gain acss to thir scrts with a lot mor as Kp bing this prson thy njoy and thy will kp talking This is just simpl information gathring Now for avoiding confrontation Whn somon approachs you asking what you ar doing and you do not want to answr spak badly of s omthing or somon thy dislik, lik say th Dwarvs dislik th Orcs and vic vrca Us this to your advantag If say you ar an lf and a dwarf approachs and asks what you ar doing hr and ad rsss you by rac, rspond with somthing lik \"Hy, at last I'm not an Orc\" gt along a bit thn say goodby to thm Thn say you ar caught following somon Th bst way out of this situation is saying you thought thy might b undad Unlss you fl it is saf to rval to thm why you wr trailing thn say wh y you wr following But mayb thy ar som popular and vain fool, act lik your a fan of thirs, complimnt thr go Of cours you want to practic all ths skills, start small tim thn mov upwards Kp it up and you will develop your own style.    END VOLUME ONE", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Digging: Dwarf Edition", "Nabbasan", "\n Welcome to the Art of Digging: Dwarf Edition.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Digging: Dwarven Edition", "Nabbasan", "About the Author: \n Argos Cuthalion, born Argos Tho'lagg, was born to Ivan and Hildeguard Tho'lagg in the city of Kal'Urguan. His mother Hildeguard, died right after Argos was born, leaving Ivan to fend for his son alone. Ivan supported Argos and himself by mining. Despite the strenuous amount of labor, Ivan enjoyed his job as a miner. Sadly, when Argos reached the age of 12, Ivan and a group of 7 other miners were lost when the mine collapsed, leaving Argos alone. Despite losing his father due to the mine collapsing, Argos always loved digging. He had the same job that his father had until the age of 31. \n Money was starting to run out for Argos, and was forced to sell his home in Kal'Urguan, and leave the city. Out in the wild, Argos was barely able to fend for himself. If it wasn't for the help of one elf, Argos wouldn't be in the position that he is in today. That elf, was Amras Cuthalion, lord of Cuthalion Estate. Amras approached Argos while Argos was chopping trees, and saw him as an ally. Amras offered Argos a plot of land in what is now Cuthalion Estate. There Argos built his house, and started earning money. After all he had been through, he finally felt like he had a home and a family again. After months of service, Lord Amras accepted Argos into the family, giving him the name Argos Cuthalion. \n Argos Cuthalion still lives in Cuthalion Estate, and with the help of his friends, is ready for adventure! \n Chapter 1: Introduction \n Welcome to The Art of Digging: Dwarven Edition, by Argos Cuthalion. This book will go in detail on the basics, different techniques, safety, and the love of digging. Let's get started! \n Chapter 2: Safety \n As you know, digging can be a very hard task if not properly prepared. Here is a list of a few precautions you should take before heading into the mine for some digging. \n 1. Always make sure you have more than one pick. You never want to go with just one pick into a mine, because you might need it to find your way out and/or need it to get some extra ore before some other miner takes it. \n 2. Always make sure you have plenty of food.. You never know how long you will spend in the mine. Could be a few hours, days, even weeks. So always keep a stash of food. \n 3. Always bring wood. Wood is no where to be found under ground, so always keep a stash of it in your inventory. \n 4. Bring plenty of torches. There is no such thing as too many torches. \n 5. Bring a weapon. Whether it's a bow or sword, always bring a weapon. Everything from spiders to zombies can be found deep underground. \n 6. Return when you think it is necessary. Don't ever take a chance when you are about to enter a new area. Return your ore and other loot before exploring new places. \n 7. Always have a goal. What is the point of traveling deep undergound without a damn good reason for it?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Dueling", "hmqb", "Chapters: 1. What you do not want to do and common mistakes", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Farming.", "bpwoods97", "Farming is a hard thing to master, but can fork up a good profit, once you get good enough at it of course.     \nThere are only a few things you need to start farming. First of all, you need a hoe. The hoe is every farmers vital tool. Without a hoe, you cant farm. Secondly, you need something to grow . For starters, just use seeds for growing wheat. Beginners usually cant grow more than wheat at first so dont expect to make alot of cash right away. Farming takes time, and should be given the time it needs to become an expert. As you get better, you can grown more things, like pumpkins and melons. Thirdly, you need somewhere ideal, close to water to grow any plant at all. Water is what keeps the crops alive, so always keep them near water. \nSo lets get started farming. What you need to do first is find where you want to plant your crops. Remember, this must be close to water. Then what you do, is take out your hoe, and hoe the grass where you are planting, until it becomes right for planting. After that, you must take out your seed of choice, dig a small hole in the tilled dirt, and plant the seed.  Next, you simply wait. Wait until the crop is done growing. This is the hardest part of farming, as you must have alot of patience . Once the crop is done growing, it is ready to be harvested. To harvest the crops, take your hoe, and simply dig them up! But be gentle with them, or you could kill them. Also, NEVER walk on your crops, this will kill them as well. After you've harvested your crops, do what you like with them. With sugarcane you can make books, with wheat you can make bread, with barley you can make ale, and many other things with all the crops you can grow. \nIn conclusion, once you have completed all these steps, just repeat them. It's as simple at that!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art Of Killing Undead", "silco97", "One might find undead to be scary or hard to kill when infact they are extremly simple to kill if you know the right way to do it. \nChapter 1 What to do When You See One-When you come across an undead do not use arrows, do not use your words or run away.  All these are hopless and will get you killed.  What you must do is get extremly close to your undead and do not get in any range so he can use lightning or fireballs.  If you stay close he will not be abel to do any of his magic effectivly. \nChapter 2 How To Fight Him-Now that you are this far with out dieing you should only use a iron sword or better.  If your using a diamond sword its simply a matter of haking him to death.  If not and you have an iron sword circle around him and get his health low enough so he starts running away.  At this point chase him and kill him. \nChapter 3 The Loot-The stuff you get from an undead is the best part now.  You will usually get a diamond sword or two and a golden staff.  The golden staff is the best part.  that is because they can be sol for up tp 1000 minas each.  So undead killing is quite a good way of making a quick \$.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Lumberjacking", "JoakimVonAnka", "Pickaxes, axes, hoes, bookshelfs and chests are good examples of things that wood is needed for. Therefore is The Art of Lumberjacking a important skill to master. Without wood it's almost impossible making anything. In this book I'm going to explain The Art of Lumberjacking and how it's should be executed. To begin with, you need a axe. You might find one in a nearby shop or you just craft one yourself. Train your lumberjacking skills with a wooden one until you reach level 5. This gives you the ability to be able to use a stone one. There is three sorts of logs and trees to be founded in Aegis. Oaks, birch and pine. The most common ones are oaks and pines. Therefore is redwood (The logs from pines) a important piece in elven architecture. Oak logs are also important in some human cities to. Except from these normal trees, there is a few very extraordanary ones. The willow in Ravenhold is a very good example of that. There is also many trees that still haven't been founded by a living soul. Now back to The Art of Lumberjacking. Remember to always use a axe of any kind while woodcutting. If you try to chop a tree with your fist, you will start taking damage. It's also good to know what the trees in Aegis drops. The most key item is logs. Logs is often used as building material, but also for wooden planks which is another drop from trees. Sticks is also obtainable from trees. Another key item is saplings. Saplings is the key to a successful tree farm and forest. From the placing of saplings you also level up in farming. The last thing that trees drop is apples. This is a very good drop because it gives the lumberjacker a good storage of food. The trees is very important for various of things. In the elven nation the trees are homes for many elves. For dwarfs the wood is needed for their tools and mineshafts. And for orcs and humans the wood is a important piece of their architecture. Therefore we should take care of our nature and always replant to keep our land as fertile as possible. This book is written by Asyrian...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Potion Brewery", "XSilverWolfX", "Potion brewing, also known as apotheracy, is a very complex thing to learn. The very basics themselves could be difficult for someone without a clever mind to wrap their heads around. All potions start with a base liquid. Most start with water, but in my years learning apotheracy from my mintour and with my own studies, I've learned slime gel and lava is used in some instances.                    There are different types of potions and different levels to those. Some potions can even be combined for double the effect if mixed properly. New combinations and potions are  being discovered constantly by people like myself and my mintour. Right now I'm learning about a potion that can slow down age and make you look younger. This is achieved by years of studying the elven body.  I know of mages who have mastered this technique, but with spells and not potions. Currently the best I've come up with is reversing age by ten years. Other potions I've learned over the years are swiftness, breathing underwater, and others that should not be mentioned here. It should also be noted that I have not mastered these by far. It takes years of studying and expirimenting. (( he did it to me too :l bookworm -erase (( he did it to me too :l", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of the Ale", "drplat", "Not many can boast to brew as fine as I, Petyr of AlKhazar. I have decided to write a book revealing some of my craft. I did not start out a fabulous brewer, no. The art of ale takes in-field experience to master. First off, I will describe our ingredients. We do use the typical ale ingredients, for a start. However, the Cat and the Fiddle Ale has some special parts. For instance, we add yellow wildflowers to our brew. Too many of these causes hallucinations, which is illegal. We use a legal limit that still causes some airy-headed pleasure. We have tried mushrooms in the past, but the taste was never satisfactory. Sometimes we add some cocoa to our special drafts for flavor. Second, I will describe the process our ale undertakes. The fermenting container is of extreme importance. I have tried all sorts of materials to use. Stone containers give a good flavor, but it is not rich enough. Birch has an awkward aftertasete, most say. We've even tried iron and gold containers! It tasted nasty. The secret, I've found, is Darkwood. This rare component provides a rich flavor, and feels very full and hearty. It accents the flavors we add. How long we brew for, I cannot say. I can't reval everything! The third step is filteration. We use fine wool filters to do this process. The maturation is what helps provide potency and feeling. The time of day you brew and the location are two key steps. After all of these long steps, the great results are obvious! Our beer is acclaimed across the land, even by dwarven taverns! I know you will enjoy it if you try. Present this book to me, and I will give you a 10m discount on your first beer! Thank you for reading, I hope to see you soon! - Brewer Petyr, of the Cat and the Fiddle.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of War", "urgeoholiker", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of War by Lord Achilles", "covcath", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of War Chapter I", "l337Ninja", "The art of war is of vital importance to the State. It is a matter of life and death, a road either to safety or to ruin. Hence it is a subject of inquiry which can on no account be neglected. The art of war, then, is governed by five constant factors, to be taken into account in one's deliberations, when seeking to determine the conditions obtaining in the field. These are: (1) The Moral Law; (2) Heaven; (3) Earth; (4) The Commander; (5) Method and discipline. The Moral Law causes the people to be in complete accord with their ruler, so that they will will follow him regardless of their lives, undismayed by any danger. Heaven signifies night and day, cold and heat, times and seasons. Earth comprises distances, great and small; danger and security; open ground and narrow passes; the chances of life and death. The Commander stands for the virtues of wisdom, sincerely, benevolence, courage and strictness. By method and discipline are to be understood the marshaling of the army in its proper subdivisions, the graduations of rank among the officers, the maintenance of roads by which supplies may reach the army, and the control of military expenditure. These five heads should be familiar to every general: he who knows them will be victorious; he who knows them not will fail. Therefore, in your deliberations, when seeking to determine the military conditions, let them be made the basis of a comparison, in this wise: Which of the two sovereigns is imbued with the Moral law? Which of the two generals has most ability? With whom lie the advantages derived from Heaven and Earth? On which side is discipline most rigorously enforced? Which army is stronger? On which side are officers and men more highly trained? In which army is there the greater constancy both in reward and punishment? By means of these seven considerations I can forecast victory or defeat. The general that hearkens to my counsel and acts upon it, will conquer: let such a one be retained in command! The general that hearkens not to my counsel nor acts upon it, will suffer defeat:--let such a one be dismissed! While heading the profit of my counsel, avail yourself also of any helpful circumstances over and beyond the ordinary rules. According as circumstances are favorable, one should modify one's plans. All warfare is based on deception. Hence, when able to attack, we must seem unable; when using our forces, we must seem inactive; when we are near, we must make the enemy believe we are far away; when far away, we must make him believe we are near. Hold out baits to entice the enemy. Feign disorder, and crush him. If he is secure at all points, be prepared for him. If he is in superior strength, evade him. If your opponent is of choleric temper, seek to irritate him. Pretend to be weak, that he may grow . arrogant. If he is taking his ease, give him no rest. If his forces are united, separate them. Attack him where he is unprepared, appear where you are not expected. These military devices, leading to victory, must not be divulged beforehand. Now the general who wins a battle makes many calculations in his temple ere the battle is fought. The general who loses a battle makes but few calculations beforehand. Thus do many calculations lead to victory, and few calculations to defeat: how much more no calculation at all! It is by attention to this point that I can foresee who is likely to win or lose.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art Of War Magic", "silco97", "1. The monment to prepare your offense is the moment the enemy becomes vulnerable to attack \n.Knowledge of the enemy mage's mind is of the foremost importance. Once you know his mind, you will know his weaknesses. \n2 The enemy's vulnerability may be his strongest point; your weakness may enable you to strike the decisive blow. \n3. When planning a campaign, take account of your destruction and healing. A skillful battlemage ensures that they are in balance; a weight lifted by one hand is heavier than two weights lifted by both hands. \n4. When the destruction and healing are in balance,the army will move effortlessly, like a swining door on well-oiled hinges.  When they are out of balance, the army will be like a three-legged dog, with one leg always dragging in the dust. \n5. Thus the army strikes a blow, it will be like a thunderclap out of a cloudless sky.  The best victories are those unforeseen by the enemy, but obvious to everyone afterwards. \n6. The skillful battlemage ensures that the enemy is already defeated before the battle begins.  A close fought battle is to be avoided; the fortunes of a war may turn aside the most powerful sorcery, and courage may undo the best-laid plans.  Instead, win your victory ahead of time.  When the enemy knows he is defeated before the battle begins, you may n not need to fight. \n7. Victory inbattle is only the least kinf of victory.  Victory without battle is the acme of skill. \n8.Conserving your power is another key to victory. Putting forth your strength to win a battle is no demonstration of skill.  This is what we call tactics, the least form of tthe art of war magic. \n9. The battle is only a leaf on the tree; if a leaf falls, does the tree die? But when a branch is lopped off, the tree is weakene; when the trunk is gridled, the tree is doomed. \n10. If you plan your dispsition well, your victories will seem easy and you will win no acclaim.  If you plan your dispostion poorly, your victories will seem difficult, and your fame will be widespread.  \n.Those commonly belived to be the greatest pratitoners of war magic are almost always those with the least skill.  The true masters are not known to the multitude.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ascended", "silco97", "The Vision \nThe Aengul, Aeriel, appeared to four of the Aenguls' most direct mortal descendants in the form of a mongoose, warning of a new threat of the World's Peace.  She told of an Ancient Evil that would reach out to taint the pure souls of Aegis, and that only they could fight it.  Aeriel awakened in these four the ancient knowledge of their immortal ancestors, granting them many boons. \nFour Become five \nThe four mortals, the elf Riizu and the dwarves Tsu, Candle, and Arcadius, set out in search of this new threat.  On their journey, they encounteres a fifth of the Aenguls' Bloodline, ans so awakened in him his inheritance.  The dwarf Omni, being a deaf mute, quickly grew frustrated with his in ability to communicate with his brothers. Sue knew of his malady and set about constructing a spell to allow Omni to speak.  When the spell was finished, though, it did not work as intended.  It did not grant Omni the ability to hear or speak, but instead forged a telepathic bond between the five brothers.  Finally being able to hear the others after a fashion, Omni told his brothers of how Aengul appeared before him and told him to travel. She did not say where to, only that he must walk a long way and would meet the others like himself. He was told that he must bring him a seedling from the Cloud Temple, and plant it only when he had reached a safe haven. \nHaven \nFor many days and nights the five travel, leaving small shelters along the way. Each time they stopped, they thought to make themselves a home, but Rizzu-who had taken", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ascended", "impymut", "They saved my father when I was young, they gave me at least one more day with him... How, Chembob?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ascended And The Undead", "Demonxerov2", "Now, if you dont know who these two are, your behind on your history Let me start by saying these two are completely different and you dont want to mess with eith er of them. Now lets start with the ascended. They are a race of angel like cratures that try to help people in need. There are very few that i know of, and they are quite peaceful there are also rumors that they are invincible. Now the undead are completely different. They are more of a hellish race, and bad dinner gues t. they constantly try  to stir up trouble and are hard to kill. They Also have some god named ibliss. Now that you know who these two are, You should know what to do if you are ever confronted by them.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassin's Beginning", "sx421", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassin's Creed", "legofanatix", "The wisdom of our Creed is revealed through these words. We work in the Dark to serve the Light. Where other Men blindly follow lies, remember nothing is true, everything is permitted. Where other Men are limited, by morality or by law, remember, nothing is true, everything is permitt ed. Nothing is true, everything is permitted. We are Assassins. By : Goleth", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassin's Story", "sx421", "I pooped my pants", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassin's Way", "legofanatix", "The wisdom of our Creed us revealed through these words. We work in the Dark to serve the Light. Where other Men blindly follow lies, remember nothing is true everything is permitted. Where other Men are limited by morality or law, remember nothing is true everything is permitted. Nothing is true, everything is permitted. We are Assassins. By Goleth", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassin.", "MinistryofGamess", "Guthan, the assassin, is a very greedy man. He does everything for money. He steals, robs and assassinates others for his own good. Though no guard was ever able to catch him. After he comitted a crime he disappeared in the shadows of the night. Rumours spread over the lands about his hiding place. Some say he lives in the wilderniss, far away from Al'Khazar. Others say he lives in the sewers, but one thing is sure, none shall find him. Other rumours concern about his childhood. The most legit one goes as follows. Guthan was a born thief, eversince he was born he tried to steal. He stole teats from other children, playing blocks and milk. When he grew up he stole soccer balls from his school during the breaks. He stole lunch from other children without them even knowing it. His parents tried to learn him not to steal, but they failed. A thief is who he is, and you can't change a person's personality. As Guthan grew up even more he started on the serious crimes; assassinations. The King's road is his, none shall pass without getting robbed. He uses his environment to hide, rob and disappear. You might never know when he steps up to you and threatens you. But you can't avoid him, Guthan is everywhere ...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassins Of Retra", "LROWNAGE", "By now you know who we are and the power we posess. After the recent assassination of your beloved corrupt official, we are now in power. We may be killers, but we are no butchers. The great daemon Retra has gifted us and sent us to do his work. We are his servants. No evil is inside this brotherhood, in fact we are saving Aegis from itself. The monarchs and leaders you know are corrupt, greedy. We are here to help you. Our deeds are not taken lightly, we make a monument to all who we release. We are respectful towards them. We shall be in the news a lot in the coming days, but fear not. From the evil world you know as Aegis, Retra shall lead us all into a new era of peace. The revolution has only just begun. We spill the blood of others, to save yours. We are the Assassins of Retra.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassins Tomb", "Jarhead90", "I grew up in a small village always wondering what it was like outside of my home. Our elders never let the childeren go out side past the village gates. They always said that evil forces lurked past the gates. Of course none of us belived them. But one day a boy named ALzar ventured past the gates. We herd yelling comeing from the forests. Screams of bloddy murder. A women ran from the woods. She was screaming \"ASSASSIN,ASSASSIN, he killed the boy\". Our village warrior went into the woods looking for ALzar. An hour later the warrior returned but no ALzar. The next day our elders said the stories where to wasn us about the assassins. They said that along time ago the assassins ruled all of our land. Everyday the assassins would torture and kill our people. Until one day a great warrior known throughout the land. He was the Great Roman. When he arrived he was wearing a marroon silk cape that only great riches could aford, a red and golden tunic stitched into it was pictures of lions and eagles, finally he had the most gold armor anyone would ever see. He said in a great voice \"I am here to kill the assassins. All of them. In return you shall give me your finest women, and your best cattle.\" Our elders agreed. The very next day our elders picked our finest women, and our best cattle. The Roman put is armor on for battle and went into the forest. We herd clashing of blades. The sound was of that of lightning strikeing the earth. In only 3 hours Roman returned. He brought the head of their leader. And said \"He deserves a tomb, build it and you can keep your women and cattle.\" So our village's finest builders built the most spectactular tomb you would ever see. And with that Roman left to hunt more fiends. Our builders and elders hid the tomb. And to this very day no one has found it. I am older now more adventurious too I will find the tomb. And have the sword of the assassin's in my hands. I will rule this land. For the fathers before me I will find it. \n Its been ten long years searching all of this land. Yet no tomb. Maybe it is just a story. NO! it cant be I will find the tomb no matter what. \n I have found the assassins tomb! I walk inside I see gold all around. Diamond sculptures. And then I see it the sword of their leader. I reach for it so swiftly. I cant belive I have the Assassin's sword. I shall defeat all of my enemies! No matter who! Then out of no where the man's village elders jump out. \"You have chose greed and power over your own friends and family\" the elders say simultaneous   -ly. \"You will pay for your glutany. NOW DIE!\" the elder adds. With a swift swipe of his hand the man turns into stone. With the sword clutched into his grips. The man got what he wanted the sword of the Assassins. But greed has a price my friends. Let this story teach you not to be greedy. Or thy shall be striken down by God.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assassins: Part I", "starkiller2010", "Chapter 1: The Creed \n The Assassins follow three main rules:  \n 1. Stay your Blade from the Flesh of an Inoccent. \n 2. Hide in Plain Sight. \n 3. Never Compromise the Brotherhood. \n  \n Chapter 2: The Maxim \n The Assassins have a maxim which was first said by one of the greatest Assassins of all time: Altair Ibn-La'Ahad. \n \"...Our Creed does not command us to be free. It commands us to be wise\" \n This comes to the main belief the Assassins follow \"Nothing is True; Everything is Permitted\" \n \n  More to come in  The Assassins: Part II...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Assualt of Al'Kazaar", "jontillmon", "Lighting was streaking across the sky, I ran up to the grand gates of Al'Kazaar. I knew nothing of", ""),
        StaticBook("The Atonomy Of A Slime", "silco97", "By: Ambros \nSlimes are the rarest of the monsters that creep in the night.  They also offer the best prize upon there death. When you kill a slime,if you kill it, you will recive a rather rare slime.  A slime ball, these balls of bluish green geletian consist of an unknown element that appears to be what keeps the slimes alive.  Through my studies I have found that the average slime comes in greens blues or even purples.  This usually depends on the climate in which you find the slime.  The slime's body is a large square surrounded by a thick layer of protecting that is sticky and smells.  The basic body is many cells grouped to form one large slime.  Which consists of a nucleus that controls the slime and many other smaller cells that have other functions.  Slimes have no need of mating though. You see when ingered a slime will brake into smaller slimes wich will eventually grow into adults. I find the best way to deal with unwanted slimes is to cirner them but leave a space for you to attack but make the place small enough so the slime cant hurt you.  Dealing with a slime in the open is rather risky and should not be attempted with out a bow.  The slimes are extremly dangeros because they have the ability to grab hold of you and suck the life out of you.  In conclusion slimes are rare finds and should be dealt with properly.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Attack", "jigg21", "It was a cool, damp night in Aegis. Thunder boomed in the distance as I look over the walls of the keep.. Over the horizon the dwarfs marched, marched into our territory. Clouds and lightning filled the skies the mortals were attacking our citadel. We quickly became outnumbered as many of my brothers died.. Vulgrak and I kept on fighting.. The mortals forces quickly grew and grew as we weakened and ran out of staffs. They invaded our fort with satisfaction in their eyes..  Vulgrak and I soon became the last warriors of Iblees as many were slain.. We kept our ground at top of the citadel, but soon we ran out of staffs.. They were advancing further and further up the keep.. They were slaying our minions.. Advancing towards us.. We knew we had to flee the area or suffer the same faither as the rest.. We quickly jumped off the citadel and rank far east. We heard the booming of battle cries in the distance soon they died down as we advanced further East.. We knew we were the last survivors..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Attack Of The Undead", "CornOnTheMob", "\n It was a cold night, freezing, as John closed the door of his house and settled in for the evening. \n He grabbed a loaf of bread, chewing thoughfully as he watched the fire burn. Then it happened, it was just a sudden scream from nowhere, he looked through his window, and He saw them. \n There were hundreds of them, running through the streets, attacking people. he didn't recognise them at first, but they we're grey, red eyes, full of rage. John grabbed his dagger, eyeing the window suspiciously. He climbed to the second story of his home as he watched the Undead ravage the city below. \n He looked down from the second story of his home, hefting his dagger, watching them. They attacked house after house, dragging out victims and killing them, soulless eyes staring down at them. John shuddered. \n It was a while later then, the undead were still out there, going through house after hous e. He thought he was safe, but then they spotted him. \n They all suddenly ran to his door, breaking through with ease, he tried to hide hoping they wouldn't see, but they did. \n He knew his only hope was to escape. Luckily, his second floor had a door which he thought to barricade, so he had time, he broke his window, and jumped. \n He came to seconds after, the undead coming back to him, his legs were in agony, but he rna, going for the woods, hoping to live. He went for miles, never looking back, then he fell in a cave. \n He woke hours later, the dawn brilliantly coming up through the hole he fell in. He was in a cave, John noted, a luckily monsterless cave. He looked up through the ohle. It was a straight cliff up, no real handholds, his leg were sprained anyways. He knew his only way out was through the cave, he seemed to vaguely remember it , It must've been a cave he visited in years past. Long ago. He rubbed his legs a bit and wen t off.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Attack on Celestine", "AlphaCentaurus", "I was in my house when it happened. It started with the sound of shouts and ringing metal. Given how quiet Celestine usually was, I went out to see what the commotion was. \n When I arrived, I saw clusters of men in armor fighting at the gates. Sword rang on sword and muffled screams and grunts poured from the mass. Rows of archers poured arrows into the ranks of soldiers. \n My first question was: Who were these people? They looked like commoners, with no uniforms or distinct markings. Their equipment ranged from highly wealthy to a mere wooden stick. I wondered why they were here, after that. Celestine was too far out of the way for mere bandits, but too passive for any sort of organized army. \n But I needed to act first and ask questions later. I pulled out my bow and began to fire shots at the opposing army. It was hard to tell who was who underneath the armor, but I didn't do much in any case. Most of my arrows dashed off of armor. Occasionally one would hit flesh and sink in deep, bringing a matching scream. \n Dashing towards the conflict, I saw the entrance to the gatehouse. Luckily we had prepared for events such as these, and had taken appropriate measures. I hit the switch for the drawbridge and four armored men fell into the pit below. I then went forward to join the conflict with my sword. \n What happened next is a jumbled mess of events. I remember the stink of sweat and the sticky feeling of wet blood under my hands. Flashes of pain would cut their way across my back and hands as enemies struck. As soon as we thought we had killed all of them another wave rose up behind the first. The guards had never trained for anything like this. For the most part we were mere militia. Our only advantage was better equipment. But we still faltered. Step by step, we were pushed back. I saw friends and fellow guards fell to either side of me. Their faces were obscured by helmets, so I did not know who fought beside me. Just that we fought for the same thing. Celestine. \n We would surely have failed if not for the Teutonic Order. I don't know why they helped us. But they rose up behind the enemy, ranks and ranks of armor and blades. They slammed into the enemy like a battering ram.  \n Soon, there was no one left. The battlefield stood quiet. As we cleared away our wounded, I gazed up at the walls with an expression of sadness for those who we lost. But at the same time, I looked on with a feeling of pride. For despite the odds, Celestine still stood strong.", ""),
        StaticBook("the attack on the rebel camp", "roflcats", "we where told to line up at the fountain. we assembled the orc hoard and advanced on on the camp we told them to leave we gave them a day. they didnt. we attacked and killed them and looted everysingle chest. we then retreated we came back for a secand attack and most of the fighting begins. we burned and destriyed the camp we then went back for a third attack we captured and executed the humans and destryed the whold camp finish help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Attunement Ceremony - Forging the Link", "drplat", "For a Dedicant, the attunement ceremony is the final step of initiation. This forges a link between nature, the rest of the Druidic Order, and themselves. The guide leading the ceremony must be careful to do such properly. \n I personally choose to do this ceremony by the Birch Pond. I have them close their eyes, and I begin to coax their minds into accepting the spirits of n ature around them. At first, I merely whisper to their minds, hoping to soften their natural defenses. Once their mind is unshielded, it is possible for enlightenment occur. It is different for everyone, but most report vivid images of the forest talking to them. In my opinion, the visions should not necessarily be told to everyone. They reveal something true about a person's inner being which should only be known to them. Of course, later, they may choose to use this information when choosing a title or totem. \n The correct chanting must be performed and not stopped until you have internally communicated with the Dedicant afterwards. Be wary of pushing on the Dedicants to forcefully, for the mind is a fragile thing. Make sure that while forging the link, they do not react negatively, harming your mind as wel l as their own. \n Scribed by Petyr the Salmon Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("The Autobiography Of Dammon Othmar", "sniperking90100", "I was born on the Twenty-ninth day of the First month on a forgotten season born from the womb of my mother, Viktoriya, and of the seed of my father, Nekoda. I spent most of my childhood in the outskirts of the Oren Capital city in a small farm house, helping my father with the wheat and my mother with the house work. Although no matter how much I worked my father was never satisfied. My mother on the other hand was kind always telling of stories of Robin Hood and his many tales of ingenuity and thievery. I knew since the moment I was born get along with each other, they constantly argued with one another normally ending with father beating my mother or threating her with her life and once mine. Countless seasons came and went. When I came to age (roughly sixteen) I was to start a right of passage. But right before my right before my right of adulthood, my mother went missing and my passage was blocked until she was found, as father was hesitant to explaidn, she was necessary for the passage. After a week of searching for my mother, the city guard kicked down the door to my home and knocked me and my father unconscious........... and I saw the Dark, Silent entity of the void... ......When I awoke I found myself covered in cuts and bruises and looking up surrounded by Iron bars, stone and two small beds, one I laidd in and on where a broken man laid. I walked up to the mysterious man; He was covered in dried blood and bandages and before I could speak the words I was looking for a man, who I suspected to be the jailor, threw open the prison door, pushed me aside and picked up the wounded man with a faint crack in his bones. As they left I saw through the bandages I finally recognized the man's face, it was the face I had known all my life, it was the face of my father. My father never came back. I lived in that god forsaken place for what seemed an eternity. In that time I learned much. I learned why I was here from the insults of the prison guards. The day I was taken away, a villager found the mutilated corpse of my mother and had hanged my father for the crime, and that they burned the farm during the search for evidence. I on the other hand was a supposed accomplice in the endeavor and was to serve for twenty seasons. When I was able to leave that little spot of damnation. I was given the bloodied clothing worn by my father and a kick in my rear. I walked to what seemd the ancient remains of my former home and searched the wreckage knowing that I would find little to nothing. But among the burnt lumber and charred stone I found a wind worn cloak, stuck due to a piece of timber. As I grabbed the cape I also found a surprisingly intact tome, I picked it up and read the almost golden title, \"Robin Hood\". After I saw that story book I realized that I had spent so many seasons honing those same skills that Robin Hood had, and so I decided that I would follow the same path as him. For many years I stole and killed for currency along until I, Ironically, was stabbed and left for dead by a bandit. I walked for many days crossing mountains and deserts along with a countless number of the Undead, attacking me every moment of my travels. That was until I saw a man building a tower on the coast. That man's name was Jullian Septimus. He offered me shelter and food , he also told me of Verreberek, He spoke of a \"Port in the Storm\" . A place deep in the north where people can rest and thrive......... I have decided to help this man with his goals and be of what use to this dream.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ayleids", "Minnan1", "help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ayleids Volume I", "Minnan1", "Chapter I: Meaning of Ayleid \n \nAyleids, also known as The Ancient Ones or Hearthland High Elves , where the first and most powerful race in the world. Their name comes from unknown origins, although is rumored that the words Ayler (Wise) and Eidsan (Ones) might've been the creators of the name Ayleids , wich would be translated as The Wise Ones. Very little is known about their language and culture, for they were seized by the human empire during the First Era. Ayleids are known to posses the most powerful magic and knowledge of all beings. Most of this knowledge was erased to prevent catastophic events in the world.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ballad of Chris", "Groundhawg", "A man named Chris he came to town! \n He didn't know he'd make us frown. \n He bought a house, so humble strong. \n He didn't know he'd not be here long. \n He sold his wares from out the door. \n The shattered law lay on the floor. \n   The guard came to take him in. \n He ran so fast he escaped Flynn! \n To the chapel he did go.  \n Priests locked the door with Chris on show! \n Chris hid with them, hid from the guard. \n Had they been able they'd hit him hard! \n The guard and priests they fought with words! \n Across the city, the shouting was heard! \n Three days, three nights the battle ran! \n Three days, three nights with sword in hand! \n Until one day agreement was found. \n Throw him out, out on the ground! \n And to this day he can't return! \n For if he does he'll surely burn. \n The guard now know his little tricks.  \n They'd kill him fast, if just for kicks! \n And now you know the tale of Chris! \n If you see him, don't give him bliss! \n Kick his ass and take his name! \n In the end his life he'll miss!", ""),
        StaticBook("the ballz", "FalseImpact", "the ballz were big", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ban", "Maiavel", "\nThe Great Druid can impose a strong, nonviolent sanction upon those who have offended the circle. All must shun someone placed under the ban; no druid in the circle will aid, speak to, or associate with the target of the ban. When an entire town or village suffers the ban, no druid may enter that area or speak to or aid any resident. Some druidic allies volunteer to follow the custom of the ban as well. \nThe great druid has the right to pronounce a ban on any druid in the circle. A ban also can cover nondruids, whole communities, or druids visiting from other domains (except the Grand Druid and personal servants), to demonstrate the circle's displeasure. \nTo pronounce the ban, the great druid stands up during a moot and announces to the group the reasons to impose the ban. Then the subject of the ban--if present--answers the accusations before the assembly. Finally, the High Council of the Moot votes on the matter openly, usually at sunset. If a majority of the council votes in favor of the ban, it passes. If not, the great druid should start keeping an eye on the circle's archdruids--the opposition to the ban likely reflects an impending challenge. \nA ban punishes a druid for violating the tenets of the druidic order or reprimands a character whose actions, while within the bounds of the druidic ethos, nevertheless were contrary to the Order's interests. A ban generally lasts 10 summers. However, the inner circle can vote to lift a ban early or (once the time is up) to extend it. The shunning does not extend outside the domain, so banned druids usually choose to go into exile--the result the great druid probably intended in the first place.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bandit", "jessbot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Banstir Family", "TheMiner15", "they where jewish", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bard", "Respiren", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Basics of Alchemy", "silco97", "If you are reading this book right now it probebly means you are intrested in alchemy.  Well you have opened the right book because this book will explain anything and every thing you need to know for a starting alchemist. \nChapter 1 The Supplies \nAt first alchemy may seem overwhelming to you.  When infact to become a good alchemist you need the right materials.  So it is indeed very overwhelming, this is ok many great alchemits started out how you are now, young, brave, and stupid.  This chapter will explain how you can one day become a good alchemist.  \nBowls-This is a very importent supply as you will be mixing all of your ingredients in this bowl. \nBucket-This is needed for collecting hazerdous materials such as lava. \nProper Working Place-You need a quite working place in order for you to concentrate as messing up could prove fatel. :;Furnace-This will be used for smelting materils to change its chemical compound into something else. \nCrafting Table-This is used for mixing materils to form the desired material. \nChapter 2 Basic Compounds-You must be woundering what is a compound. Well In this book you will find the answers you so desire.  A compound is a mixture of elements that are mixed to form a new mixture.  In this section you will learn about the compounds every alchemist should know.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle at Alstion", "123devmo321", "I charged up the tower, fire all around me. I heard the terrible screams of men and women being slaughtered by the beasts. An insane man yelled that \"The Fallen One\" would win, devour our souls. I got to the top of the tower, looked at the... thing... that was causing the mayhem. ....Maybe I should tell you how this all happened. It all started on a bright sunny morning, a very peacefull day. I was on an ordinary walk to Alk'Khazar to meet some of my friends. When i heard General Giffords yelling at some guards to armor up. I asked what was going on, but the General wouldn't tell me. Seems he didn't really know himself. They departed towards the north, so I followed. Soon time shifted, darkness filled Aegis, we were all terrible confused. Lightning soon started to tear open the sky in great,vivid flashes of blue light. blue light. The guards and i charged into Alstion, it was a war-zone. Dead bodies laid in the streets, zombies roamed the city. The few survivors fought valiantly against the creatures, but stood no chance without the reinforcments. Being a druid, I cleared the area, then opened a makeshift medical tent, where I healed the many injured. After about two hours of intense battle, The Wandering Wizard showed up. He helped us secure the area, and I saw my opporitunity. Now, back to where I left off. I was face to face with this creature, scared out of my mind. I could sence it's evil, I could smell it's rotting flesh. I attacked, swung my sword at him and pushed him off the tower. He fell to his death. The battle was won, the lightning has stopped. Victory to the living once more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle at Snowy feilds II", "XxDukesterxX", "So the Battle was one, we gathered all our resources, tendered to the injured and Upgraded the wall. Me and my Mercenrie friend Were ordered to Rebuild the broken outta wall. We where strictly ordered to build the wall 7 High and 3 wide, The wall was Mighty , Suddenly, The alarm raised once again, The Undead, Had returned for more. I was situated to lead the Bowman into the Battle, I told my Bowman to Scale the walls and and get the High ground. My bowman where scared, I could see it in their eyes, But no matter they would fight to the death . Suddenly, the mixed army of the Undead became in Range of our Bows, We Unleashed hell on them But it wasnt enough, The smashed against the wall like water on rock. Destroying all in their Path, Then, Orpheus Fell to his death, It was down to me. We fell back to the centre city in the safety of the Inner walls I ordered the men to hide for the Ambush, And then, there was silence. Suddenly the Gate came crashing down, the Undead flooding in like an Angry Mob . I gave the order to my fearful troops to attack, so then it began, We fort Well, We fort Hard. the battle raged on for Days and nights, Suddenly The Leader of the Undead attack fell of the City walls, Men and elves Laughed loudly as their Leader fell to his death, The Undead Routed, We had won the battle once again. The next day When all men and Elves where sleeping, They came, Silently They burned all buildings inside the city and turned the city, Into ruin. And that is the Story, of Snowy feilds.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Celestine", "firespirit44", "One day, Queen Cassandra came to speak to our Hochmeister, Gaius Marius in Nuremberg. I was standing guard outside with the rest of the Sarients. She pleaded for help, that her town Celestine was going to be attacked under false rumours. Gaius, being a noble and wise Hochmeister, agreed that the attack was unjustified, and has promised the orders full backing for Celestine. Intel came in that there was a strike force of more than 30 people headed towards Celestine, accompanied with Ascended Battle Mages. They called themselves the \"Free Comapny\" Our Hochmeister rounded up the Sarients, barked out orders to the OrdenMarshal, and to the man to ge ar up. We're headed for war. We assembled about 10 veteran fighters. The names if I can recall are: Jorgen, Samuel, Mirtok, Ventraux, Syblix, Calanon, Calamori, Viadar, Nroca, We split our forces into two, and hid on both sides of the road. When the men from the \"Free Company\"  cam rushing to the gates, we rushed out from hiding and killed all of them It was a bloodbath, we did not lose a single man. It was a glorious battle, we eliminated over a third of the attacking force. After the battle we wen t to the Celestine Tarvern and ate cake and drank ale merrily. Markus! help Fuck. help me store this", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Galahar", "ikeyman232", "It was still a chilly day, during the Harvest. Snow ws still on the ground here. The Teutonic order had the city, but rebels retook it. Then the fighting begins. Teutons versus rebels. From my view, I believe it was the Rebels who controlled the city. Arrows upon arrows flew across the sky, the sky covered in a silvery-gold. Taunts and remarks filled the ears. Confused passer by try to join the fghting, or leave off. Hooded rebels be firing from the rooves, and lowly soldiers wait on the grown. One by one, soldiers are hit, falling, facing death strait. This might be named the most confused battle in history. No one knows which side is which. The rebels are fighting for who knows... They control the city, but they are warning of an Orc war party approaching. The rebels have opened the gates, but opened the trap. Now the real fighting begins. I've seen many hit with arrow, and many bleeding out. Inocents are now being hit. The Dwarven legion is here. People will now die. Soldiers from all sides are shooting and shooting, no swords have been used. Thrym! I've found a friend. The Orcs are with the Loyalists. Dwarves with the rebels. Eze'kiel Tarus is the head. \n Tarus says that he got the idea to rebel, from an old friend. \n They fight for A new ruler. No \"King Errors\" \n They are fighting the Orcs and Cross. \n They are with The Dwarves and Orens military. \n Shoi and many Ascended are here, for a reason I do not know.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle OF Kal'Urguan", "Ratemenatorz59", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Kramore", "scout3399", "A book on the recent battle in Kramore. I was there... it twas a good fight. (How do you delete writings from books.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Krumgar: A Dwarven Druids Tale", "Saviordude", "It started like any other day, I was at tha grove tending to tha plants when John came up to me. He asked me if I wanted to go and help the orc, because he got a letter sayin' something bad was goin' to 'appen. Being the helpful lad that I am, I agreed and set off with 'im. As we neared tha city, I could 'ear the sound of thunder, and the sky was alight with flashes of light. Enterin' through the gates, I could see that the city was in chaos. Zombies swarmed the sands, and the air was filled with arrows shot by the skeleton archers. We pushed through the mob, and we reached the entrance to Sanjezal. All around us, brave warriors from every race clashed with the monsters, as they attempted to assault the undead keep that had been spawned. Takin' up are positions, we lent our aid to the injured, makin' sure that they could continue tha fight. Finally, we managed to crawl into tha fortess, dodging tha fireballs of tha ghasts. We were bein' pushed back, and I thought we wouldn't make if. Then, as if blessed by god 'imself, an orc lifted 'is blade and struck down the leader of the undead. With their command gone, they fled the field of battle, vowing to return. And with their departure the cries of tha victories rang out. In tha end, we 'ad lost many lifes. The capital of Krumgar was damaged, and it would take months to repair it all. But we 'ad showed that we can prevail against Iblees on our own. And next time he shows up, we'll do it again.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Sanhar", "Pepernoot", "The beginning of the battle was not in Sanhar, but in Al'Khazar. But that was just a diversion of the undead. The real battle started at noon, when the sun was at its highest point. And the real force of the undead arrived when night fell over Sanhar. \n Suddenly screams and battle taunts filled the air. Fireballs were hitting the city, and lightning struck the Orc warriors. The orcs responded with warscreams, and formed formations, while trying to avoid being hit by the magical strikes. Orc archers fired back at the undead, and some arrows even hit. But a lot of orcs fell, and were wounded. Some of the people who helped fled, in fear of their lives. But there were too many orcs for the undead to kill. Brave orcs charged towards them, and died while trying to kill the undead. The undead tried to stay in a tower, but the orcs fought them off. Some orcs believe the spirits of Krugmar helped them in the battle. \n \n Even though the undead had damaged the city, which was being rebuild the orcs managed to recover and repair the city in days. \n \n This report was written by Cerlos, with help from the eyewitness, and fighter in the battle Shaman Krink \n 30th of Suns Smile, 1315.", ""),
        StaticBook("The battle of sanhar", "mingsly", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Snowy Feilds", "XxDukesterxX", "Our story begins At the gates of Oren . I and A friend of mine where Travelling Mercenaries, I being Elf and him being Human. We came across the Grand Lands of Oren when we came to their Capital city, However. The city was under great Fear, Word had it that the Undead where attacking the Guild of KotF At Snowy feilds They gathered their Best warriors to Aid the Men at Snowy feilds, We went with them as we had To help our Friends at Snowy feilds. It was a long March, We lost half our men on the way due to Disheartening from the Lightning. We eventually Arrived, after a long march, we made it. The city had almost fallen, we had arrived in the nick of time, We ran straight towards the city gate, Battle cries everywhere. Suddenly an Undead army Rised up in front of the gate, The two forces smashed together Clashing Armour With bones, We overcame the first wave. We came into the city like a flood of water, We fort hard, but well Orpheus' battle orders were spread over the battlefeild, Then. We spotted the Enemy Leader. On a rooftop around 180 feet high, No man could kill him surely? But I was there, Headbowman of the South, I set up my Target and I shot a deadly Arrow into his flesh . The Undead Leader, Had fallen. The enemy fled North over the Mountains, Into shadow. The day had been ours! We toasted our Drinks in memory of the Men and Elves we lost in the Battle. But no matter what, The Undead will return to Snowy feilds . Eventually, But we shall be ready.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of South Laurien", "Saviordude", "The sky shook as magic carved it's way from the heavens to the treetops of Laurien. Me an Lex'Lur ran throught the city, trying to get to the source of the attack. Climbing the trees, we avoided the fireballs that were thrown at us. Finally getting past the flames that were eating away at the city, we saw her standing on the highest tree. It was her, Cassandra. \"It is Cassandra herself, there is no hope!\" came a cry from the crowd. But lo, Prince Native himself appeared, and he rallied us against our attackers. \"Slay the ghouls that claw at our feet!\" he cried. So with sword in hand, I joined the soldiers in their tasks. As soon as we dealt with them another threat arose. \"The sky!, look at sky!\" Looking up, I shouted in fear. The sky swarmed with ghasts, raining death upon us. Scrambling to mount a defense, many allies died in the resulting attack. We finally managed to take them down, one brought down by my own arrow. Iblees's power waned, and his curse of night was lifted. Weakened, Cassandra left, and we set to work putting out the fires. In the aftermath many lifes were lost, and Prince Native was wounded. But we had defended Laurien, and the trees would live to see another day.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Takien Falls", "SuperZac", "It was not long ago from the time of this writing that a great Battle took place at Takien Falls. Nae, I doubt you have heard of this place; it is deeper into the wilds than even the great Explorers of Malinor had ever ventured. Word of this battle did not reach many ears, it was only by chance I even heard tell of it. I was just sitting in my library, thinking, when I heard a pounding on my gate. Investigating, I found a bloodied man, nearly too weak to stand. He claimed to be the lone survivor from his side of a battle, and he had traveled many leagues searching for help. I knew his time was near and there was nothing I could do to save him, and yet, I was intrigued. I am not a cruel elf, so I let him in and brewed him a tea of hern leaves to ease the pain of his final hours. Sitting him down in my favorite chair, I beseeched him to tell me his story. So it was that I recorded, in full, the Battle of Takien Falls:  \"My name is General Hakim, of the Seventh Tribe. I come from the far north, where there are Seven tribes of Humans, Elves, and Dwarves living unkown to the multitude of Aegis. We live in quiet indifference to the troubles of the people down here. Honest work and peaceful existence are our two codes. And yet, in all places where intelligent beings dwell, there must be some disturbance. 'Tis ineviteable; whether it be gold, power, or simple wickedness, none can live in peace for long. Since the formation of our tribes, naught but two centuries ago, the Orcs have always wanted a place in our Counsels. Alas, there were those of us who shunned the orcs, and that mistake has costed us dearly ever since. The orcs formed the Eight Tribe, and they built a city of their own not far away from our tribal clusters. They mostly to themselves, but occasionally, battles broke out and political slander exchanged. Thirty years ago, Aelpho'Razok took up the leadership of the Eight Tribe. While in the past some of leaders had been aggresive, this Razok was practically insane. He bided his time for those thirty years, learning the secrets of dark Sorcery. Seven days ago, he began rallying his people for war. Without warning, the great army of orcs laid waste to tribe after tribe, a fell mix of primal bloodlust and Razok's evil sorcery. So it was that us of the Seventh Tribe woke that morning to see six thick pillars of black smoke rising from each of the Tribe's respective towns. We amassed our forces, which were significantly greater than those of the the other tribes, and prepared to meet with the Orken army at our gate. At that time, a fierce thunderstorm struck, and the sky was filled with drops of water and bolts of white fire. Then, the orc invaders hit us. At first, we had the upper hand because of our skilled archers. But alas, they were only skilled because of our prowess for hunting, and the rest of our warriors were mediocre. It was then that we found that the orcs had been trained since birth to fight in hand-to-hand combat. Our ranks were mowed down easily. We were already almost outnumbered when Razok, curse his name, appeared and began his Dark chants. Suddenly, the orcs retreated! We of the Seventh Tribe were jubiliant for a few moments, thinking that we had finally driven off the invaders. Then, the first bolt struck. At first, we thought it to be normal lightning, as we were in a thunderstorm. But we quickly discovered the truth. This bolt did dissapear. No, it stayed, growing thicker and turning a purplish hue. Without warning, a barrage of these fell purple sparks began raining down into our ranks. Explosions filled the air, and I could see my men being thrown into the sky only to crash down to the dirt, (or onto a fellow soldier), and lay there, motionless. 'That was why the orcs retreated,' I thought to myself. 'They didn't want to be blasted as well.' A bolt of lightning exploded near me, and I saw no more. When I awoke, I was aware that I was covered with debris and corpses. Struggling out of the wreckage, I found my self at the base of a large pile composed mostly of what was previously my beloved village, and its inhabitants. The stone wall still stood, and on the other side of the sooty, fenced-in clearing, the orcs feasted and made merry. I was filled with a manical anger then, and, seeing the scum Razok among them, I lifted a nearby sword and charged at him. He nor his soldiers had time to react; I had pierce d the beast's heart before he had even seen what was running at him. And as the blade ran through his unworthy flesh, a surge of energy pulsed through the air, and his corpse exploded within a great ball of purple fire. I remember nothing after that until I woke up on the shores of a strange, icy lake. I was weak and vulnerable, but I managed to struggle through the Wilds, until I stumbled upon this place. You know the rest.\" His narrative complete, I could tell he was in a considerably weaker state than before he started. \"Brother,\" I told him. \"You and I both know you have naught long to live. Such plights take a heavy toll on the body.\" I was indeed sorry. He replied, with a trace of a grin on his face, \"Aye, my good elf, I know it. But remember this: The orcs may have destroyed our city and our people, but the Seventh Tribe shall stand forever.\" With this, he clasped my shoulder, and he was no more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of the Manor", "The_Blind_Seer", "War has been declared on the Manor down the road It has been aproved by the Queen, Cheers are heard through Al'Khazar .  The Captain has rallied his troops. The streets rumble as the army of Al'Khazar march their way to their foe. Its getting closer, the quiet before the storm begins.   The first Lightning has erupted as they begin to cross the river,  As they enter the river many lightning strikes hit one spot tearing through the first wave of attackers. The battlefield is slilent, much death is everywhere. people lieing in the sand scorched and burnt. The second wave attacks, taking out the two in the manor, a Gaurd has succesfully entered, believing they have one. Lighting struck once more, more fighting and death fill the grassy manors fields. The last of the Undead were killed off, yet lightning still strikes, Al Khazar has won. \n \n In memory of those who lost their lives in the battle. \n The Al'Khazar Gaurds \n The Gaurdians \n The International Army              \n   \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Wrath's clutch", "Dendrophile99", "It was a cold night and lightning had filled the sky with its unholy glow, i had ventured out of the city of Kal'Urguan to see where the lightning was coming from.  All of a sudden I hear shouts from the brave dwarf skippy, shouting that a wolverine fella named Orik was captured. I was naturally scared but I   venuted anyway, with campington at my side, when I arrived it was chaos. Lightning and shouts of the wounded, the cackles of the undead, this was no  skirmish, it was a battle!  I met up with Stronghold and we both took shots at the undead on their high  spires.  I was hit by lightning and quickly scurried to the nearest water, my skin and armor scorched, I prevailed like those around me, the battle seemed hopeless. Then there was a shout, a command telling the men that the back entrance had been breached. I quickly ran to the back of the fortress  to enter, but to no avail, all around me men fell. I was hit by something, and drowning in water I struggled for survival and hiding. I had been scared, ducking for cover, but then i saw it, my fellow dwarves charging before me advancing through the mess of men and undead, I quickly rose up  charged in and was back in   the battle, fighting my way in the fortress.  As we advanced, there was a shocking discovery, we had turned the corner and there was too many undead minions to count!  We slew the minions with zeal and ferosity and moved on to the inner keep.  There my comerades slew the undead in all their unholiness.  We Quickly secured the tower and rescued any prisoners the undead had captured.  There were many cheers and horahs fer the men, we had overcome the odds, for justice.  Victory, victory was ours, I could have not imagined  I lived and all because of the Ascended.  They protected us, sacrificed their lives fer us, and won us the battle.  Many will celebrate, however I will return to Kal 'Urguan, garb me self  some ale, and remember the fallen. ;; Guard Gragon of Kal'Urguan", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Wrath's Clutch", "Amethain", "The battle is nearing and an uneasy silence falls over the camp.  There is no more continuous taunting by Kane and his ally Dusk.  All is silent, the calm before the storm. I hear a call, \" All wardens to the outpost for a pre-battle meeting.\" With my pulse pounding I enter into the Officer's building.  I know while we are having our counsel of war, the other races are as well.  Orcs, Men, and Dwarves alike, all planning the same massive assault on the undead keep of Wrath's Clutch.  Our officers decide upon a plan, I am to assist in a flanking manouvere base with two other wardens.  We set out from the base long before the battle is to begin. \nWe circle far around the enemy's fortress and reach the far side of Wrath's Clutch.  From there I was seperated from the other two wardens.  Unsure of what to do I returned to the outpost and joined the main assault against the Clutch.  I was uneasy and fearful,  the undead's thunder roared across the battlefield.  The battle cry sounds and we race across the open sands to the relative safety provided by the walls.  The undead lightning was striking all around us, my head began to throb from the endless noise.  The walls were breached and we flood into the Clutch.  I was running through those dark and narrow passages searching for enemies, when I hear a shout and cry of death. It was an elf, I see the villian who killed my kin and give pursuit.  He turned a moment too late, as I bring my iron sword crashing through his head, thus ending his corrupted life. \nThe thunder has lessened considerably as I make my way into the courtyard, where a great battle was underway.  The foul undead had summoned ungodly amounts of skeletons, zombies and and other abominable creatures.  The dwarves were nowhere to be seen and the men and elves were losing strength.  After the creatures had been vanquished we searched the keep looking for the undead necromancers.  I descended into the lower levels of the keep which lead underground.  I was attacked from behind and knocked unconscious. \nMy head throbbed mercilessly when I awoke, I had been stripped of all my armor and weaponry.  I cautiously crept up the stairs and came upon a set of iron armour which I promptly put on.  I had a set of armor but nothing to fight with except my hands. I returned to the ground level of the keep only to find the battle raging on.  The wardens had managed to corner the damned undead in their spires, but were unable to overcome them.  I ran seeking shelter as lightning smote the ground all around me.  I felt the intense heat burn my flesh and nearly cook me alive in the iron armor. \nMaking quick glance up the spire I see the undead spewing lightning and fire across the battlefield.  I see Wrath himself laying waste to our troops with his magical golden staff and dark powers.  I dive for cover as another blast of lightning and fire ignites the battlefield of Wrath's Clutch.  I see many bodies falling off the tall tower, as well as much weaponry and tools falling into the shallow waters.  I dive into the water and gather as many tools and weapons as I can hold.  In the safety of the ruined clutch  I examined what I had gathered.  A few stone implements, chain armor, and a magical staff like I had seen Wrath using to destroy our men.  I did not want the enemy to re-obtain one of these powerful staves o I left for a short while the battle to ensure the safety of the magic staff.  Upon arriving back at the forward walls of our base I see one of my superiors, Glade Guard Arthane Lazul. I showed him the staff and placed it into his care for the remainder of the battle. \nI then returned to the front lines, and could see that the battle had raged on while I was away.  Through the noise of battle I faintly hear a lady shouting.  I was unaware who she was, as I could not see her.  I realized that she was in distress when she began shouting about how she was at the top of the spire held captive by the undead sorcerors.  There was a large hole in the wall at the bottom of the spire, which opened to the ladder, which led to the top of the spire.  Me and our allies fought our way to the floor below the roof only to find obsidian blocking further acension.  We were stalled for a while in this room before I dislodged some of the cobblestone from the walls and created a way up to the roof of the spire.  We leaped onto the rooftop and began destroying every evil creature in sight.  The lady was screaming throughout the whole fight, which did not last long.  With the tower won, and the fell creatures subdued we began our descent with the lady.  She was quickly escorted off of the battlefield whilst I returned to the ever raging battle. \nLighting poured down once again with renewed energy and I hear Ariel shout \"Flee my followers!\"  All of the leaders began shouting \"Retreat! Back to the outpost!\"  Our entire army ran through the gates as massive explosions began to shake the entire outer wall.  I a shout \"Put out those fires!\"  I raced to the walltop with many others and we beat out the flames.  It felt like a losing battle against the fires, as I would put one out ten more would spring up from the constant downpour of lightning.  I can see the flashes everywhere, the roaring of the thunder is almost unbearable now. \nI then hear a loud cheer arise from the ranks \"HUZZAH! The battle is won!\"  Wrath had been defeated.  I felt only sorrow at this moment. Yes, Wrath had been defeated, but at what cost? I look out over the battlefield and tears sprang to my eyes.  Fires still raged across the across the trees nearby and many brave souls bodies burned in the morning light. The undead necromancer must have paid close attention to the beautiful trees surrounding the battlefield as they were burning out of control.  I could only watch in agony as they burned to the ground.  I wept that day for all my fallen comrades many of whom I did not know their names. \nThe Clutch is being reclaimed by nature, grass springs up out of the scorched ground inside the courtyard.  Trees and flowers were planted there as well.  I wander aimlessly through the bloodied ruins.  From the walltop I see Prince Mylas erecting a memorial for our fallen kin. The battle of Wrath's Clutch is over.  We have won.  I shall never forget the valiant oldiers who gave their lives to remove the foul undead from the land.  Here I end my tale of the battle of Wrath's Clutch.  ~Warden Initiate Amethain", ""),
        StaticBook("The Battle of Wrath's Clutch", "Da_Emperors", "During the battles of Undead and Humans, Wrath's Clutch is one never to be forgetten. The Battle took many nights and days but lasted with the glow of lighting. The Orgins of this battle took place in near the fort where the Elves made a fort. There fort was one that was a ok one but the trees made easy targets and burnable. Death was near for them. Raids and Attacks took place for a full week (IRL). Until the dwarfs can in for the final push. The Elves where not able to kill of Wrath nor would have ever. The Dwarfen Legion was the side turner that finished off the sides. The Final siege broke into the walls and took out nearly all of Wrath's Men. I survived. About 5 men and Wrath's Wife where alive and hide done in the Mines. As Wrath and the Undead Lighting striked the Fort and killed Ascended. They had managed to capture the QUeen Cassie of Celestine.. One Ascended Warlord came into my face and tryed to kill me off with lighting. I am finsihed him and killed off more. That night i killed of 20 people . I remeber the screams of children and blood of women in the streets. I remeber the undead looking over me as if they wished to kill me for not killing more! I can not write anymore about that, ask me in person. In the end of the battle, The Elves and the Dwarfs had won. The Undead left the FOrt and Wrath amde a new one. However Wrath did get quite the Gold from the battle. The Elves may have won but where the biggest losers. They lost over 80% of there warden force in the battle and the fort. The Fort is in Ruins now with a memorial that makes others remeber what occured that night. Read Wrath's Cluth for more information.", ""),
        StaticBook("The beauty of the nether", "sconn", "My portal is almost complate. Just a couple more obsidian blocks. Already I can feel it pulling my into itself. It has just such an inviting look. I am still afraid that the neighbours will try to investigate my home. For i have heard that the portal itself produces a loud sound. I will lock my front doors now. I do not anyone bothering me in my research. I wonder how it looks. I have read a book of a traveller that actualy entered the nether. He says that a mortal being cannot live there for too long. He says that there are beings there that we could never imagine. I will see this for myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Begging Soul of Tharn", "fiercedragon", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beggining", "DefunctDivine", "In the beggining, there were three. Bael, Skarner, and Skylart. The three resolved to form a group of adventurers, a guild, if you will, which they centered around a sandstone tower. After the tower reached it's fourth floor, and the guild it's fifth member,", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_24(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The Begining", "SpazmaticSniper", "Hello Dear, I hope your in the mood for a game. Its kind of like Hide and go seak, but with clues. And a small reward at the end", ""),
        StaticBook("The Begining of Tur'Evolon", "Epic_Potatoe", "Nailena was a citizen of Laurelin, who saught something more of herself She wanted to mean something To be the leader of a   great city One day, she gathered some of her friends, and set off on adventure They ventured through unknown wilderness, and an ancient temple On the fifth day, they came across a beautiful landscape Nailena knew this was where the city would  be held She did not want her city to be like the others, however She wished to unite the races together, hopefully ending racial conflict And so stood Nailena the commoner, Argon the Warden, and Deltaro the commoner The soon to be council of Tur'Evolon   \n The road to Tur'Evolon was the first thing built. The name was thought of as the road was built. People flocked to Tur'Evolon, helping build the city. Structures were built, the city began to flourish, and was on a path to a great future.", ""),
