        StaticBook("The Beginning", "Xenoamor", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning", "Xanivic", "Day 1 - I found a peculiar, abandoned house. I decided to inhabit it due to me not being able to seek land close to Kal'Urugan that I could've constructed a home on. Although, this house is fairly close to outer Kul'Urugan. 'Tis good. It's right across the bridge.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning (Offcial Journal)", "Xanivic", "Day 1 - I found a peculiar, abandoned house. I decided to inhabit it due to me not being able to seek land close enough to Kal'Urugan that I could've constructed a home on. Although this house is fairly close to outer Kal'Urugan. Day 2 - Discovered an abandoned town that with a chest fully stored with untouched books. I decided to take them home and begin my writing practices. I wrote a small story later in the night. The title is 'The End of Hope'. I believe my writing abilities are significantly increasing. Later today I came across a lone Orc, I followed him down a road... and ended up encountering an Undead stronghold. 'Twas a disturbing sight. The wretched Eye of Iblees stood above the stronghold, threatening all that  confronts it. A couple of other lads came along and assisted us in trying to breach the gate that separated the long, obsidian crafted bridge, and the stronghold walls made of netherrack. An Undead spotted us, and the loud voice of Iblees pounded our ears with such ferocity. The Undead began summoning several bolts of lightning... a cluster of bolts struck the Orc and severly injured him. Suddenly, the Undead summoned his disgusting minions which slayed a Human that had joined our party prior to this ordeal. I loathe Undeads. Day 3 - It's around midnight. I just traveled back from Laurelin. Earlier, at around 1 AM Cassandra, the Undead Queen destroyed Vex, and The Prophet (supposedly the oldest Undead.) and now she aims to terminate Overlord_Tyrius (I believe that's the correct spelling). My eyelids have grown heavy, my body exhausted. It was a long day today. One last thing before I close my eyes to sleep, I discovered something, perhaps a book which supposedly has Undead inscriptions and spells within the pages of the book. It goes by the name of... Necromicon? I believe that's correct. It would be an interesting artifact to obtain. Goodnight. It's around 1 in the afternoon. Earlier this morning I came across a young lad who offered me a home in his town that's being constructed. I'm not too sure if I want to relocate my studies, and supplies at the moment, I truly like the place I live in now.' He did, however, agree with including the abandoned house where I live now into his town. It may cause quite a few problems.. I don't want thieves and scavengers stealing my books and such. Day 4 - Seems I haven't written in awhile. I began a new book. It'll be very interesting. \n Day 4 still. Nothing exciting happened today. Although I did create a record keeping book. Decided to do so just for studies and picking out patterns... which will contribute to my plots. Also, I'm using the book of Anonymous Inscripted Texts as a Libram as well. The words within these pages are divine, ones of which only the Aeamon/Ascended spoke in the ancient times. \n It's near the end of today. Kragrum suffered a relentless attack from arachnids, and giant s as well as the Undead themselves. It ended quite soon. The orcs were able to repel the Undead. Soon after this occurance, I attended a lovely elven wedding. I had predicted (as written in my record book, that something would take a turn for the worse. An Undead minion thought he could convince the people at the wedding to submerge themselves into the life of cruetly, and ferocity. The life of an Undead. He was soon slain, though. It made me chuckle. Also, a man was arrested for commiting a silly crime that I wasn't able to fully discover. \n - I have stopped writing in my journal for now. I don't think I will return to it due to having many other tasks, as well as having records and archives book that keeps track of important occurances. \n * This is the last entry by Auckes. ~ \"Not sure what day it is. The year is 1322 and it is 8:54 PM , Tolta, 24th of Malins Welcome. \"", ""),
        StaticBook("The beginning of Aegis", "loion", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning of Tharns Story", "fiercedragon", "As Tharn was born his parents left him at the doorsteps of a druids grotto. His parents were assassins and they could not keep him in fear they might harm him. Back to the story,The druid raised Tharn as any other druid child but Tharn new something was diffrent from him and the other children. So he ran away and lived in the wilds. after many years he got tired of the wilds and went back to his home with the druids. He found there were no druids he remembered there. As he entered he found another elf. His name was Respiren. And Respiren was very kind and let him stay for some time. finaly one day he asked,\"Could you do me a favor and look for a man named Merchant_Golden_ric chards 1 . So i traveled to Oren to find this man as i did not know where to look. So on the road he found a bandit. The bandit told me to give him all my stuff and I refused. He tried to stab me and missed. I moved back in the trees and hid until he passed me. I thought to myself \"Run this is your chance!\" Then something over took me and i attacked. i then became a bounty hunter. With his corpse beneath me I took all his items. On the rest of the way to Oren I did not have anymore trouble. I did not fine the Merchant in Oren. I did not find the merchant in Oren so I went back to Laurelin. As I approached the grotto I saw 2 other men there other than the druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning of The End", "Darkdragon274", "My name is Relgard. I am a Deputy of the White Ravens. I am being hunted by the Wardens. They are hunting me because I am fighting their evil reign, with the help of others. This is the story, from the beginning, to now; The Beginning of the End. I cannot write all things, and I cannot write perfectly as I sit here, waiting. Some ravens are talking to our allies, some keeping lookout. Our agent within the wardens is spying. \n It all started months ago, me and my loyal friend Duncan were searching for an undead worshipper. We say commotion in Laurelin, and watched. There had been an arrest for two people, a boy named Sparrow, and a man named Caden. We tried following them, for Sparrow had been arrested for worshipping the dead. We were outside the base of these people, the Wardens, when they took the first offense. They arrested Duncan. \n I tried to stop them, but couldn't. I had to run. I returned to the Raven base and alerted my allies. Duncan was later released. Weeks later I met a couple called \"The Burkesters\". They were nice people. Good friends. They would soon play a vital role in all things. \n I was returning from a battle in Kramoroe, where I had fought orcs trying to toll people when I saw commotion at the Burkesters's house. I investigated. Two sons wer ebeing born. \n Nothing big happened for a while, until one day, Duncan told me that Leka, Burk's wife, was arres ted. The wardens though she was a minion of Iblees. She was not. Duncan and I set out to help our friend. While we were traveling, we met Caden again. He was, by then, leader of the Rebels against the Warde ns. We also came across Zoe, an Ex-Raven friend of mine. We continued and finally entered the keep. \n<How to Enter> Facing North Gate from North: Follow outer wall Counter-Clockwise Until you reach a desert. You can jump here. Follow inner wall same Direction Soon you will find trees. Some can be jumped on to get over the inner wall. End Instructions. \n We got in, but were caught. I was later returned to the wardens. mercy and gien to Seventh of the Ravens. Leka later died, and most of the world was against the Wardens. They tried, and failed, to attack Oren, due to my warning them in time. I later heard some of the Druids speaking of the Wardens in a negative Tone I talked, and gained an alliance for the rebelion. I also heard unsettling news. Caden was captured, and the wardens were no longer letting prisoners leave. Then I recieved bird from the agent. The wardens were coming for me and a druid. I escaped to the ravens, the druid was captured. \n While hiding with the Ravens I began this book. Now we've started attacking. We did a jailbreak and got the druid out. Now we are working to break the warden's alliances so we have all the men. Things are looking up, and the agent is still loyal. Relgard, 22/FirstSeed/1328", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning to the End", "Scyhell", "You were created to think that everything you did was grand. But what they did not tell you was that you were a pawn. A minor piece to this massive game, unyielding to the Hell being cast down. What you think is your freedom is actually a trap to keep you caged. Look at the window, does it not open when you try? In the end, you will see how they molded and shaped you to preform this way. What will you do when they take everything from you? Rise up and take back the means to defend yourself. You may die a thousand deaths but it will show them you are unwilling to give up.", ""),
