        StaticBook("The Book", "Hwaldar", "It is such...an unbelievable feeling. It feels so great to write! I never thought that Sah'Ron and Arc'Ana would ever think off this. It is such a great feeling,to have a place to put my thoughts into. Such a great feeling,to have all my hopes,joys and tears, to be written and kept safe inside this book Too bad,the War will start soon and we all must go... \n \n54th Year,The Second Seed", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book", "doggydigger", "This is a book. I like books So i wrote this And its going to be awsome. So yah this is my book. A work of art if you ask me. But you didnt so im mad at you. . So now im at a party thingy. I dont know what its about. I just know its a lame pary. Err party Well theres no food or cake. Just  A few elves. Its an ok party i guess. People i dont know everywhere. . Well there important people here. Well its a slow start. But everyones talking. Im so hungry though. Oh its was a burning forest Well where having a party in a ex forest Well i guess i party hasnt started :/ )) (( i didnt mean to put that )) Well... . Im done writing So enjoy . No i dont want to stop . The pary started And now everyones danceing and that jaz.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book of Aegis", "Ohaythar121", "Year 84 \n Second Seed \n Writings of the Wandering Wizard \n Chronicles of the Ancient History \n The Cloud Temple of Aegis \n There were no planes of existance. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a ligth we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a deity in contrast to the emptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this deity existed. It is, in fact, herecy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing god was this deity. \n Truly none can describe the majesty of the creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of the Seven Skyes. With his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur, and it happened THe rooling seas, proud mountains, and vast landscapes, all in a second. created by God. \n The World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the world to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and good our actions can be. \n The first mortal being created was man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, Gods creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and The Daemon, the two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more. \n God then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and man lived. God then took the man and put him in the center of all Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know", ""),
