        StaticBook("The Book of Dawn", "MrJakKiD", "Idea #1- Dawns Inn Delux Well.. This idea is one of my more decent ones this is a huge inn in its own plot along the kings road as not everyone can journey to Al'Khazar Ill be willing to help build this but you may need to get a magical charm to protect the things yourself as i cannot produce this Dont let the word deluxe fool you its a bigger inn is all it means and its on the kings road so it will get alot of attention as every person who knows these lands knows dawns bakery means Home. i may add to this idea later in a future publication but i shall continue with the next one! Idea#2 And for the other thing", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book of Eliphas, Chapter 1", "l337Ninja", "Greetings, if you are holding this, you hold in your hands the Book of Eliphas, a source of great power. If you think yourself unworthy, burn this book in the flames of the Nether. Only there may this book be destroyed, for there it was made.  If you are worthy, continue   reading.        Next Page        \\[[ The Power To Enter Hell ]]/ In order to enter Hell, or as the mortals call it, the Nether, you must first construct the device neccesary to create the link between the worlds. In order to maintain this link, you will be forced to acquire the proper materials. The only material that can withstand the taint of Hell is obsidian. But be warned, Iblees will be drawn to holes in his realm. If you create a hole in his realm, you are calling upon yourself the forces of the Dark God himself. You have been warned, do not ignore my warning.                        Once you have assembled 14 cubic meters of material, arrange them in a 5 meter by 2 meter rectangle, and begin the activation ritual. May Iblees forgive your intrusion to his realm.  [End Of Chapter]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book of Eliphas, Chapter 2", "l337Ninja", "\\[ On Evading And Engaging The Undead ]/ Note: The Undead are deadly and should be AVOIDED AT ALL TIMES. The lessons in this book are to be a last resort, in the event you are attacked. Evading the Undead: First off, remember this: the undead don't take prisoners. If you run into Undead, you should always run. NEVER engage a Undead in combat without overwhelming numbers, or you will be destroyed. Remember, lightning is a sign the Undead are near. Playing hero does not mean giving the monks more bodys to tend to. Now, let us begin with how to avoid them. First thing, remember that the Undead are not after you specifically. If there is a guard or guard post nearby, the chances thay they will ignore you if you run triple. If you can, use forests or tunnels, where their mobs cant get you and their lightning cant reach you. If you are surrounded, but they don't notice you, try to conceal yourself until they move to the next target. Remember, the Undead are not the people to stay idle for long. But, if conflict cannot be avoided, there are tools at your disposal to combat them. First, if you can you must keep your distance. This will prevent the mobs from surrounding you. Also, a bucket of water will be useful as they are know to summon and use fire on the battlefield. If you can, set up explosive traps before hand to deal with the horrors they will summon. If you wish for the invasion to cease, you must cut off their reinforcements at the heart, by striking at their portal. Only then will the threat be cancelled completely. If you wish to strike at their morale (remember, they still have souls, albight twisted ones), you must target theirProphet and Overlord, the commanders of Undead operation. If they are slain the invasion will fail, and the Undead will be without a leader. Good luck, and may the gods protect you from harm.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book Of Eliphas, Chapter 3", "l337Ninja", "\\[ The Path To Temptation. ]/  The path to heresy is not a straight path, as most people assume. It is a winding path, filled with heresy and guilt. For the man of strong will, this path is a dagger to the soul, damming them to a life of pain and guilt over their past acts. The best way to avoid temptation is to never start. One action leads to another, with each event snowballing over time, transforming the character of the person entirely. So, if you expierence temptaion, you must purge it completly before it takes root and begins its long, deadly takeover. In this case, blessed is the mind that does not listen, for he shall not be lead into temptation.", ""),
