        StaticBook("The Book Of Shadows", "MarioMixer", "This book should not be opened is engraved on the front cover* *you turn over the hard cover* *you see the page covered in blood and ink* *suddenly you see the ink move into words* *the words read ''your soul is mine now''* *shadows from the room cover your clothes and face and cause you to pass out* *you awaken that you cannot think straigt* [[if you have found this book msg mariomixer or pm on forums]] hail", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book of the One", "luckmor", "The One is not a god.  The One is not mortal.  The One does not live, not as we live. The One is everything and nothing, it is everywhere and nowhere, it is, and is not. The One is what all was in the beggining, what all are now, and what all will be. The One is the Universe. The One is made up of the multitude of cosmic entities that exist. But, while to our understanding, the Universe is old, the One is but a babe. And this babe has no parents.  It can only learn by experimentation. And that is what we are.  An experiment of the universe. We are the One's teachers.  We are the One's foster parents. It is up to us to teach it what is right and what is wrong. We must be good to one another, so that the One can learn that this is right. Thus ends the first words of the speaker for the One.\n Our purpose ends not there, good friends.  The One creates our souls, as well. Each one of our souls is a part of the One.  When we are born, that part of the One becomes our soul.  When we die, that part of us is sent back to the One with our experiences. What we felt, the One feels.  What we loved, the One loves.  What we were, the One becomes, at least in part.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Book of Thrym Deepdelver", "NoobCrafter14", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Books of Tris'Fal library", "Pepernoot", "Hail! I have made a checklist to know what books we still need, and which books we already have! \n *You see a list in the book* ((http://dl.dropbox.com/u/12430155/Books.html))  Updated 12st of The Amber Cold, 1316", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bored War", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Tolta, 17th of Suns Smile, 1336 \n*\n The Orcs start a war and the Elves offer their aid. Wounded Krugmar soldiers enter Laurelin with battle reports; there are not many. \n*\n Shouts to reclaim land are made, curses for Humans and Dwarves resound in the air, and many arm themselves for an impeding onslaught.\n*\n \nThe young Krug is of the utmost importance it seems, as despite the few Orcs whom managed to venture to Laurelin, they still safely brought the child within the borders of Malinor to protect. \n Not long before the Highborn Theyador marches the Wardens out. \n*\n As the crowd files out of the gates I retreat to summon my wolves, by which time I realise I will be the last to exit the gates, and hurry to avoid losing the assembly. \n*\n Any hope of recording the following events diminish as my path becomes restricted by the abrupt lowering of the portcullis. \n*\n I am trapped, seperated from my canine companions; peering through the glass reveals the man inside the gatehouse making mocking gestures at my helpless circumstance. \n*\n Several others look on, idly observing my dilemma, when the false gatekeeper starts to threate n the lives of the chirr kin. A druid approaches and inquires into the situation, and before long he realises the gravity of what is occuring, requesting vehemently to let no harm  befall the wolves. \n*\n Peering through the wooden gate at an angle that affords me no good vision, I start to hear th e desperate and painful whines, and the subtle sound of a blade making its way through air firstly, and then flesh. Shouts amidst the crowd; violence continuing; staring blankly as my mind struggles behind what emoti on has already realised; yet denies. The gate is being raised. \n*\n Bow in hand, my solemn reverie draws to a  close. A lady lies wounded upon the floor and several others are giving chase to the culprit. \n*\n A few lengthy strides; a drawn bow. But no mark. He is gone. I curse whatever powers rule over fortunes, and turn to see the body of the woman gone already.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Boy", "jacksonsp1170", "the boy im gay title fresh", ""),
        StaticBook("The Brats", "ErcMan", "There were once two little children, more annoying than the ludest of babies, who were named Jayden and Rhylain. One day their mother had to leave for the day so she asked Abaddon the dwarf top babby-sit them. Abaddon was a man of favors, so he siad yes. We they got back to his house, he told dem da ground rules. They were so disrespectfu he put dem in his basement. They got louder an dmore annoying so he relaesed his pet dog on them . When their mother got back she cried and Aboddon told her the doy had fougt a spider recently and got rabies, witch is whty it went crazy. Abaddon was believed by the woman who went on to have more kids who  were more respectful and everyone lived on happily ever after. THE END.", ""),
