        StaticBook("The cake is a lie!", "Sevenfournine", "First preheat your furnace. Grind three bundles of wheat into flour using a pestle and mortar, add that to a medium to large mixing bowl. Next add two scoops of sugar, make sure to mix the two well. Crack one egg and add both the yolk and white into the mixture. Add three buckets of cow's milk, after mixing all together add to a cake tray. Cook in stove until golden brown, finally cut into six pieces and server.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Call of the Spirit, By Dedicant Saviticus Treebeard", "Saviordude", "This being a record of my communication with the spirit Thyrst, and of the art of staffmaking. \n \n There I stood, in the gates of Kal'Urguan planning my day when I was overcome with a vision. I stood within a forest, more beautiful then even that of Malinor. Before me stood a figure. At first glance I thought he was an ent, but upon closer inspection he turned out to be a man, made of the forest. \"Do not be afraid Saviticus, I mean you no harm.\" He said, his voice that of the oak. \"I have come to teach you, and to strengthen your ties to the spirits\" Pausing for a moment, he continued. \"Go forth into the forest, and find the sapling if the mighty pine, and I will continue your teaching.\" With this, the vision ended, and I set forth into the forest to complete my task. \nI travelled for many hours, before I came upon a sapling in the ground. \"Pick me!\" it cried. \"Pick me, I shall serve you!\" And so I gently scooped it out of the earth, and held it in my hands. As I did so, another vision came over me. \"Very good Saviticus, this one shall do fine.\" Thryst said, looking over my find. Now, go forth and find a clearing, and plant this sapling. Then, feed it the bones of the dead, and I shall place a part of me into it as it grows\" The vision ended, and once again I headed off to finish my task. \n Finding a clearing, I planted the sapling, and fed it the bones. Before my eyes it shot into the sky, twisting and turning as an ethernal glow blanketed it. Growing brighter, it led me into another vision. \"Now Saviticus, your final task awaits you. Clear this tree of it's leaves and chop it down, making sure to mark where it stood. Then, craft the wood of the tree into planks so you may better work with it. With the dirt on which it stood as it's center, place into the earth the planks in a circle, 5 feet wide. Then, with the rest of the wood, craft a staff, you'll know what to do.\" The vision faded, and I set upon crafting the circle. \n After crafting the circle and staff, I rested. During my sleep, I had a dream. In the dream I stood inside a large circle, staff in my hand. Pointing it at the center, the earth spilt at that point, and a forest grew from the crevice. Waking from my slumber, I now knew what I had to do. Walking up to the circle, I lifted the staff above my head. \"Thyrst!\" I cried, as the wind starting to pick up. \"I ask you to lend me your power, and bless this staff with the grace of nature!\" Striking the earth in the middle of the circle, a bright light shone from the ground and consumed me. \n When I awoke, Thryst stood before me, a ghostly spirit. \"Well done Saviticus, you have crafted your staff and empowered it with natures grace, along with a part of my spirit. This staff shall be your companion for the rest of your days, and it shall serve you well\"          \n He turned away from me, facing the rising sun. \"I will meet you again Saviticus when you are ready, until then go forth and teach your fellows what I have taughten you.\" With that he faded away, and I began my travel back to Kal'Urguan.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Caravan Must Be Destroyed", "skinner452", "Men have been lost, and even more have been left behind. We have attacked about 3 times, all have been unsuccessful. We must go to battle, all the men of Aegis unite to fight them off. They are no normal villains, they ally with the undead and hold minions in their base. They are too close to Kal'Urguan, we must attack with hundreds of men and destroy their horrid castle of evil. This great war will happen soon, and we will destroy this evil in our lands. Let us succeed in battle as the footsteps of hundreds come storming in from the roads of Aegis as we unite to destroy these fowl  villains. The Caravan must be destroyed.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cat and the Hat.", "Desires", "The sun did not shine, it was too wet to play, so we sat in the house all that cold cold wet day. I sat there with Sally, We sat there we too, and I said, \"Oh I wish we had something to do.\" Too wet to go out, to cold to play ball, so we sat in the house, we did nothing at all. So we all could do is to, sit sit sit SIT, and we didn't like it, not even one little bit, and THEN something went bump, how that bump made us jump. We looked and we saw him stepped onto the mat, we looked and saw him, the cat and the hat.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Catchphrase", "xNoTiiFy", "Your outta the wardens!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cathaldus Diary, a P.O.V of Keep Walking, a Tale of Truth.", "Caden_Cathaldus", "Hail! I am Caden Cathaldus, this is my diary. If you do not understand this, read Sillion's Keep Walking: A tale of truth. I will not be filling this diary with anything usless. I will only fill it with important things, or things important to me. Hail to whom it may concern. I am in prison for 3 murder accounts. One of them is true. I have escaped prison. This is my first day of FREEDOM! I see someone coming. Who the hell is it? They're saying \"Hail\" Damn, I'm in an OBVIOUS bush! Day 3 of freedom: This man's name is Sillion Luthais. Human, fairly nice. I'm not sure. Day 6: Okay. I trust this man. He gave me a sword. He calls it a Falchion. I've only practic- ed with a Cutlass. Day 10: I'm growing acustom to this Falchion thing. It's ver elegant. Like me! Day 13: DEAR GOD, IT'S AN ORC! First time I've seen one scince I'shaak. Day 16: This orc is Gruol. Sad story he has. This place has potential. Sillion doesnt agree. Day 20: This is a town now. Ever scince I made the friendly Orc bar & grill. Day 30: I brought Qwert here. I hope everyone likes him. Day 30 (again fellows): I forgot to tell you who Qwert is. Long story, he is a dwarf I met. Day 47: The town is almost finished. We have a trade route with another town. We're building a church. Day 50: I managed to hire some gaurds. 30.00 Minas a day. It is fair. I hope to get more. Right now we only have one day gaurd, and one night gaurd.", ""),
        StaticBook("the cave", "Firefoot17", "a man made cave lies under the house's, most likely used by a gang to steal  iteams   butthea", ""),
        StaticBook("The Challenge", "Maiavel", "\nThe challenge remas one of the oldest druidic traditions. It purges the weak and complacent, ensurg that the highest ranks of the druidic order rema filled with strong and cunng dividuals. The masters of the druidic order are not politicians, but men and women of action. They believe that the challenge, by brgg ambition to the open, allows them to by-pass some of the worst excesses of hypocrisy and behd-the-scenes power plays found  other religions. \nThe challenge operates under prearranged rules: Characters who violate the letter of the rules will fail to advance  rank, just as if they had suffered defeat. Always a one-on-one battle, the challenge does not allow even servants or animal companions of the combatants to participate. \nFirst, the two parties must agree upon the time of the duel--if they can't agree, it will take place at the next moot. Druids consider it impolite to set a challenge outside of a moot, although it's still done. \nSecond, the challenge needs a witness--a druid whose rank equals or exceeds the challenger's. Hierophant druids      work well as witnesses, as do druids or archdruids visitg from different circles or from the Grand Druid's entourage. This dividual must witness the terms of the challenge and make sure the combatants obey the rules. The great druid of the circle always names the witness, even if the challenge volves that very leader.   \nThird, the terms by which the battle will be fought are set out by mutual agreement. Once agreed upon and witnessed, the terms may not change. If neither side can agree on the terms, the witness selects them and proclaims the duel an all-out battle until one druid surrenders or becomes incapacitated. \nTerms to discuss include: The size of the battlefield, whether to allow weapons, magical items, granted powers, and spells, whether  to alter the normal battle-oriented conditions of the duel. \nThe challenge begins with the witness's invocation, asking Nature (Or the Aspects) to watch over the duel. This means that challengers who defeat foes through cheating will find themselves unable to gain a rank after all, and incumbents who cheat automatically lose the rank. Once the witness concludes the invocation, the druids enter the battlefield from opposite ends, and the contest begins.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Chicken in the Tub", "Alectriciti", "I'm riding a chicken in the Hot Tub. I ride this bird while writing this word. Singing a song, short or long. Thinking of temptation while in deep meditation. Riding my chicken is such a sensation. I've caused too much strife between me and my wife. I've broken her down, now what's worth my life? I let us get hit by those fiery darts. The arrows and piercings that shred through hearts. Rhisereld is pure, just like my niece is. I swear to fix these broken pieces.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Chronicles of Balthazar, Volume 1, Prolouge", "MrHobo", "That which came before \n I awoke with a start. The noises... I could hear them again. As with the other occasions-no, as always-they came from the closet. I bickered with myself, deciding whether or not to oepn the door... No, I decided. I shan't. 'Tis not the time. Who, of all in Aegis, could know what lies across the misty waters? If danger should lurk 'hind the door, what shall I do? Stab it with my sharp tounge? Batter it with my blunt insults? Nay, I will wait. Mayhap one night, soon, but now is not the time. \n I glide up the stairs, dagger (silver, of course) sheather to my side, wooden stake within my leather pack, and a multitude of other odds, ends, and trinkets. I slip in bed, heart racing with anticipation. Will I finally go tonight? I blink, surprised. A wave a dreainess washes over me. Maybe it can wait another night... \n My eyes fly open the same night. This time, the noises sound... Different, for lack of a better word.. It doesn't sound like the indescribale fear it in the past placed upon my heart. It sounds of... A whisper? My name, perhaps? The voice is soothing, warm as a ray of sunlight... I recognize it. I gasp, shocked at the voice. Realization soon follows my surprise. It is Indelwhen. The secret love of my life, who knows of me not, for all that I am, or shall ever be, is this accursed peasent, alone forever in this forsaken kingdom of Malinor. It is decided. I shall venture beyond the riverbend tonight, and find whatever", ""),
        StaticBook("The Chronicles Of The band of Brothers. Volume 1", "Crippledbaboon", "I have been in this world a while now, met some friendly people. However there are these few inparticular that from the start struck me as interesting. The characters running around, shouting. These, \"boys\" shall we call them, have in some way, out of dozens of other people, intertwined their fates with mine! And for some odd reason, although we have already have a few scraps, we are loyal to eachother until the bitter end! I have come to categorise these boys and broke down their personalitys so i may know them better. Here I shall provide a small biography of each one. Skip this if you are not a patient reader. Aeden - He is that of the elf race, a wise person who seeks only to learn who he truly is. Romanen - The warrior of the group. Although he's not the wisest of the bunch, he is loved no less! Haelphon - Also a brave warrior, he will stop at nothing to help his friends. Loyal till the death. help god damn this infernal writing", ""),
        StaticBook("The Chronicles Of The band of Brothers. Volume 2", "Crippledbaboon", "And so, now that you better know these characters, you will feel more enveloped in the story. I would also like to mention i am writing this, as the adventure still rages on! Even now i have only just sobered up from drinking ale ( i thought it was milk you see ) with Haelphon! So forgive me if my grammar is a bit sloppy still. When we formed our small gang it was me, and Hael. Then came Aeden, and we travelled the path less walked, off in hope of finding Oren! One night we stopped at a nearby chapel to recollect the past day and get to know eachother. So, one by one, we walked to the front of the pews, and told our stories and our childhoods. In doing so we attracted the attention of one such Romanen, whom then entered the chapel, and told his story also! By the time they had finished it was day, so we set off. Leaving my story for another time! Hail Woadleaf! I am going to be moving them to the archive by the new home(s) Mine was a farmer... of course, im still not sure My father.. Oh he was a good man.. I dont think so, why?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Chronicles Of The band Of Brothers. Volume 3", "Crippledbaboon", "And so, we set off, to find Olen, the city of gold! Seeing as we were all of the human race, save Aeden. We though it appropriate to head to the capital for humans! Once we had reached Olen docks/market post we though to take rest and gather our bearings. After doing so we head straight on to Al'Khazar! On the journey there not much had occurred. When we got there though, that was when things got out of hand... As we strolled down the dark eerie tunnel, Aeden called for us to stop. He asked hesitantly... \" What if they have changed? \" ( Bearing in mind he is 270 years old ) After assuring him everything was going to be ok we ventured in, curious to what we would see...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cinders of Paper", "CONORDUDE8", "I am Cralt. And this Text, Shall hold me, Not be possesed, But my Literature shall give me im Immortality in a way. \n As i write this, I gaze upon the Trees of Laurelin, Now deserted. \n I remember the old crowds, the Vibrant trades, I am, one of the Oldest elves, luck with ascended, brought me to a feeble 112. \n As I light a small Fire for the Winters, I hope i can teach others my Believings. ,my beliefs of hope, Freedom, and the write where people get a say! \n I scribe, As my true birthday of 732 Arrives, and i still havent acchieved anything. I want freedom for people, i know i can speak for people, and i will one day. \n Maybe one day, I will become a Prince of Laurelin, Or a Viscount, And Represent the people . \n I write this, For Knowledge, that this can be stored, for eternity, In my small Bookshelf And maybe one day, I can open a grand Library Of Laurelin, For all to see. \n I hope, I can show something, And show people: I AM SOMEBODY", ""),
