        StaticBook("The Classroom Rules", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Listen to what your teacher says, write it down if you wish. \n \n Do not speak unless you are spoken to \n \n Answer a question to the best of your ability, there is no \"correct\" answer. \n \n Try not to move around too much during class, it may distract the teacher. Sit nicely in your desk to makes the teacher's job easier. \n \n If there is a pressing matter and you must leave, ASK, even though your request may be denied.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Coming of the Elves", "SuperZac", "Long ago, in the ancient days of the world, this fair land of Aegis was bleak and barren. No grass shielded the soil and no tree cleansed the air. So it was, and so it would still lik ely be had it not been for the Elves. It was a hot day when their first ships arrived; fair ships with large gray sails that moved like fluid with the wind. The first brigade of ships landed at what is now known as Laurelin. And their great King, who's name was so beautiful that it is now impossible to utter, leapt out of the ship and landed on the dry earth. \"This land shows much promise,\" he said, and with that, he knelt down, said a few words of the ancient magic, and a Tree started to grow from the spot. At first it was a sapling like any ordinary tree. But by the time the sun was low on the horizon, it had grown nearly ten feet tall, and it' s branches were enough to shelter the Elf-children that night. So it was that, from that first tree an entire forest was born. The other elves put their magic to use as well when they arrived, making the flowers and the grass. In less than a year the entire city of Laurelin and grown right out of the ground. And while none now remember those times, (for time ravages even those who are immortal), all Elves possess a great love for the plants and trees. So it was that the fair Elves came to Aegis, and turned it from desert wastland into the beautiful land you see before you today. All races of Aegis are in the Elve's debt for this act, but many a wise elf has claimed that the debt has already been paid in full.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Communist Party by Chairman Thorin Elm-Hammer", "joshlmr", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Compound", "Jaknifed", "Things To do: \n Finish Clearing First Floor. \n Construct Housing District \n Construct Crafting District (Blacksmith Forge, Bakery, etc.) \n Finalize Farmland Upstairs (Farmhouse, Chicken Pen, Animal Pen, Grinder) \n  \n Construct Mushroom Farm \n Build Port (Possiblly removed, We shall see) \n Build Destination Routeable minecart system. (I will be doing this and it will be automated)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Construction of Shal'Hial", "Bloodlest", "Finally I have struck gold! Would would have known that skeletons would go into our mines and take this precious metal. I had enough metal to make something useful... But I am no shaman and cannot cast magic... Magic is for those who can not fight physically. I have decided to make a sword out of this gold, and hopefully get it enchanted! I seem to have across a error. The gold metals won't fuse together! It is making me quite", ""),
        StaticBook("The construction of the snowy fields guild hall", "redbaron", "The snowy fields guild hall was a slow process but the rewards for my patients were much worth it.  The architect of this town is amazing.  what he has created could be the worth prizes and its weight in gold.  Something i could never accomplish myself the horrible architect that i am. It first began with the main floor and then went up. they built the study of the guild master, at this time his name was ogland, and then went up another level building his private quarters.  after that they started to go down building the great library that in his day ogland created many some books for the guild. Zerragon and Ogland talked about its construction and Ogland told him what he though would be needed for the guild hall to be a excilent study ground for what they found under snowy fields. After the library was finished they started to move farther down.  Building the class rooms where ogland instructed the apprentices about the ancient ascended text in the all. then the living quarters were made for the mages. there was about 3-4 of them created. Once the guild hall was completed, the guild master at that time went straight to work. Hoping that he may discover snowy fields little secret.", ""),
        StaticBook("The cook book", "similan", "1. How to make bread: Get 3 Wheat line them up and you have bread 2. How to make sugar: Get a sugarcane plant and mash it up and now you have sugar The cook book help help", ""),
        StaticBook("the cook book of minecraft.", "colin1389", "mushroom soup: first you need one red mushroom and one brown mushroom. put both mushroom in to a wooded bowl and mash the mushroom to gether. till the mushroom have mixed. them put it in the bowl. you done. enjoy! cooked pork. first heat the hoven to 450.f. and cook the pork for 10-15 minutes. then let cool for 5 minutes.       enjoy!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cow Says \"MOO\"", "brnavin", ">you find a picture of a cow on the cover< the cow says \"Moo\" The Pig says \"Oink\" The sheep says \"Baah\" The Chicken says \"BaCock\" >you find a page written on< The Cow says \"Oink\" The Pig says \"BaCock\" The Sheep says \"Moo\" The Chicken says \"Baah\" >the book ends with drawings of animals<", ""),
        StaticBook("The cracks in the tree.", "Respiren", "High Prince I do write to ye with a great concern. The Grand highborn has come before the druids , into our sacred grove, and in an act of great malice commited a heinous crime. He did burn the young trees before us, laughing all the while . I do fear for his stability and sanity, too long have the Wardens become isolated from Malinor, living on the outskirts amongs the corpses of trees .  They have raided our home brandishing swords, and taken dedicant's into prolonged custody, with only insidious whispers on the winds as reasoning. It is time once more for the Wardens to walk among us. To watch over our gates. Our fellow elves. And the forests of Malinor. \nDo ye not see how the confines of the dead trees affects my brother! Let him free amongst the wilds! \n Below their great camp lies an affront to Nature. A great chamber resides there where they do house the minions of the undead . Here they do kill innocent spiders for sport, rather than protecting and hunting among the woods of Laurelin. \n It has been eleven days now, my brother has killed himself amongst their cells, they watched him hang without lifting a hand, except to loot his corpse. Archdruid Dusk did stay the course, cold and hungry, held until the young elflings were overcome by their better natures, and did disregard the 'Grand' Quazar's cruel orders.", ""),
        StaticBook("the creature and assasin", "Pheonixpro1", "after i attacked the assasin, i healed the princess with soem special potions respiren gave me to use on injured people we waited for tthe guards to come down and take him out but the assasin was too skillful for the guards to fight and he escaped me and triloq where annoyed that if they done something useful rather than questioning something that couldnt speak the princess wouldn't be attacked she thanked me, for saving her and then we left we came back and the creature was there again and the princess was keeping \"evern\" in captivity this is not fair i wanted to bring him back to laurelin to heal him and protect him the guards didnt like my idea and threated me and triloq if we didnt leave we would die the princess interupted said thanks about before and then we left for laurelin", ""),
