        StaticBook("The Cripsons", "Rathriel", "Cripson or any of his followers shall not be threatened, arrested or killed by Elves of Laurelin for any actions that happened before today (( 8:26 PM Pacific Standard Time, July 15 )) If you have a problem with this agreement please contact Head Diplomat Lafthi (MC Rathriel)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cry for Freedom", "martinvilla822", "Your hands upon a deadman's sword, and you're looking at the fight. Your heart is worn, and the seams are torn, and they've given you reason to fight. And you're not gonna take what they've got to give, and your not gonna let them take your will to live, because they've taken enough and you've given them all you can give , and luck won't save them tonight. They've given you reason to fight. And all the storms you've been chasing, about to rain down tonight. And the pain you've been facing, about to come to the light (x2)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Current Status of Politics in Aegis", "Taxidermist_Dave", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Curse of the Bad Potato.", "Epic_Potatoe", "When I was a child, I knew something was wrong with me. I had no limbs or organs, and the children from the homeless shelter tried to eat me. I was in fact, a potato. \n I grew up with no friends, parents who hated my existence, and no siblings. Most mornings I awoke with the thoughts of suicide. I slowly grew up i the world of Aegis, and applied to enter the Pathfinders. I was accepted and astonishlingly, everyone overlooked my...condition. well, almost everyone. \n This one Pathfinder names Valiant would taunt me forever, calling me a \"Bad Potato\" It drove me insane, the way he would smack me on the head, insulting me. Eventualy, he left the Pathfinders and I was free of the humiliation. So you see kids, the Curse of the Bad Potato is not to be joked about. You're parents must damn well be carefull when at the bar eying a potato. So the moral of this story? Usa proper potato protection. \n \n The End.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Curse of Winfield Residence", "UndeadEd", "This is a report of the happenings of the last weeks in Winfield Residence , where I, Orphideus Maximus Winfield, currently live. It all started not such a long time ago when I was travelling across the nation of Oren (choice) until I saw a strange sign near the residence looking out over the ocean. I walked towards it and read it. 'Feel free to move in' it said.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cursed Stones", "silco97", "There is a stone, dark and evil that is only found in the depths of the earth. It taints the air around it turning stone to mossy ore.  They sat when you touch it you can hear the voice of Iblees through it.  Its power is strong giving one the ability to summon monsters of all kinds to their aid.  Very few have seen one and even fewer have touched one and survived. There is said to be a master stone to all of the others.  It is black and has never been seen. Even Undead shake at the thought of being near it.  In this stone is the power of Iblees himself. Created by his best blacksmith it can trigger all other cursed stones to command. \nWhen one with a weak of mind has touched it and found its power they want more. They will protect their stone not letting it leave their sight.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cursed Sword (Quest Completed)", "Hwaldar", "Pick up the Kar'Lan Sword if you dare... \nIt will make your life most dear... \nBut be warned,young traveler \nIf they catch you with it \nYou will have to pay...", ""),
