        StaticBook("The Cycle", "Timayame", "While we are distractd by our lives what happenes on the blind side? where do all the bodies come and go? Why are they there? when will they stop coming? No man has the answer to this question and no man ever will... for the event of violence and war will never change. Its in our blood and al all there will be is blood....", ""),
        StaticBook("The dairy of Father Eynon", "Benboboy", "Tolta, 10th of The Grand Harvest, 1339: I have been practising my teleportation skills today, but those endermen are hard to catch. I went to the library in the keep in Galahar today and found out some strange things about Daemons , It appears they seek mortals of a pure soul and give them tasks. That would explain the Daemon in my church the other day. I belive one of the Oren guards killed an undead and brought its staff to the daemon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Damage Within", "muchoman798", "\nFor obvious reasons, I am not disclosing my name on this pamphlet. \nThe Kingdom of Oren is being killed from within. The King is neglecting the safety of the people. That means you and the author of this pamphlet. Do you want to know how? \nFirst and foremost, the neglecting of the guards of Oren. He does not pay them nor does he have them be trained, rather he just sends them into battle to die pointlessly. This makes many desert, which means you are unsafe. Unsafe from bandits. Unsafe from murderers. Unsafe from the Undead. \nIn addition, he permitted his men to make a false peace treaty with the Undead. This only hurts us by giving us a false sense of security. The treaty was broken by the Undead, who now prove wiser than our own King. \nOne last thing. The King would rather spend money adding a tower to his personal Keep for his safety than fortifying Al'Khazar, as the walls have many holes. \nDo not stand for this. \n~ L", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dancing Dwarf Menu", "vegan166", "Cooked Pork, 10 minas Elven Wine, 20 minas Cooked Fish 6 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dangerous Slime", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "The slime is a green, rare, animate , and cube shaped gelatinous enemy. It may appear in various sizes, and will attack anybody if they get too close. If you defeat a large slime, don't celebrate, because it will split into smaller slimes, that will continue to attack you. If you do happen to defeat a slime, they may drop slimeballs, a rare item. \n Slimes move by hopping, and they hop towards the closest person within their view. If slimes do not see anybody, they will hop in a straight line, in whatever direction they were facing. Small slimes deal no damage to a person, but will attempt to push them around. Large slimes deal direct damage to a person, so remember to keep some distance. In shallow water, slimes can hop fast enough to fight a current, but in deep water they will sink to the bottom, and won't be able to hop while they are completely submerged. You may be able to tell if a slime is near, by listening for a slapping kind of noise. \n This is all the information I have to offer, I hope it serves you well. \n -Salamandra", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dark", "Saviordude", "Hello. You seem to have been lucky enought to find this book. Why is this lucky? Because you hold in your hand a book that could change your life. Imagine being able to be anything you want to be. Or to live forever, with age never being a problem again. These things are possible, but in order for you to get them we need your help. Yes, you. Only you can help us help ourselves, others, and you. For we need members, people who will help get things done so we can live in the utopia that we have invisioned. We need an army. So send us a letter, the address is written in the backcover. \n We'll be waiting \n - The Dark \n \n *You seen an address scribbled down at the end. ((Saviordude))*", ""),
