        StaticBook("The Death of King Enor And the Siege of Al'Khazar", "firespirit44", "Itnan, 23rd of the Amber Cold, 1338 It was a sad day for Oren and Al'Khazar when the undead decided to strike. King Enor was whisked awa y by a evil magical smoke, casted by the undead. The undead unleashed lightning, horrible creatures such as Ghasts, Pigmen, and some unindentified beings. Slimes that have been tainted with the Fire of Iblees. We are unsure of its existence behind it, but I'm sure the mages will categorize soon enough. As of now, Oren no longer exists", ""),
        StaticBook("The Death of the Wandering Wizard", "everblue2er101", "On Ahad, the 8th of the Deep Cold, 1336, the world of Aegis was struck by a terrible tragedy. I, Josef Timothee, record here my own experience during these events. \n I was in Al'Khazar when a voice rang out, filling all of Aegis. It identified itself as the Wandering Wizard. He said that he had three relics that needed to be taken to the Cloud Temple. If they were to fall into Undead hands, he claimed, terrible trouble would result for the people of Aegis. He sent forth a cry over all the lands, asking for support on the journey from Al'Khazar to the Cloud Temple on the King's Road. A large crowd assembled with him in Al'Khazar, mostly humans but representatives from other races there as well. \n The procession headed down the King's Road and was immediately attacked. Lightning rained down from the skies, and monsters appeared out of thin air. But those in the crowd were ready, and struck back against Iblees minions. The monsters were defeated through sheer numbers of those opposing them, as well as the powerful magic of the Wandering Wizard. All along the journey, he kept up words of encouragement and urged the crowd onwards. The lightning and monsters were relentless, delaying the journey terribly. \n By the time the procession reached the Cloud Temple many had died trying to protect the Wizard en route. It was there that the Undead suddenly struck the most violently I have ever witnessed, not only casting lightning powerful enough to damage the Cloud Temple, but also changing the landscape around it to look like the Nether. Among this, explosions and lightning were striking everywhere, causing great suffering. The Wizard urged all present to take shelter in the Cloud Temple. I took this advice, having been clipped by lightning and set ablaze. Once inside, the extent of the damage was clear. Hundreds entered the Temple, many wounded by burns or monsters. The Temple shook as explosions rocked it from outside and pieces of it broke off. Then... \n A new voice rang out, saying that the Wizard had been slain by the Undead. The outpouring of grief was immediate, and the attacks on the Temple ceased. Someone shouted that the Undead had taken three objects from the Wizard that looked like eggs. The skies lightened, the landscape changed back, and the crowd left the Temple. But the world was altered permanently with the death of the Wandering Wizard. It remains to be seen what the Undead will do with the stolen relics.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Decloration of Peace", "MrJakKiD", "This is the decloration of a Peace treaty and Alliance between The Avengers and the fine town of Kramoroe Signed- Thork 5th Avenger and and Mayor Malco, Witnessed by 7th Avenger Verren", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dedicant's Vow", "drplat", "\"I will walk the forest with my new kin, I will swim the river of truth, wherever it takes me, As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need, I will help preserve the balance, even as dusk approaches, I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\" - Scribed by Petyr the Salmon Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dedicant's Vow", "ElynxYon", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Deep Cold - by Azriel Lucius", "KrasnayaArmiya", "I never knew who brought me into this world. . .perhaps for the best. I remember the cold, the type that could cut into your very essence. I remember two very individuals. . .I remember the barest of essentials. Then I remembered the fire. A jolt of pain shakes me as I recall these painful, sharp memories. I lay awake at night pondering them, trying to familiarize myself with them. . .to gain some semblance of a memory. . .but it is in vain. As I sit here in my Quarters, writing, I can hear the wind cutting through the air of the cold expanse we call the North. It sounds identical to the ghastly moans of the Scourge, the blight on this land, and then I am reminded there are much more pressing matters at hand. The earliest memory I can recall is my life in Alk'Hazar, capital of the Kingdom of Oren. I was but a street urchin, living off of what I could scrounge up. I was not nefarious in my deeds, rather it was necessary for my survival. In my spare time, I would engross myself in whatever literature came my way. Be it through the news postings, discarded novels. . . I was soon quite the orator. However, the City Guard soon became wary of me and I was forced to relocate. A Northerner, I made my way to the North. I managed to carve out my own dwelling in the landscape before the harsh cold claimed me. . . I also managed to fashion my own armaments out of the elements of the Wilds. I managed to secure myself a stable, albeit isolated living. I would hunt only when necessary, and take from nature only what I needed. However, the calm was shattered with the arrival of the Undead. One cold night, I awoke in a cold sweat to images of hellfire and brimstone. Distorted, sharp images of painful torment racked my brain and pierced the back of my eyes, remnants of my dream. The atmosphere was unsettling, and I realized that something was amiss. I quickly gathered my vestments and weaponry and made my way to the biting cold, only to encounter what I had just envisioned. Fire, shooting high up into the heavens was visible from a distance. Screams and cries of agony were ever present. The settlements nearby were clearly under siege by some machination of evil. Suddenly, the air nearby was unsettled by some force of manevolence. I quickly ducked as a sword was driven through the entryway I was just positioned in front of and turned to face my assailant. I came face to face with glowing red eyes, sunken into a rotten face mostly shrouded by a black hood, complimented by a black robe. I could not make out his features, but could vaguely make up a cruel sneer. The years of hunting experience coming to fruition, I quickly side-stepped his next thrust and buried my sword deep into the unholy assailant. He let out what could only be described as an unworldly wail, and vanished in a plume of dark, singed smoke. I knew from that moment that my life would never be the same again. . . read 1  -read 2 read -3 \\", ""),
        StaticBook("The delights of mobs", "pugsy", "Mobs such as a pig or chicken can be great companions or food if you really need some now you must know a mobs preferences to become friends the following list contains all mob likes", ""),
        StaticBook("The Demon With The White Eyes", "Chrisld", "If you ever see the man with white eyes...      \n Just run! He will kill you no matter how good items you have! The demon with the white eyes is called Herobrine... He can kill you just by looking at you... Remember that you can always run to fight another day!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Destroyer of a Soul", "MrZombez", "\n I hate you with a necessary hate \n First, I sought patience: passionate was she: \n My patience turned in very scorn of me \n That I should dare forgive a sin so great \n As this, through which I sit disconsolate; \n Mourning for that live soul, I used to see; \n Soul of a saint, whose friend I used to be: \n Til you came by! a cold, corrupting fate \n Why come now? You whom I cannot cease \n With pure and perfect hate to hate? Go, ring \n The death-bell with a deep, triumphant toll! \n Say you, my friend sits by me still? Ah, peace! \n Call you this thing my friend? this nameless thing? \n This living body, hiding its dead soul?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Devourer of Souls", "colwin1", "The bay was foggy, and the air was biting cold. Centuries old wood creeked as Porvian paced on the docks. His breath hang in front of him as though it were suspended in time itself. The only thing keeping his spirits up was the crystal clear sky. The constellations danced.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diamond", "xXSweet_TearsXx", "The first day of a new life I was there with Nico and Lucas in a abandon mineI missed my house,we didnt have much food leftAll I did was to sit down and think,just now i tought about how I ended up here It all started the day i moved to my house,Nico and Lucas where there to help me put in the furnituresAfter a while we sat down and ate some cake i  made We started planning a trip to the elvenmine next day so next day we took some food and started walking to the mineWhen we almost where at the end we found a mine,it was some signs there but we didnt read them so we walked in and got lost and here we sit In the middel of the silenc we heard a scream it sad \"Nico? Lucas? Loretta?\" It was my dad, an then the planks we sat on fall down,I wake up by Nico he was jellying \"Loretta wake up, wake up pleaze\" I wake up , i noticed the Big hole in the roof I saw some thing shiny in the wall some blocks awayIt was a diamond I sad \"Lucas its a diamond in the wall!!\" he was fast to answer \"Yes i know Nico is picking it up\"he had a big smile in his face,\"There you are\"My dad was up in the hole and gave us a ropeThen Lucas came with a big smile and all off us climed up The end Hope you like it,from Arya(xXSweet_TearsXX)This is my first one so i hope you like it", ""),
        StaticBook("The diamond is a rare ore. Can be found in deep height.", "Darksalvo", "You can do many things with a diamond, like make tools or armors. The diamonds have an high price too, like 200 minas each.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary of A lumberjack", "GrimReaper98", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The diary Of Cralt/Conor Darith", "CONORDUDE8", "for many years ive travelled this world, under multiple aliases, and under many people's orde when i was Conor, the peaceful trader i had a relationship with the high prince, i was almost a viscount, but my sister died, so i left to the lands to the north when i returned, i rebuilt a character, Cralt, the mysterious hunter, and tradesman I have yet to \"meet\" the High Prince since, i hope to tell him the truth though i would keep the secret to him, and myself\n mysterious tradesman, and hunter OOC:ignore previous line, stuffed up. a man named makia just walked up to me, im not much of a social one, but i still make time to talk. we just finished our conversation, apparently he is  becoming a guard not many elves become guards of oren, so he is a lucky one, ((sorry for grammar errors, got forgetful) \n the defences of oren have tightened, prince brett perea has been commanding his troops and there are several guards on the walls, they ask about you before you are allowed to enter the gate, i made up a few lies, tradesman and what not \n I mean no harm to Oren, dont get me wrong, just i like to be secretie. *Secretie. erase secretie ignore past few lines, i meant secretive. I'm low on health after a recent hunt, Skeletons and Zombies attacked me i would leave Oren, but it is too risky, so i am going trading... Whoppee... Found inn, time too eat :D \nI am currently just wandering the city, in search of food and arrows, for the next hunt \nAfter a long time, i plan on venturing aegis, and set up a small camp but i have a feeling he is stealing from me... I have just came back from a hunt, a few bandits got in my way they got their punishment tough and hard. i think i have finally found a place to buy arrows, at a man named the alchemists place. i am making 3 copies of this, to keep it safe \nOrcs are despised of by men, i dont know why, but there is definite political tension between the two. as an elf, i am meant to be one with nature, but i was born different. i just found a mineshaft, which i have expanded upon, it is great, i've found several pieces iron here, and i have made a chest to store my treasures \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary Of Ellesar", "Drakoranok", "My name is Ellesar Amandil, I am 9 years old and I am going to write once a month! I am 9 and 1 month, I was in the forest with Christy and we saw an Orc! It was hideous. I am 9 and 2 months, Christy died, we were playing in some fields when a Orcish Poacher kille d her when she was defending a lost dog. I am 9 and 3 months, I HaVE A BOYFRIEND! His name is Edward, he's sooo cute! I am 9 and 4 months, Edward and I KISSED 4 days ago! It was the best time of my life! I am 9 and 5 months, Edward took me too the lake, we... Had fun let's say. I am 9 and 6 months, Edward and I are going to the lake every day, and I love it! I am 9 and 7 months, Edward is missing, he went out hunting with my dad and hasnt come back! I am 9 and 7 months and 12 days, dad's back... But Edward... He's.... dead... I am 9 and 8 months,Mother has caught a disease and I am going out to get herbs every day. I am 9 and... Oh what does it matter, WHY DOES THERE HAVE TO BE SO MUCH DEATH. Mother gone... I am 9 and 9 months, The food is getting scarce and we keep selling jewlerry for food. I am 9 and 10 months, They sold a CHILD! She was only 7 and they sold her! I am 9 and 11 Months, 11 children are gone and we are still scrace on food. I am 10, its my birthday and... They sold me... MY OWN PARENTS! Why.... : :I am 20 and 4 months, It's been so long, and i'm married! He's SO handsome!  His name is Adorellan and he proposed to me on the steps of The Clous Temple of Aegis!", ""),
        StaticBook("The diary of Father Eynon.", "Benboboy", "I also read about the Daemons after one visited my church and gave some knights a task. It appears they only go to those with a pure heart and offer them rewards by completeing tasks. title The Dairy of Father Eynon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary of Finiarel Alfakyn", "mercury199", "(The entry appears to be dated in the year 1147 ) Faolin is a kind master he is just and good of heart mind and character ( nothing interesting for several more pages ) ( this entry seems to be dated 1158 ) I was struck cross the back by a man today in the market. I turned to him, but to my surprise he had backed away. I stared at him, and a hush fell over the crowd, I stared into his eye and sudenly I coul hear what he was thinking. It was as if I myself had thought of his idea's. I began to look around in his mind, and saw he had only accidentaly struck me thinking I was another. I opened my mouth to speak and, Faolin clamped a hand over my mouth and dragged me off. ( The enbteries mostly pretain to extensive study in magic lore swordsmanship writing and all other schollarly pursuits, little is interesting ) ( This entry is dated 1160 ) I asked Faolin about my parents today, after trying to avoid the subject several times. He said this, \" your mother and father were very good freinds of mine, they loved you very much but had to leave you for your own protection, They were very good people and some of the finest elves I will ever meet. \" I was content with that and did not press him more. ( More borring entries ) (More borring entries ) ( this entry is dated 1179 ) Durring My meditation today I explored a part of my mind I had never seen before, nor ever thought to look to. It was strange but powerful, this part almost felt like another being, I felt such power for it though, It was like the Greatest thunderstorm you've ever seen put into a tiny it was incredible, Who would have known, I will share this information with Faolin. ( Later in the entry ) Faolin was most displeased by my realization, He told me not to tread in such area's. And that he would adress that later. ( An entry that appears to be hastely scrawled in no date is given ) The visions of what I see are but shadows of a greater truth, that no mortal can comprehend . I am lost but never have I been more found. I understand I have a purpose, but I know not what it is ( MOre enrys about daily life farming, writing ect. ) ( the next several pages are completely soaked in blood ) (Dated 1200) Faolin was slain by a group of men, there appeared to be just a few but in th bushes were over 60 in total. Their leader Tokenbrand killed the closest thing I had to a father, Faolin died in my arms. A power seemed to posses me then I felt as if not from this world, but yet from another, I could see my body begin to glow, I rose up in the air and then I remember nothing else. The next thing I remember I'm laying in a puddel and it's raining all around me. I used the skill's i learned to reveiw what had transpired. I slew all of them in one go. I noticed myself then in the puddel, Blue lines had criscrossed my whole body, like vines. I know not what they do yet. ( the next entries are infrequent ) ( this entry appears to be a list ) \n My curses \n I am a Master of Destruction and slaughter \n I must sense everything that every living thine go i feel every living thing it's pains it's pleasures all the time \nI have been deformed and cursed by these blue lines \n I have been told I am immortal but do not know this to be true or false ( something scribbled in the margin) \n I can heal with this too not just kill. ( Many entries later ) ( Dated 1247 ) I placed my hand around the mans torn throat he treid to resist but could not. I could still see live in his eyes. there was so much blood, I saw then the lines on my arm begin to softly glow. They seemed to mix with the blood and tint it a slight blue color. Then they grew as vines tend to and pread across the mans neck and over his face still glowing. They wove around his neck and when they reached his eyes there was a flash, and they were gone. The man rose then, I cannot know who was more amazed he or I. ( alot more entries ) ( this one is undated ) The visions the keep comming but they are allways events that come to pass. I need to find what they mean. I have made this descision, I will leave Arvendur by boat and travel where the winds take me. ( dated 1284 ) They call this land the aegis tis a sutible place for my new home. ( the rest of the entreis talk about some visions that have happened, then about the undead and eventually the decision to find the Ascended and seek help ) To who every finds this send me a pidgeon ( mercury199 )", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary Of Jayrius", "piecup", "Well this is it. I finally got myself A diary after traveling to the old reed farm across the lake.   \n Today Alvaska was acting very strange...I found an odd orb after killing some.. monster. I have no idea what it was but I kept the orb as a tophy. Alvaska started looking at it and it made him go all crazy. They even told me that I ran away with it at one point. I think that just lying to me about that. Im sure I would have rememberd it.  Well that's all that I'm going to write for today. Oh, my birthday is coming up soon. \n I really hate that Burkeseter jerk...He really bugs me. He's so annoying. \nIm trying to convine alvaska to study the orb, I dont think it's working \nMy room is so small. I really wish that I could get a bigger one. It's time I go to bed. I hope that noone reads my Diary while i'm gone on my way to my room I saw some deamon! It's trying to break down the door. I dont know how much time I have left before it gets in... Well. I tried killing it then Alvaska. then it dissapeared. \n anyway...back to my room \n I just woke up. Im going to see if there's any work that needs to be done \n im going outside to kill the undead Im sorry that my writing is rather illigable Im not very good at writing.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary Of Jingle Claw", "kyleinator", "Dear Diary", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary of Mylas", "Architecus", "Hmm. Day One:  I ate a Sandwich.  It was good,  it wasn't made out of sand. I was dissapointed.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary of Pious Oakwood", "TheNander", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary of Zeruel Skov", "zeruel", "Day 1: Seeing the bright light of day again is harsh to my eyes, I may have to get glasses... Day 2: Al'khazar looks much different from when I was put into the deep, the walls are higher the buildings are more expensive, and the Minas dosen't go as far as it did before... I tried to get a job at the local mine, but now they insist that I get a permit! A Permit!? To Mine?! what is this? I spent years toiling in that work camp and now you say I have to BUY a permit to toil in it some more? rubbish Day 3: My minas are running short, I fear I wont be able to live in the city much longer. I spent the night on the street, can't help but think of those beggars from my childhood Day 6: I spent the last of my minas on some food and a pair of ruddy leather greaves, I decided to leave the city and head north, I know the undead carry the cash they carried from thier days in amoungst the living, Perhaps I'll find a nice place to settle and build a little shack. Day 7: first night in the wilds, its cold out here, perhaps I shouldn't have bought those specticles and bought a warmer tunic, haven't found any food yet, running low on reserves... Day 10: So cold, I struggle to write this as my fingers grow more numb with each passing second, no food, no reasonable shelter, I see crafting tables and torches spread around the landscape, it tells me that I am not the first one to attempt such a journey. I wonder the fate of the others before me Day 12: found a chicken, I killed it and ate it raw just to stave off the inevitable, encountered  the first of the undead, a group of zombies, moving sluggishly in the cold. I managed to evade them and continue north. t Day 13: surprisingly warm today, found a penninsula jutting out into a body of warm water, I suppose there is a god, and he has sent this blessing to me. I have discovered though that the further north you go, the number of undead I encounter goes up exponentially I found a makeshift quarry nearby that someone else started, I found his remains laying in the corner clutching a pickaxe. I took it up and did what I did best. I dug out a vast cavern Day 20: I feel I may just make it, discovering that I can recover the apples of nearby trees has done wonders, the cavern I have been digging has become very wide, but unfortunatly the stone below is far to hard to break through, my building supplies are growing very large Day 60: the Keep is completed, A simple wall right now, but I plan a much grander design. I managed to put in a small farm and plan to reenforce the wall. Day 65: built some shelters the cavern below is giant now, every so often I find the undead crawling from the earth and moving toward me, as if they know I live just above them. forged a sword from some iron I managed to dig up. was able to dispatch them with little difficulty. Day 70: Met another poor soul today, in even worse condition then I was when I got here, ran into a group of those pig demons, and was injured pretty badly. took him in and treated his wounds as best I could, but he passed shortly after, I buried him just outside the wall and came to the conclusion that I would never turn away anyone that came to my doorstep. I turned the keep into more of a monastary, I hope that I can at least be of some help to anyone that passes by. Day 93: I am no longer alone, It appears as though civilization is catching up with me, to the south west a large factory is being built, I question if this will bring more travelers. Day 156: the Factory has been completed i hear the men work when the wind blows in my direction, and indeed the number of people traveling north has increased, I can hardly keep up with demand. I fear that soon I must go further north, to escape the encoraching city. But that option is not without risk, I know the undead citadel is in that direction and the closer I get to the structure the more likely I am to garner notice by them. I must choose carefully. Day 160: I met with the people at the factory, and even managed to work out a deal with the owner to buy thier products at facotry direct prices, this will help with the demand, but I must admit that the sheer number of people I've encountered lately has been making me uncomfortable. Perhaps it is time to move... Day 180: I now have a neighbor. Alfin Who I am convinced is a dwarf, although it is hard to tell. my remote outpost is no longer very remote. I wonder how useful my refuge is now... Day 185: I have decided, to find more purpose in my life, I must move. I will travel further north, and hope that the undead don't find me. I will miss the people at the factory. especially Zyn, who has shown me great kindness. I intend to come back and visit often, but a more remote location is required I feel. I shall leave this diary and most of the supplies I have gathered here, in hopes that some will still find use for it. to anyone that reads this: I hope you will travel further north and find me in your travels. and to all those in the Factory, Thanks. you have shown me the first kindness since my release from the dark of prison. for that I am forever greatful.                                   Farewell", ""),
