        StaticBook("The Dragonborn: Prologue", "DecoLamb", "When Aegis erupted into life before the eyes of the Wandering Wizard, A dragon was formed from the magma and steam caused by the many volcanoes. As the dragon was formed from the volcanic magma, the Wandering Wizard let these dragons roam free, but over time they caused havoc and mayhem amongst the population. The Wizard, wanting to keep his land and people alive cast the dragons into an unknown realm. The dragons roamed this new land, it was there end, it was..the end. Some dragons found a ((stupid thing booten me D:< ))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dragonslayer Clan.", "Supertimmy4ever", "In a land far, far from Aegis there was a proud clan. it was the Dragonslayer clan known for slaying dragons. it was a great clan rich and powerfull with around of 1000 members. there was no war but also no peace, it was a gray era for the whole land. there where bandits and enemy clans, and the rulers where corrupted. the Dragonslayers made change in this world killed the clans and the Rulers. then there came a peacefull period, for a short time.... \n some Dragons of the notrth heard of the welthy clan and they came to kill... one dragon named Gortrok was the leader he killed half of the clan only for there gold my parents and a few members survived and flied to Aegis, on the way i was born. now i am here with no parents and no reletives, for now because there where survivors and i am gooing to seek them", ""),
        StaticBook("The Drake Family Lineage", "deanofantastico", "A list of known successors to Ulric Drake.\n \n Kair Drake : 1016-1064 \n Marus Drake : 1023-1087 \n William Drake : 1039-1052 \n Andas Drake : 1040-1093 \n Talan Drake : 1062-1136 \n Candas Drake : 1086-1139 \n Standar Drake : 1101-1176 \n Oxland Drake : 1148-1201 \n Ulric Drake II : 1192-1315 \n Robin Drake : 1229-1274 \n Robin Drake II : 1285-present", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dream", "Ohaythar121", "\n I fell into a deep slumber in my Grove, with only my nose sticking out of the tepid water. The minute creatures of this beautiful land swimming about my well-worn and tanned skin. THen, I entered the deepest sleep of my life. \n Once that undiscernable descent was over, I was sitting in a chair. A beautiful chair, carved with multiple trees, grafted into one another. All of the chair molded into a magnificent, supple work of art, as it seemed to almost breath under me. However, I wasn't sitting on it in the normal sense, I was hovering over it, only inches. But, whenever I attempted to run my ethereal hand along the grain of the wood, I just couldn't. Then, my head snapped forwards, my body settling as close as possible to the chair. But, the chair was not sitting in a room, or a finely decorated nook. But a void, indescribable. It wasn't black, or white, or anything. It was just pure nothing, unimaginable to the Aegian mind. I stared for what seemed like an eternity, contemplatign everything, yet nothing. It seems odd in retrospect, but at the time, I was feeling purly normal. Then, it was as if a rip was made in the void, a tear in the fabric of everything and nothing and out came, lo and behold a vine, like the ones living on and in me. It slithered out, and wrapped around my chest. It pulled me from the chair, and the chair dissapeared into the nothing. Then another tear appeared, and another, and another, and another. The surface of the void was like a 2 dimensional plane, constantly being ripped apart. And out of all of the tears, came a vine, and all wrappearound me until I could only see a green writhing mass. Suddenly, the vines dissapear, and I appear as I am now, in my leathers, covered in a collection of vines, living and breathing in my body, and on it. But, the void was gone, and in its place was a field. A neverending field of green, with grass up to my waist. So, I walked. \n After what seemed years of walking, I just stopped. I looked up at the sky, and, just like the void, it tore open. But, instead of a vine, out came a woman She was a comely elvish woman, wrapped in garb of plants. Just looking at her invoked a feeling of warmth, and comfort. Yet, at the same time, a sense of overwhelming awe. HEr hand slowly came down, glowing lightly, and tapped my forehead. And when it touched my skin, it was like everything beautfiul, and glorious, and wonderful in all of Aegis popped into my mind, and it was gone. In it's place was the Void. But, the Void was different, it had a different feeling I suppose. It's impossible to describe, it was like that feeling of when you remember something after thinking long and hard, but everywhere at once. And there was the chair. I slowly moved until I sat just barely hovering over it again. But this time, I drifted down, and sat in the chair. And when I did, Alk, my friend who had died only a few days before appeared before me. He was in the prime of his life, dashingly handsome, and proud. Beside him was my old companion Gruol, also in his prime. Both of them looked at me, I had never seen them in this time of their life, so I cherish the memory and they said, \"Sillion, do it, for us, for Aegis, for yourself.\" THen I awoke, and the sun rose over my Grove, and I knew what I had to do.", ""),
        StaticBook("The dream.", "GuhdarN", "I am dazed by this dream... I'm writing now just minutes after I awakened by a huge bang on the lowest floor, probably the door. But when I looked out of my window to see where the moon was I saw someone not far away from my neighbor's house. His face was hidden by his hood. He glared at me, these seconds felt like minutes... Eventually he turned his back and he disappeared in the alley. \n The dream, it was a nightmare about... My father. \n It was just like when it happened... When I killed him. I had no clue that it was a dream at that time. But I saw the dream outside of my head, as if I was an observer... Like a spirit. \n I could see myself awakened by the screams of my defenseless brother in the dining room. \n \n I was able to follow myself, I saw how I was thinking how I would put a stop to this. I saw in my dream how I took a large burning piece of wood from the fireplace, and how I thought that this was the best idea to end this never ending beatings by our father. \n \n I did not even spoke a word. Though it looked like the real me saw how I watched the event. It felt like \"he\" was looking for eye contact with my \"spiritual me\" and when he got it. He nodded... \n \n I was standing in the doorway when I watched this event that happened many decades ago. I had repressed it, also my mind was playing with my memories for some reason, I forget things easier. But now after this dream, I remember the death of my father like it happened yesterday. \n \n I could see myself beating him in the back of his head... Repeatedly. He did not even see who was hitting him. \n I kept hitting him with the wood, even when he was lying down... Lifeless. Until my brother shouted with verge of tears that I would stop. \n \n As I remember my father, he was a very large orc, nearly four heads both longer and wider than me. And that he did not care about no one except himself. But after an entire childhood with beating his children and sometimes worse than \"just\" beating. Maybe he was worth such a deat? \n My real me said load that \"Finally dis iz ohver!\". Thereafter he turned to my \"spiritual me\" and gave me a look, a look that was peaceful, eyes that smiles. I felt that I recognized those eyes, as if it was a different person...? \n \n While I wrote the last sentence, I shivered. Felt like that my spine become as cold as a gust from the wind of the Snowy Fields...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid Circle", "Respiren", "*Journeying (away >14days) \n Archdruid Swifthide (FTFY)\n\n Druid Longstride (-unknown-)\n\n: Wayward Druid Respiren (Respiren)\n\n Dragon Druid Apollan (Elite117)\n\n Druid Tharn Grey Wolf (fiercedragon)\n\n: Wandering_Druid_Mithrandir (CrunchySushi)\n\n \n\n Druid Cleric Mahten (urpenguin)\n\n Raven Druid Syn Valkerye (Xerxes_XIII)\n\n Raziel Druid of the Mist (Raziel_Farenhaal)\n\n Druid of the Quill Olwe (WhiteReaper) \n\n Guardian Druid Leul (DeathyGrim) \n\n Ner'Zhul Druid of the Fang (*orc) \n\nStorm Druid Tempir (BoltofFusion) \n\n Archdruid Rowan {Doma} (iBurn)  \n\nWild Druid Theyador (Harrfuzz) \n\n Makia Druid of the Horizon (TheMtDragon) \n\n Dawn Druid Maiavel (Maiavel) \n\n  Oasis Druid John (123devmo321) \n\n Druid Beastmaster Randar (yankee203) \n\n Black Druid Crow (crowbarr85) \n\n Druid_Guardian_Beleran (ShiftyMcGee) \n\n \n: Warden_Felore_Nightstalker (Pilotace1812) \n Druid Initiate Petyr (drplat) \n \n\nRedwood Druid Boney (mdhegs)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid Guide to Herbalism Vol 1.", "Respiren", "To see things in the seed, that is genius \n Lao Tzu \n \n -Herbalism- \n It is like the seed put in the soil - the more one sows, the greater the harvest. \n \n\n 'Gathering Experience' \n\n Sugar Cane 3 \n Cactus 3 \n Wheat 5 \n Flower 10 \n Mushroom 15 \n Pumpkin 55 \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n Herbal knowledge increases the nourishment of vittles\n LVL   Bonus", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid Heirarchy", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Demi-Aspect \n Heirophant \n Grand Druid \n Arch Druid \n Head Teacher \n Druid Guides \n Druid \n Druid Dedicant \n Lost Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("The druid soup.", "MeGoRage", "If you want to make a tasty soup that keeps you warm in these cold days, follow this recipie . Start by mixing together the two mushrooms in a bowl. Then you add, Water, salt and pepper. The next step, goes on if you want. Its about the taste. If you want a spicy taste, you should mix in some more pepper and a Raouk root root from the Raouk tree. The Raouk does a spicy taste, but keeps the original taste of 'shrooms If you want a more tropical taste, i suggest you crack some melon seeds and put in. They make it taste fresh and sweet, and its good for the children. And if you want a more meaty type you can put some grilled, spicy pork, that i suggest you make yourself. Then its a great meal, that keeps you full all day. You can also test putting in some fruits and vedgetables, like apples and good saplings. They will make the soup taste good, but aslo make you healthy. Ask me, Tennyson if you want more types of food books! #Tennyson#", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid's Guide To Herbalism Vol 1.", "Respiren", "Herbalism :It is like the seed put in the soil - the more one sows, the greater the harvest.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid's Guide To Herbalism Vol 2.", "Respiren", "Herbalism \n It is like the seed put in the soil - the more one sows, the greater the harvest. \n -Gathering Experience- \n Sugar Cane -3- Cactus -3- Wheat -5- Flower -10- Mushroom -15- Pumpkin -55- \n -Abilities- \n 'Green Terra' \n Take your hoe in your right hand, to triple experience and perhaps yield too. \n 'Green Thumb' \n Take seed in your right hand to spread verdure over soil and stone. \n Instantly replant wheat - with every 200 years of communion you may skip a day of wheats week .\n 'The sum is greater than the whole' +.1 chance for double yield every year. \n'Vegan Cookery' \n Healing bonus from bread and mushroom broth 50 years of gathering for a half-hearted benefit, another half every century, up to 4 health at 750 years. \n-Nurturing Growth- \n Wheat says '2 is company, three is a crowd. If you wish to sow, put me up to four from water and in a row. ' \nThe bones of the unliving will provide a meal of bread, raise the tree, and spring life from the soil. \n -A Royal Herbalist's Advice- \n Keep farming. The sun nearly always shines! Crops never cease to grow . Be ready to harvest all things in their time. And farm many things: Sugar Cane, Mushrooms and of course Wheat! \n -Prince Toren", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid's Life", "Elite117", "Enjoy some stew \n Talk with friends \n Watch the stars Dozes off to sleep", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid's Silverspoon IV", "Respiren", "\n- Mushroom Soup- \n A most delicious and nourishing broth, both for the hungry and convalesent. Rumours abound of Archdruid's who have lived unusually long lives by it's propitiate satiation, often becoming confused for oak trees when in old age, they acquire what druid's call 'Bark Skin.' \n Archdruid Hippocrates is often famously quoted, '*slurrp... Delicious, it tastes better every century.' \n - Preparation- \n Crush equal measures of Brown and Red mushrooms in a mortar and pestle, place in bowl, season to taste, no spoon required.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druidic Arcanum, Book of Spells", "Respiren", "Herein lies the Incantations of the Druids, by which the bard doth draw on Nature's magic.\n -Rank-\n-Ollaire [The Beginner]- \n Natures Touch - 1 Heart Heal to Target (3 Second CD) [10% Mana] \n Malins Wall - 3 Tall 2 Wide Leaf Wall (5 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n \nPeople of The Tree - Bonemeal 1 Spot (20 Second CD) [10% Mana] \n \n - Cli, [The Pillar] - \nNatures Grasp - 2 Heart Heal to Target (6 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n \nMalins Box - A Box Made of Leaves (5 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n \nPower of the Forest - Bonemeal a 5x5 Area (20 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n - Anruth [The Noble Stream] - \n \nNatures Vigour - 3 Heart Heal to Target (8 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n \nMalins Trap - A Box Made of Leaves w/ Cobweb in The Middle (5 Second CD) [20% Mana] \n \nPower of Malinor - Bonemeal a 10x10 Area + Blocks Turn to Grass for 10 Seconds (25 Second CD) [25% Mana] \n - Ollamh, [The Doctor] - \nThe Healing Touch of Malin - 5 Heart Heal to Target (10 Second CD) [40% Mana] \n \nPower of The Trees - A Box Made of Leaves w/ Cobweb in The Middle + Cactus on One Wall (25 Second CD) [40% Mana]\n The Power of Aegis - Bonemeal a 20x20 Area + Blocks Turn to Grass for 10 Seconds (30 Second CD) [40% Mana]\n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druidic Guide", "Saviordude", "It has come to my attention that they Druids are lacking in moral guidelines. Without such guidelines, there is a risk that a Druid might fall into an immoral style of living, freely worshiping Iblees without shame. So it is with that possible outcome in mind that I have written a short guide on how to live your life in accordance with nature. \n \n -Killing an innocent upsets the balamce of Aegis. Only draw arms against those who have malice in their hearts. \n -Worship not Iblees, for he defiles the land with his plague. \n -Mediate daily, both to keep a calm mind and a gentle soul. \n -Treat all of natures creations with respect, taking only what you need to get by. \n -Be happy with what you have, and steal not from others.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druidic Order", "Respiren", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druidic Order, Vol 1", "Respiren", "Druids divide Aegis into domains, defined by the mountains the rivers, the sea and the land. \n - The Circles - \n All Druids within a domain are within a circle, named for the area the domain occupies, or sometimes it's founder or the druid's worship.\n The members of a circle hold themselves responsible for the well-being of the wilderness and the continuation of the orderly cycles of Nature within their domain. \n A few traditions chapter have grown up to govern the harmonious workings of a circle: initiations, the challenge, the ban, the moot, and selection of acolytes. All druids, from the humblest initiate to the great druid, may freely follow their own interpretation of druidic beliefs and act however they believe best serves Nature. \n- Circles and Branches- \n There are often different branches of druid's in a circle forest druids, plains, mountain, desert and arctic druids...etc. \n -Initiates-\n The cornerstones of the druidic order faith. faith. They normally live in stone, wood, or mud-brick cottages and act as the protectors of a tract of wilderness or a sacred grove. \n -The Inner Circle-\n The inner circle contains nine of druid rank, three archdruids, and a single great druid. To enter the inner circle one must be experienced, a vacancy must open up, or the rising druid must be victorious over another in the druidic challenge .\n \n - Druids - \n A circle never has more than nine druids, though initiates are known as druids too. \n - Druids - \n A circle never has more than nine, though Initiates are often known as Druids too. Using druidic resources they agressively root out emergent threats to the wilderness within a domain. Druids attend the High Council of the Moot, and act based on the needs of the circle as a whole. Serving as a mentor takes up much of druid's time, too. It is their responsibility to initiate new druids into the Order. \n - Archdruids -\n Each circle can have only three archdruids and, as with the druid rank, advancement requires either filling a vacancy or winning a challenge against a seated archdruid. An archdruids role resembles that of a druid, with two differences. Archdruids concern themselves more with maintaining the balance of Nature, making sure no one alignment or ethos comes to utterly dominate the domain. Also, archdruids spend time training to step into the role of the great druid. To accomplish both these goals, they devote much time to travel.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druidic Poem", "Kahzo", "Roses are red\n Violets are blue\n This task blows ass And so do you", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druids", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Druids wield power over plants, animals, and the weather, not to include the elements. The protect the wilderness and maintain a balance between good and evil . Druids make their own staffs I got a look at their notice board, here is what it said: \n Nalfein = Offense: Killing Druids \n Vardak Offense = Repeated Possession \n Thork Offense = Murder of Arch Druid John \n Deltaro Offense = Abandonment", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dum Dum Potion", "Thatpyrodude", "Banok here, I have created a new potion \n I call it the Dum Dum Potion \n It makes someone a Dum Dum until they get the antidote \n Ingrediants \n 1 bowl \n 3 roses \n and many more things \n antidote: \n four Grftal flowers \n Cow hide \n Ender Pearl \n and one secret thing that I would rather not put it is in my head though *hands him the book", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dungeon of Daemon and Aemon", "Lomaticc", "Just before the turn of the tide, the Ancient servents of God, The Daemons, were cast into the world of Aegis to fill the core with precious metals. \nTwo brother Daemon's felt the need to inject the world of Aegis was both unwise and unworthy of such a young and hostile world. The two brother's , Daemon, heir to the throne of all Daemon's consulted with his younger brother Aemon on the matter. They were advised of God's planned creations of humans, orcs, dwarves, and elves. \nAgain, the brothers felt it was unwise to give such precious metals away so freely, the humans and their ease of being corrupted, the dwarves and their greed for more riches, the orcs and their hostile ways unappreciative of such precious materials, and the elves who the brothers fought over frequently on whether they deserved the right to such treasures. \nThe brothers took it upon themselves to alter God's plans and devise a scheme so that only the worthy of all the living would pocess the treasures of the Ancient world. Daemon set forth and from the ground ressurected the Great Tower of Daemon and Aemon , high and mighty, ever watchful for those worthy travellers to step foot inside. \nAemon took part in constructing a manner of how the precious metals shall be taken if a wor thy traveller shold take the risk. Aemon, a skilled strategist incorporated a long, twisting, mind boggling maze. Rooms filled with chests, and within those rooms even more rooms, until the entire underground was consumed with what is now known as The Dungeon of Daemon and Aemon . \nDaemon thought this was too insufficient and the brothers agreed that a worthy traveller had to know not only skill of mind, but also skill of hand to find the precious metals within. Daemon infested the dungeon with monsters from all around the world of Aegis. The deadliest of spiders with venom so powerful only the strongest at heart would survive it's bite. Pigmen who's screetch so loud that only those with the ears of patience would resist becoming eternally deaf. Zombies that ... well were just there to kill of anyone unskilled at fighting! \nLegend tells us that buried deep in the heart of the Dungeon is the only known exit. Few have survived it's darkness and many go mad before they are eventually slain by the monsters inside. Only the most worthy find themselves overwhelmed with the treasures hidden by the ancient Daemon and Aemon, just as they planned. \nCopyright @ William", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dusk of Man", "Jakbenimble", "The strength of man is a fragile thing, easily broken. Men spend their days struggling for recognition or power. They try to hold onto what they've got while reaching for more. This is why they shall never survive as a race. \n Men are divided by their beliefs and goals. They fight petty wars amongst themselves while their enemies grow. When their enemies finally strike, their divisions will be their downfall. The Dusk of Man draws close, and cannot be forstalled. When they finally pass from Aegis, what will they leave behind? Books of Knowledge which they find so precious. Monuments to their greed, pride and mortality. But these too shall disappear, as all things do, in time.", ""),
        StaticBook("the dwarfe fight", "cocokyle", "", ""),
        StaticBook("the dwarfs tale", "TWC7", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dwarven Army V.01", "DrZig", "Chapter One The Dwarven Army is an army of the most ruthless fighters! The Dwarves are the best melee fighters in the land! They poop and crap alot!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Eerie Spider", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "The Spider, a creature with 8 legs and piercing red eyes that glow in the dark. Because of the spider's size, it cannot fit through regular doorways, but can fit in passages with opposite integers to the door; for example, let's say a door is 1x2, 1 wide by 2 tall, the spider could fit in a space that is 2 wide, and 1 tall. A spider's hissing noise can alert you to it's presence, therefore you should know when one is coming your way. However, spiders can climb any surface, no matter how steep, making them extremely capable of surprise attacks from above. Spiders are easy to hit with arrows and swords, because of their size, but because of their nature, they jump around when attacking, increasing the difficulty of defeating them. Fighting a spider in a mountainous region almost guarantees your defeat, because it will jump after you, and because of it's climbing abilities, will catch up with you very quickly. \n Some spiders are said to let Skeletons ride on their backs, and this combination has been named: Spider Jockey. The Spider Jockey can move quickly, while shooting arrows at the same time, not to mention the ability to climb wherever it pleases. The Spider Jockey is very hard to kill. The spider's bite is not poisonous, but it's cousin, the Cave Spider's, is. \n The Cave spider, a very hostile version of the spider, is more dangerous for several reasons. The cave spider is much smaller than the regular spider, but retains the same speed and maneuverability as the regular spider, making it harder to hit. Cave Spiders also possess a venomous bite, that quickly invades the victims body and seeks to ravage it from the inside out, sickening the victim, and causes death if not treated. This bite can be cured by ingesting plain cow's milk. Also, armor does not effect the bite of a Cave Spider. Even if you had armor on, seek a healer's help immediately. \n -Salamandra", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elder Scrolls", "MamaLuigi412", "The Elder Scrolls are hidden in far away mountains to the north, trying to find them is a  stupid mistake, you will die of hunger or monsters even the weather would kill you because of how cold it is there.  The one thing that attracts people to it is that the power it contains, a unusual power which no undead or ascended have  known of. It is said that the power can control anyone or mess up there minds resulting in killing them self or other people for no reason.  The Hardest part is obtaining the scrolls, they are hidden in a huge underground shrine with mythical creatures guarding it, and many traps and puzzles along the way, which are very hard and mind twisting.  So do not try to obtain them, it would most likely result in death, a very painful one...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elder Shaman Brevias", "StandUnited", "Brevias, one of the many wonderful shaman in Aegis. Brevias, the man who can cure many illnesses, and many sicknesses. Good ol' Brevias, the one who entered the Nether, and survived to live the tale. Growing up from a young age, Brevias had a growing passion to become a Shaman. He would study for countless hours, hoping to reach is true potential. While practicing one day, he blinded himself, trading his sight, for true vision. So to speak, he can see through his \"third eye\" Brevias could see in a whole new way. He had to meditate on his own, for weeks on end, to gain his true sight. By the time Brevias was in his teenage years, he had comepleted his shaman trials. He secluded himself in the wilds, to spend his time communication with the spirits. He would meditate for hours on end, and was totally taken by nature. Brevias was achieving his goal from childhood. He was as happy as he could ever get. He was always smiling, interacting with the aniamls, and ever since, has been wandering. Now, he's in his 30s, helping whoever is in need, healing many, and following his dream.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements Of Harmony", "Harrfuzz", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements Vol. 1 Fire", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Fire has been an important part of all cultures and religions in the past to modern day Aegis. Fire is bright, strong, takes charge, and wants control. Fire is never subtle, it proudly shows itself. Fire never stops unless acted upon by another element or force, and it consumes everything it touches.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements Vol. 2 Water", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Water, the neccesity of life. All animals, plants, and even we, the races of Aegis, need it to survive. Water can often be associated with emotion, art, time, and especially healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements Vol. 3 Earth", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Earth is the first thing you need for almost everything, to ensure stability and endurance. Earth is a reliable element, peaceful and tranquil. Earth is the most passive and strong element, although it can be quite destructive.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements Vol. 4 Air", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Air is invisible, unpredictable, unreliable, soothing, inspiring, and destructive. Air is the representation of everything we cannot see; our spirits, our souls, our minds, and our hearts. Of that what lies beneath, or beyond some scholars say. The unpredictable and changing wind can become a devestating Hurricane, or a playful breeze.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elven Fighting Style", "silco97", "By:Ambros \nElves are probebly the oldest of all the races, and so they are the most well combat developed.  The created the bow and arrow as well as to what I belive forged the first sword. This book will explain to any one who wishes to know how to fight in the ways of an elf. Note that many of these meathods were made by me and are not truly the ancient elf way. \nChapter 1: The Discipline: The elven race is the most noble of the races and so has the most diciplined of the fighting styles.  All elven fighting styles have one rule in commen.  The rules of combat. \nRule 1-Respect your teacher \nRule 2-Your weapon is your guardien not your servent. \nRule 3-Self praise and over confidence is not the way. All these rules make up the elven code of combat.  There are many side rules and sayings but the main three are most importent. \nChapter 2: The Weapons: There are three basic weapons to the elven combat your fists, your sword ,your bow.  Now the three basic styles focus on these three weapons.  The styles will be listed later.  The elven sword is most commenly gold or iron but due to other influences iron swords are more commen now.  The fist is probebly the the most difficult to master due to its risk in close combat.  \nChapter 3 The Bow Style Or Rakurai: The Bow is what the elves are best known for and so it has become their signiture weapon.  Now the basic style suggests that you fire only a few arrows but each one is fired with great prosision so that only several aroows must be used. Now every arrow you fire will arch downwards slightly so angeling perfect is the key. ((It is said that holding down your fire key they will shoot faster. However when you rappidly click they shoot much quicker.)) ((Also when you fire an arrow at the enemy when it makes contact the enemy will flash red. At this while they are flashing red they are immune to arrows. This is why shooting arrows with persision is better then shooting with speed. Also each arrow will deal 2 hearts when hit)) \nChapter 4: The Sword: Swords are basic and easy to use as the diamond one seems most preffered amongst elves.  The basic elven sword of diamond will deal 5 and a half hearts of health per hit. while the golden will deal 2 and a half these are mainly used for rituals.  Elves also seem to prefer a hit and run techine by hitting opponint with a sword then backing up to fire some arrows. \nChapter 5: Hand To Hand Rather self explainitory much like that of a sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elven Map", "u000893", "Today I was out workin on thee docks when Gulik showed up with this weird map. When he showed me it was very vague and I couldn't make out any landmarks but it seemed to be coverd with elveish trees *shiver* I hate them Male Elves I hope soon to send a message to the dreaded elves not sure which one to show it to. Oh you scared me there Sorry there Gulik just knocked at the door", ""),
        StaticBook("The End", "susitsu", "The end is nigh, the undead shall take this land, it exists only because they are only biding their time They will come and take all life, it is the inevitable, those who do not believe will be devoured, t hose who do will be granted a more powerful existance The End is near.  The true masters of the land are coming to take it, Iblees the fallen will be the true god. PLedge yourself to Iblees and you will be brought salvation. All hail the Fallen One", ""),
        StaticBook("THE END", "abxyxx", "this is the end of me bloody holmes killing me", ""),
        StaticBook("The End", "Lokito", "Prophets have fortold of a great scourge that will attack our lands in the near future. Cities will fall into darkness within days and the loss of life will be unbelieveable.", ""),
        StaticBook("The End", "Sode1", "I have been dreaming lately. Having vivied dreams of fire and rebirth in these dreams i have seen our great tree ...it was burning... i also in my meditations have seen them, they are coming, some are good and will help us , some are iblees's helpers destroyers of forests and life . i speak of dragons the dark ones, they are neutral but are easily influenced by iblees's magic and are made to breath fire upon us it seems that there are two kinds of them, one usually large and dark with a wingspan of 2 blocks . the other red about the same length but more keen to do good , i hear the red ones are tamable, i have been studying alchemy with mania for a while and it seems that there is a new realm that has come into existance , the Ender also refered to as the end. These dragons i speak of come from there , perhaps an expedition there would grant us a weapon against iblees with mania being able to weild \"the tongue\" im sure this is possible perhaps we will be able to tame these beasts ! , magesticly soaring through the air on the back of a dragon.. Imagine That. Enough about dragons, there is a new threat, the undead will soon take this land . i hear rumors of a new and though it seems far from now it will come soon. i have already began preparing the boats will be ready, and hopefully my brothers will make it too, it will be a sad day yes, but there will always be a time of rebirth as for me, i will give this body back to the gods and be reborn in the new world of course i will be the same being, but not born out of a mother born from an eruption of fire and lava, as always. born screaming and steaming into the word if you read this it is probably in the new land, and you need not to worry for this new land is grea t you must embrace it and learn it, earn the right to be there not as a refugee but as a pilgrim this is the exodus There is no time for banditry the rich will need the poor and the poor will need the rich and yet those cowards remain in the arms of aeriel with all theire riches and the undead like bloody leeches at iblees's foot I bid you good luck reader, this new and is yours. *you see a fingerprint and a scribbled name it reads \"Fabelnight\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The End", "michavdgaag", "Dear Friends, \n Me and Heril leave this place in order to avenge the Death of Zoe. \n I do not think we will return, so I say this for the last time. \n Farewell my friends, now that we will allways be with you. \n \n See you soon Zoe... \n \n PS: Belyn can have my shop", ""),
        StaticBook("the end", "Demonxerov2", "ALL HAIL IBLISS, THE END IS COMING! THE END IS COMING! ALL SHALL BATHE IN THE BLOOD OF THE HOLY! NO ONE WILL SURVIVE! ALL HAIL IBLISS, ALL HAIL- at this point the author was execeuted.", ""),
        StaticBook("The End Begins", "masterjcr", "I am writing this from a tree in the Forests outside the Elven city in Malinor in warning for all th", ""),
        StaticBook("The end is near.", "Sledder", "As the thousand mindless come my way, they hunger for my flesh to tear away They want to eat my brain hear me scream in pain. Rip my chest apart tear out my heart They want me to join their army of the dead There is no where I can run and nowhere I can hide My fear makes me wish I had already died. Their soulless eyes hunt for me. From this nightmare I can not be free. As they slowly begin to close in I realize I cannot win out of weapons and out of time No escape that I can find I come to embrace my horrible fate I shall join the thousand mindless on this day.", ""),
        StaticBook("The end of Aegis", "sconn", "Some say the world will end in fire. Some say in ice. From what I've tasted of desire i hold with those who favor fire. But if it had to perish twice, I think I know enough of hate to say that for destruction ice is also great. And would  suffice.", ""),
        StaticBook("The End of Aegis", "William_Talbot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The End of Hope", "Xanivic", "It struck us... struck us like a bolt of lightning. None of the folk in Aegis knew what had happened. With the Undeads proceeding from the northern lands, the inhabitants of Aegis had no escape. Nowhere to run. Nowhere to hide. The womens' screams, the childrens' cries... The darkened sky casted over the land, somber. Griefing in agony and hopelessness.  After a few days of the sudden destruction near Oren, silence conquered. Aegis didn't speak a single word. The atmosphere was silent to the point where the only thing heard was the thoughts of a wanderer. He stood around 5'6. Bearded with leather rings choking the ends of his beard. He wore light brownish and beige armor. His face... his face had a distinctive scar that slithered diagnally from the left side to the right side of his beaten face. His right eye was a light green color. The color of the algae filled seas. As he walked the road to the Cloud Temple from Kalurugan, his thoughts were flooded with horror. A single tear streaked down his cheek as he whispered  a forgein language, \"Aley bastia.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The End Times", "Mingpow321", "I write this after returning to the Keep from Alk Khazar. I still see it before my eyes, the complet complete anihilation of every living thing. They won't stop before everyone dies. The Keep may be on one of the last safe refuges in all of Aegis. I yet hold hope though because I follow Aeriel and whe when I do die, because I surely will, I know that I have gone to a better place with her. I hope that before my time comes I can drop every Undead that crosses my path, they will die... This really might be the end, or maybe for some it is the beginning, I suppose it isn't my place to know but there is one thing I know for sure. Those who follow Aeriel shall always prevail. And now I take my leave, and to whoever is reading this I hope you take its words to heart for they are the tr truth.     The End by Arn Jarlsson", ""),
        StaticBook("The End: The Beginning", "Chrome_", "I'm part enderman. I wasn't born this way, though. Here's how it happened according to my remaining memory: \n It was a cold, stormy night in the land of Aegis. I was wandering around near Krugmar when I had encountered strange ruins. When I had started to explore them, I was running out of torches. When I looked backward to try and escape the winding catacombs and come back later for torches, I saw the most horrid sight I had ever seen. Desperate to get away from the demented monster, I ran headfirst into the darkness. The creature was nearly 3 metres away from me when I jumped into some strange contraption. Little did I know it lead to another dimension. I ran right into the creature's homeland. The End.", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_25(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The Ender Crystal", "BladeCreep", "The Myths of the Old Lands speak of a Crystal, so Powerfull that it controlls all Undead Though Wizard found this Crystal to be too Powerfull, so they shattered it, and spread it across the lands of Aegis. not yet. it's fucked up how?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Enderman Theory", "StrifeOr", "Hello . I am Strife Talados, and I will be sharing findings on a mysterious creature known as \"Enderman\".", ""),
        StaticBook("The Endermen", "Taxidermist_Dave", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Endermen's Curse", "anthrowolfgirl", "For whomever is reading this you've come across information that can be vital for your life.y As the title says, this book is about a curse that was to be never spoken of. The Enderman's curse, a horrible burden to your life, It has pained few people includin mysel Many people do not understand the strange Enders, only to kill them on site with out question If you have been able to kill one without a scratch, you my friend are lucky. Before we go on you need to know about the curse itself. The curse has different effects for some people, it can be physical or mental. The physical effects are the eyes, turning the color into the deep pools of purple. There is also the staining of the clothes turning them into a dark color. The mental is different. Insainity, rage, regret. These are the emotions thats you feel inside you. It is also the emotions of the Enders. Now you are probably wondering how do you get the curse? Well its only two words The End. No, its not the end of the book, its the portal that seperates life and death. Now is the time to tell you the story of how I myself got the curse. Before I settled in Galahar I travled with a small giuld. We were camping in the forest, then we heard a scream out in the distance. I reconized the scream. It was from one of my friends, John. We quickly gathered our swords and bows, and head twoards him. I soon realized why he screamed. We were falling onto a ravine, or at least I thought it was. We landed roughly, ignoring the pain in our body we checked to see if John was alright. George, our leader of the giuld realized that there were books and house like hallways. The other members looked at eachother and nodded, agreeing that we would explore. As we wandered we heard the teleporting of Enders fading in and out. I thought I was going insane. Finally we reached a room, it was strange, there were steps that led to a hole surrounded by stone. A stone that we've never seen before. As we studied it, we figured out the the slots in the stone could fit a Enderman's eye. We all looked twoard John, he had always collected the eyes and he had a collection. John nodded to us, knowing what he had to do. he slowly placed each eye into the slot, and each one that he put gave me chills on my spine. When the final one was placed we were pushed back by a powerful force. All I felt was pain and unknown rage, I had an intent to kill... I will never forget that feeling. After getting over the shock I saw George pulling John up from the portal. But his eyes, they were never the same grey eyes that always looked in intent. They were now the eyes of Enders. As I looked around to see my other friends and comrads, i tried not to throw up. Many of my friends were mauled from the lash of power that was emited from the portal. While others were, laughing insanly or just staring with the same eyes John has.. George and I looked at eachother and said silent prayers to our friends. As we walked back I saw my reflection in a puddle, what I saw vrought me to my knees. My ocean blue eyes that were so full of life, deepened onto a harsh dark purple. My clothes that were already stained with blood, were swirling with the darkness of the night but I felt nothing, only one emotion was clear to me, rage. As I looked at George, he knew that smething was wrong with him also, but he just smiled sadl y. After that night, we were never the same. After a few months my appearence became normal, and so did my emotions. but There was one thing that scared me. In the back of my mind I felt the curse put upon me by the Enders settle in, and I knew when the killing intent and rage would come. Once every three years. With that one time I will go through the pain I felt and relive the day we were cursed apon.   And so I tell you this my friend, dont ever underestimate the enders. If you encounter one of the portals to The End, I give you my dearests sympathy", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ent", "silco97", "The Ent are ancient creature that are belived to be the wisest of the creatures that hail from woods The word ent means Gaint as they are many feet tall.  They are often seen as trees with large stump like feet.  Often having a number of things growing on them such as moss and such they are at peace with nature and all that is of nature.  Many say the ents were created to protect the woods from any who wich to harm it.  Ents speak in a chanting like fashion rolling words. The druids have always seen the ent as an ally in protecting the woods they love.  Although the ents are in few numbers now.  The progressing of indutrialness has driven many from their homes and forced to die due to the lack of woods. Will ye put this in the library?", ""),
        StaticBook("The epic adventures of saxychase", "saxychase", "Well on my way to the Dwarven Capital .", ""),
        StaticBook("The Epic Book", "Crippledpope", "If you're reading this, you love undead, and noone likes you.", ""),
        StaticBook("the epic book", "Egg_Noodlez", "there once was a guy named johnny. the end :) then he farted new", ""),
        StaticBook("The Epic Tale Of Rinru", "sbenning", "Rinru was born in a faraway town, high up in the mountins At only three weeks old. his town was attcked. by the hooded ones that call themselves The Und.ead.  His parents were taken away by The Und.ead. and. locked. up in a prison He was the only surviver  \n Cold., hungry and. alone, he was taken in by a Dwarven couple, who  ad.opted. him He was then raised. as a d.warf for fifteen years By this age he realised. that he wasn't like the other d.warfs \n He asked. his \"parents\" if he was d.ifferent, and. they realised. it was time to tell him of his real parents After they had. told. Rinru what happened. to his parents, he mad.e a vow And. that was to avenge his parents d.eath \n At the age of eighteen, Rinru bold.ly left home and. set his sights on the capital of Oren The grand. city of Al'khazar After a week of traveling across the mountain pass he finally mad.e it \n There, he mad.e good. friend.s with Daniel and. Robert Banstir And. since Rinru had. no where to stay they invited. him to stay in a house of thiers by the arena Rinru stayed. there for about five years until he bought a room in the Drunken Dwarf's Inn \n He stayed. there for two year, but left as it was a remote area Rinru then applied. for a job in the Oren Guard. He then moved. into a room in Silverpoint tower in Galahar, which is owned. by the Banstirs untill he became a member of the Guard. \nHe then trained as a recriut for two weeks, manning the gate and partoll ing the city. Rinru was offered a place to be a full Oren Guard and accepted it. Not soon after, he was told that the dwarfs were being attacked by the orcs. Then the Oren Guard march in the help the dwarfs and defeat the orcs \n Rinru is now twenty-seven years old, is doing well in the Guard and was one of the only people who weren't injured when The Undead attacked Galahar.", ""),
        StaticBook("The escape of the Orks and Elf", "Telandriel", "Note: This book might include Dwarves at later times 2 days ago I went to live by myself, in the desert between the lands of the Elves and Orks . There I made myself a nice underground house and hunted some monsters . There I met two orks, both very nice. For some time we hunted monsters together. But then came the still unknown army and they killed us all and stole all our stuff . Then we decided to go together from that moment. Also, we decided to leave the big city's and live in the wilds. So that's how it all began. Two Orks and one Elf, fighting for their freedom, fighting for the Wilderniss, fighting for the North . End op prologue. Hmm, maybe it's end OF prologue, but still, continue. So we went out for the north on our way seeing many houses, we looted most of them, for most were deserted.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Essence of Magic", "Eric_Armadillo", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Essence of Todd Tanner", "Todd877", "This book is a plot device, used to make it so that my reroll character will know everything my previous character knew. If you find this book, please destroy it. This is all OOC by the way.", ""),
        StaticBook("The eulogy of Michael", "browler4153", "Michael was born into a family of many, 7 to be exact, he was the youngest of that family so he has many people to learn from. His father was an excellent human name Hunter and his mothers name was Mailor, But Michael was named after his grandfather . Then, at 7 years old Michael lost his whole family to Orcs when they raided his families farm in the north. He stayed at his families farm for years, surviving on his own by hunting and harvesting his families crops. Michael always had an ambition to protect others, since he didnt want others to have to deal with what he did when he lost his family. \n After many years, Michael left the family farm to go out into the world and seek a job. He was soon noticing that he wasnt getting very far, So he wandered along the kings road and he came across a mossive guildhouse made of dark wood, he saw some men inside and he told them he sook to join the guild, they hastily let him in and over the next few months he excelled greatly in the guild called International Army, but then, once he reached the highest rank a player could get, the orcs destroyed the guildhouse, as they had destroyed his home when he was younger, So him and the guild moved on, and after many weeks of spending the night in inns they finnally got a plot in Alras for the guild, the IA was disbanded and was turned into the Warriors of Aegis, and Michael became one of the 3 \"Lords\" or main leaders of said guild. He helped them build the guildhouse in Alras, where it now stands, and that is the story of Michael, leader, friend, guildmate, guildmaster, lord, and most of all, Warrior!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Evershifting Seasons", "ggt3416", "PREFACE\n This story is one I can recite word for word. It is a tale my mother would, on occasion, offer to me on sleepless nights. Here it has been rendered into verse to share with you Aegeans.\n \nThe Evershifting Seasons, a poem by Alys.\n \nMaidens four, \n Father Sun with his wife begot,\n Bound by blood and appearance alike,\n Tempers diverse as feather and rock.\n \nWinnitea the elder,\n Bitter and callous,\n Antithesis of the naivette,\n Sprea the vivacious.\n \nSomarea the volatile,\n Her passions rarely contained,\n By none other than Autea the gentle,\n Wisdom accompanied by a fertile mind.\n \nHis daughters the solar god adored,\n Dropped between them a contraption,\n Of which none ever bored,\n Entranced by its simple amusement.\n \nA clear barrier of winding contours,\n Flowing grains of yellow trapped,\n One was not enough for the four,\n Snatching desperately from sisters' hands.\n \nInevitably the toy hit the floor,\n Its fragments littering those sisters' feet,\n The grains flowed no more,\n Heralding sobs of dismal despair.\n \nOh how the sisters tried,\n Held out the hems of their dress,\n And dropped the grains inside,\n Determined to save their precious plaything.\n \nThus the sisters ran round and round,\n Collecting the sand as they went along,\n All in vain as it fell to the ground,\n Collecting the sand the last sister held.\n \nAs she runs by Aegis lands,\n Each sister a season makes,\n Forever gathering the hourglass sands,\n Her nature affecting Nature Herself.\n \nThe seasons' departure and return are among the few certainties of this world, next to the inescapable death of every mortal. With each shift of the seasons, they guide us towards change and flexibility. Although the sisters are forever cursed to gather the numerous grains of sand, dropping them as they go along, some grains do remain and the four's efforts accumulate slowly. Thus, we too, should keep walking, even only to end up in the same place, because every spring, summer, autumn, and winter is never quite the same.", ""),
        StaticBook("The existance of a being named Kalen", "501warhead", "My life has been a confusing one \nTo say the very least I shall start from the begining \nI was born to a human family My father was a blacksmith My mother was the one who cared for me in my youth \nShe was a wise woman, he was a stout, strong, well-built man. \nHis face was marred forever with ash \nHer face was kind and loving as she delt correction. \nWhen I left them, my goal was to be like my father \nI struggled in the wilderness to build my life \nI tried many a time to get a job, but alas twas not my fate to do such \nI journeyed through the wilderness daily, killing creatures as I went . \nOne day I was killing monsters and I found a trench \nI decided to follow the trench \nAfter a while I found a elf and a masked human working on the trench I started to help . The masked man shouted at me to leave, but I told them I was only there to help. The elf agreed with me and the man calmed down. So I began to work on the trench, and the elf and man walked off. \nLater the masked man returned, impressed with my work . He asked me to join a group called the 'Rangers' \nAllow me to clear it up, at this point you probably know they they are \nBut the rangers bad name came from their leader, NOT the people under him. \nI agreed and became a ranger. I was their smith and engineer, knowing the art of 'Redstone' quite well. I progressed up the ranks rather quickly . \nI trained often, becoming skilled with the sword . \nOne day we heard of a threat for the north - near to us. We began to amass a army, prepare for war, and finally armor ourselves \nThis threat, though we did not know it at the time, was the undead. \nBut alas!Our encounter was never to be with the undead. We prepared, but dought began to creep into us . And then the night came... \nPeople were sick of the command of the rangers, the masked man, Nords. He was tyrannical, and even we the rangers saw this. \nThey amassed a military force and set to end us. They beset upon us and attempted to kill us all. \nWe stood strong, prepared for war we slaughtered all who came. \nThe elves eventually became involved, but still were not a match. \nEventually the wizard became involved for the humans...and slaughted us all. \nI barely escaped with my life, and eventually found the elves. they spared my life on the condition I help them take down a bandit camp. \nI agreed and I went out to bring it down, we killed them all. \nWe took vengance for the fallen guards of laurelin. \nThe elves were thankful for my help and made me a honorary memeber of the 'Pathfinders'. \nEventually, from running atop the trees, and practicing with bows. I became agile and my form adapted to my new comrads. \nI was almost a elf, and still am not fully a elf. \nI gradually progressed up the ranks, getting to the 3rd highest rank after Blackthorn.  \nDuring this time some of the pathfinders went out banditing, and earned a terrible title for the pathfinders. \nSo people began to hate us, and I saw this. I did NOT want the pathfinders to be the new 'Rangers' \nI confronted the other two leaders about this, and we decided to change our name. \nWe became the Wardens, and I was the third in command of laurelins military. \nAfter a while I was in Kal'Alras, and I was approached by the Supreme Judge, Syrio Forel. \nHe told me about the corruption of the goverment, what was wrong with it. \n he asked me to help fix it. \nI agreed and contacted the high prince and Prince Flefal, and we set out. \nWe approached the current Overseer, Rasun, in a council. \nHe steped down and Syrio Forel became Overseer, and I helped build the city of Alras. \nAnd so this is my life up to now, I hope you can benift from this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Expedition - Dycarean", "loliwannaplay", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Expedition Journal Of Dolir The Deathless", "monkeychez", "Day 1- There have been rumors of an \"undead presence in the north, i am heading that way now, out of Laurelin, to go and see what i can find! Day 2- I am leaving Laurelin with some coal, iron tools, and a handfull of torches. Apparently, some Elves hinted me that the clouds only move north. So, that is the way i'll head! I am staying in an Elve's abode, in the outskirts of Laurelin I was told of the destruction to winterfell, caused by the undead. The Elf gave me a book of the destruction. It described the horror scene that occored in Winterfell, bodies charred from fires, rubble... and apparently the undead left portals there. I must head to Oren now, to get direction to Winterfell. Day 3- The Elf has dicided to come along on my journey to Oren. Day 3- We met a priest on the way to the Human's capital. He told us that behind Al'Khazar is a road to Winterfell, and they are in the works of rebuilding... Mabe some clues are still there... Oren is much larger than i remember... going in what seems like circles. Day 4- Got lost in Al'Khazar, going back t the king's road for directions. Day 5- After looking around for life in Al'khazar, nobody was around. So i began to leave the city when a man came running through. I chased him into the woods, only wanting to get directions, but he got away. He lead me to a bridge that lead to one of my race's cononies. I am heading there now. I lost my Elven companion... I hope he is alright.... Made it to Kal' Ras", ""),
        StaticBook("The Exploits Of BlackThorn Vol.1", "BenjaminKayEight", "I Set together the wardens (then known as the pathfinders many moons ago but unfortunately i had to leave for lands afar befor it was ready while i was away in this far away land i met many foul creatures all of which i managed to destroy with the little supplies i had while i was away i left Atles my 2nd in command to look after the pathfinders unfortunatly several pathfinders whos names have been cast into hell itself were destroying the pathfinder name by banditing making the people of the land think we were all bandits, so the conclusion was made to put the cretins on the kill on sight list and change the name of the pathfinders, and so the Wardens were born!. after this matter there was an invasion by the undead horde during this invasion my faithful 2nd in command Atles dies in battle leaving the inexperienced noble Kalen in charge. After this battle with the lack of command the wardens started to fall into disdane. But after many moons The fateful leader BlackThorn (Me) returned to bring order to the wardens and teach Kalen the ways of Leadership, making him my new 2nd in command.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Explosive Order", "Clausij", "The Explosive Order is devoted to the worship of Sssboom the creeper god. Members of The Explosive Order are asked to create images and statues of Sssboom to celebrate him and create places of worship. The Explosive Order was founded in this realm by Clausij Anarion after spending 500 years in Sssboom's realm far beyond the stars. There he learned everything about The Explosive Order and was instructed to bring the teachings of Sssboom back to his homeland of Aegis. If You wish to Join The Explosive Order Seek out Clausij and if he deems you worthy you shall be allowed to join.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Eyes Of Vardak Begining", "Vardak", "Test", ""),
        StaticBook("The Eyes Of Vardak. Begining.", "Vardak", "The eyes, started out as a curse given to me in an unfortunate event. After I assisted in crushing the rebels, I was tasked with taking down the ruins. I did so, but before I had gotten there. Undead had appeared. They were channeling their spells to bring a portal into the world. I killed them, and reached for their staves, in that instant, the staves flew into my body. They exploded inside me and released raw chaotic energy. I passed out. \nI woke up. Staves in hand and my eyes glowing a dark red. I could feel the energies overflo wing out of my eyes, covering portions of my head, flickering like a flame. After a while, I adapted slightly to my eyes. I had found their use. They allowed me to track Undead. \nFrom that point foward. I named them \"The Hunter's Mark\".", ""),
        StaticBook("The Eynon family", "Benboboy", "The Eynon family has a horrible pas, he Eynon's are a very big family and many years ago worshipped Iblees, They were huned and killed so mos of he family fled ino he world. They hid heir rue names from everyone. A few generaions laer, he Eynon's sared using he name again, as mos had forgoen hose days. There are no many lef in he Eynon family ha remember hem oo, even hough he Eynon's have a very long lifespan because of heir elf gene carried from faher o son.   The Eynon's try to forget their terrible past and are haunted by it still. They do not worship Iblees any more, and hope that one day the family shall be together again . The Eynon's have many secrets about the undead and of Iblees but do not share them with the world .", ""),
        StaticBook("the fall of dawn's bakery", "sconn", "Dawn's bakery is a mess. It is infested with life. The only way to solve this problem is to kill Dawn Perea. Meet me infront of the bakery right now.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fall Of Snowy Fields", "RustyJusty123", "Snowy Fields was once a bright and spritual little town. The lords of the town made the come to life. It was a happy strong town, Yet the undead lurked around. The day everyone was worrying about the undead building a keep not far from snowy fields. Yet people stayed and defended the town and stayed on guard. First stay of war: Snowy Fields falls, people flee to Alkhazar or Alstion. Second Day: Undead leave, come in@ hail", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fall of the Doma", "iBurn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fall of Wrath's Clutch", "Zezimus", "This book is a personal recount of the events that occured before, during and after the Battle of Wrath's Clutch. While, I cannot say that I know all that happened on that day, I will tell you everything that I know, in hopes that this will one day be viewed by the historians of Aegis. \n Wrath's Clutch had been a menace to the citizens of Aegis for many long years. Soon after I arrived in Kal'Urguan, I heard a number of different stories of Wrath and his undead army and how they captured unwary travellers, torturing them inside their fortress, whether for information or just sadistic entertainment. Even the Dwarves stuggled to hold back the tides of undead as they forever grew in power and terrorised the settlements around Kal'Urguan. \n I first came face to face with the undead during the siege of Kal'Urguan. I was just a regular citizen back then but with a strong will to fight. I took my position at the main gate and listened as the screams of the undead grew ever closer. I watched as the guards took their positions along the walls and the Elven Wardens marched in to the city to help with defences. It all happened very quickly after that. A guard was killed right in front of me and as I tried to push forward, an arrow struck me in the  eye, leaving me unconscious for much of the battle. However, I soon recovered in time to join a counter attack on the shores of Wrath's Clutch. The attack succeeded in driving the undead back to their fortress but we sustained heavy losses and I, along with another Dwarf was forced to hide in a cave as we waited for more reinforcements. I eventually managed to return to Kal'Urguan alive and well. The city was filled with celebrations of our victory but little did we know that this was only the beginning. \n Around a week after the battle, it finally began to look as if organised action was taking place against Wrath's Clutch. The Elven Wardens had built an outpost in front of the fortress, while the Dwarven Legion was deploying soldiers to the front line. I had begun starting my training as a guard of Kal'Urguan so I got the chance to volunteer for a scouting mission into the fortress. With me, were a couple of guards a diplomat. It was our plan to gather whatever information we could to discover what Wrath was planning. Skirmishes had already taken place throughout the day and it was looking as if the fortress would soon give in to our attacks. We climbed up the back wall of the fortress and entered inside through one of the towers. From there, we entered into a room that just happened to be opposite a room where a meeting was taking place between Wrath and his minions. We overheard that they would soon be leaving the fortress if they could not defend themselves any longer. Determined to make sure that they would not get out of the fortress alive, we attempted to make our way back to Kal'Urguan. However, as we were climbing back down the wall, a figure approached us. At first, I did not recognise the face but I could see the dark, disfigured face, staring up at me. As we all stopped climbing, the figure cried out in rage. Lightning struck near me and I was forced to dive off a tower and into the sea. Thankfully, we all survived the encounter and met up at Kal'Urguan but I was informed that the figure had been Wrath himself. He now knew that something was wrong. \n On the eve of the final battle, I joined with the diplomat who had scouted Wrath's Clutch with me to inform the Elves of Wrath's plans. We traveled to the Warden's outpost and informed them that they should be ready to attack the fortress soon. The Elves agreed and we returned to Kal'Urguan, feeling optimistic that something was going to be done. However, upon our return, we were informed by the Lord Marshall Thorik that he had received a message, informing him that Wrath now planned to launch an attack on the Warden's outpost. It was now, inevitable, the final battle was about to begin. \n The Dwarven Legion was mustered together along with any volunteers that we could find. Orcs, humans and elves traveled from across Aegis to join an ever growing army that would soon launch a final assault on Wrath's Clutch. We gathered, armour weapons and supplies and met up outside the walls of Kal'Urguan. From here, we marched upon Wrath's Clutch with victory close in sight. Upon reaching the fortress, ladders were raised along the sides of the walls so that we could climb up and enter into the centre section of the fortress. As I entered, I saw the Wrath's minions flee into the lower sections of the fortress, as I tried to shoot them with my bow and arrow. The initial attack had overwhelmed them and they had been forced to hide in the caves below, leaving hideous beasts to deal with the attackers. The fight was long and bloody. Wrath and his minions eventually returned to the surface, in an attempt to hold a last stand against the allied forces. However, it was no use, his minions were overwhelmed and he was soon slain by Chaecus Braveaxe of the Dwarven Legion. His fortress had been overrun and it's walls began to collapse under the pressure of the battling armies. Under the combinded power of the armies of Aegis, Wrath's Clutch was finally defeated. \n Despite, the great victory for the nations of Aegis, things did not stay peaceful for long. The fall of Wrath's Clutch was overshadowed by the deteriorating situation in Oren, while the Dwarves and Elves began to dispute over who should take claim to Wrath's Clutch. While the Warden's were forced out by the Dwarven Legion, the remnants of Wrath's armies continued to plague the land, infiltrating cities and spreading the word that Wrath still lived. Whether or not this rumour is true or just a creation of his  supporters, I do not know. However, I sit here now, gazing upon the ruins of Wrath's Clutch, remembering the great battle that took place that day. I am now a Legionnaire in the Dwarven military and I write this book in hopes that it will inspire others to fight against the undead hordes and protect Aegis. Let it be known, that with the combined power of all the nations of Aegis, evil can be defeated!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fallen Flower", "Bubbli", "The tales of this story aren't that of fantasy, it does not come to that of a happy ending. This is a tale of a quiet little halfling, a flower, stolen from the garden of life much to early. Twisted and Tormented from the life she once knew. From the happiness and peace she once knew. The young white Lily began to be tainted in blood to now her petals are torn and stained red. \n The day began as any other. Lily, tending to her wheat fields in the town of Dunwood. But this was not just an ordinary day. For when the night falls on this day, her life will never be the same. \n A request from Dawn's Bakery came in for a small delivery of wheat. Normally the Halflings of Dunwood wouldn't deliver such a small amount. But Lily couldn't disappoint Dawn, and from her own garden gathered the bits of ready to harvest wheat, and set off to delivery them. Part ways there she came upon two cloaked figuares. Lily, always fearful of strangers, tried her best to take a longer route around them as to not get there attention. She passed the sandy fields, and just before the Golden Harvest area came to her sights there they were again. A man cloaked in gray and aman cloaked in gold. They slowly walked towards her. Lily began to open her mouth but could not speak, a foul stench of rotting flesh surrounding her. Frozen in fear, she did not know who this men were, but it was if her feet were shackled in place. And before she knew it, they were inches from her. \n A voice like no other came from one of them, the air around her grew cold. \"Overlord, why did you take such an intrest in such a weak creature as this?\" As the man in gray turned his head to the other. \"I'am not to sure Prophet, but I do not ignore that gift of sense that was blessed to me by Iblees.\" I did not know nothing that these men were talking about, all I knew that every fragment of my body was screaming for me to flee. I clenched my fists tightly and with every ounce of energy I had left in this small body of mine turned and ran. But I knew. I knew it was to no avail. As if by magic many monsters appeared in front of me and grabbed hold of me, as to be controlled by these men, I tried to scream and couldn't, it just began to get darker and darker, until I was just surrounded in complete darkness. I was not to wake for what seemed like weeks. And when I did, I was surrounded by the sounds of creatures screaming.  The lava was pouring from every wall, the smell of fire and ash surrounded me. But this was only the beginning to what I was to deal with. Nightmares isn't enought to describe what I was going to endure. I was to suffer what seemed like years of torture and torment, by these two men. I don't remember much before that or after that. All I remember now is where my loyalties are. I serve only for Iblees. For no other God saved me from those times. The things I have learned from back when I was mortal no longer matter. All that matters now  is to serve the Master that took all my fears away. I'am no longer timid, shy, worthless, or weak. I have been given something much more. More than anyone ever could offer me. I will show others what I have been shown. And they will understand that in this world there is no place for weak beings. This is the first Volume of my stories. The beginning of my new life. A life that is deprived of living. Being reborn as an Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fallen King", "KuroiHonoo", "The King has fallen, \n Edmund has fallen. \n He abandoned his children, \n He abandoned his city. \n  \n \n The portal summoned, \n The Undead rising, \n Al Khazar belong to Ibless. \n \n \n \n Hope decended, \n A miricle to all, \n Aeriel herself appeared! \n \n \n \n The portal was sealed, \n The Undead retreated, \n Our temporary peace reclaimed! \n \n \n \n However, Chaos remained. \n The kingless kingdom argued, \n We toil over who will reign. \n \n -Neutral Grey", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fallen Shadow", "SimplePancake", "The Fallen Shadows are a group of people who are masters with a sword . They are extremely strong, and have a very good sense of battle. If they ever need assisstance, they will call on their teamates, and will have archer support. These soldiers have a decent amount of command over the council, but in matters of war, They have command over almost every person . These soldiers are the commanders of the Shadow Knights, and have full control over them . In Times of peace, these soldiers shall go over to the undead to help prevent the countless. In Times of peace, these soldiers shall go over to the undead to help defend the countless attacks against them. If these soldiers do not follow command from the leader, there will be punishment. Punishments -1. Slavery", ""),
        StaticBook("The Falos Family", "XSilverWolfX", "The Falos family has lived in the northerner part of Aegis for centuries. My great ancestors moved here to seek refuge from a warlord in another Kingdom farther North East. Most of the Falos family were just regular farmers. One of them my Great Great Grandfather though was a great wizard. His name was Tysp Falos. Tysp was a man like no other. He was born into the life of farming and at the mere age of eleven years old he left his family's farm to seek a new and better life. Even though Tysp's Father warned him not to he hated living on the farm. He found the small frontier town of Winterfell where a local inn keeper took him in a gave him shelter. One day a strange hooded man came to the inn. Tysp listened as the two men talked in low voices. When the hooded man opened the door he was shocked to see the child. He shoved passed him and wen't on. As he walked out the door he dropped a note. As Tysp was about to tell him he read the title \"Mage Gabe Dead, in Search of Replacement\" The next day Tysp left the inn and followed the snowy tracks of the mysterious man. After days of traveling he reached an enormous Tower and more smaller ones below it. As he went on somone grabbed him by the arm. It was the hooded man and he was overly shocked to see the same boy he saw a few days ago. He brought him before the ARch Mage himself to see what to do with him. A few days later Tysp was a mage in the achademy learning the ways of Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Families of Duralsavot.", "ZazarusDious", "Silvermein : Ameth : Bronzehammer : Durzus : Ga'zud : Stonebeard", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fantastic Girl volume 2", "gombie", "Me wake up 1 day. Me eat cerial flakes and milk. I run on road and see guard. Me say hello .Then i want to cerial flakes eating. End The", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fate of Kal'Urgan and The Dwarfs", "Awesome0Person", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Feared Creeper", "danyn2907", "The Creeper (\"Creeperus Explodius\") is truly but a humble creature when left alone.  But when frightened the creature responds with a natural self defense- or defense to others.  The creeper's defense is triggered when agrivated.  It triggers a small spark to be created in the throat which goes down a small thread-like organ that triggers the Tienti Organ near the creeper's heart. This creates a chemical reaction to take place- similar to spliting a pixel. This causes all the things around the creeper to burst into a flame- invisible to the elvern, human, dwarvern, or orcan eye. \n Creeper Safety \n As we all know the creepers are one of the most dangerous creatures to roam the lands.  But over the years scientists such as myself found out some patterns that creepers seem to folow. First creepers only attack if they can sense you with their \"eye holes\". They are not quite eyes but sensing organs that detect movement within a 10 square block radius. When these foul beasts do attack however, they straif to the left as if avoiding your strikes.  If these creatures get behind you... Hopefuly the monks are back... \n Creeper Diet \n Creeper's seem to not live long enough to require an actual meal but when they do they preffer to eat either the coal out of the stone or munch on some sulfur. \n What entertains a Creeper \n  Creepers are very fond of- Riding in Minecarts\n Killing Itself \n Killing others while killing itself \nCreeper Variations\n After recent studies I have concluded that if a so called Creeper is struck by a single bolt of redstone radiation (also called \"lightning\") it's Tienti Organ becomes super charged and the creeper becomes mad with a urge to kill. It is suggested that anyone who witnesses such a phenomenom should stay as far away as possible from said creeper. \nCredits\n I thank the Creeper for letting me watch it over a long period of time and and my partner Relok'oth for helping me find said creeper.", ""),
