        StaticBook("The Final Memory Of Icarus", "mattr41018", "Icarus, An Elf hated by many, loved by few... I am writing this to my very few friends among the wardens, of which I have not the time to name. To them I leave my Holy axe. I feel as if the shunning force that sent me away, was the fact of my injinuity. It lead me to disobey orders, even if they were crazy... Some might ask, \"Am I sorry?\" The answer is no... I am not... I am not sorry at all. My experience as a waren lead me to be tougher, stronger, better, faster.... I will never forget this time... My holy axe is in the Initiate chest...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Final Words of Robert Banstir", "TheImpulseHQ", "This is Robert Banstir, of House Bannist... I dont have long left, they are coming for me, i can already feel the thunder striking, wait, silence, my guards are dead // I dont have Long, the Undead are after me after i killed one of their order. They will torture me and make me reveal where the Mormonts live, No, i must die I will get Majester, i will tell him i am already dying, he will stab me through the chest quick, painless They are breaking in, Majester is with me, i must - The Book is burned from here on-", ""),
        StaticBook("The finder of this book can trade this in for full access to my citys skills training, 5000", "Reckreation", "minas anda free home!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Findings of Aegis", "PyroFuzion", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The First", "Bal0rCIM1", "The First person who found the Undead city goes by the name of Balorcim The Ascended. The date of the founding was on July 10th 2011! help P.S. OOC: That last line HELPm I meant to type -help. Shut up! lol", ""),
        StaticBook("The First Book of Alriet", "Aceeri", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The first Mackay expedition to The Verge", "WWIflyingace", "\n I have found a portal outside the cloud temple that leads to a new land called \"The Verge\" The Verge is an island off the coast of Ageis and very near to the edge of known exploration. Sensing an oppertunity, I grabbed my supply box and packed up. \nI have vetured through the portal.  The strange magics decided to drop me in a cave, some 60 meteres below ground.  I trekked onward, discovering massive ruins. The ruins appeared to be of an ancient library, its books long since rotted away. \n After what I believe was three days of wandering in the subterranian labyrinth, I have finally found a giant staircase leading to the surface. \n This land is huge!  After veturing off the island with the labyrinth, I laid eyes upon a bustling commotion of colonization.  Most of the colonists were intrepid dwarves, setting up new enterprises.  I have walked past their land claim into a small desert.", ""),
        StaticBook("The First Tournament of the Arena", "TheGiver17", "The First Tournament of the Arena is an epic tale. It was a fierce battle between the Blue Team and the Red Team. \n   \n  The Red Team started off by winning the first battle, but soon after, the Blue Team went on to win four straight victories, and then several more thereafter. The Red Team was destroyed. \n This left the Blue Team members to fight amongst themselves. There was Leafwind the  Strong, Ademas the Terrible, Veritable the Wise, Balin the Hammer. The team members were reluctant to fight each other, but there was no turning back. The great comrades Leafwind and Ademas were up first. It was an astounding battle. Ademas was hardly putting up a fight. Leafwind's quick slashes instantly slew Ademas with hardly any contest. Poor Leafwind felt sad for his friend, but warriors must move on. Next up was Veritable and Balin. The two battled fiercely until the end. It was extremely close with Balin almost slaying Veritable, but is was the latter who came out on top. \n For the Final Round it was Veritable versus Leafwind. The battle commenced immediately and Leafwind took the upper hand with his quick strikes. But Veritable was putting up a good fight. The two were gasping for breath and bleeding openly when it was Leafwind who struck the final blow... \n As Veritable fell lifeless to the ground a deafening roar from the crowd drove out all sense from Leafwind. He stood motionless for a few moments until it all became clear to him. He could now hear the crowd chanting his name, \"Leafwind! Leafwind!\" The King Perea came up to him and awarded him his prize of 10,000 minas. Leafwind was the First Arena Champion!", ""),
        StaticBook("The First Wisethorn", "sconn", "The creator made the world and all its inhabitants. His own breath lives inside of us. We are created to prove our pureness. But before us there were only the trees and flowers on Aegis. But the trees and plants were not always as they are. When the creator made great mountains and filled masive ocains he made the first tree to inhabit Aegis. This tree was the only living being on Aegis at the time. It had red stringy leaves and almost black wood. Today we call it Wisethorn. The creator observed the growing numbers of his new species. The Wisethorn trees were not like the trees we live by. They had a mind of there own and a gift to feed of sanity. They talked to eachother . Sharing information. They were such an powerfull being. Soon the creator made a choice. The trees will only bring to much knowledge to mortals. And too much insanity. The creator could not risk it. He looked at the huge forest of them. The trees suddenly caught on fire. The cried to eachother of the pain. But the creator was meryfull and soon decided to give them a quick death. The tree were gone. All but one. The creator came to it. He did not want to loose all his work on the species so he left one. He knew that it will reproduce so he crumbeled the earth below it. The tree sunk into the dirt and stone. It was left in the dark searching for other beings. It was still just a sappling. So it waited. Listening to the thoughts of the new born people. Gaining knowledge beyond our own. It knew everything. It was the ultimate source of knowledge. But it had no Wisethons to share it with. So it sterted learning the language of mortals. It could not speak it. But ocasionaly it had a short connection with a being. It could have been a wolf or pig. But our minds were harder to get in to. I was the first human to get this connection. It told me everything i am writting in this book. The Wisethorn told me the place it was burried in. And i eventully found it. It was something i never saw before. I took it to Al'khazzar and hid it in my house. I ocasionally get another connetction. The most recent one told me that the creator took away its power to reproduce. Now i raise money for a sanctuary in which i can learn the secrets of the great Wisethorn. Hopefully i will soon find others that wish to learn about the Wisethorn. It will need some time to grow tho. Let us hope that many will join and the Wisethorn will reveal everything. (the rest of the book is covered in bloo) It has shown me my end. I must leave.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Five Spirits", "Toastersaurus", "The first spirit was called Entan he was a spirit of earth. His voice was deep. He told me of how people are always taking parts of him and his friends to build shelter and he can't do much about it. A few times he has shook to scare those people away but they continue to take from him anyway. The second spirit was of a simple baker who murdered and robbed. Her name was Athena. She said she had a simple life with the man of her dreams. They were planning on having children. But one night as she was closing she was stabbed. The bandit looked her in the eye. She said he was a goblin or some kind or dark elf. He had yellow eyes and he watched her fall to the ground as she was bleeding. He then smashed the windows. Then she was just left there to die. The third spirit was another person who had died. But he was a great warrior. A human called Randalf His final fight was in a duel between him and the Rex. Mograka'Gorkil shattered his armour and didn 't fight fair in Randalf's eyes. He was then decapitated. Randalf looked at me with anger and then vanished. The fourth spirit was called weeper. A spirit of air. He had a whispy voice. He was very closed up to me and didn't tell me much. He seemed to dislike me. I asked him why but he simply screeched and disappeared with the wind. The final spirit was a spirit of fire. She was called Sizno. She seemed rather insane and kept talking about how she could destroy me. And other people. She then circled me in a big fiery ring. She wanted to know about me and I told her many things. She then said she was uninterested and Left with the flames around me bursting in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flow", "LoKeenx", "Natures cynical ways are like an ocean wave. The tides eb and flow consistent revolving cycle such is the way of the world. Nature gives the blessing of life, and takes it away, for the gift of life is not eternal, it too must flow away, like the tide. One must become part of nature, and embrace the cycle of life, and then become part of it. This is the flow, of every existing thing.", ""),
        StaticBook("The FOA New Recruit Guide", "visualjaw", "Welcome new recruit!  \n \n If you are reading this guide, you have most likely been enrolled in the Follower's of Aeriel! This guide has been written to orientate and guide new recruits. Upon acception into the FOA, you should make your way to the FOA Encampment in the North. Once there, you should talk to an Officer who will guide you through the induction. You should also don your chosen FOA uniform at this point. \n \n The Officer commanding your division will now assign you to some quarters. Your next actions should be to seek training and teaching from an Officer. You should also familiarise yourself with the encampment and all of its facilities. They include: \n \n The Farm. \n The Library. \n The Workshop/Smith. \n The Medical Tent. \n The Barracks. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Followed", "Javelberg", "The first thing that hits you, is the dark. The never-ending darkness laid out before you. They say it drives men crazy, oh the screams. The screams of tainted souls all stuck in  realm of neither life or death,Forever doomed just waitin g... Waiting for what you may ask ? Nor you or me knows the answer,but sometimes traveller i can hear them,hear them whisper my name.. In the darkness they call out to me,tring to eat my very flesh and bone, chewing feasting. I can feel them long for my soul! I know it is only a matter of time..Blood..blood is what they hunger for..\"We are nor living nor dead. We are the chosen, The breed of eternity.\" Those cursed words they...they repeat and repeat inside my mind! I not sure..i..the tunnels,they seems to never end! Tunnels of pure madness and evil . They call me the \"walker\" for what reason i do not know. A wanderer, some stranger, to al that i meet. The spirits, they call to me, on by one... and one by one i fight to drive them off. There walls..the terrible walls.. The darkness is a blinding sight  yet it makes me feel enlightned far more than before. And the silence,the silence who tears the very sense out of your mind. I was a man once, a mortal just like you traveller...with a family, friends, I had it all.. but that was before that night. \"That night\" i tell you was the day i lost it all.. my home burned.. my people massacred.. Well, some where lucky, and were able to survive for a little while.. My family did not have that fortune. My wife was first, Torn apart by some sort of device, it tore her limb after limb,i could do nothing more than to watch in pain and silence.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Follower's of Aeriel ranks", "tigergamer", "The ranks go as follows from highest at the top and lowest at the bottom. -The FoA Commading ranks- Enlightened Guide's General - Head of FoA Commander - Second in command, Only answers to the General Major - The rank below Commander Captain - Rank below Major -The FoA Officer ranks- Lieutenant - Has command over the Recruits and Private's Corporal - Under the rank of Lt. -The Fighters of FoA- Private - A member in the FoA guild Recruit - A member in training to become a Private of the guild -Special ranks of the FoA- Architect - Incharge of the buildings in the keep, and building them Medic - Heals injured people and incharge of the Medical section -The FoA divisions- Resources Milita Search and Rescue, Fortifcation, -FoA Allies- The Enlightened, The White Ravens, Others against the undead. -Guides- Garn - Justicar Selina - Seeress Shoi - Preceptor, Zephyr - Guardian, None - Praetor", ""),
        StaticBook("The forbidden Magicks.", "Wolfie_Seekar", "To my Readers: this books contents are dangerous, if you don't wish to risk your life for power, toss this in the nearest fire, and forget it ever existed.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Forest Cleansing", "CONORDUDE8", "The Elves Have many traditions, Many Involving nature, but their most significant... The Forest Cleansing: \n Elves forest are prided on beauty, many clean and perfect, to uphold this, many have preformed The cleansing of the Forest \n This sacred ritual is Often told to be dark, and evil, and is believed to be Unused since High Prince Native came.\n \n To perform this Ritual, you must mix Glowstone and water, to form a thick brew , You then must mix a spider eye that has been fermented, and poor the brew into the roots of the Tree, You then Must wait to a full moon, and then Stick the handle of a staff into the bark. \n Then, The High Druid must Chant Ancient beliefs, Mainly of Dark elves, of the moons Powers of Many\n It is Believed the Hide of a cow must be pasted over the largest root, and the blood of a... Dark elf, must be pasted over the Hide, and Shielded from all Water, and sun. \n Then, it must be Struck by the energy of the clouds,  And It is then believed that the Forest Would be guarded from all Dark energy, For 500 years, and it msut be repeated again, one day.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Forging of the Blade", "firespirit44", "The hammer strikes the steel, forming the soon to be blade, \n \n It tempers it, tames it, creating an edge. \n \n It goes to the fire then back to the anvil the forging renewed. \n \n Shape and edge created its the perfect union of soul and steel \n \n Then to the oil, the steel drinks hungrily desperate for life \n Its taken to the stone, the process almost complete. \n Its sharpened to perfection, honed to completion. \n The finality of the blade, the completion of its edge, and the epitome of perfection. \n With the blessing of Urguan it is done.", ""),
        StaticBook("The fortress is on its way. The walls need to be bigger for defence against any force", "SkittleGhost", "Supplies are low for the walls. Mining is becoming a problem as there are no open mines close", ""),
        StaticBook("The Founding Dream", "Saviordude", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Founding of Masyaf: Chapter One", "Meet2012", "The Brotherhood was founded on the beliefs of honor, loyalty, and sanctity.  Goleth , the guild's founder, traveled to the grand city of Aeriel on a business trip.  Upon arrival he came upon a young elf by the name of Ev.  Ev had been on guard duty, and had been having trouble with the local Templar society.  Their leader, Titus, had been disobeying the laws of the city, claiming that being the leader of the Templars was above the position of any town guard. \n Many citizens had filed complaints with Ev, telling of attacks and unlawful entry to their homes. Even denizens from beyond the city walls had been having problems with him. \n  Ev and Goleth spoke for a long time of Titus' power-drive, and decided that he must be brought down. \n \n End of Chapter One", ""),
        StaticBook("The Founding of Masyaf: Chapter Two", "Meet2012", "Upon confrontation, Titus blatently denied every case that had been stated. When Ev spoke of being attacked, Titus claimed that there was a monster behind him, (on the well lit town wall) so he was trying to kill it. Titus called the other Templars to assemble, bringing forth eight armored knights.  Ev left at that time, not wishing to start a war. \n Shortly after the accusations, Ev recieved a report that Titus was seen leading two undead minions through the town.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fourth Book of Alriet", "Aceeri", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fox As Herdsman", "monkeychez", "Once on a time there was a woman who went out to hire a herdsman, and she", ""),
        StaticBook("The Free Word of Oren", "Pepernoot", "Greetings, I am a citizen of Oren. I write this because I think things should change. As you probably know the Oren politicians have one goal in their life, Personal gain. They do not care what happens in the kingdom, as long as they are safe,  and their purses are filled with Minas. The best example for this is the fall of Snowy Fields, and Alstion. They could have helped, but the king, nor the high pries, nor any of the elite helped. Many people lost everything they owned, some even their lives. \n A few days ago I was in Al'Khazar, and I could not believe what I saw. The princes had a tea party right on the main square. There even were clowns and jesters to entertain her. Shouldn't this money be spent on recruiting and training the guards to a force the undead won't laugh at. This is enough for now, I will keep writing for as long as I can. \n -\"The writer\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The future.", "Bgrape", "I have seen it. I have seen the day that Iblees has been revived and destroyed the  world. Many shall die fighting and the rest shall run. 5 and only 5 shall win the war against Iblees and his legions of the undead. The first person is and elven druid. The second is a fierce dwarf. The third is humble human. The fourth is a strong orc, and finally a pale faced man. The world shall be reborn if they win and Iblees shall be defeated yet again, but if they fail the world shall die and be covered in blood and darkness for all eternity. From the Prophet Demor Novee.", ""),
