        StaticBook("The Gems -Quest", "darkjames", "This quest needs you to obtain 5 gems \nThe gems must be obtained from enderman...the foulshades that roam at night. \nif you  obtain them, talk to the herald. \n \n \n Now you got them! Great! if you didnt, dont read. \nNow go search for 5 beefs of cow, and 5 spiderweb. then come to the herald. Ehmm \n \n \n \n Great! Now the last part, go acquire 1 iron and 1 map[or compass] and then Bring it all to the herald!  Lat Want quest?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Genesis", "generalrex1", "In The Beginning God Created The Heavens And The Earth. Now The Earth Was Formless And Empty,Darkness Was Over The Surface Of The Deep, And The Spiri t Of God Was Hover Above The Waters", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ghost Children", "Happy_Go_Unlucky", "A long time ago, an undead strayed from the path. Looking for a victim, he made it through the dark. He walked across the forests, tainting in his wake. And came across an orphenage, he took the bait. The children laughed and played, in the morning sun. Little did they know, the undead was a-coming. The monster made his move, his skin was much flayed. He cut the little children. One by one. The matron came to see, a downfall of the glee. She too was cut up. Dun dun dun. Now the little children, and their matron too. Haunt the olden orphenage. Boo, hoo. Hoo.  Help us. ----------------", ""),
        StaticBook("the giving of kramoroe", "kwakamungus", "I Malco, past mayor of the town of kramoroe give owner and lordship of the land to Warlord Mogroka Rex of Krugmar and any who appose this will have to see to Warlord Mogroka signed Malco Camp Elder of The Traviling Merchant Camp they were beneath thr fort", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Gift", "monkeychez", "First of all, i want to thank you for picking up this book, and seeing what is in store for you. This book is a tale of the grandest gift of all, the mind. Beings such as you and i, are blessed with such an advanced mind, that i couldd write this, and you could read it. The reasone for this is because you were hand picked, by a higher being, as many call him, or her, or whatever you believe in: God. Now, there is a reasone God put you in this positione. Otherwise, you would be a cow, or a pig, or some lesser being that cannot comprehend the amazing gift that we were bestowed at the time of our births. And what does God want me to use our mind for? You might ask. Well, your destiny is is your work of art, your greatest feat, that others will look upone when they see you. When you become a very important persone, or a homeless persone, fighting to live each day. You need to think of one thing when your destiny has been carved, and set into the stone of life. \"Did i use our Godlden gift to its limit\"? And any way you answer that questione, remember onee thing: what you do in this life, is what you will be remembered for. Done't waste your talent, your oportunity... Your.. gift. Live your live one the great green grass beneath your feet to the fullest extent possible. And remember: there is always someonee watching your actiones. erase one", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Harvest", "freakout286", "Hello, boys.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Trail", "Alectriciti", "There is a tale of a Golden Trail. \n The trail is walked upon those who prevail. \n The path is so narrow unlike other roads. \n Walking this path is like speaking in code. \n \n \n  \n Don't walk down pathes that return only pain. \n Those pathes are so wide like an infinite plane. \n \n At the end of the trail, we'll be so tired. \n But we will be greeted, praised and admired. \n \n We won't be strumming harps or have dumb wings. \n Glory awaits us with wonderful things! \n \n We'll be wrapped in clothes oh so delightful. \n It will be new to us, yet almost frightful. \n \n The world at the end of the trail above. \n Welcomes all creatures who are bound to love: \n Patience, kindness, selflessness, joy, \n Life and laughter to each girl and boy. \n \n \n I can't walk this narrow path all by myself. \n I need a companion beside this wood elf. \n Someone to keep me on that path compelled. \n Only one person. You, Rhisereld.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golem Book Joke Book", "kevins87", "a rolling Golem Gathers No Rust 1. What is Black And Blue And is going to show you the definition of Pain I Put The G in GOlem hahaha.3", ""),
        StaticBook("The Good, and The Bad Chronicals", "CorprlSkyler", "WARNING: This is a true story. And a journal of a Drifter... \n Chapter: 1 The passed few weeks have been odd... I have been the best man I could be, inbracing the great good inside of me! I have done many things to help people. Though now I am poor... I have givin minas to the orphanage, I have wanted to give clothes to them also... But the High Priest couldn't let give it to them for me. It was need to be presented by the k by the King, or Senschal. \n I have givin a 1000 mina home to a man, for free. I have givin a man 500 minas becasue he was new to the World of Aegis... And also help him find an apratment to live in. But now, is it all for nothing? I do not know... I wish to be good, but will evil over power me before I am cured perminantly? \n Chapter: 1 \n I mean Chapter: 2 haha Evil seems to overcome me, it seems as something is swallowing me... Evil seems chasing me, it seems right for me... While I was hunting, a man came up to me and laughed, he said \"You carry a stone sword\" I said back to him \"yes I am a poor man\" He said \"May Iblees bless you\" and gave me obsidain... I was praying for light after that. Another man came, a man in a black robe... He asked what I was praying for, I said \"They seem to huant me\" I told him about what happened earleir. He said a man like that gave me this. And handed me a pice of hellish dirt, I do not know how to explain it. Then he said search,, and walked away... I later asked him for a another clue. He said I should search for a group... That was it. \n Chapter: 3 I am now the Twilight Drifter. I am too different, I can not blend in. I must be cured, or fall to the curse of evil... I need help, and soon. I do not know what to do, other than talking to ascended, maybe I can join them, and become the man I am ment to be. I do not know if they will accept, in my state of condition. I am a mixed man... If they do not accept I may fall into Undead hands... I hope for the best, and I pray more often. But I can not hold off much longer. \n My name is Skyler, something only old old friends know. Sometimes I forget about it and I do not think it is my real name, but it is. This book is to remind me of what is good and bad \n ((BAD GRAMMER/SPELLING INTENDED))", ""),
        StaticBook("The goose", "orishmark", "Once there was a lovely goose there was no hope so he let loose He came back on one dreaded day and found out he he some egg to lay these eggs turned out to make some new born geese then these were later eaten by some meese it's... special", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Book Of Greed's Hand aka Dice!", "Charles_Grimlie", "Simple steps to play against house (single player) pay house 50 minas, then roll a 20 sided die ((/roll 20)), winner is determined depending on who has the highest number! To play against more people (multiplayer) pay house a entry of 50 minas, when all players pay house will tell everyone to roll, everyone will roll a 20, who ever has the highest number wins the pot to keep the business going house will always extract 25% of the pot for his own profit.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Cathedral of Kal'Uruguan", "blackhawk77g", "The Grand Cathedral of Kal'Uruguan was built in 1302 and finished in 1308. The Cathedral is complete with a masterfully build water flow system, a grand altar and several other quaint features that will impress the most bitter of guests. By 1313 a priest by the name of Gordok (also known as Gropier) suggested that he build a shop in the outer courtyard area to help increase the amount of church funds and increase his own wealth. The request was granted and now \"The Little Shop by the Altar\" resides near the entrance to the Cathedral. Also located in the outer church area is the Kal'Uruguan Catacombs. It is there where the cities dead are laid to rest. To find out more about the Cathedral, feel free to come visit anytime! Donations are always accepted!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Central Trade Station", "Martin123martin", "The Grand Central Trade Station or GCTS is a way for people to trade their items that they might fin d or make on a regular basis and and quickly sell them to the public. In other words, it is an autom ated way for a person to sell their items at their own price to another person by coming to just one", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Champion", "xXMrAkatoshXx", "The champion was born in a village near eastern Kal'urgaun his family was porn and barley had enough food to survive", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Guild of Stone Masonry of Aegis Handbook", "kanokarob", "Introduction \nThe Masons exist for a single purpose, to build for those who hire them. erase", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Task of Ambros", "silco97", "I am setting of today into the wilds to begin my task.  I must live in the wilds for 1 elven week and the only thing I may bring is this book 1 loaf of bread and a wooden sword. I hope i may become humble by doing this and learn what it mean to become one with nature. \nFirst day of Travel \nThis will be my first day of travel before my task begins.  I have eaten well so I was not hungry although i fear the night and what it has in store for me. I have made a small hole in the earth to stay in for the night.  I would never think i would spending the night with worms and mice until I was dead.  But here I am doing it, I will have bathe when I return. I am camping just outside of the small not so well known village of Talun.  It was a nice village beside the fact that no one was there \n2nd Day of Travel \nI wake up to a dawn of wet mud and worms.  A pleasent smell........ I have gone through much progress toady.  I have crafted torches with wood and charcol. I have also killed several birds for there good meat that they have on their legs.  I tryed to kill a wild boar although it was thin and under fed and it had no meat on its bones. I have also made a wooden sword out of a rather short oak tree and find it to be wounderfully flimsy.  I have dug a small hole of dirt and placed torches inside of it so I may have light to write in it.  The worms are still around me and still give off the smell of wet mud.  I fear if I dig one more hole I may turn into a worm me self! My eyes feel as if sand if layerd on them and are closing ever so slowly.  I must stop writting and sleep a bit for next dawns travel. \n3rd Day of Travel  \nas I wake up to a orange morn I hear sheep and cows not far off. this will be my last day of travel before my trial will begin. I came across a crater filled with a purple rock and netherrack around it.  I seemed to have hit the ground with quite a force to leave cuch a hole.  Near it I found a dinky little inn called Harrens Hunting Lodge.  Quite a wounderful little site so see in these woods. I came across a massive city with stone walls and a wide moat.  Never have I seen it but my is it grand.  I did not enter incase that would be breaking the rules of my task but I was a sight to see.  I have also entered the frigid north.  The crunch of snow now fills my ears, it is a nice sound to hear as I have not been up north for many years. when I was diggin my hole today because the trees were pines and are bad for climbing .write I found a chunk of coal blocking my way.  It left my hands black from its ashen dust. The ground here is hard and is hard to dig.  I will have a shallow hole tonight.  So cold infact the my normal worm freinds that I have grown found of are not here.  Worms are simple creatures. Why cant we be like them?  I do not know, they seek what is best, not what will bring them pain. \n1st day of trail \nI woke up early today eager to start my day of trial.  Bur I hear the sound of a spider out side I must make a quick escape while it is away I killed the fuzy little vermin.  With a wooden sword! I came across some ruins today up north.  The wet snowy land they sat in had grwon moss on the ancient stone of which they were made of.  Many years ago they must have had some good architecs I dug into a tree for tonights shelter.  It was a small tree just big enough to house me.  The plush leaves under my aching feet is going to quickly make me doze off. \n2nd Day of Trial I woke up when it was still dark out today.  Although I hade a nice dreamless sleep with much rest. as the northern spell began to ease into soft rolling hills I felt at peace to get away from that blasted north that I had grown to hate.  Although the rolling hills were not as they seemed. A flat plain of grass with stumps were trees once stood dotted the landsacpe.  I looked in horror, who do such a thing and defile the land in such a way.  I quickly ran to the nearest tree, which was severl miles away and planted the seeds I had knocked off of it.  Let us hope they will grow. I also came across a hole of a hobbit.  It was wounderful, cotten walls and wooden floors gave it a good feel.  Although I hit my head on the roof several times because of its lowness. I dug another hole to stay in and found my olf freinds again sticking out of the wet mud. Although the ground here was not as wet.  It was dry, at least the smell is no longer here. All land is diffrent, like us as beings of Aegis, but we all have one thing the same, we can grow. I woke up rather late today.  I must be getting use to this way of life.  I do enjoy sleeping in dirt. I have netered a land untouched by people.  The air is clean and the grass is a glossy green pleasent to my old eyes. I came across a large city like area far from the normal populated area of Aegis.  It was not well built though.  vines grew from the cracks in the bricks the buildings were built of and sand seeped through the cobblestone street.  I could not dig a large hole today, my back has a sharp pain and my hands are covered in bliters.  What task have i gotten my self into, a truly large one. I must press on upon the next morn.  I feel the whisper of life and nature getting louder. Arg I forgot to title today.  Any who read this the time i write \"I woke up today\" is were \"Trial Day 3\" should be.  i hope I do not conffuse my self by writting this.  I am very tired if i am doing These small errors in nothing more then writting! \n4th day of trial \nAt last the final day of trial.  I am sad though, i have grown to love the free lands of Aegis. Ack I ate a leg of a raw chicken.  It tasted foul and I had to go release my stomach in the grass the other days meal pouring out. I do not feel good, i am out of breath and my back can hardly move with out making the noice that bones make when they crack.  I must rest I have been walking for a bit now and my legs are bent as they can no longer support me.  My food ha ran dry and my mouth craves water to quench it. I have sat under a tree, be no means a large tree a simple pak tree with a short trunk. Just tall enough for me to sit under.  What relife for my back and feet.  Although my stomach still aches,  the trees fruit has given me food.  The trees wood is strong and will make a good staff to take the journey home with.  I have broken a branch to carve a staff with, using my small wooden sword I have widdled away the dark oaken bark to show the light colored wood A cool breeze has come to me while I widdle.  tommarow I shall set off for home. I must have fallen asleep under the tree for it is morn, as I got to my feet a seed fell from my lap.  This tree has served my needs well, I shall never forget what it has done for me.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Adventures of Tegchen", "ikeyman232", "It was the 3rd of the first seed. A cold and harsh day, with leaves and flowers attempting to bloom, despite the frost. Little flowers, struggling, burtsing through, their color bursting with light. Above the bakery hut, in a small apartment, a baby was being gifted from god into the world. A father in horror, watching his wife go through the pain and agony of birth. Wonders of life do not come free. As the baby arrived, the sun bloomed its first rays on the town since winters . beginning. The baby came out with blond hair and light hazel eyes. The baker and his wife raised the baby until he was 15, when he finally was confirmed by the pastor of the village parish. Though, this confirmation was diffrent from most others, as during the confirmation, Tegchen began to glow with a holy energy. The pastor began to get a little afraid, and stopped the confirmation early, saying Tegchen was good to go. When Tegchen left that day, he took all the belongings his parents gave him, and began his journey. Quite the holy journey, this will be. When he left on his way, he decided, he would want to settle in a small town or village, not a town. He felt correct in a small village, because he never was interested in cities. The first town he came across was the town of Nox, a small Human merchant town. As Tegchen was a Human, he was greeted with open arms there, and began a job as the  priests apprentice. His job was to ready all candles, write small tomes for children, and help the priest with ceremonie Tagchen continued along as the apprentice, until he was aged 20, when he took over the church. As this was the only church in town, he was the High-Priest of Nox. On his very first day, the church was robbed. The holy symbol of Aeriel was taken. He aimed, to take it back. The first thing he did, was search for clues. He did not tell anyone, as it would alert the guards, and as he was very smart, he knew the thief would know. If the thief knew, he would run farther. Tegchen knew that he wasen't far off. Tegchen then remembered, what happened that day, in the church. He focused his energy as hard as he could on a piece of tattered cloth he found that was hanging from one of the pews. He channled his energy hard, and soon enough, he saw what happened. He was dealing with too Orc thieves, who were going to sell it to buyers for 5,000 minas. He then found out where they went, a small cave outside the town. He called for his apprentice, equiped his stave, and pulled over his cloak. The apprentice was to run the church for the time being. Tegchen left the town, and made his way off to the cave he traced it to. The cave was dark as night, and he could not see a thing. It was very damp, and he could see a stream running through the sides of the rock, eroding it away. Day by day, night by night. As he delved deeper, he began to see light, and crouched over. He could easily see, these were not the Orcs to be messing with. He then got up, and his anger overtook him, and he confronted the Orcs like a fool. \"I Demand you hand that back to me. Now!\" he shouted. The Orcs laughed, and nodded their heads. \" Chu shoulda nev come tu dis place.\" the taller Orc stated. They came closer, and closer, until he could hear the mighty breathing, of what he thought was a boa r He could not take it any longer, and enraged, he started to glow with that holy light that one day. The Orcs luaghed and charged. Tegchen developed a small ball of light in his hand, and amazed, he threw it at the bigger one. It hit him directly and made him fall back a little, except he got right back up, and came swinging.  As both Orcs lunged, Tegchen generated a small ball of light on both hands, and combined them for an epic blinding light, and when the light subdued, all he saw was two lifeless bodies of the two Orcs that had messed with the wrong priest. He then picked up the symbol. Put it in his bag, and walked out into the blinging sunlight.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Ale Conspiracy", "LROWNAGE", "Our story begins in a small human town, not important in any way, shape or form. And our lead character, a small and rather chubby dwarf. He went by the name of Oltri Harddigger, but was more commonly known as Quicksilver. Quicksilver got his name from the fact that he was the one man who owned a quicksilver sword. He found it when rooting around the old ruins of an Aengul worshippers' temple. He was the land's most famous and successful detective. His deductive powers were envied by many other investigators and companies. One of his most famous cases is that of the old ale brewery by the edge of the town. Residents affectionately call the case \"The Great Ale Conspiracy.\" It involves the old lady who lives down the road, one Mrs Adleson. She came pounding on Quicksilver's door asking for his help. As he would, Quicksilver sprinted down his stairs and opened the door. Old Mrs Adleson must have been in a hurry, as she hadn't changed out of her nightdress. She quickly got to the point. \"Mr Harddigger, I need your help! I hear odd noises coming from the brewery!\" Quicksilver knew the brewery had been shut for a long time, 7 years in fact. He replied, \"I'll give i' a look oveh Mrs Adleson, no need ter worry yerself.\" He strolled over to the brewery, allowing himself a small smile. Mrs Adleson was the only one who didn't call him Quicksilver. He thought to himself \"Mrs Adleson's gettin' old now. 70, old fer a 'uman. As he neared the brewery, he remembered why it had shut down. The owner, Joe Savon, had left unexpectedly and the place had been left to rot. He neared the front doors and quickly turned to the left, nearing a broken window. He climbed through, patted himself down and looked around. Broken kegs, rusty tankards, but nothing out of the ordinary. He walked swiftly around the large room, surveying all he could. After a good 10 minutes of investigating, no answers jumped out at him. He left the brewery and headed to Mrs Adleson's house. He found that she was not at home, so he left a note on her door telling her of the emptiness However, that next night he found that Mrs Adleson was knocking at his door once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("the great battle", "colin1389", "i was buying some more bread when darkness fell the sky was lit with flash of light as we sreams of tairer come for the dwarf capitl. smoke rose from the city. the pleople around me gasped in horror some of the men said we must go help. so we gather some weapons and food and set off. we ran and ran. we finly got there the city was in ruins. then i saw some thing out of the croner of my eye. it was a gaint! some of the men ran for cofer. the other who stay attack wildly at the beast. it hit hard knocking some of the men out. kill one other. are attacks seemed usedless against the beast. i herd something like a canon fire.it was a canon! it hit the beast. it fell to the grond dead. we cheard. it was over. the end.", ""),
        StaticBook("The great Battle of Kal'Urgan", "Starsweeper", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Battle of Kal'Urguan", "Starsweeper", "This is the tale of the Great Battle of Kal'Urguan, long forgotten but recently discovered to be  true \n It was a dark November day that hellish Fall. The High Council room was silent as the King entered it. As he sat down the Archbishop Candor said with        a grin on his face, Yer Highness, It be so good ta be seein' ya well again! I took charge O' the council while ye was     gone.\" The King replied with a horse voice, \"Tat be good, ten let tis meeting be started.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Book of Psychology", "1337Sammiches", "When you think about psychology, you probably think about psychotic people. Psychology is much more than a way to diagnose someone with a mental disease. Psychology is the study of the human mind and how it works. So, let's begin with our first lesson: Manipulation. For some, it's easy to manipulate the human mind. It's all about perception and how you look at things. If you pay close attention to the behaviors of a person, you can find out their quirks. Now, if you take those quirks into consideration, you can really get into someone's inner thoughts. If you notice they have trust issues, throw out a wild idea of why they do. Usually, they shoot down that clam, then confess that they had issues as a child, or something like that . Now you have something to work with. Take this information, then keep repeating the wild claims until they spill all of the information and then you can truly know why they have issues with trust. Then, you can prove that they should not worry about trust.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Crusade", "Fluffy5", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Jourey", "LaGeG", "Leokin started off in his world as a wandering soul with his brother", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Seed", "LordCtmon", "Chapter 1 The Begining \n \n In the time of the creation of Aegis.A seed fell from the sky,however it was no ordinary seed .It was the seed of life which fell into Aegis that grew into the tree of life,which all races were born,the Humans,the Orcs,the Elves,and the Dwarves. All these races expanded over the lands,but one race was never discovered. It is the race of the pumpkins. The Pumpkins had the shape of a human,but their heads were Pumpkins.They speak human tounge and are powerful fighters! \n Chapter 2 The Discovery \n I was out traveling when I stumbled apon a book. This book was torn and ripped. It took awail to figure out the information inside with the  rips and tears. What I found amazed me,there was more than humans,orcs,elves,and dwarves. There are Pumpkins! I read on in the book trying to find every bit of information I could fin d on the pumkins,but at the end of the book it said that the pumpkins are in search of the tr ee of life. I plan to find one of these Pumpkins and try to learn from it and more about it. \n Chapter 3 The Fight \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Tree", "_Shoi_", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great War", "mylimo7", "The Great War all started when the Undead moved to this world. They didnt seem as a big threat untill they attacked the City of Oren. With a massive force they seige the Gate House of the city. There were many guards to defend the city. And the battle has been won by the Humans. With the undead weaker from the defeat they start to ambush our Reconnisance groups. One time our King himself led a taskforce to The North. We didnt make it taht far. We were ambushed by a single Undead Supporter, and he killed the King. Luckily the King was restored back to health and we took no deaths. \n \n A couple weeks later we send a massive force down the road to the North. We were quickly ambushed as we left the city gates. Hundreds of zombies and giant mutants Surrounded the road to the north. We took many deaths, but we still won the battle. With so many deaths in our Force, we had to choice but to retreat. The Undead Stops us that time. \n \n \n With the Undead countering all our actions we had no choice but to stay in the Fortress of or en. Every small scouting mission there are no reports of undead. The guards that go on potral, report saying there are undead on the way... The Undead never come. \n \n \n *These Events Were based On What really Happened* \n \n \n There were other encounters with the Undead Most of the time there was only 1 person. The undead are weak, and arn't going to attack any time soon. There was this one prediction of the Undead Taking over Oren....  *By The Seconds Days Sunset The Undead Will Rise and Take Oren* Most people think this is a unreal prediction. While there is no evidence supporting this Prediction. But there also is no evidence supporting that either. But noone knows the Answer. The Undead Still remain on this world. \n \n There has been also a couple flaws in the Generals Reaction to these threats. When there is a threat from the undead, the general quickly make action (which is good). He Lines his men up and makes them wait in line for 3 days times. But if there is a real threat well fight them back. \n \n Overall the undead is no match for the Oren Guards and the Human spirit. \n \n Published By Nashtoff Book Shop", ""),
        StaticBook("The Greater Darkness", "dagothagahnim", "There is a greater darkness \n      than the one we fight. \nIt is the darkness of the soul \nthat has lost its way. \nThe war we fight is not against \npowers and principalities, \nit is against chaos and despair. \nGreater than the death of flesh is the \ndeath of hope, the death of dreams. \nAgainst this peril we can never surrender. \nThe future is all around us, \nwaiting in moments of transition, \nto be born in moments of revelation. \nNo one knows the shape of that \nfuture, or where it will take us. \nWe know only that it is always born in pain.", ""),
        StaticBook("The green figure!", "theo13", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Greenburrow Trait", "Dr_Lyle", "Long ago when the Greenburrow family was known as The Eyes a special ability was passed down from person to person, it was not easy to awaken, the person must survive a near death experience for it to be awakened.  \n After many years the knowledge of the familys history was diluted to the point of members thinking that their family was always just a quiet farming clan. Lyle is the first in ten generations to have this ability, what the ability does is it allows one to manipulate  what people feel, from calming them down to forcing them to tell the truth. and for every ten people with this ability there was one who could, in times of great need could summon immense power, enhancing their abilities, Lyle is one of these few people.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Gruol Diaries, a P.O.V of Keep Walking, a Tale of Truth", "Norser", "I was one of the highest ranking orcs. I was almost the Rex's PERSONAL guard. Then I was outcasted... Kicked from the ranks.  THIS, is my story. The story of the friendly orc.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guard of Whisper Isles", "Dudeinhat1", "\n When i got the portal to work, I didn't expect it to take me to such a  impressive world. Although very primitive i managed to find my way to  a city built on a mountainside. I met few people there, nobody willing  to hire. So i set off back to the cloud temple where i met a guard from  Whisper Isles named Abrar Syed. He showed me to the guard barracks  where i quickly became the guard manager. Why did i get this job? I am in no way skilled with the sword. I would try to quit but i need the money if im going to get a home here. Why me? If I were a regular guard  I might get a bit more freedom. No. I can't go a single step without someone calling for me. \"DUDEK!\" they shout, \"MANAGER\" they say. Will  I ever get so see the world? Or will i be held back by the chains of duty.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guard of Whispering Isles", "Dudeinhat1", "\n When i got the portal to work i didn't expect it to take me to such a... Primitive pAi. clear", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guard Rec. Handbook Vol. 2 - Promotion Tips", "henriiquen", "Being a full guard  requires responsability and experience. This book isn't going to teach you how to become a full guard, but it shall help you reach out these requirements. \n \n 1 - Respect and Education. - The first and most important thing to a guard its Respect. \nStart working your respect to your superiors by completing the duties you're ordered to attend, and be sure to never disrespect any of them, that's the first thing you should know about respect. Also be respectful to our people, for they are citizens of Oren like every one of us.  \n \n\n 2 - Self Defense. - Every guard should know how to handle a weapon, especially if you want to be a Full Guard any time soon. \nIt's a good idea to choose a weapon of your liking and start training with it whenever you are off duty. \nSince a guard can't do much with fragile weapons such as the ones made of wood or stone, I highly recommend you to master the Iron-made weapons , as those are more resistent and do more damage, in case you need to hurt anything, or anyone. \n\n  \n 3 - Survival. - A guard must know how to survive over many situations and places. This section is optional, but I'd like to recommend these training methods. \nIf when you are hunting, or just training your weapon skills (like I've mentioned on the previous section.) you happen to come across some meat-edible animal, like the pig. I suggest you to harvest it's meat, or do some fishing if you don't feel like killing the poor creature, it will do you good if you don't have nothing to eat on your journey. \nTry doing some cooking for a change, that might give you some sense of survival and independence.   \n \n 4 - Behavior. - A true guard always serves his kingdom with might. \nAlways seek to help the people around you, but also expect some of them to be messing around. For that, you are granted the permission and also the duty to arrest and/or escort out of the city anyone who disturbs the peace. If you can't handle the arrest alone, always seek another guard or superior to help you out.  \n \n  And that is basically what you need to do in order to reach those \"requirements\" I have established on the first page, as long as you follow the tips found in this book and do your duties ( which can be found on the Vol. 1 of this Handbook ) for a good time, showing you're worth the job and have enough responsability to handle it.    \n \nKeep up the good work!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guard Recruit Handbook", "RossssM", "Welcome to the Oren Guard! This book will tell you the basics for the day-to-day life of a guard. There are various things you need to know before we can consider promoting you to a full guard. \nGate Duty: Gate duty can be a boring task, But it is one of the most vital procedures of the guard. \nWhen on gate duty, Simply ask he/she who wants in for their 'Name and Business?' If, which they usually do, give a reasonable explanation, you open the gate for them to get in. Note: Do not let anyone in who wears dark hooded robes with the occasional exceptions. There are gatehouses both south (Main Gate) and north. Non-Guards are not allowed in and you should, if necessary use force to remove them. (Only once warned forcefully.) \nArresting: The first step to arresting is to make sure you have a valid reason for arresting. If you do then you must go through this process. (Say in brackets 'Attempting Arrest'... Then ask he/she If they choose to go peacefully or resist. If they go peacefully, either escort them out of the city or jail them. If they resist however, you must both do the command /roll 20. Now, however gets the highest number wins and goes through with their prefered option. On the side of a guard, if you win, you simply do * Cuffs, if the crime doer wins they can escape, you need to let them run away.) Remember, make the criminal go down the stairs and into the cell first! Dont fool yourself by the criminal locking you in! \nPatrolling: Patrolling the King's Road is another duty of the guards. Do not patrol yourself, make another guard/rec. come with you. Just walk to Kramoroe and back, asking people on the way if they have been having any troubles and questioning suspicous characters suitably. Fend off any bandits you come across on your way. Do not engage in combat unless necessary. \nThat is about it for the basics. You need to get a copy of the 'Rulebook' which specifies crimes and their punishments. Good Luck! Guard Well!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guardians", "Willizl33t", "How stupid do you think I am?    \n \n Ha!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guardians and Jade", "ZeSybbyl", "I have just encountered a woman called Jade StarSomething, she seemed lovely, untill I told her I was very proud to work for the Sword of Lorem, she seemed to get distant, then we ran through the city untill we ended up in some back alley I never knew existed , she said she came from a gang called the Eternal Assassins or something, I asked if there were more of her. she said there were, I asked here where they all are and she said that they were in hiding from a guild called the Guardians, and that is were we come in , she says she had already contacted us, and that you had not replied, she asked me what our reply was. I said I hadn't been with you long enough to know, we talked more, and she to conquer all of Oren. While I am not sure what to beleive, I am passing it onto you in the form of the book. Remember, she is looking for you, find her, and sort this out. \n \n \n Sincerely, Medril. ((something weird happened, on page 3 its supposed to say that the Guardins want to conquer all of Oren)) ((and she wants our help)) \n I must speak with you ASAP \n \n I have met her father and lord, and he has employed as a guard for his wood and sandstone fort on the Misty Veil road. If you wish to find me, Travel along the road through Alras and on a cobblestone bridge until you come across a Fort. I look foward to hearing from you", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guardians are now the Ceilus Army", "tyking919", "Baruk started a rebellion against me and his traitors all joined him. That includes Jordan, Gavin, Kiwian, and more but those who i trusted the most. Before that though i had a feeling of tension between some members . It was a sad day when I made the decision to remove my title as general but I was so lucky because Baruk gave up and made his own guild. That is why I feel that my trust is to never agian to be given to anyone! So those true to the Guardians come join the Ceilus Army. Even if you were a Guardian before i will not trust you intill you prove yourself.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guardians Personel Roster V1", "begginfokillz", "OFFICERS OF THE GUARDIANS: Adian (Leader), Floob (Master Assassin), Dimitri (Vetran) ENLISTED PERSONEL: Rinn, Blind_Seer, Credwileon, Grodtar, Alkenaar", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guardians: Who we are, What we are, What we do, and Why we do it.", "begginfokillz", "This recruitment pamphlet is supplied by The Guardians. Please share it. TY we are the guardians, the defenders of the people of aegis from the undead! we fight not for glory, but for the people of aegis. we will stand firm and but we need help. we need men. we need YOU! we have noticed your merit, your potential. we noticed YOU! you have proven yourself to us, and we require your aid. we are at the forfront of the fight against the undead, and we need more men like you to serve and protect the people of aegis. we are the benefits of joining us are many, nad the downsides are none. we supply food, shelter, and gear. in return, we demand your service to the people of aegis we want the you to fight, to farm, to make friends, and make allies if you are intrested, please meet Guardian Priest Dimitri at this place: East Oren Trading Co. Appartments (owned by chase132). We can talk then. we hope you join us. we want you in our brotherhood of cheerful service", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guards Guide v1", "mrperea", "A Guard is always faithful to Oren \nA Guard Protects to the people first \nA Guard follows all Laws \nA Guard will never betray the Royal Family \nA Guard follows all orders, even till death \nA Guard will always fight the Undead \n *--*Guard Ranks*--* \n General \n Captain \n Sergeant \n Guard \n Guard Recruit \nAll Recruits Get a Bed in the Barracks \nVeteran Guards get a home in the Military District \n*---Standard Guard Kit---* \nIron Armor \nDiamond Sword \nFood", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guards Tale", "mylimo7", "The Official \"The Guards Tale\"  Copyright \n \n Chapter 1 The Beginning : The Guards Tale all started on one night in the dwarf kingdom. On that very night Throdo at the age of 12 was with his family. While they were playing together they were broken in by ravishing bloodthirsty orcs! Throdo was hidden in the basement by his mother. Throdo Then climbed out the window and fled in to the Wilderness \n \n Chapter 2 : After Spending hours in the wilderness he returns to his burnt home. His family was dead, but his mother was tooken by the orcs! Throdo scavenged the food he can get, and then left his home. Knowing he will never return he keeps walkign forward.... \n \n Chapter 4 : Throdo for the next 2 or 3 months lives in the wilderness. Fighting all the mosnters taht come after him he survives. After traveling for days he stumbles on a small town of Whisper Isle he lives there for 3 years untill moving along . He meets up with a friend and together they travel to Oren.\\ \n \n Chapter 5 The Ending : After reaching Oren with his friend they split into there seperate ways. Never seeing his friend again. To make money in this big town, he becomes a guard. He lives in an abandoned house outside of the city for 2 years. He lives there untill he can afford a apartment. As a guard he had 2 conflicts with the undead. He became strong by fighting them. He never was able to find his mom which was his only regret, And in all, he still protects oren from any threat. \n \n The End \n \n Published By Nachotp BookShop", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guards Tale 23-7-2011", "rapptor13", "Date:23-7-2011 Day One", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guide", "Jerry_Man", "I premise these writings with a statement that I am no prophet. I have neither received the words of God nor had a visitation from Aeriel or another celestial body. I have not heard God's words but have felt his hand on my mind bringing forth revelations of His presence in Aegis. I make no claim to having God's sovereign will or divine intent revealed to me but to proclaim that which I have understood of the glorious Creator God. \nWe have made ruin of that which God intended of Aegis. Iblees' presence is purposed to guide us away from the evil which we find so natural to commit and towards what which is pleasing to God that we might one day be welcomed to ascend the seven skies. But we have collectively negated these warning signs and Iblees' power has been unleashed across Aegis. The horrors of the Nether are now an inescapable and experiencable reality that all men may tremble at the evil which spews forth. Yet still, without clear guidance, we inhabitants of Aegis have pushed the  boundaries that this world we now reside in suffers corruption to its' core.\n \nLet these commands be known. Change your ways lest God abandon you.\n-Place no man before God. No man's word supersedes that of God's, even that of your superiors.\n-God values all his children. Taking another's life declares that you think yourself equal to God.\n-Forgiveness wins over revenge. If God, in his perfect glory, can summon the grace to forgive your wrongdoings, moreso should you. \n-Violence stems from hate. Striking another with words is as deplorable as striking with sword.\n-Respecting others means respecting what is theirs. To steal is to consider yourself more deserving of that which you did not work for. \n-Unwilling servants bring death to their master. Harbor no control over another man's soul or body.\n-The refining fire burns hotter for finest purity. Be glad when you are tested greatly, for great opportunity is to follow. \n \n. \n I am Elindor and I bring the message that all may be guided in their path to God.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guide To Dueling", "hmqb", "Dueling is as much an art form as a method of combat, and as such there is rules. One common thing to avoid is the direct charge where you rush at your enemy. The Guide to Dueling", ""),
        StaticBook("The Guide To Magic", "silco97", "Have you ever seen a scribe readying a page to copy a piece of text? The scribe scrapes the sheet clean, then carefully traces out perfectly straight lines to contain the text and set it in order. Finally, the scribe sharpens a quill and carefully forms each letter in the text, stringing the characters together to form words, paragraphs, and finally the whole page. Preparing a spell is like that. I have my spellbooks, the original manuscript. I begin the processes by resting my mind and body, erasing the detritus from the previous day. Sleep wipes my mental parchment clean. When I awake, a focus for a while. I cast off the details left over from my dreams and set my thoughts in order, just like a scribe setting the rules and margins on a page. When I finish, I have built a mental structure for my spells. This is the essence of magic. As I have continued to hone my magical art, I find I can create more and more mental pages to contain my spells. When I have created as many blank pages as my mind can hold, I turn to my spellbook and copy the spells I need. I don't use pen and ink, of course, I carefully review the arcane formulae recorded in the book and fill the empty structures in my mind with magical power. There's no feeling quite like finishing preparation for a spell. Thoughts swirl like autumn leaves through my mind. By sheer force of training and will, I force those mental leaves into motes of arcane power. The motes collect on the framework like beads of dew on a spider's web. The final result is a thing of stunning and sublime beauty. With every breath I take, I can feel the structure thrum with power \n -Ambros", ""),
