        StaticBook("The hidden soul", "Victor214", "The hidden soul is hidden behind the hardest challenge of this cruel world. Meet me in The Cassino Royale Inn. TO go there, go to the elven mine, then , you will find a small farm plot, behind this farm plot, you will find a road pointing  the south t east. then, follow this road and turn left in the first possible road. Then just go forward and meet me  there", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Council", "patato12", "The High Council Consist's of Three Member's. The Current Council Is James Bryce Micheal Each member has an Equel vote and has the right to be heard. In Event of a Death or Capture of One of the council member's The_One will step up to to take position in the council If a fued break's Out between two member's of The Guild. The council will hold a trial and then a vote and find a suitable Soulution or punishment .", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Prince of Malinor and The story of Laurelin", "zevandir", "A powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of Laurelin's trees. I met him at the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple. We set off on foot to a mountain gorge I had come across that would act as a natural barrier to our foes. Once we arrived, the Druid wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch at his hip every so often. He showed me the seeds in said pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a shine very similiar to glowstone. Whilst my brigade of builders were creating the city's defensive wall, trees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the trees grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above us. It was a wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similiar glowstone sheen, and sprinkles of metallic dust swirled down from the tree tops. \n \nThere was still, however, a large clearing in the centre of the city. This of course was for the mother tree. A tree to harbour them all. He grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and look over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid then walked to the centre of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds. leaves suddenly spun around him wildly, and a wonderful green color radiated from him like an aura. \nThe tree' trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. I was rather frightened when I saw this, hoping he hadn't cast the spell incorrectly. As the Mother Tree grew to its ultimate height, I saw a small opening half way up the tree. Low and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where the stone alter shall lie.\" \n \nOnce the trees seemed to stop growing, we climbed up the trees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become of the finest city's of Malinor, and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of druid magic. Here. (( drop it in a shelf, leftclick an empty book on the shelf Here is two copies. Firstly, the History of this nation capitol.", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Princes Proposition.", "shiftnative", "Perhaps, High King. I could have a seat in your throne room? I stood aside your claim to the throne in earlier times and it would honor me so.", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Princes Word", "shiftnative", "I the High Prince of Laurelin, express my interesting in this meeting place. When it is finished, I will return.", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Princess Soriuss", "shiftnative", "Soriuss, in her younger life. Travelled to Laurelin seeking kinship with the elves. Upon arriving, she met the Arch Mage of Aegis. And her brought her to Native, The High Prince. He thanked the Mage and looked dazed as he saw Soriuss in a beautiful green dress And leaf crown. Native showed her around Malinor and taught her how elves manage their forest, She came along with him helping him on his duties. Creating roads, selling and establishing homes. and genuinely enjoyed helping Native. They grew closer and eventually got married in the Sister City and many came to pay their respects to the Elves. For many years they developed Malinor together and tried their best to bring smiling faces to their borders. One night, amongst the treetops, Soriuss fell ill and was making her way back to their Home in the mothertree. She was found in the night on the forest floor unconcious. Her soul was put to rest that night in the sanctity of the forest. Native now lives in Mourning, doing what he can to preserve her spirit. Yes", ""),
        StaticBook("The History Of Animeius", "bigdogsebo", "Animeius was once the proud leader of the Aegis Freedom Fighters. That was until one day He had just sent out a scouting party under the command of his most trusted advisor Levaticus. Levaticus was scouting the perimeter when the undead attacked. Animeius was the only capable fighter still at the Aegis Freedom Fighters Keep He Was there with only women and children The undead attacked in number but the keep was still over ran. Animeius led all of the women and children into the hold for their final stand. Animeius Slayed six undead before he was captured. The next day Animeius wakes up and he is in the woods with nothing but the clothes on his back. He slowly limps back to his keep to see if anyone survived. As he approaches the keep he sees his best friend Levaticus laying in a pool of his own blood. He runs to levaticus \"Levaticus what happend \" \"we heard the fighting and came running but\" *cough *cough \"it was to late\" \"There all dead\" \"every single one of them slaughtered\". \"We will get you help levaticus\" \"My lord there is no help for me now\" \"Just promise me you wont let them all die in vain\" \"Levaticus you have my word as a man and as your friend I will wipe all of the undead scum off of this land\" \"You were always a great friend Animeius\" * Cough Cough *stops Breathing \"Nooooo!\" Animeius Gathers all he can and heads to find a place with people who will help him wipe out the undead He Happens upon a small keep. The keep is home to the Knights of the North. He joins the Knights of the North and he will do all that he can to wipe out the undead scum from this land.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Corvus Animas", "emberhard", "The begining of recorded history for this town starts with the guild, The White Ravens converting so me ruins into a settlement . Under there watch and command the town quickly grew in popularity, population, and wealth. The WR overseer at that time was Heril, and the sherif, Mork., at this time the town was also named \"The Greater Ravin City\" \n A few other important names at this time world be Seventh, the primary architect, and Mork, the sherif ;; Eventualy the WR gave up thier complete control over the town's government, and Eledyr was elected mayor, however the WR would continue to have great influence, as well as still have the cit y under thier protection.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of De Marr Felekan", "Lokito", "This is the lore of the Carved Temple, \"De Marr Felekan\", as told by Omithiel. Scribed by Lokito. \n 'Twas the year 800, of the second seed. In Lands afar where mist and clouds pass by, where the trees and grass grow tall and old, there be a temple high up in the skies, where it has stood for many ages. This temple which rests on the mountain be carved from the very peak of the mountain, and in this temple at the very top lies an ancient jewel which the dwarves prize greatly, but it has been shattered and broken due to an evil that is still yet unknown. The pieces of the stone lie scattered across the land of Aegis and have yet to be discovered, but first, let me tell you how it all began. \n When the city of Kal'Urguan was still young and small, several dwarves went out mining like any normal day, looking for jewels. While mining, a shine appeared within a rock, and they discovered something more grand than all the jewels of Aegis. They were so amazed and excited that they brought it to the King as a gift. The King looked upon the stone and was so awed by its amazing glow that he called upon the priests to inspect it. The priests looked upon the stone as it laid there glowing, and they discovered it had ancient magical properties. As the King stared at the stone, he ordered the dwarves to construct a temple far away from the city, far away from the civilizations of Aegis, to be safe from the world and its wars and troubles. so he ordered almost all of the dwarves who were miners, craftsmen, blacksmiths, farmers, scholars, monks, priests, and warriors to go somewhere far away and to construct a temple for the stone that glowed.  As the workers traveled far from the rest of the world, they came to a large mountain, and on this mountain the peak reached high into the sky, and the grass and trees grew tall where no man had ever set foot. They started the construction on the peak of the mountain. \n Hammers, chisels, picks, and shovels all clanked, smashed, banged, clanged, and cracked so much that one could hear it and feel the ground shake from many miles away.  The dwarves worked hard day and night on the temple. As many winters passed and all the dwarves became exhausted, they finally carved the temple.  They proudly crowned the temple with the glowing stone, and at last it was completed. After the temple was constructed, many priest and monks came to the temple as a pilgrimage to see the stone and to pray to the god of Aegis. After some time, the priests examined the stone's magical properties and found that it could control the weather, and they were filled with joy. For many years they prayed, and the dwarven priests and monks made pilgrimage to the temple from time to time, until one fateful night. As the moon glowed a pale light, and the monks and priests slept ever so soundly, the air was still and the night was silent. Then a thunderous crack was heard, waking the monks and priests in fright. They climbed the stairs all the way to the top of the temple, and they found the stone shattered and broken. Their faces were blue as lapiz when they saw the stone, and it's glow started to faint. Then they heard a terrible laughter that was as loud as thunder, and they saw a shadow appear and quickly disappear. The priests and monks were outraged at whoever could have done this as they laid there on the top of the temple staring at the stone, it's glow already gone and now seeming as if it were an ordinary jewel. \n Today the temple still stands as a place of prayer and pilgrimage.  It now has new additions as it now contains all of the dwarven literature and history of the dwarven race. The stone is still there even though many wars have passed, but it lays there shattered and broken.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Erojin", "erojin", "Upon a time ago there had been a man named Erojin.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Evaral, the first city of the Elves", "HiddenForge", "A long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding areas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these trees, for the magik embeded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all others previousely known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries later, a Astronomical Strom swept across the land,  Felling the Magikal Trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the gound and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning Protected in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but the Earth  still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to reach for the sky! They trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace one again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from  new predators and spirits that rose with the Storm. And then a terrible thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the new forests beyond its border. They spread out far accross the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting what they left behind. By this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the first tree, which happened to reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable  armor to help the remaining elves in their journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them. Until one day, many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still ou t there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Fort Norodrun", "Calum510", "Fort Norodrun is a secure fort to the north of Oren. It was founded by the three Darkbringer brothers: Cedric Darkbringer, Kalum Darkbringer and Kutul Darkbringer. They were merely explorers, searching for refuge. They came across an old abandoned fortress, and swiftly started making repairs to it. Cedric was appointed to gether the recources, Kalum the main architecht and Kutul, the 'lord'. After finishing the most part of the fort, Kutul met a mysterious charchter name Gaarag, who instantly had great ambitions for the place. We name it fotr Norodrun, and started expanding, houses, farms, taverns, mines, you name it. We hired labourers who we would pay to mend, expand and repair walls, build projects and collect recources. Soon the fort came to what is today. Norodrun biographies: <Cedric Darkbringer> One of the three brothers to find the fort, and appointed to recource collection. Recently, has became the Overseer of buisnesses, etc. for the purpose of trading and collecting more recources for the fort. Known to despise his brother, Kutul, for his superiority in the early days of the fort's history. <Kalum Darkbringer> A quite fellow, who met Kutul on king's road on the way to Oren. He had no real ambition in his life than a job and a house really, but meeting the Darkbringer's changed that. He joined them on there ventures to the north, and founded the fort with the two brothers. He changed his name to Darkbringer later in his life, and the founders of Fort Norodrun were then known as 'The Three Brothers'. Kalum is the head architect of Norodrun, and loves to build things. However, he does tend to stay out of the fort affairs and will try to avoid combat. <Kutul Darkbringer> The one of the three brothers with the highest hopes for the future. He is the 'lord' or the 'count' of fort Norodrun. Although a great leader he is, his Ambition can sometimes be his downfall.", ""),
        StaticBook("The history of James Thatcher", "tuarzen007", "James Thatcher ------------------ Help me", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Magic", "TehLulu", "Transcribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  Before the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power. \n The power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil. \n But the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his minions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world... \n But it was not to last. The power of Iblees was great, even in the Void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope for salvation... \n With the failing of the barrier protectingthe world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat unfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there. \n \n So it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other darkness...They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be  made...", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Rasun'Dural", "Rasun37", "Hail. My name is Rasun. I don't remember much of my childhood. The main thing I remember when I was young was the Orc attack on my old village. They came in, smashing and bashing everyone, screaming their terrible war cries. One crashed into our home and stole all our minas, and attacked my family. I... was hiding. I watched the whole scene from a window outside. When I was sure the orcs had gone, I went into my home. Only my mother, Gimlond, had survived. She told me to leave and grow up to fight the evil orcs, but I insisted that she come with me. However, she refused. So I left. ... Several years had passed, I believe I was around 17 when I came across an amazing sight along my travels. I watched as six wolves took down a mighty moose and killed it with cunning skill. I watched in amazement as they carried it back to their cave for the pack to eat. I decided to keep wandering. About ten minutes later, I heard a small whimpering noise. I looked abd looked and found two small wolf puppies lying in a ditch. One of them seemed hurt. Heading down, I was able to save them. Luckily I remembered the location of the cave. The wolf pack was searching restlessly for their puppies. I slowly approached, with the pups following. The alpha-male stared at me with bristling fur, then when he saw the pups, he calmed a bit. The puppies ran up squealing to their father. The father looked up at me... as if... he had forgiven me... as if... he now trusted me. I wandered away a bit, and found a cave to rest for the night. I was awoken the next day by a licking tongue! Jolted awake I saw the mother and the two puppies. They semmed to want me for something. I followed then back to their den and found the father standing there looking at me. And to my amazement, seemed to beckon me into the den. One thing they didn't have in there was light, and little did I know, there was a skeleton waiting in the shadows. The pack was inside, eating moose from the previous night. I went there, and out of my starvation, ripped into it. I must have looked like a wolf myself. When I was finished eating, I went to go rest in the other part of the cave. Then the skeleton attacked. He shot me in the leg, and I screamed in pain. The wolves came running in and leaped upon the skeleton ripping it apart. Bones were scattered across the floor . I took them up, and gave some to the puppies. They looked at me with loving eyes and I knew they trusted me, forever. Dural became my new name, which means spirit of a wolf. Once the puppies, whom I named Falias and Azili. had grown up, I left. Whenever I turned around, they were following me! So I set off with them Coming to a place called the Cloud Temple of Aegis, I found many different races there. Humans, Elves, Orcs, and even Fellow Dwarves. I went up to the dwarves and they told me they come from a grand underground city where all dwarves live. They gave me a map, and I was on my way. Arriving at the city, some looked at me with scorn for having wolves, while others looked friendly. This place, is where I decided to live my life in peace. Kal'Urguan is what it is called. Even though my best friends, Falias, and Azili, have passed on since then, I am happy. I, Rasun'Dural, have a fierce, loyal, brave, and cunning spirit of the dead father of that great wolf pack I met long ago, deep in the Wilds of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Sagemarsh", "lordnaylor", "Sagemarsh was a town accros the great sea, Birthplace of anthony , it was a small and friendly town where everyone knew each other where peace was the norm . Everyone hada job and traded materials, Money was not used much. Anthony's family had moved when Anthony turned 18, Anthony had to stay as he was part of the Royal guard of Geldia, he had been placed at Sagemarsh to keep it safe from any creatures that seek death help help one night Anthony was awoken by those words As he went to investigate he noticed that the town gate had been opened this made anthony nervous, he knew what came out of the dark  . , he closed the gate and went to see what all the noise was about as he entered the farm where the noise had come from the smell of burning flesh filled his nose but he could not smell and fire this confused anthony, he continued through the building .    As he entered the storage room two chared bodies where hanging from the wall !  However there was no blood..... no fire and no damage to the building .  Anthony woke the rest of the guard. They searched the Town for the killer but found no-one .  A week passed and no evidence was found of who killed the farmers then on the 8th day A town guard spotted a light in the distance . He watched it all night.  In the morning He and 3 other guards went to investigate while anthony and the rest of the guard stayed back . They never returned   Anthony was woried about the guards by nightfall and convinced anthoer guard that at dawn they would good look for them Little did they know only one of them would see dawn  As the sun set a ear shatering scream was heard from the direction on the light Thousands of Undead attacked the town, people paniked and ran away, out of the southen gate As the town burned he heard anothrt scream up ahead as anthony crept through the undergrowth he saw his towns people being killed by the undead Anthony left quickly and he ran east for 5 days and 5 nights, Eventualy he reached the coast and the large port of Groth Gultar, he bought a ride to Agis where he hoped he would be safe But agis was under attack from the undead aswell . Anthony found a small town called Talamh and bought a house, and he is now waiting the day when he can get the revenge on the undead for killing his entire town   \n This \n is \n the \n story \n so far From the memoray of Anthony aged 21", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Snowy Fields, part I", "Tarannon", "Tarannon and Zerragon, two childhood friends and adventureres, decided to explore the vast unmapped North, and if luck and fortune was with them, wanted to form their wn little community, even a town. \n A few days march North of Al'Khazar, they found a beautiful piece of landscape which perfectly fit in their vision for a little village. Long snowfilled fields as far as the eye could see. They b uilt a couple of small houses first to keep themselves warm, and to serve as a base while they start ed digging for resources and explore the lands surronding their new houses. \n Then, they made a fantastic discovery. Hidden underground they found the remnants of an old ruin, but upon closer exam ination, they found out the ruins actually were a temple. Some inscriptions on the withered old sand stone looking material indicated that this was an old temple dedicated to the Aengul, and linked with the history of the Ascended. The two friends immediately began fortifying the town, in a valian t attempt to keep the undead from getting their hands on this sacred place. \n Large walls were buil t in record time, a deep moat, drawbridges and portcullises, and several guards were hired - all in an attempt to protect the temple. And all to no avail.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Snowy Fields, Part II", "Tarannon", "THE FALL OF SNOWY FIELDS\n The new defences made in Snowy Fields after the discovery of the ancient Aengul Temple, did seem to stem the undead advance to a certain degree, and a period of relative calm and a sort of cease-fire lulled the inhabitants of the town in to a false sense of safety. \n This illusion was brought down, however, after some overzealous heroes tried to attack the nearby un dead for several times. The consequences of their actions were outright war, and retribution of the undead were sadly directed at the peaceful Snowy Fields. The attacks became more savage and brutal, and Tarannon and Zerragon spent most of their time repairing their town. \n After a few months of re lentless attacks on Snowy Fields, the two friends felt they had no other choice than to abandon thei r beloved town and home. \n They barely managed to rescue their most important valuables, before the decisive battle stood. The undead had won, and Tarannon and Zerragon was forced to explore the realm of Aegis once again, in search of a new place to settle. \n \n At the time this book was written, t he ruins of Snowy Fields was in the control of the Undead, and used as a base for attacks on Alstion and other parts of the North.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Snowy Fields, part III", "Tarannon", "TARANNON'S LETTER AFTER THE FALL \n \n It is with deep sadness that I have to admit that Snowy Fields has fallen - and with the utmost of hatred and bitterness that I have to admit that the undea d and their followers have won. Me and Zerragon see no other choice than to salvage what we can, and travel to another part of the realm. A peaceful part, if such a thing exists, that is more suited to our serene nature. We want to build and create - and not have to sit by and watch as the undead d efiles our creations.\n To the valiant heroes that have fought in the defense of the town, we salute you! Songs will be written abour your bravery and heroism, and you all have our eternal gratitude. Especially our Captain, Tylos. We wish you the best of luck, wherever fate takes you. If you ever wa nt another job as a guardscaptain, look us up in a few months time, when we have found our peaceful valley or serene mountain to settle. \n To Ogland, our very first resident, and our most dedicated resource throughout the building of Snowy Fields; I hope you find another place to settle down as the splendid guildmaster you have shown you are, and deserve to be. Your hard work on our moat and the endless amounts of sandstone you've contributed to the building of the mages guild and restoration of the temple, is not forgotten, nor will it ever be. When our new settlement is finished, we will initiate contact and hope you will co me and visit us. Who knows, we may even have put up some creations in honour of the Heroes of Snowy Fields, whom you are amongst. \n \n And for now, fare well, my dear friends, and may luck shine upon you the rest of your lives. I expect to see you again in the future, in a new and truly peaceful to wn, somewhere in a remote part of Aegis. \n \n With regret and sadness, but also hope for the future,\n Tarannon Falastur\n Former Lord of Snowy Fields.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Tenzath", "StrifeOr", "In the year 1001, the village of Tenzath was created by the kingdom of Oren. They quickly prosepered, and they rapidly multiplied The main leader is called a Doyen Their main militia is the Zenban Their secret operations are Zabimas", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of Tetsuya's Seat of Knowledge", "Hyperblock", "In the near past of the lands \n of Aegis there once lived a man, \n whose name was Daichi. He possessed a farm in the \n very eastern wilderness of Oren. \n It is told that the nearest settlement was thousands of \n ells far away towards South \n which was the young town of Whisper Isle. Other rumors say that \n the nearest town was the very beginning of today's Alstion Town. Daichi however was \n married to a truly beautiful woman who was called Miharu. The couple was blessed with \n four children, three of which were boys and one was a girl. Their names were Isamu, Kano, \n Tetsuya and Mitsuko. The whole family lived peacefully on a piece of land where \n they cultivated true pillars of sugar cane next to large fields of, honestly, two ells high wheat \n capable to nourish not only their family but also a whole peripheral area of the Whisper Isle. \n And so the family lived on and the children grew as Isamu developed a real \n brave personality, exploring the neighbouring planes and never recoiled from solving \n a conflict with a fight. Kano however was of a different kind. It was the water, that he called his true home. Rumors tell that he could fly through the water and it is said that Kano, \n or the Krugmar Kannonball like the Orcs used to say, could travel the distance between the coast of Sanjezai amd the town of Whisper Isle in only 1/8 of one day. Mitsuko, the daughter, had such a bright and lively character that every room she entered seemed to shine. She was talented in fishing. Sons and daughters of Orc families tell us about a girl that once caught fish in the great lakes of Krugmar far north of Sanjezai and that girl brought boys with her so they could carry the baskets filled with tens of thousands of lots of fish home. The third son Tetsuya was the closest to his father. Daichi had developed and early interest into the beauties and wonders of Aegis' nature. Tetsuya took ober his passion soon and began to study these laws, of whoch his father had spoken. His effort was soon to be rewarded with success and by utilising these laws Tetsuya early found technical applies. He built complex machines and mechanisms that were supposed to protect the family's land from the hostile looting hordes of Krugmar. And so the children grew up and reached a mature age.  But soon the talents of Daichi and Miharu 's sons and daughter would cause a stir in the Orc towns and villages. Large groups of outlaws gathered, convinced that there had to be a secret Oren settlement near the borders of Krugmar. Humans always acuumulate wealth. Wealth that would empower the families of the Orc villages. Wealth which would allow these villages to turn into great towns and make all their people and economy flourish. So groups of hundreds of Orcs gathered to fight against the Oren settlement and so they headed North-East to the great pillar mountains in the planes in the far East of Oren. Thus, it occured one day that Kano who was doing his morning swim heard the dull noise of large feet pounding the soft ground and so he decided to swim South-West to investigate and find out the source of that strange noise. His heart stopped when he saw hundreds and more Orcs carrying heavy weaponry and armory heading straight towards his beloved family's farm. He swam as fast as he could back home to warn everybody. But even though he tried as hard as possible, it was already too late. A scout had already discovered the young Kan as he was swimming, the Orc drew his bow and so Kano was the first child of Daichi to be killed by the horde. Mitsuko who was fishing in the farm's pier was the second one hearing the Orcs' march. After only seconds the noise turned into the terrible sound of hundreds animals' battle cry. Daichi recognised its meaning immediately and ordered all family members to hide inside an emergency bunker underneath the house that had been built exclusively for this kind of raid. Daichi armed himself and went into the forest to get Tetsuya who had been asked to collect wood. He wandered around and shouted Tetsuya's name into the forest when suddenly he saw smoke rising up from his farm. Finnaly, Daichi found Tetsuya who was told the terrifying news and together they made their way back to the farm to save the family. The terrible battle cries had already disappeared and the both managed to reenter the farm. Tetsuya and Daichi were totally shocked as they saw the house burning down to its foundation. Both prayed that the Orcs had not found the secret bunker and they bursted into the house to save their loved ones. Daichi saw that the hidden door was uncovered and opened. He entered the bunker and all Tetsuya heard after that was a terrible long cry that teared up the air around him, animal screaming followed by fighting noises and finally an opressive silence. Minutes passed by until he dared climbing down the moist ladder. He saw the most dreadful thing a conscious being could ever experience and moreover, he faced the ugliest and smelliest creature he had ever seen in his entire life. In just a fraction of the shortest moment Tetsuya recognised that the Orc was wounded an as fast as lightning he grabbed his father's sword and stabbed into its wound right into the stomach and the creature made a terrible scream before it fell onto the ground. Tetsuya had no feeling for time anymore. He stood all alone in that room with dead bodies, maybe minutes, maybe hours. So it happened that Tetsuya lost his whole family and he stood alone with nothing but his father's iron sword and a pickaxe he made by himself. A young man of 21 who would need to learn how to survive on his own or he should inaccessible. He digged deep into the ground and refilled the surface over him so nobody could ever find him. Over years, Tetsuya lived secretly and hid from other beings that passed by. He only left his hideout on order to obtain necessary ressources for building or food. And so Tetsuya fell to his passion of investigating the laws of nature and he discovered that all the wonders, every motion, reaction or else appeared to obey to certain laws. Laws that could be found out. Nature would then become predictable. Certain effects could be utilised to achieve specific objectives. The ability of recognition that had been given to the races of Aegis by God had lead to the birth of what shall be called \"Scientia\" from now on. And as Tetsuya's trust returned over the years he decided to establish a library where once he had settled to share all the knowledge he would acquire in the future for progress and the newborn spirit of Scientia shall introduce reason to all beings' minds and all sorrow and pain shall be extinguished in a peaceful and new future. \n \n The End", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of the Ascended", "ComradeRenzbro", "When Iblees was banished from Aegis long ago a few of the ancient race \"Aenguls\" decided to stay behind and live with the other races of Aegis. They had many descendants that many see today, all of the people that live in Haven are Ascended The Aengul, Ariel appeared to four of the most direct mortal descendants of the Aenguls in the form of a mongoose to warn them of coming war and disruption of the Peace. During the Ascendeds travels they met another direct descendant and he joined in their efforts. They were told by the spirit of the Aengul to travel with a sapling from the Cloud Temple and plant it somewhere specified by the spirit herself. They travelled for many many days leaving several shelters on their path that you can still find tod ay. After many days and thoughts of giving up they found a spot to make a grand city of the Ascended. They were unsure why the spirit wanted this spot but soon found out when digging the foundations of the wall and finding a small circular cavern in which the spirit told them to plant the sapling, which is now one of the most holy entities of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of The Elves", "sx421", "A long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to settle on a beach.  This beach was bestowed with Magikal Power from a long gone time. It let all plants grow abundantly there and in the surrounding areas . The sand there made glass as hard as steel and which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as elves, planted their Magikal seeds, great First Race, later known as elves, planted their Magikal seeds, great towering Trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these trees, for the Mag Magik embedded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spr  trees, spreading their seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all the others  previously known. The Elves lived in the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help  them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day, many centuries later, a Astronomical Storm swept  across the land, Felling the Magikal trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth,  melting the ground into pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burn t all the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during", ""),
        StaticBook("The history of the Ferox Legio", "biggs7", "help delete help", ""),
        StaticBook("The history of the Roberts family", "Idioticozzy", "The fist known person of the Roberts family was Ian. He was brave and couragous, and fought many battles for the king back then, Horen. He married a woman called Eleanor, they had three children. One was called Iastor, one called Isldor and a girl called Elan.", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of the Thatcher House", "tuarzen007", "The Thatchers were a middle class family, who lived in Al'Khazar. The Parents, James and Alcia , both had jobs and were able to support their families. Hail Aye, It has been", ""),
        StaticBook("The History Of The Undead", "silco97", "\nPhillip and Rodrick \nTwin brothers wereborn in the great city of Alkazar with names Phillip and Rodrick.  The two weren't raised with a wealthy family.  Their mother owned a shop trying to make a living selling flowers to pay their fathers bar debt.  Since they didnt want to work, and neither had much faith in the Temple, they turned to the streets to occupy their time, stealing from shops and noblemen.  It was a matter of time until their stealing hands weere caught. A fat pig of a noble ,named Natvel owned a farm the boys vivited often to steal from.  Tierd of these troublesome boys ,he hired a privet guard composed of bandits and highway men to watch his farm.  The twins returned to Narvel's farm in hope of stealing more of the fat noble's abundance of food; but were no match for the new guards.  Narvel was planing to hang the two boys for their crimes of theft, but Rodrick , always  quick to temper, wouldnt sit and be bullied into submission.  He kicked the guard trying t put him in the noose and lunged at Narvel, stabbing at his throut with a small blade he hid in his boot.  In this time, Phillip manage to slip away, using his brothers distraction to flee knowing if stayed, there would br nothing he could do to help his brother.  Phillip snuck through the alleys of Alkhazar, dove through the sewers, and escaped into the bay running north into the woods. Rodrick, however, was captured for not just stealing, but killing a noble.  Death alone would not be enough for his crimes, so he was sent to Winterfell where he was sentenced to finish out his life rotting in a tiny cell. In the Northern woods, past Snowy hills of Alstion and Winterfell, across the, and over the vast mountains that claim the north, Phillip was growing weak from hunger and enraged in his inability to find his way home, much less save himself or even his brother.  The sun was setting again as it had for weeks since Phillip was last in Alkazar. Unable to defend himself from the evil that lurks in the woods at night, phillip took shelter in a cavern. As he rested his head on the smoothest stone he could find, Phillip bagan to feel a pulse emitting from the ground. Curious and desperate, he followed the pulsing deeper into the cave. As he felt his way through the dark tunnel, he came upon a smooth, stone frame that was hot to the touch.  Just as he stood up in front of it, the inside of the frame burst with light, showing a purplr vortex within. Drawn by the pulsing beat, Phillip stepped into the portal.  Twisted, pulled and whipped around, he flew through the portal and out into a strange land we now know as the Nether.  There, he found a shrine not far from the portal.  Phillip carelessly stumbled to the shrine, feeling as though his soul was being ripped out of him in all directions.  The moment he toushed the shrine, an agonizing pain shot up his arm, through his bosy, legs, and into his head. A thunderous voice met him with so much pain and torment in every word. It spoke to him horrors no man shoul ever hear, piercing the heart that makes Phillip human.  After much torment, the voice said to Phillip. \"You can save your brother and the two of you shall rule those who made you suffer.  Let this body go, your mortal soul will change in the power i bestow upon you. Serve and you shall rule all.\" The power given to him from the voice known an Iblees bound his soul the Nether, keeping him tied ti Iblees' power, but making him lose his physical grasp from Ageis.  Phillip, grew to depite his name, finding comfort in the name Freyj as suggested to him by Iblees. With the great magic he has, he pulled a city from the Nether using the fire and souls around him, binding their will to forge what is now called Drauchreich. Freyj now uses these souls bound to Draucherich to fight for him in Iblees' name, moving to take Aegis, the land that Iblees was vanished from.  With that, Freyj, overlord of the undead horde, stepped back through the portal and brining the hell of the Nether back with him.  Rodrick was stuck in Winterfell Tower for what seemed like eternity. Locked locked away and forgotten, his mind grew twisted and further removed from Aegis. One night a terrible blizzard, Rodrick heard an echo of a voice coming from outside the prison.  Again and again it would call to him, rippimg at the back of his eyes to see through the dark. Outside from the hole he sould peek through, fire exploded on the horizen. A wall of flames with a face bursting from embers.  The guards came to Rodrick cell to find him racing around the room screaming madness. The guards stood at the cell mocking him until Rodrick lunged at the door, reaching through and grabbing one of their throuts.  Blood spilled everywere as the bell rang sounding the alarm. The other guards lunged through stabbing the maddened Rodrick in the side, leaving him to bleed. Freyj had come with a horde of undead, ripping open the  the tower to free his brother. Before his brother could die, Freyj made a sacrifice to a few captured guards, brining Rodrick, taking to the name Rott, back from the brink of death, but not entirly alive.  In the Nether, Rott pleged to a nearby village in his name.  Iblees founf Rott to be a Prophet of the Undead, from Rotts ability to brong pain and suffering to those who would dare defy Iblees. With that, Rott summoned a city from the Nether to Aeigs, to spread corruption and turn the world of Aegis into the Nether so iblees can be one step closer to freedom. \nEnd Of the Brothers Reign \nOverlord Freyj and Prophet Rott burned their way through the nothern lands to the gates of AlKhazar spawning the armies of Iblees in every alley and summoning undead giants in every square.  Undead necromancers went from roof to roof setting the city ablaze looking for the one that could bring Oren to it's knees. Malinor, Kal'Urguan' Sanjezal, and Alras came to Alkhazar's aid.  As the fires burned twords the Kepp, the king Perea made haste to the bakery with intent of saving the Queen Dawn. He searched the bakery high and low , but was trapped as the windows blew in with a mighty flame and the support fell across the door. Fire raged around the room as Overlord Freyj and Prophet Rott became locked in battle with the grand king. It wasent lonf until the years of cake and ale slowed the kingg sown leavind him at the feet of the merciless", ""),
        StaticBook("The History of The Whisper Isles", "itechify", "One of the first human settlements outside of the capital city, the King of Oren ordered Lord Tyrion Lannister to go south and provide a new community from which fish and glass could be collected to help support the growing kingdom. \nNow a picturesque community on the shores of the massive and majestic Whisper Lake, The Whisper Isles struggles to provide goods and shelter to travelers on the King's Road and to combat the criminal efforts of bandits in the surrounding wilds.", ""),
