        StaticBook("The Holmes Handbook", "indy58", "The Holmes consists of 9 ranks Each of which requires a certain amount of skill to reach Our Chief is Scott_Jones. Adian is a rookie like me,Vargon Holmes Are detectives,and often go off on cases . Me (typo) Some rules are: Call everyone above yer rank sir, Never go on patrol alone,And more that are on the wall of the Holmes office I ave a typo but okay (typo) We need more members,so recruit anyone ye can! Allways RP when ye kill,too,we don't want anyone banned. .If a criminal attacks,attack back!If they run,chase! hey martin (typo)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holmes Oath and Values", "martinvilla822", "As a Holmes I promise to defend the weak, protect those in need to help those who are in need of assistance, to do good deeds for honor and not for fame or glory.  To show bravery and valor in all situations, to be loyal to the Holmes and defend others. To give and not to count the cost, to fight and not to heed the wounds, to toil and not to seek for rest, to labor and not to ask for reward. And to protect my friends,family and my fellow Holmes.   The Values: 1 Honor, 2 Justice, 3 Bravery, 4 Loyalty", ""),
        StaticBook("The holy book of ID's", "fabian9696", "1: Smoothstone  2: Grass  3: Dirt  4: Cobblestone  5: Planks  6: Sapling  7: Bedrock  8: Water  10: Lava  12: Sand  13: Gravel  14: Goldore  15: Iron ore  16: Coal ore 17: Wood  18: Leaves  19: Sponge  20: Glass  21: Lapiz ore  22: Lapiz block  23: Dispenser  24: Sandstone  25: Noteblock  26: Bed  27: Powered rail  28: Detector rail  29: Sticky piston       30: Cobweb 31: Tall grass  32: Dead shrubs  33: Piston  35: Wool  37: Yellow flower  38: Redrose  39: Brown mushroom  40: Red mushroom  41: Gold block  42: Iron block  43 Dubble slabs  44: Slabs  45: Bricks  46: TNT  47: Bookshelves  48: Moss stone  49: Obsidian  50: Torch  51: Fire  52: Mobspawner  53: woodstairs  54: Chest  55: Redstone wire  56: Diamond ore  57: Diamond block  58: Crafting bench  59: Seeds  60: Furnace  61: Burning furnace  64: Wooddoor  65: Ladder  66: Rail  67: Stone stairs  69: Lever  70: stone pressure plate  71: Iron door  72: Wood pressure plate  73: Redstone ore  75: Redstone torch (off)  76: Redstone torch  77: stone button  78: Snow  79: Ice  80: Snow block  81: Cactus  82: Clay block   83: Sugare cane  84: Jukebox  85: Fence  86: Pumpkin  87: Netherstone  88: Slowsand  89: Lightstone    90: Portal  91: Jack-O-lantern  92: Cake  94: Redstone repeater  95: Locked chest  96: Trapdoor", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Grail", "Fluffy5", "After 110 days of travelling, We've finally arrived at the temple. This is the Temple of the Holy Grail, We finally found it! Hidden in the deep desert of Utran, Surrounded by many secrets and mystery's One of the Knights said: \"Is this the place where the Holy Grail is hidden?\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Lie", "GrimReaper98", "What write command? Delete", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Lie: By Falgor the Goblin", "Jerry_Man", "IBLEES AND AERIEL: figments of ourselves \n \nThey are just figures of our imagination enforced by the ones the beleive in them the most. As these 'gods' are beings sculpted by the races of Aegis, who has ever truly seen them? The first to receive the taint is hiding himself in the nether and declaring himself THE Iblees. Because these alleged 'celestial bodies' were once people who died after achieving great things and amounting many followers they became recognised as forms or equals to God. A figure following both of them simultaneously immortalised them within history's pages, making of the two deceased what they are today.\n \nFollowers of either Iblees or Aeriel havevoluntarily accepted a form of mental sickness that impairs the better judgement towards what which they expect their God to command. Followers submit their lives to the purpose of their own envisionment of either Good or Evil.  Likewise with the Creator God, His image is created in the moment a populant of Aegis hears of this God and does not exist beyond this personal vision.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Sword of Ambros", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Was originally given to Salamandra when he was a Mage, by Ambros. Salamandra then gave the sword to Deltaro, when he stated he was leaving to find a Daemon Temple.  Salamandra hoped the sword would guide him on his journey. No words back yet...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Horrors of Sleep", "MrZombez", "Sleep brings no joy to me \n Remembrance never dies \n My soul is given to mystery \n And lives in sighs \n Sleep brings no rest to me; \n The shadows of the dead \n My wakening eyes may never see \n Surround my bed \n Sleep brings no hope to me \n In the soundest sleep they come \n And with their doleful imag'ry \n Deepen the gloom \n Sleep brings no strength to me \n No power renewed to brave \n I only sail a wilder sea \n A darker wave \n Sleep brings no friend to me \n To soothe and aid to bear; \n They all gaze on, how scornfully \n And I despair \n Sleep brings no wish to fret \n My harassed heart beneath;  \n My only wish is to forget \n In endless sleep of death erase all", ""),
        StaticBook("The House Drake was formed in 1013 by Ulric Drake when he was appointed", "deanofantastico", "Margrave of Eridell, a flourishing trading town situated on rolling plains not far from a dense forest. It was here in Eridell, where the Housed Drake grew into a powerful noble house. \n \n Margrave Ulric married a fair women named Wyia in 1015 and had several children, though all but Kair Drake, their first born son, perished in a dragon raid in 1032. \n \n Over the next 140 years, Eridell started to decline in prosperity. Constant attacks by bandits and tribes on both the town and the traders, gave the area a bad name. The decrease in trade casued tension in the town with many either leaving or others who started to rebell. \n \n In light of these events; in year 1173, the current Margrave, Standar Drake, sent his son and daughter away with his most trusted friend under instruction to keep them safe and take them far from Eridell. erase", ""),
        StaticBook("The House of Harrach", "Garukumus", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The house on the hill", "MinistryofGamess", "There once was a girl, called Emily. She was living in a big manison. However when the Minas Crisis broke out, she had to move out with her family. The only house her family could afford was an old, abandoned house on a hill. She moved out of her manison and moved in the abandoned house with her family. She was very anxious about her new home, everything was cracking and was about to fall apart. This didn't gave her a safe feeling. Also she could not sleep at night. Eversince she moved in her new house she got nightmares, all about the same subject. It was about some strange voice, influencing her to do certain actions. Every night it became worse! It all started with stealing a single dollar from her mother. But every night the crime turned out more evil! Untill one night, Emily had a great day, she played on the hill with her older brother. He's called Thomas, he is two years older than Emily. After this great day her mother tugged her in and she started to sleep. When she fell asleep and entered her dream she heard the voice again. 'Pick up the lighter in your mothers' purse Emily!' The voice said. Emily got out of bed and sneaked through the house towards her mothers' purse. She took out her mothers' lighter as the voice ordered her. 'Now, you shall walk towards this city which whom calls Laurelin and you shall set it afire!' The voice said. Emily left her house, in the middle of the dark and walked towards Laurelin. However, none of the monsters was attacking her! This was never seen before except by the undeads! She posessed over great powers! This might mean the end of the Aegis! If she learns how to use her powers properly evil will rule over the lands of the Aegis! When she reached Laurelin she heard the voice speaking to her! 'You shall go to the main tree and you shall set it in flames!' Emily walked up towards the top of the biggest tree in Laurelin. She set fire to the leaves! The tree was on fire! Rapidly the fire extended over all Laurelin! Families with children were burned to death! Emily tried to flee, but before she could reach the ground, the fire caught her! Her body was burning in the flames, when all of a sudden a dark beast showed up! The horror! The beast spoke; 'Burn Elves! In the name of IBLEES!'. It was Iblees! 'And you Emily! Rise up! Embrace the flames of Iblees!'. Emily, with a burned body, only an undead could survive such damage, she stood up. She walked towards Iblees! They reached out their fingers towards each other, and when the fingertops met, Emily's eyes turned red! Iblees was transferring his powers in Emily! After he was done Emily opened her mouth, 'I shall lay waste to the lands of Aegis, I shall defeat all those who stand in my way! Nothing will stop me!'. Iblees laughed! This means, the end ... of Aegis!", ""),
        StaticBook("The house on the hill II", "MinistryofGamess", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The House Outside Alk'Hazar a Story of Life, Love, and Iblees Worshipers", "Caden_Cathaldus", "Like the title Gruol? The House Outside Alk'Hazar, a Story of Life, Love, and Iblees Worsipers. Outside Alk'Hazar there was a little house built be a nice but juttery architect, and paid for by a Hail!", ""),
        StaticBook("The house outside Alk'Hazar, a Story of Life, Love, and Iblees Worshipers.", "Caden_Cathaldus", "Right outside Alk'Hazar there is a cozy little house made buy a nice but jittery architect. and a soft headed little girl. Caden Cathaldus, who is I before any more talk of the little House Outside Alk'Hazar is spoken of in this story any more, must tell you the beginning. Before you read this read \"Keep Walking: a Tale of Truth\". That will tell you how we got to this point. At this point in time the dead are walking among the living in Aegis. More and more humans, elves, dwarves, and orcs are being turned into Iblees worshipers. Which comes the tragic tale of our friend Guraim. ------- Chapter 1: The sad sad tale of Guraim. ---------- Guraim was an old friend of mine, in particular Sillion's. But, at about this point, Guraim had became an Iblees worshiper. In case you've been living in a mineshaft for 300 years, Iblees is the Dark God (which doesnt deserve to be capitalized, but it is formal), who opposes God. He summoned these wretched beasts upon the land. A blight of people turned against each other. The undead united by one common goal. Serve Iblees. The beings of Aegis united by a different common goal. Kill the undead. Then along came a spider. That spider being the Ascended. I say spider with the upmost respect, trapping discusting insects and taking their blood. The Ascended, in my opinion are the essence of God. The undead the opposite. But, back to the point. Guraim worships Iblees. We used to talk about life, the bigger picture. At the time of me writing this, the last thing Guraim said to me was, \"I want to take your eyes out, light you on fire, and make you watch yourself burn. Thats when me and Sillion made the descision to hunt down Iblees worshipers. Thats when we found Eoll. ----- Chapter 2: The \"I dun wanna\" Lawyer------ Eoll ran up telling me there was a man stuck in a hole. I didnt even know Eoll at the time. But I saved Will from the mineshaft. I took him in and told him about the Iblees worshiper plan. He said he wanted to live here. I asked him what his story was. His response; \"My parents are alive but they hate me. They wanted me to become a lawyer, so on my twelfth birthday he took me to court. And I was the besy ****ing lawyer Aegis has ever seen!. So I ran away a year later.\" Of course my natural response was to try to get his parents' love back because mine were dead and I missed them. Of course, his mind wasnt a bit changed. Then my old friend Gruol came around. Gruol is an orc. -----------Chapter 3: Revenge of The Bitchy Old Orc---------- Gruol was an old friend. When I thought Sillion was a bitch, he was less of a bitch. When I thought Gruol was a bitch, Sillion was less of a bitch. So basically all of the time Sillion Gruol were bitches. But, besides that, friends. But I really dont know wheter to hug or kill Gruol. He is an old man, and needs alittle help, but refuses to take it,which is why I feel so protective over him. But every time I try to help him he tells me to **** off. Like his teeth. They are bascially broken. If they arent filed they will start hurting. even if he just eats his soup, which again he refuses to do. He is annoying, a bastard, thinks he's not old. But somehow, I can still find hope in this broken old soul. And why? Dont ask me cocksucker, Im not sure why I can still love this old bag of shit, but its like a childhood toy. Like the ones made of pine tree wood. Well, that's how you're raised in Laurelin. But whenever those old wooden elf peice of shit toys break, people throw them out. But me and Gruol is different. Gruol is broken, but I keep him. Thats what friendship is about. At this point in time this is like a journal. Right now, nothing is going on, but I will create another chapter when something interesting pops up. OOC: soorry bout the language i get carried away in the story and get into character too mmuch. Every story i write is like that))", ""),
