        StaticBook("The Humans", "gustaz", "The Legen of aegis The most beautifull world History started from the Human... The humans were the first race on the world of aegis The human at first started living from wood They did know how to make items from wood and once a day they found stone and started Mining Then The Forests created a new creature... The Elf,Son of nature ------The Elf----- The Elves are the most populated race in the world They are the sons or daughters of nature And there are Dark elves Which are More powerfull and even they are better", ""),
        StaticBook("the hunt", "Sykora87", "Sykora and relyt \n we leave for the north to hunt undead portals to save the world (am i crazy) \n we found diamonds then lost em to winterfell \n nothing so far \n to the undead city \n starnge house no monsters in days \n Starting to be just wild areas and mountains no undead city \n fell in a hole \n we might never find it \n WE FOUND IT x -4083 y:70 z:32 \n we found a large floating city with many catherdrelss we venture on \n we found the portal to the city \n to the portal For the Vanguard the portal didnt work \n we will set up camp \n i finished the fort \n Reylt should be back soon \n after weeks of serching and days of building i egerly await the other vanguard to bring supplies so we can catalog more of our find and stop the undead if they are coming \n For The Vanguard", ""),
        StaticBook("The Hunt for Vengeance", "TheWoWMasta", "Chapter One: The Seeker \n Discordian sat in a lonely tavern, collecting his thoughts and worrying about where he would go first. He had a pack full of food and plenty of weapons and supplies. He has no map, no compass, just instincts. If he was to succeed in his quest, he would have to travel into the cold, desolate norths of Aegis . The Princess had been killed, and it was his duty to protect her, but he had failed. His guilt led him to the fate he had today. Discordian left the tavern, a heavy rain pouring down on him through the streets of AlKhazar. \n \n Chapter Two: North Discordian sat in an abandoned watchtower. He was taking shelter from the night. A cozy fire was burning in one corner, the other sat his pack. His head was filled with determination and triumph. He was very hungry, and pulled out a lovely roast chicken. Roast chicken and watermelons are his favourite foods. Day was fast approaching, and he decided to head out, sword in hilt. \n \n Chapter 3: The Hunter \n Discordian sat in yet another abandoned watchtower. They seemed to be littered all over the north. He could see his target in sight, Cassandraland. There he would obtain information on how to find Nefas. Nefas was his target, the one who killed the princess. To kill Nefas, would gain him great respect, and thanks of the king. He would not be able to take on a small undead force himself, but he would be able to kill off a few of them. \n \n Chapter 4: Truth \n The day grew dark, and Discordi-- \n *The remaining pages are torn out, maybe someone else has them..*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Hunters Creed", "coastercam0", "Go on Edicts of the Hunters of the South: \n1. Never shall you attack nor steal from your brothers. On penalty of expulsion or death. \n2. You shall obey orders from the senior hunter during a hunt, bar circumstances in which the first law is being violated. \n3. You shall forfit half of all your profits for the good of the Guild. \n4. There will be no senseless or lawless killing of civilians during your travels. \n5. You will not accept contracts from other groups that have not been approved by your superiors. \n6. Respect nature, Respect the Hunt. \n You will kill the undead and monsters in this world to maintain the balance of good and evil throughout Aegis. \nFollow These rules and you will be a righteous man of the Hunt. Good Hunting.", ""),
