        StaticBook("The Journal of Korin Hoget", "DwarfGuy45187", "Ah I have decided that I need to write this all down. I've recently become a Rookie Guard of Kal'Urgan. It seems I might not stay in my little town much longer. I will probably buy a house in Kal'Urgan . Craglode! My cousin ah I still need to protect that idiot though . Hey Craglode want to read my journal? Yeah I would never let him do that Sure I guess I will Never! You gave me yours Ha I read his! Hello Dain I think I will add you into my journal meeting you Ah I have met someone called Dain Earthheart he is a great miner Im lost in the mine in Kal'Urgan! Thinking I will never leave! After many days I've finally found my way out Ah evil Plague! stuck in Kal'Urgan not slept for days barely awake Protecting the city from Wrath was hard Wrath has killed a guard trainee im quite sad as of now.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Lily", "Bubbli", "Being ever so timid. It hs been quite troublesome t times. But tody things hve tken  turn! My new journl will strt here...\n I ws wndering bout in the town  Al'khzr, quite the bustling town. People didn't seem to notice me much, but tht's fine by me. As I myself re rther frid  strngers. I found myself by  lrge structure with  sign tht red \"Aren.\" I hve herd stories  these plces. I fer them. A plce where people purposely hurt ech other? Anyhow. While I stred t this building, someone cme up to me. But I ws not scred  him. He ws like me! A hlfling. He introduced himself s Len. He ws very kind, nd humble. He told me  this plce, quite the wlk wy. Took us nerly  dys wlk to get there, but once we rrived... It ws mzing. A lovely little frm with vst whet frms. Quint homes built into the erth. And even  Ale grden! A humble little lke nd  wterwheel thts just wonderful. After showing me bout, Len introduced me to two other Hlflings. Kip nd Mr. Gimblo. Kip ws busy building wy, so I didn't wnt to disturb him. Gimblo ws very nice. An much older Hlfling. Suddenly  mn cme. He cme rther loudly. But I didn't sty long enough to her wht he ws tlking bout. He spoke with Gimblo. Len brought me bck to Kip nd they both fered me  plce in this beutiful town. I ws so hppy, nd humbled to finlly find  plce tht it felt s though I belonged. Len took me to  plot tht he sid ws going build me  home! It even hd  tiny pond. I loved it. Suddenly I herd shouting! Tht mn  before ws running  Mr. Gimblo, s he chsed him with  ! I hid behind  tree. He chsed him out  the town, while Len rn fter Mr. Gimblo to clm him down. After  moments time hd pssed, Mr. Gimblo trotted bck to his home while grumbling nd Len cme bck nd begn constructing my home. As for the other mn. He looked quite sd, he turned nd left... So much hs hppened tody, nd it's only been one dy! I cn now see tht this is the plce for me, this new plce I cll home, this beutiful little town, this plce clled Dunwood.   \n A new dy hs strted in this mgicl plce  Dunwood. Len worked well into the night to finish  quint home for me. I ws so hppy.  I could not wit to get strted decorting it. I tried my hnd t building   fireplce, but it just didnt seem right. Suddenly  knock t my door. It ws Kip! I welcomed him into my home, but once he cught sight  my fireplce, he let out  gffw! \"Wht re you doing building  fireplce out  wood!?\" He gsped. \"Are you trying to burn down your house?!\" He turned nd rn out. Thn he returned s quickly s he turned nd left, but now crrying supplies. He begn fixing up my fireplce with stone nd brick. A more pproprite fireplce. In the midst  his building, Mr. Gimblo stopped by just s I ws setting down  rug. He mde     comment bout it, which in turn mde me doubt it in my choosing. So I rolled it bck up nd plced down  more modern one. A   time hd pssed, nd with  exhusted sigh, Kip rised his hed, wiped the swet  his brow nd smiled. Content with his work. It ws  mgnificent fireplce. I couldn't hve sked for  better one. I thnked Kip, nd he left. Night hd fllen, nd I ws exhusted. I took  wlkthrough my home, unble to hide the smile on my fce. Absorbing tht this is ctully my home. I crwled into bed, nd for the first time in  long time. I felt t home. And slept more soundly thn I hd ever since I ws  child. And dremt  more exciting dys like this, in this plce clled Dunwood. \n I woke up the next morning, full  energy nd will! The new sunrise brings  new dy  dventure for me. I decided to tke  wlk to the surrounding res. Tking in the wrmth  the sun, nd the coolness  the breeze, the scent  the flowers, nd the mist  the se. I cme upon  mountin side, not fr  Dunwood. There I sw it. A wooden cbin. I ws  quite frid, s I thought someone might be inside. I dred not pproch it. I rn s quickly s I could be to town. Just to lert ny  the other residents  this plce I found. Mr. Gimblo ws the first I found. I told him wht I hve come cross nd he seemed   intrigued. He sked tht I would show him the plce. We trecked f nd finlly I found it gin. He pproched it with no hesittion. He begn to peek into the windows nd serch ll round it. \"There's fresh swdust here. But I don't like people so close to Dunwood\" He cme to the conclusion we should gther this wood for our own supply. We hurried bck to Dunwood but by the time we hd returned it ws lredy quite drk. So we decided to hed out t dwn. We sid our goodnights nd deprted till morning. Dwn cme nd I ws so excited to hed out. I hurried to the home  Mr. Gimblo, knocked on his door nd he greeted me with  stone xe for myself. We deprted to the tril we hve now memorized nd rrived t the cbin. We begn with the ro. I gripped the stonexe nd swung with ll my might. Chopping wy the plnks  by . By high noon I ws exhusted. But in my rush in the morning, I hd forgotten my lunch. Mr. Gimblo seemed   nnoyed but shred some  his lunch with me. With   new found energy we finished bout hlf  the structure, nd the night begn to loom on us. We heded bck home for some well deserved rest, nd t dwn once more we would hed out gin. The morning cme, nd I decided to prepre myself better for the dy. I grb n extr few s  pork. And n extr  crfted", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Malin Famaen", "Agith", "Tolta, The 17th of Malins Welcome, 1338 \n \n Today is the first day of my isolation to the world. I have taken up refuuge in the home I onced lived in, which now lays abandoned . I have found myself growing to resent the deity I've come so close to; this, \"relic\" that has apparently been bestowed upon me is more of a curse rather than a blessing. I am going to work on fixing this resentment through meditation and a life of peace. I am going to make myself an agenda. \n 1. I will begin the study of alchemy, as well as other sciences to sharpen my mind . \n Second, I will work to regain faith in Aerial, I will do this through meditation and study . \n 3. I will learn more about this relic of a dagger. \n \n \n Tolta, 17th of The Grand Harvest, 1339 \n Much has occurred since I last wrote, I found myself unable to write down my thoughts . I have learned much from hours of meditation, finding much comfort in the fact that I have come to inner peace with myself. I am still frusturated with the way my life has turned out, though I am comfortable with it . At times I feel as though I am not a single entity, but that I am part of universe. That dagger, I've come to name it Ral'kog, though the name has little siginifance toward any of the blades history, as I have yet to discover anything of the sort. I have made little process with alchemy, and have focused to hone my abilities with a blade , though little has occured as of this point in time. I will hopefully write more often, however for now this will be the end of my second entry in this journal.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal Of Miguel", "Noble_4", "Day 1 I am with my friend Frowman, we have picked up much information on undead, we went to haven to talk to the Ascended about it. They were not their but the FOA captain was he liked our information and decided to tell his leader about it, who happened to be an Ascended Acolyte. We decided to investigate further, Frowman went to Al'Khazar I went south to investigate the undead I had heard the were stationary there and saw a few headed that way. I packed up and set out. Day 2: I am headed south to investigate the Undead i packed little because of my low supply on items and money, but i had some food and a few tools and a sword. I traveled for what seemed like hours till i found any sign of civilization. I saw a giant tree, bigger than any tree in all of Malinor. I investigated the tree, only to find nothing. It was ashame it was just a giant strucure", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Mylas", "Architecus", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Pious Oakwood", "TheNander", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Rak'Tahl Bloodsmith", "Firtahl", "I just returned from the Mines of mine home city, Kal'Urguan. I was able to get a small sum of gold an iron ores, and a grand deal of Cobblestone. I was disappoint to hear that mine mother was nay in the city, but perhaps some other time \nIt's been many moons since Kal'Menor has gone into reconstruction. I have made meself a small home near the city. I have been visit Kal'Urguan for supplies, and hunting monsters by night. My birthday just passed this month, the 17th of Snows Maiden, I am 39. \n Today I arrived in my home to find myself robbed. I will have to revisit Kal'Urguan. \n I cut much the forest around my cave down. Tomorrow I shall plant more saplings. Travellers came by, requesting to see what had changed in the valve. I admitted them, seeing no harm in it. I will check the city out for meself tomorrow as well. I added a food celler to my storage area. Perhaps I shall also brighten the place up a bit. \nI finished the two guest rooms, unfurnished, after I returned from Kal'Menor. It is still under construction, after three long years. The Elf, Drawf, and Human that requested to see the city returned to me, and asked to see the Valve. I told them that I could nay show them it without proper permissions... After they left, I overheard the Elf that the Dwarven guard called \"Darfin\" Talk about his research on the undead... He said That their only known weakness is hand to hand combat, if ye can get past their minions... \n I have completed the dock, and the guest room furnishings. As I was out today, I came across a zombie. After killing the zombie, I found a map... from my travels, it looks like Laurelin's northern wall. I happened across a Wolverine fort today, after I was hunting monsters. I gambled for a bit, then sold 4 stacks of cobblestone. Walked away with 125 minas more. On the way home, I found a dog, and managed to tame him.. I shall name him Malro. :It's been quite an eventful few days... I met a man, Gaius, who has taken me in to his Order of Knights. I was brought from Al'Khazard with a man name Glylith. A young fellow with a good mind. I've been given home and shelter. I'm currently on my way back from my old home with my belongings and Glylith, who is in search of ways to tame a wolf we recently found. Malro has gone missing... I hope he returns. \n It has been several days since Glylith has decided he will tame this canine, one way or another. My dog returned while he was away, thankfully. \n It has been very many moons since I last picked up this book. I lost Malro, and several canines after him, all of  which fought bravely. I was promoted to Arms Warden of the Order after I built the barracks and armory. I aspire to becom e the infantry marshall, and make mine father proud.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Saviticus Treebeard", "Saviordude", "Entry 1\n \n Aye, today is a great day fer me. After spending a rowdy afternoon at the Kal'Urguan pub with Petyr, I decided to rekindle me dream of ownin' a pub. I went and talked to Prince Native about gettin ' replace gettin ' -> gettin' some land to build me pub, he instead redirected me to a large, vacant buildin' an' told me I could 'ave it to use as me pub. After thankin' him heartily, I got to work workin' on renovating it. After I was all done, Hoggarth popped by and we 'ad a chat. I do miss that fellow. Finally, I passed around a round to all me friends to celebrate me luck. Except Petyr, he fell asleep.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Shenrak Milau", "LemonJamulus", "So it is that I find myself once again in a house of God. I have already spent several days since my arrival in Aegis wandering penniless down the byways of the land, ever persued by the mindless puppets of the undead. Every inn has refused me shelter and it seems that god himself plots against me. Except that he has offered me shelter here. And for this, i shall remain ever in his service. The study of the arcane and holy may occur more often in my works from now on.", ""),
        StaticBook("The journal of thought", "monkeychez", "You know, the world has become such a corrupted place, it isn't even fair. One major concept of life people should always know, is that without a proper balance of good and evil, the world would tear itself apart. Now think of this... The Ascended are here in Aegis to protect the people of Aegis safe, much like an army of a nation, but for everyone. Well, there is one major factor tangled in this mess known as the world.... Say the Ascended were to perhaps one day... Rid the world of evil. Well, what would happen? The Undead, stopped from their doing and the Ascended, finishing their fight? It would NEVER happen. You see, if the Ascended were to ever win this everlong battle of good versus evil, what Would become of them? They would go down in history, be heroes... But for how long? Life would go along... The memory would rot, just like the bark of a tree. There is an answer in all this mess. by the way. The Ascended NEED the Undead. Its vice-versa with the Undead, as well. But on a MUCH, much smaller scale. The Undead have to fight five races and a super power. They will always have a struggle. With, or without the Ascended. So, what is to make from this? Well, here is the final words on that ... The Undead, nor the Ascended, will never truley win, even if you think its in plain sight... THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Wyrix", "Xentonic", ";; Entry One- I have arrived at the Cloud Temple of Aegis. Time to begin my adventures. I plan to become a great Hero one day. I wonder if i will realise this dream. ;; Entry-2 I need tools. I will begin in the wild and make what I need then I Shall head to Oren. ;; Entry-3 I cant find a job. I will hunt monsters to survive. This will be tough,", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journal of Zolgash", "Amarnra", "Chapter One: History I am an orc. Before anyone who may in the future reads this book wonders, what the hell is an orc doing writing a book?! Why does he have such good grammar? I'll tell you why about three years ago in a battle with some enemies I have yet to determine (Atlthough I do remember a giant dwarf. And I mean GIANT!) I was hit on the head with an axe. That is the scar you would see if you met me today. I do remember very vaugley something else... A mage, or group of mages casting a powerful spell. Maybe it was a curse? I do not remember. But there was a powerful discharge of magic which knocked me unconscious. The next thing I remember is waking up in bed. All my previous memories erased and only the memory of the axe and the magic remain. I do not believe that an axe strike from the dwarf caused my Amnesia. But the Magic Discharge. I believe I need a mage to fix my memory. The bed I woke up in was that of some elves. I did not undrstand anything they were sayin in fact, i did not remember how to speak or walk at all. I was like a baby A helpless, helpless baby. They taught me their ways. How to speak, write. They taught me the ways of the forest and how to shoot a bow, how to tend to crops and the trees and how to treat animals. But that life was not for me. Exploring. I set off from the elves. Their lives were not for me. I felt deep down in my bones I was meant to be an orc. So I left. Eventually came across the capital with the help of a very find human whom the name of I have forgotten. Should I meet him again I shall remember. I met up with an orc at the gates. They taught me Ug- Hello and Gug'ye - Goodbye. They eventually left to check on their shinies (Things) and I came across another Orc. I had to prove to them I was not weak and that I could fight. I live for the fight! They taught me more of the language. their mannerisms. I told them my story, the one at the start of this book. I am now exploring, collecting more things. I shall write in this journal my story from here on in. \n Chapter Two: The Castle After many days and nights of exploring and killing the undead for money and for loot I came across a castle. I met up with a company of two orcs and they explained to me that for that castle to remain the occupants must pay them 3 diamonds every muun (sunday). Aparently these occupants had been evading the payments and decided to build defences and ready for war with the orcs. I had recently enlisted in the Orc army as a runt and was undecided on the matter. I then approached the gate later on when the other orcs had left in my own private investigation of the matter. I met a man on the walls. A human. He claimed that he does not know the reason why the orcs are attacking and says that they just began attacking. Me being an orc obviously raised suspiscions within him as he raised a bow at me. I promptly left. The next day a green man (I had no idea what race he was of) and a Dwarf by the name of Axehammer. By the look of his uniform I would say he was a captain. Captain Axehammer. I had a conversation with them and The Captain Axehammer claimed he was trading with the green man and the Green man said that the orcs were attacking their castle. The Dwarf went with the Green man to see if this claim was true. The green man was under the same impression as the man at the gates. I followed them to the walls and then pointed out an obvious fault with their bridge mechanism which allowed anyone to operate it. They Thanked me. I saw an elf nearby. Obviously not a friend of the Castle Occupants as they were asking the Elf what he was doing in their lands. Whilst he was on the bridge someone pulled the lever and the bridge withdrew, leaving the elf to fall into a pit. The Castle occupants laughed. I was interested at this behaviour. It did not seem very friednly towards the elves, perhaps the elves would join forces with the orcs against this cast le? The occupants of the castle then offered me to join them. I declined and said that I was not ready to decide on the matter. I need to think things over, get some more evidence. I need to find out who is wrong so I can join their side in the battle. Oh how I crave a battle! \n Chatper Three: Explorations \n I took refuge in an abandonded fort tonight. I heard the grunts of some Zombie Pigmen outside the walls and decided they would make good target practice. I shoot one of them with four arrows and it fell over dead. The other two stood in shock as their companion died. I shot 6 arrows in total, three into each of the other zombie pig men and mortally wounded them. I then pulled out my axe, jumped down and finished them off. Their warm blood splattering everywhere was refreshing. I found quite a lot of minas on their corpses. It amazed me how they always seemed to have some on them, it was like they murder innocent adventurers and steal all of their money. I have never seen one in the act, but I shall make it one of my ambitions to catch them in the act. I continued exploring the next morning. I came across a bridge which had a giant hole in the middle. I easily jumped across so see what was on the other side. On my right all I could see was destruction. Not only to the environment but all of the buildings la y abandonded and in ruin. A mighty stone fort stood in the distance, i went to investigate. On the front of the fort stood a sign. It simply stated: \"Tribute to Orcs for protection and land. use T. Elm-Hammer\" It was a very Dwarven sounding name, and the fort looked dwarven, so I assumed thaat the dwarves built it. Underneath the sign was a chest, guarded by key and enchantments. I guessed that not even my mighty axe could break through. I walked into the keep and looked up. Above the door stood another sign: \"This Tower is Protected by the Orc Nation T. Elm-Hammer\" I then decided to meet with this \"T. Elm-Hammer\" figure. I wanted to know what life was like living in this fort. \n \n \n . ((The writing on this page slowly fades to nothing, as if the writer ran out of ink.))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "stridharn", "I am Alyssa Stone. Writer of The Journey, a true story. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "Undeelad", "On my long journey to find the necronomicon, i encountered this strange home. But i didnt touch anyt", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "martinvilla822", "Chapter 1 It was a normal day in Aegis I was on my way back to the Holmes HQ. When i saw another Holmes Callum and a group of other people talking about something  important. I went closer and heard them talking about a journey to the Undead. I had heard rumors that they had returned to collect more souls. I went to them and asked what were they doing.They told me they were to go on a journey to travel to the kingdom of the Undead in an attempt to infiltrate their evil domain in the Nether. Chapter 2 We set off to journey to Winterfell after hearing news of The Undead there .The group composed of I Martin,Callum,Bastion,Elrond Balcorim ,Braimoth and An Elvish Princess We had heard that the undead were near the town of WinterFell.Wemade our way to WinterFell thru oren as we made our way to the town we saw  2 burning towers.We hurried to the town gates but when we arrived they were locked we made our way over the wall and as we got inside the town what we had feared had come true the town was attacked by the undead the tents and shops were burning.We split up to search for any survivors and clues as i went near the Eastern gate i saw what the portal that was used by the undead to arrive in WinterFell i called the others and when they arrived we searched the area more I went inside the shamans tent and saw something that was not welcoming there were pieces of Netherrack on the walls and floor of the tent i showed the others the netherrack in the tent and we agreed that we must go thru the portal but it was closed we needed a flint and tinder and i had one in my pocket and went near the portal and used the flint and tinder on it but it did not work i tried it again but still it did not activate when we examined it closer it was broken the Undead must have destroyed it in order to keep anyone from following them    Chapter 3 Since the portal was destroyed we needed to take the long way to Striqaephoth knowing that it was the only other place with a portal.   Chapter 4", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "Domainoft", "As we walked the road with the Ascended Beyone Alras, there was much lightning  A man named John_Locke bravely fought a villian who tried to kill me this night, the villian lay dea  I will write your tales of adventure as we go as we stood our ground at laurelin The ascended fought with us most bravely And the horde of spides amassed against us in the trees The storm of arrows quickly dispached them WE WILL NOT BE TAKEN SO EASILY Then the lightning started I feed the soilders as they grew hungry, It is my privilege. I bandaged those who's wounds needed heal All of the sudden, a black box appeared Spewing even more of the evil vile spiders to plauge the forest, still the lightning burned our beloved trees The undead filled the sky, such a terrible sight to behold rumors soar,, we lost the bridge, while the Imperial army arrived. A giant appeared for the undead, what a sight of terror I have food, go to the signs two more giants, will this night ever end Iblees shouted \"those who wish to join, leve the vile race of elfs and come out side the gates\" Undead in the sky a box appears inside the gates We have beaten back the undead for now. Day is upon us It is good to see that the sages have not left us, they fight brilliantly by the side of Aegi on the road back to \"kal something\" I passed a blue robed figure.... he disapeared without a trace", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "Deadmoon81", "Well my day stated off like any other day, with the sun shining and the air cleann. The morning dew was sparkiling, and it almost made me forget that I was hunting for food for my brother and myself. It was just so beautyfull that it was hard to focus on the task on hand. Thats when i saw a big, fat pig walk accross the fi eld across from me. I pulled my bow string back and took a deep breathe. I took my time, for this was the only animal that i had seen since about a day ago. Lining the bow up with the pig I realesed my fingers and let the arrow fly. It hit the pig near the back right hip. I ran over to it and slid my iron sword into its neck tellling it thank you softly.   I then slung the dead animal over my shoulder and walked back to the camp to meet my brother \n I returned to the camp and my brother was not there. At first i thought he had gone herb hunting again, but after hours of no return I went to search for him in a near by cave. The cave was narrow and wet. I did not wan to stay down in that cave for long so I quickend my pace. Not to far into the cave I saw a light coming through a hole in the wall. I peered inside and saw a goblin hobbled over something. It was ahrd to see so i moved to another hole, but this one was bigger. I looked inside once again to see my brothers pale white face on the ground. At first I could not belive how this happened, but soon recovered from my shock. Insted of talking to the goblin I pulled my dark, Black bow from my back. I pulled my bow string back as far as it would go and realsed the arrow. As the arrow left the bow it seemed to have a blue glow on it, but that could ahve been my eyes. When the arrow found its way to the goblin it met it in the chest directly. In a shattering blow, the goblins chest plate fell into 4 pieces. help earse", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey 2", "Undeelad", "Congratulations again young one. Now that i know how smart you are, i will give you hints to the nex Book But this first I am traveling looking for the undead. It doesnt matter if you like them or not but this story is ancient, and worth thousands of minas So tell the tale of undeelad Tell them all that i am looking for ancients. and the ancients are one of the undead Goodbye Next book is straight from here :)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey 3", "Undeelad", "Hello my child You have found the last book in this mysterious series. Talk to Undeelad And your future will be revealed", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey By: Martin Loyola", "martinvilla822", "()() A Message From The Author: This book is based on real life events ()() Most in Aegis wouldn't dare go near an Undead nor near their Kingdom or better yet some never even live through the journey. However I went on a Valiant Quest to that terrible place..... ()()() Chapter 1 ()()() I was wandering back to the Holmes HQ after a long day of patrol, and as I arrived to HQ I saw a peculier sight. A group of people all huddled outside HQ all talking about something important. As I went closer I saw two people that I recognized, Bastion a fellow Holmes and Callum a Lost One, but there were four other people there who I did not know . Listening closer to the conversation they were apparently talking about how The Undead have returned to Aegis, the one telling them off this was an Ascended named Tot, he was telling them about a Quest to journey to the Kingdom of The Undead known as Drauchriem which was located in the Nether. The Nether a place that was described as a terrible place made of Lava and Netherrack , And lled with terrible creatures such as Ghasts and Pigmen. I went moved slowly towards them and asked them if I could join in their valiant quest. They all agreed to let me into this Quest. But little did I know of what horrors I would face . ()()() Chapter 2 ()()() As we began to get ready to leave for the journey I went to get to know who I would be travelling with. When I began talking with them I learned of their names Tot The Ascended , Elrond, Briamoth and an Elvish Princess. We gathered some food, weapons and tools. We decided to travel to the town of Winterfell after hearing news of Undead sightings there. We passed thru Alk Hazar as we went farther North we neared an Orc encampment. As we got closer we saw two burning towers in the distance coming from the encampment . When we arrived to the encampment the gate was shut and most of the buildings a blaze in  fire. We climbed over the wall and began searching the area for any survivors and who or what caused this. As we split up to search the area I went to the center area of the encampment. While I was searching the area I noticed the shamans tent had some strange red material on its walls as I went closer to the tent to get a better look I saw the ghastly sight. Netherrack was growing along the walls of the tent and SoulSand on the ground. I rushed outside of the tent and called the others to get to the tent. As I waited the foul stench of the Neatherrack began leaving the tent and mixing with the air . When they arrived I showed them what I had found inside the tent. They were all equally shocked as I was to the sight of the Netherrack and SoulSand. We then went to the West side of the camp and saw something we would have never expected We saw a most enlighting and at the same time terrifying sight. It was an closed Nether Portal the one thing we have been looking for  to get to the Undead's Kingdom. ()()() Chapter 3 ()()() We were ready to jump thru the Portal but all we needed now was to try and activate it . I pulled out a Flint and Steel that I had brought with me. As I began to slowly use the Flint and Steel to activate it", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey I Had", "RustyJusty123", "I was walking one day and I ran into a small town called \"Snowy Feilds\". It was a small town at the time. I decided I would ask for any work. Sure enough there was. I became a Guard and lived in the Guard house. As days went by I got enough money to buy a small home. I finnaly settled in and had peace. Every day I would guard the wall and let travelers into the town. But one day as I walked out of my house, People were gathered by the gate about to get ready to go to battle. I said what was going on and as I have heard an Orc post was being under attack, So i armored up and followed everyone. It was a terrible sight to see. There was lava every where and lightening hit every where. I heard people cry for help and shouting \"fall back!\". The battle lasted a while, I was wounded and had to fall back. I regrouped with some soliders and went back into battle. When the battle was over, the city was in ruins and there was nothing we could of done to stop it. We won the battle but did not save the Post. I headed back that day and went on with my life. \n One day I was patrolling the outside of \"Snowy Fields\" and I saw a man who ran at me and bit me. He was undead and I never saw it coming. I killed him and went back home to tend my wound. I started feeling different from then on. Im sleepy and hurt a lot. I feel like one day I will turn into the thing that I fought.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey of a Disciple", "impymut", "\n Today I became a Disciple of Valor! They have just accepted me as a new member. The initiation was fairly easy, but they have not given me a task as of yet.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey of Merchant", "Reilock", "Day 1 The weather is awfully bad today, such a bad start for my trade. I have manage to gathered 9 stacks of wheat 8 stacks of wood and 4 stacks of stones hopefully, if things goes well, I will be able to sell all this items and pay my debt This whole adventure thing is not my kind of thing however, Laurelin has been desserted lately it's a rare occassion to see any traveler visiting Laurelin business has been bad and if this keeps up, i have to move out from here It is best if i take a sleep before tomorrow's journey  Day 2 This is it, the time has come for me to leave Laurelin All my life I have been staying in Laurelin and now it is time for me to bid farewell all the memories that I have are left inside my house. As I slowly make my way towards the city's gate, the memories of the past stabs my chest making my heart tremble with sadness. Gathering all my courage, i left the city not even looking back for once Shortly after my departure, i was making my way to the Kingdom of Oren hoping that things will go better there and i could start a new life. As i walk to the Temple of Aegis, I sensed so.meone was following me. Thoughts started to gathers through my head. Is it a Thief? Bandit? What should I do? I do not have enough money to pay them. Are the going to take my life? It's too so.on! I just started my journey. God please help me I don't want to die! as I pray hard, a shadow slowly lurks towards me. I closed my eyes and prated even harder when suddenly, so.meone touch my back. My whole body tensed. I wanted to run, but my body won't allow me to do so. Is this the end of me? It is a bad idea after all to leave Laurelin I should have trusted what Karin said. I should not have left Laurelin . \" Got you! I knew it, you are still a scaredy cat after all!\" said the shadow behind me I know that voice! that was Karin's voice! I turn my head slowly and saw Karin standing behind smiling at me. Knowing that i was safe, my body gave up and I suddenly fell into the ground. Karin just stood there and smile at me. To be continued!", ""),
        StaticBook("the Journey of Skyler", "skyhalk98", "thank you for grabbing this book. I'll introduce myself. My name is Skyler,I am 16 years old, I live in Masyaf but will soon be moving away. I have purple eyes and black hair. One of my best friends in life has been Goleth. He has helped me through hard points in my life. me and him grew attached to eachother when he had no home and needed somewhere to stay. I, being nice, let him stay with me. We had a great time together. We one day decided to move away to a bigger land plot and own more land. After a picnic one day i decided to go for a walk. on that walk I found a new island we could move to. I went home to tell him where it was. We started packing the moment I told him. Before i knew it me and him were moving to out new home. End of Chapter 1", ""),
        StaticBook("the Journey of Skyler -Chapter 2-", "skyhalk98", "The new island we were moving to had wide fields,large forests and many ponds and lakes. It was a true heaven,unlike the old house. When we first arrived we started to make progress on our new house. We used materials from the land around us. In the end I believe it took us a week to build and over 250 logs. With the final part of our house done, the shower, we took a step back to admire our work. We had made a 3 story house with large enough farms to support a family of atleast 5. The first night we spent in the house were the best. After time went by we got ajusted to the new house. But, after a few weeks in the house I began to have some bad nightmare's. In the night Goleth would always comfort me, make me feel safe. There was one night when Goleth had a nightmare he stabbed his pillow with his dagger. Awhile after this I had to go to a different city for a few weeks, It must have been hard for Goleth to survibe the island without me, but he pulled through. End of book 2", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey Of The Five", "greenmilkweed", "Day 1: We have shelter in a small cave, But hopefully We will not be attacked by foul creatures. Tomorrow, We shall go farther south untill we find the perfect spot to begin our town. \n       \n Day: 2 We have reached more sea, And a curious landmark in the shap of a skull..... one of us five has decided to leave us.... We say our farewells and leave.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey of the Swordsman", "Pieworship", "I began to wander after I left my home in Alkaz'ar, and I was never the same after that. Having had my parents deaths at an early age, I was raised by humans that were very determined. I as found after I had been dropped from the arms of the undead that had killed my elvish parents. Even at such an early age, I had learned the ways of the sword to an extent where I could defend myself against zombies. However, my human parents had managed to further that skill, and in the end, I was able to fight of large hoards of monsters with a stone sword. For I never took to mining very passionatly, and I did not \"waste\" my time with ores.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey Through Aegis", "sx421", "Starting off as a soul, you walk through the first gates but you are alone. The moment you walk through the last gate you see ghost, you feel as you are connected. As you look around you see more and more of the souls. you can't feel your skin so you look at your hands.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey to a New Land", "KarmaDelta", "Journal Entry Day 4 ,    We thought we lost Madame Nailena, but it seems hope prevailed. They also dont seem to know who I am or what I am capable of. I wish to tell them but I cannot. I seem to dwell more on the princess. I still dont know if she is taken or not. I hope she isnt.  Journal Entry Day 7, We found a mysterious shrine to something called a \"Wyred\". We just skipped past it and moved on. We also found the site of the new city. We dont know the name yet but it will be amazing. Journal Entry Day 8, We have begun preperation for a new city. We still dont know what to do but we are working on hard on making it a beatiful place. We have also decided to make the new city approved to all races. All I have to say is...... This is going to be interesting.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey to Himmelen", "Pizzafreak5", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey to the Undead City", "MinistryofGamess", "Today, 13-7-11 I ar my journey o he undead ciy. I am accompaned by my dear friend Darfin.  We leave he Valve and head off o he Norh! We followed he road o Oren, bu we lef he road o he Norh! I was in he middle of he dark, skeleons and zombies were around. We had o be careful! \n  \n   Day wo: We sared he day wih gahering some porkchops. We cooked hem. They were so delicious.! Afer breakfas we coninued our advenure o he ciy! We found some cobblesone on he way providing a bridge! People mus. have passed his already! I was cerain, people have been here! We found a lile hous.e wih a ches and a workbench. We mus. coninue! We found lava flowing ou a mounain! We mus. be on he righ rack! We found anoher lava pi! We mus. be close! We found a pink sheep! We have no shears o ge he wool bu we have a lovely experience! We haven' seen any sign of undead any more for a long ime, we are losing hope! I's geing nigh, we climbed up a ree and se our camp. We put some torches around us.   We decided to rest, we shall continue our journey tomorrow! \n Day 3: It suddenly started raining! I felt the presence of the undead! At last we found a road! It was very long! I thought this was the way to the undead city! I saw another lava flow from a mountain, I knew we were very close! The road ended up at a house with a sign saying 'Here is the home of the damned. We are coming' Also there was a bookshelf with a book saying that the first person to discover the city was  Balorcim, the Ascended on the 10th of July.  When I turned around I saw it! The undead city! We reached our goal! Now we must set up a camp. We shall spy on them and come back with information! As we approached the city we noticed that we could not enter it because it was too high. There must be a way! \n Day 4: We made ourselves a little home with a farm in a mountain to stay the nights and do research. We found a monster spawner near our house! \n Day 6: We went out again in the morning to check the undead city for undeads! We succesfully met an undead, two even! They shall discuss our request of being an undead. We will probably need to face hard challenges. But we are up for it!  \n Day 6: I am going back to the city again to spy on them! We couldn't find any undead this day, we return to our home. \n Day 6:", ""),
        StaticBook("The journey.", "STgamer", "Two strong elves enter the woods, \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journeys Of Alfred", "Volutional", "I wus' wanderin' in Oren, and I happened across a lovely little town. Unfortunatly, there were no signs, but t'was a nice little hamlet. Map to the location --> ( -1499 755)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journeys of Eric the Homeless Traveler:  Book 1", "URCRAZYERIC", "Our story follows the life of a homeless traveler named Eric, formerly known as Crazy Eric . I am Eric . ;;  I have traveled to many places, some of them including Kal'Urgan, Laurelin (Which I visit very f requently), Valen-something, Kal'Rog, and many other major cities. Personally, my favorite of these is Laurelin. ;;  But nevermind that. ;;  Very recently, I visited Evolo-whateveritscalled, and I saw an untamed wolf En Route. Excited, I screamed, \"OH MY GOD IT'S A LITTLE CUDJO!!!!\", and began a frantic search to find bones. Of course, of the 31 or so skeletons I killed, none of them dropped any bones. ;;  I then became lost, and so, I travelled to Val-something, where I searched for Evolo-whateveritscalled, but it was a fruitless effort. ;;  Upset by this, I then searvhed and searched for more skeletons, but, again, to no avail. And so, I (Unsurprisingly,) searched for the Cudjo I had found before. I found him rather quickly. Sadly, I made my way back to Laurelin, and had a brilliant idea just as the little Cudjo faded from view. ;;  \"THAT'S IT!!!!\", I cried, \"I'LL USE A FISHING POLE AS A LEASH!!!!\" ;;  But as the fishing pole latched on to little Cudjo, he took his last breath, his laast view of the cruel world that he was about to leave. ;; ;;  Obviously, he died. ;; ;;  Enraged at myself for making such a stupid, obvious mistake, I fled to a pub not far away. ;; ;; ;; ;;  And so here I am, in the attic of The Happy Halfling, writing of my recent adventure . ;; ;; ;; ;; ;; ;; ;; ;; ;; ;;  To be continued.... Oh, and as I made my way back down to the entrance floor of The Happy Halfling, I found a tamed Cudjo of somebody else's ownership,", ""),
        StaticBook("The joy of fire", "sconn", "Burn me. Burn me in the fire. Flames licking at me, at this burning pyre. crackling wood. Sparks popping on my skin. The pleasure uncompareble. Im burning again. That is the melody i have singed while i stood in the fireplace. My skin started to burn, I could smell burning meat. My eyes were stinged by the smoke. My hair dissaperred instantly. I have decided to rid myself of my mistakes and body. I wanted the body that imprisonet me to burn. And so it did. When bubles began to form under my skin i yelled: I sacrifice myself to Iblees, I rid myself of my mortal mistakes. Then at that moment i heard laughter and joy. I heard children playing. Then my whole life flashed in front of me. I could see everything from my birth to this moment. I started to regret the decision. But the fire, the fire offered such comfort and pleaure. At that very moment I realised my insanity. I realised the true joy of life. I remembered the felling when i gave the orphan some money years ago. My hatred of my body drove me insane. I jumped out of the fire, and started to roll on the floor. I was purified by the fire. But my insanity has not left me completely. ok", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jurnal Of a Spy", "Roxses20", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jurnal Of arkenos Kilth", "CentralGuard", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Key to the Great Mysteries", "l337Ninja", "Behind the veil of all the fieratic and mystical allegories of ancient doctrines,  behind the darkness and strange ordeals of all initiations, under the seal of all sacred writings, in the ruins of cities, on the crumbling stones of old temples and on the blackend visage of the gates of Al'Khazer, in the monstrous or marvelous paintings which interpret to the faithful of Iblees the inspired pages of the Dark God, in the cryptic emblems of our old books on alchemy, in the ceremonies practised at reception by all secret societies, there are found indications of a doctrine which is everywhere the same and everywhere carefully concealed. This doctrine seems to have been the nurse or god-mother of all intellectual forces, the key of all divine obscurities and the absolute queen of society in those ages when it was reserved exclusivly for the education of nobles and kings. It commands the elements, knows the language of the stars and directs the planetary courses; when it speaks the moon falls blood-red from heaven; the dead rise in their graves and utter ominous words, as the night wind blows through their skull. This omnipotent doctrine, this bringer of life and death, this creator of empires, is magic. Magic is the key to all power and knowledge. If you have the magic, you have the world.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kin", "ReaperT", "The Kin, a mythical group known only to a few. Those who do know of them fear them greatly. Their leader, is a great and powerful wizard. Some say that this wizard saw the banishment of Iblees. Others claim that it is just several beings each inheriting control of the Kin. Those presumptions would be correct. \nThis story is not about each of those leaders, but about the first of the Kin. This \"man\", may be the sole cause of people's fear of the Kin. But, I must start in the beginning, for the story to make sense. \nIt all started before the war with Iblees. A young elf named Crine was studying magic . He felt that his father, Malin, was not quite allowing him to grow. After several attempts to get his father to teach him more powerful magicks, Malin shunned his son and tried to prevent him from learning any magic. He sent him to work as a soldier where his mind could be occupied by other things. \nOf course Crine did not like that, but he could not disobey his father. Crine was forced from his life of peace and happiness and was thrown into the military. Of course, none knew that the army of Iblees was being created at this time. Once the first attacks of the undead came, the army was thrown into action.", ""),
        StaticBook("the kind deserved his death. im glad he has died. this is the happiest day of my life.", "cub3mast3r", "", ""),
        StaticBook("the king deserved his death. i was very delighted to hear the news of his death.", "cub3mast3r", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The King's Army", "patato12", "Narrator: Our story begin's in the Kingdom of Alras When a struggle between good and Evil Young Gordok entered the Gates and before him a Giant city with the flag blowing in the wind then a heavy storm is seen on the horizon but it does not appear to be a regular storm and that's where our story begin's \n Scene One A man enter's the stage he see's the storm Looming The War signal Goes off The king's men start to hand out weapon's and armour Gordak find's Himself with with an iron sword given to him by James Then he hear's a Yell the Undead have made a obsidian Tower ((Black wool)) ((gordak and his new found friends fight toward's the tower ((fight scene Guy dresses up as a mob)) Gordak then get's the leather armour From the dead zombie ((man playing zombie drops leather)) He rushes up to the mighty tower his commrades falling all around him then off to the left he see's a minion they have the king chained up Gordak rushes up and kills the man freeing the king he run's up to the tower Realizes he can't scale these mighty walls run's into a nearby shop he finds a ladder then scales the tower Slaying the undead monster The king then comes to him Puts his hand on Gordok shoulder and say's neal The king Unsheath's his diamond sword then knight's Gordak King Prononces Him Sir Gordak Of the Alras Military", ""),
        StaticBook("The King's Army (Play)", "Relinquo_Angelus", "((Narrator)): The day begins as young Dane enters through Alras Gate. He stares in wonder at the shops, browsing here and there at the many wares available in the markets . A strom rolls among the heavens; lightning likes whips crack down from between sinister clouds, alighting roof tops. The ground itself smoulders from the heat.\n \n((Undead Lord)): *flips set switch and sets fire to shop with steel and flint*\n \n((Narrator)) A call for help is heard some small distance away.\n \n((King Syrio)): \"Help! Help! Help!\n \n((Minion)): \"Shut up, old man! And stay quiet!\"\n *shackles King Syrio*    \n((Dane)): \"Halt Minion! Leave the King be!\"\n \n((Narrator)): A small pause before the reply: \n((Minion)): \"Never...\"\n (pause) \"Taste my blade!\" *swings at Dane* \n((Dane)): *parries the strike, realigns his blade, and plunges the sword into the villians heart*: : \"Now you die, foul Minion!\" \n((Minion)): *falls to the ground* (drop leather armour and fall into stage hole) \n \n((Dane)): *leads King Syrio to a nearby shop.* \"You should be safe here sir.\" \n \n((King Syrio)): \"Aye, thank ye lad. You are a noble warrior Dane.\" \n \n((Dane)): \"Thank you my liege.\"\n \n((Narrator)): An evil Undead Overlord appears upon the dark tower. \n \n((Undead Lord)): \"Ahaha! You mortal fools! Worship Iblees or die at my hand!\"\n \n((Dane)): *attempts to scale tower, but fails* (goes to store for ladders and climbs tower) \"Come peacefully and surrender or die.\" \n((Undead Lord)): \"NEVER!\" *points staff at Dane* \n \n((Dane)):  *sidesteps and pushes the Undead Lord*\n \n((Undead Lord)): *falls* \n((Dane)): *leaps after him* \n((Undead Lord)): \"You will NEVER KILL ME!\"\n \n((Dane)): *pierces the Undead Lord's heart*\n \n((Undead Lord)): *drops staff and dies* \n \n((Narrator)): Dane picks up the staff and snaps it over his knees, as King Syrio appears from the shops. \n((King Syrio)): \"You sir are a brave and honourable man. Kneel sir, and tell me your name.\" \n \n((Dane)): \"Dane von Lickton, my King.\" \n \n((Narrator)): Dane bows as he gives the king his name, with an air of pride about him as recieves praise. Syrio draws his sword and places it upon Dane's shoulder. \n \n((King Syrio)): Dane von Lickton, for your bravery I pronounce you knighted. Arise, Sir Lickton; w arrior of Alras.\n \n((Narrator)): The young Dane has now become a fully fledged defender of Alras, and happily lives p rotecting the city from evils.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kings message to the people", "diiiiiiib", "help , please people i need the money which you guys give me to hold the power to create a ally with the undead , this secret is only in the Kings Tower . thank you people . all dwalfs will be honoured", ""),
        StaticBook("The Knightmare", "Yusoyung", "The knightmare was a guild that used the tactics of trade. They would hire mercenaries to go kill people to gather there belongings. The guild would then send merchants to sell these products in the four nations. They will kill evil guilds to make sure know one will know who they really are. edit", ""),
        StaticBook("The Knights Code of Chivalry", "TheRedNinja", "The Ten Commandments of the Code of Chivalry. I. Thou shalt believe all that the Church teaches, and shalt observe all its directions. II. Thou shalt defend the Church. III. Thou shalt repect all weaknesses, and shalt constitute thyself the defender of them. IV. Thou shalt love the country in the which thou wast born. V. Thou shalt not recoil before thine enemy. VI. Thou shalt make war against the Infidel without cessation, and without mercy. VII. Thou shalt perform scrupulously thy feudal duties, if they be not contrary to the laws. VII. Thou shalt never lie, and shall remain faithful to thy pledged word. IX. Thou shalt be generous, and give largess to everyone. X. Thou shalt be everywhere and always the champion of the Right and the Good against Injustice and Evil. The Code of Chivalry. ^Live to serve King and Country. ^Live to defend Crown and Country and all it holds dear. ^Live one's life so that it is worthy of respect and honor. ^Live for freedom, justice and all that is good. ^Never attack an unarmed foe. ^Never use a weapon on an opponent not equal to the attack. ^Never attack from behind. ^Avoid lying to your fellow man. ^Avoid cheating. ^Avoid torture. ^Obey the law of king, country, and chivalry. ^Administer justice. ^Protect the innocent. ^Exhibit self control. ^Show respect to authority. ^Respect women. ^Exhibit Courage in word and deed. ^Defend the weak and innocent. ^Destroy evil in all of its monstrous forms. ^Crush the monsters that steal our land and rob our people. ^Fight with honor. ^Avenge the wronged. ^Never abandon a friend, ally, or noble cause. ^Fight for the ideals of king, country, and chivalry. ^Die with valor. ^Always keep one's word of honor. ^Always maintain one's principles. ^Never betray a confidence or comrade. ^Avoid deception. ^Respect life and freedom. ^Die with honor. ^Exhibit manners. ^Be polite and attentive. ^Be respectful of host, women, and honor. ^Loyalty to country, King, honor, freedom, and the code of chivalry. ^Loyalty to one's friends and those who lay their trust in thee.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Knights Of Phoenix Hold - By Ulric Black", "olifudge", "The Knights were founded By WeeFreeMen And Olifudge on the seventhof august The plan was to form a group who would protect the forest and fight the Evils of the world soon after founding the Knights two men stroled into town These men became our Captains soon after many others came in and we began making to construct the mighty Phoenix Hold!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Knights of the North", "DBHAShadow", "The order began in the north, near the town of , back before it was rebuild, back before it was razed to the grnd by the fl Undead. There began a noble order of Knights, guardians of the north, protectors of the people from monsters and men o wld wish harm upon others. It was a simple time before the undead, men and women of the north wld come to the knights with request for  against warring nations or factions. At the time man wld face only man, or beast, or monster. Then, they arrived , beasts most fld and horrid, the undead scrge rose like a plague and quickly spread thrgh the northern lands. They ere in turn followed by those o wld convert and begin to praise the dreaded Iblees. The Knights of the North back then, mostly t of pride only allowed the most educated people to join their order, the only other way in, other than a rather tstanding life of school  and training was to be simply born into the order. Due to their exclusive membership, althgh each possessing great skill, they lacked the numbers to even try and compete with the Undead horde that set upon   Winterfell. Having been driven t of their home in the north, at few remaining members settled down  where they cld, some like Khnum and Casamir tried their hand at farming. \n Settling down in the east, near Wrath's clutch, Casamir and khnum took to the hard life of farming. Trying to live off the land, they got by as best they cld, making the odd minas here and there. One day everything changed, thugs, minions of Wrath fnd them in the nearby cntryside just off of king's road at their home, they demanded minas or life. Giving all the minas they had earned to these men made the two realize they cldn't escape the undead, not even this far from winterfell. With a new purpose and cause, the two began to organize and plan, Casamir rallied the local militias and even the knights of oren into the first assult on the clutch that Casamir wld be a part of. After beating the undead and forcing the clutch to be silent for a while, Khnum and Casamir scted the area for a suitable place. Coming across an old walled off mine entrance they knew they had fnd the right place. They quickly worked in cover of night and cleared the land arnd this mining tpost, they then erected walls further t, and removed the old walls. keeping the mine entrance and repurposing the facilities that lay beneath the surface the keep of the new Knights of the North was born to challenge wrath. \n With a new keep to call home, and a sense of reawakened purpose, Casamir brght Sir Thurgo into the fray, as an old friend he summoned the Dwarven blacksmith to his  aid. The first of the recruits to arrive, and remain was Bob, followed by Augor, then Uhtred then Animeius, then Rigrud, then Bonks, and many more. As the Ranks swelled so did the number of Knights within the new order,  the first to be knighted was Augor, followed very closely by Uhtred, Thurgo himself became a Knight. However before all this, Casamir wld lead three more raids upon the Clutch, with the aid of Oren knights yet again. Finally the Wardens, and the Dwarven guard set up near the Clutch, and together their combined might overwhelmed the    foul keep and drove them out. \n Since then things have been relativly peaceful, more recruits join the order daily, and the order's numbers grow and expand, men climb ranks and aspire for greatness. That concludes the order's history from past to present, what tales of glory will you inspire ?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kogash Alliances", "Swgrclan", "Alliances: War Nation of Krugmar, (Including all clans).", ""),
        StaticBook("The l'Arnan Journal", "MuddyCake", "This Journal is the log of my travels around the world of Aegis. Day One - After reaching Al'Khazar, I was near destitute until the famed Throdo Therving, one half of the famed Therving Brothers, gave me four-hundred minas. Immediately, I set about buying food and tools, namely a pick, an axe, a shovel, and a sword. Unsure of how to make money, I lingered around Oren for a while before travelling to Laurelin It was a beautiful place, seemingly untouched by any evil influence, and its natural beauty soothed the mind. Now with a plan, I shall set out to the wilds. Day Two - Penniless once more, I now go to Al'Khazar, and after drowining my sorrows in the von Schlitzen tavern, I meet a man, no, more of a youth, named Alexandre L Maestren. You must forgive my bad use of past and present; It is hard to keep track of what I am doing with so many ideas in my mind right now. We agreed to set forth into the wilds to forge ourselves new lives. Day Three - We left Kal'Alras behind, and the King's Road, going North-West, and so we shall go until we reach a suitable place. Day Eight - We have been through seas and passed several hospitable towns; sadly we cannot linger for long, lest we get sidetracked. Day Ten - We have reached somewhere in the middle of nowhere. We are stashing our things, lest something befall us and we lose our posessions. We shall rest here for a while. Day Thirteen - Maestren found some iron, and nowe both have iron weapons. Day Twenty - No entries for a while, but we have set up some farms and other things. No sign of Zombie Pigmen, and this hill seems secure. Skeletons and zombies cannot get here. \n Day Twenty Three - Bad inkblots and writing\n however, I have mastered the arts of writing neatly and paragraphed. \n It is just the two of us out here. I believe we needmore to come, else this place become too lonely. eraseall eraseall", ""),
        StaticBook("The Land", "emberhard", "You said earlier that I could get that grant of land for my buisness, I was just wondering where it was or if I am to just lay claim to an area \n Signed Emberhard \n ps How is the Mine idea coming along?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Land of Arvender", "mercury199", "The land of Arvender is a faroff land from the Aegis. It is populated mostly by Elves and men but there are also dwarves and orcs dwelling in it's cities. Tis a land of wonder and purity but also of great inspiration and creation. In the capital city Eridryl the rivers run gold and the sky is clear as the purest diamond. The land is of great natural wealth and that is it's downfall. Many outsiders come to the land seeking riches and bring violence with them. Where blood has been spilt the land turns a blacked color scorched of purity and life, left baren for the death collectors those in the hooded robes that stalk the land. They are older even than the elves. But they are a forsaken race devoit of compasion or love. There story is parallel to the creation of this land I write about. They were once a race born of light and life, children of the stars. They lived without fear hate anger or pain, but were warned not to wander from the land. One day a curious one seeking knowledge stepped off the coast of", ""),
        StaticBook("The Language of the Forgotten", "danyn2907", "\"@\$#%&%% \$^*)><\$@\$%*\" \n This writing was found in a temple deep underground", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Girl Alive", "leeloongsam", "A girl was the only person in her world. Therefore, that made her God. As she came to understand her situation, she realized she was on a island . The island had a mansion, which was connected to an old castle via a passageway. She didn't know why such a bizarre structures were built there in the first place. There was no need to know. Besides, she was simply there from the beginning, so she didn't question her surroundings. A mountain of preserved goods and other necessities were stored inside the castle's warehouse. Hunger wasn't a problem, though she starved until she realized the goods were edible. However, she almost perished several times due to sickness.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Journal of Kela'Vala", "MarieC90", "I write this journal on my deathbed, so that others may continue on my work... I have made the worst mistake, sin, a Father can. One-hundred and fifty years ago, in the year 1139, my son wandered away from me while playing outsid e. ...He never returned. He was always a precocious lad, my dear Rek'Vala. Always getting into trouble, but never so much so that I could not get him out! But Luraza, this new land we moved to before he was born, apparently offered new dangers. The one which finally claimed him was the mines... I spent the last one-hundred and fifty years searching, digging, tunnelling. Work unsuited for an Elf such as myself. But I am on my deathbed. I can continue no longer. Please...please. Someone, find him. He must be still alive! I refuse to accept his death! The others called me mad, but there are adequate supplies down there... Surely....Surely....", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Man At The Keep", "gombie", "As we are walking forward with an group of 4 men. We entered snowyfields you could feel the breeze on your skin. We were looking for any sign of the So called 'Undead' . I think poeple were having to much Fantasy agian. How could possibly someone be undead!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Sunset: Part I", "Maverick27070", "It was dark. A damp dew was forming on the grass outside the tall imposing gates of Al'Khazar . The wind was blowing hard, making the gate sway too and fro in it's settings. Two lone Oren Guards stood to attention outside the gate, a duty they hated with a passion like no other. This was going to be a pivitol night for both of them, as they were about to f ind out first hand. The Undead were coming in force, and nothing was going to stop them.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Testimony of Warden_EG_Icarus", "mattr41018", "I, Icarus of the Wardens, of insane mind, and unsound body, Reliquish this book to my friends, and peers in the wardens. I write in here, any Hiers i may have in this world... If i am to die, at any time I relinquish all of my items to the elf named Rattalyn... The history between me and Rattalyn is not necessary for this... Just tell her, that I love her... oh, and tell her to tell Torok, I am sorry...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Truth", "Hwaldar", "He knew they would not believe me... \nHe knew they will be harsh... \nI leave this book to you...To prove His final word... \nHwaldar had a Brother \nHe never knew about \nBut now he knows the cruel truth... Ag'Na'Rok... \nHe was his little brother \nStolen by the darkness \nStolen by the One...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Words of Amras", "Ranovak", "Hello dear reader, for whom this book might have fallen into. I address you this book which once belonged to an officer in the Elven military, the Wardens. \n If you are in possession of this book, I have long since left the wardens. I have paid my final goodbyes to Quazar and other officers, and left in silence. Do not fear my reasons, they are not ill. I write this in the comfort of my library, as I pack for a life of wandering. \n My reasons for departure are mixed. I have grown tired of a life of bloodshed and battle, of warriors and rebels. I am an elf of peace, I have grown dull from the sounds of painful screams, from the war drum as we storm our enemy's bases. Now I write, I have given up my power as a war noble, and replaced it with the life of an ascetic. Do not fear, this is not the last you have seen of me, I will travel all of Aegis, searching for truth, and documenting it with my journal. \n I leave behind all my worldly possessions, so they do greater good for the wardens then for me. All possessions I carry in my tent; I give to Quazar to share amongst the wardens. My collection of books; I give to Elessar, the young elf hungers for knowledge. And most importantly; I leave my library in charge of Durzio, I hope I made no mistake in doing this. \n Now spread amongst the wardens are what used to belong to me, Amras'Tullum. I apologize for not saying a proper goodbye upon my departure but alas my yearning for a life outside the wardens has grown strong. Do not feel disappointed in my somber departure, I shall be back, not as a warden, but as a guest. Until that day comes I hope the wardens remain strong, and Malin guide they're path to justice and peace. \n My parents were both druids, maybe my journey will start there.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Writ of Lady Faelyn Evindal", "TehLulu", "I write this as a last testament of sorts. I feel myself growing weaker as the days go by, and my heart cannot bear for this knowledge to be lost to the world. I have lived for going on hundreds of years, yet for so long I have kept this a secret. Before my marriage to Sir Evindal and my return to Malinor,   I lived another life for several decades. \n When I was young, naive, and fairly blind to the ways of the world, I met a human man by the name of Ereen who came to Malinor on a mission.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last writings of Robert Banstir", "TheImpulseHQ", "*The Diary is half burned, and covered in blood*//Dear the Reader, i am Robert Banstir Head of House Bannist, Eldest of the Banstir Family, Bywater is being besieged and the Undead have teamed up with the Raiders, they are killing everyone , Daniel stands beside me, my other brothers are dead. I hope the Momronts are- No time for that, I know information that must not get in the hands of the undead, i must be killed, Only Majester is alive to do it, I must get to oren and- *From here on the book is too burned to read*", ""),
        StaticBook("THE LAURELIN WEEKLY", "hydromr", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Law", "Lymdil", "As citizien you are: \n Not allowed to harvest crops of others without their permission \n Not allowed to step/destroy their crops \n Not allowed to make big changes in Town without Permission of Frado or Lym \n Not allowed to tell various people our Location. Please show the Town only to those you trust and who actually are nice persons! double-colon \n Please give Feedback. For more information contact Frado or Lym. We help you!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Law", "jeremybombed", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Law of Alras", "Steve_00", "Hold this law book and repeat after me", ""),
        StaticBook("The Law of the Brethren", "fatwampa", "The Dark Brotherhood\n There is but one law. Passed down from generation to generation, this law has bound those that have served in the Brotherhood since the elder era. All that have ever sworn their alliegence to the Brotherhood have followed this decree. To break this law is to betray everything they stand for. To break it is to turn your back on the brethren. The Law is this; Respect the Brotherhood. That is all\n Never has one law caused so much violence and destruction. Nor has one law ever created more fellowship. Since the beginning of the Dark Brotherhood, not one Law was created but this. This is the only law\n There has only been two different interpertaions of this Law.", ""),
        StaticBook("The lay of Nimrodel", "ForestMaid", "\n An elven maid there was of old A shining star by day Her mantle white was hemmed with gold Her shoes of silver grey \n A star was bound upon her brows A light was on her hair As sun upon the golden boughs In Lorien the fair \n Her hair was long, her limbs were white And fair she was and free And in the wind she went as light As leaf of linden tree \n Beside the falls of Nimrodel By water clear and cool Her voice as falling silver fell Into the shining pool \n Where now she wanders none can tell In sunlight or in shade For lost of yore was Nimrodel And in the mountains strayed \n The elven ship in haven grey Beneath the mountain-lee Awaited her for many a day Beside the roaring sea \n A wind by night in northern lands Arose and loud it cried And drove the ship from elven strands Across the streaming tide \n When dawn came dim the land was lost The mountains sinking grey Beneath the heaving waves that tossed Their plumes of blinding spray \n Amroth beheld the fading shore Now low beyond the swell And cursed the faithless ship that bore Him far from Nimrodel \n Amroth was an elven-king A lord of tree and glen When golden were the boughs of spring in fair Lothlorien \n From helm to sea the saw him leap As arrow from the string And dive into the water deep As mew upon the wing \n But from the west has come no word And on the hither shore No tidings elven folk have heard Of Amroth ever more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The leaders of the Anarchy Knights", "wowblizz", "Lord Captain- Naksa :Arch Mage- Argyron", ""),
        StaticBook("The Leaders of the Humans", "Elite117", "As recorded by Apollan . The Human leaders have mixed feelings. Continue brother", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legacy of Medrike", "Medrike", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legency of Horen", "rapptor13", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend Of Adamanticus", "Caesar135", "Thanks", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Haren", "everblue2er101", "*The book is very old. It has clearly been through a lot, seen multiple owners and aged greatly. Pages are torn, words are smudged and it is in a different dialect difficult to understand. *", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Lord Burnout", "LROWNAGE", "Long ago in a dwarven town, there were two families. One was called the Grimlocks, the others Tyners. They never liked each other. In fact, they hated each other so much they began a feud. As the town and it's neighbouring towns became engulfed in battle, hop was lost. However, the Grimlocks had a secret weapon. A weapon that could win them this war. It was called Burnout. Burnout was a brilliant warrior. With Medley Grimlock as his mentor, he came to love the family. When the war began he fought alongside his master. The ultimate challenge he faced was horrific to him. He watched Medley die. And when that happened, something inside him snapped. Burnout was gone, and in his place an evil fiend. This was Lord Burnout. He slaughtered everyone and continued to even after the war. Many warriors tried to stop him, but he was too strong. After taking a lightning bolt from a mage, he changed back to Burnout. But not for long. In the second that Burnout had returned, he realised his corruption. Unable to take the killing that he'd done, he ran. And up to this very day, no one knows where he is. And this tale is now but a legend. But, if he's still around, he will return. It's only a matter of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Nagi", "Jon021", "Opens on a scene of the village of kamui narrator: This legend begins in the peaceful village of Kamui narrator: this village only seemed peaceful, for a fearsome beast, Orochi, terrorized it by demanding a sacrifice of the maiden of his choosing narrator: This town also happens to be the home of the great warrior Nagi, who trained every day to hone his already impressive skills mr. grapefruit crosses to nagi's training ground, where he is training Mr. Grapefruit(distressed): Nagi! Wonderful warrior, there is a dangerous beast roaming our town! Nagi: What sort of beast, Old man Grapefruit? A demon of the evil variety? Mr. Grapefruit: What other kind of demon is there? This beast is certainly one of them. He disguises himself as a white wolf! The townsfolk and I think he is a servant of Orochi, the horrible beast Nagi: I shall fight and slay him tonight when he comes! He shall not see tomorrow's morning! Nagi continues training while Mr. Grapefruit walks off to his own home suddenly Nami, the love of Nagi appears and comes to Nagi Nami: Nagi! The night that Orochi chooses his sacrifice draws nearer still. I am very worried for my own well being and of us Nagi: don't worry, my dear. I am sure he will chose some other maiden, as he has for a long time. Nami: I still fear it. And I have heard of this lupine servant of his who roams the town in the night Nagi: do not worry, I shall slay that foul beast tonight! He shall plague us no longer. scene fades away to the town at night the wolf walks through the town and past nagi's home, from which nagi jumps out form replace form from write -help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Pork", "dudog", "One day The leaders of the four core races were meeting in the Cloud Temple. While they were leaving, the Dwarf King spotted something pink in the grass. The leaders drew their swords and went to investigate. They prepared for battle but the pink creature just stood their. \"What is it?\" the Orc leader asked. \"It's a... Pig!\" The Elven Prince said. The leaders started back towards their cities. On the way back the Human King found another pig. He took out his sword and killed the pig, leaving a small peice of pork behind. The Human King ran towards the other leaders and explained his discovery. The four leaders each had a bite of the new food. Pork is now one of the yummiest and healthiest foods in Aegis. If you eat pork in every meal you will live to the old age of 27.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Shiranui", "Jon021", "\nAct one: scene opens on the small town of Kamui \n narrator: This is the small town of Kamui, home of the great warrior Nagi \n Nagi comes and begins training \n \nNarrator: unlike most small towns, this was not a peaceful one \nNarrator: Every year a maiden would be selected from the town to be sacrificed to Orochi, a horrible beast \n\nNarrator: the day of the selection was drawing close, and Nagi was worried that \n Nami, his love, would be chosen \n Old man Orange approaches Nagi \n Old Man Orange: Nagi! Great warrior of Kamui ! As you know, the day of the selection draws near, and there is a fearsome white wolf-beast who roams the town at night. We fear he is a servant of Orochi. He must be slain! \n Nagi: Of course, Old Man Orange, I shall slay the beast tonight! He shall not see the light of tomorrow! \n Old Man Orange: Good. Good. I know that the beast will be no match for you! \n Old Man Orange leaves Nagi to his training \n Nami approaches Nagi \n Nami: Nagi, my love, the night of the selection approaches! I am concerned about being sacrificed to that horrible beast. \nNagi: do not worry, Nami. All the maidens concern themselves with this every year. You will not be chosen. \n Nami: I think you are right. Farewell my love. \n leaves Nagi to his training, while Nagi goes in his home \n Night falls over Kamui, and Shiranui comes out and paces the road \n Nagi appears and stands before Shiranui \n Nagi: Foul beast! I shall slay you tonight! \n Shiranui growls and bares his fangs at Nagi \n the two fight, with Shiranui eventually defeating Nagi \n Nagi: urgh..... your power... where does it come from? \n Shiranui disapears into the night, and Nagi drags himself to his home \n The sun rises over Kamui \nOld Man Orange approaches Nagi \n Old Man Orange: Nagi! I trust that you slayed the beast last night. \n Nagi: No... he defeated me.. \n Old Man Orange: What?? The great warrior defeated? What has happened to the world? It has descended into madness! \n Nagi: Do not worry. I shall fight the beast every night until it is slain! \n \nNarrator: Nagi fought the beast ever night until the night of the selection came . The white arrow marking the home of the maiden to be sacrificed flew into Nami's home. \n Nagi runs to Nami \n Nagi: No! My love! Do not go! \n Nami: I must, lest the beast lay ruin to the town \n Nami puts on the sacrificial gowns and leaves for Orochi's lair \n Nagi comes after her and enters the beast's lair \n Nagi slowly approaches a great stone circle with a bell in the center \n Orochi (unseen): Mortal! Who are you? You are not my sacrifice! \n Nagi: I am Nagi! The great warrior of Kamui! You shall not have Nami, my love! \n Orochi: Fool! You shall feel my wrath for interrupting my sacrifice \n Oroch shows himself, with all his heads looking threateningly at Nagi \n Orochi and Nagi fight, Orochii knocks Nagi to the ground \n Orochi: Hah, mortal! You are no match for me! \n as Orochi is about to deal the final blow, Shiranui attacks his head, saving Nagi \n Shiranui stands before Nagi, protecting him from Orochi's attacks \n Nagi stands up \n Nagi: Orochi! We shall slay you! (raises sword into the air) \n the three of them fight, with Shiranui and Nagi winning \n as Nagi and Shiranui are about to deal the final blow, Orochi wounds Shiranui, and knocks him to the ground, while Nagi delivers the final blow, slicing off all 8 of Orochi's heads \n Nami is brought into the chamber to be sacrificed, and sees Nagi and Orochi's body She runs to Nagi \n Nami: Nagi! You defeated him! \n Nagi: It was not just me, my love. The wolf- (sees Shiranui on ground) \n Nagi runs to Shiranui with Nami coming behind \n Nagi carries the wolf back to Kamui \n Nagi, Nami and Old man Orange are gathered around Shiranui \n Old Man Orange: We distrusted this wolf... and he was our only ally.  We shall erect a temple and a statue to honor his sacrifice! \n Shiranui licks Nagi's and Old Man Orange's feet before closing his eyes \n last scene shows the statue of Shiranui", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of The Coral Key: Part 1", "itechify", "*Opening the tome you feel an ocean breeze* \nThe brothers, John and Simon, loved to play by the beach. They loved it so much, that when their parents died, they buried them in the sand. After losing them, the two boys were distraught. They were alone. They only had eachother. So, they got rid of their house, and moved to the beach that they loved. \nLiving near their parents graves was comforting. They almost felt as if they were still alive with them. One day while the boys were out fishing, they saw a glow in the water. Simon was puzzled, but he needed to know what it is. He proceeded to jump into the water. He was about to get to the glowing item, but suddenly he was taken by a jetstream, unable to  get to the surface. He started to panic. He needed air. He knew it was over for him, so he accepted his fate. He let the jet stream take him. Looking back, he sees John is also in the jetstream.", ""),
        StaticBook("The legend of the Knights", "Busenki", "There were once two knights, one the knight of God and one an evil knight. They met on a bridge one day and looked at each other deep in the eyes. Without a word the evil knight drew his sword and charged without a word, just like all the cowards do these days. The honorable knight dodged the evil knights attack but did not draw his blade. For a second the evil knight was confused as to why his enemy did not strike back while he had the chance. The knight of God said \"You consider me an enemy, yet we have never met before. You strike like a coward. The water below should not be defiled by your foul blood. You are not worthy of my blade, the blade guided by God almighty himself.\" The evil knight hissed as he striked again. The knight of God deflected the blade, sending it through the evil knight's stomach. \"See? It is not I that have slain you, but the darkness in your heart. The work of God is stronger then any evil in this world.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend Of The Were-Spiders", "greenmilkweed", "In the most darkest.. scariest.. horrific corners of the world.. the Were-Spiders lie. Half woman, half arachnid.. Lurk through the shadows waiting for the next poor soul to be her feast. Sewing webs of blood, catching their prey with grace, Then feeding on the flesh. These beasts of beauty and grace, T'was not began the way they lurk. In the early ages, these beautiful women had not webs, had not the craving for Blood and flesh. Regular women they were.. 'till the day of their highest sins. Doing the opposite of their commands, courting men, week by week. Month by month. Until the day a dark man who bestowed upon the dark magicks traveled to towns the women were rumored to be in. Casted a great spell of darkness over these women he did. Reason? They did not do as what they were told to do. Mostly dark haired women, Black to red eyes. Hidden fangs beneath their suducing faces. Eight long black legs, an abdomen of a spherical shape capable of weaving webs the size of a lake. From then on is the waist up of a normal woman. Now, Watch your every step into darkness. The undead aren't the only thing to worry of anymore.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend Of TwilightStorm", "TwilightStorm", "This book tells the tail of Twilight Storm. Inside you will find information about his life. His life began in a small cottage located within the forest surrounding the great city of Laurelin. He lived  there happily with his family for many years and learned to love nature.  \"Nature is everywhere and everything. Even the smallest ant is a part of nature.\" His father once said.   Around the time of Twilight's fifteenth birthday his home was attacked! The aggressors were followers of the Undead. Right before the attack happened Twilight's mother hid him in the cellar of their cottage. After doing this she went to  his father fight the Undead followers. They fought bravely but in the end both were slain. Hours later when Twilight thought it to be safe he emerged from the cellar. He emerged to find both of his parent dead on the floor of their home and all of his possessions gone. This  scarred and panicked the young elf. During his panic he fled his home going deeper into the forest. He lived alone in the forest with nature for it  was the only thing that comforted him in life. He lived alone in the forest for about ten years. About the time of his twenty-fifth birthday  he spotted a young elf walking through forest alone. He asked the elf what he was doing out in the forest all alone and told him it dangerous. The elf replied saying that his village was destroyed by Undead followers of Dwarven descent about a week ago. Feeling bad for the young lad Twilight gave him some bread and asked him to live with him. He did this because he knew the pain of losing a family. The young elf accepted and procliamed that his name was Volthias, Volthias Dramos. Twilight was very entertained by the name and took him under his wing. They made periodic trips to Laurelin to sell the lumber and animal hides they collected. During one of these trips Twilight decided that Volthias had come of age to wield a sword so he bought him a brand new iron sword. Volthias was amazed that his new older brother would buy him such an item. As soon as they returned to their home he immediatly went off into the forest to slay some spiders. This was not his best idea for after he killed one spider about three more popped out of the web and surrounded him. He though that his time had come, but suddenly from out of the bushes Twilight burst with bow in hand and shot off two arrows with blazing speed at the spiders . Two of them fell where they stood as Twilight produced a sword and proceded to stab it into the last spiders head, killing the beast. As Twilight brought Volthias back to their camp he gave him a lecture on why he should not go into the forest alone. Volthias learned from this experience and became a better swordsman from it. After about fifty years of life in the forest both decided that it was about time to go and do something new. They left the forest to find a good career that involved killing the Undead. They traveled and traveled until they arrived at Kal'Urguan. Once there they spoke with an elf, Thimble was his name. He was but a year older than Twilight and told them of the United Aegis Coalition and their cause. Both Twilight and Volthias thought that the UAC would be a great cause to join so they accompanied Thimble on the White Road on the way to Haven and the UAC. Once they arrived at the UAC they met a dwarf who also wished to join their noble cause. Volthias was a little cautious at first but soon learned to trust the fellow. The dwarf's name was Blaedr Stouthammer. He was a very likeable fellow adept at building and crafting. The three of them approached the UAC base together whilst Thimble went on to talk to the Ascended. Once the three had arrived at the UAC base they were met by UAC Lt. Erik who told them that in order to join they must speak with Sornof, but instead of talking to Sornof they them that in order to join they must speak with Sornof, but instead of talking to Sornof they talked to UAC Captain Maur who inducted them into the order. After they were given housing and such they were greeted by the great and wise Sage Arcadius who made them official members of the UAC. Soon after that the three went and furbished their new homes. Once their homes were furbished Thimble arrived at the UAC base once more. He was then asked to remodel the chapel that the UAC had been building. Twilight, Volthias, and Blaedr all helped him with this task.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend Of Valknor", "MrJakKiD", "As a young boy Valknor was very inquisitive.. He explored everywhere in his parents estate He was a very sickly child and didnt have many friends..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legend of Vardak. Chapter 0 The Begining.", "Vardak", "Born in the nation of Oren. Vardak's parent's, both diplomats from the Sootrock Tribe had come to save their tribe from the incoming darkness that would fall upon the land. \n As they reached the gates of the human capital. Both Vardak's mother and father were", ""),
        StaticBook("The Legion", "Kal_Derra", "Mercenaries For Hire\n \n Need someone to protect you on your travels?\n Need someone to guard your shop?\n Need someone to patrol your ground?\n \n We would be pleased to help out.\n \n Ned information on a person or building?\n Want to take a place by force?\n \n We are your men.\n \n Want to be a member of The Legion?\n \n We welcome you in our ranks.\n \n Visit us in Al'Khazar\n (new district behind the main gate;fhh6)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life and Times of Twidget Hucklefinn", "KingOchros", "Short Story One: The Grape Fell Far From the Vine. Twidget Hucklefinn was an odd fellow at the ripe young age of thirteen. Twidget indulged in much exploration in the woods nearby his home; In fact, he was out in the ws woods* more than he was anywhere else. As I just mentioned, Twidget was an odd fellow. How you might ask? Well, perhaps a story would explain better. One evening, while Twidget was out in the woods, he became very lonely and a sudden idea struck. \"Why don't I find a friend? It would certainly be more fun than standing around all day.\" He tho thought* to himself. And that is exactly what He did. Twidget climbed to the top of a nearby hil hill* and looked out in the distance. Lo and behold, He was a figure of small stature seamingly stuck in a hole that was quite deep. \"I'll go help him! He'll be my friend.\" Twidget s said. As he came up to the hole, he realised that the small figure was like nothing he'd seen before. He gasped \"What are you\", as he looked at the crooked man with beady eyes and a rather blue complexion. \"What is wrong with your face?\" He asked. \"Child, help me out of here, and I shall reward you handsomely with anything you desire\" said the devilish imp. \"Okay, would you be my friend?\" Twidget asked. \"Anything, just help me out\" He replied. the hole. \"Now you shall have no friends\" he said. Twidget was saddened, but suddenly realised \"Wait, if I am stuck here, I shall surely die. I shall have many friends where I go!\" Of course he didn't die, but everyone knew from that day forth that he was very odd.", ""),
        StaticBook("the life in a dwarven city", "verrenn", "Its very humorous the dwarven people are much more... how do i put it... ahh yes! funnyer tha n us humans, elves, and orcs. \n but when you think of dwarves you think of them as drunk and mindless. BUT to me they are not drunken idiots they are worriors and well they do drink ale everyonce in awile... *sigh* and i must end this book with a sad chapter not all is well in a dwarven city some people dont like management so they must... overthrow i guese you could say .", ""),
        StaticBook("the life in holmes", "oskka99", "the crimes arnt getting any better still there are many gangs of bandits on the run, not only bandits the undead are worse .", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of a Druid", "jdpowercool", "The life of a druid can be harsh, at times. Not many people, even the elves can understand us.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of A Guard", "rapptor13", "Paragraph.1 The Beggining Hello Iam Gornak I made this book for ppl To Let them know how a life of a guard is Iam Guarding Al'khazar now for about 5/6 Days Iam Currently Defending the gate to be sure there arent entering any undead I  think whe already got 2 Undead,s in our City Dalek and another Guy", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of a Simple Shaman", "_Player_2_", "My name be Krogath, a shaman who lives a simple life. I walk around with my wooden staff and ask for guidance every night from spirits, i pray for power and strength to support other orcs", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of Ailean Vol. 1", "pogi400", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life Of Dran", "drangob", "Dran'gob was born into a bandit family who lived far south of Krugmar. When Dran'gob got into an argument with his father his father challenged him to a duel, which Dran won easily. After that he was exiled by his own grandfather and made his way to the capital of Krugmar. \n When Dran arrived at Sanjezal a guard who went by the name Bein showed him the sights and told him of the Orcish culture and systems. From this point Dran looked up to Bein'lur and saw him as his mentor and teacher of life . Dran decided to join up with the guards, but as he tried to a new idea was being formed by Bein. Bein was forming the Ferox Legio. Dran quickly joined up and gained the rank of Tribune for his efforts in building Fort Ferox. He stood by and watched the guilds progress, making sure to contribute as much as he could. He was then promoted to Optio, then Primus of Fort Ferox. Then Legatus of the Ferox. \n When the Riverside wars were taking place Dran did not take much of a part. But when Bein'lur took control and created Sanhar Dran stood by his side and took orders to create the town. When Sanhar was built and working, Bein'lur felt the strain of all the reponsibility and gave Leadership of the Ferox Legio. Dran was delighted and started to construct the Sanhar guildhouse. Around the guildhouse Upper Sanhar started forming. Dran gained the title of Consul of Citizens for creating so much of the town and remaining loyal to Dominus Bein'lur throughout.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life Of Goleth The Assassin", "legofanatix", "hello hello", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of Laurlien", "Rutheniel", "Nothing, Just a bit odd we'd run into each other here", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life Of Lodrick ((Written By Jack))", "jigg21", "In the north the wind blew forcefully against my cabin. I was lost in the fire, gleaming into not taking my eyes off of it. Something horrible was happening a creation of a monster. A man who born to serve, The Fallen One Iblees.. Thunder boomed in the distance and lightning crackled in the skies as Lodrick was born in the Cloud Temple.. Lodrick, was a weird child, usually he would be found speaking to himself and chanting weird things in his basement.. His parents were slaughtered out of cold blood quickly after his arrival on Aegis.. One day the dwarfs spotted Lodrick feasting upon a dwarf remains around a shrine of Iblees..  This was to be known as Lodrick's first sacrifice to Iblees.. Rain trickled on the ground the day he was caught, and the dwarfs tortured him and  threw him in a cave far away from civilization.. There Lodrick grew strong feeding Iblees with sacrifices. Lonely travelers were caught, tortured, and sacrificed.. Lodrick grew stronger and stronger.. He dedicated his life to Iblees.. Lodrick quickly became a.. *You see scatch marks and blood on this page.. You quickly realized this book wasn't finished and something must of happened to Lodrick's cousin Jack..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life Of Pisellone The Axe", "pisellone", "Pisellone, like everyone in Aegis, came to life at the cloud temple He was a dwarf. A powerful one to be exact. He clad himself in a beautiful golden armour set. At once he set of for The great city of Kal'Urugan It was a dangerous journey, he had to fight of many monsters with his bare fists . But he made it to the city. It turns out that the Dwarves were at war with th orcs! He joined up as soon as he found out and went on many raids, when he was gravley injured He dragged himself back to Kal'urguan but many things had changed. The city was not a secret anymore \n No one would take pity on him, ME I was left to DIE! I dragged myself down the mine to this spot  I nursed myself back to health Now I am old I still have scars on my body and mind that my people turned me away (END)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of PyroFuzion", "PyroFuzion", "Eating, Sleeping and Gaming!", ""),
        StaticBook("The life of Rob_Mills.", "boodilly", "I was born and raised on a small farm and mill outside oren. I was an unusual child, helping with the farm work, but making books and teaching myself to read. I lived a peaceful life, even if I was unusual till I was 13. War broke out with a large band of rogue orcs, humans, and dwarfs. The kings army needed more guards, so they drafted every boy who could hold a sword. This is how I became a swordsman. I stayed in the guard till recently,when I joined the holmes gr oup. Also, I kept my love of reading a secret though my army days, but brought it out recently. This happened when the Whisper Library opened, and I became a librarian.", ""),
        StaticBook("The life of Shez'lur", "biggs7", "Shez'lur was born into a poor family, although he was poor, he possessed extraordinary intelligence .His mother and father did all they could for him, but Shez'lur was destined to live the life of pov erty read", ""),
        StaticBook("The Life of Thrym", "NoobCrafter14", "The account of the life of Thrym. Scibed by Thrym this writing is accurate. \nWhen I awoke in the Cloud temple many years ago I was but a beardling. I did not know where I was or where to go. Following the instuctions of the monks I learned that by using my soulstone I could travel to the capitol of the dwarves. I did not know the way the land seeming unfamiliar. When I arrived in Kal'Urguan, transported by the powers of Aegis, I met a dwarf known as Gotrek Firemane. He was an Overseer in the Whisphering Isles. \nGotrek and I talked and he invited me to his home. Upon arriving he treated me kindly and gave me ale then let me stay to sober up. He treated me with all the hospitality a dwarf could and I remembered him ever after. \nA while after a Herald from the Valve showed up to Kal'Urguan. He was known as Martin Benedict. He was trying to rally the dwarves to put aside racial differences with the rest of Aegis and join together to combat the undead. He and I talked and I travelled with him to the valve to join the heraldry. He became my mentor after I was accepted and alone and with him I travelled all over Aegis proclaiming a joint front against the Undead. My time in the Valve was brief but even today I remeber the way to Kal'Menor. \nAfter a while I left the Valve to join the new dwarven army, the Free Dwarfs Army. It was while I was in the FDA that Martin and I came into contact again. \nMartin and some others including Kootry, a forest dwarf, and Sornof, an orc, had formed a guild that was dedicated to a united force against the undead. This guild was known as the United Aegis Coalition. I would help Martin and the few guild members there to build there fort near Haven from time to time but eventually Martin convinced me to leave the FDA and join him in the UAC. \nI was in the UAC for many years. I was there when Martin became ascended, when Kootry came into power, when Martin returned to take leadership as the UAC had declined from what it once was, I was there when Martin died finding Arcadius and when Sornof took control. I have faught many battles many in my time in the UAC. While in the UAC I made friends such as Maur, Renzbro, Sornof and Olde Beer Belly. \nSadly not even the UAC could last forever. It was soon turned in the FoA, a task force of the ascended. Blaedr, also a friend of mine, was put in charge. Sornof was enraged at being demoted. I honestly believe he was one of the best leaders the UAC had and was sad to see him go. The last I saw of Sornof was him in a rage leading off some men to attack the undead. I stayed for a while in the FoA under Blaedr who I had respect for. But, it was no longer the UAC, no longer what I had joined. So, I left. I meant to return but now I don't believe and don't wish to ever return to the FoA. \nI left the FoA to visit Kal'Urguan the place I had lived for long years. There I met Gotrek again. It had been many years but I had never forgotten him. Gotrek was now the Grand Master Smith of the Dwarves. This was exactly what I had been looking for. I had travelled to Urguan to become a blacksmith. When I saw him and heard what he was doing now I requested to apprentice under him. I was accepted and became apprentice to Grand Master Smith Gotrek Firemane. While in training with him he was performing powerful enchantments and while I stood by watching his work one enchantment was very powerful and the magic seeped into the silver trinkets I had forged and was toying with in my right hand. There was a flash of light and then dark. When I awoke my Master was looking at my right arm and I beheld that it was now, from the elbow down, made completely of silver. My master said he sensed magic in it and was going to study it further. That day I left my surname of Deepdelver behind. I was now Thrym Silverfist. \nThrough my time in Urguan I have been here for the reign of two kings and am here for the reign of the third. The first was Belin The Industrious who made Kal'Urguan a jewel in Aegis again. The next was Algrim The Weak who was a good king but weak and turned to evil. The King that is mi'lord now is Gotrek who was my master. Long Live the King!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lion Hunts at Sunrise", "DarkAnimus", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The List", "Lokito", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Little Blue Book", "l337Ninja", "\"Knowledge is power, guard it well\" Motto of the Praesidium Tenus Scientia", ""),
        StaticBook("The Little Seed", "ErcMan", "There once was a little seed planted in a farm. While he stayed small the other all grew 2 up around him. He felt small and sad. Over the time of a week the seed grew into a stalk, 3 while the wheat woundered about him to theirselves, the little seed kept growing. Since 4 he was thinner then the wheat they made fun of him, and this only made him sadder. 5 The next day when he awoke, all the other plants were smaller he had grown into a melon he 5 he was so happy to have grown so large. After the wheat saw he had grown the praised his write e", ""),
        StaticBook("The Little Unicorn", "hughlorin", "Once upon a time there was a little unicorn. He was a humble and kind unicorn, and always stopped to help someone in need. But he was always picked on by the bigger unicorns, because his horn wasn't as long as their big unicorn horns. They always made him feel terrible. Yet he kept being nice to them, no matter what they said. \n One day, disaster struck the little unicorn's home, and all the unicorns were captured. All of the unicorns were scared. \"What ever will we do?\" \"We will be slaves!\" Many unicorns wept, while others tried to escape. The little unicorn, being among the ones captured, spoke up. \"I'll see if I can get us out,\" he said. All the other unicorns laughed at this and hurled insults at him. \"You can't save us! You're to small!\" \"You're only half my size! You can't help!\" But still the little unicorn went on despite the scorn. \n He flew up to the top of the cage they were trapped in and, because of his size, he flew right through the bars the bigger unicorns couldn't get through. He flew down to the doors and used his small horn to unlock the doors. The unicorns praised the little unicorn and loved him. They learned that just because someone is different than you doesn't make them any less valuable. \n THE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lobster Unicycle Ride.", "jens6851", "Tam: Hello Mum. Hello Dad. Father: Hello Tam, hows my pride and joy?    Tam: Fine thanks.   Mother:Well Tam you have fin ally done it. You are famous now. And i cant say im very pleased about it.   Tam:What do you mean \" im famous\"?   Mother:I mean this,young lady. Look at this. You have made front page News!   Tam: *reads* Giant Lobster Rides Unicycle Coast to Coast Hmmm what makes you think th at it was me?  Mother: Well Tam, i dont know anyone else who dresses up like a lobster and has her o wn unicycle!   Tam: Fair point.   Father:Coast to coast. Well done Tam!  Mother George!  Stop encouraging her! What on earth were you thinking, Cycling all the way to The Atlantic dressed as a bloody lobster?!   Tam: I was just doing my job.    Mother: What does this have to do with your job? you are supposed to stand in front of the restaurant and hand out menus.   Tam: Mr_muckwater told me to go out and get alot of attention. What i did is called a publicity stunt.   Father: Good for you Tam! Mother: George!  Father: Which route did you take?   Tam: Well, first i took the bus to boness,then i cycled the A904 to Falkirk, then the B816 to Bonnybrigde...   Mother: To Bonnybridge! What if Great Aunt Catherine had seen you?!   Tam:oh.. he did.   Mother: What?! Tam: I mean her. She looks like a he, but i had to stop and use her loo   Mother: You Dident! Tam: Dident i??  Mother: TAM!  Tam: She was very happy to see me. though i did give her a bit of a shock. Father: Dont worry i will talk to Catherine. What has Mr_Muchwater said? Tam: Oh, hes ever so pleased. He said i even made the London papers   Mother: What?! Tam: Hes given me a raise and a bonus. And these free dinner coupons for you and Mum. Father Excellent Tam!  Mother:Tam, i think you are taking this job much too seriously... Tam: No im not.  Mother: Tam, you have had that outfit on for two days straight! Tam: three actually.  Mother: Dont tell me you wore that outfit to school! Tam: OK.  Mother: Did you wear it in school??  Tam: No   Mother: Good.  Tam: I put it on at t at lunchtime. I only wore it to Chemistry and English.  Father: And what did you teachers say", ""),
        StaticBook("The log of a hunters bow", "joshey8555", "Day 1 Today i ventured into the ruins below my house, bad, bad mistake at least 5 giant spiders awaited to kill me... thats not all that awaited, a creature i had not seen before now, a dark creature that had purple smoke pouring from its body like smoke from a wood fire, this smoke chilled my body aas", ""),
        StaticBook("The Log of Groobs", "Groobs03", "first off i dont like to write, so this isnt going to happen", ""),
        StaticBook("The lolely creeper", "Xyloph", "Once upon a time there were a lonely creeper He was sad because people thought he was a peeper They exluded him from their society he thought \"Its all because of their anxiety\" The creeper did not know what he should do Friends he wanted, that was true If he approched anyone he would explode The bonds they shared, would erode Like the might dwarven mountains Or the great city of orens fountains He did not wish to be alone Friends of his own, he had to moan But his heart was ablaze, his feelings a maze Never wanted to give up the thought of a true friend Once upon a day, not to his dismay A human child visited him, The light were dim and they became friends forever. The end. title The lonely creeper aah messed up another book messed up another book :S  erase  erase [Read]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lone Hunter", "Xeniith", "Years ago, there was a hunter named Aaron. One day, when he was in the forest, he returned to find that his parents were brutally murdered. Bludgeoned to death. One can only imagine the pain this moment caused for him. From this pain, he had broken the wall between reality and his imagination. Ever since then, he is not only unable to speak, but sees things in a much more disturbing light than any normal person. When he left his blood-soaked home, he slowly started to lose his mind. He eventually lost his will to speak, his will to move, and his will to live. He was taken in by a kind man who helped him regain his strength, and a portion of his sanity. In exchange, the man asked Aaron to marry his daughter, Alysia. He refused, and regrets this decision to this day. He traveled off into the woods in shame, looking for a place in this world. Certain he would never find a home for himself, he stopped searching.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lone Warrior", "Austinpowers999", "Many years ago when Al'Khazar was a meer town There was a lone Warrior called Cal'em he trained his skills in swordsmanship training to honour himself and his family. He was told by his master to Fight until death; never surrender fight until death. His family was killed my the lowest spawns of evil speaking the name would make others awe the group of warriors whom killed his fanily where a group of mighty warrior s So Cal'em assebled the createst warrior from each nation Kalrun The Dwarf. Master of the axe Grom the Orc. The fiercest warrior in what today is Krugmar Tallenia the best archer in all of Malinor These warriors fought for honour. They banded together to take out this mighty evil They all honed and trained there skills for many years The band of the 4 warriors marched together all in full armour made from the hardest dwarven diamond The sharpest orc swords The largest Dwarven battle axes The deadliest Elven arrows The greatest human Shields These warriors headed north to fight the great evil When they arrived to the Evil's Stronghold they realised that there numbers were in the thousands to 4 great warriors Momments later in funneled thousands on thousands of Human. Orc. Elvens and Dwarf alike To assist in this great battle In the four warriors charged leading there new formed army to battle The evil sent a volley of arrows at the army; The arrows blocked the sun from the sky Then storms came in with amighty rumble THUNDER came crashing down It struck a few mem all of they died on the strike The four warriors entered the castle while there army fought outside They killed men mercilessly When they reached th- *The Pages are then torn leaving you to think what happened next* Cal'em The Human of the north Talelia the Archer of te Woods", ""),
        StaticBook("The lonely book", "HeelioBagoon", "There once was a book that was verry lonely.  He was lonely in and empty library. Ralm needs to add books.", ""),
        StaticBook("The lonely creeper", "Xyloph", "Once upon a time there were a lonely creeper It was all alone in the world because all the other creepers got blown up Well, some got slewn by mighty warrior And some just plainly fell into holes But this lonely creeper was no ordinary creeper He had a heart of gold and would never, ever hurt people! He wandered far and wide in search of other creepers But he found none Suddently he found a small village called oren It was just founded, not long ago It was more of an area than a village, the creeper realized and began to see the big picture If he met a human he would be forced to explode! The creeper got very sad and tears started flowing from his eyes He began to travel and found a small, dark cave on the edge of the village He lived there for a while, but at sometime a human child wandered in \"Hello\" said the child The creeper couldnt understand humand language and just replied \"SSSS\" help thought the creeper if he human, or humands as he said, approached him he would explode! and kill the human child The creeper ran away but the human child followed The child would not give up on befriending the creeper and a bond that would last a long time was formed The end! book was not a success cancel", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lonely Halls Of Haven", "monkeychez", "I roam the halls of Haven, every step i take is an echo reaching ever so far. I wander... Alone, hoping to find some greeting source of life. I hope to find another of my kind, perhaps a Sage, but nothing. All that is there, is me and my shadow. So here i roam, the lonely halls of Haven.... Forever, and ever.... I go back to my house, alone. And hear the sound of nothingness. It makes me ponder my feelings... Even if the Undead are the threat, i can still know for a fact... they are happy, and together.                                                        - Dolir", ""),
        StaticBook("the lonely life of Albert Sparxz", "Benboboy", "Albert began his life in a large kingdom to the south, he was the castle mage in the capital city. Magic users were very rare in that part of the world and the kingdom could not find a better wizard. The bad thing about this is he was a terrible wizard. He did a lot more harm than good. Eventually the king exiled the wizard after he realised he was no use, Albert then lived in a ruined tower for 23 years when one day a traveler told Albert of a grand place with many city's. He set of to this new place and went to seek wizard training. None of the mages would accept him, they would call him terrible names. He went to find a new home but had no money. A group of bandits attacked the poor soul on the road stealing what he had, and leaving his corpse on the side of the path to rot. This has been a story to inform you that not every dream comes true, most of the time you will be knocked to the ground over and over again, just like poor Albert was... \n-Father Eynon", ""),
