        StaticBook("The memorial", "GoldenGFX", "I thank you all for coming to honour the Sages.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Men of Winterfell", "deanofantastico", "\n One would think that because of the harsh and unforgiving life in one of the most remote town s in the kingdom of Oren that the folk that inhabited it would mirror the land that they live on ; cold, harsh and unmerciful. This couldn't be further from the truth. \n \n Due to the many cold and weary travelers who find themselves at the grand gates of Winterfell with no guards in sight it was decided that the construction for a Lodge for these travelers began. Within the first day of its opening a patron already spent the night and he was full of praise and thanks for having such a lodge. Many Lords would request payment to stay in a lodge of the same quality but Lord Nairog Stark of Winterfell allows all who wish to stay shelter for free. \n \n The kindness of these rugged northerners was also shown when an Fantasti, Winterfell 's scout found an Oren Archer who had been slain and his equiptment stolen. Seeing lightening splitting the sky he gave the Archer a bow over 40 arrows and a set of Iron armour form his own self without demanding anything in return. \n \n i hope this book shows the true character of the Men of Winterfell.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Message", "callum2357", "(( Hang on (( Hang on", ""),
        StaticBook("The message of Rogan", "Smithy_Boy", "I am Rogan, this is my task fer ye. If ye are reading this then ye are holdin' my book . My task fer ye is to read my message an' then pass this book te a friend. Now that you 'ave heard my task, hear me message. My message i ............   Hero's come in all sizes, in all races an' all places. if ye are a hero then ye should act like one an' show th' undead yer wrath in any way ye can! pass this message te anyone ye can, any race, any place. until it gets back te me. if ye see me then tell me ye had my book. an' don't forget about my message that's all i 'ave te say, th' rest is up te you. it contains a message of peace an' unity remeber that.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Methodius Way", "ctg33k", "help I have traveled farther North than many would approve of.  I am cold and lost. God help me.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mind Of A Hobbit. Volume I", "Crippledbaboon", "Hail there friend! My name is Bircalin and welcome to my mind! Today is Ahad, 15th of Snows Maiden, 1304. I am of 32 years. For standard men this is middle aged. However for us hobbits, this is the coming of age! I write this in the grand archive of RavenLodge. The people here are so kind and helpful, unlike in other lands. There is a druid who lives in Laurelin named Respiren. He gave me a home here in RavenLodge after one of the Holmes named Midnus had given me a small, cosy home in Laurelin. Respiren had learnt how i was seeking money in the land and told me of the empty archives here. I told him i would gladly fill these archives for payment. He could not promise me money but a better home, safer, in the district of RavenHold. And so, here i am, filling these grand passageways of bookshelves, filling them with my mind and knowledge all i can. However i am not alone in this... I have mustered together a gang. A \" Band of Brothers\" We call it. At this moment in time it is seven strong. There is Aedan, an elf who seeks nothing but to know himself better. Haelphon, a human who seeks redemption in the world of Oren. Romanen, a warrior who seeks nothing more than to live a decent life. He works as a guard in Oren presently. He seems happy there. Verigan, a man with no story to himself, sometimes he will just appear, with no word or sound. But simply follow me and the others through our travels. Then there is Bog, an orc, the muscle of the Brothers. Do not be mistaken however, he has the heart of a druid within. Kind to all living creatures in Aegis. But when enraged he can release mighty power. And then, a female elf.. i forget her name.. she is kind. Aedan takes kindly to her. I am not yet sure the meaning to his actions but i have a vague perception. That, is our band of brothers, and Volume I to my mind, The Mind Of A Hobbit.", ""),
