        StaticBook("The Mister and his Stories VOL 1", "JoeqMafia", "Young and handsome, the boy was. Walking down the Kings Road. He swept back his soft brown hair. He looked up at the bright, golden sun. He thought to himself, what an amazing day, he listened to the chickens cluck as he passed by the new Barn. He took a turn down a long wooden path. As he does every week. After walking down the path for two minutes he came up to the Mister's house. He called him Mister ever since he could speak, because the man would never tell his name. He sat in his creaky chair and smiled. \"Hello William!\" Mister said, \"your here early.\" he grinned. \n \"I wanted to get started early! So when I finish you can finish that story you have been telling me.\" William replied while grabbing the hoe and shears. Mister smiled, then said \n \"This one has a great ending. I can't wait to tell you.\" \n William laughed. \"That's what you say about each one.\" Mister just chuckled and then looked up at the trees. William started his job. He worked on Mister's farm and then Mister would give him some food and money. It was the best way to get money for his parents. His mum doesn't appreciate William being with Mister, so William tells his parents that he works at a factory in Oren. He had been telling that lie for 7 years so that he could hear the Mister's wonderful stories. Once William finished working on the farm. He took the wheat to the basket in the kitchen. He ran back outside on the porch where Mister sat. He pulled up the small green chair with the paint chipping off and sat uncomfortably. William looked up at Mister, shaking his knees with exictment. Mister began to continue his story of a man who was afraid of nothing. Who fought many foes saving princesses. His stories were always filled with passion, love, and action! He ended this story with a bang. He had the heroic man defeating an evil wizard. The man won, and saved the town. William sat in the tiny chair bouncing. When Mister said \".\" William sprouted up out of his chair and yelled \"That was amazing Mister!\" \n \"I knew you'd love the ending. Now you better get going before your parents ask were've you been.\" Mister said looking at his old golden clock. \"I will tell you my next story next week.\" \n \"Okay.\" William's smile faded, \"Bye Mister.\" \n \"Farewell William.\" Then William went home.  \n The End,", ""),
        StaticBook("The Modern History of The Undead", "itechify", "Twin brothers were born in the Great city of Al'Khazar with the names \"Phillip\" and \"Rodrick\". The two weren't raised with a wealthy family. Their mother owned a shop trying to make a living selling flowers to pay their fathers bar debt. Since they didn't want to work, and neither had much faith in the Temple, they turned to the streets to occupy their time, stealing from shops and noblemen. \nIt was a matter of time until their stealing hands were caught. A fat pig of a man noble, named Narvel owned a farm the boys visited often to steal from. Tired of these troublesome boys, he hired a private guard composed of bandits and highway men to watch his farm. The twins returned to Narvel's farm in hopes of stealing more of the fat noble's abundance of food; but were no match for the new guards. Narvel was planing to hang the two boys for their crimes of theft, but Rodrick, always quick to temper, wouldn't sit and be bullied into submission. He kicked the guard trying to put him in the noose and lunged at Narvel, stabbing at his throat with a small blade he hid in his boot. \nIn this time, Phillip manage to slip away, using his brothers distraction to flee knowing if he stayed, there would be nothing he could do to help his brother. Phillip snuck through the alleys of Al'Khazar, dove through the sewers, and escaped into the bay running north into the woods. Rodrick, however, was captured for not just stealing, but now killing a noble. Death alone would not be enough for his crimes, so he was sent to Winterfell where he was sentenced to finish out his life rotting in a tiny cell. \nIn the Northern woods, past the Snowy hills of Alstion and Winterfell, across the sea, and over the vast mountains that claim the north, Phillip was growing weak from hunger and enraged on his inability to find his way home, much less save himself or even his brother. The sun was setting again as it had for weeks since Phillip was last in Al'khazar. Unable to defend himself from the evil that lurks in the woods at night, Phillip took shelter in a cavern. As he rested his head on the smoothest stone he could find, Phillip began to feel a pulse emitting from the ground. Curious and desperate, he followed the pulsing deeper into the cave. As he felt his way through the dark tunnel, he came upon a smooth, stone frame that was hot to the touch. Just as he stood up in front of it, the inside of the frame burst with light, showing a purple vortex within. \nDrawn by the pulsing beat, Phillip stepped into the portal. Twisted, pulled and whipped around, he flew through the portal and out into the strange land we now know as the Nether. There, he found a shrine not far from the portal. Phillip carelessly stumbled to the shrine, feeling as though his soul was being ripped out of him in all directions. The moment he touched the shrine, an agonizing pain shot up his arm, through his body, legs, and into his head. A thunderous voice met him with so much pain and torment in every word. It spoke to him horrors no man should ever hear, piercing the heart that makes Phillip human. After much torment, the voice said to Phillip \"You can save your brother and the two of you shall rule those who made you suffer. Let this body go, your mortal soul will change in the power I bestow upon you. Serve me and you shall rule all.\" \nThe power given to him from the voice known as Iblees bound his soul to the Nether, keeping him tied to Iblees' power, but making him lose his physical grasp from Ageis. Phillip, grew to despise his name, finding comfort in the name Freyj as suggested to him by Iblees. With the great magic he has, he pulled a city from the Nether using the fire and souls around him, binding their will to forge what is now Drauchreich. Freyj now uses these souls bound to Drauchreich to fight for him in Iblees' name, moving to take Aegis, the land that Iblees was banished from. With that, Freyj, Overlord of the Undead Horde, stepped back through the portal and bringing the hell of the Nether back with him. \nRodrick was stuck in Winterfell Tower for what felt like eternity. Locked away and forgotten, his mind grew twisted and further removed from Aegis. One night in a terrible blizzard, Rodrick heard an echo of a voice coming from outside the prison. Again and again it would call to him, ripping at the back of his eyes to see through the dark. Outside from a hole he could peek through, fire exploded on the horizon. A wall of flames with a face bursting from embers. The guards came to Rodricks cell to find him racing around the room screaming madness. The guards stood at the cell mocking him until Rodrick lunged at the door, reaching through and grabbing one of their throats. Blood spilled everywhere as a bell rang sounding the alarm. The other guard lunged through stabbing the maddened Rodrick in the side, leaving him to bleed. Freyj had come with a horde of undead, ripping open the tower to free his brother. Before his brother could die, Freyj made sacrifice to few captured guards, bringing Rodrick, taking to the name Rott, back from the brink of death, but not entirely alive. In the Nether, Rott pledged to Iblees and made sacrifice to a nearby village in his name. Iblees found Rott to be a Prophet of the Undead, from Rotts ability to bring pain and suffering to those who would dare defy Iblees. With that, Rott summoned a city from the Nether to Aegis, to spread corruption and turn the world of Aegis into the Nether so Iblees can be one step closer to freedom.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Monastery of the Empyrean", "DolphinTuna", "Remember, no matter how your life has turned for the worst, you can always count on the Monastery fo help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "Maiavel", "\nThe Moot is a gathering of the entire circle, traditionally held at the Solstices and Equinoxes. By ancient custom, Moots are called four times a year at these set dates, once", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "urpenguin", "To any Druids that Reamain. I wish to call a formal moot to discuss what has happend in the past days. As i am the only Arch druid That reamins i need to appoint two more. and Discuss the future. The order has grown to an terribly small size barley any our left. I wish for this moot to be held as soon as possible.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mormont Family and its History", "JonnyC2011", "The Mormonts are a well known Northerner family that come from the Snowy wastes far in the North. They have always lived in the snowy wastes, spread around city to city. The bloodline of the Mormonts first comes into sight in the year 974, when Janok, my (Bergthor's) Great Great Grandfather owned a large Lumber Company. This lead unsuspectingly into a mass stream of wealth, as Janok sold his Lumber to the towns and cities who needed the Lumber for construction and expanding. This then led onto a massive reputation boost with many people both business wise and also with royalty and nobility. The Mormont family continued to prosper as the years went by. Janok and his wife Frieda had a son named Yarin, who was brought up to be part of the nobility of the land. It was custom, that when a family member passed on, that the eldest sibling would inherit most of the inherited wealth. And so it was that the Mormont family never found themselves short of wealth, as their dealing with towns and cities alike, from their Lumber Company carried on to provide much wealth.  \n This led up to the year 1091, when Yarin was becoming old. The towns and cities had no more need of the Mormont's Lumber Company, as cheaper alternatives had sprouted up by this time, they were cheap enough that Yarin could not compete with their prices. So, after many years of fortune, the Mormont Lumber Company had to be closed down indefinitely. This was not done without much sadness from the Mormonts as it had been their life, and much effort had been put into the company in order to make it work. \n However, all was not lost. Just when things seemed completely lost King Frammoth of the far Northern city of Namzarth paid Yarin and his wife Sofia a visit. He proposed that for all the Wood they had supplied to the city, and how much good they had done for everyone that he would take his two children Dravveth and Camille into Wardship. They would still be known as Mormonts but would live with him in his palace as if they were his own. After much thought Yarin agreed to this, as there was nothing much else that he could do for his two children. He had just enough for himself and Sofia to live on, and so promptly agreed. After some months of living in the palace Dravveth (who was now training as a Soldier) and Camille (who spent time learning etiquette) recieved word that both of their parents had recieved a disease and were extremely ill. Upon rushing back to their family home, they arrived to see their parents both upon their death bed. Oddly though, both Yarin and Sofia had a smile upon their faces as Yarin said \"We have done the best thing for you, make us proud...\" With that said, they both passed on together, as it seemed like they had waited for their siblings to arrive just to utter those words. \nAs the years moved on, and Dravveth and Camille grew  older they were given the titles of Lord and Lady as well as a settlement to look after each which netted them some wealth from taxes. In the year 1136, Dravveth was called to battle due to his heavy involvement with the guard, and to both Camille and all of the population, did not return. No-one knows what exactly happened to Dravveth, but he was presumed dead. A few years passed, and Camille gave her hand in marriage to a fellow noble Lord named Percey, who Camille had admired for many a year. Not much else is known about Percey's and Camille's marriage and life, but it was said that Percey adopted the Mormont name, in honour of the help the Mormonts had given to the city. They also had a son, named Harold (my father) who was to lead an \"interesting\" life. When Harold was old enough, he married a farmgirl from the outskirts of the city known as Marie. This was done in secret as marriage between the noble and lower class was strictly forbidden. However, it wasnt long before rumours went around that Marie was pregnant, and that Harold was the father of this child. So under the cover of darkness one night,  Marie ran away eager to get away from all of the people and the rumours. It was said that she fled to the distant city of Al'khazar, where she had her son. After proclaiming Marie had left him and calming things over with the people and the King, Harold managed to just hold onto his claim to nobility. One year later, Harold re-married to a fellow noble Lady named Lucinda, and had a son, Bergthor Mormont (me). Bergthor grew up in the embrace of his parents and became skilled with an Axe and as a Lumberjack. But as he grew older, he heard about the possibility that he had a half-brother. The older he got, the more eager he became to find his brother. His parents told him he was forbidden to look into this, but it was always on his mind. \n When Bergthor's parents passed away, it was a sad day indeed. They were missed by all of the people in the city, and more than ever by Bergthor. But it opened up an oppertunity for Bergthor to trace down his brother. He packed up and headed for the long treck to Al'khazar, where he used some of his remaining wealth tho buy a plot of land on the Beachfront and built a large Manorhouse there. It was the year 1316, when Bergthor was making his regular trip to the market to stock up on food for the winter months when he was stopped by  a smart looking nobleman. He stopped Bergthor and asked if he would care for a drink at the nearby Tavern. Bergthor clearly obliged and asked for the noble's name. \"Sconn\", said the man, \"Diplomat Sconn Mormont\". Bergthor was amazed by this as he had finally found his brother after all this time, and in such peculiar circumstances. He took Sconn to his Manor and asked about his parents. Sconn repeated the story of his mother, Marie and Harold. As to which Bergthor offered Sconn his own personal quarters in his Manor, to which Sconn gladly accepted. While in Al'khazar, Bergthor also managed to discover that he was a distant cousin of Robert Banstir, a noble of Al'khazar. This opened up a completely new side to the Mormont family tree. Not much at all is known to the Mormonts of the Banstir family, but Bergthor embraced his new found family relation. Bergthor still resides with his brother Sconn at his Manor, with Robert Banstir and his family living closeby as one big family.", ""),
        StaticBook("The murder of Apollen, by Karnin_Korfi (thatguy) and subsequent banditry.", "Respiren", "As told by Wayward_Druid_Respiren 'One of our fellow elves, Apollen was slain by a bandit at our gates .' This is how our story begins.   A fellow elf by the name of Apollen stumbled into my grotto, lamenting his recent death at the hands of one Karnin_Korfi (thatguy). Divining his true name we approached Prince Flefal, for advice. After some discussion our beloved prince placed a 2700 minas bounty on this bandits head in order that justice may be served. And justice, it seemed was served quickly. \n Apollen however was still without his precious map, so I ventured to find this bandit to talk.\n After searching many days I found him with 3 others near east whisper.... laying a foundation not just with orcs and bandits, but the very one that claimed his bounty. I approached them, and they faced me with much hostility, denying that they we're the culprits that killed my fellow elf Apollen. while the four watched with rapt attention. A fifth approached from behind via the lake. And drove his blade into the bandit, killing him, then making a quick escape. His fellows quickly turned on me, yelling 'DRUID' 'now you DIE'. At which point outnumbered, I fled. pursued and out within an inch of my life. It was only with the deterrant of bow, and healing broths that I managed to escape to east whispering isle, with a shadow of a heart. and with night falling, to my grotto to make this report. \n -Wayward Druid Respiren \n with gratitude to Elvador_yoleri, for accompanying me in my frail state. And the moral? Do not interact with bandits, and place a higher acceptance fee on bounties.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Myth of the Great War", "Respiren", "Almost two thousand years ago a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards -one good and one evil- that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until they were utterly triumphant, seeking to purge their rivals from the earth. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning final victory .\n In the process of their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devastation on the world forests blazed up, islands sank into the sea, entire races became extinct. Eventually, the the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict. Shocked by the destruction, the Goddess sent a vision to a single  human: the woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a druidic order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology. With the guidance of her goddess, the  Order grew in strength until finally it had the power to intervene in the wizard war. The force of young druids pooled  their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts. Once the former wizards now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the Order began to heal the world.  Since then, the druidic order  continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars of good  and evil no longer mar the precious earth. But, the Order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the  guilds of warring wizards- those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows. Each guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered. \n -As recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons.", ""),
        StaticBook("The myths of Aegis", "Javelberg", "Chapter one:The hidden sewer city. \nI went to Oren the otherday  and came to overhear two men talking about the sewers. I pretended not to listen but they knew i did so they changed the subject to the weather...aint that a classic? Anyways i walked around a corner just so could hear them and heard them saying something about a city under this city,in the sewers. An as i am i could not let this go by so i begun to ask about the sewers and all i heard where rumor s . After i had been asking around there was one man who didnt say much but what did i have to lose? I went forth to the man and asked about the city...follow me was all he said and suprised as i was i did nothing more than follow the man down the sewers. We walked,and walked,and walked some more. I must tell that finding the city is NOT an easy task just being able to find it is a price! Anyways when we got there i my eyes where met by an extraordinary sight . It looked just like a pirate city and it was a true experience to gotten the chanse to see it! There was also some shop,but most where fencers i think. They had this big ship who made the center of the city. And i looked for an entry but it seems to be none. After a while i found a button and when i pushed it a door in the wall opened up. As i went though the door shut behind me and i seems to be trapped! As i walked a few step i came to a room where the floor and walls was coverd in blood . My heart began to beat faster than normal and i thought i have to get out of here! I heard the locked door open and two men who where getting closer,and heard one of them saying that the button to get out is on the beneath them under the wooden plank. The men walked past me,im glad they had their rum i must say! And i manged to get to the button and the door flew open emitting a loud rocky noise,that ofcourse alerted the two men upstairs. So thereforth all i could do was to run and finding a spot to hide,but they where catching up so i had no other choise than to surrender. But the blessings of malin where upon me i tell you! I heard a sound like when the winds blows past your ears and in less of a second the two pirates where laying on the floor and one of them did not move at all! I looked behind me and saw a man with a mask made of iron,green clothes and a bow. I asked who he was but i got no answer,all he said you shall not be down here elf! With no other choice,like i could say anything anyways i made my way to the surface. As i reached the surface i took a deep breath of air and went on with my day. By Scribe Duvain I suggest attending to this matter and we shall continue later", ""),
        StaticBook("The name of a book.", "susitsu", "Well, Ive been thinking, Ive met a lot of people since I began my journey to destruction and...I'm n ot sure that's what I want anymore. Someone I guess I could call a friend seems to try to help peopl e. I'm considering asking her if she can help me learn how to...enjoy life. These people Ive met, th ey don't want me to do rash things that will endanger my life, they seem to have fun around me. I wo uld like to have fun around them too... End Entry 1", ""),
        StaticBook("the nameless enlightining", "Megaman765", "after my glorious demise i have seen the glory behind pure anarchy before i was but a Grothonian who did not understand anything and was naive in how the worldI functions. now I have been tasked by the nameless to perserve all thing anarchy and without anarchy no one will strive and the world will remain still which is not right! thank you nnameless lord for opening my taped eyes and giving me purpose beyond purpose now I shall become the druid of the worlds source of greatness CHAOS ENSUES ANARCHY IS SUSTIDANCE MAY WE ALL EMBRACE DESTRUCTION! THERE SHALL NOT BE PEACE IN HIS UNKNOWN NAME!!!!!!!!!!!!! i have it now well good luck then sorry i can not help you unless no you wouldent have interest I hear nature screaming in terror and joy if you killed me you did nothing for iam a disimbodied soul in a suit of armor so more torment on yo u I have met an asended he im glad he fight for without conflict the land will burn one day peace is the true disturbance", ""),
        StaticBook("The Nature's Bounty Catalog", "Elite117", "This is a list of all the items that are sold at Nature's Bounty. Due to demand some items may not be available all the time. Prices are not listed as they tend to change over time for a number of reasons. Items sold are the following: \n Mushrooms (Red and Gray) \n Wooden Bowls \n Mushroom stew \n Wheat \n Bread \n Apples \n Pork (cooked and uncooked) \n Eggs \n Cake \n Sugar Cane \n Bones \n Leather \n Leather Armor \n Wool (Colors vary) \n Dyes \n Feathers \n Arrows \n Bows \n Wood Logs (Oak, Pine and Birch) \n Wooden Planks \n Saplings (Oak, Pine and Birch) \n String \n Cobwebs \n Leaves \n Seeds Cactus \n Paper \n Books \n Bookshelfs \n Bones", ""),
        StaticBook("The Necropolis", "nachotp", "The Necropolis is a big city, A city not like others, A city where humans can't live, neither elves or dwarves, A city where only the ones that had already died may enter, They say it sucks your soul, and once you are in the city, you are part of it, The thing is that the city cannot be reached by walking, In this case you need to go through a Portal, made of pure obsidian, a portal where you can hear screams coming out of it, a portal where only the braviest enter, and once you go through it, everything changes, you are in another world, in this world there are natives, The zombie pig-mans, they wield swords of an unkown material, hey aren't agressive but, once you attack one, they all will strike together, without mercy, without fear. \n But they are not the only ones that live there, there are also giants beast that when you aproah to them they will fire at you a fireball that will explode in touch, Leaving death behind although people have been able to deflect them, they are still a dangerous threat, these giant beast named \"Ghasts\" can be defined like a squid but bigger, and it also flies, the beasts protect the necropolis from intruders, leaving only the citizens, If you hurt one of them, They will scream so loud that any other ghast will hear, any other citizen will hear, Almost the entire dimension. \n Thi dimension doesn't have grass, neither water, The only thing you see is: Netherrack, Soulsand, Glowstone, Gravel, Mushrooms, and Lava, a lot of Lava. The Ilumination Produced from the Glowstone and Lava is the only light you will see, and you won't see much, your soul gets weaker every milisecond you are in there. \n One interest thing is that, the netherrack, covering most of the land can be putted on fire, and the fire will remain forever, prople want to bring netehrrack to make great fireplaces.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Nether", "baigoth", "the nether is a crarry place there is gass everywere iven in you pants pig zombies everywere even in your pants even thouh thay dont attack you unlest you atack them but stell aaaaar!!!! write", ""),
        StaticBook("The Neverending Night", "Pizzafreak5", "Lo and Behold the Never Ending Night. Quiver and Flee. From the Peril that it Brings. The Bane of all. The Horrors it Releases. Never, for so long has Aegis been Beaten. No Body can Move. No Body Dares to set foot in the Neverending Night. The terrors are many as grains of sand on a Beach. They fear no sun, no death by fire. For Darkness no longer gives way to Light, Death gives no thought to Life, and Night smothers the Day. For we live in Neverending Night.", ""),
        StaticBook("The New Elven Military", "om_bananas", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The New Ferox Legio", "TheImpulseHQ", "This Book is about the new Ferox Legio, if you dont like the Legio, Put the book Down, and prepare to die :Now, The Ferox Legio is a Paramilitary Guild that is to protect Aegis Unfortunately, right now we can only protect Laurelin and Krugmar becuase the leaders of the other countries wont give us Guildhouses :The Ranks: The Legio is controlled by the Legatus The Legatus chooses Primus's for his Guildhouses, they then choose Optios to help them, then they elect 3 Tribunes to help them also There are then Centurions, who are the Captains and Hastati, veteran soldiers, then Decanus's Normal soldiers Then the lowly Munifex, standard Recruit Guildhouses: We have guildhouses in Laurelin and Sanjezal they protect those lands and give free rooms to those who join the legio Why you should join: You should join becuase of the benefits like a Free room, Nice community, Warlike Passion Love of food and ale and discounts on different things Written by: Dominus Bein, Legatus of the Ferox Legio", ""),
        StaticBook("The New UAC History", "sparten4ever92", "The UAC, the greatest mititary power in Aegis. You may know the leaders. But do you know How it all began? It began long ago nearly 10 years before the Fall of King Perea. Nobody knew the name Sornof, or Martin Benedict, or Kootry, except there close friends. Then one day as if by fate Sornof met Martin. They met to settle a war between the races of Humans, Orcs, and Dwarves They met in a casino not far from Al'Kahazar. They then journey to Kal'Urguan to meet Belin who would be a key part in ending the war. Finally, they had to meet with one more war group. Petri's Mercenaries. This is where they met Aldo the Ambassador. He was a key part in the formation of the UAC however never fully joined. Then after long journeys and quests the war was over. They all went to Sanhar to celebrate. Sornof got there first and he met a young lad by the name of Kootry, he was followed by a band of dwarves who cattered to him. He proposed a grand army of Aegis to fight the Undead Hordes. Sornof took him to the Arena and San Jezal and held a grand council of the two groups. There Aldo, Bog (like Aldo never became UAC but key in the formation), Martin, Kootry, and Sornof, settled on an agreement. It would be to protect and preserve Aegis in everyway. From a small street theft to a grand attack by the Undead. Sornof named their group the United Aegis Coalition. From there they traveled to form a council. They first went to Laurlin and found High Prince Native. They met with him and he agreed to join the cause. then to Kal'Urguan to meet with Belin who would lend food and weapons to the few present. Then Oren, where they met with King Perea who would agree but never come to the council. This is the Old History of the UAC. Read more in new Volumes", ""),
        StaticBook("The New UAC History V.2", "sparten4ever92", "King Perea Later would die at the Hands of the Overlord. He could've been at a council that night in Haven but instead stayed in Oren deeming the Meeting unessacry. Soon after the Undead Killed King Perea there was a recruitment boom. They accuired men like Wang, Abeam, Thimble, Thrym. Maur, and Fast. Kootry then purchased a large plot of land in Kal'Urguan to build a new base. This base took a year to build and lasted only three. Martin, now ascended, deemed it unsafe after the betrayl of General Wango. During the time after Martin took command again . But not long after he died finding Sage Arcadius who is now the UAC representive in Haven. Which brings us to current history where the UAC continues to raid the Undead Keep in the North while building up strength in Haven. One day they hope to destroy the forces of the Undead for good..", ""),
        StaticBook("The New Wraths Clutch", "xNoTiiFy", "As durzio and I have recently interogated the Uruk, Chaos. He gave us some information on Wrath's clutch and the undead. I went for a scouting mission and a little farther past the whispering isle's, I found the new Wrath's Clutch. I found it necessary to write this book and give some co-ordinates to the fort. (x-597) (y-487). If you would like to find the fort, go to these co-ordinates, and you will notice a very large building. That would be it. It has many towers that are as high as the clouds. It's extremely hard to miss.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Newfag", "Boofdawgz", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Nical", "ScottyBleez", "Testing The Black Cross has attacked yet again. I'm considering running away but I must stay . Nothing has happened. But, Alanor is acting very suspicious. He had a wound in his hand and said something about a master. But I have also discoverd that he has a very weird religous monument in his house. I'm going to get to the bottom of this! hello okay Alanor did betray us. His so called Master was a Black Hand. I confronted Alanor and we started to fight. But I was Aided by a friendly man. He got away but me and the man were confronted by the Black Cross. I risked my life to save his. Me and Azzura have left. it has been quite a day]]", ""),
        StaticBook("the night", "sivert", "The night is comming. the creepers are killing The cows are ded. The unded is atacking. And the zoombies is powerful.", ""),
        StaticBook("The NightWalker Records", "Pravino", "Name: Eledyr\n Rank: NightWalker \n \n Name: Brandon \n Rank: NightWalker \n \n Name: Bofaim \n Rank: NightWalker \n \n Name: Vain \n Rank: DarkWalker : \n \n Name: Oshaim \n Rank: NightWalker I will make any Allegience book next", ""),
        StaticBook("The nords", "greener161", "This is the book which tells you everything about the nords. Ok we first start with the leader which are Bowrim and Samuel ranks are follow: 1. nord recruit 2. nord trainee footsman 3. nord footsman 4. nord warrior 5. nord huscarl 6. nord champion footsman-onlyone 7. cheif footsman only one 1. nord recruit 2. nord trainee huntsman 3. nord huntsman 4. nord veteran huntsman 5. nord champion hutsman only one 6. nord chief huntsman only one 1. nord slave 2. nord mage apprentice 3. mage 4. nord summoner only one 5. nord warlock 6. nord chief warlock", ""),
        StaticBook("The North", "Sode1", "I must travel north to find these beings the king is dead, looks like they did it for me ,I dont think i hate them anymore , im more curious though if i do see one i wont let it live , The new king he is nice he made banok a diplomat .Arkensald is no where to be seen neother is syn The only ones left are me and banok ,Aegis is not like it used to be now i must embark on this perilous journey its been a few months.. I was on my way to Central Aegis , with a group of halflings They cam e In a rain of arrows and hail of swords i protected the halflings ,i was stabbed many times but kept my body in the right position i shoved them in a crack on the road ,they then took me to theire realm it was dark and hor rible everything you touched burned you they took me to theire castle it was vast and intimidating then i saw him. i must not speak his name he burnt me he cut me he crushed me under burning rocks i managed to escape and fed myself on small mushrooms wich i made into shoes ,i stumbled out into ourworld again a faint blur of Sableroth's face and then i found my self in a room with burning insense and 2 druids chanting mystical rhymes i had a huge red line on my back it constantlystung", ""),
        StaticBook("The North", "lil_rhys", "My name is Rhys Llywellyn, son of Llywellyn and Helen, I am a true Northerner. I write this now to inform the reader of how the north once  was and how she has now fallen so low.                                                   She was beautiful, her cold winds lapped our legs and her snow made us joyful and enthralled and her beauty, wether it be her tall mountains or her frozen rivers, was more beautiful than anywhere else. But despite this what happened to her was not her fault.                          The undead had arrived. Those who followed the fallen one, Iblees,", ""),
        StaticBook("The Northern Expedition", "Lagomorphia", "Several decades past, before the undead menace reared its head, there were tales of evil practices in the far north. These were intolerable to the civilised kingdoms, and in a grand gesture the King of Oren sent his six finest knights and a force of over a hundred men there, officially to bring order to the people there, but their true purpose was to spread the King's influence to the unruly lands. At the head of the army was Sir Erverin, a distinguished knight famous for his unique greathelm and for driving the bandit cartel known as the Poisoned Daggers from Oren. \n Little was known of what they found there, as only one man ever returned, a traumatised soldier called Orvl.  Most thought he was driven mad by whatever they found there, as did nothing but gibber that everyone was dead. He also spoke of a threat that had emerged from a eerie purple portal, of evil infused lighting twisting soldiers into monsters, and of Sir Erverin, standing over the corpses of his five knightly companions, staring at the portal, and, sword raised, charging into the darkness. \n The man was assumed to be an insane wreck, so the King and his advisors assumed his tale was a fabrication formed of madness and decided that the people of the far north had simply slain Sir Erverin and his army. That assumption would prove costly. \n Recently a man, or a close approximation of one, returned to Aegis, wearing a greathelm almost identical to the one that Sir Erverin once wore. Instead of the buoyant, fun loving personality of Sir Erverin, the man is focused only on his task. Instead of Erverin's trusting nature, the man is paranoid. Instead of seeming human, the man is cold, he does not bleed, and two sinister red glows can be seen through the eyeslit of his helmet. The man, if he is even that, calls himself Evern. Could he be the famed knight of old, returned from the dead to fight the undead? Is he alive, or as undead as the wretched creatures he fights? Only one thing about him is certain: his burning hatred for the undead menace. \n A note is scrawled below. \"Evern was killed by Vikram Mournstone two years ago. Fatally wounded from Vikram's attack, he returned to the nether, leaving his helmet, and any remnants of his soul with Thaern, one of the Oren Guard. \"", ""),
        StaticBook("The northern rangers", "redbaron", "The norther rangers are protectors of the north. They live in the ruins of an old tower that was guarded by there ancestors. They were there when iblees attacked winterfel and alstion.  Ogland was there. I am Ogland and this is my story about the Northern Rangers and what they did. Living in the snow, its cold very cold... a constant white. i look over and see the orcs of the north, not very accepting of vistors are they. My partner Desrik is no where around, off in the citys i supposed. i decide to start my day by getting out of bed and frying up some  bacon with a glass of ale as i look into the frozen ocean. There is a storm brewing, Sentinel tower provides little protection against wind on the upper levels so i head down to the warmth of the basement to enjoy my meal. Then the storm hit, a powerful blow it seemed, i heared the ruins of the structure groan. The floor boards squeak and it starts to feel colder. Today is not a good day i thought to myself.  I prepared myself, putting my tunic on, strapped up my hood and headed out into the cold to find my way to snowy fields and find my friend zerragon to sell my wools i have been collecting. i made a titty sum on 250 minas and then head back to the ruins of sentinel tower. I was almost there, i could see the faint light of my fire through the blanket of snow. A blurr happened and i was knocked to the ground. I looked up to stare into the face of an undead, it smelled of dieing flesh. Its deep red eyes penetrating mine almost taking control of me, then in screamed i wild cry and tried to thrust its sword into my chest. i woke out of the trance at the perfect time and rolled away nearly being jabbed. The Undead being did another scream, raised its hand, and let a vicious looking fireball hurtle towards being.  My face went white with horror just barely ducking under if and i head the snap of a tree behind me, i jump forward almost falling on me and crushing me. I looked up and heard what sounded like a sick twisted laugh coming from him. I didnt waste time and i went straight to the attack, i pulled out my bow a fired an arrow right towards his neck, he lifted his sword and seemed to flick it away with a flip of his wrist. How could anything be this powerful i thought to myself. There was a flash of light and i heard a war scream and a orc burst out of the bush and hit the undead with all his power. It was a orc named brevias, a orc Shaman who was one of the orcs of the north. The undead seemed amused and grabbed the orc out of mid air and through his mighty power threw him back into a tree right beside me and the tree cracked and fell The orcs eyes rolled back before he came back to himself. \"Brevias are you okay\"! i yelled towards the orc. Brevias got up and snarled \"Men attack\"! the forest seemed the shake with the approach of the orcs, The undead seemed suprised and lighted his hand... Then was gone, disapeared out of thin air. I looked at brevias still in shock and said, \"the troubles over i guess\". He seemed to find that funny and looked at me and said in a serious voice \"No Human. The trouble is just beginning.  The undead are waging war\".", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oasis Crafters Guild Application", "Ansh98", "Thank you for applying for the Oasis Crafters Guild.  We hope you have a great time with us. \n In order to join the guild, you must answer these questions. To answer, you must  your answers in a book. Your answer book must be placed in the \"Applications\" chest. These questions are very easy so there is no need to stress.    However, we advise you to please remain honest! Make sure your answers are in complete sentences as well. \n \n 1. What are your strengths and how will you apply them? \n \n 2. Nobody is perfect.  What are your weaknesses? \n \n 3. Do you prefer building alone, or in a group? Why? \n \n 4. Why do you want to join this guild? \n \n 5. What do you think the purpose of this guild is? \n \n 6. Have you yet built anything in New Oasis or plan on doing so? What is it? \n \n 7. Who are the owners of this guild? ((Usernames are fine.  Just OOC)) \n \n 8. Why did you choose this guild in particular? \n \n 9. Do you prefer building statues and monuments, or buildings and houses? \n \n 10. On a scale of 1-10. how good of a builder would you consider yourself? \n \n That wasn't so hard!  Now go ahead and place your book into the \"Applications\" chest! ((Title your book \"-name- ((Username)) Application\". We hope start building with you soon!  Good luck to you and get building!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oasis Crafters Ranking Guide", "Ansh98", "In The Oasis Crafters, we consist of 8 proud categories. These catergories are: \n \n Defensive Building \n Home Building \n Castle Building \n \n Farming \n Landscaping \n Material Removing \n Interior Design \n \n Misc. \n \n In each category, there are ranks. These ranks determine how well you are in your category. Remember, you can only be involved in 1 category so choose wisely! Refer to the individual book in the archives to learn more about each category. Each rank are as follows: \n \n Apprentice \n Fledgling \n Respected \n Dean \n \n There are only 1 Dean per category! Each rank are based off of build points.  A single build point is earned in two ways. \n When you work on a group project, you get a build point per hours spent ((IRL)). The other way in earning a build point is if you complete an individually assigned project. The points required for each rank are as followed: \n \n Apprentice - 0 \n Fledgling - 15 \n Respected - 40 \n \n Deans are selected there own way. Refer to \"Dean Challenging\" in the archives. Again, be sure to refer to each individual book of each category to learn more! In order to join a category, notify Mr. Longfellow or Mr. Dunn. We hope for you to join a category that you feel comfortable with!  Build on!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oath Of the Black Hand", "simonbane", "By the Blood of your Mortal Vessel, do you promise to guide your members?   \n Will you strike down The Black Hand's Foes without Mercy or Hesitation? \n Do you Understand your place here? Will you obey your leaders without a    second thought? \n Then take your blade, cut your hand, and let your blood flow through the sapling of life \n Throw this into the flames before you! \n I welcome you, brother, to your new family, the Black Hand  Step up Sconn! Then take your blade    and draw your blood. \n Infuse this with the sapling, representing life. And toss this into the fire. \n Then I welcome you, to your new family, The Black Hand.", ""),
        StaticBook("The oath of the Bloodsworn", "wolfermane", "I solemnly swear to uphold the law of the Bloodsworn To fight for my brothers and sisters in battle To never betray my Comrades And to follow the orders of those above me I swear in blood to uphold these laws *cuts hand*", ""),
        StaticBook("The oath of the Bloodsworn", "RawK95", "I solemnly swear to uphold the law of the Bloodsworn To fight for my brother and sisters in battle To never betray my Comrades And to follow the orders of those above me i swear in blood to uphold these laws *cuts hand*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Odyssey", "OmtraSpectral", "Book one \n Athena Inspires the Prince \n Sing to me of the man, Muse, the man of twists and, and turns driven time and again off course, once he had plindered the hallowed hieghts of Tro", ""),
        StaticBook("The Odyssey book one Athena Inspires the Prince", "OmtraSpectral", "Sing to me of the man, Muse, the man of twists and turns driven time and again off course, once he had plundered the hallowed heights of Troy. Many cities of men he saw and learned their minds, many pains he suffered, heartsick on the open sea, fighting to save his life and bring his comrades home. But he could not save them from disaster, hard as he stove the the recklessness of their own ways destroyed them all, the blind fools, they they devoured the cattle of the sun and the Sungod wiped fom the sight of day their return. Launch out on his story, Muse, daughter of Zeus, start from where you will-sing to out time too. \n By now all the survivors, all who avoided headlong death were safe at home", ""),
        StaticBook("The Odyssey book one: Athena Inspires the Prince", "OmtraSpectral", "Sing to me of the man, Muse, the man of twists and turns driven time and again off course, oe", ""),
        StaticBook("The Official Shad'rin Recruitment", "CONORDUDE8", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Official Swift Elf Manual", "danyn2907", "\n     Index\n Chapter 1:  Daily Chores\n  Chapter 2: Ranks \n Chapter 3: Escorts\n Chapter 4: Battles\n \n Chapter 1: Daily Chores\n Every swift elf must do a number of things each day in order not to lose rank, position, or badge.  This chapter will explain what each elf must do. \n 1: Each day a Swift Elf must go to the crucible to train- the amount of time depends on the el lf. 2: Each Swift Elf must go out and gather materials at least once every two days. \n 3: A swift Elf must patrol an assigned road or visit an assigned nation once every four days. \nRanks\n", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_27(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The Ogra Way", "mrmongolion", "In the beggining there was A giant Orb Of enrgy Bouncing through the universe It blew up and Formed the galaxy of ours, it created our world. Pieace by Pieace it slowly constructed our w orld then as the it formed erosion and weathering caused from the astroids holding water or x type oxygen that only our species could breathe, it blew all over the world could beathe . soon after the great nool of the skys created all species starting with the orcs ,then soon after came the human,then the elves,and last the dwarves", ""),
        StaticBook("The Old Ferox Legio", "TheImpulseHQ", "text help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Old Gods", "Kealyn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Old Minion Order", "Da_Emperors", "The Old Minion Order was once a powerful state where people became slaves for the undead. The Undeads where nothing but Slaves of the Undead. Collecting Resources, Working on gathering Gold and constantly being hurt. I am the Captain of that old order, however not anymore. I have wrote this so you all understand about the Undead. I am the most trusted source on them as i have spend my life with them, a Captain and a slave. On to the true issue, the undead minion order. Once the strongest and once the weakest. The are observed and guided by the Overseers. Handpicked Leaders by Undead. The Overseers include Ar'kelos (Maybe Undead now and Lodrick. There is one more i don't remeber. I can promise you they have ties with the Undead Still, Ar'Kelos indeed. The Undead Leaders, LeftClick (Undead Commander) and Deathmetus look over us. As well as Bravais. The Undead are still looking into recreating the Order. There to many of them, The Minion Order. Then two captains where created. Captain Jayius(Myself) and as well as Juvens.  Please, If you wish to finish them off. Meet Me not Juvens. As Juvens has ties with him. I Jayius will write again.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Old S.A.", "charliescott123", ".Theagorn House under construction. .Cactus Trap Bridge. .Double Gate. .Captians Quarters. .The Harveey has a room.  .Colonal Woodgate Dorm. .Four watchTowers . .RedBains Room. .No S.A. Sign. .Seems like theve gone roge. .Nobody here. .Brotherhood of Umbra . .Wanted Board= Man Lumber yard= Destroyed .Farm for sale. .2000\$. .Many wooded tools. .Large farm= Greifed. .Place lookes deserted. Report Finished .Coordanats of new base. y.75.62 z.852 ok", ""),
        StaticBook("The Once Beautiful City", "DustyHat", "A long time ago in a beautiful city read the forums and lore section to read the whole story", ""),
        StaticBook("The Open Quiver, Prices", "OliTassell", "Arrows: \n70 per 32 \n 130 per 64 \n240 per 128 \n \n  \n  Bows:  \n20 Each \n \nLeather: \n6 Each", ""),
        StaticBook("The opposing force", "callum2357", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Orc Dictionary", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "-Written by: Varag'Gorkil -Rewritten by: Salamandra \n \n Ug : Hail/Hello \n Throm'Ka : Formal Greeting \n Yub : Yes \n Nub : No \n Gug'ye : Goodbye \n Lat : You \n Rulg : Thanks \n Blah : Talk \n Gruk : Understand \n Dabu : Yes/My pleasure \n Bubhosh : Big/Great \n Snaga : Slave \n Nubhosh : Bad/Small \n Buub : Pig \n Pushdug : Stinky \n Glob : Fool \n Klomp : Attack/Kill \n Flat : Dead \n Blarg : Home \n Brudda : Krugmar Orc \n Stowts : Dwarf \n Twiggie/Treehugger : Elf \n Squeals : Halflings \n Quickspawn/breedurs : Humans \n Skah : F*** (Curse word) \n Agh : And \n Buurz : Dark \n Mojo : Magic \n Krimp : Control/Snare/Trap \n Uzg : World \n Goi : City \n Lusk : Axe \n O'lig : Bow \n Ligz : Arrow \n Zult : Sword \n Stik : Staff \n Blah : Speak, speech, talk \n \n Counting \n \n Ash : 1 \n Dub : 2 \n Gakh : 3 \n Futh : 4 \n H : 5 \n H'ash : 6 \n H'dub : 7 \n H'Gakh : 8 \n H'Futh : 9 \n HH : 10 \n Dubty : 20 \n Gakhty : 30", ""),
        StaticBook("The Orc Report", "Corpean", "Ahad, 22nd of The Second Seed, 1330 Orcs near their territory, not near kings road today. Possiably more on the move, orginizing. Armed Guards near the Orc entrence, full iron gear diamond swords. Mercenarys are now guarding the Orc City. No armor visbale. Infultraded Orc Warlord house no guards in sight. Is to quiet in the capitol something is up. Found the warlords hunting chest. Directly north of the Orc Capitol city walls. Orc military personal just apeared in the city. Moving away", ""),
        StaticBook("The Orcish Dictionary", "Austinpowers999", "To who ever is reading this; do you have trouble understanding orc speech well this is a guide to he lp you; over the next few pages I will write most orcish words I know so you can use them when speak ing to orcs; I'm sure this would impress them Anyways to start off with basic words Ug - Hail ;; Ug - hail \n Throm'ka - Is a Formal Greeting\n erase all", ""),
        StaticBook("The Orcish language", "coconuta", "Hail: UG \n \n Dah skal latz be : Who are you? \n \n 'umie : human", ""),
        StaticBook("The Orcs", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Shamans are mediators between the living and the deceased. Requires lifelong dedication to become a Shaman, and only a few take up the position . Shamanism is the most basic level of interacting with spirits. They believe there to be different types of spirits; Major, Ancestors, and Lesser Spirits a Shaman's staff is enchanted with a spirit or ancestor. Each type of staff has a different spirit in it, either Lesser, Ancestor, or Major. Diamonds are not used, because they are used to contain souls, not spirits.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Order of Druids", "Respiren", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Order of the White Lotus", "Rathriel", "The Order of the White Lotus Members, \n Dwarves: Hiebe and GrimBeard \n Elves: Lafthi, Vacant \n Humans: Dalejin, Vacant Orcs: Brevias and Tre'Bok", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Carnival", "Lexperiments", "The Oren Carnival is a great spot for new travellers to the human nation. When it opened, there were many events and activities there. I shall explain them to you now.  \n \n The best activity, The Fight Pits, is where challengers fistfight each other until death or until someone submits. There is usually a very good prize for winning, usually in the thousands. If one died, he is ressurected by the monks and immediately sent back here. One usually teleports him or her. The first tim it was used, the Wizard took on challengers. Many died and were teleported back. \n \n There is the rollercoaster, Queen Dawn's Revenge. There is not much very important about it. When it was released, the rollercoaster was failed and goes backwards at some point. \n \n The last activity is The Shooting Range. Two archers go against each other, trying to hit a moving target. Each archer gets 0 shots. The winner gets a small prize for winning the game. \n \n    \n \n  There is also a fortune teller booth. Someone, most likely the Wizard, will tell your fortune for free there. It's a fun little activity with sometimes amusing results.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guard - [Guards Time-Zones]", "henriiquen", "1# High Constable - Felix [GMT] \n2# Guard Captain - Ashkae Jago [GMT] \n3# Guard Lieutenant - \n4# Guard Sergeant - Hayden [GMT] \n5# Guard Sergeant - Huron [?] \n6# Recruitment Officer - Handa [-3 GMT] \n7# Guard - Ceril [EST] \n8# Guard - Thaern [GMT] \n9# Guard Bowman - Kalno [-3 GMT] \n10# Guard Bowman - Johnny [-8 GMT] \n11# Guard - Killzar [?] \n12# Military Blacksmith - Darfin [?] \n13# Guard - Janos [?] \n14# Guard - Zebana [?] \n15# Guard - Lotharious [?] \n16# Guard - Obin [?] \n17# Guard Blacksmith - Darfin [?]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guard - Application Form", "henriiquen", "[MCname] : \n[Time-Zone] : \n[How much time you can be online per day] : \n[How long have you been playing on the server?] : \nName : \nYour Race : \nYour Age : \nYour Reasons to join the Oren Guard : \nYour Experience : \nHave you faced any evil before? What kind? : \nDo you know how to handle a weapon? [Sword/Axe Skill Level. Note: To become a full guard you must achieve at least 30 Sword Skill] : \nDescribe Yourself : \nDescribe what \"Being a Guard\" means to you : \nHow would you treat a citizen in need? : \n \n\"NOTE : All Guards starts as Recruits and only get their wage when promoted to Full Guard.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guard - Militia Application Form", "henriiquen", "[MCname] : \n[Time-Zone] : \nName : \nYour Reasons to join the Militia : \nYour Experience : \nDo you have a house or shop in Al'Khazar? : \nEver come up against an Undead? Ever killed one? : \nHow skilled are you fighting? [Sword/Axe Skill Level] : \nDescribe Yourself : \n \n\"NOTE : The members of the Militia will be geared with armor, weapons and food. But no wages.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guard - The Guard Weekly Budget", "henriiquen", "This book will go as follows : \nRank (How Many) - Weekly Wage (Each) [RL] \n \nOren Military Captain - 1500 Minas \nOren Guard Lieutenant (1) - 1000 Minas \nOren Guard Sergeant (2) - 750 Minas \nOren Guard Rec. Officer (1) - 750 Minas \nOren Guard Blacksmith (1) - 750 Minas \nOren Guard (7) - 500 Minas \n \nTotal Budget - 9000 Minas per Week [RL]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guard - The Official Guards List", "henriiquen", "1# Oren High Constable - Felix [RossssM] \n2# Oren Military Captain - Ashkae Jago [Jadles] \n3# Oren Guard Lieutenant - Hayden [hayden34666] \n4# Oren Guard Sergeant - Thaern [w1lll]  \n5# Oren Guard Sergeant - John [aTbagger] \n6# Oren Guard Rec. Officer - Handa [henriiquen]  \n7# Oren Guard - Ceril [Cerilean] \n8# Oren Guard -  \n\n9# Oren Guard Bowman - Kalno [guigiz] \n10# Oren Guard Bowman - Johnny [Jdsd] \n11# Oren Guard - Killzar [Killzar]  \n12# Oren Guard -    \n13# Oren Guard Blacksmith - Darfin [Improvsior] \n14# Oren Guard - Lotharious [sammeister97]  \n15# Oren Guard - Janos [benny508]  \n 16# Oren Guard - Zebana [clayman730] \n17# Oren Guard -  \n \n \n ---- Guard Recruits ----  \n \n1# Oren Guard Rec. - Atlas [L4dykiller]   \n2# Oren Guard Rec. - Sir Grimbeard [dirtyhary] \n3# Oren Guard Rec. - Sanirus [Harv0kz]  \n4# Oren Guard Rec. - Jack [Jackbjossi]   \n5# Oren Guard Rec. - Rerowin [SnazzyEnglishman]     \n6# Oren Guard Rec. - Zod [Jr4Life24]  \n7# Oren Guard Rec. - Discord [TheWoWMasta]   \n8# Oren Guard Rec. - Kalturanis [secret759] \n\n9# Oren Guard Rec. - Tamara [Luiginova] \n10# Oren Guard Rec. - Gortan [TheHarveey]  \n11# Oren Guard Rec. -  \n \n \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guards", "AlphaCentaurus", "In my various encounters with the Oren guards I have been arrested 16 times. Twice I have been very nearly executed. My crimes have ranged from entering through the docks, wearing dark robes, harassment, resisting arrest, assaulting guards, drunkeness, verbal abuse of guards, indecent exposure, general disrespect, disturbing the peace, traveling the rooftops, destroying property, causing unrest, attacking royaltly, trespassing, praising Iblees, and other assorted crimes. Most of this I have done in disguise, but when wearing my robes, most guards recognize me. \n I've come to several conclusions about the guards. They're a fairly selfish, petty bunch. They applied to their posts out of a need to rule others. I dislike most of them. They're sadistic and have caused me a good deal of trouble. Including quite a bit of minas, but I've avoided that in many cases by merely serving a term in their jail. \n They tend to be fairly incompetent in capturing prisoners. They simply don't know their way around the city. It's easy to elude them by dint of escaping to the rooftops or the sewers. It seems like there is no training process. I tend to regret it when I do meet one who can handle himself, because they travel in groups. It's hard to evade five armored guards even when you are highly competent. \n I'm not quite sure why I antogonize the guards so. I think I enjoy it because it's entertaining. I like hearing their shouts as I dash across the roof of Dawn's bakery. And I don't want to conform to their silly rules. I should not be arrested just because of my attire. Nor should I be arrested because of my wanting to explore the city. \n    You see, I spent much of my childhood here. I was a beggar. And when others were not generous enough to give, I took. In most cases I was never noticed. When I was noticed, I usually made it away before a guard showed up. But when I was unlucky enough to attempt to pickpocket a guard, or stumble while escaping, I would be captured. I was merely a nuisance - to them, I wasn't even worth jailing. I would be beaten or otherwise abused. \n I hope you can see how this turned me against them. \n Even now, I do not have the power to resist. But should I come into that power... I will exact my revenge on the guards. And then some.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Guards, Members and ranks", "coconuta", "High Constible: \n Felix Farnsworth \n \n Captains \n \n Ashkae Jago \n Eze'Kiel Taurus \n \n Sergeant's : \n Thaern \n John \n \n Guards: \n Ceril \n Zebana \n Johnny \n Kalturanis \n Aragon \n Zod \n Ellser \n \n Recruits: \n \n Edward \n Luke \n Aldron \n Gortan \n Mystogan \n Sorrok \n Ella \n Silent \n Kaneous \n Borgore", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Rangers - The Official Ranger's List", "henriiquen", "1# Oren High Constable - Felix [RossssM] \n 2# Oren Ranger Captain - Rio [coconuta] \n3# Oren Ranger Lt. -  \n4# Oren Ranger Sergeant - ? \n5# Oren Ranger - Aren [tyber1231]  \n \n - Ranger's Recruits - \n 1# Oren Ranger Rec. - Sollaren [cobrabird] \n2# Oren Ranger Rec. - Luke [andyboy124] \n3# Oren Ranger Rec. - Pikel [paragonwarrior] \n4# Oren Ranger Rec. - Cailexaner [lukeskyfoker] \n5# Oren Ranger Rec. - Ehil [blah_1123] \n6# Oren Ranger Rec. - Veigar [lilletron] \n7# Oren Ranger Rec. - Oscar [idiotcozzy] \n8# Oren Ranger Rec. - Theon [austinxmas11] \n9# Oren Ranger Rec. - Jay [?] \n10# Oren Ranger Rec. -> Arlen [guesswork12] \n11# Oren Ranger Rec. -> Solom [dnadan2] \n12# Oren Ranger Rec. -> Rumli [MrDexter]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Regular -First Issue!- 7/23/2011", "nitsuadeschenes", "This is the Oren Regular's first issue! This is the first and only newspaper in all of Aegis! It will feature columns, news, reviews, interviews, and more! \n \n WORLD EVENTS: \n \n -The Attack on Oren- \n \n The night draws upon the world of Aegis. What was a sunny and bright day turns to an ominous overcast. Rain coats the kingdom in an eery sheen while thunder cracks out in lashes of fury against the night sky. The city stirs in anticipation. Moans sound from the North, then... the General shouts for guards and militia alike to report to the barracks. \n At the barracks the King and General don their diamond armor and rally the troops. Ready for battle they approach the Northern wall where Captain Grimbeard meets them. \n They have few men but the expert commanding of General Giffords and Captain Grimbeard turn the small force into an unbreakable shield. The undead relentlessly pound against the Northern wall. \n After many hours victory seems near, many undead fall under the combined weight of the archers on the walls and the soldiers on the ground. \n But then something arrives... an earsplitting moan echoes in the helms of the soldiers. The ground heaves with the weight of something massive. The King yells \"GIANT ZOMBIE\". The General rallies his men together and with Grimbeard at the lead they charge the abomination. After along and hard battle they fell the beast. Some  wounded but the kingdom is safe. \n After the battle the General had this to say, \"For the King\". \n  \n \n ADVERTISEMENTS: \n \n Banok's Arms & Armor \n The prices at this amazing armor shop  the lowest in all of Alkhazar! The shop is always open, making for a convenient shopping experience. The owner, Banok, is a skilled blacksmith, making some of the finest steel in the world. \n This shop is located at the harbor in Oren, across from the Queen's Bakery and under the Frosty Dwarf's Tavern. \n Stop by and see what made this Arms shop so phenomenal! \n \n INTERVIEW: \n \n - The Seneschal - \n We were able to interview the Seneschal of Oren and ask him a few quick questions concerning the kingdom and its affairs. \n Q: Do the recent undead attacks pose a threat to the citizens of Oren, do they worry you? \n A: The undead have done little to Alkhazar. Oren is well defended and although Winterfell and Alstion were attacked most made it out alive. \n Q: The city is rapidly growing,  there plans to re-expand the city borders or develop sections of the city like you did with the docks? \n A: Yes, we  setting up new homes in the Trade District. We  also setting up a new district by the Temple. It will be an entertainment district housing homes, shops, and the Grand Arena \n Q: How  relations with the other nations? There  rumors of orcs attacking citizens of Aegis without reason. \n  \n A: Relations are generally good but some orc groups have declared war on Oren. These groups are small, unorganized, and pose no threat to Oren, however. \n  \n \n COLUMNS: \n Oren Regular Column \n Alright ladies and gents, I'm going to introduce you to the first copy of the Oren Regular Column. My name is Tim Drossen and I'll be the lead columnist for The Oren Regular. Any other columns not by me will be marked by the author's name at the end of the column. I'll be doing personal opinions, views, rants, and short fictional stories. If you have any comments about any story, feel free to stop by the shop and yell them at me! I'll be in my office ignoring your shouts. Enjoy! \n \n RANT: \n That ****ing Fisherman \n \"One of these days that fisherman will slip and I'll be waiting\" - Kendrick \n This rant is going to sound absurd, and guess what, it is. Fisherman Petra is the most annoying man in the kingdom of Oren! All he does is pace back and forth on the docks, eyeing people suspiciously, claiming everyone is doing something wrong. When we were building our establishment in the harbor he called me out numerous times! What am I doing you ask?? BUILDING MY OWN DAMN STORE THATS WHAT! His constant peering into other people's business rivals the curiousity of a newborn. Shameful. I have never seen the man fish. Not once. EVER. He claims to be a fisherman, constantly commenting on how good the  day is for fishing (No matter the weather mind you) yet I've seen him do nothing but pace that dock every day and night. I'd be shocked to learn that the man even sleeps! I say we cut him into tiny pieces and use him for bait! He'll be much more useful then... \n \n That concludes the first issue of the Oren Regular! We hope you liked what you saw, we know there were a few typos but we tried to keep it spotless. Please bear with us as far as deliveries go. Until mailboxes are implemented if we don't catch you online it will be very hard to deliver the paper to you.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Regular -Second Issue!- 7/24/2011", "nitsuadeschenes", "Welcome to the second issue of the Oren Regular In this issue we will feature an interview with Captain Grimbeard a retelling of the Siege of Whisper Isles an advertisement by Chase and some columns by Tim Drossen \n \n WORLD EVENT: \n \n Siege of Whisper Isles \n It was dawn many had believed their troubles over The falling night removed the dangers that came with it Today however was the exception \n The pounding of feet echoed on the King's Road as a small army rushed toward Whisper Isles Prince Perea himself in the lead The undead had once more covered the lands in darkness As the army approached they saw necromancers on the rooftops hurling fireballs and lightning strikes down \n The army charged into the fray The battle was fierce necromancers' magic flying through the  air slaying many soldiers More undead revealed themselves and joined the battle The Prince either wounded or concerned for his troops called for a retreat Many of the soldiers didn't hear or couldn't break off and stayed in the engagement Then a Templar by the name of Xero took lead of the surviving troops He yelled for guards to form defenses and protect homes \n After what seemed an eternity the battle suddenly died down The battle was won but at a very high cost The Templar had a few words to say after the battle \"Hmmm a very slim victory The undead are strong but we shall prevail\" \n \n ADVERTISEMENT \n \n East Oren Trading Co \n We offer the lowest prices at East Oren Trading Co We also offer apartments at affordable costs for those who need a home   We'll also match ANY price in Alkhazar If you see another store selling an item for less than  us then tell us and we'll check and match it \n This store is located in the Old Marketplace in Oren \n \n INTERVIEW \n \n Captain Grimbeard \n Q: How do you feel about the recent attack on Whisper Isles? It was a very slim victory \n A: Well Whispers Isles' Guards should have been more aware \n Q: The defense was led by a mixed group of troops and even so the battle was nearly lost \n A: Even so we can't afford to send patrols down to Whisper Isles every ten minutes to protect them. They need to build better defenses a wall and defensive structures. \n Q: If attacks on outer cities increase will you spread the guard out to the cities or withdraw them to the capital? \n A: Well that is a question for the General or King but I would withdraw them to the Capital and make heavy patrols around the city. \n Q: How is the military district coming along? \n A: It is coming along tremendously! Semund and the King have helped with construction and the new barracks provide a great place for troops. However we do need to increase security of the area. \n The Captain also wanted to mention something any civilian caught opening the gate will be fined 300 minas Prince's orders. \n \n COLUMN: \n I'm going to apologize in advance for this column. I've been a very busy man and I had planned to write two items for every Sunday edition. But I could not do that today. I have what is below you written. I also recorded the Siege of Whisper Isles report. \n \n Rant: A Cake and Sour Ale Party \n This was meant to be in the first issue but it was delayed so the story may seem dated. I went to the cake party at the Cloud Temple with our head editor Kendrick in hopes of cornering the Wandering Wizard into an interview. We couldn't find him so we sat back and enjoyed the party... for a moment. Then some fool arrived drunk beyond comprehension. He was a wanted man and his presence and shouting created unrest in the party. But it didn't stop there after the party had been riled up by the wanted man an undead cretin arrived. He began shouting about his lord and how the mortal races are doomed. Yada yada yada. That sets off some people in the crowd and it becomes a yelling match between supporters of the undead Iblees and more. I hate undead as much as the next person but it's a cake and ale party! Leave your troubles at the foot of the temple and shush about the squabbles of outside. Take a break from life and enjoy! This mainly goes toward the undead fool who started the whole thing! Learn to relax a little even if it's only for a few minutes. \n \n CONCLUSION \n OOC: I wanted to apologize for the delay on this copy and some of the syntax errors. I was not home yesterday to write the book ahead of time and my alarm did not go off so I didn't wake up early enough to finish this on time. We're trying to give you the best RP newspaper but understand we do have lives with problems that interfere with this. ALSO FOR SOME GOD AWFUL REASON EVERY PERIOD IN THE BOOK DISAPPEARED", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oren Regular -Third Issue!- 7/27/2011", "vsurestrike", "I wish I wasn't the one reporting this, sadly Kendrick is missing and Brian is ben ridden with wounds, so it falls to me to lay down a great tragedy before you. Our King lies slain at the hands of the Undead. How this befell us shall be written in the following paragraphs. There is no column today and only one article. Sorry, but there isn't much of a point of doing anything else. Friday's should see everything return to \"Normal\". Also if you don't know, today's paper is free of charge, to honor our fallen King. \n The Fall of a king \n The darkness of the night fell upon Al'Khazar, some noted that it has fallen ealier than usual, but not much was thought of it. Simple people went among their nightly rituals, window shopping on their way home, grabbing a bite to eat at the local tavern, everyday people carrying out everyday tasks. The routine lives if people that knew very little of war, their home's guarded by the mighty Oren Gaurd. This perfect life, the obliviousness to the outside world was about to be shatterd. The flash of lighting and the boom of thunder, calling cards of the undead, sounded to the north, many tossed this aside as nothing, then again and again it hammered down upon the Earth, the sound so intense that it did not allow normal conversations. Cries came from the Northern Gate, Whilst their message was long, only one word sank into the minds of the people that heard them,,, \"Undead.\" \nThe Northern gate was quickly pounced on and seized, the undead necromancers summoning hoards of there undead minions. The first of many giants then appeared in the area's square, it's lumbering footsteps shaking those who were not fully aware of the surrounding chaos out of their ignorance. A sea of undead creatures rode through the city from the north. The many attempts to stall or halt the advances were enveloped by the tidal wave of monsters. More giants joined the fray, their steps shaking the very roots of the city. Man, Dwarf and Elf lay slain in the streets, their bodies often surrounded by scores of mangled undead corpses that they had taken down with them. Now, we were not the only ones to suffer losses in this battle, the undead lost more than just front lune minins, a few necromancers were reported as having been slain, however of those reports we can never be sure since the undead take their dead with them. The necromancers had the nerve however, to use the great golden star a top the chrch as a place to summon their dark magics from. \n The defenders slowly becamed scattered and only small pockets held out. The keep became Al'Khazar's final stronghold. The Undead pushed their way up the steps and a pitched battle raged in front of the doors that led to the keep. Here is where we found our king, locking swords with one of the leaders of the Undead. The Wandering Wizard was also reported to have been near the battle, slaying an Overlord. In the chaos of battle, not everything was certain, but when the dust cleared, another Undead Overlord lay slain and our King lay dead. We had dealt a stinging blow to the Undead, at the cost of our King. His death was as least honorable, he died among the people of his city, fighting to the last. After the drive on the Keep was forced back, the Undead once again vanished into the night, leaving their minions to torment us. \n Cleaning up the city lasted many nights, the remaining Undead had to be purged from the streets. Missions into the sewers were not uncommon, the mindless zombies seeking shelter from the sun's glare. The surviving guard tried to keep order as those left alive remained to lick their wounds. A group of guards went to the North to explore what they believed to be the source of these vile undead, they returned refused to comment. The Seneschal took power after the king's death and took this opportunity to start remodeling the city. The Temple District, having received the most damage, is now under a complete overhaul and a new Keep will be constructed. It shows that Edmund plans to be very active whilst he rules.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Origin of th Shad'Rin", "Shadowninji", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Outcast's Lore", "extrasleepyalex", "He stared out over Laurelin, the place he once called home. Although he was not an elf, he was still accepted into their city. He loved the Elven capital, but knew he must leave. He was caught stealing from a food stall, desperate to feed his family. The judge banished him from the capital with a heavy heart. However, they were dark times. he was desperate to clear his name, for it was unknown to even him if he had stolen it . These were dark times, and racism was a high in Aegis. As a human, he did not see much of this but in the recent times,hatred of humans had become popular. At a time, the Gauntlet was used for c riminals, and he knew he was next for the death penalty if he did not oblige with the court.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Outpost", "coopmaster", "I am starting outpost all around ageis. I don't know how successful I'll be but this is the firs part of my plan to be powerful in this server. My first outpost is beyond Kal'Urgan.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Outpost", "nitsuadeschenes", "The harsh bite of winter is merciless on the skin, cold gnaws at the fingertips and winds burn the eyes. The lone traveler pushes aside the trees in search of something. He is in search of a home, and he finds it in the cold embrace of the North. \n He works his stone axe and frostbitten hands to the breaking point. He fells trees and drills through stone. He's ready. His materials are gathered and his location has been chosen . He begins his long day of work, constructing a home fit for the North, safe from the monsters and the snowy abyss. \n Two weeks later... his home is complete, his resources have expanded. But he is still alone. He goes to Oren in search of something to fill the horrid and terrifying feeling that drives men to insanity, solitude. \n In his travels he finds his object of desire. The Trisians, a guild for peace and for the protection of the innocents. \n He is no longer a lone traveler braving the harsh world of Aegis, he is a Trisian with a grand outpost and an army of allies. This is his world... This is Kendrick's world.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Outpost of the Undead", "123devmo321", "Next to Snowy Field, there lies a high tower, with three towers sourrounding it. Facing from Snow Fields, you will see a small camp area on the right, it contains the slaves for the Undead. The three towers on each side of the main base, contain no apparent use except for scouting the surrounding area. There's a high wall surrounding the main Tower, with a courtyatd around it. Inside the entry room of the tower, there are two levers, one will completely engulf the courtyard with fire and the other will only ignite a small area. There is a lift in the entry room, that will lead you to a small observation area on top of the tower . Each corner of the Entry room contains a double set of iron doors for exit and entry of the tower. There's a small stairway that leads down to an obsidian hallway, with \"half\" portals that haven't been ignited, laced through it. At the end of the hallway, there is another stairway, that leads down to the quarters. There are three hallways in each segment, all are laced with spare rooms. There is only one segment on each floor. On the bottom floor, there is a hallway with three rooms, all seemingly empty. \n.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Paladin Code", "Saviordude", "A Paladin is graceful, and will protect his allies with his life if need be. \n A Paladin has humility, and understands to be truely great one must remain humble. \n A Paladin is merciful, and will never willingly hurt a creature who is not evil. \n A Paladin is Peaceful, and will hold himself in a non-warlike manner \n A Paladin is prudent, and is aware of the strength of his allies, never placing them in a situation where they could be greatly harmed. \n A Paladin is pure, and holds himself to a strict standard: Do no evil, lest ye become it. \n A Paladin has temperance, and has self-restraint in all their actions. \n A Paladin is dilligent, examining his opponets and surroundings thoroughly. \n A Paladin is honest, and will never tell a grevious lie. \n A Paladin is honorable, and will hold himself to a high standard of combat. \n A Paladin is an angent of justice, and must uphold the law to it's fullest extent. \n A paladin is patient, and will never rush in without thinking. \n A Paladin has zeal, and will never turn down an honorable challenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pass of Ul'gra", "trotski24", "The pass of Ul'gra is an incredibly important turning point in dwarven history, as this pass was where Orcs and Dwarves first battled.  It had been a mere 137 years since the fathers of each race had fought Iblees but still in the short period all of the races except the Elves (whom remained secluded in their forests aand would do so for another 83 years) had expanded their borders to the limit and at the Pass of Ul'gra a party of Dwarves and orcs met", ""),
        StaticBook("The Past", "susitsu", "There in the darkness of my memories lies the events that formed who I am now. A dark beginning and a brighter end. It all started with being raised by only my father, a monster of a man, and a taker of lives. He raised me to be a genuis, a killer, and emotionless. I was to bring down society. All I ever witnessed in my lifetime was blood shed, on the surface, it was what I wanted, but deep down I knew that was wrong. He forced me to kill, to take someones life, it was an innocent elf who had wondered by the forest we lived in. At this point, he left, telling me to travel to Al'Khazar in four days, he was going to attempt to kill the king. I waited four days, covered in blood, my mind tearing in all directions, I didn't know what to think. At the end of the third day, I felt this sudden pleasure to the blood, it felt good, the thought of killing now appealed to me. I washed off the blood, and traveled to Al'Khazar to see someones public execution. It was my father, he had been captured on walking into the town and had been arrested for numerous c rimes. He didn't even make it to the king at all. I watched his head get chopped off and left, I felt freedom. but I knew, I would continue to kill, following his footsteps.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Path Of Shamanism", "Areontrade", "Sabet, 21st of The Amber Cold, 1338- My Lessons under the shaman named Draygo are going well. He has instructed me to speak to the spirit I see when I meditate, It appears to be a tree. A tree as wide as krugmar and as tall as the world cactus. Leaves as green as the warlord. Upon meditating I see the tree again and for the first time, approach it. I gather up my strength and speak to the spirit I see, in the form of a tree. \"Spirit, Who lat be?\" I asked, and the tree responded. \"I Am Athaki.\" \"Athaki.\" I repeat. Then ask a new question. \"What be lat, Athaki?\" Again the spirit responds to me. \"I am the element of wood, the first in an element cycle.\" \"For wood feeds fire, fire creates earth.\" \"Earth bears metal, metal collects water.\" \"Water nourishes wood, wood parts earth.\" \"Earth absorbs water, water quenches fire.\" \"Fire melts metal, and metal chops wood.\" The cycle of the elements of Aegis? I thought, Or are there more than the one we know? : Talking to this spirit, I had so many questions. But two came to my mind. So I asked the spirit. \"Why did YOU out of all spirits come to me?\" Like me other questions he answered me instantly as if he knew what I was thinking. \"I am one of your first spirits you will meet and get to know.\" \"It was by YOUR choice that It was me, by YOUR feelings and the spirits surrounding you.\" Did I dare ask the other question boring into my head? Yes. \"Who be da other spirit over der?\" And pointed towards the winged-Lizard. This time, Athaki didn't want to answer, but he did anyways. \"That is Kematian, the spirit of death in your eyes and ears that is who he is.\" I am ending this account for today, for I hear Craotor Calling a warparty. ~Zerak.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Path To Northold", "canuslunis", "Head to Al'Khazar Next exit via the North Gate Then follow the path marked to Winterfell At some point the road splits, follow the fork Labelled to New Alstion Follow that path past the first wooden bridge until you hit the second When you reach the second bridge turn left Travel cross-country until you reach a wide stone slab path Follow that path past the buildings until you reach Celistine When you reach Celistine walk round the left edge of the moat follow the moat-edge until it turns right again do not turn right though carry on straight forward away from Celistine Keep walking away from Celistine and you should see either the Keep or inn of Northold", ""),
        StaticBook("The Path We Took", "Herex", "We started off not bad finding our way pretty easy we did start to get lost at parts. We had set up somewhere to stay for awhile. The next morning we woke up and we needed to fask", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pearl", "Swgrclan", "Ciar. This parchment will explain why I turn... strange while I hold a Pearl. Long ago, when I was a mere child, a spirit by the name of \"Nax'Ram\" possessed my tribe leader. My tribe leader, now possessed by Nax'Ram, made a ban against Shamanism, and replaced it with Black magic. I did not heed this ban, and for that, my father was killed by Nax'Ram. It was an attempt to scare me from learning what I am destined to become. I have been walking for 28 years trying to find a master, only to be rejected. Hate, and anger built up inside me. Nax'Ram was attracted by my spiteful spirit. He has hidden himself in my soul. And he wishes to be set free, to use my body to reek havoc. The Ender Pearl... lets him out. That is not me. It is Nax'Ram. This may be sudden, but I must say it. Do not be warry of me. Keep the pearls hidden.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Perception of Evil", "Jallentime", "One of the hardest concepts I have ever tried to express to someone is that of empathy. The capacity to recognize and share feelings between sentient beings often goes unnoticed, working in the backgrounds of society, but silently controlling the entire system. The reader may ask, \"But what IS empathy? How have I never heard of it?\" and I always answer in the form of an example, \"It's like when you notice someone is sad and you feel like comforting them, or when someone is angry and you want to calm them.\"] More specifically it is brains perception of and reaction to emotion. Empathy explains why people do not run through the streets murdering people. It also explains why the societies of Aegis have developed the way that they have more or less. Of course this does not explain why Orcs tend to be capable warriors and Elves tend to be capable dancers. But I digress, the purpose of this book is to understand what \"Evil\" truly is. For the majority of Aegis it is common conception that Evil is a constant everlasting monstrosity that plauges the land. Others look to the churches and temples to distinguish between \"Good\" and \"Evil\" for them. But for every race in existence the manifestation and epiphany of evil is that of the Undead and Iblees. The Undead are a vast and capable army of warriors and warlocks from the dark realm known as the Nether. Their goal is none other than the complete and utter conquest of Aegis. The populace of Aegis will be killed off or enslaved for the remainder of their lives. To most people this constitutes as an immediate Evil title being placed upon the Undead. However if we take into example the similar circumstances of Oren's attempt at politically (and silently) assuming control of Kramoroe from Laurelin without any form of documentation, we can be sure that \"Evil\" is not solely restricted to the Undead. However the way that Oren went about doing things brought no bloodshed or death in general. Even when finally confronted by the townsfolk of Kramoroe the Oren representative abandoned his mission and left Kramoroe in peace. This is where the Undead's example differs entirely. The undead do not care about the ramifications of their actions and would happily see a complete genocide of the races of Aegis. My research on the Undead always comes up with one very distinct finding with every experiment. The undead have an extremely degraded and often nonexistent form (or lack of) Empathy. The brains of the Undead corpses I experiment on almost always have a somewhat decomposing brain. But only in the same areas that emotions and some forms of logic are located in. I have therefore concluded that, theoretically, an exremely powerful and precise form of healing magic may be able to reverse the affects of the Undead brain degredation. This is purely speculation however, and has not been tested at all. Although if this theory turned out to be correct it would open up a broad horizon of philosophical questions aimed at whether the Undead can potentially be cured. Which also opens up questions as to if such magic can even exist. But I digress, in the plainest words possible, the existence of \"Evil\" is purely up to how an individual views it. Whether as a constant tangible force, or an temporary intangible perspective. Unlike cruelty, which is entirely separate but related concept that is very real and understood. The Undead may not be \"Evil\" Per se but they are most certaintly Cruel, and a very real threat to Aegis. In conclusion I hope the reader now understands the Undead, \"Evil\", and Cruelty much better than before and promotes your own research and action against them. By Delaselva of Kramoroe.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Perspective of Evil", "Jallentime", "How is everyone today gentlemen? Well there goes my book Well there goes my book Well there goes my book *sigh", ""),
