        StaticBook("The Retard Book of Retards", "Benah", ". If you are reading this retard you are a retard. Retard Go and retard on the toilet retard You are a retard help Yourself retard Onece upon a time a retard named Retard was building a retard box-like house. Then his retard running hoers said ''The writer of this book is retard''. And then the retard named retard got his imaginary gun shot that retard hoers in his retards.((trollface.jpeg))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Return of the Archmage", "edronos", "Day 1 \n \n Hwaldar has found me again, speaking of troubles concerning the Guild. He mentioned the voidwalker, Whisperer. According to him, they are good friends, and Whisperer even proved useful as of late. Apparently, Hwaldar has been tricked out of his position, having to appoint Everard as Archmage in his place, things safe for Hwaldar. \n He desires to usurp the Arcane Mage. \n When I asked what he needed, he said one thing: You are my new apprentice. \n I met him in the Tower, confused but nonetheless intrigued. He claimed influence over Guild matters, despite his recent expulsion, and while the invitation to apprenticeship honor s me and magic is the stuff of dreams, I have no aspirations for magehood. If I did, I believe this invitation would only serve to disappoint. Regardless, I let the curious mage speak. \n He began by speaking to Golems and other such creatures touched or hitherto wrought by magics. Immediately, my mind shifted to Whisperer, the voidwalker, who has created quite the stir as of late. Hwaldar continued, professing on the magics of \"entity creation\", with which entire beings can be born of the mind. \n The conversation consistantly shifted to Whisperer from then on. Apparently, the voidwalker is one such \"mind-man\", possibly born insane and sent to the Void through use of unstable and young understood magic. Since then, Whisperer has returned, disoritented and furious. Then, Hwaldar touched on how to destroy one such entity. \n Earlier on in the conversation, Hwaldar spoke of \"bursts\" that occur when unstable  materials are used in entity creation. These bursts can affect the magician or the environment, but the results are always  undesirable. Something similar can be used to \"overload\" a mind-man, who does not fear physical force. Apparently, any repeated use of magic upon one such entity, the ethereal voidwalker, will  cause the creature to burst themselves, as they absorb all magics they come in contact with. \n It's curious that the mage would reveal to me exactly how to destroy one such as Whisperer , whom he claims to be a close friend. It remains to be seen what Hwaldar is trying to get at. He's made it quite clear that he has a scheme bubbling beneath his hood. How I fit into those plans, and what he intends for the Guild, I am not sure.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Return of the Archmage pt. 2", "edronos", "\nDay 3 \n I've learned a few things in the last two days. Firstly, Hwaldar wishes to spearheard a guild to rival the Mages'. It's doubtful he'll get far. By now, he's spouted foggy threats that will likely amount to smoke. Secondly, there is a spy within the Guild itself. \n Bell came to me today with a strange book that detailed a meeting I had with the Arcane Mage. It mentioned me by my full name, which is strange as I don't give out my surname to anyone... Also, the author claims that I spoke about Hwaldar, about how he's a sleeper agent for the Undead. However, in saying so, the author said too much. \n That night, in the Tower, I said nothing of Hwaldar, as far as I can recall. The topic of discussion was Whisperer, as I had written a small treatise on the voidwalker meant for the Arcane Mage to review. In fact, Hwaldar was barely touched upon until his return, some time after. Possibly, this ghostwriter believes Whisperer and Hwaldar to be one and the same. It's not entirely farfetched, as Hwaldar has admitted friendship with the voidwalker, and Whisperer has admitted ties with the Undead. Just as well, with the stir amongst the magi, the two names find conversation hand-in-hand. Regardless, Hwaldar has taken on an entirely different face, for now. Sleeper agent, this author says? I'll have to investigate. \n Moreover, if this book is valid, it means there is a foreign agent within the Guild, and he made the mistake of being too specific and left it behind. There were only two others, that I know of, in the Tower that night: Cataris and a certain \"Frozen Blade\". I have reasons to supsect both of them. I would also like to note that nobody writes unless they mean to be read. Could this be a ruse meant to serve as impetus of more internal strife? I don't know, exactly . \n Lastly, the book mentioned one last thing. It revealed that \"both guilds are watching Hwaldar closely.\" Bell believes this second guild is a reference to the Undead. Possibly. However, I cannot confirm as there is too little to go on. Hwaldar mentioned a rival guild he wanted to start. Maybe he's planted a spy to watch over his investments? Or, maybe the book was planted to further reinforce the notion of another guild? Too many questions have spawned as a result of this mysterious text. \n I will seek to answer these questions, but my name is beginning to reach too many people's ears already. This book Bell showed me hasn't helped.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Return Of The Banstirs", "drangob", "The extraordinary affair which sent me and my brother into the hellish world beneath us is quite a tale. Without halt, i shall tell it to you reader, as i can tell you are enthralled already! The little village which we crafted, Bywater it was. Came under attack from the undead and their raider allies! They attacked because Robert, my brother knew a bit of information that those undead bastards didnt want getting out. So they attacked us! My family and our guards were quite slaughtered! Robert, I and one of our guards named Majester were the only ones who were living after the attack happened. We escaped in the middle of the attack, but the undead knew Robert had the information. They tracked us down to kill Robert! They didnt want people to know The King of all people was working with the undead! Robert had a plan, it was to save the Mormonts and me. By taking getting himself killed! The attempt failed, i was with him when it happened. A horrific sight indeed. While Robert lay there, dying. The undead broke in. They captured us. took us away to their awful land. We escaped. But when we got back to Aegis it was not how it should have been, we were insane. Not knowing who we were. Robert, spoke to Grimbeard i know not of that conversation. But he regained his sanity, his identity. I at this point was still insane, out in aegis, doing i dont know what! Anyway robert found me, told me who i was.. and i remembered. We came back to our homes.. Remet the mormonts and returned to normal life. Robert now a knight.. We are back as we should be.. Only loosing our old Village and gaining some scars from the Undead as they tortured us then healed us, repeating the process.. again and again. I have a tip for you, Reader. Stay away from the undead. They do a lot of harm. The king is gone, and the affair is truely over. As we are glad of it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Right Decision", "loion", "My name is Ramirez. I am meaningless in this world. Though i have some influence, it has'nt been enough to turn the tides of the battle  so i have done something wrong. I have sided with the undead and the followers   and other unusual people. Though here i do things of evil, at least i have an great influence. I am not meaningless. \n How it happend i sided with the undead? Well my friend Fyrste, which once were a dwarf, came to Kal'Alras, undead. I killed him. Now he speaks to me, of destruction betrayal, and doom.  He said i was going to turn traitor. Too late. I already am one. I have done numerous jobs for my boss. Assassinations, scouting, material hunting. I am going to tell my friends here, why i did all of this. One reason. I know how to survive. I do not like what i am doing. At all. But i see the future, and the future is Iblees. So i decided to stay alive. Unlike every fool in Kal'Alras. What i will turn into, is unknown. Just an traitor, Undead, or something third. But i know, I will never be the same Ramirez ever again. Farewell friends. The travels with you before this corruption were fun. But now it's more  serious \n I will miss you all, deep in my heart only however. Farewell... \n -Ramirez \n P.S. Algoda. I want you to show this to everyone who knew me.", ""),
