        StaticBook("The Spirit icos", "Toastersaurus", "The water spirit is a calm flowing spirit. That likes to move slowly around. It dislikes storms, They make it angry and when this happens it is dagerous for people to be near it. It is strong it large amounts and is weak when all alone. Overall the spirit likes to be relaxed and doesn't mind if people flowing with it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit of the Aengul - A Ship's History", "_Earendil_", "In The First Seed of a year not far past the beginning of the 14th century, the world of Aegis behel d del The Spirit of the Aengul - A Ship's History the grand abode of the Ascended race. \n However it was not long before the great Sages of the Haven realized that the journey to their lands was a long and sometimes treacherous one, especially for those not young or well equipped.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spring of Kulthrim", "mercury199", "Kulthrim was a just elf, he had studied and become a druid, and through meditation his conection with nature deepened and grew. He went through the land and where he steped flowers would sprout . One day he happened upon a small pond, it was filled with fish but none very big, all the fise h appeared to he wraught with sorrow. confused he asked the fish, why art thou so sad ? They replied, we live in a stagnant pool with no fresh food or places to go, and our pool is fad ding, those who live in this wood must take from it to survive and so we shall die. Kulthrim hea rd their plea and responded. He broke a whole in the bottom of the pond into a cavern. But still the fish were not satisfied, they said we will fall through as will the water, we need a source of water to replenish the pond. Hearing this Kulthrim looked around, he spotted a small hill with stone peaking out at the top. drawing forth all his power he, drew forth water from the rock and let it flood the pond. The fish were saved and he, was on his way .", ""),
