        StaticBook("The Stone of Salden", "sparten4ever92", "./\"\\ **^)) #@((* -+)( S[{}] \"/\\ \" !~#= --------------------------- Tolta, 17 of Snows Maiden, 1101 The new Father has found my recipes. It seems he wishes to take it from me! But Alass! Nobody will steal my Stone! Kamees, 12 of The Second Seed 1102 They have found me and the scriptures all is lost. I have scribbled the recipe at the top of the book in hieroglyphs. Only the best will know. Here I will die.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Stories of a Brewing Halfling", "u000893", "*this book contains all the past events that have happened to logan*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Stories of Sanme.", "xXsAnMeXx", "Sanme was a troubled boy living outside of Oren, He was an Orphan he learnt to read and write by him self. Training: He learnt to use a bow and arrow at around the age of 13, and since then has been practising on various other people/mobs.   He is currently looking for a army / guild or even a protective roll within a city. He would come to great lengths to get a job. Day 1: I am woodcutting to get some payment, and which i am selling to some shops. There was a strange man in robes, that appeared to be following me through the woods. Strange Kid... Day 2: Again collecting wood also some food to survive. Day 3: I was out in the woods again, and it seems that the Strange robed kid was there.  I didnt think he was Spying on me at all, though the sense of him being there did creep me out a bit. Day 4: Seems to be a kid jumping off roofs in the city, I do wish he doesnt break his bones. Day 5: Went out to the woods for even longer, it seems that the Strange Robed man was still there looking at me, with his red blazing eyes that looked so creepy at nighttime.   Day 6: Ive met Various new people on my trip, of finding wood. I think i made 2 new friends. I am currently sitting in the town Inn, and thus getting infomation about the 'World of aegis 'World of Aegis' and its very facinating. Lets see what i can get out of them. It seems i have arrived at the Northern part of Aegis, Ive met new people on my way here. Ive seen dedicated people, that protects the World of Aegis and the Civilisations. I Quite like these guys. Yes... I quite like it here.", ""),
        StaticBook("the story and life of collgrin the orc", "collgrin", "hello readers, I collgrin shall take you deep into the le of me as collgrin . Lets start from the very beggining and hopefully you will continue to read and understand where i have come from ever since I was born me and my family have been tormented because of what my parents did . i never knew till i met a orc shaman when i was about 8 and he showed me what was in my past venture they tossed out my brother and left him to die after learning this information he had traveled back to his home where his parents outcasted him forced to live on his own he went and looked for shelter realizing it was the same bridge my brother was tossed off of i put a sign up saying R.I.P never will i forget that day . \nThat morning i awoke to the presence of human outlaws. they kidnapped me and put in a cage on wheels to be transported to a place where slaves were sold as soon as i realized this i broke the gate and used my bare hands to slice through outlaws i eventually escaped with nothing but my strength and fear of humans ,of course i now know they were no more than outlaws and they dont speak for all humans, !  once I traveled a half a passday i came upon a resting home in some forgotten town where orcs have showed me what it is like to have power and allies they were just owners of tribes but to me that was just a dream i never dreamed  so i soon find out later that my parents were both nomads so im guessing my brother is as well as for me ,well im a nomad too as proud of thats as i am,i sometimes wish i can use magic like that shaman that helped me too me he is a lifesaver a trusting orc brother,one that will not go the easy way out or take a road of evil thats just who i want to be \nso thats my past and to this day at age 23 and im still living it Free and in wild land i have yet to settle in any city or find any job other than hunting.this is enough for food and rest but not enough to pursue any career if u want to hear more about me and my travels please read my other books ---too get the books message me and u shall get them", ""),
        StaticBook("The Story o' Gotrek", "DwarfGuy45187", "Gotrek was like any other Dwarf, mined and smithed by learning it from their fathers. Now, this was very early in the dwarven years as most dwarves used stone pickaxes. News came from the mines of a new stronger ore...Iron they called it. Now, the dwarves had no way of smelting this ore, but after many ideas Gotrek came out with the idea of a furnace where it heated the ores so hot that it turned liquid, and then pours this liquid into a mold. From this mold was a square shape and made the new \"ignots\" they were called stackable. Now, Gotrek amazed the Dwarves again, by using the same heating idea to mold the ignot flat and then pounded out the sides to make the first, very crude, sword. Gotrek and a few others perfected this ability and named it Blacksmithing.... from all the black smoke they breathed when working. With these new ideas out, many new and wonderous tools were made to advance the dwarven empire. Weapons for the troops, and armor stronger than Leather, to protect them. After this Gotrek was named Paragon for his great ideas. He lived out his days working in the Great Forge which still stands today. He grew very old and died, but not without showing a new way to smelt an even stronger ore... Diamond.....", ""),
        StaticBook("The Story of a Druid", "Caesar135", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The story of a girl", "radioactivkitten", "When I was born, my mother and father immediatly found a perfect spouse for me. Of course, It was only for the social class aspect. My mother and father were not there much, for they were very famous. So, I was raised by my nanny. My nanny was like my mother, I loved her so much. We used to explore the nature together. Yet, On my 17th birthday, She died. Leaving me alone, to be married to a man I did not love. \n I remember when She told me all the fairytales about true love, and I dreamed about love. I pictured my love as an amazing man that was beautiful and kind, like no other. Of course I knew that i could not marry the other man then, if I wanted true love. So on the night before the wedding I ran away. \n I got to Laurelin, where I met a man named Deltaro. He offered me housing and help. I accepted, and we became great friends. One day he asked me if he could adopt me as his daughter. I accepted quickly. A few days after arriving i met a man named Lafthi. He was a prince. Everything about him was so.. perfect... I wanted to be his so bad. yet when the true side was exposed of him, I relized it was all a lie. The person who truly cared was a Orc I had met after being saved from a incident. His name was Thral'Mar and we became best friends. I began to have feelings for him.. we both ended up confessing our love for each other, and moving into a house togehter. I realized, that no man is perfect, and that I was in love. \n The End", ""),
