        StaticBook("the tales of the sands", "Egg_Noodlez", "Once, there were two great heroes, Honeydew and Xephos . The were spawned in to minecraftia in alpha, the earlist known verson.  they built a hous on the beach but after a night they would never forget they left. They moved into the yogcave and started to build when a dark stranger showed up, Israphel. they chased after the stranger and stumbled across the small village of Terrorvale. they found a starcase under a grave and desended to israphel's castle. they fought Israphel but he escaped through a hell gate into the nether. title", ""),
        StaticBook("the tales of verrenn PT. 1", "verrenn", "DAY 1 \n We have just had a snow storm last night it was nothing severe just a couple broken windows. DAY 2 \n nothing happend today but... there are more and more undead. day 12 \n just left the town i live in came to laren for a bit nearly died by the undead day 16 \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Taming of the Wolf", "Respiren", "Homo homini lupus est\n -Finding the Pack-\n\n Seek them out on the plains and amongst the forests at dusk and dawn. Stride to and from their realm shedding the blood of animals. Look for them amongst the savaged mutton. You will find them roaming, in packs up to 8. Draw their gaze with a bone, or some tasty pork . \n -Caring for the Pack- \n The quickest way to a wolves heart is through it's stomach. \n -Wolf-Whispering- \n Listen to your wolf, he will ask you when he is hungry, and his tail will rise in good health and appreciation. Listen for their contented bark, listen for their requests in their tilted glance and plaintive cry. \n - A wolf is a man's best friend. -  \nyour pack will protect you always, attacking those who would do you harm, and hunting that which you would strike.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tasty Wolf Tavern Menu", "starkiller2010", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tavern Times", "459pm", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tavern: A Recollection of Funny Ale Stories", "drplat", "Hello all, this is Brewer Petyr. As we all have found out, some of life's funniest moments are accompanied by alcohol. As a well-known  brewer, tavern owner, and merchant, I have had my fair share of these. I hope that you enjoy. Chapter 1 - Tom All of those who frequent AlKhazar know of Drunken Tom. Most do not know of him before he was an alcoholic, however... I cannot say I knew him before he was an alcoholic either. Even the first time he came to the Cat and the Fiddle, he was inebriated! There are many memories of Tom, but my favorite would be the time he brought a woman. I do not know whether the woman was there out of love or out of pay, but I would guess the se cond. Well, like most nights, Tom had a bit too much ale. He started talking about the woman's sister, who he'd apparently bedded. The woman took her pitcher and smashed it in his face! only the Wizard knows how much prayer the monks needed to fix him up! And the worst part? She never compensated me for the glass! Chapter 2 - The Book-Owner I will not mention the name of this bloke, for he might be embarrassed. however, he is very inolved with books. He frequents the tavern often, and I know him well. He'd always been a bit prone to over-drinking, but one night, he went far. His speech was incomprehensible! He could hardly stand! I seated him down for a while, and he ended up passing out! THankfully no guards were there to arrest him for drinking past the legal limit. Chapter 3 - The Ghost Did you know that spirits drink? I didn'! I did know I enjoy drinking spirits,... Well one night, a ghost, right before my eyes, materializes and asks for two ales! It was nasty watching the ale drip through his transparent body. Yet, if one pays, who am I to refuse? I believe he stole the cup as well.. I will haunt him until I receive that. Chapter 4 - The Dward and the Guard Dwarves are drinkers. We all know that. However, something about the military turns a man into a drinker as well. The inevitable result is a drinking contest between a Dwarf and an Oren Guard. I remember not who initiated the conteset, but I damn well remember the end! It had been about twelve glasses of AppleAle each, my most potent brew. Both were on the verge of passing out, but both determined. At that point, I was handing away the beer, for it was so entertaining. As they were drinking the thirteenth, a most surprising occurence occured. An orc shaman walks in and order fifteen AppleAles! He drank all of them within five minutes. After watching him, both the dwarf and the guard passed out! Fifteen AppleAles should incapacitate the normal man. The moral: Don't challenge the shamans! Chapter 5 - The Wizard of Aegis walks in and orders........ nay, best I don't tell this story ! I hope you found this delightfully entertaining. I enjoyed writing it, and look forward to more stories in the future! Copyrighted by Brewer Petyr.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Templars", "people884", "hi hi The Templars of Aerial are guarding the temple. Me Arion Orion i am  a rookie Templar and i made my help", ""),
        StaticBook("The Templars", "drumstick607", "Hello my name is Saurcria Obadiah, I am writing in a time of death and despair. I fear that this book will contain my last words, they are nearing our keep quickly. I am the leader of a well known group named The Obadiah Clan or better known as the Templars My four brothers and I are the leaders, I am the master of all though. They are what i dubbed Nobles leader of the paths of members, I help them with that aswell. I believe my templars will end soon, many have died. I write for a later Descendent of mine to succeed where I did not. If this book were to fall into the wrong hands, well I cannot even think of the evil that would happ en This book is magical, but when found my descendents can use it for good to stop evil. They have just reached our gate use the papers I hide within to help! The room you find this in is the room i died in, I hid it of course though, GOOD BYE!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Templars", "RustyJusty123", "They're very few Templar's in Ageis. Most of them have died off defending their homes and or cities. Only a few remain in the North, fighting off the Undead. If you ever see a Templar ,know that they are always there to help you. You may not see them around in one loctation all the time, since most Templar's move constinetly. Templar's are a master of Sword and and Speed. This allows them to beable to cut their enemys and be able to avoid the uncoming attack. Templars know the land well, they can help you get to place you need to get to. Most Templars keep to themselves these days, but if you run into one its worth trying to get directions. If you ever were to try to find a Templar, always check the roads, thats where they usually are, going on another journey across Ageis.", ""),
