        StaticBook("The Theory of Magical Engineering", "SapphireShard", "Firstly, you will need a suitable conduit for the Magical Imbue. Any piece of equipment should suffice, although wood lacks the endurance for a imbue. I suggest using Iron - rough, yet strong and dependable. (Much like dwarves, harhar!) Then, you will need to create the Magical Imbuement to be used on the empty shell (Catalyst). This is the tricky part! You will need to lay magical runes onto the Catalyst, runes that- summarise what the object's use will be. For Instance, a crossbow created to pierce metal should be imbued with runes of Breaking, Unbinding, Smashing ectetera. Hopefully, this will help you create magically imbued item of your own! If you want to know more, you should consult my other guides on Artificing. Thanks for Reading! PS. This book has been imbued with runes of self-destruction. Ha Ha, Gotcha!", ""),
        StaticBook("The thief caught", "tomsim9611", "i was tending to the farm when i heard noise from Charons house. I went to investigate to find an elf looking through his possessions . I interrorgated him and he admitted to stealing from aradrome and libertas . i then went with him to his house. Looked through his chests and didnt find anything. I told him to stay away from libertas and aradrome. To live at that house till further notice and that we would get in touch when we had decieded his fate. we will all need to meet about this so we can decide what we shall do next. Leave suggested times of this meeting on the message board. ; Theifs name: Dandard_Liticus (NinNinja) ; Signed William Jones (tomsim9611)", ""),
