        StaticBook("The Undead", "Sode1", "So cunning they be sneaking around through the night , no justice exept for the occasional slit throat amongst the ranks Laurelin is not as safe as it used to be , I hunt them tis a risky buisness was'nt assigned by the crown either i chose to do this , its my duty..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead Are Comeing", "baigoth", "Today at Crater Lake Village i had a dream in my sleep about the time the undead attacked the the KofT town and seeing them distrouing the town then i wock up as a had a bad dream. I got up and looked around Crater Lake Village and being happy wat Crater Lake Village has become a lovly village nely a town as a sore the inn that was geting built and the farm and the short nice looking tower on the top of the hill. After that i was worred that Crater Lake will turn into a pial of ash that then Crater Lake will never come back.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead City", "GoldenGFX", "There I was.. in front of these Mossy Ruins.. There was two others there, an elf, and an orc. \n The Orc was lost in though, the Elf acting strangely. He was offering me a house to stay, over and over.. I was declining this offer, as I knew something lie under these Ruins. \n Suddenly, the orc.. spoke. He told us of them.. the undead, being in his head. He was being tourtured, and we couldn't help. I ask the Elf to leave, as he was not helping the situation, and he refused. \n The Orc was driven mad, and he stabbed himself. I was angry at the Elf, I blamed him, and I felt bad in the end. But I tried to leave it, and he halted me. I stopped, when suddenly, and undead appeared out no where behind the elf. We ran at him, and in a very raspy voice.. he said, \"I will be back...\" \n He used his soulstone, and dissapeared. Soon, just as he said, he returned, and came out of a wall, that opened by the press of a button. I yelled at the undead, \"Open that wall again!\" He took out his staff, and tried to kill me. \n I survived, and he did not. I managed to claim his staff as a prize. I camped out there, talking with the elf. I asked him, if he wanted to help, he should stand in the ruins, in front of the opening wall. \n A moon later, the undead returned. He opened the wall, and I dashed by him. Shot down a ladder on the right, down a hall on the left.. when I saw it. A portal to the Nether, and their homeland. \n I stepped inside.. and my bones chilled. I appeared, and infront of me was a spiral staircase, with portals down it. I went down the staircase, to the glass bottom, which had lava below it. Suddenly, I cringed with pain, as it was painfull to keep the Undead out of my head, and letting them abduct me. I entered one of the portals, and I appeared back in Aegis, on their floating city. On a platform that was there, I called upon the Gods, to pin me, my soul, to that location, right outside of the portal into the nether. They listened, and now I can get back there, whenever. \n Eventually, I found a pool of water I could jump into off of the city. I climbed in, and followed the clouds South. Eventually, I found myself back in Oren.    I went to my house in Stoneleaf, and stored the staff of the Undead, and my armour, as I feared that I would lose it because of what the Nether did to my health. \n After storing all my things, I activated my soulstone, and appeared back on the floating city. I went into the portal, and began to collect information. I want down a bridge, and to the left was something called \"The Crypt\" In \"The Crypt\" were tombs, and I thought they must be those of Undead.  I got away from there, and went into their library.   The library was empty, as far as I could see, so I continued on. I ended up in their Nexus next.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead City", "SirPwnzalot700", "The Undead city is located at 4052, 83, 75", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead Invasion Of Oren", "monkeychez", "On a busy afternoon in Oren... Something evil emerged.... I was buying an apartment at the time, when a thunderstorm began. Nobody was very concerned, as a thunderstorm is a natural occurance... But when the ligtning was more coordinated, and more constant, we knew what was happening. The thunder rumbled the town as the Undead, in snowyfield at the time, were getting closer. Men and woman hid in their shops and homes, the king and queen in a bakery... A man offered me a staff, to help with my magic. Not too long after, the outskirts of the city were coated with Undead. I swept in, setting the ground ablaze.... Parts of the ground reflected the evil we were facing... Giants were stomping about, the chatter of skeleton archers firing... the moans of the damned, but they were no match for those who fought. The men and woman hacking away at the Undead scum were doing a wonderful job. Our hopes were high when Sage Okonkwo arrived. He was in the towers and trees setting ablaze the other enemies like me. After a while of fighting... My staff's power was no more, and broke in two. I unsheathed my trusty diamond sword, and began to slay at the beasts. We cleared the edge of the city, and began to push to the castle... The streets were swarmed, fires ablazed from every building. I climbed atop the walls and headed towards the castle ... When i arrived, the Undead were on top of the castle And remembering seeing the king with his wife, i stormed the castle... When i got inside through a large hole, there were roughly ten others They were dispatching of the zombies inside the castle. I went to to take a peek above. Proceeding to climb the flame scorched and horribly battered ladder, there were many Undead on top... I saw High Prince Navive, and The Elven princess i believe. Anyhow, when i got atop the castle, i charged the closest Undead. A horrible mistake on my side.... Anyhow, the Undeads prevailed to an extent.... The king was killed, but the whereabouts of his wife are still unknown. The Wandering Wizard was able to return the Undead back to the hell in which they came from... The badly injured survivors of the battle helped dispatch of the rest of the zombies in the city, and snuffed fires. Is Aegis safe? For now... But what is to come? Prophets fortell Kal'Urguan is next To be invaded, but that may be rumors, or is it? THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead Raid.", "Crippledbaboon", "I am standing here, back in the courtyard of Al'Khazar, whilst being shoved to and fro. This is most peculiar, all these people. Rallied together, for an attack. An attack on the undead! Today we strike back at the scum that riddle Aegis! i dont have long before i die. This is terrible, men are dying all around me, the sky is", ""),
        StaticBook("The undead seem to have a camp between the orc city and whisper isles, in a ruin", "Pauldell1", "Yes Yes, I am ready", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead tryed to destroy Guardians", "tyking919", "They attack when no one was there. They caught a tower on fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead War", "awesomerer", "day one: the undead menace began their assault on the city of Winterfell\n the city was lost in a matter of minutes. we had no idea what to do. \njust after we lost the city of winterfell  they attacked at  Alstion. with the combined power of some of the vanguard, royal guard, and many other  citizens  able to hold back the enemy until . they retreated \nday two the undead attacked at Snowy Fields and were held back again with the help of the vangu ard. they came back later that night and attacked again but  ready. . we had archers mounted on the walls and plenty of men on the ground.  the undead didnt stand a chance. in minutes we were through the attack and were chasing the necro mancer back into the woods. \nlater that night the group of brave soldiers and citizens who  defeated the undead in Snowy fields headed off towards an orc camp where the undead were spotted . unfortunately many warriors were lost on the way to camp. the camp was saved though. \nday three: the necromancers went to oren. attacking the city at its heart. the necromancers wer e running on top of buildings and were dodging all attacks we could make. finally they vanished.  but the attack was still going on. suddenly a few warriors spotted the fiend on the observatory. they all immediately set out for the huge tower hoping to slay the monster before he could get to  the queen. we surrounded the necromancer at the observatory and after a few attempts at  killing us warriors on the ground the fiend vanished ending the attack on oren .", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead, Iblees and Spiritual Suppression", "Jerry_Man", "The undead beleive what they are told to beleive. Contrary to my own desire that they live with a more enlightened perspective on the world, the worshippers of Iblees are glorified puppets. \nThey foolishly beleive that Iblees' power is equal to God and they suffer no consideration that this period of liberated darkness shall draw to its end and God will banish them all to an eternity of suffering. \nBeseeching them for knowledge I found none. They were blinded by the little power they were given and ever fearful that Iblees would be discontent with their contribution but only so much as Iblees commands them. They have lost all personal desire to learn and connect with others. They've become like a circus dog doing tricks for its master. \nThey beleive nothing spiritually exists but that which Iblees informs tham. I was foolish to expect that such inextinguishable hatred was in any way related to God. \nIblees rebelled and wasthus expelled from God's presence, leaving behind all happiness, freedom and love. The undead follow a twisted and villanous creature who has been trapped in his torment so long that he only finds joy in others' torment. \nIblees hates us mortals because God loves us unconditionally, and even if we were to fail, as he did, we would still receive his love. Iblees is motivated by his pure hatred towards God and, consequently, the people of Aegis. The attacks against us serve no further purpose than to bring Iblees a glimpse of his forbidden happiness. He will never stop these attacks for as long as we suffer because of them. \nWe are God's pride, he would never leave us to be consumed by this shadow. That is why we will win this war. That is why we will triumph over the shadow.  Because we must.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead, What we Know", "Rathriel", "Because Bell was able to turn an undead recruit, we have gained the following information on the undead. First, there are around 8-9 full undead with 10 currently being recruited into the undead. Some of there 10 have already been transformed and are thus, full undead. Bell has had some success converting these followers of Iblees back to the light and thus, there are only 9 recruits now. Some of the recruits include: Kevin, Wrath, Guraim, Balion, Sloth, and Lodrick. It seems that the Orc Shaman Brevias has also turned to the undead. Also, the undead have started to construction of a new keep between the Kingdom of Alaras and Kal'Uruguan. It differs from its sister in the north in the fact that it is built of cobble.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Undead-Serving Zombie", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "A zombie is a hostile humanoid, with green skin and clothes. Zombie spawn in dark areas without much light, and move towards a person if they come near. A zombie, along with skeletons, will be set on fire if sunlight touches them. \n Zombies wander around, moaning when nobody is near, but snarl when attacking. They attack a target on sight, and pay no attention to cliffs or other obstacles in their paths, therefore they do not think about anything but their target. Zombies do not try to avoid being hit, they continue to pursue a person as if it were an instinct. \n Zombies are believed to be souls of the dead, resurrected by the Undead. They have no control of their actions, and do not think. They merely serve the Undead in killing citizens and warriors of Aegis. \n -Salamandra", ""),
        StaticBook("The United Aegis Coalition Ruling Council", "CountJuno88", "The names and chain of command for the UAC Ruling Council shall be listed as follows: \n 1. UAC_Governor_Martin  MC: CountJuno88 \n 2. UAC_Supreme_General_Kootry  MC: HaVoC_aMz \n 3. UAC_Chief_Wango  MC: Yes_Will_Let_U \n 4. UAC_Builder_Thimble  MC: transphat \n5. UAC_Smithy_Enadael_Falaos  MC: SuperZac  \n6. UAC_Intelligence_Latsi MS: GoldenGFX  \n These are my most trusted advisors. I have spoken with Thimble and Kootry. I shall inform the others ((IRL)) tomorrow. \n         Sincerely yours in all things, \n Martin Benedict", ""),
        StaticBook("The universe", "Slayer15855", "There once was a man, this man lived on a hill. \n On this hill there was a home, in this home there is a cat. \n In this cat there was a worm, in the worm there was a cell. \n In this cell there is a universe...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Unknowing Fisherman", "CorprlSkyler", "\n This is a guide for the unknowing fisherman. Fishing is a very \"try hard\" task. You must be patient, and know how to reconise a fish when on the line. \n A fishing boat can allways help you, when fishing. Fishing boats help you get out in the open, where theres bigger fish. Fishing boats also help you get to other great fishing holes. \n In conclusion, fishing is a very illegant skill. Good fishing to you, and I hope to have tought you something. \n Thank you for reading this book!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Untold Story of the Aegian Assassins", "starkiller2010", "The Aegian Assassins are a group of men fighting for the freedom of Aegis. They have been hired by many leaders to \"clean\" the streets of Aegis and to destroy the incoming attacks of the Undead and other evil creatures. Nobody knows much about them but we believe that they are descendants of the gods, for they have special abilities which let them see people's mind and intentions. It is how the could differentiate liars from traitors. They walk around Aegis in search of people who wish to be free, in order to recruit them and to bring peace onto all of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Untold Story of the Assassins", "starkiller2010", "A very long time ago there were a group of people who stood on their own. They did not follow any rules from any nation but yet all they did was to bring peace amongst all aegians. They freed everybody from the terrible bandits and from all kinds of enemies such as the Undead or other threateners of any nation. People believe that they are descendants of eagle gods for they are brave. strong and know exactly where and when to be. We do not know if they still exist today, but Aegis would not have been the same without them.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Vanguard", "Sykora87", "\"To protect those in need and punish those who bring harm to the innocent, keep a watchful eye on our home of kamoroe and give our life befor the death of one of its citizens. These are the words of The Vanguard. \n Ranks of The Vanguard \n Soldier Ranks page \n -Enlisted Man- Swords/Axes[0-8], Little/no battle Exp. *wears Leather armor* \n -Private- Swords/Axes[8-12] Some Battle Exp. *Wears Leather* \n -Corporal- Swords/Axes[12-25] Battle Exp. *wears iron* \n -Sergent- Swords/Axes[25-30] Battle exp. *wears Iron* \n -Lieutenant- Swords/Axes[30-35] Alot of Battle Exp. *wears Diamond/Iron* \n -Captain- Swords/Axes[35-??] Alot of Battle Exp. *wears Diamond/Iron* \n Archer Ranks Work Just like Soilder Ranks Just Replace the Swords/Axes Skill with Bow Skills and add different names \n -enlisted man Archer- \n -Recruit Archer- \n -Archer- \n -Marksmen Archer- \n -Master Archer- \n *********** \n Rules Dont Steal or kill. (unless they are Bandits) Share resources.  Be respectful to all races. ************** \n No One Hunts Alone", ""),
        StaticBook("the venture of aegis", "CONORDUDE8", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Verge", "123trevmo321", "A strange voice swept across Aegis. We all knew something big was about to unfold. And so it did. Hundreds of people, all races joined together to investigate this strange portal. Screaming, darkness, no one knew where to go. The same voice that spoke of this even said to claim your land while you can... now we are slpit up in groups of our race, or group, or family.. The Wandering Wizard found The Verge. Some were exited, some were fearful, some didnt make it. The new land was empty for a few days. Only a handful of people were there. But soon the land will be overcrowded and the people dont like pushing and shoving. And so The Portal never went unused. People dividing the land, making homes, shops, and a new life. (Narrated by Ice Druid Jameson, and author of The Verge) Look for my next book, The Verge part II", ""),
        StaticBook("The Verge", "AcerBuddy", "Dear Reader. It is Kamees, 26th of the Second Seed, Year 1331 I am Haelphon, Lord of Malinor Prince Mylas, Princess Lirinya, a man named Nero and I have landed upon a very small, but lovely island. We have claimed it as our own, and for now, we are going to begin delving into its lovely ambience. Stay fair, - Haelphon  OOC: keep heading up, and wehn you reach the lake, continue staight Hail! Today is Joma, 27th of the Second Seed, Year 1331 Today I have build a home for my friends and I People seem to enjoy this new colony! I am about to mine, the resources are plentiful! Tata for now!  ~Haelphon Hail reader, it is time I updated you on our events! \n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Verge", "DanielJamieson97", "Note: I've heard about some place called the Verge. A lot of people have been going there lately, and from what they say, it isn't very safe. Evil Beings wander the surface freely, and barely a village has been established yet. I've decided to head there, and document the state of affairs in the Verge. \n I access the Verge via a mysterious white portal, just down the stone road from Cloud Temple. The portal looks different from most, as it has no defining magical aura to it, it's just a white shape with purple gel in the corners, and ice around the walkway. It's whiteness appears to be snow, however, one could mistake it for a sheep's wool. \n Upon entrance to the Verge, I was immediatly put into a dark, lifeless room with evil smoke rising from the floor. It seem's very evil, and only occasionaly do people run past, either through the darkened room, or towards the portal. When I followed the path, I went through a couple of small tunnels, which led into a massive room. It appeared to be made of stone brick, but some of it as mossy. It was clear to the naked eye, that the main route I had to take take is over the stone brick pathway, and not into the wild stone. The area was dimly lit by some form of red torch, I believe it's known commonly as a \"Redstone Torch\", some form of device that can provide power to contraptions. The path led to a bridge, with holes missing in it, filled with cobwebs. It was very dangerous to cross, and the dangers of falling in are very high. My best bet was to run along the edges of it, there's less holes there! At the end of the bridge is two, odd white spirals. They look like they shoudln't be there, I ignored them, and followed the road into the tower. It was a wide tower with a large staircase spiraling up it. Following the spiral staircase leads to the lush, green land of the Verge. Directly in front of the exit was a mushroom tower-like home. It was quite interesting to look it, but it doesn't stand out much, I ignored it, incase some crazed old man owns it. \n The stories that people bring back from the Verge are clearly over-exagerated. It's peaceful, pretty, and green. There aren't any evil beasts to be seen, but still, there's something not quite right about it. Something's strange. I can just feel somethings not there, the air feels odd. I don't know what, but something make's the place feel evil. I wander over to the Mushroom Tower Building, and notice a small leafy hut beside it. It appears to me, that the druids are already in the Verge. Nothing seems strange about the building, which is odd, considering what the druids are like! I gave up looking towards that direction, and turn back towards the exit of the dungeon. I never noticed when I came out that the tower seems odd. I've never seen a building like it before, it's somehow, special. It has beautiful arches, and carvings. As I wandered towards it, I fell into a hole. The hole led to some form of barracks, with beds and a furnace. Luckily, there's a ladder, and I managed to clamber out! Night began to fall again, and I could see some form of light source on the horizon. I decided it would be best to run towards it, I presumed it must've been safe. It turned out to be The Temple of Mother Aegis, which had been recently restored by the Druidic Order (according to a sign on the door). \n I wandered inside and found it had a lot of pews, and a small lectern at the front. I lay down on a pew, and slept for the night. A load noise woke me up in what appeared to be the early hours of the morning. Some woman had ran past the outside of the building screeching, but before I could run after her, she was gone. I wandered through the night, and found a den of spiders. I was unarmed, and had no choice but to run. The spiders were too fast though, and managed to bite me a good few times, before I reached safety. Now, I began to realise the stories I have heard are true. Upon running around, I discovered some small, secluded settlements, all appeared to be abandoned though. Whether their inhabitants were away, or dead, I do not know. I met some chapping you elf, whom's name I do not know. Upon asking what he thought of the verge he replied: \"I believe though dangerous and infested with vile monsters, it makes a nice vacation spot. And if I were to go back in time, I would take my wife here on our honeymoon!\" After the last comment, he grinned and ran off into the forests. There appeared to be literally thousands of spiders roaming the land, although, the majority were passive, and didn't try and fight me. I ran down the road, following the elf, and found myself on a wooden bridge. In the distance I coiuld see high walls, and tall towers. Night began to fall, so I was forced to charge down the route, heedless of any others near me. In front of me were a large group of skeletons, and behind me spiders. I planted myself in the ground until morning, praying to the gods that no creature would spot me! \n Morning took ages to come, and when it did come, nothing was better. Still everything appeared dangerous, even though the skeletons burned. I began to starve, and had nowhere to head for food. I sprinted towards a large city like structure, and ran inside. Luckily, there was a dwarf inside, who gave me food, and sent me on my way. He explained that it isn't safe to be in the Verge without proper arms and equipment. I followed the mans advice, and pulled out my mystical soul-stone, and concentrated on casting the spell. Moments later, I was in the bustling city of Al'Khazar. \n An accurate summary of the Verge, would most likely be; It's a violent, un-safe, evil land, upon which no un-trained or un-armed man should walk. The creature's are evil, and many of the people crazy. Do not go there unless you have food for at least a few months, and weapons to support yourself.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Verge", "jibtherandom", "Day 1 I have just started this diary I just got my house extended,Probably goingtomove to Aegis toge Going to Aegis to Get Some Meat,The only food avaible here is Melons,Apples and Bread along with fis h Hope I will get back soon.Curse these Spiders I am setting off to Krug Mar then to EVWEN LANDS Yes my writing is scruffy I didnt get to write much But It is night And sleep draws near,Had to get my mine closed by julian So i hope I can go mining soon So I must be to sleep now Dear reader,.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Verge II", "123trevmo321", "People are are settled now.. They have villages and homes and a new life here. Meanwhile I, Jameson am residing at The Druids new grove. This is my second home. More dedicants finishing trials and becoming Druids, its a marvelous thing to see. Its a shame how some beautiful things can turn ugly so suddenly. A couple of days ago, there was one day where Ghasts tore this land apart. Then the day after, powerful, more stonger monsters would attack the innocent. After those few days of horror the people rebuilt and acted like nothing had happend. Guess thats how its always going to be.. I dont even know why i am writing in this book, why im talking to you.. I guess we will have to wait and see what happens next wont we? Final entry: Always...Ice Druid Jameson", ""),
        StaticBook("The Victim", "Undeelad", "Finally, I can roam Aegis...with evil in my veins. It was time to murder.", ""),
