        StaticBook("The Wardens: A History", "501warhead", "Writen by Kalen Forseth, the last true pathfinder. \n\"May the way always be clear\" \nIn this book I wish to shed light upon the Wardens, and their intended formation. \nThe first most basic fact you must understand though...  \nIs that the Wardens were originially named The Pathfinders, and This is their Story \nThe Pathfinders were formed by Elven-Lord Blackthorn \nAs a faction of the Malinor militaries. They were the scouts and archers of Malino r \nGuided by him, they had a barracks high in the tree tops, and had three teirs of ranks. \nAnd one leader teir of rank. \nThe first teir was initiates, second was members, and third was veterans. \nThe final teir were Blackthorn's personally hand picked Second and Third. \nThis went along well for a time. I joined as an initiate, and due to my skill with making lock \nI was promoted to third tier quickly. All was well and fine, until Blackthorn  left. \nBlackthorn left on a trip into the wilderness for undisclosed reasons, and left Altes incharge \nDue to my closeness with Altes, this made me a second. \nWe decided to make a outpost in the wilderness, and did so. We headed south of Laurelin and grew a consealing grove of trees, and proceeded to fortify it \nAfter a while, we decided to make it a permanant HQ, and began by planting a  Sapling of the druid tree of Laurelin \nIt grew for a while, and all was fine. \nAnd then The night of Pampo Peara's supposed death, in the city of Al'khazar \nWe mobilized and marched toward Al'Khazar, and arrived during the conflict. \nI immediantly began giving commands, why Atles forged ahead. \nI began to follow Altes as I finished with orders, and found him atop the keep. \nI watched him struck down where he stood, and it was the end of him. \nI became the leader of the wardens, The Warhighborn. \nThey were still the Pathfinders at the time, and thats when I made my first act of office \nSomething to note here to explain why I did this, former pathfinders, at this time now long banished from our ranks Had commited a heinous act of hatred in the past toward the race of Orcs. \nBreaking off from us for a while, and communication, they headed to an Orc  Villiage \nAnd proceeded to murder all the Orcs in cold blood, and loot the bodies and homes. \nThe Orcs hated our very beings, and I made a decision to drop our names as Pathfinders \nAnd shed our infamy with the name. I debated long and hard on a future name, and originally I intended for the name to be The Nature-Wardens, protecting elven nature all over the world, and with it Elven interests. This name was quite long, and gave the impressi on of druids. \nI decided to shorten the name to The Wardens, and finalised it. \nThe Ranks were to be as intended: \nInitiates, training to be Glade or Eternal Guards, would live together as a group and learn to share and think as one. From there they would be promoted to which ever they chose. \nGlade guards were the archer infantry of the Wardens, 5 of these would be in a squad. \nEternal Guards were the Sword infantry of the Wardens, 10 to a squad. \nWaywatchers were assigned a sector to watch and led a squad of 15. \nAll Waywatchers reported to their respected noble, who in turn reported to the Highborn Counci l \nNobles were Waywatchers who proved their worthiness and managed 3 waywatchers each. \nAnd finially, Highborn. \nHighborn were originally suppost to be a trimuvate, a triple council. \nThe War-Highborn was always considered the leader. He chose battle tactics. \nThe Archer-Highborn Was to second the War-Highborn and decide which men went where \nAnd The Guide-Highborn was to advise the both on where and what to attack. \nEach highborn was part of a council, to which all inter-military, and the declerations of war went to, and a vote was taken. \nInter-Faction matters would be settled with 2/3 votes, yay or nay. \nWar was only to be declared should all members of the Highborn Council Yay. \nThis was the intended structure of the wardens, all being able to trace a path from recruit to War-Highborn \nThis was all upset with the return of Blackthorn. \nI will reveal at this time, a secret that was kept for a long while. I know not wether It still holds true, but I shall say it non-the-less \nThe Wardens were all initated into the ranking with a vow. One of secrecy and honor. \nEach new recruit pledged...Not to Malinor, Laurelin, the princes, or even the High  Prince or Princess. \nEach new initiate pledged undying allegiance to the Highborns, and no one else. \nA deep secret we guarded jealously, and told none. \nWhen Blackthorn returned from the wilderness... \nHe saw what had happened. He was happy. \nBut then he looked closer, and saw a feirce resolve within the members of the Wardens \nA loyalty to me, the current leader in their eyes. They heard me shout, \n\"This is Blackthorn! OUR LEADER!\" \nBut in their hearts they denied it. My heart? I loved Blackthorn like a brother \nAnd was betrayed... \nA meeting of The Wardens was held. \nAccording to some sources I know, and my own conclusions, the majority of these members were recruited by Blackthorn and brought up around him. Those I knew were not present, \nFor the most part. \nA rigged council if I've heard of one, but my complaints are hallow. I no longer care for what The Wardens have become. \nAnyway, the vote was nearly unanimous, I was removed from power. \nWhen those loyal to me found out, a revolt was put into the workings immediantly. \nI did not know of this act and went to visit the new camp. \nUpon arriving...Blackthorn shot me with an arrow through my left eye. \nIt carved behind my ear, and the scar is still red to this day... though my hair is to long to see it through. \nI contacted my sources, and learned of the rebellion. \nI wept for what Blackthorn had become, he had abolished the council, and set himself as 'grand-highborn' none could dispute him now. power, unchecked. \nMoving on, when I learned of the rebellion, I put a stop to it. \nI quieted the members there of and told them it was for the better. \nTo this day I wonder what would have happened if I persued it? \n-The Wardens: A History", ""),
        StaticBook("The warmth of belief", "sconn", "(The pages of this book seem to be burned but only on the very sides of them) I spent years in search of them. They are well disguised, or they don't even know who they are. But there are firers burning inside of them. Even if they don't know. They are mysterious but also very noticable. Only the ones of faith will know who they are. And the rest should stop reading before i find out. People say that the one named Iblees is one of them. They are right. But that doesn't make the others evil. Daemons are what they are called. They are a scorching fire that worshipps our creator. But we worship them. The people that don't worship them will tell the others lies. So i will continue with the code that i taught a few of my trusted friends. 1772 227393 362627393 2836 383392 32456 7890 261. 919046 7645 041875 79615 01548913. 02465749 91556  747516 714! 29576 973256 579386. 3948 546 3465  7634652. If you do not know how to follow the instructions from the book i gave you tell me and i will explain.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Warrior and the Child", "Telandriel", "Once upon a time, there was a warrior, named Telandriel. He was very skilled with his bow, but also undefeatable with the sword. His master told him to kill a child. Telandriel didn't feel like doing it, but since he was a warrior, he had to. When he came to the child he grabbed his bow and was ready to fire when the kid said: \"Hey, sir, what are you doing! I don't want to die.\" He continued: \"Well, if you can drink this growse juice, I will not fight back and scream when you try to kill me.\" The warrior, who was not smart, did it immediately. The juice was poison and the warrior died . This is why, being smart is better than being strong.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Warrior's Cry", "martinvilla822", "It would seem, that we know, where we are, and where we go. For when we, look around, we can see, what we've found. And our journey, will take us, back where, we belong, take us home. And we'll fight, till the dawn, thru the night, till tomorrow's morn. We'll defend, all that's right, stand for all mankind. For the glory of mankind , we won't fall behind, we will fight. For our homes, for our wives, for our children, we sacrifice our lives. We will stand, all for one, one for all, till we've won. And so let it, be known that, through all of our  might. We have fought, we have won on this day!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Warrior's Guide to Fighting", "greeneggsnham555", "This Book will teack you some of the best ways to fight \n BODY POSITION  \n Bend your legs \n Extend your Elbows \n Hold your sword at a 45 Degree angle \n Do not show weakness! \n TECHNIQUE \n Slash fast if possible; Slow attacks will make you open for counters When Jabbing do not throw your whole body out there, just a quick motion of the arm", ""),
        StaticBook("the Warriors of the Golden Sun", "0rpheus", "The warriors started a humble beginning in the north fields beyond the undead fort known as \"Unk\" Christopher Wallace and Orpheus Shifsin, ex members of the KotF, a guild ransacked and destroyed by the undead, joined up and started the guild, from there on they had the help of thir friend Gaius Ma rius, who recruited ex members of the KotF Tesawa and Redujin, Tesawa joined the Warriors and quickly became Orpheus's Golden Royal Knight, and Redujin wished to go his own way and join a life of peace,", ""),
        StaticBook("The Way For me to Learn magic", "gombie", "* sits - erase backslash", ""),
        StaticBook("The Way Of My Magic", "gombie", "Guard", ""),
        StaticBook("The way of the scouts", "greener161", "Hello you must be an new cadet and looking to join the scouts In the scout you must have good eye-sight, sneaky and good swordsmen 1. never attack someone unless they attack you. yes out hail", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ways Of A Worrier", "silco97", "Combat has existed for many years and diffrent styles have been created to perfect these. Although combat is not an easy skill to master.  It requires skill and and strength but also fenece and and elegence.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ways Of Mining By: Ambros", "silco97", "Notes: There are many approaches a miner can take to mining.  This book explains several ways Chapter 1 Shaft Mining  Methods: Staircases, This for of mining is a commen technique as it is an easy way to reach lower levels of the earth saftly and easaly.  Simply dig down at an angle so that you leave a stair case behind you. Chapter 2 Spiral, A more advanced technique as it takes longer to build but it is much safer. stand above were you wich to mine and dig in a square that goes down but leave space along the sides for you to get back up.  Much like that of a stair case.  This can be done how ever wide you wish. Chapter 3, Orginized Mining, Probebly the best way to mine as it covers the most space quick. You simply dig out in diffrent branches that are arranged in the best way to cover the most space. Chapter 4 Cave Mining, the best way to find rare ores but is very dangerous.  As monsters love caves.  Although make sure you carry lots of tourches and dont get lost! This book is meant to help the stumped miner on his quest to riches.", ""),
        StaticBook("The ways Of The Creeper By: Ambros", "silco97", "I have travelled many miles and I have seen many kingdoms and there diplomacy.  Although usin  g all of my knowledge I have created what i call the The Creeper Meathod. This involves using how the creeper deals with things and putting it into the ruling of kingdoms. No this is not exploding when you are disturbed but rather a peacefull rout. The creeper does not flal its arms about like a zombie or human but it only uses force when needed.  So putting this into polotics I guess you could say that this is a diplomacy of mockery.  I belive that violence is not needed if you do not need it.  So using you words and mind rather then yoursword then much violence could be stopped.  Now how do you overthrough an empire with only words.  Well thats when the explosian comes in.  You have made the other empire attack you with your mockery but you havent attacked  back because its best only to defend.  I f you can outlast the enemy then you send in all of your forces quickly destroying the weakend enemy empire.", ""),
        StaticBook("The weak", "Sledder", "Sleepless nights await me, as the memories of the past flash before my eyes. Taunting me of that night, when I was vulnerable, and weak-hearted.  years later, it still haunts me, much more then it mocks me, revelation after revelation, the longest muses all lead to one conclusion. It wasn't my fault; I wasn't asking for it. The chronicle of the dark ages of my life; repression and regression shadow it. Lit candles in the pitch black comfort me, but the reckless winds keep ousting it. Perhaps it wasn't meant to be. Visions tattered with gory images scream out to me; reprisal is necessary, much so then the well-being of the soul. For it bathes the soul in a false sense of calamity. The birds sing of treason on a cold summer night, tears escape flowing smoother then the route of slave ships bound to the promised land.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Weird Adventure.", "Spinzir", "I remember, not long ago that i went trough the 3 gates. The first i did was to meet with my elven friend, Airion. We headed towards the Great kingdom of Oren. As night struck, Me and Airion seperated in the city. When we met up the next day, I had achieved nothing. While Airion had gotten ahold of 2 stacks of Diamonds. Not to be let out into a bad start, Airion gave me half the prize of his deeds.  \n  Shortly after i got the diamonds, Airion stood with a sword faced towards an Orc. A selfclaimed son of the Princess, Although i did not beleave my, turned out to be The Princess's son. Pok, his name was. A large crowd had gathered around the two. Words spread around with hatred, but the guards were quick, and soon Airion and i were looking for an Inn, to spend the night. Pok, the Orc, showed me to Dawn's bakery.  While waiting for this Dawn, I overheard Pok talking with a girl. What they were talking about will remain secret, But shortly after everything got quiet, \n One day, while looking around the market, I had just bought a bow and a bunch of arrows. I saw a Dark looking fellow, In Dark robes and Purple trims, This did not look like Hwaldar, the mage. While he asked where the king lived, i didn't respond. And then he went down into the sewers. Of course that could not be right, So i followed him down there. He had disappeared. I searched the sewers quite a while, And then i found a strange lit up area. There was a staircase wich i followed. Soon, i heard a voice say \"Get out\", It was the Princess, I jumped down to her and she told me to get out of the Keep, Surprised of my location i randomly walked the path wich i thought,", ""),
        StaticBook("The White Grove", "Relinquo_Angelus", "Originally a repose for miners returning from their labours underground, the closing of the Laurelin Mine has meant fewer pay a visitation to The White Grove. \n Now the birch trees and flowing pond are a destination for a handful of local residents seeking tranquility. \n The author of this book himself is fond of writing under the shade of the white trees as the water plays its subtle harmony.", ""),
        StaticBook("THE WHITE RAVENS", "pheonix_292", "join the WHITE RAVENS and be a man of action. The White Ravens are a group of warriors and mercenaries. If you are interested contact me (WR_inductor_claud( write THE WHITE RAVENS NEED YOU!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("the white ravens", "nikias_1996", "I write this in my romm in the castle time is short thats why i write this in a hurry.", ""),
        StaticBook("The White Ravens", "PilotAce1812", "All of the white ravens are guilty Spys name is Cael (jexdane) I do not know that names of tehm but i reconized seventh and triloqe", ""),
        StaticBook("The White Rose", "Ivrae", "Alas, how unprepared I was at first that day when Love came to wound me, and step by step made himself the lord of my life, and took his place at the head. I did not think that rasping power of his could ever lessen by a jot the firmness or the strength of my well-tempered heart: but so it is when we overestimate the truth. From now on all defence comes too late, other than to prove whether Love listens to mortal prayers much, or little. I do not pray, since there is no purpose, that my heart should ever burn less fiercely, but only that he might share part of the fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("The White Tree and the Gray Boy", "moloha", "The White Tree and the Gray boy \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n There once lived a young Dark elf with a Gray face and Crimson eyes. \n The young elf led a happy life for quite some time! His mother a master of agriculture, his father, a powerfull battle-druid! \n The Young one, had a close connection with nature. He sang to it, and nature grew all around him! But everything comes to an end. Even happiness. \n One day, as the young Dark Elf was returning from his walk, he saw a giant smoke cloud coming from the direction of his house. Running towards the direction of the smoke, he could start hearing screaming. \n As soon as he had reached the origin of the smoke, he saw the birch tree he and his parents were living in, collapse. Horrified he went through the cinders . In the very middle of what was supposed to be his parents bedroom he found their bodies \n Carved on the floor he saw some magical runes. Translating them he found out that they said \"DEATH TO THE TREE LOVERS\". \n Enraged, the Gray Boy started singing. A small sapling emerged from the remains of his house . It was feeble but the Gray Boy took it, replanted it and nurtured it. \n 200 years later, the tree was growing strong, and the Gray Boy, started living in the tree. Together with the partner of his heart, they helped the tree to grow. \n Some time later, druids came. And those druids, in their efforts to help the forest, accidentaly destroyed the tree. The Gray Boy managed to save a sapling and with the parter of his heart, they took it somewhere safe and let it grow while they lived beside it. And that's here both of them are now. Moloha, Aviala and the Little White Tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("The wild adventures of Clever", "Eltyer", "Has to be made.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wild Expedition", "Epic_Potatoe", "write -title adventure! 4 travelers decide to adventure the unknown together! Nailena, Deltaro, Loganos, and I, have departed into the wild. We have come across ruins of the figure \"Wyrd\" on this third day. We are taking shelter for the night, and then at dawn, we hope to start building a town. I need some sleep, I will write more tommorow. Today, we discussed where and what to build", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wilds Survival Guide: Volume 1: The Law of Club and Fang", "racingbrother", "I'm Gio Carminian, an expert at being able to survive in the wilds for days on in without taking anything at the beginning of my journey. Each time I go on one of these journeys I come back with a fair amount of loot and minas. In this volume of books, I will teach you how to do the same. This is, the wilds survival guide. \n  The first rule you must learn while living in the wilds is then wild's one and only law, the law of club and fang. Basically this rule states that the strongest man, animal, or monster will survive and be succesful. Another way of looking at it is that the man with a iron sword beats a man with his fists. I will be teaching you how to become a master of this law. ;;  Tip I: The first thing you need to do is to have a weapon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Will of Apollan", "Elite117", "This is to be considered my, Dragon Druid Apollan's last will and testament. I leave all my worldy possestions to my nephew Zeusan. This is to include all my minas and items and all my pieces of property. Including my room in the Grand Tree and the manor in Serpent's Ridge. My position as Archdruid I give to my very close friend Makia who has been with the order since the begining.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Will of Bael'Gorkil", "DefunctDivine", "I hereby bequeath, all of my world possessions to my friends across aegis, so told by this will. I wish that my house be returned to Mogroka, whom I've found a great leader, and a strong combatant. The bread in my chests are to be given to the gorkils aswell.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Will of John, Arch Druid", "123devmo321", "Mahten is to be the next Arch Druid and to get all of my armor and weapons. Respiren is to get all of my plants and seeds and such.  Aearia is to recieve my ores and tools. Petyr is to receive one fish . The fish is dead, it is a salmon.  Anything and everything else is to go to Saviticus.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Will of Saviticus Treebeard", "Saviordude", "Last Will And Testament of Saviticus Treebeard: \n I Saviticus Treebeard certify that I am of sound mental health and contractual capacity. \n I hereby revoke all other wills and codicls I may have previously executed. \n I appoint Petyr Brandbuck as executor of this will. \n I empower the executor to pay all my funeral, depts, taxes, and other expenses.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Will Of Yohom", "friar5", "I have a shtrange disheashe. Nobody knowsh what it ish yet, but I fear it might... Take my life... hic! So here is my will. 1. Give my sword to mork. 2. Give my farm to Valbad. 3.Bury me in my farm. 4. Give Grill To Arunis 5. Tell my daughter that I am horribly Ill, and to come to the Inn 6. Everyone, have a good life.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wind Druid", "jdpowercool", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wind Whispers", "connor1465", "The wind whispers, it speaks to me ((can you delete a line in a book?)) The Wind Whispers ((How do I get rid of a line in a book?))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Winding Vine", "Ohaythar121", "\n A thriving tree \n A dying soe \n A budding bush \n And a faltering song \n Tthe flow of energy is infinite and endless \n But the lives of men are streaking blaze \n If all of nature has shown me a thing \n All of life is a winding vine", ""),
        StaticBook("The winterfall invasion", "redbaron", "My name is Ogland and i am a Northern Ranger and this is my story on what took place that sad day in northern history. I was walking in the sentinel tower ruins when i heard the screams, and smoke billowing in the north. Me and desrik, my partner in the north both northern rangers rush towards Winterfell. We see a man running towards us, then a explosion, we rush over and we see he is burnt to a crisp. \"Its the undead\"! said Desrik. i nodded in return and look forward to the city. smoke rose in steady patterns. The famous jail tower was exploding slowly. From the inside the undead minion was inside! I reached the front gate and saw the huge tower, then a man sitting on top. He looked at me and laugh then lifted his arm, his hand started to glow. A searing fire ball flew from his arm and nearly hit me, smashing into the wall behind me throwing several archers flying. i rushed and quick as i could towards the towers with desrik right behind me. i slammed through the front door and almost fell into fire acouple feet from the door barely escaping a rather crispy death Desrik pointed to some stairs so we ran up them, they never seemed to end. Then we saw him, a man clad in full diamond and a sword painted with death. Another man stepped behind him carrting a bow. He shot a arrow ment to kill at me but i was able to jump out of the way. Desrik wasnt so lucky.. the arrow hit him right in the side of the arm. He yelled out in pain and then fell back down the stairs. I had no time to react because the archer turned towards me again firing a volley of arrows. i ran along the wall of the tower before i was close enough when i swung my sword at his knee. Crippling it, he didnt seem to feel a thing. I swung one more time right for his neck depcapitating it. His body walked on even without the head. I look around panicing because the stairs were on fire and there was no espace . i saw a window over looking the fast ocean so i ran for it. hitting the window with all my might shattering it. i looked in fear as the fast incoming water. i smacked into it loosing my breath. Desrik came out of no where and grabbed me from the water with his good arm. The last thing i remember before blacking out was seeing the man on the roof...", ""),
        StaticBook("The winterfell invasion", "redbaron", "My name is Ogland and i am a Northern Ranger and this my my story oh what took place that side day in northern history.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wisdom of Druid's", "Respiren", "Harvest the full ripened grain, with seed in hand. \n -Ancient Druid Saying \n", ""),
        StaticBook("the wise man", "bondb", "Life's tragedy is that we get old to soon and wise to late-Ben franklin When you do the common things in life in an uncommon way, you will command the attention of the world-George Washington : : maybe this world is another worlds hell-Aldous Huxley : : Knowledge speaks, But wisdom listens-Jimi Hendrix", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wisethorn bow", "sconn", "The Wisethorn connected with my mind today. It had no voice. It was like i knew that it was talking to me. And i knew what it was talking about. I only heard whispers in a toungue that seemed it was lost hundreds of years ago. The whispers soon filled my mind and drove my into thinking thoughts that were clearly not my own. The Wisethorn told me that connected too long i might go insane. But i am starting to get used to the connection. It told me how to make its wood weak and how to make it strong. Aparently the wood can be bathed in a mixture of honey and fish oil. It said that i should make myself a bow out of its wood as a gift for saving it. Suddenly it moved towards me and pointed a branch at me. I was calm. Its whispers made me calm. I was told to take the branch and make a bow. That is what i did. I prepared the mixture and suprisyngly it worked. The wood became flexible. I made a bow but it seemed that it will break if touched. The i heard more whispers. Now in the languagw of humans. Our connectin was getting stronger. It seemed that i knew what to do to make it stronger. I made a fire and threw the bow in. It worked. The Wisethorn became a part in my mind, teaching me when i didn't even know. The bow was now as hard as iron  and as flexible as paper. I took a leaf of the Wisethron and made soem string. That also proved to be a great sucsees. I knew more about the world every second. THe bow is the greatest weapon i have ever seen. It can easely compare to elven longbows. And the arrows fly as fast as lightning.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wispering Isles", "Pepernoot", "The Whispering Isles are currently under Krugmar rule, afer a recent deal between the Warlord and the King of Oren, Enor Sheffield. The Isles are still governed by Lord Brett Perea.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wolf", "sconn", "In vicious packs these creatures roam, from their mouth form spit and foam. When moonlight falls like a beam, they howl at it like as if it's a scam.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wolf and the Writer. By Rayle Seek", "StandUnited", "Slowly but surely Lucky crept up behind me, unaware I was writing. He then proceded to pounce onto me, in the process, knocking down my Golden Harvest Bread. Lucky isn't a person, he is a wolf. Yes I know, I'm insane to have tamed a wolf. But I've trained him well, and hes been my best friend and companion for 20 years. Im a writer, Im 30 years old, and am still going strong. What gives me my inspiration is Lucky. Without him, some of the many ideas would not have app appeared. Without Lucky, I am nothing. I remember it like it was just this morning. As a young boy, I was walking around in Winterfell, watching the snow fall gently. The snow was soft, can voered the ground like a blanket. With slow strides, and idled through the winter wonderland, admiring the beauty. I found something, moving underneath the snow. It was breathing heavily. To my suprise, it was a wolf! A wolf, with smooth white fur. It allowed him to blend in with the snow, so no one would be able to see him. I walked over to this wolf, to now hear is soft whimpering. I searched him, until I saw his leg, covered in a red substance. Looking closly, I found that it was blood, covering bite marks. He had proubly got into a fight with maybe his bretheren, and ended up losing. I tried picking him up but he kept growling at me. Knowing that I wouldn't get him to let me help, I grabbed one of my pieces of cooked pork. I gave it to him, and he instantly wagged his tail furiously. Slowly, and gently, I picked him up and carried him to my hut. When I was 6, my father and mother both died. There was a raid in our town, Fire, swords clashing everywhere, it was gruesome. In the process, both my Father and Mother were stabbed in the chest. I ran away, no where to go, no where to live, nothing to do. I then established this little hut, and got a job as a writer, yes, a writer at 10 years old. I did well. Pretty well. Very Well. 20,000 minas under a week. I could have made a mansion! But, I made a small hut, since it was only me and Lucky who would live there. Most of my money was spent on bookcases, carpet, torches, food, beds, chests, and weapons. Everything needed for me to survive. Then I started to buy many books, to start writing. Over the years, Lucky grew more and more attached to me. I actually had started my own life. Don't get me wrong, I missed my parents, but I have to admit, I was doing well without them. So here I write, I've established a home, a friend, a life. Soon, I become a renouned writer. With Lucky by my side, my inspiration skyrocketed. Until that dreaful, dreaful day.. I came home to find Lucky gnawing on his bone faster than usual. Something was obviously wrong, but I was stupid to not look into it. The next morning I woke up, only to see my best buddy, and companion, my best friend. Lifeless, fully pale, not one inch of life on him. It was devastating...truely devastating. Without my best buddy, how would I be able to write anymore? I was depressed. So very depressed. Every minute seemed like 8 years. I couldn't handle it. I've decided to kill myself, my life could not go on. The Knife to my chest now, and im going to............(book ends mysteriously) Never to be continued...", ""),
        StaticBook("The wolfpack", "sconn", "In vicious packs these creatures roam, From their mouths form spit anf foam. With greyish blur and shaggy fur. Moon beams fall. Light up all. From silvery woods there comes a call. To the mysterious full moon they howl. Which injures but illuminates they're nightly prowl. Brown dear. Very near. It is broght down full of fear. Deadly bight. Very tight. Every wolf shall feast tonght.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wolverine Hand Signal Handbook", "Groobs03", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wonderful Atrosities of EnderMen", "Noble_4", "The black tall mysterious figure", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wonders of the East", "drplat", "", ""),
        StaticBook("The word of Iblees", "pugsy", "\"He is ready. To take back Aegis. and that we will do it for him.\" This is the word of the overlord and so it is absolute!", ""),
        StaticBook("The words are there, but my voice will not sound.", "X01", "Notes clear I have no voice I am tired of all the pain, death, and hate.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Works Of The Mind", "monkeychez", "You know, the mind is such an amazing thing. Beings... They learn so fast. You and i are lucky. Very lucky. I was able to write this, and you were able to read it. The things that come from us... Either works of art, or horribly awful things that nobody should have ever known, is a gift. You should be thankful for that. Every day, if you did not know already, is a major learning experience. And you may  not know it, but every day, a bit of your routine changes. You walk a little different, breathe a little different, hold a cup of ale a little different. For better or for worse, it happens. And at the end of your existance, will you be able to think with that gift you have and say to yourself, \"Did i use my gift to my limit\"? And you can either be proud, or wallow in dissapoint, and sorrow, that your gift that many others would die for, went to waste. Perhaps this book may be your wake up call. Get to changing the world!", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_29(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The world of Aegis", "brent42817", "\n by Craglode \n I have decided to start writing about stuff that happens in Aegis \n ENTRY 1: This is actualy just a journal about me... Anyways I have bought a plot in the Cn Cuthalion Estate . I have built a house made of stone bricks and cobblestone. I think it's pretty good since I've added flaming netherack and vines. ENTRY 2: delete", ""),
        StaticBook("The World.", "DarkAngill", "The world. A vast land of many wonders. Along with these wonders there are grave terrors. Theres things in this world that shouldnt even exist. Many things such as zombies and pigmen. Along time ago the world wasnt like this. There was no terror. There was no evil. When the undead showed their face for the fist time; things went out of controle. People, dead people started to walk. Spiders began to attack. And pigs even began to come back to life and act as humans. So many people were lost the first few days the undead appeared. And so many are still dieing. This is our world.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Worst Person Ever", "Aceeri", "There once was a little faggot named Alpaca. He wandered the streets raping little children and hookers. Until, a person came a long and raped him so hard he got HIV . So after 10 years of giving birth to 19125971285798 unidentified specimines, he died of AIDS. THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("The writings of a magician.", "redbaron", "\n Magic... the devotion you need for it!  Everyday i feel my strength slipping away. Each spell, each enchantment.  my pyhsical strength grows thin. \n Although i look at life with a new understanding.  The world seems different. The undead dont seem so bad.  Now that i think about it whats so bad about them? \n Iblees has cursed the minds of the weak.  The weak want power.  They cry out for it.  Breath it, taste it... This brings up another problem i have with aegis.  Power hungry men and woman who enjoy seeing the weaker die. I met this woman named ivrae.  She somehow knew our king in another land. She is the kings advisor, and wears a crown like shes some sort of queen. It makes me sick, power is something that should only be given to responsible people of the lands. Yesterday she talked to me apprentice when he tried to buy a house, she said she didnt have time for citizens!  She is the most unresponsibile being i've ever seen in these lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Writings Of Ezio", "PakastainiPaul", "Look I am no one special . But there comes a time where people need to stand up for them self and thier nation.", ""),
        StaticBook("The writings of Nosor", "trotski24", "I see it now the darkness it is everywhere. In the forests and the cities. I need disiples to aid me we must eradicate the darkness! I am getting old I will die soon. Maybe I can become an undead? No thats an awfull idea perhaps they have books in their libary that will help me? I should go ahead with the plan to attract help. Yes I will go ahead with the plan but first I must talk with Iou", ""),
        StaticBook("The Writings of Prince Nathile", "silco97", "In this book I Ambros have written down the reasurch of the cursed stones of Iblees. I went to a library finding a book and have written down what i read in hear. \nThe Second Seed Of 1278 21 Day \nI have killed the man that has been chasing me for months. He said my soul would be good to add to the others.  this haunted me until I came across him on the road.  I pulled out my sword smitting his ruin on the road side.  His neck severed, I checked his pockets to see if he had any thing valuble the only thing I found was a stone warm to the touch. Its power is great I can feel it, it shall be an air to my throne and every one of my sons shall carry it. \nThe Second Seed Of 1278 29 \nI have awoken in my sleep to find my stone resting in my hand were I left it.  I think every one knows about it and wants to take it. I can not be safe in my own castle. I must take it to the wilds there i will live with it in harmony and no one shall steal it then. \nThe Grand Harvest Of 1278 4 \nI keep it in my pocket always I can not let it out of my sight. It haunts me with dreams i no longer want it, but no I must have it, it is mine and it shall always Be with me. \nThe Grand Harvest Of 1278 17 \nIt huants me I can not eat I am scared to sleep.  My sight it fails me life is cruel and the stone is a curse.  The stone is my prize though I shall keep it always. \nThe Grand Harvest Of 1278 28 \nIt sucks at my soul it talks to me I can no longer walk I must crawl apon the ground my back has grown arched \nThis next part that I read in the journal was cover in black gue as if rotting inerds were sprayed across it.", ""),
