        StaticBook("Thoughts", "123devmo321", "These writings are my own ideas and thoughts of what transpired during the thirty years I, Druid John, had been deceased. \n \n I hardly know what to think, but I must of have been brought back for a reason.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thoughts of a Multi-Concussed Dwarf", "InsaneMurdock", "Ahad, 8th of The Grand Harvest, 1304\n \n Bah, that blasted party had no Ale. Or maybe I had too much and don't remember. I am about to go on duy, guarding Kal'Urguan. Hopefully it goes quick, I'm thirsty.... \nMe and some other Dwarvin pals founded ALE: Aegis League of Excursionists. \n I don't really care for the name. I only agreed cause of it being called \"Ale\". I would prefer something with just Dwarves in it. \n FT", ""),
        StaticBook("Thoughts of Dark One", "gao252", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Thoughts of Eirin", "gao252", "I'm becoming dissapointed. I came to the White Ravens hoping for a job of thought. So far, all they have to offer me is to be the librarian. I was looking for something that requires more thought than that. You don't need thought to give people books. If I could get position that allows me to put my thought to use, I could do some amazing things. But no, all they have is a petty librarian. ((im on the phone ((im on the phone im on the phone", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar", "AutarchCosmos", "Name: Thral'Mar DeathHammar ((Swgrclan))\nAge: 40\n He can FARM at a moderate level. \nHe cant MINE.\n He can FIGHT at an advanced level.\n He can read and write.\n Note: Wants to learn magic.\n Note: Great concentration.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar's Agreement", "ParagonWarrior", "Our former Recuit Thral'Mar has thought his services as a worker not to be fitting. \nInstead we hav e come to an agreement of him travelling North for supplies more specifically Wool. \n I came to the agreement of 100 Minas per stack of Wool and also letting him have a room in the barracks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar's Revelation", "Swgrclan", "In this book, you will find the life story of Thral'Mar, the Orc Shaman. When Thral'Mar was a child, ancestors visited his father, which was his only family on account of his other family members either dying, or not meeting him. The ancestors told his father that he would have great powers one day, powers of the Shaman. After the visit from the ancestors, Thral's father, Gar'Osh, made an Oath he would teach his son the elemental ways. Thral'Mar being only Nine, could not be taught this magic, but five years later, when Thral became Fourteen, Gar'Osh started to teach Thral Shamanism. Coincedently two days later, a strange spirit visited the leader of Thral's tribe and asked for a trade. The trade being getting rid of Shamanism, a pure and holy magic, for a darker, but more powerful magic. The magic of the Undead. The tribe leader, being a smart fellow, knew of what Undead magic could do to his land and his people. He declind the \"trade\", but the spirit could not take no for an answer. The spirit grew angry and decided to possess the tribe leader, taking over his body and mind. A day later, the now-possessed tribe leader decided to ban Shamanism for Undead Magic. The tribe's people were angred at this all-too-sudden ban of the holy and natural magic. When Thral recieved news of the ban, he was furious. He grunted the ban off, and decided to teach himself Shamanism. But he was caught practicing it. The possessed tribe leader was angred by this treachery, and decided to do something so brutal and cruel, no Orc would dare go against his Laws again. he would execute Thral'Mar's father.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar's Study on the Ender Pearl", "Swgrclan", "Irba, 18th of the Amber Cold, 1324. Today, I begin my study of the strange Jewels known as the \"Ender Pearls\". I have found out from an hour of examination, the obvious qualities the Pearl holds. The color is a rather sinister looking darkish-blue green, and it is about the size of a Diamond. It weighs as much as chuck of coal does. It shines like Gold. I feel no magical presence when holding the Pearl. People say that it can give the ability to teleport when held, but I am too tired to test this rumor. I shall study more, tomorrow. Irba, 32nd of The Deep Cold, 1324. I have tested the density the Pearl holds, and it will not break. I can use a sledge hammer on it, and it will not have a scratch. The pearl might be infused with some protection magic, but I feel no magical bond on the pearl. This is very strange. I collected another pearl and hit them together multiple times, but to no avail. These pearls are harder than diamonds. I am tired from trying to break these things. Ill make more tests tomorrow. I've been hearing rumors of the origin of the Endermen. The rumors say they came from another plane of existance. Others say this plane of existance is what the world is in the future, and that the Endermen are either adaption of all races to the harsh land, or a huge taint of Iblees. All of this is confusing. If there is a way to go to this future land of Desolation and Darkness, I must use this method to travel there and study.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar's Theory on \"The End\".", "Swgrclan", "There is little information or study on this strange and mysterious \"End\". I know as much as I can handle. The information about this strange place is too immense. But I know enough, and Im kind enough to print my knowledge. This \"End\" is another plane of existance. Another dimension. Like the Nether. Execept it is special. It does not hold any mad god intent on destroying all life. Or any good god, that wishes to create life. It holds desolance. Nothingness. All devoid of life. It is not another Hell. It is the future of this planet. Of course, this is theoreticuel. But my theory has logic. These \"Endermen\" are not feral Aliens hell bent on destroying all life. They are intelligent beings. The strongholds made of mighty stone Brick were not made by us. The Endermen made these strongholds, to protect what brang them here. What the strongholds protect are Portals. Portals, not to another planet or continent unexplored by Aegis World-Troters, but the Future. The distant future. A future where there is nothing but sand and structures made by the Endermen. In this future, there is no vegatation. No trees. No lush fields of Grain. No water. Just sand, and the beings who walk on it. It might sound insane, but these Endermen might not be an entirely new species. They can be an adaption to the new, harsh land. And they come here, to the past, to collect resources, so they can rebuild the future. To make it lush again, and to make it full of life. The End could be another chapter in Aegis's history. If one is to look at what I saw, they would think God left Aegis, and Iblees took over. That is not the case. If Iblees were to take over, this future Aegis would be another Nether. Just fire and death. But it is not fire and death. It is devoid of everything. God left the future Aegis for some specific reason, and so did Iblees. I feel as if we did something to terrible, even for God to handle. But I feel \"The End\" is in the VERY distant future. Dwarves, Orcs, Humans, and Evles cannot simply change into tall, black beings with purple eyes. Adaption takes much time. And so does a destruction of a planet. So, to put it bluntly, my theory states that this plane of existance is actually the distant future of Aegis, and everything that inhabit it. The Endermen could be us, just trying to find a way to rebuild the planet  to be life-like once more. So we should not fear Endermen. We need to assist them if they do not attack. Of course, this is just a theory. I thought hard about this. This seems to logical to be wrong. I hope people will not walk into the future Aegis and think it is some dead planet, controlled by Iblees. I thank you for reading my book. May the spirits be with us all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral'Mar's Traveling Journal", "Swgrclan", "I have decided to make a journal, revealing what I do in my travels. Today I came across many ruins, holding no valuable items. Undead must of either killed or scared the inhabitants away. I also discovered a underground base for worshippers of Iblees. It's abandoned, but I put a sign warning people to not enter the forsaken place. Came across a village today. The inhabitants got massacured. Pigmen did it. I will find them. Found the pigmen. Kill them all. They slashed my eye, though.. its not bad, fortunatly. It'll Heal. I keep feeling like Im being watched. Im not suprised if I am. In the North, theres plenty of strange people, and plenty of Undead and other creatures. I found a strange temple. By the ancestors, it was a Shaman temple! I found reagents for a golden Staff.. Ill forge it right now.   The staff I made gives off a faint aura. I could use this staff when I learn to cast magic. I'm in a Tundra, now. It's damn cold out here, but I feel I must keep going. Theres something I feel I'll find... I didnt find any hidden treasures, but I found a... Pool of Magma in the middle of the Tundra. Very strange. I think this is unexplored land, for I have not found any structers or Ruins. When I gather the Items I need for trade, I will use my Soulstone to take me home. Hmmm... Found a large vein of Clay. I think I know people who buy bricks... Hehe, I fell into a hole. Its goes.... downward. Deep into the earth. Can't get out, so Ill Cook the bricks and ore I collected in my travels, and cast a spell to go home. It's getting boring down here. Damn clay won't cook quickly. I doubt anything will find me In this hole. The wait is worth it, though. I'll get good pay. But.. that village that was was attacked by those god damn pig men is... terrifying. The villager's corpses were so mutilated that I thought they were not Human, Orc, Elf, or Dwarves. Terrible. Im going home. The clay is finished. I have amassed 54 Bricks, 58 pieces  of Wool, and twenty Iron ingots in this trip. Money, here I come. Went on another trip. Two bundles of wool and two bundles of bricks, and thrity iron ore. Got 660 Minas out of that. Im rich! Im planning to go again soon. I am leaving, again, for another supply trip. I have discovered Haven - the city of the Acecended. Its marvelous even on the outside. I also slew an Endermen. It seemed... feral, and it dropped a pearl. These beings just appeared recently. I feel they came to this planet by means of teleportation, or through a portal. I am currently studying these strange beings. They seem almost intelligent, and most of them are not hostile. I came across another Enderman, but it was fighting a skeletel archer! I assisted it, and it gave me wool and spoke a string of syllables in a language I do not know of. This proves these Endermen can be intelligent, and not brutes that kill you on sight. Most of the ones that attack might be insane from wandering in a place far from their home. I've come across a few pockets of snow, and its getting colder out here. I must be near a Tundra, like my last trip. I only hope I don't fall into a hole again. I found a small village. It was abandoned. It held little loot, only a few pieces of wool and Cocoa beans. I have placed a sign that it has been abandoned. I've been doing that often. I found a dog. it was injured, so i took it in and healed it. It follows me now. I shall name him.... Marbles. Well, I have enough Iron and wool. I shall go home now, with a new friend. I found Marble's Pack, or family, on the way back to home. He seems happy with them. I went on another trip. I hit the jackpot, this time. I found a GIANT vein of iron inside an abandoned Iron mine, and already collected as much wool I can find. I also found a chest lying around nowhere and found tons of wheat. Im going to be rich!", ""),
        StaticBook("Thral's Idenity Record", "Swgrclan", "Date of Birth: Joma, 20th of Snow Maidens, 1284 Race: Orcish/Shaman Bloodline. First and last name: Thral'Mar DeathHammer.", ""),
