        StaticBook("Thul's Drawing Book", "Slic3man", "*Sketched here is a picture of Thul trying to hug Hael but he is turned away from Thul* \n  \n *A chart of a vial then branches leading to the vial to different recipes that can be made* \n \n *On this part it shows a drawing of a giant tree, with a sign \"The Grove Of Thul and Argos\" \n \n *This drawing shows a dwarf and two elves reaching out for thul, but one elf is turned away* \n \n *A sketch shows Orcs dragging Thul away from Laurelin* : : \n \n *The next two pages show a before and after sketch of a half faced orc then a whole faced one \n \n *A sketch of a giant sprawling tree, Home of the Mages Guild of Laurelin* *Here lies a drawing of a big Orc, with his jaw being made of iron and made with bolts* \n \n *Here lies a drawing of a big strong Orc, his jaw made of iron and covered in bolts* \n \n *Another sketch shows a pink haired grey Orc, with a warm smile on her face* \n \n *This drawing shows Hael walking away from thul while thul tries reaching up for Hael* \n \n *Next is a sketch of Hael looking down on Thul as Thul cries** \n \n *A sketch of a young elf, next to Argos, then Thul crying* \n \n *a sketch shows a giant white snake, spirit like*", ""),
        StaticBook("Thysa's Journal", "Juggernogg", "At first, i thought that getting some bones from the dead that walk with no flesh would be easy, but i was very, very wroung these creatures are dangerous to say the least. They do not die unlike most creatures and the worst part is even when they do die they have a tendency to turn to dust which is of no use to me as i need there bones, but i have still collected a small amount of the dust due to it seemingly haveing the abbilty to grow plants and tree's where most people would thing was impossible, but so far today i have collected six bones im on my way to the thirty two i need, but that is all for today the sun set's, and the foul creatures rise. ;; Last night i did not see any of those foul creatures, but that may of been because half the night i was bussy running away from soem crazed axe weilding madman who kept chanting something about the moon and the sea, I did how ever get to observe a rather strange piglike creature kill another of its own kind then walk away leaving the body of the dead to be eaten by the green skinned dead. Still only have six of the thirty two bones i need, but hopefully tonight will be better then last, but i think i hear that madmans shouting again so i will end this here. Last night i was lucky i got a total of six more bones from thos creatures I was almost drown today throgu hwhen i stepped on a patch of sand i thought was stable but it anded up sinking underneath me, i was lucky that there was a vine close by well night falls again, i must go hunt more of these creatures. No luck today, stumbled upon a small village however, the locals there seemed nice they even gave me some supplies before i left, in return i helped them grow trees around there small village, to mask them from the outside world, what lovely people. With not a worry in the world today i decided to think about question's that the druid may as of me, i thought hard and grew tired quickly, i will be going to sleep soon so that tonight i may hunt. I found five more bones today, bringing the count up to Seventeen I also found some strange building built completly out of some sort of strange Moss coverd stone and leaves... what a strange building it is. Today i met a strange old man, who told me that there are alot of these strange creatures to the north of oren i think i will travel there today. Today i wanderd into a village that seemed alright, until the locals there tried to kill me and eat me... there are some strange people out in outa regions", ""),
