        StaticBook("title Black-Cross: Info book", "Tassyk", "The information from the black cross wasn't too exciting. After exploring their base i found nothing of interest. Although something that caught my eye was their spies: RobinDrake, Albrecht and Therving . They are probably no different to we assassins though. But what made me a little curious was that they were on red alert, and hid all info. I shrugged all this off though and headed back . Whislt exploring a tower i found a old guild's base. They are obviously abandoned, their base was destroyed and all their chests were empty. But they had a wooden pole with some signs on it. On mentioning The Black Cross. They were Untrusted to this guild . And i don't think they were villians because they were foes with Orpheus, who are trying to dominate Aegis . I do not know for sure, but i think that guilds name was: The Spies. That is all i learnt from my scount mission", ""),
        StaticBook("title Borrin's Journal", "huddwudd5", "", ""),
        StaticBook("title Brad Plizga's Journal", "Plizga123", "Day 1 --------- Today, I crafted this book. I hope to be writing my adventures in it. title title Plizga123's journal erase \n Whoever finds this.... Keep it safe.... This isnt Brad.... I stole it. I will find whoever has this book and a reward will be in place. DO NOT take this as a joke. Dont tell anyone. ~G G", ""),
        StaticBook("title Buying Plots", "Treco", "Hello King Enor chat I have, at the moment, more than 20.000 minas. I know that you don't have much time, so I am writting this letter. I am very sucessful with my sale / rent of houses, many people coming to Al'khazar. But I have a problem. I'm not finding any low price houses. But I found a place next the beach. There is no houses and no plots for sale there. So, I'm asking for you if could you open some small plots for sale there. If yes, just sell them to me, please. A suggestion: plots with a 9x9 area and a minimum distance of 3 blocks between them. That is for avoid problems. If you are interested, please contact me. Thank you. *Signed:   Treco P.S.: ((I wrote \"chat\" after your name by mistake.))", ""),
        StaticBook("title Council Meeting One", "ljcrzynfree19", "Towns colors are decided as black and blue \n Guards need to get paid to make sure they actually work \n if people wish to live on the mountain, they must first leave their old house in the halls Auction for new housing Friday (08/07) \n Ale is guuuud", ""),
        StaticBook("title Culture in the East", "drplat", "It is I, Felus! This tome is dedicated to explaining some of the customs and rituals of the East . The people, unlike other cultures, are naturally very quiet and mysterious. To become trusted with them requires quite some finesse. If one is to outgoing and bold, they will immediately reject you. What is needed is to be equally as guarded. Eastern People take privacy very seriously. Entering in other's houses results in harsh punishment, and stealing is either death or exile . Women and men are equals in their culture, with no clear dominant gender. The government varies from village to village, but a common theme is to have two Political Leaders, One Spiritual Leader, and then the rest equal. The Easterners reject a class based system, and were perplexed when I tried to explain it. Decisions are reached by voting. The Political Leaders suggest laws, the Spiritual Leader approves the suggestion, then all vote. The leaders are responsible for assigning citizens their jobs. All basic goods are shared amongst all, while more valuable goods are private. I mentioned different villages earlier, and I will elaborate. The exact number of villages is unknown, but all are in a general alliance. There is one official capital, but I shall neither name it nor give descriptions here. Only those who have gained complete trust with a village may see and enter the Capital. I will say one thing: It is a glorious place indeed. Tresspassers are instantly killed. There are 3 Head Leaders of all based in the Capital, whom I will also not name. This is all that I shall say in this tome. I hope you have enjoyed this knowledge, and more i s coming!", ""),
