        StaticBook("title Journal - Sanirus Hadrian", "Harv0kz", "Day 1. I have just gotten this book, I shall use it to chronicle all my activites until my death . Joining the Oren guard was a wise move, but it was also oppourtunistic. I know I'm not in it for the money, but with my anger for the undead, I fear it will be a short . *Text trails off......* Day 2. I begin to regret joining the guard. Earlier today, more insults were hurled at us I fear that my job could be in jepoardy, and hence death. \n Day 3. I had to reitre from training temporarily, losing to a Oren guard member,  was fine, however, that puts my strength into doubt. I wonder if, possible,", ""),
        StaticBook("title Journal, Sanirus.", "Harv0kz", "Upon losing my first Journal, I have taken efforts to make money and buy a new one. Many things have happened, and it has been a year or two since my incident. I strive hard to train and heal my muscles, yet they refuse. I only hope that, through time, they begin to fully heal . As I grow weary of standard guard duties, and the lack of pay.  I have almost taken part in a civil war, and nearly gotten killed twice.   We must all have a side in conflict soon, regardless of where we come from. Our past. Our race. Our conflicts. Our age. Our class. Our social status. It will no longer matter. Not with this war. \n And so with that introduction in mind, I start anew, not as a warrior of vengence, but of honor. Let this be the record of my tales. Should it be found, then read, for I may have intresting stories to share when my life ends. In combat or of old age.", ""),
        StaticBook("title Kal'Brysst", "cgw123", "Kal'Brusst", ""),
        StaticBook("title Kill list", "Toastersaurus", "", ""),
        StaticBook("title Life of Alek - part 1.", "Aandie", "Staring at the carnage, praying that the sun would never rise.. living another day in diguise These feelings can't be right, lend me your courage to stand up and fight, on tonight.. A dwarf.. crushed by war sings and humns: \"Ooo-ooh.. Stand up and fight\". The fighting rages on and on.. to challenge me you must be strong.. I walk your land but don't belong, two hundred soldiers can't be wrong. It's no fun but I've been here before.. I'm far from home and I'm fighting our war.. Some scared, others killing for fun, I killed a mother infront of her son.. Fight for honor, fight for your life.. Pray to God that our side is right.. Even though we won, I still may lose.. Until I make it home to you, me beloved elser.. I see our mothers filled with tears.. Children grew up so fast, where did all those years go? Memories won't let you cry, unless I don't return tonight.. So many soldiers on the other side.. I take their lives so they can't     take mine.. Nobody tells me all the reasons we're here.. I have my weapons so there's nothing to fear.. Watching the death toll rise.. wondering how I am still alive.. Stranger's blood on my hands.. I've killed all I can.. There are no silent nights.. watching your brothers all die.. To destroy all their plans without no thought of me .. No thought of me, no thought of me.. \n Saddened dwarf hums once again \"Oohhhhh...\". Walk the city lonely.. Memories that haunt are passing by.. A murderer walks your street tonight.. Forgive me for my crimes.. and don't forget that I was so yooung.. Fought so scared in the name of God and Country.. \n \n Story of a dwarf, who was crushed by war, lost friends and family.. Written by man from the words of a dwarf.", ""),
        StaticBook("title LOJA DO MAGAO pupum", "joaosleny", "", ""),
        StaticBook("title Loth's guide to fortune", "sammeister97", "1.Get a good paying job,this can be working as a guard,at a shop,or even by joining a guild \n 2.Buy a small house,or rent a room from an inn.To store your precious items \n 3.Make wooden tools head into the wilds and mine some stone so you can make stone tools,ensure you make lots of stone tools and store them incase you get stolen from .Ensure you have a decent amount of materials at all time \n4 Once you have enough money from your job or hunting start a small buisness or buy a house for your self,or even buy your self a good set of armour to keep you safe and to help you while hunting . \n 5.maintain your buisness and make it bigger buy making multiple shops. \n \n \n Now your started you may do what you want,make your mark on the world or rise through the ranks of the guard or even become the most well know buisness alive...", ""),
        StaticBook("title Love", "radioactivkitten", "The story Of Thral Mar and Zynaera It was said that a Orc would never marry, yet I beleived different. When I was a girl, I was Engaged to a man I had never met. Of course, My parents only wanted to climb higher on the social chain. I ran away the day before my wedding to meet a man named Deltaro. He instantainously offered me housing and food, and I was very greatfull. soon after I was considered his daughter, and i had a sister Named Alys. \n One day I met a man Named Prince Lafthi. I dreamed about being his princess. He seemed to be very reserved and didnt firmly say if he liked me or not. Yet I was crazy about him, and my father asked me about him all the time. Of course, I never answered him. During a trip to Krugmar,  I was attacked by a group of men. A strong man, like no other, saved me. Lafthi did nothing. I ended up not talking to Lafthi. \n  That man was Thral Mar, A Orc much different from the rest of his tribe. He was fluent in English, extremely polite, and loving. I loved that he was different. It was all I ever dreamed of. A man who was different from most, and amazing. \n I assume most people are amazing once you get to know them, but he was amazing from the start we walked all over Aegis, exploring the different lands. My favorite was the Dwarf Land. It was an amazing cave, unlike any other. We began to grow close quickly. \n One day, he told me of a lost love. I told him I never loved Anyone untill then. He didnt understand what i said until i finally explained. He told me he loved me too. We kissed, and I looked over to see my father staring. I giggle. And that was just the beggining. \n We had so much fun togther exploring. Untill one day he told me He was going to war. he told me he loved me. And left. He told me he might not come back", ""),
        StaticBook("title Lukas's Journal", "ljcrzynfree19", "7/03: Railway to Kal'Aras complete. Kal'Bryst meeting planned for tommorow, considering every member is present. (Royced) Acusing people of steeling in Kal'Uraguan's market, Gotrek can vou as witness, but the drunkard is probably just trying to get attention again \n 7/04 Trying to sell dark wood to Prince Native, still no luck.", ""),
