        StaticBook("title Promise of The Setting Sun", "TomMeijer", "You promised me you'ld stay for the sunset, and when the moon shines through the darkness, we would find the path that leads us home and on the path maybe... You'd sing me a song. You promised me that you'd always be there, hold my hand if ever I'm real scared, help me stand up tall if I fall down, help me wash away all my bluest days. Oh, how could you promise that you always would be there, why'd you have to go away somewhere, every morning into every night, you watch over me like the sun in the sky, am I all alone or standing in your light, maybe I could... Maybe, sing you a song tonight... You promised me we'd stay for the sunset.. Tonight.. read erase read -erase erase read off help", ""),
        StaticBook("title Rhymes of the East", "drplat", "These rhymes have been collected by Felus. Poem 1:", ""),
        StaticBook("title Rise of the Undead", "ljcrzynfree19", "\"yeaarhraha\" painfull screams echoed over the horizon, a red mist illuminated the thick vibrating mist. Darkness fell in a sudden wipe, as if demon magic had plunged the world into doomsday. Winterfell was the subject of an unjustified, murderous rampage, as swarms of creatures covered in rags ravaged the remains of the abanded Prison. Winterfell was hell as meteor strikes showered in furious clusters of firey rain. The presence of the \"undead\" was all but too obvious. lightning struck innocent men who had stormed into the towering monstrosity, to defend those allready present in curious fustration, clambering to the highest point in the prison tower to escape the frequent explosions of metal shards and destroyed rock, shooting through around the prison complex.", "")
    )

