        StaticBook("Torak's Report", "vegan166", "Mgroka's son builds a fort in a nomadic village security hole in sanhar was patched by an acrobat and a goblin mogroka ended up getting excessively drunk and started a scene in Yaghy's Pub Yaghy sanhar complete for residential and business puposes orc population is up way more then it used to be", ""),
        StaticBook("Torak's Report of Krugmar #1", "vegan166", "Sanhar has just been finished, they may be rebuilding it. Orcs looking for new jobs since the building of Sanhar is done. Fixed the great arena of Krugmar. Lots of fights raging as usual. GOSSIP PAST HERE: A female dwarf admits here love for the rex. The orc interviewed at the time exclaims,\"They'll have little green babies soon.\" And last, and greatest, I haven't got my skull crushed! *chuckles* lafthi", ""),
        StaticBook("Torak's Report of Krugmar numba two", "vegan166", "Mgroka's son has built a new fort in a nomadic village. A security hole in Sanhar is patched. Sanhar ready for settlement. Orc population is rising. GOSSIP PAST HERE: Mogroka ended up getting excessively drunk, and started a scene in Yaghy's Pub.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torn Journal Entry", "RHcrow", "The mages pursue me and my followers.  They killed Dimitrii when they cornered him in the orc lands orc lands \n He took down three mages and one of the Archmage's own guards. His death is a setback to our goals.  The Wars have gone on almost two thousand years and I miscalculated the mage guild's strenghth. However I will replace Dimitrii and we will rid the world of the infection. -Gestahl.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torn Letter", "Archmage_Cataris", "When the sun rises in the west and sets in the east. When the seas go dry and mountains blow in the wind like leaves. Then i will return, and not before. \n - Frederik Nine Lives", ""),
        StaticBook("Torn letter", "Ep152", "With Bawapy at my side and the thunder roaring outside, I could feel myself slipping from my soul. From my life. I could remember my past experiences, everything I did and felt. Except... something was different.. Her... I let out a final breath and something happened. I was familiar with it by now. I had died. Then I woke up in a cold dark cell. It was tiny, I could barely stand up in it. \n \n I've been in here for a couple of days, the one keeping me here... I know her face... *the writing gets messier and more rushed* here she comes, it's- *a claw mark is left where a name should be. All that is left is one last letter. 'e'. *", ""),
        StaticBook("Toro's Adventure!", "Paulie1333", "This Journal Belongs To Toro (Paulie1333), And Was Started In Oren, Al' Khazar On The 18th Of Suns Smile, 1324, Irba!   \n  I woke up in a place called the \"Temple Of Aegis\", I was greeted by a group of Ancient Monks! They gave me this weird looking substance, and told me to keep it with me \"Always\" I held onto it for a while, wondering what it actuallly did, Until all of the sudden, I was warped to the home of the Dwarves! It was called \"Kal, Urguan\", It looked like a lovely place, So i decided to take a look around As I was walking up the cobble lane, I was greeted by a few guards, They told me that this was  my new home town! I was dearly shocked, but it wasn't long before I had seen the whole city. By then, I had met a few of the locals and they were kind enough to lend me some tools. I then started to help contribute to the city by spending a few hours in the mine helping dig a massive plot for a new underground village. I then decided to pack some stuff and head out of town, Meeting a friendly Orc on the way! He was heading to \"Oren\", So I tagged along with him for the journey. He gave me a few \"Cooked PorkChops\" for the journey there. When we arrived at \"Oren\", we went our seperate ways. After having a look around town, I decided to buy this Book, and write a journal, and that led me to   local pub which im currently in, writing a book and admiring the ocean seas from a window! \n  \n A few days have come and gone, since my last journal entry. and alot has happened, so ill start from the beginning. One night I was reading another's book, when I noticed a girl in the corner of the pub with a drawing pad, she kept looking at me, I thought she was drawing me, but I never found out. Soon after that, A massive bar fight broke out, I slipped out the front of the pub and watched through the window, just to be safe. It went on for quite a while, Blood everywhere! Until they both got taken away to be dealt with. The next day I was chatting with them in the pub and they started talking about a man, named \"Wrath\". They had plenty of stories to tell about him. He was one evil buggar! killed by wrath aswell as many others. Fable and Haelen (The other 2 I was talking to), have both seen Wrath, Haelen was even captured by Wrath and kept in a cell, He eventually got broken out tho. We shared stories all night, and before we knew it, Morning had come. In the middle of the town, there was a man about to jump off a building a commit suicide, he kept saying he had nothing to live for. I didn't find out what happened to him, becuase I was about to die of hunger, But I prayed for the best. Later, Fable and I were talking, Until we noticed someone was following us, we chased after him, but he just dissapeard? Some strange things kept happening around town, I heard whispers coming from a group of, hooded men, They were talking about someone planning an attack on Oren. I Believed it was Wrath, but I guess i'll have to wait and see.  \n Other than that, I found an entrance to the sewers which leads to some cool places, im still working on getting a fishing rod and Yet again, Im sitting outside the pub listening to the ocean waves crash into the city harbour.", ""),
        StaticBook("ToSidgyr!", "patu97", "title UnNamed erase title UnNamed", ""),
        StaticBook("town application idea", "exodawn", "bla okay erm guys, about the town appp when the restes hits i want to make a town app so we can continue kal'sharock. now i have some idea for the town but thats mostly the layout of it. i have been thinking al day at work for some lore of the town, but couldn't come up with any thing good so my question is: if you all have ideas for the town lore, so we can write a prper application for kal'sharock, for the ones that play skirim, i had in mind that the town will look a lillte bit like whiterunn,. well i hope that you all help with this. if you like ofcourse. and if you know any nice and good players for in the town please, make a note with tere names. Ogrhen battleborn ps i will make a bitt of an idea for the town in my singelprayer and post it on the foems", ""),
        StaticBook("Town Coordinates Of Theragorn", "gombie", "X- 1039 Y= 73 Z= 859", ""),
        StaticBook("Trading Station Rules", "Jaknifed", "\nWelcome to The Trading Station \nPlease buy and sell at each interval of a good's refinement process. \nExample: \nSell Wheat To The Shop \nBuy Wheat from the Shop \nSell Bread to the Shop \nThis ensures the micro economy is stimulated. \nAs well as allowing me to gain a small amount of profit for allowing you to use my facilities. \nYou will make .75 minas per piece of bread you make. \nI shall recieve .25 minas total when the bread eventually sells. \nYou are welcome to buy this bread and sell it wholesale to anyone you chose. Or for your own use. \nJust make sure you buy and sell at each interval or your privileges will be revoked. \nAll goods that move in and out of this shop are yours to do with as you please. \nWith the exception of any outstanding orders The Wandering Merchant may have. \nThese goods will be able to be sold to the shop but not purchased. \nPlease note: Weapons are for our use only. It gives the hunters something to swing with. \nArmor however may be sold wholesale as well. \nThank you \nZyn, \nThe Wandering Merchant", ""),
        StaticBook("Translated Artifact", "urpenguin", "At The Bright Of Spiders Eye\n Are you scared to 'zhin through the snaking caverns Are you worried that the spiders run away Are you petrified of being given above to Nemiisae Fall below onto your knees little elf And hold y our hands with palms above turned and dalduna beloved spider Here Jameson i have finised the translation", ""),
        StaticBook("Translated copy of Liber Mortuorum \"Book of the Dead\"", "Domainoft", "The old magic of undead is a mystery. This is your first urna, fire and necromancy. Many do not understand the undead. Are more destructive men. Open mind be corrumpted. Yet the power of it is a hungry kind. Iblees curse very strong, and is very difficult for any man will to resist. Iblees first speaks of power. Many in power have great love and guidance of her. All attacked attacked me first to the hight of the undead were cast by the amounts of balls, lightning and fire. Then, get close with the guidance of men. And summon the ministers of hell.", ""),
        StaticBook("translation of that old book", "friar7", "shall we go kick undead ass? hmm? grr mork is awsome, alvaska dosnent let me write :~(", ""),
        StaticBook("Translation of the Liber Mortuorum, Book of the Dead", "Pepernoot", "\"The old magic of the undead is arcane. This is your first fire and necromancy here (?). Many people don't understand undead. They are very destructive to man. They are corrupted in their mind. They are hungry for power. Iblees' curse is very strong, and difficult for a man to resist. Iblees first speaks of the power (?). They have many (people) in power that love her (?) guidance. At first they attack from high with lightning and fireballs, then when they get close, they summon the beasts of hell.\" \n \n \n Translated by Cerlos Ithelias. Notes: The writer of the book appears to have a poor knowledge of the language he wrote it in. It might also be my errors though.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translation; English to Katta Dari Lidah", "ErcMan", "Hello is Halo. My is Saya. Name is Nama. Is is Adalah. Sit is Tuan. Do is Melakukan. Need is Perlu. Help is Membantu. Money is Uang. Am is Pm. Dwarf is Kerdil. Human is Manusia. Can is Dapat. Have is Tulah. Good is Baik. So is Sehingga. How is Baginmana. Are is Yang. The is Yong. You is Anda Food is Makukan. Bye is Bye. Yes is Ya. Great is Besar. Seed is Benih. Farewell is Selamat Tinggal. Word of Tongue,Language name, is Katta Dari Lidah. Pumpkin Men, What we call the family, is Labu Kuning Laki-Laki .", ""),
        StaticBook("Travel Encyclopedia Volume I: Dwarves", "greggbot", "Dwarves live in the great city of Kal'Urguan, which is mostly underground. In the center lies their castle, in which the king lives. There is a marketplace in the entrance hallway, and the mines branch off of this hallway. There is also outer Kal'Urguan, where they do most of their trading with other races. \nDwarves are well known for their love of ale and mining, but they also enjoy a good fight. At the back of their city, there is an arena where they fight for entertainment. Dwarves are also renowned smiths, with the best skill and equipment in all the land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Travel Journal", "Cloudheart", "The Travel Journal of: Tend'el \nFirst scribed on Kamees, 19th of Snows Maiden, 1312 \n \nI am visiting the Mage's Tower. I believe I can faintly sense Slayer now. I must be such a failure at magic; he and Bell instructed me so greatly and I have still awakened so little. \n \nThinking on Bell only reminds me that I have lost her. \n \nI...I...did not know how hard that line would be to write. I cared for you dearly Bell, loved you even. Moreso than the love men share so commonly with their partners. You became a friend, and I never concerned myself for your aid, only you with mine. I would ask for forgiveness, butut that is pleading to the page, sulking in sorrow. \n \nYou taught me better than that. I must ask for forgiveness from God for my mistakes, and forgive myself, then press on. We have to accept the consequences of our actions and change for the   better. You would have told me so, right Bell? Right? \n \nI am so confused, Bell. If only I had your buoyancy of spirit. \n \nSecond Entry: Ahad, 8th of The Deep Cold, 1314 \n \nVery tired, buteen walked to and from the guildhouse in Laurelin and my Inn, putting pieces of the guildhouse away for safe-keeping in my cellar. I'm also writing a few books of my own, butut as of right now that's not really going anywhere. \n \nThird Entry: Kamees, 26th of Malins Welcome, 1314 \n \nI have met for the second time with a man by the title Lord Lucius Murmillo. He showed me a small wooden church down the path from my inn. Upon meeting him for a second time, in a few days he had built an entire wall for a city to help supplicate the Dwarven Kingdom. He says he studied architecture at a young age in Laurelin. I believe I'll be helping him with his town, so an old goal of mine and Lex of the Dwarves can be realized. I just met up with Bawapy, we've been reminiscing, butut he is sad about Ademas. I found out the Dwarves' city of Outer Kal'Urguan is falling due to a craig...or quake. Lucius told me the Elf who live on the other side of the small forest is Godswood. He goes there to pray. \n \nFourth Entry: Joma, 27th of Malins Welcome, 1314 Helped a Dwarf move out of his home with Lucius, went by the name of Rolden. Such a shame too, his home could have been fixed up to look like those Halfling Homes. \n \nFifth Entry: Sabet, 28th of Malins Welcome, 1314 \n \nI have spoken to Felune. It appears Ademas is gone to be with God now. His final rest is come. I regret not being a part of the last batte, butut my friend would have understood. I have now just been told of a new complication in the Ragthieu story. The Fighter, The Archer, The Spellsword (Ademas), and The Blacksmith. These are the men that have significance in that family, I was told the story would end with Ademas' son. He must be trained. \n \nSixth Entry: Sabet, 28th of The First Seed, 1315 \n \nWell, this is strange. I just woke up in the birthing place of the Cloud Temple. I must investigate. I am now more than miffed. Someone is claiming I attacked them, and I just found I my road was repaved...in WOOD! \n \nSeventh Entry: Joma, 13th of The Second Seed, 1315 \n \nI just considered that I have never mentioned my birthday to anyone. I believe it's perfectly understandable, considering my less than understandable childhood, but being 121 I believe it's time to mention it. I was born on 7th of The Amber Cold, 1193. That is all I will speak of my childhood for now. I am not in the mood. \n \nEighth Entry: Irba, 25th of The Grand Harvest, 1315 \n \nWe made a miscalculation in building the wall of Lord Lucius' Estate. It's rather embarassing. We must move the whole wall down one. \n \nNinth Entry: Tolta, 3rd of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n \nIt is the third, and my birthday is fast approaching. I believe I should begin making preparations, perhaps a cake? Sadly, I wonder who will even show up. I feel so alone as of late, like no one is around. But I mustn't sink into depression. We choose to wallow, don't we? Then I choose to press forward, for the brighter days are nigh. \n \nTenth Entry: Irba, 4th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n \nI went travelling today. I swam toward some great trees that were bare after leaving the mines under the Desert Star. As of now, I am spending the night in an inn owned by an Orc and his elven niece. I couldn't sleep. My birthday is coming soon. Why is it unsettling me? I must spread the word of the Dragon's Breath Inn. I said I would try. \n \nEleventh Entry: Joma, 6th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n \nI spoke to Alvaska, who has changed the name of the Grey Wardens to the White Ravens. He knows of Lucius Murmillo, and tells me it is a foolish idea to help him. He and the AFF, who are allied, disagree with Murmillo's vision of Feudalism. They believe such a system will cause the weaker people to rise up and overthrow Murmillo. This is foolish, these three keeps could band together for unity among this great piece of la nd. I don't know who to trust, and will keep myself far from seeking power, but I must unite thes e kingdoms. Even if Lucius does not know how to lead, I can help him. I fear I have ambitions of overthrowing Lucius...what right do I have? I must remember my own teachings, and Bell's. Greed, and Lust for power is foolish. Even if the castle is in a forest I only HELPED create (I must remember that I didn't finish the forest and Leafwind helped greatly, even if I did start the movement) It is not mine, nor a creation from my mind. It would be like unto usurping a painter's masterpiece. \n \nTwelfth Entry: Sabet, 7 of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n \nMy birthday has come and gone, I spent the day working on another man's castle. I did not even make myself cake. It is oddly, warmly familiar of my first few birthdays, the elves who had took me, a vagabond on the street, in and told me in sweet words how precious my birth was. They all knew the secret that I had not. They allowed me to be that dirty, carefree boy. I can only imagine the kindness they shew me, shielding me from what had happened. No boy...nay, I even, a man...can handle what happened to you. Mom. Dad. I am sorry I could not have healed you of the illness that took you. I swear I will not be consumed in searching for cures. I will live the life you allowed me. I am sorry I had to know, to know of you. They kept it from me and I pried. I know you would have had me ignorant, so I could live a life without knowing. I never knew either of you. I love you, I love you both. But I know that you would have me never love you, and thus never hurt. I now know that every piece of knowledge has its own price. God give me strength. \n \nThirteenth Entry: Ahad, 8th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n \nI sense that evil has awoken. Was it like this for Bell? or Slayer? Did they awaken by sensing? As foolish as chasing this feeling is, I must go. I should know if it is an arbitrary thought or if anyone is in danger. \n \nFourteenth Entry: Sabet, 7th of The Deep Cold, 1320 \n \nFour long years have passed, like nothing. I have been working with Lord Murmillo, whom I know on a first name basis so really Lucius. We have, in this amount of time, created a village worth standing, a short walk from my inn. Aeriel's Crown. We are planning on starting an academy. I hope this would please Bell. I trust Slayer knows I do not mean to shirk my responsibilities as a Guildmaster in Laurelin. But what am I to do? I have been hard at work here, and the magic he eagerly promised has not yet found its fruition in me. I hold fast that he was right though, and in this line of thought, help edify a place of scholasticism. \n \nBut I long for adventure, as my boyish youth once longed for it. \n \nFifteenth Entry: Joma, 20th of Malins Welcome, 1322 \n \nI have awoken. I hardly know where I am, and feel as if I have been shaken from a deep dream. I spoke to one of Murmillo's Bannerman, Ser Twi Osit. I have lost 2 years, since my last entry...in the journal! What happened? Last I remember I was holding the book. Now I awake in a refurbished part of the castle in Aeriel's Crown. A new town has sprung up for Aegis' Sake! I need to see Slayer. I need to heed the words of Bell, and see the Druids. Perhaps I misunderstood Eindry'el's Curse. Will I forget everything? As much as I hate the druids, they might know something. Ser Twi also tells me that the Undead are massing under a man named Wrath. \n \nThe world is so cruel and confused now. I am befuddled by my own village. Even the open world on the King's Road brings me unknown sights. \n \nSixteenth Entry: Kamees, 5th of The Amber Cold, 1325 \n \nJust 2 days from my birthday I have finished the construction of my establishment - The Blue Print! I should have a sale in celebration, up until my birthday! \n \nI was blessed enough to enjoy a birthday dinner with Lucius, as well as three members of the Whispering Order, the militia of Whispering Isles. The members were the General, Alethion, and the two Commanders, Anora and Akorta. It appears I slipped up and forgot how old I was when I was speaking to my guests. How foolish of me to forget my own age! I told them it was my 131st birthday, when in actuality I turned 132. Oh well, it is a small trifle. \n \nSeventeenth Entry: Itnan, 16th of The First Seed, 1328 It has been two years. The time has passed amicably enough. I long for adventure, once again. It also deeply wounds me, that I have not seen my closest friends, the men of Wilder Farms for as long as it has been. Is it I who has grown apart? Or can blame be placed in such things?", ""),
        StaticBook("Travel Journal", "iCreAtureeee", "Dreticus's House is at -2000, -2000", ""),
        StaticBook("Travel Journal", "Destroyer_Bravo", "Joma, 20th of the Sun's Smile, 1331 oday I get prepared for the long journey. omorrow I set out to Al'Khazar. \nSabet, 21st of the Sun's Smile, 1331. It is night. I am now setting off. I will rest at WInterfell when I get there. Update: Instead of travelling to Winterfell, I will rest at Crimson Vale instead. But, the gates are locked... I will just sit here till tomorrow. Now it is almost day. I am leaving Crimson Vale. \n  Two hours later, I finally dawn upon Al'Khazar. The city doesn't awe me anymore though, because I have traveled through here many   times. Night. I finally am leaving Al'Khazar. Midinght. I have stumbked upon Commander Maur on the road. Itnan, 23rd of the Sun's Smile. I just realized that I have to go back. Well, off I go. \nTolta, 24th of the Sun's Smile. I have found Shoi and my superiors by Alras. \nKamees, 26th of the Sun's Smile, 1331. Finally... Away from Wrath... Lately, me, Shoi, and some other agents of the FoA were captured by who I guess is Wrath. I recognized the voice from years past... Daybreak. I will be travelling to The Cloud Temple and Laurelin to link up with the others by soul transport. I will not be bringing this journal along. This is the final entry... For now \n  Chapter Two. \n Itnan, 30th of the Amber Cold, 1331 I finally made it back...I can guess it took me a month or two, although I did stop by Kal'Urguan. \n Tolta, 31st of the Amber Cold, 1331. Still no sign of Shoi and the others... \n Kamees, 12th of the Deep Cold, 1331 Nothing happened that day. \nEpilogue, the disbanding of the FoA led to my retern to Kal'Urguan. I have lost many good friends, and am probably never to retern there.", ""),
        StaticBook("Travel Juornal", "mattr41018", "10/2: I started in the warden base, I will Probably stay here all day, the meeting is today, so i am kinda stuck here. The meeting is in 2 hours... I am so Nervous, I hope not to mess anything up... AT the meeting, its all hell broken loose as we work to organize ourselves... I am sitting waiting as Quazar prepares to deliver his speech. This is what he said: Now the purpose of this meeting is to inform the members of the wardens of recent events and to organize native i am his replacement. I understand we have been disorganized as of late. I would like to reward thoughs who faithfully served the wardens and continue to to so. Now I would ask all initiates to step forward. you are now promoted to rank of guard. Durzio, Tarethiel, and Amaya, have been promoted. Now Please take your seats again . Elessar Please step forward. now please tepeat after me, I pledge my loyalty and honor to the Wardens of Malinor. I will honor and respect the rules and pbligations of the wardens. I will follow without question the orders given by offices of the wardens and I will not be dissmissed from the wardens without proper aproval. Congradulations and welcome. now all guards step forward. Except those that were jsut promoted. I will anounce who is promoted to the rank of Waywatcher Moonbeard, and Alex, That is all for now, this does not mean you will not be promotd in the near future, So please do not lose faith, Not please take your seats. Further promotions will be delt with on a more private basis. Now please step forward if you hold the rank of Waywatcher, Even the new ones. I will allow each of you to choose two guards for you squads. You will be in Charge of squads so we are mroe efective in battle . Felore is in charge of squad 1, alex of squad 2, and moonbeard of squad 3. this doesnt have to be completed as of now. I will put up a board in which you will lsit your squad members. Take your seats please. Ah, DArk rage, step forward. You are nw promoted to the rank of waywatcher . You will be in charge of squad 4. We will be setting those up soon. Now please take your seat. Gwahir, you will be in chage of sqaud 5. All current guards please line up. Gladeguards on my right, Eternal guards on the left. step forward sypher you are now promoted to Guard. Squad 1 will be a group composed of Gladeguards. Squad 4 will be composed of Gladguards as well squads 2, 3, and 5 will be composed of Eternal Guards. Bayron and Amaya are assigned to squad 1 Tarethiel you are assigned to group 4 Now, Sypher you are assigned to squad 4. saud 2 Icarus and Durzio are assigned to squad 4 Enelya is assigned to squad 5 Squads have been assigned, theere will be a squad board in which you may check you status of which squad you are assigned to  . because new members will be added as they come . take your seats . Meeting is now Adjourned thank you for attending, you attendence is noted  .", ""),
        StaticBook("Travelling with Kasil", "xxXHunterXxx", "Today me and Kasil have been travelling... He has taken me to different areas... of my childhood. he took me to the old tower that our long lost friend, Aaron... Aaron's father owned a tower as tall as the tallest tree in the world! I really like how...he's taking me back to our childhood...how he was nicer. \n He next took me to our other old play area, where we had snowball fights it was under the tree where we engraved our names on the wall with the flint stones onto the bark of the tree. .... I really want to know.... why is he showing me this stuff...he's being strange. \n Finally he took me to where I used to live...before the blasted Guardians attacked my village, It was the windmill where I and him began our friendship, he came to my door introducing himself along with his parents when he was new to the village...but after a week... both our parents all died..we both ran away, seperated for 5 years. \n Kasil gave me a rose and put it in my hair shortly after! I am so happy! Kasil also hugged me for the first time in 5 years!", ""),
        StaticBook("Travelogue- The Verge", "1337Sammiches", "The Verge... odd name, isn't it? The Verge is a chain of islands that recently appeared in Aegis. Not many know of its history, or even its land. I, however, will travel to this land and record my findings as I explore the Verge...  \n I travelled to the Al'Khazar marketplace to find a sword of the finest iron. This sword, along with my trusty hand-me-down claymore, will be what little protection I will have.", ""),
        StaticBook("Travels", "TommyRedblue", "We traveled. It rained. We were strong", ""),
        StaticBook("Travels of a Forest Dwarf", "abovehill7", "", ""),
        StaticBook("travels of abovehill7", "abovehill7", "I was given boots by lolindar the dark I shall keep them as an heirloom I have found the dragon of iblees! I wonder if i shall evr become one of the gruesome undead or the holy ascended... only time will tell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Travels of Arik, Chapter I", "YifengZhong", "Kamees, 33rd of The Second Seed, 1337 \n I leave the sanctuary on my journey to Laurelin . However, the road is treacherous and I am weary of the rise in Orc Highwaymen. I've donned some rather expensive armor in hopes I can get away if a troupe of  those moronic baffoons get ahold of me.  May He watch over me. \n Kamees, 33rd of the Second Seed, 1337 \n I just awoke from the inn at which I stayed the night.  The woman looked fearful of me. It probably had something to do with my armor  , I tried to explain to her that she had nothing to fear-if only she knew. \n Anyway I set off towards the Elven lands once more now. \n I have finally arrived in Malinor, I sit at the Inn outside the Sister City now hmmm. *a section of the text has been scratched out* . Home to Alys, the elf, the druid, the beauty. She is married to the man Voak, who I suppose is a good match for them. They want to have children together soon.  I wonder how that will work.  \n I find myself wanting to take her and sacrifice her now, but that would be a quick pleasure. It would do well to take my time and relish the opportunity to betray a friendship. Anyway, the sun is rising, I have been traveling through the night to arrive in Malinor, I need sleep. . Joma, 34th of the Second Seed, 1337 \n Voak takes me to speak to the druid I failed at killing.  I hope he's not around. I have not yet devised a way to slip him a golden apple for I do not yet know his name.  Or who he - Actually, I have just learned that there is something afoot at the druid grove. Excellent.", "")
    )

    private fun _AEGIS_31(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Travels of Arik, SonofNone", "YifengZhong", "Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1337 \n I sit in Malinor, at a pool overlooking the forest. I sit next to a man who was once a sage, this is interesting. \n Tolta, 24th of Snows Maiden, 1337 \n I have encountered my deluded friend Gabriel attempting to kill what appeared to be An undead.  Some mage of sorts at any rate We set off to the sanctuary now.", ""),
