        StaticBook("Tressure Map", "Reckreation", "If ye seek the tressure of Blackbeard go to al'khazar stand on the King Cross centre. Head 30 blocks west then 40 blocks south then 50 blocks west Ye be needing to get wet to find my tressure so if ye be scared of water STAY AT HOME!", ""),
        StaticBook("tressuremap", "Reckreation", "From the centre of The Kings Cross in Al'khazar (the floor logo) Move 30 blocks west. Move 40 blocks to the south Move 40 blocks to the west If you cannot swim leave this book. Find the tunnel with the X", ""),
        StaticBook("Treyarc's Interview for Apprenticeship", "XSilverWolfX", "1.How would you respond to a lunatic banging on the gates saying \"Let me in!\" Answer: Ask them what is wrong, and why they are doing that. Depending on the answer let them in or not. And my prior knowlage of the area and person. 2. What do you think being a Ranger's Apprentice means? (( Lag spike, just got all those answers (( bookworm erase isn't woring :O Answer: To learn the ways of a Ranger, what to do. How to do it. When to do it. Learning none stop and practice live training. Correcting your self in anyway possible. How you can get better and never stop learning and training. (( Not if I'm taking you as an apprentice :) (( Ignore all OOC in this book :) )) 3. Crowley classic scenario, on a scale from 1 - 10, 10 being the highest. Answer: 8.5/10. He did good and didn't slip for the trap, but he made it pretty obvious towards the end that he might not be a lumberjack, because he said he lived in the city and worked from there and the woods around it. Clear your inventory", ""),
        StaticBook("Trial 1", "pugsy", "You have been watched for some time and we see ou are fit to join our ranks. This book will give instructions on what ou must do for our first trial \n  For our first trial (Should ou choose to accept it) is to list all names of close fellows and  . people of importance \n (Please leave a book containing those details in the same chest ou got this one from when done)  Your mortal life is forfeit if ou do not assist in suppling names. \n Your mortal life is forfeit if ou do not assist in suppling names as of now ou know too much to go back and leave", ""),
        StaticBook("Trial of Mind", "Carnivore91", "Greetings student. Today you have been chosen to try the Trial of Mind. This was made to test your ability to think a problem through and strengthen your mind. Today you will be given a simple riddle and in order to survive you must get it right. The riddle for you to answer is this: I am found in the earth, when you are mining I like to show myself to you often. Some like to ignore me and leave me behind, but sometimes when you harvest me I can change into a more useful form that is widely used. What am I? \n You must travel through this maze. Along the way you will see signs with a possible answer on the m. Do not jump into the first one you see, make sure you find them all and decide on the correct one. If you answer wrong your life will be taken, but if you answer right you pass the test and shall be that much closer to becoming a Shaman! Good luck to you, and may the spirits and your mind guide you in the correct path.", ""),
        StaticBook("Trials of a Shaman", "kookamooka", "Hail reader, I am Kooka'Duras, Kooka for short. This book is for all apprentice shaman, it will record my journey from an untrained Shaman with no teacher, to, hopefully, a Shaman worthy of Or'Ta's acceptance. Hail, warlod Hail Bruddahs Bruddahs, you know a good place to rest?", ""),
        StaticBook("Trials of Redeye", "Ultion", "My first day in this newland, It's wonder's are amazing and limitless. I find myself in a small hovel outside the orc capital in this land. The hovel is based in a lit forest, it is ripe with nature. The orc shaman's native of this land, are crude, nothing more than glorified savage's. My  master would not be . pleased", ""),
