        StaticBook("UAC: The Beginning Of Justice!", "transphat", "The UAC, or United Aegis Coalition, is a racially diverse group of justice bringers. It's chief purpose is to break down the racial barriers of Aegis, and rid it of the evil Undead. Located near Haven, and heavily influenced by the Ascended, The UAC is considered one of the greatest groups of Aegis. help ? \n test paragraph fsdsdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdfdhjdfkhsdgfsjdugfskhfbgkdfhugkaefhbgafhjkvbdfhvbadfkjvb shgibsdfvjksnfgusehrtngiljkdfnvjshogsilrngjkdfg \n second test paragraph jarlgsjkdfngsjkdfnglskdjfgs", ""),
        StaticBook("Ulrics Journal", "olifudge", "no from here", ""),
        StaticBook("Ulysses", "dagothagahnim", "It little profits that an idle king, \nby this still hearth, among these barren crags, \nmatches with an aged wife, I mete and dole \nunequal laws unto a savage race, \nthat hoard, and sleep, and feed, and know not me. \n \nI cannot rest from travel: I will drink \nlife to the lees: All times I have enjoyed \ngreatly, have suffered greatly, both with those \nthat loved me, and alone; on shore, and when \nthrough scudding drifts the rainy Hyades \nvest the dim sea: I am become a name; \nfor always roaming with a hungry heart \nmuch have I seen and known; cities of men \nand manners, climates, councils, governments, \nmyself not least, but honoured of them all; \nand drunk delight of battle with my peers; \nfar on the ringing plains of windy Troy. \nI am part of all that I have met; \nyet all experience is an arch wherethrough \ngleams that untravelled world, whose margin fades \nfor ever and for ever when I move. \nHow dull it is to pause, to make an end, \nto rust unburnished, not to shine in use! \nAs though to breath were life, life piled on life. \nWere all to little, and of one to me \nlittle remains: But every hour is saved \nfrom that eternal silence, something more, \nA bringer of new things; and vile it were \nfor some three suns to store and hoard myself, \nand this gray spirit yearning in desire \nto follow knowledge like a sinking star, \nbeyond the utmost bound of human thought. \n \nThis is my son, mine own Telemachus, \nto whom I leave the scepter and the isle \nwell-loved of me, discerning to fulfill \nthis labour, by slow prudence to make mild \na rugged people, and through soft degrees \nsubdue them to the useful and the good. \nMost blameless is he, centered in the sphere \nof common duties, decent not to fail \nin offices of tenderness, and pay \nmeet adoration to my household gods, \nwhen I am gone.  He works his work, I mine. \n \nThere lies the port; the vessel puffs her sail: \nthere gloom the dark broad seas. My mariners, \nsouls that have toiled, and \nwrought, and thought with me \nthat ever with a frolic welcome took \nthe thunder and the sunshine, and opposed \nfree hearts, free foreheads you and I are old; \nold age had yet his honour and his toil; \ndeath closes all: But something ere the end, \nsome work of noble note, may yet be done, \nnot unbecoming men that strove with Gods. \nThe lights begin to twinkle from the rocks, \nthe long day wanes, the slow moon climbs, the deep \nmoans round with many voices. Come, my friends, \n'tis not too late to seek a newer world. \nPush off, and sitting well in order smite \nthe sounding furrows, for my purpose holds \nto sail beyond the sunset, and the baths \nof all the western starts, until I die. \nIt may be that the gulfs will wash us down, \nit may be we shall touch the Happy Isles, \nand see the great Achilles, whome we knew. \nThough much is taken, much abides. \n \nAnd though we are not now that strength, \nwhich in the old days moved earth and heaven, \nthat which we are, we are. \nOne equal-temper of heroic hearts, \nmade weak by time and fate, but strong in will \nto strive, to seek, to find, and not to yield.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ulysses Cole's Application", "Ansh98", "1. I am good at building and I will use that skill to build. \n \n 2. I'm not very patient. \n \n 3. Alone because it is easier for me to do things without other people in my way. \n \n 4. Mostly to help people, also to gain fame. \n \n 5. To build marvelous structures and become a great guild. \n \n 6. I made the Ulysses building along with the walls and battlements. \n \n 7. Ansh98 and Jtringl  \n \n 8.  Near my home and it has potential. \n \n 9. Buildings and homes \n \n 10. 7, I still have room for improvement. Here. \n \n [ACCEPTED] (Member has half price Membership)", ""),
        StaticBook("Un-titled", "Archmage_Cataris", "To whom this reaches. \n \n The \"Black Crosses\" is not as it seems, their real name is the Teutonic Order. Their \"member list\" is fake to protect their real members and identities. Their goals are to crush and destroy all guilds in Aegis that are dividing Oren, i fear they will try to sieze the crown, they have already started a rebellion that failed, in time they will gain more power and i have no doubt, they will take the crown. Gaius is not as i thought him to be, i once thought he was trying to achieve the Greater Good, but instead it seems he is a cruel, harsh man who will put the world into darkness to achieve what he thinks is good. Their city is located in the East of Al' Khazar, South of the Mages Tower and Old Kal' Bryst. Their members are Gaius Marius, he leads the Order. Samuel Bealcrest, Glylith, Viadar, Tesawa, Jagen, Mirtok, Garaag. The rest, i have forgotten. Please, whomever finds this, give it to one of power and stop this evil that threatens to throw the world into Darkness, we need to fight the Undead, not madmen, but the madmen must be taken down so we can fight the the Undead. I dont have anymore time, they are coming. \n \n *The book is un-named and un-authored, it also appears to have been written in a hurry*", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead", "patthebakr", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead", "HICHERV07", "The Undead, evil creatures origionatingfrom the Nether, are a interesting and dangerous race, they singlehandedly have sent the human kingdom of Oren down on its knees as they exist just a few days travel away from the great city of Al Kazar, but why? , why do the undead what to bring destruction upon the kingdom of men? , to find out the answer of this question, you must know the history of these people . The undead, worship the god of the Nether called Iblees, in Ancient history Iblees was banished from the world for all existance and eterinity, and waited for his chance at rev enge, soon enough, Iblees was able to exact his revenge, the two brothers from Al Kazar, Phillip and Roderick, were corruped by Iblees and 'transformed' into the beigns we now know as Freyj and Rott, their sole purpose?, to combine the Nether and Aegis into one, allowing Iblees to once again roam the lands of man. This can all be misinterpreted, Freyj and Rott can both be lunatics, spreading a false word, and Iblees could mean a diffrent message?. Though we will never know for sure......", ""),
        StaticBook("undead", "Lord_Zack", "lodrik he was the one that showed me true power. he is normally hooded hmmm oh! he says he is in the fear family now the other is a dwarf named kevin. in the same family mork i knew him as agony... i wrote down all he said", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead", "ninjamana", "Banished to a different realm of existence for all eternity, Iblees counted the years away. He feeding on the souls that would drift into his plane after death. It was just a matter of time until the opportunity arose for revenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead An Informational Look", "deathmetus", "The undead are the chosen followers of Iblees. They are run by a hiearchal system. They can command great magic and generally live in what we call the Nether.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Associate List.", "cometking123", "Al' Khazar is in a state of ruin. And This is why. People are not the people you want to think about, because in the end they'll just stab us in the back. This is a list of all known Undead informants and benefactors. Use it well. \n Crowley Falos, Lance Ulric.", ""),
