        StaticBook("Undead attack strategies", "SirPwnzalot700", "a Theres simple Rules to attacking Undead I will be writing a book on how a good commander is to attack. Like the Black Fortress where the walls are impenetrable ... Use Strategy and cunning to defeat them I was walking past Snowy Feilds when I see a army spreading out and attacking the Black FOrtress . They were disorganized I tryed to take command with some others helping me We build some simple walls to protect us Soon it was a fortress We survived during the night and hid in bunkers In day we attacked Rule one. Never attack at night there much more powerful Rule two Either send out for supplies and men or... Build your own supplies like wood and mine for c obblestone . We harrased them killing them off We then had to fall back when the tides turned on us If you use this strategy always be prepared to retreat and call it a victory . Use this to Drain there supplies OOC Though I think they spawned there golden staffs or theyve got 1000's . Second Strategy . Theres towers around there base , Get archers in the tower and rain down upon them Then send fighters through a passage Which I am not writing down. Sorry. When inside go in the tower and flick the switch! Which will turn on a massive fire trap in the city I only know it is in the tower Though I know who does know here it is Hold the tower and send a lot of man to hold the Ruin entryway Which is Behind the Fortress, when there just bottle them up there until its not worthit to come out Take the fortress Thats the offensive Strategy Theres always the CHARGE THE GATE tactic but that has only lead to massive armies to be destroyed If someone says that there either stupid or trying to trick you into doing it... If yuo try the second tactic make sure there all good and armed and 100% sure there on yuor side If anyone joins your group quietly... tell them to go unless yuo know them That happened to us and at the pitch of the battle they turned... Do not distrubute this book since only people that I trust will see it ever!", ""),
