        StaticBook("Undead Gate In Ruins", "monkeychez", "On my travels to Oren, i located a lad", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead info #1", "Juggernogg", "Foudn undead fortress it is heavily protected only entrense is through the front gate Netherack around the maine spire can be set alight only way in would be to let them trick you into entering when it is raining run through the fire into the main spire and to turn the fire off while men rush in . \n Large amounts of Undead haters outside their gates many of whome are very touchey with who they speak to \n harvest sergent Hale is corrupt DO NOT TRUST HIM!!!! \n I GOT IN!!!! some foolish undead left the gate open Fire is opperaterd by a single switch to ignite all or several ones for each quarter of the fort Doors can be locked but seem not to be much *passes book", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Information", "monkeychez", "A man named Tyrion Lannister is apparently an Undead recruiter, he wears dark robes,  and is a very important part of the Undead. He has gone by two reported names: The Novelist, and Unknown. Since many have robes like his, he is one of the hardest Undead to identify. I was also told of Freyj, the Undead leader. Some of his poetry has been circulated into Aegis. And it is rumored it has soul-corrupting qualities . He has black robes with a yellow trim, very similar to a Sage's robes. He has a symbol on his back. A circle, within a circle, with a dot in the center. Apparently all Undead have this symbol . His is yellow, and pawns are purple. The Novelist does not have this symbol on his robes. There are also reports about the Undead's \"Induction Ceremony\" The man i interviewed got his information on this form a man named \"Val\" The Elf i interviewed, Mysterious_Monk, Was fond friends with Val. He said his friend sacrificed himself . And he said when an Undead completes his trials, he must go to the Undead city. And if he is reborn, he is accepted to be an Undead. His friend was not accepted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Information", "JustinMC98", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Keep Report", "Tyber1231", "This is writing of Aren Wayworn, Recruit of Followers o' Aeriel, on 25th of Malin's Welcome, 1314  . ; This is report of atrempt to infiltrate Striqaephoth with help of FOA_Recruit_Glow and Elven_Royal _Guard_Alastor. ;The so called Floating City looks terrifying. From the bottom it is surrounded by large area of Sou lsand and Netherrack, with several pools of lava, taking source from the air platfroms above. Above all, the terrain looks demoralizing and hard to move around, due to lava and soulsand widely s pread there.  \nThe only small weakness of the terrain is small terrain outcropping from the Northern side of the city . If able to fly through the gap (About 15 blocks), you can safely land on ofe of the platforms. For more brave people who have large supply of food/protection against fire there is a way of ge tting in by going up one of the lava flows. Personally, i do not recommend such a way. \nNow the defence capabilities. Defence of Striqaephoth is relatively easy. As getting up i nearly impossible, several Undead can stop the entire army. Due to their capabil ity of magic, based on fireballs and summonings, they can easily halt attackers, and deal heavy casualities to them. Catwalks connecting each floating island are also good and safe spot for archers. \nConclusion of my report; in any case, I STRONGLY suggest not using large armed forces, but a g roup of Commandos, who can clear the gap of over 15 blocks, what for me seems clearly impossible . My conclusion comes to the fact that this city can be overtaken only by using spies or commandos . Group of spies who have gotten into ranks of the Undead, could take over the keep, while an offi cial, front attack would be a distraction. \nThis is a work of an amateur, who based his conclusion on several ventures to the Undead's cit y. It might not be as accurate as offical reports (If any), but i based it on my personal experi ence, and i believe in it. I hope this report is  reflecting well the capabilities of Striqaephoth. \nThis report is intended for future use, as info on enemy's fortress in case of war.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Keep Scout Report", "Tyber1231", "\nThis is writing of Aren Wayworn, Recruit of Followers O' Aeriel, wrote on 28th Malins Welcome, 1314. \nThis report concludes reconeissance of  Undead Keep, with help of FOA Recruit Glow and Elven_R oyal_Guard_Alastor. \nSurrounding Terrain. Surrounding of so called Floating City of Striqaephoth is terrifying. Lar ge area of land around the city seems like taken straight from the Nether. Terrain consists main ly of Netherrack, with large patches of Soulsand, which makes movement very hard. What makes movement even more dangerous are scattered around lava pools, overflowing and causing fire hazard to anyone who is not Undead. Those pools take source from the Sky platfroms above. Whole terrain is very demorilizing, hard and dangerous to move about. I suggest not staying in that surrounding for long. \nWays of getting in. From what i seen, getting in is nearly impossible. There is no staircase, hidden entrance or any other way of getting in from the ground level. Althought, during my search, i've spotted a small terrain outcropping being relatively close to what seems to be some sort of a church. Unfortunatelly, the gap between the ground and the platfrom at this point consists of over 15 blocks, what seems quite impossible for me. Althought good use of magic might allow to transport several people through the gap. A more Extreme Method of getting in would be by going up by one of the lava flows, taking source on the sky platforms. Someone with high enough supply of food or protection against fire could make it up the lava flow. It's an extremely dangerous method and i suggest using it as a last resort of getting in. \nDefence Capabilities. Striqaephoth is relatively easy to defend. As it would be hard and slow As it is nearly impossible to get in, several Undead could halt the entire army. As they base their attacks on range and summonings, they can protect the city dealing heavy casualities to the atackers. I do not advise front attack. \nWays of attack. Based on my earlier statements, i suggest either using Commandos, who might clear the gap of about 10-15 blocks. Other, more reliable way would be using spies or double-agents. They could attempt to take over the city or eliminate the Undead, who would be focused n fighting off the attackers. In case of that scenario, frontal attack would be a distraction. Of course it might happen that spies will join the enemy or they will be turtured and forced to tell the plan of attack. All ways of attack i stated are dangerous and would have a high risk of failing. \nConclusion. Concluding my report, i stronly suggest using small group of people, who would attempt to take over the city.  I strongly disaprove a frontal attack. \nThis is a work of an amateur, who based his work on visual recognition and his suggestions and predictions. It might vary from theofficial reports (If there are any) , but i believe it is cor rrect, as i wrote what seemed reasonable and real. \nThis report is recommended for future use, in case of assault on the Floating City.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Minion", "digdog7789", "I have became a undead minion today. There was a war against us today.I killed 4 guy's. The war is going on right now acculaty.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Names Log", "Darkdragon274", "Korbec \n Lodrik Hmm Showed Iblees to Korbec, Fear Family \n Dwarf named Kevin, Fear Family Korbec: Hunts in Desert So, where were you when they arrested you? Hunting camp: past alras Past Kaxil fort to left here, should I go store these notes from prisoner?", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead names OOC", "king_creeper3", "AllenTheGreat Lymdil éwrite Sledder help", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Notes", "Alectriciti", "Black robes. Colourful trims. Golden staff, glowing when held. Red eyes, that stare deeply into your very soul. Wreaking with evil, always plotting mischief, their lust for blood and death to iblees. The undead can be seen through those following notes.  Must write!  I see them in my sleep all the time. I can't get away from them! I'm covered with darkness, they fall on me, tear me apart like they did my family. But I see a light within that darkness that shines. Could it be something? These nightmares bring me fear, yet hope at the same time. NOW I HEAR THEM SCREAMING MY NAME! They want me dead... or... do they want me undead!? The undead... They are driving me insane!", ""),
        StaticBook("undead notes.", "Shuness", "Overview \n I, Shuness, am keeping these notes to better ourselves against undead. Perhaps I can find a weakness to their power. \n Abilities \n Undead have magic avalible to them, and can apparently set fire with this. They may also be able to generate items, need conformation though. Also rumors of a separate dimention, where undead are the only ones unefected by enviroment. \n Motive \n Undead appear to have different motives. Some apparently \"feed\" on souls. Others supposedly hunt for an artifact, which will most likley bring apocolypce to our land. \n Apearace \n Hooded, with red eyes glowing from within their cloaks. according to kayle, they sound like snakes, cloaked in black hoods, with some gold trim.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Observstions", "legoman144", "Itnan 16th of The Deep Cold 1340: Undead still inhabiting old safehouse. Although much less activity than before the raid. Kamees, 5th of The First Seed, 1341. Watched undead capture a lone traveler on the road. Couldent stop too many of them... Went back saw the body, those bastards skinned him alive...", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Plans", "muchoman798", "\n Sir, I am a fresh Undead, but I have plans to take Al'Khazar. It will be easy. They have so many weaknesses. Here are the details of my plan. \nFirst, we pay the guards. The human king does not pay them, so they will be easy to get on our side. The money will quickly convince them. \n Then, we can send our Undead in through all of the weak points. There are so many, that it will be easy to sneak at least three teams in, and one can just go through the front gate, as we now are allowed to walk through all of the cities in Oren. Foolish humans. Next, we just send a false representative to the King in order to get into his keep. From there, we can get all of our men to him, and Oren will fall. It is so simple only because the King has left them wide open. We can do this tomorrow if you'd like. \n I would like to note this is NOT an Undead plan. This is a human pointing out the flaws in our defenses. Now I have your attention. I would like you to see the problems the King has created for us. We can easily fix this. \n Do not stand for this. Save Oren \n ~ L", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Poem", "Steelwolf19", "People live and people die the sun rises and the sun falls. hearts fill with joy and hearts become cold. Moon becomes bright and moon becomes dark. Souls become happy and soul bitter. But I am the darkness of the moon, my soul is bitter and my heart is cold. I still live but hope no more.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead research notes", "pugsy", "When you open this book there are small notes jotted around the pages Ive noticed from what I have heard the recruits for undead need to take 3 trials", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Rumors", "monkeychez", "Rumor #1: Near Winterfell, Undead ruins lie.... Since the gate to the Nether is in Winterfell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead self-defense", "Bodobo", "This is a book about the undead and their methods to attack. 1. How to know who is an undead - you can't see who is an undead and who is not. The undead wear nor mal clothes", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Song", "Cookie9000", "The Undead are loose and Iblees may win. His assassins have come to rip off your skin. Evil eyes will see you if you try to stand still. The Undead will get you, for Iblees they kill. Hack 'em up, Chop 'em up, cut 'em to bits Or else they will get you while laughing in fits. If the Undead don't get you Iblees will try. To reach out and touch you, your skin he will fry. Your mind he will flail, your soul he will take. You'll sleep with the dead, for life you'll forsake. You'll die with Iblees till the end of time. He hates that you live, Your life is the crime. The Undead might get you, it says so in text. If the Undead don't get you then Iblees is next. Lest he who's born true can fight for our lives. He of the Shadow touched, the one with Blue eyes. ... -Alanor Hedgewell", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Song", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Found by a Shad'Rin scribe in an abandoned library* \n The Undead are loose, and Iblees may win. His assassins have come, to rip off your skin. \n Walk away slow or they'll tear you apart, and laugh all day long  as they rip out your heart. \n Evil eyes will see you if you try to stand still, The Undead will get you, for Iblees they kill. \n Hack'em up, Chop'em up, Cut'em to bits, or else they will get you while laughing in fits. \n If the Undead don't get you, Iblees will try. To reach out and touch you, your skin he will fry. \n Your mind he will flail, your soul he will take, You'll sleep with the dead, for life you'll forsake. \n You'll die with Iblees till the end of time, he hates that you live, your life is the crime. \n The Undead might get you, it says so in text. If the Undead don't get you, then Iblees is next. \n Lest he who's born true can fight for our lives. \n He of the Shadow touched, the one with Blue Eyes. \n [[Thanks to ShadowNinji]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Southern Bases", "Da_Emperors", "In the South the Undead have a great deal of bases. There was the old keep of the Undead which was destroyed and turned into ruin. There where a system of outhomes in the south as well. Leftclick is a Undead that works in the Elven Coucil . The Main base was the Minions Base where we slaved. There is a farm, where 250 melon plants grow food. So many workers slave there and produce gold and  other resources. There are a few other bases in the South, however that is the main account.", ""),
