        StaticBook("Van's Decent", "KingToten", "Night 1: Last night's nightmare was more terrifying then the last. I hope i dont die from This. Night 2: This night... i couldnt even cope with. If i dont get help soon ill be in trouble. Night 3: I cant help but feel something is watching me in my sleep. Something not normal..", ""),
        StaticBook("Vance, the Northerner.", "ErcMan", "Meh. help Vance sucks. The End. By: Bloddar", ""),
        StaticBook("Vanguard Logs-", "AcerBuddy", "Irba, 4th of the Grand Harvest, 1339. It appears a man by the name of Ben Powell and a man by the name of Vulcus Solarius were assaulted while on an unauthorized mission. They say a Starwalker by the Name of Polcari had other Vanguards with him. He was not instructed to do so, and action will be taken against the Walker Guild. -------------- The Vanguards tell us Polcari the StarWalker attacked first. Polcari tells us the Vanguards attacked first. Rovik Tharn withdrew, and did not assault. Polcari says that Bofaim and Moses are his witnesses. Ben Powell was stabbed, allegedly by Polcari. (( Polcari states he did not stab, only punch)) Polcari then stated he was verbally taunted, spaking the engagement. Issue is now under further investigation. --------- Irba, 11th of The Grand Harvest, 1339. Belyn re-entered our realm. We saw it fit, and knocked her out of the Right Tower, then killed her in the forest. We see it possible for her return. ------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Vanguard's Creed", "Aerinyes", "I will always protect Malinor. \n I will never accept defeat. \n I will never leave a fallen comrade. \n I will never quit.\n So help the grace of Malin, I swear it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vargon", "indy58", "name:Vargon\n \nAge:37 \nMedical info:Taint of Iblees shows up some times but will be cured soon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vargon's profile", "indy58", "Age:45 Hight:5 foot Race:Dwarf personality:Smart and fun loving.Can be serious when needed favourite weapon:Swords Likes:Other Dwarves,mining,lava,diamond,riches Dislikes:Orcs,Bandits,Undead,Annoying people Biography:He was small when he joined the holmes,Hiding in a church.He thinks he was accepted Because Bastion was interested in his name,as holmes were on lock down. Other info:None", ""),
        StaticBook("Vargon's View", "indy58", "My personality:Brave sneaky,childish and dwarven:) My goals:Arrest an Undead and bring him to justice. What i would enjoy doing:Detective:P", ""),
        StaticBook("Vargon's view 2", "indy58", "If this little dwarf were to describe himself,I would say funny,annoying and foolishly brave. My goals?Justice,mining diamond/gold and being a good dwarf. I would like to be a detective and I qualify as one,too. I qualify because of my eavesdropping skill and ability to stay hidden when needed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Varstivus's Journal", "tthorn3", "Hello, if you are reading this you have found my journal. I put all my recapies in here  in case I am ever to forget them. What are the chances of that though? Anyhow, on to the subject I am writing today. Nether wart. It is the basis for all potions, however it is held by only a few, powerful individuals. In other words no one can make potions without their say so. I understand that you must be very rich to get some of this material . This material is a primer, almost all potions are based off of it. \n I have been finding it hard to get my hands on any of this stuff let alone other potion materials . \nI have just been accepted as a battlemage! Oh happy day! As the Apothecary I shouldn't h ave to fight much, but I am told to train a bit more with my sword \nDay 2: I met a wonderful human named Camou today. He even offered me a home in his township. This seems fishy though. He's too polite. I'm not sure I should trust him. Just in case, I did not tell him I am a battlemage. He doesn't seem to recognise the rune so I think I'm safe.   For now that is. \nI have heard that the high princess's adopted orc son was taken by orcs today. The problem is that I was there and did NOTHING. I feel horrible. I must be as bad as one of those humans... only taking action when they see themselve's in danger. Thankfully the child agreed to go with the orcs before any more blood was shed. I feel sorry for the child, but I also feel sorry for those who were wounded in the battle. \nDay 3: I hear there are undead attacking, However I value my life. I do not wish to join as I value my life. \n I finally decided to go to Alras to battle the undead. I feel that I made the right decision in the end. I am still recovering from a slash to the knee from an insane man who was trying to kill one of my patients! The gall of him! he had injured his leg in the battle and couldn't move well so I numbed his wound with some watermelon juice, and a splint.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vault Chest Sconn ((sconn)) 2x chest [paid 2000 minas]]", "Shadowninji", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Vault Information", "HoovHoovie", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Vem's Adventures", "krist110", "Hi if you are reading this then, you shouldn't so go away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Venchello's 2nd Diary", "Lord_Venchello", "Sadly, My First Book.. Of which i had a copy of, On me. Was Lost. Now whoever has found it, will know all of my research. And my personal Thoughts. Then again, There wasnt Much in there, But the Thief and the Strange eyed Rosea Lady. Interesting Though, I've Come Across Supplies that were better than my old. Heh, With these i've made a NEW Book. And will continue to write about what i see. \n I've Made a Copy Of this Book, It is hidden in a place only i know of. \n People have found my Copy of the Diary. If they are not ally, they will die. \n My Home is now complete, I've always lived in the wild. But not i live in luxary. My Order protects the area, And i supply Sugar Cane and Wheat to those who wander by. I could not find a job, So i made one of my own. Now i need Permits for mining. These are my new goals. I also need Minas and More help. Venture on i shall.", ""),
        StaticBook("Venchello's Diary", "Lord_Venchello", "Day 1: I can feel, See, Smell.. Everything seems.. Alive now.  Before felt much like a dream. I've wandered these lands for years. But no one knew i was even near them. Almost as if.. I were some sort of phantom OR ghost. \n Day 2: I've left a temple of which i was located. Wandering the land.. I was lost. Met a few fellows along the way. Looks nice, well.. kind of. Not really.. These men surrounded me, telling me not to move.. and that they would kill me if i did.. They wanted my money. Which i had none of. The only thing i had.. was a strange Item. I tried to get out of the matter unhurt.. Sadly. A Mage of some sort struck me with lighting, and i soon passed out. Waking up again - At the Temple. \n Day 3: Theres much i haven't Written in these Books. Things i cant remember ,But i try my best. I am currently Looking for work. Which is hard to come by . I have no home.. No job. No food or money. The Road to darkness.. is easy. but does not pay off in the end. I MUST find a good paying work. ~ Side Note, A man named Garret. Seems to trap his homes. And is a Secret Theif. ~ \n Seems i've come across an Elvin Village. Sadly i do not know if im welcomed. Elves Have many nice homes for sale.. None in my Price range though. Pigman Attacked me in City limits when gambling with four others. Sadly i was wounded.. When i returned all that i carried was gone. \n Dear Diary, Vardak is CRAZY! Dilara_Von_Rosea, (( Lotteje13)) Has a dark future ahead of her.. it. Haha.. \n Day 16: I have a new Goal. My power.. Must Grown. A strong Army.. is about to awake.", ""),
        StaticBook("Veneton's Improvement Ideas", "EgXPlayer", "In this book I will show you,how to improve New Terriko. First of all,We need to use the free space near to the gates as farm land.I will explain now,why. Then we need to build some Starter Inns.The new citizen would go to our city and live there.We will give them bread(thats the reason of the farm) and they would trust us.They will be patriotic.After they have earned the money,to buy a plot of land a build a house,we should tell them to join the Army.(With signs in the City).Of course they will,they are patriots.Our nation will get bigger.Big Nation and a big Army means power and thats what we want! Since I dont know how to improve mistakes,Im sorry xD Jordan Hope you wont forget it xD Ehh", ""),
        StaticBook("Veneton's Improvement Ideas [2]", "EgXPlayer", "In this book I will continue my ideas of the first book. In the first one,I told you about making your city bigger,then your army. Thats not all though.What you need now,is that Army/Citizen got the motivation,so they wont leave in bad times. For the motivation of the army,you should have greetings like \"Hail Terriko\",\"Hail Wolverine\".With that,the motivation should grow. In peace and war times,you should give them bread/food. The citizen's motivation should grow by events/giveaways and stuff like that,where they can meet the Major and the HC members. Their motivation will grow too,if they could vote for the HC members and the Major. Thats the base of democracy and democracy is THE motivation for the people to stay here. Also,they should have the feeling of beeing protected.Thats why you need guards at each gate.If your city will grow,other nations will notice that and send spys to your nation.Thats why you need a very good protection.", ""),
        StaticBook("Verigan's Knighthood Guide", "Spartan216", "If you wish to be a knight you must first have done a good worthy deed to and recieve no reward. Second you must have joined or made a kingdom or group of fellow knights. Third advertise your services and ask for a small reward. Example 50 minas or less. If you are challenged you shall go by the rules of Chivalary and not cheat. If you break the code of honor you will be considered a 'Evil knight' aka a recreant knight. Fourth find a lord or prince of a land to serve . And Fifth always be kind to others even if they are'nt to you. Follow this Guide and you shall be a Succesful knight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Veritable story", "bluedude10", "To day i was in second place in the Tournament in Al\"kalzer it was a hard fight. -Day one- There are two teams when they fight they till they are almost dead then get warped out when we Almost kill the other team we have to fight are own team. Leafwind won this time i get it next Time. -Day Two- I found out a undead was hiding in the city he has a purple and black robe on he Tryed to get this book im writing in. he chased me threw two towns i lost him. I got pit in jail because i ran away from a guard and open the dity gate not my best day. I might get exiled from the city if i do what this guys does not want me to do tough day. Day five. I saw the princess today she kept looking at me nawn stop sort of freaked me out. A man has a sword in my face today not doing to well in this city. The undead thing is back. He has green eyes and is hiding in the city Im keeping an eye on him he seems he does not want them to know hes Undead he might try to He might be getting stuff so he and other undead can raid the city.", ""),
        StaticBook("Verrenn's alchemy book", "verrenn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Verrenn's journal", "verrenn", "I love her... but it is getting harder to see her because of zatazen... i dont think she loves me though... i would like to know but... i think it would be odd to  ask her if she loved me or not... i guese i sould get over it or ask ... if i get the chance to ask that is i most likely wont because of kendra and zatazen but i have a little bit of an advantage they love each other so we can seperate for awile tortering them alittle but... zatazen gets the best of me i can never withstand him he is eather", ""),
        StaticBook("verrenn's story of oren.", "verrenn", "*sigh* No one is of any help. i have conntacted the holmes, and i have conntacted the oren guard but... i dont think they balieve what i have seen. I have seen the robed figures and the are pale... i have spent a week now spying on them and i have got evidence... i just... dont know how i would give it to the guards and holmes i am stuck in a crevice i have only 2 ways to go try to stop the undead or just let it go but if i let it go this city is probobly doomed but if i try to take on the undead i know i will die. maby it is best i just... let it go .", ""),
        StaticBook("verrenns jurnal", "verrenn", "day 1 in oren \n maby city life isnt so good... i hate my curiosity and the undead are in the city... \n well thats the end of this day... i dont know how long i can live here without a home...", ""),
        StaticBook("Verses of Aegis.", "Toto798", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Very Important", "mylimo7", "\"There was Zebana, Something the wise, like Wilfred Wilfred The wise.\" That all I am for sure.", ""),
        StaticBook("VERY IMPORTANT READ ASAP", "Ever", "hide yo kids, hide yo wife", ""),
        StaticBook("Vigleiven", "Vigleiven", "Hello, my name is Vigleiven. I don't like people that don't like me, so I destroy them. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vigleiven's Diary", "Vigleiven", "I am writing this at Castle Lykos. 21st of The First Seed, 1326.  Several months back, at the cold winter in Al'Khazar, I was shopping around in the trade district.    I met a man called Will, he invited me to his cause. We traveled for days, we e tired. Finally we got to their shack. I lived there for weeks.  There e 3 brances in the organisation. The bow which is a group of supportive hunters, the sword which was the fighing branch filled with mercenaries. And finally the knife which was the spy section of it. I was in the bow section, I slew monsters for a living. I wasn't really allowed to do much. Then we started building a castle and we moved there. The castle was named Castle Lykos, from our leader Lykos. I lived there for months. I was treated badly, only people I liked there was Will Chapman and Redbain. Rest of them  were total bastards. I got all me stuff and ran to Al'Khazar. Today is 31st of The Second Seed, 1326. I prayed at the Temple of Horen. I am now going to my new home, far away in the North. May I meet Will or Redbain again. Farewell, it's a long walk. It's early morning, I am leaving Al'Khazar. It's day, I'm in the forests Nort of Oren. The landscape is beautiful, it never was like this before! I have hit snow! It got alot colder, ahh I'm going to stand it ho. I found another wall, this one is wooden. I found a large ocean, I must make a boat and sail now. It's day two, the weather is sunny and tropical. I can hear the seagulls singing at the shore. I have hit a desert, I am already starting to get thirsty. I'm ontop of a massive cliff! The wind be massive! I found a lava lake near a forest. I'm here! I can see the beautiful wooden structures from a far distance! It appears to be empty. I set up a few melon and wheat farms. I met the two men at the base. They are kind, we get along well. We began building lots of buildings, a smithy, docks a tavern. It's storming and cold, I am building the tavern alone. The tavern is finally finished, well, almost. I need to add some finishing touches to it. I have build a ship! I'm on a boat. I started bulding a guild house, for the officers or normal recruits to stay in. 14th of Malins Welcome, 1326, noone's at the base. I now claim the house meself. It's mine!", ""),
        StaticBook("Vigleiven's Journal.", "Vigleiven", "Irba, 18th of Snows Maiden, 1327. \n \n My name is Vigleiven Auldwind, I be keeping this journal to write my adventures in. Today is a sunny day, nothing of interest is happening.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vikram Mournstone", "Alectriciti", "Vikram Mournstone completed both initiate course and advanced course on the day he was recruited. He has shown service, but his motives behind the servant heart seem disturbing. write He recently asked for a rank up. We have to be careful with this one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Village of Dunwood", "MrZombez", "Dunwood, village of the Halflings. It is found west of the grand city of Al'Khazar, past the Golden Harvest Headquarters. Is is situated between the mountain named Elduren, and the old ruins. It is there that the Halflings can reside in peace, avoiding the hustle and bustle of the big cities , and having the solitude of the closed gate community. Members of the community all work together , sharing the profits and fruits of the land. The people of Dunwood are very close, they are friendly to one another, and are willing to share their findings with the community, storing them in warehouses throughout the village. \n The town itself is a lush, grassy and hilly area. The homes that dot the land are built into the small hills, keeping warmth during the winter and sound dampening, reducing annoyances from neihbours.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vincents accident", "vice7", "when I was a mere twenty years old I was a miner in the dwarven capital. I was mining with some friends when we found a rich diamond vien. My friend named kalgrin didnt particulary want to mine it all out though. So he pitched the idea to use his fathers TNT to blow out all the diamonds. I thought it to be a foolish idea. But by the time I had turned around they were already placing the TNT in massive quanities. i thought they were fools  so i watched them place well over 200 blocks of tnt around the diamonds. When they were finshed Kalgrin dropped a torch by accident and lit the TNT. The fuse was just long enough for us to get behind some blast shields I had set up. but i realized all to late that my above average hieght as a dwarf was about to cripple me forever. the blast shields were designed to be  exactly 5ft tall. I was 5 3/4 ft tall. i had realized this the very moment before the explosion, but could not react in time. The TNT did work, too well in fact. It had shattered the diamonds and turned the shards of diamond into shrapnel. The explosion had knocked me unconscious. when i awoke the i was in the dwarven hospital. my friends were standing around me, Kalgrin with tears in his eyes. The doctor walked in with with a sad look on his face. and tole me. that the explosion had lodged 7 large and serrated shards of diamond in my neck. the shards were located in midst of my vocalchords, and would cut them slightly if i spoke. By the will of god the shards were oriented in a way that i could speak very briefly. but excessive talking would cause my vocalchords to rub against the serrated shards. Causing me to bleed profusely, and cough up massive amounts of blood the pain was unbearable, and there was nothing the doctors could do. After hearing this Klagrin was inconsoleable he kept screaming \" WHAT HAVE I DONE\" he could bearly speak through his tears after he had stopped screaming. he kept apoligizing to me, over and over day after day. for weeks he did this. while i was in the hospital i only said one thing to him after that. \" if you want me to forgive you then bring me a large silver ribbon made of silk. He was perplexed why i had asked him to bring me such an odd item but he did so, eager to be forgive n when he brought me the long ribbon. I tied it around my neck to hide the horrid scar the shards had made. \"I may not have the ability to speak anymore. But i will not allow the world to see this scar as a sign of my crippledness.\" i had written this down on paper for all to see. when kalgrin was finished this aloud. I tore the paper from his hand and cast it into the fire of the hearth in my room. I stood, towering above all my friends and doctors. with rage in my eyes. with one swift movement of my hand i had grabbed my pickaxe, and brought its flat side against kalgrins thick iron helmet. burying in in the thick meatl of his mining helmet. I was careful not to kill him though, I would not let my anger consume me in such a way. i picked up my pickaxe, helmet still attached and with a quick motion of my hand i  knocked  the helmet free. I then walked out of the hospital much to the worry of my doctors. I reached the main hall of the dwarven capital. People stared and gaped at my size and imposing disposition. and the crowd quickly made a path for me to walk through, i did with my head held high, and my pickaxe slung across my back. i walked out of the capital and towards my new life in the world of aegis, and for thirty years not looked back. now at age fifty, still very young in dwarven years i ventured back to the dwarven city. and here i stay ever looking for who or what my father was. accident or not, by the will of god i recieved this curse of silence. I have become stronger because of it. Nothing can stop me now... as i write this i remember this one saying i would say in when i was very young. it was... Cry havoc and let slip the dogs of war!", ""),
        StaticBook("Violetta's Krugmar", "ViolettaUnicorn", "Well, Krugmar.. Orc lands.. A sandy land.. The green skinned inhabitants are kind of Violent.. The land is quite filled with sandstone.. Well.. there are about three building styles if im working it out correctly.. Each one is in another town In Sanjezal.. The capital.. The walls are sandstone and inside the city there arwe red and black wool rooves.. I know i shoulod not know that. As its a place for only orcs.. I will carry on writing when im out of this place! (Im hiding in an orc cave! Im standing in Sanhar now.. One of the main towns of Krugmar.. a great sprawl of sandstone and cactus' You can definatly tell sanhar is Orcish.. its all quite foul and dangerous with all the cactus' And its a maze! especailly the slums! Go there to see the confusion! The strangest town in Krugmar is the Gorkil town It looks like any other town.. all stone I must say.. the outside doesnt look orcy at all... But inside its the usal sandy affair In the restricted area of the Gorkil town there is a strange monument of colourful wools and gems and things.. A magical floating peice of stone marks the enterance to the Restricted area. I have decided to write a book on each Kingdom i go in my travels! Thank you for reading my Krugmar Guide", ""),
        StaticBook("Viridian Gambling Slip -20 minas", "AutarchCosmos", "This slip can be traded in at 'The Viridian' for a sum of 20 minas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Visions.", "Brevias", "I saw a wolf, hunting in the snowy forrests north of the Kingdom of Oren. It was killing and devouring pigs at an alarming rate. After every pig it would devour, it would grow fatter, slower, and even started to turn a bit pink...   He had turned into a pig himself, and was devoured by another wolf. \n  In this vision I saw a vast desert. It was barren, except for cacti scattered in the distance. One cacti began to move. I seemed to grow appentheges, and move about. Eventually all the cacti began to grow limbs and move about the desert. This reminded me of the orcish people.  Immitating their love for the desert.", ""),
        StaticBook("Visitor list", "Pepernoot", "-Ebs\n-High King Syrio\n-Aulus\n-Valon\n-Nashtoff\n-Dom\n-Ambros\n -Wyvernos \n-Brandon Roze  \n-Tot\n -Bito\n -Rivell Gordian\n -Wyvernos\n -Haelphon\n   -Rio Coconuts\n -Estaro Ithelias\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Magic", "XBLxSNAZZLEZ", "Indelwhen was explaining that some man was using Void Magic. This is when I first heard of it. She came to the mage's tower, and began speaking to Ambros about the matter.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vokarius' Strang Travels VI", "Vokarius", "I came upon a place called Libertas. Never had I seen such a place like this. Now I stand before a watchtower of Adradrome. Who or what are the Adradrome? The fortress before me is massive, with red As I stared at the large fortress before me, I was set upon by a large force of pigmen I barely survived with my life. With the coming of daylight I was hoping I would be safe! The gates of the city of Adradrome were still closed to me. I yelled and shouted. No one came. I decided to explore around the great walls of this city. I found entrance by swimming the bay and entering one of the towers. I entered the city with peaceful intentions, but with my sword close at hand. The city was creepy in how empty it was. I found a ship in the bay being constructed. I decided to make a camp there. The monster attacks outside the city had been brutal. I was concerned about night travel. This city was huge, but still being built. I knew nothing about it. Who lived here? Where were the builders? Mysteries upon mysteries. When the sun rose, I would leave this place and continue my journey. As the sun came up, I left this new city, heading onward. Now I gaze upon a great tree that appears to have builds built into and upon it. I must know more. It will likely be dangerous The great tree is used by someone named Drixyt. I will seek this person out. I did not find the owner, but I found the guest room. The great tree is hollowed out. And huge. It could hold a whole city by itself. Bigger than even the great trees back home. And under the tree, under the water, I found a room of glass. A secret layer? Who knows. No, the glass room is a temple to some god or goddess, unknown. I leave this holy place with a sense of peace. And then I was finally to the village of Libertas. A small village, made of mostly wood and filled with dogs. Literally, there were hounds everywhere. Lots of plots for sell also. Libertas was a quaint town, small, but hopefully growing. I continue on my travels. In the dead of night, I came upon a beautiful garden, with a stone fountain. Surronded by zombies I hid in one of the buildings, protected by the light. Who had built this random structure? And near that beautiful garden, I looked upon a desert and fire. Hellfire and darkness. Fire from the evils of hell it appeared. What was it I looked upon? An undead fortress? I did not know. I had never seen such an odd mixture. Lava, hellstone, and... fields of wheat for miles. What was this place? There had to be a evil portal around here with all of that hellstone. But all of this farming and foodstuff could feed an army. I tried, but I found no hellgate. It would have been nice to been able to tell the others where one was so it could have been closed. I have travelled so far the world is covered in snow and the sea ice. It is cold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Volas's Journal", "urpenguin", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Volthias' Diary", "NeonVolcom", "?", ""),
        StaticBook("Volthias' Journal", "NeonVolcom", "Day 1. A young elf gave me a loaf of bread today. He looks around 25 years of age. He welcomed me into his home, told me he would take care of me. He's the only nice person I've met since my village was burnt to the ground. He calls me his little brother. He feeds me, he clothes me he even took me to a large Elven city. I forget the name, but the city was beautiful. Day 8 My big brother took me to the ocean today! We spent the whole day fishing, I caught over five different fish! My brother was so proud of me! Day 62 My brother and I are building a tree fort! Day 116 I love my big brother Twilight! He bought me a new sword! I can't wait to kill those big spiders he tells me to stay away from", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume 1 - Zombies; the Walking Dead", "Lord_Kashi", "The first type of monster I encountered upon my travels in Aegis was the most common, but dangerous nonetheless. Some like to call them The Walking Dead, others prefer the term Zombies. The beasts are recently deceased people, whose souls have been taken by the undead as they died, and are not allowed to pass through to be with Aeriel. They are still covered in skin, though it is rotten on many, and unruly to look at. Some wear the chainmail armour they were buried with, some carry decorative weaponry; though none know how to use it, as they all fight with their fists. Some may prefer to take the armour or weapons for themselves, others may prefer to take only money. The Walking Dead will, like all other creatures of the night, disintegrate upon death, so you will know when you have killed it... \n I have recently discovered these monsters are known as Zombies", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume one Rezolio journal", "Rumplestilts", "Entry one: Still trying to gain status as swift elf. Trying to explore but finding it difficult", ""),
        StaticBook("Von Hollow's rise to power", "Green_Mind", "A magical book was handed to me today. The one I am currently writing in. Yet, not neccesarily the same. It is of power unknown to me.. Most fascinating! \n I was told by the elf who so kindly gave it to me for free, to write this journal, about anything that crossed my mind. Therefore. I will write my story, and how I came to power, or how I lost it before I had the chance to gain anything at all. \n \n Day one: I will start my journal at this point. Myself and some volunteered workers I found in the city has spent the last two weeks building a manor. And how glorious it turned out to be. It is indeed worthy of my ambitions to gain vast power and fortune. to acomplish this, I plan to establish a town centered around my manor. With time, people will shout my name, hailing me as the mayor of the town I've established. From there on out, I'm sure to gain some level of influence on the world. One way or another. \n On a different note: The last two weeks has been eventfull, but one thing caught my attention. Several attacks by the undead with increasing numbers each time, has left me worried. What do they want? \n I'm sure time will tell... DAY 7: We have established the outer border of what is soon to be a thriving village. I met a writer who lives across the lake, and promptly asked him to come live with us. He said he would think about it for a few days. Hopefully, he'll accept. We need writers capable of filling entire libraries with their black-inked words. DAY:19 A few people have joined the ever-growing village, and much has been built allready. We have set up farms, and it looks like it's going to be a rich harvest. We have yet to name the village. DAY 24: An increasing numbers of wolves have entered our land. This has lead to the unfortunate death of many sheeps. Our hunters have been unable to find the pack. Some say it's not even regular wolves, their tracks are much bigger. I'm sure there's nothing to worry about. Day 49: The high king of Alras has requested a meeting with me. I do not know what he wants to discuss. But I assume it has something to do with the current expansion of Alras. There have been regular sightings of the beast, and it appears it only comes at night. I have yet to see the thing myself. Some of the villagers believe it to be a creature of legends, a so called \"Werewolf\". I'm not certain I agree with them. They have started forging weapons of silver in various forms. It's madness.", ""),
        StaticBook("VonEbs' Will", "VonEbs", "In the case that I have died, I want to give you, my friends and family, directions on what to do with my estate. Firstly, I wish to give Aedan, a dragonlord, my gold sword, so he can protect his family. Next, I give Indelwehn my Timepiece. I was never late when I wore this. I hope it serves you as well as it has served me. The entirety of the remaining estate, the house in old Laurelin, the ranch, my stores, and my books, will go to my nephew, Nicolas. The book, Afterthoughts, is to go to my beloved Felore, who has done so much for me. To her, I also give my compass. I hope she will never lose her way with this in her pocket. Finally, I give my first bow to Felore, who strung it for me all those years ago when we met.", ""),
