        StaticBook("Vrild", "c_h_r_i_s121", "He was a dwarf, and like all dwarfs he was very small, he had a ginger beard and a silver helmet. He was some how assosiated with the clan Drograk . But i am yet to find out how, i must keep praying. I think he worked for them.. No! It wasn't work. He was.. A slave yes, he is tellin' me now, he was a slave to the clan, he said he worked in the mines . He mined and, smithed for the clan, his main mineral was gold and he made the best and most ornate jewelery in the land. But seeming he was a slave no one paid him for it. . Infact i think he made some items for Gorthok and Dragga, they where a Golden pin for Dragga, and two golden bands for both of Gorthoks muscular arms. He says he was very good friends with them, infact they tried to help him escape slavery Dragga and Gorthok devised a brilliant plan. Vrild slept in a small tent next to his masters larger one with a chain and ball straped round his ankle it was heavy enough that only another orc could carry it . There plan all started on a cold night, there was a thick layer of fog wich was unusual for the desert , they waited for every one to fall asleep and snook into Vrilds tent Gorthok carried the ball and Dragga lifted Vrild onto her sholders . They must of carried im for 10 minuets atleast he said , and when they stopped Gorthok pulled out a spell book and fireballed the chain off the ball, unfortunatly he coulnt get the band off his leg so he left it on . Dragga pointed out the nearest city and he left Vrild never saw them again.", ""),
