        StaticBook("w Haradrias' Biography", "Keksbendiger", "I was born 439 years ago. My father Edrym studied the lore of the world and my mother Valindra leaded an Inn. It was a nice Inn, so many Humans from Oren, like the famous merchant Sir Louis William Rockland, came to stay there. All rooms had 2-3 windows that you could watch the beautiful view of Malinor. The Inn was high in the trees, so you thought, you can touch the clouds. My parents bought a big house in the middle of Malinor, the highest in the trees. It was the best place to get a look over all places of Malinor. Valindra was sad, that she didn't build her Inn there. We had a large balcony between the leaves of the tree. In front of the entrance to our house we had our own Guards. They had to let people in or kick them out, when they were unwanted. My little friends came", ""),
        StaticBook("Wahsrofs Journal", "Wahsrof", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Walking Blight, the story of Kazen", "IlumTarus", "His hand spun as he held the hilt of his blade The soft smack of meat on dirt was heard Kazen sat down in the pool of blood, a bone splinter was in his closed lips, his eyes closed He thought to himself admist the gore and gib around him, \"How'd it come to this?\" His eyes twitched, a voice pierced what was left of his concious \"It was always me\"  \n CHAPTER ONE Flashbacks The sounds of the slight scrawls of scribes and children were heard, Kazen sat in the front of his class, head down, as he dipped his feather into the inkwell The Master of the Class quietly walked up and down the halls, lecturing, \"Long ago the great one forged the world as we knew it In his lonesome world, he splintered, and made company\" The man moved a chalk stick, showing a diagram from one, to many \"These splinters were the elements, and in relfect themselves, they had the power of Great one\" Turned to the class a bit, \"In time, they grew tired of their own company They made people to  relfect themselves Each differant in their own way\" He drew more branches down the diagram, which began to look like a tree \"Some served the gods, diligently Others were more wicked, so they stole fire from the gods\" These words echoed through Kazen asthough he were hollow Steal fire from the gods \n CHAPTER TWO Omniscent Voices Kazen quietly sat outside on the school yard, he was chewing on a leaf that made him particularly pe rky \"Hey! You! Quiet kid!\" Kazen turned over quietly to a tall menacing man, who was taller then him signifcantly \"Your the kids whos parents were banished?\" Kazen didn't reply, he looked down and continued to chew \"I was talking to you dirtbag\" The kid sent his hand over Kazen's head, clasping it, and tossing hi m back Kazen bounced off the ground a bit and sighed \"Yeah Can you leave me be? I'm not proud of that part of my family's history\" The kid pointed and laughed, \"Hah! I told ya'! This kids the descendant of dark bloods!\" A few others joined in, Kazen felt his eyes closing to block them out \"Kill them\" A voice echoed from the deepest parts of his skull His eyes jumped open, flinging left to right asthough there were something on them he was shaking  off  Kazen's eyes shot left and right again No one would talk to me- where does this emenate from ? \"I emenate from you. Your gift. Your tool of malace powered by hate and yearning of blood. \"  \n CHAPTER THREE. Reality. Kazen took a long, deep breath, asthough he hadn't had air in so long. He'd come to notice whatever was inside him took over himself when he was away. He woke up next to two more bodies. A man and women. He choked on some sobs a bit. \"I can't control this, I'm in way over my head!\" Sent his fist at the puddle of blood around him, letting the blood fly up in retaliation. \"I just wanted them to stop- I wanted peace. Now I have nothing!\" The voice rang from his skull, \"You have me- and as long as you do, you'll have piece. Pieces of people, that is.\" \"I hate you, Elieon...\" \"Watch your tongue, boy. That word is powerful in the wrong hands and knowledge.\" CHAPTER FOUR. Going on with life. Kazen stepped forward, out of the body strewn field he was in. He was hunted, he'd always be hunted. No matter what Elieon said he'd never have peace. He was cursed. Long ago his family stome from the fire god, giving it to the Dark God. The Dark God returned the favor, giving them a wealth of power. Although, this power was at c ost. Demons posessed these people in order to give them power. It lingered in bloodlines.", ""),
        StaticBook("wallace the ninja is cool", "tomf1982", "i sit here, trapped on a small safety tower i built to keep safe as i am waiting for my friend (who died throught the night) i sit here, waiting. wondering when will he return?. its been a while now i dont know if he is coming. i saw what i thought was a torch in the distance. i wondered if i should wait or if i should civilisation. I chose to wait/ im running away from the monastery! they kept me as hostage and they made me do all their jobs for them! they said that i would become the earth monk! ye hright! im running now for the inn! i just passed one of the members! \"WHERE ARE U GOING?\" he said, i told him i was going to the shops im on the kings road now, on my way back to the inn!", ""),
        StaticBook("Wallace's Bible", "tomf1982", "This is the holy word of the Ascended Wallace, it will tel you the right things to do by your will. Now, please read on, to ensure you live a good and holy life - Wallace Chapter 1 - Introduction of Wallace Wallace, he was born a little south of Al,Khazar and lived there through his childhood he lived on a farm, with little to do, so all day he would practice combat skills with a scarecrow i n the field. One day, a skeleton attacked him in the house. He grabbed his wooden sword and fended it off until i t fell. He finished the skeletons life with one stab. He wondered \"How did the skeleton get in?\" \"Did not my father see the skeleton?\" so he rushed downstairs to see his father and Mother. They were gone. Wallace was scared and confused he was by himself out on a farm, kilometres away from town. He was panicing. So he grabbed his sword and some food and he rushed to the city of Al,Khazar. There were lots of people there telling him he was a scrub, a nobody, that he should leave. So he did he ran very far past aegis and the cloud temple, and eventually he got lost and found what seemed to be an inn there, he found a dwarf, named alex, who let him stay. He stayed at the inn, he liked the community there so he stayed. and he has lived at the inn ever since i just finished the first chapter of my book! it has 5 pages! oh.. crap", ""),
        StaticBook("Wallace's File", "nachotp", "Name: Wallace \n Job: Farmer \n Age: 22 \n Halfling \n [MC Name: tom1982 ]", ""),
        StaticBook("Wandering Soul", "WizardInACan", "*Note* Actual story* UPon entering this world I was left with no task, no hope of anything. I wandered around doing nothing. Till one day when I was at the docks and I saw four men. Three of which , swords drawn, circled around the fourth. I saw the excitement of them arresting, him fleeing and all of us chasing him. Sadly he disappeared. I wanted those mens lives as a Holmes. I was accepted and have never been happier or filled with so much pride. My first job was clear, take Greed in for questioning, though it was not so easy. There was no succes in our mission. I did however find my enemy. I started to do some detective work. I found out some much. I was selfish and prideful wanting it all. to myself. But I was respectful knowing my leaders would want to know this information. And that is where my stoey ends and my life begins. MY goals are to defeat Greed, become lead detective one day, and to own my own shop. I view myself as stubborn, but humble. Selfish at times. I take pride in my work and I am very respectful, since I was raised as a warrior. I knew what respect is. I would enjoy doing what my dream is, to  become Head Detective. Yours truly, Molta", ""),
