        StaticBook("What happened? What did I do Wrong?", "TheRedNinja", "I dont know, im just lost I have tried everything. I reform the Government, Fix the guards, Rebuild Al'khazar from the ground up with my own hands I made a tax system to help pay the guards, but no they said the taxes were to high. I rescinded the tax reformation and decided to supply the gurd from new buildings in Al'khazar That failed... Failed to stop the Riots, Failed to stop the books... I talked with the men of the print, at first they wanted to kill me, but soon started to help It isnt enough... They took Snowyfields, the town which Oren didnt claim I sent what i could to aid them. It wasnt enough... They took Alstion I didnt have the men All i had was a feeble Guard I hear shouting, whispers of Hatred, they want my head grimbeard was a enemy but really a friend I sent suppies and men to rebuild and defend Alstion the best we could It isnt enough why why isnt it enough nothing will apease the masses the Undead i can hear the bones rattleing the lightning striking I took the Undeads Fort why why didnt that help they just rebuilt closer The Undead ruined me Undead why. why wasnt it enough The undead will pay I will go north far to the North I put my High Priest in charge Until if i return....", ""),
        StaticBook("What he did", "Rhisereld", "You were from the North, I was from the South   \nWe were from opposite places, different towns \nBut I knew it was good, and you knew it was too \n \nSo we moved together like a ball and chain \nMinds becoming two halves of the same \nIt was real, but in the shadows it grew  \nBecause you've got a secret \nDon't you babe? \n \nI would have shouted aloud, broken through \nI would've given it all to belong to you \nBut there were different plans and different rules \n \n You said, \"Where I'm from there's a lock and key \nIf you'd be so kind as to follow me \nI will show you the way to the rest of my sins.\" \nBecause you've got a secret, don't you babe? \nYes, you've got a secret, don't you babe? \nAnd I should know \nYes, I should know \n \nSo this room was damp where your sins laid  \nThere was that smell in the air of an old place \nThat hadn't seen much daylight in years \nAnd you threw me down, said, \"If you don't mind, \nI'm gonna leave you here until night time \nThen we can do what we want, my baby, \nOut of the spotlight.\" \n \nBecause you've got a secret, don't you babe? \nYeah, you've got a secret, don't you babe? \nAnd I should know, oh \nYeah, I should know  \n \nFor I am your secret \nAren't I, babe? \nYeah, I am your secret \nAren't I, babe?", ""),
