        StaticBook("Whidoc's Journal", "braner321", "((Back story: Son of the Halfling, Biodoc Goodbody, Whidoc is an eager lad with a yearing for knowledge. Back in his original home of the port town, Nepo, Whidoc spent many hours tinkering with many things. He also had a collection of books that sadley he had to leave back in Nepo. This journal is a recolection of things that have happened to Whidoc. The journal starts with Whidoc sitting on the ship, ready to leave for Aegis.  )) \n Day 1 ((really Day -4)): Well, this is it. Good bye Port-Town of Nepo. I will miss you dearly. Today I set off for the land of Aegis. The land where my father has settled in. He sent me a letter a few days ago requesting that now is the time for me to move from our home in Nepo to his new home in a Halfling village called Dunwood. He speaks well of it and it's Ale. He says that there are many friendly people there. He tells me that the Elders of Dunwood have agreed to my arival and that I shall be welcomed in as one of the villagers right away. My father also told me in his letter that the land of Aegis is full of much Magic. Magic. The word just makes me wonder of what I may come to encounter with my arival....Oh, orc brains ((Nepodian swear)) the Captain is requesting that all passengers assist up deck. Well, I guess this cheap ride had to have some catch. \n Day 2: No time to write, I must continue working. The seas are rough. Rougher then any storm that has ever gone through Nepo. \n Day 3: Food...Not a morsale has been seen since the first day. Cheap buggars are trying to kill us I swear. *drawing of a nice, hot porkchop and a glass of frosty ale* \n Day 4: The Captain, that buggar. He was hording all the food for himself. A mutiny occured and was resolved with the dismisal of the Captain....Forcefully. He was tied to the mast. A new Captain has taken his place. He gave us what was rightfully ours. I ate so much! Then again, when don't I. I have done more thinking of the Magic that was mentioned...One of the stories in my father's letter was of A Great Wandering Wizard. He said that he was odd...But more powerful then any being in Aegis. *Drawing of a robed figure looking at the moon on a grassy hill* \n Day 5 ((First day in the lands of Aegis)): I arrived in the port of the human city, Al'Khazar. It was a very busy port. I stopped at a bakery owned by a lady by the name of Dawn. I had an apple and a porkchop. I also had a mug of her ale. It tasted very sweet. I liked it, when I get the chance I'll have to have some more another time. The next item on my agenda was to find me father. He said to meet him at the King's Cross in the city. I found it pretty fast. Many people were there conversing. I waited, and waited, and waited. Eventually a man by the name of Tom Proudfoot came into the City shouting. He was shouting about something, I couldn't hear him well so I got closer. If only I had known....*tear drops stain the page* I aproached closer to learn that...that...a bandit had killed my father...His body was found on the side of the King's Road. He had many stab wounds, his pockets empty and his fists clentched and bruised on the knuckles. I assume that meant that he died punching the bandit who probobly had armor on.... Not even a day in Aegis, and my own father was murdered...Some great place to live. After identifying the body as my father's, I went to the bar and drank...and drank...and drank. The ale burned my throat by the time I was done and my eyes hurt from the tears. I bumped into Tom who I then asked, drunk and all, where my father had his house. He lead my to Dunwood. Here, I found my father's house. It was lovely. I could tell that if he hadn't died that I would be happy here. I found my father's room. I cried myself to sleep in his bed. \n Day 6: I woke up today to the sound of my stomach growling. I checked the pantry, but found no food. I then searched my father's chest and found an old, battered, short ((right size for a halfling)) sword. I then went out to get breakfast. While killing the many pigs the littered the land, I noticed an odd looking pig. He looked sickly, so I was going to put him out of his misery. I made a grave mistake. Little did I know that the \"sickly\" pig was a decaying Pig Man of some sort. I was greeted by the slaughtering of this pig by many others like him. I was never so scared in my life. So I ran. I managed to kill a few that were close. But I still decided on running. I ran inside my father's, I mean, my house....feels odd saying that... I grabbed a set of iron armor that was a little big on me. Probobly big on my father too. I put it on and killed the rest of the decaying Pig Men that had followed me to Dunwood. I then saw another Halfling. I followed him into town, forgetting I had my armor on. He turned around and started screaming ghost. I ran after him, scared out of my breeches upon thinking there was a ghost behind me. He then turned around and started sayying that it couldn't be and that Biodoc was dead...stupid me. I then took my helmet off to reveal that I was not Biodoc. I introduced myself to him. He said his name was Petyr. The lad my father spoke so much of in his letters. At that moment an elderly Halfling came over. His name was Orlin, he said. I introduced myself to him. He then told me that he was the Bishop of Dunwood and that he could show me my father's grave site. We stopped at my house and I grabbed a few, personal belongings of my father's that I thought should be buried with him. I brought some roses, his favorite pipe and his favorite hoe. I layed these thing on his grave and payed my respects. I then entered the Catherdral . It was very...halflingish. And by that I mean it was in a hill. Anayways, I then talked to Orlin about my father's services. We settled on a few things and left it there. On my way home, therewere more decaying Pig Men. I killed them, but it made me notice something... That killing is not something a halfling should be doing. It's in-humane. I then took a vow to never kill anything human-like again, unless provoked. And seeing as I am a patient Halfling, that's hard to do. I then went to Al'Khazar. There, I bought an odd looking and feeling staff. I then brought it home and started to study it. I have deemed it from some of my father's notes on something similar, to be a Magic staff. It's interesting...it intrigues me very much so. Following that I went and saw my father's grave once again. \n Day 7: Today I had a regular breakfast of apples, bacon and toast. I decided to walk the King's Road today. No bandits. However, I did stumble upon a man who was tending to an orchard. I handed him an apple he dropped. That made me feel beter. I then continued to the Temple of Aegis. There I met up with a lady named Freya. I went with her and an elf, to Laurelin. There, the elf showed us the archives. I had no time to study them for I had to return to Al'Khazar. I went back down along the King's Road. In the city, I had a nice steak and an ale. I then went to the King's Cross and saw Freya and others. There, all of us had much fun. The most fun I've had in this land....I went home after that and went to bed. Dead tired. \n Day 8: Today, I spent much time in peaceful Dunwood. But, around late afternoon, I went to Al'Khazar. There, I was going to comute to Laurelin. I was going to spend the rest of the day in the archives. On my way there, I ran into a robed fellow who had overheard my reason for leaving the city, when I told the guard at the gate. I simply told him that I was going to Laurelin to study the archives. I told him of my curiosity in Magic. He told me to let him read my journal sometime, should I be interested in Magic. He seemed like an educated fellow. Maybe some day I may let him read this. Maybe in return, we could share notes sometime. I might be able to learn something new...Oh, how I love knowledge. In the Archives, I found only one thing of notice. A book on the creation of Laurelin. I scribbled a few notes and returned to Dunwood. It was late now. So I must rest.  \n Day 9: I started today with a little farm work. I could only manage to do one of the smaller fields. The physical strength to do all that work was tough. I'd rather just stick to my book work next time... Seeing as there is no room in the storage hut..I have taken it upon myself to keep the wheat until I am instructed what to do with it. For now, I will use some to make lunch for today. Magnificent! Wonderful! Outstanding! The fellow who asked about my research bumped into me while in Al'Khazar today! I remembered his name...Cataris of the Mages Guild. We took a walk to a hidden library of his. I learned so much from it. I am very thankful for being able to have such a pleasure. He is a good man, that Cataris he is! As a thank-you to him, I gave 'im some good old Halfling wheat. I'm sure he will enjoy it. For now, I will go to bed. What a day.... \n Day 10: I left the town today early in the morn. I spent the day in Al'Khazar. Torwards the late afternoon, a guard named William came into the town today with his group. He had been cut by an undead blade. Nobody had a clue what to do, so I decided to be the Hero . I took him to the church and wash out the cut with Holy Water. That must have helped because the pain disapeared. I then soaked a rag in the water and dressed his wound with it. Helping him made me feel very good. Especially since I be no Doctor. I shall remeber his name , William of the Oren Guard. I only hope that his bravery to continue to fight the undead presses on.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whidoc's Notes on Magic", "braner321", "I don't know much of Magic...But hopefully these notes can help me remember what i've learned and seen. \n In the Laurelin Archives, I found a book stating that the city was created by use of Druid Magic. It involved seeds and his magical abilities. \n It has been said the A great Wandering Wizard also has been the protector of Aegis and weilds great Magic. None of his spells are known to me... \n It is also said that there are Undead in this world that weild strong magic. Their spells include lightning, fireballs, raiseing dead and changing the landscape to a living hell. \n There is a race of people called the Ascended. It is said that they too weild Magic. I have no record of their spells or magic. I don't know much of them besides that they have a city called Haven and that they weild Magic. \n There is a shop in Al'Khazar that claims to have magical goods, such as a Magic Gold Bar. The wears are obviously a scam to get minas...greedy liars... \n  so much knowledge must lie there. \n  inside the rumored Guild of Magic. But, alas, it is only a rumor. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Whisper isle suspects for undead", "Demonxerov2", "im pretty sure that the shop keeper that sells fishing equipment is undead. as is scoipin possible hawkes. not sure who else to include. will keep writing more names if they come up", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Isles", "Angelus_Obscurus", "Come one and all to the all new Whispering Isles! \n Whispering Isles offers you beautiful beach front houses, a lovely view of the ocean, and nice cozy homes. at affordable prices! Some come down the Whispering Isles today and grab yourself a lovely home! You keep it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Isles: Premium Housing", "Brettdude20", "Come to the Whispering isles to cash in on our luxury housing. Oue premium houses offer the best stands of living with your own private island to enjoy. So come to the Isles, just north of the cloud temple and enquire to Lord Brett Perea about buying a home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order", "Angelus_Obscurus", "Hello Traveller, If you are reading this now then i'm guessing you've come across one of the many fliers scattered around the lands, This flier is an invitation to join the Whispering Order! \n Who are the Whispering Order you ask? We are a Malitia that is based in the beautiful Whispering Isles! We are under the Command of Lord Brett Perea and swear our selves to protecting everything that's good about Aegis. For more information please stop by our barracks in Whispering Isles and speak with either: Commander Akorta, Commander Annora, or General Alethion. \n \n We would also like to let you know that there are many great houses for sale in Whispering Isles, great for a vacation or just a nice please to live all year round! Speak to Lord Brett Perea to inquire about housing!", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order - Higher Ranks", "Rhisereld", "Privates: \nZephyr Galewind - !\nHenry - %\nWallace - ^ \n \nCorporal: \nAirion - @ \n \nSergeant: \nRaick - Conster_monster \n \nCommander: \nAkorta - Angelus_Obscurus \nAnnora - isagirl \n \nGeneral: \nAlethion - Alectriciti \n \n \nSeven.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order and You", "Angelus_Obscurus", "People of Aegis as you all may well know dark times are upon us, and now with the Kingdom of Oren in Chaos due to the King betraying his people it is time for us to step in. With this notice i invite to join The \"Whispering Order\" The Whispering Order is a small group of Soldiers that show their loyalty to Lord Brett Perea. We focus on one thing, Getting the job done. \n If you choose to accept this please make your way to Whispering Isles Barracks and speak with either Commander Akorta or General Alethion. \n May you all stay safe.     After i hand out this batch i'm going to remake it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order Recruitment", "Angelus_Obscurus", "Races of Aegis! Dark times are upon us, the Ascended have left us, the Undead are raining hell down on us, and now the Oren king has been killed, We here at the Whispering Order are here to fix this. \n Apply now at the Whispering Order Barracks in Whispering Order to get a spot today! \n \n When signing up to the Whispering Order you'll know that you are doing the right thing in the world Aegis, we strictly do good in this world, But we do not care for someones background, as long as they do what's good now, so do what's right. \n \n Speak with Commander Akorta, Annora, or General Alethion at the Barracks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order Recruitment Flier", "Angelus_Obscurus", "People of Aegis it is time to take our stand! Our Stand against the all evil in the world. This is the Whispering Orders goal, to remove all evil from the land and to keep every innocent safe! This flier is your personal invitation to the Order, you just have to simply return this to one of the officers at the barracks at Whispering Isles. \n For more information about the Whispering Order come speak with us at the barracks. \n \n Also, Whispering Isles has great prices on a wide range of houses, you could buy it for a vacationing house or somewhere to live in general, you can expect nice weather all year round. To inquire about a house come speak with Lord Bret Perea.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order Recruits", "Rhisereld", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispering Order Special Offer", "Angelus_Obscurus", "Greetings people of Aegis! \n The Whispering Order has a special offer for anyone that has their hands on one of these fliers, This Offer is exclusive to any new recruits to the Whispering Order. The offer is that: Any new recruit who hands on this flier will recieve 500 Minas off any house in Whispering Isles! All you have to do is hand this into one of the Officers at the Whispering Order. \n \n Note, that you have to join The Whispering Order in order to recieve this discount on a house. \n \n For more information about joining or just general information come to the Whispering Order barracks in Whispering Isles.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whispers of Aegis", "serenityonyx", "Ye may listen for but an instance, but in that instance Mother Aegis whispers, her soothing vocals ebb and wave upon each brook and river, flowing out into the vast seas, her voice, one that is destined to live on forever, that has lived through countless untold centuries.  from foothills of the high country it babbles downhill dawn to dusk, by groves and ditches and hedgerows, winding its way endlessly through all nooks of the land. \n Each birdsong carries her message, their music drifting in the breeze, the sounds of exhilarated winds make rustle in the leaves of the all knowing oak, some of the tranquil notes that Mother Aegis brings.  though she doth have a wrathful temper, and when she shouts out her anger all things from her seek a place to hide. \n While her rage swells the fear of the land is her cry, shuddering the earth lays waste to man-forged scapes, she roars and her lightening flashes in the skies ,she crackles when her forests burn, leaving naught but blackness and smoke everywhere. With the power of Mother Aegis in a fury, none can hope to compare nor wish to bring about her tempest. \n Ye hear her whispers in all things... And though she herself does not have a time span mere mortals such as we whom live but upon her land for a short while should listen, even for an instance to the whispers of Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("WHITE RAVENS", "pheonix_292", "join the WHITE RAVENS and be a man of action. the White Ravens are a group of of warriors and mercenaries if you are interested contact me (WR_inductor_claud) THE WHITE RAVENS NEED YOU!!! hail marcus excuse me how are you? how are you", ""),
        StaticBook("White Ravens Recruitement", "nikias_1996", "White Raven Guard Labon: gathered supplies for the guards", ""),
        StaticBook("White_Raven confidential report. Mork's patrol log.", "friar7", "I was going to conduct some nomad orcs i had seen in the distance, there were 15 of them, al. they didn't like the sound of \"true justice\" and \"the bane of undead\", on the contrary, they liked the undead, said that they respect them becase the raise hell. i warned them that making foe's with us could be VERY dangerouse. They said that they would make an organization, for the purpose of killing us. then all went dark........ i had, luckely, been expexting this, i falsed them, they think we operate in oren therefor throwing them off our trail. i still fear that if we don't wipe them out, the good orcs of the warlands will be in danger of a terrorist group. This concludes my patrol log.", ""),
        StaticBook("Who are the Druids?", "Eralesh", "In the noble city of Al'Khazar, I asked a guard about the Druids. Here is his answers: \n ''I don't really know much about Druids, they are dark and mysterious. I just know that they have a little church in the Verge. I don't think they are evil, I think they work for the betterment of Aegis. Yes, I have met a Druid, he was really cheerful and honest. I have only one advice: \n    Never judge a Druid before you have met one!''", ""),
        StaticBook("Who the hell am I? *torn page*", "Ep152", "I don't think the idea of adding titles to journal entries will catch on... It's been a week since I returned from being kept prisoner in my own blade. Though this entry is not about that. Recently I have been thinking about that shady figure I met up with all those years ago... My curse was gone, they hadn't succeeded in killing me, what if they come back for more? What if this person, this... thing... is planning something? I don't know what to think anymore... The most I've been at peace lately has been when I relax in a small cave I found under Bell's memorial. It's like she's with me when I'm there, it makes me feel at ease. It's where I write my journal entries most of the time now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Who the hell am I? Part II", "Ep152", "My deep dark depression shrouds me even more every day... The only thing keeping me active is my attack plans on the undead. Though there hasn't been much actuall attacking recently. The house is even darker now. No one really talks, and if they do, not for long. \n Except for two days ago... I've been contemplating whether or not to write this in my journal... Here goes... Two days ago, I was in the house, reading some old journal entries out of boredom when I heard a faint knock on the front door. When I opened the door, there stood my sister, Felune. \n \n That was the first time I had ever seen her in person. When she finally convinced me that I wasn't dreaming, she dropped this one me... \"Ademas, you need to come with me now. You have a son. He lives in an inn on the Kings Road, close to Al'Khazar.\" \n \n What have I gotten myself into...", ""),
        StaticBook("Why am I out here!?", "Alectriciti", "How could I have been so foolish? What was it that brought me out here? I can't leave Rhisereld! I told her I wouldn't! Oh Rhise, please forgive me! I don't know why I'm out here... The last time I saw you, you were talking with Natheus. You felt awful, and so did I... If you ever find this book, know that it was foolish of me to step outside the house when you told me to leave you alone. I went to clear my mind and I became lost. I don't know why... but I felt as if something dark was pulling me away from you... as if it wanted us to be apart. And it succeeded! Rhise! *scribbles all over the wrinkled page* (in tiny letters \"I can't stand losing you.\") I HAVE to get back to you love. I have to. Whatever drew me out here, it was not right. Something bad is going to happen, I just know it! I'm making a compass, it should help me get home. All I need is redstone. It's nearly impossible to find unless it's in a nearby dungeon. As soon as I do, i swear I'm rushing home. I want to hold you in my arms and cradle you like I did at your house by the mountain. I want to protect you from the undead, and the evil that exists in these lands. \n \n *you notice many pages torn out here* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n It's complete, I have built a compass. It will guide me home to you. I fear something has happened to you. I can't stand being here any longer! I love you so much Rhisereld, and I'm coming home to prove it!", ""),
        StaticBook("Why do I feel this way.", "LolitaDoll", "I fear I am going mad even as I write these words. Why is it I feel this way about him? I know what he has done to me, and I know I should despise him for it. Then why is it my heart soar when I see him, and flutter when he speaks?  I can't count how many nights I lay in bed thinking of those weeks at Alethion's Hold. Just the mere memory of his skin caressing mine, sends shivers throughout my body. Of course at the time, all I could think of was his wife and how devestated she would be if she saw him in such a lustful state, so I resisted with all I could.  Though eventually I gave in.... and what a glorious feeling it was! My skin still tingles to this very day with the thought of his hips pressing into mine and his breath coming in short gasps as he pushes into me over and over and over.   even as he stands with his wife and kisses her gently, I smile, my own thoughts taking control, and I imagine wrapping my legs around his thrusting hips as I cry out for more! : I regret now turning him over to the Order, for if I hadn't we would both be happily enjoying eachother's flesh still. ' I want to straddle him, and drive my hips down on his ! I fear I may go mad with this desire for another woman's husband, but at the same time, I don't wish to be sane...", ""),
        StaticBook("why not to drink", "0_DK_0", "you get a shorter life and SUGAR is much better!", ""),
        StaticBook("Why..", "Nanomatrix", "I had no choice in the matter, it was to dangerouse to continue on, the ascended and I cam up with the plan to keep you all safe, whilst still able to server aerial I know, it was not right, and as the dwarf messanger told me you were very distraight over the fact that i was not comming back, but i am alive. atleast be happy that i am alive and well I can understand if you do not wish to know me anymore, but i thought it was right to come back and tell you the truth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Why?", "Roxses20", "I have prayed for you but you dont answer. i have killed for you but still no answer. whitch one is better good or evil eaither way im ignored. is there no place for me. im stuck with no way out . im starting to think does it matter whitch side i choose. they both are the same but yet differnt", ""),
        StaticBook("wichtige Orte", "neandro95", "Sandstone STützpunkt:Caden brachte mich her,nördlich der Hauptstadt", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilderness Survival Guide", "Kended", "Hello there' ye fair travelers. This be the guide of Surviving out there en' the wild. It's a hard life out there, with many things aimed' at killin' off ye'! Hopefully this can help ye' out. So, lets start off with the pressin' matter of survival and daylight. Ye' be wanting te' get outta' any wild areas, make ye' self to a town,or if not, make ye' self a shelter. Start this here' task by getting supplies,dirt,wood,cobble,any thing'll do. If ye' plan to be stayin' for the night, make it small, that way ye dont attract attention to ye' self. If ye' plan to be there for a bit, make ye' base hidden. Perhaps in the' base of a great mountain. After ye' do that, ye got the pressin' matter of food to cova'. It' ain't hard if ye' know where te' look. Many things can be made into some yummy food! *Laughs* When' me here, was a young lil' dwarf, mi' parents were kidnapped and i was alone! But ye' know me, i'm a hard ol' dwarf, *Laughs* it takes more than loneliness to kill me' I taught me' self to know bad food from good food, and i' survived! Lets start, this here' chickens in aegis be too' small to eat! Ye' might as well eat feathers! Ahhh, and this here cows seem rather thin' too mi' pals! So that be' leavin' us with this here pigs, they happen to be rather' fat in this here' world! They are ye' primary source of food, but there be more! Ye' can find mushrooms in caves and under some trees mi' pals! They can make a harty stew for yer. If ye' got a bowl, ye' can get two types of mushrooms and mix em up! There be some cakes' ye can eat, but alas, i was never taught on how to make em'. Alrighty, that be coverin' the food, ye' then got the dangers of this' here outside world! Let's start us off with the spiders, they jus' be some overgrown vermin with a taste' for some meat! They' be attackin' anything that moves. Next ye' got these here, oh what'da call em...Walking dead? They' be the ones with flesh and want some mor'. They luckily be rather slow, so ye' can outrun em. Alas, we come to the walkin' bones! They be' huntin' ye down with bows & arrows! They' don't seem to be too fast though', so ye' can outrun em, but they got' range! Ye' can't be forgettin about this here, walkin green men! They be explodin' themselves on ye' and trying to take ya' with them to hell! Ahh...so we covered shelter, and food! This here' be all I can teach ye' without findin' ya in Aegis! Last thing' before I go.... there may be bandits, there may be murderers, there may be thiefs.... but' when there be a cold' chill headin' down yer' spine... and ye' feel like you're not alone...If ye' ever sense and unexplainable presence, and ye' be alone...just run lad'! There be unexplainable presences in this world! I hear them as undead, and if ye' aren't armed, even if ye' be armed, they seem to be capable of unimaginable powers...much more' than any of the other races..... If ye' ever feel you need help, seek me out friend, for I be stayin' in oren,under a a bridge....or maybe even that there inn....G'day friend, keep this book special! May the dwarven king watch over you, and may ye' feel the strength of 10 men!", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilderness Survival guide with Christian", "welshguy", "So are you always getting hungry? Can't find shelter for night? Getting slain by other Adventurers? Well you came to the right book! I can show you how to survive the Wilderness \n Chapter 1 Hunger So the first thing you should do is get food for the night by attacking Pigs,Cows and Chicken . \n Tip \n use furnaces to cook food if you want to get the heartiest of food! \nChapter 2 \nMonsters So if your adventures have taken you to the depths of night Then don't panic! Just obey these instuructions 1. try to avoid combat, your health is most important 2. Don't go fighting without swords! As your fists are no match to zombie flesh Now the best things for these encounters \n Zombies: Weak but if grouped are lethal! \n Skeletons: Try to move in circles when attacking as they need time to aim! \nPigmen: Do not look at them as they will be extremly deadly if provoked \nSpiders: You can use speed attacks to attack or if you need to run sprint! \nChapter 3 \n Other Adventurers \n It is always nice to meet and greet others but  remember not all adventurers love a nice chat but Your Minas! \nso i hope this helps future adventures and remember...Stay safe!", ""),
        StaticBook("Wildewyn Woods", "Jon021", "\nScene Opens on clearing in the middle of Wildwyn Woods in the middle of the night \nRougon Wildwen enters \nBushes rustle \nRougon: Who's there? \nBushes rustle once more \nRougon turns to the bush \nRougon: Who are you? What do you want with me? \nSomething growls \nRougon yelps in terror and proceeds to exit \nAll that is heard is the sound of Rougon being mauled \n \n \nScene opens on small town in Wildwyn Woods \nTownsfolk are about their normal activities, IE buying bread, etc. \nOrgoron Wildwen enters \nOrgoron: Help! My brother's been murdered! \nall the townsfolk gather around as Orgoron drags his brother's dead body to the center of town \nMarya: what happened to him? \nOrgoron: I don't know! I just found him in the woods, mangled as he is now. \ntownsfolk murmer about the strange event \nGnargnon: his wounds look like a beast mauled him! \nAryan: what kind of beast? A zombie? A hoard of pigmen? A spider? \nGnargnon: none of those. Nothing has claws that could do this. These are worse than a wolf's claws . \nAll the townsfolk murmer, shocked. \nThe town elder, \nHydragnon, enters \nHydragnon: people! People! What is it that brings you into this huddle ? \nAryan: Rougon's been murdered! \nHydragnon examines Rougon's mangled body \nHydragnon looks up grimly \nHydragnon: this is like that- Nothing I've ever seen before! \nOrgoron: whatever it is, it's running free in the woods! That's where I found his body. \nHydragnon: nobody go out during the night! Ever! Marya: but Elder, why not?  \nHydragnon: It's-er-whatever did this is out there! \nDragnon enters \nDragnon: Father, we obviously need to get rid of this thing. If we can't go out at night, we can't kill the beast . So, who will come to slay the beast with me? \na hushed silence falls over the townsfolk \nOrgoron: I will! I need to avenge my father! The beast will be slain! We are the two best w arriors in the village! the beast won't stand a chance! \nOrgoron and Dragnon leave the village at night, armored and armed \nIn the morning, Gnargnon is walking through the woods, and finds Orgoron dead and Dragnon barely alive. \nDragnon: urg... \nGnargnon: Dragnon! It didn't kill you? What was it? \nDragnon: D-d-don't go into the w-woods at night. \nDragnon dies after delivering that message \nGnargnon: Dragnon! Help! I found them! \nGnargnon enters the village carrying Orgoron's dead body, and Aryan carrying Dragnon's. \nHyrdragnon: No! NO! My son! He should have never gone out there! \nGnargnon: those were his last words, \"Don't go into the woods at night.\" \nHyrdragnon weeps over his dead son's body \nHydragnon: why did you have to go out there? Why? Why? \nGnargnon: Elder.. Do you know what the beast is? \nHydragnon: How should I? You think I've been out there? Of course not! \nHydragnon marches off, taking his son's body \nNight falls over the village \nAryan, Marya, and Gnargnon all meet in the town square \nGnargnon: something is strange with the Elder. He always seems to know what the beast is. \nAryan: maybe we be should leave it alone. After all, he just lost his son. \nMarya: if we don't get rid of the beast, we'll lose many more than them \nGnargnon: We best investigate then. Let's pay the Elder a visit. \nThe three enter Hydragnon's house to find it empty \nAryan: where could he be? I doubt he went into the woods. \nGnargnon: he might have. But we can't go, because we'll likely be killed. \nMarya: we can ask him in the morning. \nThe three leave the elder's house \nThe sun rises over the town, and the elder is loitering in the town square \nGnargnon approaches the elder \nGnargnon: Elder? Where were you last night? You weren't at home. \nHydragnon: I-I was out burying Dragnon \nGnargnon: In the woods? \nHydragnon: the woods? of course not! \nGnargnon: do you know something about the beast, Elder? Hydragnon: Y-yes. \nGnargnon: What? Spit it out! \nHydragnon: It's a man and a wolf.. One by day, the other by night. \nGnargnon: so someone in town could be it.. \nHydragnon: yes. I doubt they'd tell you who they are. \nGnargnon: we need to find out who it is, and quickly. \nGnargnon leaves Hydragnon's home and Hydragnon sighs with relief \nGnargnon meets Aryan and Marya to discuss the news \nGnargnon: the elder told me what the beast is. It's a man by day and a wolf by night \nAryan: so s-someone in the town is the beast?! \nMarya: I'm certainly not the beast! \nGnargnon: nor I! \nAryan: nor I! \nGnargnon: then who is it? \nAyran: wait... if they were the beast, they'd have to leave the village at night... and Hydragnon wasn't here that night... \nGnargnon: you aren't saying he's the beast! \nAryan: that is exactly what I'm saying. \nMarya: then we need to get rid of him! \nGnargnon: we need to pay the Elder another visit. \nAll three of them go the Hydragnon's house \nHydragnon: Aryan, Marya, and Gnargnon. How can I help you? \nGnargnon: we need you in the town square \nMarya, Aryan and Gnargnon drag Hyrdragnon into the town square and tye him by his hands and feet to the ground in chains", ""),
        StaticBook("Will", "Thaddeus12", "What are you doing in my house", ""),
        StaticBook("Will Forestin's Life Of Adventure", "HarrisonBitzis", "Ok.... Where to start... Im new, sorry. Ive never written a book... Well  I guess Ill start at the begginning... Chapter 1 This is my life Before my adventures in aegis began. I Was A NobleMan, Rich and powerful.. Back Then, I wasnt Will Forestin. I was Will Howards. Youll learn why in a minute.... I didnt WANT to be a noble man was the problem. I loved adventure, exitement! My dad... Wanted me to be a lawyer. When i was twelve, My Father took me to a court meeting. I didnt want to go, but i had to. Unfortunately, I was excellen. A fine lawyer Indeed. Problem was i didnt want to be one So i set out for Adventure That Night. I just Left.... It was only a while before I found a hobby. i came accross the dwarven cities, and soon began to love architecture. I built alot, alot alot alot. I loved it. but then.... A band of hunters waas coming to town. they were friendly, but i felt strange... Then i noticed A female Hunter amongst the group... She was beautiful, tall, Blonde, Bright blue eyes.... Sorry, back to the story. I wanted to approach but i felt... strange, like i said. So i followed the hunters out of the city. I followed for many days, and one night, decided to scout around their camp, see what was happening. I was half around the camp when a hand siezed my wrist. I looked up to see those bright blue eyes. I thought se would kill me, but no. she smiled. \"yo remind me of...\" She stopped. I wanted to ask, but before I got the chance we were running. I guess she quit, I thought to myself. I was glad however. We found a town and she told me to stay, so i did. I didnt know i was STAYING for 5 years. She left me alone, and i was mad, dont get me wrong. I was VERY mad. \"5 years go by slower than usual when your alone. in Kal' Urguan, I at least had friends.\" I said. I was wandering through the forest when i felt hands on my back. I instanly turned around and attempted to puch them when i saw who they were THEY was SHE and SHE was HER. And By her, I mean the huntess. She Smiled and said \"I'm no creeper!\" I was glad. very,very, VERY glad. I soon learned her name. Alyss... It was a nice name. I got along with her very well, She taught me to use a bow, And I taught her how to use a sword. on her 20th birthday, I went out Hunting with her. But it was no ordinary hunting trip. I had made a silver necklace, and i was going to propose. I had an old friend enchant the neckleace, so that it was warm when you wer in love, neutral for when you wer... well neutral, and cold when you disliked. We came across a flower garden and thats when it happened. I said, the words \"Will you marry me?\" And showed her the necklace. She said \"Ye-\" and thats all she got to. She had a knife in here side, and i didnt know from who. Then, i found out. It was an undead, A blasted creature in a black robe. I was enfuriated, and i swiped the swprd, but he dodged. Then, 9 more undead emerged from the woods, and all armed with stalves. One shot and my sword was vaporized. I grabbed my hunting knife, and Alyss' off her... Corpse..... And threw mine at on of them. he fell dead, and the rest charged. Unfortunately for them, they charged to their deaths. Every one was dead. all of them. But my heart was dead, too. I buried her at in the garden. I lost my hunting knife, and the knife I wear to this day is hers. I also took The necklace and swore to never take it off. For 3 years, I wore the necklace, and for all three it was Bitterly cold. I went back to my parents house, expecting love, and what I got was hate. They Shunned me for leaving. They legally stripped me of my last name. I made up Forestin Because Alyss taught me to love the forest. And from there i marched to oren. Chapter 2. It was a whiles journy, and i was a sad man. I met many companions, but only one truly caught ,y attention His name was Oakenshield, or at least thats what he told me. he was selling iron, and i bought. he asked me to travel with him, and life couldnt get much worse, so i said yes. We traveled for a while, and I became to grow fond of the dwarf. He was friendly. I felt something I hadnt felt for a while. Warmth. my body had beenchilled to te bone by the necklace, so warmth felt.... Odd. On a path to Kal'Urguan Oakenshield Told me to wait for him at holmes, and he would be there in a minute. I was walking when I heard lightning. And then, I blacked ou t. I didnt know what had happened but I woke up near death. I couldnt find Oakenshield, and a familiar feeling fell upon me. Cold. It was normal, so i didnt care about the cold. the only thing i cared about was losing a friend. my only friend, gone. Chapter 3 This is where it really starts. After wandering the world for a bit, I decided to take a break, and I rested at an inn that night. I woke up around midnight and heard something. i heard \"do you value 50 minas over your life?\" it was a threat, I realized, And i interrupted, chasing the man to the holmes station. He tried to play innocent, but it failed. He was sentanced to jail, but he was crafty. He trapped the gaurd in the cell. luckily, an orc caught him. The orcs name was Pancake, Shaman Pancake. Shaman Ordered him to community service, building 100 houses, and we agreed. well, everyone but me. Halfway down the road, Shaman Pancake stopped us. He siad \"wait. This man has killed, stolen, and who knows what else. in an orc country, that is worthy of death.\" I smiled, But Boney wasnt about to give up. He Jumped from the bridge, and Almost escaped, but i stuck him with the sword. Boney was dead. Chapter 4 I was glad to be done with boney, but noticed, that I liked the crimefighting. It was the thrill I hadnt felt for years. I went to Lautelin Next, hoping to find more to do around the world, When a small ill-fate fell upon me. Someone had Trap-doored the inn, and i fell in one. I got out, with help however. and went outside. Right then, a blonde haired elf smiled Warmly at me. He said,\" Was it you wjo was trapped in the pit?\" I said yes, recognizing him as someone who tried to help me. I rewarded him, and he asked me a favor...... Chapter 5 This Elf's Name Was Caden, Caden Cathaldus, and he needed help with tracking down a girl... Why, i did not know, but i joined him, and he escorted me to his house. I had a home Chapter 6", ""),
        StaticBook("WILL OF ALLIX FABLENIGHT", "Sode1", "I Allix Fablenight have passed away. I give all my minas to my son, Adion and all my belongings to the druidic order and my fatefull friends Martin Loyola Mania Valkerye and Aetar Anarion I wish them all good luck.", ""),
        StaticBook("Will Of Banok Gray", "Thatpyrodude", "I leave everything i own to my son Sean Gray \n I love you son", ""),
        StaticBook("Will Pay-slip", "WOOSH10001", "Golden Harvest Pay-Slip\n Recruit Will\n 10/20/2011\n Signed Overseer Maximus", ""),
        StaticBook("Will's Journal", "HarrisonBitzis", "Going to start writing this tomorrow... I've noticed people tend to document things that happen in their lives. And I've decided to do so. So.. This is page one of Will Forestin's Journal....? ~Will Forestin Help Is something I could use at the moment. Why do people have to get so involved? I just sighed, just so you know. Alright, Here we go. DAY 1; Well there, Aegis.. I don't know why I'm adressing you, I'd doubt you'll ever read this, but if you do, congradulations! You've discovered my Journal! Hope you enjoy, and if you read to the end, Make sure you contact me! If I'm still alive, that is. Now, into the actual documentation. This isn't a play, silly, get to rk, Will! ((WORK)) Er.. Now that I think about it, I'd rather not talk about what's going on in my life. But, I just said this will probably never touch anyone that isn't me, so.... I've got next to nothing to lose! Sometimes, I feel like SUCH a horrible person. I next to broke a sweet girl's heart today. Stupid me.... But this is not reflection! This is for me to DOCUMENT. So I will state events of the day as I go along. -You see various splotches where the ink has bled through onto another page.- So today I went to Talun -Written much more ornately than other words on the page s- Me and a few friends partook in building activities, making gates and whatnot. The wierdest thing happened afterwards.... Well at first, we climbed to the top of the mountin outside of the city. And.... Slimes. Popping out of the water. For those of you who have never SEEN a slime, it's... It's a big green block. A big, heavy block. I got knocked unconsious by one, and as my friends scrambled to kill them... They were GONE. All gone. No more. I woke up to no slimbs. ((SLIMES*)) And when I awake, a large population of spiders pops out of our forests. I must've upset mother nature. I'll have to speak with the druids about this, But none-the-less, We had spiders left and right. I even encountered a rare blue cave spider, highly venenmous. We all evaded being bit fairly well, and if we did get bit, it wasn't venomous. Wait, -Will scratches out Venemous both times, and replaces it with spelling.- I have the strangest muscle spasms ((LAG)) Sometimes. But either way, we eventually drove off the spider infestation. And... That's today for you? (( Thanks to Mylas for having that RP event with us! The hundreds of spiders were GREAT! Mylas/Architecus is responsible for these events. )) I'll see you in my next moments of documentation! ~Will Forestin \n DAY 2; Hello Journal. I right with happy spirits. Things are.. Well, today was fun. Let's say that. First thing; Quite distressful, actually, I learned that Luke Bradswashe, An old friend, is... Dead. Apparently, he had an \"Accident,\" but I know better. A man claiming to be his brother showed up with Luke's keys. And they were smeared in blood. I assumed this man was the killer, But am yet to confirm the fact. Afterwards, I entered AlKhazar once more, to encounter Botar Blackrock. Unfortunately, he has to ask about my problems. And I've had quite a few.. Girl, problems recently, if you will. And he decides to bring that up. But like the little bugger that I am, I was able  change the subject... For a moment. He was back on it in an instant, and found out who I've had troubles with. Since this is NOT reflection, I won't write feelings. But I've had an.. Interest, in a certain elf recently.... Just an interest! Nothing more! This is not REFLECTION! Er.. -You see a line slashed through, \"This is not REFLECTION!\" And by it, a new sentance- No one's going to see this! I can reflect if I want to! So what if I talk about my feelings? I LOVE HER. She's beautiful, she's smart, she's cunning.. All the things I look for. Not so sure I'll be able to write the name without dying... Okay.. I'll.. I'll TRY. E...O...I...N. Eoin. E-O-I-N. She's.. Well, I didn't like her at first. But, that's for another day. For now, I'll tell you what's happened. Reflection can be tiring. I was walking around with Botar-He had discovered this- When we encountered... Eoin. So Botar casually approaches me, \"Is that her?\" I gulp and nod, and stare at her.. Big.. Green.. Eyes-The word drifts off- Ooh, Excuse me. Lost focus for a moment. So, I'm looking at her, and I hear shouts from the sewer. \"Is that Will's Voice I hear?\" I go down to help Alkeenar, A man I've helped covert to the good side. And of course, Botar, and Eoin come down, and everyone else... And after that situation is resolved... Bloody... Botar decides to irritate me. He whispers, \"Ask her out or I do.\" My heart freezes. The man's got nerve... But either way, I don't engage in more than casual conversation. And.. Then Botar... He says, \"Hey, Miss. Will likes you but is to afraid to talk to you.\" Luckily for me, I'm a good liar, but I don't think it went over well. I'm sure I was beet red.... But either way, Eoin leaves awkwardly and I'm stuck in the sewers, Alone and sad. Lynx Gwai, God bless him, Decides to cheer me up. He offers me a trip to New Alstion.. And tells me to invite Eoin. I.. I try and invite her without choking up, and he helps me through it. She said yes, surprisingly enough. And, Just my luck, Half way into the trip, we're ALL lost. Me, with my cunning sense of direction, was able to locate the town. Eoin, not sure, stumblde around for a moment. Er.. -Crosses out the misspelled \"stumbled\" And replaces it properly.- Much better. Lynx was only a second or so behind me, and decides to sleep until she Arrived. And, after a few obsenely awkward moments, a few friends show iup... No, -crosses out the \"i\" In \"up.\"-, Better! Much, Much better! Where were we? Ah, yes. Throdo Therving and Cedric Evalyn arrived, screaming their heads off. This is where things get interesting. Don't remember exactly what happened, but I know Eoin hit a wall. She was stumbling along in a pumpkin and slammed into a wall. I take the pumpkin off her, and idiotically enough, I put it on. Throdo had been doing some.. Wierd, stuff, so I was off my rocker. I slam my head into everything in the room. Being stupid and all, I wasn't paying attention to anyone or anything. Eventually, they got the pumpkin off of me, which took forever. And Eoin.. Slapped me, for some reason. Some reason. And if THAT wasn't enough, Throdo had to punch me in the face. I fell down, with what felt like a broken Jaw. I didn't show it, but pain was spreading through my body as I struck the floor. So what any other person might do, I crawl away. Throdo tries to stop me, and so does Eoin, but.. I don't stop. I make it back to the inn, and find myself alone for a while. And then, the next face I see is Eoin's. Beautiful.... Er.. Either way! She decides to take care of me, how sweet... EITHER WAY, I end up with a borken jaw. I was in front of a girl, a quite attractive one, so I tried not to scream as my jaw was snapped back into place. Things worked out pretty well from there. Eoin took care of me. She was... Nice. but I wasn't. I broke away while she slept, and ran away. She actually cared about me, and decided to follow. My jaw began to feel better as I ran, but I heard a muffled shout. \"Help!\" It was Eoin. I didn't see her at first. And then; Bang. Her. Under the ice. God... Either way; She was stuck. And drowning. I had to pull her up, and with her lean figure, it wasn't to hard. .. I find it wierd to write about such things. EITHER WAY! I get her out; But the poor soul was freezing. I had to help-Somehow. So i do what I can. I take her to civilization and care for her. She ended up wearing my spare clothes, which I was surprised fit her. But either way, that's about where things ended. She was all better- I was all better. I had fun today. I guess that's the end of todays documentation. Will Forestin, signing out! ~Will. TEST. TESTING TESTING, ONE TWO THREE. (( Bookworm's are down, sorry, Had to do that. Ignore that. I'll be back LATER! ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Will's_Writy-Mahoozit", "HarrisonBitzis", "Herm..... What does one call a book in which you write something? I've heard \"Journal\" And \"Diary\" Used, but I want to be.. original. So this is my... Writey-Mahoozit! That's It's name. Writy-Mahoozit. So... Erm.. Great introduction, Hm? I'll... I'll write more tomorrow? See you.. Then... ~Will", ""),
        StaticBook("Will_Cadaver's speach", "boodilly", "Our pork is the best!", ""),
        StaticBook("William's Notes", "William_Talbot", "", ""),
        StaticBook("William's WoodWork", "Lomaticc", "Building a home? Shop? Kingdom? Don't have time to chop down wood? Stop by William's WoodWork, Oren's Carpenter! We supply logs and planks. We also offer home furnishing with our collection of wooden furniture. Did we mention we sell unused books and bookshelves? Stop by and see what all the woodpecking's about! Located right after you enter Alkhazar, follow the right path to William's Woodwork, across the street from the Oren Regular Newspaper!", ""),
        StaticBook("Willizl33t Redpoints", "monkeychez", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Willow's Diary", "Ivrae", "Arf, I'ma dog.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wills Journal", "coastercam0", "\nEntry 1: Day one of my banishment. Almost regret doing this to myself, but I have to regain my honor if I am to ever return. I'm writing this while resting on the way to Al'Khazard. Unfortunately my soulstone failed the first time around and I'm walking... Once I get there I'm meeting with one of the few contacts I have left in Al'Khazard. \nEntry 2: Just met with my contact, says theres a man headed towards Winterfell selling diamonds at dirt price. At this news my heart sank, obviously Winterfell is not his destination. Unless he plans to sell them to the dead. Saw Henry as well, told him what happened. Good lad, hope to see him grow as a great hunter some day. \nEntry 3: Got kicked out of Al'Khazar for public intoxication. At this point I doubt I will ever see the keep again. The trail is cold, and I don't know what to do. I'm off to Winterfell. Maybe I can actually find something there. I plan on visiting contacts in Laurelin on the way for info. \nEntry 4: I got robbed twice on the way to Laurelin. This is not a good day. The second group tried to kill me after. \nEntry 5: Finally made it. Cold, hungry, and damn tired. I had to buy food off of travelers, no idea where anything is in this mess of trees. Still going to Winterfell, no idea where it is. I'm lost. \nEntry 6: Finally got outta the brush. Doesn't change the fact that I have no idea where I'm going. \nEntry 7: Somehow come across a dwarf town, couldnt get in because there apparently is a plague. There were crowds of people trying to get out and in, both without and with disease. \nEntry 8: I came across the home of the elven princess and druid near our keep today. I had a nice chat and told him I had been banished (not why of course) and he and the princess wished me luck and gave me supplies. Before I left, I handed them my will in case I die. I now head for winterfell again. \nEntry 9: Got to new haven, but at this point, I couldn't go on. No armor or arrows and most importantly, not an animal in sight. Need to go back to the keep and ask for supplies. Hopefully they agree. \nEntry 10: Well I'll be damned. Same bastards who robbed me a week ago found me. They're letting me write one final entry. I'm worried though, this is very close to the elven estate. The princess and druid are capable warriors but I doubt that they can stop these 3. They've taken my weapons already, foolish of me. Should of fought back. They ARE letting me write this though. That's kind I guess. Then again it's probably a last request thing. I'm stalling right now. They're about sending one of them off to find a place to rob. I'll try to lead them away from the elven estate, if they find the keep, well then they'll be the ones dead. Looks like they've had enough of me wasting their time. Bastards want my journal now, great thought they were gonna let me go. I tried my best. Good Hunting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wills Last Testament", "coastercam0", "To my friends, and brothers. If you are reading this, then I have failed my mission and I am dead. Do not feel sadness or guilt, for you men gave me what little happyness I have had in this life. A life filed only with sorrow for so long until I became a hunter. This is my final word, if any should find my journal, place it in the library. To my friends and brothers, I give you my earthly possessions. \nTo Wyrix, faithfull as always, I give you my golden sword. You are a good hunter, and I knew since I met you, that you were destined for greatness. \nTo Thole. my loyal man at arms, I have never seen you waver, and for that I give you my armor (even in death I will tease you for your hatred of it) \nTo Vigleiven, my partner in crime, I'm afraid I overworked you, have my cot. \nTo Douglas and the Mages, I know my tempers flared after the incident, but you were all my good friends, to you anything that remains. \nNiko and Sir Drunk all the time, It was an honor serving with you. I wish I could give you more then my thanks. :Henry, I'm sorry for the way I acted in the bar. I was in distress. I know I was not the best man, but to me you were like a son. I hope one day, you will grow to embody all the good traits a hunter should have. \nTo all my brothers I did not write about, I am sorry. In these times, my mind is foggy. It was an honor serving with you all. \nAnd finally. Lykos. My master, friend, and lord. I never forgot the day you talked me out of joining the Oren Guard. I never got to thank you for that. I guess I never will. But know, that joining and serving you was the best decision of my life. I want you to have my journal, if it is ever found. I'm sorry that in the end, I failed you. I admit I was terribly hurt when I was accused as the thief by you. Know I respect you far too much to do any wrong. I regret none of my time with you. \nDay, we hide, Come night, we rise. \nGood Hunting. \nWill Chapman. -Hunter to the end. \nTo the kind elves Bircalin and Princess Indelwehn, all my saplings, leaves ,flowers and seeds. Although I did not know them well, They were good friends.", ""),
