        StaticBook("Worn Book", "AlphaCentaurus", "*The writing is faded and the pages torn. You can only make out scattered words here and there.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Worn Journal", "ilikepiefoo", "When When I first came into Aegis I was like many others small insecure and unkowing of who or Where I was . A monk had told me that I was destined for greatness and that I should go out and find my place in the world. I took that monk's advice and headed out exploring the world and attempting to find where I belonged . I came upon the twin watch towers by the end of my first night. Curious I went to the top of the tower to look for any landmarks I should travel to when it was day. That is when I was attacked by a group of Orcs. No names no words just pure hateful malice. I was stricken down and awoke inside the cloud temple once again but not without loss...the monsters they had ripped my left eye from my socket to keep as a trophy. The wandering wizard had claimed that he banished them from Aegis permanently when I had re-arrived at the twin towers. When I had finally battled my way to Oren king Perea's coup had succeded and he was searching for guards not wanting to miss a chance at revenge against those wretched sand snakes I joined. My first task was to patrol the roads from the cloud temple to Al'Khazar I had help an Ares Stark joined me in this duty. We arrived at the cloud temple without incident and had begun the trek back to the city that is when", ""),
        StaticBook("WR Sanirus Guard report I", "Harv0kz", "White Raven Guard Sanirus, Report I, Escorting High Merchant Tuk \n Number of present people: 3 \n Events as Follows: \n We started from the Keep, and moved towards Laurelin, a long and uneventful walk. When we reached Laurelin, Tuk chanced an encounter with a blind elf I did not catch the name off, and another female elf named Liriyana ((not sure about exact spelling)). Tuk then proceeded to ask her to store three thousand Minas, for reasons Tuk did not state. The female elf agreed. A long private conversation I was unable to listen to then happened between them and High Prince Native. After a while, the High Prince appears, and Tuk conducts trade with him, selling off six redlog log stacks, and 36 pumpkins. Most of the important things ended then. We proceeded back to the keep. \n End of Report", ""),
        StaticBook("Wrath's Clutch", "Da_Emperors", "When i worked under Wrath as a slave after my Captainship was done. I found out who really supported the Undead. The Person that i knew as Wrath was in the trials himself! He let AllentheGreat into Wrath's Clutch! Wrath's Clutch was one of the strongest forts. Inported Netherrack traps from the undead and lava bombs. Only Undead and Wrath had the full knowlegde of the base. However it didn't seem it could be taken over till the Battle of Wrath's Clutch Wrath is Undead now. His fort may be destroyed ((Read The Battle of Wrath's Clutch)) Now he has another one in the process and now down fort. this one is one in the waters somewhere, a large tower Never trust Wrath or his men! And never trust the Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wrath's Clutch", "blackhawk77g", "A fortification of pure evil, founded by the immortal undead leader Wrath. Destroued by the combined forces of the elves and the dwarfs. \n \n ((Oct.10, 2011)) \n The elves are unhappy about giving their land that they \"won\" at Wrath's Clutch to the dwarfs. A few of the Wardens seemed fairly hostile to dwarfs after learning about this. The elven diplomat Torak has no knowledge or opinion on the matter. The elves are mostly unhappy due to their tearing down of Fort Fairleaf, a  fort that was built before the siege of Wrath's Clutch.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wrath's Evil", "KPDGaskell", "Wrath, the head of the 'guild' know as the keepers, and a true menace to the land. His cronies use dirt tricks, such as offering jobs, to get you into their dungeons, and turn you into a slave.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of Permission", "Baronvo", "To all whom it may concern, \n \n I, Everard Hightower, High Priest of Oren, Arch-Mage of the Mage's Guild, give permission to the United Aegis Coalition to search for evidence of secret passages in the sewers which might lead to the undead. \n \n Signed, \n \n High Priest Everard Hightower", ""),
        StaticBook("write", "deanofantastico", "", ""),
        StaticBook("write", "begginfokillz", "the greenskins, damn.... they took the major hostage. we need to take him back. Day 2: Damnit, we were assigned a rescue op...the major is as good as dead, being captured by greenskins and all. Day 7: we have been holed up in this farm for days, and the major...he had to have death. it was a mercy. Day 12: still holed up. Day 22: FINALY! THat rat bastard captain came through! We will Win! Day 23; Sniper took the captain out. Damnit. Green bastard has my squad pinned. Day 24 Sniper hit me. Day 26: last stand, i guess. time to fight to the death. As i write this page, i fear it will be my last. TO GLORY!.... write done nevermore who is in charge of the guards? i hear you have a prisoner", ""),
