        StaticBook("Xel: Properties of redstone and design", "Whisper342", "Much of the book has burnt edges.  Every page is filled with writings about redstone and how it works. Much of the book has burnt edges and every page is filled with experiments. Along with each experiment are detailed results that most people know of today. On some pages there are designs.  Some are simple like operating a door. While others are quite a bit more advanced and the purpose isn't so clear.", ""),
        StaticBook("Xero's Dark Past", "Demonxerov2", "in well, that must have been a crappy start... okay then, i wrote this because nobody knows more about xero then me. Its true you know! Xero was raised in a small poor town, where life was always hard to survive. Then when the town became under seige by a neighboring nation, sides were taken. Xero fought for the rebels, A group that spoke out against the corrupt government. although he had many battles, he only lost one. Unfortuneately, it was the most important this battle was the one the decided who would get the town. Xero had been shot in the arm, an d couldnt fight, however Xero had made his last stand and burned the town down before he was overwhelmed and imprisoned. His shackles were released however by a unknown ally, or so he thought. the man had only freed him so that he could be imprisonned in his laboratory, where he conducted horrible experiments on him. Soon enough, or hero 's luck, the necromancer was slain by one known as apollyon. Free of the horrid master, Xero decided to team up with this man, since they forged such a strong friendship before. Now we skip later on in his life where he met his first love. He tried to woo her, and finall y after many attempts succeeded, unfortunately though, he was only being used. Some dark order was trying to use him to summon their demon, in which they needed five human souls. Xero managed to get a kiss out of his love, and secretly a key to. the cells he and his companions were held in. although they got out of the builder, building, Xero returned days later to put a end to this minor evil. They were expecting him and trapped him in a cage before stealing his soul and feeding it to their demon . now they only needed four more, but suddenly instead of falling down dead like anticipated, Xero became a vessel filled of rage and unleashed his wrath onto the order. After he returned, he started wearing a cloak that was given to the dead on their buriel. He was worried, due to his lack of soul, that he would become undead. he sought help from a old group of monks. they told him that he had something that they didnt, compassion, happiness, anger, his emotions that made him human. He thanked the monks before returning to his home, only to find the order had been reawakened. Now he had fought against them once more, however in battle he had lost his control, and showed no mercy to the order this time. After finishing them off, he noticed that the people around him were frightened, not of the wreckage from the city, but of his rage. Due to this, Xero left, and with him so did apollyon. now they are drifters, moving around from town to town, Their reasons unknown, and help or hinder many that they meet. That is the true story of Xero, Please contact Nexus the dwarf if you have something to add", ""),
        StaticBook("Xero's journal: Book 1", "Demonxerov2", "so... i was told that keeping a journal might be a good hobby. i decided to give it a try today i was working on my house, when darrian had came and gave me some work he told me to even out a hill, make a stone outline on the wooden path, and build a new staircase for the mountain i already completed two of the task with ease, but have yet to start on the third because nailena asked me to work on her robes for her. so i fixed them to a certain height, and she said to make it shorter. and by that, i ment longer so i did just that. afterwards i was persuaded to make clothes for some guy, he had his friend pay though i ended up giving the money back, because his request was just brutal... ly hard to make. darrian thinks i'm useless, that im just some dumb soldier boy. i think i'll prove him wrong having fun down there? i said to some guy he had built some monster contraption need something he asked flesh thats what i heard as if it was being chewed on when i went in, i saw what must had been 20-30 spiders and they were all too big to get through i also saw the queen spider, and i slew them all", ""),
        StaticBook("Xight's Journal", "Xight", "Day 1 \n \n I have ventured into the capital of Oren, Al'khazar. A wierd city indeed, with people bustling about everywhere. I have toured the city, looking for work and ways in which I can help. I hear that there are many undead minions plauging the oren mine, perhaps i shall go there so are many undead minions plauging the old Oren Mines. Perhaps I shall pay it a visit. \n \n Day 2 \n \n I have travelled out of Al'khazar and am heading towards the mines. I should be there by nightfall, hopefully before those undead minions come out to play. I have been in the mines for days, clearing out the vast number of undead there. I am in need of food supplies now, and shall head back into town when I see that the work done here is pleasing to my eyes. \n \n Day 3 \n \n I have just left the Oren Mines, and am heading back toward the city of Al'khazar. Hopefully I will make it back before midnight. \n \n Day 4 \n \n I have returned to AL'khazar, and a devastating scene. The undead have left their mark, after their relentless assult on the Capital of Oren. The main gate, literally blown to pieces during their assult. Upon seeing this, I have turned around, and am traveling away, to other cities. I have not forgotten my soul purpose for visiting these cities... I have built a small shelter to the left of the Royal section of Al'khazar, outside the city walls On top of the mountain next to the sanctuary. I think I will be heading to King's Road, to search for answers there. \n \n Day 5 \n \n I have come across a group of 4 very odd looking men... They seem to be looking for trouble for the orcs. I have decided to follow them. \n \n Disaster! They have noticed me and thrown me deep into an underground cave which looks as though it has no end. Pray to the god of Aegis that i make it out alive... \n \n Day 7 \n \n I have made it out alive. Barely, but alive. It seems as though it will take awhile for my wounds to heal, before I am ready to travel again. \n \n Day 10 \n \n I have healed my wounds, and am ready to depart from my shelter again. This time, for the great city of Alras. \n \n I have made it to Alras within a day's travel, and boy! What a sight to behold. The city is magnificent, but somewhat deserted... It is late, travelling out of the city, I have come across a King, High_King_Syrio. He has offered me some work, the collection of wool. Although it does not suit me much, I shall carry out the task nonetheless. Hunting sheep and whatever beast I come across.", ""),
