        StaticBook("Zatazen's journal", "verrenn", "I miss her... i cant show it... i cant tell anyone... \n i am deaply saddend... i wish i could see her again... but... i have to kill my brothers first... i... love her... i dont know what i am going to do *a couple of tears are on the page* \n if only i could see her one more time... *the rest of the pages are torn out* \n *there are a few words on the back of the back cover*", ""),
        StaticBook("Zatazen's journal 2", "verrenn", "I can hear her in my dreams... i cant escape them... one moring when i woke up... i saw her... i could not think of anything to say... all i could say was her name... i reached to touch her hair... she vanished... i dont think i can take this anymore... I am ont the brink of losing my self... the next day i couldnt do anything... i missed her so much i was... crying... I am losing the will to find her... she is so close... but to far to where i cant see her... hre voice is all that keeps me just afloat... just to where i can continue... I am losing her... *a few tears are on the pages* i cant take hearing her... but not seeing her... i need to keep fighting... fighting to see her again... please... give me a sign your out the re atleast an image... i want to see you again kendra... that is all i want... all i want is to see you again...", ""),
        StaticBook("Zelphar's Aegisian Travels", "Paulie2499", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Zerial", "rocktoke", "Me is an orc, me has always been searching for answers about where my parents went . Me gain many friends while i was a kid, one of them Gezmar. he showed me a tower, the Shaman tower . me wanted to become one and seek spirits. he introduced me to a novice shaman, named draygo. I followed this shaman to a place called \"The Shrine\" . he started to ask me questions about my parents, but since i didnt know anything about them i didnt answer. then suddenly he told me to stand in a circle or 8 torches, and pray to Krug I started to pray.... I found myself in a huge temple, i became dizzy very fast. i suddenly woke up with Draygo yelling \"Wake up!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Zerion's Life", "PyroFuzion", "Zerion's life began in a village not far from Kal'Urguan. His father trained him up to fight and protect himself. His mother taught Zerion how to make and cook food. It all began when Zerion's family and village set out on a ship to find food for their  village. They battled through rough seas and fought dangerous creatures. But... the next day there was a great, powerful storm, which left them ship-wrecked. Zerion managed to swim away, surviving off natural fruit and nuts. With Zerion's family and village dead, Zerion found the courage to find a new home... a new village. Zerion finds himself in Aegis once again. After Zerion reported the tragic news to his surrounding villages, he became a member of Holmes! The Holmes was very welcoming to Zerion, they gave him a room and food, they even took care of him if was hurt or sick.  Zerion found he was a good farmer! He was always replenishing the food  chests. He enjoyed being social and friendly to the other citizens of Aegis. One day, Zerion had to take a message from The Wandering Wizard to The Kings of Oren and Kal'Urguan! Zerion enjoys meeting and greeting people. Zerion used to provide a touring service for people who were new to Aegis just like Zerion. Zerion is enjoying his life as being a Holmes! Zerion spends most of his time mining or  harvesting crops.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zevandir's Adventure", "zevandir", "Today is the day I begin this journal, but not the day I started my adventure. \nLet me start from the beggining, It was a nice day, and Laurelin seemed to be without room for adventure. So I set off. \nI set off with my armour and weapon, basic tools and some food, plus my tent of course, My journey also had a very distinct purpose. The world of mortals and feeble beings was growing o So my quest was to discover the homes of the Ascended and the Undead, or die trying. So after visiting my home and friends in Kramoroe, I began walking along the King's Road. I saw no bandits, so my walk passed quickly, and before long, I arrived at Alstion. This is a sma ll town, close to the borders of Oren, and there was little for me there. Continuing on it began to rain. Seeking shelter, I ran for a huge tower. THe prison tower of winterfell. A man there sheltered me before giving me directions to the city of the Ascended. However, these directions were vague, and I chose to ingore them and continue on towards where I hoped the outpost of the Undead might be. I passed many small huts and a large castle, but the outpost of the Undead remained elusive. I am injured now, and slightly scared. I have slain many spawn of Iblees, but it is time to start heading for home. My supplies are dwindling, and I feel hoplessly lost. It is only the sun that guides me now. I cannot remember the number of nights I have spent in this frosted land, and I feel that I get no closer regardless of the steps I take. It is a hopeless journey, and yet one that fills me with dread. I fear I shall have no more luck with finding the Ascended city. Maybe it is time to settle down, and stop this strange wondering and travelling. I am currently running along a mountain spin, with vast plains on either side. The view is amazing but night falls, and I long for my treetop home. \n \nI have made very little progress today, crossing but a small ocean and a ridge of hills. It is due to my sickness, I believe, I was greatly injured a few nights ago, trying to steal precious hours of travel. I paid for that with a weeks rest, and now I have decided to order this journal. As such I shall write tomorrow night's entry with a different format, in the hopes a reader of my journal amy better understand my adventures. \nDay 12 \nThank the God and all the Aenguls of the sky! I have found a hut! I must be nearing civilization! It shall not be long now before I can resume my search for the city of the Ascended I sleep now, but soon I shall awake to continue on to my destination. \nDay 15 \nMy journey has come to nothing, I arrived at my old camp, a thousand miles from where I started. I shall search again, but not today.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zevandir's Log", "zevandir", "\n5th July in History", ""),
        StaticBook("Zevandir's Newbie Guide", "zevandir", "Hello new traveller of Aegis! Aegis is a vast and wonderful world, with much to explore. This book is a wonderful investment, as it will teach you the basics and help  you get started. \nYou have probably already chosen a name and race. If you havn't, lets do that now. \nAll the commands in Aegis are preceeded by / so we type /setname <RP Name. <Race> remember not to include the '<' and '>' symbols. Well done! Now, lets go over some rules. The main rule of Aegis is RolePlaying. One definition of RolePlaying from the Oxford dictionary is 'The changing of one' behaviour to fulfill a social role.' RP'ing generally means acting a certain way to play a certain role. This is the main rule of Aegis, and failing to comply will probably get you banned. Please note that the World of Aegis is patrolled by multiple military groups, you can join one of these military groups, a great way to earn Minas and have fun. Minas is the in game currency, and is used to buy houses, shops and goods. Minas is also what bandits want when they attack, and they will RP holding you up. A Bandit role is very carefully monitored, you MUST RP banditing someone. Random PVP and killing will get you banned, and Bandits prefer to loot and steal before fighting. \nRaces. Races are the main factions of Aegis. Dwarves, Elves, Orcs and Humans. Each faction has its own Kingdom, and each faction is rather different from the others. For example, the Elves are rule by an Elven Council and a High Prince, with tree-like architectur e. The Orcs live in the desert and use sand and sandstone, ruled by a dictator-like Rex. Aegis is a wonderful land, full of diverse cultures and people. However, Aegis is also inhabited by the Spawn of Iblees [Read the History of Aegis for more]. These evil beings are exactly that, evil. They will try to kill you on sight, and are very strong. The spawn of Iblees are also different from regular monsters. \nZombies hit harder, reach further and are very resilient to your attacks. \nCreepers do not damage the land, do slightly less damage, but have far more health. Meaning they cang et closer and explode before you can kill them. \nSpiders are best avoided unless behind a fence, these demons of the night fall onto your head and rip out your brains, they are faster, stronger and have more health than you, but you have skill, cunning and a will to survive, making you far more dangerous if properly trained. You are probably thinking, I guess I'll just make a dirt shelter for the night. Well, in Aegis, you can't. You must buy some form of house in a protected city, or venture into the dangerous, unrpotected wilds, where no guards patrol and your stuff isnt safe. Houses cost anything from 1,000 to 30,000 Minas, and until then you will have to risk living in the wilds or someone elses house. There are also Inns along the main roads that service travellers, and you could pay a small fee to live there until you own your own home. Well, you are now ready for the World of Aegis! \nLook out for the new series, Races! \nAll written and transcribed by Zevandir. All rights registered.", ""),
